    "homepage_text": "Xiyao Wang's Homepage\nXiyao Wang\nHome\nPublications\nCV\nXiyao Wang (王玺尧)\nEmail: xywang@umd.edu\nGoogle Scholar\nGithub\nAbout me\nI am a third year Ph.D. student in\nUniversity of Maryland, College Park\n, \n                        where I am fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Furong Huang\n. \n                        My research interest is foundation models and reinforcement learning, including world models for robotics, halluciantion in vision language models, large language model and vision-language model reasoning, etc. \n                        My long-term goal is to make agents more efficient and reliable.\n                        Before that, I received my Bachelor’s degree in Network Engineering from\nUniversity of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC)\n.\nI am currently on the industry job market, seeking research scientist positions starting in May 2026.\nHere is my\nCV\n. Please feel free to contact me if you think I could be a good fit.\nNews and Highlights\n[2025.03]\nLLaVa-Critic is accepted by CVPR 2025!\n[2025.01]\n2 paper accepted by NAACL 2025!\n[2024.04]\n1 paper accepted by ACL 2024!\n[2024.04]\n2 paper accepted by ICML 2024!\n[2024.01]\n2 paper accepted by ICLR 2024 (one as spotlight)!\n[2023.11]\n1 paper accepted by NeurIPS 2023!\n[2023.05]\n1 paper accepted by ICML 2023! See you in Hawaii!\n[2023.01]\n1 paper accepted by ICLR 2023!\n[2022.01]\n1 paper accepted by ICLR 2022. Many thanks to my collaborators!\n[2021.03]\nWe won Runner-Up Award in NTIRE 2021 Challenge on Nonhomogeneous Dehazing and our paper got accepted by New Trends in Image Restoration and Enhancement Workshop in CVPR 2021! Many thanks to my Teammates!\nPublications\nPlease see\nhere\nfor a full list of my publications.\nICLR 2024\nCOPlanner: Plan to Roll Out Conservatively but to Explore Optimistically for Model-Based RL.\nXiyao Wang\n, Ruijie Zheng, Yanchao Sun, Ruonan Jia, Wichayaporn Wongkamjan, Huazhe Xu, and Furong Huang.\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations, 2024\nPaper\nCode\nHTML\nICML 2023\nLive in the Moment: Learning Dynamics Model Adapted to Evolving Policy.\nXiyao Wang\n, Wichayaporn Wongkamjan, Ruonan Jia, and Furong Huang.\nIn the 40th International Conference on Machine Learning, 2023\nPaper\nCode\nHTML\nICLR 2023\nIs Model Ensemble Necessary? Model-based RL via a Single Model with Lipschitz Regularized Value Function.\nRuijie Zheng*,\nXiyao Wang*\n, Huazhe Xu, and Furong Huang.  (* Equal Contribution)\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations, 2023\nPaper\n(Code coming soon!)\nHTML\nICLR 2022\nTransfer RL across Observation Feature Spaces via Model-Based Regularization.\nYanchao Sun, Ruijie Zheng,\nXiyao Wang\n, Andrew Cohen, and Furong Huang.\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations, 2022\nPaper\nCode\nHTML\nCVPRW 2021\nA Two-branch Neural Network for Non-homogeneous Dehazing via Ensemble Learning.\nYankun Yu, Huan Liu, Minghan Fu, Jun Chen,\nXiyao Wang\n, Keyan Wang.\nIn New Trends in Image Restoration and Enhancement Workshop, CVPR 2021\nPaper\n(Code coming soon!)\nPlease see\nhere\nfor a full list of my publications."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Huazhe Xu::http://hxu.rocks/": {
