    "homepage_text": "Xueyi Liu\nXueyi Liu\nI am a third-year Ph.D. student in the\nIIIS\nat Tsinghua University, advised by Prof.\nLi Yi\n. Previously, I obtained my bachelor's degree in Computer Science from the\nCS Department\n, THU. My research interests center around computer vision and embodied AI.\nEmail\n/\nGithub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nX\n/\nWeChat\nResearch\nDexNDM: Closing the Reality Gap for Dexterous In-Hand Rotation via Joint-Wise Neural Dynamics Model\nXueyi Liu\n, He Wang, Li Yi\nICLR\n, 2026\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nslides\nTL;DR\n: \n                Neural Sim-to-Real Unlocks Unprecedented Dexterity.\nDexTrack: Towards Generalizable Neural Tracking Control for Dexterous Manipulation from Human References\nXueyi Liu\n, Jianibieke Adalibieke, Qianwei Han, Yuzhe Qin, Li Yi\nICLR\n, 2025\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nslides\nTL;DR\n: \n                DexTrack presents a neural tracking controller for dexterous robot hand manipulation, with high adaptability, generalization, and robustness.\nQuasiSim: Parameterized Quasi-Physical Simulators for Dexterous Manipulations Transfer\nXueyi Liu\n, Kangbo Lyu, Jieqiong Zhang, Tao Du, Li Yi\nECCV\n, 2024\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\n🤗demo\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nslides\nTL;DR\n: \n                QuasiSim presents a parameterized family of quasi-physical simulators and a physics curriculum programmed from that family for transferring kinematics-only human manipulation demonstrations to dexterous robot hand simulations.\nGeneOH Diffusion: Towards Generalizable Hand-Object Interaction Denoising via Denoising Diffusion\nXueyi Liu\nand Li Yi\nICLR\n, 2024\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\n🤗demo\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nslides\n/\nposter\nTL;DR\n: Generalizable HOI denoising model.\nFew-Shot Physically-Aware Articulated Mesh Generation via Hierarchical Deformation\nXueyi Liu\n, \n              Bin Wang, He Wang, Li Yi\nICCV\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nslides\nTL;DR\n: Few-shot articulated object generation via hierarchical deformation.\nSelf-Supervised Category-Level Articulated Object Pose Estimation with Part-Level SE(3) Equivariance\nXueyi Liu\n, \n              Ji Zhang, Ruizhen Hu, Haibin Huang, He Wang, Li Yi\nICLR\n, 2023\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\nmedia\n(in Chinese)\nTL;DR\n: Part-level SE(3) equivariance for self-supervised articulated object pose estimation.\nAutoGPart: Intermediate Supervision Search for Generalizable 3D Part Segmentation\nXueyi Liu\n, \n              Xiaomeng Xu, Anyi Rao, Chuang Gan, Li Yi\nCVPR\n, 2022\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\narXiv\n/\nvideo\nTL;DR\n: Search for intermediate supervisions to improve the generalizability of part segmentation networks.\nSimilarity-aware Positive Instance Sampling for Graph Contrastive Pre-training\nXueyi Liu\n, \n              Yu Rong, Tingyang Xu, Fuchun Sun, Wenbing Huang, Junzhou Huang\ncode\n/\narXiv\nTL;DR\n: Sample positive instances from a hierarchical graph encoding graph instance similarities for graph contrastive learning.\nNetwork representation learning: A macro and micro view\nXueyi Liu\nand Jie Tang\nAI Open\n, 2021\narXiv\nTL;DR\n: A comprehensive survey on graph representation learning.\nUnderstanding WeChat User Preferences and “Wow” Diffusion\nFanjin Zhang, Jie Tang,\nXueyi Liu\n, Zhenyu Hou, Yuxiao Dong, Jing Zhang, Xiao Liu, Ruobing Xie, Kai Zhuang, Xu Zhang, Leyu Lin, Philip S. Yu\nTKDE\n, 2021\narXiv\nTL;DR\n: Predict WeChat users' click and ``wow'' behaviours.\nHonors/Awards\nOutstanding Bachelor Thesis of Tsinghua University, 2023\nOutstanding Graduate of Tsinghua University, 2023\nComprehensive Excellence Scholarship, 2020,2021\nAcademic Excellence Scholarship, 2022\nServices\nReviewer:\nCoRL, ICML, ICLR, NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, ACM TIST\nTemplate stolen from\nJon Barron\n. Thanks for stopping by :)\nLast updated: Feb, 2026"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Ji Zhang::https://jizhang.art/": {
