    "homepage_text": "Wei Li's Homepage\nWei Li（李伟）\nAbout Me\nI am an Associate Professor at the Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences. My journey in this field began at the same institute, where I earned my Ph.D. in 2019.\nMy research primarily explores the fields of\nCross-Modal Generation\n,\nNatural Language Generation\n, and\nMulti-modal Learning\n. A significant aspect of my work is dedicated to UNIfied-MOdal learning (\nUNIMO\n). This approach aims to integrate various data modalities, such as text, images, and other modalities, for advanced multimodal understanding and generation.\nFor a detailed look at my work and researches, feel free to explore my academic profiles:\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nDBLP\n. If you have any inquiries or wish to discuss academic collaborations, please do not hesitate to\nemail me\n.\nNews:\n[2024.05.16]\n4 paper\nhave been accepted by ACL 2024, 3 Main Conference + 1 Findings.\n[2023.05.02]\n1 paper\n(WeCheck) for NLG factuality evaluation, has been accepted by ACL 2023, Main Conference.\n[2023.04.27]\n1 paper\n(FactGen) for faithful text generation, has been accepted by Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research, 2023.\n[2022.10.07]\n3 paper\nhave been accepted by EMNLP 2022, 1 Main Conference + 2 Findings.\n[2022.03.10]\nA survey\non faithfulness in natural language generation has been published on arxiv.\n[2022.02.24]\n2 paper\nhave been accepted by ACL 2022, 1 Main Conference + 1 Findings.\n[2021.08.26]\n1 paper\nhas been accepted by EMNLP 2021, Main Conference.\n[2021.05.06]\n3 paper\nhave been accepted by ACL 2021, Main Conference.\n[2021.04.14]\n1 paper\nhas been accepted by SIGIR 2021, Full Paper.\n[2020.04.03]\n1 paper\nhas been accepted by ACL 2020, Main Conference.\nPublications:\n[ACL 2024]\nWei Li*\n, Xue Xu*, Jiachen Liu, Xinyan Xiao.\nUNIMO-G: Unified Image Generation through Multimodal Conditional Diffusion.\n[\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2024]\nWenhao Wu,\nWei Li*\n, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Sujian Li.\nInstructEval: Instruction-Tuned Text Evaluator from Human Preference.\n[\nPDF\n]\n[ACL 2024]\nXuhui Jiang, Yinghan Shen, Zhichao Shi, Chengjin Xu,\nWei Li*\n, Zixuan Li, Jian Guo, Huawei Shen, Yuanzhuo Wang.\nUnlocking the Power of Large Language Models for Entity Alignment.\n[\nPDF\n]\n[ACL 2024]\nZixuan Li, Yutao Zeng, Yuxin Zuo, Weicheng Ren, Wenxuan Liu, Miao Su, Yucan Guo, Yantao Liu, Xiang Li, Zhilei Hu, Long Bai,\nWei Li*\n, Yidan Liu, Pan Yang, Xiaolong Jin, Jiafeng Guo, Xueqi Cheng.\nKnowCoder: Coding Structured Knowledge into LLMs for Universal Information Extraction.\n[\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2023]\nWenhao Wu,\nWei Li\n, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Sujian Li and Yajuan Lyu.\nWeCheck: Strong Factual Consistency Checker via Weakly Supervised Learning.\n. Main Confereance of ACL 2023, long paper. [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[JAIR 2023]\nZhibin Lan,\nWei Li\n, Jinsong Su, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Wenhao Wu, Yajuan Lyu.\nFactGen: Faithful Text Generation by Factuality-aware Pre-training and Contrastive Ranking Fine-tuning.\nJournal of Artificial Intelligence Research, 2023.\n[Arxiv 2022]\nWei Li\n, Xue Xu, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Hu Yang, Guohao Li, Zhanpeng Wang, Zhifan Feng, Qiaoqiao She, Yajuan Lyu, Hua Wu.\nUPainting: Unified Text-to-Image Diffusion Generation with Cross-modal Guidance.\n[\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[EMNLP 2022]\nWenhao Wu,\nWei Li\n, Jiachen Liu, Xinyan Xiao, Sujian Li and Yajuan Lyu.\nPrecisely the Point: Adversarial Augmentations for Faithful and Informative Text Generation.\n. Main Confereance of EMNLP 2022, long paper.\n[EMNLP 2022]\nWenhao Wu,\nWei Li\n, Jiachen Liu, Xinyan Xiao, Ziqiang Cao, Sujian Li and Hua Wu.\nFRSUM: Towards Faithful Abstractive Summarization via Enhancing Factual Robustness\n. Findings of EMNLP 2022, long paper.\n[EMNLP 2022]\nZixuan Li, Zhongni Hou, Saiping Guan, Xiaolong Jin, Weihua Peng, Long Bai, Yajuan Lyu,\nWei Li\n, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nHiSMatch: Historical Structure Matching based Temporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning\n. Findings of EMNLP 2022, long paper [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[Arxiv 2022]\nWei Li\n, Wenhao Wu, Moye Chen, Jiachen Liu, Xinyan Xiao and Hua Wu.\nFaithfulness in Natural Language Generation: A Systematic Survey of Analysis, Evaluation and Optimization Methods\n(52 pages). [\nPDF\n]\n[ACL 2022]\nWei Li\n, Can Gao, Guochenng Niu, Xinyan Xiao, Hao Liu, Jiachen Liu, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang.\nEnd-to-End Unified Vision-Language Grounded Learning\n. Findings of ACL 2022, long paper [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2022]\nZixuan Li, Saiping Guan, Xiaolong Jin, Weihua Peng, Yajuan Lyu, Yong Zhu, Long Bai,\nWei Li\n, Jiafeng Guo, Xueqi Cheng.\nComplex Evolutional Pattern Learning for Temporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning\n. ACL 2022, short paper, Main Conference. [\nPDF\n]\n[EMNLP 2021]\nMoye Chen*,\nWei Li*\n, Jiachen Liu, Xinyan Xiao, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang.\nSgSum: Transforming Multi-document Summarization into Sub-graph Selection\n. EMNLP 2021 long paper, Main Conference. (* indicates equal contribution) [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2021]\nWei Li*\n, Can Gao*, Guochenng Niu*, Xinyan Xiao*, Hao Liu, Jiachen Liu, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang.\nUNIMO: Towards Unified-Modal Understanding and Generation via Cross-Modal Contrastive Learning\n. ACL 2021 long paper, Main Conference. (* indicates equal contribution) [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2021]\nWenhao Wu,\nWei Li\n, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Ziqiang Cao, Sujian Li, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang.\nBASS: Boosting Abstractive Summarization with Unified Semantic Graph\n. ACL 2021 long paper, Main Conference. [\nPDF\n]\n[ACL 2021]\nZixuan Li, Xiaolong Jin, Saiping Guan,\nWei Li\n, Jiafeng Guo, Yuanzhuo Wang and Xueqi Cheng.\nSearch from History and Reason for Future: Two-stage Reasoning on Temporal Knowledge Graphs\n. ACL 2021 long paper, Main Conference. [\nPDF\n]\n[SIGIR 2021]\nZixuan Li, Xiaolong Jin,\nWei Li\n, Saiping Guan, Jiafeng Guo, Huawei Shen, Yuanzhuo Wang and Xueqi Cheng.\nTemporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning Based on Evolutional Representation Learning\n. SIGIR2021 Full paper. [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[ACL 2020]\nWei Li\n, Xinyan Xiao, Jiachen Liu, Hua Wu and Haifeng Wang.\nLeveraging Graph to Improve Abstractive Multi-Document Summarization\n. ACL 2020 long paper, Main Conference. [\nPDF\n] [\ncode\n]\n[FGCS 2020]\nWei Li\nand Hai Zhuge.\nProbabilistic inference on uncertain semantic link network and its application in event identification\n. Future Generation Computer Systems, pp: 32-42, 2020\n[TKDE 2019]\nWei Li\nand Hai Zhuge.\nAbstractive multi-document summarization based on semantic link network\n. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering, 2019\n[IEEE Access 2019]\nWei Li\n, Dezhi Cheng, Lei He, Yuanzhuo Wang and Xiaolong Jin.\nJoint Event Extraction Based on Hierarchical Event Schemas from FrameNet\n. IEEE Access, 2019\n[EMNLP 2018]\nWei Li\n, Xinyan Xiao, Yajuan Lyu and Yuanzhuo Wang.\nImproving neural abstractive document summarization with explicit information selection modeling\n. Proceedings of EMNLP2018, the 2018 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing.\n[EMNLP 2018]\nWei Li\n, Xinyan Xiao, Yajuan Lyu and Yuanzhuo Wang.\nImproving neural abstractive document summarization with structural regularization\n. Proceedings of EMNLP2018, the 2018 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing.\n[COLING 2016]\nWei Li\n, Lei He and Hai Zhuge.\nAbstractive news summarization based on event semantic link network\n. Proceedings of COLING 2016, the 26th International Conference on Computational Linguistics: Technical Papers.\n[COLING 2016]\nLei He,\nWei Li\nand Hai Zhuge.\nExploring differential topic models for comparative summarization of scientific papers\n. Proceedings of COLING 2016, the 26th International Conference on Computational Linguistics: Technical Papers.\n[EMNLP 2015]\nWei Li\n.\nAbstractive multi-document summarization with semantic information extraction\n. Proceedings of EMNLP2015, the 2015 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing.\nExperience:\n[Nov 2023 - Now]: Associate Professor, Institute of Computing Technology,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n,\nPersonal Pages\n[July 2021 - Nov. 2023]: Senior Engineer, NLP & KG Department,\nBaidu Inc.\n[July 2019 - Oct. 2021]: Postdoc,\nBaidu Inc. and Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications\n. Supervisor: Prof.\nHaifeng Wang\nand\nJunping Du\n[Sept. 2012 - June 2019]: PhD, Institute of Computing Technology,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n. Supervisor: Prof.\nYuanzhuo Wang\n[Sept. 2008 - June 2012]: B.E, School of Computer Science,\nWuhan University"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Linchao Zhu::https://ffmpbgrnn.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://ffmpbgrnn.github.io/",
