  "deep_homepage::Kaisheng Ma::https://group.iiis.tsinghua.edu.cn/~maks/leader.html": {
    "homepage": "https://group.iiis.tsinghua.edu.cn/~maks/leader.html",
    "all_emails": [
      "kaisheng@tsinghua.edu.cn",
      "kaishengthu@163.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "ARChip Lab-About our Leader\nWelcome to ARChip Lab\nEmail: kaishengthu@163.com\nARChip Lab\nHome\nAbout our Lab\nAbout our Leader\nPeople\nResearch Directions\nPublications\nProjects\nJoin us\nNews\nAbout our leader\nKaisheng Ma - Principal Investigator\nBe Confident !\nWith My Doctoral Superviser Vijay N.\nSupercomputing Center\nBio:\nKaisheng Ma is a tenured associate professor of computer science in Institute for\nInterdisciplinary Information Sciences\n(IIIS),\nTsinghua University\n. He leads the\nAlgorithms, Architecture and Chipset Lab (ARChip)\n. His research interests lie in the interdisciplinary fields of human-machine interface (HMI), brain-spired AI algorithm design, computer vision for self-driving, compact model design, computer architecture and microelectronics. He believes in vertical integration for systems, with a special emphasis on implanted medical and neural devices, and chip level system solutions for self-driving systems. He publishes papers on conferences including NeurIPS, ICCV, AAAI, CVPR, ISCA, ASPLOS, MICRO, HPCA, DAC etc.\nHe received his Ph.D. in Computer Science and Engineering at the Pennsylvania State University, following Professor\nVijaykrishnan Nanrayanan\n@ Penn State,\nYuan Xie\n@ UCSB (Now at Alibaba\nDAMO Computing Lab\n),\nJack Sampson\n@ Penn State. His previous research on Nonvolatile Processor and Energy Harvesting won\n2018 EDAA Best Dissertation Award\n(\nPenn State News\n).\nTalks:\nTitle: Knowledge Self-distillation and Scalable Neural Networks: Towards Accurate, Efficient and Robust Neural Networks\nTitle: Sparse-aware DNN Architecture Design: Insights from Resource Utilization and Memory Bandwidth\nNews:\n[Springer Book Chapter] Kaisheng Ma, Shuangchen Li, Vijaykrishnan Narayanan, and Yuan Xie. \"Nonvolatile Processor Architecture Exploration for Energy-Harvesting Application Scenarios\". In Embedded, Cyber-Physical, and IoT Systems, pp. 175-202. Springer, Cham, 2020. is awarded as\ntop one percent high-impact publications in Springer Nature Research Highlights from China Collection Award 2020.\n(\"Top one percent highly cited papers in their academic fields as of July/August 2020, according to Essential Science Indicators, and highly downloaded, cited and mentioned book chapters, according to SN Insights\".)\nContact information:\nEmail: kaishengthu@163.com | kaisheng@tsinghua.edu.cn\nOffice: Tsinghua University, Beijing, China.\nÂ© Copyright  2020  ARChip Lab  -  All rights reserved"
  },
