    "homepage_text": "Xiongye's Home Page\nXiongye Xiao\nxxiao9@utk.edu\nGoogle Scholar\nI am a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Min H. Kao Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science at the University of Tennessee, Knoxville (UTK). Prior to joining UTK, I received my Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering from the University of Southern California and my B.S. in Control Science and Engineering from Zhejiang University. My research focuses on AI for Science, Network Science, and Machine Learning, with a goal of developing advanced physical, mathematical, and computational tools to study multiscale structures and dynamics and map them to functions (see my\nresearch vision\n). My work primarily involves complex network analysis, neural operators, multimodal learning, and generative modeling, while also exploring their applications in various scientific fileds including neuroscience and materials science.\nPublications\nAwards\nMentorship\nBio\n-\nInspired\nAI\n[\n3\n,\n19\n]\nMaterial\nDiscovering\n[13]\nComplex\nSystems\nModeling\n[\n2\n,\n26\n]\nFunctions\nStructures\nDynamics\nTheoretical\nFoundations and\nMethods\nApplications and\nImpact  Areas\nObjectives\nGraph theory;\nComplexity analysis\n[\n1\n,\n10\n]\nAdvanced AI models\n[\n9\n,\n11\n,\n17\n]\nNeural operators\n[\n2\n,\n4\n,\n7\n]\nMaterial Science\nStructure\n-\nproperty\nLaws\n[\n13\n,\n16\n,\n18\n,\n23\n]\nBioscience\nGene + Protein +\nBrain\nnetworks\n[\n1\n,\n8\n,\n14\n,\n15\n,\n24\n]\nScientific AI\nScience for AI\n[\n6\n]\nAI\nNetwork Analysis\nPDE Learning\n📄 Theoretical Foundations and Methods\n[\n1\n]\nDeciphering the Generating Rules and Functionalities of Complex Networks\nNature Scientific Reports\n, 2021\nXiongye Xiao\n, Hanlong Chen, and Paul Bogdan\n[\n2\n]\nCoupled Multiwavelet Neural Operator Learning for Coupled Partial Differential Equations\nICLR\n, 2023\nXiongye Xiao\n, Defu Cao, Ruochen Yang, Gaurav Gupta, Gengshuo Liu, Chenzhong Yin, Radu Balan, Paul Bogdan\n[\n3\n]\nNeuro-Inspired Information-Theoretic Hierarchical Perception for Multimodal Learning\nICLR\n, 2024\nXiongye Xiao\n, Gengshuo Liu, Gaurav Gupta, Defu Cao, Shixuan Li, Yaxing Li, Tianqing Fang, Mingxi Cheng, Paul Bogdan\n[\n4\n]\nMultiwavelet-based Operator Learning for Differential Equations\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2021\n[Spotlight, top 2%]\nGaurav Gupta,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Radu Balan, and Paul Bogda\n[\n5\n]\nA Structure-aware Framework for Learning Device Placements on Computation Graphs\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2024\nShukai Duan†, Heng Ping†, Nikos Kanakaris†,\nXiongye Xiao\n†, Peiyu Zhang, Panagiotis Kyriakis, Nesreen K Ahmed, Guixiang Ma, Mihai Capota, Shahin Nazarian, Theodore L Willke, Paul Bogdan\n[\n6\n]\nNeuron-based Multifractal Analysis of Neuron Interaction Dynamics in Large Models\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR)\n, 2025\nXiongye Xiao\n, Heng Ping, Chenyu Zhou, Defu Cao, Yaxing Li, Yizhuo Zhou, Shixuan Li, Nikos Kanakaris, Paul Bogdan\n[\n7\n]\nNon-Linear Operator Approximations for Initial Value Problems\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR)\n, 2022\nGaurav Gupta,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Radu Balan, and Paul Bogda\n[\n8\n]\nGenerator Based Approach to Analyze Mutations in Genomic Datasets\nNature Scientific Reports\n, 2021\nSiddharth Jain†,\nXiongye Xiao\n†, Paul Bogdan, and Jehoshua Bruck\n[\n9\n]\nMulti-scale Generative Modeling for Fast Sampling\narXiv preprint\n, 2024\nXiongye Xiao\n, Shixuan Li, Luzhe Huang, Gengshuo Liu, Trung-Kien Nguyen, Yi Huang, Di Chang, Mykel J Kochenderfer, Paul Bogdan\n[\n10\n]\nGraph Theoretical Description of Phase Transitions in Complex Multiscale Phases with Supramolecular Assemblies\nAdvanced Science\n, 2024\nRuochen Yang, Kalil Bernardino,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Weverson R Gomes, Davi A Mattoso, Nicholas A Kotov, Paul Bogdan, André F de Moura\n[\n11\n]\nMulti-scale Conditional Generative Modeling for Microscopic Image Restoration\narXiv preprint\n, 2024\nLuzhe Huang,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Shixuan Li, Jiawen Sun, Yi Huang, Aydogan Ozcan, Paul Bogdan\n[\n12\n]\nMulti-scale Conditional Generative Modeling for Microscopic Image Restoration\nICASSP 2024-2024 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing\n(ICASSP)\n, 2024\nAnzhe Cheng, Heng Ping, Zhenkun Wang,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Chenzhong Yin, Shahin Nazarian, Mingxi Cheng, Paul Bogdan\n📄 Scientific Applications\n[\n13\n]\nBiomorphic Structural Batteries for Robotics\nScience Robotics\n, 2020\nMingqiang Wang, Drew Vecchio, Chunyan Wang, Ahmet Emre,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Zaixing Jiang, Paul Bogdan, Yudong Huang, and Nicholas A. Kotov\n[\n14\n]\nNetwork Science Characteristics of Brain-derived Neuronal Cultures Deciphered from Quantitative Phase Imaging Data\nNature Scientific Reports\n, 2020\nChenzhong Yin†,\nXiongye Xiao\n†, Valeriu Balaban, Mikhail E. Kandel, Young Jae Lee, Gabriel Popescu, and Paul Bogdan\n[\n15\n]\nUnifying Structural Descriptors for Biological and Bioinspired Nanoscale Complexes\nNature Computational Science\n, 2022\nMinjeong Cha, Emine Turali-Emre,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Ji-Young Kim, Paul Bogdan, Scott VanEpps, Angela Violi, Nicholas A. Kotov.\n[\n16\n]\nSpanning Network Gels from Nanoparticles and Graph Theoretical Qnalysis of Their Structure and Properties\nAdvanced Materials\n, 2022\nDrew A. Vecchio, Mark D. Hammig,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Anwesha Saha, Paul Bogdan, and Nicholas A. Kotov.\n[\n17\n]\nAI and the Clinical Immunology/Immunoinformatics for COVID-19\nArtificial Intelligence in Covid-19\nZikun Yang,\nXiongye Xiao\n, and Paul Bogdan\n[\n18\n]\nCoupled Self-Replication and Self-Assembly of Inorganic Nanoparticles into Biosimilar Networks\nAngewandte Chemie\n, 2024\nNicholas Kotov, Connor McGlothin,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Paul Bogdan, Kody Whisnant, Emine Turali-Emre, Dickson Owuor, Jun Lu, J Scott VanEpps, Drew Vecchio\n[\n19\n]\nLeader-Follower Neural Networks with Local Error Signals Inspired by Complex Collectives\narXiv preprint\n, 2023\nChenzhong Yin, Mingxi Cheng,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Xinghe Chen, Shahin Nazarian, Andrei Irimia, Paul Bogdan\n[\n20\n]\nLeveraging Reinforcement Learning and Large Language Models for Code Optimization\narXiv preprint\n, 2023\nShukai Duan, Nikos Kanakaris,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Heng Ping, Chenyu Zhou, Nesreen K Ahmed, Guixiang Ma, Mihai Capota, Theodore L Willke, Shahin Nazarian, Paul Bogdan\n[\n21\n]\nDiscovering Malicious Signatures in Software from Structural Interactions\nICASSP 2024-2024 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing\n(ICASSP)\n, 2024\nChenzhong Yin, Hantang Zhang, Mingxi Cheng,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Xinghe Chen, Xin Ren, Paul Bogdan\n[\n22\n]\nGenerator Based Approach to Analyze Mutations in Genomic Datasets\nNature Scientific Reports\n, 2021\nSiddharth Jain†,\nXiongye Xiao\n†, Paul Bogdan, and Jehoshua Bruck\n[\n23\n]\nGraph theory-based bio-derived solid lubricant\nMatter\nDhanush U Jamadgni, Paul Gregory,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Andrew Martin, Daisy Kiptoo, Alana M Jones, Kien Trung Nguyen, Souvik Banerjee, Anastasia Visheratina, Nancy Muyanja, Boyce Chang, Paul Bogdan, Nicholas A Kotov, Martin Thuo\n[\n24\n]\nSpiking dynamics of individual neurons reflect changes in the structure and function of neuronal networks\nNature Communications 16 (1), 6994\nRuochen Yang, Heng Ping,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Roozbeh Kiani, Paul Bogdan\n[\n25\n]\nHDLCoRe: A Training-Free Framework for Mitigating Hallucinations in LLM-Generated HDL\nIEEE International Conference on LLM-Aided Design, 2025\nHeng Ping, Shixuan Li, Peiyu Zhang, Anzhe Cheng, Shukai Duan, Nikos Kanakaris,\nXiongye Xiao\n, Wei Yang, Shahin Nazarian, Andrei Irimia, Paul Bogdan\n[\n26\n]\nEnd-to-End Learning Framework for Solving Non-Markovian Optimal Control\nICML 2025\nXiaole Zhang†, Peiyu Zhang†,\nXiongye Xiao\n† , Shixuan Li, Vasileios Tzoumas, Vijay Gupta, Paul Bogdan"
