  "deep_homepage::Xiao Liu::https://xxxiaol.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://xxxiaol.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "liuxiao@uchicago.edu",
      "lxlisa@pku.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/xxxiaol",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiao Liu\nXiao Liu (刘潇)\nEmail\n:\nliuxiao [AT] uchicago [DOT] edu / lxlisa [AT] pku [DOT] edu [DOT] cn\nI am a postdoctoral scholar at Data Science Institute, University of Chicago, working with Prof.\nChenhao Tan\nand Prof.\nJames Evans\n. I obtained my Ph.D. degree in Wangxuan Institute of Computer Technology, Peking University, advised by Prof.\nYansong Feng\nin 2025. I was a visiting Ph.D. student at University of California, Los Angeles, working with Prof.\nKai-Wei Chang\nin 2023. I received the BSc degree from School of Electronic Engineering and Computer Science, Peking University and BEc degree from National School of Development in 2020.\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nGithub\n] [\nX\n]\nResearch Interests\nI am deeply engaged in\nadvancing the complex reasoning abilities of language models\n, aiming to help humans with real-world challenges. My current research focuses on\ncausal reasoning with LLMs\nand\nAI for Innovation\n.\nSelected Publications\n(See\nGoogle Scholar\nfor the full list)\nRefTool: Enhancing Model Reasoning with Reference-Guided Tool Creation\nICLR 2026\nXiao Liu\n, Da Yin, Zirui Wu, Yansong Feng\nTool\n,\nQuantitative Reasoning\n,\nCausal Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nFrom Single to Societal: Analyzing Persona-Induced Bias in Multi-Agent Interactions\nAAAI 2026 (Oral)\nJiayi Li*,\nXiao Liu*\n, Yansong Feng\nMulti-agent\n,\nLLM for Social Good\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nImproving Research Idea Generation Through Data: An Empirical Investigation in Social Science\nAI4Science Workshop at Neurips 2025 (Spotlight)\nXiao Liu\n, Xinyi Dong, Xinyang Gao, Yansong Feng, Xun Pang\nAI for Innovation\n,\nQuantitative Reasoning\n[\npaper\n]\nRead it in Two Steps: Translating Extremely Low-Resource Languages with Code-Augmented Grammar Books\nACL 2025\nChen Zhang*, Jiuheng Lin*,\nXiao Liu\n, Zekai Zhang, Yansong Feng\nReasoning with Code\n,\nLLM for Social Good\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nEliciting and Improving the Causal Reasoning Abilities of Large Language Models with Conditional Statements\nComputational Linguistics 2025, Presented at ACL 2025\nXiao Liu\n, Da Yin, Chen Zhang, Yansong Feng, Dongyan Zhao\nCausal Reasoning\n,\nReasoning with Code\n[\npaper\n]\nAre LLMs Capable of Data-based Statistical and Causal Reasoning? Benchmarking Advanced Quantitative Reasoning with Data\nACL 2024 (Findings)\n,\nAI4Research workshop @ IJCAI 2024 Highlight Paper\nXiao Liu\n, Zirui Wu, Xueqing Wu, Pan Lu, Kai-Wei Chang, Yansong Feng\nQuantitative Reasoning\n,\nCausal Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nTeaching Large Language Models an Unseen Language on the Fly\nACL 2024 (Findings)\nChen Zhang,\nXiao Liu\n, Jiuheng Lin, Yansong Feng\nLLM for Social Good\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nCASA: Causality-driven Argument Sufficiency Assessment\nNAACL 2024\nXiao Liu\n, Yansong Feng, Kai-Wei Chang\nCausal Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nDynosaur: A Dynamic Growth Paradigm for Instruction-Tuning Data Curation\nEMNLP 2023\nDa Yin*,\nXiao Liu*\n, Fan Yin*, Ming Zhong*, Hritik Bansal, Jiawei Han, Kai-Wei Chang\nInstruction Tuning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nThe Magic of IF: Investigating Causal Reasoning Abilities in Large Language Models of Code\nACL 2023 (Findings)\nXiao Liu\n, Da Yin, Chen Zhang, Yansong Feng, Dongyan Zhao\nCausal Reasoning\n,\nReasoning with Code\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nCounterfactual Recipe Generation: Exploring Compositional Generalization in a Realistic Scenario\nEMNLP 2022\nXiao Liu\n, Yansong Feng, Jizhi Tang, Chengang Hu, Dongyan Zhao\nCausal Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n] [\nwebsite\n]\nThings not Written in Text: Exploring Spatial Commonsense from Visual Signals\nACL 2022\nXiao Liu\n, Da Yin, Yansong Feng, Dongyan Zhao\nSpatial Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nEverything Has a Cause: Leveraging Causal Inference in Legal Text Analysis\nNAACL 2021\nXiao Liu*\n, Da Yin*, Yansong Feng, Yuting Wu, Dongyan Zhao\nCausal Reasoning\n[\npaper\n] [\ncode\n]\nAcademic Services\nArea Chair\nACL Rolling Review\nReviewer\nACL, EMNLP, NAACL, COLM, ICLR, CSCW, Computational Linguistics, TKDD, TKDE, IPM\nVolunteer\nACL 2024, NAACL 2024, EMNLP 2022, ACL 2021, NAACL 2021, EMNLP 2020\nCo-Organizer\nAI & Scientific Discovery Online Seminar\nTeaching\nMentor\nData Science Clinic, University of Chicago, Winter 2026\nTeaching Assistant\nFoundations of Natural Language Processing, Peking University, Spring 2024\nTeaching Assistant\nEmpirical Methods for Natural Language Processing, Peking University, Spring 2023\nTeaching Assistant\nIntroduction to Computation B, Peking University, Fall 2020\nSelected Awards\nOutstanding Graduate\n, Peking University, 2025\nWangxuan Scholarship\n, Wangxuan Institute of Computer Technology, 2020\nNational Scholarship\n, Peking University, 2018\nWebsite design\n:\n✩\n✩\n✩"
