  "deep_homepage::Yang Gao::https://sites.google.com/site/yanggaoalex/home": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/site/yanggaoalex/home",
    "all_emails": [
      "gaoyang_alex@hotmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/yg211",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yang Gao\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYang Gao\nYang Gao (高扬)\nResearch Engineer, Google DeepMind\nPersonal Email: gaoyang_alex@hotmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nDBLP\nI am a Research Engineer at Google DeepMind, focusing on Reinforcement Learning for language models, and robust evaluation of AI systems. I joined Google Research in December 2021 and moved to DeepMind in June 2024 as part of the integration of Google Brain/Research and DeepMind. From 2021 to 2023, I was a key contributor to the design and implementation of Google Scholar's first neural-based system for paper recommendation and indexing. Since October 2023, my work has centered on Google Gemini, specifically on the development, improvement, and red-teaming of Reward Models and Verifiers.\nPrior to my industry experience, I held a Lecturer (Assistant Professor equivalent) position at\nRoyal Holloway University of London\n(2019-2021). My academic career also includes a postdoctoral fellowship at TU Darmstadt (2017-2019) in the Ubiquitous Knowledge Processing (\nUKP\n) Lab under the supervision of Prof. Iryna Gurevych, an Assistant Professorship at\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n(2015-2017), and doctoral research at Imperial College London (2011-2015) in the Computing, Logic and Argumentation (\nCLArg\n) Lab with Prof. Francesca Toni. For further details please refer to my\nCV\n.\nPublic service\n: I am actively involved in academic service, including co-founding the\nEval4NLP workshop series\n. For conference reviewing, I served as Publication Co-Chair for EMNLP 2020 and Area Chair for ACL 2020, in addition to serving on the Programme Committees of major AI/ML conferences such as NeurIPS, ICLR, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, IJCAI, KR, and AAAI. My journal reviewing contributions include serving as a\nStanding Reviewer\nfor Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics (TACL).\nFunding\n: I was the principal investigator of project 61602453 funded by the National Natural Science Foundation of China, from Jan 2017 to Dec 2019.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
