    "homepage_text": "Qi Liu's Homepage\nSearch\nQi Liu\nAssistant Professor at the University of Hong Kong\nThe University of Hong Kong\nBiography\nI am an assistant professor at\nthe Department of Computer Science\n,\nthe University of Hong Kong\n, and a cofounder of\nReka\n. I earned my Ph.D. in\ncomputer science from\nthe University of Oxford\n. In the past, I obtained a Master of Science degree from\nthe National University of Singapore\n, and a Bachelor of Engineering degree from\nShandong University\n. My research interests include natural language processing and machine learning. My research is centered on enabling computers to comprehend human language. I also spent some time at\nGoogle DeepMind\n,\nFacebook AI Research\n, and\nMicrosoft Research\nbefore and during my PhD study.\nI have multiple fully-funded PhD, MPhil, postdoc, RA, and intern positions available at the University of Hong Kong.\nEmail\nme for more information.\nReka is hiring for platform and machine learning.\nEmail\nus for more information. We are an AGI company committed to the development of large foundation models.\nInterests\nNatural Language Processing\nMachine Learning\nArtificial Intelligence\nEducation\nPh.D. in Artificial Intelligence\nUniversity of Oxford, Advisors: Phil Blunsom, Matt Kusner\nM.Sc in Computer Science\nNational University of Singapore, Advisor: Anthony K.H. Tung\nBEng in Computer Science\nShandong University\nExperiences\nResearch Scientist Intern\nGoogle DeepMind\nJul 2020 –\nJun 2021\nLondon\nAdvisors: Phil Blunsom, Dani Yogatama, Lei Yu, Laura Rimell\nResearcher\nFacebook AI Research\nAug 2018 –\nAug 2019\nNew York City\nAdvisors: Douwe Kiela, Maximilian Nickel\nResearch Intern\nMicrosoft Research\nMar 2018 –\nJun 2018\nCambridge\nAdvisors: Alexander Gaunt, Marc Brockschmidt, Miltos Allamanis\nResearch Assistant\nSUTD\nFeb 2017 –\nFeb 2018\nSingapore\nAdvisor: Yue Zhang\nResearch Intern\nMicrosoft Research\nSep 2016 –\nDec 2016\nBeijing\nAdvisors: Ying Yan, Thomas Moscibroda\nSelected Awards\nForbes 30 Under 30 Asia List\nForbes\nFeb 2023\nAMiner AI Most Influential Scholar\nAMiner\nJan 2022\nGoogle DeepMind Scholarship\nGoogle DeepMind\nSep 2019\nLee Kuan Yew Global Business Plan Competition Winner (3 out of 550)\nSMU\nAug 2017\nNUS Research Scholarship\nNUS\nSep 2014\nPublications\nQuickly discover relevant content by\nfiltering publications\n.\nYazheng Yang\n,\nYuqi Wang\n,\nYaxuan Li\n,\nSankalok Sen\n,\nLei Li\n,\nLin Qiu\n,\nQi Liu\n(2026).\nUnleashing the Potential of Large Language Models for Predictive Tabular Tasks in Data Science\n.\nIn\nTKDE\n.\nPDF\nShicheng Li\n,\nLei Li\n,\nKun Ouyang\n,\nShuhuai Ren\n,\nYuanxin Liu\n,\nYuanxing Zhang\n,\nFuzheng Zhang\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nXu Sun\n(2025).\nTEMPLE: Incentivizing Temporal Understanding of Video Large Language Models via Progressive Pre-SFT Alignment\n.\nIn\nAAAI\n.\nPDF\nDuzhen Zhang\n,\nChenxing Li\n,\nJiahua Dong\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nDong Yu\n(2025).\nExploring Stability-Plasticity Trade-offs for Continual Named Entity Recognition\n.\nIn\nTASLP\n.\nPDF\nLinli Yao\n,\nYicheng Li\n,\nYuancheng Wei\n,\nLei Li\n,\nShuhuai Ren\n,\nYuanxin Liu\n,\nKun Ouyang\n,\nLean Wang\n,\nShicheng Li\n,\nSida Li\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nYuanxing Zhang\n,\nXu Sun\n(2025).\nTimeChat-Online: 80% Visual Tokens are Naturally Redundant in Streaming Videos\n.\nIn\nACM Multimedia\n.\nPDF\nMukai Li\n,\nLei Li\n,\nShansan Gong\n,\nQi Liu\n(2025).\nGIRAFFE: Design Choices for Extending the Context Length of Visual Language Models\n.\nIn\nACL\n.\nPDF\nLei Li\n,\nYuancheng Wei\n,\nZhihui Xie\n,\nXuqing Yang\n,\nYifan Song\n,\nPeiyi Wang\n,\nChenxin An\n,\nTianyu Liu\n,\nSujian Li\n,\nBill Yuchen Lin\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n(2025).\nVLRewardBench: A Challenging Benchmark for Vision-Language Generative Reward Models\n.\nIn\nCVPR\n.\nPDF\nZhihui Xie\n,\nJiahui Gao\n,\nLei Li\n,\nZhenguo Li\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n(2025).\nJailbreaking as a Reward Misspecification Problem\n.\nIn\nICLR\n.\nPDF\nLei Li\n,\nYuanxin Liu\n,\nLinli Yao\n,\nPeiyuan Zhang\n,\nChenxin An\n,\nLean Wang\n,\nXu Sun\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n(2025).\nTemporal Reasoning Transfer from Text to Video\n.\nIn\nICLR\n.\nPDF\nXijia Tao\n,\nShuai Zhong\n,\nLei Li\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n(2025).\nImgTrojan: Jailbreaking Vision-Language Models with ONE Image\n.\nIn\nNAACL\n.\nPDF\nLei Li\n,\nZhihui Xie\n,\nMukai Li\n,\nShunian Chen\n,\nPeiyi Wang\n,\nLiang Chen\n,\nYazheng Yang\n,\nBenyou Wang\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n(2024).\nVLFeedback: A Large-Scale AI Feedback Dataset for Large Vision-Language Models Alignment\n.\nIn\nEMNLP\n.\nPDF\nChang Ma\n,\nHaiteng Zhao\n,\nLin Zheng\n,\nJiayi Xin\n,\nQintong Li\n,\nLijun Wu\n,\nZhihong Deng\n,\nYang Lu\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n(2024).\nRetrieved Sequence Augmentation for Protein Representation Learning\n.\nIn\nEMNLP\n.\nPDF\nLei Li\n,\nYuqi Wang\n,\nRunxin Xu\n,\nPeiyi Wang\n,\nXiachong Feng\n,\nLingpeng Kong\n,\nQi Liu\n(2024).\nMultimodal ArXiv: A Dataset for Improving Scientific Comprehension of Large Vision-Language Models\n.\nIn\nACL\n.\nPDF\nPeiyi Wang\n,\nLei Li\n,\nLiang Chen\n,\nDawei Zhu\n,\nBinghuai Lin\n,\nYunbo Cao\n,\nQi Liu\n,\nTianyu Liu\n,\nZhifang Sui\n(2024).\nLarge Language Models are not Fair Evaluators\n.\nIn\nACL\n.\nPDF\nMukai Li\n,\nLei Li\n,\nYuwei Yin\n,\nMasood Ahmed\n,\nZhenguang Liu\n,\nQi Liu\n(2024).\nRed Teaming Visual Language Models\n.\nIn\nACL Findings\n.\nPDF\nReka team\n(2024).\nVibe-Eval: A hard evaluation suite for measuring progress of multimodal language models\n.\nIn\nTech Report\n.\nPDF\nReka team\n(2024).\nReka Core, Flash, and Edge: A Series of Powerful Multimodal Language Models\n.\nIn\nTech Report\n.\nPDF\nYazheng Yang\n,\nYuqi Wang\n,\nGuang Liu\n,\nLedell Wu\n,\nQi Liu\n(2024).\nUniTabE: Pretraining a Unified Tabular Encoder for Heterogeneous Tabular Data\n.\nIn\nICLR\n.\nPDF\nJiankai Sun\n(2023).\nA survey of reasoning with foundation models\n.\nIn\narXi