    "homepage_text": "Xiaomeng Yang\nXiaomeng Yang\nA first-year PhD student at Northeastern University.\nFollow\nBoston, MA\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nWelcome,\nI am a first-year PhD student at Northeastern University, co-advised by\nProf. Yanzhi Wang\nand\nProf. Xuan Zhang\n. My research focuses on multimodal AI, generative models, and their applications to scientific challenges.\nPreviously, I completed my master’s degree at University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, where I worked with\nProf. Yu Zhou\non visual text analysis and understanding. I graduated with dual bachelor degrees from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign and Zhejiang University, majoring in Computer Engineering.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Xiaomeng Yang\nXiaomeng Yang\nA first-year PhD student at Northeastern University.\nFollow\nBoston, MA\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nYou can download my cv here:\nXiaomeng’s Curriculum Vitae\n.\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Engineering, Northeastern University\n2024-2029 (Expected)\nM.S in Computer Application Technology, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences (UCAS)\n2021-2024\nB.S. in Computer Engineering (with Honors), University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\n2017-2021\nB.E. in Electronic and Computer Engineering, Zhejiang University (ZJU)\n2017-2021\nPublications & Manuscripts\nXiaomeng Yang\n, Zhi Qiao, Yu Zhou. IPAD: Iterative, Parallel, and Diffusion-based Network for Scene Text Recognition. Accepted by IJCV, 2025.\nXiaomeng Yang\n, Zhi Qiao, Jin Wei, Dongbao Yang, Yu Zhou. Masked and Permuted Implicit Context Learning for Scene Text Recognition. In IEEE Signal Processing Letters, 2024.\nXiaomeng Yang\n, Dongbao Yang, Zhi Qiao, Yu Zhou. Accurate and Robust Scene Text Recognition via Adversarial Training. Accepted by ICASSP, 2024.\nGangyan Zeng, Yuan Zhang, Yu Zhou,\nXiaomeng Yang\n, Ning Jiang, Guoqing Zhao, Weiping Wang, Xu-Cheng Yin. Beyond OCR+VQA: Towards End-to-End Reading and Reasoning for Robust and Accurate TextVQA. In Pattern Recognition, 2023.\nGangyan Zeng, Yuan Zhang, Yu Zhou,\nXiaomeng Yang\n. Beyond OCR+VQA: Involving OCR into the Flow for Robust and Accurate TextVQA. Accepted by ACM MM, 2021.\nGangyan Zeng, Yuan Zhang, Yu Zhou,\nXiaomeng Yang\n. A Cost-Efficient Framework for Scene Text Detection in the Wild. Accepted by PRICAI, 2021.\nYucheng Jin,\nXiaomeng Yang\n, Chengting Yu, Liangjing Yang. Educational Data Mining: Discovering Principal Factors for Better Academic Performance. Accepted by BDET, 2021.\nReseach Experience\nLinguistic Information Enhanced Scene Text Recognition\nUCAS | Research Assistant, Advisor: Prof. Yu Zhou\nJun. 2022 – Apr. 2024\nTomorrow Advancing Life | Research Internship, Advisor: Zhi Qiao\nJun. 2022 – Apr. 2024\nAdversarial Training for Scene Text Recognition\nUCAS | Summer Internship, Advisor: Prof. Yu Zhou\nMar. 2023 – Aug. 2023\nInvolving OCR into the Flow of TextVQA\nUCAS | Research Assistant, Advisor: Prof. Yu Zhou\nOct. 2020 – Sep. 2022\nCost-Efficient Scene Text Detection\nUCAS | Summer Internship, Advisor: Prof. Yu Zhou\nMar. 2021 – Jun. 2021\nEducational Data Mining\nZJU | SRTP Program, Advisor: Prof. Liangjing Yang\nOct. 2019 – Aug. 2020\nWaterway Segmentation and Transfer Learning of Building Segmentation\nUIUC | Individual Study, Advisor: Prof. Volodymyr Kindratenko\nSep. 2019 – Dec. 2019\nSkills\nLanguage skill:\nEnglish: Advanced, Chinese: Native\nProgramming languages:\nPython, C/C++, Java, JavaScript, HTML/CSS\nOther Library and Tools:\nPyTorch, TensorFlow, Numpy, Scipy, Linux, Git, Arduino, Unity3D"
