    "homepage_text": "Weizhong Zhang\nWeizhong Zhang\nHome\nBiography\nResearch\nPublications\nProjects\nTeaching\nCourses\nWeizhong Zhang\nTenure-track Professor,  Ph.D. Advisor\nSchool of Data Science\nFudan University\nContact\nweizhongzhang@fudan.edu.cn\nAbout Me\nI am now a Tenure-track Professor at School of Data Science, Fudan University. I was a Postdoctoral Researcher and Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology, working with\nProf. Tong Zhang\n. Before that I was also a Research Scientist in Tencent AI Lab. I received my Ph.D. on Computer Science at Zhejiang University under my supervisors\nProf. Xiaofei He\nand\nProf. Deng Cai\n. I was a Joint PhD student in The University of Michigan, Ann Arbor under the supervision of\nProf. Jieping Ye\nand\nProf. Jie Wang\n. I have broad interests in machine learning, deep learning algorithms, federated learning etc. My current research focuses on developing algorithms to improve the training/inference efficiency and generalization ability of deep neural networks and their applications in other areas (e.g., computer vision). I have published more than 40 papers in peer-reviewed top-tier journal papers (JMLR, IEEE TPAMI, IEEE TKDE, etc.) and conference papers (ICML, NeurIPS, CVPR, etc.).\nOur team recruits several self-motivated students (Ph.Ds., masters, undergraduate students, interns, gap year students) to work on model compression, federated learning, efficient training/finetuning/inference algorithms for LLM and diffusion models etc.  If you are interested in my group, please contact me as soon as possible.\nResearch Interests\nMachine Learning\nModel Compression, Efficient Training/Inference Algorithms\nFederated Learning\nOut of Domain Generalization\nMachine Learning Methods in other areas (e.g., computer vision)\nNews\nZhikang Xie (undergraduate student) is  supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Youth Student Basic Research Program) 2025\nZihao Chen (undergraduate student) is  supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Youth Student Basic Research Program) 2024\nCompress Large Language Models via Collaboration Between Learning and Matrix Approximation.\nYuesen Liao, Zhiwei Li, Binrui Wu, Zihao Cheng, Su Zhao, Shuai Chen,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n.\nThe 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\nComputation and Memory-Efficient Model Compression with Gradient Reweighting.\nZhiwei Li, Yuesen Liao, Binrui Wu, Yuquan Zhou, Xupeng Shi, Dongsheng Jiang, Yin Li,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n.\nThe 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\nEfficient Representativeness-Aware Coreset Selection.\nZihao Cheng, Binrui Wu, Zhiwei Li, Yuesen Liao, Su Zhao, Shuai Chen, Yuan Gao,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n.\nThe 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\nComputational Budget Should Be Considered in Data Selection.\nWeilin Wan,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n, Cheng Jin.\nThe 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\nComplete Structure Guided Point Cloud Completion via Cluster- and Instance-Level Contrastive Learning.\nYang Chen, Yirun Zhou,\nWeizhong Zhang\n, Cheng Jin.\nThe 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\nPopulation Normalization for Federated Learning.\nZhuoyao Wang*, Fan Yi*, Peizhu Gong, Caitou He, Cheng Jin,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n.\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2025.  (CVPR 2025)\nTowards Robust Influence Functions with Flat Validation Minima.\nXichen Ye, Yifan Wu,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n, Cheng Jin, Yifan Chen#.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning, 2025. (ICML 2025)\nDreamText: High Fidelity Scene Text Synthesis.\nYibin Wang,\nWeizhong Zhang\n, honghui xu, Cheng Jin.\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, pp. 2124-2133. 2025.  (CVPR 2025)\nTAGCOS: Task-agnostic Gradient Clustered Coreset Selection for Instruction Tuning Data.\nJipeng Zhang, Yaxuan Qin, Renjie Pi,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n,  Rui Pan, Tong Zhang.\nFindings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: NAACL 2025.  (NACCL Findings 2025)\nAchieving Ensemble-Like Performance in A Single Model: A Feature Diversification Framework for Image-Text Matching.\nZhao Zhou, Yiqun Wang,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n, Yingbin Zheng, Xiangcheng Du, Cheng Jin#.\nAnnual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 2025.  (AAAI 2025)\nExpanding The Scope of Negatives: Boosting Image-Text Matching with Negatives Distribution Guided Learning.\nZhao Zhou,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n, Xiangcheng Du, Yingbin Zheng, Cheng Jin#.\nAnnual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 2025.  (AAAI 2025)\nOptimized Gradient Clipping for Noisy Label Learning.\nXichen Ye, Yifan Wu,\nWeizhong Zhang\n, Xiaoqiang Li, Yifan Chen, Cheng Jin.\nAnnual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 2025.  (AAAI 2025)\nSelected Publications (*equal contribution，#corresponding author)\n1. Yuesen Liao, Zhiwei Li, Binrui Wu, Zihao Cheng, Su Zhao, Shuai Chen,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n. Compress Large Language Models via Collaboration Between Learning and Matrix Approximation. The 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\n2. Zhiwei Li, Yuesen Liao, Binrui Wu, Yuquan Zhou, Xupeng Shi, Dongsheng Jiang, Yin Li,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n. Computation and Memory-Efficient Model Compression with Gradient Reweighting. The 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\n3. Zihao Cheng, Binrui Wu, Zhiwei Li, Yuesen Liao, Su Zhao, Shuai Chen, Yuan Gao,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n. Efficient Representativeness-Aware Coreset Selection.The 39th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2025.  (NeurIPS 2025)\n4. Weilin Wan,\nWeizhong Zhang#\n, Cheng Jin. Computational Budget Should Be Considered in Data Selection. The 39th Annual Conference on Neu