    "homepage_text": "Zhun Deng's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZhun Deng's Homepage\nZhun Deng\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science, UNC Chapel Hill\nEmail:\nzhundeng\nat cs dot\nunc\ndot edu\nOffice:\nSitterson Hall 225\nGoogle Scholar\nTwitter\nHi\n! I am a tenure\n-track A\nssi\nstant Professor at the\nDepartment of Computer Science\n,\nUniversity of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\n. Previously\n, I\nwas\na\npostdoctoral researcher at\nC\nolumbia University\n, hosted by\nToniann Pitassi\nand\nRichard Zemel\n.\nI\ncompleted my\nPh.D. in\nComputer Science at\nHarvard University\nunder the guidance of\nCynthia Dwork\n.\nPrior to Harvard, I received\nmy\nB.Sc. in Mathematics\nfrom\nChu Ko\nc\nhen Honors College\n,\nZhejiang University\n.\nI am broadly interested in problems at the frontier of machine learning\n, statistics, and theoretical computer science\n.\nMy goal is to introduce rigorous theoretical tools to establish practically useful frameworks for efficient, safe, and responsible machine learning.\nNews\n0\n9\n/2025 - Two papers accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025\n:\nstatistical inference under performativity\nand\nperformative risk control\n.\n0\n5\n/202\n5\n-\nTwo papers accepted by\nICML 2025\n:\nauto-evaluation of tail behaviors of LLMs\nand\nconformal tail risk control for LLM alignment\n.\n01\n/2025 - I start as an assistant professor at UNC CS!\nClick here for older news\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
