    "homepage_text": "Chuan Wen's Homepage\nChuan Wen\nSAI, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nwenchuan <AT> sjtu.edu.cn\nAbout Me\nI am a tenure-track Assistant Professor at\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\n, Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI obtained my Ph.D. degree from\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Science (IIIS)\nat\nTsinghua University\n, advised by Prof.\nYang Gao\n.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDuring my Ph.D., I was fortunate to visit Berkeley Artificial Intelligence Research (BAIR), advised by Prof.\nPieter Abbeel\nand Dr.\nXingyu Lin\n.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI also worked closely with Prof.\nDinesh Jayaraman\nat UPenn\nGRASP lab\n.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPrior to that, I received my bachelor degree from\nEE Department\nin\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n, under the supervision of Prof.\nYa Zhang\nand Prof.\nXinbing Wang\n.\nMy research interest focuses on Embodied AI in general. My goal is to achieve generalist robots with advanced system, hardware, and algorithms.\nRecruitment\nWelcome highly self-motivated Ph.D. candidates, Master students, and undergraduate interns to join our lab. If you are interested, please feel free to send me your resume and transcript via email.\nNews\n[02/2026] Three papers (\nSOE, FP3, MotionTrans\n) were accepted by ICRA 2026!\n[01/2026] Our paper\nTranslating Flow to Policy via Hindsight Online Imitation\nwas accepted by ICLR 2026!\n[09/2025] Two papers (\nEfficientVLA, FFCP\n) were accepted by NeurIPS 2025!\n[08/2025] Our paper\nKineDex: Learning Tactile-Informed Visuomotor Policies via Kinesthetic Teaching for Dexterous Manipulation\nwas accepted by CoRL 2025!\n[07/2025] I joined SJTU as a tenure-track Assistant Professor!\n[06/2025] I graduated from Tsinghua University with my Ph.D. degree! Huge thanks to my advisor Prof. Yang Gao and my collaborators!\n[11/2024] Our paper\nData Scaling Laws in Imitation Learning for Robotic Manipulation\nwas accepted by ICLR 2025!\n[01/2025] I was awarded the\nByteDance Scholarship\n. Thanks ByteDance!\n[11/2024] Our paper\nData Scaling Laws in Imitation Learning for Robotic Manipulation\ngot the best paper award at CoRL 2024 X-Embodiment Workshop!\n[09/2024] Our paper\nGeneral Flow as Foundation Affordance for Scalable Robot Learning\nwas accepted by CoRL 2024!\n[05/2024] Our paper\nAny-point Trajectory Modeling for Policy Learning\nwas accepted by RSS 2024!\n[01/2024] Three papers (\nRelatiViT, Seer, ADS\n) were accepted by ICLR 2024!\n[09/2023] I embarked on my visiting scholar journey at Berkeley Artificial Intelligence Research (BAIR) under the expert guidance of Prof. Pieter Abbeel and Dr. Xingyu Lin.\n[01/2023] Our paper\nPredictive Inference with Feature Conformal Prediction\nwas accepted by ICLR 2023!\n[07/2022] Our paper\nResolving Copycat Problems in Visual Imitation Learning via Residual Action Prediction\nwas accepted by ECCV 2022!\n[05/2022] Our paper\nFighting Fire with Fire: Avoiding DNN Shortcuts through Priming\nwas accepted by ICML 2022!\n[05/2021] Our paper\nKeyframe-Focused Visual Imitation Learning\nwas accepted by ICML 2021!\n[12/2020] We gave a talk about our paper in 2020 NeurIPS MeetUp, Beijing! (\nVideo\n)\n[09/2020] Our paper\nFighting Copycat Agents in Behavioral Cloning from Observation Histories\nwas accepted by NeurIPS 2020!\n[01/2020] I started research internship at Berkeley Artificial Intelligence Research(BAIR), advised by Prof. Trevor Darrell and Prof. Yang Gao.\nPublications\nImplicitRDP: An End-to-End Visual-Force Diffusion Policy with Structural Slow-Fast Learning\nWendi Chen, Han Xue, Yi Wang, Fangyuan Zhou, Jun Lv, Yang Jin, Shirun Tang, Chuan Wen‡, Cewu Lu‡.\nPreprint\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nARMADA: Autonomous Online Failure Detection and Human Shared Control Empower Scalable Real-world Deployment and Adaptation\nWenye Yu, Jun Lv, Zixi Ying, Yang Jin, Chuan Wen‡, Cewu Lu‡.\nPreprint\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nBest Paper Award at IROS 2025 Human-in-the-loop Workshop\nTimeRewarder: Learning Dense Reward from Passive Videos via Frame-wise Temporal Distance\nYuyang Liu*, Chuan Wen*, Yihang Hu, Dinesh Jayaraman, Yang Gao.\nPreprint\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nSOE: Sample-Efficient Robot Policy Self-Improvement via On-Manifold Exploration\nYang Jin, Jun Lv, Han Xue, Wendi Chen, Chuan Wen‡, Cewu Lu‡.\nICRA 2026\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nMotionTrans: Human VR Data Enable Motion-Level Learning for Robotic Manipulation Policies\nChengbo Yuan, Rui Zhou, Mengzhen Liu, Yingdong Hu, Shengjie Wang, Li Yi, Chuan Wen, Shanghang Zhang, Yang Gao.\nICRA 2026\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nFP3: A 3D Foundation Policy for Robotic Manipulation\nRujia Yang*, Geng Chen*, Chuan Wen‡, Yang Gao‡.\nICRA 2026\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nTranslating Flow to Policy via Hindsight Online Imitation\nYitian Zheng, Zhangchen Ye, Weijun Dong, Shengjie Wang, Yuyang Liu, Chongjie Zhang, Chuan Wen‡, Yang Gao‡.\nICLR 2026\nPDF\n/\nArxiv\nEfficientVLA: Training-Free Acceleration and Compression for Vision-Language-Action Models\nYantai Yang, Yuhao Wang, Zichen Wen, Luo Zhongwei, Chang Zou, Zhipeng Zhang, Chuan Wen‡, Linfeng Zhang‡.\nNeurIPS 2025\nPDF\n/\nArxiv\nKineDex: Learning Tactile-Informed Visuomotor Policies via Kinesthetic Teaching for Dexterous Manipulation\nDi Zhang, Chengbo Yuan, Chuan Wen, Hai Zhang, Junqiao Zhao, Yang Gao.\nCoRL 2025\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nData Scaling Laws in Imitation Learning for Robotic Manipulation\nFanqi Lin, Yingdong Hu, Pingyue Sheng, Chuan Wen, Jiacheng You, Yang Gao.\nICLR 2025\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nBest Paper Award at CoRL 2024 X-Embodiment Workshop\nGeneral Flow as Foundation Affordance for\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tScalable Robot Learning\nChengbo Yuan, Chuan Wen, Tong Zhang, Yang Gao.\nCoRL 2024\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nAny-point Trajectory Modeling for Policy Learning\nChuan Wen*, Xingyu Lin*, John So*, Kai Chen, Qi Dou, Yang Gao, Pieter Abbeel.\nRSS 2024\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\n/\nCode\nCan Transformers Capture Spatial Relations between Objects?\nChuan Wen, Dinesh Jayaraman, Yang Gao.\nICLR 2024\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nImitation Learning from Observation with Automatic Discount Scheduling\nYuyang Liu*, Weijun Dong*, Yingdong Hu, Chuan Wen, Zhaoheng Yin, Chongjie Zhang, Yang Gao.\nICLR 2024\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nSeer: Language Instructed Video Prediction with Latent Diffusion Models\nXianfan Gu, Chuan Wen, Jiaming Song, Yang Gao.\nICLR 2024\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nPredictive Inference with Feature Conformal Prediction\nJiaye Teng*, Chuan Wen*, Dinghuai Zhang*, Yoshua Bengio, Yang Gao, Yang Yuan.\nICLR 2023\nPDF\n/\nCode\nResolving Copycat Problems in Visual Imitation Learning via Residual Action Prediction\nChia-Chi Chuang*, Donglin Yang*, Chuan Wen*, Yang Gao.\nECCV 2022\nPDF\n/\nCode\nFighting Fire with Fire: Avoiding DNN Shortcuts through Priming\nChuan Wen, Jianing Qian, Jierui Lin, Jiaye Teng, Dinesh Jayaraman, Yang Gao.\nICML 2022\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nKeyframe-Focused Visual Imitation Learning\nChuan Wen*, Jierui Lin*, Jianing Qian, Yang Gao, Dinesh Jayaraman.\nICML 2021\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nFighting Copycat Agents in Behavioral Cloning from Observation Histories\nChuan Wen*, Jierui Lin*, Trevor Darrell, Dinesh Jayaraman, Yang Gao.\nNeurIPS 2020\nPDF\n/\nWebsite\n/\nArxiv\nHandwritten Chinese font generation with collaborative stroke refinement\nChuan Wen, Yujie Pan, Jie Chang, Ya Zhang, Siheng Chen, Yanfeng Wang, Mei Han, Qi Tian.\nWACV 2021\nPDF\n/\nArxiv\nAuthor name disambiguation on heterogeneous information network with adversarial representation learning\nHaiwen Wang, Ruijie Wang, Chuan Wen, Shuhao Li, Yuting Jia, Weinan Zhang, Xinbing Wang.\nAAAI 2020\nPDF\n/\nArxiv\nRI-SSGE: a framework with rule inference and sentence schema graph embedding for knowledge base query construction\nXiaoyang Huo, Chuan Wen, Yuchen Yan, Ruijie Wang.\nTURC 2019\nPDF\nPublic Services\nReviewer Services: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, RSS, ICRA, CoRL, T-RO, RA-L, AAAI."
