    "homepage_text": "Zijing Shi | University of Technology Sydney\nZijing Shi\nPostDoc\nUniversity of Technology Sydney\nzijing.shi-1[at]uts.edu.au\nAbout Me\nI am Zijing Shi, currently a Postdoctoral Research Associate at\nAAII UTS\n. I completed my Ph.D. at UTS under the supervision of\nProf. Ling Chen\n.\nMy research focuses on building intelligent agents that are not only\nefficient\nbut also\ntrustworthy\nin open environments. Specifically, I work on:\n1) Designing\nLLM- and RL-based agents\nfor natural language interaction;\n2) Exploring\nvalue alignment\nand\nbias mitigation\nin these agents.\nNews\n[Dec. 2025]\nReceived the UTS AAII Student Best Paper Award in the category of AI Theory and Algorithms.\n[Jan. 2025]\nOne paper on planning capabilities of game agents has been accepted at ICLR conference.\n[arXiv]\n[Dec. 2023]\nOne paper has been accepted at AAAI 2024 (Oral, SRRAI Track).\n[Dec. 2023]\nAchieved HDR WiEIT (Women in Engineering and IT) Award.\n[Oct. 2023]\nAchieved 1st place in School of Computer Science Research Showcase.\n[Jan. 2023]\nOne paper has been accepted at the EACL 2023 conference.\n[Jan. 2023]\nOne paper has been accepted at the ICLR 2023 conference.\nShow More\nSelected Papers\nICLR\nMonte Carlo Planning with Large Language Models for Text‑based Game Agents\nZijing Shi\n, Meng Fang, Ling Chen\nICLR\n2025.\nPDF\nCode\nAAAI\nLarge Language Models are Neurosymbolic Reasoners\nMeng Fang*, Shilong Deng*, Yudi Zhang*,\nZijing Shi\n, Ling Chen, Mykola Pechenizkiy, Jun Wang\nAAAI\n2024.\nPDF\nCode\nAAAI\nHuman‑Guided Moral Decision Making in Text‑based Games\nZijing Shi\n, Meng Fang, Ling Chen, Yali Du, Jun Wang\nAAAI (Oral)\n2024.\nPDF\nCode\nACL\nCHBias: Bias Evaluation and Mitigation of Chinese Conversational Language Models\nJiaxu Zhao*, Meng Fang*,\nZijing Shi\n, Yitong Li, Ling Chen, Mykola Pechenizkiy\nACL\n2023.\nPDF\nCode\nICLR\nStay Moral and Explore: Learn to Behave Morally in Text‑based Games\nZijing Shi*\n, Meng Fang*, Yunqiu Xu, Ling Chen, Yali Du\nICLR\n2023.\nPDF\nCode\nEACL\nSelf‑imitation Learning for Action Generation in Text‑based Games\nZijing Shi\n, Yunqiu Xu, Meng Fang, Ling Chen\nEACL\n2023.\nPDF\nCode\nTeaching and Services\nTeaching\n2024: Teaching Assistant – Introduction to Artificial Intelligence, UTS (Undergraduate 41040; Postgraduate 42172)\n2024: Teaching Assistant (Online) – Oxford Machine Learning Summer School (OxML)\nJournal Reviewer\nNeural Computing and Applications\nIEEE Transactions on Artificial Intelligence\nConference Reviewer\n2025: ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS, AAAI, COLM, ACL, EMNLP\n2024: ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS, AAMAS, ACL, EMNLP"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Meng Fang::https://mengfn.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://mengfn.github.io/",
