    "homepage_text": "Jinjin Gu - Home\nToggle navigation\nJinjin Gu  @\nHome\nCV\nResearch\nPublications\nTeam\nOpenings\nJinjin Gu\nTenure-Track Faculty Member\nINSAIT\n- Institute for Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence and Technology,\nSofia University \"St. Kliment Ohridski\"\nEmail:\njinjin.gu @ insait.ai\nLinks:\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nbilibili\n/\ntwitter\n👁️ Visual Perception\n🛠️ Visual Processing\n🎨 Visual Generation\n🧠 Visual Reasoning\nI am a tenure-track faculty member at\nINSAIT\n, in Sofia, Bulgaria, where I will lead a group working on visual cognition and intelligence. My research interests include visual perception, visual processing, visual generation, and visual reasoning.\nLooking for self-motivated Postdoctoral Researchers and PhD Students in the field of computer vision and multimodal intelligent systems at INSAIT.\nFor more information, please refer to the\nRecruitment page\n.\nPrevious\nNext\nBefore joining INSAIT, I received my Ph.D. from the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Sydney in 2024, under the supervision of\nProf. Wanli Ouyang\n. Prior to that, I obtained my Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science and Engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\n(CUHKSZ)\nin 2020. Previously, I worked closely with\nProf. Chao Dong\n.\nMy research contributions have received over 11,000 citations, achieving an H-index of 32. In 2024, I was named among the\ntop 2% of scientists worldwide\nby Stanford University, and I received the\nYunfan Award\nat the World Artificial Intelligence Conference (WAIC) in 2023.\nHighlighted Research Topics\nImage / Video Processing, Restoration and Enhancement\nAgentic AI for Visual Media\nInterpretability of Visual Models\nMulti-Modal Language Model Applications\nNews (\nSee all news\n)\nJan. 2026\nWe are very pleased that our workshop\nAgentic AI for Visual Media\nhas been accepted as a full day workshop at CVPR 2026. We are looking forward to seeing you in Denver!\nDec. 2025\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to serve as an Area Chair for ICML 2026.\nAug. 2025\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to serve as an Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\nJul. 2025\nThrilled to launch\nHYPIR\n—a revolutionary paradigm bringing diffusion-quality image restoration at lightning-fast GAN speeds!\nJul. 2025\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to join the European Laboratory for Learning and Intelligent Systems (ELLIS) as a Member.\nApr. 2025\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025.\nMar. 2025\nOne paper is accepted by TPAMI. Congratulations to Jinfa Hu.\nMar. 2025\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to serve as an Area Chair for ACM MM 2025.\nFeb. 2025\nOne paper to appear in CVPR 2025. Congratulations to Zhiyuan.\nJan. 2025\nThree papers (including one spotlight) to appear in ICLR 2025. Congratulations to Keda, Fanghua and Kaiwen.\nNov. 2024\nDr. Jinjin Gu is honored to serve as an Area Chair for ICML 2025.\n... see all News\n© Copyright 2025 Jinjin Gu.\nLast updated: May 10th, 2025.\nINSAIT - Institute for Computer Science,\nArtificial Intelligence and Technology\nContact:\nSynergy Tower, Sofia Tech Park\n1784 Sofia, Bulgaria\n(\nGoogle Map\n)\n\n---\n\nJinjin Gu's CV\nToggle navigation\nJinjin Gu  @\nHome\nCV\nResearch\nPublications\nTeam\nOpenings\nCurriculum Vitae\nDownload\nCurriculum Vitae (PDF) (updated: 2025.6)\n.\nTimeline\nEducation\nThe University of Sydney\n.\n2020 – 2024, Ph.D., Electrical & Computer Engineering.\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\n.\n2015 – 2020, B.Eng., Computer Science and Engineering.\nAcademic Positions\nINSAIT (in partnership with ETH and EPFL)\n, Sofia, Bulgaria.\n2025 – present, Tenure-Track Faculty Member.\nShenzhen University of Advanced Technology\n, Shenzhen, China.\n2024 – 2025, Research Assistant Professor.\nShanghai AI Laboratory\n, Shanghai, China.\n2024 – 2024, Research Scientist.\nHonors\nStanford University’s list of “World’s Top 2%” scientists\n(2024)\nFaculty of Engineering Career Advancement Award, The University of Sydney (2023)\nWAIC Yunfan Award, Rising Star Award\n(15 winners under the age of 30 worldwide, 2023)\nHuawei Camera, Academic Rising Star Award, Second Prize (2022)\nSenseTime Scholarship\n(Top 29 students selected from across China, 2019)\nSenseTime Research Intern Star (2018)\nSenseTime Outstanding Research Intern (2018)\nResearch Experience\n2022.3 – 2024.7.\nShanghai AI Laboratory\nResearcher. Mentor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n.\n2021.4 – 2022.9. Shenzhen Institute of Artificial Intelligence and Robotics for Society (AIRS)\nResearch Assistant. Mentor:\nProf. Junhua Zhao\n.\n2020.8 – 2022.4.\nSenseTime Research\n.\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nDr. Jimmy S. Ren\n.\n2020.3 – 2020.8. Platform and Content Group (PCG), Tencent. Applied Research Center\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nDr. Ying Shan\n,\nDr. Yu Li\n.\n2019.11 – 2022.4. Shenzhen Institutes of Advanced Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences.\nX-pixel Group\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n.\n2019.4 – 2019.11. The Chinese University of Hong Kong.\nMultimedia Laboratory\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Bolei Zhou\n.\n2017.11 – 2019.4.\nSenseTime Research\n.\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n,\nProf. Liang Lin\nand\nDr. Jimmy S. Ren\n.\n2017.6 – 2017.8. Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Xiaolin Wu\n.\nServices\nArea Chair:\nInternational Conference on Learning Representation (ICLR), 2026\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2025\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025\nACM Multimedia Conference (ACM MM), 2025\nConference Reviewer:\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2021, 2023\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2020, 2022, 2024\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2022, 2023\nWinter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV), 2022\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2025, 2026\nJournal Reviewer:\nNature Communication\nIEEE, Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nIEEE, Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nIEEE, Transactions on Multimedia (TMM)\nIEEE, Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT)\nIEEE, Transactions on Cybernetics (TCYB)\nIEEE, Transactions on Industrial Informatics (TII)\nIEEE, Transactions on Biometrics, Behavior, and Identity Science (TBIOM)\nIEEE, Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing (JSTSP)\nACM, Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications (TOMM)\nSpringer, International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\nSpringer, The Visual Computer (TVCJ)\nElsevier, Computer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU)\nPublic Library of Science, PLOS One\nReScience C\nEvents\nWorkshops:\nCo-organizer - New Trends in Image Restoration and Enhancement workshop (\nNTIRE\n),\nCVPR 2021\nCVPR 2022\nTalks\nToward “Intelligent” Low-level Vision.\nInvited Talk at Huawei Noah’S Ark Lab, 2024.2\nUnderstanding Generalization Problem in Low-level Vision.\nInvited Talk at Huawei, 2023.4\nInvited Talk at Shanghai AI Lab, 2023.7\nRethinking Alignment in Video Super-Resolution Transformers.\nInvited Talk at Shanghai AI Lab, 2022.9\nbilibili (CN)\nGeneral Low-Level Vision: Evaluation and Interpretability.\nInvited Talk at Long Feng Science Forum from CUHK-Shenzhen, 2022.8\nInvited Talk at Huawei, Shanghai, 2022.8\nNTIRE 2022 Challenge on Perceptual Image Quality Assessment.\nTalk at CVPR 2022, NTIRE Workshop. 2022.6.\nInterpreting Super-Resolution Networks\nInvited Talk at Student Forum on Frontiers of AI (SFFAI), Shenzhen, 2021.9.\nbilibili (CN)\nSlides\nEvaluating and Interpreting Super-Resolution Networks.\nInvited Talk at Huawei 2012 Lab, Shenzhen, 2021.6\nInvited Talk at Kuai Shou, 2022.6\nNTIRE 2021 Challenge on Perceptual Image Quality Assessment.\nTalk at CVPR 2021, NTIRE Workshop. 2021.6.\nYouTube\nImage Processing Applications: Challenges and Opportunities.\nInvited talk at Tsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School, 2021.5.\nSlides\nInterpreting Super-Resolution Networks with Local Attribution Maps.\nInvited talk at Extreme Mart, Shenzhen, 2021.3.\nbilibili (CN)\nInvited talk at CSIG-Guangdong Province CVPR 2021 Online Academic Report, 2021.5.\nbilibili (CN)\nInvited talk at Tsinghua AI TIME Online Academic Report, 2021.7.\nbilibili (CN)\nTwo-phase Hair Image Synthesis by Self-Enhancing Generative Model.\nTalk at Pacific Graphics 2019. Korea University, Seoul, Korea, 2019.\nSuppressing Model Overfitting for Image Super-Resolution Networks.\nTalk at CVPR 2019, NTIRE Workshop. Long Beach, California, USA, 2019.\nNew Trends On Single Image Super-Resolution.\nInvited talk at CUHK(SZ). Shenzhen, Guangdong, China, 2019.\nESRGAN: Enhanced Super-Resolution Generative Adversarial Networks.\nTalk at ECCV 2018, PIRM Workshop. TUM, Munich, Germany, 2018.\nTeaching\nELEC5304: Intelligent Visual Signal Understanding\nTime\n: Semester 1, 2024\nRole\n: Lecturer\nTechX Academy Bootcamp\nTime\n: Summer 2021\nRole\n: Instructor\nDescription\n: Designed and taught a 10-day course on “Introduction to Data Science”\nCourse Content\n:\nBig picture of Data Science\nLinear Models: Linear Regression, Logistic Regression, Generalized Linear Models, Softmax Regression\nNeural Networks, Convolutional Neural Networks\nOther Classification Methods: Decision Tree, Random Forest, Boosting Methods, Support Vector Machines\nUnsupervised Learning: K-means, Manifold Learning, Principal Component Analysis\nIntroduction to Natural Language Processing\n© Copyright 2025 Jinjin Gu.\nLast updated: May 10th, 2025.\nINSAIT - Institute for Computer Science,\nArtificial Intelligence and Technology\nContact:\nSynergy Tower, Sofia Tech Park\n1784 Sofia, Bulgaria\n(\nGoogle Map\n)\n\n---\n\nJinjin Gu's CV\nToggle navigation\nJinjin Gu  @\nHome\nCV\nResearch\nPublications\nTeam\nOpenings\nCurriculum Vitae\nDownload\nCurriculum Vitae (PDF) (updated: 2025.6)\n.\nTimeline\nEducation\nThe University of Sydney\n.\n2020 – 2024, Ph.D., Electrical & Computer Engineering.\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\n.\n2015 – 2020, B.Eng., Computer Science and Engineering.\nAcademic Positions\nINSAIT (in partnership with ETH and EPFL)\n, Sofia, Bulgaria.\n2025 – present, Tenure-Track Faculty Member.\nShenzhen University of Advanced Technology\n, Shenzhen, China.\n2024 – 2025, Research Assistant Professor.\nShanghai AI Laboratory\n, Shanghai, China.\n2024 – 2024, Research Scientist.\nHonors\nStanford University’s list of “World’s Top 2%” scientists\n(2024)\nFaculty of Engineering Career Advancement Award, The University of Sydney (2023)\nWAIC Yunfan Award, Rising Star Award\n(15 winners under the age of 30 worldwide, 2023)\nHuawei Camera, Academic Rising Star Award, Second Prize (2022)\nSenseTime Scholarship\n(Top 29 students selected from across China, 2019)\nSenseTime Research Intern Star (2018)\nSenseTime Outstanding Research Intern (2018)\nResearch Experience\n2022.3 – 2024.7.\nShanghai AI Laboratory\nResearcher. Mentor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n.\n2021.4 – 2022.9. Shenzhen Institute of Artificial Intelligence and Robotics for Society (AIRS)\nResearch Assistant. Mentor:\nProf. Junhua Zhao\n.\n2020.8 – 2022.4.\nSenseTime Research\n.\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nDr. Jimmy S. Ren\n.\n2020.3 – 2020.8. Platform and Content Group (PCG), Tencent. Applied Research Center\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nDr. Ying Shan\n,\nDr. Yu Li\n.\n2019.11 – 2022.4. Shenzhen Institutes of Advanced Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences.\nX-pixel Group\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n.\n2019.4 – 2019.11. The Chinese University of Hong Kong.\nMultimedia Laboratory\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Bolei Zhou\n.\n2017.11 – 2019.4.\nSenseTime Research\n.\nResearch Intern. Mentor:\nProf. Chao Dong\n,\nProf. Liang Lin\nand\nDr. Jimmy S. Ren\n.\n2017.6 – 2017.8. Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nResearch Assistant. Advisor:\nProf. Xiaolin Wu\n.\nServices\nArea Chair:\nInternational Conference on Learning Representation (ICLR), 2026\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2025\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025\nACM Multimedia Conference (ACM MM), 2025\nConference Reviewer:\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2021, 2023\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2020, 2022, 2024\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2022, 2023\nWinter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV), 2022\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2025, 2026\nJournal Reviewer:\nNature Communication\nIEEE, Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nIEEE, Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nIEEE, Transactions on Multimedia (TMM)\nIEEE, Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT)\nIEEE, Transactions on Cybernetics (TCYB)\nIEEE, Transactions on Industrial Informatics (TII)\nIEEE, Transactions on Biometrics, Behavior, and Identity Science (TBIOM)\nIEEE, Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing (JSTSP)\nACM, Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications (TOMM)\nSpringer, International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\nSpringer, The Visual Computer (TVCJ)\nElsevier, Computer Vision a