    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYi Zhou\nHOWDY!\nI am an Associate Professor in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at Texas A&M University. Before, I worked as an Assistant Professor in the Department of\nElectrical and Computer Engineering at\nThe University of Utah (2019-2024). I was a postdoc fellow in the Department of ECE at Duke University (2018-2019) supervised by Dr.\nVahid Tarokh\n. I obtained a Ph.D. degree in ECE from The Ohio State University in 2018 under the supervision of Dr.\nYingbin Liang\n.\nResearch interests:\nLLMs and their applications to broad engineering fields\nN\nonconvex\n&\nstochastic optimization for\nML\nReinforcement learning and multi-agent system control\nML for EDA/CAD/HPC\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Tianle Cai::https://www.tianle.website/": {
