 GAN architectures\nDo GANs actually do distribution learning?\nGeneralization and Equilibrium in GANs\n​\n​\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant for\nCOS 324 Intro to Machine Learning, Fall 2018.\nTeaching Assistant for\nCOS 445 Economics and Computation, Spring 2019\n​\n​\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nYi Zhang - Academic Homepage\ntop of page\nYI ZHANG\nzhayi0928{at}gmail.com\nI am a Senior Researcher in the\nMachine Learning Foundations group\nat\nMicrosoft Research Redmond.\nI did my Ph.D. at\nPrinceton University where I was privileged to be\nadvised by\nSanjeev Arora\n.\nI\nreceived the\nWallace Memorial Fellowship in Engineering,\none of the highest honors awarded to Ph.D. students. Prior to Princeton,\nI received one Bachelor's degree from Shanghai Jiao Tong University and another one from the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor where I was advised by\nHonglak Lee\n.\nI am a proud dad of a 2-year-old\nultra-cute\nShiba Inu named Lambo. He goes by Bobo or 啵啵, at his insistence.\nResearch\nTextbooks are all you need\nSuriya Gunasekar\n,\nYi Zhang\n,\nJyoti Aneja\n,\nCaio César Teodoro Mendes\n,\nAllie Del Giorno\n,\nSivakanth Gopi\n,\nMojan Javaheripi\n,\nPiero Kauffmann\n,\nGustavo de Rosa\n,\nOlli Saarikivi\n,\nAdil Salim\n,\nShital Shah\n,\nHarkirat Singh Behl\n,\nXin Wang\n,\nSébastien Bubeck\n,\nRonen Eldan\n,\nAdam Tauman Kalai\n,\nYin Tat Lee\n,\nYuanzhi Li\nSparks of Artificial General Intelligence: Early experiments with GPT-4\nSébastien Bubeck\n,\nVarun Chandrasekaran\n,\nRonen Eldan\n,\nJohannes Gehrke\n,\nEric Horvitz\n,\nEce Kamar\n,\nPeter Lee\n,\nYin Tat Lee\n,\nYuanzhi Li\n,\nScott Lundberg\n,\nHarsha Nori\n,\nHamid Palangi\n,\nMarco Tulio Ribeiro\n,\nYi Zhang\nLearning Threshold Neurons via the \"Edge of Stability\"\nKwangjun Ahn\n,\nSébastien Bubeck\n,\nSinho Chewi\n,\nYin Tat Lee\n,\nFelipe Suarez\n,\nYi Zhang\nNeurIPS 2023\n(#)\nYuhong Li\n,\nTianle Cai\n,\nYi Zhang\n,\nDeming Chen\n,\nDebadeepta Dey\nUnveiling Transformers with LEGO: a synthetic reasoning task\nWhat Makes Convolutional Models Great on Long Sequence Modeling?\n(#)Yi Zhang,\nArturs Backurs\n,\nSébastien Bubeck\n,\nRonen Eldan\n,\nSuriya Gunasekar\n,\nTal Wagner\n[code]\n[Seb's amazing presentation]\nRip van Winkle’s Razor: A Simple Estimate of Overfit to the Test Set\nSanjeev Arora, Yi Zhang\nOn Predicting Generalization using GANs\n(#)Yi Zhang, Arushi Gupta, Nikunj Saunshi, Sanjeev Arora\nICLR 2022\nSpotlight\nWhy are Convolutional Nets more Sample-Efficient than Fully-Connected Nets?\n(#) Zhiyuan Li,  Yi Zhang, Sanjeev Arora\nICLR 2021\n​\nOver-parameterized Adversarial Training: an Analysis Overcoming the Curse of Dimensionality\n(#) Yi Zhang*, Orestis Plevrakis*, Simon S. Du, Xingguo Li, Zhao Song, and Sanjeev Arora\nNeurIPS 2020\n​\nNo-Regret Prediction in Marginally Stable Systems\nUdaya Ghai, Holden Lee, Karan Singh, Cyril Zhang, and Yi Zhang\nCOLT 2020\n​\nA Sample Complexity Separation between Non-Convex and Convex Meta-Learning\n(#) Nikunj Saunshi, Yi Zhang, Mikhail Kohdak, and Sanjeev Arora\nICML 2020\n​\nCalibration, Entropy Rates, and Memory in Language Models\nMark Braverman, Xinyi Chen, Sham M. Kakade, Karthik Narasimhan, Cyril Zhang, and Yi Zhang\nICML 2020\n​\nExtreme Tensoring for Low-Memory Preconditioning\nNaman Agarwal, Xinyi Chen, Elad Hazan, Cyril Zhang, and Yi Zhang\nICLR 2020\n​\nExplaining Landscape Connectivity of Low-cost Solutions for Multilayer Nets\n(#) Rohith Kuditipudi, Xiang Wang, Holden Lee, Yi Zhang , Zhiyuan Li, Wei Hu, Sanjeev Arora, and Rong Ge\nNeurIPS 2019\n​\nEfficient Full-Matrix Regularization\nNaman Agarwal, Brian Bullins, Xinyi Chen, Elad Hazan, Karan Singh, Cyril Zhang and Yi Zhang\nICML 2019\n​\nSpectral Filtering for General Linear Dynamical Systems\nElad Hazan, Holden Lee, Karan Singh, Cyril Zhang, and Yi Zhang\nNeurIPS 2018\nOral Presentation\nStronger Generalization Bound for Deep Nets via a Compression Approach\nSanjeev Arora, Rong Ge, Behnam Neyshabur, and Yi Zhang\nICML 2018\n​\nTowards Provable Control for Unknown Linear Dynamical Systems\nSanjeev Arora, Elad Hazan, Holden Lee, Karan Singh, Cyril Zhang, and Yi Zhang\nICLR 2018 Workshop\n​\nNot-So-Random Features\nBrian Bullins, Cyril Zhang, Yi Zhang\nICLR 2018\n​\nDo GANs learn the distribution? Some Theory and Empirics\nSanjeev Arora, Andrej Risteski, and Yi Zhang\nICLR 2018\n​\nGeneralization and Equilibrium in Generative Adversarial Networks\nSanjeev Arora, Rong Ge, Yingyu Liang, Tengyu Ma, and Yi Zhang\nICML 2017\n​\nTowards Understanding Invertibility of Convolutional Neural Networks\n(#) Anna Gilbert, Yi Zhang, Kibok Lee, Yuting Zhang, and Honglak Lee\nIJCAI 2017\n​\nConvolutional Neural Networks with Low-Rank Regularization\n(#) Tai Cheng, Xiao Tong, Yi Zhang, Xiaogang Wang, and Weinan E\nICLR 2016\n​\nDeep Visual Analogy-Making\n(#) Scott Reed, Yi Zhang, Yuting Zhang, Honglak Lee\nNIPS 2015\nOral Presentation\nMisc.\nDissertation\nBlog posts featuring my works\nPredicting generalization using GANs\nRip van Winkle's Razor, a simple estimate for adaptive data analysis\nProving generalization of deep nets via compression\nLimitations of Encoder-Decoder GAN architectures\nDo GANs actually do distribution learning?\nGeneralization and Equilibrium in GANs\n​\n​\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant for\nCOS 324 Intro to Machine Learning, Fall 2018.\nTeaching Assistant for\nCOS 445 Economics and Computation, Spring 2019\n​\n​\nbottom of page"
