  "deep_homepage::Zhengyao Jiang::https://zhengyaojiang.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://zhengyaojiang.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/WecoAI",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhengyao-jiang-387b44145/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhengyao Jiang | Cofounder & CEO, Weco.ai\nZhengyao Jiang\nCofounder & CEO,\nWeco AI\nZheng = j-uhng; yao = y-aoww; Jiang = gee-ahng.\nI'm Zhengyao Jiang, Cofounder & CEO of\nWeco AI\n, and a computer scientist by training.\nI believe the scientific method is, at its core, an algorithm: hypothesize → experiment → analyse. As more of our frontier knowledge is encoded in software, from high-frequency trading systems to generative AI training pipelines, the next leap in AI will come from machines that can run the scientific innovation algorithm at scale and encode the knowledge into code.\nWeco AI\nis my bet on that future. Our AIDE algorithm converts the slow, manual “hill-climb” of research engineering into a fast, evaluation-driven search that routinely uncovers non-obvious, high-performing solutions. Think of it as a knowledge-generation engine that learns directly from empirical feedback rather than human hunches.\nThis focus on AI systems that learn from external feedback traces back to my PhD work at University College London, supervised by\nTim Rocktäschel\nand\nEdward Grefenstette\n, where I studied how reinforcement-learning agents can extract maximum value from every interaction with the environment. The same principle now guides everything we build at Weco: squeeze the most insight out of each compute cycle, and let the machine iterate toward discovery.\nFeatured Publications\nAIDE: AI-Driven Exploration in the Space of Code\nZhengyao Jiang, Dominik Schmidt, Dhruv Srikanth, Dixing Xu, Ian Kaplan, Deniss Jacenko, Yuxiang Wu\narXiv preprint arXiv:2502.13138, 2025.\n[\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n]\nH-GAP: Humanoid Control with a Generalist Planner\nZhengyao Jiang, Yingchen Xu, Nolan Wagener, Yicheng Luo, Michael Janner, Edward Grefenstette, Tim Rocktäschel, Yuandong Tian\nICLR 2024 (Spotlight).\n[\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n]\nEfficient Planning in a Compact Latent Action Space\nZhengyao Jiang, Tianjun Zhang, Michael Janner, Yueying Li, Tim Rocktäschel, Edward Grefenstette, Yuandong Tian\nICLR 2023.\n[\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n]"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Shaolei Zhang::https://zhangshaolei1998.github.io/": {
