  "deep_homepage::Ruihua Song::https://gsai.ruc.edu.cn/english/rsong": {
    "homepage": "https://gsai.ruc.edu.cn/english/rsong",
    "all_emails": [
      "rsong@ruc.edu.cn"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "﻿\nRuihua Song\nRuihua Song\nTenured Associate Professor\nDr. Song Ruihua, National Distinguished Professor of High-level Talents, is a tenured associate professor at Gaoling School of Artificial Intelligence, Renmin University of China. She has been Lead Researcher of Microsoft Research Asia and Chief Scientist of Microsoft XiaoIce. Her algorithm completed the first collection of AI-created poems in human history, \"The Sunlight Loses the Glass Window\", on May 2017. From 2021 to 2022, as an academic leader, she released Wenlan image-text alignment models, which were transferred to products by Kuaishou, OPPO, etc. In 2023, as a core member, she released Yulan large language model. She has published more than 100 academic papers and applied for more than 30 patents. She has been nominated for the WWW 2004 Best Paper Award and won the 2022 First Prize of the Natural Science Award of the Ministry of Education. She serves SIGIR, ACL, KDD, WWW, EMNLP, CIKM, etc. as Track Chairs, Area Chair, Senior PC, or PC. Her recent research interests include multimodal understanding, creation, and interaction.\nEnter Personal Website\nEducation\n2006.9 -2010.12, Dept. of Computer Science, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, Ph.D.; PhD thesis: Research on Web Information Retrieval Evaluation; Co-Advisors: Prof. YU Yong and Dr. HON Hsiao-Wuen\n2000.9 - 2003.1, Dept. of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, M.E.; Master thesis: Information Retrieval Based on Structural and Semantic Information; Advisor: Prof. MA Shaoping\n1996.9 - 2000.7, Dept. of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, B.E.\nWork Experience\n2020.9 – now, Gaoling School of ArtificialIntelligence, Renmin University of China; As a tenured Associate Professor; Research Interests: multimodal understanding and generation.\n2017.7–2020.8, Microsoft Software Center Asia; As a PrincipleData & Applied Science Lead; Research Interests: AI based creation, session-oriented chatbots, and multi-modality\n2003.4–2017.7, Microsoft Research Asia; As a Lead Researcher; Research Interests: Social and Mobile Computing, Web Information Retrieval, and Information Extraction\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\nMultimodal Understanding and Generation\nSocial and Mobile Computing\nWeb Information Retrieval\nWeb Information Extraction\nPublications\nMultimodal  Understanding and Generation\n?\nWenhui Tan, Bei Liu, Junbo Zhang, Ruihua Song, Jianlong\nFu.\nRoLD: Robot Latent\nDiffusion for Multi-task Policy Modeling\n.\nIn\nProceedings of the 31st International Conference on Multimedia Modeling,\n340-353, 2025.\n(Best Paper Award)\n?\nYuchong Sun, Bei Liu, Xu Chen, Ruihua Song, Jianlong Fu.\nViCo: Engaging\nVideo Comment Generation with Human Preference Rewards\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 6th ACM International\nConference on Multimedia in Asia, 2024.\n(Best Student Paper\nRunners-up Award)\n?\nXihua Wang, Yuyue Wang, Yihan Wu, Ruihua Song, Xu Tan,\nZehua Chen, Hongteng Xu, Guodong Sui.\nTiVA: Time-aligned\nVideo-to-audio Generation\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 32nd ACM International Conference\non Multimedia, 573-582, 2024. (Oral)\n?\nQian Cao, Xu Chen, Ruihua Song, Xiting Wang, Xinting\nHuang, Yuchen Ren.\nSee or Guess: Counterfactually\nRegularized Image Captioning\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 32nd ACM International Conference\non Multimedia, 965-974, 2024\n?\nChuhao Jin, Kening Ren, Lingzhen Kong, Xiting Wang,\nRuihua Song, Huan Chen.\nPersuading across Diverse\nDomains: a Dataset and Persuasion Large Language Model\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 62nd Annual Meeting of\nthe Association for Computational Linguistics, 1678-1706, 2024\n?\nYuchong Sun, Che Liu, Kun Zhou, Jinwen Huang, Ruihua\nSong, Wayne Xin Zhao, Fuzheng Zhang, Di Zhang, Kun Gai.\nParrot: Enhancing\nMulti-turn Instruction Following for Large Language Models\n.\nIn\nProceedings\nof the 62nd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics,\n9729-9750, 2024\n?\nYan Zeng, Hanbo Zhang, Jiani Zheng, Jiangnan Xia,\nGuoqiang Wei, Yang Wei, Yuchen Zhang, Tao Kong, Ruihua Song.\nWhat Matters in\nTraining a GPT4-Style Language Model with Multimodal Inputs?\nIn Proceedings of the 2024\nConference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational\nLinguistics, 7930-7957, 2024\n?\nYihan Wu, Ruihua Song, Xu Chen, Hao Jiang, Zhao Cao, Jin\nYu.\nUnderstanding\nHuman Preferences: Towards More Personalized Video to Text Generation\n.\nIn Proceedings of the ACM on Web Conference\n2024, 3952-3963, 2024\n?\nHongpeng Lin, Ludan Ruan, Wenke Xia, Peiyu Liu, Jingyuan\nWen, Yixin Xu, Di Hu, Ruihua Song, Wayne Xin Zhao, Qin Jin, Zhiwu Lu.\nTikTalk: A\nVideo-Based Dialogue Dataset for Multi-Modal Chitchat in Real World\n.\nIn\nProceedings of the 31st ACM International Conference on Multimedia, 1303-1313,\n2023\n?\nXu Gu, Yuchong Sun, Feiyue Ni, Shizhe Chen, Xihua Wang,\nRuihua Song, Boyuan Li, Xiang Cao.\nTeViS: Translating\nText Synopses to Video Storyboards\n.\nIn Proceedings of the 31st\nACM International Conference on Multimedia, 4968-4979, 2023\n?\nYihan Wu, Junliang Guo, Xu Tan, Chen Zhang, Bohan Li,\nRuihua Song, Lei He, Sheng Zhao, Arul Menezes, Jiang Bian.\nVideodubber:\nMachine Translation with Speech-aware Length Control for Video Dubbing\n.\nIn\nProceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 37 (11),\n13772-13779, 2023\n?\nYuchong Sun, Hongwei Xue, Ruihua Song, Bei Liu, Huan\nYang, Jianlong Fu.\nLong-form\nVideo-language Pre-training with Multimodal Temporal Contrastive Learning\n.\nAdvances\nin neural information processing systems 35, 38032-38045, 2022\n?\nQian Cao, Xu Chen, Ruihua Song, Hao Jiang, Guang Yang,\nZhao Cao.\nMulti-modal\nExperience Inspired AI Creation\n.\nIn\nProceedings of the 30th ACM\nInternational Conference on Multimedia, 1445-1454, 2022\n?\nNanyi Fei, Zhiwu Lu, Yizhao Gao, Guoxing Yang, Yuqi Huo,\nJingyuan Wen, Haoyu Lu, Ruihua Song, Xin Gao, Tao Xiang, Hao Sun, Ji-Rong Wen.\nTowards Artificial\nGeneral Intelligence via a Multim