  "deep_homepage::Houqiang Li::http://staff.ustc.edu.cn/~lihq/en/": {
    "homepage": "http://staff.ustc.edu.cn/~lihq/en/",
    "all_emails": [
      "lihq@ustc.edu.cn"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home - Houqiang Li's Homepage\nSkip to content\nHouqiang Li\nContact\nDept. of EEIS, University of Science and Technology of China\n443 Huangshan Road, P.O.Box 4 Hefei, Anhui, 230027,China\nEmail:\nlihq@ustc.edu.cn\nTel:\n+86-551-63601340\nFax:\n+86-551-63601342\nBio\nHouqiang Li is a professor and the Vice Dean of the School of Information Science and Technology, University of Science and Technology of China (USTC), and the Director of MOE-Microsoft Key Laboratory of Multimedia Computing and Communication. He received the B.S., M.Eng., and Ph.D. degrees in electronic engineering from USTC in 1992, 1997, and 2000, respectively. His research interests include image/video coding, image/video analysis, computer vision, deep learning and reinforcement learning, etc.. He has authored and co-authored over 300 papers in journals and conferences, and holds over 60 granted patents.\nHe is a fellow of IEEE. He is the associate editor (AE) of IEEE TMM, and served as the AE of IEEE TCSVT from 2010 to 2013. He served as the TPC Co-Chair of VCIP 2010, and he will serve as the General Co-Chair of ICME 2021. He is the winner of National Science Funds (NSFC) for Distinguished Young Scientists, the Distinguished Professor of Changjiang Scholars Program of China, the Leading Scientist of Ten Thousand Talent Program of China. He is the recipient of National Technological Invention Award of China (second class) in 2019 and the recipient of National Natural Science Award of China (second class) in 2015. He was the recipient of the Best Paper Award for VCIP 2012, the recipient of the Best Paper Award for ICIMCS 2012, and the recipient of the Best Paper Award for ACM MUM 2011. He received the award for the Excellent Ph.D Supervisor of Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS) for four times from 2013 to 2016.\nAreas of Interest\nImage/Video Coding and Transmission\nVideo Coding and Compression Standards\nImage and Video Coding Based on Deep Learning\nStereoscopic and 3D Coding\nVideo Coding Error Control\nVideo Coding Rate Control\nVideo Adaptation\nImage/Video Processing, Analysis and Computer Vision\nImage/Video Denoising, Enhancement, and Inpainting\nImage/Video Interpolation and Super-Resolution\nImage/Video Representation\nImage/Video Segmentation\nImage/Video Object Detection/Recognition/Tracking\nSign Language Recognition and Translation\nImage/Video Captioning\nMultimedia Search\nNear-Duplicate Image Retrieval\nLarge-Scale Indexing\nRanking and Re-Ranking\nMobile and Location-Based Multimedia Search\nSearch by Example\nDeep Learning and Reinforcement Learning\nPretrained Models in Deep Learning\nGenerative Adversarial Networks\nMultiagent Reinforcement Learning\nComputer Game Based on Reinforcement Learning\nTeaching Course\nâInformation Theoryâ\nâDigital Image Analysisâ\nâDigital Image Processingâ\nBack to top"
  },
