    "homepage_text": "Jiebo Luo's Home Page\nProfessor Jiebo Luo\nAlbert\r\n              Arendt Hopeman Professor\nDepartment of Computer\r\n                                  Science\n3101 Wegmans Hall\nUniversity of Rochester\nRochester, NY 14627\nEmail: username -at- domain.edu\nwhere username = jluo,\ndomain = cs.rochester.edu\nPhone: 585-276-5784\nProspective Students\nComputer Vision\nUrban Computing\nHealth/Wellness Analytics\nScene Classification\nBig\r\n              Data\nContextual Inference\nMachine\nLearning\nVision+Language\nMultimedia\nVideo\r\n              Analytics\nHuman-Centered Media & Interaction\nGeo Tagging\nAction Recognition\nHeterogeneous Information Networks\nSocial\r\n              Multimedia  Data Mining\nCrowdsourcing\nUser Profiling 360\nComputational Social Science\nMedical Image Computing\nAIGC\nAI for Science  Multimodal LLM\nNews\n2025\n11/13/2025:\nProf. Luo attends the\nIEEE Computer\r\n                                                          Society Awards\nCeremony\nto receive the\r\n                                                          2025\nEdward\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          J. McCluskey\r\n                                                          Technical\r\n                                                          Achievement\r\n                                                          Award\n10/10/2025: Congrats to\nJie\r\n                                                          An\n,\nwho\r\n          graduated in 2025 from URCS and is now an\nApplied Scientist with Amazon AGI (was\r\n                                                          previously a\r\n                                                          Research\r\n                                                          Scientist with\r\n                                                          Meta Reality\r\n                                                          Labs)\n,\r\n                                                          for winning\r\n                                                          the 2025\nACM SIGMM Award for\r\n                                                          Outstanding\r\n                                                          PhD Thesis\nfor his PhD\r\n                                                          thesis\r\n                                                          entitled \"\nText-to-Video\n\n\r\n                                                          Generation\r\n                                                          Based on\r\n                                                          Diffusion\r\n                                                          Models\n\"\n09/03/2025: An Interview with Prof. Luo by\r\n                                                          the\nIEEE\r\n                                                          Computer\r\n                                                          Society\n,\r\n                                                          entitled \"\nCuriosity\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Drives Broad\r\n                                                          Innovation and\r\n                                                          Real-world\r\n                                                          Solutions\n\"\n08/22/2025: \"\nText-to-Video\n\n\n\r\n                                                          AI Blossoms\r\n                                                          with New\r\n                                                          Metamorphic\r\n                                                          Video\r\n                                                          Capabilities\n\"\r\n                                                          is a recorded\r\n                                                          segment by\nThe\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Academic\r\n                                                          Minute\n.\r\n                                                          Hosted by Dr.\r\n                                                          Lynn\r\n                                                          Pasquerella,\r\n                                                          President of\r\n                                                          The American\r\n                                                          Association of\r\n                                                          Colleges and\r\n                                                          Universities,\r\n                                                          The Academic\r\n                                                          Minute\r\n                                                          features a\r\n                                                          different\r\n                                                          professor each\r\n                                                          day, drawing\r\n                                                          experts from\r\n                                                          top\r\n                                                          international\r\n                                                          research\r\n                                                          institutions.\r\n                                                          The module is\r\n                                                          syndicated to\r\n                                                          several\r\n                                                          stations\r\n                                                          throughout\r\n                                                          North America\r\n                                                          and streamed\r\n                                                          via the web\r\n                                                          internationally.\n05/07/2025: Congrats to newly minted Dr.\nHang Hua\nwho is joining\nMIT-IBM Watson AI Lab\n04/02/2025: Congrats to newly minted Dr.\nJie\r\n                                                          An\nwho is joining\nMeta Reality Labs\n03/31/2025:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Prof. Luo\nattends the\ninduction ceremony of\r\n                                                          Fellow of\r\n                                                          AIMBE\n(\nAmerican\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Institute for\r\n                                                          Medical and\r\n                                                          Biological\r\n                                                          Engineering\n)\n2024\n10/30/2024: Prof. Luo is a\nKeynote\r\n                                                          Speaker\nat\r\n                                                          the 2024\nACM\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Multimedia\r\n                                                          Conference\n10/16/2024: Prof. Luo wins the inaugural\nDebra\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Haring\r\n                                                          Excellence in\r\n                                                          Research Award\n,\nwhich recognizes \"a faculty member who has\r\n                                                          done research\r\n                                                          that has had a\r\n                                                          transformational\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          impact on the\r\n                                                          field, or who\r\n                                                          has\r\n                                                          accumulated a\r\n                                                          body of\r\n                                                          research that\r\n                                                          has changed\r\n                                                          the field in\r\n                                                          positive\r\n                                                          ways.\"\n10/10/2024: Some members of VIStA watched\r\n                                                          the\r\n                                                          magnificent\r\n                                                          aurora\r\n                                                          together off\r\n                                                          Webster Pier\r\n                                                          in Rochester,\r\n                                                          NY\n09/12/2024: Prof. Luo is an invited speaker\r\n                                                          at the\nGlobal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          AI Summit\r\n                                                          (GAIN)\n08/29/2024:\nCongratulations to\nHanjia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Lyu\nfor\r\n                                                          being awarded\r\n                                                          the 2024\nGoogle\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          PhD Fellowship\n08/27/2024:\nIEEE CS releases an\ninterview\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          with Prof. Luo\r\n                                                          at CVPR 2024\non industry\r\n                                                          vs. academic\r\n                                                          careers, why\r\n                                                          publishing,\r\n                                                          why attending\r\n                                                          conferences,\r\n                                                          how to choose\r\n                                                          research\r\n                                                          topics, and so\r\n                                                          on.\n08/07/2024: Our study that shows the tech\r\n                                                          community is\r\n                                                          split over AI\r\n                                                          is covered by\nFuturity\n,\nQuantum\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Zeitgeist\n,\r\n                                                          and\nCODU\r\n                                                          Compute\n.\n05/18/2024: Our study on the factors\r\n                                                          contributing\r\n                                                          to\r\n                                                          crowdfunding\r\n                                                          success is\r\n                                                          featured in\r\n                                                          the\nWall\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          Street Journal\n05/15/2024: Prof. Luo receives another\r\n                                                          major award -\r\n                                                          the 2024\nEdmund\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          A. Hajim\r\n                                                          Outstanding\r\n                                                          Faculty Award\n04/08/2024: (Day of Total Solar Eclipse):\r\n                                                          Prof. Luo\r\n                                                          receives the\r\n                                                          2024\nWilliam\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          H. Riker\r\n                                                          University\r\n                                                          Award for\r\n                                                          Excellence in\r\n                                                          Graduate\r\n                                                          Teaching\n,\r\n                                                          which\r\n                                                          recognizes a\r\n                                                          faculty member\r\n                                                          who has\r\n                                                          excelled in\r\n                                                          graduate\r\n                                                          instruction,\r\n                                                          particularly\r\n                                                          in the\r\n                                                          University's\r\n                                                          doctoral\r\n                                                          programs.\n03/28/2024: Congratulations to Alexander\r\n                                                          Martin for\r\n                                                          winning the\r\n                                                          2024\nCharles\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                                                          L. Newton\r\n                                                          Prize\n(awarded to\r\n                                                          senior\r\n                                                          engineering\r\n                                                          students who\r\n                                                          show a special\r\n                                                          proficiency in\r\n                                                          an engineering\r\n                                                          subject and\r\n                                                          have conducted\r\n                                                          research,\r\n                                                          given a\r\n                                                          presentation,\r\n                                                          or published a\r\n                                                          paper)\n01/15/2024: Congratulations to Alexander\r\n                                                          Martin for an\r\n                                                          Honorable\r\n                                                          Mention in the\n2023-2024\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\r\n                     ...[truncated]"
