  "deep_homepage::Lizhen Qu::https://research.monash.edu/en/persons/lizhen-qu/": {
    "homepage": "https://research.monash.edu/en/persons/lizhen-qu/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Lizhen Qu\n      -  Monash University\nMonash University Home\nSearch content at Monash University\nView Scopus Profile\nLizhen Qu\nDr\nSenior Lecturer\n,\nDepartment of Data Science & AI\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-7764-431X\nEmail\nLizhen.Qu\nmonash\nedu\n2008\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nBiography\nDr. Lizhen Qu is a senior lecturer at the Faculty of Information Technology at Monash University, a founding member of the AIM lab, and an expert in robust and privacy-preserving neuro-symbolic methods for natural language processing (NLP) and multimodal applications. His work seamlessly integrates deep learning, logical reasoning, and causality. In particular, his team were the first to investigate the negative impact of spurious correlations in dialogue research using causality theories and proposed algorithms to improve the robustness and generalizability of models across domains. In addition, he has conducted extensive research on a wide range of NLP applications, with a special focus on legal AI, digital health, and social NLP.  Prior to his current role, he served as a research scientist at Data61/CSIRO, and completed his PhD at Saarland University and the Max-Planck-Institute for Informatics. He also actively contributes to the NLP community, serving as an Area Chair for ACL Rolling Review (ARR), OpenReview Co-Chair for ACL 2025, and Workshop Co-Chair for IJCNLP-AACL 2025.\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n1\nFinished\n4\nActive\nTMLGenAI:\nTrustworthy Generative AI: Towards Safe and Aligned Foundation Models\nPhung, D.\n(Primary Chief Investigator (PCI)),\nVu, T.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nQu, L.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nLe, T.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nHaffari, R.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nWebb, G.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nNicholson, A.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nKe, Q.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nCai, J.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)) & Bui, T. (Chief Investigator (CI))\n11/06/24\n→\n30/06/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nHARNESS:\nHierarchical Abstractions and Reasoning for Neuro-Symbolic Systems\nRezatofighi, H.\n(Primary Chief Investigator (PCI)),\nGarcia De La Banda Garcia, M.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)), Li, Y.-F. (Chief Investigator (CI)),\nStuckey, P.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nGasevic, D.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)), Gutierrez, J. (Chief Investigator (CI)),\nQu, L.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nIgnatiev , A.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nSwiecki, Z.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nVered, M.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nChen, G.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nHaffari, R.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)) &\nSay, B.\n(Chief Investigator (CI))\n20/06/23\n→\n20/02/27\nProject\n:\nResearch\nCSIRO Next Generation Graduates Program:\nAI in Mental Health\nMcNaney, R. (Primary Chief Investigator (PCI)),\nOlivier, P.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nYap, M.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nCai, J.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nWu, L.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nWatterson, J.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nHaffari, R.\n(Partner Investigator (PI)),\nQu, L.\n(Partner Investigator (PI)),\nWilson Rajaratnam, S.\n(Partner Investigator (PI)),\nWang, T.\n(Partner Investigator (PI)),\nSharp, G.\n(Partner Investigator (PI)), Alvarez-Jimenez, M. (Chief Investigator (CI)), D'Alfonso, S. (Chief Investigator (CI)) & Kostakos, V. (Chief Investigator (CI))\nPola Practice Pty Ltd\n,\nCrank Group Pty Ltd\n5/04/23\n→\n31/12/27\nProject\n:\nResearch\nAccessible Data Exploration and Analysis for Blind People\nMarriott, K.\n(Primary Chief Investigator (PCI)),\nButler, M.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nZukerman, I.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)),\nQu, L.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)) & Lee, B. (Partner Investigator (PI))\nARC - Australian Research Council\n28/02/23\n→\n27/02/27\nProject\n:\nResearch\nCross-lingual text summarisation with a plan\nLi, Y.-F. (Primary Chief Investigator (PCI)),\nHaffari, R.\n(Chief Investigator (CI)) &\nQu, L.\n(Chief Investigator (CI))\n1/06/22\n→\n31/08/22\nProject\n:\nResearch\nResearch output\n56\nConference Paper\n9\nArticle\n1\nPaper\nAudio Is the Achilles’ Heel: Red Teaming Audio Large Multimodal Models\nYang, H.,\nQu, L.\n, Shareghi, E. &\nHaffari, R.\n,\n2025\n,\nNAACL 2025, Annual Conference of the Nations of the Americas Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics Proceedings of the Conference Volume 1: Long Papers.\nChiruzzo, L., Ritter, A. & Wang, L. (eds.). Kerrville TX USA:\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics (ACL)\n,\np. 9292–9306\n15 p.\n2025.naacl-long.470\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference Paper\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nAutomating IRAC analysis in Malaysian contract law using a semi-structured knowledge base\nKang, X.,\nQu, L.\n,\nSoon, L.-K.\n, Li, Z. &\nTrakic, A.\n,\n7 Jul 2025\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nArtificial Intelligence and Law.\n44 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\n2\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nNEUSIS: A Compositional Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Autonomous Perception, Reasoning, and Planning in Complex UAV Search Missions\nCai, Z.\n, Cardenas, C. R.,\nLeo, K.\n,\nZhang, C.\n, Backman, K., Li, H.,\nLi, B.\n, Ghorbanali, M., Datta, S.,\nQu, L.\n, Gutierrez, J.,\nIgnatiev, A.\n, Li, Y.-F.,\nVered, M.\n,\nStuckey, P. J.\n,\nDe La Banda, M. G.\n&\nRezatofighi, H.\n,\nSept 2025\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters.\n10\n,\n9\n,\np. 9502-9509\n8 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nScalable Frame-Based Construction of Sociocultural Norm Bases for Socially Aware Dialogues\nQu, S.,\nWang, W.\n, Zhou, X., Zhan, H., Li, Z.,\nQu, L.\n,\nLuo, L.\n, Li, Y. F. &\nHaffari, G.\n,\n7 Nov 2025\n,\nIn:\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications.\n21\n,\n11\n,\n17 p.\n, 317.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nWhen Refreshable Tactile Displays Meet Conversational Agents: Investigating Accessible Data Presentation and Analysis with Touch and Speech\nReinders, S.\n,\nButler, M.\n,\nZukerman, I.\n, Lee, B.,\nQu, L.\n&\nMarriott, K.\n,\nJan 2025\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics.\n31\n,\n1\n,\np. 864-874\n11 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\nResearch\n›\npeer-review\n9\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 66 research outputs"
