    "homepage_text": "Pengyi Li\nPengyi Li (李鹏翼)\nPhD student, Tianjin University\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nTwitter\n/\nZhihu\nI am a second-year PhD student at Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) Lab, Tianjin University (TJU), advised by Prof. Jianye Hao. I received my Bachelor's degree from the TianJin University too.\nResearch interest\nI focus on research on the\nReinforcement Learning\nand\nEvolutionary Algorithms\n, which include\nMulti-agent Reinforcement Learning, Multi-objective Reinforcement Learning, Multi-task Reinforcement Learning, and Evolutionary Reinforcement Learning\n. Recently, my emphasis has been on how to build better policy search algorithms and general policy.\nPublications and preprints\nPapers sorted by recency. Representative papers are\nhighlighted\n.\nEmbodiedScene: Towards Automated Generation of Diverse and Realistic Scenes for Embodied AI\nJinbin Qiao*,\nPengyi Li*\n, Peilong Han, Yan Zheng, Jianye HAO\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n) World Model Workshop\nBest Paper\n, 2025\nProject Link\nR*: Efficient Reward Design via Reward Structure Evolution and Parameter Alignment Optimization with Large Language Models\nPengyi Li\n, Jianye Hao, Hongyao Tang, Yifu Yuan, Jinbin Qiao, Zibin Dong, Yan Zheng\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2025\nLink\n/\nBibtex\nCleanDiffuser: An Easy-to-use Modularized Library for Diffusion Models in Decision Making\nZibin Dong, Yifu Yuan, Jianye Hao, Fei Ni, Yi Ma,\nPengyi Li\n, Yan Zheng\nArxiv Preprint(\nArxiv\n), 2024\nArXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nEvoRainbow: Combining Improvements in Evolutionary Reinforcement Learning for Policy Search\nPengyi Li\n, Jianye HAO, Hongyao Tang, Xian Fu, Yan Zheng\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2024\nLink\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nValue-Evolutionary-Based Reinforcement Learning\nPengyi Li\n, Jianye HAO, Hongyao Tang, Yan Zheng, Fazl Barez\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2024\nLink\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nDiffuserLite: Towards Real-time Diffusion Planning\nZibin Dong, Jianye Hao, Yifu Yuan, Fei Ni, Yitian Wang,\nPengyi Li\n, Yan Zheng\nArxiv Preprint(\nArxiv\n), 2024\nArXiv\n/\nBibtex\nBridging Evolutionary Algorithms and Reinforcement Learning: A Comprehensive Survey\nPengyi Li\n, Jianye Hao, Hongyao Tang, Xian Fu, Yan Zheng, Ke Tang\nArxiv Preprint(\nArxiv\n), 2024\nGithub Repository\n/\nArXiv\n/\nBibtex\nSample-Efficient Quality-Diversity by Cooperative Coevolution\nKe Xue, Ren-Jian Wang,\nPengyi Li\n, Dong Li, Jianye HAO, Chao Qian\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2024\nOpenReview\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nRACE: Improve Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning with Representation Asymmetry and Collaborative Evolution\nPengyi Li\n, Jianye Hao, Hongyao Tang, Yan Zheng, Xian Fu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2023\nLink\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nERL-Re^2: Efficient Evolutionary Reinforcement Learning with Shared State Representation and Individual Policy Representation\nJianye Hao,\nPengyi Li\n(Student First Author), Hongyao Tang, Yan Zheng, Xian Fu, Zhaopeng Meng\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2023\nArXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nPMIC: Improving Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning with Progressive Mutual Information Collaboration\nPengyi Li\n, Hongyao Tang, Tianpei Yang, Xiaotian Hao, Tong Sang, Yan Zheng, Jianye Hao, Matthew E. Taylor, Wenyuan Tao, Zhen Wang\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n)\n, 2022\nLink\n/\nCode\n/\nBibtex\nHyar: Addressing discrete-continuous action reinforcement learning via hybrid action representation\nBoyan Li, Hongyao Tang, Yan Zheng, Jianye Hao,\nPengyi Li\n, Zhen Wang, Zhaopeng Meng, Li Wang\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2022\nArXiv\n/\nBibtex\nMisc. open-source projects\nAwesome-Evolutionary-Reinforcement-Learning\n⭐ 285\nPengyi Li\nMay 2023\nProject Page\n/\nPaper\n/\nBibtex\nERL-Re^2 Implementation\n⭐ 64\nPengyi Li\nFebruary 2023\nProject Page\n/\nPaper\n/\nBibtex\nRACE Implementation\n⭐ 34\nPengyi Li\nMay 2023\nGithub\n/\nPaper\nPMIC Implementation\n⭐ 20\nPengyi Li\nSeptember 2022\nGithub\n/\nPaper\n/\nBibtex\nContact\nYou are very welcome to contact me regarding my research. I typically respond within a few days.\nI can be contacted directly at\nlipengyi\n[at]\ntju.edu.cn"
