    "github": "https://github.com/Agent-3154",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Botian XU (许博添) - Robotics & Reinforcement Learning Researcher\nBotian XU (许博添)\nHi, there. I am currently a PhD student at\nCUHK MAE\n. I received my B.S. in Computer Science from\nSUSTech\nin 2022.\n                After that, I spent 3 gap years at Tsinghua University, with\nProf. Yi Wu\nand\nProf. Huazhe Xu\n, working on\n                reinforcement learning and robotics.\nInterests:\nReinforcement Learning for Legged Robots\n3D Modeling and Perception for Robot Agents\nI am lucky to work closely with\nLiu Cao\n,\nQingzhou Lu\n, and\nHaoyang Weng\n.\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nbtx0424@outlook.com\nNews\nSept. 2025:\nOur paper\nFACET:\n                    Force-Adaptive Control via Impedance Reference Tracking for Legged Robots\nis accepted\n                for oral presentation at\nCoRL 2025\nin Seoul, Korea.\nAug. 2025:\nI ended my journey at\nTEA Lab\nand became a PhD student at\nCUHK MAE\n.\nSelected Publications\nFACET: Force-Adaptive Control via Impedance Reference Tracking for Legged Robots\nBotian Xu*, Haoyang Weng*, Qingzhou Lu*, Yang Gao, Huazhe Xu\nCoRL 2025 (Oral, top 10%)\nArtFormer: Controllable Generation of Diverse 3D Articulated Objects\nJiayi Su*, Youhe Feng*, Zheng Li, Jinhua Song, Yangfan He, Botao Ren, Botian Xu\nCVPR 2025 (top 15%)\nOmniDrones: An Efficient and Flexible Platform for Reinforcement Learning in Drone Control\nBotian Xu*, Feng Gao*, Chao Yu, Ruize Zhang, Yi Wu, Yu Wang\nIEEE RA-L & IROS 2024\nProjects\nOmniDrones\n[GitHub]\n[Docs]\nAn efficient and flexible platform for reinforcement learning in drone control, built on Isaac Sim and supporting various multi-rotor configurations."
  },
