    "homepage_text": "Bei Chen's Homepage (éè)\nBei Chen\néè\nSenior Researcher\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nNo.5 Dan Ling Street\nBeijing, China, 100080\nEmail: beichen at microsoft dot com\nBiography\nI am now a senior researcher at\nMicrosoft Research Asia\n. I joined Microsoft in 2017 after receiving my Ph.D. degree from\nTSAIL Group\nin\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nTsinghua University\n. I was jointly supervised by\nProf. Bo Zhang\nand\nProf. Jun Zhu\n.\nBefore that, I received the B.E. degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nof\nHarbin Institute of Technology\nin 2012.\nMy research interests are primarily on machine learning and its applications in natural language processing and data mining, especially latent feature models, probabilistic graphical models, Bayesian nonparametrics, reinforcement learning and deep learning.\nPublications\nQian Liu, Shengnan An, Jian-Guang Lou,\nBei Chen\n, Zeqi Lin, Yan Gao, Bin Zhou, Nanning Zheng, Dongmei Zhang.\nCompositional Generalization by Learning Analytical Expressions\n, In Proc. of the 34th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems, 2020. (NeurIPS 2020)\nQian Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Jian-Guang Lou, Bin Zhou, Dongmei Zhang.\nIncomplete Utterance Rewriting as Semantic Segmentation\n, In Proc. of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2020. (EMNLP 2020)\nYuntao Li,\nBei Chen\n, Qian Liu, Yan Gao, Jian-Guang Lou, Yan Zhang, Dongmei Zhang.\nâWhat Do You Mean by That?â A Parser-Independent Interactive Approach for Enhancing Text-to-SQL\n, In Proc. of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing, 2020. (EMNLP 2020)\nQian Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Jiaqi Guo, Jian-Guang Lou, Bin Zhou, Dongmei Zhang.\nHow Far are We from Effective Context Modeling? An Exploratory Study on Semantic Parsing in Contex\n, In Proc. of the Twenty-Ninth International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2020. (IJCAI 2020)\nYu Zeng, Yan Gao, Jiaqi Guo,\nBei Chen\n, Qian Liu, Jian-Guang Lou, Fei Teng, Dongmei Zhang.\nRECPARSER: A Recursive Semantic Parsing Framework for Text-to-SQL Task\n, In Proc. of the Twenty-Ninth International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2020. (IJCAI 2020)\nYongshun Gong, Zhibin Li, Jian Zhang, Wei Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Xiangjun Dong.\nA Spatial Missing Value Imputation Method for Multi-view Urban Statistical Data\n, In Proc. of the Twenty-Ninth International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2020. (IJCAI 2020)\nQian Liu, Yihong Chen,\nBei Chen\n, Jian-Guang Lou, Zixuan Chen, Bin Zhou, Dongmei Zhang.\nYou Impress Me: Dialogue Generation via Mutual Persona Perception\n, In Proc. of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, 2020. (ACL 2020)\nQian Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Haoyan Liu, Jian-Guang Lou, Lei Fang, Bin Zhou, Dongmei Zhang.\nA Split-and-Recombine Approach for Follow-up Query Analysis\n, In Proc. of Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing, Hong Kong, China, 2019. (EMNLP 2019)\nHaoyan Liu, Lei Fang, Qian Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Jian-Guang Lou, Zhoujun Li.\nLeveraging Adjective-Noun Phrasing Knowledge for Comparison Relation Prediction in Text-to-SQL\n, In Proc. of Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing, Hong Kong, China, 2019. (EMNLP 2019)\nWeiwei Cui, Xiaoyu Zhang, Yun Wang, He Huang,\nBei Chen\n, Lei Fang, Haidong Zhang, Jian-Guan Lou, Dongmei Zhang.\nText-to-Viz: Automatic Generation of Infographics from Proportion-Related Natural Language Statements\n, In Proc. of IEEE VAST INFOVIS SCIVIS, Vancouver, BC, Canada, 2019. (VIS 2019)\nYihong Chen,\nBei Chen\n, Xiangnan He, Chen Gao, Yong Li, Jian-Guang Lou, Yue Wang.\nLambdaOpt: Learn to Regularize Recommender Models in Finer Levels\n, In Proc. of ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining, Anchorage, AK, USA, 2019. (SIGKDD 2019) [\nCode\n]\nQian Liu,\nBei Chen\n, Jian-Guang Lou, Ge Jin, Dongmei Zhang.\nFANDA: A Novel Approach to Perform Follow-up Query Analysis\n, In Proc. of AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Honolulu, USA, 2019. (AAAI 2019)\nYihong Chen,\nBei Chen\n, Xuguang Duan, Jian-Guang Lou, Yue Wang, Wenwu Zhu, Yong Cao.\nLearning-to-Ask: Knowledge Acquisition via 20 Questions\n, In Proc. of ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining, London, United Kingdom, 2018. (SIGKDD 2018) [\nPoster\n]\nJun Zhu and\nBei Chen\n.\nLatent feature models for large-scale link prediction\n, Big Data Analytics, 2017.\nJun Zhu, Jiaming Song, and\nBei Chen\n.\nMax-Margin Nonparametric Latent Feature Models for Link Prediction\n, arXiv:1602.07428, 2016.\nBei Chen\n, Ning Chen, Jun Zhu, Jiaming Song and Bo Zhang.\nDiscriminative Nonparametric Latent Feature Relational Models with Data Augmentation\n, In Proc. of AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Phoenix, USA, 2016. (AAAI 2016)\n[\nAppendix\n]\nBei Chen\n, Jun Zhu, Nan Yang, Tian Tian, Ming Zhou and Bo Zhang.\nJointly Modeling Topics and Intents with Global Order Structure\n, In Proc. of AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Phoenix, USA, 2016. (AAAI 2016)\nBei Chen\n, Ning Chen, Yong Ren, Bo Zhang.\nNonparametric Latent Feature Relational Models with Data Augmentation\n,  in International Conference on Machine Learning, Workshop on Divergence Methods for Probabilistic Inference, Beijing, China, 2014.\nExperiences\n2016.06 - 2016.10\niDST, Large Scale Learning-Analytic Algorithm, Alibaba Cloud Computing, Beijing, China\nLarge-scale machine learning algorithms on distributed platform.\n2014.10 - 2015.06\nMicrosoft Research Asia, Beijing, China\nDiscourse analysis and discover patterns in scientific writing based on topic models.\nAward:\nStars of Tomorrow Internship Program\n2014.09\nCross-Modal Interaction in Natural and Artificial Cognitive Systems, Hamburg, Germany\nDiscuss on interdisciplinary research of computer science, cognitive science, psychology and robotics.\nSelected Awards\nGoogle Anita Borg Memorial Scholarship: Asia Pacific, 2016\nHeilongjiang Provincial Excellent Graduate, 2012\nIBM Outstanding Student Scholarship, 2011\nPivot of Merit Student of HIT, 2010\nTencent Technology Excellence Scholarship, 2010\nFirst Prize and Best Women's Team in ACM/ICPC the 4th Northeast China Multi-provincial College Programming Contest, 2010\nSecond Prize and Best Women's Team in ACM/ICPC the 5th Heilongjiang Province College Programming Contest, 2010\nSecond Prize and Best Women's Team in ACM/ICPC the 4th Heilongjiang Province College Programming Contest, 2009\nLast updated on December 2020."
