    "homepage_text": "Qiang Fu\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nQiang Fu\nQiang Fu\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nCV\n/\nContact\nI am\na second-year Ph.D. student in the Department of Computer Science at\nYale University\n, where I am fortunate to be advised by Prof.\nAndre Wibisono\n.\nPrior to Yale, I obtained my B.S. and M.S. degrees in Mathematics from\nSun Yat-sen University\n. During my master’s, I worked as a remote researcher advised by Prof.\nAshia Wilson\nat MIT.\nMy research lies broadly in optimization, statistics and machine learning. Recently, I am interested in inference and alignment mechanisms that improve the efficiency, reliability and reasoning capabilities of large-scale AI systems.\nPublications and Preprints\nStochastic Gradient Variational Inference with Price’s Gradient Estimator from Bures-Wasserstein to Parameter Space\nKyurae Kim,\nQiang Fu\n, Yi-An Ma, Jacob R. Gardner,\nTrevor Campbell\narXiv preprint\n, 2026\nHamiltonian Descent Algorithms for Optimization: Accelerated Rates via Randomized Integration Time\nQiang Fu\n, Andre Wibisono\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS), 2025 (\nSpotlight\n)\nFrom Randomized Hamiltonian Flow to Fast Stochastic Optimization\nAustin Feng,\nQiang Fu\n, Xiuyuan Wang, Andre Wibisono\nNeurIPS Workshop on Dynamics at the Frontiers of Optimization, Sampling, and Games\n, 2025\nMean-field\nU\nnderdamped Langevin\nD\nynamics and its\nS\npace\nt\nime\nD\niscretization\nQiang Fu\n, Ashia Wilson\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML),\n2024\nAccelerated\nS\ntochastic\nO\nptimization\nM\nethods under\nQ\nuasar-convexit\ny\nQiang Fu\n, Dongchu Xu, Ashia Wilson\nInternetional Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML)\n,\n2023\nThe\nF\nractional Laplacian\n-\nbased\nI\nmage\nI\nnpainting\nXiangkai Lian,\nQiang Fu\n, Weijie Su, Xinyu Zhang, Jia Li, Zheng-\na\nn Yao\nInverse Problems and Imaging\n,\n202\n4\nTeaching\nTA, CPSC 5860/4860: Probabilistic Machine Learning, Spring 2026\nService\nReviewer of AISTATS 2023, ICLR 2025–2026, NeurIPS 2025 (top reviewer), ALT 2026.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
