    "homepage_text": "Yichao Du\nYichao\nDu\nEmail: X@mail.ustc.edu.cn, where X=duyichao\n🎓: Hi there👋, I am a\nfirst\nsecond-year PhD student at the\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\n, working with Prof.\nEnhong Chen\nand Prof.\nTong Xu\n. I am a member of the\nBDAA Lab\nand the\nState Key Laboratory of Cognitive Intelligence\n. Currently, I am working as a research intern at Tencent AI Lab, mentored by\nZhirui Zhang\n. Prior to that, I worked as a research intern in the Language Technology Lab at Alibaba DAMO Academy.\n🎯: I am working in the field of NLP & Data Mining. My current research interests (in bold) and past experience can be summarized as follows:\nLarge Language Models\n: Multi-Agent; Evaluation; Multimodal LLM\nMultilingual and Multimodal Translation\n: End-to-End Speech Translation; Multilingual Neural Machine Translation\nData mining in healthcare: ICD coding; Extreme Multi-Label Classification\nKnowledge Graph: Entity Linking\nNews\nJan 19, 2024\nOne paper is accepted by ICLR’2024, about\nselective rationalization\n!\nDec 13, 2023\nOne paper is accepted by ICASSP’2024, about\nfederated speech-to-text modelling\n!\nOct 8, 2023\nOne paper is accepted by TASLP’2024, about\ndatastore distillation for kNN-LM/kNN-MT\n!\nOct 8, 2023\nThree papers are accepted by EMNLP’2023, about\ntheoretical understanding of kNN-MT\n,\ninteractive machine translation (oral)\nand\ninterventional rationalization\n!\nJul 10, 2023\nOur\nMineTrans speech translation system\nis accepted by IWSLT’2023, which win the\nchampionship\n🏆 in the (End-to-End) Speech-to-Speech Translation track.\nJan 21, 2023\nTwo papers are accepted by ICLR’2023, about\nfederated machine translation\nand\nefficient kNN-MT\n!\nOct 6, 2022\nOne paper is accepted by EMNLP’2022, about\nretrieval-augmented generation for speech translation (oral top3%)\n!\nSep 13, 2022\nOne paper is accepted by NeurIPS’2022, about\ndisentangled representation learning (spotlight top 8%)\n!"
  },
