    "homepage_text": "Xilin Chen----Visual Information Processing and Learning (VIPL)\nä¸­å½ç§å­¦é¢\nä¸¨\næä¸»ç«\nä¸¨\nä¸­æ\nLocationï¼\nHome\n>\näººåä¿¡æ¯\n>\nXilin Chen\nPeople\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Research Fellow\nPostdoctoral Fellow\nEngineer\nPast Member\nXilin Chen\nXilin Chen\nProfessor, ACM Fellowï¼IEEE Fellowï¼IAPR Fellow, CCF Fellow\nEmailï¼\nxlchen at ict dot ac dot cn\nResearch areaï¼\nComputer Vision, Pattern Recognition, Multimedia, Multimodal Human-computer Interaction\nDr. Xilin CHEN is a professor with the Institute of Computing Technology (ICT), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS).He is a Fellow of ACM, IEEE, IAPR, and CCF. His research interests include computer vision, pattern recognition, multimedia, and multimodal human-computer interaction, especially focusing on bio-inspired feature representation and learning, human-centered perception and analysis, and scene understanding. He is / was a PI for the major and key projects of the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), as well as the major projects of Science and Technology Innovation 2030 and the 973 Program. He was an Associate Editor of IEEE Trans. on Image Processing, and IEEE Trans. on Multimedia, and is currently Senior Associate Editor of Journal of Visual Communication and Image Representation. Associate Editor of Journal of Visual Communication and Image Representation, Associate Editor-in-chief of Journal of Computer, Associate Editor-in-chief of Artificial Intelligence and Pattern Recognition. Dr. Xilin Chen served as a General Chair / Program Chair of several international and domestic conferences and program committee, and is / was a (Lead) Area Chair of ICCV CVPR / NeurIPS for more than ten times.\nDr. Xilin Chen has been awarded the second prize of Chinaâs State Natural Science Award and the first prize of Natural Science of China Society of Image and Graphics. Dr. Chen was awarded the Beijing Municipal Teaching Master Award for his educational efforts. Dr. Chen has co-authored one book and published more than 400 papers in referred journals and conferences.\nExperience\nAcademic service\nJournal services\n[1] ââSenior Associate Editor, Journal of Visual Communication and Image Representation,âElsevier.\n[2] ââInformation Sciences Editorial Board Member, Fundamental Research, Elsevier.\n[3] ââAssociate Editor, Research, AAAS.\n[4] ââAssociate Editor, Virtual Reality and Intelligent Hardware, Beijing Zhongke Journal Publishing Co. Ltd.\n[5] ââAssociate Editor, Visual Computing for Industry, Biomedice and Art, Springer.\n[6] ââAssociate Editor, IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (2009-2014).\n[7] ââAssociate Editor, IEEE Transactions on Multimediaâ (2016-2020).\nConference services\n[1]\nâ\nââProgram Chair, the 18th IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition (FG 2024), May 27-31, 2024, Istanbul, Turkey.\n[2]\nâ\nââGeneral Chair, 2022 IEEE International Conference on Visual Communications and Image Processing (VCIP 2022), December 13-16, 2022, Suzhou, China.\n[3]\nâ\nââGeneral Chair, the 13th IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition (FG 2018), May 14-18, 2018, Xiâan, China.\n[4]\nâ\nââGeneral Chair, the 10th IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition (FG 2013), April 22-26, 2013, Shanghai, China\n[5]\nâ\nââProgram Chair, the 12th International Conference on Multimodal Interfaces and Workshop on Machine Learning for Multi-modal Interfaces (ICMI-MLMI 2010), November 8-11, 2010, Beijing, China.\n[6]\nâ\nââArea Chair, the Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2025 / 2024 / 2023\n).\n[7]\nâ\nââArea Chair / Lead AC , IEEE / CVF International Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV 2025 / 2023 / 2019\n).\n[8]\nâ\nââArea Chair / Lead AC, IEEE / CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR 2025 / 2023 / 2021 / 2020 / 2019 / 2017\n).\n[9]\nâ\nââArea Chair, the European Conference on Computer Vision (\nECCV 2024 / 2022\n).\n[10] âSenior PC, the ACM International Conference on Multimodal Interaction (\nICMI 2024 / 2022 / 2020 / 2019\n).\nResearch content\nResearch project\nInvited Talks and Papers\nKeynotes / Plenary Talks\n[1] ââThe Art of Non-Verbal Communication: Decoding Facial Expressions and Gestures for Seamless Human-Robot Interaction. 18th IEEE Computer Society Workshop on Biometrics in conjunction with CVPR 2023, June 18, 2023.\n[2] ââScene Graph Generation and Its Applications. Machines Can See 2022, July 1, 2021.\n[3] ââTowards Understandable Computer Vision. The 16th International Conference on Control, Automation, Robotics and Vision, December 15, 2020.\n[4] ââChallenges in Facial Expression Understanding. The 2nd International Workshop on Deep Learning for Pattern Recognition, co-location with ICPR, August 20, 2018.\n[5] ââTowards Scene Understanding, IAPR Joint International Workshops on Statistical Techniques in Pattern Recognition and Structural and Syntactic Pattern Recognition, August 18, 2018.\n[6] ââObject Categorization in Real World, Korea Computer Congress, June 30, 2016.\n[7] ââSign Language Recognition and Translation Based on Kinect, Microsoft Research Asia Faculty Summit, October 27, 2012.\nPapers\nPlease Refer My Google Scholar Profileï¼\nhttps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=vVx2v20AAAAJ&oi=ao"
  },
