    "homepage_text": "Dian Wang\nDian Wang\nPostdoc at Stanford\nFollow\nStanford, California\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nTwitter\nYouTube\nI am a Postdoctoral researcher at Stanford University working with\nProf. Shuran Song\nand\nProf. Jeannette Bohg\n. I obtained my Ph.D. at Northeastern University with\nProf. Robert Platt\nand\nProf. Robin Walters\n. My research interests include machine learning and robotics, with a focus on improving sample efficiency and generalization of robot learning.\nEmail: dianwang at stanford dot edu /\nCV\nNews\n07/2025: Super excited to start my postdoc at Stanford with Prof. Shuran Song and Prof. Jeannette Bohg!\n04/2025: Honored to receive\nNortheastern Outstanding Ph.D. Student Award in Research\n!\n03/2025: Invited talk at\nBoston Symmetry Day\n.\n11/2024:\nEquivariant Diffusion Policy\nis nominated as an Outstanding Paper Award Finalist at CoRL 2024!\n10/2024: Robin and I presented\nPushing the Limits of Equivariant Neural Networks\nat the\nNeurReps Speaker Series\nat MIT.\n09/2024: Three papers are accepted at CoRL 2024,\nEquivariant Diffusion Policy\nis accepted as an oral presentation.\n09/2024: I had a great time visiting the UPenn GRASP lab and presenting at the GRASP SFI seminar. Recording of my talk:\nlink\n.\n07/2024: We are organizing the\nWorkshop on Geometric and Algebraic Structure in Robot Learning\nat RSS 2024.\n07/2024: Blogpost in GRAM Workshop @ ICML 2024:\nCorrect, Incorrect and Extrinsic Equivariance\n.\n06/2024: I am proud to be part of the\nKhoury Story\n!\n04/2024: I will be returning to the Boston Dynamic AI Institute as a summer intern.\n09/2023: Our paper\nA General Theory of Correct, Incorrect, and Extrinsic Equivariance\nis accepted at NeurIPS 2023.\n07/2023: Recording of our\nWorkshop on Symmetries in Robot Learning\nis available\nhere\n.\n06/2023: I am honored to receive the\n2023 JP Morgan Chase PhD Fellowship\n!\n04/2023: I give a guest lecture,\nEquivariant Learning for Robotic Manipulation\n. The lecture summarizes our latest research, so be sure to check it out!\n03/2023: We are organizing the\nWorkshop on Symmetries in Robot Learning\nat RSS 2023.\n02/2023: I will be joining the Boston Dynamic AI Institute as a summer intern.\n01/2023: Our paper\nThe Surprising Effectiveness of Equivariant Models in Domains with Latent Symmetry\nis accepted at ICLR 2023 as a spotlight presentation.\n01/2023: Two papers are accepted at ICRA 2023.\nmore ▾\nPublication\nEquivariant Diffusion Policy for Sample-Efficient Robotic Manipulation\nDian Wang\n, Stephen Hart, David Surovik, Tarik Kelestemur, Haojie Huang, Haibo Zhao, Mark Yeatman, Xupeng Zhu, Boce Hu, Mingxi Jia, Jiuguang Wang, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nIJRR 2026\nPDF\nRAVEN: End-to-end Equivariant Robot Learning with RGB Cameras\nDavid Klee*, Boce Hu*, Andrew Cole, Heng Tian,\nDian Wang\n, Robert Platt\n†\n, Robin Walters\n†\nICLR 2026\nPDF\nA Practical Guide for Incorporating Symmetry in Diffusion Policy\nDian Wang\n, Boce Hu, Shuran Song, Robin Walters\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nNeurIPS 2025\nWebpage\nPDF\n3D Equivariant Visuomotor Policy Learning via Spherical Projection\nBoce Hu,\nDian Wang\n, David Klee, Heng Tian, Xupeng Zhu, Haojie Huang, Robert Platt, Robin Walters\nNeurIPS 2025,\nSpotlight\nWebpage\nPDF\nResidual Rotation Correction using Tactile Equivariance\nYizhe Zhu, Zhang Ye, Boce Hu, Haibo Zhao, Yu Qi,\nDian Wang\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nPreprint\nWebpage\nPDF\nGeneralizable Hierarchical Skill Learning via Object-Centric Representation\nHaibo Zhao, Yu Qi, Boce Hu, Yizhe Zhu, Ziyan Chen, Xupeng Zhu, Owen Howell, Haojie Huang, Robin Walters,\nDian Wang\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nPreprint\nWebpage\nPDF\nHierarchical Equivariant Policy via Frame Transfer\nHaibo Zhao*,\nDian Wang*\n, Yizhe Zhu, Xupeng Zhu, Owen Howell, Linfeng Zhao, Yaoyao Qian, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nICML 2025\nWebpage\nPDF\nPush-Grasp Policy Learning Using Equivariant Models and Grasp Score Optimization\nBoce Hu*, Heng Tian*,\nDian Wang\n, Haojie Huang, Xupeng Zhu, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nRAL 2025\nWebpage\nPDF\nLearning Efficient and Robust Language-conditioned Manipulation using Textual-Visual Relevancy and Equivariant Language Mapping\nMingxi Jia, Haojie Huang, Zhewen Zhang, Chenghao Wang, Linfeng Zhao,\nDian Wang\n, Jason Xinyu Liu, Robin Walters, Robert Platt, Stefanie Tellex\nRAL 2025\nWebpage\nPDF\nCoarse-to-Fine 3D Keyframe Transporter\nXupeng Zhu, David Klee*,\nDian Wang*\n, Boce Hu, Haojie Huang, Arsh Tangri, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nPreprint\nPDF\nMATCH POLICY: A Simple Pipeline from Point Cloud Registration to Manipulation Policies\nHaojie Huang, Haotian Liu,\nDian Wang\n, Robin Walter\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nICRA 2025\nWebpage\nPDF\nEquivariant Diffusion Policy\nDian Wang\n, Stephen Hart, David Surovik, Tarik Kelestemur, Haojie Huang, Haibo Zhao, Mark Yeatman, Jiuguang Wang, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2024,\nOutstanding Paper Award Finalist\n🏆\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nTalk\nCode\nOrbitGrasp: SE(3)-Equivariant Grasp Learning\nBoce Hu, Xupeng Zhu*,\nDian Wang*\n, Zihao Dong*, Haojie Huang*, Chenghao Wang*, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2024\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nIMAGINATION POLICY: Using Generative Point Cloud Models for Learning Manipulation Policies\nHaojie Huang, Karl Schmeckpeper*,\nDian Wang*\n, Ondrej Biza*, Yaoyao Qian, Haotian Liu, Mingxi Jia, Robert Platt, Robin Walters\nCoRL 2024\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nEquivariant Offline Reinforcement Learning\nArsh Tangri, Ondrej Biza,\nDian Wang\n, David Klee, Owen Howell, Robert Platt\nPreprint\nPDF\nFourier Transporter: Bi-Equivariant Robotic Manipulation in 3D\nHaojie Huang, Owen Lewis Howell*,\nDian Wang*\n, Xupeng Zhu*, Robert Platt\n†\n, Robin Walters\n†\nICLR 2024\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nLeveraging Symmetries in Pick and Place\nHaojie Huang,\nDian Wang\n, Arsh Tangri, Robin Walters\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nThe International Journal of Robotics Research. 2024\nPDF\nCode\nA General Theory of Correct, Incorrect, and Extrinsic Equivariance\nDian Wang\n, Xupeng Zhu, Jung Yeon Park, Mingxi Jia, Guanang Su, Robert Platt, Robin Walters\nNeurIPS 2023\nPDF\nTalk\nCode\nEquivariant Reinforcement Learning under Partial Observability\nHai Huu Nguyen, Andrea Baisero, David Klee,\nDian Wang\n, Robert Platt, Christopher Amato\nCoRL 2023\nWebpage\nPDF\nCode\nOn Robot Grasp Learning Using Equivariant Models\nXupeng Zhu,\nDian Wang\n, Guanang Su, Ondrej Biza, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nAutonomous Robots. 2023\nWebpage\nPDF\nCode\nThe Surprising Effectiveness of Equivariant Models in Domains with Latent Symmetry\nDian Wang\n, Jung Yeon Park, Neel Sortur, Lawson L.S. Wong, Robin Walters\n†\n, Robert Platt\n†\nICLR 2023,\nSpotlight\nWebpage\nPDF\nOpenReview\nVideo\nTalk\nCode\nSEIL: Simulation-augmented Equivariant Imitation Learning\nMingxi Jia*,\nDian Wang*\n, Guanang Su, David Klee, Xupeng Zhu, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nICRA 2023\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nEdge Grasp Network: Graph-Based SE(3)-invariant Approach to Grasp Detection\nHaojie Huang,\nDian Wang\n, Xupeng Zhu, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nICRA 2023\nWebpage\nPDF\nCode\nOn-Robot Learning With Equivariant Models\nDian Wang\n, Mingxi Jia, Xupeng Zhu, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2022\nWebpage\nPDF\nOpenReview\nVideo\nCode\nLeveraging Fully Observable Policies for Learning under Partial Observability\nHai Huu Nguyen, Andrea Baisero,\nDian Wang\n, Christopher Amato, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2022\nWebpage\nPDF\nOpenReview\nVideo\nCode\nBulletArm: An Open-Source Robotic Manipulation Benchmark and Learning Framework\nDian Wang*\n, Colin Kohler*, Xupeng Zhu, Mingxi Jia, Robert Platt\nISRR 2022\nPDF\nCode\nEquivariant Transporter Network\nHaojie Huang,\nDian Wang\n, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nRSS 2022\nICRA 2022 Workshop on Scaling Robot Learning,\nBest Paper Award Finalist\nWebpage\nPDF\nCode\nSample Efficient Grasp Learning Using Equivariant Models\nXupeng Zhu,\nDian Wang\n, Ondrej Biza, Guanang Su, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nRSS 2022\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nCode\nSO(2)-Equivariant Reinforcement Learning\nDian Wang\n, Robin Walters, Robert Platt\nICLR 2022,\nSpotlight\nWebpage\nPDF\nOpenReview\nVideo\nTalk\nCode\nEquivariant Q Learning in Spatial Action Spaces\nDian Wang\n, Robin Walters, Xupeng Zhu, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2021\nWebpage\nPDF\nOpenReview\nPoster\nVideo\nCode\nDesign Guidelines for Human-Robot Interaction with Assistive Robot Manipulation Systems\nAlexander Wilkinson, Michael Gonzales, Patrick Hoey, David Kontak,\nDian Wang\n, Noah Torname, Amelia Sinclaire, Zhao Han, Jordan Allspaw, Robert Platt, Holly Yanco\nPaladyn, Journal of Behavioral Robotics. 2021\nPaper\nAction Priors for Large Action Spaces in Robotics\nOndrej Biza,\nDian Wang\n, Robert Platt, Jan-Willem van de Meent, Lawson LS Wong\nAAMAS 2021\nPDF\nCode\nPolicy learning in SE (3) action spaces\nDian Wang\n, Colin Kohler, Robert Platt\nCoRL 2020\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\nTalk\nCode\nTowards Assistive Robotic Pick and Place in Open World Environments\nDian Wang\n, Colin Kohler, Andreas ten Pas, Alexander Wilkinson, Maozhi Liu, Holly Yanco, Robert Platt\nISRR 2019\nWebpage\nPDF\nVideo\n* indicates equal contribution;\n†\nindicates equal advising.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
