      "atlaswang@utexas.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Atlas Wang | Texas ECE - Electrical & Computer Engineering at UT Austin\nSkip to main content\nBack to Faculty Directory\natlaswang@utexas.edu\n512-471-1866\nOffice:\nEER 6.886\nAtlas Wang\nAssociate Professor\nTemple Foundation Endowed Faculty Fellowship #7\nProf. Zhangyang “Atlas” Wang is a tenured associate professor and holds the Temple Foundation Endowed Faculty Fellowship #7 in the Chandra Family Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at The University of Texas at Austin. He is also a faculty member of UT Computer Science, and the Oden Institute CSEM program. Since May 2024, Dr. Wang has been on leave from UT Austin to serve as the full-time Research Director for XTX Markets in New York City, leading groundbreaking efforts at the intersection of algorithmic trading and deep learning.\nPreviously, he was the Jack Kilby/Texas Instruments Endowed Assistant Professor in the same department from 2020 to 2023; and an Assistant Professor of Computer Science and Engineering at Texas A&M University from 2017 to 2020. Alongside his academic career, he has also explored multiple exciting opportunities in the industry. He was a visiting scholar at Amazon Search from 2021 to 2022, leveraging geometric deep learning for recommendation systems. Later, he took on the (part-time) role of Director of AI Research & Technology for Picsart from 2022 to 2024, where he led the company’s ambitious initiative in video generative AI. He earned his Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering from UIUC in 2016, under the guidance of Professor Thomas S. Huang, and his B.E. in EEIS from USTC in 2012.\nProf. Wang has broad research interests in machine learning and optimization. Currently, his research passion centers on establishing the theoretical and algorithmic foundations of generative AI and neurosymbolic AI. His primary goal is to develop structured, modular representations that enable efficient and robust learning in overparameterized model spaces, unifying neural computation with symbolic reasoning. These drive progress across core AI architectures - from Transformers and large language models to diffusion models and 3D scene representations - while also catalyzing interdisciplinary advances, including AI-enabled medicine. His research is gratefully supported by NSF, DARPA, ARL, ARO, IARPA, DOE, as well as dozens of industry and university grants. Prof. Wang co-founded the new Conference on Parsimony and Learning (CPAL) and served as its inaugural Program Chair. He regularly serves as conference (senior) area chairs, journal editors, invited speakers, tutorial/workshop organizers, various panelist positions and reviewers. He is an ACM Distinguished Speaker and an IEEE senior member.\nProf. Wang has received many research awards, including an NSF CAREER Award, an ARO Young Investigator Award, an IEEE AI's 10 To Watch Award, an AI 100 Top Thought Leader Award, an INNS Aharon Katzir Young Investigator Award, a Google Research Scholar award, an IBM Faculty Research Award, a J. P. Morgan Faculty Research Award, an Amazon Research Award, a Sony Faculty Research Award, an Adobe Data Science Research Award, a Meta Reality Labs Research Award, and two Google TensorFlow Model Garden Awards. His team has won four best paper awards (NeuS 2025, CVPR 2025 AI4CC, IEEE SPS 2024, LoG 2022) and two honorable mentions (MLSys 2025, VLDB 2024). He feels most proud of being surrounded by some of the world's most brilliant students: his Ph.D. students include winners of eleven prestigious fellowships (NSF GRFP, Google, Apple, NVIDIA,  IBM ×2, Amazon×2, Adobe, Qualcomm, and Snap), among many other honors.\nResearch Areas\nDecision, Information, and Communications Engineering (DICE)\nResearch Interests\nMachine Learning\nComputer Vision\nOptimization\nResearch Groups\nWireless Networking and Communications Group (WNCG)\nVisual Informatics Group\nCenter for Autonomy\nGroup Website\nGroup Website\nGoogle Scholar\nRelated Articles\n• Wang Receives Science of Trustworthy AI Grant\n• Postdoc Jianing Zhu Receives 2025 TrustAI Rising Star Award\n• AI Models Get Brain Rot, Too\n• Four Texas ECE Students Awarded Amazon AI PhD Fellowships\n• Texas ECE Grad Student Peihao Wang Receives Google PhD Fellowship\n• Peihao Wang Named Stanford Rising Star in Data Science\n• Atlas Wang Receives NSF AIMing Award for AI Research\n• Wenyan Cong Receives Best Paper Award at CVPR Workshop\n• Researchers Receive Outstanding Paper Award at MLSys 2025\n• Atlas Wang and Peihao Wang Receive DARPA Disruptive Idea Paper Award\n• Atlas Wang and Alumni Receive IEEE SPS Young Author Best Paper\n• Peihao Wang Receives Best Paper at ACM SIGGRAPH Asia 2024\n• Ruisi Cai Receives 2025 NVIDIA Graduate Fellowship\n• Junyuan Hong Named Best Paper Award Finalist at VLDB2024\n• Wuyang Chen Receives Two Dissertation Awards\n• Texas ECE Student and Postdoc Named MLCommons Rising Stars\n• Jon Tamir and Atlas Wang Receive Google Research Scholar Awards\n• Atlas Wang has been named one of \"AI's 10 to Watch\" by IEEE\n• Four Texas ECE Students Win Prestigious NSF Graduate Research Fellowships\n• Yifan Jiang Receives 2023 Apple Scholars in AI/ML PhD Fellowship\n• Shiwei Liu and Visual Informatics Group Receive Best Paper Award at LoG 2022\n• Dejia Xu Receives Snap PhD Fellowship\n• Three Texas ECE Teams Win Qualcomm Innovation Fellowships\n• Atlas Wang Receives INNS 2021 Aharon Katzir Young Investigator Award\n• Tianlong Chen Awarded Adobe Research Fellowship\n• Researchers Develop New Method to Predict and Optimize Performance of Deep Learning Models\n• Five Texas ECE Faculty Receive NSF CAREER Awards\n• Prof. Atlas Wang Receives Multiple Grants for work on Artificial Intelligence\n• New 6G Research Center Unites Industry Leaders and UT Wireless Experts\n• Texas ECE PhD Student Tianlong Chen Receives 2021 IBM PhD Fellowship\n• 5 Questions with Cockrell’s Newest Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence Expert, Atlas Wang\n• Reducing energy use in neural networks\n• Shrinking massive neural networks used to model language\n• Atlas Wang Receives Adobe Data Science Research Award\n• New Faculty Join Texas ECE\n© The University of Texas at Austin 2025 |\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nWeb Accessibility\nECE Direct\nCanvas\nENGR Direct Faculty & Staff\nENGR Direct Students\nUT Direct\nUT Directory\nContact Us\nGiving\nUser Login\nSubscribe to Emails\nFollow Texas ECE"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Jimeng Sun::https://www.sunlab.org/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.sunlab.org/",
    "all_emails": [
      "jimeng@illinois.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/sunlabuiuc",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jimengsun/",
    "homepage_text": "Sunlab - AI for Healthcare Research\nDr. Jimeng Sun\nToggle menu\nDr. Jimeng Sun\nHealth Innovation Professor\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\nDr. Jimeng Sun is a Health Innovation Professor at the Siebel School of Computing and Data Science and Carle Illinois College of Medicine at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, where he leads groundbreaking research at the intersection of artificial intelligence and healthcare. As co-founder of Keiji AI, he is pioneering the transformation of clinical trials through advanced AI optimization and predictive modeling, accelerating drug development and improving trial success rates.\nResearch Excellence & Impact\nDr. Sun's research portfolio spans the full spectrum of AI-driven healthcare innovation, from clinical AI systems and drug discovery to AI for clinical trials and machine learning for biosignals. His work has produced transformative advances in:\nClinical AI Systems & Healthcare Analytics:\nDeveloping interpretable models like RETAIN for healthcare prediction, building sophisticated patient similarity measures, temporal clinical event prediction models, and designing AI systems for medication recommendation and clinical outcome prediction that are actively deployed in healthcare settings\nDrug Discovery & Development:\nCreating novel molecular optimization frameworks, drug-target interaction prediction models, and AI-driven therapeutic discovery platforms including the acclaimed Therapeutics Data Commons\nAI for Clinical Trials:\nPioneering patient-trial matching systems, clinical trial outcome prediction models, and optimization frameworks for trial design and patient recruitment through advanced deep learning and graph neural networks\nMachine Learning for Biosignals:\nAdvancing expert-level sleep staging with deep neural networks, creating automated seizure classification systems, and developing AI models for EEG interpretation and cardiac monitoring from physiological data streams\nWith over 40,000 citations and an h-index of 101, Dr. Sun has authored more than 500 publications in top-tier venues including Nature, NEJM AI, and leading AI conferences. His research has been recognized with prestigious awards and has directly influenced clinical practice through collaborations with major healthcare institutions.\nIndustry Collaboration\nNamed one of the Top 100 AI Leaders in Drug Discovery and Advanced Healthcare, Dr. Sun bridges academic research with real-world healthcare applications. Through Keiji AI and partnerships with industry leaders including IQVIA, Medidata, and GE Healthcare, his innovations are transforming how clinical trials are designed, conducted, and analyzed.\nHis collaborative network spans premier healthcare institutions including Massachusetts General Hospital, Beth Israel Deaconess, Northwestern, Vanderbilt, and OSF Healthcare, ensuring his research addresses the most pressing challenges in modern medicine.\nAcademic Background\nDr. Sun received his B.S. and M.Phil. in Computer Science from the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology and his Ph.D. from Carnegie Mellon University.\nView Publications\nResearch Interests\nKeiji AI\nAcademic & Professional Profiles\nGoogle Scholar\nDBLP\nPubMed\nLinkedIn\nX/Twitter\nJoin Sunlab: Where AI Meets Real-World Healthcare Impact\nAt Sunlab, we're not just publishing papers—we're building real-world AI systems that improve healthcare. Led by Prof. Jimeng Sun, we work on cutting-edge topics like clinical foundation models, interpretable ML, and generative AI for medicine. You'll get to collaborate with top hospitals, industry leaders, and an ambitious team pushing the boundaries of what's possible in AI for health.\nIf you want your research to matter—not just in theory, but in practice—Sunlab is the place to be.\nFor Prospective CS Students\nInterested in applying AI to healthcare? Join Sunlab to work on cutting-edge research at the intersection of machine learning and medicine. To get started, check out PyHealth—our open-source framework for healthcare ML—and contribute a pull request. Then reach out to me to discuss further opportunities!\nExplore PyHealth\nFor Industry Collaborators\nWe welcome collaborations with hospitals, pharma, and healthtech companies. At Sunlab, we have a strong track record of delivering robust models, scalable software, and high-impact publications through joint projects. Feel free to contact me directly to explore partnership opportunities.\nContact us\nFor Medical students, Residents and Fellows\nSunlab is looking for motivated clinicians with coding skills (Python or R), basic machine learning knowledge, and at least two months of dedicated time to work on impactful research projects in predictive modeling and generative AI. This is a great opportunity to build technical skills, contribute to publications, and stand out in academic medicine or digital health. If interested, please email me your CV and code samples.\nContact us\nLearn about AI in Health!\nOur AI for Health webinar series brings together cutting-edge research, real-world applications, and thought leaders from academia and industry to explore how AI is transforming healthcare. Whether you're a student passionate about impact-driven innovation or a collaborator from pharma, hospitals, or tech, this series is your gateway to the latest in predictive modeling, clinical decision support, and beyond.\n🔬 Explore Future Webinars\nCheck out our upcoming webinar schedule and topics\nView Schedule\n📬 Get Notified\nJoin our mailing list for webinar updates and announcements\nJoin Mailing List\n📺 Catch Up on Past Talks\nWatch previous webinars on our YouTube channel\nYouTube Channel\nBe part of the conversation shaping the future of AI in medicine.\nPublications\nView Dr. Sun's research publications, conference papers, and journal articles.\nBrowse Publications\nResearch Team\nMeet the graduate students, researchers, and collaborators in our lab.\nMeet the Team\nSoftware\nExplore PyHealth, our comprehensive Python library for healthcare predictive modeling.\nView Software"
  },
