    "homepage_text": "Yifan ZHANG's Homepage\nYifan Zhang (张祎凡)\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nCity University of Hong Kong (Dongguan)\nOffice: AC4, 502\nEmail: yif.zhang@cityu-dg.edu.cn\nAbout Me\nI am constantly looking for self-motivated RAs to start and build our team together!\nResearch Interests\nMy current research interests include spatial-temporal modelling, motion planning, trajectory prediction, car-following model, lane-change model, and intelligent transportation systems.\nNews\nThe paper \"ICSFuzz: Collision Detector Bug Discovery in Autonomous Driving Simulators\" is accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing\n.\nThe paper \"STRAP: Spatio-Temporal Pattern Retrieval for Out-of-Distribution Generalization\" is accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025\n. See you in San Diego!\nThe paper \"Network-wide Freeway Traffic Estimation Using Sparse Sensor Data: A Dirichlet Graph Auto-Encoder Approach\" is accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n.\nOur model \"Parallel ModeSec\" won the first place in 2025 WOD Challenges - Interaction Prediction Challenge!\nThe paper \"Rethinking Graph Domain Adaptation: A Spectral Contrastive Perspective\" is accepted by\nECML-PKDD 2025\n. See you in Portugal!\nThe paper \"MoGERNN: An Inductive Traffic Predictor for Unobserved Locations in Dynamic Sensing Networks\" is accepted by\nTransportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies\n.\nThe paper \"CASAformer: Congestion-Aware Sparse Attention Transformer for Traffic Speed Prediction\" is accepted by\nCommunications in Transportation Research\n.\nResearch and Education\nBefore joining CityU-DG, I was a Postdoc Research Fellow at the\nInstitute for Transport Planning and Systems of ETH Zürich\n. My major research interests lie in autonomous driving, motion planning, car-following model, lane-change model, and intelligent transportation systems.\r\n\t\t    \tI completed my doctoral degree under the supervision of\nProf. Jianping Wang\nat City University of Hong Kong in Summer 2022.  My doctoral thesis focuses on Human Driving Behavior Modeling and Applications in Autonomous Driving.\nI obtained my M.Eng. degree and B.Sc. degree from ENSIIE, France (2014-2017) and Xidian University, China (2011-2015), respectively.\nPublications\n[TR-Part B 2026]\nLinghang Sun\n,\nYifan Zhang\n, Cristian Axenie, Margherita Grossi,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"The Fragile Nature of Road Transportation Systems\"\n. Accepted by\nTransportation Research Part B: Methodological\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[TDSC 2026]\nWeiwei Fu,\nHeqing Huang\n,\nYifan Zhang\n, Ke Zhang, Jin Huang, Wei-Bin Lee,\nJianping Wang\n.\n\"ICSFuzz: Collision Detector Bug Discovery in Autonomous Driving Simulators\"\n. Accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nWeb page\n]\n[NIPS 2025]\nHaoyu Zhang, Wentao Zhang, Hao Miao, Xinke Jiang, Yuchen Fang,\nYifan Zhang*\n\"STRAP: Spatio-Temporal Pattern Retrieval for Out-of-Distribution Generalization\"\n. In\nNIPS 2025\n.\n*Corresponding author.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[ECML-PKDD 2025]\nHaoyu Zhang, Yuxuan Cheng,\nWenqi Fan\n, Yulong Chen,\nYifan Zhang*\n\"Rethinking Graph Domain Adaptation: A Spectral Contrastive Perspective\"\n. In\nECML-PKDD 2025\n, vol 16018. Springer, Cham.\n*Corresponding author.\n[\nPaper\n][Project]\n[TITS 2025]\nQishen Zhou,\nYifan Zhang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n,\nYibing Wang\n,\nSimon Hu\n.\n\"Network-wide Freeway Traffic Estimation Using Sparse Sensor Data: A Dirichlet Graph Auto-Encoder Approach\"\n. Accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[TR-Part C 2025]\nQishen Zhou,\nYifan Zhang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n,\nYibing Wang\n,\nSimon Hu\n.\n\"MoGERNN: An Inductive Traffic Predictor for Unobserved Locations in Dynamic Sensing Networks\"\n. Accepted by\nTransportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[CommTR 2024]\nYifan Zhang\n, Qishen Zhou,\nJianping Wang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"CASAformer: Congestion-Aware Sparse Attention Transformer for Traffic Speed Prediction\"\n. In\nCommunications in Transportation Research\n.\n[\nPaper][\nProject\n]\n[ESWA 2024]\nYifan Zhang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"A Time-varying Shockwave Speed Model for Trajectory Reconstruction using Lagrangian and Eulerian Observations\"\n. In\nExpert Systems With Applications\n, 2024, 124298, ISSN 0957-4174.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[VTC 2023 Fall]\nYang Lu,\nYifan Zhang\n, Tuo Shi,\nJianping Wang\n, Jen-Ming Wu, Bingyi Liu.\n\"Empirical Study and Signal Intensity Prediction for Cellular Vehicle-to-Everything (C-V2X)\"\n.In\n2023 IEEE 98th Vehicular Technology Conference (VTC2023-Fall)\n, Hong Kong, October 2023.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[TIV 2023]\nZihao Wen*,\nYifan Zhang*\n,\nXinhong Chen\n,\nJianping Wang\n, Yung-Hui Li, Yu-Kai Huang.\n\"TOFG: Temporal Occupancy Flow Graph for Prediction and Planning in Autonomous Driving\"\n.In\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles\n, Volume 9, No. 1, pp. 2850-2863, January 2024.\n*Co-first author.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[ICRA 2023]\nZihao Wen*,\nYifan Zhang*\n,\nXinhong Chen\n,\nJianping Wang\n.\n\"TOFG: A Unified and Fine-Grained Environment Representation in Autonomous Driving\"\n.In\n2023 IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\n, London, UK, June 2023.\n*Co-first author.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[TITS 2023]\nYifan Zhang\n, Qian Xu,\nJianping Wang\n,\nZuduo Zheng\n,\nKejie Lu\n.\n\"A Learning-Based Discretionary Lane-Change Decision-Making Model With Driving Style Awareness\"\n.In\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n, Volume 24, No. 1, pp. 68-78, January 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[TR-Part C 2022]\nYifan Zhang\n,\nXinhong Chen\n,\nJianping Wang\n,\nZuduo Zheng\n,\nKui Wu\n.\n\"A Generative Car-following Model Conditioned on Driving Styles\"\n.In\nTransportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies\n, Volume 145, 2022, 103926, ISSN 0968-090X.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[TIST 2021]\nYifan Zhang\n, Jinghuai Zhang, Jindi Zhang,\nJianping Wang\n,\nKejie Lu\n, Jeff Hong.\n\"Integrating Algorithmic Sampling-Based Motion Planning with Learning in Autonomous Driving.\"\n.In\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology\n, 13, 3, Article 39, June 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[AAAI 2020]\nYifan Zhang\n, Jinghuai Zhang, Jindi Zhang,\nJianping Wang\n,\nKejie Lu\n, Jeff Hong.\n\"A Novel Learning Framework for Sampling-Based Motion Planning in Autonomous Driving\"\n.In\nProceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n, New York, USA, pp. 1202-1209, April 2020.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\n[IoT 2021]\nJindi Zhang,\nYifan Zhang\n,\nKejie Lu\n,\nJianping Wang\n,\nKui Wu\n,\nXiaohua Jia\n, Bin Liu.\n\"Detecting and Identifying Optical Signal Attacks on Autonomous Driving Systems\"\n.In\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal\n, Volume 8, No. 2, pp. 1140-1153, 15 January, 2021.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[MASS 2019]\nQian Xu,\nYifan Zhang\n,\nJianping Wang\n,\nKejie Lu\n.\n\"Evaluating and Boosting Reinforcement Learning for Intra-domain Routing\"\n. In\nIEEE 16th International Conference on Mobile Ad Hoc and Sensor Systems (MASS)\n, Montery, CA, USA, pp. 265-273, November 2019.\n[\nPaper\n]\nConferences and Presentations\n[TRB 2025]\nYifan Zhang\n, Qishen Zhou,\nJianping Wang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"Are State-of-the-Art Deep Learning Traffic Prediction Models Truly Effective?\"\n. In\n104th TRB Annual Meeting\n, DC, USA, January 2025.\n[hEART 2024]\nLinghang Sun\n,\nYifan Zhang\n, Cristian Axenie, Margherita Grossi,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"The Fragile Nature of Road Transportation Systems\"\n. In\n12th Symposium of the European Association for Research in Transportation\n, Helsinki, Finland, June 2024.\n[\nPaper\n]\n[EURO 2024]\nJiarui Zhang, Xiaojie Luan, Haiying Li,\nYifan Zhang\n.\n\"Scenario-driven Algorithm Selection for Transportation Planning Problem\"\n.In\n33rd European Conference on Operational Research\n, Copenhagen, Denmark, June 2024.\n[\nAbstract\n]\n[STRC 2024]\nYifan Zhang\n,\nAnastasios Kouvelas\n,\nMichail Makridis\n.\n\"A Time-varying Shockwave Speed Model for Trajectory Reconstruction using Lagrangian and Eulerian Observations\"\n. In\n24th Swiss Transport Research Conference\n, Ascona, Switzerland, May 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject\n]\nHonors and Awards\nPostgraduate Studentship (CityU, 2018-2021)\nHong Kong Computer Society Student Sponsorship 2020\nAcademic Services\nReviewer of Transportation Research Part C, IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles, IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems, IEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems, Journal of Advanced Transportation, IROS 2024, TRB 2024, etc.\nICRMS 2022 Session Chair\nNSL Newletter\n\"Drive Forward: Revolutionizing Traffic with Advanced Vehicle Trajectory Reconstruction\".\nTeaching Experiences\nAt CityU-DG:\nInstructor for CS5487 Data Engineering.\nInstructor for CS2310 Computer Programming.\nTutor for SDSC6011 Convex Optimization.\nTutor for CS1302 Introduction to Computer Programming.\nAt CityU:\nTutor for CS3201 Computer Networks. (2018-2021)\nTutor for CS3103 Operating Systems. (2018-2021)\n| The page template is designed by\nW3layouts."
