    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Zhao Zhang's HomePage\nZhao Zhang  (张钊)\nAssociate Professor\nInstitute of Computing Technology,\nChinese Academy of Sciences\nEmail: zhangzhao2021 AT ict DOT ac DOT cn\nBiography\nI am an Associate Professor at\nInstitute of Computing Technology (ICT), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS)\n, \n    where I obtained my Ph.D. in 2021. I am more than lucky to be co-supervised by\nProf. Qing He\nand\nProf. Fuzhen Zhuang\nduring my doctoral studies.\n\n    Before coming to ICT, I got my B.Eng. degree in Computer Science and Technology from\nBejing Institute of Technology.\nFrom Sept. 2019 to Sept. 2020, I visited the\nUCL NLP Lab\nat University College London (UCL), where I worked with\nProf. Sebastian Riedel\nand\nDr. Pasquale Minervini\n.\nMy research interests lie in data mining and machine learning, with a special focus on the representation and application of knowledge graphs.\n    Currently, I am working on the following topics:\nLarge Language Model (LLM), LLM Hallucination, LLM Reasoning, Retrieval-augmented Generation (RAG)\nKnowledge Graph (KG), KG Construction/Embedding/Completion, KG for NLP Tasks\nRecommendation System (RS), LLM-based RS, KG for RS/Information Retrieval (IR), Fairness-aware RS\nSpatio-temporal Data Mining, Multivariate Time Series Forecasting, Traffic Forecasting\nRecruiting: I have\nseveral\n1-2 openings for visiting (bachelor, master, or Ph.D.) students on Knowledge Graph, Recommendation System, or other Data Ming and NLP topics. Both remote and onsite visiting are welcome. Ping me if interested!\nEducation\nInstitute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nPh.D. in Computer Science, 2015.09 - 2021.01\nAdvisors:\nProf. Qing He\nand\nProf. Fuzhen Zhuang\nBeijing Institute of Technology\nB.Eng. in Computer Science and Technology, 2011.09 - 2015.06\nExperience\nResearch Intern, Dept. of ICBU Technology, Alibaba Group, Hangzhou, China. 2020.09 - 2021.01\nHost:\nDr. Dehong Gao\nVisiting Scholar, UCL NLP Lab, University College London, London, UK. 2019.09 - 2020.09\nAdvisor:\nProf. Sebastian Riedel\nResearch Intern, Talent Intelligence Center, Baidu Inc., Beijing, China. 2019.04 - 2019.09\nHosts:\nDr. Hengshu Zhu\nand\nProf. Hui Xiong\nResearch Intern, Dept. of Knowledge Graph, Baidu Inc, Beijing, China. 2016.07 - 2017.05\nHost:\nDr. Zheng-Yu Niu\nPublications\n[Google Scholar]\n2026\nWei Chen, Xingyu Guo, Shuang Li,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yan Zhong, Fuzhen Zhuang, Deqing wang. Learning Adaptive Distribution Alignment with Neural Characteristic Function for Graph Domain Adaptation. International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026.\nWei Chen, Xingyu Guo, Shuang Li, Yan Zhong,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Hongrui Liu, Libang Zhang, Guo Ye, Huimei He. Learning Structure-Semantic Evolution Trajectories for Graph Domain Adaptation. International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026.\nZhuo Chen, Fei Wang, Zixuan Li,\nZhao Zhang\n, Weiwei Ding, Chuanguang Yang, Yongjun Xu, Xiaolong Jin, Jiafeng Guo. KnowCoder-A1: Incentivizing Agentic Reasoning Capability with Outcome Supervision for KBQA. The Web Conference (WWW), 2026.\nFuwei Zhang, Xiaoyu Liu, Dongbo Xi, Jishen Yin, huan chen, Peng Yan, Fuzhen Zhuang,\nZhao Zhang\n. Multi-Aspect Cross-modal Quantization for Generative Recommendation. The 40th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2026.\nJiawei He, Zhanpeng Guan, Fuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yongjun Xu. Bootstrapping in the Loop: Multi-hop Question Answering via Alternating Decomposition and Retrieval. The 19th ACM International WSDM Conference (WSDM), 2026.\nXiaoyu Liu, Fuwei Zhang, Yiqing Wu, Xinyu Jia, Zenghua Xia, Fuzhen Zhuang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fei Jiang, Wei Lin.: CAT-ID2: Category-Tree Integrated Document Identifier Learning for Generative Retrieval In E-commerce. The 19th ACM International WSDM Conference (WSDM), 2026.\n2025\nYujie Li, Shao Zezhi, Chengqing Yu, Tangwen Qian,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yifan Du, Shaoming He, Fei Wang, Yongjun Xu. STA-GANN: A Valid and Generalizable Spatio-Temporal Kriging Approach. 34rd ACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management (CIKM), 2025.\nWei Chen, Meng Yuan,\nZhao Zhang\n, Ruobing Xie, Fuzhen Zhuang, Deqing Wang, Rui Liu. FairDgcl: Fairness-aware Recommendation with Dynamic Graph Contrastive Learning. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2025.\nFuwei Zhang, Xiaoyu Liu, Jia Xinyu, Yingfei Zhang, Shuai Zhang, Xiang Li, Wei Lin, Fuzhen Zhuang,\nZhao Zhang\n. Multi-level Relevance Document Identifier Learning for Generative Retrieval. The 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), 2025.\nFuwei Zhang, Xiaoyu Liu, Jia Xinyu, Yingfei Zhang, Zenghua Xia, Fei Jiang, Wei Lin, Fuzhen Zhuang,\nZhao Zhang\n. HierGR: Hierarchical Semantic Representation Enhancement for Generative Retrieval in Food Delivery Search. The 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), 2025.\nWei Chen,\nZhao Zhang\n, Meng Yuan, Kepeng Xu, Fuzhen Zhuang. FCKT: Fine-Grained Cross-Task Knowledge Transfer with Semantic Contrastive Learning for Targeted Sentiment Analysis. The 34th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI), 2025.\nYiqing Wu, Ruobing Xie,\nZhao Zhang\n, Xu Zhang, Fuzhen Zhuang, Leyu Lin, Zhanhui Kang, Zhulin An, Yongjun Xu. ID-centric pre-training for recommendation. ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS), 2025.\nChengqing Yu, Fei Wang, Zezhi Shao, Tangwen Qian,\nZhao Zhang\n, Wei Wei, Zhulin An, Qi Wang, and Yongjun Xu. GinAR+: A Robust End-To-End Framework for Multivariate Time Series Forecasting with Missing Values. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2025.\nZhanpeng Guan, Fuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Fei Wang, Zhulin An, Yongjun Xu. AdaE: Knowledge Graph Embedding with Adaptive Embedding Sizes. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2025.\nMeng Yuan,\nZhao Zhang\n, Wei Chen, Chu Zhao, Tong Cai, Deqing Wang, Rui Liu, Fuzhen Zhuang. HEK-CL: Hierarchical Enhanced Knowledge-Aware Contrastive Learning for Recommendation. ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS), 2025.\nYiqing Wu,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fei Wang, Yongjun Xu, Jincai Huang. Toward more economical large-scale foundation models: No longer a game for the few. The Innovation, 2025.\nZhanpeng Guan,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yiqing Wu, Fuwei Zhang, Yongjun Xu. Should We Use a Fixed Embedding Size? Customized Dimension Sizes for Knowledge Graph Embedding. The 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics (COLING), 2025.\nYuxiao Gao, Fuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Xiaoshuang Min, Fuzhen Zhuang. Mixed-Curvature Multi-Modal Knowledge Graph Completion. The 39th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2025.\nWei Chen, Guo Ye, Yakun Wang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Libang Zhang, Daixin Wang, Zhiqiang Zhang, Fuzhen Zhuang. Smoothness Really Matters: A Simple yet Effective Approach for Unsupervised Graph Domain Adaptation. The 39th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2025.\n2024\nYuting Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yiqing Wu, Ying Sun, Fuzhen Zhuang, Wenhui Yu, Lantao Hu, Han Li, Kun Gai, Zhulin An, Yongjun Xu. Tag Tree-Guided Multi-grained Alignment for Multi-Domain Short Video Recommendation. ACM MULTIMEDIA (MM), 2024.\nFuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Zhiqiang Zhang, Jun Zhou and Deqing Wang. Multi-view Temporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning. 33rd ACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management (CIKM), 2024.\nCaijun Xu, Fuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang and Rui Liu. Exploring High-Order User Preference with Knowledge Graph for Recommendation. 33rd ACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management (CIKM), 2024.\nYiqing Wu, Ruobing Xie,\nZhao Zhang\n, Xu Zhang, Fuzhen Zhuang, Leyu Lin, Zhanhui Kang, Yongjun Xu. DFGNN: Dual-frequency Graph Neural Network for Sign-aware Feedback. 30th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD), 2024.\nYanjie Gou, Yuanzhou Yao,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yiqing Wu, Yi Hu, Fuzhen Zhuang, Jiangming Liu, Yongjun Xu. Controllable Multi-Behavior Recommendation for In-Game Skins with Large Sequential Model. 30th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD), 2024.\nChengqing Yu, Fei Wang, Zezhi Shao, Tangwen Qian,\nZhao Zhang\n, Wei Wei, Yongjun Xu. GinAR: An End-To-End Multivariate Time Series Forecasting Model Suitable for Variable Missing. 30th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD), 2024.\nZezhi Shao, Fei Wang, Yongjun Xu, Wei Wei, Chengqing Yu,\nZhao Zhang\n, Di Yao, Tao Sun, Guangyin Jin, Xin Cao, Gao Cong, Christian S.Jensen, Xueqi Cheng. Exploring Progress in Multivariate Time Series Forecasting: Comprehensive Benchmarking and Heterogeneity Analysis. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2024.\nFuwei Zhang,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Yu Zhao, Deqing Wang, Hongwei Zheng. Temporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning with Dynamic Memory Enhancement. IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), 2024.\nZhuo Chen,\nZhao Zhang\n, Zixuan Li, Fei Wang, Yutao Zeng, Xiaolong Jin, Yongjun Xu. Self-Improvement Programming for Temporal Knowledge Graph Question Answering. The 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING), 2024.\nHuajie Zhang, Yuxin Ying, Fuzhen Zhuang, Haiqin Weng, Ying Sun,\nZhao Zhang\n, Yiqi Tong and Yan Liu. Multi-round counterfactual generation: interpreting and improving models of text classification. The Web Conference (WWW), 2024. Short Paper\nWei Chen, Yuxuan Liu,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Jiang Zhong. Modeling Adaptive Inter-Task Feature Interactions via Sentiment-Aware Contrastive Learning for Joint Aspect-Sentiment Prediction. The 38th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2024.\nWei Chen, Yiqing Wu,\nZhao Zhang\n, Fuzhen Zhuang, Zhongshi He, Ruobin Xie, F