    "homepage_text": "Kuanming Yao, Ph.D.\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nKuanming Yao, Ph.D.\nWelcome to my homepage\nI am Kuanming Yao (姚宽明), a postdoctoral researcher in soft bioelectronics\nCurrently working at interconnected & integrated bioelectronics lab, UCLA\nDr. Kuanming Yao\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n(Apr. 2024 -)\nDepartment of Electrical & Computer Engineering\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles (UCLA), CA, U.S.\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n(Feb. 2023 -\nMar. 2024\n)\nLaboratory of Soft Bio-electronics\nCity University of Hong Kong, Hong Kong\nAdvisor: Prof. Xinge Yu\nPh.D.\n(\nSept\n. 20\n19\n-\nJan. 2023\n)\nDepartment of Biomedical Engineering\nCity University of Hong Kong, Hong Kong\nSuper\nvisors: Prof. Xinge Yu & Prof. Lidai Wang\nB. Eng.\n(\nSept\n. 20\n15\n-\nJun. 2019\n)\nCollege of Energy Engineering\nZhejiang University, Hangzhou, China\nAdvisor: Prof. Jianjian Wei\nLinks\nContact\nUCLA\nLos Angeles, CA, U.S. 90095\nNews\nPress coverage\n26\n.\nApr\n. 202\n5\nDr.  Yao\ngave an 40 min online talk at International Institute for intelligent Nanorobots and Nanosystems, Fudan University. Many thanks for the invitation from Prof. Enming Song!\n15. Jul. 2024,\nTechXplore\nFlexible, permeable and 3D integrated electronic skin combines liquid metal circuits with fibrous substrates\n5. Nov. 2024\nDr.  Yao gave an invited 30 min live talk on iCANX youth talks. Many thanks for the invitation from Prof. Dangxiao Wang!\n1\n5\n.\nJul\n. 202\n4\n,\nNipponese News\n柔軟で透過性のある3D統合型電子皮膚は、液体金属回路と繊維基板を組み合わせています。\nAug\n. 2024\nDr.  Yao\nstarted to serve as a guest editor for\nBiosensors\n| special issue: Advanced Bioelectronics for Healthcare Monitoring and Disease Diagnosis\n.\nSubmissions are welcomed!\n10.\nMar\n. 2023,\nAsia Research News\nUltrathin, wireless palm patch brings touch to virtual reality\n1. Apr. 2024, Los Angeles\nDr.  Yao joined Interconn\nected & Integrated Bioelectronics Lab (\nI2BL) in UCLA as a postdoc scholar!\n21\n.\nJan\n. 202\n3, Forbes\nThe Whole World In Your Hand: Major Advances In Haptic Technology\n2\n8\n.\nMar\n. 202\n4, Hong Kong\nThe last working day in Soft bio-integrated Electronics Lab. Thanks Prof. Yu and all my friends!\n15\n.\nDec\n. 202\n2, CityU\nCityU researchers develop wireless, ultrathin “Skin VR” to provide a vivid, “personalised” touch experience in the virtual world\n10\n.\nDec\n. 2023\n, Hangzhou\nThe 5th International Conference on Flexible Electronics.\n15. Dec. 2022,\nIMechE\nUltrathin haptic device provides ‘vivid touch sensation in virtual worlds’\n20. Feb. 2023 (Inarg dinner on 26. June. 2023)\nDr.  Yao was awarded the winner of HKMHDIA Student Research Award 2021-2022\n15\n.\nDec\n. 2022,\nEurekAlert!\nCityU researchers develop wireless, ultrathin 'Skin VR' to provide a vivid, 'personalized' touch experience in the virtual world\n16. Dec. 2022\nKuanming Yao successfully passed the Ph.D. oral defense in BME, CityU. Many thanks to Prof. Xinge Yu, Prof. Lidai Wang, Prof. Chenjie Xu, Prof. Chung Tin and Prof. Zijian Zheng!\n4. Nov. 2022, TechXplore\nWeTac: A small, soft and ultrathin wireless electrotactile system\n20.\nOct. 2022\nOur paper\nentitled \"\nEncoding of tactile information in hand via skin-integrated wireless haptic interface\" (\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s42256-022-00543-y\n)\nwas selected as the cover of Oct. issue of\nNature Machine Intelligence\n26. Jul. 2022, TVB HK\n城大研發電子皮膚觸感反饋技術 冀提升虛擬實境體驗\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
