    "homepage_text": "Beomseok Kang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBeomseok Kang\nHello\n🌞\nP\nostdoctoral researcher at Seoul National University, hosted by Prof. Jae-Joon Kim.\nPh.D. from\nElectrical and Computer Engineering at Georgia Tech, advised by Prof. Saibal Mukhopadhyay.\nW\norking on\nefficient learning and inference methods for large deep learning models\n.\nbeomseok@snu.ac.kr\n;\nbeomseokg@gmail.com\nResearch Interest\nEfficient ML\nUnsupervised Learning\nDomain Adaptation\nEducation\nPh.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Georgia Institute of Technology\nThesis: Data and Computation-efficient Deep Learning for Multi-agent Systems\nM.S. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Georgia Institute of Technology\nThesis: Energy-aware DNN Quantization for Processing-In-Memory Architecture\nB.S. in Electrical Engineering, Sungkyunkwan University\nGPA: 4.47/4.5, Department Rank: 1/336\nExperience\nPostdoctoral Researcher\n, Seoul National Univer\nsity\n, 202\n4\nDec - present\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nJae-Joon Kim\nResearch Assistant\n, Georgia Institute of Technology, 20\n20\nAug\n- 2024 Dec\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nSaibal Mukhopadhyay\nResearch Intern, SRI @ Princeton, 2023 and 2024 Summer\nMentor: Dr. Niluthpol Chowdhury Mithun\nVisiting Student, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 2019 Jan - Aug\nAdvisor\n: Prof\n.\nJee\nhwan Kim\nHonor\nSejong Science Fellowship\n, National Re\nsea\nrch Foundation of Korea (NRF), 2025 Mar - 2030\nMar\n(expected)\nAcademic Service\nConference/Journal Reviewer\nDesign Automation Conference (DAC) TPC member\n— 202\n6\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) reviewer —  2024, 2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\nreviewer\n— 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\nreviewer — 2025, 2026\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\nreviewer\n— 2025\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nICCV\n)\nreviewer\n— 2025\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nBeomseok Kang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBeomseok Kang\nHello\n🌞\nP\nostdoctoral researcher at Seoul National University, hosted by Prof. Jae-Joon Kim.\nPh.D. from\nElectrical and Computer Engineering at Georgia Tech, advised by Prof. Saibal Mukhopadhyay.\nW\norking on\nefficient learning and inference methods for large deep learning models\n.\nbeomseok@snu.ac.kr\n;\nbeomseokg@gmail.com\nResearch Interest\nEfficient ML\nUnsupervised Learning\nDomain Adaptation\nEducation\nPh.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Georgia Institute of Technology\nThesis: Data and Computation-efficient Deep Learning for Multi-agent Systems\nM.S. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Georgia Institute of Technology\nThesis: Energy-aware DNN Quantization for Processing-In-Memory Architecture\nB.S. in Electrical Engineering, Sungkyunkwan University\nGPA: 4.47/4.5, Department Rank: 1/336\nExperience\nPostdoctoral Researcher\n, Seoul National Univer\nsity\n, 202\n4\nDec - present\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nJae-Joon Kim\nResearch Assistant\n, Georgia Institute of Technology, 20\n20\nAug\n- 2024 Dec\nAdvisor\n: Prof.\nSaibal Mukhopadhyay\nResearch Intern, SRI @ Princeton, 2023 and 2024 Summer\nMentor: Dr. Niluthpol Chowdhury Mithun\nVisiting Student, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 2019 Jan - Aug\nAdvisor\n: Prof\n.\nJee\nhwan Kim\nHonor\nSejong Science Fellowship\n, National Re\nsea\nrch Foundation of Korea (NRF), 2025 Mar - 2030\nMar\n(expected)\nAcademic Service\nConference/Journal Reviewer\nDesign Automation Conference (DAC) TPC member\n— 202\n6\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) reviewer —  2024, 2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\nreviewer\n— 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\nreviewer — 2025, 2026\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\nreviewer\n— 2025\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nICCV\n)\nreviewer\n— 2025\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
