    "homepage_text": "Cuiling Lan - Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nCuiling Lan\nPrincipal Researcher\nAbout\nDr. Cuiling Lan is a Principal Researcher at Microsoft Research Asia. She received her B.S. degree and Ph.D. degree in Electrical Engineering from Xidian University in 2008 and 2014, respectively. She had been a research intern at Microsoft Research Asia for more than three years. She was awarded MSRA Fellowship 2011. She was also a visiting student to University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) from 2012 to 2013.\nHer research interests include agentic media, multimodal large language models, reinforcement learning, post-training methodologies, and representation learning.\nInternship: I am looking for highly motivated interns with strong coding skills, a passion for research, and a solid background in agents and VLM/LLM post-training. If you are interested, please send your CV to\nculan@microsoft.com.\nOpens in a new tab\nResearch areas\nArtificial intelligence\nComputer vision\nResearch groups\nIntelligent Multimedia Group\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit\n\n---\n\nCuiling Lan - Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nCuiling Lan\nPrincipal Researcher\nInternship Opportunities\nInternship opportunity! We are looking for highly motivated interns with strong coding skills, a passion for research, and a solid background in agents and VLM/LLM post-training. If you are interested, please send your CV to\nculan@microsoft.com.\nOpens in a new tab\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nS