  "deep_homepage::Yan Lu::https://jason-cs18.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://jason-cs18.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "jasonengineer@hotmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/Jason-cs18",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yan-lu-95401110b",
    "homepage_text": "Yan Lu (鲁炎) - Homepage\nYan Lu (鲁炎)\nMLSyser\nReliable and Efficient Systems for Multimodal Models and Agents\nNew York, United States\nWebsite\nEmail\nResearchGate\nLinkedIn\nDBLP\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nBio\nHe is a research scientist at Meta. His current focus is to develop efficient and reliable systems for multimodal models and agents. In the past, I built scalable and efficient edge-ai applications, such as video analytics and talking-face synthesis.\nPreviously, he was a postdoc at NYU systems group working with\nProf. Jinyang Li\n. He obtained a computer science Ph.D. at New York University where he worked with\nProf. Sam Bowman\n. Prior to joining NYU, he earned his M.Tech from Purdue University and B.Tech from Sichuan University. He collaborates closely with\nProf. Yuanchao Shu\nfrom Zhejiang University,\nDr. Shiqi Jiang\nfrom Microsoft Research, and\nProf. Huanle Zhang\nfrom Shandong University. He is the co-founder of\nMengJiTech (孟及科技)\nwhich is a startup focusing on AIGC.\nNews\n2023.01\n: MVDAOD was selected as AAAI 2023 oral (10.71%)!\n2022.11\n: MVDAOD was accepted to AAAI 2023! Thanks for all collaborators!!!\n2022.11\n: Starting internship at Microsoft Research Shanghai!\n2022.11\n: e2e-detection is released!\n2022.10\n: Turbo was accepted to Sensys 2022!\n2022.09\n: One paper was conditionally accepted to Sensys 2022!\n2022.07\n: One paper got accepcted to TIOT 2022!\nSelected Research Papers\n[\nICPADS 2025\n] Runzheng Wang, Jiahua Wang,\nYan Lu\n, Lei Fu, Huanle Zhang. “FastAvatar: Enabling Fast Talking-Face Synthesis on Resource-Constrained Devices via Multimodal Caching and Adaptation”.\nAccelerating on-device talking-head synthesis model inference via a multimodal cache.\n[\nAAAI 2023 (Oral)\n]\nYan Lu\n, Zhun Zhong, Yuanchao Shu. “Multi-View Domain Adaptive Object Detection in Surveillance Cameras”.\n[arxiv]\n[\nPDF\n] [\nPDF (including appendix)\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nbib\n]\nLeveraging multi-views from overlapping cameras to learn a robust backbone for downstream unsupervised domain adaptation tasks.\n[\nSenSys 2022\n]\nYan Lu\n, Shiqi Jiang, Ting Cao, Yuanchao Shu. “Turbo: Opportunistic Enhancement for Edge Video Analytics”.\nACM SenSys 2022\n. [\nPDF\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nCode\n] [\nProject page\n] [\nbib\n]\nUsing data enhancement to help video analytics applications capture hard samples and improve the accuracy in further.\n[\nTIOT 2022\n] Zheng Dong,\nYan Lu\n, Guangmo Tong, Yuanchao Shu, Shuai Wang, Weisong Shi. “WatchDog: Real-time Vehicle Tracking on Geo-distributed Edge Nodes”.\nACM Transactions on Internet of Things, 2022\n. [\nPDF\n] [\nbib\n]\nAccelerating vehicle tracking with a distributed resource manager!\n[\nSEC 2019\n]\nYan Lu\n, Yuanchao Shu, Xu Tan, Yunxin Liu, Mengyu Zhou, Qi Chen and Dan Pei. “Collaborative Learning between Cloud and End Devices: An Empirical Study on Location Prediction”. In\nthe Fourth ACM/IEEE Symposium on Edge Computing, 2019\n. [\nPDF\n] [\nbib\n]\nImproving edge device learning with the global knowledge!\nIndustry Experience\nResearch Intern\n, Wireless Group @ Microsoft Research in Asia\nNov 2022 - May 2023, Mentored by\nDr. Shiqi Jiang\nResearch Intern\n, Recommendation Systems Group @ Airbnb\nMay 2020 - Aug 2020, Mentored by\nDr. Wei Zhang\nResearch Intern\n, Mobile and Networking Group @ Microsoft Research in Asia\nDec 2017 - Aug 2018, Mentored by\nDr. Yuanchao Shu\nand\nDr. Yunxin Liu\nResearch Assistant\n, Intelligent Agents Group @ Chinese Academy of Sciences\nFeb 2016 - Aug 2016, Mentored by\nDr. Xinhua Zeng\nProfessional Services\nConference Reviewer: Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI).\nJournal Reviewer: The ACM International Conference on Pervasive and Ubiquitous Computing (UbiComp), IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing (TMC).\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
