    "homepage_text": "About - Xiangyu Peng / Becky\nXiangyu Peng\nPh.D. at Georgia Tech, supervised by Prof. Mark Riedl.\nFollow\nAtlanta, GA, US\nEmail\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nAbout\nI am Xiangyu Peng, Ph.D. in Machine Learning @ Georgia Institute of Technology. I am advised by\nDr. Mark Riedl\n, and my\nresearch\nfocused on\nNatural language generation\n,\nGame AI\n,\nExplainable AI\n, and\nDeep reinforcement learning\n.\nYou can reach me at xiangyupeng1994 at gmail dot com..\nUpdate\nFeb 5th, 2024\nBegin my full-time job as Research Scientist at Salesforce Research.\nJan 4th, 2024\nSuccessfully defended my dissertation.\nJuly 17th, 2023\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nStory Shaping: Teaching Agents Human-like Behavior with Stories\nby Proceedings of\nAIIDE-23\nMay 8th, 2023\nWork as Research Intern in\nMicrosoft Research\n.\nMay 1st, 2023\nPass my\nthesis proposal\n.\nJan 21st, 2023\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nModel Ensemble Instead Of Prompt Fusion: A Sample-Specific Knowledge Transfer Method For Few-Shot Prompt Tuning\nby Proceedings of\nICLR-23\nOct 6th, 2022\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nGuiding Neural Story Generation with Reader Models\nby Findings of\nEMNLP-22\nOct 6th, 2022\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nInferring the Reader: Guiding Automated Story Generation with Commonsense Reasoning\nby Findings of\nEMNLP-22\nSep 14, 2022\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nInherently Explainable Reinforcement Learning in Natural Language\nby\nNeurIPS-22\nMay 16, 2022\nWork as Research Intern in\nSalesforce Research\n.\nMarch 18, 2022\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nInherently Explainable Reinforcement Learning in Natural Language\nby\nRLDM 2022\nOCT 9, 2021\nGive a talk on Explainable Reinforcement Learning Agent With Stacked Hierarchical Attention in Explainable Graph-Based Machine Learning Workshop in AKBC-21\nOCT 9, 2021\nGive a talk on Explainable Reinforcement Learning Agent With Stacked Hierarchical Attention in Explainable Graph-Based Machine Learning Workshop in AKBC-21\nSPT 10, 2021\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nExplainable Reinforcement Learning Agent With Stacked Hierarchical Attention\nby the Explainable Graph-Based Machine Learning Workshop in AKBC-21\nMay 17, 2021\nWork as PhD intern in Salesforce~ Focus on NLG reserach.\nAPR 15, 2021\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nAugmented Neural Story Generation with Commonsense Inference\nby The 3rd Workshop On Narrative Understanding in NAACL-21\nAPR 15, 2021\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nAutomatic Story Generation: Challenges and Attempts\nby The 3rd Workshop On Narrative Understanding in NAACL-21\nDEC 01, 2020\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nDetecting and Adapting to Novelty in Games\nby Reinforcement Learning in Games workshop at AAAI 2021.\nOCT 30, 2020\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nDetecting and Adapting to Novelty in Games\nby Creativity and Robotics workshop at ICSR 2020.\nOCT 23, 2020\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nImproving Neural Storytelling with Commonsense Inferences\nby NeurIPS WiML 2020.\nOCT 12, 2020\nAcceptance of my Paper:\nReducing Non-Normative Text Generation from Language Models Reducing Non-Normative Text Generation from Language Models\nby INLG 2020.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Xiangyu Peng / Becky\nXiangyu Peng\nPh.D. at Georgia Tech, supervised by Prof. Mark Riedl.\nFollow\nAtlanta, GA, US\nEmail\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nCV\nUpdated on July 19, 2023"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Kai Wang::https://guaguakai.com/": {
    "homepage": "https://guaguakai.com/",
    "all_emails": [
      "kaiwang@g.harvard.edu",
      "kaiwang.gua@gmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/guaguakai",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/guaguakai/",
    "homepage_text": "Kai Wang\n0\nSkip to Content\nKai Wang\nCV\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nKai Wang\nCV\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nUsing AI to Create Social Impact\nKai Wang\nContact me\n: kaiwang.gua@gmail.com\nOffice\n: Gatech CODA building room S1309\nMy research focuses on developing artificial intelligence, machine learning, optimization, and multi-agent systems solutions to create social impact, specifically in the area of health, public health, and environmental sustainability.\nExamples include assisting health workers in maternal and child health, designing AI early warning system for children’s health, sustaining wildlife conservation using game theory models, and monitoring the environmental impacts of industrialization.\nMy work has been recognized and supported by\nSchimidt Science AI2050\n,\nSiebel Scholars\n, NSF CISE Core Medium, and Children's Healthcare of Atlanta Pediatric Technology Center at Georgia Tech (PTC)\nInterested in joining the team? Please check\nhere\nfor more details.\nI am an Assistant Professor at\nGeorgia Tech, School of Computational Science and Engineering\n. I received my Ph.D. in Computer Science from Harvard University under supervision of\nProfessor Milind Tambe\n.\nResearch Interests\nOptimization, machine learning, reinforcement learning, online learning, algorithmic game theory, multi-agent systems. Please see the following pages for more information.\nTheory in ML and optimization\nReinforcement learning\nSocial Impact Applications\nWe work closely with NGOs and hospitals to design and deploy AI solutions in social impact applications. Our goal is to ensure the AI algorithms actually work in practice to create real-world impact.\nLearn more\nFollow my journey"
  },
