    "homepage_text": "About me - Zihan Liu\nZihan Liu\nSenior Research Scientist at Nvidia. Working on chat models, RAG, retrieval and multimodal.\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am\nZihan Liu\n(刘子涵). I am a Senior research scientist at\nNvidia Applied Deep Learning Research (ADLR) Team\n. I received Bachelor Degree from\nZhejiang University\n, and Ph.D. Degree from the Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering,\nThe Hong Kong University of Science and Technology\nunder the supervision of\nProf. Pascale Fung\nin\nCenter of AI Research\n. I work on LLMs reasoning, post-training, and RAG.\nHighlights\n[2025/05]\nAceReason-Nemotron\n: Advanced LLM reasoning models on Math and Code.\n[2024/12]\nAceMath\n: Frontier math reasoning models.\n[2024/09]\nNVLM\n: Open Frontier-Class Multimodal LLMs.\n[2024/09]\nChatQA-2\n: Long Context (128K) RAG model.\n[2024/07]\nRankRAG\n: SoTA RAG model with rerank.\n[2024/05]\nChatQA-1.5\n: Surpassing GPT-4 on Conversational QA and RAG.\nPlease feel free to contact me via email.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Zihan Liu\nZihan Liu\nSenior Research Scientist at Nvidia. Working on chat models, RAG, retrieval and multimodal.\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in GitHub, GitHub University, 2012\nM.S. in Jekyll, GitHub University, 2014\nPh.D in Version Control Theory, GitHub University, 2018 (expected)\nWork experience\nSummer 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Tagging issues\nSupervisor: Professor Git\nFall 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Merging pull requests\nSupervisor: Professor Hub\nSkills\nSkill 1\nSkill 2\nSub-skill 2.1\nSub-skill 2.2\nSub-skill 2.3\nSkill 3\nPublications\nTeam yeon-zi at semeval-2019 task 4: Hyperpartisan news detection by de-noising weakly-labeled data\nGeneralizing Question Answering System with Pre-trained Language Model Fine-tuning\nLearning to Learn Sales Prediction with Social Media Sentiment\nCaire: An end-to-end empathetic chatbot\nIncorporating Word and Subword Units in Unsupervised Machine Translation Using Language Model Rescoring\nLightweight and Efficient End-to-End Speech Recognition Using Low-Rank Transformer\nHierarchical Meta-Embeddings for Code-Switching Named Entity Recognition\nZero-shot Cross-lingual Dialogue Systems with Transferable Latent Variables\nAttention-Informed Mixed-Language Training for Zero-shot Cross-lingual Task-oriented Dialogue Systems\nZero-Resource Cross-Domain Named Entity Recognition\nLearning Fast Adaptation on Cross-Accented Speech Recognition\nMeta-Transfer Learning for Code-Switched Speech Recognition\nCoach: A Coarse-to-Fine Approach for Cross-domain Slot Filling\nLearning Knowledge Bases with Parameters for Task-Oriented Dialogue Systems\nCross-lingual Spoken Language Understanding with Regularized Representation Alignment\nOn the Importance of Word Order Information in Cross-lingual Sequence Labeling\nCrossNER: Evaluating Cross-Domain Named Entity Recognition\nMultimodal End-to-End Sparse Model for Emotion Recognition\nAdaptSum: Towards Low-Resource Domain Adaptation for Abstractive Summarization\nContinual Mixed-Language Pre-Training for Extremely Low-Resource Neural Machine Translation\nVision Guided Generative Pre-trained Language Models for Multimodal Abstractive Summarization\nXPersona: Evaluating Multilingual Personalized Chatbot\nMulti-Stage Prompting for Knowledgeable Dialogue Generation\nTalks\nTalk 1 on Relevant Topic in Your Field\nMarch 01, 2012\nTalk at UC San Francisco, Department of Testing, San Francisco, California\nTutorial 1 on Relevant Topic in Your Field\nMarch 01, 2013\nTutorial at UC-Berkeley Institute for Testing Science, Berkeley CA, USA\nTalk 2 on Relevant Topic in Your Field\nFebruary 01, 2014\nTalk at London School of Testing, London, UK\nConference Proceeding talk 3 on Relevant Topic in Your Field\nMarch 01, 2014\nConference proceedings talk at Testing Institute of America 2014 Annual Conference, Los Angeles, CA\nTeaching\nTeaching experience 1\nTeaching experience 2\nService and leadership\nCurrently signed in to 43 different slack teams"
