    "homepage_text": "Chenfeng Xu | UT Austin Computer Science\nSkip to main content\nChenfeng Xu\nAssistant Professor\nChenfeng Xu is an incoming Assistant Professor of Computer Science at The University of Texas at Austin. His research focuses on efficient machine learning and systems for ML/robotics. His methods have seen broad industry uptake and open-source use, with applications across mobile/embedded devices, robotics, and autonomous driving etc. Chenfeng Xu received his Ph.D. from UC Berkeley in 2025.\nResearch\nResearch Areas:\nArtificial Intelligence\nIntelligent Robotics\nMachine Learning\nSystems and Networking\nResearch Interests:\nEfficient Machine Learning, System for Machine Learning, Generative AI and Robotics\nContact Info\nChenfeng Xu\nAssistant Professor\nHomepage\nxuchenfeng@utexas.edu"
  },
