    "homepage_text": "Zeyu Zhou\nZeyu Zhou\n...\nHi! I am a PhD student at\nPurdue ECE\nwhere I work with\nDavid I. Inouye\n. I have a track record of publishing in top conferences like NeurIPS, ICLR, and AISTATS, and industry research experience at Amazon and Bloomberg.\nMy research focuses on the\ndevelopment and evaluation\nof Machine Learning (ML) models, including conventional deep learning models and foundation models, that are\nrobust and trustworthy\nwhen faced with\ncomplex data shifts in test cases\nand\nundesirable bias in pretraining data\n, enabling safe and effective deployment in dynamic real-world environments.\nTo solve this problem, I have leverage tools including (1) causality (\nNeurIPS24\n,\nICLR24\n) (2) Generative AI models (\nICLR23\n,\nAISTATS22\n, Amazon Internship)(3) domain knowledge (Bloomberg Internship)\nFeel free to drop me an email if you are interested in my research or just want to chat. I am always open to new ideas and collaborations.\n🔍\nI am expected to graduate in Fall 2025 (flexible). Please let me know if you have any openings for a Machine Learning Researcher/Engineer or a Quantitative Researcher\nNews\nOct 19, 2024\nI will attend\nNeurIPS 2024\nat Vancouver, Canada. I am looking forward to meeting you there!\nSelected Publications\nNeurIPS\nCounterfactual Fairness by Combining Factual and Counterfactual Predictions\nZeyu Zhou\n, Tianci Liu , Ruqi Bai , Jing Gao , Murat Kocaoglu , and David I Inouye\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n, 2024\nICLR DPFM\nImproving Practical Counterfactual Fairness with Limited Causal Knowledge\nZeyu Zhou\n, Ruqi Bai , and David I Inouye\nICLR Workshop on Navigating and Addressing Data Problems for Foundation Models\n, 2024\nICLR\nTowards Characterizing Domain Counterfactuals For Invertible Latent Causal Models\nZeyu Zhou*\n, Ruqi Bai* , Sean Kulinski* , Murat Kocaoglu , and David I Inouye\nThe Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations\n, 2024\nICLR\nEfficient Federated Domain Translation\nZeyu Zhou\n, Sheikh Shams Azam , Christopher Brinton , and David I Inouye\nIn The Eleventh International Conference on Learning Representations\n, 2023\nAISTATS\nIterative Alignment Flows\nZeyu Zhou\n, Ziyu Gong , Pradeep Ravikumar , and David I Inouye\nIn International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics\n, 2022\n\n---\n\nCV | Zeyu Zhou\nCV\nBasics\nName\nZeyu Zhou\nEmail\nzhou1059@purdue.edu\nSummary\nAI Researcher\nWork\n2023.06 - 2023.08\nMachine Learning Quant Research Intern\nBloomberg, NY\nTime Series\nFinancial Data\nMissing Data\nOut-of-distribution Generalization\n2022.06 - 2022.09\nApplied Scientist Intern\nAmazon, WA\nDeep Generative Models\nCounterfactual\nCausalML\nEducation\n2021.08 - 2025.05\nIN, United States\nComputer Engineering\nPurdue University\n2019.08 - 2021.07\nIN, United States\nPhysics\nPurdue University\nTransfer to ECE\n2015.09 - 2019.06\nHubei, China\nPhysics\nWuhan University\nInterests\nDistribution Shift\nTrustworthy ML\nRobustness\nFairness\nCausality\nDeep Generative Models\nProjects\n2023.12 - Present\nCounterfactual Fairness\nBuilt dedicated deep generative models and corresponding post-processing algorithms for achieving counterfactual fairness.\n2023.08 - Present\nFault-tolerant Machine Learning\nDesigned algorithms that are robust to missing data in the setting of Vertical Federated Learning.\n2023.01 - Present\nDomain Counterfactual\nProposed a novel design of deep generative models for estimation of counterfactual samples.\n2022.03 - 2023.05\nFederated Domain Generalization\nDeveloped algorithms for training generative models in a federated setting, enabling the use of SOTA Domain Generalization methods.\n2020.08 - 2022.03\nEfficient Distribution Matching\nProposed efficient algorithms for mapping between high-dimensional distributions.\n2018.08 - 2019.05\nFault-tolerant Quantum Computation\nTested dynamically error-corrected gates for designing robust unitary gates and implementing fault-tolerant quantum computing architectures.\nAwards\n2017\nNational Scholarship\nWuhan University\nAward Top 2 in the major\n2016\nNational Scholarship\nWuhan University\nAward Top 2 in the major"
  },
