    "homepage_text": "Xiao Wang — Wang Lab\nMenu\nWang Lab\nXiao Wang, Ph.D.\nassociate Professor\nXiao Wang is a core institute member of the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard and an associate professor in the Department of Chemistry at MIT. She started her lab in 2019 to develop and apply new chemical, biophysical, and genomic tools to better understand tissue function and dysfunction at the molecular level. Wang joined the MIT and Broad after conducting postdoctoral research at Stanford University Bioengineering with Professor Karl Deisseroth, where she was a fellow of the Life Sciences Research Foundation. Wang received her B.S. in Chemistry and Molecular Engineering from Peking University and her Ph.D. in Chemistry from the University of Chicago with Professor Chuan He.\nPosition\n2019-2024 Assistant Professor at MIT Chemistry; Core Member at Broad Institute\n2024-present Associate Professor at MIT Chemistry; Core Member at Broad Institute\nEducation\n2006-2010 B.S. Chemistry and Molecular Engineering, Peking University\n2010-2015  Ph.D. Chemistry, University of Chicago\n2015-2019  Postdoctoral Fellow, Stanford University\nTeaching\n5.07, Introduction to Biological Chemistry, Fall semester\n5.64/HST.539, Frontiers of Interdisciplinary Science in Human Health & Disease, Spring semester\nHonors and Awards\n2024 Sloan Research Fellowship\n2022 Packard Fellowship for Science and Engineering\n2022 Merkin Institute Fellowship, Merkin Institute for Transformative Technologies in Healthcare\n2021 NIH Director’s New Innovator Award (DP2)\n2021 Ono Pharma Breakthrough Science Initiative Award, Ono Pharma Foundation\n2021 Edward Scolnick Professorship, Broad Institute\n2020 Thomas D. and Virginia W. Cabot Professorship, MIT\n2020 Searle Scholar in Biomedical Research and Chemistry\n2016 Life Sciences Research Foundation Fellowship, Life Sciences Research Foundation & Gordon and Betty Moore Foundation\n2015 Elizabeth R. Norton Prize for Excellence in Research in Chemistry, the University of Chicago\n2015 Award for Outstanding Self-Financed Students Abroad, China Scholarship Council\n2013 Helen Sellei-Beretvas Fellowship, the University of Chicago\n2009 First Prize in the 11th National University Challenge Cup Competition in Academic Science and Technology\n2009 China National Petroleum Corporation Scholarship, Peking University\n2008 Xia Guang Scholarship, Peking University\n2006 Freshman Scholarship, Peking University\n2006 Gold Medal in National Chemistry Olympiad for high school students"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Kun Zhang::https://kunzhang.org/": {
