    "homepage_text": "Eunho Yang\n      -  Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nKorea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology Home\nSearch content at Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology\nView Scopus Profile\nEunho Yang\nAssociate Professor\nKim Jaechul Graduate School of AI\nEmail\neunhoy\nkaist.ac\nkr\nh-index\n3691\nCitations\n29\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2006\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation\no (2004) B.S., Seoul National University\no (2006) M.S., Seoul National University\no (2014) Ph.D., University of Texas at Austin\nProfessional Experience\nDr. Eunho Yang is a tenured associate professor in the Graduate School of AI and School of Computing at KAIST. Before joining KAIST in the summer of 2016, he spent two years as a research staff member at IBM T.J. Watson Research Center.\nResearch interests\ngeneral statistical machine learning with a special focus on high-dimensional statistics and diverse machine learning algorithms with the recent focus on the generative models\nMajor Research Achievements\no One paper was accepted to CVPR 2024\no Two papers were accepted to ICLR 2024\no Two papers were accepted to NeurIPS 2023\no One paper was accepted to ICCV 2023\no Two papers were accepted to INTERSPEECH 2023\no Two papers were accepted to ICML 2023\no Two papers were accepted to CVPR 2023\no One paper was accepted to ICASSP 2023\no Two papers were accepted to ICLR 2023\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Eunho Yang is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nExperimental Result\nComputer Science\n100%\nSpeech Recognition\nComputer Science\n82%\nData Augmentation\nComputer Science\n70%\nText To Speech\nComputer Science\n66%\nGraphical Model\nMathematics\n66%\nTraining Data\nComputer Science\n55%\nGraph Neural Network\nComputer Science\n53%\nMultitask Learning\nComputer Science\n53%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n51\nConference contribution\n38\nConference article\n17\nPaper\n13\nArticle\n1\nMore\n1\nReview article\nCloudFixer: Test-Time Adaptation for 3D Point Clouds via Diffusion-Guided Geometric Transformation\nShim, H., Kim, C. &\nYang, E.\n,\n2025\n,\nComputer Vision – ECCV 2024 - 18th European Conference, Proceedings.\nLeonardis, A., Ricci, E., Roth, S., Russakovsky, O., Sattler, T. & Varol, G. (eds.).\nSpringer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH\n,\np. 454-471\n18 p.\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science (including subseries Lecture Notes in Artificial Intelligence and Lecture Notes in Bioinformatics); vol. 15089 LNCS).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\n›\npeer-review\nPoint Cloud\n100%\nTest Time\n100%\nGeometric Transformation\n100%\nFacilitated Diffusion\n100%\nDiffusion Model\n37%\nDeep Learning-Based Landmark Detection Model for Multiple Foot Deformity Classification: A Dual-Center Study\nLee, S. J., Yoon, H., Bae, S., Paik, I., Moon, J. H., Park, S., Jang, C. W., Park, J. H., Choi, E.,\nYang, E.\n& Shin, J. C.,\nAug 2025\n,\nIn:\nYonsei medical journal.\n66\n,\n8\n,\np. 491-501\n11 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nRetrospective Study\n100%\nWeight Bearing\n100%\nFoot Malformation\n100%\nDiagnostic Imaging\n25%\n1\nScopus \n citations\nDIVIDE AND TRANSLATE: COMPOSITIONAL FIRST-ORDER LOGIC TRANSLATION AND VERIFICATION FOR COMPLEX LOGICAL REASONING\nRyu, H., Kim, G., Lee, H. S. &\nYang, E.\n,