  "deep_homepage::Xiaoyu Wang::https://www.xiaoyumu.com/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.xiaoyumu.com/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Xiaoyu's personal web\nI was a Cofounder & Chief Scientist of Intellifusion, where I managed AI teams including Computer Vision, Natural Language Processing, Computer Graphics, Data Mining and AI Infra for product and research.\r\n\t\t\tPreviously I was a founding member of\nSnap Research\nLos Angeles, CA, and served as Chair of Computer Vision from 2015 to 2017. Prior to joining Snapchat, I was a Research Staff Member at\nNEC Labs America\n, Cupertino, CA.\r\n\t\t\tI did one intern at\nIBM T.J. Watson Research Center\n, White Plains, New York and two at\nNEC Labs America\n. \r\n\t\t\tI was leading the R&D of \r\n\t\t\tvideo analysis system at a startup company\nwhen pursuing my Bachelor degree.\r\n\r\n\t\t\tI am a Fellow of IEEE and a Fellow of AAIA. I received the Industrial Leader Award, by the Asian-Pacific Signal and Information Association. I also served as area chair for prestigious AI conferences such as CVPR and NeurIPS.  I like to build things or organization from scratch.\nNews\nI will serve as an IEEE Fellow Committee Member for IEEE fellow evaluation, 2024 - 2025\nI will serve as an Area Chair for CVPR 2024/ECCV 2024/NeurIPS 2024\nI will serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2023\nI will serve as an Area Chair for CVPR 2023\n\n---\n\nWelcome to Xiaoyu's personal web\nAbout the website\nThe website is developed with Django. Most of the webpages are static. The publication page is automatically generated from a bib-like file. Messages inputed to the search form are redirected to google scholar search. The header picture is taken when I visited Santa Barbara."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Gang Niu::https://niug1984.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://niug1984.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "gang.niu.ml@gmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Gang Niu (Senior Research Scientist at RIKEN)\nGang Niu (Senior Research Scientist at RIKEN)\nHome\nPublications\nInvited Talks\nProfessional Services\nCodes and Data\nMiscellaneous\nHome\n[\nShort Bio\n,\nNews\n,\nResearch Interests\n,\nJob Experience\n,\nEducation\n]\nGang Niu, D.Eng.\nSenior Research Scientist (indefinite-term),\nImperfect Information Learning Team,\nRIKEN\nCenter for Advanced Intelligence Project.\nNihonbashi 1-chome Mitsui Building, 15th floor,\n1-4-1 Nihonbashi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo 103-0027, Japan.\nE-mail: gang.niu.ml at gmail.com\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nSemantic Scholar\n,\nDBLP\n]\nShort Bio\nGang Niu is currently an indefinite-term senior research scientist at RIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project.\n            He received the PhD degree in computer science from Tokyo Institute of Technology in 2013.\n            Before joining RIKEN, he was a senior software engineer at Baidu and then an assistant professor at the University of Tokyo.\n            He joined RIKEN as a research scientist in 2018, and he was tenured in 2020 and promoted to senior research scientist in 2023.\n            Gang published more than 130 journal articles and conference papers, including 42 ICML, 27 NeurIPS, and 17 ICLR (1 outstanding paper honorable mention) papers.\n            He co-authored the book “Machine Learning from Weak Supervision: An Empirical Risk Minimization Approach” (the MIT Press).\n            On the other hand, he served as a senior area chair/senior meta-reviewer 6 times and an area chair/meta-reviewer 27 times.\n            He is also serving as an associate/action editor of IEEE TPAMI, MLJ, and TMLR.\n            Moreover, he served as a publication chair for ICML 2022, and co-organized 18 workshops, 1 competition, and 3 tutorials.\n            Last but not least, he is currently an IEEE senior member.\nNews\n2026/01/23: Serve as a senior area chair for ICML 2026.\n2025/05/11: Serve as a senior area chair for NeurIPS 2025.\n2024/09/28: Serve as an action editor of Machine Learning (Springer Nature).\n2024/06/10: Serve as an associate editor of IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence.\n2024/05/22: Serve as a senior area chair for NeurIPS 2024.\n2023/04/01: I am promoted to senior research scientist!\n2022/08/23: Our book “\nMachine Learning from Weak Supervision: An Empirical Risk Minimization Approach\n” was published by the MIT Press.\n2022/04/20: Our paper “\nPiCO: Contrastive Label Disambiguation for Partial Label Learning\n” received an outstanding paper honorable mention at ICLR 2022.\n2022/03/24: Serve as an action editor of Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n2022/01/27: Serve as a publication chair for ICML 2022.\n2020/10/01: I am tenured!\nResearch Interests\nWeakly supervised learning\n(including but not limited to\nsemi-supervised learning, positive-unlabeled learning, and label-noise learning)\nIn-context learning and test-time adaptation\nDeep learning and representation learning\nJob Experience\nSenior Research Scientist\n, Since April 2023\nRIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project, Tokyo, Japan.\nAdjunct Full Professor\n, Since January 2021\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Southeast University, Nanjing, China.\nResearch Scientist\n, April 2018--March 2023 (Tenured in October 2020)\nRIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project, Tokyo, Japan.\nVisiting Scientist\n, September 2017--March 2018\nRIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project, Tokyo, Japan.\nAssistant Professor\n, September 2015--March 2018\nDept. of Complexity Science and Engineering, The University of Tokyo, Tokyo, Japan.\nSenior Software Engineer\n, April 2014--July 2015\nDept. of Natural Language Processing, Baidu, Beijing, China.\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n, October 2013--March 2014\nDept. of Computer Science, Tokyo Institute of Technology, Tokyo, Japan.\nEducation\nDoctor of Engineering\n, September 2013\nDept. of Computer Science, Tokyo Institute of Technology, Tokyo, Japan.\nSupervised by Prof. Masashi Sugiyama.\nMaster of Engineering\n, July 2010\nDept. of Computer Science and Technology, Nanjing University, Nanjing, China.\nSupervised by Prof. Lin Shang.\nBachelor of Science\n, July 2007\nDept. of Mathematics, Southeast University, Nanjing, China."
  },
