    "homepage_text": "Jian Liang\nHome\nExperience\nEducation\nGroup\nResearch\nPublications\nActivities\nMiscellaneous\nAbout Me\n梁坚 (Jian Liang, Tim)\nAssociate Professor\nNLPR, Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n95 Zhongguancun East Road, 100190, Haidian, Beijing\n👻\nResume\n♟\nGithub\n🎖\nGoogle Scholar\n📄\nArxiv\n⇰\nliangjian92🌀gmail.com\nor\njian.liang🌀nlpr.ia.ac.cn\nBefore joining CASIA in June 2021, I was a research fellow at the Vision and Learning Group, National University of Singapore, working with\nDr. Jiashi Feng\nfrom June 2019 to April 2021.\nI obtained Ph.D. in\nPattern Recognition and Intelligent Systems\nfrom CASIA in Jan 2019, under the supervision of\nProf. Tieniu Tan\nand co-supervision of\nProf. Ran He\nand\nProf. Zhenan Sun\n, and received my bachelor degree in\nAutomation\nfrom Xi'an Jiaotong University in June 2013.\nMy current research interests mainly focus on representation learning, knowledge transfer, trustworthy AI (including security, privacy, or robustness in AI), and their applications in various computer vision problems.\nI am open to discussion or collaboration. Feel free to drop me an email if you're interested.\nNews (the past year)\n[2026/01] Two papers have been accepted to ICLR 2026.\n[2026/01] One paper has been accepted to IEEE TIP.\n[2026/01] I am invited as an Area Chair of ICME 2026.\n[2025/11] I am invited as an Area Chair of ICML 2026.\n[2025/09] One paper has been accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025/09] I am invited as an Area Chair of CVPR 2026.\n[2025/08] I am invited as an Area Chair of ICLR 2026.\n[2025/08] One paper has been accepted to IEEE TMM.\n[2025/08] One paper has been accepted to ACM CSUR.\n[2025/07] One paper has been accepted to ACM-MM 2025.\n[2025/06] One paper has been accepted to ICCV 2025.\n[2025/06] I am invited as an Area Chair of WACV 2026.\n[2025/02] Two papers have been accepted to CVPR 2025.\n[2025/01] One paper has been accepted to ICLR 2025.\nRecent Work\nA Comprehensive Survey on\nTrustworthiness in Reasoning\nwith Large Language Models\nAbstract:\nYanbo Wang, Yongcan Yu, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He\nTechnical report, 2025\nPaper\n/\nTaxonomy\n/\nCode\nAdapting Vision-Language Models Without Labels\n: A Comprehensive Survey\nAbstract:\nHao Dong\n♯\n, Lijun Sheng\n♯\n, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He, Eleni Chatzi, Olga Fink\nArxiv technical report, 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nLoRA-Pro: Are\nLow-Rank Adapters\nProperly Optimized?\nZhengbo Wang, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He, Zilei Wang, Tieniu Tan\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), Spotlight, 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nThe Illusion of Progress? A Critical Look at\nTest-Time Adaptation\nfor Vision-Language Models\nLijun Sheng, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He, Zilei Wang, Tieniu Tan\nNeurIPS Datasets and Benchmarks Track, 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nR-TPT: Improving Adversarial Robustness of Vision-Language Models through\nTest-Time Prompt Tuning\nLijun Sheng, Jian Liang\n©\n, Zilei Wang, Ran He\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nTest-Time Immunization: A Universal Defense Framework Against\nJailbreaks\nfor (Multimodal) Large Language Models\nYongcan Yu, Yanbo Wang, Ran He, Jian Liang\n©\nArxiv technical report, 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\nDo We Really Need Curated Malicious Data for\nSafety Alignment\nin Multi-modal Large Language Models?\nYanbo Wang, Jiyang Guan, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nCooperative Pseudo Labeling for\nUnsupervised Federated Classification\nKuangpu Guo, Lijun Sheng, Yongcan Yu, Jian Liang\n©\n, Zilei Wang, Ran He\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nExploring Vacant Classes in\nLabel-Skewed Federated Learning\nKuangpu Guo, Yuhe Ding, Jian Liang\n©\n, Ran He, Zilei Wang, Tieniu Tan\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nRanking Vision-Language Models\nin Fully Unlabeled Tasks\nAbstract:\nYuhe Ding, Bo Jiang, Aihua Zheng, Qin Xu, Jian Liang\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (TMM), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\nOut-of-Distribution Detection\n: A Task-Oriented Survey of Recent Advances\nShuo Lu, Yingsheng Wang, Lijun Sheng, Aihua Zheng, Lingxiao He, Jian Liang\n©\nACM Computing Surveys (CSUR), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nUni-Layout: Integrating Human Feedback in Unified\nLayout Generation\nand Evaluation\nShuo Lu, Yanyin Chen, Wei Feng, Jiahao Fan, Fengheng Li, Zheng Zhang, Jingjing Lv, Junjie Shen, Ching Law, Jian Liang\n©\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM), 2025\nPaper\n/\nLink\n/\nCode\nLast updated on Jan 2026. The CSS file is adapted from\nBen Recht's webpage\n."
