    "homepage_text": "Liang Wang's Homepage\nLiang Wang (\n王亮\n)\nHi! I am Liang Wang, a final-year PhD student at\nInstitute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CASIA)\n. I am affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Multimodal Artificial Intelligence Systems (MAIS), supervised by Prof.\nLiang Wang\n(by coincidence, my PhD supervisor's name is spelled identically to mine), and co-supervised by Prof.\nShu Wu\nand Prof.\nQiang Liu\n.\nMeanwhile, I am also a visiting PhD student at National University of Singapore (NUS), affiliated with\nZhangLab\n, under the supervision of Prof.\nYang Zhang\nand mentored by Dr.\nZhiyuan Liu\n.\nIn addition, I am a research intern at\nDP Technology\n. Previously, I was fortunate to be a research intern at\nAlibaba DAMO Academy\n, supervised by Dr.\nYu Rong\n. I also had internship experiences at Bytedance and Meituan.\nI received a B.E. in Software Engineering from Tongji University.\n📍\nFeel free to reach out if you are interested in my work or would like to get in touch with me.\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\n/\nCV[PDF]\nEmail:\nliang.wang[at]cripac.ia.ac.cn / liang.wang[at]u.nus.edu\nResearch Interests\nCurrently, I am focusing on the research of AI for Science, Generative Models, and LLM Reasoning.\nPreviously, I also worked on Graph Machine Learning and Data Mining.\nAI for Science\nGenerative Models\nLLM Reasoning\nGraph Machine Learning\nData Mining\nNews\n[Sep 20, 2025] Two papers on enzyme design (\nEnzyControl\n) and molecular representation pre-training (\n3D-GSRD\n) are accepted by NeurIPS 2025!\n[Jul 10, 2025] Our paper \"DiffSpectra: Molecular Structure Elucidation from Spectra using Diffusion Models\" is released on arXiv!\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[May 26, 2025] Our survey paper \"Materials Generation in the Era of Artificial Intelligence: A Comprehensive Survey\" is released on arXiv!\n[Paper]\n[Awesome Paper List]\n[Apr 17, 2025] I will attend ICLR 2025 from Apr 24 to Apr 28. Looking forward to seeing you in Singapore!\n[Feb 14, 2025] Our survey paper \"Diffusion Models for Molecules: A Survey of Methods and Tasks\" is released on arXiv!\n[Paper]\n[Awesome Paper List]\n[Jan 23, 2025] One paper on molecular representation pre-training (\nMolSpectra\n) is accepted by ICLR 2025!\n[Dec 10, 2024] One paper on knowledge graph completion (\nS\n2\nDN\n) is accepted by AAAI 2025!\n[Dec 9, 2024] I will attend NeurIPS 2024 from Dec 10 to Dec 15. Looking forward to seeing you in Vancouver@Canada!\n[Nov 1, 2024] Invited to give a talk on molecular representation learning and property prediction at DP Technology.\n[Slides]\n[Sep 26, 2024] One paper on molecular property prediction (\nPin-Tuning\n) is accepted by NeurIPS 2024!\nSelected Publications\n(Full Publication List)\nAI for Science\nEnzyControl: Adding Functional and Substrate-Specific Control for Enzyme Backbone Generation\nChao Song, Zhiyuan Liu, Han Huang,\nLiang Wang\n, Qiong Wang, Jianyu Shi, Hui Yu, Yihang Zhou, Yang Zhang\nNeurIPS 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n3D-GSRD: 3D Molecular Graph Auto-Encoder with Selective Re-mask Decoding\nChang Wu, Zhiyuan Liu, Wen Shu,\nLiang Wang\n, Yanchen Luo, Wenqiang Lei, Yatao Bian, Junfeng Fang, Xiang Wang\nNeurIPS 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nMolSpectra: Pre-training 3D Molecular Representation with Multi-modal Energy Spectra\nLiang Wang\n, Shaozhen Liu, Yu Rong, Deli Zhao, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang\nICLR 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\n[Slides]\n[Blog (Chinese)]\nPin-Tuning: Parameter-Efficient In-Context Tuning for Few-Shot Molecular Property Prediction\nLiang Wang\n, Qiang Liu, Shaozhen Liu, Xin Sun, Shu Wu, Liang Wang\nNeurIPS 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nGraph Machine Learning\nRethinking Graph Masked Autoencoders through Alignment and Uniformity\nLiang Wang\n*, Xiang Tao*, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang\nAAAI 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nDIVE: Subgraph Disagreement for Graph Out-of-Distribution Generalization\nXin Sun,\nLiang Wang\n, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Zilei Wang, Liang Wang\nKDD 2024\n[Paper]\nGSLB: The Graph Structure Learning Benchmark\nZhixun Li,\nLiang Wang\n, Xin Sun, Yifan Luo, Yanqiao Zhu, Dingshuo Chen, Yingtao Luo, Xiangxin Zhou, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang, Jeffrey Xu Yu\nNeurIPS 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nData Mining\nS\n2\nDN: Learning to Denoise Unconvincing Knowledge for Inductive Knowledge Graph Completion\nTengfei Ma, Yujie Chen,\nLiang Wang\n, Xuan Lin, Bosheng Song, Xiangxiang Zeng\nAAAI 2025\n[Paper]\nBi-Level Graph Structure Learning for Next POI Recommendation\nLiang Wang\n, Shu Wu, Qiang Liu, Yanqiao Zhu, Xiang Tao, Mengdi Zhang, Liang Wang\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nSemantic Evolvement Enhanced Graph Autoencoder for Rumor Detection\nXiang Tao,\nLiang Wang\n, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang\nWWW 2024\n[Paper]\nPreprints\nDiffSpectra: Molecular Structure Elucidation from Spectra using Diffusion Models\nLiang Wang\n, Yu Rong, Tingyang Xu, Zhenyi Zhong, Zhiyuan Liu, Pengju Wang, Deli Zhao, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang, Yang Zhang\narXiv preprint 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Model Checkpoints]\n[Datasets]\nDiffusion Models for Molecules: A Survey of Methods and Tasks\nLiang Wang\n, Chao Song, Zhiyuan Liu, Yu Rong, Qiang Liu, Shu Wu, Liang Wang\narXiv preprint 2025\n[Paper]\n[Awesome Paper List]\nMaterials Generation in the Era of Artificial Intelligence: A Comprehensive Survey\nZhixun Li*, Bin Cao*, Rui Jiao*,\nLiang Wang*\n, Ding Wang, Yang Liu, Dingshuo Chen, Jia Li, Qiang Liu, Yu Rong, Liang Wang, Tong-yi Zhang, Jeffrey Xu Yu\narXiv preprint 2025\n[Paper]\n[Awesome Paper List]\nA Survey of Graph Transformers: Architectures, Theories and Applications\nChaohao Yuan, Kangfei Zhao, Ercan Engin Kuruoglu,\nLiang Wang\n, Tingyang Xu, Wenbing Huang, Deli Zhao, Hong Cheng, Yu Rong\narXiv preprint 2025\n[Paper]\nProjects\nPyGCL/PyGCL\nPyGCL\n: An easy-to-use library for graph contrastive learning with PyTorch. It implements a wide variety of contrastive objectives, data augmentations, contrasting modes and other utilities useful for implementing and evaluating contrastive learning on graphs.\nGSL-Benchmark/GSLB\nGSLB\n: An open-source library built for easy implementation and evaluation of graph structure learning model family. It offers a versatile control of graph dataset loading, structure learners, structure processors, and a bunch of reproduced models.\nServices\nConference Reviewer\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024, 2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2025\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD), 2024, 2025, 2026\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2026\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2025, 2026\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE)\nIEEE Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics (TCBB)\nEducation\nVisiting PhD\nat National University of Singapore\n2025 - 2026 (Expected)\nResearch Interests: AI for Science, Generative Models, LLM Reasoning\nPhD (selected for the PhD honors program)\nat Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n2021 - 2026 (Expected)\nMajor: Pattern Recognition and Intelligent Systems\nBachelor\nat Tongji University\n2017 - 2021\nMajor: Software Engineering"
  },
