    "homepage_text": "Rong Jin-Department of Immunology-Peking University School of Basic Medical Sciences\nHome\nOverview\nAbout\nDean's Message\nLeadership\nContact us\nDepartments & Institutes\nFaculty\nAcademicians\nPrincipal Investigators\nAdjunct Professors\nEducation\nResearch\nResearch Themes\nKey Laboratories & Innovation Centers\nJoin Us\nFor Alumni\nAlumni Benefits\nAlumni events\nGive to us\nAlumni Association Office\nä¸­æ\nä¸­æ\nHome\nOverview\nAbout\nDean's Message\nLeadership\nContact us\nDepartments & Institutes\nFaculty\nAcademicians\nPrincipal Investigators\nAdjunct Professors\nEducation\nResearch\nResearch Themes\nKey Laboratories & Innovation Centers\nJoin Us\nFor Alumni\nAlumni Benefits\nAlumni events\nGive to us\nAlumni Association Office\nHome  >\nFaculty  >\nPrincipal Investigators  >\nDepartment of Immunology\nDepartment of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology\nDepartment of Biophysics\nDepartment of Cell Biology\nDepartment of Human Anatomy, Histology and Embryology\nDepartment of Immunology\nDepartment of Integration of Chinese and Western Medicine\nDepartment of Medical Bioinformatics\nDepartment of Medical Genetics\nDepartment of Microbiology\nDepartment of Neurobiology\nDepartment of Pharmacology\nDepartment of Physiology and Pathophysiology\nDepartment of Radiation Medicine\nPeking University Institute of Cardiovascular Sciences\nPeking University Institute of Systems Biomedicine\nPrincipal Investigators\nDepartment of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology\nDepartment of Biophysics\nDepartment of Cell Biology\nDepartment of Human Anatomy, Histology and Embryology\nDepartment of Immunology\nDepartment of Integration of Chinese and Western Medicine\nDepartment of Medical Bioinformatics\nDepartment of Medical Genetics\nDepartment of Microbiology\nDepartment of Neurobiology\nDepartment of Pharmacology\nDepartment of Physiology and Pathophysiology\nDepartment of Radiation Medicine\nPeking University Institute of Cardiovascular Sciences\nPeking University Institute of Systems Biomedicine\nDepartment of Immunology\nRong Jin\nåå¸æ¥æï¼2025-10-09\nJin Rong, Associate Professor (PhD Supervisor)\nContact Information\njinrong@bjmu.edu.cn\nResearch Direction\nï¼1ï¼Tumor Immunology and Lipid Metabolism\nï¼2ï¼Respiratory Diseases and Lipid Metabolism\nPersonal profile\nDr. Jinâs research focuses on T-cell development, differentiation, and lipid metabolism. Her work integrates transcriptomics, proteomics, epigenetics, and lipidomics to elucidate the phenotypic development, differentiation, function, and metabolism of T cells in the thymus and peripheral tissues. Recent studies explore: 1. Effects of fatty acids on lymphocyte function in the tumor microenvironment and underlying metabolic mechanisms. 2. Lipid metabolism regulation of lymphocyte function in intestinal and hepatic tissues.3. Mechanisms of lysophospholipids in asthma pathogenesis. She has published over 40 papers in prestigious journals ( European Respiratory Journal ,  Cell Reports ,  Cancer Research ,  PNAS ,  Cell Mol Immunol , etc.), including 20 as first/corresponding author, and holds 1 patent."
  },
