    "homepage_text": "About me - Yite Wang\nYite Wang\nResearch Scientist at ByteDance\nFollow\nBellevue, WA\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI’m a Research Scientist at Snowflake AI Research, where I train reasoning models and LLM agents, especially for structured data. Before that, I was a Research Scientist on ByteDance’s Seed-Foundation-Code team.\nI earned my Ph.D. from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign under\nProf. Ruoyu Sun\n, with co-advising from\nProf. Naira Hovakimyan\n. In my first year I collaborated with\nProf. Justin Sirignano\non deep-learning for computational fluid dynamics (CFD), and during my master’s studies I worked with\nProf. Kyle Smith\non numerical simulation for energy storage systems.\nResearch interests:\nReasoning Models; Agent; Efficient Deep Learning; Natural Language Processing; Computer Vision; Numerical Methods.\nHiring\n:\nSnowflake AI Research\nis seeking research scientist interns for remote, long-term positions (3-6 months, part-time) starting August 2025. Projects include:\nPost-training tool-augmented LLMs\nDevelopment of personalized Text-to-SQL models\nDeep Research on structured data\nDeveloping and training of data-science agents\nIf you are interested, don’t hesitate to send your resume to yite.wang@snowflake.com.\nNews\n[Feb. 2026]\nOur paper\nDARE-bench: Evaluating Modeling and Instruction Fidelity of LLMs in Data Science\nis accepted to ICLR 2026. [\narXiv\n] [\ncode\n]\n[Feb. 2026]\nWe released\nAgent World Model: Infinity Synthetic Environments for Agentic Reinforcement Learning\non arXiv. [\narXiv\n]\n[Apr. 2025]\nI joined Snowflake AI Research, working on reasoning models and LLM agents.\n[May. 2024]\nI joined ByteDance Seed-Foundation-Code as a Research Scientist working on LLM for code.\n[Mar. 2024]\nI successfully defended my Ph.D. thesis.\n[Jan. 2024]\nOur paper on model expansion was accepted to ICLR 2024.\n[Oct. 2023]\nI received the NeurIPS 2023 Scholar Award.\n[Sep. 2023]\nOur paper about dynamic sparse training for GANs was accepted to NeurIPS 2023.\n[Jan. 2023]\nOur paper about foresight pruning was accepted to ICLR 2023.\n[Mar. 2022]\nOur paper about neural architecture search for meta learning was accepted to CVPR 2022.\nPublications\nSee the full publication list on the\nPublications\npage.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nEducation - Yite Wang\nYite Wang\nResearch Scientist at ByteDance\nFollow\nBellevue, WA\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nEducation\nPh.D, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, 2024\nM.S., University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, 2019\nB.S., Zhejiang University, 2017"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Ruoyu Sun::https://ruoyus.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://ruoyus.github.io/",
