    "homepage_text": "Xiaolin Hu's homepage\nHome\nResearch\nTeaching\nPublications\nSoftware\nStudents\nLinks\nè¡ææ Xiaolin Hu\nPhD, Associate Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nState Key Laboratory of Intelligent Technology and Systems\n,\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing 100084, China\nAlso affiliated with:\nTsinghua Laboratory of Brain and Intelligence (THBI)\n,\nIDG/McGovern Institute for Brain Research\n,\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing 100084, China\nChinese Institute for Brain Research  (CIBR)\n, Beijing 100010, China\nContact:\nFIT Building 1-508, Tsinghua University\nTel: +86-10-6279 9932\nEmail: xlhu[AT]tsinghua[DOT]edu[DOT]cn\nWebsite:\nwww.xlhu.cn\nGoogle Scholar page\nA short bio\nI got my PhD degree in\nAutomation and Computer-Aided Engineering\nfrom\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\nin 2007, under the supervision of\nProf. Jun Wang\n. Then I became a post-doc researcher at the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nTsinghua University\nworking with\nProf. Bo Zhang\n. Since 2009, I have been a faculty member of this department, working in the\nTSAIL\ngroup directed by\nProf. Bo Zhang\nand\nProf. Jun Zhu\n. My current research interests include artificial neural networks and computational neuroscience.\nI'm an Associate Editor of IEEE\nTransactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n,\nCognitive Neurodynamics\nand\nCAAI Transactions on Intelligent Systems\n. Previously I was an Associate Editor of\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\nand\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n. I'm a Senior Member of IEEE.\nPostgraduate and Postdoc vacancies\nClick\nhere\nfor details.\nNews\nJune 2024:  Kai Li's thesis was   awarded the Excellent Master Thesis of Tsinghua University.\nJune 2024: Gang Zhang was awarded the PhD degree. Kate Bulatova, DariaÂ Sapozhnikova, Dung Nguyen, Michael Yuwen Zhang, Kai Li were  awarded the Master degrees.\nMay 2024: Kai Li was awarded Outstanding Graduate of Beijing.\n4/17/2024: Congratulations to Linxi Xiao, Jiongchen Zhang and Xiaopei Zhu who got the Third Prize (ä¸ç­å¥) in the\n42th Challenge Cup (æææ¯)\nof Tsinghua University!\n01/01/2024: We are going to organize\nthe 18th International Symposium on Neural Networks (ISNN 2024)\n, which will be held in Weihai, Shandong, China on July 11-14, 2024. We are calling for papers!\nJan 2024: Amaury Prat was awarded the Master degree.\nJune 2023: Zhanhao Hu and Chufeng Tang were awarded the PhD degrees.\nJune 2022: Weiyi Zhang and HÃ©ctor Martel were awarded the Master degrees.\n8/24/2022: I gaive a talk titled \"éå¯¹ç©çä¸çè¡äººæ£æµç³»ç»çå¯¹ææ»å»\" at\nVALSE\nconference. The PPT can be downloaded\nhere\n.\n5/9/2022: I gave a talk titled \"Adversarial Clothes for Fooling DNN-Based Human Detectors\" at THU-USC Faculty Research Symposium on Artificial Intelligence and Sustainability. The PPT can be downloaded\nhere\n.\n10/24/2021: In the\niFLYTEK Challenge 2021 Cultivated Land Extraction from High-Resolution Remote Sensing Image\n, Zheng Zhao, Yuqiu Zhao and Gang Zhang got the first place among 486 teams. Congratulations!\n7/16/2021: In the\nACM MM2021 Robust Logo Detection Grand Challenge\n, Hang Chen, Xiao Li and Zefan Wang got the 5th place among 36,489 teams. Results were released\nhere\n.\n7/16/2021: Aminul Huq and Albert Millan have been awarded the Master degrees.\n4/12/2021: Congratulations to Xiaodi Yuan, Yuan Gao and Yun Wu, who got the Second Prize (äºç­å¥) in the\n39th Challenge Cup (æææ¯)\nof Tsinghua University!\nNov 2020: æ¬äººè·å¾âæ¸åå¤§å­¦ç¬¬ä¹å±éå¹´æå¸æå­¦å¤§èµâå·¥ç§ç»ä¸ç­å¥ã\n9/14/2020: Congratulations to Enxian Zhou, Jiayou Zhang, Dong Wei, Zhuoer Feng and Bohan Chen, who got the Outstanding Award (ç¹ç­å¥) in the 38th Challenge Cup (æææ¯) of Tsinghua University!\n11/29/2019: é¡¹ç®âèå¯åçè®¡ç®æ¨¡åçè®ºä¸æ¹æ³âè·å¾å´æä¿äººå·¥æºè½èªç¶ç§å­¦å¥äºç­å¥ã\n1/2/2019: We are organizing a workshop\nArtificial Intelligence for Art Creation (AIART)\nin IEEE Multimedia Information Processing and Retrieval (MIPR) 2019. Welcome submissions!\n12/21/2017: In the\nAI Challenger Global AI Contest 2017 Image Captioning (Chinese) track\n, Niange Yu got the first place and won 300,000 RMB cash (~45,500 USD). Congratulations!\n12/13/2017: In the\nNIPS 2017 Competition on Adversarial Attacks and Defenses\norganized by\nGoogle Brain\n, we got the first place in all of the three sub-competitions:\nNon-targeted Adversarial Attack\n,\nTargeted Adversarial Attack\n, and\nDefense Against Adversarial Attack\n. Congratulations to all team members!\n6/19/2017: In the final of the\n4th Tsinghua University  President’s Innovation Challenge\n, our team ranked  5th. Congratulations to all members!\n4/26/2017: Congratulations to  Changran Hu, Xingyu Jin, Jian Wu, Weishu Mo and Xiaoguang Liu, who won in the\nsemi-finals of the 4th Tsinghua University  President’s Innovation Challenge\nand ranked top 10. The finals will be held in this June.\n4/24/2017: Congratulations to Shaoxiong Wang, Changran Hu, Xingyu Jin and Jian Wu, who got the Outstanding Award (ç¹ç­å¥) in the\n35th Challenge Cup (æææ¯)\nof Tsinghua University!\n4/18/2017: Congratulations to Fangzhou Liao, anonymous and Zhe Li, who got the first place in the\nData Science Bowl 2017\n. A total of 500,000 USD will be awarded to them!\n4/18/2017: Welcome to join the\n2017 Deep Learning Summer School\nat the Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University. The deadline for application is May 10, 2017.\n3/10/2017: The second\nDuke-Tsinghua Machine Learning Summer School: Deep Learning for Big Data\nis open for application now. Time: July 25 to Aug  3, 2017. Venue: Duke Kunshan University, Kunshan, China. Welcome to join us.\n3/20/2016: Xi Chen and Fangzhou Liao  attended the Kaggle competition\nSecond Annual Data Science Bowl\n. With only three weeks, the team ranked fourth among 192 teams in the final round. Congratulations!\n3/20/2016: I'm going to give some lectures at\nDuke-Tsinghua Machine Learning Summer School: Deep Learning for Big Data\n, which will be held from August 1 to 10, 2016, in Duke Kunshan University, Kunshan, China. Welcome to join us.\n12/1/2015: The PhD student  Ming Liang received\n2015 Baidu Scholarship\n. It is a prestigious award as the competitors were from  all over the world. He became  one of the ten lucky boys. Congratulations to Ming!\n12/1/ 2015: In the\nChinese Traffic Sign Recognition Competition\norganized by Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC) and Chinese Association of Automation, hold in Xi'an during Nov 8-9, 2015, our team TNS ranked 2nd. Congratulations!\nÂ© 2024 Xiaolin Hu. All rights reserved.\nå·¥ä¸åä¿¡æ¯åé¨å¤æ¡ç®¡çç³»ç»ç½ç« äº¬ICPå¤14000327å·"
