    "homepage_text": "Mingjie Sun\nMingjie Sun\nEmail: mingjies.sun [at] gmail [dot] com\nAbout Me\nI am a Member of Technical Staff at\nThinking Machines Lab\n. I obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science Department from Carnegie Mellon University, advised by\nZico Kolter\n, and my B.S. in Computer Science from\nYao Class\n, Tsinghua University.\nResearch\n* indicates\nequal contribution\nFor a complete list of technical reports, please see my\nGoogle Scholar\nIdiosyncrasies in Large Language Models\nMingjie Sun*,\nYida Yin*\n,\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\n,\nZhuang Liu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 2025\n[\npaper\n]\n            [\ncode\n]\n            [\nproject page\n]\n            [\nmedia\n]\n            [\ncmu news\n]\nTest-Time Adaptation Induces Stronger Accuracy and Agreement-on-the-Line\nEungyeup Kim\n,\n            Mingjie Sun,\nChristina Baek\n,\nAditi Raghunathan\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2024\n[\npaper\n]\n            [\nopenreview\n]\nMassive Activations in Large Language Models\nMingjie Sun,\nXinlei Chen\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\n,\nZhuang Liu\nConference on Language Modeling (COLM) 2024\nOral at\nICLR 2024 ME-FoMo Workshop\n[\npaper\n]\n            [\ncode\n]\n            [\nproject page\n]\n            [\nopenreview\n]\nA Simple and Effective Pruning Approach for Large Language Models\nMingjie Sun*,\nZhuang Liu\n*,\nAnna Bair\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2024\n[\npaper\n]\n            [\ncode\n]\n            [\nproject page\n]\n            [\nopenreview\n]\n            [\nslide\n]\nSingle Image Backdoor Inversion via Robust Smoothed Classifiers\nMingjie Sun,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2023\n[\npaper\n]\n        [\ncode\n]\n        [\nvideo\n]\n(Certified!!) Adversarial Robustness for Free!\nNicholas Carlini\n*,\nFlorian Tramèr\n*,\nKrishnamurthy (Dj) Dvijotham\n,\n            Leslie Rice, \n            Mingjie Sun,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2023\n[\npaper\n]\n        [\ncode\n]\n        [\nopenreview\n]\nTest-Time Adaptation via Conjugate Pseudo-Labels\nSachin Goyal\n*,\n            Mingjie Sun*,\nAditi Raghunathan\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2022\n[\npaper\n] \n        [\ncode\n] \n        [\nopenreview\n] \n        [\nZico's talk\n]\nDenoised Smoothing: A Provable Defense for Pretrained Classifiers\nHadi Salman\n,\n            Mingjie Sun,\nGreg Yang\n,\nAshish Kapoor\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2020\n[\npaper\n] \n        [\ncode\n] \n        [\nblog post\n]\nRethinking the Value of Network Pruning\nZhuang Liu\n*,\n            Mingjie Sun*,\nTinghui Zhou\n,\nGao Huang\n,\nTrevor Darrell\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2019\nBest Paper Award at\nNeurIPS 2018 Compact Deep Neural Networks Workshop\n[\npaper\n] \n        [\ncode\n] \n        [\nopenreview\n]\nMisc\nMy name in Chinese: 孙明杰"
