    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Xin Yu's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWelcome to Xin Yu's Homepage\nMy name is Xin Yu, a Senior Lecturer at the University of Queensland. I am an Australian Research Council Discovery Early Career Researcher Award 2023-2025 (DECRA) recipient and an awardee of the prestigious Google Research Scholar Program in 2021. Previously, I was a research fellow at the Australian National University (ANU). I received my PhD degree from the Australian National Unversity under the supervision of Prof. Richard Hartley, Prof. Fatih Porikli and Dr. Basura Fernando. I also received a PhD degree from Tsinghua University supervised by Prof. Li Zhang. I am interested in Computer Vision and Machine Learning topics.\nI am actively looking for self-motivated students with strong backgrounds in CS and math.\nContact details:\nAddress: Room 605. Building 78. The University of Queensland. Australia\nEmail:\nxin.yu@uq.edu.au\nGoogle Scholar:\nLINK\nPlease visit my new Homepage\n:\nLINK\nNews\nI will work at Google Research as a visiting research scientist from 1st April to 1st Nov 2024\n, but am still recruiting outstanding PhD students.\nMar 2024, we got\nthree papers\naccepted in CVPR 2024.\nJan 2024, we got one paper published in TPAMI.\nSept 2023, we got\ntwo papers\naccepted in NeurIPS 2023.\nJuly 2023, we got one paper accepted in ICCV 2023.\nJun 2023, I am serving as an Area Chair for CVPR 2024.\nMay 2023,\nAuslan-Daily\nand\nVideo-based Retinal Vessel Segmentation\n(RVD)\ndatasets are online now! Please check!\nMar 2023, I am serving as the Local Chair for AJCAI 2023.\nFeb 2023, we have\nthree papers\naccepted in CVPR 2023. Congratulations to Heming, Xingqun and Haoqian.\nFeb 2023, we have\ntwo papers\naccepted in ICLR 2023. Congratulations to Yadan and Ping.\nJan 2023, I have been invited to give a talk in synthetic data for machine learning workshop IJCNN 2023.\nJan 2023, we have one paper accepted by IEEE TVCG. Congratulations to Chen Liu.\nDec 2022, I have been invited to give a talk in the face analysis tutorial ACCV 2022.\nNov 2022, I am serving as Senior Meta Reviewer in IJCAI 2023.\nSep 2022, I have been awarded the\nARC DECRA Fellowship\nfrom 2023-2025.\nAug 2022, we won the runner-up award in Sign Language Spotting Challenge in conjunction with ECCV 2022.\nJul 2022, we have\ntwo papers\naccepted in ECCV 2022.\nApr 2022, I am serving as Area Chair in WACV 2023\nMar. 2022, I am serving as Area Chair in ACCV 2022\nMar. 2021, I have received the\nGoogle Research Scholar Program Award\n.\nI am awarded ICCV 2021\nOutstanding Reviewer\n. (Top 5% experienced reviewers)\nI am awarded CVPR 2021\nOutstanding Reviewer\n.\nI am awarded ECCV 2020\nOutstanding Reviewer\n.\nJune 2020, Congratulations on our paper \"Transferring Cross-domain Knowledge for Video Sign Language Recognition\" which has been\nnominated for the best paper award\nin CVPR 2020.\nMarch 2020, we have won\nthe best paper Honorable Mention\nin WACV 2020.\nResearch topics\nImage super-resolution, Deblurring, Depth estimation, Defocus estimation, Image retrieval and localization, Action recognition,  Visual Navigation, Object tracking and pose estimation.\nProfessional Activities\nPeer Reviewer: IEEE TPAMI, IJCV, IEEE TIP, IEEE TNNLS, IEEE TCSVT, IEEE TMM, IEEE SMC, MVAP, SPL, JEI, CVIU, IVC\nProgram committee member: ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, AAAI, WACV\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zi Huang::https://zi-huang-upf.github.io/": {
