    "homepage_text": "Xi Zhang\nXi Zhang\nCS PhD Candidate\nUniversity of Glasgow\nAbout Me\n👋 I’m a final-year PhD student at the\nUniversity of Glasgow\n, working with the\nAI4BioMed Lab\nand the\nInformation Retrieval Group\n(\nSchool of Computing Science\n).\n🤖 I am also the formulator of\nthe Three Laws of Self-Evolving AI Agents\n, a conceptual framework introduced in\n“A Comprehensive Survey of Self-Evolving AI Agents: A New Paradigm Bridging Foundation Models and Lifelong Agentic Systems”\n, for adaptive and collaborative AI Agents systems.\n🚀 Something Exciting Is Coming — Bridging Research and Innovation!\n📬 Open to collaborations and startup connections — feel free to reach out.\nCV\nInterests\nLanguage Game\nVibe Research\nAI Agents & AI4Health\nMultimodal Large Language Model\nRadiology Vision-language System\nWeb3 & Blockchain\nEducation\nPhD in Computing Science\nUniversity of Glasgow\nMaster of Information Technology & Project Management\nUniversity of Sydney\nB.E. in Software Engineering\nDalian University of Technology\nNews\n📝 New Blog Just Dropped!\nMar 4, 2026\nHarness Vibe Research\nRead more\nMar 4, 2026\n✒️ Invited as Reviewer for ACM HEALTH\nFeb 15, 2026\nACM Transactions on Computing for Healthcare.\nRead more\nFeb 15, 2026\n🎤 Talk at Glasgow AI4BioMed Lab!\nJan 28, 2026\nPresenting recent work at AI4BioMed Lab.\nRead more\nJan 28, 2026\n🎉 Paper Accepted at PSB 2026!\nDec 22, 2025\nOur paper is accepted for poster presentation.\nRead more\nDec 22, 2025\nSee all\nSelected Publications\nRadiology MLLMs\nCCD: Mitigating Hallucinations in Radiology MLLMs via Clinical Contrastive Decoding\nCCD is a training-free and retrieval-free inference framework that integrates structured clinical signals from task‑specific radiology expert models to mitigate hallucinations in radiology MLLMs.\nSep 27, 2025\nSurvey\nA Comprehensive Survey of Self-Evolving AI Agents: A New Paradigm Bridging Foundation Models and Lifelong Agentic Systems\nThis survey bridges foundation models and lifelong agentic systems.\nAug 10, 2025\nRadiology Report Generation\nLibra: Leveraging Temporal Images for Biomedical Radiology Analysis\nLibra, a temporal-aware MLLM, uses TAC to integrate temporal differences, achieving state-of-the-art results on MIMIC-CXR.\nJan 1, 2025\nRecent Publications\n* indicate equal contributors.\nXiaoman Zhang\n,\nJulian Nicolas Acosta\n,\nXiaoli Yang\n,\nSubathra Adithan\n,\nLuyang Luo\n,\nHong-Yu Zhou\n,\nJoshua Miller\n,\nOuwen Huang\n,\nZongwei Zhou\n,\nIbrahim Ethem Hamamci\n,\nShruthi Bannur\n,\nKenza Bouzid\n,\nXi Zhang\n,\nZaiqiao Meng\n,\nAaron Nicolson\n,\nBevan Koopman\n,\nInhyeok Baek\n,\nHanbin Ko\n,\nMercy Prasanna Ranjit\n,\nShaury Srivastav\n,\nSriram Gnana Sambanthan\n,\nPranav Rajpurkar\n(2025).\nAutomated Chest X-ray Report Generation Remains Unsolved\n.\nPSB2026\n.\nPDF\nCite\nDataset\nReXrank Challenge Website\nXi Zhang\n,\nZaiqiao Meng\n,\nJake Lever\n,\nEdmond S. L. Ho\n(2025).\nCCD: Mitigating Hallucinations in Radiology MLLMs via Clinical Contrastive Decoding\n.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDataset\nJustin Xu\n,\nXi Zhang\n,\nJavid Abderezaei\n,\nJulie Bauml\n,\nRoger Boodoo\n,\nFatemeh Haghighi\n,\nAli Ganjizadeh\n,\nEric Brattain\n,\nDave Van Veen\n,\nZaiqiao Meng\n,\nDavid Eyre\n,\nJean-Benoit Delbrouck\n(2025).\nRadEval: A framework for radiology text evaluation\n.\nEMNLP 2025\n.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDataset\nJinyuan Fang\n*\n,\nYanwen Peng\n*\n,\nXi Zhang\n*\n,\nYingxu Wang\n,\nXinhao Yi\n,\nGuibin Zhang\n,\nYi Xu\n,\nBin Wu\n,\nSiwei Liu\n,\nZihao Li\n,\nZhaochun Ren\n,\nNikos Aletras\n,\nXi Wang\n,\nHan Zhou\n,\nZaiqiao Meng\n(2025).\nA Comprehensive Survey of Self-Evolving AI Agents: A New Paradigm Bridging Foundation Models and Lifelong Agentic Systems\n.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nXi Zhang\n,\nZaiqiao Meng\n,\nJake Lever\n,\nEdmond S. L. Ho\n(2025).\nLibra: Leveraging Temporal Images for Biomedical Radiology Analysis\n.\nACL 2025\n.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDataset\nSee all publications"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Sihong Xie::https://sihongxie.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://sihongxie.github.io/",
