    "homepage_text": "æ¸åå¤§å­¦ Yong Luo--Home--Home\nHome\nRelevant Professional Activities\nProjects\nTeaching Research\nTeaching Resources\nTeaching Information\nTeaching Achievement\nEnrollment Information\nStudent Information\nä¸­æ\nYong Luo\nProfessor and Chair\nPersonal Information\nContact Information:010-62788891\nE-Mail:\nba7efdea9d368eb87ac97f7b2af8973de975c9e03ac4d72c9175554173cc333e731be362bd7b5174c28cc66bf8ddb684e10e5d456b0267ece15ba0166517040bfa5e9cd62a37d21f909af52301d9a4abe2d439d5b3e4d2c27265b23c45c9c18d223293c35c96998fa74d1fa8fe3b4c859fa3a5cc56bd63d19896d57490eafd59\nDiscipline:Atmospheric Sciences\nWork Experience\nJuly 1994 â June 2013 National Climate Center, China Meteorological Administration, Beijing, Chinaï¼July 1994 â June 2013 National Climate Center, China Meteorological Administration, Beijing, China\n--\nDeputy Director-General, April 2004 â May 2012\nProfessor, October 2002 â June 2013\nAssociate Professor, September 1997 â October 2002\nAssistant Professor, July 1994 â August 1997\nApril â September 1996, Postdoc Visiting Scientist, Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, Richland, WA, USA\nJanuary 2001 â January 2002, STA Fellow, Third Research Laboratory, Atmospheric Environment and Applied Meteorology Research Department, Meteorological Research Institute, Tsukuba, Japan\nSeptember 2010 â April 2012, Sherpa, UN Secretary General Mr Ban Ki-moonâs High-Level Panel on Global Sustainability\nOctober 2010 â December 2020, Professor and Associate Chair, Department of Earth System Science (Formerly Center for Earth System Science), Tsinghua University, Beijing, China\nJanuary 2021 â now, Professor and Chair, Department of Earth System Science, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China\nPROFESSIONAL AFFILIATIONS\nVice Chair of China WCRP/CliC and IUGG/IACS\nVice-president of the China Cryosphere Science Society\nMember of the Academic Committee of the Ministry of Education Key Laboratory of the Earth System Modelling\nMember of China GEWEX committee\nMember of the 29th Standing Council of the Chinese Meteorological Society\nMember of China IAMAS Committee\nMember of China WCRP Committee\nVice Editor-in-Chief of Advances in Climate Change Research\nVice Editor-in-Chief of Journal of Glaciology and Geocryology\nExecutive Member of the Editorial Board of Journal of Meteorological Research\nEditorial Board Member of Resources Sciences\nEditorial Board Member of Science and Technology Review\nEditorial Board Member of Journal of Nanjing Institute of Meteorology\nEditorial Board Member of Plateau Meteorology\nEditorial Board Member of Chinese Journal of Atmospheric Sciences\nResearch Focus\nThe Climate-Water-Energy research groupï¼Development and evaluation of Earth System Model, Processes and mechanisms of global energy-water cycle, Cryospheric Climatology, Detection, attribution and projection of global climate change, Land surface hydrological assimilation and climate prediction, Meteorology for renewable energy\nResearch\nSelected Relevant Publications during the recent 5 years\n[1] Mingju Hao, Yanluan Lin, Yong Luo*, Reshmita Nath, and Zongci Zhao, 2021: The impact of atmospheric moisture transport on winter Arctic warming: Radiation versus latent heat release. International Journal of Climatology. DOI: 10.1002/joc.7054\n[2] Huang, L., Steenhuis, T. S.*, Luo, Y.*, Tang, Q., Tang, R., Zheng, J., et al. (2021). Revisiting daily MODIS evapotranspiration algorithm using flux tower measurements in China. Earth and Space Science, 8, e2021EA001818. https://doi.org/10.1029/2021EA001818\n[3] Yao Yao, Yong Luo, Jianbin Huang, Jinyu Ma, 2021: Improving the downscaled springtime temperature in Central Asia through assimilating meteorological and snow cover observations. Atmospheric Research, 258 (2021), 105619\n[4] Rui Changï¼Yuping Yan, Yong Luo, Chan Xiao, Chunqiang Wu, Junxia Jiang, Wen Shiï¼2022ï¼ A coupled WRF-PV mesoscale model simulating the near-surface climate of utility-scale photovoltaic plants. Solar Energy, 245 (2022), 278â289\n[5] Wenjia Cai*, Chi Zhang*, Shihui Zhang*, Yuqi Bai, Max Callaghan, Nan Chang, Bin Chen, Huiqi Chen, Liangliang Cheng, Xueqin Cui, Hancheng Dai, Bawuerjiang Danna, Wenxuan Dong, Weicheng Fan, Xiaoyi Fang, Tong Gao, Yang Geng, Dabo Guan, Yixin Hu, Junyi Hua, Cunrui Huang, Hong Huang, Jianbin Huang, Linlang Jiang, Qiaolei Jiang, Xiaopeng Jiang, Hu Jin, Gregor Kiesewetter, Lu Liang, Borong Lin, Hualiang Lin, Huan Liu, Qiyong Liu, Tao Liu, Xiaobo Liu, Xinyuan Liu, Zhao Liu, Zhu Liu, Shuhan Lou, Chenxi Lu, Zhenyu Luo, Wenjun Meng, Hui Miao, Chao Ren, Marina Romanello, Wolfgang SchÃ¶pp, Jing Su, Xu Tang, Can Wang, Qiong Wang, Laura Warnecke, Sanmei Wen, Wilfried Winiwarter, Yang Xie, Bing Xu, Yu Yan, Xiu Yang, Fanghong Yao, Le Yu, Jiacan Yuan, Yiping Zeng, Jing Zhang, Lu Zhang, Rui Zhang, Shangchen Zhang, Shaohui Zhang, Qi Zhao, Dashan Zheng, Hao Zhou, Jingbo Zhou, Margaret Fu-Chun Chan Fung, Yong Luoâ , Peng Gongâ , 2022ï¼The 2022 China report of the Lancet Countdown on health and climate change: leveraging climate actions for healthy ageing. Lancet Public Health 2022, 7: e1073â90. https://doi.org/10.1016/S2468-2667(22)00224-9\n[6] Weixin JIN, Yong LUO, Tongwen WU, Xiaomeng HUANG, Wei XUE, Chaoqing YU, 2022: Deep Learning for Seasonal Precipitation Prediction over China. J. Meteor. Res., 36(2), 271-281, doi: 10.1007/s13351-022-1174-7\n[7] Shaw, R., Y. Luo, T.S. Cheong, S. Abdul Halim, S. Chaturvedi, M. Hashizume, G.E. Insarov, Y. Ishikawa, M. Jafari, A. Kitoh, J. Pulhin, C. Singh, K. Vasant, and Z. Zhang, 2022: Asia. In: Climate Change 2022: Impacts, Adaptation and Vulnerability. Contribution of Working Group II to the Sixth Assessment Report of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change [H.-O. PÃ¶rtner, D.C. Roberts, M. Tignor, E.S. Poloczanska, K. Mintenbeck, A. AlegrÃ­a, M. Craig, S. Langsdorf, S. LÃ¶schke, V. MÃ¶ller, A. Okem, B. Rama (eds.)]. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK and New York, NY, USA, pp. 1457â1579, doi:10.1017/9781009325844.012\n[8] Danyi Sun; Wenyu Huang; Yong Luo; Jingjia Luo; Jonathon S. Wright; Haohuan Fu; Bin Wang, 2022: A Deep LearningâBased Bias Correction Method for Predicting Ocean Surface Waves in the Northwest Pacific Ocean. Geophysical Research Letters, DOI: 10.1029/2022GL100916\n[9] Wei Cheng; Douglas G. MacMartin; Ben Kravitz; Daniele Visioni; Ewa M. Bednarz; Yangyang Xu; Yong Luo; Lei Huang; Yongyun Hu; Paul W. Staten et al., 2022: Changes in Hadley circulation and intertropical convergence zone under strategic stratospheric aerosol geoengineering. npj Climate and Atmospheric Science, DOI: 10.1038/s41612-022-00254-6\n[10] Shihui Zhang*, Chi Zhang*, Wenjia Cai*, Yuqi Bai, Max Callaghan, Nan Chang, Bin Chen, Huiqi Chen, Liangliang Cheng, Hancheng Dai, Xin Dai, Weicheng Fan, Xiaoyi Fang, Tong Gao, Yang Geng, Dabo Guan, Yixin Hu, Junyi Hua, Cunrui Huang, Hong Huang, Jianbin Huang, Xiaomeng Huang, John S Ji, Qiaolei Jiang, Xiaopeng Jiang, Gregor Kiesewetter, Tiantian Li, Lu Liang, Borong Lin, Hualiang Lin, Huan Liu, Qiyong Liu, Xiaobo Liu, Zhao Liu, Zhu Liu, Yufu Liu, Bo Lu, Chenxi Lu, Zhenyu Luo, Wei Ma, Zhifu Mi, Chao Ren, Marina Romanello, Jianxiang Shen, Jing Su, Yuze Sun, Xinlu Sun, Xu Tang, Maria Walawender, Can Wang, Qing Wang, Rui Wang, Laura Warnecke, Wangyu Wei, Sanmei Wen, Yang Xie, Hui Xiong, Bing Xu, Yu Yan, Xiu Yang, Fanghong Yao, Le Yu, Jiacan Yuan, Yiping Zeng, Jing Zhang, Lu Zhang, Rui Zhang, Shangchen Zhang, Shaohui Zhang, Mengzhen Zhao, Dashan Zheng, Hao Zhou, Jingbo Zhou, Ziqiao Zhou, Yong Luoâ , Peng Gongâ , 2023: The 2023 China report of the Lancet Countdown on health and climate change: taking stock for a thriving future, Lancet Public Health 2023, https://doi.org/10.1016/ S2468-2667(23)00245-1\n[11] Yuan, H.-H. et al. Evaluation of precipitation extremes over the Tibetan plateau using the NASA global daily downscaled datasets NEX-GDDP-CMIP6. Advances in Climate Change Research 14, 884â895, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.accre.2023.12.001 (2023).\n[12] Ziqi Ma, Jianbin Huang*, Xiangdong Zhang, Yong Luo, Minghu Ding, Jun Wen, Weixin Jin, Chen Qiao & Yifu Yin, 2023: Newly reconstructed Arctic surface air temperatures for 1979â2021 with deep learning method. Scientific Data, 10:140, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02059-5\n[13] Peidu Li, Yong Luoâ, Ze He, Junqing Zheng, Xin Xia, Zhouyi Liao, Xiaoqing Gao, 2023: A comparative study of the effects of photovoltaic power plants in desert and lake on the microclimate. Energy Reports, 10 (2023) 2128â2137\n[14] Junqing Zheng, Yong Luoâ , Rui Chang, Xiaoqing Gao. An observational study on the microclimate and soil thermal regimes under solar photovoltaic arrays, Solar Energy, Volume 266, 2023, 112159, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.solener.2023.112159.\n[15] Shu Fu; Wenyu Huang; Jingjia Luo; Zifan Yang; Haohuan Fu; Yong Luo; Bin Wang, 2023: Deep LearningâBased Sea Surface Roughness Parameterization Scheme Improves Sea Surface Wind Forecast. Geophysical Research Letters, DOI: 10.1029/2023GL106580\n[16] Jingwei Xu; Xiefei Zhi; Dmitry V. Sein; William Cabos; Yong Luo; Ling Zhang; Fu Dong; Klaus Fraedrich; Daniela Jacob, 2023: Predictability of Coastal Boundary Layer Jets in South China Using AtmosphereâOcean Coupling. Journal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres, DOI: 10.1029/2023JD039184\n[17] Lei Huang; Yong Luo; Tammo Steenhuis; Qiuhong Tang; Wei Cheng; Wen Shi; Xin Xia; Dingchi Zhao; Zhouyi Liao, 2023: An Improved SatelliteâBased Evapotranspiration Procedure for China. Earth and Space Science, DOI: 10.1029/2023EA002949\n[18] Danyi Sun; Wenyu Huang; Zifan Yang; Yong Luo; Jingjia Luo; Jonathon S. Wright; Haohuan Fu; Bin Wang, 2023: Deep Learning Improves GFS Wintertime Precipitation Forecast Over Southeastern China. Geophysical Research Letters, DOI: 10.1029/2023GL104406\n[19] Xin Zhang; Lihua Zhou; Xingying Zhang; Yong Luo; Lei Sun, 2023: A Case Study on the Impact of East Asian Summer Monsoon on Surface O3 in China. Atmosphere, DOI: 10.3390/atmos14050768\n[20] Yuan, H., Ning, L., Zhou, J. et al. HiCPC: A new 10-km CMIP6 downscaled daily climate projections over China. Scientific Data. 11, 1167 (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03982-x\n[21] Wenjia Cai*, Chi Zhang*, Shihui Zhang*, Yuqi Bai, Max Callaghan, Nan Chang, Bin Chen, Huiqi Chen, Liangliang Cheng, Hancheng Dai,Weicheng Fan, Dabo Guan, Yixin Hu, Yifan Hu, Junyi Hua, Cunrui Huang, Hong Huang, Jianbin Huang, Xiaomeng Huang, John S Ji, Qiaolei Jiang,Xiaopeng Jiang, Gregor Kiesewetter, Tiantian Li, Bo Li, Lu Liang, Borong Lin, Hualiang Lin, Huan Liu, Qiyong Liu, Zhao Liu, Zhu Liu, Yanxiang Liu,Shuhan Lou, Bo Lu, Chenxi Lu, Zhenyu Luo, Zhifu Mi, Yanqing Miao, Chao Ren, Marina Romanello, Jianxiang Shen, Jing Su, Rui Su, Yuze Sun,Xinlu Sun, Maria Walawender, Can Wang, Qing Wang, Qiong Wang, Laura Warnecke, Wangyu Wei, Xiaohui Wei, Sanmei Wen, Yang Xie, Hui Xiong,Bing Xu, Xiu Yang, Yuren Yang, Fanghong Yao, Le Yu, Wenhao Yu, Jiacan Yuan, Yiping Zeng, Jing Zhang, Rui Zhang, Shangchen Zhang,Shaohui Zhang, Mengzhen Zhao, Qi Zhao, Qiang Zhao, Dashan Zheng, Hao Zhou, Jingbo Zhou, Ziqiao Zhou, Yong Luoâ , Peng Gongâ , 2024ï¼The 2024 China report of the Lancet Countdown on healthand climate change: launching a new low-carbon, healthy journey. Lancet Public Health 2024 https://doi.org/10.1016/S2468-2667(24)00241-X\n[22] Shu Fu; Wenyu Huang; Jingjia Luo; Dongqing Liu; Danyi Sun; Haohuan Fu; Yong Luo; Bin Wang, 2024: Deep Learning Improves GFS Sea Surface Wind Field Forecast Accuracy in the Northwest Pacific Ocean. Journal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres, DOI: 10.1029/2024JD041188\n[23] Jiewei Zhou, Jianbin Huang*, Yao Yao, Yong Luo*, 2025: Dynamical downscaling projections of mean and extreme climate over the Tibetan Plateau under 2 SSP scenarios. Weather and Climate Extremes 47 (2025) 100747\nÂ©2021 Tsinghua University. All Rights Reserved  äº¬ICPå¤15006448å·  äº¬å¬ç½å®å¤ 110402430053 å·\nClick:\n| The Last Up