    "homepage_text": "Yuxuan Du\nhome\nPublication\nProject\nService\nPositions\nclose\nhome\nPublication\nEducation\nProject\nService\n☰\nYuxuan Du\nduyuxuan123[at]gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\n: I am currently an Assistant Professor in the College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU). I am also a team member of\nGenerative AI Lab (GRAIL)\nat NTU. Previously, I served as a Research Fellow at NTU and a Senior Researcher at JD Explore Academy, and also a member of\nDMT (Doctor Management Trainee)\nprogram in JD.com, Inc. I received my Ph.D. degree in the School of computer science, The University of Sydney, supervised by  Prof.\nDacheng Tao\n(IEEE Fellow) and co-supervised by Prof.\nMin-hsiu Hsieh\nand Prof.\nTongliang Liu\n. Prior to my doctoral studies, I studied Physics (national base-level physics class) at Sichuan University. Additionally, I undertook a visiting student program at SUNY Albany in 2013.\nMy work has been published in top‑tier journals and conferences across physics and computer science, including Nature Comms, PRL, PRX Quantum, npj Quantum Information, TIT, and T-PAMI. My research has been featured by major media outlets such as MIT Technology Review and Xinhua News Agency. I serve as an Editor of Neural Networks and have regularly held Area Chair roles for ICML, NeurIPS, and ICLR. I have also been recognized as a Top 2% Scientist Worldwide in the fields of AI and Physics, based on citation indicators published by Stanford University and Elsevier.\nResearch Interest\n: My research interests include quantum machine learning applications, quantum learning theory, and AI for quantum science.\nHiring\n:\nMultiple positions for Ph.D. (full scholarship and partial scholarship), Research Assistant, and Visiting Scholars at Nanyang Technological University are currently available\n. We seek students with a strong background in statistics, physics, and computer science to collaborate on research in quantum learning theory and quantum AI. Interested candidates are encouraged to contact me via email with detailed resumes. Refer to\nofficial website\nfor more details.\nNews\n[2026/01] The\nJST–A*STAR Quantum 2025\ngrant has been awarded. See\nOpen Positions\nfor postdoctoral researchers with expertise in Quantum+AI.\n[2026/01] Our paper \"\nAQER: A Scalable and Efficient Data Loader for Digital Quantum Computers\n\" was accepted to\nICLR 2026\n.\n[2026/01] We released our new paper \"\nEndowing Molecular Language with Geometry Perception via Modality Compensation for High-Throughput Quantum Hamiltonian Prediction\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2026/01] I accepted the invitation to serve as an Action Editor of\nNeural Networks\n[JCR: Q1; Impact Factor: 6.3]. Welcome to submit your manuscripts (AI for Quantum; AI by Quantum) to the journal!\nClick for more info before 2026 ⬇️\n[2025/12] Invited speaker of\nIW-QBM 2025\n.\n[2025/12] I accepted the invitation to join the Early Career Board of\nQuantum Artificial Intelligence\n.\n[2025/11] I accepted the invitation to serve as the Area Chair for\nICML 2026\n.\n[2025/11] We released our new paper \"\nSample-efficient quantum error mitigation via classical learning surrogates\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2025/10] Our book \"\nA Gentle Introduction to Quantum Machine Learning\n\"\n[PDF]\nhas been published on Springer Nature.\n[2025/09]\nThree papers\nwere accepted to The Thirty-Ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n2025. Two of them are advancing AI to reduce quantum resources in VQAs. Another one is AI for Quantum Science.\nPaper 1\nTITAN: A Trajectory-Informed Technique for Adaptive Parameter Freezing in Large-Scale VQE\n[PDF]\nPaper 2\nPALQO: Physics-informed model for Accelerating Large-scale Quantum Optimization\n[PDF]\nPaper 3\nAiDE-Q: Synthetic Labeled Datasets Can Enhance Learning Models for Quantum Property Estimation\n[PDF]\n[2025/09] We released our new survey \"\nArtificial intelligence for representing and characterizing quantum systems\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2025/08] Our paper \"\nEfficient learning for linear properties of bounded-gate quantum circuits\n\" was accepted to the 9th International Conference on Quantum Techinques in Machine Learning\n[QTML 2025]\nas a talk (37 / 264).\n[2025/08] I accepted the invitation to serve as the Area Chair for\nICLR 2026\n.\n[2025/08] Our paper \"\nRRInf: Efficient Influence Function Estimation via Ridge Regression for Large Language Models and Text-to-Image Diffusion Models\n\" was accepted to\nEMNLP 2025\n.\n[2025/07] We released our new paper \"\nDemonstration of Efficient Predictive Surrogates for Large-scale Quantum Processors\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2025/06] We released our new paper \"\nState Similarity in Modular Superconducting Quantum Processors with Classical Communications\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2025/06] I gave an invited talk \"Advancing Quantum Science in the Era of AI\" at 5th Young Academy of Sciences Summit (YASS), HONG KONG\n\"\n[Link]\n.\n[2025/05] Our paper \"\nRethink the Role of Deep Learning towards Large-scale Quantum Systems\n\" was accepted to ICML 2025\n[Link]\n.\n[2025/04] Our paper \"\nEfficient learning for linear properties of bounded-gate quantum circuits\n\" was accepted to Nature Communications\nNComms\n[Link]\n.\n[2025/04] I accepted the invitation to serve as the Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\n[2025/02] We released our new paper \"\nQuantum Machine Learning: A Hands-on Tutorial for Machine Learning Practitioners and Researchers\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2025/01] Our paper ``\nPractical Iterative Quantum Consensus Protocol with Sharding Construction\n'' was accepted to IEEE Journal on Selected Areas in Communications (JSAC) UCP-QuantumEra special issue\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/12] Our paper \"\nOptical quantum sensing for agnostic environments via deep learning\n\" was accepted to Physical Reviewe Research\n(PRR)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/10] Our paper \"\nOn exploring practical potentials of quantum auto-encoder with advantages\n\" was accepted to IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n(TNNLS)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/08] Our paper \"\nMG-Net: Learn to Customize QAOA with Circuit Depth Awareness\n\" was accepted to Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n2024\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/08] Our paper \"\nMultimodal Deep Representation Learning for Quantum Cross-platform Verification\n\" was accepted to Physical Review Letters\n(PRL)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/08] I accepted the invitation to serve as the Area Chair for\nICLR 2025\n.\n[2024/06] Our paper \"\nCoreset selection can accelerate quantum machine learning models with provable generalization\n\" was accepted to Physical Review Applied\n(PRApplied)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/06] We released our new paper \"\nQuantum Compiling with Reinforcement Learning on a Superconducting Processor\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2024/05] We released our new paper \"\nSeparable Power of Classical and Quantum Learning Protocols Through the Lens of No-Free-Lunch Theorem\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2024/04] I gave two invited talks at\n[PIERS2024]\nand UESTC.\n[2024/04] Our paper \"\nShuffle-QUDIO: accelerate distributed VQE with trainability enhancement and measurement reduction\n\" was accepted to Quantum Machine Intelligence\n(QMI)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/04] Our paper \"\nTransition role of entangled data in quantum machine learning\n\" was accepted to\nNature Communications\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/04] Our paper \"\nEfficient and practical quantum compiler towards multi-qubit systems with deep reinforcement learning\n\" was accepted to Quantum Science and Technology\n(QST)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/03] I gave an invited talk \"Multimodal Deep Representation Learning for Quantum Cross-platform Verification\" at Quantum Computer Systems Lecture Series, Notre Dame & MIT, US\n[Link]\n. The slides can be downloaded at\n[here]\n.\n[2024/01] Our paper \"\nA Time-Consistency Curriculum for Learning from Instance-Dependent Noisy Labels\n\" was accepted to Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(T-PAMI)\n[Link]\n.\n[2024/01] Our paper \"\nNeural Auto-designer for Enhanced Quantum Kernels\n\" was accepted to International Conference on Learning Representations 2024\n(ICLR 2024)\n[Link]\n.\n[2023/11] I gave an invited talk \"On the Theoretically Refined Quantum Machine Learning\" at Central South University.\n[2023/11] We released our new paper \"\nOptical Quantum Sensing for Agnostic Environments via Deep Learning\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2023/11] We released our new paper \"\nMultimodal deep representation learning for quantum cross-platform\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2023/10] I gave an invited talk \"Unveiling Quantum Deep Neural Networks: Problem-Dependent Performance Insights\" at 12th International Conference on Computing and Patter Recognition, Qingdao, China.\n[2023/10] I gave an invited talk \"Unveiling Quantum Neural Classifiers: Problem-Dependent Performance Insights\" at Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy Science.\n[2023/09] We released our new paper \"\nCoreset selection can accelerate quantum machine learning models with provable generalization\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2023/08] We released our new paper \"\nShadowNet for Data-Centric Quantum System Learning\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2023/08] Our paper \"\nDemystify Problem-Dependent Power of Quantum Neural Networks on Multi-Class Classification\n\"\n[PDF]\nwas accepted to Physical Review Letter\n(PRL)\n[Link]\n.\n[2023/08] Our two papers \"\nDemystify Problem-Dependent Power of Quantum Neural Networks on Multi-Class Classification\n\"\n[PDF]\nand \"\nTransition role of entangled data in quantum machine learning\n\"\n[PDF]\nwere accepted to the 7th International Conference on Quantum Techinques in Machine Learning\n(QTML)\n[Link]\n.\n[2023/08] I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer Editor for\nFronteir of Physics\nand a Meta-Reviewer for\nAJCAI 2023\n.\n[2023/06] We released our new paper \"\nTransition role of entangled data in quantum machine learning\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2023/04] Our survey \"\nRecent Advances for Quantum Neural Networks in Generative Learning\n\"\n[PDF]\nwas accepted by Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(T-PAMI)\n.\n[2023/04] Our paper \"\nWhich is Better for Learning with Noisy Labels: The Semi-supervised Method or Modeling Label Noise?\n\" was accepted by International Conference on Machine Learning 2023\n(ICML 2023)\n.\n[2023/03] I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nNeurips 2023\nand\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n.\n[2023/03] I gave an invited talk \"Demystify Problem-Dependent Power of Quantum Neural Networks on Multi-Class\" at Centre for Quantum Technologies, National University of Singapore.\n[2023/01] Our paper \"\nQAOA-in-QAOA: solving large-scale MaxCut problems on small quantum machines\n\"\n[PDF]\nwas accepted by PRApplied.\n[2023/01] Our paper \"\nSymmetric Pruning in Quantum Neural Networks\n\"\n[PDF]\nwas accepted by International Conference on Learning Representations 2023\n(ICLR 2023)\n(\nSpotlight\n).\n[2023/01] We released our new paper \"\nDemystify Problem-Dependent Power of Quantum Neural Networks on Multi-Class Classification\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/09] We released our new paper \"\nShuffle-QUDIO: accelerate distributed VQE with trainability enhancement and measurement reduction\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/09] Two papers are accpeted to NeurIPS 2022\n[Link1]\n&\n[Link2]\n.\n[2022/09] Our paper \"\nThe dilemma of quantum nerual networks\n\"\n[PDF]\nwas accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\n.\n[2022/08] We released our new paper \"\nSymmetric Pruning in Quantum Neural Networks\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/06] We released our new review arcticle \"\nRecent Advances for Quantum Neural Networks in Generative Learning\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/06] We released our new paper \"\nMSR: Making Self-supervised learning Robust to Aggressive Augmentations\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/05] I gave an invited talk \"Exploring Variational Quantum Algorithms via Statistical Learning Theory\" at Institute of Theoretical Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/05] We released our new paper \"\nQAOA-in-QAOA: solving large-scale MaxCut problems on small quantum machines\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/05] Our paper \"\nQuantum architecture search for variational quantum algorithms\n\" was accepted by\nNature Parter Journal Quantum Information (npj qi)\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/05] Our paper \"\nA distributed learning scheme for variational quantum algorithms\n\" was accepted by\nTransactions on Quantum Engineering\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/05] We released our new paper \"\nTheory of Quantum Generative Learning Models with Maximum Mean Discrepancy\n\"\n[PDF]\n[2022/04] We released our new paper \"\nEfficient and practical quantum compiler towards multi-qubit systems with deep reinforcement learning\n\"\n[PDF]\n[2022/04] I gave an invited talk \"Anchoring Variational Quantum Algorithms via Statistical Learning Theory\" at Tsinghua-BIMSA\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/04]  I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nNeurips 2022\n.\n[2022/03] We released our new paper \"\nUnentangled quantum reinforcement learning agents in the OpenAI Gym\n\"\n[PDF]\n[2022/03] I gave an invited talk \"Variational Quantum Computing & Learning Theory\" at Center on Frontiers of Computing Studies, Peking University\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/03]  Our paper \"\nQuantum differentially private sparse regression learning\n\" was accepted by\nTransactions on Information Theory (TIT)\n[Link]\n.\n[2022/03]  Our paper \"\nDyRep: Bootstrapping Training with Dynamic Re-parameterization\n\" was accepted by\nCVPR\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/02]  Our paper \"\nEfficient bipartite entanglement detection scheme with a quantum adversarial solver\n\" was accepted by\nPhysical Review Letter (PRL)\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/02]  Pennylane has collected our proposal of QuGAN\n[PDF]\ninto their\nDemos list\n.\n[2022/02]  I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nACMM 2022\n.\n[2022/02]  Our paper \"\nEfficient measure for the expressivity of variational quantum algorithms\n\" was accepted by\nPhysical Review Letter (PRL)\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/01] We released our new paper \"\nDo We Need to Penalize Variance of Losses for Learning with Label Noise?\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2022/01] We released our new paper \"\nQuantum circuit architecture search on a superconducting processor\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/12]  I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nICML 2022\n.\n[2021/12]  I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nIJCAI 2022\n.\n[2021/10]  Our paper \"\nOn the learnability of quantum neural networks\n\" was accepted by\nPRX Quantum\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/10]  Our paper \"\nTowards understanding the power of quantum kernels in the NISQ era\n\" was accepted by (Quantum Techniques in Machine Learning 2021) as a talk\n[Website]\n.\n[2021/08]  Our paper \"\nTowards understanding the power of quantum kernels in the NISQ era\n\" was accepted by Quantum\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/08]  Our paper \"\nExperimental quantum generative adversarial networks for image generation\n\" was accepted by PRApplied [\nEditor Suggestion\n]\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/07]  I accepted the invitation to serve as a Reviewer for\nICLR 2022\n.\n[2021/07] We organize a course \"Adanced topics of AI\" at School of Gifted Young, USTC.\n[2021/06] We released our new paper \"\nOn exploring practical potentials of quantum auto-encoder with advantages\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/06] We released our new paper \"\nAccelerating variational quantum algorithms with multiple quantum processors\n\"\n[PDF]\n.\n[2021/06] I gave an invited talk \"On exploring practical potentials of variational...[truncated]"
