    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Shaokun Zhang's Homepage\nShaokun Zhang\nResearch Engineer\nHuawei Device Co., Ltd.\nAddress: Dongguan, Guang Dong, China, 523795\nEmail: skzhang AT pku.edu.cn\nBRIEF BIOGRAPHY\nCurrently, Shaokun Zhang is a researcher at Huawei Device Co., Ltd. He received the Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from Operating System Lab, Peking University (PKU) in 2024, advised by Prof.\nDing Li\n, Prof.\nYao Guo\n, and Prof.\nXiangqun Chen\n. His research interests include mobile app testing, privacy protection, temporal data analysis, and deep learning. He has published many papers on well-known academic conferences and journals (such as ASE, CCS, HPCA, JOS, ISSRE, TITS, ESWA, etc.). He also served as a reviewer of WWW, ISSTA, CCS, TKDE, TMC, TITS, JCST, JOS, etc. He was awarded\nOutstanding Reviewer\nof WWW 2024.\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\nResearch Topics\nMobile App Analysis: Form Understanding, Cross-Platform Testing, Privacy Compliance.\nTraffic Bigdata Analysis: Multi-Variant, Mutli-Task, Large-Scale Traffic Forecasting.\nAI for Software Engineering\nIntelligent Transportation Systems\nResearch Goals\nGraph-based Cross-Platform App Analysis Systems\nEffective and Efficient Graph-based Traffic Intelligence\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nHuawei Device Co., Ltd., Dongguan, China\nSenior Engineer, Application Ecosystem Governance & Research Collaboration\n2024.03 – Present\nApplication Ecosystem Governance (UX, performance, stability, compatibility, etc.)\nDesigned and deployed deep reinforcement learning–based stability testing and record–replay automation for HarmonyOS apps, enabling\nlarge-scale scenario exploration\nand\nregression-free verification\nduring development.\nBuilt\ngovernance workflows\ncovering UX, performance, stability, compatibility, and privacy–security, significantly reducing post-release rework for third-party developers.\nDelivered\na unified testing pipeline\nintegrated into DevEco Studio, supporting early detection of functional and non-functional defects.\nCollaborated with framework, DevEco Studio, and device teams to ensure long-term maintainability and alignment with HarmonyOS evolution.\nUniversity Collaboration & Joint Research Programs\nServed as\na Huawei-side technical leader\nfor multiple academic collaborations, including joint programs with East China Normal University (ECNU) on automated testing and property-based verification.\nDefined\nresearch roadmaps\n,\ncoordinated funding\n, and\nensured alignment\nbetween industrial requirements and academic innovation.\nFacilitated\ntechnology transfer\nfrom research prototypes to production-ready components integrated into HarmonyOS developer toolchains.\nPROJECT EXPERIENCE\nHuawei–ECNU Joint Tech Program: “Property-Based Testing for HarmonyOS Apps”\nProject Leader (Huawei-side)\n2025.07 – Present | RMB 1.8M Horizontal Fund\nLed a\n12-member\ncross-organizational team (Huawei & ECNU) to deliver the\nfirst\nproperty-based testing framework integrated into DevEco Studio, the official IDE for HarmonyOS.\nDefined technical roadmap, budget plan, and\nfour\nkey milestones; introduced\nweekly agile reviews\nto align industrial requirements with academic innovations.\nBuilt an automated script-distribution engine and a DSL for functional-sequence definition, enabling\none-click rollout\nand on-the-fly updates of scenario-based tests; improved page-crawling efficiency and relevance by\n30%\nusing inline assertions to detect functional faults.\nCode accepted into\nDevEco Studio 6.1\n, now used by\n9k+\nthird-party HarmonyOS developers.\nOutcome triggered a follow-up Phase-II contract on automated UTG generation for distributed HarmonyOS applications.\nSELECTED PUBLICATIONS\n† Corresponding author.\n[软件学报'24]\n基于多模态表征的移动应用 GUI 模糊测试框架.\n(CCF-A)\n张少坤\n, 李元春, 雷瀚文, 蒋鹏, 李锭, 郭耀, 陈向群.\nIn\nJournal of Software (in Chinese)\n, July 2024.\n[TKDE'25]\nMTNet: A Multi-task Learning Framework that Integrates Intra-task and Task-specific Dependencies for Traffic Forecasting\n(数据挖掘领域顶级期刊, CCF-A, 中科院一区TOP, IF: 10.4)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Rui Wang, Hongjun Tang, Kaizhong Zuo, Peng Jiang, Peng Hu, Wenjie Li, Biao Jie, and Peize Zhao.\nIn\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering\n, November 2025.\n[ASE'23]\nHow Android Apps Break the Data Minimization Principle: An Empirical Study.\n(软件工程领域顶级会议, CCF-A, 口头报告, 接收率: 21%)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Hanwen Lei, Yuanpeng Wang, Ding Li, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen.\nIn\nIEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering\n, September 2023.\n[TITS'23]\nPFNet: Large-scale traffic forecasting with progressive spatio-temporal fusion.\n(智能交通领域顶级期刊, CAA-A+, 中科院一区TOP, IF: 9.55, 通讯作者)\nChen Wang, Kaizhong Zuo,\nShaokun Zhang†\n, Hanwen Lei, Peng Hu, Zhangyi Shen, Rui Wang, Peize Zhao\nIn\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n, July 2023.\n[TITS'21]\nA graph-based temporal attention framework for multi-sensor traffic flow forecasting.\n(智能交通领域顶级期刊, CAA-A+, 中科院一区TOP, IF: 9.55)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Yao Guo, Peize Zhao, Chuanpan Zheng, Xiangqun Chen.\nIn\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n, April 2021.\nOTHER PUBLICATIONS\n[HPCA'25]\nDPUaudit: DPU-assisted Pull-based Architecture for Near-Zero Cost System Auditing\n(体系结构领域顶级会议, CCF-A)\nPeng Jiang, Hanlin Jiang, Ruizhe Huang, Hanwen Lei, Zhineng Zhong,\nShaokun Zhang\n, Yuxin Ren, Ning Jia, Xinwei Hu, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen, Ding Li.\nIn\nThe International Symposium on High-Performance Computer Architecture (HPCA)\n, March 2025.\n[CCS'23]\nPut your memory in order: Efficient domain-based memory isolation for wasm applications.\n(安全领域顶级会议, CCF-A)\nHanwen Lei, Ziqi Zhang,\nShaokun Zhang\n, Peng Jiang, Zhineng Zhong, Ningyu He, Ding Li, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen\nIn Proceedings of\nthe 2023 ACM SIGSAC Conference on Computer and Communications Security\n, November. 2023.\n[ISSRE'23]\nReSPlay: Improving Cross-Platform Record-and-Replay with GUI Sequence Matching.\n(软件可靠性领域旗舰会议, CCF-B, 口头报告)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Linna Wu, Yuanchun Li, Ziqi Zhang, Hanwen Lei, Ding Li, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen.\nIn\nIEEE 34th International Symposium on Software Reliability Engineering\n, October 2023.\n[ISSRE'23]\nAPIMind: API-driven assessment of runtime description-to-permission fidelity in android apps.\n(软件可靠性领域旗舰会议, CCF-B, 口头报告)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Hanwen Lei, Yuanpeng Wang, Ding Li, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen.\nIn\nIEEE 34th International Symposium on Software Reliability Engineering\n, October 2023.\n[ISSRE'21]\nDependency-aware form understanding.\n(软件可靠性领域旗舰会议, CCF-B, 口头报告)\nShaokun Zhang\n, Yuanchun Li, Weixiang Yan, Yao Guo, Xiangqun Chen.\nIn\nIEEE 32nd International Symposium on Software Reliability Engineering\n, October 2021.\nINVITED TALKS\nThe OpenHarmony Technical Conference\n, Changsha, Sep 2025\nThe CCF ChinaSoft\n, Shanghai, Dec 2023\nThe 34th International Symposium on Software Reliability Engineering (ISSRE)\n, Florence, Oct 2023\nThe 38th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering (ASE)\n, Luxembourg, Sep 2023\nThe 32nd International Symposium on Software Reliability Engineering (ISSRE)\n, Wuhan, Oct 2021\nACADEMIC SERVICES\nConference Reviewer\nWWW 2024 (CCF-A)\n, Reviewer\nWWW 2023 (CCF-A)\n, External Reviewer\nCCS 2023 (CCF-A)\n, External Reviewer\nISSTA 2023 (CCF-A)\n, External Reviewer\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge Data Engineering (TKDE)\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing（TMC）\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems（TITS）\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology (JCST)\nJournal of Software (JOS)\nTEACHING EXPERIENCE\nTeaching Assistant, Operating System, Peking University (Fall 2021)\nTeaching Assistant, Operating System, Peking University (Spring 2021)\nTeaching Assistant, Operating System, Peking University (Fall 2020)\nTeaching Assistant, Operating System, Peking University (Spring 2020)\nTeaching Assistant, Operating System, Peking University (Fall 2019)\nSELECTED HONORS\nHuawei Individual Quality Star Award\n, 2025\nOutstanding Reviewer Award of WWW 2024\nMerit student, Peking University\n, 2021\nPKU Scholarship, Peking University\n, 2021\nMerit student, Xiamen University\n, 2018\nLast Updated: 2025-10"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Feiran Jia::https://feiran.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://feiran.io/",
