    "homepage_text": "Chi Wang\n      -  University of Kentucky\nUniversity of Kentucky Home\nLOGIN & Help\nLink opens in a new tab\nEnglish\nEspañol\nSearch content at University of Kentucky\nContact Expert\nView Scopus Profile\nChi Wang, Ph.D.\nProfessor\n,\nInternal Medicine\nJoint Appointment\n,\nDr. Bing Zhang Department of Statistics\nAssociate Director, Biostatistics and Bioinformatics SRF\n,\nMarkey Cancer Center / Cancer Research Priority Initiative\nMember\n,\nCenter for Computational Sciences\nMember\n,\nMarkey Cancer Center / Cancer Research Priority Initiative\nMember\n,\nMolecular and Cellular Oncology Research Program\n800 Rose Street\n40536\nLexington\nUnited States\nh-index\n5753\nCitations\n40\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1996                 …\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation/Academic qualification\nDoctor of Philosophy, Johns Hopkins University\n2009\nMaster of Science, Peking University\n2003\nBachelor of Science, Peking University\n2001\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chi Wang is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\nCancer Cell\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n100%\nMalignant Neoplasm\nPharmacology, Toxicology and Pharmaceutical Science\n40%\nCarcinogenesis\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n40%\nTumor Progression\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n38%\nProstate Cancer\nPharmacology, Toxicology and Pharmaceutical Science\n34%\nFeature Extraction\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n32%\nPolo-Like Kinase 1\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n27%\nFatty Acid Synthase\nBiochemistry, Genetics and Molecular Biology\n27%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration from the last 5 years on country level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots.\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects & Grants\n30\nActive\n126\nFinished\nFY26 Accelerate\nDurbin, E. B.\n(PI),\nJeong, J. C.\n(CoI) &\nWang, C.\n(CoI)\nKY Cabinet for Health and Family Services\n12/19/25\n→\n6/30/26\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nPediatrics\n100%\nAdolescence\n57%\nEnhancing TIL Efficacy in NSCLC through Epigenetic Reprogramming and Computational Modeling\nPlaugher, D.\n(PI),\nBrainson, C.\n(CoI),\nHao, Z.\n(CoI),\nLiu, J.\n(CoI),\nMessaoudi Powers, I.\n(CoI) &\nWang, C.\n(CoI)\nNational Cancer Institute\n7/14/25\n→\n6/30/27\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nNon Small Cell Lung Cancer\n100%\nTumor Infiltrating Lymphocyte\n100%\nMalignant Neoplasm\n100%\nTumor-Infiltrating Lymphocytes\n100%\nReprogramming\n100%\nCCSG Pilot: Uncovering Signaling Pathways Driving High Melanoma Mortality in Rural Kentucky\nPlattner, R.\n(PI),\nArays, R.\n(CoI),\nHuang, B.\n(CoI),\nRichards, D.\n(CoI),\nStapleton, J.\n(CoI) &\nWang, C.\n(CoI)\nNational Cancer Institute\n7/1/25\n→\n6/30/26\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nMelanoma\n100%\nSignal Transduction\n100%\nNerve Cell Adhesion Molecule\n38%\nSide Effect\n15%\nTargeted Therapy\n15%\nCCSG Pilot: Targeting p53/ERK1/2/DKK1 Axis for Overcoming Acquired Resistance to Chemotherapy in CRC\nWang, Q.\n(PI) &\nWang, C.\n(CoI)\nNational Cancer Institute\n7/1/25\n→\n6/30/26\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nTumor Microenvironment\n100%\nMitogen Activated Protein Kinase 3\n100%\nCancer Associated Fibroblast\n100%\nProtein P53\n100%\nChemo