    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Professor Yi Ma\nUniversity of California,\nBerkeley\nDepartment of Electrical\nEngineering and Computer Sciences\nProfessor Yi\n\t  Ma\nElectrical Engineering and Computer Sciences\nUniversity of\n\t  California, Berkeley\nOffice:\nEECS\n\t  Department, 333C Cory Hall # 1770\nUniversity of California, Berkeley, CA 94720-1770, USA.\nEmail:\nyima@eecs.berkeley.edu\nPhone:\n+1 (510)\n\t  664 4565\nTwitter:\n@YiMaTweets\nOther\n\t  Affiliations\nInstitute of Data\nScience (IDS), the University of Hong Kong\nSchool of Computing and\n\t  Data Science (CDS), the University of Hong Kong\nBerkeley\n\t  Artificial Intelligence Research (BAIR)\nBerkeley Center\n\t  for Augmented Cognition (CRC)\nBerkeley FHL Vive\n\t  Center for Enhanced Reality\nTsinghua-Berkeley\n\t  Shenzhen Institute (TBSI)\nTeaching\nResearch\nPublications\nPresentations\nStudents\nServices\nBiography\nHonors\nCV.pdf\nAppointments:\nI have officially moved to the University of Hong\n\t  Kong, and currently hold the positions:\nVisiting Professor of the EECS Department, UC\n\t    Berkeley, since January 2025.\nChair Professor in AI,\nthe School of Computing and\n\t  Data Science (CDS), the University of Hong Kong,\nsince July 1, 2023.\nDirector of\nthe School of Computing and\n\t  Data Science (CDS), the University of Hong Kong,\nsince\n\t  July 1, 2024.\nDirector of\nthe Institute of Data\n\t  Science (IDS), the\n\t    University of Hong Kong,\nsince January 1,\n\t  2023.\nNew Events:\nA New Open Source Book:\nPrinciples and\n\t  Practice of Deep Representation Learning\n,\n\t    version 2.0, March 1, 2026.\nAn Interview,\non\nYoutube Video\n, by the blogger Machine Learning Street Talk\n (MLST) about our new book.\nShort Course for the\nMathematical Foundations & Methodologies for Artificial Intelligence\nat the Institute for Mathematical Sciences (IMS), National University\nof Singapore (NUS), August 17-21, 2026.\nColloquium Lecture in the Department of Mathematics at\n National University of Singapore, August 16-17, 2026.\nKeynote at a Workshop, ICML, the COEX Convention &\n Exhibition Center, Seoul, South Korea, July 10-11, 2026.\nShort Course on \"Learning Deep Low-dimensional Models from High-Dimensional Data\", The European Summer School on Artificial Intelligence, Vienna, Austria, 6-10 July 2026.\nAttending CVPR, Denver, Colorado, June 3-7, 2026.\nGeneral Chair of International Conference on Parsimony and\n\t    Learning (CPAL), Tubingen, Germany, March 2026.\nSir Run Run Shaw Distinguished Visiting\n\t    Scholar Lecture, Chinese University of Hong Kong, February 13.\nSir Run Run Shaw Distinguished Visiting\n Scholar High-Table Dinner, Chinese University of Hong Kong, February 11.\nRecent Releases:\nProject Website\n:\nGAUSS: General Assessment of Underlying Structured Skills in Mathematics.\nRecorded video of\nPursuing the\n  Nature of Intelligence\n(with\nSlides)\n, Invited Talk at Purdue University, \n  August 1, 2025.\nRecorded video of\nPursuing the\n  Nature of Intelligence\n(with\nSlides)\n, Columbia University, \n  May 1, 2025.\nProject Website\n:\nSimDINO: Simplying\n\t  DINO via Coding Rate Regularization.\nProject Website\n:\nToken Statistics\n  Transformer: Linear-Time Attention.\nProject Website\n:\nFrom\n\t  Simple to Complex Skills: The Case of In-Hand Object\n\t  Reorientation.\nProject Website\n:\nSclaing White-Box Transformers\n  for Vision.\nProject Website\n:\nWhite-Box Transformers\n  via Sparse Rate Reduction\n.\nA New International Conference:\nConference on Parsimony and\n\t  Learning (CPAL)\n(Stanford, March 24-28, 2025).\nA New Textbook\n:\nHigh-Dimensional Data\nAnalysis with Low-Dimensional Models\n(or\na mirror site\n\t  for download \n\t    in China\n).\nA New Position Paper:\nOn the Principles of Parsimony and Self-Consistency for the Emergence of Intelligence\n.\nA New Course EECS208:\nComputational\n\t  Principles for High-Dimensional Data Analysis\n(with a\nCourse Website\nand\nLecture Slides\n).\n©2017 Yi Ma\nLast modified: Wed Mar  4 21:03:38 HKT 2026"
  },
