      "cheng@nottingham.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yuan Cheng, University of Nottingham Ningbo China\nYuan Cheng\nAssistant Professor\nShort Bio\nYuan is an assistant professor in the\nSchool of Computer Science\nat the\nUniversity of Nottingham Ningbo China\n.\r\n\t\t\t\tPreviously, he was an associate professor in the\nCollege of Computing\nat\nGrand Valley State University\nand a faculty member in the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nCalifornia State University, Sacramento\n, where he earned tenure and was promoted to associate professor in 2022.\r\n\t\t\t\tBefore his tenure at Sac State, he worked as a postdoctoral researcher at the\nInstitute for Cyber Security (ICS)\nat the\nUniversity of Texas at San Antonio (UTSA)\n, San Antonio, Texas.\r\n\t\t\t\tHe received his Ph.D. from the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat UTSA, under the guidance of\nDr. Ravi Sandhu\nand\nDr. Jaehong Park\n.\r\n\t\t\t\tHe also holds a B.Eng. degree in Information Security from the\nSchool of Computer Science & Technology\nat\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\n, Wuhan, China.\r\n\t\t\t\tRaised in Ningbo, Zhejiang, his native tongue is the Chinese dialect of Wu.\nSchool of Computer Science\nUniversity of Nottingham Ningbo China\nRoom 442, Sir Peter Mansfield Building\n199 Taikang East Road, Ningbo, China 315100\nyuan DOT cheng AT nottingham DOT edu DOT cn\nyuan AT ycheng DOT org\nPh.D., University of Texas at San Antonio, 2014\nOffice Hours\nM 3 pm - 5 pm (PMB442) or by appointment\nResearch Interests\nAccess Control\nAuthentication\nInternet of Things\nPrivacy\nSocial Computing\nTeaching\nAutumn 2025:\nCOMP3048 Compilers\nSpring 2026:\nCOMP1039 Programming Paradigms\nNews\n2/27/2026: Our paper \"A Comparative Analysis of Third-Party Script Behaviour in Consent-Based and Implicit Web Tracking\" with Chongwen has been accepted to\nACM CODASPY 2026\n. Congratulations, Chongwen!\n10/28/2025: I will serve on the TPC of\nACM CODASPY 2026\n.\n4/20/2025: Our paper \"A Zero Trust Module for Cybersecurity Education\" with Xinli and Vijay has been published in 2025 Journal of The Colloquium for Information Systems Security Education.\n4/14/2025: I will serve on the TPC of\nESORICS 2025\n.\n4/1/2025: I returned to my hometown and joined the University of Nottingham Ningbo China as an Assistant Professor.\nMap"
  },
