    "homepage_text": "Pu Hua\nPu\nHua\nI am a first year Ph.D. student in Artificial Intelligence at\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences (IIIS), Tsinghua University\nunder the supervision of Prof.\nHuazhe Xu\n. I’m also an intern at\nShanghai Qi Zhi Institute\n.\nMy research topic lies in the interdisciplinary topics of\nreinforcement learning\n, and\nrobotics\n. My dream is to\nempower robots with the capacity to act in open-world environments\n.\nI am currently working on leveraging the power of LLM and generative models to boost the performance and generalization ability of robots.\nnews\nJan 23, 2025\nOne paper\nStem-OB\nis accepted by ICLR 2025 as a\nspotlight\npaper!\nSep 06, 2024\nOne paper\nGenSim2\nis accepted by CoRL 2024!\nJan 16, 2024\nOne paper\nDrM\nis accepted by ICLR 2024 as a\nspotlight\npaper!\nSep 22, 2023\nOne paper\nRL-ViGen\nis accepted by NeurIPS 2023, Track for Datasets and Benchmarks!\nJan 23, 2023\nOne paper\nEAR\nis accepted by ICLR 2023!\nselected publications\nCoRL 2024\nGenSim2: Scaling Robot Data Generation with Multi-modal and Reasoning LLMs\nPu Hua\n,  Minghuan Liu ,  Annabella Macaluso ,  Yunfeng Lin ,  Weinan Zhang ,  Huazhe Xu ,  and  Lirui Wang\nIn 8th Annual Conference on Robot Learning\n, Sep 2024\narXiv\nCode\nWebsite\nICLR 2023\nSimple Emergent Action Representations from Multi-Task Policy Training\nPu Hua\n,  Yubei Chen ,  and  Huazhe Xu\nIn The Eleventh International Conference on Learning Representations\n, Jan 2023\narXiv\nCode\nWebsite\nYou can even add a little note about which of these is the best way to reach you.\n\n---\n\nCV | Pu Hua\nCV\nBasics\nName\nPu Hua\nLabel\nUndergraduate Student\nEmail\nhuapu0429@gmail.com\nUrl\nhttps://piao-0429.github.io/\nSummary\nA researcher in the field of reinforcement learning and robotics.\nEducation\n2024.09 - 2029.06\nBeijing, China\nPhD\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China\nArtificial Intelligence\n2020.09 - 2024.06\nBeijing, China\nBachelor\nDepartment of Electronic Engineering, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China\nElectronic Engineering\nSkills\nArticial Intelligence\nMachine Learning\nDeep Learning\nReinforcement Learning\nRobotics\nLanguages\nChinese\nNative speaker\nEnglish\nFluent"
  },
