    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Joey Tianyi Zhou\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nI am the Deputy Director, Principal Scientist II, and Investigator with the\nA*STAR Centre for Frontier AI Research (CFAR)\n, Singapore. In CFAR, I am leading ZHOU Group focusing on fundamental AI research. Concurrently, I am holding a joint appointment as the Principal Scientist in the\nCentre for Advanced Technologies in Online Safety (CATOS)\n.\nIn CATOS, I lead the \"attack team\" focused on generating Deepfake and AIGC Videos to fool human users and machine detectors (Please see some demos\nhere\n). I am also an adjunct faculty member at the\nNational University of Singapore (NUS)\n.\nI obtained my Ph.D. from Nanyang Technological University (NTU), SG, in 2015. I was a senior research engineer at Sony US Research Center, San Jose, USA.\nMy research focus is on how to enhance AI Efficiency and Robustness from a data perspective. An ideal machine learning model shall : (1) be resource-efficient for both inference and training, including computational-efficient and data-efficient; (2)be safe to various perturbations, distribution shifts, and adversarial attacks.\nA*STAR Email\n/\nNUS Email\n/\nPeople\n/\nNUS Teaching\n/\nGithub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nZHOU\n(Towards\nZ\nero-carbon,\nH\nigh-reliability,\nO\npen-environment,\nU\nnbiased AI) Research Group in CFAR\nScientists:\nYang He\n,\nJiawei Du\n,\nXin Zhang\nEngineers:\nHeng Zhao\nPh.D students:\nHeng Zhao (USTC, BSc; NTU, MSc; 2021 Intake), Yinjie Zhao (NTU, BENG; ACIS scholarship, 2023 Intake), Cheng Shen (UCI, BSc; NYU, MSc; SINGA scholarship, 2023 Intake), Zhiya Tan (SCUT, BA, 2024 Intake)\nInterns and Visiting Scholars:~30 students/scholars\nI am always actively seeking talented individuals interested in  machine learning. The following scholarships will be funded by A*STAR and your Ph.D. degree can be obtained from any Singapore university (e.g., NUS, NTU, SMU, STUD).\n\tIf you want to visit me during your studies, you may apply for a joint Ph.D. scholarship ARAP, or CFAR internship scheme CIARE, ARIA. I can host the visiting students (e.g., CSC program from China) at NUS or A*STAR CFAR. Please feel free to reach out to me.\nPhD Scholarships:\nSINGA\n,\nARAP\n,\nACIS\n,\nAISG\n. I will offer additional allowance on top of any scholarship you have.\nMaster and undergraduate Scholarships:\nSIPGA\nInterns:\nCIARE\n,\nARIA\n.\nNew!\nCall for  interns (available now):  I always seek talented students to join my team. Ph.D. scholarships or official research positions will be prioritized for excellent performers.\nNew!\nCall for research associates/fellows (available now): I need to hire research associates/fellows in NLP/ML/CV/ domains.  Strong coding and problem-solving skills are preferable.\nResearch\nResource-efficient AI\nCondenseLM: LLMs-driven Text Dataset Condensation via Reward\nMatching\nCheng Shen, Yew-Soon Ong,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn EMNLP 2025\nBreaking Class Barriers: Efficient Dataset Distillation via Inter-Class Feature Compensator\nXin Zhang, Jiawei Du,  Ping Liu,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn ICLR 2025\nDiversity-Driven Synthesis: Enhancing Dataset Distillation through Directed Weight Adjustment\nJiawei Du, Xin Zhang, Juncheng Hu, Wenxin Huang,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn NeurIPS 2024 (Spotlight Paper)\nEvolution-aware VAriance (EVA) Coreset Selection for Medical Image Classification\nYuxin Hong, Xiao Zhang, Xin Zhang,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn ACM MM 2024 (Best Paper Nomination)\nSpanning Training Progress: Temporal Dual-Depth Scoring (TDDS) for Enhanced Dataset Pruning\nXin Zhang, Jiawei Du, Weiying Xie, Yunsong Li,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn CVPR 2024\nMultisize Dataset Condensation\nYang He, Lingao Xiao,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\n, Ivor Tsang\nIn ICLR 2024 (Oral, 1.2%)\nYou Only Condense Once: Two Rules for Pruning Condensed Datasets\nYang He, Lingao Xiao,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn NeurIPS 2023\nSequential Subset Matching for Dataset Distillation\nJiawei Du, Qin Shi,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn NeurIPS 2023\nSharpness-aware training for free\nJiawei Du, Daquan Zhou, Jiashi Feng, Vincent Y. F. Tan,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n,\nIn NeurIPS 2022\nEDCompress: Energy-Aware Model Compression for Dataflows\nZhehui Wang, Tao Luo, Rick Siow Mong Goh, and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems 2022\nDual Adversarial Neural Transfer for Sequence Labeling\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Hao Zhang, Di Jin, Xi Peng\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2021\nMulti-source Meta Transfer for Low Resource Multiple Choice Question Answering\nMing Yan, Hao Zhang, Di Jin and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn ACL 2020\nA Deep Learning Framework for Hybrid Heterogeneous Transfer Learning\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Sinno Jialin Pan, Ivor W. Tsang.\nIn Artificial Intelligence 2019\nMulti-class Heterogeneous Domain Adaptation\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Ivor W. Tsang, Sinno Jialin Pan and Mingkui Tan\nIn Journal of Machine Learning Research 2019\nSafe and Reliable AI\nEstimating LLM Uncertainty with Evidence\nHuan Ma, Jingdong Chen,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Guangyu Wang, Changqing Zhang\narxiv\nIdentifying and Mitigating Social Bias Knowledge in Language Models\nRuizhe Chen, Yichen Li, Jianfei Yang, Yang Feng,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Jian Wu, Zuozhu Liu,\nIn NAACL 2025\nShortcuts Arising from Contrast: Towards Effective and Lightweight Clean-Label Attacks in Prompt-Based Learning\nXiaopeng Xie, Ming Yan, Xiwen Zhou, Chenlong Zhao, Suli Wang, Yong Zhang, and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn EMNLP 2024\nMeta Knowledge Condensation for Federated Learning\nPing Liu, Xin Yu, and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nIn ICLR 2023\nTrusted Multi-View Classification with Dynamic Evidential Fusion\nZongbo Han, Changqing Zhang, Huazhu Fu and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2022\nXAI Beyond Classiﬁcation: Interpretable Neural Clustering\nXi Peng, Yunfan Li, Ivor Tsang, Hongyuan Zhu, Jiancheng Lv, and\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn  Journal of Machine Learning Research  2022\nPointBA: Towards Backdoor Attacks in 3D Point Cloud\nXinke Li, Zhiru Chen, Yue Zhao, Zekun Tong, Yabang Zhao, Andrew Lim,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn ICCV 2021\nTrusted Multi-View Classification\nZongbo Han, Changqing Zhang, Huazhu Fu,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn ICLR 2021\nTrustworthy Multimodal Regression with Mixture of Normal-inverse Gamma Distributions\nHuan Ma, Zongbo Han, Changqing Zhang, Huazhu Fu,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nand Qinghua Hu\nIn NeurIPS 2021\nIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language Attack on Text Classification and Entailment\nDi Jin, Zhijing Jin,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Peter Szolovits\nIn AAAI 2020\nQuery-efficient Meta Attack to Deep Neural Networks\nJiawei Du, Hu Zhang,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\n, Yi Yang, Jiashi Feng\nIn ICLR 2020\nLarge Foundation Model Framework\nRethinking Agent Design: From Top-Down Workflows to Bottom-Up Skill Evolution\nJiawei Du, Jinlong Wu, Chen Yuzheng, Yucheng Hu, Bing Li,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nArxiv\nAgent Trading Arena: A Study on Numerical Understanding in LLM-Based Agents\nTianmi Ma, Jiawei Du, Wenxin Huang, Wenjie Wang, Liang Xie, Xian Zhong,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nThe 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP), 2025.\nSTADe:\nSensory Temporal Action Detection via Temporal-Spectral Representation Learning\nBing Li, Haotian Duan, Yun Liu, Le Zhang, Wei Cui,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2025\nKPL: Training-Free Medical Knowledge Mining of Vision-Language Models\nJiaxiang Liu, Tianxiang Hu, Jiawei Du, Ruiyuan Zhang,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Zuozhu Liu\nIn EMNLP 2024\nWord2Pix: Word to Pixel Cross-Attention Transformer in Visual Grounding\nHeng Zhao,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\n, Yew-Soon Ong,\nIn IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems 2024\nDifformer: Multi-resolutional differencing transformer with dynamic ranging for time series analysis\nBing Li, Wei Cui, Le Zhang, Ce Zhu, Wei Wang, Ivor W Tsang,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2023\nLocality-Aware Crowd Counting\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Le Zhang, Du Jiawei, Xi Peng, Zhiwen Fang, Zhe Xiao, Hongyuan Zhu\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2021\nNatural Language Video Localization: A Revisit in Span-based Question Answering Framework\nHao Zhang, Aixin Sun, Wei Jing, Liangli Zhen,\nJoey Tianyi Zhou*\nand Rick Siow Mong Goh\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence 2020\nAnomalyNet: An Anomaly Detection Network for Video Surveillance\nJoey Tianyi Zhou\n, Jiawei Du, Hongyuan Zhu, Xi Peng, Yong Liu, Rick Siow Mong Goh\nIn IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics & Security 2019\nAcademic Service\nAssociate Editor/Editorial Board:\n2025-present\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n2024-present\nArtificial Intelligence Journal(AIJ)\n2022-present\nIEEE Transactions on Emerging Topics in Computational Intelligence (TETCI)\n2020-2023\nIET Image Processing\n2019-2023\nIEEE Access\nSenior/Area Chair:\n2024,2025\nNeurIPS\n2023,2024,2025\nICLR\n2023,2024,2025\nICML\n2025\nKDD\n2024\nIJCAI\n2021\nICME\nProgramme Chair/Organising Committee:\nTechnical Programme Chair\nInternational Joint Conference on Neural Networks (IJCNN 2027)\nAssociate Programme Chair\nthe 34th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2025)\nIndustry Programme Chair\nInternational Joint Conference on Neural Networks (IJCNN 2025)\nWorkshop Chair\nThe 2024 IEEE Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IEEE CAI 2024)\n2020-present\nInternational Workshop on Efficient Artificial Intelligence For Edge Computing (EAI) at ICDCS\nProposal Expert Panel:\nExpert Panel in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Academic Research Fund.\nMembership:\nIEEE Senior Member\nINNS Member, AICI Section Technical Coordinator\nEAI Distinguished Member\nAwards\n2025 World Artificial Intelligence Conference: Youth Outstanding Paper Award Nomination\n2025 World's Top 2% Scientists （Career Lifetime）\n2024 ACM MM Best Paper Nomination\n2022 IEEE SmartCity Best Paper\n2020 National Research Foundation Fellow (NRF-F) Finalist\n2019 IEEE Innovation Spotlight Paper\n2019 ICCV Hands Challenge: Runner-up Prize\n2019 BOOM workshop on IJCAI: Best Paper Award\n2017 NeurIPS Best Reviewer\n2016 BeyondLabeler workshop on IJCAI: Best Paper Award\n2016 ECCV Best Student Paper Nomination\nCompetitive Funding Award\nDigital Trust Centre Innovation Grant (No:DTC-IGC-02)：\nReassemble Data Before Sharing: Innovative Privacy-Preserved Data-Sharing Solutions for Cloud Services\n, PI, Jul. 15 2025 - Jul. 14 2026\nRIE2025 Singapore-Japan Joint Grant (No:R24I6IR133):\nBreaking Multimodal Correspondence: Crafting Safer and Fairer Multimodal AIGC\n, PI, Apr. 1 2025 - 31 Mar. 2028\nAISG 2024 Research Grant (No. AISG3-RP-2024-033):\nSequential Deepfake Attribution,\nPI, 06 Jan. 2025- 05 Jan. 2028\nNational Multimodal LLM Programme (No. AISG-NMLP-2024-003):\nPrivacy^2: Fine-Tuning Encapsulated LLMs to Downstream Tasks Without Peeking on Private Data,\nCo-PI, 01 Apr. 2025- 31 Mar. 2028\nA*STAR Central Research Funding:\nTiny Machine Learning,\nPI, 2020-2026\n(imitation is the sincerest form of flattery)"
