    "homepage_text": "Haobo Fu @ Tencent\nSearch\nHaobo Fu (傅浩波)\nTech Lead, Principal Research Scientist\nTencent AI\nHaobo Fu is a tech lead and a principal researcher at Tencent AI Platform Department, Shenzhen, China. His main interests are new innovations in Artificial Intelligence (AI) for the game industry. These include\ninnovative game AI applications\nand related research&engineering topics, such as\nLLM/Game Agents\n,\nReinforcement Learning\n,\nImitation Learning\n,\nAI Infrastructure\n, etc. He got his PhD in computer science from\nUniversity of Birmingham\nin 2014, supervised by Prof.\nXin Yao\nand Prof.\nBernhard Sendhoff\n. His PhD program was fully funded by\nHonda Research Institute Europe\n. He was offered the Australian Government 2015 Endeavour Research Fellowship.\nNews\nI will be attending the 2025\nconference\non multiagent applications in China at Chengdu, China, 2025.12.20, giving a speech titled \"Policy Diversity in Game AI\".\nSix papers\nsubmitted\nto CVPR 2026\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto AAAI 2026 (Oral)\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto NeurIPS 2025\nTwo papers\nsubmitted\nto ICLR 2026\nI have accepted the invitation to be an\nArea Chair\nfor ICLR 2026.\nI have accepted the invitation to be an\nArea Chair\nfor ICML 2026.\nI have accepted the invitation to be an\nArea Chair\nfor NeurIPS 2025.\nTwo papers got\naccepted\nto ICML 2025\nOne paper\nsubmitted\nto TPAMI\nTwo papers got\naccepted\nto ICLR 2025\nI have accepted the invitation to be an\nArea Chair\nfor ICML 2025.\nOne paper\naccepted\nto AAAI 2025\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto Artificial Intelligence Journal\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto Transactions on Evolutionary Computation\nTwo papers got\naccepted\nto NeurIPS 2024\nI have accepted the invitation to be an\nArea Chair\nfor NeurIPS 2024.\nThree papers got\naccepted\nto ICLR 2024, with two spotlights.\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto AAAI 2024\nWe proposed\na robust and opponent-aware league training method\nthat achieved superhuman performance on StarCraft II using much less computation than AlphaStar.\nAccepted\nto NeurIPS 2023 as a spotlight.\nThree papers got\naccpted\nto NeurIPS 2023\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto CoRL 2023\nOn 30th May 2023, our Mahjong AI\nLuckyJ\nreached 10 dan at\nTenhou.net\n. It is by far\nthe only Mahjong AI\nthat reached 10 dan from scratch using under 1500 matches. Also, its stable rank (10.68 dan)\nsurpasses all human and AIs\nwho played more than 1000 games in the expert room at Tenhou.net.\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto ICML 2023\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto IJCAI 2023\nTwo papers got\naccepted\nto ICLR 2023\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto AAMAS 2023\nI was in the\nprogram committee\nof\nthe IJCAI 2022 Mahjong AI Competition\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto CoG 2022\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto ICML 2022\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto AAAI 2022\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto ICLR 2022\nOne paper got\naccepted\nto IJCAI 2021\nI lead a team that won the\nchampion\nof\nthe IJCAI 2020 Mahjong AI Competition\nI was in the\nGoverning Board\nof\nLinux Foundation AI&Data\nduring 2020-2021\n...\nExperience\nTech Lead, Principal Researcher\nTencent AI Platform Department, Tencent\nApril 2016 –\n                \n                  Present\nShenzhen, China\nSenior Researcher\nBig Data Lab, Baidu\nOctober 2014 –\n                \n                  March 2016\nBeijing, China\nResearch Fellow\nSchool of Computer Science, University of Birmingham\nJune 2014 –\n                \n                  September 2014\nBirmingham, United Kingdom\nFeatured Publications\nEqual contributors are\nmarked\n.\n[\nAAAI-2026\n]\nDeep (Predictive) Discounted Counterfactual Regret Minimization\nH Xu, K Li,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nNeurIPS-2025\n]\nLearning Preferences without Interaction for Cooperative AI\nH Ma, H Yu,\nH Fu\n, S Li\n[\nICML-2025\n]\nMCU：An Evaluation Framework for Open-Ended Game Agents\nX Zheng, H Lin, K He, Z Wang, Q Fu,\nH Fu\n, Z Zheng, Y Liang\n[\nICML-2025\n]\nGoal-Oriented Skill Abstraction for Offline Multi-Task Reinforcement Learning\nJ He, K Li, Y Zang,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nICLR-2025\n]\nOnline-to-Offline RL for Agent Alignment\nX Liu,\nH Fu\n, S Albrecht, Q Fu, S Li\n[\nICLR-2025\n]\nDiverse Policies Recovering via Pointwise Mutual Information Weighted Imitation Learning\nH Yang, J Yao, W Liu, Q Wang, H Qin, H Kong, K Tang, J Xiong, C Yu, K Li, J Xing, H Chen, J Zhuo, Q FU, W Yang,\nH Fu\n[\nNeurIPS-2024\n]\nEfficient Multi-task Reinforcement Learning with Cross-Task Policy Guidance\nJ He, K Li, Y Zang,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nNeurIPS-2024\n]\nOpponent Modeling with In-context Search\nY Jing, B Liu, K Li, Y Zang,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nICLR-2024\n]\nTowards Offline Opponent Modeling with In-context Learning\nY Jing, K Li, B Liu, Y Zang,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nICLR-2024\n]\nDynamic Discounted Counterfactual Regret Minimization\nH Xu, K Li,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nICLR-2024\n]\nMaximum Entropy Heterogeneous-Agent Reinforcement Learning\nJ Liu, Y Zhong, S Hu,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, X Chang, Y Yang\n[\nNeurIPS-2023\n]\nPolicy space diversity for non-transitive games\nJ Yao, W Liu,\nH Fu\n, Y Yang, S McAleer, Q Fu, W Yang\n[\nNeurIPS-2023\n]\nAutomatic grouping for efficient cooperative multi-agent reinforcement learning\nY Zang, J He, K Li,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing, J Cheng\n[\nNeurIPS-2023\n]\nA robust and opponent-aware league training method for starcraft ii\nR Huang, X Wu, H Yu, Z Fan,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, W Yang\n[\nICML-2023\n]\nOpponent-Limited Online Search for Imperfect Information Games\nW Liu,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, W Yang\n[\nICLR-2023\n]\nCurriculum-based Co-design of Morphology and Control of Voxel-based Soft Robots\nY Wang, S Wu,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, T Zhang, Y Chang, X Wang\n[\nICLR-2023\n]\nQuality-Similar Diversity via Population Based Reinforcement Learning\nS Wu, J Yao,\nH Fu\n, Y Tian, C Qian, Y Yang, Q Fu, Y Wei\n[\nICML-2022\n]\nGreedy when Sure and Conservative when Uncertain about the Opponents\nH Fu\n, Y Tian\n, H Yu, W Liu, S Wu, J Xiong, Y Wen, K Li, J Xing, Q Fu, W Yang\n[\nAAAI-2022\n]\nAutoCFR\n:\nLearning to Design Counterfactual Regret Minimization Algorithms\nH Xu, K Li,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, J Xing\n[\nICLR-2022\n]\nActor-critic policy optimization in a large-scale imperfect-information game\nH Fu\n, W Liu\n, S Wu, Y Wang, T Yang, K Li, J Xing, B Li, B Ma, Q Fu, W Yang\n[\nIJCAI-2021\n]\nCombining Tree Search and Action Prediction for State-of-the-Art Performance in DouDiZhu\nY Zhang, D Yan, B Shi,\nH Fu\n, Q Fu, H Su, J Zhu, N Chen\n[\nTEVC-2014\n]\nRobust optimization over time\n:\nProblem difficulties and benchmark problems\nH Fu\n, B Sendhoff, K Tang, X Yao\nAcademic Collaborators\nShuai Li\n, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China\nStefano Albrecht\n, University of Edinburgh, UK\nStephen McAleer\n, Carnegie Mellon University, USA\nChao Qian\n, Nanjing University, China\nYaodong Yang\n, Peking University, China\nYing Wen\n, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, China\nJunliang Xing\n, Tsinghua University, China\nKai Li\n, Chinese Academy of Sciences, China\n...\nContact\nAny form of discussion and collaboration are warmly welcomed!\nhaobofu@tencent.com\nShen Zhen, Guang Dong, China"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Ye Tian::https://yet123.com/": {
    "homepage": "https://yet123.com/",
    "all_emails": [
      "ye.tian@yale.edu",
      "ye.t@columbia.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/ytstat",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ye-tian-195761181/?locale=en_US",
    "homepage_text": "Ye Tian (田野) – Homepage\nYe Tian (田野)\nPortrait photo taken in front of Bailey Hall at Cornell with\nYongxin Shang\nand friends during our engagement celebration.\nEmail:\nUniform({ye.t@columbia.edu, ye.tian@yale.edu})\nAddress:\n300 George St, Suite 503, New Haven, CT 06511\nI am currently a Postdoc Researcher in Department of Biostatistics, Yale University, working with Prof. Hongyu Zhao in\nZhao Lab\n. I got my PhD in Statistics from\nColumbia University\nand was honored to be advised by Prof.\nYang Feng\nand Prof.\nZhiliang Ying\n. I was born in Huainan, which is a small city of China famous for its long history and the delicious tofu there. Prior to Columbia, I obtained my Bachelor’s degree in Statistics in 2019 from\nSchool of the Gifted Young (SGY)\nat\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\nand was honored to be supervised by Professor\nWeiping Zhang\n. I also spent a wonderful summer at Amazon as an applied scientist intern in 2023.\nMy research lies at the intersection of statistics and machine learning, with the goal of developing more reliable machine learning (ML) systems and understanding their underlying mechanisms. Specifically, my research focuses on a few key areas:\n(1) Reliable transfer learning and related development in genetics;\n(2) Imbalanced classification error control for minority groups;\n(3) High-dimensional statistics and general ML.\nBesides research, I love photography, running, traveling, and reading (especially Sci-Fi and history books). I also do some daily strength training.\nMy Google Scholar page\nNews\n2025-07-04: My paper “\nLearning from similar linear representations: Adaptivity, minimaxity, and robustness\n” with Yuqi and Yang has been accepted to JMLR.\n2025-03-28: I am delighted to announce that I will begin a one-year postdoc in the Department of Biostatistics at Yale University starting from August 2025, working with Professor\nHongyu Zhao\n. In August 2026, I will join the\nDepartment of Statistics, Penn State University\nas an Assistant Professor. I am deeply grateful to everyone who provided help, support, and encouragement during my job search!\n2025-01-29: I am excited to be one of the six winners of\n2025 SLDS Student Paper Awards\n! I will present my work (with Yuqi Gu and Yang Feng) at JSM 2025.\n2024-08-15: I will give a talk at\n2024 Workshop in Operations Research and Data Science (WORDS)\nhosted by the Fuqua School of Business at Duke University.\n2024-08-14: I am honored to receive the SIAM Student Travel Award to attend 2024 SIAM Conference on Mathematics of Data Science.\nSome representative works\nLearning from Similar Linear Representations: Adaptivity, Minimaxity, and Robustness\nTian, Y\n., Gu, Y., & Feng, Y.\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (2025).\n[PDF]\nNeyman-Pearson Multi-class Classification via Cost-sensitive Learning\nTian, Y.\n, & Feng, Y.\nJournal of the American Statistical Association (2025)\n[PDF]\nTowards the Theory of Unsupervised Federated Learning: Non-asymptotic Analysis of Federated EM Algorithms\nTian, Y.\n, Weng, H., & Feng, Y.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (2024).\n[PDF]\nTransfer Learning under High-dimensional Generalized Linear Models\nTian, Y.,\n& Feng, Y. (2023).\nJournal of the American Statistical Association (2023).\n[PDF]\nHonors\n2025/01: SLDS Student Paper Award\n2024/08: SIAM Student Travel Award\n2023/10: Howard Levene Outstanding Teaching Award (Department of Statistics, Columbia University)\n2023/06: NESS Student Research Award (The 36th New England Statistics Symposium, Boston)\n2023/04: IMS Hannan Graduate Student Travel Award\n2022/12: Student Paper Award (IMS International Conference on Statistics and Data Science, Florence, Italy)\n2022/11: Columbia ASGC Graduate Student Travel Award (The Arts and Sciences Graduate Council, Columbia University)\n2022/10: Columbia GSAS Student Conference Travel Award (Graduate School of Arts and Sciences, Columbia University)\nService\nReviewer\nJournal:\nAnnals of Statistics (3)\nAnnals of Applied Statistics (5)\nBernoulli (2)\nBiometrics (6)\nBiometrika (2)\nBioinformatics (2)\nComputational Statistics and Data Analysis (2)\nDementia and Geriatric Cognitive Disorders (1)\nElectronic Journal of Statistics (3)\nJournal of Business and Economic Statistics (4)\nJournal of Computational and Graphical Statistics (1)\nJournal of Econometrics (3)\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (5)\nJournal of the American Statistical Association (15)\nJournal of the Royal Statistical Society (Series B) (7)\nNeural Networks (2)\nNeurocomputing (1)\nScientific Reports (1)\nStat (4)\nStatistics and Computing (3)\nStatistics in Medicine (1)\nStatistical Papers (2)\nStatistica Sinica (7)\nTechnometrics (2)\nConference:\nAISTATS 2024 (6)\nFODS 2020 (3)\nICLR 2023 (1)\nConference session/Seminar organizers\n2024/08: Chair of the session “Applications in Statistical Learning and Data Science” at JSM 2024\n2023/08: Chair of the session “Statistical Learning Theory” at JSM 2023\n2021/08-2022/05: Columbia Statistics Student Seminar co-organizer (with Arnab Auddy)\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nYe Tian (田野)\nSign me up\nAlready have a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nYe Tian (田野)\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nSign up\nLog in\nReport this content\nView site in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nCollapse this bar\n\n---\n\nCV – Ye Tian (田野)\nYe Tian (田野)\nMy CV\nCV-Ye-Tian\nDownload\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nYe Tian (田野)\nSign me up\nAlready have a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nYe Tian (田野)\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nSign up\nLog in\nCopy shortlink\nReport this content\nView post in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nCollapse this bar\n\n---\n\nCV – Ye Tian (田野)\nYe Tian (田野)\nMy CV\nCV-Ye-Tian\nDownload\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nYe Tian (田野)\nSign me up\nAlready have a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nYe Tian (田野)\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nSign up\nLog in\nCopy shortlink\nReport this content\nView post in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nCollapse this bar"
