    "homepage_text": "Chao Qian\nChao Qian (é± è¶)\nææï¼åå¯¼ï¼é¢é¿å©ç\nProfessor\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\nNanjing University\nOffice: Room A502, International College Area, Xianlin Campus\nAddress:163 Xianlin Avenue, Nanjing, Jiangsu, China, 210023\nEmail: qianc at nju dot edu dot cn\nShort Biography\nI received my B.Sc. and Ph.D. degrees in the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nfrom\nNanjing University\nin 2009 and 2015, respectively, under the supervision of Prof.\nZhi-Hua Zhou\n. After finishing my PhD, I became an associate researcher in the\nSchool of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n, until 2019, when I returned to Nanjing University as an associate professor in the\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\n. In 2024, I became a full professor. I visited the University of the Basque Country (Spain) and the University of Birmingham (UK).  I am also a member of\nLAMDA Group\n.\n[Research Interest]\n[Recent News]\n[Publications]\n[Awards]\n[Students]\n[Professional Activities]\n[Teaching]\n[Short Bio]\n[ä¸­æç®å]\nResearch Interest\nMy research interests include artificial intelligence, evolutionary computation and machine learning. Now I am working on\nTheoretical analysis of evolutionary algorithms\nDesigning safe evolutionary algorithms, i.e., evolutionary algorithms with provable approximation guarantee\nDesigning efficient black-box optimization algorithms, e.g., Bayesian optimization, evolutionary strategies, quality-diversity, evolutionary gradient optimization, and cooperative coevolution algorithms\nLearning to optimize, e.g., learning to configure, generate and select black-box optimzition algorithms, offline optimization, and neural combinatorial optimization\nEvolutionary learning, particularly evolutionary reinforcement learning, deep learning, and ensemble learning\nApplications to solve complex real-world optimziation problems in industry (e.g., electronic design automation) and science (e.g., geoscience)\nRecent News\nI gave a keynote talk \"Evolutionary Learning: From Theory to Practice\" [\nSlides\n] [\nä¸­æç\n] at the 16th Spanish Congress on Metaheuristics, Evolutionary and Bioinspired Algorithms (\nMAEB 2025\n)\nI have been invited to be a Program Co-Chair of the 22nd Pacific Rim International Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nPRICAI 2025\n)\nI  have been invited to be an Editorial Board member of\nArtificial Intelligence\nI  have been invited to be an Editorial Board member of\nEvolutionary Computation\nI  have been invited to be an Associate Editor of\nIEEE Transactions on Evolutionary Computation\nI  have been invited to be an Associate Editor of\nIEEE Computational Intelligence Magazine\nI have been invited to give an Early Career Spotlight Talk \"Towards Theoretically Grounded Evolutionary Learning\" at\nIJCAI 2022\nI gave an invited talk \"Why Do We Need Theoretical Research of Evolutionary Algorithms?\" at ECOLE 2023 [\nSlides\n]\nI gave a tutorial \"Pareto Optimization for Subset Selection: Theories and Practical Algorithms\" at\nACM GECCO 2025\nand\nIEEE CEC 2025\nI was invited to attend the Dagstuhl Seminar \"Theory of Randomized Optimization Heuristics\"\nOur works on chip placement have won\n21st Annual Humies (Human Competitive Results) Bronze Awards\n(presented at\nACM GECCO 2024\n, Melbourne, Australia), and a Best Paper Award of\nDATE 2025\n(Lyon, France)\nOur AI4Science work \"\nReducing the Uncertainty in Estimating Soil Microbial-derived Carbon Storage\n\" has published at\nProceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS)\n, which was selected as one of the top ten scientific and technological advancements in China's ecological environment in 2024 (\nå¥é2024å¹´åº¦ä¸­å½çæç¯å¢åå¤§ç§æè¿å±\nï¼\nOur works on offline black-box optimization were reported by\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China\n(ææè¢«å½å®¶èªç¶ç§å­¦åºéå§æ¥é)\nPublications\nBook\nZhi-Hua Zhou, Yang Yu, and\nChao Qian\n.\nEvolutionary Learning: Advances in Theories and Algorithms\n. Singapore: Springer, 2019. (ISBN 978-981-13-5955-2)\nå¨å¿å, ä¿æ¬,\né±è¶\nè. æ¼åå­¦ä¹ : çè®ºä¸ç®æ³è¿å±, åäº¬: äººæ°é®çµåºçç¤¾, 2021. (ISBN 978-7-115-55803-9)\nJournal Article\n(* indicates that I am the corresponding author)\nZhengbo Lu, Ke Xue, Yiying Deng, Junxuan Fan, Peiyue Fang, Bridget S. Wade, Laia Alegret, Michael J. Benton, Yuchang Wu,\nChao Qian*\n, Xudong Hou, Yukun Shi, Peter M. Sadler, Huiqing Xu, Zhi-Hua Zhou, and Shuzhong Shen. Complex Marine Ecological Response during the Eocene-Oligocene Revealed by Global Foraminiferal Record. (\nAI for Science\n)\nNature Communications\n, 2026, in press.\nZhengbo Lu, Junxuan Fan, Bridget S. Wade, Paul N. Pearson, Yukun Shi,\nChao Qian\n, Ke Xue, Jiao Yang, Yujie Shi, and Muchen Lai. Graph-Optimized Graphic Correlation: An Automated Framework for Combining Stratigraphical Data. (\nAI for Science\n)\nLethaia\n, 2026, 60(1): 1-16. [\nPDF\n]\nHan Hu, Ke Xue, Yishen Sun, Qing Zhu, Hans K. Carlson, Ruiwen Hu, Rong-Xi Tan,\nChao Qian*\n, Weigen Huang, Jizhong Zhou, Jingdong Mao, Thomas W. Crowther, Zhi-Hua Zhou, Jiabao Zhang, and Yuting Liang. Reducing the Discrepancy in Quantifying the Temperature Dependence of Global Wetland Methane Emission. (\nAI for Science\n)\nGlobal Change Biology\n, 2026, 32(2): e70748. [\nPDF\n]\nRen-Jian Wang, Ke Xue, Yutong Wang, Peng Yang, Haobo Fu, Qiang Fu, and\nChao Qian*\n. Diversity from Human Feedback.\nFrontiers of Computer Science\n, 2026, 20(2): 2002320. [\nPDF\n](\ncode\n)\n(A preliminary version has appeared at the\n2nd Agent Learning in Open-Endedness Workshop at NeurIPS'23\n)\nChao Bian, Yawen Zhou, Miqing Li, and\nChao Qian*\n. Stochastic Population Update Can Provably Be Helpful in Multi-Objective Evolutionary Algorithms.\nArtificial Intelligence\n, 2025, 341: 104308. [\nPDF\n]\nKe Xue, Yutong Wang, Cong Guan, Lei Yuan, Haobo Fu, Qiang Fu,\nChao Qian*\