    "homepage_text": "Kun Lei\nKun Lei\nRL learner for Robotics\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nTwitter\n/\nZhihu\n/\nBlogs\n/\n微信\nI am a Ph.D. student in the joint program between\nShanghai Qizhi institute (Tsinghua)\nand\nShanghai Jiaotong University\n, advised by Prof.\nHuazhe Xu\nat\nTsinghua University\n. \n            Prior to this, I worked as a research assistant at\nShanghai Qizhi institute\n, where I am fortunate to work with Prof.\nHuazhe Xu\nat\nTsinghua University\n. I also did my research internship for four months at Westlake University. Previously, I graduated from\nSouthwest Jiaotong University\n, where I fortunately worked with Prof.\nPeng Guo\nat\nSWJTU\nand Prof.\nYi Wang\nat\nAuburn University\n.\nRL-100\nUni-O4\nResearch interest\nI am interested in research on the\nsample efficiency\nand\nadaptation\ncapabilities  of deep reinforcement learning algorithms and agents.\n            My research objective is to create reliable, robust, and efficient algorithms to tackle a diverse range of sequential decision-making problems in real-world scenarios.\nI am currently focused on the post-training of robotics (foundation) models to enhance specific objectives such as task acceleration, precision, adaptation, and/with safety considerations.\nPreviously, I conducted research on neural solvers for combinatorial optimization problems, i.e., in the field of AI for Operations Research. These neural agents have the potential to solve NP-hard problems with linear time complexity, see\nZhihu\n.\nNews\n2026.01.14\nOne paper accepted to ICRA 2026!\n2026.01.14\nI gave an invited talk at\nRLChina\n- [\nPDF\n/\nVideo\n]\n2025.12.4\nI gave an invited talk at\nRoboPapers\n- [\nPDF\n/\nVideo\n]\n2025.12.3\nI gave an invited talk at\nRobot Perception and Learning Lab\nin UT Austin\n2025.12.1\nI gave an invited talk at\nByteDance Seed\n2025.11.28\nI gave an invited talk at\nMicrosoft Research Asia (MSRA)\n2025.11.13\nI gave an invited talk at\nOpenDriveLab\nin The University of Hong Kong (HKU)\n2025.10.31\nI gave an invited talk at\nNational University of Singapore\n2025.10.30\nI gave an invited talk at\nTsinghua University\n2025.09\nI enrolled in the joint CS PhD program between Shanghai Qizhi institute and Shanghai Jiao Tong University\n2024.08-10\nI enrolled in the CS PhD program at the\nWUSTL\nand then quitted for RL-100 research\nShow more\n🚀 RL-100: Performant Robotic Manipulation with Real-World Reinforcement Learning\nA comprehensive talk by Kun Lei on achieving near-perfect manipulation performance through a three-stage framework: imitation learning → iterative offline RL → last-mile online RL.\npic.twitter.com/example\n— RoboPapers (@RoboPapers)\nDecember 4, 2025\nBlogs\n2025.11\nClassification for RL algorithms\nA Practical Way to Classify RL: by Data Source and by Update Schedule.\nTwitter\n/\nCoverd by AI科技评论\n2025.10\nBeyond Human Capability: The Robotic Era\nA three-stage framework from imitation to iterative offline and last-mile online RL that achieves near-perfect success with high efficiency and robustness.\nTwitter\nPublications and preprints (Offline & online RL algorithms and robotics)\nPapers sorted by recency, * indicates equal contribution, † indicates project lead.\nFailure-Aware RL: Reliable Offline-to-Online Reinforcement Learning with Self-Recovery for Real-World Manipulation\nHuanyu Li* ,\nKun Lei*\n, Sheng Zang, Kaizhe Hu, Yongyuan Liang, Bo An, Xiaoli Li, Huazhe Xu\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\n, 2026\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\narXiv\n/\nPaper\n/\nbib\nRL-100: Performant Robotic Manipulation with Real-World Reinforcement Learning\nKun Lei*†\n, Huanyu Li*, Dongjie Yu*, Zhenyu Wei*, Lingxiao Guo, Zhennan Jiang, Ziyu Wang, Shiyu Liang, Huazhe Xu.\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\ntwitter\n/\nblog\n/\n知乎\n/\nbib\n/\ntalk 1\n/\ntalk 2\nUni-O4: Unifying Online and Offline Deep Reinforcement Learning with Multi-Step On-Policy Optimization\nKun Lei\n, Zhengmao He*, Chenhao Lu*, Kaizhe Hu, Yang Gao, Huazhe Xu.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2024\nwith a nice rating 6688\n/\nproject page\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\ntwitter\n/\nbib\nBehavior proximal policy optimization\nZifeng Zhuang*,\nKun Lei*\n, Jinxin Liu, Donglin Wang, Yilang Guo.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2023\npaper\n/\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\nbib\nLearning Visual Quadrupedal Loco-Manipulation from Demonstrations\nZhengmao He,\nKun Lei\n, Yanjie Ze, Koushil Sreenath, Zhongyu Li, Huazhe Xu.\nIEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (\nIROS\n)\n, 2024\nproj page\n/\narXiv\n/\nbib\nPublications and preprints (RL for Operations Research)\nPapers sorted by recency.\nA Multi-action Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for Flexible Job-shop Scheduling Problem. (\nThis work has been got 300+ citations and featured as ESI Highly Cited Paper\n)\nKun Lei\n, Peng Guo, Wenchao Zhao, Yi Wang, Linmao Qian, Xiangyin Meng.\nExpert Systems with Applications (\nESWA\n, IF: 7.5)\n, 2022\npaper\n/\ncode\n/ covered by\n运筹OR帷幄\n、\n智能制造与智能调度\n、\nPaperWeekly\nLarge-scale Dynamic Scheduling for Flexible Job-shop with Random New Job Arrival by Hierarchical RL. (\nThis work has been featured as ESI Highly Cited Paper and Hot Paper\n)\nKun Lei\n, Peng Guo, Yi Wang, Jian Zhang, Xiangyin Meng, Linmao Qian.\nIEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics (\nTII\n, IF: 11.7)\n, 2023\npaper\nSolve routing problems with a residual edge-graph attention neural network.\nKun Lei\n,  Peng Guo, Yi Wang, Xiao Wu, Wenchao Zhao.\nNeurocomputing\n, IF: 5.5\n, 2022\npaper\n/\ncode\n/ covered by\n运筹OR帷幄\n、\nPaperWeekly\nMisc. open-source projects\nUni-O4\n⭐ 40\nPublic code release for \"Uni-O4\", Feb 2024\ncode\nBehavior proximal policy optimization\n⭐ 77\nPublic code release for \"BPPO\", Feb 2023\ncode\nEnd-to-end-DRL-for-FJSP.\n⭐ 265\nPublic code release for \"A Multi-action Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for Flexible Job-shop Scheduling Problem\", Sep 2022\ncode\nDRL-and-graph-neural-network-for-routing-problems.\n⭐ 198\nPublic code release for \"Solve routing problems with a residual edge-graph attention neural network\" June 2022\ncode\nDispatching-rules-for-FJSP.\n⭐ 81\nCoed for dispatching rules for flexible job-shop scheduling problems\", Sep 2022\ncode\nFJSP-benchmarks.\n⭐ 45\nThe public benchmark instances of flexible job shop scheduling problem, Feb 2022\ncode\nMIP-model-for-FJSP-and-solved-by-Gurobi.\n⭐ 45\nCoed for solving MIP model using Gurobi\", Feb 2022\ncode\nI am from Si Chuan, China. My name in chinese is 雷坤. I used to live in the charming cities of Chengdu and Hangzhou in China. Currently, I live in the vibrant city of Shanghai (as depicted in the background picture).\n© 2023 Kun Lei. Tamplate from\nNicklas Hansen\n."
  },
