    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Kevin Li\nKevin Li\nWelcome\nMy name is Kevin Li (李文亮, publish as Li K. Wenliang), \n     I am a Research Scientist at Google DeepMind and an Honorary Fellow at University College London at Wellcome Centre for Human Neuroimaging.\n     I obtained my PhD at\nGatsby Computational Neuroscience Unit\n, University College London, \n     supervised by\nManeesh Sahani\nand\nPeter Dayan\n. \n     I spent my undergraduate at University of Cambridge, supervised by\nMáté Lengyel\nfor my Master's thesis.\nMy research interest span machine learning and theoretical neuroscience, both are important for me to understanding intelligence. \n     I hope to explore and propose unsupervised and reinforcement learning algorithms, understand the learned representation by agents, and take inpsirations from biological solutions. \n     The ultimate goal is to understand principles of intelligence in artificial and biological agents.\nYou are welcome to check out my\nCV\n(\n简历\n).\nBlog Posts\nJun 9, 2020\nAmortised learning for generic generative models\nNov 23, 2018\nLearning deep kernels for exponential family distributions\nMar 18, 2018\nRepresentation of distributions in the brain\nSep 22, 2016\nThis is my first webpage"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Qi Meng::https://business.cornell.edu/faculty-research/faculty/mq56/": {
    "homepage": "https://business.cornell.edu/faculty-research/faculty/mq56/",
    "all_emails": [
      "mq56@cornell.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Meng Qi's faculty page for the Cornell SC Johnson\nSkip to main content\nActivate Search Form\nActivate Menu and Search Form\nClose Search Form\nMeng Qi\nAssistant Professor\nDownload Vita\nFaculty Area\nOperations, Technology, and Information Management\nFaculty Expertise\nOperations Management\nMachine Learning\nSupply Chain Management\nData Analytics\nHospitality and Services Design, Management and Operations\nSustainability\nContact\nCornell Peter and Stephanie Nolan School of Hotel Administration\nmq56@cornell.edu\nCornell Directory Entry\nBiography\nMeng Qi is an assistant professor of operations, technology, and information management at the Cornell SC Johnson College of Business. Her research interest is mainly about data-driven decision-making with uncertainty in operations management. Her research provides both methodologies and practical solutions combining tools and concepts from optimization, machine learning, and statistics. From an applications perspective, her research investigates practical problems in supply chain management and retail operations.\nSelected Publications\nQi, Meng; Grigas, Paul; Shen, Zuo-Jun. \"\nIntegrated Conditional Estimation-Optimization\n\"\nOperations Research\n. (forthcoming).\nQi, Meng; Shi, Yuanyuan; Qi, Yongzhi; Ma, Chenxin; Yuan, Rong; et al. \"\nA Practical End-to-End Inventory Management Model with Deep Learning\n\"\nManagement Science\n. 69.2 (2023): 759-773\nQi, Meng; Cao, Ying; Shen, Zuo-Jun. \"\nDistributionally Robust Conditional Quantile Prediction with Fixed Design\n\"\nManagement Science\n. 68.3 (2022): 1639-1658\nRecent Courses\nHADM 2011 - Hospitality Quantitative Analysis\nAcademic Degrees\nPhD University Of California, Berkeley, 2022\nBS Tsinghua University, 2016\nOpen Sidebar Menu"
  },
