    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Yi Xu\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHomepage of Yi Xu\nHomepage of Yi Xu\nYi Xu (徐一)\n[Github]\n[Google Scholar]\n[\nCV\n][\nLinkedIn\n][\n知乎\n]\nEmail:\nxu.yi@northeastern.edu\n, heiyixu@gmail.com\nWeChat:\n578138534\nResearch Summary:\nI am a Research Scientist working on autonomous driving intelligence. My long-term goal is to advance autonomous driving from modular pipelines toward unified, foundation-model-driven systems that are robust, adaptable, and deployable in safety-critical environments.\nI am open to research collaborations in autonomous driving, VLM, and VLA that advance next-generation intelligent systems.\nOur team at the Bosch Center for Artificial Intelligence has multiple summer internship openings for research on VLA+AD and related topics\n. Feel free to reach out!\nNews\n[Top]\nPaper list of\ntrajectory/motion prediction\n.\nW\nelcome to\nS\ntar and\nC\nontribute!\n[\nGithub\n][\n知乎\n]\n[Top]\nWe release\nd an LLM-based trajectory prediction survey on\narXiv\nwith a\nGitHub Repo\n!\n[Top]\nWe released an Awesome-Spatial-VLMs survey on\ntechrxiv\nwith a\nGitHub Repo\n!\n02/2026: We have\none\npaper accepted by\nCVPR 202\n6\n.\n02/2026: I joined the\nBosch Center for Artificial Intelligence\nas a Research Scientist to research vision-language-action models for autonomous driving systems.\n02/2026: We have\none\npaper on\nimproving robustness and reliability in VLMs\naccepted by\nI\nCLR\n202\n6\n.\n12/2025: I successfully defended my PhD thesis!\n10/2025: We have one extension paper on unified trajectory imputation and prediction accepted by\nTPAMI\n.\n08/2025: We have two papers on time-series representation learning & trajectory modeling accepted by\nICDM 2025\n, and we also have one paper on end-to-end autonomous driving + VLM accepted by\nCoRL 2025\n.\n01/2025: We have one paper on unified trajectory generation accepted by\nICLR 2025\n, datasets, codes, and models are\npublic\n.\n02/2024: We have two papers accepted by\nCVPR 2024\n.\n09/2023: We have one paper on adaptive optimizer design accepted by\nICDM 2023\n, and one paper on graph structure learning accepted by\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n07/2023: We have one paper on layout prediction accepted by\nACM MM 2023\n.\n05/2023: Start my summer internship at\nHonda Research Institute\n, San Jose, CA\n.\n03/2023: Give a guest lecture, \"Approach for Prediction in Autonomous Driving\", at Northeastern University, EECE 5642 Data Visualization.\n02/2023: We have two papers on trajectory imputation & prediction and future action localization accepted by\nCVPR 2023\n.\n09/2022: We have one paper on video recognition accepted by\nNeurIPS 2022\n.\n08/2022: We have one paper on video anomaly detection accepted by\nICDM 2022\n.\n07/2022: We have one paper on unsupervised anomaly detection accepted by\nCIKM 2022\n.\n05/2022: Start my summer internship at\nHonda Research Institute\n, San Jose, CA\n.\n04/2022: We have one paper on cross-domain few-shot learning accepted by\nIJCAI 2022\n.\n03/2022: We have one paper on adaptive pedestrian trajectory prediction accepted by\nCVPR 2022\n.\n09/2021: We have one paper on pedestrian trajectory prediction with active learning accepted by\nICONIP 2021\n.\n01/2021: We have one paper on pedestrian trajectory prediction accepted by\nRA-L\n/\nICRA 2021\nand one paper on vehicle\ntrajectory prediction\naccepted by\nACM Trans Intel Syst Tec\n.\n09/2020: Join\nSMILE Lab\nas a Ph.D. student at\nNortheastern University\n, Boston, MA.\n06/2020: Join\nAutonomous Delivery Center\nas a summer research intern at\nMeituan\n, Beijing, China.\n11/2019:\nWe have one\npaper on\npedestrian trajectory prediction\naccepted by\nAAAI 2020\n.\nEducation\nNortheastern University, Boston, USA\n(2020-2025)\nPh.D., Electrical & Computer Engineering, Supervisor:\nProf.\nYun Raymond Fu\n,\nThesis: Advancing Autonomous Driving: From Modular to End-to-End.\n[\nThesis PDF\n]\nXi’an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, China\n(2017-2020)\nM.Eng.,\nControl Science and Engineering\n,\nSupervisor:\nProf.\nJing Yang\n,\nThesis: Pedestrian Trajectory Prediction in Complex Scenes.\nXi’an Jiaotong University, Xi'an, China\n(20\n13\n-20\n17\n)\nB\n.Eng.,\nAutomation\n,\nThesis: Hardware-Friendly Compression Algorithm for CNNs.\nResearch Interests\nComputer Vision\nAutonomous Driving\nB\nehavior/\nA\nction\nPr\nediction\nVision-Language Models\nVision-Language-Action Models\nReal Interests\nBasketball\nPre-Prints\nYi Xu\n, Ruining Yang, Yitian Zhang, Yizhou Wang, Jianglin Lu, Mingyuan Zhang, Lili Su, Yun Fu, \"Trajectory Prediction Meets Large Language Models: A Survey.\"\n[\narXiv\n]\nDisheng Liu, Tuo Liang, Zhe Hu, Jierui Peng, Yiren Lu,\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, Yu Yin, \"Spatial Intelligence in Vision-Language Models: A Comprehensive Survey. \"\n[\ntechrxiv\n][\nGitHub\n]\nPublications\nRuining Yang,\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, Lili Su, ''Den-TP: Density-Balanced Data Curation and Evaluation Framework for Trajectory Prediction, ''\nCVPR 2026\n. []\nYiyang Huang, Liang Shi, Yitian Zhang,\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, ''SHIELD: Suppressing Hallucinations In LVLM Encoders via Bias and Vulnerability Defense,''\nICLR 2026\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nCode\n]\n.\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, \"\nGaussian Mixture Conditional Variational Recurrent Neural Network for Unified Trajectory Imputation and Prediction,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\n.\nYi Xu\n, Yitian Zhang, Yun Fu, \"MTS-DMAE: Dual-Masked Autoencoder for Unsupervised Multivariate Time Series Representation Learning,\"\nICDM 2025\n.\n[arXiv]\n.\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, \"AdaSports-Traj: Role- and Domain-Aware Adaptation for Multi-Agent Trajectory Modeling in Sports,\"\nICDM 2025\n.\n[arXiv]\nYi Xu\n, Yuxin Hu, Zaiwei Zhang, Gregory P. Meyer, Siva Karthik Mustikovela, Siddhartha Srinivasa, Eric M. Wolff, Xin Huang, \"VLM-AD: End-to-End Autonomous Driving through Vision-Language Model Supervision,\"\nCoRL 2025\n. [\narXiv\n]\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, ''\nSports-Traj: A Unified Trajectory Generation Model for Multi-Agent Movement in Sports\n,''\nICLR 2025\n.\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, ''\nAdapting to Length Shift: FlexiLength Network for Trajectory Prediction,''\nCVPR 2024\n.\n[arXiv]\nHaichao Zhang,\nYi Xu\n, Hongsheng Lu, Takayuki Shimizu, Yun Fu, ''Noise-free Out-of-Sight Trajectory Prediction with Vision-Positioning Denoising,''\nCVPR 2024\n.\nJianglin Lu,\nYi Xu\n, Huan Wang, Yue Bai, Yun Fu, \"Latent Graph Inference with Limited Supervision,\"\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nPaper\n][\nWebsite\n][\nCode\n]\nHaichao Zhang,\nYi Xu\n, Hongsheng Lu, Takayuki Shimizu, Yun Fu, ''Layout Sequence Prediction From Noisy Mobile Modality, ''\nACM MM 2023\n.\n[\narXiv\n]\nYizhou Wang, Yue Kang, Can Qin, Huan Wang,\nYi Xu\n, Yulun Zhang, Yun Fu, \"\nMomentum is All You Need for Data-Driven Adaptive Optimization,\n\"\nICDM 2023\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nCode\n]\nYi Xu\n, Armin Bazarjani, Hyung-gun Chi, Chiho Choi, Yun Fu, \"Uncovering the Missing Pattern: Unified Framework Towards Trajectory Imputation and Prediction,\"\nCVPR 2023\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nHyung-gun Chi, Kwonjoon Lee, Nakul Agarwal,\nYi Xu\n, Karthik Ramani, Chiho Choi, \"AdamsFormer for Spatial Action Localization in the Future,\"\nCVPR 2023\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nYitian Zhang, Yue Bai, Huan Wang,\nYi Xu\n, Yun Fu, ''Look More but Care Less in Video Recognition,''\nNeurIPS 2022\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nYizhou Wang, Can Qin, Yue Bai,\nYi Xu\n, Xu Ma, Yun Fu, ''Making Reconstruction-based Method Great Again for Video Anomaly Detection,''\nICDM 2022\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nYizhou Wang, Can Qin, Rongzhe Wei,\nYi Xu\n, Yue Bai, Yun Fu, \"Self-supervision Meets Adversarial Perturbation: A Novel Framework for Anomaly Detection,\"\nCIKM 2022\n.\n[\narXiv\n][\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nYi Xu\n,\nLichen Wang, Yizhou Wang,\nCan Qin, Yulun Zhang,\nYun Fu, \"MemREIN: Rein the Domain Shift for Cross-Domain Few-Shot Learning\n,\n\"\nIJCAI 2022\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nYi Xu\n, Lichen Wang, Yizhou Wang, Yun Fu, \"Adaptive Trajectory Prediction via Transferable GNN,\"\nCVPR 2022\n.\n[arXiv]\n[\nPaper\n]\nYi Xu\n*\n, Dongchun Ren\n*\n, Mingxia Li, Yuehai Chen, Mingyu Fan, Huaxia Xia, ''Robust Trajectory Prediction of Multiple Interac-ting Pedestrians via Incremental Active Learning,''\nICONIP 2021\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nYanliang Zhu*, Dongchun Ren\n*\n,\nYi Xu\n*\n, Deheng Qian\n*\n, Mingyu Fan\n*\n, Xin Li\n*\n, Huaxia Xia\n*\n, ''Simultaneous Past and Current Social Interaction-aware Trajectory Prediction for Multiple Intelligent Agents in Dynamic Scenes,''\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nYi Xu\n*\n, Dongchun Ren\n*\n, Mingxia Li, Yuehai Chen, Mingyu Fan, Huaxia Xia, \"Tra2Tra: Trajectory-to-Trajectory Prediction With a Global Social Spatial-Temporal Attentive Neural Network,\"\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters\n/\nICRA 2021\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nYi Xu\n*\n, Jing Yang\n*\n, Shaoyi Du, \"CF-LSTM: Cascaded Feature-Based Long Short-Term Networks for Predicting Pedestrian Trajectory,\"\nAAAI 2020\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nWorking\nBosch Center for Artificial Intelligence\n,\nSunnyvale, CA, USA.\nResearch\nScientist\n,\nFeb\n. 202\n6\n~\nPresent\nCruise LLC\n, San Francisco\n, CA, USA.\nResearch Intern,\nMay. 202\n4\n~ Nov. 202\n4\nMentor\n:\nXin Huang\n,\nEric M. Wolff\nProject\n: VLM + End-to-End autonomous driving.\nHonda Research Institute\n, San Jose, CA, USA\n.\nResearch Intern\n, May. 2022 ~ Nov. 2022, May. 2023 ~ Sept. 2023\nMentor\n:\nChiho Choi\n,\nEnna Sachdeva\n,\nBehzad Dariush\nProject\n: Trajectory imputation and prediction, causal inference.\nAutonomous Delivery Center\n,\nMeituan AI\n, Beijing, China.\nResearch Intern,\nJun\n. 202\n0\n~\nSept\n. 202\n0\nMentor\n: Prof.\nMingyu Fan\nProject\n:\nPedestrian\n/vehicle future trajectory prediction, active learning in trajectory sample selection.\nTeaching\nEECE 7205: Fundamentals of Computer Engineering, Spring 2023.\nDS 5230: Unsupervised Machine Learning, Fall 2023.\nDS 5500: Data Science Capstone, Spring 2024\n.\nDS 5500: Data Science Capstone, Spring 2025.\nDS 5220: Supervised Machine Learning and Learning Theory, Summer 2025.\nCS 3000: Algorithms and Data, Fall 2025.\nAwards\nNortheastern PhD Network\nTravel Award, 2022, 2023, 2024,\nand\n2025.\nTravel Award of ICDM 2025.\nTravel Award of\nCVPR\n2\n022\n.\nNational Scholarship in 2018 (The\nhighest\nhonor in China).\nExcellent Graduate Student of Xi’an Jiaotong University in 2018 and 2019.\nThird Prize in the 15th China Graduate Mathematical Contest in Modeling in 2018.\nThird Prize in the 4th China Graduate Future Flight Vehicle Innovation Competition in 2018.\nProfessional Service\nConference Reviewer\nCVPR, ICCV, ECCV,  BMVC,\nNeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, AAAI, IJCAI\n,\nFG\n, KDD, SDM, ICRA.\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI).\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP).\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS).\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT).\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles (TIV).\nACM Transactions on Knowledge Discovery from Data (TKDD).\nKnowledge and Information Systems\n(KAIS).\nNeurocomputing.\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters.\nContacts\nEmail:\nxu.yi@northeastern.edu\n,\nheyyixu@gmail.com\nWeChat:\n578138534\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
