    "homepage_text": "Rui Wang\nRui Wang\nX\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nEmail\nI'm an AI researcher at\nYutori\n.\nI currently work on building Computer-Use Agent (CUA) models through mid-training and reinforcement learning, and most recently have been driving the development of\nYutori Navigator\n.\nMy research interest lies in multimodal large language models and agentic systems, with an emphasis on long-horizon tasks and reliable evaluation in real-world settings.\nPreviously, I led post-training for\nLLaMA 3\nMultimodal on the LLaMA team at\nMeta GenAI\nand co-led\nEmu\n, Meta's text-to-image foundation model.\nI received my MS from\nCarnegie Mellon University\n.\nProjects\n(new!)\nYutori Navigator —\nhttps://yutori.com/blog/introducing-navigator\nA computer-use agent ranked #1 on Online-Mind2Web and Navi-Bench.\nLLaMA 3 —\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2407.21783\nEmu —\nhttps://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.15807"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Hualin Zhang::https://profiles.sc-ctsi.org/hualin.zhang": {
    "homepage": "https://profiles.sc-ctsi.org/hualin.zhang",
