    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hualin Zhang | USC Profiles\nUSC Home\nAbout USC\nKeck Hospital of USC\nUSC Norris Cancer Hospital\nPowered by SC CTSI\nOur site may be slower due to heavy traffic from automated \"bots\" and AI crawlers. We're working to fix this.\nFind more Research Resources\nReturn to Top\nHualin Zhang, PhD\nTitle(s)\nAssociate Professor of Clinical Radiation Oncology\nSchool\nKeck School of Medicine of Usc\nAddress\n1441 Eastlake Avenue\nHealth Sciences Campus\nLos Angeles CA 90033\nORCID\n0000-0002-3972-0107\nvCard\nDownload vCard\nOther Positions\nTitle(s)\nLead, Medical Physics Brachytherapy\nBiography\neducation and training\nUniversity of Kentucky, Lexington, Kentucky\n2005\nMedical Physics Residency\nUniversity of Basse Normandie, Caen, France\n2000\nPhysics\nLanzhou Institute of Physics, Chinese Academy of Space Technology, Lanzhou, China\nPh.D\n1995\nLanzhou University, Lanzhou, China\nMSc\n1991\nPhysics\nLanzhou University, Lanzhou, China\nBSc\n1986\nPhysics\nawards and honors\nAmerican Association of Physicist in medicine\n2024\nFellow\nNorthwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine\n2017\r\n                     -\n2018\nOutstanding Teacher\nOverview\noverview\nHualin Zhang, Ph.D., DABR, FAAPM, is an Associate Professor in the Department of Radiation Oncology at the University of Southern California. Dr. Zhang completed his medical physics residency at the University of Kentucky in 2005. He got his Ph.D. from Lanzhou Institute of Physics of China.\nDr. Zhang’s research spans several innovative modalities, including spatially fractionated radiation therapy, MRI-guided low dose rate (LDR) and high dose rate (HDR) brachytherapy, and intraoperative radiation therapies using mesh and balloon-based systems.\nDr. Zhang has authored over 60 peer-reviewed articles and delivered more than 100 scientific presentations globally. He published the world’s first textbook on spatially fractionated radiation therapy in 2023, titled by \"Spatially Fractionated, Microbeam, and Flash Radiation Therapy: A Physics and Multi-disciplinary Approach.\"\nDr. Zhang has held numerous leadership roles, including co-Chair of the American Association of Physicists in Medicine (AAPM) Task Group on Intraoperative Mesh Brachytherapy (TG-222), co-Chair of AAPM Task Group on Spatially Fractionated Radiation Therapy (TG-440), and Chair of the Physics Working Group of the RSS GRID/Lattice, Microbeam, and Flash Radiotherapy Working Groups.\nIn 2018, Dr. Zhang was awarded as the outstanding teacher at Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine.\nIn 2024, Dr. Zhang was awarded as the Fellow of American Association of Physicists in Medicine (FAAPM).\nkeywords\nBrachytherapy\n,\nSpatially Fractionated Radiation Therapy\n,\nRadiobiology\n,\nMolecular Physics\n,\nImmunology\nwebpage\nSFRT Textbook\nSpatially Fractionated Radiation Therapy\nORNG Applications\nFeatured Publications\nBibliographic\nselected publications\nPublications listed below are automatically derived from MEDLINE/PubMed and other sources, which might result in incorrect or missing publications. \r\n\t\tResearchers can\nlogin\nto make corrections and additions, or\ncontact us for help\n.  \r\n        to make corrections and additions.\nNewest\n|\nOldest\n|\nMost Cited\n|\nMost Discussed\n|\nTimeline\n|\nField Summary\n|\nPlain Text\nAltmetrics Details\nPMC Citations\nindicate the number of times the publication was cited by articles in PubMed Central, and the\nAltmetric\nscore represents citations in news articles and social media.\r\n        (Note that publications are often cited in additional ways that are not shown here.)\nFields\nare based on how the National Library of Medicine (NLM) classifies the publication's journal and might not represent the specific topic of the publication.\nTranslation\ntags are based on the publication type and the MeSH terms NLM assigns to the publication.\r\n        Some publications (especially newer ones and publications not in PubMed) might not yet be assigned Field or Translation tags.)\r\n        Click a Field or Translation tag to filter the publications.\nThe Radiosurgery Society Working Groups on GRID, LATTICE, Microbeam, and FLASH Radiotherapies: Advancements Symposium and Subsequent Progress Made. Pract Radiat Oncol. 2025 May-Jun; 15(3):300-307.\nSnider JW, Mayr NA, Molitoris J, Chhabra AM, Mossahebi S, Griffin R, Mohiuddin M,\nZhang H\n, Amendola B, Tubin S, Kang M,\nLimoli C\n, Marter K, Perez N, Rustin GO, Mahadevan A, Coleman CN, Ahmed M, Simone CB.  PMID: 39447865; PMCID:\nPMC12128894\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n1\nFields:\nNeo\nNeoplasms\nRad\nRadiotherapy\nTranslation:\nHumans\nOptimizing GRID and Lattice Spatially Fractionated Radiation Therapy: Innovative Strategies for Radioresistant and Bulky Tumor Management. Semin Radiat Oncol. 2024 07; 34(3):310-322.\nAhmed MM, Wu X, Mohiuddin M, Perez NC,\nZhang H\n, Amendola BE, Malachowska B, Mohiuddin M, Guha C.  PMID: 38880540.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n5\nFields:\nNeo\nNeoplasms\nRad\nRadiology\nTranslation:\nHumans\nWhich Modality of SFRT Should be Considered First for Bulky Tumor Radiation Therapy, GRID or LATTICE? Semin Radiat Oncol. 2024 07; 34(3):302-309.\nZhang H\n, Wu X.  PMID: 38880539.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n3\nFields:\nNeo\nNeoplasms\nRad\nRadiology\nTranslation:\nHumans\nDosimetric characterization for GRID collimator-based spatially fractionated radiation therapy: Dosimetric parameter acquisition and machine interchangeability investigation. J Appl Clin Med Phys. 2024 Aug; 25(8):e14410.\nXu Z,\nBalik S\n,\nWoods K\n, Shen Z,\nCheng C\n, Cui J,\nGallogly H\n, Chang E,\nLukas L\n,\nLim A\n,\nNatsuaki Y\n,\nYe J\n, Ma L,\nZhang H\n.  PMID: 38810092; PMCID:\nPMC11302805\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n1\nFields:\nBio\nBiophysics\nPhy\nPhysics\nTranslation:\nHumans\nIntraoperative radiation therapy with 50 kV x-rays: A multi-institutional review. J Appl Clin Med Phys. 2024 Mar; 25(3):e14272.\nSethi A, Gros S, B