    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Kaixuan Chen's Homepage\nKaixuan Chen\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science,\nAalborg University (AAU),\nDenmark\nVice Chair\nComputer Society, \nIEEE Denmark Section\nOffice 3.2.33\nSelma Lagerlöfs Vej 300\nDK-9220, Aalborg Øst, Denmark\nPhone: (+45) 71349188\nEmail: kchen.cs.aau.dk\nShort Bio\nKaixuan Chen is an Assistant Professor at the Department of Computer Science,\nAalborg University\n, Denmark. She is also a faculty member in\nCenter for a faculty member in Center for Data-Intensive Systems (Daisy)\nwith\nProf. Christian S. Jensen\nand\nProf. Bin Yang\n.\nKaixuan Chen got her doctorate at the School of Computer Science and Engineering,\nUniversity of New South Wales (UNSW)\nin April 2020. Her supervisors were\nProf. Lina Yao, UNSW\n,\nDr. Liming Zhu, Data61, CSIRO\n, and\nDr. Xiwei (Sherry) Xu, Data61, CSIRO\n.\nShe earned a Bachelor's degree from\nXi'an Jiaotong University (XJTU)\nin 2015, majoring in Telecommunication Engineering.\nCurrently, her scientific research interest is in Data Mining, Deep Learning and Sensor-based Human Activity Recognition.\nRecent News\n[Jun 2022] [CFP] Special Issue of Sensors \"\nHuman Activity Recognition Using Sensors and Machine Learning\n\"\n[May 2021] One paper was published by ACM Computing Surveys (CSUR)!\n[May 2021] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing (TMC)!\n[April 2021] One paper was accepted by e-Energy!\n[April 2021] I was invited as a Review Editor of Frontiers in Big Data!\nSee More\n[Dec 2020] I started to serve as the Vice Chair of Computer Society, IEEE Denmark Section!\n[Oct 2020] I was invited as a PC member of IJCAI 2021!\n[Aug 2020] I was awarded a Dean’s Award for Outstanding PhD Theses from UNSW!\n[Aug 2020] I started my new career at the Department of Computer Science, Aalborg University, as an Assistant Professor!\n[Apr 2020] I graduated and was awarded the degree of Doctor of Philosophy form UNSW!\n[Aug 2019] I was awarded Best Student Paper Award by the 28th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-19) workshop on AIMA4EDU!\n[Jul 2019] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)!\n[Jun 2019] I was awarded IJCAI 2019 Student Travel Grant!\n[May 2019] One paper was accepted by the 28th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-19)!\nOrganizations"
  },
