  "deep_homepage::Hongning Wang::https://coai.cs.tsinghua.edu.cn/hw-ai/": {
    "homepage": "https://coai.cs.tsinghua.edu.cn/hw-ai/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/HCDM",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Hongning Wang's Homepage\nHongning Wang\nAssociate Professor\nOffice: FIT Building, Room 3-520\nEmail: hw-ai#at#tsinghua#dot#edu#dot#cn\nI am an associate professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nTsinghua University\n. Prior to that, I spent 9 years in the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat the\nUniversity of Virginia\n. My research interest includes machine learning and information retrieval, with a special emphasis on sequential decision making problems. I graduated from the\nCS@UIUC\nin May 2014.\nNews\nOctober 1, 2025\nWe have launched an LLM-based multi-agent system for AI-empowered education and research, named\nAI Cosmos\n. On AI Cosmos, you can discuss with a group of experts and implement your ideas into executable programs under the assistance of AI agents.\nDecember 3, 2024\nOur group has won the First Prize in the\nTechnical Innovation Category of the 2024 Qian Weichang Chinese Information Processing Science and Technology Award\n!\nDecember 15, 2023\nThrilled to receive the\nKaren Spärck Jones (KSJ) Award\n2023!\nSeptember 1, 2023\nI have returned to the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nTsinghua University\nas a tenured associate professor.\nDecember 2, 2022\nVery glad to receive the Copenhaver Associate Professor appointment from the School of Engineering!\nMarch 20, 2022\nWe have reorganized our group's algorithms and released most of them through this\nGitHub site\n. You are highly welcomed to try them out and provide us feedback!\nJanuary 1, 2022\nInterested in multi-arm bandits? You can now play with such algorithms\nhere\n.\nOctober 1, 2021\nOur research in \"\nMoving offline learning to rank online, from theory to practice\n\" has been funded by NSF IIS program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nAugust 1, 2021\nI will be visiting the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nTsinghua University\nin the academic year 2021-22 for my sabbatical leave.\nDecember 6, 2020\nI am offering\nCS4780 Information Retrieval\nin the spring semester.\nOctober 1, 2020\nOur research in \"\nTowards Explainable Personalization\n\" has been funded by NSF IIS program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nAugust 27, 2020\nI am offering\nCS6501 Reinforcement Learning\nin the fall semester.\nAugust 23, 2020\nWe are giving a tutorial on\nLearning by Exploration\nat\nKDD'2020\n.\nJuly 23, 2019\nI am offering\nCS4780/6501 Information Retrieval\nin the spring semester.\nJuly 23, 2019\nOur paper \"\nVariance Reduction in Gradient Exploration for Online Learning to Rank\n\" received the\nBest Paper Award\nat\nSIGIR'2019\n!\nMay 16, 2019\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Join Network Embedding with Topic Embedding for User Representation Learning\" at\nLinkedIn\n.\nMay 15, 2019\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Learning Contextual Bandits in a Non-Stationary Environment\" at\nPinterest\n.\nFeburary 15, 2019\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Context Attentive Document Ranking and Query Suggestion in Search Tasks\" at the\nTask Intelligence Workshop\n, WSDM'2019, Melbourne Australia.\nFeburary 12, 2019\nI was selected for the\nWSDM 2019 Outstanding Senior Program Committee Award\n.\nSeptember 15, 2018\nOur research in \"\nLearning and Improving Alzheimer's Patient-Caregiver Relationships via Smart Healthcare Technology\n\" has been funded by NSF SCH program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nJanurary 24, 2018\nThanks Nvidia for the generious support of a Titan XP GPU!\nDecember 24, 2017\nOur research of \"\nThe Building Adapter: Automatic Mapping of Commercial Buildings for Scalable Building Analytics\n\" has been funded by the U.S. Department of Energy. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nSeptember 1, 2017\nOur research of \"\nCyber Physical Mappings - Empower Building Analytics at Scale\n\" has been funded by NSF IIS program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nJuly 18, 2017\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Contextual Bandits in a Collaborative Environment\" at the Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, Beijing China.\nJune 15, 2017\nWe have been awarded by the\nYelp Dataset Challenge Round Eight\n!\nJanuary 1, 2017\nOur group homepage is now available at\nHCDM@UVa\n.\nSeptember 16, 2016\nOur research of \"\nCollaborative Sensing: An Approach for Immediately Scalable Sensing in Buildings\n\" has been funded by NSF CPS program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nAugust 1, 2016\nOur research of \"\nCollaborative Learning with Incomplete and Noisy Knowledge\n\" has been funded by NSF III program. More details about this award can be found\nhere\n.\nMarch 5, 2016\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Collaborative Online Learning\" at Yahoo Search Science Team.\nDecember 30, 2015\nI have received the NSF Faculty Early Career Development Program (CAREER) Award. More details about this award can be found\nhere\nand our project website is\nhere\n.\nDecember 21, 2015\nOur proposal of \"Call for Special Issue on Search, Mining and their Applications on Mobile Devices\" has been accepted by the\nACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS)\n. Call for papers will be announced shortly.\nMarch 20, 2015\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Human-centric big data mining\" at\nCenter for Embedded Systems for Critical Applications (CESCA)\nin the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat Virginia Tech.\nJanurary 29, 2015\nI gave an invitated talk about \"Human-centric big data mining\" in\nQuantitative Psychology Group\nin the\nDepartment of Psychology\nat UVa.\nJanurary 12, 2015\nMy research is reported on\nUVa Today\n.\nDecember 22, 2014\nThe course website for\nCS6501 Text Mining\nhas been deployed.\nDecember 9, 2014\nI was selected for the\nWSDM 2015 Outstanding Reviewer Award\n.\nDecember 1, 2014\nI have position opennings for Ph.D. students for Fall 2015. If you are self-motivated and want to pursue a Ph.D. degree in the areas of data mining and information retrieval, please contact me. More information about the graduate admission at CS@UVa can be found\nhere\n. Please note the application deadline is\nDecember 15th, 2014\n.\nNovember 10, 2014\nI am going to offer\nCS6501: Text Mining\nnext Spring semester.\nAugust 26, 2014\nI am offering\nCS6501: Information Retrieval\nthis Fall semester.\nAugust 25, 2014\nI joined CS@UVa as an assistant professor.\nAward and Honor\n2023 Dec, Karen Spärck Jones (KSJ) Award;\n2022 Dec, the Copenhaver Associate Professor appointment;\n2022 Dec,\nNeurIPS 2022 Top Reviewer\n;\n2020 Mar,\nYelp Dataset Challenge\nRound Thirteen Winner;\n2020 Feb,\nGoogle Faculty Research Award\n;\n2020 Feb, finalist of\nMicrosoft Research Faculty Fellowship\n;\n2019 Jul,\nSIGIR 2019\nBest Paper Award\n;\n2019 Feb,\nWSDM 2019\nOutstanding Senior Program Committee award;\n2017 Jul,\nSIGIR 2017\nOutstanding Reviewer award;\n2017 Jun,\nYelp Dataset Challenge\nRound Eight Winner;\n2015 Dec,\nNSF Faculty Early Career Development Program (CAREER) Award\n,\nProject Website\n;\n2014 Oct,\nYahoo 2014 Academic Career Enhancement award\n;\n2014 Jul,\nU.Va. Excellence in Diversity Fellowship\n;\nInvited Talks\nNext++ Workshop, Tsinghua Singapore AI summit, December 5, 2024.\n\"AI Empowered Education at Tsinghua: Practices and Lessons Learnt\"\n.\nNext++ Workshop, Tsinghua Singapore AI summit, May 30, 2024.\n\"Human vs. Generative AI in Content Creation Competition: Symbiosis or Conflict?\"\n.\nThe 18th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n,\nKeynote Speech\n, March 18, 2024.\n\"Human vs. Generative AI in Content Creation Competition: Symbiosis or Conflict?\"\n.\nGeorgetown Computer Science Colloquium, Feburary 13, 2024.\n\"How Bad is Top-K Recommendation under Competing Content Creators?\"\n.\nIllinois Computer Science Speaker Series Lecture, Feburary 7, 2024.\n\"How Bad is Top-K Recommendation under Competing Content Creators?\"\n.\nGlasgow Information Retrieval group seminar talk, November 14, 2022.\n\"Rethink conversational recommendations and beyond\"\n.\nWorkshop on Action, Task and User Journey Modeling at Google\n, October 5, 2022.\n\"Learning from learning users: a new perspective for interactive recommendation\"\n.\nInstacart Machine Learning Seminar, September 28, 2022.\n\"A New Perspective for Interactive Recommendation\"\n.\nAI/ML Seminar, Meta AI, Jun 10, 2022.\n\"Learning from a learning user: a new perspective for interactive recommendation\"\n.\nMicrosoft Research Asia\n, Apr 29, 2022.\n\"Learning from a learning user: a new perspective for interactive recommendation\"\n.\nAI Lecture Series,\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\n,\nJilin University\n, Dec 20, 2021.\n\"Taming Latent Factor Models for Explainability\"\n.\nAI Seminar,\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\n,\nThe Hong Kong University of Science and Technology\n, Oct 26, 2021.\n\"Moving offline learning to rank online, from theory to practice\"\n.\nComputer Science Colloquium,\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nTsinghua University\n, Sept 21, 2021.\n\"Moving offline learning to rank online, from theory to practice\"\n.\nCornell AI Seminar\n, Mar 26, 2021.\n\"Moving offline learning to rank online, from theory to practice\"\n.\nbooking.com\n, Nov 9, 2020.\n\"Learning Contextual Bandits in a Non-Stationary Environment\"\n.\nUniversity of Delaware\n,\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\n, Nov 6, 2019.\n\"Taming Latent Factor Models for Explainability.\"\n.\nLinkedIn\n, May 16, 2019.\n\"Join Network Embedding with Topic Embedding for User Representation Learning\"\n.\nPinterest\n, May 15, 2019.\n\"Learning Contextual Bandits in a Non-Stationary Environment\"\n.\nTask Intelligence Workshop\n,\nthe 12th ACM International Conference on Web Search and Data Mining (WSDM'2019)\n, Feburary 15, 2019.\n\"Context Attentive Document Ranking and Query Suggestion in Search Tasks\"\n.\nUniversity of Montreal,\nLaboratoire RALI\n, December 6, 2018.\n\"Learning Contextual Bandits in a Non-Stationary Environment\"\n.\nColumbia University,\nDepartment of Statistics\n, October 8, 2018.\n\"Learning Contextual Bandits in a Non-Stationary Environment\"\n.\nUniversity of Southern California,\nInformation Sciences Institute\n, Feburary 9, 2018.\n\"Contextual Bandits in a Collaborative Environment\"\n.\nSnap Research Group, Feburary 7, 2018.\n\"Contextual Bandits in a Collaborative Environment\"\n.\nAmazon Applied Research Group, October 2, 2017.\n\"Contextual Bandits in a Collaborative Environment\"\n.\nDepartment of Computer Science, Tsinghua University, July 18, 2017.\n\"Contextual Bandits in a Collaborative Environment\"\n.\nYahoo Search Science team, March 5, 2016.\n\"Collaborative online learning\"\n.\nCenter for Embedded Systems for Critical Applications (CESCA)\nin the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat Virginia Tech, March 20, 2015.\n\"Human-centric big data mining\"\n.\nQuantitative Psychology Group\nin the\nDepartment of Psychology\nat UVa, Janurary 2015.\n\"Human-centric big data mining\"\n.\nUniversity of Delaware\n,\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\n, October 2014.\n\"A Task-based Framework for User Behavior Modeling and Search Personalization\"\n.\nThe 4th workshop on Web Search Click Data (\nWSCD'2014\n), Feburary 2014. Keynote speech on\n\"A Search-task-based Framework for Modeling User Search Behaviors\"\n(\nslides\n).\nSearch science and anti-abuse science group\n, Yahoo! Labs, October 2013. Invited talk on\n\"A Task-Based Framework for Search Log Mining and Personalization\"\n.\nAcademic Activities\nProgram committee member:\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS): 2025 (AC), 2024 (AC), 2022, 2021, 2020, 2019\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML): 2022, 2021, 2020, 2014, 2013, 2012\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR): 2025 (AC), 2024, 2023, 2022, 2021, 2020\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI): 2026 (AC), 2025 (AC), 2024 (AC), 2023 (AC), 2022 (AC), 2021 (SPC), 2019, 2018, 2017\nInternational ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR): 2023 (SPC), 2021, 2020, 2019, 2018, 2017, 2016, 2015\nInternational ACM KDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD): 2023 (AC), 2022 (SPC), 2021, 2020, 2019, 2018, 2017, 2016, 2015\nThe World Wide Web Conference (WWW): 2023 (SPC), 2022, 2020 (SPC), 2019, 2018, 2016, 2015\nACM International Conference on Web Search and Data Mining (WSDM): 2023 (SPC), 2022 (SPC), 2021, 2019 (SPC), 2018 (SPC), 2017, 2016, 2015\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL): 2023 (AC), 2019, 2018, 2017, 2015\nACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management (CIKM): 2022 (SPC), 2021 (SPC), 2020 (SPC), 2017, 2015, 2014\nJournal associate editor:\nFrontiers in Big Data\n,\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (TIST)\nJournal reviewer:\nJMLR\n,\nTKDE\n,\nTOIS\n,\nTPAMI\n,\nTOIS\n,\nNeurocomputing\n,\nBMC Bioinformatics\n,\nInformation Processing & Management\n,\nIJAIT\n,\nNeural Processing Letters\n,\nWorld Wide Web Journal\n,\nInternational Journal of Machine Learning and Cybernetics\n.\nPublic services: SIGIR 2024 General Co-Chair,\nKDD 2022\nWorkshop Co-Chair,\nKDD 2020\nStudent Sponsorship Co-Chair,\nSIGIR 2018\nStudent Sponsorship Chair,\nWSDM 2018\nDemo Track Chair,\nCIKM 2016\nPublicity chair,\nAIRS 2016\narea chair for IR Models and Theories,\nNLPCC 2015\narea chair for Search and Advertisement.\nSelected Publications\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n[\nDBLP\n]\n[\nFull List\n]\nThe GLM Team.\nGLM-4.5: Agentic, Reasoning, and Coding (ARC) Foundation Models.\nTechnical report, August 2025. (\nPDF\n,\nz.ai\n)\nYuxian Gu, Li Dong,\nHongning Wang\n, Yaru Hao, Qingxiu Dong, Furu Wei, Minlie Huang.\nData Selection via Optimal