    "homepage_text": "ZHENJIE YANG\n      -  Macao Polytechnic University\nMacao Polytechnic University Home\nEnglish\n中文\nSearch content at Macao Polytechnic University\nContact expert\nView Scopus Profile\nZHENJIE YANG\nLecturer\nLecturer\n,\nFaculty of Humanities and Social Sciences\nPhone\n2845 3593\nEmail\nzjyang\nmpu.edu\nmo\nh-index\n153\nCitations\n7\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2013\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 3\nGood Health and Well-being\nSDG 7\nAffordable and Clean Energy\nSDG 8\nDecent Work and Economic Growth\nSDG 11\nSustainable Cities and Communities\nSDG 12\nResponsible Consumption and Production\nSDG 13\nClimate Action\nSDG 15\nLife on Land\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where ZHENJIE YANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n3\nSimilar Profiles\nChina\nSocial Sciences\n100%\nRegional Cooperation\nSocial Sciences\n48%\nTechnological Innovation\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n48%\nChinese\nSocial Sciences\n45%\nMacao\nSocial Sciences\n44%\nHong Kong\nSocial Sciences\n44%\nCase Study\nSocial Sciences\n35%\nPublic Service\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n24%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n27\nArticle\n2\nConference contribution\nUrbanization and Water Resource Green Efficiency: Coupling Coordination, Dynamic Interactions, and Driving Forces\nFeng, L., Shi, Y.,\nYang, Z.\n, Chen, H., Liu, X. & Chen, J.,\nJan 2026\n,\nIn:\nWater Resources Management.\n40\n,\n2\n, 82.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nWater Conservation\n100%\nWater Demand\n100%\nMetropolitan Area\n100%\nVector Autoregression\n100%\nAgglomeration Effect\n100%\nAnalysis of China’s marine economic policy: regional policy characteristics, evolution and assessment\nShen, C.,\nYang, Z.\n& Zhan, J.,\n2025\n,\nIn:\nFrontiers in Marine Science.\n12\n, 1553962.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nBlue Economy\n100%\nEcological Balance\n25%\nDynamic correlation of environmental regulation, technological innovation, and corporate carbon emissions: empirical evidence from China listed companies\nFeng, L., Shi, Y.,\nYang, Z.\n,\nLam, J. F. I.\n, Lin, S., Zhan, J. & Chen, H.,\nDec 2025\n,\nIn:\nScientific Reports.\n15\n,\n1\n, 8433.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nGreenhouse Gas Emissions\n100%\nEnvironmental Standard\n100%\nTechnological Innovation\n100%\nSustainable Development\n12%\nAutoregression\n12%\n10\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nScientific and technological innovation cooperation network of the Greater Bay Area in South China: A social network analysis\nShen, C.,\nYang, Z.\n,\nLam, F. I.\n, Tam, S. W., Yang, W. & Li, Y.,\nJul 2025\n,\nIn:\nPLoS ONE.\n20\n,\n7 July\n, e0326515.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nChina\n100%\nHong Kong\n100%\nScience and Technology\n100%\nNetwork Analysis\n100%\nSocial Network\n100%\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nThe blame-avoiding effect of sanction-based accountability and its boundary conditions\nLi, J., Cui, M.,\nYang, Z.\n& Zheng, J.,\n2025\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nPublic Management Review.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 29 research outputs\nPress/Media\nData on Science Reported by Zhenjie Yang and Colleagues (Scientific and technological innovation cooperation network of the Greater Bay Area in South China: A social network analysis)\nLAM, F. I.\n&\nYANG, Z.\n11/07/25\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\nFaculty of Humanities and Social Sciences Reports Findings in Science (Dynamic correlation of environmental regulation, technological innovation, and corporate carbon emissions: empirical evidence from China listed companies)\nYANG, Z.\n&\nLAM, F. I.\n20/03/25\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\nResearcher's Work from Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences Focuses on Technology (The Impact of Intelligent Logistics on Logistics Performance Improvement)\nYANG, Z.\n26/02/25\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\nNew Applied Water Science Study Findings Recently Were Reported by Researchers at Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences (Two-stage efficiency evaluation of industrial water resources and the role of digital inclusive finance: insight from ...)\nYANG, Z.\n20/12/24\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\nResearch from Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences Reveals New Findings on Social Science (Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Cooperation: Historical Process and Driving Mechanisms)\nLI, L.\n,\nYANG, Z.\n&\nLAM, F. I.\n5/07/24\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\nView all 7 press/media\nYour message has successfully been sent.\nYour message was not sent due to an error.\nx\nContact ZHENJIE YANG\nSubject:\n*\nMessage:\n*\nYour name:\n*\nYour email:\n*\nSend me a copy of this message\n*required field\nSee privacy policy in the footer of the page\nCancel\nSend"
