    "homepage_text": "Hang Zhou - Hang Zhou @ UNC\nHang Zhou\nAssistant Professor\nSTOR\n&\nSDSS\nThe University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\nFollow\nChapel-Hill, NC, USA\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nHang Zhou\nI am an Assistant Professor in\nSTOR\nand\nSDSS\nat UNC-Chapel Hill. Before joining UNC, I was a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Statistics at UC Davis, working with Professors\nHans-Georg Müller\nand\nJane-Ling Wang\n. I got my Ph.D. in Statistics from Peking University in 2022, under the supervision of Professor\nFang Yao\n.\nMy current research interests include:\nTheory and methodology for:\nStatistical modeling and inference for object data, including but not limited to distributions, trees, and compositional data\nFunctional data with complex structure, including discretely observed and non-Euclidean data\nLearning theory, generalization bound for deep neural network\nModel agnostic method and its applications in real-world dataset, e.g., anomalies detection\nDynamical systems and its applications in information retrieval\nApplication areas:\nLongitudinal/Compositional data in biological and medical sciences\nBrain image data (MRI, fMRI)\nContact\nOffice: 339 Hanes Hall, Chapel Hill, NC 27599\nEmail: hzh[at]unc[dot]edu\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nSoftware - Hang Zhou @ UNC\nHang Zhou\nAssistant Professor\nSTOR\n&\nSDSS\nThe University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\nFollow\nChapel-Hill, NC, USA\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nSoftware\nfdapace: Functional Data Analysis and Empirical Dynamics\nMaintainer (Matlab version, July 2022 – July 2025)\nR package available at\nCRAN\nUp-to-date Matlab version is available for download at\nGithub repository\nfdaconcur: Concurrent Regression and History Index Models for Functional Data\nDeveloper\nR package available at\nCRAN\nCleanlab\n: Find Noisy Labels in Regression Datasets\nThe benchmarking algorithms is available at\nGithub repository\nA 5-minute quickstart tutorial can be founded\nhere"
  },
