    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About me | Tianhao Wang\nTianhao Wang\nTianhao Wang\nDifferential privacy, trustworthy machine learning, and deployable privacy-preserving systems.\nEmail\nScholar\nGitHub\nTwitter\nCV\nAssistant Professor\nUniversity of Virginia, Computer Science\nCharlottesville, VA, USA\nI am an Assistant Professor at the\nUniversity of Virginia\n, in the Department of Computer Science. I earned my PhD from\nPurdue University\nand my Bachelor's degree from\nFudan University\n.\nMy research focuses on making\ndifferential privacy\nand\nmachine learning privacy\npractical, reliable, and impactful in real-world systems.\nTheory is the foundation, but deployment is the goal. I care about privacy methods that remain useful when data, compute, and product realities are no longer idealized.\nProject 01\nOpen Advisor\nDP Advisor\nA custom GPT designed to help users evaluate whether differential privacy is appropriate for their use case and avoid common pitfalls. The tool does not collect personal information.\nFor critical decision-making settings, please consult with a human expert. Prompt and design details are available upon request.\nProject 02\nLive Demo\nPrivSyn\nAn interactive demo that walks users through generating synthetic tabular data with differential privacy guarantees. Currently tested on the Adult dataset.\nAvailability may vary due to free-tier cloud hosting constraints.\nPersonal\nPersonal\nMy wife,\nXuejun Zhao\n, is an Assistant Professor in Information Systems and Operations Management at UNC Charlotte.\nLast updated: Mar 13, 2026\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yang Zhang::https://yangzhang.dev/": {
