    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Tianlong Chen | UNC Chapel Hill\nTianlong Chen\nAssistant Professor, CS@UNC at Chapel Hill\nChief AI Scientist, hireEZ\ntianlong@cs.unc.edu\nBio\nTianlong Chen starts as an Assistant Professor of Computer Science at The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill in Fall 2024.\n  He received the Ph.D. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering from University of Texas at Austin, TX, USA, in 2023.\nHis research focuses on building\naccurate, trustworthy, and efficient machine learning\nsystems. He received\nAmazon Research Award\n(Fall 2024 and Spring 2025),\nCisco Faculty Award\n(2024 and 2025), AAAI'25 New Faculty Highlights, NAIRR Pilot Award, UNC Accelerating AI Award, CPAL Rising Star, AdvML Rising Star, OpenAI Researcher Access Award, Gemma Academic Program GCP Credit Award, IBM Ph.D. Fellowship, Adobe Ph.D. Fellowship, Graduate Dean's Prestigious Fellowship, Low-Resource Methods for NLP SAC Award at NAACL 2025, the Best Paper Award at LoG 2022, Marco Ramoni Distinguished Paper Award at AMIA-IS 2025, the Best Paper Award at GenAI4Health at AAAI 2025, Best Demo Paper Award at GenAI4Health at NeurIPS 2024, and the Best Paper Runners-Up Award at Medicine and Healthcare Bridge at AAAI’25.\nI am looking for highly motivated students, in terms of RA/TA/externship/internship/visiting students. \n    Interested candidates are strongly encouraged to contact me by email, together with resume and transcripts.\nNews\n2025\n2024\n2023\n•\nSep., 2025\n[HONOR]\nHonored to be one of the recipients of the Amazon Research Award for Spring 2025. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nAug., 2025\n[HONOR]\nGrateful to receive a gift funding from Cisco Research. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nAug., 2025\n[STATUS]\nUNITES welcomes 11 new members (8 Ph.D. + 2 Postdoc + 1 M.S.): Mohan Zhang (USTC) + Yuhang Cheng (Wuhan University) + Kangqi Ni (RICE) + Laura Yao (CMU) + Yu-Chao Huang (National Taiwan University) + Zijie Liu (WashU) + Zhuoxuan Zhang (Brown) + Shuqing Luo (PKU) + Jinhao Duan (Drexel) + Gengwei Zhang (UTS) + Zhen Xu (Zhejiang University). Three of them get delayed due to VISA constraints.\n•\nAug., 2025\n[PAPER]\n9 EMNLP'25 (6 Main + 3 Findings) accepted - Next Agent Prediction + Embodied Reward Model with Test-time Scaling + Bit Flip Error Resilience in LLMs + Instruction-Driven Routing for MoE + Adaptive Resolution for VLLMs + MedHallucinations Benchmark + Large-scale Parameter Generation + Training Strategies for MoE + Efficient Long Context Inference w. LLMs.\n•\nJul, 2025\n[PAPER]\n1 COLM'25 accepted - Multi-model Safety Alignment.\n•\nJun., 2025\n[Workshop]\nNeurIPS'25 Workshop accepted -\nLock-LLM\n. Call for Papers!\n•\nMay, 2025\n[PAPER]\n10 ACL'25 (5 Main + 5 Findings) accepted - Long-term Personalized Dialogue Agents (Intergated in Google Gemini) + Indirect Attack in Multi-Agent Systems + UQ in LLM + Efficient LLM Recommender + Multi-Agent System for Content Analysis + Multi-omics Foundation Model + Spatial2Sentence + UQ-Merging + De-Identification in MLLM + Task-specific Privacy Vulnerabilities in MLLMs.\n•\nMay, 2025\n[PAPER]\n1 JBI'25 (Journal of Biomedical Informatics) accepted - Personalized Graph Learning on EHRs.\n•\nMay, 2025\n[PAPER]\n2 KDD'25 accepted - Graph Learning w. Missing Features + Trustworthy LLM Agent (Survey + Toturial).\n•\nMay, 2025\n[HONOR]\nHonored to be selected and attend the\n12th Heidelberg Laureate Forum (HLF) 2025\n.\n•\nMay, 2025\n[PAPER]\n4 ICML'25 accepted - Communication Topology Designs in Multi-Agent System (Spotlight) + New MoE Parallism + Adaptive Multimodal Learning + Interpretable MoE.\n•\nApr., 2025\n[HONOR]\nHonored to be one of the recipients of the Amazon Research Award for Fall 2024. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nApr., 2025\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to Mohan Zhang, Pingzhi Li, and our amazing collaborators for wining the low-resource methods for NLP SAC Award at NAACL 2025.\n•\nMar., 2025\n[HONOR]\nGrateful for receiving two UNC Accelerating AI Awards from Office of The Provost at UNC. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nMar., 2025\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to UNITES and our amazing collaborators for wining the Marco Ramoni Distinguished Paper Award at AMIA-IS 2025.\n•\nMar., 2025\n[HONOR]\nGrateful for receiving the NAIRR Pilot Award in the field of Artificial Intelligence and Intelligent Systems.\n•\nFeb., 2025\n[PAPER]\n1 DMLR accepted - Diagnosis of Viral Infections via scRNA-seq Analysis.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[PAPER]\n4 NAACL'25 accepted - Collaboration-Constrained Routing for MoE Efficiency + Balanced Preference Optimization in LLM Alignment + LLM-Guided Conversation in Autobiography Interviewing + Affirmative Token Mitigation for Jailbreak Defense.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[PAPER]\n6 ICLR'25 accepted - Training-Free and Portable LLM Model Patches + Economical Multi-Agent Communication + Lifelong Multimodal Instruction Tuning + Composable LLMs Interventions + Proactive Privacy Amnesia for LLMs + Mixture-of-Graphs. Congratulations to Rana for his first 1st author ICLR paper.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[HONOR]\nI received the 2025 CPAL Rising Star Award and 2025 KAUST Rising Stars Award (Declined Due to VISA Constraints). Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[HONOR]\nI received the AAAI New Faculty Highlights 2025. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to UNITES and our amazing collaborators for wining the Best Paper Award at\nGenAI4Health at AAAI 2025\n.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to UNITES and our amazing collaborators for wining the Best Paper Runners-Up Award at Medicine and Healthcare Bridge at AAAI 2025.\n•\nJan., 2025\n[HONOR]\nGrateful to receive a gift funding from Cisco Research. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nDec., 2024\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to Xinyu Zhao and our amazing collaborators for wining the Best Demo Paper Award at\nGenAI4Health at NeurIPS 2024\n.\n•\nDec., 2024\n[PAPER]\n6 AAAI'25 accepted - Metacognitive AI in LLM + Visual Prompting Helps Sparsity + Brain Pathway Learning + UQ in LLMs + Disentangled Multimodal Learning + Sparsity Improves Certification.\n•\nDec., 2024\n[Workshop]\nTwo ICLR'25 Workshop and One PAKDD'25 Workshop accepted - Sparsity in LLM + Scalable Optimization and Adaptive Foundation Model + Pervasive Computing. Call for Papers!\n•\nNov., 2024\n[PAPER]\nOne KDD'25 accepted - C2C Recommendation Datasets (ADS Track).\n•\nOct., 2024\n[PAPER]\nFour NeurIPS'24 accepted - Flexible Modality Learning (Spotlight) + Game-Theoretic Evaluation for LLM Reasoning + Efficient, Fair, Robust Graph Learning + Model-Glue (Dataset and Benchmark Track).\n•\nSep., 2024\n[PAPER]\nThree EMNLP'24 accepted - LLM RAG Vulnerabilities + FFN-SkipLLM + Calibration LLM Pruning; Two EMNLP'24 Findings accepted - Synergized KG and LLM for AD + Cross-Lingual Multi-Hop Knowledge Editing.\n•\nJul., 2024\n[PAPER]\nTwo ECCV'24 accepted - Multiplexed Immunofluorescence Image Analysis + Facial Affective Behavior Analysis. Congratulations to Sukwon Yun for his first 1st author ECCV paper.\n•\nJul., 2024\n[STATUS]\nI started my Assistant Professor position at CS@UNC Chapel Hill.\n•\nMay, 2024\n[PAPER]\nSix ICML'24 accepted - ZO LLM Tuning + Graph Sparsification + Rliabile SMoE + Biologial-informed Protein Representation Learning + Sparse Cocktail + TrustLLM (Position Paper).\n•\nApr., 2024\n[PAPER]\nOne Bioinformatics accepted - scRNA Imputation via Bi-level Feature Propagation.\n•\nApr., 2024\n[Tutorial]\nOur tutorial of \"Mixture-of-Experts in the Era of LLMs: A New Odyssey\" has been accepted by ICML'24. See you at Vienna!\n•\nMar., 2024\n[PAPER]\nOne NAACL'24 accepted - Multiple LLM Agents Gaming.\n•\nMar., 2024\n[STATUS]\nUNITES welcomes six new Ph.D. students and one new M.S. student: Sukwon Yun (KAIST), Xinyu Zhao (Peking University), Pingzhi Li (USTC), Mufan Qiu (USTC), Huanzhi Qu (USTC), Rana Muhammad Shahroz Khan (Vanderbilt University), and Ruichen Zhang (Shandong University).\n•\nMar., 2024\n[PAPER]\nTwo CVPR'24 accepted - Diffusion Quantization + Molecular Data Programming.\n•\nFeb., 2024\n[PAPER]\nTwo ICLR'24 accepted - SMoE Merging (Spotlight) + Multilingual SMoE. Congratulations to Pingzhi Li and Xinyu Zhao for their first 1st author ICLR papers.\n•\nJan., 2024\n[Tutorial]\nOur tutorial of \"Zeroth-Order Machine Learning: Fundamental Principles and Emerging Applications in Foundation Models\" has been accepted by AAAI'24 and ICASSP'24.\n•\nJan., 2024\n[PAPER]\nOne EACL'24 accepted - LLM + Knowledge Graph.\n•\nDec., 2023\n[PAPER]\nOne AAAI'24 accepted - Metacognitive Intervention for LLMs via Sparsity.\n•\nNov., 2023\n[HONOR]\nCongratulations to Pingzhi Li and our amazing collaborators for wining the 1st place at\n2023 Quantum Computing for Drug Discovery Challenge at ICCAD\n.\n•\nSep., 2023\n[PAPER]\nTwo NeurIPS'23 accepted - Essential Sparsity in LLM + LLM Heavy-Hitter Oracle.\n•\nJul., 2023\n[STATUS]\nI started my PostDoc at CSAIL@MIT and BMI@Harvard.\n•\nJul., 2023\n[PAPER]\nThree ICCV'23 accepted - Adaptive Multi-Task Vision MoE + Robust MoE (Oral) + Generalizable NeRF w. MoE.\n•\nJul., 2023\n[PAPER]\nOne QCE'23 accepted - Sparse Circuit Design for Quantum Computing.\n•\nJun., 2023\n[HONOR]\nI received the\n2023 AdvML Rising Star Award\n. Many thanks for the acknowledgment.\n•\nMay, 2023\n[PAPER]\nOne ACL'23 accepted - Sparse LLM Tuning.\n•\nMay, 2023\n[PAPER]\nThree ICML'23 accepted - Instant Soup (Oral) + Graph Ladling + L2O Game.\n•\nMay, 2023\n[STATUS]\nI received the Ph.D. degree from ECE@UT Austin. I deeply appreciate all the support and help from my family, advisor\n(Prof. Atlas Wang)\n, collaborators, and friends!\nUNITES Lab\nU\nniversity of\nN\north Carolina, A\nI\nT\nrustworthiness,\nE\nfficiency, and for\nS\ncience (\nUNITES\n) Group\n  is an active research lab at UNC Chapel Hill.\nPh.D.\nPostDoc\nMaster\nPingzhi Li\n, B.E., USTC, Aug. 2024 -\nMufan Qiu\n, B.S., USTC, Aug. 2024 -\nHuaizhi Qu\n, B.E., USTC, Aug. 2024 -\nXinyu Zhao\n, M.S., Peking Uiversity, Aug. 2024 -\nRana Muhammad Shahroz Khan\n, B.S., Vanderbilt University, Aug. 2024 -\nMohan Zhang\n, B.E., USTC, Aug. 2025 -\nYuhang Chen\n, B.S., Wuhan University, Aug. 2025 -\nKangqi Ni\n, B.S., Rice University, Aug. 2025 -\nLaura Yao\n, B.S., Carnegie Mellon University, Aug. 2025 -\nYu-Chao Huang\n, M.S., National Taiwan University, Aug. 2025 -\nZijie Liu\n, M.S., Washington University in St. Louis, Aug. 2025 -\nRuichen Zhang\n, M.S., UNC Chapel Hill, Dec. 2025 -\nZhuoxuan Zhang\n, M.S., Brown University, -\nShuqing Luo\n, M.S., Peking Uiversity, -\nJinhao Duan\n, Ph.D., Drexel University, Jul. 2025 -\nGengwei Zhang\n, Ph.D., University of Technology Sydney, Dec. 2025 -\nZhen Xu\n, B.S., Zhejiang University, Aug. 2025 -\nRuichen Zhang\n, B.E., Shandong University, Aug. 2024 - Dec. 2025\nSukwon Yun\n, M.S., KAIST, Aug. 2024 - Dec. 2025\nLevi Harris\n, B.S., UNC Chapel Hill, Aug. 2024 - Dec. 2025\nHaiyun Lyu\n, UNC Chapel Hill, Aug. 2024 - May 2025\nMohan Zhang\n(USTC, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nHaiyang Xu\n(USTC, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nDaiwei Li\n(UCSD, Summer 2023, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nJialin Wu\n(USTC, Summer 2023, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nXinnan Zhang\n(USTC, Summer 2023, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nTiancheng He\n(SJTU+UMich, Summer 2023, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nYaoyao Xu\n(Columbia, Summer 2023, Spring 2024) [Remote]\nCan Jin\n(USTC, Summer 2023) [Remote]\nKaixin Zheng\n(Summer 2023) [Remote]\nSilin Cai\n(Summer 2023) [Remote]\nMore About Me\n• I am a big fan of Pokémon. Playing Pokémon Go is one of my daily activities. Join me, catch the Pokémon in North Carolina, and be a good Pokémon trainer!\n• I also enjoy Hip-Hop and Country music.\nAir (艾热)\nis one of my favorite Chinese Hip-Hop stars.\nThis website was built with\njekyll\nbased on a template by\nMartin Saveski\n.\nTianlong Chen\nLast updated on June 2025"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zhenyu Zhang::https://zhenyu.ac.cn/": {
    "homepage": "https://zhenyu.ac.cn/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhenyu Zhang - HomePage\nZhenyu ZHANG /\nStaff Algorithm Engineer at Baidu ERNIE/Wenxin Team\nBaidu Technology Park, No.10 Yard, Beijing, China.\nzzysay[at]gmail/163.com\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nDBLP\nBiography\nI am currently a Staff Algorithm Engineer in the\nERNIE/Wenxin (文心) Team\nat Baidu. Before that, I received my Ph.D. degree from\nUniversity of Chinese Academy of Sciences (UCAS)\nin 2022, under the supervision of Prof.\nTingwen Liu\nand Prof.\nLi Guo\n.\nMy research interests broadly include natural language processing and unified foundation model, especially unified generation and understanding now. I am also committed to the frontier exploration and application of Large Language Model (LLM) and Artificial Intelligence Generated Content (AIGC), with core contributions to ERNIE series of models like ERNIE 5.0/4.5/4.0/3.5/3.0 (LLMs/MLLMs), ERNIE-ViLG 2.0 (Text2Image), ERNIE-Layout (Document Intelligent).\nI have published several papers in AAAI, ACL, CVPR, ICLR, ICML, KDD, MM, NeurIPS, WWW, etc., and won the Best Paper Award of PAKDD 2020.\n[Hiring!] Actively recruiting research scientists, algorithm engineers and research interns for unified foundation models. Feel free to contact me!\nNews\n[2026/02] One paper about\nMultimodal Large Language Model\nwas accepted to\nCVPR 2026\n.\n[2026/02] The technical report of\nERNIE 5.0\nwas released.\n[2025/06] The technical report of\nERNIE 4.5\nwas released.\n[2025/05] Four papers about\nEfficient Large Language Model\nand\nParameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning\nwere accepted to\nACL 2025\n.\n[2025/05] One paper about\nEfficient Large Language Model\nwas accepted to\nICML 2025\n.\n[2025/02] One paper about\nMultimodal Large Language Model\nwas accepted to\nCVPR 2025\n.\n[2024/11] One paper about\nLarge Language Model Evaluation\nwas accepted to\nCOLING 2025\n.\n[2024/11] One paper about\nText-Video Retrieval\nwas accepted to\nKDD 2025\n.\n[2024/09] One paper about\nEfficient Large Language Model\nwas accepted to\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\n[2024/05] Two papers about\nEfficient\nand\nLong-Context\nLanguage Model\nwere accepted to\nACL 2024\n.\n[2023/03]\n文心一言\n(a.k.a. ERNIE-Bot), Baidu's Knowledge-Enhanced Large Language Model, was eleased.\n[2023/02] One paper (\nERNIE-ViLG 2.0\n) about\nText-to-Image Generation\nwas accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n.\n[2023/01] One paper about\nInformation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nWWW 2023\n.\n[2022/10] Two papers about\nInformation Extraction\nand\nDocument Intelligence (\nERNIE-Layout\n)\nwere accepted to\nEMNLP 2022\n.\n[2022/07] One paper about\nDocument Intelligence\nwas accepted to\nMM 2022\n.\n[2022/02] One paper about\nLanguage Model\nwas accepted to\nACL 2022\n.\n[2021/08] One paper about\nNamed Entity Recognition\nwas accepted to\nEMNLP 2021\n.\n[2021/06] One paper about\nRelation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nECML/PKDD 2021\n.\n[2021/05] One paper about\nRelation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nACL 2021\n.\n[2021/01] One paper about\nInformation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nWWW 2021\n.\n[2020/09] Two papers about\nRelation Extraction\nwere accepted to\nCOLING 2020\n.\n[2020/09] Two papers about\nNamed Entity Recognition\nand\nEvent Extraction\nwere accepted to\nEMNLP 2020\n.\n[2020/05] One paper about\nRelation Extraction\nwas won the\nBest Paper Award\nof\nPAKDD 2020\n.\n[2020/01] One paper about\nEntity Linking\nwas accepted to\nWWW 2020\n.\n[2019/11] One paper about\nRelation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nAAAI 2020\n.\n[2019/05] One paper about\nRelation Extraction\nwas accepted to\nIJCAI 2019\n.\n[2019/01] One paper about\nEntity Linking\nwas accepted to\nWWW 2019\n.\nSelected Publications ->\nFull Publication List\nBlink: Dynamic Visual Token Resolution for Enhanced Multimodal Understanding\nYuchen Feng\n¡*\n,\nZhenyu Zhang\n*\n, Naibin Gu, Yilong Chen, Peng Fu, Zheng Lin, Shuohuan Wang, Yu Sun, Hua Wu, Weiping Wang, Haifeng Wang\nThe IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition 2026 (\nCVPR 2026\n)\nHFT: Half Fine-Tuning for Large Language Models\nTingfeng Hui\n¡\n,\nZhenyu Zhang\n†\n, Shuohuan Wang, Yu Sun, Weiran Xu, Hua Wu\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL 2025\n)\nUpcycling Instruction Tuning from Dense to Mixture-of-Experts via Parameter Merging\nTingfeng Hui\n¡\n,\nZhenyu Zhang\n†\n, Shuohuan Wang, Yu Sun, Hua Wu, Sen Su\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL 2025\n)\nBeamLoRA: Beam-Constraint Low-Rank Adaptation\nNaibin Gu\n*¡\n,\nZhenyu Zhang\n*\n, Xiyu Liu, Peng Fu, Zheng Lin, Shuohuan Wang, Yu Sun, Hua Wu, Weiping Wang, Haifeng Wang\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL 2025\n)\nERNIE-ViLG 2.0: Improving Text-to-Image Diffusion Model with Knowledge-Enhanced Mixture-of-Denoising-Experts\nZhida Feng\n*¡\n,\nZhenyu Zhang\n*\n, Xintong Yu\n*\n, Yewei Fang, Lanxin Li, Xuyi Chen, Yuxiang Lu, Jiaxiang Liu, Weichong Yin, Shikun Feng, Yu Sun, Li Chen, Hao Tian, Hua Wu, Haifeng Wang\nThe IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition 2023 (\nCVPR 2023\n)\nLearning Structural Co-occurrences for Structured Web Data Extraction in Low-Resource Settings\nZhenyu Zhang\n, Bowen Yu, Tingwen Liu, Tianyun Liu, Yubin Wang, Li Guo\nThe Web Conference 2023 (\nWWW 2023\n)\nLayout-Aware Information Extraction for Document-Grounded Dialogue: Dataset, Method and Demonstration\nZhenyu Zhang\n*\n, Bowen Yu\n*\n, Haiyang Yu, Tingwen Liu, Cheng Fu, Jingyang Li, Chengguang Tang, Jian Sun, Yongbin Li\nThe 30th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nMM 2022\n)\nFrom What to Why: Improving Relation Extraction with Rationale Graph\nZhenyu Zhang\n, Bowen Yu, Xiaobo Shu, Mengge Xue, Tingwen Liu, Li Guo\nThe 59th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL 2021, Findings\n)\nDistilling Knowledge from Well-informed Soft Labels for Neural Relation Extraction\nZhenyu Zhang\n, Xiaobo Shu, Bowen Yu, Tingwen Liu, Jiapeng Zhao, Quangang Li, Li Guo\nThe 34th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2020\n)\nAcademic Services\nArea Chiar (Action Editor): ACL Rolling Review (ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, COLING).\nProgram Committee Member (Reviewer): AAAI, CVPR, IJCAI, ICLR, NeurIPS, etc.\nSelected Awards\n2023. Baidu Pride. Baidu Inc..\n2022. AIDU Talent Program. Baidu Inc..\n2022. Outstanding Graduates. Beijing Municipal Education Commission.\n2021. Best Paper Award Nominee. IEEE DSC.\n2021. Pacemaker to Merit Student. University of Chinese Academy of Sciences (UCAS).\n2020. National Scholarship for Doctoral Students. Ministry of Education, China.\n2020. Best Paper Award. PAKDD.\n2017. Outstanding Graduate. Hu'nan Provincial Education Commission.\n2017. First Prize of the 3rd National College Competition on Cloud Computing. Ministry of Education, China.\n2016. Cyber Security Scholarship. Internet Development Foundation, China.\n2016. National Scholarship for Undergraduate Students. Ministry of Education, China.\n2015, 2016. Second Prize of the 8th/9th National College Student Information Security Contest. Ministry of Education, China.\n2015. Second Prize of the 2nd National College Competition on Internet of Things. Ministry of Education, China.\nWork Experiences\n2022/07-Now: Senior/Staff Algorithm Engineer at NLP Department, Baidu Inc..\n2021/02-2021/08: Research Intern at DAMO Academy, Alibaba Group.\n2018/02-2018/06: Research Intern at AI Lab, Xiaomi Inc.."
