    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ruida Zhou\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nRuida Zhou\nRUIDA ZHOU\nEmail:\nruida [at] g.ucla.edu\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nBiography:\nI am a postdoc doctoral scholar at the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) advised by Prof.\nSuhas Diggavi\n. I obtained my Ph.D.\nin the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Texas A&M University in 2023, advised by Prof.\nChao Tian\n, and\nmy B.E. degree in Electrical Engineering from the University of Science and Technology of China in 2018, advised by Prof.\nCong Shen\n.\nResearch:\nMy research interests lie in information theory, reinforcement learning, and optimization. I leverage tools from information theory and optimization to understand and design algorithms in machine learning and reinforcement learning with provable guarantees.\nNews\n2024/\n12\n.\nWon the Best Paper Award at Workshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS 2024.\n2024/07.\nWon the Best Paper Award at the Learn to Compress Workshop at the International Symposium on Information Theory (ISIT) 2024.\n2024/03.\nThrilled to receive\nthe\n2024 Distinguished Graduate Award Excellence in Research-Doctoral\nfrom\nTexas A&M University\nQuality Graduate Student Award from ECEN @ Texas A&M University.\n2023/08.\nStarted my new life as a Postdoc at UCLA.\n2023/0\n8\n.\nSpent a wonderful summer in Dr.\nXiaoning Qian\n'\ns lab studying\non Bayesian active learning and sampling.\n2023/04.\nReceived Quality Graduate Student Award from ECEN @ Texas A&M University.\n2022/10.\nReceived\n2020-2021\nIEEE Data Storage Best Student Paper Award\nfor paper (\nLink\n).\n2022/09.\nTwo papers have been accepted in Neurips 2022.\n2022/08.\nReceived Chevron Scholarship from ECEN @ Texas A&M University.\nHonors and Awards\nBest Paper Award\nat Workshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS 2024.\nBest Paper Award\nat the Learn to Compress Workshop @ the International Symposium on Information Theory (ISIT) 2024\nDistinguished Graduate Award Excellence in Research-Doctoral\n(\n2024\n) from\nTexas A&M University\nQuality Graduate Student Award (2023) from ECEN\n,\nTexas A&M University\n2020-2021 IEEE Data Storage Best Student Paper Award\n(\n1 paper in two years\n, 2022),\nfor the paper “Capacity-achieving private information retrieval codes from MDS-coded databases with minimum message size” in IEEE Trans. Inform. Theory 2020.\nChevron Scholarship Award (2022) from ECEN department, Texas A&M University.\nGraduate Research and Presentation Travel Award (2019, 2022),\nTexas A&M University.\nIEEE International Symposium on Information Theory Student Travel Award (2019)\nHuayu Fund Scholarship\n(2017), awarded to students with strong scientific potential, USTC.\nChina National Scholarship\n(2016), USTC.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nRuida Zhou - CV\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nRuida Zhou\nCV\nCV_Ruida_2404.pdf\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Chao Tian::https://tiangroup.engr.tamu.edu/": {
    "homepage": "https://tiangroup.engr.tamu.edu/",
    "all_emails": [
      "tian@tamu.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Dr. Chao Tian\nSkip to primary navigation\nSkip to main content\nDr. Chao Tian\nMenu\nDr. Chao TIAN\nProfessor\nFellow of IEEE\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nTexas A&M University\nEmail: chao Dot tian AT tamu DOT edu\nPhone: 979-458-7822\nAddress: ROOM 301R, WEB Building, 3128 TAMU, College Station TX\nGoogle Scholar\nAnnouncements and News\nMar. 2026: Congratulations to Yuting for passing his dissertation defense!\nJan. 2026: Yu-Shin’s first-authored paper, “OD-Stega: LLM-Based Relatively Secure Steganography via Optimized Distributions,” has been accepted by EACL 2026. Congratulations to Yu-Shin for her first NLP conference paper!\nNov. 2025: Wenyuan is selected as a winner of the ECE Departmental Poster Event (two years in a row)!\nSep. 2025: Wenyuan’s first-authored paper, “Partial Information Decomposition via Normalizing Flows in Latent Gaussian Distributions,” has been accepted by NeurIPS 2025. Congratulations to Wenyuan for his first NeurIPS paper!\nApr. 2025: Dr. Tian delivered a one-day short course on Large Language Models (with Applications in Power Systems) at Oncor Electric Delivery in Fort Worth in Apr. 2025. If your organization needs a quick introduction course on LLMs, please contact Dr. Tian directly. Please also visit\nhere\nfor information on an extended 3-day short course offered via the TAMU Smart Grid Center.\nFeb. 2025: Our paper “Transforms learn variable-order Markov chains in context” was selected to receive the Best Paper Award at the\nWorkshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS\n2024! Dr. Tian was also invited to give a plenary at\nITA 2025\non this topic.\nBiography\nDr. Tian obtained his B.E degree from Tsinghua University, Beijing China, and his M.S. and Ph.D. degrees from Cornell University, Ithaca NY. He worked at AT&T Labs-Research (previously known as the Shannon Labs) as a researcher on communication and signal processing for seven years, before returning to academia. He was with the University of Tennessee Knoxville for a few years before joining Texas A&M University, where he is now a professor. He is a Fellow of IEEE.\nAwards\nFellow of IEEE\n, class of 2026.\nBest Paper Award at Workshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS 2024\n: “Transforms learn variable-order Markov chains in context”.\nBest Paper Award at the first ‘Learn to compress’ workshop @ ISIT 2024\n: “Staggered quantizers for perfect perceptual quality: A connection between quantizers with common randomness and without”.\n2023-2024 IEEE Information Theory Society Distinguished Lecturer.\n2022 ECE Department Star Faculty Award.\nCoauthor of 2020-2021 IEEE Data Storage Best Student Paper Award (awarded in 2022)\n: “Capacity-achieving private information retrieval codes from MDS-coded databases with minimum message size” in IEEE Trans. Inform. Theory 2020.\n2019 NetApp Faculty Fellowship.\nCoauthor 2017 IEEE Jack Wolf ISIT Best Student Paper Award\n: “A generic transformation for optimal repair bandwidth and rebuilding access in MDS codes” in ISIT 2017.\n2014 IEEE Data Storage Best Paper Award\n: “Characterizing the rate-region of the (4,3,3) exact-repair regenerating codes” in IEEE JSAC May 2014.\nAT&T Key Contributor Award\n: For technical contribution in AT&T / 2010, 2011, 2013.\nLiu-Memorial Award, Cornell University\n: For excellence in graduate study and research / 2004.\nGroup Members\nCurrent Students\nYuting CAI\nYu-Shin HUANG\nMohammad RAHIMI\nWenyuan ZHAO\nAlumni\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nTao GUO, ECE, TAMU, Dec. 2018-Apr. 2020; now Associate Professor at Southeast University, China.\nPh.D. Students\nKai ZHANG, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU, May 2020; now with Amazon Inc.\nTianli ZHOU, Ph.D. degree CE/TAMU, May 2020; now with Google Inc.\nRuida ZHOU, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU, Aug. 2023; now with Amazon AGI.\nAli MENATI, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU (co-advised with Dr. Le Xie), May 2025.\nMaster Students\nSara MOUSAVI, CS Master degree, UTK, Dec. 2017; obtained her CS Ph.D. degree at UTK and now with Meta Inc.\nVineet GARG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2019; now with Apple Inc.\nSiqi FAN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; obtained his CE Ph.D. degree and now with Goldman Sacks.\nJianfeng SONG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; obtained his CE Ph.D. degree and now with Siemens Digital Industries Software, Inc.\nRachel YEH, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; now with Michaels, Inc.\nLizi ZHANG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2020.\nTianrui CHEN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2021; currently a Ph.D. student at Northwestern Polytechnical University China.\nWenjing CHEN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2022; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nChandra Sekhar TEDLA, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2023; currently with Aira Techonologies Inc.\nTianle ZHANG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2024; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nPeter JUST, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2025.\nVisiting Students\nChengyuan QIAN, Jun. 2021-Apr. 2022; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nMin CHENG, Aug. 2019-Dec. 2019, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, University of Science and Technology of China; obtained her CE Ph.D. degree from TAMU 2025 and now with Amazon Inc.\nZekuan ZHANG, Jul. 2019-Sep. 2019, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, Southeast University (China).\nWenjing CHEN, Jul. 2018-Oct. 2018, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, University of Science and Technology of China.\nLei ZHENG, Oct. 2017-Apr. 2019, TAMU visiting Ph.D. student, Southwest Jiaotong University; currently Assistant Professor at Guangzhou University, China.\nJie LI, UTK visiting Ph.D. student, Oct. 2015-Oct. 2016, Southwest Jiaotong University; now as Senior Researcher at Huawei Technology, Hong Kong.\nTeaching\nTexas A&M University\nECEN 601: Mathematical Methods for Signal Processing / Fall 2022-2023\nECEN 689: Advanced Optimization Techniques and Analysis / Spring 2022, 2024\nECEN 629: Applied Convex Optimization / Spring 2018-2021, 2023, Fall 2025\nECEN 446: Information Theory, Inference, and Learning / Spring 2018, Fall 2018, 2020-2023, 2025\nECEN 681: Department Seminar Series / Fall 2019, Spring 2020, Fall 2020\nECEN 314: Signal and Systems / Fall 2019, Spring 2026\nECEN 681: ISS Seminar Series / Fall 2017, Spring 2018, Fall 2018\nThe University of Tennessee Knoxville\nECE 611: Convex Optimization / Fall 2016\nECE 342: Fundamentals of Communication / Spring 2016, Spring 2017\nECE 644: Codng and Information Theory / Fall 2015\nECE 342: Analog Communication, AM and FM / Fall 2014, Spring 2015\nColumbia University\nELEN E6884: Topics in Data Compression / Spring 2011\nELEN E6718: Algebraic Coding Theory / Fall 2011, 2012, 2013\nELEN E6712: Communication Theory / Spring 2013\nEcole Polytechnique Federale de Lausanne\nIC-62: Source Coding Theory and Practice / Winter 2006\nEditorships and Services\nEditorship\nLead Guest Editor for IEEE Journal on Selected Areas in Information Theory (JSAIT) on Data Compression: Classical Theories Meet Modern Advances / 2026-\nLead Guest Editor for IEEE BITS Magazine (IEEE Information Theory Magazine) on Data Compression and Machine Learning / 2024-\nGuest Editor for IEEE Selected Areas on Communications-Special Issue on Rethinking the Information Identification, Representation, and Transmission Pipeline: New Approaches to Data Compression and Communication / 2023-2024\nEditor for IEEE BITS Magazine (IEEE Information Theory Magazine) / 2024-\nGuest Editor for IEEE Journal on Selected Areas in Information Theory (JSAIT) on Distributed Coding and Computation / 2021-2022\nGuest Editor for Entropy–Special Issue on Information Theory and Machine Learning / 2021\nGuest Editor for IEEE Selected Areas on Communications-Special Issue on Private Information Retrieval, Private Coded Computing over Distributed Servers, and Privacy in Distributed Learning / 2020-2021\nAssociate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Information Theory / Jan. 2020-Jan. 2023\nGuest Editor for Entropy–Special Issue on Information and Coding for Distributed Storage / 2018-2019\nGuest Editor for Science China–Special Issue on Distributed Storage Coding / 2018\nEditor of IEEE Transactions on Communications / Jan. 2016-Jan. 2021\nAssociate Editor of IEEE Signal Processing Letters / Feb. 2012-Feb. 2014\nServices\nIEEE Information Theory Society Secretary / 2025-\nIEEE Information Theory Society Conference Committee Member / 2024-\nIEEE Information Theory Society Paper Award Committee Member / 2023-2024\nIEEE Communication Society Data Storage Paper Award Committee Co-chair / 2018\n\n---\n\nDr. Chao Tian\nSkip to primary navigation\nSkip to main content\nDr. Chao Tian\nMenu\nDr. Chao TIAN\nProfessor\nFellow of IEEE\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nTexas A&M University\nEmail: chao Dot tian AT tamu DOT edu\nPhone: 979-458-7822\nAddress: ROOM 301R, WEB Building, 3128 TAMU, College Station TX\nGoogle Scholar\nAnnouncements and News\nMar. 2026: Congratulations to Yuting for passing his dissertation defense!\nJan. 2026: Yu-Shin’s first-authored paper, “OD-Stega: LLM-Based Relatively Secure Steganography via Optimized Distributions,” has been accepted by EACL 2026. Congratulations to Yu-Shin for her first NLP conference paper!\nNov. 2025: Wenyuan is selected as a winner of the ECE Departmental Poster Event (two years in a row)!\nSep. 2025: Wenyuan’s first-authored paper, “Partial Information Decomposition via Normalizing Flows in Latent Gaussian Distributions,” has been accepted by NeurIPS 2025. Congratulations to Wenyuan for his first NeurIPS paper!\nApr. 2025: Dr. Tian delivered a one-day short course on Large Language Models (with Applications in Power Systems) at Oncor Electric Delivery in Fort Worth in Apr. 2025. If your organization needs a quick introduction course on LLMs, please contact Dr. Tian directly. Please also visit\nhere\nfor information on an extended 3-day short course offered via the TAMU Smart Grid Center.\nFeb. 2025: Our paper “Transforms learn variable-order Markov chains in context” was selected to receive the Best Paper Award at the\nWorkshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS\n2024! Dr. Tian was also invited to give a plenary at\nITA 2025\non this topic.\nBiography\nDr. Tian obtained his B.E degree from Tsinghua University, Beijing China, and his M.S. and Ph.D. degrees from Cornell University, Ithaca NY. He worked at AT&T Labs-Research (previously known as the Shannon Labs) as a researcher on communication and signal processing for seven years, before returning to academia. He was with the University of Tennessee Knoxville for a few years before joining Texas A&M University, where he is now a professor. He is a Fellow of IEEE.\nAwards\nFellow of IEEE\n, class of 2026.\nBest Paper Award at Workshop on Machine Learning and Compression @ NeurIPS 2024\n: “Transforms learn variable-order Markov chains in context”.\nBest Paper Award at the first ‘Learn to compress’ workshop @ ISIT 2024\n: “Staggered quantizers for perfect perceptual quality: A connection between quantizers with common randomness and without”.\n2023-2024 IEEE Information Theory Society Distinguished Lecturer.\n2022 ECE Department Star Faculty Award.\nCoauthor of 2020-2021 IEEE Data Storage Best Student Paper Award (awarded in 2022)\n: “Capacity-achieving private information retrieval codes from MDS-coded databases with minimum message size” in IEEE Trans. Inform. Theory 2020.\n2019 NetApp Faculty Fellowship.\nCoauthor 2017 IEEE Jack Wolf ISIT Best Student Paper Award\n: “A generic transformation for optimal repair bandwidth and rebuilding access in MDS codes” in ISIT 2017.\n2014 IEEE Data Storage Best Paper Award\n: “Characterizing the rate-region of the (4,3,3) exact-repair regenerating codes” in IEEE JSAC May 2014.\nAT&T Key Contributor Award\n: For technical contribution in AT&T / 2010, 2011, 2013.\nLiu-Memorial Award, Cornell University\n: For excellence in graduate study and research / 2004.\nGroup Members\nCurrent Students\nYuting CAI\nYu-Shin HUANG\nMohammad RAHIMI\nWenyuan ZHAO\nAlumni\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nTao GUO, ECE, TAMU, Dec. 2018-Apr. 2020; now Associate Professor at Southeast University, China.\nPh.D. Students\nKai ZHANG, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU, May 2020; now with Amazon Inc.\nTianli ZHOU, Ph.D. degree CE/TAMU, May 2020; now with Google Inc.\nRuida ZHOU, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU, Aug. 2023; now with Amazon AGI.\nAli MENATI, Ph.D. degree ECE/TAMU (co-advised with Dr. Le Xie), May 2025.\nMaster Students\nSara MOUSAVI, CS Master degree, UTK, Dec. 2017; obtained her CS Ph.D. degree at UTK and now with Meta Inc.\nVineet GARG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2019; now with Apple Inc.\nSiqi FAN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; obtained his CE Ph.D. degree and now with Goldman Sacks.\nJianfeng SONG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; obtained his CE Ph.D. degree and now with Siemens Digital Industries Software, Inc.\nRachel YEH, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2019; now with Michaels, Inc.\nLizi ZHANG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2020.\nTianrui CHEN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2021; currently a Ph.D. student at Northwestern Polytechnical University China.\nWenjing CHEN, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2022; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nChandra Sekhar TEDLA, ECE Master degree, TAMU, May 2023; currently with Aira Techonologies Inc.\nTianle ZHANG, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2024; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nPeter JUST, ECE Master degree, TAMU, Dec. 2025.\nVisiting Students\nChengyuan QIAN, Jun. 2021-Apr. 2022; currently pursuing Ph.D. degree at TAMU.\nMin CHENG, Aug. 2019-Dec. 2019, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, University of Science and Technology of China; obtained her CE Ph.D. degree from TAMU 2025 and now with Amazon Inc.\nZekuan ZHANG, Jul. 2019-Sep. 2019, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, Southeast University (China).\nWenjing CHEN, Jul. 2018-Oct. 2018, TAMU visiting undergraduate student, University of Science and Technology of China.\nLei ZHENG, Oct. 2017-Apr. 2019, TAMU visiting Ph.D. student, Southwest Jiaotong University; currently Assistant Professor at Guangzhou University, China.\nJie LI, UTK visiting Ph.D. student, Oct. 2015-Oct. 2016, Southwest Jiaotong University; now as Senior Researcher at Huawei Technology, Hong Kong.\nTeaching\nTexas A&M University\nECEN 601: Mathematical Methods for Signal Processing / Fall 2022-2023\nECEN 689: Advanced Optimization Techniques and Analysis / Spring 2022, 2024\nECEN 629: Applied Convex Optimization / Spring 2018-2021, 2023, Fall 2025\nECEN 446: Information Theory, Inference, and Learning / Spring 2018, Fall 2018, 2020-2023, 2025\nECEN 681: Department Seminar Series / Fall 2019, Spring 2020, Fall 2020\nECEN 314: Signal and Systems / Fall 2019, Spring 2026\nECEN 681: ISS Seminar Series / Fall 2017, Spring 2018, Fall 2018\nThe University of Tennessee Knoxville\nECE 611: Convex Optimization / Fall 2016\nECE 342: Fundamentals of Communication / Spring 2016, Spring 2017\nECE 644: Codng and Information Theory / Fall 2015\nECE 342: Analog Communication, AM and FM / Fall 2014, Spring 2015\nColumbia University\nELEN E6884: Topics in Data Compression / Spring 2011\nELEN E6718: Algebraic Coding Theory / Fall 2011, 2012, 2013\nELEN E6712: ...[truncated]"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Boyu Wang::https://sites.google.com/site/borriewang/": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/site/borriewang/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Boyu Wang's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBoyu Wang's Homepage\nAbout Me\nI am an\nassociate\nprofessor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat the\nUniversity of Western Ontario\n(Western University)\n, and an\naffiliated faculty member\nin\nthe\nVector Institute\n. Before joining Western, I was a postdoc at the\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n, with\nEric Eaton\n, and\nPrinceton University\n, with\nKenneth Norman\n. Before that, I\nreceived my\nPh.D\ndegree from\nMcGill University\nunder the supervision of\nJoelle Pineau\n, my\nM.Sc. degree from the\nUniversity of\nMacau\nunder the supervision of Dr.\nFeng Wan\n, and my B.Eng. degree\nfrom\nTianjin University\n. Currently, I am primarily working on\ntrustworthy machine learning\n, which is essential for building an intelligent agent in the real world with any amount of versatility. On the application side, I am interested in applying these techniques to\ncomputer vision/graphics, natural language processing, biomedical engineering, neuroscience, etc\n.\nNews\n[Jan 2026] Four papers have been accepted by ICLR 2026. Congrats to all the authors!\n[Jan 2026] I serve as an Associate Editor for\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (IEEE TNNLS)\n.\n[Nov 202\n5\n]\nOur collaborative project, Pin-AI, received four years of funding from NSERC and CIHR as part of the Canada-France artificial intelligence program.\n[Nov 202\n5\n] I will serve as an Area Chair for ICML 202\n6\n.\n[\nNov\n202\n5\n]\nThree\npapers from our group have been accepted by AAAI 202\n6\n. Congrats to\nHao and Ruiyi\n!\n[Oct 2025]\nI serve as an\nAction\nEditor for\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR)\n.\n[\nOct\n2025]\nRuizhi Pu has defended his thesis and\nwill be joining\nSoutheast\nUniversity as a\nn\nassistant professor. Congrats to\nRuizhi\n!\n[Sep 2025] One paper from our group has been accepted by NeurIPS 2025. Congrats to Zhihao and Jiale, both first-year PhD students.\n[Aug 2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\n[Aug 2025] I will serve as an Area Chair for AISTATS 2026.\n[Jun 2025] One paper has been accepted by Bernoulli. Congrats to Hui!\n[May 2025] Two\npapers from our group ha\nve\nbeen accepted\nby\nICML 202\n5\n. Congrats to\nRuiyi and Ganyu\n!\n[Apr 2025]\nOne paper has been accepted by\nIJCAI 2025\n. Congrats to Pengcheng!\n[Apr 2025]\nOne paper has been accepted by\nTMLR\n. Congrats to\nPengcheng and Li\n!\n[Feb 2025] Two papers\nfrom our group have been accepted by\nCVPR\n2025. Congrats to Pengcheng and Hao!\n[\nFeb\n202\n5\n] I will serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 202\n5\n.\n[Feb 2025]\nOne paper [\n1\n] has been accepted\nby\nIEEE TPAMI. Congrats to\nYuting\n!\n[Jan 2025] One paper [\n1\n] has been accepted by IEEE TPAMI. Congrats to Gezheng and Li!\n[\nJan\n202\n5\n] Four papers [\n1\n,\n2\n,\n3\n,\n4\n] from our group have been accepted by\nICLR\n2025. Congrats to\nRuiyi\n,\nGezheng, Hui\n, Qiuhao, and\nGanyu\n!\n[Jan 2025]\nChangjian Shui\nwill be joining the University of Ottawa as an assistant professor. Congrats to Changjian!\n[\nDec\n2024] I serve as an\nAction Editor\nfor\nNeural Networks\n.\n[Dec 2024] Four papers\n[\n1\n,\n2\n,\n3\n,\n4\n]\nfrom our group have been accepted\nby\nAAAI 2025. Congrats to Ruizhi, Pengcheng, Hao, and Maxwell!\n[\nNov\n2024] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nICML\n2025.\n[Sep 2024] Two papers from our group have been accepted\nby\nNeurIPS 2024. Congrats to Qiuhao and Hui!\n[Sep 2024] I will\nserve as\nan Area Chair for AISTATS 2025.\n[Aug 2024] I will serve as\nan Area Chair for\nICLR\n2025.\n[May 2024] One\npaper from our group ha\ns\nbeen accepted by\nICML\n2024.\nCongrats to Gezheng!\n[\nApr\n2024] I will serve as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS\n202\n4\n.\n[Apr 2024]\nOne paper from our group has been accepted by\nIJCAI\n2024. Congrat\ns to Nima!\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nBoyu Wang's Homepage - Contact\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBoyu Wang's Homepage\nContact\nDepartment of Computer Science\nMiddlesex College, Room 366\nUniversity of Western Ontario\nLondon, ON, Canada, N6A 5B7\nTel: 519-661-2111 ext. 86856\nE-mail:\nbwang\n\"at\"\ncsd.uwo.ca\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nBoyu Wang's Homepage - Contact\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBoyu Wang's Homepage\nContact\nDepartment of Computer Science\nMiddlesex College, Room 366\nUniversity of Western Ontario\nLondon, ON, Canada, N6A 5B7\nTel: 519-661-2111 ext. 86856\nE-mail:\nbwang\n\"at\"\ncsd.uwo.ca\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zhuo Chen::https://chord-chen-30.github.io/": {
