    "homepage_text": "Zhenyi Wang\nSearch\nZhenyi Wang\nPh.D.\nState Key Laboratory of Internet of Things for Smart City\nUniversity of Macau\nBiography\nI am Zhenyi Wang (王臻懿), currently a Ph.D. at the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering,\nUniversity of Macau (UM)\n. I am also a member of Smart Energy Group in\nState Key Laboratory of Internet of Things for Smart City (SKL-IOTSC)\n, and the awardee of SKL-IOTSC-funded Studentship. At UM, I am supervised by\nProf. Hongcai Zhang\n, focusing on demand response and trustworthy AI.\nFrom August 2024 to February 2025, I served as a visiting student researcher with the Department of Electrical Engineering (ESAT) at KU Leuven, advised by\nProf. Geert Deconinck\n.\nBefore joining UM, I earned my B.E. degree in cybersecurity from Sichuan University in 2021, advised by\nProf. Beibei Li\non smart grid security and anomaly detection.\nDownload my\nCV\n.\nInterests\nDemand Response\nElectricity Market\nCausal Inference in AI\nTrustworthy and Data-Centric AI\nCyber Physical Systems Security\nEducation\nPh.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Aug. 2021 - June 2025\nUniversity of Macau\nVisiting Student Researcher in Electrical Engineering, Aug. 2024 - Feb. 2025\nKU Leuven\nB.E. in Cybersecurity, Sept. 2017 - July 2021\nSichuan University\nNews\nMay 12, 2025\n: Excited beyond words!\nI successfully defended my doctoral thesis.\nSincere thanks to my supervisor, PhD committee, family, and friends for the generous support and help throughout this wonderful doctoral odyssey. Stay hungry, Stay foolish!\nMar. 18, 2025\n: Congratulations! Our paper “A Unified Model for Smart Meter Data Applications” has been accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n.\nOct. 18, 2024\n: I will present my Ph.D. work as a finalist at Ph.D. Dissertation Challenge in\n2025 IEEE Power & Energy Society (PES) Grid Edge Technologies Conference & Exposition\nheld Jan. 21-23 2025 in San Diego, CA. Welcome to drop by my talk.\nAug. 27, 2024\n: Congratulations! Our paper “Improving Model Generalization for Short-Term Customer Load Forecasting with Causal Inference” has been accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n.\nMay 16, 2024\n: I have passed the Qualifying Examination (QE) and Thesis Proposal Assessment (TPA), and became a Ph.D. candidate. Keep working hard!\nMar. 25, 2024\n: I will visit the\nElectrical Energy Systems and Applications\ngroup at KU Leuven from Aug. 2024 and work with\nProf. Geert Deconinck\n.\nFeb. 22, 2024\n: Congratulations! Our paper “When Pre-Training Model Meets Smart Meter Data Applications: A Preliminary Trial of General Way” has been accepted by\n2024 IEEE Power & Energy Society General Meeting (PESGM)\n. I will give the oral presentation at 2024 IEEE PESGM held July 21–25 2024 in Seattle, Washington.\nFeb. 8, 2024\n: Congratulations! Our paper “Customized Load Profiles Synthesis for Electricity Customers Based on Conditional Diffusion Models” has been accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n.\nDec. 21, 2023\n: Congratulations! Our paper “Customer Baseline Load Estimation for Virtual Power Plants in Demand Response: An Attention Mechanism-Based Generative Adversarial Networks Approach” has been accepted by\nApplied Energy\n.\nDec. 19, 2022\n: Congratulations! Our paper “Privacy-Preserving Regulation Capacity Evaluation for HVAC Systems in Heterogeneous Buildings Based on Federated Learning and Transfer Learning” has been accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n.\nNov. 13, 2022\n: Great news! We have received the\nBest Paper Award\nat\nthe 6th IEEE Conference on Energy Internet and Energy System Integration (EI2)\n. Check the\nnews\n!\nSept. 20, 2022\n: Congratulations! Our paper “Consumer Baseline Load Estimation in Demand Response: A Generative Adversarial Networks Approach” has been accepted by\nthe 6th IEEE Conference on Energy Internet and Energy System Integration (EI2)\n. I will give the oral presentation at IEEE EI2 2022 held Nov. 11–13, 2022 in Chengdu, China.\nOct. 21, 2021\n: Great news! We have won the\nFirst Prize\nand the only\nBest Innovation Award\nat\nthe 2021 Contest of AI Application in Power Dispatching\norganized by China Southern Power Grid. Check the\nnews\n!\nAug. 2, 2021\n: I am going to start my Ph.D. study career at University of Macau. Good luck to me!\nPublications\nJournal Papers (with Preprints)\nZhenyi Wang\n, Hongcai Zhang, Geert Deconinck, and Yonghua Song, “A Unified Model for Smart Meter Data Applications,”\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n, vol. 16, no. 3, pp. 2451–2463, 2025.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nZhenyi Wang\n, Hongcai Zhang, Ruixiong Yang, and Yong Chen, “Improving Model Generalization for Short-Term Customer Load Forecasting With Causal Inference,”\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n, vol. 16, no. 1, pp. 424–436, 2025.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nPeipei Yu,\nZhenyi Wang\n, Hongcai Zhang, and Yonghua Song, “Safe Reinforcement Learning for Power System Control: A Review,”\narXiv preprint\n, pp. 1–22, 2024.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nZhenyi Wang\n, and Hongcai Zhang, “Customized Load Profiles Synthesis for Electricity Customers Based on Conditional Diffusion Models,”\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n, vol. 15, no. 4, pp. 4259–4270, 2024.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nZhenyi Wang\n, and Hongcai Zhang, “Customer Baseline Load Estimation for Virtual Power Plants in Demand Response: An Attention Mechanism-Based Generative Adversarial Networks Approach,”\nApplied Energy\n, vol. 357, p. 122544, 2024.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nZhenyi Wang\n, Peipei Yu, and Hongcai Zhang, “Privacy-Preserving Regulation Capacity Evaluation for HVAC Systems in Heterogeneous Buildings Based on Federated Learning and Transfer Learning,”\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\n, vol. 14, no. 5, pp. 3535–3549, 2023.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nYiding Wang,\nZhenyi Wang\n, Chenghao Li, Yilin Zhang, and Haizhou Wang, “Online Social Network Individual Depression Detection using A Multitask Heterogenous Modality Fusion Approach,”\nInformation Sciences\n, vol. 609, pp. 727–749, 2022.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nConference Papers\nZhenyi Wang\n, Hongcai Zhang, Baorong Zhou, Wenmeng Zhao, and Tian Mao, “When Pre-Training Model Meets Smart Meter Data Applications: A Preliminary Trial of General Way,”\n2024 IEEE Power & Energy Society General Meeting (PESGM)\n, Seattle, WA, USA, 2024, pp. 1–5.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nZhenyi Wang\n, and Hongcai Zhang, “Consumer Baseline Load Estimation in Demand Response: A Generative Adversarial Networks Approach”\n2022 IEEE 6th Conference on Energy Internet and Energy System Integration (EI2)\n, Chengdu, China, 2022, pp. 1723–1728.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nYiding Wang,\nZhenyi Wang\n, Chenghao Li, Yilin Zhang, and Haizhou Wang, “A Multimodal Feature Fusion-Based Method for Individual Depression Detection on Sina Weibo,”\n2020 IEEE 39th International Performance Computing and Communications Conference (IPCCC)\n, Austin, TX, USA, 2020, pp. 1–8.\nPDF\nDOI\nCite\nExperience\nResearch Intern\nGuangdong Grid Co, China Southern Power Grid\nMar 2022 –\nMay 2021\nGuangzhou, China\nParticipated as a key member in the project about capacity evaluation in incentive-based demand response.\nResearch Assistant\nZhuhai UM Science & Technology Research Institute\nMar 2021 –\nJun 2021\nZhuhai, China\nParticipated in the project about offshore wind power, responsible for data processing and modeling.\nAcademic Services\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid\nIEEE Transactions on Power Systems\nIEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics\nIEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security\nIEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing\nIEEE Transactions on Industry Applications\nIEEE Power Engineering Letters\nJournal of Modern Power Systems and Clean Energy\nApplied Soft Computing\nIET Smart Grid\nSustainable Energy Technologies and Assessments\nSecurity and Communication Networks\nConference Reviewer\nIEEE Power & Energy Society General Meeting (PESGM 2024, 2025)\nIEEE Global Communications Conference (GLOBECOM 2024)\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024, 2025)\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2025)\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2025)\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS 2025)\nIEEE Student Conference on Electric Machines and Systems (SCEMS 2024)\nConference Organization\nOrganizing Committee Member, IEEE Student Conference on Electric Machines and Systems (SCEMS 2024)\nContact\nzhenyi.wang@connect.um.edu.mo\nRoom 5003, N21 Research Building, University of Macau, Avenida da Universidade, Taipa, Macao, China\nWeekdays 09:00 to 18:00"
