    "homepage_text": "Heng Huang - Main\nblank\nblank\nHeng Huang\nBrendan Iribe Endowed Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nm\nm\nMAIN\nm\nPUBLICATION\nm\nTEACHING\nm\nBrief Biography:\nHeng Huang received his Ph.D. in\nComputer Science\nfrom\nDartmouth College\n, and his M.S. and B.S. from\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n. He is a Brendan Iribe Endowed Professor in Computer Science at the University of Maryland College Park.\nContact Information:\nOffice: Brendan Iribe Center for Computer Science and Engineering, IRB 3238\n8125 Paint Branch Drive, College Park, MD 20742.\nEmail:\nheng@umd.edu\nResearch Interests:\nAI and Machine Learning, Health Computing, Precision Medicine\nPlease note that all my research works are publicly available\n<!---\t\r\n\t\t\t\t<DL >\nCourse Information:\nI teach\nECE 2195 Machine Learning\nin Fall 2020.\n---!>\r\n\r\n\t\r\n<!---\r\n\t\t\t\t<DL>\nNews:\nThree papers were accepted by CVPR 2025.\nSix papers were accepted by ICLR 2025.\nOne paper was accepted by USENIX Security 2025.\nFive papers were accepted by NeurIPS 2024.\nOne paper was accepted by EMNLP 2024.\nFour papers were accepted by ECCV 2024.\nThree papers were accepted by MICCAI 2024, AISTATS 2024, FPGA 2024.\nCongratulations to Peiran Yu who will join CSE@UT Arlington as a tenure-track AP!\nEight papers were accepted by ICML 2024.\n---!>\nInformation for Future Students:\nI am looking for Postdoc, PhD students,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thighly motivated for doing research in the areas of machine learning, large-scale optimization, NLP, computer vision, bioinformatics, and biomedical image analysis. If you are interested, please contact me.\nRecent Conferences related to my research:\nICLR\n, abstract due Sep 19, full paper due Sep 24\nCVPR\n, abstract due Nov 06, full paper due Nov 13\nACL\n, full paper due Jan 5\nIJCAI\n, abstract due Jan 12, full paper due Jan 19\nISMB\n, full paper due Jan 20\nICML\n, abstract due Jan 23, full paper due Jan 28\nMICCAI\n, abstract due Feb 12, full paper due Feb 26\nECCB\n, full paper due Mar 5\nECCV\n, abstract due Feb 26, full paper due Mar 6\nNeurIPS\n, abstract due May 05, full paper due May 07\nEMNLP\n, ARR due May 25\nHow to evaluate papers in top computer science conferences\n?\nFor reference purpose, there are some reasonable public CS conference ranking lists:\nRef1\n,\nRef2\n. For CS program ranking:\nCS open rankings\n."
  },
