    "homepage_text": "Yifan Gong\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYifan Gong\nYifan Gong\nAssistant Professor of Economics\n, University of Nebraska-Lincoln\nEmail:\nygong5@unl.edu\nI am a labor economist and applied econometrician. Most of my research centers around the use of expectations data in\nthe economics of education and, more broadly, labor economics. Among other things, I study 1) how individuals make decisions based on\ntheir\nbeliefs about unknown decision-influencing factors, 2)\nhow the uncertainty about these factors is resolved, 3) detection and implications of non-rational expectations, and 4) potential measurement issues of expectations data.\nI also work on the analysis of the U.S. housing market in general equilibrium settings, using both macroeconomic and urban economic models.\nPrimary Research Fields:\nLabor Economics, Economics of Education, Applied Econometrics, Urban and Housing Economics\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
