    "homepage_text": "Xun YANG\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nXun YANG\nHomepage\nXun YANG (Ph.D)杨勋\nProfessor\nDepartment of Electronic Engineering and Information Science\nSchool of Information Science and Technology\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nEmail: xyang21 AT ustc.edu.cn\nXun Yang\nnow is a Professor in\nDepartment of Electronic Engineering and Information Science (EEIS),\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC), Hefei, C\nhina.\nHe was a research fellow in\nNExT++\n, School of Computing, National University of Singapore from 2018 to 2021. Xun received his Ph.D from\nHefei University of Technology in 2017, under the supervision of Prof.\nMeng Wang\n. His research interests include information retrieval, computer vision, and multimedia information processing. Moreover, he has served as the PC member and the invited reviewer for top-tier conferences and prestigious journals including ACM MM, ACM MMAsia, AAAI, IJCAI, IEEE TCSVT, IEEE TKDE, IEEE TNNLS, and IEEE TMM.\nAcademic Experiences:\nTenure-Track Professor\n,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n,\nNov.\n20\n21\n-\nNow\n.\nPostdoc Research Fellow\n,\nNational University of Singapore\n, April 2018 - May 2021. Advisior:\nChua Tat-Seng\n(\nNExT++: NUS-Tsinghua Extreme Search Center\n)\nVisiting Research Student\n, University of Technology Sydney, Australia, October 2015 - October 2017. Advisor:\nTao Dacheng\n(\nCAI: Centre for Artificial Intelligence\n), Supported by China Scholarship Council (CSC) Scholarship\nPublications (\nGoogle Scholar\n):\n[1]\nInterpretable Fashion Matching with Rich Attributes\n.\nXun Yang\n, Xiangnan He, Xiang Wang, Yunshan Ma, Fuli Feng, Meng Wang & Tat-Seng Chua.\nSIGIR\n2019\n(Full, Accept rate: 20%)\n[2] Learning to Match on Graph for Fashion Compatibility Modeling\n.\nXun Yang\n, Xiaoyu Du & Meng Wang.\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(AAAI), 2020\n[3] Who, Where, and What to Wear? Extracting Fashion Knowledge from Social Media. YunShan Ma,\nXun Yang\n, Lizi Liao, Yixin Cao and Tat-Seng Chua.\nACM MM 2019\n(Long Paper)\n[4] Learning Using Privileged Information for Food Recognition. Lei Meng, Long Chen,\nXun Yang\n, Hanwang Zhang, Dacheng Tao, Chunyan Miao and Tat-Seng Chua.\nACM MM 2019\n(Long Paper)\n[5]\nAnnotating Objects and Relations in User-Generated Videos\n. Xindi Shang, Donglin Di, Junbin Xiao, Yu Cao,\nXun Yang\n& Tat-Seng Chua.\nICMR\n2019 (Full)\n[6]\nTransNFCM: Translation-Based Neural Fashion Compatibility Modeling\n.\nXun Yang\n, Yunshan Ma, Lizi Liao, Meng Wang & Tat-Seng Chua.\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(AAAI), 2019\n[7]\nPerson Re-identification via Structural Deep Metric Learning\n.\nXun Yang\n, Peicheng Zhou & Meng Wang.\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n(TNNLS), 2018\n[8]\nPerson Re-identification with Metric Learning using Privileged Information\n.\nXun Yang\n, Meng Wang & Dacheng Tao.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n(TIP), 2018, 27 (2), 791-805\n[9]\nEnhancing Person Re- identification in a Self-trained Subspace\n.\nXun Yang\n, Meng Wang, Richang Hong, Qi Tian & Yong Rui.\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications\n(TOMCCAP), 2017, 13(3): 27:1-27:23\n[10]\nSaliency Detection on Light Field: A Multi-Cue Approach\n. Jun Zhang, Meng Wang, Liang Lin,\nXun Yang\n& Jun Gao.\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications\n(TOMCCAP) 13.3 (2017): 32\n[11]\nEmpirical Risk Minimization for Metric Learning Using Privileged Information\n.\nXun Yang\n, Meng Wang, Luming Zhang, Dacheng Tao.\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(IJCAI), 2016, 2266-2272\n[12]\nAn Efficient Tracking System by Orthogonalized Templates\n.\nXun Yang\n, Meng Wang, Luming Zhang, Fuming Sun & Meibin Qi.\nIEEE Transaction on Industrial Electronics\n(TIE), 2016, 63(5): 3187-3197\n[13]\nTree-Augmented Cross-Modal Encoding for Complex-Query Video Retrieval\n.\nXun Yang\n, Jianfeng Dong, Yixin Cao, Xun Wang, Meng Wang, and Tat-Seng Chua.\nSIGIR 2020.\n[14]\nDeep Neighborhood Component Analysis for Visual Similarity Modeling\n. Xueliang Liu,\nXun Yang\n, Meng Wang, Richang Hong.\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (TIST)\n, 2020, 11 (3), 1-15\n[15]\nTopic-Guided Relational Conversational Recommender in Multi-Domain\n. Lizi Liao, Ryuichi Takanobu, Yunshan Ma,\nXun Yang\n, Minlie Huang, Tat-Seng Chua.\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering. 2020\n[16]\nVisual Relation Grounding in Videos\n. Junbin Xiao, Xindi Shang,\nXun Yang\n, Sheng Tang, Tat-seng Chua.\nECCV 2020.\n(Spotlight)\n[17]\nDual Encoding for Video Retrieval by Text\n. Jianfeng Dong, Xirong Li, Chaoxi Xu,\nXun Yang\n, Gang Yang, Xun Wang, Meng Wang.\nIEEE Trans. on PAMI\n. 2021\n[18]\nInterventional video relation detection\n. Yicong Li,\nXun Yang\n, Xindi Shang, Tat-Seng Chua.\nProceedings of the 29th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM)\n.  2021, 4091-4099\n[19]\nVideo Moment Retrieval with Cross-Modal Neural Architecture Search\n.\nXun Yang\n, Shanshan Wang, Jian Dong, Jianfeng Dong, Meng Wang, Tat-Seng Chua.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n. 2022, 31, 1204-1216\nProfessional Activities:\nSenior\nProgram Committee\n(SPC) Member\nfor AAAI 2022\nArea Chair\nfor\nACM Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM) 20\n22\nAssociate Editors:\nAssociate Editor\nfor IEEE Transactions on Big Data (TBD).\n(Technical) Program Committee Member:\nACM Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM) 2019, 2020, 2021\nIEEE International Conference on CVPR 2021,\n2022\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV) 2021\nACM Conference on Multimedia Aisa (ACM MMAsia) 2019\nIEEE International Conference on Cloud Computing and Intelligence Systems (CCIS 2019)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2020, 2021)\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2020)\nIEEE International Conference on Knowledge Graph (ICKG 2020)\nGuest Editors / Organizers:\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing Communications and Applications\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\nInvited Reviewer For:\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\nIEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics\nNeurocomputing\nSignal Processing: Image Communication\nHonors and Awards:\n2016, National Scholarship for Postgraduate Students (Ph.D), China (¥30,000)\n2015, China Scholarship Council (CSC) Scholarship  (AU $1,700/month*24)\n2013, National Scholarship for Postgraduate Students (Master), China (¥20,000)\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nXun YANG - About Me\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nXun YANG\nAbout Me\nUse this page to describe yourself professionally.\nWhat do you plan to do in the future. What are you doing to achieve your goals. You may also include some of your hobbies.\nBreak up this description into two paragraphs. 100 words each paragraph.\n(include word count here)\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
