    "homepage_text": "Bo Han\nBo Han\nHome\nNews\nResearch\nResearch Group\nProfessional Service\nTeaching\nCodes & Data\nAwards & Honors\nHome\nBo Han\nAssociate Professor in Machine Learning @\nDepartment of Computer Science\nHong Kong Baptist University\nFaculty of Science\nBAIHO\nVisiting Scientist @\nImperfect Information Learning Team\nRIKEN\nCenter for Advanced Intelligence Project\n[Google Scholar]\n[Github]\n[Group Website]\n[Blog]\n[RedNote]\n[Twitter]\nE-mail: bhanml@comp.hkbu.edu.hk (for general academic work) & bo.han@a.riken.jp\nTMLR Group is always looking for\nhighly self-motivated\nPhD/RA/Visiting students and Postdoc researchers. Please read\nthis document\nfor recruiting information, browse\nlink'23\n,\nlink'24\nand\nlink'25\nfor group-wise research, and check\nthis link\nfor group information and\nthis link\nfor department information. Meanwhile, TMLR Group is happy to host remote research trainees. Due to the large number of emails we receive, we cannot respond to every email individually. Thanks!\nNews\nTMLR Group is always looking for\nhighly self-motivated\nPhD/RA/Visiting students and Postdoc researchers to work on\ntrustworthy and efficient learning and reasoning algorithms\n,\ntheories and systems\n.\nVarious types of fellowship are available for outstanding applicants, such as\nHKPFS Fellowship\nand multiple government & industry-funded fellowships.\nTMLR Group is jointly looking for visiting scholars for\nAsian Trustworthy Machine Learning (ATML) Fellowships\n[\nClass 2023\n] [\nClass 2024\n] [\nClass 2025\n].\nTMLR Group releases several papers that represent our research flavors: [\nCo-teaching\n], [\nOOD Theory\n], [\nG-effect\n], [\nCounterAnimal\n], [\nSFAT\n], [\nAR-Bench\n].\nTMLR Group releases several papers that represent our current research: [\nAlphaApollo\n], [\nCRU\n], [\nCo-rewarding\n], [\nLoT\n], [\nDeepInception\n].\nTMLR Group delivers our research perspective of trustworthy machine learning and reasoning: [\nMonograph\n], [\nSummary Paper\n], [\nPosition Paper\n].\nTMLR Group delivers our group-wise research highlights: [\nHighlights'25\n].\nTMLR Group delivers several talks that represent our group-wise research thrusts: [\nVideo'23a\n], [\nVideo'23b\n], [\nVideo'24a\n], [\nVideo'24b\n], [\nVideo'25a\n], [\nVideo'25b\n].\nFeb 2026: I am honored to deliever an invited lecture at\nEuropean Summer School on Artificial Intelligence\n2026 [\nPDF\n] [\nLink\n].\nJan 2026: I will serve as Senior Area Chair for\nICML'26\n.\nJan 2026: I am honored to become an\nACM Distinguished Speaker\n.\nDec 2025: TMLR Group will author a position paper invited by\nIEEE Intelligent Systems\n[\nPDF\n].\nOct 2025: TMLR Group is honored to co-author a definition paper with\nmany great researchers\n[\nPDF\n].\nOct 2025: TMLR Group open-sourced\nAlphaApollo\n, an agentic LLM reasoning library based on verl. Check out our\npaper\nfor details.\nSep 2025: I am honored to deliever an invited lecture at\nInternational School on Deep Learning\n2026 [\nPDF\n] [\nLink\n].\nJun 2025: I am grateful to receive tenure promotion (effective Jul 2025).\nJun 2025: TMLR Group is honored to receive 2025/26\nRGC General Research Fund\n.\nJun 2025: TMLR Group has co-organized several tutorials on\nTrustworthy Machine Learning under Imperfect Data\n[\nSlides\n] [\nVideo\n] [\nLink\n].\nMay 2025:\nQizhou\nand\nJianing\nsuccessfully defended their PhD Theses. Congratulations to TMLR's newly supervised Dr. Wang and Dr. Zhu!\nMay 2025: TMLR Group is honored to receive\nINNS Aharon Katzir Young Investigator Award\n2024 [\nNews\n].\nApr 2025: TMLR Group will present \"Exploring Trustworthy Foundation Models: Benchmarking, Finetuning, and Reasoning\" [\nSlides\n] [\nVideo\n].\nMar 2025: I will serve as Session Chair of\nOral Efficient Transformer Optimization\nand\nMentor Committee\nfor\nICLR'25\n.\nJan 2025: TMLR Group is honored to receive 2024/25\nRGC Young Collaborative Research Grant\n[\nNews\n].\nDec 2024: I will serve as Session Chair of\nOral Machine Learning and Science, Safety\nfor\nNeurIPS'24\n.\nDec 2024: I will serve as Program Co-Chair for\nACML'26\n.\nNov 2024: TMLR Group is honored to receive\nIEEE AI's 10 to Watch Award\n2024 by IEEE Intelligent Systems [\nPDF\n] [\nNews\n].\nOct 2024: TMLR Group is honored to jointly receive NeurIPS'24\nWorkshop\nOutstanding Student Paper Award\n[\nPaper\n].\nJul 2024: I will serve as Session Chairs of\nOral Labels\nand\nOral Robustness and Safety\nfor\nICML'24\n.\nJun 2024: I will serve as Associate Editor for\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nJun 2024: TMLR Group is honored to receive\nDean's Award for Outstanding Achievement\n2024.\nJun 2024: TMLR Group's research is honored to be highlighted by Faculty of Science [\nNews\n].\nMay 2024: TMLR Group is honored to receive\nIJCAI Early Career Spotlight\n2024 [\nPaper\n] [\nSlides\n] [\nPoster\n].\nMar 2024: I will serve as Senior Area Chair and Workshop Co-Chair for\nNeurIPS'24\n.\nMar 2024: TMLR Group will co-author a ML monograph invited by\nFoundations and Trends\n[\nPDF\n] [\nLink\n].\nDec 2023: I am honored to receive NeurIPS'23\nNotable Area Chair\n.\nDec 2023: I regularly serve as Area Chair for NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, UAI and AISTATS (see\nProfessional Service\n).\nOct 2023: TMLR Group will co-organize\nHKBU-RIKEN AIP Joint Workshop on AI and ML\n[\nNews\n].\nAug 2023: TMLR Group will co-author a ML monograph accepted by\nSpringer Nature\n[\nLink\n].\nAug 2023: TMLR Group's\ncollaborative work\nwith Alibaba has been deployed into its online\nadvertisement platform\n[\nNews\n].\nAug 2023: I will serve as Action Editor for\nMLJ\nand\nJAIR\nand Area Chair for\nAISTATS'24\n.\nJul 2023: TMLR Group has co-authored an interdisciplinary article published by\nNature Plants\n.\nFeb 2023: I will serve as Area Chair for\nNeurIPS'23\n.\nJan 2023: TMLR Group's\ncollaborative work\nwith Tencent achieves state-of-the-art results in\nGOOD benchmark\n.\nDec 2022: I will serve as Area Chair for\nICML'23\nand\nUAI'23\nand Publication & Publicity Co-Chair for\nACML'23\n.\nDec 2022: I will serve as Session Chair of\nFeatured Papers\nfor\nNeurIPS'22\n.\nNov 2022: TMLR Group is honored to jointly receive NeurIPS'22\nOutstanding Paper Award\n[\nPaper\n].\nAug 2022: TMLR Group will jointly organize\nOnline Asian Machine Learning School\n2022.\nAug 2022: I will join the Editorial Board of\nJMLR\nand\nMLJ\nand serve as Area Chair for\nICLR'23\n.\nMay 2022: TMLR Group is honored to jointly receive NeurIPS'18\nMost Influential Paper\n[\nPaper\n].\nFeb 2022: RIKEN Team will author a ML monograph accepted by\nMIT Press\n[\nLink\n].\nOct 2021: TMLR Group is honored to receive\nMicrosoft Research StarTrack Scholars Program\n2021 (with\nAI for Science\nteam).\nMay 2021: I am honored to receive ICLR'21\nOutstanding Area Chair\n.\nJun 2020: TMLR Group is honored to receive 2020/21\nRGC Early CAREER Scheme\n.\nMar 2020: I am honored to receive\nRIKEN BAIHO Award\n2019.\nSee more news\nhere\n.\nResearch\nMy research interests lie in machine learning, deep learning and foundation models. My long-term goal is to develop trustworthy and efficient intelligent systems (e.g.,\ntrustworthy foundation models\n), which can learn and reason from a massive volume of complex (e.g., weakly supervised, self-supervised, out-of-distribution, causal, fair, and privacy-preserving) data (e.g,\nlabel\n,\nexample\n,\npreference\n,\ndomain\n,\nsimilarity\n,\ngraph\n,\ndemonstration\n,\nrationale\n, and\nprompt\n) reliably and efficiently. Recently, I develop core machine learning methodology. Besides, I am actively applying our fundamental research into the interdisciplinary domain.\nI am heading\nTrustworthy Machine Learning and Reasoning Group\n. Our current research work center around several major themes (more information\nhere\n):\nFoundation Models and Causal Representation Learning:\n[Monograph]\n[ICLR'24]\n[ICML'24]\n[NeurIPS'24]\n[ICLR'25]\n[ICML'25]\n[ICLR'26]\nWeakly Supervised and Self-supervised Representation Learning:\n[Survey]\n[NeurIPS'18]\n[ICML'19]\n[ICML'20]\n[ICML'21]\n[ICML'22]\n[ICLR'23]\nRobustness, Security and Privacy in Machine Learning:\n[NeurIPS'22]\n[ICLR'22]\n[NeurIPS'23]\n[NeurIPS'24]\n[ICLR'25]\n[ICLR'26]\nFederated, Efficient and Graph Machine Learning:\n[ICML'20]\n[KDD'21]\n[ICML'22]\n[NeurIPS'23]\n[ICLR'24]\n[ICLR'25]\nInterdisciplinary Problems (e.g., Healthcare Analytics and AI for Science):\n[NeurIPS'22]\n[Nature Plants'23]\n[ICLR'24]\n[NeurIPS'24]\n[ICLR'25]\nSelected Projects\nRGC Young Collaborative Research Grant (PC): Towards Trustworthy Foundation Models under Imperfect Scenarios [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nRGC General Research Fund (PI): Towards Dynamic Knowledge-aware Federated Learning for Foundation Models [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nRGC Early CAREER Scheme (PI): Trustworthy Deep Learning from Open-set Corrupted Data [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nNSFC General Program (PI): The Research on Trustworthy Federated Learning in Imperfect Environments [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nNSFC Young Scientists Fund (PI): The Research on the Automated Trustworthy Machine Learning [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nGDST Basic Research Fund (PI): Trustworthy Graph Representation Learning under Out-of-distribution Data [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nGDST Basic Research Fund (PI): Trustworthy Deep Reasoning with Human-level Constraints [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nRIKEN Collaborative Research Fund (PI): New Directions in Trustworthy Machine Learning [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nRIKEN BAIHO Award (PI): Development of Robust Deep Learning Technologies for Heavily Noisy Data [\nLink\n] [\nWebsite\n]\nResearch Highlights\n(* indicates advisees/co-advisees; updating through the time; see the full list\nhere\n)\nTrustworthy Machine Learning: From Data to Models.\nB. Han\n, J. Yao, T. Liu, B. Li, S. Koyejo, and F. Liu.\nFoundations and Trends® in Privacy and Security\n, 2025, [\nPDF\n] [\nLink\n] [\nMonograph\n].\nCo-rewarding: Stable Self-supervised RL for Eliciting Reasoning in Large Language Models.\nZ. Zhang*, J. Zhu*, X. Ge, Z. Zhao, Z. Zhou*, X. Li*, X. Feng*, J. Yao, and\nB. Han\n.\nIn Proceedings of\n14th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR'26)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nBlog\n].\nFrom Passive to Active Reasoning: Can Large Language Models Ask the Right Questions under Incomplete Information?\nZ. Zhou*, X. Feng*, Z. Zhu, J. Yao, S. Koyejo, and\nB. Han\n.\nIn Proceedings of\n42nd International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'25)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nBlog\n].\nRethinking LLM Unlearning Objectives: A Gradient Perspective and Go Beyond.\nQ. Wang*, J.P. Zhou, Z. Zhou*, S. Shin,\nB. Han\n, and K.Q. Weinberger.\nIn Proceedings of\n13th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR'25)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nBlog\n].\nW-DOE: Wasserstein Distribution-agnostic Outlier Exposure.\nQ. Wang*,\nB. Han\n, Y. Liu, C. Gong, T. Liu, and J. Liu.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n, 47(5): 3530-3545, 2025, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nBlog\n].\nCan Language Models Perform Robust Reasoning in Chain-of-thought Prompting with Noisy Rationales?\nZ. Zhou*, R. Tao*, J. Zhu*, Y. Luo*, Z. Wang, and\nB. Han\n.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37 (NeurIPS'24)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nData\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nBlog\n].\nA Sober Look at the Robustness of CLIPs to Spurious Features.\nQ. Wang*, Y. Lin, Y. Chen*, L. Schmidt,\nB. Han\n, and T. Zhang.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37 (NeurIPS'24)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nData\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nBlog\n].\nOn the Learnability of Out-of-distribution Detection.\nZ. Fang, S. Li, F. Liu,\nB. Han\n, and J. Lu.\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (JMLR)\n, 25(84): 1-83, 2024, [\nPDF\n].\nCombating Exacerbated Heterogeneity for Robust Models in Federated Learning.\nJ. Zhu*, J. Yao, T. Liu, Q. Yao, J. Xu, and\nB. Han\n.\nIn Proceedings of\n11th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR'23)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n].\nLatent Class-Conditional Noise Model.\nJ. Yao,\nB. Han\n, Z. Zhou, Y. Zhang, and I.W. Tsang.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\n, 45(8): 9964-9980, 2023, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n].\nWatermarking for Out-of-distribution Detection.\nQ. Wang*, F. Liu, Y. Zhang, J. Zhang, C. Gong, T. Liu, and\nB. Han\n.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 35 (NeurIPS'22)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nSpotlight\n].\nIs Out-of-distribution Detection Learnable?\nZ. Fang, S. Li, J. Lu, J. Dong,\nB. Han\n, and F. Liu.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 35 (NeurIPS'22)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nOral, Outstanding Paper Award\n].\nCausalAdv: Adversarial Robustness through the Lens of Causality.\nY. Zhang*, M. Gong, T. Liu, G. Niu, X. Tian,\nB. Han\n, B. Schölkopf, and K. Zhang.\nIn Proceedings of\n10th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR'22)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n].\nConfidence Scores Make Instance-dependent Label-noise Learning Possible.\nA. Berthon*,\nB. Han\n, G. Niu, T. Liu, and M. Sugiyama.\nIn Proceedings of\n38th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'21)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nLong Oral\n].\nHow does Disagreement Help Generalization against Label Corruption?\nX. Yu*,\nB. Han\n, J. Yao, G. Niu, I.W. Tsang, and M. Sugiyama.\nIn Proceedings of\n36th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'19)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nLong Oral\n].\nTowards Robust ResNet: A Small Step but A Giant Leap.\nJ. Zhang*,\nB. Han\n, L. Wynter, B. Low, and M. Kankanhalli.\nIn Proceedings of\n28th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI'19)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n].\nCo-teaching: Robust Training of Deep Neural Networks with Extremely Noisy Labels.\nB. Han\n, Q. Yao, X. Yu, G. Niu, M. Xu, W. Hu, I.W. Tsang, and M. Sugiyama.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 31 (NeurIPS'18)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n] [\nMost Influential Paper\n].\nMasking: A New Perspective of Noisy Supervision.\nB. Han\n, J. Yao, G. Niu, M. Zhou, I.W. Tsang, Y. Zhang, and M. Sugiyama.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 31 (NeurIPS'18)\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nPoster\n].\nSelected Publications\n(* indicates advisees/co-advisees; see the full list\nhere\n)\nMachine Learning with Noisy Labels: From Theory to Heuristics.\nM. Sugiyama, T. Liu,\nB. Han\n, N. Lu, and G. Niu.\nAdaptive Computation and Machine Learning series\n, The MIT Press, 2026, [\nLink\n] [\nMonograph\n].\nTrustworthy Machine Learning under Imperfect Data.\nB. Han\nand T. Liu.\nComputer Science series\n, Springer Nature, 2025, [\nLink\n] [\nMonograph\n].\nTrustworthy Machine Learning: From Data to Models.\nB. Han\n, J. Yao, T. Liu, B. Li, S. Koyejo, and F. Liu.\nFoundations and Trends® in Privacy and Security\n, 2025, [\nPDF\n] [\nLink\n] [\nMonograph\n].\nA Survey of Label-noise Representation Learning: Past, Present and Future.\nB. Han\n, Q. Yao, T. Liu, G. Niu, I.W. Tsang, J.T. Kwok, and M. Sugiyama.\narXiv preprint arXiv:2011.04406\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nSurvey\n].\nAlphaApollo: A System for Deep Agentic Reasoning.\nZ. Zhou*, C. Cao*, X. Feng*, X. Li*, Z. Li*, X. Lu*, J. Yao, AlphaApollo team, B. Miranda, T. Liu, S. Koyejo, M. Sugiyama, and\nB. Han\n.\narXiv preprint arXiv:2510.06261\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nProject\n] [\nBlog\n] [\nSystem\n].\nDeepInception: Hypnotize Large Language Model to Be Jailbreaker.\nX. Li*, Z. Zhou*, J. Zhu*, J. Yao, T. Liu, and\nB. Han\n.\narXiv preprint arXiv:2311.03191\n, [\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n] [\nProject\n] [\nBlog\n] [\nNews\n] [\nDeepTech\n].\nCo-rewarding: Stable Self-supervised RL for ...[truncated]"
