    "homepage_text": "Juanhui Li\nJuanhui\nLi\nlijuanh1@msu.edu, Michigan State University\nJuanhui Li is a PhD student in the\nData Science and Engineering (DSE) lab\nat Michigan State University, under the supervision of\nDr. Jiliang Tang\n. She got a Master degree in Computer Science and technology in 2020 from Sun Yat-sen University (SYSU).\nHer current research interests include graph mining such as link prediction and knowledge graph. She’s also interested in integrating language models with graphs.\nnews\nJan 22, 2025\nOur paper\nLearning with Less: Knowledge Distillation from Large Language Models via Unlabeled Data\nhas been accepted by NACCL 2025!!!\nSep 25, 2024\nOur paper\nMixture of Link Predictors\nhas been accepted by NeurIPS 2024!!!\nJun 5, 2024\nWe released our paper\nNode-wise Filtering in Graph Neural Networks: A Mixture of Experts Approach\n!!!\nMay 28, 2024\nI’m an applied scientist intern in Amazon at Palo Alto!!!\nMay 17, 2024\nOur paper\nLPFormer: An Adaptive Graph Transformer for Link Prediction\naccepted at\nKDD 2024\n!!!\nFeb 14, 2024\nWe released our paper\nEnhancing ID and Text Fusion via Alternative Training in Session-based Recommendation\n!!\nFeb 13, 2024\nWe released our paper\nMixture of Link Predictors\n!!\nJan 16, 2024\nOur paper\nRevisiting Link Prediction: A Data Perspective\naccepted at\nICLR 2024\n!!!\nOct 24, 2023\nSo glad to recevice the NeurIPS scholar award!!\nOct 17, 2023\nWe have a new preprint paper\nAdaptive Pairwise Encodings for Link Prediction\n!\nOct 7, 2023\nOur paper ‘Distance-Based Propagation for Efficient Knowledge Graph Reasoning’ accepted at\nEMNLP 2023\n!!\nOct 1, 2023\nWe have a new preprint paper\nRevisiting Link Prediction: A Data Perspective\n!\nSep 22, 2023\nOur paper\nEvaluating Graph Neural Networks for Link Prediction: Current Pitfalls and New Benchmarking\naccepted at\nNeurIPS 2023\n!!\nSep 11, 2023\nOur paper\nLearning Representations for Hyper-Relational Knowledge Graphs\naccepted at\nASONAM 2023\n!!\nJul 9, 2023\nI’m attending the ACL 2023 at Toronto, Canada!!\nJun 23, 2023\nI’m the PC member in CIKM 2023 for long/short paper\nJun 18, 2023\nWe have a preprint paper:\nEvaluating Graph Neural Networks for Link Prediction: Current Pitfalls and New Benchmarking\nMay 1, 2023\nOur paper\nAre Graph Neural Networks Really Helpful for Knowledge Graph Completion?\naccepted at\nACL 2023\n!\nMar 31, 2023\nOur paper\nGraph Enhanced BERT for Query Understanding\naccepted at\nSIGIR 2023\n!\nYou can even add a little note about which of these is the best way to reach you.\n\n---\n\ncv | Juanhui Li\ncv\nGeneral Information\nFull Name\nJuanhui Li\nEmail\nlijuanh1@msu.edu\nEducation\n2020-present\nPhD\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering, Michigan State University, Michigan, USA (remote during 2020-2021 due to Covid-19)\n2017-2020\nM.E.\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangdong, China\n2013-2017\nB.E.\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangdong, China\nExperience\n2024.05-2024.10\nApplied Scientist Intern\nAmazon\n2020-2021\nResearch Intern\nBaidu Inc., China\n2019.10-2019.12\nVisiting Student\nDSE Lab, Michigan State University, Michigan, USA\nHonors and Awards\n2024\nICDM Female Student Award Shortlist Candidate\n2023\nNeurIPS Scholar Award\n2022\nKDD Travel Award\n2022\nWSDM Travel Award\nOther Interests\nCat\nAnime; Manga"
  },
