    "homepage_text": "LUO'S RESEARCH - Home\nLUO'S RESEARCH\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\n​Xiao LUO\nPH.D. in Microelectronics, Advisor: Prof. Yingquan Peng\nLanzhou University, CHINA\nNow as Assistant Professor in the Dalian Institute of Chemical Physics (DICP),\nWu Lab\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nResearchGate\nORCID:\n0000-0002-4069-2342\nResearcherID\n:\nAAD-7084-2019\n​​I am currently an assistant professor in DICP, CHINA. I received my B.S. in Microelectronics from Sichuan University in 2012 and my Ph.D. in Microelectronics and Solid-State Electronics from Lanzhou University in 2017, and joined Kaifeng Wu's lab at the DICP thereafter. My research focuses on excited state dynamics in hybrid organic/quantum-dot systems with applications include solar cells, luminescent solar concentrators (LSCs), light-emitting diodes (LEDs) and photodetectors. I am passionate about Science, Technology and Engineering education of all levels and dedicate to its promotion via seminars, guest lectures and outreach activities. During my research career, I am skillful in tracing the frontier of a research topic, designing my experiment, and writing research paper. I have expertise in organic electronics, device physics, plasmonics and so on. Research interests include optoelectronic device physics and structural designs, flexible electronic systems, light-matter interaction, ultrafast spectroscopy and dynamics. Up to now, I have published 40 peer-reviewed articles including in JACS, Nano Lett. Journals, with H-index=10. I am serving as a reviewer for several peer-reviewed international journals including Nano-Micro Letters, Organic Electronics, ACS Applied Materials & Interfaces, Journal of Materials Chemistry C and Journal of Molecular Structure. I have received a number of awards including the Doctoral National Scholarship, the 2017 session of Lanzhou University outstanding graduates, Merit Postgraduate Scholarship of Lanzhou University and the First Prize for the School's Annual Academic Conference.\nPlease contact me via emails:\n[email protected]\nPowered by\n通过可定制的模板创建自己独特的网站。\n入门\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - LUO'S RESEARCH\nLUO'S RESEARCH\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\nContact Me\n​If you have any questions or suggestions about my Research or Homepage, please do not hesitate to tell me, and I will improve it as soon as possible.\nDalian Institute of Chemical Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n457 Zhongshan Road, Dalian 116023,China\nXiao LUO (RA)\nTel: +86 151-9315-1014\n​E-mali:\n[email protected]\n*\nIndicates required field\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nComment\n*\nSubmit\nPowered by\n通过可定制的模板创建自己独特的网站。\n入门\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - LUO'S RESEARCH\nLUO'S RESEARCH\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\nContact Me\n​If you have any questions or suggestions about my Research or Homepage, please do not hesitate to tell me, and I will improve it as soon as possible.\nDalian Institute of Chemical Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n457 Zhongshan Road, Dalian 116023,China\nXiao LUO (RA)\nTel: +86 151-9315-1014\n​E-mali:\n[email protected]\n*\nIndicates required field\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nComment\n*\nSubmit\nPowered by\n通过可定制的模板创建自己独特的网站。\n入门\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - LUO'S RESEARCH\nLUO'S RESEARCH\nHome\nAbout\nRESEARCH\nPUBLICATIONS\nNEWS\nACADEMIC ACTIVITIES\nContact\nContact Me\n​If you have any questions or suggestions about my Research or Homepage, please do not hesitate to tell me, and I will improve it as soon as possible.\nDalian Institute of Chemical Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n457 Zhongshan Road, Dalian 116023,China\nXiao LUO (RA)\nTel: +86 151-9315-1014\n​E-mali:\n[email protected]\n*\nIndicates