  "deep_homepage::Changsheng Xu::https://nlpr.ia.ac.cn/mmc/homepage/csxu.html": {
    "homepage": "https://nlpr.ia.ac.cn/mmc/homepage/csxu.html",
    "all_emails": [
      "csxu@nlpr.ia.ac.cn",
      "csxu@csidm.sg"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Changsheng Xu\nWelcome to join us!\nCASIA\n|\nNLPR\n|\nCSIDM\nHome\nNews\nPeople\nResearch\nPublications\nResources\nRecruitment\nContact\nCHANGSHENG XU\nProfessor\nNational Lab of Pattern Recognition\nInstitute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences\n95, Zhongguancun East Road, Beijing 100190, P.R.China\nEmail: csxu at nlpr.ia.ac.cn\nExecutive Director\nChina-Singapore Institute of Digital Media\n21 Heng Mui Keng Terrace, Singapore 119613\nEmail: csxu at csidm.sg\nDr. Xu\nis a Professor in National Lab of Pattern Recognition, Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences and Executive Director of China-Singapore Institute of Digital Media. His research interests include multimedia content analysis/indexing/retrieval, pattern recognition and computer vision. He has hold 30 granted/pending patents and published over 200 refereed research papers in these areas. Dr. Xu is an Associate Editor of IEEE Trans. on Multimedia, ACM Trans. on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications and ACM/Springer Multimedia Systems Journal. He received the Best Associate Editor Award of ACM Trans. on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications in 2012 and the Best Editorial Member Award of ACM/Springer Multimedia Systems Journal in 2008. He served as Program Chair of ACM Multimedia 2009. He has served as associate editor, guest editor, general chair, program chair, area/track chair, special session organizer, session chair and TPC member for over 20 IEEE and ACM prestigious multimedia journals, conferences and workshops. He is an\nACM Distinguished Scientist\n,\nIEEE Fellow\n, and\nIAPR Fellow\n.\nProfessional Activities\nJournal Editorial Boards\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Transactions on Multimedia\nAssociate Editor, ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications\nAssociate Editor, Springer/ACM Multimedia Systems Journal\nEditorial Board, Journal of Multimedia\nEditorial Board, International Journal of Multimedia Tools and Applications\nEditorial Board, International Journal of Multimedia Intelligence and Security\nLead Guest Editor, Special Issue on Object and Event Classifications in Large-Scale Video Collections, IEEE Transactions on Multimedia\nLead Guest Editor, Special Issue on the Best Papers of ACM Multimedia 2009, ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications\nGuest Editor, Special Issue on Web-Scale Near-Duplicate Search: Techniques and Applications, IEEE Multimedia\nGuest Editor, Special Issue on Intelligent Multimedia Interactivity, Pattern Recognition Letter\nGuest Editor, Special Issue on Internet Multimedia Computing and Service, Multimedia Tools and Applications\nConference Chairs\nGeneral Chair, International Conference on Internet Multimedia Computing and Services, Chengdu, China, 1-3 Aug 2011\nProgram Chair, Pacific-Rim Conference on Multimedia, Sydney, Australia, 20-22 Dec 2011.\nProgram Chair, National Conference on Multimedia, Luoyang, China, 24-25 Sept 2010.\nProgram Chair, ACM Multimedia Conference, Beijing, China, 19-24 Oct 2009.\nProgram Chair, International Conference on Internet Multimedia Computing and Services, Kunming, China, 23-25 Nov 2009.\nGeneral Chair, Pacific-Rim Conference on Multimedia, Tainan, Taiwan, 9-13 Dec 2008.\nGeneral Chair, Asia-Pacific Workshop on Visual Information Processing, Tainan, Taiwan, 15-17 November 2007.\nProgram Chair, Asia-Pacific Workshop on Visual Information Processing, Beijing, China, 7-9 November 2006.\nSelected Publications\nJournal Papers\nT. Zhang, S. Liu,\nC. Xu\n, M. Yang, Robust Correlation Filter for Visual Tracking,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing,\n2017, accepted.\nJ. Gao, T. Zhang, X. Yang,\nC.Xu\n, Deep Relative Tracking,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing,\n2017, accepted.\nJ. Sang, Q. Fang,\nC.Xu\n, et.al., Exploiting Social-Mobile Information for Location Visualization,\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology,\n2017, 8(3): Article No.:39.\nQ. Fang,\nC.Xu\n, et.al., STCAPLRS: A Spatial-Temporal Context-Aware Personalized Location Recommendation System,\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology,\n2016, 7(4): Article No.:59.\nX. Yang, T. Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, et.al., Deep Relative Attributes,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2016, 18(9): 1832-1842.\nX. Yang, T. Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, Semantic Feature Mining for Video Event Understanding,\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications,\n2016, 12(4): 55.\nM. Yan, J. Sang,\nC.Xu\n, et.al., A Unified Video Recommendation by Cross-network User Modeling,\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications and Applications,\n2016, 12(4): 53.\nQ. Fang,\nC.Xu\n, J. Sang,  Folksonomy-based Visual Ontology Construction and Its Applications,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2016, 18(4): 702-713.\nS. Qian, T.Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, Jie Shao, Multi-Modal Event Topic Model for Social Event Analysis,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2016, 18(2): 233-246.\nQ. Fang,\nC.Xu\n, J. Sang,  Word-of-Mouth Understanding: Entity-Centric Multimodal Aspect-Opinion Mining in Social Media,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(12): 2281-2296.\nJ. Sang, Z. Deng,\nC. Xu\n,   Cross-OSN User Modeling by Homogeneous Behavior Quantification and Local Social Regularization,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(12): 2259-2270.\nC. Sun, B. Bao,\nC.Xu\n, Knowing Verb from Object: Retagging with Transfer Learning on Verb-Object Concept Images,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(10): 1747-1759.\nW. Min, B. Bao,\nC. Xu\n,   Cross-Platform Multi-Modal Topic Modeling for Personalized Inter-Platform Recommendation,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(10): 1787-1801.\nM. Yan, J.Sang,\nC.Xu\n, YouTube Video Promotion by Cross-network Association: @Britney to Advertise Gangnam style,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(8): 1248-1261.\nQ. Fang, J.Sang,\nC.Xu\n, Relational User Attribute Inference in Social Media,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(7): 1031-1044.\nZ. Yuan,\nC.Xu\n, J. Sang, S. Yan, Learning Feature Hierarchies: A Layer-wise Tag-embedded Approach,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(6): 816-827.\nW. Guo, L. Cao, T. Han,\nC.Xu\n, S. Yan, Max-Confidence Boosting with Uncertainty for Visual Tracking,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing,\n2015, 24(5): 1650-1659.\nB. Bao,\nC.Xu\n, M. Wei, Cross-Platform Emerging Topic Detection and Elaboration from Multimedia Streams,\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing Communications and Applications,\n2015, 11(4): 54.\nT.Zhang, B.Ghanem, S.Liu,\nC.Xu\n, N. Ahuja, Robust Visual Tracking via Exclusive Context Modeling,\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics,\n2015, 45(99):1-13.\nJ. Sang, T.Mei,\nC.Xu\n, Activity Sensor: Check-in Usage Mining for Local Recommendation,\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology,\n2015, 6(3): 41.\nC. Sun, T. Zhang,\nC. Xu\n,   Latent Support Vector Machine Modeling for Sign Language Recognition with Kinect,\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology,\n2015, 6(2): 20.\nC. Kang, S. Xiang, S. Liao,\nC.Xu\n, C. Pan, Learning Consistent Feature Representation for Cross-Modal Multimedia Retrieval,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(3): 370-381.\nX. Yang, T.Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, Automatic Visual Concept Learning for Social Event Understanding,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(3): 346-358.\nX. Yang, T.Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, M.Yang, Boosted Multi-Feature Learning for Cross-Domain Transfer,\nACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing Communications and Applications,\n2015, 11(3): Article 35.\nB. Bao, W. Min, T. Li,\nC. Xu\n,   Joint Local and Global Consistency on Inter-document and Inter-word Relationships for Co-clustering,\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics,\n2015, 45(1): 15-28.\nX. Yang, T.Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, Cross Domain Feature Learning in Social Multimedia,\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia,\n2015, 17(1): 64-78.\nS. Qian, T.Zhang,\nC.Xu\n, Social Event Classification via Boosted