    "homepage_text": "Jiajin Tang\nJiajin Tang   唐嘉晋\ntangjj (at) shanghaitech.edu.cn\n[GitHub]\n[Google Scholar]\nBio\nI am a PhD student (from 2021 to 2026) in\nShanghaiTech University\nadvised \r\n                    by Prof.\nSibei Yang\n.\r\n                    Previously, I obtained my Bachelor's degree from the\nSouthWest University\nin 2021.\r\n                    My research interests lie in computer vision, natural language processing, and their intersection. My current research\r\n                    focuses on Vision-Language Understanding and Large Vision-Language Models.\nNews\n2025-09\n: 1 paper are accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025! 🎉🎉🎉🎉\n2025-06\n: 4 papers are accepted by\nICCV 2025! 🎉🎉🎉🎉\nPublications\nSuperChat: Employing Super Image for Spatiotemporal Video Understanding\nIn submission 2025\nJiajin Tang\n, Sibei Yang\nDiscovering Compositional Hallucinations in LVLMs\nNeurIPS 2025\nGe Zheng,\nJiajin Tang\n, Jiaye Qian, Hanzhuo Huang, Cheng Shi, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\nClosed-Loop Transfer for Weakly-supervised Affordance Grounding\nICCV 2025\nJiajin Tang*\n, Zhengxuan Wei*, Ge Zheng, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nSim-DETR: Unlock DETR for Temporal Sentence Grounding\nICCV 2025\nJiajin Tang*\n, Zhengxuan Wei*, Yuchen Zhu, Cheng Shi, Guanbin Li, Liang Lin, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nWhy LVLMs Are More Prone to Hallucinations in Longer Responses: The Role of Context\nICCV 2025\nGe Zheng*, Jiaye Qian*,\nJiajin Tang\n, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nAugmenting Moment Retrieval: Zero-Dependency Two-Stage Learning\nICCV 2025\nZhengxuan Wei*,\nJiajin Tang*\n, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nRethinking Query-based Transformer for Continual Image Segmentation\nCVPR 2025\nYuchen Zhu*, Cheng Shi*, Dingyou Wang,\nJiajin Tang\n, Zhengxuan Wei, Yu Wu, Guanbin Li, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nPart2Object: Hierarchical Unsupervised 3D Instance Segmentation\nECCV 2024\nCheng Shi*, Yulin Zhang*, Bin Yang,\nJiajin Tang\n, Yuexin Ma, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDDCoT: Duty-Distinct Chain-of-Thought Prompting for Multimodal Reasoning in Language Models\nNeurIPS 2023\nGe Zheng*, Bin Yang*,\nJiajin Tang*\n, Hong-Yu Zhou, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nTemporal Collection and Distribution for Referring Video Object Segmentation\nICCV 2023\nJiajin Tang\n, Ge Zheng, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Project]\nCoTDet: Affordance Knowledge Prompting for Task Driven Object Detection\nICCV 2023\nJiajin Tang*\n, Ge Zheng*, Jingyi Yu, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Project]\n[Code]\nContrastive Grouping with Transformer for Referring Image Segmentation\nCVPR 2023\nJiajin Tang\n, Ge Zheng, Cheng Shi, Sibei Yang\n[Paper]\n[Code]"
