    "homepage_text": "Qiang He | Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nSkip to content\nSkip to main navigation\nReport an accessibility issue\nThe University of Tennessee, Knoxville\nToggle navigation\nMENU\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nQiang He\nProfessor\nResearch\nBiological treatment processes\nWater and wastewater quality\nEnvironmental microbiology\nRenewable energy\nEducation\nPhD in Environmental Engineering (2003), University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nMS in Biological and Agricultural Engineering (2000), Kansas State University\nBS in Biochemical Engineering (1993), East China University of Science and Technology\nPublications\nChen, S., and\nQ. He\n. 2015. \"Enrichment and specific quantification of\nMethanocalculus\nin anaerobic digestion.\"\nJ. Biosci. Bioeng.\nIn press.\nAbstract\nChen, S., and\nQ. He\n. 2015. \"Persistence of\nMethanosaeta\npopulations in anaerobic digestion during process instability.\"\nJ. Ind. Microbiol. Biotechnol.\n42(8): 1129-1137.\nAbstract\nZhang, Z., H. Li, J. Hu, X. Li,\nQ. He\n, G. Tian, H. Wang, S. Wang, and B. Wang. 2015. \"Do microorganism stoichiometric alterations affect carbon sequestration in paddy soil subjected to phosphorus input?\"\nEcol. Appl.\n25(3): 866-879.\nAbstract\nChen, S., Z. Zhu, J. Park, Z. Zhang, and\nQ. He\n. 2014. \"Development of\nMethanoculleus\n–specific real-time quantitative PCR assay for assessing methanogen communities in anaerobic digestion.\"\nJ. Appl. Microbiol.\n116(6): 1474-1481.\nAbstract\nZhang, Z., J. Shen, H. Wang, M. Liu, L. Wu, F. Ping,\nQ. He\n, H. Li, C. Zheng, and X. Xu. 2014. \"Attenuation of veterinary antibiotics in full-scale vermicomposting of swine manure via the housefly larvae (\nMusca domestica\n).\"\nSci. Rep.\n4: 6844.\nAbstract\nBowers, B. F., B. Huang,\nQ. He\n, X. Shu, X. Jia, and B. C. Miller. 2014. \"Investigation of sequential dissolution of asphalt binder in common solvents by FTIR and binder fractionation.\"\nJ. Mater.