    "homepage_text": "About me Chi Zhang’s Homepage\nChi Zhang\nPostDoc\nFollow\nChina\nTsinghua University\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nAbout me\nChi Zhang is a Postdoctoral Researcher in the\nSoftware System Security Assurance Group\nat\nTsinghua University\n, supervised by Associate Professor\nYu Jiang\n. He received his Ph.D. in 2025 from the Software Engineering Group at Nanjing University, under the supervision of Professor Linzhang Wang. In 2018, he earned dual bachelor’s degrees in Computer Science and Economics from\nSichuan University\n. From August 2022 to August 2023, he conducted research at the\nTrustworthy Engineering of Software Technologies (TEST) Lab\nat the National University of Singapore, supervised by\nManuel Rigger\n.\nHis research interests lie at the intersection of software engineering and machine learning, with a focus on static analysis, fuzzing, and integrating artificial intelligence to enhance software engineering practices. His work emphasizes detecting software bugs, and he has successfully identified nearly 80 bugs in mainstream database management systems.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV Chi Zhang’s Homepage\nChi Zhang\nPostDoc\nFollow\nChina\nTsinghua University\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nCV\nEducation\nPh.D in Version Control Theory, GitHub University, 2018 (expected)\nM.S. in Jekyll, GitHub University, 2014\nB.S. in GitHub, GitHub University, 2012\nWork experience\nSpring 2024: Academic Pages Collaborator\nGithub University\nDuties includes: Updates and improvements to template\nSupervisor: The Users\nFall 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Merging pull requests\nSupervisor: Professor Hub\nSummer 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Tagging issues\nSupervisor: Professor Git\nSkills\nSkill 1\nSkill 2\nSub-skill 2.1\nSub-skill 2.2\nSub-skill 2.3\nSkill 3\nPublications\nConstant Optimization Driven Database System Testing\nChi Zhang and Manuel Rigger. 2025. Constant Optimization Driven Database System Testing. Proc. ACM Manag. Data 3, 1 (SIGMOD), Article 24 (February 2025), 24 pages.\nStep-wise Execution of Data-Centric Systems\nChi Zhang. 2024. Step-wise Execution of Data-Centric Systems. In Companion Proceedings of the 2024 ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Systems, Programming, Languages, and Applications: Software for Humanity (SPLASH Companion’24), October 20–25, 2024, Pasadena, CA, USA. ACM, New York, NY, USA, 3 pages.\nEvaluating the Effectiveness of Deep Learning Models for Foundational Program Analysis Tasks\nQian Chen, Chenyang Yu, Ruyan Liu, Chi Zhang, Yu Wang, Ke Wang, Ting Su, and Linzhang Wang. 2024. Evaluating the Effectiveness of Deep Learning Models for Foundational Program Analysis Tasks. Proc. ACM Program. Lang. 8, OOPSLA1, Article 112 (April 2024), 29 pages.\nFinding Cross-Rule Optimization Bugs in Datalog Engines\nChi Zhang, Linzhang Wang, and Manuel Rigger. 2024. Finding Cross-Rule Optimization Bugs in Datalog Engines. Proc. ACM Program. Lang. 8, OOPSLA1, Article 98 (April 2024), 27 pages.\nPhysical Devices-Agnostic Hybrid Fuzzing of IoT Firmware\nLingyun Situ, Chi Zhang, Le Guan, Zhiqiang Zuo, Linzhang Wang, Xuandong Li, Peng Liu, and Jin Shi. 2023. Physical Devices-Agnostic Hybrid Fuzzing of IoT Firmware. IEEE Internet of Things Journal, vol. 10, no. 23, pp. 20718-20734, 1 Dec.1, 2023.\nFirmware Fuzzing: The State of the Art\nChi Zhang, Yu Wang, and Linzhang Wang. 2020. Firmware Fuzzing: The State of the Art. In 12th Asia-Pacific Symposium on Internetware (Internetware’20), May 12–14, 2021, Singapore, Singapore. ACM, New York, NY, USA, 6 pages. https://doi.org/10.1145/3457913.3457934\n物联网固件安全缺陷检测研究进展\n张弛, 司徒凌云, 王林章. 物联网固件安全缺陷检测研究进展[J]. 信息安全学报,2021,6(03):141-158.\nTalks\nFinding Cross-Rule Optimization Bugs in Datalog Engines\nOctober 24, 2024\nTalk at OOPSLA 2024, Pasadena, California, United States\nStep-wise Execution of Data-Centric Systems\nOctober 22, 2024\nTalk at SPLASH 2024 Doctoral Symposium, Pasadena, California, United States\nAutomatically Testing Datalog Engines to Find Optimization Bugs\nMarch 31, 2023\nTalk at NUS PLSE Seminar, Singapore\nInfrared: A Meta Bug Detector\nOctober 07, 2022\nTalk at NUS PLSE Seminar, Singapore\nFirmware Fuzzing: The State of the Art\nMay 13, 2021\nTalk at Internetware’2020, Online\n物联网固件安全缺陷检测研究进展\nNovember 23, 2019\nTalk at NASAC‘2019, Hangzhou, Zhejiang, China\nTeaching\nTeaching experience 2\nTeaching experience 1\nService and leadership\nCurrently signed in to 43 different slack teams"
