    "homepage_text": "Xidong Wu\nXidong Wu\nUndergraduate\nNortheast University&University of Dundee\nAbout\nCurrently, I am in the joint training program between Northeastern University School of Medicine and the University of Dundee in the UK, and I am a student majoring in Biomedical Engineering. Biomedical engineering is a highly cutting-edge and interdisciplinary field that integrates knowledge systems from multiple disciplines such as medicine, biology, and engineering. It is committed to tackling complex challenges in the healthcare field and contributing to the cause of human health. My research focuses on medical signal and image analysis, and utilizes artificial intelligence algorithms to carry out computer-aided diagnosis and treatment decision-making related work.\nThe research projects I have participated in mainly cover two directions. One is the construction of an electrocardiogram signal classification model and the deployment of embedded devices. At present, I am committed to building an open source sharing platform aimed at unifying evaluation standards, building the industry's largest benchmark, and promoting the standardization and normalization of the field of electrocardiogram signal analysis. Secondly, it is to explore the application of large-scale models such as SAM and CLIP in the field of medical imaging, including image segmentation and cross disciplinary research with genomics. By combining advanced artificial intelligence technology with medical image analysis, we expect to make breakthrough progress in precision medicine and personalized treatment, providing stronger technical support for medical diagnosis and treatment.\nPublications\nMDF: A model dispatching framework with Noise-Estimator-Centric experts for robust biosignal classification\nZhengyang Miao,\nXidong Wu\n, Liping Xie\n✳\nInternational Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing\n(ICASSP)\n[Accept]\nMultiscale feature enhanced gating network for atrial fibrillation detection\nXidong Wu\n, Mingke Yan, Renqiao Wang, Liping Xie\n✳\nComputer Methods and Programs in Biomedicine\nIF 4.8\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n[Code]\nMSCGN: Multiscale complementary gating network for time series classification\nXidong Wu\n, MingKe Yan, Haotian Tan, Dongchen Wu, Liping Xie\n✳\nBiomedical Signal Processing and Control\nIF 4.9\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\nOG-SAM: Enhancing Multi-Organ Segmentation with Organogenesis-Based Adaptive Modeling\nXidong Wu\n#\n, Hao Chen\n#\n, Zhuoyuan Li, Chao Li\n✳\nInternational Conference on Medical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention Workshop\n(Oral)\n[PDF]\n[Oral]\n[BibTeX]\nElement-wise Product Enhanced Lightweight Model for Efficient ECG Arrhythmia Detection on Embedded Devices\nHaotian Tang, MingKe Yan,\nXidong Wu\n, Hongkai Lai, Yang Zhang, Hanyu Cui, Liping Xie\n✳\nComputer Methods and Programs in Biomedicine\nIF 4.8\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\nPhysioSAug: A novel data augmentation method based on diffusion probabilistic model for disease classification using physiological signals\nHaotian Tang, Hanyu Cui,\nXidong Wu\n, Liping Xie\n✳\nEngineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence\nIF 7.5\n[Under Review]\nAdaptive Aliasing Denoising Module for Noise-Robust Time Series Classification\nXidong Wu\n#\n, Haotian Tang\n#\n, Dongchen Wu, Bojun Jiang, Hanyu Liu, Liping Xie\n✳\nEngineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence\nIF 7.5\n[Under Review]\n[Preprint]\nTime-varying and time-invariant Feature Fusion Network and Multi-Loss Openset Framework for Open-Set Recognition of ECG\nDongchen Wu\n#\n,\nXidong Wu\n#\n, Mingji Chen, Chaoqun Yu, Liping Xie\n✳\nNeural Networks\nIF 6.3\n[Under Review]\nPredicting the mechanism of pyramidal neurons in synaptic integration by high-frequency electrical stimulation and patch clamp\nXidong Wu\n✳\nThe International Conference on Modern Medicine and Global Health\n(ICMMGH)\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n#: Co-first author; ✳: Corresponding author\nHonors and Awards\nAug 2024: Northeast University third class scholarship\nMar 2024: Northeast University Innovation Individual Award\nAug 2023: Northeast University Second Class Scholarship\nEducation\nNortheastern University\nUndergraduate Course\n2022 - 2026\nUniversity of Dundee\nUndergraduate Course\n2022 - 2026\nAcademic Services\nAcademic Services\nCurrent Neuropharmacology\nReviewer\nCurrent Medical Imaging\nReviewer\nBiomedical Signal Processing and Control\nReviewer\nMICCAI 2025: CMMCA Workshop\nReviewer\nEngineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence\nReviewer\nPersonal News\n🎉\nFeb 2025:\nA feature about my research achievements and academic work was published on the\nofficial website of the School of Biomedical Engineering, Northeastern University\n.\nSkills\nTensorFlow\n,\nKeras\n,\nPytorch\n,\nPython\n,\nOverleaf\n© 2023, Xidong Wu. All rights reserved."
