    "homepage_text": "Zifan Shi\nZifan Shi\nHello! I am a research scientist at Adobe Research.\n                I obtained my PhD degree at the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), supervised by\nProf. Dit-Yan Yeung\nand\nProf. Qifeng Chen\n. \n              \n                During my PhD study, I was a visiting student researcher at Stanford University, advised by\nProf. Gordon Wetzstein\n.\n\n                Before that, I obtained a Bachelor's degree at Nanjing University.\nMy research interests include world model, generative models and 3D&4D vision.\nIf you're interested in collaborating or doing an internship with me, please don't hesitate to get in touch!\n:)\nEmail1\n/\nEmail2\n/\nGithub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\nNews\n[04/2025]:\nOne paper is accepted to SIGGRAPH TOG 2025.\n[03/2025]:\nOne paper is accepted to CVPR 2025.\n[11/2024]:\nOne papers is accepted to 3DV 2025.\n[07/2024]:\nTwo papers are accepted to ECCV 2024.\n[02/2024]:\nOne paper is accepted to CVPR 2024.\n[01/2024]:\nOne paper is accepted to ICLR 2024 (Spotlight).\n[09/2023]:\nOne paper is accepted to NeurIPS 2023 Datasets and Benchmarks Track.\n[07/2023]:\nOne paper is accepted to ICCV 2023.\n[02/2023]:\nTwo papers, with one highlight, are accepted to CVPR 2023.\n[10/2022]:\nOur survey on 3D generative models is available now.\n[09/2022]:\nOne paper is accepted to NeurIPS 2022 (Spotlight).\n[07/2022]:\nOne paper is accepted to ECCV 2022 (Oral).\n[07/2021]:\nOne paper is accepted to IROS 2021.\n[03/2021]:\nOne paper is accepted to CVPR 2021.\nPublications\n(* indicates equal contribution)\nRigAnything: Template-Free Autoregressive Rigging for Diverse 3D Assets\nIsabella Liu\n,\nZhan Xu\n,\nYifan Wang\n,\nHao Tan\n,\nZexiang Xu\n,\nXiaolong Wang\n,\nHao Su\n,\nZifan Shi\nSIGGRAPH TOG\n2025\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\nExploring Sparse MoE in GANs for Text-conditioned Image Synthesis\nJiapeng Zhu\n*,\nCeyuan Yang\n*,\nKecheng Zheng\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nYifei Zhang\n,\nQifeng Chen\n,\nYujun Shen\nCVPR\n2025\nPaper\n/\nCode\nLearning Naturally Aggregated Appearance for Efficient 3D Editing\nKa Leong Cheng\n,\nQiuyu Wang\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nKecheng Zheng\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nOuyang Hao\n,\nQifeng Chen\n,\nYujun Shen\n3DV\n2025\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\nGRM: Large Gaussian Reconstruction Model for Efficient 3D Reconstruction and Generation\nYinghao Xu\n*,\nZifan Shi*\n,\nYifan Wang\n,\nHansheng Chen\n,\nCeyuan Yang\n,\nSida Peng\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\nECCV\n2024\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nHugging Face Demo\nReal-time 3D-aware Portrait Editing from a Single Image\nQingyan Bai\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nOuyang Hao\n,\nQiuyu Wang\n,\nCeyuan Yang\n,\nXuan Wang\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nQifeng Chen\nECCV\n2024\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nHugging Face Demo\nGaussian Shell Maps for Efficient 3D Human Generation\nRameen Abdal\n*,\nYifan Wang\n*,\nZifan Shi*\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nRyan Po\n,\nZhengfei Kuang\n,\nQifeng Chen\n,\nDit-Yan Yeung\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\nCVPR\n2024\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\nDMV3D: Denoising Multi-View Diffusion using 3D Large Reconstruction Model\nYinghao Xu\n,\nHao Tan\n,\nFujun Luan\n,\nSai Bi\n,\nPeng Wang\n,\nJiahao Li\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nKalyan Sunkavalli\n,\nGordon Wetzstein\n,\nZexiang Xu\n,\nKai Zhang\nICLR\n2024\n(Spotlight Presentation)\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\nGenDeF: Learning Generative Deformation Field for Video Generation\nWen Wang\n,\nKecheng Zheng\n,\nQiuyu Wang\n,\nHao Chen\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nCeyuan Yang\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nChunhua Shen\narXiv\n2023\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\nBenchmarking and Analyzing 3D-aware Image Synthesis with a Modularized Codebase\nQiuyu Wang\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nKecheng Zheng\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nSida Peng\n,\nYujun Shen\nNeurIPS\n2023 Datasets and Benchmarks Track\nPaper\n/\nCode\nLinkGAN: Linking GAN Latents to Pixels for Controllable Image Synthesis\nJiapeng Zhu\n*,\nCeyuan Yang\n*,\nYujun Shen\n*,\nZifan Shi\n,\nDeli Zhao\n,\nQifeng Chen\nICCV\n2023\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\nLearning 3D-aware Image Synthesis with Unknown Pose Distribution\nZifan Shi\n*,\nYujun Shen\n*,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nSida Peng\n,\nYiyi Liao\n,\nSheng Guo\n,\nQifeng Chen\n,\nDit-Yan Yeung\nCVPR\n2023\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nDemo\nDiscoScene: Spatially Disentangled Generative Radiance Field for Controllable 3D-aware Scene Synthesis\nYinghao Xu\n,\nMenglei Chai\n,\nZifan Shi\n,\nSida Peng\n,\nIvan Skorokhodov\n,\nAliaksandr Siarohin\n,\nCeyuan Yang\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nHsin-Ying Lee\n,\nBolei Zhou\n,\nSergey Tulyakov\nCVPR\n2023\n(Highlight Presentation)\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nDemo\n3D Generative Models: A Survey\nZifan Shi\n*,\nSida Peng\n*,\nYinghao Xu\n*,\nAndreas Geiger\n,\nYiyi Liao\n,\nYujun Shen\narXiv\n2022\nPaper\n/\nGithub\nImproving 3D-aware Image Synthesis with A Geometry-aware Discriminator\nZifan Shi\n,\nYinghao Xu\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nDeli Zhao\n,\nQifeng Chen\n,\nDit-Yan Yeung\nNeurIPS\n2022\n(Spotlight Presentation)\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nDemo\n3D-Aware Indoor Scene Synthesis with Depth Priors\nZifan Shi\n,\nYujun Shen\n,\nJiapeng Zhu\n,\nDit-Yan Yeung\n,\nQifeng Chen\nECCV\n2022\n(Oral Presentation)\nPaper\n/\nProject Page\n/\nCode\n/\nDemo\nStereo Waterdrop Removal with Row-wise Dilated Attention\nZifan Shi\n,\nNa Fan\n,\nDit-Yan Yeung\n,\nQifeng Chen\nIROS\n2021\nPaper\n/\nCode\nNeural Camera Simulators\nOuyang Hao\n*,\nZifan Shi *\n,\nChenyang Lei\n,\nKa Lung Law\n,\nQifeng Chen\nCVPR\n2021\nPaper\n/\nCode\nExperiences\nVisiting Researcher, Stanford University\nHost by\nProf. Gordon Wetzstein\nOct 2023 - Mar 2024\nResearch Scientist Intern, Adobe\nHost by\nDr. Zhixin Shu\nMay 2023 - Aug 2023\nResearch Intern, Ant Research\nHost by\nDr. Yujun Shen\nJun. 2022 - Apr. 2023\nResearch Intern, Bytedance\nHost by\nDr. Yujun Shen\nSep. 2021 - May 2022\nSelected Awards\nNeurIPS Travel Award, 2022\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship, 2019-2023\nDong-Liang Special Scholarship, Nanjing University, 2018\nFirst Prize of the National Elite Program Scholarship, 2017\nNational Scholarship, 2016\nThank\nDr. Jon Barron\nfor sharing the source code of his personal page."
