    "homepage_text": "Sida Peng\nSida Peng (彭思达)\nTenure-track Assistant Professor\n3D Vision Group\nSchool of Software Technology\nZhejiang University\nEmail: pengsida at zju dot edu dot cn\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n][\nGitHub\n]\nShort Bio\nI am an assistant professor (ZJU-100 Young Professor) at Zhejiang University. I received my Ph.D. degree from College of Computer Science and Technology at Zhejiang University in 2023, supervised by Prof. Xiaowei Zhou and Prof. Hujun Bao, and obtained my bachelor degree in Information Engineering from Zhejiang University in 2018.\n        I received the\n2024 CCF Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award\nand was selected as the\n2022 Apple Scholar in AI/ML\n. I have been maintaining\na handbook on learning research\n, which have received more than 10,000 stars on GitHub.\nI work closely with Prof. Xiaowei Zhou. We are looking for students, postdocs and research assistants. Please\napply to our lab here\nif you are interested in working with us.\nNews\n[2025-12] Invited to be a member of the Technical Papers Committee for SIGGRAPH Asia 2026.\n[2025-12] One paper accepted to TPAMI 2026.\n[2025-09] One paper accepted to TOG 2025.\n[2025-07] One paper accepted to ICCV 2025 Highlight.\n[2025-04] Received the\n2025 China3DV Outstanding Young Researcher Award\n.\n[2025-04] One paper selected as CVPR 2025 Oral.\n[2024-12] Received the\n2024 CCF Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award\n.\n[2024-11] Received the Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award of Zhejiang Province.\n[2024-09] Recognised as one of the\nTop 2% Scientists Worldwide 2024\nby Stanford University.\n[2024-08]\nEasyVolcap\nis selected as the 2024 CCF Excellent Open-Source Graphics Software Award.\n[2024-07] Two papers accepted to SIGGRAPH Asia 2024 (1 Journal Track and 1 Conference Track).\n[2024-07] Eight papers accepted to ECCV 2024.\n[2024-05] Invited talk at VALSE 2024 on NeRF Tutorial (\nslides\n).\n[2024-04] Invited talk at The Chinese University of Hongkong, Shenzhen, on Physical World Simulation.\n[2024-04]\nHaotong\nis awarded the Ph.D. Student Fund 2024 of the National Natural Science Foundation of China.\n[2024-04] One paper accepted to SIGGRAPH 2024.\n[2024-04] Four papers selected as CVPR 2024 Highlight.\n[2024-03] One paper accepted to TPAMI 2024.\n[2024-03] Invited talk at The University of Hong Kong on Real-Time Dynamic View Synthesis.\n[2024-02] Seven papers accepted to CVPR 2024.\n[2024-01]\nInvited talk at GAMES Webinar\non Modeling of Dynamic Urban Scenes.\n[2024-01]\nInvited talk at VALSE Webinar\non learning research (\nslides\n).\n[2024-01] One paper accepted to ICLR 2024.\n[2024-01] One paper accepted to TPAMI 2024.\n[2024-01]\nMy article on learning research\nhas been accepted to CCCF 2024.\n[2023-12] Our proposal for 1st Workshop on Neural Volumetric Video has been accepted to CVPR 2024.\n[2023-12] Invited talk at NVIDIA on Real-Time Dynamic View Synthesis.\n[2023-09] One paper accepted to SIGGRAPH Asia 2023 Technical Communications.\n[2023-09] Two papers accepted to NeurIPS 2023.\n[2023-08]\nInvited talk at the SSP\norganized by China Computer Federation.\n[2023-08] Invited talk at Shanghai Jiao Tong University on learning research (\nslides\n).\n[2023-08] One paper accepted to SIGGRAPH Asia 2023.\n[2023-07] Joined the School of Software Technology at Zhejiang University as an assistant professor.\n[2023-07] Three papers accepted to ICCV 2023.\n[2023-06] Honored to be selected as the\n2023 WAIC Rising Star\n.\n[2023-06] Our team won\nthe first place in Image Matching Challenge 2023\n(1st in 494 teams).\n[2023-06] Invited talk at Shanghai AI Laboratory on learning research (\nslides\n).\n[2023-06] Defended my Ph.D. thesis on\nImplicit Neural Representations for Dynamic Human Bodies\n.\n[2023-05] Wrote\na handbook on learning research\nand released it on GitHub.\n[2023-03] Nine papers accepted to CVPR 2023 (2 highlights).\n[2022-10] Received the 2022 National Scholarship.\n[2022-03] Honored to be selected as the\n2022 Apple Scholar in AI/ML\n(15 in the world were awarded).\n[2022-03] Three papers accepted to CVPR 2022 (1 oral).\n[2021-10] Received the 2021 National Scholarship.\n[2021-06] Neural Body was selected as the CVPR 2021 best paper candidate (top 0.5%).\n[2021-03] One paper accepted to CVPR 2021.\n[2020-10] Received the 2020 National Scholarship.\n[2020-10] Honored to be selected as the\n2020 CCF-CV Excellent Young Researcher\n(3 in China were awarded).\n[2020-03] One paper accepted to CVPR 2020 oral presentation (top 5%).\n[2019-10] Received the 2019 National Scholarship.\n[2019-03] One paper accepted to CVPR 2019 oral presentation (top 5%).\n[Show more]\nResearch Summary\nI like advancing spatial agents and solving fundamental research problems that arise from important challenges. I also like exploring the capability boundaries of new techniques in addressing these challenges.\nAfter the CVPR 2025 submission, I decided to pursue research projects that address crucial problems in the industry with significant impact. Such problems typically lack well-established solutions, necessitating us to explore new techniques and provide new insights. \n    I would avoid participating in projects that lack both practical value and unresolved problems, as I believe they only produces useless papers, consuming my passion for research.\nThe following are my target systems:\nIn the past few years, I have focused on developing two systems: Driving Simulator and Volumetric Video.\nMoving forward, I will focus on training spatial agents and developing their fundamental abilities.\nClosed-Loop Simulator\nSpatial Agent Foundation\nVolumetric Video\n[Show the research progress]\nClosed-Loop Simulator\nSpatial Agent\nModel Training\n[Show the research progress]\nCamera Pose Estimation\nDepth Estimation\nObject Motion Estimation\n[Show the research progress]\nLower-cost Capture\nFaster Reconstruction\nLower Storage\nFaster Rendering\nSelected Preprint\nMatchAnything: Universal Cross-Modality Image Matching with Large-Scale Pre-Training\nXingyi He, Hao Yu,\nSida Peng\n, Dongli Tan, Zehong Shen, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nSelected Publications\n(* denotes equal contribution, and\n†\ndenotes the corresponding author)\n2026\nInfiniDepth: Arbitrary-Resolution and Fine-Grained Depth Estimation with Neural Implicit Fields\nHao Yu, Haotong Lin, Jiawei Wang, Jiaxin Li, Yida Wang, Xueyang Zhang, Yue Wang, Xiaowei Zhou, Ruizhen Hu,\nSida Peng\n†\nCVPR 2026.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nIntrinsicAnything: Learning Diffusion Priors for Inverse Rendering Under Unknown Illumination\nSida Peng\n, Jiarui Guo, Xi Chen, Yuan Liu, Dongchen Yang, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nTPAMI 2026.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\n2025\nStreet Gaussians: Modeling Dynamic Urban Scenes with Gaussian Primitives\nSida Peng\n, Yushi Long, Yunzhi Yan, Haotong Lin, Chenxu Zhou, Haiyang Sun, Kun Zhan, Xianpeng Lang, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nTPAMI 2025.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nTowards Depth Foundation Model: Recent Trends in Vision-Based Depth Estimation\nZhen Xu*, Hongyu Zhou*,\nSida Peng\n, Haotong Lin, Haoyu Guo, Jiahao Shao, Peishan Yang, Qinglin Yang, Sheng Miao, Xingyi He, Yifan Wang, Yue Wang, Ruizhen Hu, Yiyi Liao, Xiaowei Zhou, Hujun Bao\nCVMJ 2025.\n[\nPaper\n]\nSplit4D: Decomposed 4D Scene Reconstruction Without Video Segmentation\nYongzhen Hu, Yihui Yang, Haotong Lin, Yifan Wang, Junting Dong, Yifu Deng, Xinyu Zhu, Fan Jia, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou,\nSida Peng\n†\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025 Journal Track. TOG 2025.\nHierarchy UGP: Hierarchy Unified Gaussian Primitive for Large-Scale Dynamic Scene Reconstruction\nHongyang Sun*, Qinglin Yang*, Jiawei Wang*, Zhen Xu, Chen Liu, Yida Wang, Kun Zhan, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou,\nSida Peng\n†\nICCV 2025.\n[\nPaper\n]\nReTracker: Exploring Image Matching for Robust Online Any Point Tracking\nDongli Tan, Xingyi He,\nSida Peng\n, Yiqing Gong, Xing Zhu, Jiaming Sun, Ruizhen Hu, Yujun Shen, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nICCV 2025\nHighlight\n.\n[\nPaper\n]\nStreetCrafter: Street View Synthesis with Controllable Video Diffusion Models\nYunzhi Yan*, Zhen Xu*, Haotong Lin, Haian Jin, Haoyu Guo, Yida Wang, Kun Zhan, Xianpeng Lang, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou,\nSida Peng\n†\nCVPR 2025.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nPrompting Depth Anything for 4K Resolution Accurate Metric Depth Estimation\nHaotong Lin,\nSida Peng\n†\n, Jingxiao Chen, Songyou Peng, Jiaming Sun, Minghuan Liu, Hujun Bao, Jiashi Feng, Xiaowei Zhou, Bingyi Kang\nCVPR 2025.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nLiDAR-RT: Gaussian-based Ray Tracing for Dynamic LiDAR Re-simulation\nChenxu Zhou*, Lvchang Fu*,\nSida Peng\n†\n, Yunzhi Yan, Zhanhua Zhang, Yong Chen, Jiazhi Xia, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2025.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nMulti-view Reconstruction via SfM-guided Monocular Depth Estimation\nHaoyu Guo*, He Zhu*,\nSida Peng\n, Haotong Lin, Yunzhi Yan, Tao Xie, Wenguan Wang, Xiaowei Zhou, Hujun Bao\nCVPR 2025\nOral presentation\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nFreeTimeGS: Free Gaussian Primitives at Anytime Anywhere for Dynamic Scene Reconstruction\nYifan Wang*, Peishan Yang*, Zhen Xu*, Jiaming Sun, Zhanhua Zhang, Yong Chen, Hujun Bao,\nSida Peng\n, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2025.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nInteractive Demo\n][\nMedia Coverage\n]\n2024\nStreet Gaussians for Modeling Dynamic Urban Scenes\nYunzhi Yan, Haotong Lin, Chenxu Zhou, Weijie Wang, Haiyang Sun, Kun Zhan, Xianpeng Lang, Xiaowei Zhou,\nSida Peng\n†\nECCV 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nGRM: Large Gaussian Reconstruction Model for Efficient 3D Reconstruction and Generation\nYinghao Xu, Zifan Shi, Yifan Wang, Hansheng Chen, Ceyuan Yang,\nSida Peng\n, Yujun Shen, Gordon Wetzstein\nECCV 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n]\nNeural 3D Scene Reconstruction with Indoor Planar Priors\nXiaowei Zhou, Haoyu Guo,\nSida Peng\n, Yuxi Xiao, Haotong Lin, Qianqian Wang, Guofeng Zhang, Hujun Bao\nTPAMI 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\n4K4D: Real-Time 4D View Synthesis at 4K Resolution\nZhen Xu,\nSida Peng\n, Haotong Lin, Guangzhao He, Jiaming Sun, Yujun Shen, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nDetector-Free Structure from Motion\nXingyi He, Jiaming Sun, Yifan Wang,\nSida Peng\n, Qixing Huang, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2024.\nFirst Place in Image Matching Challenge 2023\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nSpatialTracker: Tracking Any 2D Pixels in 3D Space\nYuxi Xiao, Qianqian Wang, Shangzhan Zhang, Nan Xue,\nSida Peng\n, Yujun Shen, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2024\nHighlight\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nEfficient LoFTR: Semi-Dense Local Feature Matching with Sparse-Like Speed\nYifan Wang*, Xingyi He*,\nSida Peng\n†\n, Dongli Tan, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2024\nHighlight\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nAnimatable Implicit Neural Representations for Creating Realistic Avatars from Videos\nXiaowei Zhou,\nSida Peng\n†\n, Zhen Xu, Junting Dong, Qianqian Wang, Shangzhan Zhang, Qing Shuai, Hujun Bao\nTPAMI 2024.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nA Guide to Conducting a Research Project\nSida Peng\nCCCF 2024.\n[\nArticle\n][\nProject Page\n][\nTalk\n]\n2023\nEasyVolcap: Accelerating Neural Volumetric Video Research\nZhen Xu, Tao Xie,\nSida Peng\n, Haotong Lin, Qing Shuai, Zhiyuan Yu, Guangzhao He, Jiaming Sun, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2023 Technical Communications.\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nIm4D: High-Fidelity and Real-Time Novel View Synthesis for Dynamic Scenes\nHaotong Lin,\nSida Peng\n†\n, Zhen Xu, Tao Xie, Xingyi He, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nRepresenting Volumetric Videos as Dynamic MLP Maps\nSida Peng*\n, Yunzhi Yan*, Qing Shuai, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nLearning Neural Volumetric Representations of Dynamic Humans in Minutes\nChen Geng*,\nSida Peng*\n, Zhen Xu*, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nGrid-guided Neural Radiance Fields for Large Urban Scenes\nLinning Xu*, Yuanbo Xiangli*,\nSida Peng\n, Xingang Pan, Nanxuan Zhao, Christian Theobalt, Bo Dai, Dahua Lin\nCVPR 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n]\nImplicit Neural Representations with Structured Latent Codes for Human Body Modeling\nSida Peng\n, Chen Geng, Yuanqing Zhang, Yinghao Xu, Qianqian Wang, Qing Shuai, Xiaowei Zhou, Hujun Bao\nTPAMI 2023.\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\n2022\nTotalSelfScan: Learning Full-body Avatars from Self-Portrait Videos of Faces, Hands, and Bodies\nJunting Dong, Qi Fang, Yudong Guo,\nSida Peng\n, Qing Shuai, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nNeurIPS 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nEfficient Neural Radiance Fields for Interactive Free-viewpoint Video\nHaotong Lin*,\nSida Peng\n*, Zhen Xu, Yunzhi Yan, Qing Shuai, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nMPS-NeRF: Generalizable 3D Human Rendering from Multiview Images\nXiangjun Gao, Jiaolong Yang, Jongyoo Kim,\nSida Peng\n, Zicheng Liu, Xin Tong\nTPAMI 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nNerfCap: Human Performance Capture with Dynamic Neural Radiance Fields\nKangkan Wang,\nSida Peng\n, Xiaowei Zhou, Jian Yang, and Guofeng Zhang\nTVCG 2022.\n[\nPaper\n]\nLearning to Estimate Object Poses without Real Image Annotations\nHaotong Lin*,\nSida Peng\n*, Zhize Zhou, Xiaowei Zhou\nIJCAI 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nNeural 3D Scene Reconstruction with the Manhattan-world Assumption\nHaoyu Guo*,\nSida Peng\n*, Haotong Lin, Qianqian Wang, Guofeng Zhang, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2022\nOral presentation\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\n3D-aware Image Synthesis via Learning Structural and Textural Representations\nYinghao Xu,\nSida Peng\n, Ceyuan Yang, Yujun Shen, Bolei Zhou\nCVPR 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nNeural Rays for Occlusion-aware Image-based Rendering\nYuan Liu,\nSida Peng\n, Lingjie Liu, Qianqian Wang, Peng Wang, Christian Theobalt, Xiaowei Zhou, Wenping Wang\nCVPR 2022.\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nTowards Efficient and Photorealistic 3D Human Reconstruction: A Brief Survey\nLu Chen,\nSida Peng\n, Xiaowei Zhou\nVisual Informatics 2022.\n[\nPaper\n]\n2021\nAnimatable Neural Radiance Fields for Modeling Dynamic Human Bodies\nSida Peng\n*, Junting Dong*, Qianqian Wang, Shangzhan Zhang, Qing Shuai, Xiaowei Zhou, Hujun Bao\nICCV 2021.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n][\nExtension\n]\nNeural Body: Implicit Neural Representations with Structured Latent Codes for Novel View Synthesis of Dynamic Humans\nSida Peng\n, Yuanqing Zhang, Yinghao Xu, Qianqian Wang, Qing Shuai, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2021\nBest paper candidate\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\n2020\nPVNet: Pixel-wise Voting Network for 6DoF Object Pose Estimation\nSida Peng\n*, Xiaowei Zhou*, Yuan Liu, Haotong Lin, Qixing Huang, Hujun Bao\nTPAMI 2020.\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nDeep Snake for Real-Time Instance Segmentation\nSida Peng\n, Wen Jiang, Huaijin Pi, Xiuli Li, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nCVPR 2020\nOral presentation\n.\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\n2019\nGIFT: Learning Transformation-Invariant Dense Visual Descriptors via Group CNNs\nYuan Liu, Zehong Shen, Zhixuan Lin,\nSida Peng\n, Hujun Bao, Xiaowei Zhou\nNeurIPS 2019.\n[\nPaper\n][\nSupplementary Material\n][\nProject Page\n][\nCode\n]\nPVNet: Pixel-wise Voting Network for 6DoF ...[truncated]"
