    "homepage_text": "Xidong Feng\nXidong\nFeng\nResearch Scientist, Google DeepMind\nI am a Research Scientist in\nGoogle DeepMind\n. I am graduating from Computer Science, University College London, advised by Prof.\nJun Wang\n. Previously I did my undergraduate at the Department of Automation, Tsinghua University.\nMy research interests lie in Large Language Model, Single-agent/Multi-agent and Meta Reinforcement Learning.\nnews\nJul 30, 2024\nHappy to announce that I will be joining the Discovery Team at Google DeepMind as a Research Scientist this November!\nMay 1, 2024\nOur new work\nAlphazero-like Tree-Search can Guide Large Language Model Decoding and Training\nhas been accepted by the ICML 2024, check our\ncodebase\n.\nDec 1, 2023\nTwo of my cofirst-authored papers have been accecpted in JMLR, including\nTorchOpt\nand\nHeterogeneous-Agent Reinforcement Learning\n, check them out!\nselected publications\n2023\nICML 2024\nAlphazero-like Tree-Search can Guide Large Language Model Decoding and Training\nXidong Feng*\n, Ziyu Wan*, Muning Wen, Ying Wen, Weinan Zhang, and Jun Wang\narXiv preprint arXiv:2309.17179\n, 2023\nHTML\nCode\nJMLR\nHeterogeneous-Agent Reinforcement Learning\nYifan Zhong*, Jakub Grudzien*,\nXidong Feng*\n, Siyi Ji, Jiaming Ji, and Yaodong Yang\nJournal of Machine Learning Research\n, 2023\nHTML\nCode\nJMLR\nTorchOpt: An Efficient Library for Differentiable Optimization\nJie Ren*,\nXidong Feng*\n, Bo Liu*, Xuehai Pan*, Yao Fu, Luo Mai, and Yaodong Yang\nJournal of Machine Learning Research\n, 2023\nHTML\nCode\nNeurIPS 2023\nChessGPT: Bridging Policy Learning and Language Modeling\nXidong Feng\n, Yicheng Luo, Ziyan Wang, Hongrui Tang, Mengyue Yang, Kun Shao, David Mguni, and\n2 more authors\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n, 2023\nHTML\nCode\n2022\nNeurIPS\nA Theoretical Understanding of Gradient Bias in Meta-Reinforcement Learning\nXidong Feng*\n, Bo Liu*, Jie Ren, Luo Mai, Rui Zhu, Haifeng Zhang, Jun Wang, and\n1 more author\nIn NeurIPS\n, 2022\nHTML\nCode\n2021\nNeurIPS\nNeural auto-curricula in two-player zero-sum games\nXidong Feng*\n, Oliver Slumbers*, Ziyu Wan, Bo Liu, Stephen McAleer, Ying Wen, Jun Wang, and\n1 more author\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n, 2021\nHTML\nCode\nYou can even add a little note about which of these is the best way to reach you."
