    "homepage_text": "Home - Peng Cheng\nHome | Peng Cheng\nPeng Cheng\nResearcher in Spatial Intelligence.\nFollow\nShanghai, China\nTongji University\nEmail\nGithub\narXiv\ndblp\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nHome\nI am a Researcher in the\nSchool of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nTongji University\n. I was a Junior Researcher in the School of Software Engineering at\nEast China Normal University\nfrom March 2019 to January 2025. I received my BS and master degrees at Xi’an Jiaotong Univeristy in 2012 and 2014. I received my Ph.D. degree in Computer Science and Engineering, supervised by\nProf. Lei Chen\nat Hong Kong University of Science and Technology in 2017. Then I worked with Prof. Lei Chen as a Post-Doc from October 2017 to March 2019.\nCV\nShort biography\nIn a nutshell\n2025–now:\nResearcher\n,\nTongji University\n, Shanghai, China\n2019–2025:\nJunior Researcher\n,\nEast China Normal University\n, Shanghai, China\n2014–2019:\nPh.D & Post-Doc\n,\nHKUST\n, HK SAR, China. Supervisor:\nLei Chen\n2012–2014:\nM.S.\n,\nXi’an Jiaotong University\n, Xi’an, China\n2008–2012:\nB.S.\n,\nXi’an Jiaotong University\n, Xi’an, China\nContact\nRoom 332, Jishi Building,\n4800 Cao'an Road,\nJiading District, Shanghai, China\nShow in Google Maps\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Peng Cheng\nCV | Peng Cheng\nPeng Cheng\nResearcher in Spatial Intelligence.\nFollow\nShanghai, China\nTongji University\nEmail\nGithub\narXiv\ndblp\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in GitHub, GitHub University, 2012\nM.S. in Jekyll, GitHub University, 2014\nPh.D in Version Control Theory, GitHub University, 2018 (expected)\nWork experience\nSummer 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Tagging issues\nSupervisor: Professor Git\nFall 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Merging pull requests\nSupervisor: Professor Hub\nSkills\nSkill 1\nSkill 2\nSub-skill 2.1\nSub-skill 2.2\nSub-skill 2.3\nSkill 3\nPublications\nPaper Title Number 1\nYour Name, You. (2009). \"Paper Title Number 1.\"\nJournal 1\n. 1(1).\nTalks\nQuasi-Bayesian learning\nNovember 08, 2017\nSpotlight talk at Criteo - Machine Learning in the real world, Paris, France\nA Primer on PAC-Bayesian Learning\nJune 10, 2019\nTutorial at ICML 2019, Long Beach CA, USA\nTeaching\nTeaching experience 1\nTeaching experience 2\nService and leadership\nCurrently signed in to 43 different slack teams"
