    "homepage_text": "About | Yao Lu\nAbout | Yao Lu\nYao Lu\nAssistant Professor\nSchool of Computing\nNational University of Singapore\nCOM2-3-42\nMy passions lie at the intersection of AI, systems and their applications in science and beyond. Throughout my academic and industry journey, I have engaged with various tiers of the technology\nlandscape and acquired hands-on experience in data science, core systems, advanced cloud infrastructures,\nand a diverse range of AI applications. The research topics I am interested in include:\nNext-Gen AI infrastructures:\nI build ML, data, and cloud systems to enpower AI in the era of large generative models and agents.\nRL and agents in science & beyond:\nA comprehensive playground for systems, data, and AI research aimed at real-world impact. Currently exploring AI applications in finance.\nBefore joining NUS, I was a researcher at\nMicrosoft Research Redmond\nfor about 10 years (intern > contractor > full time). I received PhD from the\nUniversity of Washington\nin 2018"
  },
