    "homepage_text": "Jongmin Lee (이종민)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJongmin Lee (이종민)\nJongmin Lee\nI am an assistant professor in AI at Yonsei University. Before joining Yonsei, I was a postdoctoral researcher at UC Berkeley, advised by\nPieter Abbeel\n. I received my PhD from KAIST, where I was fortunate to be advised by\nKee-Eung Kim\n.\nE-mail: jongminlee [at] yonsei.ac.kr / jongmin.lee012 [at] gmail.com\n🎓\n[Google Scholar]\n🌍\n[DILLab homepage]\nExperience\nMar 2025 - Current: Assistant\nP\nrofessor in AI at\nYonsei University\nMay 2022 - Feb 2025: Postdoc at UC Berkeley (Advisor:\nPieter Abbeel\n)\nApr 2021 - Aug 2021: Research Scientist Intern at\nDeepMind\n(Host\n:\nArthur Guez\n)\nEducation\n2017. 03.  - 2022. 02: PhD, School of Computing,\nKAIST\n, Korea (Advisor: Kee-Eung Kim)\nThesis: Algorithms for Safe Reinforcement Learning\n2015. 03. - 2017. 02.: MS, School of Computing,\nKAIST\n, Korea (Advisor: Kee-Eung Kim)\nThesis: Constrained Bayesian Reinforcement Learning via Approximate Linear Programming\n2009. 03. - 2014. 02.: BS, Department of Computer Science and Engineering,\nSeoul National University\n, Korea\nNotice\nJoin us! We are actively recruiting research interns and graduate students (M.S./Ph.D.) who are passionate about AI, sequential-decision making, and reinforcement learning. If you are interested, please refer to\nhere\n.\nPublications\n(*: equal contribution, ^: equal advising)\nInternational\n[C2\n8\n]\nPartially Equivariant Reinforcement Learning in Symmetry-Breaking Environments\n[paper]\nJunwoo Chang, Minwoo Park, Joohwan Seo, Roberto Horowitz,\nJongmin Lee^\n, Jongeun Choi^\n(^: co-corresponding)\nICLR 2026\n[C27] FairDICE: Fairness-Driven Offline Multi-Objective Reinforcement Learning\nWoosung Kim*, Jinho Lee*,\nJongmin Lee^\n, Byung-Jun Lee^ (*: equal contribution, ^: co-corresponding)\nNeurIPS 2025\n[C26] SEMDICE: Off-policy State Entropy Maximization via Stationary Distribution Cor