    "homepage_text": "Zhijie Deng's Homepage\nZhijie Deng (邓志杰)\nAssociate Professor, Ph.D. Advisor\nQing Yuan Research Institute\n&\nSchool of Computer Science\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nShanghai, China\nOffice: 剑川路930号A栋318C\nEmail:\nzhijied@sjtu[dot]edu[dot]cn\n,\ndengzhijiethu@gmail[dot]com\n[Google Scholar]\n[DENG Lab]\n[GitHub]\n[Zhihu]\n[X]\nBiography\nI am an Associate Professor at\nQing Yuan Research Institute\nand\nSchool of Computer Science\nat\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n. I obtained the Ph.D. degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nTsinghua University\nin June 2022, under the supervision of\nProf. Bo Zhang\nand\nProf. Jun Zhu\n. Before that, I received the B.S. degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nTsinghua University\nin 2017. I was a visiting scholar from July 2016 to September 2016 in\nMachine Learning Department\n,\nCarnegie Mellon University\n, advised by\nProf. Eric P. Xing\n.\nMy principal research interests lie in the development of machine learning and statistical methodology, spanning generative models, spectral methods, Bayesian inference, etc. The developed methods have been applied to scenarios such as image/language/video generation, Embodied AI, semi-/self-/un-supervised learning, PDE solving, uncertainty quantification, and trustworthy ML.\nOpenings\nI am looking for\ninterns\n,\nvisitors\n, and\npostdocs\nwho have a strong background in mathematics/physics/computer science and are eager to get involved in cutting-edge, fundamental AI research (especially in fields of\nmulti-modal generation\nand\nembodied AI\n). If you are interested, feel free to drop me an\nemail\n.\nSelected Publications\n[More]\n* equal contribution. † corresponding author.\nMulti-Modal Generation (with Applications in World Model and VLA)\nThink-Then-Generate: Reasoning-Aware Text-to-Image Diffusion with LLM Encoders\nSiqi Kou, Jiachun Jin, Zetong Zhou, Ye Ma, Yugang Wang, Quan Chen, Peng Jiang, Xiao Yang, Ju