    "homepage_text": "Dr Fei   Deng | UNSW Research\nSkip to main content\nResearcher\nBiography\nDr Deng is currently an NHMRC EL1 Fellow and NSW Cancer Institute ECR Fellow. Dr Deng received his Ph.D. degree from the University of New South Wales (UNSW), Sydney, Australia. Dr Deng’s research interests include point-of-care biosensing devices, CRISPR biosensing device and in vivo biosensing device. To date, Dr Deng has published over 50 journal articles, including Nature Communications, Nucleic Acids Research, AFM, Trends in...\nview more\nDr Deng is currently an NHMRC EL1 Fellow and NSW Cancer Institute ECR Fellow. Dr Deng received his Ph.D. degree from the University of New South Wales (UNSW), Sydney, Australia. Dr Deng’s research interests include point-of-care biosensing devices, CRISPR biosensing device and in vivo biosensing device. To date, Dr Deng has published over 50 journal articles, including Nature Communications, Nucleic Acids Research, AFM, Trends in Analytical Chemistry, Small, Water Research, BBI etc. In addition, he has secured over $12M research grants, including AEA, CRCP, NHMRC Idea Grant, ARC Discovery Project, NSSN etc. His biosensor research has been internationally recognized, leading to a 2025 NSW Premier’s Awards (Finalist), an ECR Award from Royal Society of NSW, an ECR Award from ECAN, and multiple travel grants. Additionally, his innovations have gained significant industry recognition, leading to a startup company (Casbio Pty Ltd, co-founder) and a research consultant of Avicena Systems Limited.\nMy Grants\nNHMRC Investigator EL1, 2025, sole-CI\nEarly Career Fellowship of Cancer Institute NSW, 2025-2027, sole-CI\nNICE-UNSW \"Proof-of-Scale\" Fund, 2024-2025, CIA\nAustralia's Economic Accelerator, 2024-2025, CIA\nCooperative Research Centres Projects, 2024-2026, co-CI\nUNSW-Tsinghua Collaborative Research Seed Program, 2023, co-CI\nNHMRC Idea Grant, 2024-2026, co-CI\nARC Discovery Project, 2024-2026, co-CI\nUNSW_NMHA Seed Funidng, 2023, co-CI\nTorch Innovation, 2023, CIA\nHealth Security Systems Australia, 2023, co-CI.\nNSSN Grand Challenge Fund, 2023, co-CI.\n3Rs Grant from UNSW, 2022, co-CI.\nIndustry competitive research award, 2022-2024, co-CI.\nTwo Innovation connections grants, 2021 (RG211246, RG210091), CI on both.\nOne EDI and ECAN seed funding from UNSW, 2021, CIA.\nMy Awards\nFinalist for Outstanding Early Career Researcher Award, 2025 NSW Premier’s Awards\n2024 Paper of the Year – Biosensing & Imaging, School of Biomedical Engineering\nDiversifying Visitors to UNSW Engineering Scheme Award 2025 ($8000)\nEarly Career Research and Service Citation Award, Royal Society of New South Wales\nAustralian Centre for NanoMedicine (ACN) Travel Award ($3000)\nDiversity in Engineering Academic Visitors Funding Award ($5000)\nUNSW Engineering ECA Awards – Innovation and Engagement Award\nDiversity in Engineering Academic Visitors Funding Award (\n$5000\n)\nARC Centre for Nanoscale BioPhotonics (CNBP) Travel Award ($2000)\nAustralian Centre for NanoMedicine (ACN) Travel Award ($2000)\nEDI and ECAN seed funding from UNSW ($1000)\nMy Research Activities\nPatent\nCRISPR/Cas-associated detection assays, methods and kits. (2023) National Phase Patent. International application No. PCT/AU2022/050829.\nUltrasensitive CRISPR biosensors assisted by nucleic acid mediators. (2023) National Phase Patent. International application No. PCT/AU2023/051144.\nBiosensor. (2023) Australian provisional patent No. P0046904AU\nMy Research Supervision\nSupervision keywords\nclinical diagnostics\nbiosensing techniques\nAreas of supervision\n1. Point-of-care biosensing\n2.CRISPR biosensing\n3. In vivo biosensing\nCurrently supervising\nPhD Supervision Experience\nJoint-supervising PhD\nresearch project: CRISPR sensor for precision oncology (R. Xue), 2025-now\nCo-supervising PhD\nresearch project: AI-assisted, microfluidics-enabled CRISPR biosensors for precision diagnosis (R. Wang), 2025-now\nCo-supervising PhD research project:\nDevelopment of\nrapid and sensitive methods for the detection of waterborne pathogens\n, 2024 (J. Arona)\nCo-supervising PhD research project:\nProgrammable nucleases and applications in biosensing, 2023 (X. Zhai)\nJoint-supervising PhD research project:\nNovel biosensors for exosome detection, 2023 (P. Mohammadnejad)\nCo-supervising PhD research project:\nCapture and detection of waterborne parasites using existing and emergent technologies, 2021 (T. Hall)\nThesis students\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project:\nProgrammable RNA detection with CRISPR/Cas12 (X. Ruan), 2025\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: Optimizing Lentiviral Mediated Stem Cell Genetic Engineering (D. Kulkarni), 2025\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: Longitudinal Tracking of Stem Cell Fate in Inflammatory Environment (H. Wu), 2025\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: Exploring the Synergistic Effects of SOXF and Physiological Flow in Human Vascular Development (J. Xu), 2025\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: iPSC derived Cardiomyocytes for Cardiovascular on Chip model (Q. Tang), 2025\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: CRISPR based autocatalytic sensor for the detection of DNA methylation towards precision cancer diagnosis (K. Chen), 2024\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: CRISPR sensor for the detection of RNA methylation towards precision cancer diagnosis (F. Wu), 2024\n.\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: AlphaFold 3 powered CRISPR base aptamer sensor for the detection of small proteins (J. Zhang), 2024\nPrimary-supervising UG Thesis project\n: CRISPR base electrochemical biosensor for cancer diagnosis (L. Stewart), 2024\nPrimary-supervising PG Thesis project\n: The development of in vivo biosensor for long-term monitoring of inflammatory biomarkers (W. Fu), 2024. She was awarded the\n“Great Science Produces Great Patient Outcomes Award”\nat UNSW BESS x GSBmE Biomedical Engineering Projects Showcase and Industry Night 2024.\nPrimary-supervised PG Thesis project\n: CRISPR/Cas powered aptasensor for the point-of-care diagnosis of IBD (K. Lyu), 2024\nPrimary-supervised PG Thesis project\n: Precision diagnosis of single gene diseases using CRISPR technology (Y. Lin), 2024\nPrimary-supervised UG Thesis project\n: Precision diagnosis of inflammatory bowel disease using CRISPR technology (S. Xue), 2023-2024\nPrimary-supervised UG Thesis project\n: CRISPR/Cas12a Mediated Biosensing Assay for Point-of-Care Testing of Calprotectin (S. Chia), 2023\nPrimary-supervised PG Thesis project\n: Point-of-care testing of procalcitonin using lateral flow assay (J. Deodhar), 2023\nMy Teaching\nIndustrial Training Coordinator, Biomedical Engineering, 2025\nInstructor, Biomedical Instrumentation - BIOM9640, UNSW, 2022-2023\nInstructor, Applications of Light in Engineering, Technology and the Life Sciences - BIOM9811, UNSW\nView less\nLocation\nEngineering\nContact\n0451876009\nfei.deng@unsw.edu.au\nFollow\nMy ResearchGate\nMy Google Scholar\nPublications\nby Dr Fei   Deng\nJournal articles\n56\nConference Papers\n8\nPreprints\n1\nView all »\nORCID as entered in\nROS\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-5606-0278\nUNSW Sydney NSW 2052 Australia Telephone +61 2 93851000\nAuthorised by Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research)\nUNSW CRICOS Provider Code: 00098G ABN: 57 195 873 179\nJoin the conversation\nFacebook\nTwitter\nUNSW Youtube\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nInstagram\nMember Group of Eight\nMember Universitas 21\nMember Global Alliance of Technological Universities\nMember Association of Pacific Rim Universities\nMember\nPLuS Alliance\nHome\n2025 Strategic Initiatives\nUNSW Futures\nInterdisciplinary Research\nWorld Class Research Infrastructure\nGrand Challenges\nThought Leadership & Public Engagement\nKnowledge Exchange\nARTU -  Aggregate Ranking of Top Universities\nContact Us\nDeputy Vice-Chancellor (Research & Enterprise)\nPro Vice-Chancellor (Research)\nGraduate Research\nScholarships\nApplying for a Scholarship\nThesis\nThesis Preparation\nExamination\nGraduation\nHelp and Advice\nArc UNSW – Postgraduate Council\nArc UNSW – Student Life\nFinancial Support\nNew to UNSW Research\nEvents & Workshops\nStudy with Us\nResearch Training\nExtend Your Career\nNetworks\nNew to UNSW Research\nResearch Career Opportunities\nResearch Impact\nUNSW Areas of Research Strength\nFellows of Learned Academies\nResearch News & Stories\nResearch Integrity\nResearch Ethics & Compliance Support\nResearch Integrity for Staff\nSupervisors and Research Integrity\nResearch Ethics and Compliance Support\nAnimal Research Ethics\nHuman Research Ethics\nRadiation Safety\nResearch Export Controls\nResearch Strategy Office\nAbout the RSO\nPartner with us\nContact Us\nPartner With Us\nServices for Researchers\nResearch Grants and Contracts (RGC)\nAbout Us\nCurrent Funding Opportunities\nResources and Quicklinks\nSystems\nResearch Infrastructure\nAnalytical Centre (MWAC)\nContacts & About Us\nData Management, Storage and Tools\nNetwork Labs\nShared Research Equipment\nUNSW Research Infrastructure Scheme\nPartner With Us\nPricing Tool\nResearcher Hub (UNSW login)\nCurrent Funding Opportunities\nResearch News\nUNSW Centres and Institutes\nFind a Researcher\nFAQ: Researcher Profiles - Tags & Codes"
