    "github": "https://github.com/congwang0705",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/cong-wang-2310b314b/",
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Cong Wang's Homepage!\nHome\nBiography\nResearch\nPublication\nCollaborator\nWelcome to Cong Wang's Homepage!\nCong Wang (王聪)\nCV\nDoctor & Associate Professor\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence, OPtics and ElectroNics (iOPEN)\nNorthwestern Polytechnical University (NWPU)\n127 West Youyi Road, Beilin District\nXi'an 710072, China\nE-post: congwang0705@nwpu.edu.cn (domestic), congwang0705@gmail.com (overseas)\nGoogle Scholar Profile\n,\nResearch Gate Profile\n,\nLinkedIn Profile\nAbout me\nI received the B.S. degree in automation (Supervisor: Professor\nYuncan Xue\n) from College of Internet of Things (IOT) Engineering,\nHohai University (HHU)\n,\r\nthe M.S. degree in mathematics (Supervisor: Professor\nJianbin Yang\n) from College of Science,\nHohai University (HHU)\n, and the Ph.D. degree in mechatronic engineering\r\n(Supervisor: Professors\nMengchu Zhou\nand\nZhiwu Li\n) from School of Mechano-Electronic Engineering,\nXidian University (XDU)\nin 2014, 2017, and 2021, respectively.\r\nI was a Visiting Ph.D. Student (Co-advisor: Professor\nWitold Pedrycz\n) in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Alberta, Edmonton, AB, Canada.\r\nI was a Research Assistant (Co-advisor: Assistant Professor\nJun Zhao\n) at the School of Computer Science and Engineering, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore.\r\nI was a Visiting Ph.D. Student (Co-advisor: Professor\nShuzhi Sam Ge\n) in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, National University of Singapore, Singapore.\r\nI was also a postdoctoral fellow under the supervision of Professor\nXuelong Li\n. I am currently an Associate Professor in the School of Artificial Intelligence, OPtics and ElectroNics (iOPEN), Northwestern Polytechnical University, China. My research interests include information computation, G-image processing, fuzzy theory, as well as wavelet analysis and its applications. I am Associate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systems and a member of Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE), Chinese Association of Automation (CAA), China Computer Federation (CCF), China Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics (CSIAM), Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI), and China Society of Image and Graphics (CSIG).\nRecent Events\nIn May 2024, one paper has been accepted by IEEE TSMCA\nIn Apr. 2024, one paper has been accepted by IEEE TGRS\nIn Feb. 2024, two papers have been accepted by IEEE TFS\nIn Jan. 2024, one paper has been published in IEEE TCYB\nOur source codes have been released publicly in\nGithub\nOur source codes have been released publicly in\nMathWorks\nIn Oct. 2020, my homepage has been issued\nRecent Publications\nCong Wang\n, Guodong Sun, Cailing Wang, Zixuan Gao, and Hongwei Wang*, ‘‘Monte Carlo-based restoration of images degraded by atmospheric turbulence,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Systems, Man and Cybernetics: Systems\n, accepted, 2024. (SCI Q1, IF: 8.7)\nCong Wang\n, Xin Tan, Bo Li*, and Mengchu Zhou*, ‘‘Noise-estimation-dominated fuzzy segmentation strategy for accurate implantation of implantable cardioverter defibrillators,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systems\n, to be published, doi: 10.1109/TFUZZ.2024.3364970. (SCI Q1, IF: 11.9)\nCong Wang\n, Mengchu Zhou*, Witold Pedrycz, and Zhiwu Li*, ‘‘Comparative study on noise-estimation-based Fuzzy C-Means clustering for image segmentation,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n, vol. 54, no. 1. pp. 241-253, Jan. 2024. (SCI Q1, IF: 11.8, Regular Paper)\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Zhiwu Li*, and Mengchu Zhou*, ‘‘Kullback-Leibler divergence-based Fuzzy C-Means clustering incorporating morphological reconstruction and wavelet frames for image segmentation,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n, vol. 52, no. 8, pp. 7612–7623, Aug. 2022. (SCI Q1, IF: 19.118, Regular Paper)\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Zhiwu Li*, Mengchu Zhou*, and Jun Zhao, ‘‘Residual-sparse Fuzzy C-Means clustering incorporating morphological reconstruction and wavelet frame,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systems\n, vol. 29, no. 12, pp. 3910–3924, Dec. 2021. (SCI Q1, IF: 12.253, Full Paper) [\npdf\n]\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Zhiwu Li*, Mengchu Zhou*, and Shuzhi Sam Ge, ‘‘G-image segmentation: Similarity-preserving Fuzzy C-Means with spatial information constraint in wavelet space,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systems\n, vol. 29, no. 12, pp. 3887–3898, Dec. 2021. (SCI Q1, IF: 12.253, Full Paper) [\npdf\n]\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Mengchu Zhou, and Zhiwu Li, ‘‘Sparse regularization-based Fuzzy C-Means clustering incorporating morphological grayscale reconstruction and wavelet frames,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systems\n, vol. 29, no. 7, pp. 1826–1840, Jul. 2021. (SCI Q1, IF: 12.253, Full Paper) [\npdf\n]\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Zhiwu Li, and Mengchu Zhou, ‘‘Residual-driven Fuzzy C-Means clustering for image segmentation,’’\nIEEE/CAA Journal of Automatica Sinica\n, vol. 8, no. 4, pp. 876–889, Apr. 2021. (SCI Q1, IF: 7.847, Regular Paper) [\npdf\n]\nCong Wang\n, Ziyue Yan, Witold Pedrycz, Mengchu Zhou, and Zhiwu Li, ‘‘A weighted fidelity and regularization-based method for mixed or unknown noise removal from images on graphs,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, vol. 29, no. 1, pp. 5229–5243, Dec. 2020. (SCI Q1, IF: 10.856, Regular Paper) [\npdf\n]\nCong Wang\n, Witold Pedrycz, Jianbin Yang, Mengchu Zhou, and Zhiwu Li, ‘‘Wavelet frame-based Fuzzy C-Means clustering for segmenting images on graphs,’’\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n, vol. 50, no. 9, pp. 3938–3949, Sept. 2020. (SCI Q1, IF: 11.448, Regular Paper) [\npdf\n]\nFull list of publications\n.\nLast updated: 05/2024"
  },
