    "homepage_text": "Yixin Liu | Yixin Liu’s Homepage\nYixin Liu\nI’m a final-year Ph.D. student in the Computer Science department at Yale University working on Natural Language Processing.\nMy advisor is Professor\nArman Cohan\n, and I was very fortunate to have Professor\nDragomir Radev\nas my advisor during my first two years at Yale.\nBefore coming to Yale, I received my master’s degree from the Language Technologies Institute at Carnegie Mellon University, working with Professor\nGraham Neubig\nand Professor\nPengfei Liu\n.\nI started my NLP research during my undergraduate study at Fudan University, where I worked with Professor\nXipeng Qiu\n.\nBeyond academic research, I also worked as a research intern at Meta GenAI/FAIR, Google DeepMind and Microsoft Research.\nMy research focuses on improving language model capabilities in domains that are challenging to evaluate and optimize, by (1) developing robust evaluation methodologies (\nICLR 2026\n,\nNeurIPS 2025\n,\nNAACL 2025\n,\nNAACL 2025 Findings\n,\nNAACL 2024 Findings\n,\nEMNLP 2023\n,\nACL 2023\n), and (2) designing training algorithms that explicitly incorporate both human and automatic evaluations as supervision (\nICLR 2026\n,\nICLR 2026\n,\nNAACL 2025 Findings\n,\nNAACL 2024\n,\nACL 2023\n,\nACL 2022\n,\nACL 2021\n,\nNAACL 2021\n).\n[\nGitHub\n] [\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nSelected Work\nExamining Reasoning LLMs-as-Judges in Non-Verifiable LLM Post-Training\nYixin Liu\n, Yue Yu, DiJia Su, Sid Wang, Xuewei Wang, Song Jiang, Bo Liu, Arman Cohan, Yuandong Tian, Zhengxing Chen\n[arXiv]\nCOMAL: A Convergent Meta-Algorithm for Aligning LLMs with General Preferences\nYixin Liu*\n, Argyris Oikonomou*, Weiqiang Zheng*, Yang Cai, Arman Cohan\n*Equal Contribution\nICLR 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nReferences Improve LLM Alignment in Non-Verifiable Domains\nKejian Shi*,\nYixin Liu*\n, Peifeng Wang, Alexander R. Fabbri, Shafiq Joty, Arman Cohan\n*Equal Contribution\nICLR 2026\n[Paper]\n[code]\nOn Evaluating LLM Alignment by Evaluating LLMs as Judges\nYixin Liu\n, Pengfei Liu, Arman Cohan\nNeurIPS 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nReIFE: Re-evaluating Instruction-Following Evaluation\nYixin Liu*\n, Kejian Shi*, Alexander R. Fabbri, Yilun Zhao, Peifeng Wang, Chien-Sheng Wu, Shafiq Joty, Arman Cohan\n*Equal Contribution\nNAACL 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nRe-evaluating Automatic LLM System Ranking for Alignment with Human Preference\nMingqi Gao*,\nYixin Liu*\n, Xinyu Hu, Xiaojun Wan, Jonathan Bragg, Arman Cohan\n*Equal Contribution\nNAACL 2025 Findings\n[Paper]\nUnderstanding Reference Policies in Direct Preference Optimization\nYixin Liu\n, Pengfei Liu, Arman Cohan\nNAACL 2025 Findings\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nBenchmarking Generation and Evaluation Capabilities of Large Language Models for Instruction Controllable Summarization\nYixin Liu*\n, Alexander R. Fabbri*, Jiawen Chen, Yilun Zhao, Simeng Han, Shafiq Joty, Pengfei Liu, Dragomir Radev, Chien-Sheng Wu, Arman Cohan\n*Equal Contribution\nNAACL 2024 Findings\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nOn Learning to Summarize with Large Language Models as References\nYixin Liu\n, Kejian Shi, Katherine S He, Longtian Ye, Alexander R. Fabbri, Pengfei Liu, Dragomir Radev, Arman Cohan\nNAACL 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nImproving Large Language Model Fine-tuning for Solving Math Problems\nYixin Liu\n, Avi Singh, C. Daniel Freeman, John D. Co-Reyes, Peter J. Liu\n[arXiv]\nRevisiting the Gold Standard: Grounding Summarization Evaluation with Robust Human Evaluation\nYixin Liu*\n, Alexander R. Fabbri*, Pengfei Liu, Yilun Zhao, Linyong Nan, Ruilin Han, Simeng Han, Shafiq Joty, Chien-Sheng Wu, Caiming Xiong, Dragomir Radev\n*Equal Contribution\nACL 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nOn Improving Summarization Factual Consistency from Natural Language Feedback\nYixin Liu\n, Budhaditya Deb, Milagro Teruel, Aaron Halfaker, Dragomir Radev, Ahmed H. Awadallah\nACL 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nBRIO: Bringing Order to Abstractive Summarization\nYixin Liu\n, Pengfei Liu, Dragomir Radev, Graham Neubig\nACL 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nOn Learning Text Style Transfer with Direct Rewards\nYixin Liu\n, Graham Neubig, John Wieting\nNAACL 2021\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nServices\nArea Chair\n: ACL Rolling Review\n(ARR)\nProgram Chair\n: New England NLP 2025\n(NENLP2025)\nConference Reviewer\n: ACL Rolling Review, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Kaize Ding::https://kaize0409.github.io/": {
