    "homepage_text": "Fuhai Li\n      -  WashU Medicine Research Profiles\nWashU Medicine Research Profiles Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at WashU Medicine Research Profiles\nView Scopus Profile\nFuhai Li\nAssociate Professor of Pediatrics, Associate Professor of Computer Science & Engineering\nDivision of Newborn Medicine\nRoy and Diana Vagelos Division of Biology & Biomedical Sciences (DBBS)\nDBBS - Biomedical Informatics and Data Science\nDBBS - Cancer Biology\nDBBS - Computational and Systems Biology\nInstitute of Clinical and Translational Sciences (ICTS)\nInstitute for Informatics, Data Science and Biostatistics (I2DB)\nCenter for Translational Bioinformatics (CTBI)\nSiteman Cancer Center\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-3773-146X\nWilling to Mentor\nAvailable to Mentor:\nPhD Students\n4282\nCitations\n2005\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nResearch interests\nMy recent research has focused on the integration and interpretation of diverse and heterogeneous pharmacogenomics data using statistical and machine learning approaches for i) understanding driver genetics/functional (mechanism), ii) discovering novel combinatory therapies to overcome intrinsic/acquired drug resistance (with reduced toxicity and synergy effects), and iii) uncovering and perturbing the tumor-stroma interaction to understand the roles of tumor micro-environment/niche in disease development.\nAvailable to Mentor:\nPhD Students\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Fuhai Li is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person and are generated automatically. Together they form a unique fingerprint. Contact the Profiles team with questions.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nSignaling Pathway\nKeyphrases\n100%\nDrug Combination\nKeyphrases\n83%\nHigh Content\nKeyphrases\n77%\nCoherent anti-Stokes Raman Scattering\nKeyphrases\n67%\nGraph Neural Network\nKeyphrases\n63%\nOmics Data\nKeyphrases\n62%\nCell Segmentation\nKeyphrases\n60%\nSignaling Network\nKeyphrases\n58%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n68\nArticle\n22\nConference contribution\n4\nConference article\n3\nReview article\n5\nMore\n2\nChapter\n2\nEditorial\n1\nPaper\nAPOE-stratified Proteomic and Metabolomic Analysis Reveals Mitochondrial Dysfunction Inflammation and Lipid Dysregulation in Alzheimer's Disease\nLi, F.\n, Chen, Y., Western, D.,\nAli, M.\n, Liu, M., Gong, K., Xu, Y., Lowery, J.,\nHoltzman, D.\n, Robins, C., Eicher, J. D., Huang, Y. N., Liu, S. W., Park, T., Saykin, A. J., Nho, K., Moqri, M., Mohs, R. C., Farinas, A. & Moran-Losada, P.\n& 3 others\n,\nOh, H. S. H., Wyss-Coray, T. &\nCruchaga, C.\n,\n2026\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nAdvanced Science.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nAlzheimer's Disease\n100%\nProteomic Analysis\n100%\nInflammation\n100%\nApolipoprotein E\n100%\nMitochondrial Dysfunction\n100%\nGraphSeqLM: A Unified Graph Language Framework for Omic Graph Learning\nZhang, H., Huang, D., Chen, Y. &\nLi, F.\n,\nMay 23 2025\n,\nWWW Companion 2025 - Companion Proceedings of the ACM Web Conference 2025.\nAssociation for Computing Machinery, Inc\n,\np. 1510-1513\n4 p.\n(WWW Companion 2025 - Companion Proceedings of the ACM Web Conference 2025).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nOmics\n100%\nGraph Learning\n100%\nGraph Neural Network\n100%\nLanguage Model\n100%\nGraph Sequence\n100%\nIntelligent biology and medicine: Accelerating innovative computational approaches\nLi, F.\n, Liu, L., Wang, K., Liu, X. & Zhao, Z.,\nJan 2025\n,\nIn:\nComputational and Structural Biotechnology Journal.\n27\n,\np. 32-34\n3 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nEditorial\nOpen Access\nComputational Approach\n100%\nOral Presentation\n100%\nMedicine\n100%\nArtificial Intelligence\n100%\nOral\n100%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nM3NetFlow: A multi-scale multi-hop graph AI model for integrative multi-omic data analysis\nZhang, H.,\nGoedegebuure, S. P.\n,\nDing, L.\n,\nDeNardo, D.\n, Fields, R. C.,\nProvince, M.\n, Chen, Y.,\nPayne, P.\n&\nLi, F.\n,\nMar 21 2025\n,\nIn:\niScience.\n28\n,\n3\n, 111920.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nComplex Disease\n100%\nPrecision Medicine\n100%\nCase Study\n100%\nPrediction Accuracy\n100%\nEvaluation Result\n100%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nNovel Computational and Artificial Intelligence Models in Cancer Research\nLiu, L.,\nLi, F.\n, Liu, X., Wang, K. & Zhao, Z.,\nJan 2025\n,\nIn:\nCancers.\n17\n,\n1\n, 116.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nEditorial\nOpen Access\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nView all 102 Research outputs"
