    "homepage_text": "Zhen Wang\nZhen Wang\n王震\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nEmail\nGitHub\nTwitter\nGoogle Scholar\nJob market 2025–2026.\nCV\n|\nResearch Statement\n|\nTeaching Statement\nHi! I am currently a\nMoore Foundation Postdoctoral Fellow\nhosted at UC San Diego, working with\nEric Xing\n(CMU & MBZUAI) and\nZhiting Hu\n(UCSD).\nI received my PhD from the Computer Science department at The Ohio State University previously, working with\nHuan Sun\nand\nYu Su\n, where I developed foundational frameworks for knowledge-centric AI systems. My work has been supported by and recognized with the\nGordon and Betty Moore Foundation Fellowship\n,\nOpenAI Research Grant\n(sole-PI, 1 of 11 teams worldwide),\nRising Star in Data Science\n(UChicago),\nBest Paper Award at SoCal NLP\n,\nAmazon Alexa Prize Winner\n(proposal and team leader), and more. I have led collaborations with\nMIT-IBM Lab\n,\nMicrosoft Research\n,\nNEC Labs\n, and academic institutions including CMU, MBZUAI, five UC campuses and three national labs through\nthe UC-LEAP project\n.\nResearch Overview\nView Details →\nMy research focuses on the\nfoundations of reasoning, planning, and agency in AI\n, and applies them to\naccelerate and democratize knowledge and scientific discovery\n. I aim to build AI systems that can autonomously\nreason, act, and discover\n, and am interested in deploying them as\nAI co-scientists\nthat can speed up research across biology, materials science, social science, and beyond. My recent works explore:\nDeliberative reasoning & world models\n(\nEMNLP'23\n,\nCOLM'24\n,\nACL'23\n,\nEMNLP'24\n,\nICLR'26\n)\nAutonomous agents & trustworthy deployment\n(\nNeurIPS'25\n,\nICLR'24\n,\nAmazon Alexa Prize\n,\nFIRE-Bench\n)\nCompositional & self-specializing foundation models\n(\nICLR'23\n,\nICLR'25\n,\nNeurIPS'23 Oral\n)\nFoundation models and AI co-scientists for discovery\n(\nNeurIPS'25\n,\nNature'25\n,\nCancer Discovery R&R\n,\nUC-LEAP Grant\n)\nSelected Honors\nGordon and Betty Moore Foundation Fellowship\n2025\nOpenAI Research Grant Award\nResearch into Agentic AI Systems; one of 11 teams selected worldwide\n2024\nRising Star in Data Science\n, University of Chicago\n2022\nBest Paper Award\n, SoCal NLP Symposium\n2023\nAmazon Alexa Prize Winner\n, TaskBot Challenge (3rd Place)\n2022\nGraduate Research Award\n(Mike Liu Scholarship), OSU\n2022\nNews\nMar 2026\nInvited talk at the\nStanford NLP Seminar\non \"Building AI that Reasons to Accelerate Real-world Discovery.\"\nFeb 2026\nReleased arXiv versions of\nscPilot\nand\nCellMaster\n, scientific copilot agents towards AI co-scientists, collaborating with human scientists in executing comp-bio analyses and discovering new insights from data directly.\nJan 2026\nReleased\nFIRE-Bench\n, benchmarking full-cycle scientific discovery automation with verifiable evaluation.\nJan 2026\nNabla-Reasoner\nwas accepted to ICLR 2026: latent test-time reasoning with first-order optimization in logit space.\nDec 2025\nHonored to organize\nLAW 2025 workshop (Bridging Language, Agent, and World Models) at NeurIPS 2025\n. Thanks to our amazing co-organizers, Ziqiao, Jessy, Melanie, Jianwen, Kelsey, Alane, Jacob, Tianmin, and Zhiting; and speakers, Sherry, Chelsea, Francois, Eric, Danijar, Philop, Stephen, Ying Nian, and Keyon. Check the recording of their talks\nhere\n.\nDec 2025\nPresenting two papers at NeurIPS 2025:\nscPilot\n(first omics-native reasoning agents) and\nDeepPersona\n(generative engine for real-human personas).\nNov 2025\nInvited talk at UCSD CSE AI Seminar: \"\nBuilding AI That Discovers\n.\"\nOct 2025\nReceived the\nGordon and Betty Moore Foundation Fellowship\nfor the Natural Sciences to support research on AI-driven scientific reasoning and discovery.\nSep 2025\nPart of\nnewly accepted Nature paper\non multi-omics discovery; contributed TaijiChat, a Paper Copilot.\nSep 2025\nscPilot\naccepted to NeurIPS 2025: omics-native reasoning for grounding LLMs in raw omics data.\nSep 2025\nReleased preprint:\nMutationProjector\n: cancer genomics foundation model for tumor mutation profiles.\nAug 2025\nAttended\nUC-LEAP\nKick-off at\nUCSB\n: exploring AI agents for Materials Science.\nJul 2025\nSpeaking at\nACL 2025 BoF: Bridging Human Study and LLM Agents for Social Simulation\n.\nJul 2025\nHosting\nLAW 2025 workshop\nat NeurIPS 2025 in San Diego this December!\nJun 2025\nAttended\nDL4SCI 2025\nat Berkeley: diving into AI for automated scientific discovery.\nJan 2025\nReleased blog:\nChatGPT's Second Year: 10 Aha Moments of 2024\nJan 2025\nSelf-MoE\naccepted to ICLR 2025: transforming monolithic LLMs into modular self-specialized experts.\nOct 2024\nReleased\nDecentralized Arena\n: democratic LLM benchmarking where models judge each other.\nHF Leaderboard\nOct 2024\nReleased\nTxT360\n: first dataset to globally deduplicate 99 CommonCrawl snapshots.\nDataset\nSep 2024\nDRPO\naccepted to EMNLP 2024: first tuning-free method for self-aligning LLMs with human preferences.\nJul 2024\nSelected for\n2024 AI+Science Summer School\nat University of Chicago.\nJul 2024\nLLM Reasoners\naccepted to COLM 2024. Check the 1k+ star\nGitHub package\n!\nFeb 2024\nReceived\nOpenAI research grant\nto support agentic systems research.\nJan 2024\nPromptAgent\naccepted to ICLR 2024: first principled framework for API-based prompt optimization.\nNov 2023\nReceived\nTop Reviewer Award\nat NeurIPS 2023.\nNov 2023\nBest Paper Award\nat\nSoCal NLP 2023\n.\nOct 2023\nReasoning via Planning\nfeatured in\nState of AI Report 2023\n!\nOct 2023\nRAP\naccepted to EMNLP 2023 Main: augmenting LLM reasoning with world models and planning.\nSep 2023\nToolkenGPT\naccepted as\noral presentation\nat NeurIPS 2023: augmenting LLMs with efficient tool learning.\nFeb 2023\nStarted postdoc at UCSD, collaborating with teams from CMU and MBZUAI on large language models research.\nJan 2023\nMultitask Prompt Tuning\naccepted to ICLR 2023.\nNov 2022\nPassed PhD defense: \"Toward Knowledge-centric Natural Language Processing: Acquisition, Representation, Transfer, and Reasoning.\"\nJun 2022\nTacoBot earned\n3rd place\nin inaugural\nAlexa Prize TaskBot Challenge\n.\nMay 2022\nJoined\nMIT-IBM Watson AI Lab\nas research intern on efficient LLM adaptation.\nMar 2022\nReceived\n2022 Graduate Research Award\nfrom the CSE department.\nDec 2020\nSelected as\nRising Star in Data Science\nat the University of Chicago CDAC.\nResearch Highlights\nFull List on Google Scholar →\nMethodological Contributions\nReasoning and Planning:\nLAW 2025 (NeurIPS 2025)\n,\nRAP (EMNLP 2023)\n,\nLLM Reasoners (COLM 2024)\n,\nThinkSum (ACL 2023)\n,\nPromptAgent (ICLR 2024)\n,\nDRPO (EMNLP 2024)\n,\nNabla Reasoner (ICLR 2026)\nFoundation Model Training:\nMultitask Prompt Tuning (ICLR 2023)\n,\nSelf-MoE (ICLR 2025)\n,\nToolkenGPT (NeurIPS 2023 Oral)\nKnowledge Extraction with Weak Supervisions:\nSurfCon (KDD 2019)\n,\nX-MedRELA (ACL 2020)\n,\nConPI (WSDM 2021)\nScientific Testbeds & Impact\nAI for Life Science:\nScientific Foundation Models (\nMutationProjector\n), AI Co-scientists (\nNature 2025\n;\nscPilot, NeurIPS 2025\n;\nCellMaster\n), Biomedical Graph Learning (\nBioNEV, Bioinformatics 2019\n)\nAI for Material Science:\nTritonDFT (Multi-agents for DFT Automation)\n,\nUC-LEAP (Low-Energy, AI-Informed Phase Transitions)\nAI for Social Science:\nComputational social simulation (\nDeepPersona\n;\nS3-Sim Human Simulator\n),\nTacoBot (Alexa Prize 2021)\nOpen-Source Infrastructure\nReasoning Library:\nLLM Reasoners\n(2.3k+ GitHub stars),\nPromptAgent\n(350+ GitHub stars)\nModel Evaluation:\nDecentralized Arena\n,\nFIRE-Bench\n(Reliably benchmarking scientific (re-)discovery)\nPre-training Data:\nTxT360\n(58K downloads last month, globally deduplicated corpus across 99 CommonCrawl snapshots)\nVisit my\nPublications page\nfor the complete list of papers and research contributions.\nMiscellaneous\nOutside of research, you'll likely find me hiking, playing pickleball, or planning my next adventure in national parks. I'm a passionate sports fan, cheering for the\nBuckeyes\n,\nDodgers\n,\nLakers\n,\nInter Miami\n, and\nChiefs\n.\nReading is also my main way of thinking outside of code and experiments. I enjoy essays, literary fiction, science fiction, and books on philosophy and ideas. Recently I've been reading 许知远的《伯克利的魔山》,\nThe Complete Short Stories of Ernest Hemingway\n, and George Zarkadakis's\nIn Our Own Image\n, among others."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Chenyu You::http://chenyuyou.me/": {
    "homepage": "http://chenyuyou.me/",
    "all_emails": [
      "chenyu.you@stonybrook.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/charlesyou999648",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chenyu-you-b07475a4/",
    "homepage_text": "Chenyu You\nChenyu You\nHome\nBio\nResearch\nGroup\nTopics\nPapers\nProspective\nStudents\nTeaching\nCourses\nService\nRecent\nChenyu You\nChenyu You\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics & Statistics\nDepartment of Computer Science\nStony Brook University\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\nIntroduction\nChenyu You is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Applied Mathematics & Statistics and Department of Computer Science at Stony Brook University. \nHe is also the core faculty member of the\nCVLab\n,\nAI institute\n,\nand affiliated with the\nInstitute for Advanced Computational Science\n.\nPreviously, he received his Ph.D. in 2024 from Yale University under the advisement of\nJames S. Duncan\n, \nhis M.S. in 2019 from Stanford University under the advisement of\nDaniel Rubin\n, \nand his B.S. in 2017 from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute under the advisement of\nGe Wang\n, all in electrical engineering.\nHe has also spent wonderful time at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, \nas well as\nGoogle Research\n.\nResearch\nMy group studies focuses on fundamental and applied problems in\ncomputer vision\nand\nmachine learning\n, with a focus on\nAI for health\n.\nWe build intelligent systems that learn from complex data, reason about and interact with the real world, and drive meaningful impact on healthcare.\nBesides learning algorithms, we ask: how AI should represent knowledge across imaging, text, and multi-omics data; what principles ensure robustness, trustworthy, and clinical reliability; and how algorithmic advances can translate into real-world healthcare domains. \nOur research aims to answer these questions by advancing machine learning methods in close collaboration with biomedical and clinical science.\nFoundation:\nHow do we build world foundation models that generalize across diverse clinical tasks?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nMedSAM\n/\nMONA\n/\nARCO\n/\nKGAE\n/\nUniHGKR\nReliability:\nHow can we build complex AI systems that clinicians can trust and rely on?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nSpuriousMemorization\n/\nCFR\n/\nCASTformer\nAccess:\nHow can we turn advances in AI into efficient, deployable tools that improve healthcare and advance scientific discovery?\nRepresentative projects\n:\nCSR\n/\nCSRv2\n/\nOTSurv\n/\nMORSE\nHere is some information for prospective students and visitors.\nNews\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TAI\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nFour paper accepted at CVPR 2026.\n[2026.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MIDL 2026.\n[2026.02]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive the Excellence in Teaching Award for Fall 2025.\n[2026.01]\nPAPER\nTwo papers on\nultra-sparse embeddings\nand\nsparse feature attention\naccepted at ICLR 2026.\n[2026.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive CPAL Rising Stars Award 2026. Many thanks for the acknowledgment!\n[2026.01]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2026.\n[2026.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive Tinker Research Grant Award from Thinking Machines Lab!\n[2025.12]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging Distinguished Associate Editor Certificate of Excellence!\n[2025.12]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MIDL 2026.\n[2025.11]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Associate Editor for Medical Image Analysis!\n[2025.11]\nPAPER\nOur work\nCoMA\n, a multi-agent complex human motion generation framework, is accepted at AAAI 2026. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.11]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive AAAI New Faculty Highlights 2026. Many thanks for the acknowledgment!\n[2025.11]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Associate Editor for Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n[2025.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TMI (Impact Factor 9.8).\n[2025.10]\nSERVICE\nThrilled to serve on the\nSUNY AI Symposium Planning Committee\n!\n[2025.09]\nPAPER\nOur work\nMartian World Model\naccepted at NeurIPS 2025. [\nNews\n]\n[2025.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at RSNA 2025\n(Oral)\n.\n[2025.09]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair CVPR 2026.\n[2025.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at EMNLP 2025.\n[2025.07]\nAWARD\nThrilled to receive the Excellence in Teaching Award for Spring 2025.\n[2025.07]\nAWARD\nCongratulations to my Ph.D. student, Qin Ren, on winning the MICCAI 2025 NIH Registration Grant!\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur work\nOuroboros\non cycle-consistent rendering via diffusion models is accepted at ICCV 2025. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur work\nOTSurv\n, leveraging Optimal Transport for survival analysis, is accepted at MICCAI 2025. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.06]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nUncovering Memorization Effect in the Presence of Spurious Correlations\n” has been formally accepted by Nature Communications. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ACL 2025.\n[2025.05]\nPAPER\nOur work\ncontrastive sparse representations (CSR)\naccepted at ICML 2025\n(Oral, Top ~1%)\n. [\nCode\n|\nHugging Face Blog\n]\n[2025.04]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at AIME 2025.\n[2025.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at EMBC 2025\n(Oral, Top Paper Award)\n.\n[2025.03]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ACM TKDD.\n[2025.03]\nPAPER\nOur work\nUniHGKR\n, a universal retrieval-augmented generation framework, is accept at NAACL 2025\n(Oral)\n. [\nCode\n]\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair EMNLP 2025.\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair COLM 2025.\n[2025.02]\nTALK\nInvited as panel speaker at the AAAI Bridge: AI for Medicine and Healthcare.\n[2025.02]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve on scientific committee for the 11th Workshop on Medical Computer Vision at CVPR 2025.\n[2025.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Nature Reviews Bioengineering.\n[2025.01]\nSERVICE\nInvited to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2025!\n[2025.01]\nEDITOR\nThrilled to serve as Guest Associate Editor for IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging!\n[2024.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MedIA (Impact Factor 10.9).\n[2024.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE TMI (Impact Factor 8.9).\n[2024.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Computerized Medical Imaging and Graphics.\n[2024.10]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer (Highest award).\n[2024.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MedIA (Impact Factor 10.9).\n[2024.09]\nAWARD\nWorld’s Top 2% Scientists by Stanford University.\n[2024.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nMONA\nhas been formally accepted by\nIEEE-TPAMI\n(Impact Factor 20.8). [\nCode\n]\n[2024.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at BMVC 2024\n(Oral)\n.\n[2024.06]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nMedical image registration via neural fields\n” accepted by Medical Image Analysis (MedIA) (Impact Factor 10.9). Congrats to Shanlin, and all collaborators!\n[2024.06]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI 2024.\n[2024.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at UAI 2024.\n[2024.04]\nAWARD\nPrivileged to be elected into\nSigma Xi\n!\n[2024.03]\nSERVICE\nThrilled to serve as Area Chair MICCAI 2024!\n[2024.02]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nCalibrating Multi-modal Representations: A Pursuit of Group Robustness without Annotations\n” has been accepted at CVPR 2024.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2024.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at CVPR 2024.\n[2024.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ICLR 2024.\n[2024.01]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as WACV 2024 Outstanding Reviewer.\n[2024.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Imaging Neuroscience.\n[2023.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE SaTML 2023.\n[2023.11]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nSegment Anything in Medical Images\n” has been formally accepted by Nature Communications.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.10]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at WACV 2024.\n[2023.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IEEE BIBM 2023.\n[2023.10]\nAWARD\nThrilled to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nRethinking Semi-Supervised Medical Image Segmentation: A Variance-Reduction Perspective\n” has been accepted at NeurIPS 2023!\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at NeurIPS 2023!\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at npj Digital Medicine (Impact Factor 15.357).\n[2023.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Physics in Medicine and Biology.\n[2023.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-MLCN 2023.\n[2023.06]\nPAPER\nFour papers accepted at IEEE NSS-MIC-RTSD 2023 (1 Oral).\n[2023.06]\nPAPER\nSix papers accepted at MICCAI 2023.\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Investigative Radiology (Impact Factor: 10.065).\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nThree papers\nearly accepted\nat MICCAI 2023!\n[2023.05]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at ACL 2023.\n[2023.02]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nACTION\nhas been accepted at IPMI 2023.\n      [\nCode\n]\n[2023.02]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IPMI 2023.\n[2023.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at Medical Physics.\n[2022.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at WACV 2023.\n[2022.09]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nCASTformer\nhas been accepted at NeurIPS 2022!\n[2022.09]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at NeurIPS 2022!\n[2022.08]\nTALK\nGave a talk at\nMeta AI Research (FAIR)\nEastcoast Vision Group about Contrastive Learning.\n[2022.08]\nAWARD\nVery honored to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Platinum Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2022.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at WACV 2023.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-STACOM 2022.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-DeCaF 2022.\n[2022.07]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-DGM4MICCAI 2022.\n[2022.06]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at MICCAI 2022.\n[2022.05]\nPAPER\nOne paper\nearly accepted\nat MICCAI 2022!\n[2022.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at NAACL 2022.\n[2022.03]\nPAPER\nOur paper\nSimCVD\nhas been formally accepted by\nIEEE-TMI\n(Impact Factor: 10.048).\n[2022.03]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ICLR-PAIR2Struct 2022.\n[2022.03]\nSTATUS\nI will be interning at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, New York, starting from June 2022.\n[2022.02]\nAWARD\nVery proud to be recognized as a\nDistinguished Referee\nfor Medical Physics.\n[2021.12]\nAWARD\nAwarded 2021 - 2022 Yale Fellowship.\n[2021.12]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at AAAI 2022.\n[2021.11]\nPAPER\nOne paper has been formally accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (IEEE-TPAMI)\n(Impact Factor 17.861).\n[2021.10]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at WACV 2022.\n[2021.09]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at NeurIPS 2021.\n[2021.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at EMNLP 2021.\n[2021.06]\nPAPER\nThree papers accepted at Interspeech 2021.\n[2021.05]\nAWARD\nGlad to be recognized as CVPR 2021 outstanding reviewer.\n[2021.04]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at IJCAI 2021 (Acceptance Rate: 13.9%).\n[2021.03]\nAWARD\nVery proud to be recognized as Medical Physics Journal Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2021.02]\nAWARD\nVery honored to be recognized as IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (TMI) Distinguished Reviewer.\n[2021.01]\nPAPER\nTwo papers accepted at IEEE-ICASSP 2021.\n[2021.01]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at ICLR 2021\n(Spotlight)\n.\n[2020.11]\nAWARD\nAwarded 2020 - 2021 Yale Fellowship.\n[2020.10]\nAWARD\nProud to be an Outstanding Reviewer for MICCAI 2020.\n[2020.08]\nPAPER\nOne paper accepted at MICCAI-MIL3ID 2020.\n[2020.07]\nPAPER\nOur work\nNuSeT\n, a high quality tool box for cell segmentation and analysis, accepted at PLOS Computational Biology. [\nCode\n]\n[2019.10]\nAWARD\nAwarded 2019 - 2020 Yale Fellowship.\n[2019.09]\nPAPER\nThree full papers accepted at Proceedings of SPIE.\n[2019.06]\nAWARD\nOur paper “Recovery of Latent Vectors and Exploration of Latent Space from StyleGAN” received the\nStanford CS230 Final Project Prize\n,\n      mentored by\nProf. Andrew Ng\n.\n[2019.06]\nPAPER\nOur paper “\nCT Super-resolution GAN Constrained by the Identical, Residual, and Cycle Learning Ensemble(GAN-CIRCLE)\n”\n      has been formally accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (IEEE-TMI)\n(Impact Factor: 10.048). [\nCode\n]\n[2019.01]\nPAPER\nOne papers accepted at Medical Physics.\nContact\nEmail: chenyu.you [AT] stonybrook [DOT] edu\nAddress: Math Tower 1-A148, Stony Brook, NY 11794\nPage generated by\njemdoc\n.\n\n---\n\nChenyu You – Biography\nChenyu You\nHome\nBio\nResearch\nGroup\nTopics\nPapers\nProspective\nStudents\nTeaching\nCourses\nService\nRecent\nBio\nChenyu You is an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics & Statistics\nand\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nStony Brook University\n. \nHe is also the core faculty member of the\nCVLab\n,\nAI institute\n, and affiliated with the\nInstitute for Advanced Computational Science\n.\nHis research focuses on both fundamental and applied problems in computer vision and machine learning, often with a focus on generalization, and making machine learning more reliable. Our applied research includes applications to healthcare, biomedical imaging, and cognitive neuroscience. \nHe received his Ph.D. in 2024 from Yale University under the advisement of\nJames S. Duncan\n, his M.S. in 2019 from Stanford University under the advisement of\nDaniel Rubin\n, and his B.S. in 2017 from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute under the advisement of\nGe Wang\n, all in electrical engineering. \nHe has also spent wonderful time at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, as well as\nGoogle Research\n.\nHe serves on the\nMedical Image Computing and Computer-Assisted Intervention Society (MICCAI)\n, \nand the\nSUNY AI Symposium Planning Committee\n, \nand as associate editors for\nIEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging\n,\nMedical Image Analysis\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n,\nPattern Recognition\n,\nand\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n.\nHe has received AAAI'26 New Faculty Highlights, CPAL'26 Rising Stars Award, Tinker Research Grant Award, ICML'25 Oral Presentataion Award, EMBC'25 Top Paper Award, MICCAI'25 NIH Registration Grant Award, IEEE TMI'25 Distinguished Associate Editor Certificate of Excellence Award, and Yale George P. O’Leary Graduate Fellowship, \nand has been ranked as the World's Top 2% most-cited scientists by Stanford University since 2024, is a member of the\nSigma Xi\nscientific research society, and received the Excellence in Teaching Award for Spring and Fall 2025.\nPage generated by\njemdoc\n.\n\n---\n\nChenyu You – Biography\nChenyu You\nHome\nBio\nResearch\nGroup\nTopics\nPapers\nProspective\nStudents\nTeaching\nCourses\nService\nRecent\nBio\nChenyu You is an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics & Statistics\nand\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nStony Brook University\n. \nHe is also the core faculty member of the\nCVLab\n,\nAI institute\n, and affiliated with the\nInstitute for Advanced Computational Science\n.\nHis research focuses on both fundamental and applied problems in computer vision and machine learning, often with a focus on generalization, and making machine learning more reliable. Our applied research includes applications to healthcare, biomedical imaging, and cognitive neuroscience. \nHe received his Ph.D. in 2024 from Yale University under the advisement of\nJames S. Duncan\n, his M.S. in 2019 from Stanford University under the advisement of\nDaniel Rubin\n, and his B.S. in 2017 from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute under the advisement of\nGe Wang\n, all in electrical engineering. \nHe has also spent wonderful time at\nFacebook AI Research (FAIR)\n, as well as\nGoogle Research\n.\nHe serves on the\nMedical Image Computing and Computer-Assisted Intervention Society (MICCAI)\n, \nand the\nSUNY AI Symposium Planning Committee\n, \nand as associate editors for\nIEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging\n,\nMedical Image Analysis\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks a...[truncated]"
  },
  "deep_homepage::S. Kevin Zhou::https://knzhou.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://knzhou.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
