    "homepage_text": "Cheng Chen\nHome\nAbout me\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nServices\nCheng Chen\nTenure-track Associate Professor\nSoftware Engineering Institute\nEast China Normal University\nOffice: Math Building 304\nEmail: chchen@sei.ecnu.edu.cn\nAbout Me\nI am currently a tenure-track associate professor in Software Engineering Institute of East China Normal University. Previously I worked at Nanyang Technological University as a research fellow. I received my PhD degree from Shanghai Jiao Tong University, where I was fortunate enough to be advised by Yong Yu and Zhihua Zhang. During the PhD, I visited the math department of UC Berkeley, hosted by Ming Gu. Prior to that, I received my bachelor's degree from ACM Class at Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nProspective students:\nI am always looking for outstanding and highly self-motivated students to work with me. Please email me with your CV and transcripts if you are interested.\nResearch Interest\nMy research interest is in developing practical machine learning algorithms with strong theoretical guarantees, with a focus on\nonline learning\nreinforcement learning\nfast and scalable optimization methods\nmatrix low-rank approximation\nstreaming numerical linear algebra"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yue Hu::https://hu-yue.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://hu-yue.github.io/",
