    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yue Hu\nSearch\nHi! I’m\nYue Hu\n, a\nrobotics researcher\n.\nI am an\nAssistant Professor\nin the Department of\nMechanical & Mechatronics Engineering\nat the\nUniversity of Waterloo\n. Head of the\nActive & Interactive Robotics Laboratory (A.I.R. Lab)\n.\nMy main research interests are social-physical human robot-interaction, optimization and optimal control for robots, collaborative robots, humanoid robots, and human motion analysis.\nHere you can find preprints of my publications, overviews of past and ongoing research projects, teaching materials (coming soon), and my contact information.\nShort bio\nContact me\nYue Hu\nAssistant Professor,\nDepartment of Mechanical & Mechatronics Engineering, University of Waterloo\nI am a tenure track Assistant Professor in the Department of Mechanical & Mechatronics Engineering at University of Waterloo since 2021, I belong to the Automation and Control group, and I am leading the\nActive & Interactive Robotics Laboratory (A.I.R. Lab)\n.\nI am also one of the co-chairs of the\nIEEE-RAS Technical Committee on Model-Based Optimization for Robotics\n.\nBefore Waterloo, I lived and worked in several countries.\nI got my bachelor degree in Electronics Engineering in 2011 from University of Genova, in Italy.\nThen in 2013 I obtained my masters' degree (MSc) in Advanced Robotics (EMARO - European Master on Advanced Robotics) from both University of Genova and Ecole Centrale de Nantes (France).\nFrom 2013 to 2018 I was in Heidelberg, Germany, working mainly on the humanoid robot iCub, and the analysis of human walking. I carried out my PhD in robotics (Computer Science) with the Optimization in Robotics and Biomechanics (ORB) group, at Heidelberg University, under the supervision of Prof. Dr. Katja Mombaur and Dr. Francesco Nori (Italian Institute of Technology). I obtained my degree with Summa cum laude in April 2017. I was then postdoc at ORB until February 2018.\nIn 2018 I was postdoc at the Dynamic Interaction Control Research Line lead by Dr. Daniele Pucci, at the Italian Institute of Technology in Genova, Italy, where I worked mainly on whole-body control and teleoperation of the iCub.\nBetween 2018 and 2021 I was in Japan, developing my own research direction of active physical human-robot interaction, starting from (but not limited to) collaborative manipulators.\nFrom 2018 to 2020 I was a JSPS (Japan Society for the Promotion of Sciences) postdoctoral fellow under the supervision of Dr. Eiichi Yoshida, and in collaboration with Prof. Gentiane Venture and Dr. Mehdi Benallegue at the CNRS-AIST JRL (Joint Robotics Laboratory), National Institute of Advanced Industrial Sciences and Technology (AIST), in Tsukuba.\nBetween 2020 and 2021, I was an assistant professor at the GVLab lead by Prof. Gentiane Venture, in the Department of Mechanical Systems Engineering at Tokyo University of Agriculture and Technology.\nCV\nEducation\nPhD in Robotics (Computer Science), 2017\nHeidelberg University (Germany)\nMaster in Advanced Robotics (EMARO, double degree), 2013\nUniversity of Genova, Ecole Centrale de Nantes\nBachelor in Electronics Engineering, 2011\nUniversity of Genova\nInterests\nSocial and physical human-robot interaction\nOptimization and optimal control for robots\nCollaborative robots\nHumanoid robots\nHuman motion analysis\nHuman factors\nHuman-centered robotics\nAcademic experience\nAssistant professor (tenure track)\nDepartment of Mechanical & Mechatronics Engineering, University of Waterloo\nSep 2021 –\n              \n                Present\nWaterloo (ON), Canada\nTeaching, supervision, and research\nAssistant professor\nDepartment of Mechanical Systems Engineering, Tokyo University of Agriculture and Technology (TUAT)\nDec 2020 –\n              \n                Aug 2021\nTokyo, Japan\nTeaching and research\nJSPS (Japan Society for the Promotion of Sciences) postdoctoral fellow\nCNRS-AIST JRL (Joint Robotics Laboratory), National Institute of Advanced Industrial Sciences and Technology (AIST)\nNov 2018 –\n              \n                Nov 2020\nTsukuba, Japan\nResearch\nPostdoc\nDynamic Interaction Control (DIC), Italian Institute of Technology (IIT)\nMar 2018 –\n              \n                Oct 2018\nGenova, Italy\nResearch\nPostdoc\nOptimization in Robotics and Biomechanics (ORB), Heidelberg University\nMay 2017 –\n              \n                Feb 2018\nHeidelberg, Germany\nResearch\nResearch projects\nOngoing and past projects\nMore info coming soon.\nInterface, modeling, and control of Meca500 R3\nActive physical human-robot interaction\nTelepresence for walking and manipulation of humanoid robots\nWalking of the iCub humanoid robot\nModeling and analysis of compliance during human walking\nModeling and control of the HeiCub humanoid robot with SEA\nRecent publications\nMissing preprints (PDF) coming soon\nYue Hu\n,\nNaoko Abe\n,\nMehdi Benallegue\n,\nNatsuki Yamanobe\n,\nGentiane Venture\n,\nEiichi Yoshida\n(2022).\nToward Active Physical Human–Robot Interaction: Quantifying the Human State During Interactions\n.\n  In\nIEEE THMS\n.\nPDF\nDOI\nMarie Yamamoto\n,\nYue Hu\n,\nEnrique Coronado\n,\nGentiane Venture\n(2021).\nImpression evaluation of robot’s behavior when assisting human in a cooking task\n.\n  In\nIEEE RO-MAN\n.\nYue Hu\n,\nNaoko Abe\n,\nMehdi Benallegue\n,\nNatsuki Yamanobe\n,\nGentiane Venture\n,\nEiichi Yoshida\n(2021).\nActive Physical Human-Robot Interaction: an experiment towards quantifying human interactions\n.\n  In\n3rd International Jc-IFToMM Symposium\n.\nSee all publications\nRecent & Upcoming Talks\nResearch with the iCub - from walking to teleoperation, what’s behind successful demos\nAbstract The iCub humanoid robot was not meant for walking when it was first “born” in 2008, but a new design of the legs introduced in …\nMon, Nov 8, 2021\n              \n              1:00 PM\nWaterloo, ON, Canada (Online)\nYue Hu\nInteract with me, Active Physical Human-Robot Interaction\nAbstract Two research directions have been trying to breach the barrier between humans and robots: physically (pHRI), and socially …\nMon, Jul 19, 2021\n              \n              11:30 AM\n              \n              — 3:30 PM\nMunich, Germany (Online)\nYue Hu\nSee all talks\nSupervision\nStudents and projects\nCurrently considering applications from students at all levels:\nUndergraduate\n: URA (Undegraduate Research Assistant), Co-op (USRA - Undergraduate Student Research Awards), or if you want to volunteer!\nFYDP/Capstone\n: reach me out if you think I can help and advise your team! Available also to provide ideas for potential projects.\nMASc and PhD\n: please contact me directly. If you are a domestic applicant, if eligible, please apply to scholarships such as\nOGS\nand\nNSERC CGS\n. If you are an international applicant, your application will be subject to available funding.\nContact me\nif you are interested in any of the projects listed in this website or doing research in topics including (but not limited to): human-robot interaction, optimal control applied to robotics, collaborative robotics, humanoid robotics, human motion analysis.\nContact\nyue.hu@uwaterloo.ca\nUniversity of Wateloo, Waterloo(ON), Canada\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
