    "homepage_text": "Huiqi Li\n      -  Beijing Institute of Technology\nBeijing Institute of Technology Home\nEnglish\n中文\nSearch content at Beijing Institute of Technology\nView Scopus Profile\nHuiqi Li\nSchool of Information and Electronics\nh-index\n5298\nCitations\n40\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2000                 …\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nPersonal profile\nLi Huiqi\nProfessor\nDate of birth: June 1972\nOffice Tel: 010-68918239\nE-mail: huiqili@bit.edu.cn\n2011 to date: Doctoral Supervisor, School of Information and Electronics, Beijing Institute of Technology\n2004-2011: Senior Research Fellow at Infocomm Research Institute of Singapore\n2002-2004: Research Fellow, Department of Computer Science, National University of Singapore\n1999-2002: PhD in Image Processing, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore\n1995-1999: Worked as an engineer in the overall Department of Beijing Control Instrument Research Institute\n1993-1995: Master of Automatic Control in Harbin Institute of Technology\n1989-1993: Majored in Automatic control at Harbin Institute of Technology\nResearch Interests\nMedical Image Processing, Intelligent Medicine, Artificial Intelligence\nEducation\n2011 to date: Doctoral Supervisor, School of Information and Electronics, Beijing Institute of Technology\n2004-2011: Senior Research Fellow at Infocomm Research Institute of Singapore\n2002-2004: Research Fellow, Department of Computer Science, National University of Singapore\n1999-2002: PhD in Image Processing, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore\n1995-1999: Worked as an engineer in the overall Department of Beijing Control Instrument Research Institute\n1993-1995: Master of Automatic Control in Harbin Institute of Technology\n1989-1993: Majored in Automatic control at Harbin Institute of Technology\nProfessional Experience\n2011 to date: Doctoral Supervisor, School of Information and Electronics, Beijing Institute of Technology\n2004-2011: Senior Research Fellow at Infocomm Research Institute of Singapore\n2002-2004: Research Fellow, Department of Computer Science, National University of Singapore\n1999-2002: PhD in Image Processing, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore\n1995-1999: Worked as an engineer in the overall Department of Beijing Control Instrument Research Institute\n1993-1995: Master of Automatic Control in Harbin Institute of Technology\n1989-1993: Majored in Automatic control at Harbin Institute of Technology\nResearch Achievement\nHe has published more than 100 SCI/EI papers in medical image processing and pattern recognition related fields, and more than 10 international and domestic patents. Representative papers of the first author and corresponding author are as follows:\nElsevier China High Citation Scholar (2014-2019: Biomedical Engineering, 2020: Electronic Science and Technology)\nBeijing Institute of Technology. Beili \"Teacher Commendation Conference Teaching Education Human Commendation 2020\nExcellent Doctoral Thesis Advisor of Beijing Institute of Technology 2020\nChinese Institute of Electronics Excellent Master Thesis Advisor 2019\nBeijing University Excellent Undergraduate Graduation Design Instructor 2019\nExcellent Master's Thesis Advisor, Beijing Institute of Technology 2015, 2018-2020\nBest Paper Award at the 11th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications (ICIEA) 2016\nBeijing Institute of Technology \"Outstanding Young and Middle-aged Teachers Development Support Program\" selected 2011\nMinistry of Education \"New Century Talent Support Program\" selected 2011\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Huiqi Li is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n5\nSimilar Profiles\nExperimental Result\nEngineering\n100%\nCataract\nMedicine and Dentistry\n77%\nComponent Analysis\nEngineering\n66%\nPrincipal Components\nEngineering\n66%\nRegion of Interest\nEngineering\n62%\nAnomaly Detection\nComputer Science\n60%\nMedical Image\nEngineering\n58%\nFeature Extraction\nEngineering\n55%\nView full fingerprint\nResearch output\n84\nArticle\n80\nConference contribution\n3\nChapter\n3\nPaper\n5\nMore\n3\nConference article\n1\nComment/debate\n1\nShort survey\nA spatiotemporal model for future fundus image prediction with irregularly sampled sequential data\nLi, M., Zhao, H.,\nZhang, W.\n, Xu, J. &\nLi, H.\n,\nJan 2026\n,\nIn:\nApplied Soft Computing.\n186\n, 114062.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nExperimental Result\n100%\nState-of-the-Art Method\n100%\nMotion Estimation\n100%\nProgression\n100%\nPrediction Network\n100%\nImproving OCTA Imaging Through Cross-Domain Adaptation: A Noise-Guided Framework Using Intralipid-Enhanced Rat Data\nYang, B., Tan, B., Gu, Z., Schmetterer, L.,\nLi, H.\n& Cheng, J.,\n2026\n,\nMedical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention, MICCAI 2025 - 28th International Conference, Proceedings.\nGee, J. C., Hong, J., Sudre, C. H., Golland, P., Alexander, D. C., Iglesias, J. E., Venkataraman, A. & Kim, J. H. (eds.).\nSpringer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH\n,\np. 282-292\n11 p.\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science; vol. 15966 LNCS).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\n›\npeer-review\nOptical Coherence Tomography Angiography\n100%\nIntralipid\n100%\nDomain Adaptation\n100%\nHuman Subject\n40%\nNon Invasive Procedure\n20%\nRetSTA: An LLM-Based Approach for Standardizing Clinical Fundus Image Reports\nCai, J.,\nZhang, W.\n, Liu, H., Wang, N. &\nLi, H.\n,\n2026\n,\nMedical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention, MICCAI 2025 - 28th International Conference, Proceedings.\nGee, J. C., Hong, J., Sudre, C. H., Golland, P., Alexander, D. C., Iglesias, J. E., Venkataraman, A. & Kim, J. H. (eds.).\nSpringer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH\n,\np. 544-553\n10 p.\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science; vol. 15965 LNCS).\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nConference contribution\n›\npeer-review\nDiseases\n100%\nAdaptive multi-scale feature extraction and fusion network with deep supervision for retinal vessel segmentation\nZhu, X., Cao, B.,\nZhang, W.\n&\nLi, H.\n,\nJun 2025\n,\nIn:\nMultimedia Systems.\n31\n,\n3\n, 197.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nVessel Segmentation\n100%\nFeature Extraction\n100%\nMultiscale\n100%\nScale Feature\n100%\nSegmentation Performance\n33%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitation\n(Scopus)\nA degradation-aware enhancement network with fused features for fundus images\nHu, T., Yang, B.,\nZhang, W.\n,\nZhang, Y.\n&\nLi, H.\n,\n25 Mar 2025\n,\nIn:\nExpert Systems with Applications.\n266\n, 125954.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nReceptive Field\n100%\nGeneralization Ability\n50%\nImage Quality\n50%\nAided Diagnosis\n50%\nReal Image\n50%\n2\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 175 research outputs"
