    "homepage_text": "Chengsen Wang - Homepage\nChengsen Wang\nA PhD student at BUPT, with primary research interest in time series analysis and genomic foundation model.\n📫 Feel free to discuss and collaborate with me!\nBeijing, China\nEmail\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nI’m a PhD student in the class of 2023 at the\nNetwork Intelligence Research Center (NIRC)\nwithin the\nBeijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT)\n, advised by Prof.\nQi Qi\nand Prof.\nJingyu Wang\n. My primary research interests focus on time series analysis and genomic foundation model. I have published several relevant papers in top conferences with total\ngoogle scholar citations 231\n.\nIf you are interested in collaborating on research projects, offering internship opportunities, or exchange programs, I would be thrilled to connect with you. You can also find my CV here:\nEN\n/\nZH\n.\n🔥 News\n2025.09\n:  🎉🎉🎉\nMCAKE: Memory-Augmented Autoencoder with Contrastive Learning for Unsupervised Anomaly Detection\nhas been accepted by\nTKDD 2025\n.\n2024.12\n:  🎉🎉🎉\nChatTime: A Unified Multimodal Time Series Foundation Model Bridging Numerical and Textual Data\nhas been accepted by\nAAAI 2025 [oral]\n.\n2024.09\n:  🎉🎉🎉\nRethinking the Power of Timestamps for Robust Time Series Forecasting: A Global-Local Fusion Perspective\nhas been accepted by\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\n2023.09\n:  🎉🎉🎉\nDrift doesn’t Matter: Dynamic Decomposition with Diffusion Reconstruction for Unstable Multivariate Time Series Anomaly Detection\nhas been accepted by\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n📖 Educations\n2023.09 – Present\n, PhD Student, Computer Science and Technology, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications.\n2022.09 – 2023.06\n, MS Student, Computer Science and Technology, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications.\n2018.09 – 2022.06\n, Undergrad Student, Automation, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications.\n🛵 Experiences\n2025.02 – 2025.05\n, Research Intern, Noah’s Ark Lab, Huawei Technologies.\n🌱 Services\nConferences\nReviewer, The Thirty-Second SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (SIGKDD 2026, h5=124)\nReviewer, The Forty-Third International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2026, h5=272)\nReviewer, The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2026, h5=362)\nReviewer, The Fortieth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2026, h5=232)\nReviewer, The Thirty-Ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2025, h5=371)\nReviewer, The Forty-Second International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2025, h5=272)\nReviewer, The Thirteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2025, h5=362)\nReviewer, The Thirty-Eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024, h5=371)\nJournals\nReviewer, IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE, h5=126)\nReviewer, IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS, h5=165)\n📝 Publications\nAAAI 2025 [oral]\nChatTime: A Unified Multimodal Time Series Foundation Model Bridging Numerical and Textual Data\nChengsen Wang\n, Qi Qi, Jingyu Wang, Haifeng Sun, Zirui Zhuang, Jinming Wu, Lei Zhang, Jianxin Liao\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nNeurIPS 2024\nRethinking the Power of Timestamps for Robust Time Series Forecasting: A Global-Local Fusion Perspective\nChengsen Wang\n, Qi Qi, Jingyu Wang, Haifeng Sun, Zirui Zhuang, Jinming Wu, Jianxin Liao\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nNeurIPS 2023\nDrift doesn’t Matter: Dynamic Decomposition with Diffusion Reconstruction for Unstable Multivariate Time Series Anomaly Detection\nChengsen Wang\n, Zirui Zhuang, Qi Qi, Jingyu Wang, Xingyu Wang, Haifeng Sun, Jianxin Liao\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n👀 Visitors\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
