      "rzhang8@uncc.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Dr. Ran Zhang's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWelcome to Dr. Ran Zhang's Homepage\nRan Zhang, Ph.D.\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nThe William States Lee College of Engineering\nUniversity of North Carolina at Charlotte\n9201 University City Blvd, Charlotte, NC, 28223-0001\nOffice: EPIC 2332\nEmail:\nrzhang8@uncc.edu\nor\nrzhang8@charlotte.edu\nTel: (704) 687 8425\nOfficial Website\n|\nGoogle Scholar Site\nBiography |\nCV\nDr. Ran Zhang (S’11 - M’15 – SM’22) is currently an Assistant Professor at\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\n,\nUniversity of North Carolina, Charlotte\n, NC, USA. He\nreceived his\nB.E. degree on Electronic Information Science and Technology in 2016 from the\nDepartment of Electronic Engineering\n,\nTsinghua University\n, China. He received his Ph.D. degree on Electrical\nEngineering\nin 2016 from the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\n,\nUniversity of Waterloo\n, Canada, under the supervision of Professor\nXuemin (Sherman) Shen\nand Professor\nLiang-liang Xie\n. From 20\n18 to 2023, Dr. Ran Zhang worked as an assistant professor at\nDepartment of Electrical and Engineering\n,\nMiami University\n.\nFrom 2015\nto 2018,\nDr. Ran Zhang worked as a system engineer in\nOttawa Research Center, Huawei Technologies, Canada.\nResearch Interests\nUnmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) Based\nCommunications\nCheck out our latest videos on\nStudent Drone Projects\n!\n[\nAutonomous and Distributed Multi-drone Platform\n(Ongoing)\n]\n[\nRoboMaster TT Drone - SmartRecognition and Synchronization\n]\nRadio Resource Management in Future Mobile Communication Systems\nMachine Learning (Deep learning and Reinforcement learning)\nChannel Coding (Polar Coding) Design for 5G New Radio\nVehicular Cyber-Physical Systems\nSmart Grid\nOpening Positions\nWe have open positions for\nself-motivated\nPh.D.\nand\nMaster\nstudents with strong interests in areas of wireless communications and networking, machine learning, and\nUnmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) based\ncommunications. Graduate applicants please email me your resume with subject “\nPhD/Master\nApplication_UNCC: Applicant Name\n” to\nrzhang8@charlotte.edu\n, and cc\nzhangran2006@gmail.com\n.\nUndergraduate students are very welcome\nto join in the research projects\n.\nPaid positions are available.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
