    "homepage_text": "Shaozhe Hao\nShaozhe Hao\n郝绍哲\nCS Ph.D. candidate @ HKU\nszhao [at] cs [dot] hku [dot] hk\nI am a last-year Ph.D. student in the\nSchool of Computing and Data Science\nat\nthe University of Hong Kong\n, advised by\nProf. Kenneth K.Y. Wong\nand\nDr. Kai Han\n(co-advisor). Before that, I obtained my B.E. degree from Huazhong University of Science and Technology.\n\t\t\tMy research focuses on visual representation learning and generative models.\nI am currently a Research Scientist Intern at\nMeta FAIR\nin Paris. I am also actively seeking full-time positions starting from early 2026.\nNews\n[Sep 2025] One paper about video editing dataset is accepted to\nNeurIPS 2025 (Datasets and Benchmarks)\n.\n[May 2025] One paper about LLMs for visual generation is accepted to\nICML 2025\n.\n[Feb 2025] One paper about robust subject-driven generation is accepted to\nCVPR 2025\n. Congratulations, Shuya!\nMore\n[Jan 2025] One paper about unifying visual generation and representation learning is accepted to\nICLR 2025\n.\n[Aug 2024] One paper is accepted to\nWACV 2025\nin Round 1 (12.1%). Congratulations, Zhi!\n[Jul 2024] Two papers about diffusion models are accepted to\nECCV 2024\n, with one selected as an\nOral\n.\n[Mar 2024] One paper, CiPR, about generalized category discovery is finally accepted to\nTMLR\n.\n[Sep 2023] One paper about controllable generation is accepted to\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n[Feb 2023] One paper about compositional zero-shot learning is accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n.\n[Jul 2022] One paper about masked face recognition is accepted to\nICIP 2022\n.\n[Sep 2021] I start my Ph.D. journey at HKU.\nPublications\n(\n*\nEqual contribution;\n#\nCorresponding authors;\n†\nProject lead)\nBiGR: Harnessing Binary Latent Codes for Image Generation and Improved Visual Representation Capabilities\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nXuantong Liu\n,\nXianbiao Qi\n†\n,\nShihao Zhao\n,\nBojia Zi\n,\nRong Xiao\n,\nKai Han\n#\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nICLR 2025\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nElucidating the Design Space of Language Models for Image Generation\nXuantong Liu\n,\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nXianbiao Qi\n†\n,\nTianyang Hu\n#\n,\nJun Wang\n,\nRong Xiao\n,\nYuan Yao\n#\nICML 2025\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nArtiFade: Learning to Generate High-quality Subject from Blemished Images\nShuya Yang\n*\n,\nShaozhe Hao\n*\n,\nYukang Cao\n#\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nCVPR 2025\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nCusConcept: Customized Visual Concept Decomposition with Diffusion Models\nZhi Xu\n*\n,\nShaozhe Hao\n*\n,\nKai Han\n#\nWACV 2025\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nConceptExpress: Harnessing Diffusion Models for Single-image Unsupervised Concept Extraction\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nKai Han\n#\n,\nZhengyao Lv\n,\nShihao Zhao\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nECCV 2024 (\nOral\n)\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nBridging Different Language Models and Generative Vision Models for Text-to-Image Generation\nShihao Zhao\n,\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nBojia Zi\n,\nHuaizhe Xu\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\nECCV 2024\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nViCo: Plug-and-play Visual Condition for Personalized Text-to-Image Generation\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nKai Han\n#\n,\nShihao Zhao\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\narXiv, 2023\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nCiPR: An Efficient Framework with Cross-instance Positive Relations for Generalized Category Discovery\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nKai Han\n#\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nTMLR 2024\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nUni-ControlNet: All-in-One Control to Text-to-Image Diffusion Models\nShihao Zhao\n,\nDongdong Chen\n#\n,\nYen-Chun Chen\n,\nJianmin Bao\n,\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nLu Yuan\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nNeurIPS 2023\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\nLearning Attention as Disentangler for Compositional Zero-shot Learning\nShaozhe Hao\n,\nKai Han\n#\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n#\nCVPR 2023\n[Project page]\n[arXiv]\n[Code]\n[Video]\nProfessional Service\nReviewer for:\nCVPR, NeurIPS, ECCV, AAAI, TMLR, TPAMI, IJCV, TIP\nTeaching Assistant for:\nCOMP3317 Computer Vision (Spring 2022, 2023, 2024)\nCOMP7310 Artificial Intelligence of Things (Fall 2023)"
