    "homepage_text": "Junjiao Tian\nJunjiao Tian\nHi, I am Junjiao Tian!\nI am a research scientist at Meta GenAI. I earned my PhD from the Robotics Perception and Learning Lab (RIPL) at Georgia Tech, advised by Prof.\nZsolt Kira\n. \n            I also contributed to the Bot Intelligence Group (BIG) at Carnegie Mellon University under Prof.\nJean Oh\n. \n            My research focuses on algorithmic methods to enhance the robustness of deep learning models.\nGoogle Scholar\nPh.D. Student in Robotics\nGeorgia Tech\nAug 2019 - Aug 2024\nM.S. in Robotics\nCMU\nSep 2017 - May 2019\nB.S. in ECE\nB.S. in MechSE\nUIUC\nSep 2013 - May 2017\nPublications\nRethinking Weight Decay for Robust Fine-Tuning of Foundation Models\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS24)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Chengyue Huang, Zsolt Kira.\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nCode\n]\nDiffuse, Attend, and Segment: Unsupervised Zero-Shot Segmentation using Stable Diffusion\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(CVPR24)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Lavisha Aggarwal, Andrea Colaco, Zsolt Kira, Mar Gonzalez-Franco.\n[\nPaper\n]\n         [\nProject Page\n]\n         [\nCode\n]\nFast Trainable Projection for Robust Fine-tuning\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS23)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Yen-Cheng Liu, James Seale Smith, Zsolt Kira.\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nCode\n]\nTrainable Projected Gradient Method for Robust Fine-Tuning\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(CVPR23)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Xiaoliang Dai, Chih-Yao Ma, Zecheng He, Yen-Cheng Liu, Zsolt Kira.\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nCode\n]\nStriking the Right Balance: Recall Loss for Semantic Segmentation\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation\n(ICRA22)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Niluthpol Mithun, Zach Seymour, Han-Pan Chiu, Zsolt Kira\n[\nPaper\n] \n        [\nCode\n]\nA Geometric Perspective towards Neural Calibration via Sensitivity Decomposition\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS21)\n(Spotlight < 3%)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Dylan Yung, Yen-Chang Hsu, Zsolt Kira\n[\nPaper\n]\n          [\nCode\n] \n          [\nProject Page\n]\nExploring Covariate and Concept Shift for Out-of-Distribution Detection\nNeurIPS Workshop on Distribution Shift\n(NeurIPS21)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Yen-Chang Hsu, Yilin Shen, Hongxia Jin, Zsolt Kira\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nProject Page\n]\nPosterior Re-calibration for Imbalanced Datasets\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS20)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Yen-Cheng Liu, Nathan Glaser, Yen-Chang Hsu, Zsolt Kira\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nCode\n]\nUNO: Uncertainty-aware Noisy-Or Multimodal Fusion for Unanticipated Input Degradation\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation\n(ICRA20)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Wesley Cheung, Nathan Glaser, Yen-Cheng Liu, Zsolt Kira\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nCode\n]\nImage Captioning with Compositional Neural Module Networks\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(IJCAI '19)\nJunjiao Tian\n, Jean Oh\n[\nPaper\n]\nIndustry Experience\nGoogle - AR experiences (2023)\nMeta Reality Labs - Mobile Vision Team (2022)\nSamsung Research America - AI Center (2021)\nSRI International - Center for Vision Technology (2020).\nExtracurricular\nAcademics Vice President of\nRoboGrads\nat Georgia Tech (Fall 2020 - Spring 2021)."
