    "homepage_text": "Xiaodong Liu | Home Page\nXiaodong Liu\nProfessor of Economics, University of Colorado Boulder\nResearch Interests: Econometrics, Applied Microeconomics\n·\nCV\n·\nGoogle Scholar Profile\n·\nFull Publication List\nSelected Publications\nChih-Sheng Hsieh, Michael König, Xiaodong Liu and Christian Zimmermann (2025)\n.  \n  Collaboration in Bipartite Networks, conditionally accepted,\nAEJ: Microeconomics\n.\n  (\npaper\n,\nappendix\n)\nHyunseok Jung and Xiaodong Liu (2026)\n.  \n  Testing for Peer Effects without Specifying the Network Structure,\nJournal of Econometrics\n,\n  253, 106124.\n  (\npaper\n,\nappendix\n)\nChih-Sheng Hsieh, Michael König and Xiaodong Liu (2025)\n.  \n  Endogenous Technology Spillovers in R&D Collaboration Networks,\nThe RAND Journal of Economics\n,\n  56, 419-443.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nXiaodong Liu and Ingmar R. Prucha (2025)\n.  \n  On Testing for Spatial or Social Network Dependence in Panel Data Allowing for Network Variability,\nJournal of Econometrics\n, 247, 105925.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nChih-Sheng Hsieh, Michael König and Xiaodong Liu (2022)\n.  \n  A Structural Model for the Coevolution of Networks and Behavior,\nThe Review of Economics and Statistics\n, 104, 355-367.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nLung-Fei Lee, Xiaodong Liu, Eleonora Patacchini and Yves Zenou (2021)\n.  \n  Who is the Key Player? A Network Analysis of Juvenile Delinquency,\nJournal of Business & Economic Statistics\n, 39, 849-857.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nMichael König, Xiaodong Liu and Yves Zenou (2019)\n.  \n  R&D Networks: Theory, Empirics and Policy Implications,\nThe Review of Economics and Statistics\n, 101, 476-491.\n  (\npaper\n,\nappendix\n)\nXiaodong Liu and Ingmar R. Prucha (2018)\n.  \n  A Robust Test for Network Generated Dependence,\nJournal of Econometrics\n, 207, 92-113.\n  (\npaper\n,\nappendix\n)\nEthan Cohen-Cole, Xiaodong Liu and Yves Zenou (2018)\n.  \n  Multivariate Choices and Identification of Social Interactions,\nJournal of Applied Econometrics\n, 33, 165-178.\n  (\npaper\n,\nappendix\n)\nWilliam Horrace, Xiaodong Liu and Eleonora Patacchini (2016)\n.  \n  Endogenous Network Production Functions with Selectivity,\nJournal of Econometrics\n, 190, 222-232.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nXiaodong Liu (2014)\n.  \n  Identification and Efficient Estimation of Simultaneous Equations Network Models,\nJournal of Business & Economic Statistics\n, 32, 516-536.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nXiaodong Liu, Eleonora Patacchini and Yves Zenou (2014)\n.  \n  Endogenous Peer Effects: Local Aggregate or Local Average?,\nJournal of Economic Behavior & Organization\n, 103, 39-59.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nLung-Fei Lee, Xiaodong Liu and Xu Lin (2010)\n.  \n  Specification and Estimation of Social Interaction Models with Network Structures,\nThe Econometrics Journal\n, 13, 145-176.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nLung-Fei Lee and Xiaodong Liu (2010)\n.  \n  Efficient GMM Estimation of High Order Spatial Autoregressive Models with Autoregressive Disturbances,\nEconometric Theory\n, 26, 187-230.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nXiaodong Liu, Lung-Fei Lee and Christopher R. Bollinger (2010)\n.  \n  An Efficient GMM Estimator of Spatial Autoregressive Models,\nJournal of Econometrics\n, 159, 303-319.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nXiaodong Liu and Lung-Fei Lee (2010)\n.  \n  GMM Estimation of Social Interaction Models with Centrality,\nJournal of Econometrics\n, 159, 99-115.\n  (\nworking paper version\n)\nWorking Papers\nXiaodong Liu and Erhao Xie (2025)\n.  \n    A Cognitive Hierarchy Model of Social Interactions. R&R,\nInternational Economic Review\n.\nZhongjian Lin, Xiaodong Liu and Ning N. Yu (2024)\n.  \n    Ordered Discrete Choices with Hoberogeneous Peer Effects.\nCourses Taught\nEcon 8838 – Advanced Econometrics II (2nd-year Ph.D.) –\nCourse Website\nEcon 8828 – Advanced Econometrics I (2nd-year Ph.D.) –\nCourse Website\nEcon 7828 – Econometrics (1st-year Ph.D.) –\nCourse Website\nEcon 4818 – Introductory Econometrics (Undergraduate) –\nCourse Website\nEcon 3818 – Introduction to Statistics (Undergraduate) –\nCourse Website"
