    "homepage_text": "Home | Jing Liu - Homepage\nJing Liu\nSenior Researcher, MSR-Asia\nEmail: jingliu3[at]microsoft.com\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]  [\nCV\n]\nBiography\nJing Liu is a senior researcher at Microsoft Research Asia. She earned her\nPh.D. in the computer sciences department, University of Wisconsin–Madison,\nunder the guidance of Prof.\nAndrea Arpaci-Dusseau\nand Prof.\nRemzi Arpaci-Dusseau\n. Jing was a recipient of a Meta Ph.D. Research Fellowship.\nHer research focuses on building instance-customizable operating systems and system stacks — systems that adapt at runtime to hardware and workloads without breaking compatibility, so that each workload instance can approach its own optimal performance. This includes both rethinking system architecture to make it customizable and designing mechanisms that turn traditionally fixed decisions into customizable ones while preserving compatibility.\nMore recently, she has been exploring how to enable in-situ code generation as part of core systems. The idea is to enable large language models (LLMs) write policy code that customizes kernel and system behavior on a per-instance basis (workload + hardware) at runtime, while keeping the system safe and responsive as workloads evolve. You can find more details in our recent work,\nKernelX\n.\nI’m actively looking for interns; feel free to drop me a line.\nNews\nAugust 2025: Aeolia is accepted to SOSP ’25. Congrats to the team!\nAugust 2025: Invited to serve on the OSDI ’26 program committee.\nJune 2025: Serving as Shadow-PC Co-chair for Eurosys ’26, check info\nhere\n!\nFeb 2025: Ananke won the Erik Riedel Best Paper Award at FAST ’25!\nJan 2025: Depsurf is accepted to Eurosys ’25.\nPublications\nZhongjie Chen, Wentao Zhang, Yulong Tang, Ran Shu, Fengyuan Ren, Tianyin Xu, and\nJing Liu\n.\n“\nPrincipled Performance Tunability in Operating System Kernels\n.” arXiv Preprint, 2025.\npaper\nYaoqi Chen, Jinkai Zhang, Baotong Lu, Qianxi Zhang, Chengruidong Zhang,\nJing Liu\n, Jingjia Luo, Di Liu, Huiqiang Jiang, Qi Chen, Bailu Ding, Xiao Yan, Jiawei Jiang, Chen Chen, Mingxing Zhang, Yuqing Yang, Fan Yang, and Mao Yang.\n“\nRetroInfer: A Vector Storage Engine for Scalable Long-Context LLM Inference\n.”\nIn Proceedings of the 52nd International Conference on Very Large Data Bases\n(VLDB ’26), Boston, USA, 2026.\nChuandong Li, Ran Yi, Zonghao Zhang,\nJing Liu\n, Changwoo Min, Jie Zhang, Yingwei Luo, Xiaolin Wang, Zhenlin Wang, Diyu Zhou. “\nAeolia: A Fast and Secure Userspace Interrupt-Based Storage Stack\n.” In Proceedings of the 31st Symposium on Operating Systems Principles (SOSP ’25), Seoul, South Korea, 2025.\npaper\nShawn Zhong,\nJing Liu\n, Andrea Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nRevealing the Unstable Foundations of eBPF-Based Kernel Extensions\n.” In Proceedings of the 20th European Conference on Computer Systems (Eurosys ’25), Rotterdam, Netherlands, 2025.\npaper\n,\nslides\n,\nposter\n,\ncode\n,\nwebsite\nJing Liu\n, Yifan Dai, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nFast, Transparent Filesystem Microkernel Recovery with Ananke\n.”\nIn Proceedings of The 23rd USENIX Conference on File and Storage Technologies (FAST ’25), Santa Clara, CA, USA, 2025.\npaper\n,\nslides\n(\nErik Riedel Best Paper Award\n)\nJing Liu\n, Xiangpeng Hao, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Tej Chajed. “\nShadow Filesystems: Recovering from Filesystem Runtime Errors via Robust Alternative Execution\n.”\nIn 16th ACM Workshop on Hot Topics in Storage and File Systems (HotStorage ’24), Santa Clara, CA, 2024.\npaper\n,\nslides\nYifan Dai,\nJing Liu\n, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nSymbiosis: The Art of Application and Kernel Cache Coordination\n.” In Proceedings of The 22nd USENIX Conference on File and Storage Technologies (FAST ’24), Santa Clara, CA, USA, 2024.\npaper\nJing Liu\n, Anthony Rebello, Yifan Dai, Chenhao Ye, Sudarsun Kannan, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nScale and Performance in a Filesystem Semi-Microkernel\n.” In Proceedings of the 28th ACM Symposium on Operating Systems Principles (SOSP ’21), Virtual Event, Germany, 2021.\npaper\n,\nvideo-long\n,\nslides-long\n,\nvideo-short\n,\nslides-short\n,\ncode\nIrene Zhang, Amanda Raybuck, Pratyush Patel, Kirk Olynyk, Jacob Nelson, Omar S. Navarro Leija, Ashlie Martinez,\nJing Liu\n, Anna Kornfeld Simpson, Sujay Jayakar, Pedro Henrique Penna, Max Demoulin, Piali Choudhury, and Anirudh Badam. “\nThe Demikernel Library OS Architecture for Microsecond, Kernel-Bypass Datacenter Systems\n.” In Proceedings of the 28th ACM Symposium on Operating Systems Principles (SOSP ’21), Virtual Event, Germany, 2021.\npaper\nJing Liu\n, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Sudarsun Kannan. “\nFile Systems as Processes\n.”\nIn 11th USENIX Workshop on Hot Topics in Storage and File Systems (HotStorage 19), Renton, WA, 2019.\npaper\n,\nslides\nIrene Zhang,\nJing Liu\n, Amanda Austin, Michael Lowell Roberts, and Anirudh Badam. “\nI’m Not Dead Yet! The Role of the Operating System in a Kernel-Bypass Era\n.” In Proceedings of the Workshop on Hot Topics in Operating Systems (HotOS ’19), Bertinoro, Italy, 2019.\npaper\nSuli Yang,\nJing Liu\n, Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nPrincipled Schedulability Analysis for Distributed Storage Systems using Thread Architecture Models\n.” In Proceedings of the 13th Symposium on Operating System and Design Implementation (OSDI ’18), CA, USA, 2018.\npaper\nRamnatthan Alagappan, Aishwarya Ganesan,\nJing Liu\n, Andrea Arpaci-Dusseau, and Remzi Arpaci-Dusseau. “\nFault-Tolerance, Fast and Slow: Exploiting Failure Asynchrony in Distributed Systems\n.” In Proceedings of the 13th Symposium on Operating System and Design Implementation (OSDI ’18), CA, USA, 2018.\npaper\nJing Liu\n, Tongwei Ren, Yuantian Wang, Sheng-Hua Zhong, Jia Bei, and Shengchao Chen. “\nObject proposal on RGB-D images via elastic edge boxes\n.” In Neurocomputing, 2017 May, 236:134-146.\npaper\nJing Liu\n, Tongwei Ren, Bing-Kun Bao, and Jia Bei, “\nDepth-aware layered edge for object proposal\n.” In Proceedings of IEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME ’16), Seattle, USA, 2016.\npaper\nJing Liu\n, Tongwei Ren, and Jia Bei. “\nElastic edge boxes for object proposal on RGB-D images\n.” In Proceedings of International Conference on Multimedia Modeling (MMM ’16), Miami, USA, 2016.\npaper\n,\nslides\nExperience\nInstructor, Computer Science Department, UW-Madison, WI. (Summer ’23)\nCS537 Operating Systems\nTeaching Assistant, Computer Sciences Department, UW-Madison, WI. (Spring ’22, Spring ’23)\nCS739 Distributed Systems\nInstructor: Prof.\nAndrea Arpaci-Dusseau\nResearch Intern, Microsoft Research, Redmond, WA. (May. 2018 - August. 2018)\nMentor:  Dr.\nIrene Zhang\n.\nResearch Assistant, State Key Laboratory for Novel Software Technology, Nanjing University. (Mar. 2014 - Jun. 2016)\nAdvisor: Prof.\nTongwei Ren\n.\nTeaching Assistant, Software Institute, Nanjing University.\nComputer Operating System. (Spring ’15, Spring ’16)\nInstructor: Prof.\nBing Luo\n& Prof.\nJidong Ge\n.\nHonors & Awards\nErik Riedel Best Paper Award, FAST ’25\nMeta PhD Research Fellowship, 2022 - 2024\nTravel Grant: OSDI ’22, OSDI ’18, and SOSP ’17\nSummer Research Award, CS@UW-Madison, 2017\nGraduate Research Fellowship, UW-Madison, 2016 – 2017\nDepartmental Best Undergraduate Thesis, University Highest Honor, 2016\nNational Encouraging Scholarship, Ministry of Education of China, 2014 & 2015\nNational Scholarship, Ministry of Education of China, 2013\nEducation\nPh.D. Department of Computer Sciences, UW-Madison, USA. August 2024\nB. Eng., Software Institute, Nanjing University, China. June 2016\nService\nShadow PC Co-chair, Eurosys ’26\nProgram Committee, SOSP ’25, APSys ’25, NSDI ’26, OSDI ’26\nExternal Review Committee, ATC ’24\nATC/OSDI Artifact Evaluation Committee, 2022\nTopic (OS & Emerging Hardware) Moderator, SOSP ’21 Diversity Workshop\nExternal Reviewer, FAST ’18"
