    "homepage_text": "Hong Zhou | UCLA Profiles\nUCLA.edu\nOur site may be slower due to heavy traffic from automated \"bots\" and AI crawlers. We're working to fix this.\nProfiles\nReturn to Top\nHong Zhou\nTitle(s)\nProfessor, MIMG\nSchool\nMedicine\nORCID\n0000-0002-8373-4717\nvCard\nDownload vCard\nBiography\neducation and training\nBaylor College of Medicine, Houston\nPhD\n05/1995\nBiochemistry\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China, Hefei, China\nB.S.\n07/1986\nPhysics\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China, Hefei, China\nM.S.\n12/1989\nSolid-state physics\nawards and honors\nThe Pew Charitable Trust\n1999\nPew Scholar\nAmerican Academy of Microbiology\n2024\nElected Fellow\nOverview\noverview\nDr. Zhou is a professor in the Department of Microbiology, Immunology and Molecular Genetics and the founding director of the UCLA Electron Imaging Center for Nanomachines.\nwebpage\nMIMG Department at UCLA\nProfessor Zhou's research lab page\nThe EICN facility established by Prof. Zhou\nmedia links\nAAM fellow\nORNG Applications\nFeatured Publications\nFeatured Content\nFeatured Videos\nBibliographic\nselected publications\nPublications listed below are automatically derived from MEDLINE/PubMed and other sources, which might result in incorrect or missing publications. \r\n\t\tResearchers can\nlogin\nto make corrections and additions, or\ncontact us for help\n.  \r\n        to make corrections and additions.\nNewest\n|\nOldest\n|\nMost Cited\n|\nMost Discussed\n|\nTimeline\n|\nField Summary\n|\nPlain Text\nAltmetrics Details\nPMC Citations\nindicate the number of times the publication was cited by articles in PubMed Central, and the\nAltmetric\nscore represents citations in news articles and social media.\r\n        (Note that publications are often cited in additional ways that are not shown here.)\nFields\nare based on how the National Library of Medicine (NLM) classifies the publication's journal and might not represent the specific topic of the publication.\nTranslation\ntags are based on the publication type and the MeSH terms NLM assigns to the publication.\r\n        Some publications (especially newer ones and publications not in PubMed) might not yet be assigned Field or Translation tags.)\r\n        Click a Field or Translation tag to filter the publications.\nStructure, identification, and characterization of the RibD-enolase complex in Francisella. Protein Cell. 2025 Dec 01; 16(12):1048-1053.\nLiu X, Clemens DL, Lee BY, Aguirre R,\nHorwitz MA\n,\nZhou ZH\n.  PMID: 40470850; PMCID:\nPMC12742849\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n1\nFields:\nBio\nBiochemistry\nCel\nCell Biology\nCryoDataBot: a pipeline to curate cryoEM datasets for AI-driven structural biology. bioRxiv. 2025 Sep 10.\nXu Q, Wu L, Rebelo M, Feng S, Yu X, Farheen F, Kihara D,\nZhou ZH\n.  PMID: 40964354; PMCID:\nPMC12439935\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\nCurvature Generation and Engineering Principles from Shewanella oneidensis Multi-flagellin Flagellum. ACS Nano. 2025 Jul 22; 19(28):25682-25696.\nLou Q, Fan H, Liu Y, Miller JF, Huang Y,\nZhou ZH\n.  PMID: 40627653; PMCID:\nPMC12291594\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\n2\nFields:\nNan\nNanotechnology\nTranslation:\nCells\nStructure of a new capsid form and comparison with A-, B-, and C-capsids clarify herpesvirus assembly. J Virol. 2025 Jul 22; 99(7):e0050425.\nStevens A, Kashyap S, Crofut E, Alvarez-Cabrera AL, Jih J, Liu Y-T,\nZhou ZH\n.  PMID: 40607812; PMCID:\nPMC12282113\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\nFields:\nVir\nVirology\nTranslation:\nHumans\nCells\nSarcospan protects against LGMD R5 via remodeling of the sarcoglycan complex composition in dystrophic mice. J Clin Invest. 2025 Sep 02; 135(17).\nMokhonova EI, Helzer D, Malik R, Mamsa H, Walker J, Maslanka M, Fleser TS, Afsharinia MH, Liu S, Holmberg J,\nZhou ZH\n,\nDeeds EJ\n, Hansen KC, McNally EM,\nCrosbie RH\n.  PMID: 40549548; PMCID:\nPMC12404760\n.\nView in:\nPubMed\nMentions:\nFields:\nMed\nMedicine (General)\nTranslation:\nHu