    "homepage_text": "Chen Xu's Homepage\nNews\nFeb 2025\nIn SIGIR 2025, three papers were accepted!\n        One paper\nElasticRank\nis about fairness using the elastic theory in economics.\n        One paper is the toolkit\nFairDiverse\nAnother paper\nCreAgent\nis about provider simulators in RS. Thanks to all the contributors!\nFeb 2025\nThe toolkit for implementing fairness and diverse IR algorithms have been published in\ngithub\nand\nArvix\n. It contains fairness and diversity 28 models with 16 IR base models! If you are intested, please give a try!\nJan 2025\nOne paper about Federated Learning for LLMs-based recommender systems has been accepted in NAACL findings!  Congrats to Jujia!\nJan 2025\nOne paper about fairness for LLMs-based recommender systems has been accepted in ICLR2025!  Thanks to all the contributors!\nSep 2024\nI am joining the IRLab as a visiting PhD student in 2024.10.17 !\nProf. Maarten de Rijke\nwill be his host. I will be working on fairness in recommender systems.\nSep 2024\nOne paper about implicit fairness for LLMs-based recommender systems has been accepted in EMNLP 2024 findings!  Thanks to all the contributors!\nAugust 2024\nOne paper about long-term fairness in recommendation has been accepted in TOIS 2024!  Thanks to all the contributors!\nJuly 2024\nI will visit the University of Amsterdam, and be supervised by\nProf. Maarten de Rijke\nin Oct 2024\nJuly 2024\nOne paper about fairness re-ranking has been accepted in CIKM 2024! Congratulations to Xiaopeng on his first paper!\nJuly 2024\nOne full paper is awarded as SIGIR 2024 Best Paper Honorable Mention! Thanks to all the contributors!\nApril 2024\nOne full paper is accepted in\nSIGIR2024\n, about fairness re-ranking models.\nJan 2023\nOne full paper is accepted in\nWWW2024\n, about fairness in retrieval process.\nChen Xu (徐晨)\nPhD Student\nIIR Lab\nGaoling School of Artificial Intelligence\nRenmin University of China\nRenmin University of China, No. 59 Zhongguancun Street, Haidian District, Beijing, China, 100872\nEmail: chenxu0427ruc AT gmail.com/xc_chen AT ruc.edu.cn\n•\nGoogle Scholar\n•\nGitHub\nI am a Ph.D. student, supervised by\nProf. Jun Xu.\nPrior to that, I received a double Bachelor's Degree in engineering and economics. My research interests include information retrieval, fairness.\nEducation\nRenmin University of China\nPh.D. in Computer Science, 2021 - present, China\nAdvisor:\nProf. Jun Xu\nRenmin University of China\nBachelor in Computer Science and Economics, 2017 - 2021, China\nAdvisor:\nProf. Jun Xu\nExperiences\nVisiting Ph.D. Student\n, NExT++ Lab, National University of Singapore Sep 2023 - July 2024\nAdvisor:\nProf. Tat-Seng Chua\nMentors:\nProf. Wenjie Wang\nVisiting Ph.D. Student\n, IRLab, University of Amsterdam Oct 2024 - Oct 2025\nAdvisor:\nProf. Maarten de Rijke\nToolkits and Software\npdf\nFairDiverse: A Comprehensive Toolkit for Fair and Diverse Information Retrieval Algorithms\nChen Xu\n, Zhirui Deng, Clara Rus, Xiaopeng Ye, Yuanna Liu, Jun Xu*, Zhicheng Dou*, Ji-Rong Wen, Maarten de Rijke\nGithub\n,\nDocuments\nTutorials, Surveys, and Workshops\npdf\nBias and Unfairness in Information Retrieval Systems: New Challenges in the LLM Era\nSunhao Dai,\nChen Xu\n, Shicheng Xu, Liang Pang, Jun Xu, Zhenhua Dong\nKDD2024;\nSurvey Link\npdf\nFairness in Information Retrieval from an Economic Perspective (SIGIR 2025)\nChen Xu\n, Clara Rus, Yuanna Liu, Marleen de Jonge, Jun Xu, Maarten de Rijke\nPublications\nGoogle Scholar\n*Corresponding author\npdf\nFairDiverse: A Comprehensive Toolkit for Fair and Diverse Information Retrieval Algorithms\nChen Xu\n, Zhirui Deng, Clara Rus, Xiaopeng Ye, Yuanna Liu, Jun Xu*, Zhicheng Dou*, Ji-Rong Wen, Maarten de Rijke\nSIGIR 2025 (resource paper)\npdf\nUnderstanding Accuracy-Fairness Trade-offs in Re-ranking through Elasticity in Economics\nChen Xu\n, Jujia Zhao, Wenjie Wang, Liang Pang, Jun Xu*, Tat-Seng Chua, Maarten de Rijke\nSIGIR 2025\npdf\nCreAgent: Towards Long-Term Evaluation of Recommender System under Platform-Creator Information Asymmetry\nXiaopeng Ye,\nChen Xu\n, Zhongxiang Sun, Jun Xu, Gang Wang, Zhenhua Dong, Ji-Rong Wen\nSIGIR 2025\npdf\nBridging Jensen Gap for Max-Min Group Fairness Optimization in Recommendation\nChen Xu\n, Yuxin Li, Wenjie Wang, Liang Pang, Jun Xu*, Tat-Seng Chua\nICLR 2025\npdf\nA Study of Implicit Ranking Unfairness in Large Language Models\nChen Xu\n, Wenjie Wang, Yuxin Li, Liang Pang, Jun Xu*, Tat-Seng Chua\nEMNLP findings 2024\npdf\nA Taxation Perspective for Fair Re-ranking\nChen Xu\n, Xiaopeng Ye, Wenjie Wang*, Liang Pang, Jun Xu*, Tat-Seng Chua\nSIGIR 2024\n(Best Paper Honorable Mention)\npdf\nBankFair: Balancing Accuracy and Fairness under Varying User Traffic in Recommender System\nXiaopeng Ye,\nChen Xu\n, Jun Xu*, Xuyang Xie, Gang Wang, Zhenhua Dong\nCIKM 2024\npdf\nFairSync: Ensuring Amortized Group Exposure in Distributed Recommendation Retrieval\nChen Xu\n, Jun Xu*, Yiming Ding, Xiao Zhang, Qi Qi\nWWW 2024\npdf\nLTP-MMF: Towards Long-term Provider Max-min Fairness Under Recommendation Feedback Loops\nChen Xu\n, Xiaopeng Ye, Jun Xu*, Xiao Zhang, Weiran Shen, Ji-Rong Wen\nTOIS 2024\npdf\nSyntactic-Informed Graph Networks for Sentence Matching\nChen Xu\n, Jun Xu*, Zhenhua Dong, Ji-Rong Wen\nTOIS 2023\npdf\nLlm-based federated recommendation\nJujia Zhao, Wenjie Wang*,\nChen Xu*\n, See-Kiong Ng, Tat-Seng Chua\nNAACL2025 findings\npdf\nP-MMF: Provider Max-min Fairness Re-ranking in Recommender System\nChen Xu\n, Sirui Chen, Jun Xu*, Weiran Shen, Xiao Zhang, Gang Wang, Zhenhua Dong\nWWW 2023\n(Spotlight-Best Paper Candidates)\npdf\nUncovering chatgpt’s capabilities in recommender systems\nSunhao Dai, Ninglu Shao, Haiyuan Zhao, Weijie Yu, Zihua Si,\nChen Xu\n, Zhongxiang Sun, Xiao Zhang, Jun Xu\nRecsys 2023 FAST track\npdf\nDually Enhanced Propensity Score Estimation in Sequential Recommendation\nChen Xu\n, Jun Xu*, Xu Chen, Zhenhua Dong, Ji-Rong Wen\nCIKM 2022\npdf\nSemantic Sentence Matching via Interacting Syntax Graphs\nChen Xu\n, Jun Xu*, Zhenhua Dong, Ji-Rong Wen\nCOLING 2022\nProfessional Services\nInvited Reviewer for\nTOIS, TIST, TKDE, JISIST, JIR\nProgram Committee Member of\nCIKM, EMNLP, KDD, WWW\nHonors\nBest Paper Honorable Mention in SIGIR 2024\n;\nSpotlights-Best Paper Candidates in WWW 2023\n;\nBest Oral and Poster Presentation at NCTIR, 2025\n;\nLast update: Oct, 2023. Webpage template borrows from\nProf. Xiangnan He\n."
  },
