    "homepage_text": "Jian Wu - Department of Decision Analytics and Operations, City University of Hong Kong\nmenu\nHome\nJian Wu 吴鉴\nDepartment of Decision Analytics and Operations\n,\nCollege of Business\n,\nCity University of Hong Kong\n83 Tat Chee Ave, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong\nEmail:\njian.wu\n[@] cityu.edu.hk\nBio\nI am an Assistant Professor of Management Sciences in the College of Business, City University of Hong Kong. Before joining CityU, I obtained my Ph.D. from Mitch Daniels School of Business at Purdue University, under the supervision of\nProf. Qi Annabelle Feng\n,\nProf. J. George Shanthikumar\n, and\nProf. William B. Haskell\n. My research focuses on decision-making under uncertainty in supply chain management.\nEducation\nPurdue University\n,\n2019 - 2025\nPh.D. in Operations Management\nThe University of Hong Kong\n,\n2015 - 2019\nB.Eng in Industrial Engineering and Technology Management (First Class Honor)\nThe University of Wisconsin-Madison\n,\nJanuary - May 2018\nExchange Student, International Academic Programs (IAP)\nJournal Publications\nSolving the Price-Setting Newsvendor Problem with Parametric Operational Data Analytics (ODA).\nManagement Science\n(with L. Y. Chu, Q. Feng, J. G. Shanthikumar and Z. J. M. Shen)\n[SSRN]\nContextual Data-Integrated Newsvendor Solution with Operational Data Analytics (ODA). Forthcoming,\nManagement Science\n(with Q. Feng and J. G. Shanthikumar)\n[SSRN]\nWorking Papers\nPreference Robust Optimization with Quasi-Concave Choice Functions in Multi-Attribute Decision Making: Characterization and Computation.\nUnder review\n. (with W. B. Haskell, W. Huang and H. Xu)\n[arXiv]\nOperational Data Analytics (ODA) Embedded Neural Network Learning for the Newsvendor Problem with General Demand.\nWork in progress\n(with Q. Feng and J. G. Shanthikumar)\nProximal Systems for Inventory Management under Positive Lead Times.\nWork in progress\n(with Q. Feng, J. G. Shanthikumar and Y. Yang)\nTeaching\nInstructor, MGMT361 Operations Management, Spring 2024, Purdue University\nTeaching assistant, MGMT565 Strategic Sourcing and Procurement, Fall 2021, Fall 2022, Purdue University\nTeaching assistant, MGMT568 Supply Chain Analytics, Summer 2022, Purdue University\nTeaching assistant, MGMT664 Supply Chain Management, Summer 2021, Purdue University\nHonors and Awards\nBilsland Dissertation Fellowship,\nPurdue University\nDSB Certificate for Outstanding Teaching,\nPurdue University\nDSB Doctoral Student Research Funds 2022, 2024,\nPurdue University\nKrannert Award for Doctoral Study in Supply Chain & OM 2019-20,\nPurdue University\nChina Soong Ching Ling Foundation Scholarships 2015-19\nPresentations\nContextual Data-Integrated Newsvendor Solution with Operational Data Analytics (ODA).\nPOMS Annual Conference, Virtual, 2022\nINFORMS Annual Meeting, Indianapolis, IN, 2022\nINFORMS Annual Meeting, Phoenix, AZ, 2023\nPOMS Annual Conference, Minneapolis, MN, 2024\nSolving the Price-Setting Newsvendor Problem with Parametric Operational Data Analytics (ODA).\nSeminar at Management Science and Engineering, Tsinghua University, 2023\nPreference Robust Optimization for Quasi-Concave Choice Functions.\nKrannert Doctoral Research Symposium, Purdue University, 2020\nService\nSession Chair, INFORMS Annual Conference 2022, 2023, 2024, POMS Annual Conference 2025\nReviewer for Management Science, Production and Operations Management, Naval Research Logistics, International Journal of Production Research"
