    "homepage_text": "Qinghua Hu\nQinghua Hu (è¡æ¸å), Professor\nCollege of Intelligence and Computing, Tianjin University, China\nDean of the School of Artificial Intelligence\nDirector, Tianjin Key Lab of Machine Learning\nService\nHonors\nFund\nPublications\nHome\nQinghua Hu is Dean of School of Artificial Intelligence, the Vice Chairman of Tianjin Branch of China Computer Federation, the Vice Directior of SIG Granular Computing and Knowledge Discovery, Chinese Association of Artificial Intelligence. He is Associate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Fuzzy Systemsï¼ACTA AUTOMATICA SINICAï¼Engergies . He now is supported by Key Program, National Natural Science Foundation of China. His research is focused on uncertainty modeling in big data, machine learning with multi-modality data, intelligent unmanned systems. He has published more than 200 peer-reviewed papers.\nEducation\n2012.4 - Present,Â        School of Computer Science and Technology, Tianjin University, full professor\n2009.10 - 2011.10,    Â Department of Computing, Hong Kong Polytechnic University, Postdoctoral Fellow\n2002.9 - 2008.11,       School of Aerospace, Harbin Institute of Technology,  Ph.D\n2000.9 - 2002.7,         School of Energy Science and Engineering, Harbin Institute of Technology,  Master\n1995.9 - 1999.7,Â      Â   School of Energy Science and Engineering, Harbin Institute of Technology, Bachelor\nResearch\nMultimodal machine learning\nUncertainty modeling in big data\nIntelligent unmanned system\nFault diagnosis\nSpace weather forecasting\nContact me\nRoom 515, Building 55B, Machine Learning and Data Mining\nCollege of Intelligence and Computing, Tianjin University, Jinnan, Tianjin, China"
  },
