    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/xinyi-wang915",
    "homepage_text": "Xinyi Wang - Homepage\nXinyi Wang\n王馨仪\nUniversity of Bristol\nPhD student@UoB. Working on computer vision, and video/image quality assessment.\n1.25, 1CS, Bristol, UK\nEmail\nResearchGate\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nI am a final-year PhD student in the\nVisual Information (VI) Laboratory\nat the\nUniversity of Bristol\n, supervised by\nDr. Angeliki Katsenou\n,\nDr. Shawn Shen\nand\nProf. David Bull\n, and funded by the\nUKRI MyWorld Strength in Places Programme\n.\nMy main research interests include video quality assessment and computer vision. I am particularly interested in topics such as content delivery, interactivity, and audience understanding, with a primary focus on video quality assessment for user-generated content (UGC).\n🔥 News\nNov 2025\n: The paper “\nCAMP-VQA: Caption-Embedded Multimodal Perception for No-Reference Quality Assessment of Compressed Video\n” was accepted by IEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV 2026).\nSep 2025\n: The paper “\nGuiding WaveMamba with Frequency Maps for Image Debanding\n” was accepted by Picture Coding Symposium (PCS 2025).\nMay 2025\n: The paper “\nDIVA-VQA: Detecting Inter-frame Variations in UGC Video Quality\n” was accepted by IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP 2025).\nApr 2025\n: The paper “\nFrame Differences Matter in Quality Assessment of Compressed Videos\n” was accepted by IEEE 25th International Conference on Digital Signal Processing (DSP 2025).\nFeb 2025\n: The paper “\nFoundations of Measuring Power and Energy Consumption in Video Communication\n” was accepted by IEEE Access. I contributed as a co-author.\nJun 2024\n: The paper “\nRate-Quality or Energy-Quality Pareto Fronts for Adaptive Video Streaming?\n” was accepted by IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP 2024). I contributed as a co-author.\nFeb 2024\n: The paper “\nComparative Study of Hardware and Software Power Measurements in Video Compression\n” was accepted by Picture Coding Symposium (PCS 2024). I contributed as a co-author.\nMay 2023\n: The paper “\nUGC quality assessment: exploring the impact of saliency in deep feature-based quality assessment\n” was accepted by Applications of Digital Image Processing XLVI, SPIE Optical Engineering + Applications 2023.\nOct 2022\n: 💪 I join the Visual Information (VI) Laboratory, University of Bristol as a\nPhD student\n!\nPublications\nVideo/Image Quality Assessment\nWACV 2026\nCAMP-VQA: Caption-Embedded Multimodal Perception for No-Reference Quality Assessment of Compressed Video\nXinyi Wang\n, Angeliki Katsenou, Junxiao Shen, David Bull\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n] [\n🤗Hugging Face\n]\nPCS 2025\nGuiding WaveMamba with Frequency Maps for Image Debanding\nXinyi Wang\n, Smaranda Tasmoc, Nantheera Anantrasirichai, Angeliki Katsenou\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n]\nICIP 2025\nDIVA-VQA: Detecting Inter-frame Variations in UGC Video Quality\nXinyi Wang\n, Angeliki Katsenou, David Bull\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n] [\n🤗Hugging Face\n]\nDSP 2025\nReLaX-VQA: Residual Fragment and Layer Stack Extraction for Enhancing Video Quality Assessment\nXinyi Wang\n, Angeliki Katsenou, David Bull\nPaper “\nFrame Differences Matter in Quality Assessment of Compressed Videos\n” accepted by IEEE 25th International Conference on Digital Signal Processing.\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n] [\n🤗Hugging Face\n]\nSPIE Optics + Photonics 2023\nUGC quality assessment: exploring the impact of saliency in deep feature-based quality assessment\nXinyi Wang\n, Angeliki Katsenou, David Bull\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n]\nSustainable Video Communications\nIEEE Access\nFoundations of Measuring Power and Energy Consumption in Video Communication\nChristian Herglotz, Angeliki Katsenou,\nXinyi Wang\n, Matthias Kränzler, Daniel Schien\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n]\nICIP 2024\nRate-Quality or Energy-Quality Pareto Fronts for Adaptive Video Streaming?\nAngeliki Katsenou,\nXinyi Wang\n, Daniel Schien, David Bull\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n]\nPCS 2024\nComparative Study of Hardware and Software Power Measurements in Video Compression\nAngeliki Katsenou,\nXinyi Wang\n, Daniel Schien, David Bull\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n] [\nCODE\n]\nQoMEX 2023\nVideo Quality Sufficiency for Sustainable Video Streaming\nAngeliki Katsenou,\nXinyi Wang\n, David Bull, Daniel Schien\n[\nARXIV\n] [\nPAPER\n]\nEducations\nOct 2022 - Present\nPhD in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK.\nSep 2020 - Nov 2021\nMSc (Distinction) in Image and Video Communications and Signal Processing, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK.\nSep 2016 - Jun 2020\nBEng (1st Class Hons.) in Telecommunications Engineering with Management, Queen Mary University of London, London, UK.\nSep 2016 - Jun 2020\nBEng in Telecommunications Engineering with Management (Joint Programme with QMUL), Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Beijing, China.\nExperiences\nSep 2024 - Present\nGraduate Teacher Level 2, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK\nTeaching Assistant for units in the School of Computer Science:\nCOMSM0160\nAdvanced Visual AI\nCOMSM0127\nImmersive Interaction and Audio Design\nCOMS30087\nImage Processing and Computer Vision\nTeaching Assistant for units in the School of Engineering Mathematics and Technology:\nEMATM0066\nVisual Analytics\nSep 2023 - Aug 2024\nGraduate Teacher Level 1, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK\nTeaching Assistant for units in the School of Engineering Mathematics and Technology:\nEMAT10100\nEngineering Mathematics 1 &\nEMAT20200\nEngineering Mathematics 2\nEMATM0066\nVisual Analytics &\nCOMSM0088\nAdvanced Data Analytics\nDec 2022 - Feb 2024\nResearch Assistant, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK\nResearch Assistant in Sustainable Video Communications\nJan 2023 - Dec 2023\nSCEEM Student Helper, University of Bristol, Bristol, UK\nApr 2019 - Sep 2020\nResearch Assistant, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China\nOct 2019 - Jan 2020\nTechnical Assistant Intern, Intel, Beijing, China\nHonors and Awards\nJun 2023\nSPIE Optics + Photonics 2023 Student Conference Support\nOct 2022\nMyWorld Scholarship\n(UKRI MyWorld Strength in Places Programme (SIPF00006/1))\nConference and Journal Service\nReviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (T-CSVT)\n2025 17th International Conference on Quality of Multimedia Experience (QoMEX)\n2025 Picture Coding Symposium (PCS 2025)\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
