    "homepage_text": "Shikun Zhang -\nToggle navigation\nSign in\nSign up\nconf.researchr.org\n/\nShikun Zhang\nconf.researchr.org general profile\n* ICSE 2018 * profile\nASE 2019 profile\nASE 2022 profile\nASE 2025 profile\nICSE 2020 profile\nICSE 2021 profile\nICSE 2026 profile\nICSME 2024 profile\nISSTA/ECOOP 2024 profile\nSANER 2024 profile\nNot registered as user\nName:\nShikun Zhang\nCountry:\nChina\nAffiliation:\nPeking University\nContributions\n2026\nInternational Conference on Program Comprehension\nAuthor of An Empirical Study on Data Influence-Based Pretraining Data Selection for Code Large Language Models within the Research Track-track\n2025\nASE\nAuthor of R3-Bench: Reproducible Real-world Reverse Engineering Dataset for Symbol Recovery within the Research Papers-track\n2024\nICSME\nAuthor of Improving long-tail vulnerability detection through data augmentation based on large language models within the Research Track-track\nISSTA\nAuthor of CoderUJB: An Executable and Unified Java Benchmark for Practical Programming Scenarios within the Technical Papers-track\nSANER\nAuthor of SWAT4J: Generating System Call Allowlist for Java Container Attack Surface within the Research Papers-track\nAuthor of ALANCA: Active Learning Guided Adversarial Attacks for Code Comprehension on Diverse Pre-trained and Large Language Models within the Research Papers-track\n2022\nASE\nAuthor of Low-Resources Project-Specific Code Summarization within the Research Papers-track\n2021\nInternational Conference on Program Comprehension\nAuthor of Exploiting Method Names to Improve Code Summarization: A Deliberation Multi-Task Learning Approach within the Research-track\n2020\nInternational Conference on Program Comprehension\nAuthor of Exploiting Code Knowledge Graph for Bug Localization via Bi-directional Attention within the Research-track\n2018\nInternational Conference on Program Comprehension\nAuthor of CoBOT: Static C/C++ Bug Detection in the Presence of Incomplete Code withi