    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Qi Tian - Home Page\nWelcome to My HomePage\nQi Tian\nChief AI Scientist, Huawei Consumer Business Group (CBG) &\nDirector of Guangming Laboratory, Shenzhen, China\nPh.D., Fellow of IEEE, ACM, AAAI, CAAI, CCF; IEAS Academician\nBantian Campus, Longgang District\nShenzhen, P. R. China 518129\nEmail: wywqtian at gmail dot com\nMy Google Scholar\nMy DBLP\nHome\nNews\nHonors and Awards\nService\nPublications\nDr. Qi Tian\nis currently the Chief Scientist in Artificial Intelligence at Huawei Consumer Business Groupp (CBG). He was the former Chief Scientist in Artificial Intelligence at Huawei Cloud, and Chief Scientist in Computer Vision at Huawei Noah’s Ark Laboratory from 2018-2024. Before he joined Huawei, Dr. Tian was a Full Professor in the Department of Computer Science, the University of Texas at San Antonio (UTSA) from 2002-2019. He is an ACM Fellow (2024), IEEE Fellow (2016), AAAI Fellow (2026), IEAS Academician (2021), CAAI Fellow (2022), CCF Fellow (2023), a Yangtze River Chaired Professor  of the Ministry of Education (2017), an Oversea Expert by the Chinese Academy of Science (2014). He received the prestigious 2025 SIGMM Technical Achievement Award (one per year) and 2021 Wu Wenjun Outstanding Contribution Award for Artificial Intelligence by CAAI (three per year).\nDr. Tian received his Ph.D. in ECE from University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC) in 2002 under supervision of Dr. Thomas S. Huang and received his B.E. in Electronic Engineering from Tsinghua University in 1992 and M.S. in ECE from Drexel University in 1996, respectively. Dr. Tian’s research interests include computer vision, multimedia content analysis, image and video indexing and retrieval, machine learnin, and AI for science, and published over 800 refereed journal and conference paper . He was the co-author of eight best papers including ACM Multimedia 2022, ICME 2019,\netc\n.\nDr. Tian’s past research projects were funded by ARO, NSF, DHS, Google, FXPAL, NEC, Blippar, SALSI, CIAS, Akiira Media Systems, HP and UTSA. He received 2017 UTSA President Distinguished Award for Research Achievement and 2010 Google Faculty Research Award. He is the Associate Editor of IEEE TMM, TCSVT, ACM TOMM, MMSJ, and MVA. Dr. Tian has served as SIGMM Executive Committee Member-at-large (2019-present ), Chair of Visual Signal Processing & Communication Technical Committee (VSPC-TC), IEEE Circuits and Systems Society (CASS), 2018-2020, founding member of International Steering Committee for ACM International Conference on Multimedia Retrieval (ICMR, 2009-2014), ACM Multimedia Conference Review Committee Member (2009-2012), and International Steering Committee Member for ACM MIR (2006-2010), ACM ICIMCS 2013, ICME 2006 and 2009, PCM 2012, and IEEE International Symposium on Multimedia 2011. He has served as general chair for ACM Multimedia Asia 2020, ACM Multimedia 2015, program coordinator for ACM Multimedia 2009, and area chairs for various international conferences including ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, ACM Multimedia, ACM ICMR,\netc\n. He has also served in various organization committees as Panel and Tutorial Chair, Publicity Chair, Special Session Chair, Track hair in numerous ACM and IEEE conferences such as ACM Multimedia, VCIP, PCM, CIVR, ICME, and served as TPC members for prestigious conferences such as ACM Multimedia, SIGIR, ICCV, and KDD.\nIn industry, as the Chief Scientist in Artificial Intelligence at Huawei, Dr.Tian has been applying the AI algorithms to real-world scenarios. He realized that AI will never be successful if engineers keep customizing an algorithm for each scenario that can incur heavy human labor. To overcome the difficulty, he led the team to construct a series of Pangu large-scale pre-trained models. As one of his representative work,  Pangu-Weather was published in\nNature\nin July 2023. Together with Google and Nvidia, Pangu-Weather was part of “the AI weather forecaster” recognized as\nScience’s 10 breakthroughs of 2023\n. In February 2024,  Pangu-Weather AI Model was ranked 1st in\nTop 10 Scientific Advances of 2023, China\nby the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC).\n—  Last Updated:  March, 2026   —"
  },
