    "homepage_text": "Percy Liang\nPercy Liang\nAssociate Professor of\nComputer Science\n(and courtesy in\nStatistics)\nDirector of\nCenter for Research on Foundation Models (CRFM)\nHuman-Centered Artificial Intelligence (HAI)\nArtificial Intelligence Lab\nNatural Language Processing Group\nMachine Learning Group\nGates 366\n[Publications]\n[Marin]\n[CodaLab]\n[sfig]\nIf you are interested in doing research with me, please join the\nMarin community\n, where we develop foundation models openly.\nResearch\nI am drawn to simple things, want to understand things deeply, and like to build useful systems.\n  I am interested in:\nWhat new possibilities do foundation models unlock?\n      Can we\nsimulate societies\nor solve\nhard ML problems\n?\nHow do we build foundation models from first principles?\n      How do we\nweight multiple datasets\n?\n      How do we grapple with\ncopyright and fair use\n?\n      How do we\nattribute model predictions back to training data\n?\nI am also a strong proponent of efficient and reproducible research.\n  We have been developing\nCodaLab Worksheets\n,\n  a platform that allows researchers to run and manage their experiments by maintaining the full provenance\n  of an experiment from raw data to final results.\n  Our papers are on CodaLab as\nexecutable papers\n.\nHere is some\ncode for older projects\n.\nCurrent Ph.D. students and post-docs\nRohith Kuditipudi\n(co-advised with\nJohn Duchi\n)\nSteven Cao\n(co-advised with\nGregory Valiant\n)\nQian Huang\n(co-advised with\nJure Leskovec\n)\nAhmed Ahmed\n(co-advised with\nSanmi Koyejo\n)\nMoo Jin Kim\n(co-advised with\nChelsea Finn\n)\nKen Liu\n(co-advised with\nSanmi Koyejo\n)\nSuhas Kotha\n(co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n)\nAnne Ouyang\n(co-advised with\nAzalia Mirhoseini\n)\nKaiyue Wen\n(co-advised with\nTengyu Ma\n)\nMarina Zhang\n(co-advised with\nCarlos Guestrin\n)\nA. Feder Cooper\n(post-doc, co-advised with\nDan Ho\n)\nSam Park\n(post-doc, co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n)\nAlumni\nJonathan Berant\n(post-doc 2015, co-advised with\nChris Manning\n, now associate professor at Tel-Aviv University)\nRoy Frostig\n(Ph.D. 2016, now research scientist at Google Research)\nSida Wang\n(Ph.D. 2017, co-advised with\nChris Manning\n, now research scientist at Meta)\nYuchen Zhang\n(post-doc 2018, co-advised with\nMoses Charikar\n, now researcher at Bytedance)\nHe He\n(post-doc 2018, now assistant professor at New York University)\nArun Chaganty\n(Ph.D. 2018, now research scientist at Google Research)\nKelvin Guu\n(Ph.D. 2018, now research scientist at Google DeepMind)\nJacob Steinhardt\n(Ph.D. 2018, now assistant professor at University of California Berkeley, founder of Transluce)\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n(post-doc 2019, co-advised with\nJohn Duchi\n, now assistant professor at Stanford University)\nFanny Yang\n(post-doc 2019, co-advised with\nJohn Duchi\n, now assistant professor at ETH Zurich)\nPanupong (Ice) Pasupat\n(Ph.D. 2019, now research scientist at Google)\nDaniel Selsam\n(Ph.D. 2019, co-advised with\nDavid Dill\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nRobin Jia\n(Ph.D. 2020, now assistant professor at University of Southern California)\nStephen Mussmann\n(Ph.D. 2021, now assistant professor at Georgia Institute of Technology)\nPranav Rajpurkar\n(Ph.D. 2021, co-advised with\nAndrew Ng\n, now associate professor at Harvard University)\nFereshte Khani\n(Ph.D. 2021, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nAditi Raghunathan\n(Ph.D. 2021, now assistant professor at Carnegie Mellon University)\nChris Donahue\n(post-doc 2022, now assistant professor at Carnegie Mellon University)\nPang Wei Koh\n(Ph.D. 2022, now assistant professor at University of Washington)\nNiladri Chatterji\n(post-doc 2023, co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n, now research scientist at Meta)\nShibani Santurkar\n(post-doc 2023, co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\nand\nTengyu Ma\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nDimitris Tsipras\n(post-doc 2023, co-advised with\nGregory Valiant\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nYuhuai (Tony) Wu\n(post-doc 2023, co-advised with\nJay McClelland\n, co-founder of xAI)\nYoav Levine\n(post-doc, 2023, now co-founder of AAI Technologies)\nAnanya Kumar\n(Ph.D. 2023, co-advised with\nTengyu Ma\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nMina Lee\n(Ph.D. 2023, now assistant professor at University of Chicago)\nJohn Thickstun\n(post-doc 2024, now assistant professor at Cornell University)\nJohn Hewitt\n(Ph.D. 2024, co-advised with\nChris Manning\n, will be assistant professor at Columbia University)\nShiori Sagawa\n(Ph.D. 2024, now research scientist at OpenAI)\n(Sang) Michael Xie\n(Ph.D. 2024, co-advised with\nTengyu Ma\n, now research scientist at Meta)\nMichi Yasunaga\n(Ph.D. 2024, co-advised with\nJure Leskovec\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nSarah Cen\n(post-doc 2025, co-advised with\nDan Ho\n, now assistant professor at Carnegie Mellon University)\nSherry Yang\n(post-doc 2025, now assistant professor at New York University)\nRishi Bommasani\n(Ph.D. 2025, co-advised with\nDan Jurafsky\n, now senior research scholar at Stanford HAI)\nYann Dubois\n(Ph.D. 2025, co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nSidd Karamcheti\n(Ph.D. 2025, co-advised with\nDorsa Sadigh\n, will be assistant professor at Georgia Institute of Technology)\nXiang Lisa Li\n(Ph.D. 2025, co-advised with\nTatsunori Hashimoto\n, will be assistant professor at University of Washington)\nNelson Liu\n(Ph.D. 2025, now research scientist at OpenAI)\nJoon Sung Park\n(Ph.D. 2025, co-advised with\nMichael Bernstein\n, now founder and CEO of a startup)\nTeaching\nLanguage Models from Scratch (CS336)\nAdvances in Foundation Models (CS324)\nArtificial Intelligence (CS221)\nStatistical Learning Theory (CS229T/STATS231)\n[\nlecture notes\n]\nEducation/Experience\n2012: post-doc at Google\n2011: Ph.D. from\nBerkeley\n(advisors:\nMichael Jordan\nand\nDan Klein\n)\n2005: MEng from\nMIT\n(advisor:\nMichael Collins\n)\n2004: B.S. from\nMIT\nHonors\nPresidential Early Career Award for Scientists and Engineers (2019)\nIJCAI Computers and Thought Award (2016)\nNSF CAREER Award (2016)\nSloan Research Fellowship (2015)\nMicrosoft Research Faculty Fellowship (2014)\nGraduate fellowships: NSF, NDSEG, GAANN, Siebel Scholar\nProgramming contests:\n      2nd place at 2002\nACM ICPC World Finals\n,\n      silver medalist at\nIOI\n2000\nMusic competitions (piano): Winner of KDFC Classical Star Search (2008, over-21 division),\n      MIT Concerto Competition (2004),\n      Phoenix Young Musicians Competition (2000)"
