  "deep_homepage::Gang Chen::https://gchenpu.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://gchenpu.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/gchenpu",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About - Gang Chen\nGang Chen\nProfessor in the Department of Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (AOS) at University of California-Los Angles (UCLA)\nFollow\nLos Angeles, California\nResearchGate\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nAbout\nThe focus of my research group is the fundamental dynamics in atmospheric circulation and chemical transport. Through a combination of theory and numerical modeling, we develop toolboxes to understand the global circulation of the atmosphere, from tropical Hadley cell circulations to extratropical storm systems, from tropospheric extreme weather to stratospheric polar vortex breakdown events, and from transport of water vapor to stratosphere-troposphere exchange of ozone. These processes are instrumental to our understanding of weather extremes (e.g. winter blizzards or heat waves), hydrological extremes (e.g., drought or flooding), or extreme air pollution. Our research can be categorized in two interrelated themes.\nGlobal atmospheric circulation and regional weather extremes\nTransport of atmospheric moisture and chemical species\nFor example, transport and mixing near the tropopause (~10km above the ground) can be illustrated in the animantion of Ertel’s Potential Vorticity (left) and O3 mixing ratio (right):\nRecent Publications\nLu, Kezhou, Gang Chen, Bowen Ge, Rong Fu, Weiming Ma and Hailong Wang, 2026:\nThe Role of Land-Atmosphere Feedbacks in Midlatitude Wintertime Surface Temperature Variability\n,\nGeophysical Research Letters\n, 53, e2025GL120713, doi:10.1029/2025GL120713.\nChen, Gang and Xiuyuan Ding, 2026:\nBenchmarking the Dynamic Modes of Stratosphere-Troposphere Coupling in Northern Annular Modes (NAM) in CMIP6 Models\n,\nGeophysical Research Letters\n, 53, e2025GL121278, doi:10.1029/2025GL121278.\nRan, Huanhuan, Lin Wang, Thomas Spengler, Gang Chen, Ping Huang and Kaiming Hu, 2025:\nLong-Term Trends of Northern Hemisphere Marine Cold Air Outbreaks during Boreal Winter: Influence of Sea Ice Retreat and Atmospheric Circulation\n,\nJournal of Climate\n, e240658, doi:10.1175/JCLI-D-24-0658.1.\nNie, Yu, Ying Sun, Xuebin Zhang and Gang Chen, 2025:\nHuman-Induced Changes in Extreme Cold Surges across the Northern Hemisphere\n,\nNature Communications\n, 16, 8086, doi:10.1038/s41467-025-62576-2.\nGe, Bowen, Gang Chen, Jian Lu and Wenyu Zhou, 2025:\nMoist Energy Constraints on Surface Temperature Variance Under Climate Warming\n,\nJournal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems\n, 17, doi:10.1029/2024MS004612.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nGang Chen\nGang Chen\nProfessor in the Department of Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (AOS) at University of California-Los Angles (UCLA)\nFollow\nLos Angeles, California\nResearchGate\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nEducation\nPrinceton University, Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences Program, Ph.D., 2002-2007\nPeking University, Dept. of Atmospheric Science, B.S., 1998-2002\nWork Experience\nUCLA, Dept. of Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences, Professor, 2019-present\nUCLA, Dept. of Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences, Associate Professor, 2016-2019\nCornell University, Dept. of Earth and Atmospheric Sciences, Associate Professor, 2015-2016\nCornell University, Dept. of Earth and Atmospheric Sciences, Assistant Professor, 2009-2015\nMIT, Program in Atmospheres, Oceans and Climate, NOAA C&GC Postdoctoral Fellow, 2007-2009"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Gongfan Fang::https://fangggf.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://fangggf.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
