    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/GodXuxilie",
    "linkedin": "https://linkedin.com/in/xilie-xu-1b547a268",
    "homepage_text": "About Me – Xilie Xu\nXilie Xu\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nHere is\nXilie Xu (徐曦烈)\n.\nI am a quantitative researcher at Baiont Quant. I recieved my PhD degree from\nthe School of Computing\nof\nthe National University of Singapore\nfortunately advised by\nProf. Mohan Kankanhalli\n. Before that, I received my bachelor’s degree in Computer Science from\nTaishan College\nat\nShandong University\nin 2021.\nNews\n[Aug 2025] I joined Baiont Quant as a quantitative researcher focusing on applying AI technologies to analysing financial data.\n[Jul 2025] I fortunately passed my thesis examination and have been conferred a Doctor of Philosophy degree.\n[Mar 2025]: The paper \"Privacy-Preserving Low-Rank Adaptation for Latent Diffusion Models\" recieved\nbest paper award\nat\nCoLoRAI\n!\n[Dec 2024]: One paper regarding privacy-preserving low-rank adaptation was accepted by AAAI'25! Congratulations to Zihao!\n[Sep 2024]: One paper regarding robust alignment was accepted by NeurIPS'24! Congratulations to Keyi!\n[Jul 2024]: Our team\nNUSafe\nwon the championship of\nthe ICML 2024 TiFA Workshop MLLM Attack Challenge\n!\n[Jun 2024]: I started the quantitative research internship at\nBaiont Quant\n!\n[May 2024]: I will attend ICLR 2024 conference at Vienna, Austria. See you there! Welcome to check our posters\nPromptAttack\nand\nAutoLoRa\n!\n[Apr 2024]: I gave a talk titled as \"Towards Effective and Efficient Evaluation of Large Language Model's Adversarial Robustness\" at N-CRiPT Technical Workshop, NUS.\n[Mar 2024]: I gave a talk titled as \"An LLM can Fool Itself: A Prompt-Based Adversarial Attack\" at\nN-CRiPT\nSeminar, NUS.\n[Feb 2024]: Our\nblog titled as ''\nTowards Robust Foundation Models: Adversarial Contrastive Learning\n''\nwas published at\nICLR Blogposts 2024'\n!\n[Jan 2024]: Two papers---both\nAutoLoRa\nand\nPromptAttack\n, were accepted by ICLR'24! Congratulations to Keyi!\n[Dec 2023]: Our\nPromptAttack\nwas accepted by\nAAAI'24 Workshop on Responsible Language Models\n!\n[Dec 2023]: I was invited as a reviewer for ICML'24.\n[Dec 2023]: I will attend NeurIPS 2023 conference at New Orleans, US. See you there! Welcome to check our\nSpotlight Poster\nand\nPoster\n!\n[Dec 2023]: I posted a tutorial to our NeruIPS'23 works regarding adversarial contrastive learning on\n知乎 (Chinese Quora)\n! 欢迎大家关注点赞👍！An English version of the tutorial is\nhere\n!\n[Nov 2023]: I gave a talk titled as \"Towards Building Robust Foundation Models\" at\nN-CRiPT\nSeminar, NUS.\n[Oct 2023]: We are glad to release\nRobustSSL Benchmark\n: a benchmark for robustness transferability of robust self-supervised learning (RobustSSL)!\n[Sep 2023]: Two papers regarding efficient and effective robust self-supervised pre-training were accepted by NeurIPS'23!\n[Sep 2023]: I was invited as a reviewer for ICLR'24.\n[Aug 2023]: I gave a talk titled as \"Towards Effective and Efficient Self-Supervised Robust Pre-training\" at AIGC’23, Shanghai, China.\n[Apr 2023]: I built the homepage of\nN-CRiPT Technical Workshop 2023\nand presented a\nposter\nat the workshop.\n[Dec 2022]: I successfully passed the PhD Qualification Examination!\n[May 2022]: One paper regarding robustness of two-sample tests was accepted by ICML'22!"
  },
