    "homepage_text": "Wei Wei's Homepage\nWei Wei\nweiwei@weiwei.one\nHome\nPublications\nBiography\nContact\nWelcome\nI am currently a research scientist at Google, where I work in the\nCloud AI group\nheaded by\nAndrew Moore\n. I am also an adjunct faculty member in Computer Science at Stanford univeristy. I teach\nFair, Accountable, and Transparent (FAccT) Deep Learning\nat Stanford together with\nJames Landay\n. I have broad interests in machine learning and have worked on a wide range of problems such as conversational models and adversarial robustness. Before I joined Google, I got my Ph.D. from the School of Computer Science at Carnegie Mellon University. You can find me on my\nGoogle AI homepage\n, my\nstanford webpage\n, my\nscholar profile\n, and my old\nCMU homepage\n.\n\n---\n\nWei Wei's Homepage\nWei Wei\nweiwei@weiwei.one\nHome\nPublications\nBiography\nContact\nContact\nMailling Address:\nWei Wei\n1600 Amphitheater PKWY\nMountain View, CA\n94043, USA\nOffice:\n1190 Bordeaux Drive , Building MP 4\nSunnyvale, CA\n94089, USA\n\n---\n\nWei Wei's Homepage\nWei Wei\nweiwei@weiwei.one\nHome\nPublications\nBiography\nContact\nBiography\nSummary of career via email addresses:\nweiwe@google.com\nFeb, 2017 - Present, Research Scientist, Google Inc.\nweiwei@cs.stanford.edu\nMar, 2020 - Present, Adjunct Lecturer, Stanford University\nweiwei@cs.cmu.edu\nAug, 2010 - Dec 2016, Ph.D. Student, Carnegie Mellon University"
  },
