    "homepage_text": "Tang Li - Homepage\nTang Li (李唐)\nUniversity of Delaware\nPh.D. candidate in DeepREAL Lab, CIS Department.\nNewark, DE, USA\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nI am a Ph.D. candidate in the\nComputer & Information Science Department\nat the\nUniversity of Delaware\n.\nI work under the advice of Prof.\nXi Peng\nin the\nDeepREAL Lab\n.\nMy research interest includes Interpretable Machine Learning, Vision-Language Models, Scientific Machine Learning, and Out-of-distribution Generalization. I have published papers\nat the top-tier AI/ML conferences, such as NeurIPS, CVPR, ICML, ECCV, AAAI, etc.\nI’m actively looking for full-time or internship research roles in the industry. If you think there’s a fit, feel free to reach out!\n🔥 News\n2025.05\n: Passed my Ph.D. Dissertation Proposal defense.  🎉🎉\n2025.03\n: I will join the Amazon Science\nBrand Protection team as summer intern in June.\n📝 Publications\nICML 2025\n“Why Is There a Tumor?”: Tell Me the Reason, Show Me the Evidence\nMengmeng Ma\n,\nTang Li\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\nIn Proceedings of the International Conference on Machine Learning, 2025. (acceptance rate 26.9%)\nAAAI 2025 Oral\nInterpretable Failure Detection with Human-Level Concepts\nKien X. Nguyen\n,\nTang Li\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\nIn Proceedings of the Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2025. (acceptance rate 4.7%)\nOral Presentation Award\nAAAI 2025\nBeyond Accuracy: On the Effects of Fine-tuning Towards Vision-Language Model’s Prediction Rationality\nQitong Wang\n,\nTang Li\n,\nKien X. Nguyen\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\nIn Proceedings of the Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2025. (acceptance rate 23.4%)\nNeurIPS 2024\nBeyond Accuracy: Ensuring Correct Predictions with Correct Rationales\nTang Li\n,\nMengmeng Ma\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\n|\nVideo\nIn Proceedings of the  Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024. (acceptance rate 25.8%)\nECCV 2024 Strong Double Blind\nDEAL: Disentangle and Localize Concept-level Explanations for VLMs\nTang Li\n,\nMengmeng Ma\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\n|\nVideo\nIn Proceedings of the European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2024. (acceptance rate 4.5%)\nStrong Double Blind\nICML 2024\nBeyond the Federation: Topology-aware Federated Learning for Generalization to Unseen Clients\nMengmeng Ma\n,\nTang Li\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\n|\nVideo\nIn Proceedings of the International Conference on Machine Learning, 2024. (acceptance rate 27.5%)\nCVPR 2023\nAre Data-driven Explanations Robust against Out-of-distribution Data?\nTang Li\n,\nFengchun Qiao\n,\nMengmeng Ma\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nCode\n|\nVideo\nIn Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023. (acceptance rate 25.8%)\nNeurIPSW 2021 Best Paper Award\nDeep Learning for Spatiotemporal Modeling of Urbanization\nTang Li\n,\nJing Gao\n, and\nXi Peng\nPaper\n|\nVideo\n|\nAward\nIn Proceedings of the Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) Workshops on Machine Learning in Public Health (MLPH), 2021.\nBest Paper Award\n💼 Experience\n2025.06 - 2025.09\n, Applied Scientist Intern, Brand Protection Team, Amazon Science\n, Seattle, WA, USA.\nDeveloped IPP-R1 multi-modal large language reasoning model for IP infringement detection.\nSupervised by Dr.\nChenge Li\nand Dr.\nShaonan Zhang\n.\n🏅 Honors and Awards\n2025.05\nOutstanding Graduate Research Assistant Award 2025, University of Delaware.\n2025.01\nOral Presentation Award\n, the Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI).\n2024.10\n$2,500\nCIS Outstanding Conference Travel Award, University of Delaware.\n2024.09\nStrong Double Blind Award\n, European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV).\n2024.08\n$2,500\nCIS Outstanding Conference Travel Award, University of Delaware.\n2024.07\n$5,000\nAPI credit from the\nOpenAI\nResearcher Access Program.\n2024.05\nDistinguished Graduate Student Award 2024, Computer & Information Sciences, University of Delaware.\n2023.03\n$1,000\nDepartment Travel Award for Outstanding Conference Publications, University of Delaware.\n2022.05\nDistinguished Graduate Student Award 2022, Computer & Information Sciences, University of Delaware.\n2021.12\nBest Paper Award\n, MLPH Workshop, Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS).\n📖 Educations\n2020.08 - present\n, Ph.D. in Computer Science, University of Delaware, Newark, DE, USA.\n2018.08 - 2020.05\n, Master in Computer Science, George Washington University, Washington D.C., USA.\n2013.09 - 2017.06\n, B.Eng. in Software Engineering, East China Normal University, Shanghai, China.\n💬 Invited Talks\n2024.12\n, the  Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024.  |\n[video]\n2024.09\n, the European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2024.  |\n[video]\n2023.05\n, the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023.  |\n[video]\n2021.12\n, MLPH Workshop, Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2021.  |\n[video]\n💻 Professional Services\nConference Reviewer\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023-2025.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2025-2026.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2025-2026.\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023-2026.\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV) 2025.\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2024.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), 2022.\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2025-2026.\nBritish Machine Vision Conference (BMVC), 2024-2025.\nIEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV), 2026.\nJournal Reviewer\nFrontiers in Artificial Intelligence, 2025.\nDSI Fellow\n*2022.03 - 2025.08, University of Delaware Data Science Institute (DSI), USA.\n👨‍🏫 Teaching\nCISC 484 (Introduction to Machine Learning), Teaching Assistant, Fall2022.\nCISC 220 (Data Structure), Teaching Assistant, Fall2023, Spring2024.\nCISC 108 (Introduction to Computer Science), Teaching Assistant, Fall2020, Spring2021, Fall2021.\nCISC 181 (Introduction to Computer Science II), Teaching Assistant, Spring2022, Spring2023.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
