    "homepage_text": "Siyuan Feng\nSiyuan Feng\nAssistant Professor\nShanghai Innovation Institute\nI'm an assistant professor at\nShanghai Innovation\n            Institute\n. My research interests include\ndistributed machine learning system\nand\nmachine\n            learning compiler\n. I'm serving as Apache Software Foundation Member and member of Apache TVM\n          Program Management Committee (PMC). My work focuses on developing efficient compilation and optimization\n          techniques for machine learning systems, accelerating the development and deployment of emerging models on\n          emerging platforms.\nI got my Ph.D. degree at Shanghai Jiao Tong University, majored in Computer Science. I was a\n          member of\nAPEX Lab\n, advised by\nProf. Weinan Zhang\nand\nProf. Yong Yu\n, closely collaborating with\nTianqi Chen\nvia open-source community.\nLatest Updates\nJuly 07, 2025\nI'm looking for self-motivated Ph.D. students who like coding and have interests in(distributed) machine learning system and AI infrastructure. Prospective students should have strong programming skills and genuine passion for systems research. Feel free to contact me via email with your CV and research interests if you are interested.\nHighlights\nRecent Publications\nNex-N1: Agentic Models Trained via a Unified Ecosystem for Large-Scale Environment Construction\nPreprint, 2025\nReSpec: Towards Optimizing Speculative Decoding in Reinforcement Learning Systems\nPreprint, 2025\nExpert-as-a-Service: Towards Efficient, Scalable, and Robust Large-scale MoE Serving\nPreprint, 2025\nView all publications →\nFeatured Projects\nApache TVM\nOpen Machine Learning Compiler Framework.\nMLC-LLM\nUniversal LLM Deployment Engine with ML Compilation.\nPyPTO\nPyPTO: Parallel Tensor/Tile Operation Programming Paradigm.\nNex-N1\nAgentic Models Trained via a Unified Ecosystem for Large-Scale Environment Construction.\nView all projects →\nRecent Talks\nTVM-FFI: Open ABI and FFI for Machine Learning Systems\nThe 8-th AI Compiler Meetup, Dec 2025\nPyPTO: Tile 编程与白盒编译\nOpen Source Summit @ HUAWEI, Dec 2025\nHistory and Outlook of the Ecosystem for AI\nThe 6-th Turing Technology Summit @ HUAWEI, Oct 2025\nView all talks & blog posts →"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Rui Xia::https://ruixia.netlify.app/": {
    "homepage": "https://ruixia.netlify.app/",
    "all_emails": [
      "rx220@cam.ac.uk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/XiaRui1996",
    "linkedin": "/www.linkedin.com/in/rui-xia-567b56150",
    "homepage_text": "Rui Xia\nSearch\nRui Xia\nPhD Student in Machine Learning\nUniversity of Cambridge, Computational and Biological Learning Lab\nBiography\nI am a PhD student in Machine Learning at University of Cambridge (\nComputational and Biological Learning Lab\n). My supervisors are\nProfessor Guillaume Hennequin\nand\nDr Alberto Bernacchia\n. Prior to my PhD, I completed MPhil in Machine Learning and Machine Intelligence at University of Cambridge, supervised by\nProf Richard Turner\n. I also obtained a B.Sc. in Applied Mathematics from University of Singapore, supervised by\nProf Vincent Tan\n.\nMy current project studies meta-learning from a dual machine-learning and biological perspective. My research interests also include probabilistic modelling, explainable AI and causal inference. I aim to develop trustworthy algorithms that combine fast and transferable learning, robustness, and interpretability.\nInterests\nMeta Learning\nProbablistic Modelling\nBiological Learning\nExplainable AI\nCausal Inference\nEducation\nPhD in Machine Learning\nUniversity of Cambridge\nMPhil in Machine Learning and Machine Intelligence, Distinction, 2020\nUniversity of Cambridge\nBSc in Applied Mathematics, specialised in Mathemtical Modelling and Data Analysis, 2019\nNational University of Singapore\nPublications\nYan Li\n,\nRui Xia\n,\nChunchen Liu\n,\nSun Liang\nMay, 2022\nIn\nAAAI(2022)\nA Hybrid Causal Structure Learning Algorithm for Mixed-type Data\nInferring the causal structure of a set of random variables is a crucial problem in many disciplines of science. Over the past two decades, various approaches have been proposed for causal discovery from observational data.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nRui Xia\n,\nWessel Bruinsma\n,\nWilliam Tebbutt\n,\nRichard E. Turner\nOctober, 2020\nIn\n3rd AABI\nThe Gaussian Process Latent Autoregressive Model\nMany real-world prediction problems involve modelling the dependencies between multiple different outputs across the input space. Multi-output Gaussian Processes (MOGP) are a particularly important approach to such problems. In this paper, we build on the Gaussian Process Autoregressive Regression (GPAR) model which is one of the best performing MOGP models, but which fails when observation noise is large, when there are missing data, and when non-Gaussian observation models are required.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nVideo\nMPhil Thesis\nRui Xia\n,\nVincent Y. F. Tan\n,\nLouis Filstroff\n,\nC \\'edric F\\'evotte\nOctober, 2019\nIn\nECML PKDD\nA Ranking Model Motivated by Nonnegative Matrix Factorization with Applications to Tennis Tournaments\nWe propose a novel ranking model that combines the Bradley-Terry-Luce probability model with a nonnegative matrix factorization framework to model and uncover the presence of latent variables that influence the performance of top tennis players.\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nSlides\nExperience\nPhD Student\nDepartment of Engineering, University of Cambridge\nOct 2022 –\nPresent\nCambridge, United Kingdom\nEPSRC Doctoral Training Partnership (DTP) PhD studentship at the Department of Engineering\nAlgorithm Engineer\nDAMO Academy, Alibaba\nJul 2020 –\nSep 2022\nHangzhou, China\nResearch on causal inference, including counterfactual regression, causal discovery on mixed-type data, and uncertainty study of Bayesian network structural learning.\nResearch on XAI, including feature attribution, algorithm recourse, and mixture of experts.\nApply research methods on real-world problems, such as root cause analysis on shopping behavior data and explanability on electricity load forecasting.\nData Science Intern\nLAZADA SOUTH EAST ASIA PTE LTD\nMay 2018 –\nAug 2018\nSingapore, Singapore\nTeaching Assistant\nNational University of Singapore\nJan 2017 –\nDec 2018\nSingapore, Singapore\nContact\nrx220@cam.ac.uk\nPeterhouse, Cambridge, CB2 1RD\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
