    "homepage_text": "﻿\nWenbing Huang\nWenbing Huang\nTenure-track Associate Professor\nWenbing Huang is now a tenure-track associate professor at Gaoling School of Artificial Intelligence (GSAI), Renmin University of China. Before joining GSAI, he worked as an assistant researcher at AIR, Tsinghua University, and senior researcher at Tencent AI Lab. His research focuses on the representation, generation, and prediction of complex systems driven by geometric deep learning. He has proposed a series of geometric deep learning approaches, with graph neural networks as representatives, effectively realizing the representation and generation of  atomistic systems such as chemical molecules, proteins, antibodies, crystals, and the representation and behavior learning of complex systems like embodied intelligent agents, physical environments, and social networks. His achievements have been applied in areas such as AI for Science, physical simulation and decision-making, and social network analysis.\nEducation\n2012.09 – 2017.07 PhD in Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, Supervised by Prof. Fuchun Sun.\n2016.03 – 2017.03 Visiting PhD in Australian National University,  Jointly Supervised by Prof. Mehrtash Harandi.\n2008.09 – 2012.07 BE in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics, Beihang University.\nWork Experience\n2023.07 – Now Associate Professor, Renmin University of China\n2022.09 – 2023.07 Assistant Professor, Renmin University of China\n2019.10 – 2022.09 Postdoc, Assistant Researcher at Tsinghua University\n2017.07 – 2019.09 Senior Researcher at Tencent AI Lab\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\n\"There is no royal road to geometry.''   --- Euclid\nThe Geometric Learning And Discovery (GLAD) group is mainly interested in the following directions:\n1. Geometric Deep Learning (GDL): Model images, videos, spatio-temporal data, social networks, and scientific data as geometric objects with certain symmetry, such as sets, manifolds, graphs, etc, and then developing specific machine learning models to represent and process these data. Particularly for graph data processing via GNNs, we research the expressivity of GNNs, how to train GNNs efficiently, how to perform self-supervised GNN learning.\n2. GDL for Robot Sensing and Decision-Making: Towards tactile data representation, video analysis, sound signal processing, multi-modal data sensing and fusion; model-based reinforcement learning, imitation learning with imperfect supervision.\n3. Science-Informed GDL: Embed the knowledge from Geometry, Quantum Mechanics, Computational Chemistry, Computational Biology, and other science domains into existing GML models, with the application to multi-body problem, molecular dynamics simulation, drug design, protein docking, antibody design, crystal material design, and so on.\nPUBLICATIONS\n2026\nAn Equivariant Pretrained Transformer for Unified 3D Molecular Representation Learning\nRui Jiao, Xiangzhe Kong, Li Zhang, Ziyang Yu, Fangyuan Ren, Wenjuan Tan, Wenbing Huang, Yang Liu\nNature Communications\n2025\nAnnotation-guided protein design with multi-level domain alignment\nChaohao Yuan, Songyou Li, Geyan Ye, Yikun Zhang, Long-Kai Huang, Wenbing Huang, Wei Liu, Jianhua Yao, Yu Rong\nSIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD)\nLink\nLearning 3D Anisotropic Noise Distributions Improves Molecular Force Fields\nXixian Liu, Rui Jiao, Zhiyuan Liu, Yurou Liu, Yang Liu, Ziheng Lu, Wenbing Huang, Yang Zhang, Yixin Cao\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nLink\nLatent Retrieval Augmented Generation of Cross-Domain Protein Binders\nZishen Zhang, Xiangzhe Kong, Wenbing Huang, Yang Liu\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nLink\nMOF-BFN: Metal-Organic Frameworks Structure Prediction via Bayesian Flow Networks\nRui Jiao, Hanlin Wu, Wenbing Huang, Yuxuan Song, Yawen Ouyang, Yu Rong, Tingyang Xu, Pengju Wang, Hao Zhou, Wei-Ying Ma, Jingjing Liu, Yang Liu\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nLink\nGeometric Mixture Models for Electrolyte Conductivity Prediction\nAnyi Li, Jiacheng Cen, Songyou Li, Mingze Li, YANG YU, Wenbing Huang\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nLink\nUniversally Invariant Learning in Equivariant GNNs\nJiacheng Cen, Anyi Li, Ning Lin, Tingyang Xu, Yu Rong, Deli Zhao, Zihe Wang, Wenbing Huang\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nLink\nReasonmed: A 370k multi-agent generated dataset for advancing medical reasoning\nYu Sun, Xingyu Qian, Weiwen Xu, Hao Zhang, Chenghao Xiao, Long Li, Deli Zhao, Wenbing Huang, Tingyang Xu, Qifeng Bai, Yu Rong\nThe Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)\nLink\nHeMeNet: Heterogeneous Multichannel Equivariant Network for Protein Multi-task Learning\nRong Han, Wenbing Huang, Lingxiao Luo, Xinyan Han, Jiaming Shen, Zhiqiang Zhang, Jun Zhou, Ting Chen\nThe AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nLink\nPeptide Design through Binding Interface Mimicry\nXiangzhe Kong, Rui Jiao, Haowei Lin,, Ruihan Guo, Wenbing Huang, Wei-Ying Ma, Zihua Wang, Yang Liu, and Jianzhu Ma\nNature Biomedical Engineering\nPowder diffraction crystal structure determination using generative models\nQi Li, Rui Jiao, Liming Wu, Tiannian Zhu, Wenbing Huang, Shifeng Jin, Yang Liu, Hongming Weng, Xiaolong Chen\nNature Communications\nLink\nZero-Shot Cyclic Peptide Design via Composable Geometric Constraints\nDapeng Jiang, Xiangzhe Kong, Jiaqi Han, Mingyu Li, Rui Jiao, Wenbing Huang, Stefano Ermon, Jianzhu Ma, Yang Liu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\nLink\nUniSim: A Unified Simulator for Time-Coarsened Dynamics of Biomolecules\nZiyang Yu , Wenbing Huang, Yang Liu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\nLink\nUniMoMo: Unified Generative Modeling of 3D Molecules for De Novo Binder Design\nXiangzhe Kong, Zishen Zhang, Ziting Zhang, Rui Jiao, Jianzhu Ma, 