    "homepage_text": "Niao He - ETH Zürich\nNiao He\nETH Zürich\nHome\nProf. Niao He\nPeople\nPublications\nTeaching\nOpenings\nStudent Projects\nContact\nNiao He\nI am currently an Associate Professor in the Department of\nComputer Science\nat\nETH Zürich\n, and leading the\nOptimization & Decision Intelligence (ODI) Group\n. I'm also a core faculty member at:\nInstitute of Machine Learning\nETH AI Center\nETH Foundations of Data Science\nMax Planck ETH Center for Learning Systems\nMy work lies in the interface of optimization and machine learning, with a primary focus on the algorithmic and theoretical foundations for principled, scalable, and trustworthy decision intelligence.\nI am also interested in developing machine learning models and algorithms for interdisciplinary applications in operations management, mechanism design, control & robotics, etc.\nThanks to Swiss National Science Foundations,  ETH Foundations, NCCR Automation for generously funding our current research.\nAcademic Positions\nPresent\n2025. 01\nAssociate Professor\nComputer Science\nETH Zürich\n2024. 12\n2020. 12\nAssistant Professor\nComputer Science\nETH Zürich\n2020. 12\n2016. 01\nAssistant Professor\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering\nCoordinated Science Laboratory\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nEducation\nPh.D.\n2015\nPh.D. in Operations Research\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\nSchool of Industrial & Systems Engineering\nAdvisor: Arkadi Nemirovski\nM.S.\n2015\nM.S. in Computational Science & Engineering\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\nCollege of Engineering\nB.S.\n2010\nB.S. in Mathematics\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nSpecial Class of Gifted Young\nHonors, Awards and Grants\n2023\nSNSF Starting Grant\n2023\nSNSF Sinergia Grant\n2021\nELLIS Scholar\n2020\nCAS Beckman Fellow\n2019\nNSF HDR TRIPODS Grant\n2018\nNCSA Faculty Fellow\n2018\nList of Teachers Ranked as\nExcellent\n(UIUC)\n2018\nNSF CISE CRII Award\n2017\nList of Teachers Ranked as\nExcellent\n(UIUC)\n2017\nSIAM Early Career Travel Award\n2016\nList of Teachers Ranked as\nOutstanding\n(UIUC)\n2016\nAISTATS Best Paper Award\n2016\nCollins Scholar (UIUC)\nConferences Program Committee\nArea Chair: NeurIPS 2020, ICLR 2021, UAI 2021, ICML 2021, COLT 2022, ICML 2022, NeurIPS 2023\nSenior Program Committee: AAAI 2019\nProgram Committee: ICML 2015-2019, NeurIPS 2016-2018, AAAI 2017, AISTATS 2016"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Pengfei Wei::https://wpf89928.github.io/pengfeiHomepage.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://wpf89928.github.io/pengfeiHomepage.github.io/",
