    "homepage_text": "Nan Wang's Site\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nNan Wang's Site\nDr Nan\nWANG\nMotto:\nLay a solid foundation\nand the time will come for you to shine!\nEmail:\nnan\n.\nwang at\ndata61.csiro.au\nLocation: Australia\nI am a\nR\nesearch\nScientist\nat\nCSIRO\n's Data61\n(\nAustralia's National Science Research Agency\n)\n.\nI\nobtained\na\nPhD in computer science in 2023\nfrom\nthe\nAustralian National University, Australi\na\n. I also hold an MSc degree in software engineering from\nImperial College London, UK\nand a\nDiplôme d'Ingénieur\n(Engineering Degree) in computer science from\nENSEA (Grande École), France\n.\nI am a professional engineer accredited by\nEngineers Australia\nand\nhave 4 years of industrial experience\nas a software engineer\n.\nI am passionate about developing practical privacy-enhancing technologies, with a focus on applied cryptography and zero-knowledge proofs.\nHere are the top conferences in my research field and\nan exhaustive list of\nt\nop\nv\nenues\nin Computer Security & Cryptography by Google Scholars.\nTop4 Security\n:\nOakland\nS&P, USENIX\nSec\n, CCS, NDSS\nTop3 Crypto\n: Euro\nC\nrypt, Crypto, Asia\nC\nrypt\nMy publications span various prestigious conferences, e.g., Oakland S&P, U\nSENIX Sec,\nAsia\nC\nrypt, PETS, ACM e-Energy, and journals, e.g., IEEE TCC. I am the recipient of the Best Paper Award at ACM e-Energy21.\nAny kind of academic collaborations are welcome!\nNews\nResearch Highlights\nAwards\nTalks\nCodebases\nNews\n2026\n02/2026                  I am honoured to have secured a research grant as Chief Investigator from the MAGIC Monero Fund!\n01\n/202\n6\nI am honoured to join the program committee of\nSecureComm 2026\n!\n2025\n11/2025\nOur new\narticle \"Understanding the LLM's Adversarial Landscape\"\nis a\ncc\nepted\nin IEEE S&P Magazine\n2025!\n06/2025                  I am honoured to have been promoted to a Research Scientist at CSIRO’s Data61!\n06/2025\nI am honoured with a\nScience Excellence Award 2025 and a Customer First Award\n2025 from SCS, Data61, CSIRO!\n202\n4\n12/2024\nOur new paper,\nBulletCT\n,\nis 1 of\n2\n1 papers unconditionally accepted\nto\nUSENIX Security 2025 (\nTop4 Security\n, CORE A*)\n,\nrepresenting the top 1% of all submissions!\n11/2024\nI am honoured to join the artefact evaluation program committee of\nUSENIX Security 2025\n!\n10/2024\nI am honoured to join the program committee of\nICICS 2025\n!\nClick to see more!\n09/2024\nI am serving as a reviewer for\nIEEE Transactions on Forensics &\nSecurity (TIFS)!\n08/2024\nI am serving as a reviewer for\nIEEE Transactions on Services Computing\n(TSC)!\n07/2024\nI am honoured to give a talk of our paper \"FlashSwift\" in PETS 2024\n(CORE A)\nat the\nlink\n!\n07/2024                  I am honoured to give a talk of our paper \"SwiftRange\" in Oakland S&P 2024\n(\nTop4 Security\n, CORE A*)\nat the\nlink\n!\n02/2024\nI am honoured with an\nEarly Career in Science\nAward\n2023 from SCS, Data61, CSIRO!\n02/2024\nOur new paper\n\"FlashSwift\" is accepted to PETS 2024 (CORE A)\n!\n01/2024\nI am serving as a reviewer for\nIEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing\n(TDSC)!\n202\n3\n07/2023\nOur new paper \"SwiftRange\" is accepted to\nOakland\nS&P 2024\n(\nTop4 Security\n, CORE A*)!\n07/2023\nI am honoured to join the\nCybersecurity and Quantum Systems group\n, Data61, CSIRO, Australia!\n202\n2\n12/2022\nI am honoured to give a talk of our paper \"Flashproofs\" in AsiaCrypt 2022\n(\nTop3 Crypto\n, CORE A)\nat the\nlink\n!\n07/2022\nOur new paper\n\"Flashproofs\" is accepted to AsiaCrypt 2022 (\nTop3 Crypto\n,\nCORE A)\n!\nResearch Highlights\nSecurity:\nOakland\nS&P\n×1 (\nTop4, 2024\n),\nUSENIX Sec\n×1 (\nTop4, 2025\n),    PETS ×1 (2024)\nCrypto:\nAsiaCrypt\n×1 (\nTop3, 2022\n)\nBest Paper:\nACM e-Energy\n×1\n(2021)\nAwards\nScience Excellence Award\nSoftware and Computational Systems (SCS) Program, Data61, CSIRO (202\n5\n)\nCustomer\nFirst\nAward\nSoftware and Computational Systems (SCS) Program, Data61, CSIRO (2025)\nEarly Career in Science Award\nSoftware and Computational Systems\n(SCS)\nProgram, Data61, CSIRO (2023) (\nLink\n)\nBest Paper Award                                             ACM e-Energy (2021) (\nLink\n)\nProfessional Engineer                                     Engineers Australia (2023)\nTalks\nUSENIX Sec 2025 (\nTop4 Security\n)\nBulletCT: Towards More Scalable Ring Confidential Transactions With Transparent Setup\n(\nVideo\n)\nGriffith University\nThe landscape of Zero-Knowledge Range Proofs\nPETS 2024\nFlashSwift: A Configurable and More Efficient Range Proof With Transparent Setup (\nVideo\n)\nOakland\nS&P 2024 (\nTop4 Security\n)\nSwiftRange: A Short and Efficient Zero-Knowledge Range Argument for Confidential Transactions and More (\nVideo\n)\nAsiaCrypt 2022\n(\nTop3 Crypto\n)             Flashproofs: Efficient Zero-knowledge Arguments of Range and Polynomial Evaluation with Transparent Setup (\nVideo\n)\nCodebases\nUSENIX Security 2025\nBulletCT\n(Java)\nPETS 2024\nFlashSwift\n(Java)\nAsiaCrypt 2022\nFlashproofs\n(Java & Solidity)\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
