    "homepage_text": "Lei Chen's Homepage\nSearch\nLei Chen\nPhD Student\nSimon Fraser University\nBiography\nI’m a PhD student from vision and media lab at Simon Fraser University under supervision of Dr. Greg Mori. My research interests include weakly-supervised learning and visual grounding as well as deep generative models.\nDownload my\nresume\n.\nInterests\nVisual Grounding\nWeakly-Supervised Learning\nGenerative Models\nEducation\nPhD Candidate in Computing Science\nSimon Fraser University\nMSc in Computing Science, 2015\nSimon Fraser University\nBSc in Information Engineering, 2013\nHuazhong University of Science and Techology\nPublications\nHyper-Lifelong GAN: Scalable Lifelong Learning for Image Conditioned Generation\nAccepted to CVPR 2021\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nGreg Mori\nCite\nAdapting Grad-CAM for Embedding Networks\nAccepted to WACV 2020\nLei Chen\n,\nJianhui Chen\n,\nHossein Hajimirsadeghi\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nPiggyback GAN: Efficient Lifelong Learning for Image Conditioned Generation\nAccepted to ECCV 2020\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nJiawei He\n,\nMegha Nawhal\n,\nFrederick Tung\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nLifelong GAN: Continual Learning for Conditional Image Generation\nAccepted to ICCV 2019\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nLei Chen(co-first author)\n,\nFrederick Tung\n,\nJiawei He\n,\nMegha Nawhal\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nObject Grounding via Iterative Context Reasoning\nAccepted to ICCV 2019 Workshop\nLei Chen\n,\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nJiawei He\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nAttending to Distinctive Moments: Weakly-supervised Attention Models for Action Localization in Video\nAccepted to ICCV 2017 Workshop\nLei Chen\n,\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nLearning to Forecast Videos of Human Activity with Multi-granularity Models and Adaptive Rendering\nAccepted to BMVC 2018\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nJiacheng Chen\n,\nRuizhi Deng\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nLigeng Zhu\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nDeep Structured Models For Group Activity Recognition\nAccepted to BMVC 2015\nZhiwei Deng\n,\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nYuhao Liu\n,\nSrikanth Muralidharan\n,\nMehrsan Javan Roshtkhari\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nObject Detection in Surveillance Video from Dense Trajectories\nMengyao Zhai\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nJinling Li\n,\nMehran Khodabandeh\n,\nGreg Mori\nCite\nLearning Action Primitives for Multi-level Video Event Understanding\nAccepted to ECCV 2014 Workshop\nTian Lan\n,\nLei Chen\n,\nZhiwei Deng\n,\nGuang-Tong Zhou\n,\nGreg Mori\nPDF\nCite\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
