    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/cheng-wang-88b08310b/",
    "homepage_text": "Cheng Wang - Research Homepage\nCheng Wang\nSenior Applied Scientist | Machine Learning Researcher\nNews\n[Feb 26, 2025] I am SPC member for IJCAI 2025, Area Chair for ACL 2025\n[Jun 28, 2024] One paper accepted at TMLR\n[Feb 11, 2024] I am SPC member for IJCAI 2024\n[Mar 01, 2023] I am SPC member for IJCAI 2023\nAbout Me\nWelcome! My name is Cheng Wang. I am currently a Senior Applied Scientist at Amazon. Prior to that, I was a Research Scientist at NEC Laboratories Europe. I received my PhD from\nHasso-Plattner-Institute\n, University of Potsdam in 2017. There, I was supervised by\nProf. Dr. Christoph Meinel\n, my research topic was \"Multimodal Deep Learning\".\nResearch\nMy research focuses are (1) machine (deep) learning methods, e.g, learning algorithms, sequence-to-sequence learning, representation learning, neural architectures, uncertainty estimation/quantification, model calibration and interpretability; (2) their applications to real-world tasks, e.g., information retrieval, recommender systems, natural language processing, computer vision and multimodal learning. I am particularly interested in sequential models (Transformer/GPT/RNNs/LSTMs etc) and state machines related to them.\nPublications\n[Jun 28, 2024]\nTowards Unbiased Calibration using Meta-Regularization\n- TMLR\n[Dec 4, 2022]\nState-Regularized RNNs to Extract Automata\n- IEEE Trans. PAMI\n[Nov 4, 2022]\nCalibrating Imbalanced Classifiers with Focal Loss\n- EMNLP Industry Track\nContact\nEmail: dr.rer.nat.chengwang@gmail.com\nLinkedIn:\nlinkedin.com/in/chengwang"
  },
