    "homepage_text": "Welcome! | Tian Xu Laboratory\nSkip to Main Content\nTian Xu Laboratory\nMENU\nYale School of Medicine\nMENU\nResearch\nGenetic Basis of Metastatic Behavior\nSize-Control Mechanisms in Development & Tumorigenesis\nPioneering New Genetic Methodologies\nDeciphering Mammalian Biology and Disease by Large-Scale Transposon Mutagenesis in Mice\nLab Members\nAlumni\nPhoto Galleries\nNews & Events\nLatest Journal Content\nTools & Resources\nYSM Home\nINFORMATION FOR\nAbout YSM\nFaculty\nStaff\nStudents\nResidents & Fellows\nPatients\nResearchers\nAlumni\nWelcome!\nOur laboratory is interested in utilizing model organisms to understand cancer biology and developmental mechanisms. In particular, we are developing and using new genetic approaches to identify genes that are involved in tumor growth and metastasis, and are exploring the developmental and biochemical functions of these genes.\nTo learn more about our research activities, please see our\nResearch\nsection.\nAbout Tian Xu\nCopy Link\nTian Xu is an Adjunct Professor in Genetics at Yale School of Medicine. He is currently Vice President at\nWestlake University\n.\nAdditionally, he serves as an Adjunct Professor and Director of the\nInstitute of Developmental Biology and Molecular Medicine at Fudan University\n, Shanghai.\nContact Information\nCopy Link\nDaming Li\nAssociate Research Scientist in Genetics\nEmail\n:\nda-ming.li@yale.edu\nPhone\n: 203-737-4452\nPrincipal Investigator\nCopy Link\nTian Xu, PhD\nProfessor Adjunct of Genetics\nView Full Profile\nBack to Top\nYour browser is antiquated and no longer supported on this website. Please update your browser or switch to Chrome, Firefox or Safari.\nYou can update your IE here:\nhttps://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/17621/internet-explorer-downloads\n[6602,3275,3053]\n{\"namedChunks\":[\"modules-page-components-ComponentWrapper\",\"features-generic-content-components-GenericContent\",\"modules-profile-components-profile-contact-widget-ProfileContactWidget\",\"modules-footer-components-Footer\"]}"
  },
