    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhuo-huang-06863628a/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhuo Huang - Academic Page\nZHUO HUANG\nPhD student at The University of Sydney\nNews:\n01/2026, I gratefully received the USYD Faculty of Engineering Career Advancement Award.\n10/2025, I was invited to give a talk on \"Machine-Supervised Learning\" at SJTU International Young Scholar Workshop, thanks to Prof. Chen Gong.\n10/2025, I started my visiting at RIKEN AIP, Japan, Tokyo.\n09/2025, I was invited to give a talk on \"Generalizable Machine Learning\" at Sydney University Data Society (SUDATA).\n09/2025, I was invited to give a talk on \"Out-of-Modal Generalization\" at Annual Conference on Postgraduate Research in Engineering Student Society (PRESS).\n06/2025, One paper in Machine Unlearning got accepted at ICML 2026, congrats to Mr. Puning Yang and Dr. Qizhou Wang.\n06/2025, I was awarded CVPR 2025 Outstanding Reviewer.\n04/2025, I started my visiting at MBZUAI, Abu Dhabi, UAE.\n04/2025, I attended ICLR 2025 at Singapore.\n03/2025, I was awarded with RSF and PRSS Funding from Faculty of Engineering and The University of Sydney, respectively.\n03/2025, One paper was accepted as an Oral presentation at ACM MM 2025, congrats to Mr. Xiaohao Liu and Prof. Xiaobo Xia.\nI am a final-year PhD candidate in Computer Science at the University of Sydney, supervised by Prof.\nTongliang Liu\n. I was a visiting PhD student at RIKEN AIP, hosted by Prof.\nMasashi Sugiyama\n. I was a visiting PhD student at MBZUAI, hosted by Prof.\nTongliang Liu\n. I was a visiting PhD student at Tsinghua University, hosted by Prof.\nHang Su\n. I was an intern at JD.com, working in the ML group led by Prof.\nLi Shen\n. I was awarded the Faculty Career Advancement Award, the TML Research Gold Award, the LEAP Fellow, the National Scholarship, and various Outstanding Reviewer Awards and Outstanding Dissertation Awards.\nI was an academic tutor for COMP5328/4328: Advanced Machine Learning and COMP5318: Machine Learning and Data Mining, and I was the lecturer for Computer Science tutorial: Machine Learning under Distribution Shifts.\nI am fortunate to work with some brilliant minds:\nProf. Masashi Sugiyama\n, RIKEN AIP & The University of Tokyo\nProf. Gang Niu\n, RIKEN AIP\nProf. Tongliang Liu\n, The University of Sydney\nProf. Chen Gong\n, Shanghai Jiaotong University\nProf. Bo Han\n, Hong Kong Baptist University\nProf. Mingming Gong\n, The University of Melbourne\nProf. Hang Su\n, Tsinghua University\nProf. Yinpeng Dong\n, Tsinghua University\nProf. Li Shen\n, Sun Yat-sen University\nProf. Yu Yao\n, The University of Sydney\nProf. Xiaobo Xia\n, University of Science and Technology China\nDr. Qizhou Wang\n, RIKEN AIP\nMr. Ziming Hong\n, The University of Sydney\nMr. Muyang Li\n, The University of Sydney\nMr. Quan M. Tran\n, The University of Sydney\nMr. Andrew Cao\n, The University of Sydney\nMr. Puning Yang\n, MBZUAI\nMr. Xiaohao Liu\n, Nanyang Technological University\nMy research interests mainly include, but not limited to:\nGeneralizable AI:\nICLR23\n,\nCVPR23\n,\nICLR24\n,\nIJCV24\nMulti-Modal Learning:\nICML24\n,\nACM MM24\n,\nICLR25\nTrustworthy Machine Learning:\nNeurIPS21\n,\nNeurIPS23\n,\nNeurIPS24\n,\nICML25\n,\nTMM22\nAgentic AI:\nPhysical AI:\nFor more publications, please refer to\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nYou can reach out through:\nEmail:\nWechat:\nQR code\nScan to connect on WeChat\nLinkedin:\nProfile"
  },
