    "homepage_text": "Shenghai Yuan\n☀️\n🌙\nSecond Year Master @Peking University\n👋 About Me\nGreetings!\nI am currently a second-year master of computer science and technology at\nSchool of Electron and Computer Engineering\n,\nPeking University\n, advised by Prof.\nLi Yuan\n.\n            I received my B. Eng in\nSchool of Computer Science and Technology\n,\nGuangdong University of Technology\n.\n            My research interests include but are not limited to\nVideo Generation\n,\nWorld Model\n,\nGenerative AI\n, and\nEfficient AI\n.\n🔥 News\nJul 2025\n🎉 Joined ByteDance as a Research Intern.\nDec 2024\n🎉 I received my B.E. degree from\nGuangdong University of Technology (GDUT)\n, awarded the\n          Outstanding Graduate, ranking\n1\nst\n/815 in overall scores for four years\n          (2020-2024)!\n🎨 Selected Works\n🌟 Helios: Real Real-Time Long Video Generation Model\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\n2026\n)\nThe first 14B video generation model that achieves minute-scale, high-quality video synthesis at 19.5 FPS\n            on a single H100 GPU (about 10 FPS on a single Ascend NPU) — without relying on conventional long video\n            anti-drifting strategies or standard video acceleration techniques.\n[\nPaper\n]\n            [\nCode\n]\n            [\nPage\n]\n            [\nHuggingFace\n]\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n🌟 Identity-Preserving Text-to-Video Generation by Frequency Decomposition\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nCVPR 2025 Highlight🌟\n)\nA tuning-free DiT-based controllable IPT2V model to keep human-identity consistent in the generated video.\n            The approach draws inspiration from previous studies on frequency analysis.\n[\nPaper\n]\n            [\nCode\n]\n            [\nPage\n]\n            [\nPoster\n]\n            [\nHuggingFace\n]\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n🌟 Open-Sora-Plan\nOpen-Sora-Plan Team,\nShenghai Yuan\n(2024)\nPioneering open-source effort to reproduce Sora. Responsible for the high-resolution, long-duration video\n            generation architecture and curating open-source high-quality video datasets.\n[\nPaper\n]\n            [\nCode\n]\n            [\nHuggingFace\n]\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\n🌟 MagicTime: Time-lapse Video Generation Models as Metamorphic Simulators\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nTPAMI 2025\n)\nA metamorphic video generation model based on the given prompts. The main idea is to enhance the capacity\n            of generation models to accurately depict the real world through our proposed methods.\n[\nPaper\n]\n            [\nCode\n]\n            [\nPage\n]\n            [\nPoster\n]\n            [\nHuggingFace\n]\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nOpenS2V-Nexus: A Detailed Benchmark and Million-Scale Dataset for Subject-to-Video Generation\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nNeurIPS 2025\n)\n[\nPaper\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nPage\n]\n                [\nPoster\n]\n                [\nHuggingFace\n]\nChronoMagic-Bench : A Benchmark for Metamorphic Evaluation of Text-to-Time-lapse Video Generation\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nNeurIPS 2024 Spotlight🌟\n)\n[\nPaper\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nPage\n]\n                [\nPoster\n]\n                [\nHuggingFace\n]\nLHNetV2: A Balanced Low-cost Hybrid Network for Single Image Dehazing\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nTMM 2024\n)\n[\nPaper\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nPoster\n]\nLHNet: A Low-cost Hybrid Network for Single Image Dehazing\nShenghai Yuan\n, et al. (\nACM MM 2023\n)\n[\nPaper\n]\n                [\nCode\n]\n                [\nPoster\n]\n💻 Work Experience\nByteDance & Tiktok, China\nJul. 2025 - Feb. 2026, Research Intern. Mentor:\nXiao Yang\n🎓 Education\nPeking University, China\nDec. 2024 - Present, Master of Philosophy\nGuangdong University of Technology, China\nDec. 2020 - Jul. 2024, Bachelor of Engineering\n🏆 Awards\nNational Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education, China, 2025\nNational Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education, China, 2023\nNational Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education, China, 2022\nNational Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education, China, 2021\n🤝 Academic Service\nReviewer:\nCVPR 2026, ICCV 2025, NeurIPS 2025, CVPR 2025, SIGGRAPH 2025, ACM MM 2024, ACM MM 2023\nTalk:\nByteDance-Helios\n,\nAITIME-ConsisID\n,\nTechBeat-ConsisID\n,\nCV3D-OpenS2V\n,\nAITIME-ChronoMagic\n,\nVALSE-ChronoMagic"
  },
