    "homepage_text": "Han Zou\npowered by\nWeb\nImage\nSort by:\nRelevance\nRelevance\nDate\nWeb\nImage\nHan Zou\nPostdoctoral Scholar\nDepartment of EECS\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nEmail: hanzou@berkeley.edu\nAddress: 406 Cory Hall,\nBerkeley, CA 94720\nGoogle Scholar\nResearchGate\nLinkedIn\nEXPAND ALL SECTIONS\nCOLLAPSE ALL SECTIONS\nIntroduction\nI am a Postdoctoral Scholar in\nthe Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Sciences\nat\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\n, mentored by Prof.\nCostas Spanos\n. I received my Ph.D. in Electrical and Electronic Engineering from\nNanyang Technological University\nin 2017 advised by Prof.\nLihua Xie\nand Prof.\nAlexandre Bayen\n. My research focuses on machine learning, deep learning, transfer learning, RF sensing, mobile and ubiquitous computing, and multimodal sensor fusion with applications in location intelligence, human activity recognition, location-based and context-aware service, smart buildings, and Internet of Things (IoT).\nDemos on YouTube »\nIndoor Localization Live Demo at UCB »\nNews\nNews\nOur paper \"\nMachine Learning empowered Occupancy Sensing for Smart Buildings\n\" was accepted at\nClimate Change and AI Workshop\n,\nICML 2019\nOur paper \"\nWiFi and Vision Multimodal Learning for Accurate and Robust Device-Free Human Activity Recognition\n\" was accepted at\nMULA Workshop\n,\nCVPR 2019\nOur paper \"\nConsensus Adversarial Domain Adaptation\n\" was accepted at\nAAAI 2019\nOur paper \"WiFi-enabled device-free human activity recognition via deep learning\" was published in\nEnergy and Buildings\nOur paper \"Unsupervised WiFi-enabled IoT Device-User Association for Personalized Location-based Service\" was published in\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal\nOur paper \"Device-Free Occupancy Detection and Crowd Counting in Smart Buildings with WiFi-enabled IoT\" was published in\nEnergy and Buildings\nOur paper \"Device-free Occupancy Sensing Platform using WiFi-enabled IoT Devices for Smart Homes\" was published in\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal\nOur two papers on WiFi occupancy sensing, as well as outliers detection in multiple time series have been accepted at\nAAAI 2018\nOur\nWiFi-based Non-intrusive Indoor Positioning System (WinIPS)\nwas fully operational in CREST Lab, Cory Hall, UC Berkeley\nPublications\nSelected Publications: Journals Articles\nIOTJ\nUnsupervised WiFi-enabled IoT Device-User Association for Personalized Location-based Service\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Costas Spanos\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal, 2019 (IF=9.515)\n[PDF]\nIOTJ\nMultiple Kernel Semi-representation Learning with Its Application to Device-Free Human Activity Recognition\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Reza Arghandeh, Costas Spanos\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal, 2019 (IF=9.515)\n[PDF]\nENB\nTowards occupant activity driven smart buildings via WiFi-enabled IoT devices and deep learning\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Costas Spanos\nEnergy and Buildings, 2018 (IF=4.495)\n[PDF]\nENB\nDevice-Free Occupancy Detection and Crowd Counting in Smart Buildings with WiFi-enabled IoT\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Costas Spanos\nEnergy and Buildings, 2018 (IF=4.495)\n[PDF]\nTWC\nWinIPS: WiFi-Based Non-Intrusive Indoor Positioning System with Online Radio Map Construction and Adaptation\nHan Zou\n, Ming Jin, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE Transactions on Wireless Communications, 2017 (IF=6.394)\n[PDF]\nTWC\nA Robust Indoor Positioning System based on the Procrustes Analysis and Weighted Extreme Learning Machine\nHan Zou\n, Baoqi Huang, Xiaoxuan Lu, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie\nIEEE Transactions on Wireless Communications, 2016 (IF=6.394)\n[PDF]\nENB\nWinLight: A WiFi-based Occupancy-driven Lighting Control System for Smart Building\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Hao Jiang, Szu-Cheng Chien, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nEnergy and Buildings, 2018 (IF=4.495)\n[PDF]\nENB\nNon-intrusive Occupancy Sensing in Commercial Buildings\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang, Jianfei Yang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nEnergy and Buildings, 2018 (IF=4.495)\n[PDF]\nSensors\nBlueDetect: An iBeacon-Enabled Scheme for Accurate and Energy-Efficient Indoor-Outdoor Detection and Seamless Location-Based Service\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang, Yiwen Luo, Janjie Zhu, Xiaoxuan Lu, Lihua Xie\nSensors, 2016 (IF=3.031)\n[PDF]\nSensors\nA Fast and Precise Indoor Localization Algorithm based on an Online Sequential Extreme Learning Machine\nHan Zou\n, Xiaoxuan Lu, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie\nSensors, 2015 (IF=3.031)\n[PDF]\nIOTJ\nRobust Device-free Occupancy Sensing Platform using WiFi-enabled IoT Devices for Smart Homes\nJianfei Yang,\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal, 2018 (IF=9.515)\n[PDF]\nT-CYB\nRobust Extreme Learning Machine with its Application to Indoor Positioning\nXiaoxuan Lu,\nHan Zou\n, Hongming Zhou, Lihua Xie, Guang-Bin Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, 2016 (IF=10.387)\n[PDF]\nT-TVT\nCareFi: Sedentary Behavior Monitoring System via Commodity WiFi Infrastructures\nJianfei Yang,\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie\nIEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology, 2018 (IF=4.432)\n[PDF]\nSensors\nFusion of WiFi, Smartphone Sensors and Landmarks using the Kalman Filter for Indoor Localization\nZhenghua Chen,\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang, Qingchang Zhu, Yeng Chai Soh, Lihua Xie\nSensors, 2016 (IF=3.031)\n[PDF]\nSensors\nBuilding-in-Briefcase: A Rapidly-Deployable Environmental Sensor Suite for the Smart Building\nKevin Weekly, Ming Jin,\nHan Zou\n, Christopher Hsu, Chris Soyza, Alexandre Bayen, Costas Spanos\nSensors, 2018 (IF=3.031)\n[PDF]\nSensors\nMapSentinel: Can the Knowledge of Space Use Improve Indoor Tracking Further?\nRuoxi Jia, Ming Jin,\nHan Zou\n, Yigitcan Yesilata, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nSensors, 2016 (IF=3.031)\n[PDF]\nIMWUT\nSugarMate: Non-intrusive Blood Glucose Monitoring with Smartphones\nWeixi Gu, Yuxun Zhou, Zimu Zhou, Xi Liu,\nHan Zou\n, Pei Zhang, Costas Spanos, Lin Zhang\nACM on Interactive, Mobile, Wearable and Ubiquitous Technologies (IMWUT), 2018\n[PDF]\nUS\nPlatform and Algorithm Development for a RFID-based Indoor Positioning System\nHan Zou\n, Lihua Xie, Qing-Shan Jia, Hengtao Wang\nUnmanned Systems, 2014\n[PDF]\nSelected Publications: Conference Proceedings\nAAAI'19\nConsensus Adversarial Domain Adaptation\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Huihan Liu, Hari Prasanna Das, Costas Spanos\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2019\n[PDF]\nAAAI'18\nWiFi-based Human Identification via Convex Tensor Shapelet Learning\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Weixi Gu, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2018\n[PDF]\nAAAI'18\nNon-Parametric Outliers Detection in Multiple Time Series A Case Study: Power Grid Data Analysis\nYuxun Zhou,\nHan Zou\n, Reza Arghandeh, Weixi Gu, Costas Spanos\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2018\n[PDF]\nIEEE ICC'18\nDeepSense: Device-free Human Activity Recognition via Autoencoder Long-term Recurrent Convolutional Network\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE International Conference on Communications, 2018\n[PDF]\nIEEE ICMLA'17\nMultiple Kernel Representation Learning for WiFi-based Human Activity Recognition\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE International Conference On Machine Learning And Application, 2017\n[PDF]\nIEEE GLOBECOM'17\nFreeCount: Device-Free Crowd Counting with Commodity WiFi\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Weixi Gu, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE Global Communications Conference, 2017\n[PDF]\nIEEE WCNC'17\nAdaptive Localization in Dynamic Indoor Environments by Transfer Kernel Learning\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Hao Jiang, Baoqi Huang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference, 2017\n[PDF]\nIEEE GLOBECOM'16\nConsensus-Based Parallel Extreme Learning Machine for Indoor Localization\nHan Zou\n, Zhirong Qiu, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie, Yiguang Hong\nIEEE Global Communications Conference, 2016\n[PDF]\nIEEE WCNC'16\nStandardizing Location Fingerprints Across Heterogeneous Mobile Devices for Indoor Localization\nHan Zou\n, Baoqi Huang, Xiaoxuan Lu, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie\nIEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference, 2016\n[PDF]\nIEEE SECON'17 Workshop\nFreedetector: Device-free Occupancy Detection with Commodity WiFi\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Weixi Gu, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE International Conference on Sensing, Communication and Networking Workshops, 2017\n[PDF]\nIEEE INFOCOM'16 Workshop\nWinIPS: WiFi-based Non-intrusive IPS for Online Radio Map Construction\nHan Zou\n, Ming Jin, Hao Jiang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Communications Workshops, 2016\n[PDF]\nACM MobiCom'17\nWiFi-based Device-Free Human Activity Recognition via Automatic Representation Learning: Poster\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Weixi Gu, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nACM International Conference on Mobile Computing and Networking, 2017\n[PDF]\nACM MobiCom'16\nA Transfer Kernel Learning Based Strategy for Adaptive Localization In Dynamic Indoor Environments: Poster\nHan Zou\n, Yuxun Zhou, Hao Jiang, Baoqi Huang, Lihua Xie, Costas Spanos\nACM International Conference on Mobile Computing and Networking, 2016\n[PDF]\nACM UbiComp'16\nExploiting Cyclic Features of Walking for Pedestrian Dead Reckoning with Unconstrained Smartphones\nBaoqi Huang, Guodong Qi, Xiaokun Yang, Long Zhao,\nHan Zou\nACM International Joint Conference on Pervasive and Ubiquitous Computing, 2016\n[PDF]\nProjects\nProjects\nWinIPS: WiFi-based Non intrusive Indoor Positioning System\nLocation-based Services\nIndoor Localization\nWiFi\nWe designed WinIPS, a novel non-intrusive (no App installation) WiFi-based indoor positioning system (IPS) with a user-friendly web interface for reliable indoor navigation and real-time occupancy sensing. WinIPS has been deployed and implemented in 11 distinct indoor environments with 95000 ft2 in U.S.A., Singapore, Taiwan and Germany.\nWinLight: A WiFi-based occupancy-driven lighting control system for smart building\nLocation-based Services\nIndoor Localization\nSmart Home\nWe developed an occupancy-driven lighting control system, WinLight, that is able to turn on/off lights automatically based on the real-time location of the customer estimated by our WiFi-based IPS. Moreover, it adjusts the brightness level of each lamp according to customer's luminance preferences to realize personalized lighting comfort in smart home.\nSeamless Indoor Outdoor Navigation\nLocation-based Services\nWiFi\niBeacon\nWe developed a framework by integrating GPS (outdoor), iBeacon (semi-outdoor) and WiFi (indoor) for accurate and energy efficient indoor-outdoor detection with fast-response, and seamless navigation in all environments.\nIndoor Navigation on Google Glass\nLocation-based Services\nIndoor Localization\nWearable Device\nWe integrated our WiFi-based IPS to realize seamless indoor positioning and navigation services for customers with optimal path guidance on wearable devices such as Google Glass.\nPatents\nPatents\nIntelligent IoT Device with Wireless-enabled Device-free Occupancy Sensing\nHan Zou\n, Costas Spanos, Yuxun Zhou\nUS Patent Application: 62/742,111, 2018\nWiFi-enabled Device-free Human Identification\nHan Zou\n, Costas Spanos, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Lihua Xie\nUS Patent Application: 62/675,473, 2018\nWiFi-enabled Device-free Gesture Recognition\nHan Zou\n, Costas Spanos, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang, Lihua Xie\nUS Patent Application: 62/675,479, 2018\nUnsupervised WiFi-enabled Device-User Association for Personalized Location-based Service\nHan Zou\n, Costas Spanos, Yuxun Zhou, Jianfei Yang\nUS Patent Application: 62/675,485, 2018\nDevice-Free Sedentary Period Detection Using Commodity WiFi Signals\nLihua Xie, Jianfei Yang,\nHan Zou\n, Hao Jiang\nUS Patent Application: 62/716,266, 2018\nAwards\nAwards\nCITRIS Seed Grant, 2018.\nNVIDIA GPU Grant, 2018.\nMicrosoft Indoor Localization Competition 3rd Place Award, 2014.\nMicrosoft Indoor Localization Competition 4th Place Award, 2015.\nSinBerBEST Graduate Scholarship, National Research Foundation, Singapore, 2012-2016.\nService\nProfessional Service\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking, IEEE Transactions on Wireless Communication, ACM Interactive, Mobile, Wearable and Ubiquitous Technologies (ACM IMWUT), Information Sciences, Energy and Buildings, IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, IEEE Wireless Communications Letters, IEEE Internet of Things Journal\nTechnical Program Committee\nACM CHI [2019], IEEE GLOBECOM [2016], IEEE CASE [2015], IEEE ICCA [2014, 2016, 2017], SmartGridComm [2016]"
  },
