    "homepage_text": "Tianyu Li\nTianyu Li\nIncoming Assistant Professor, University of Wisconsin-Madison\nAbout\nI obtained my PhD from MIT EECS working with\nProf. Samuel Madden\n. My research focuses on designing\n  strong abstractions for stateful cloud systems to unlock developer\n  productivity and infrastructure innovation. Before MIT, I worked with\nthe infamous Andy Pavlo\nat CMU, where I received my bachelor's\n  and master's degrees in computer science.\nI will be joining the\nUW-Madison Database Group\nas an assistant professor in 2026! I am recruiting 2-3 MS/PhD students for Fall 2026 in cloud, data processing, or AI systems. Please reach out if you are interested in chatting.\nPublications\nPlease see my\nGoogle Scholar Profile\n.\nTeaching\nCS839: Next-Generation Data Systems, Fall 2026, UW-Madison\n6.5830/6.5831: Database Systems, Spring 2026, MIT\nService\nVLDB 2027, Program Committee\nSIGMOD 2027, Program Committee\nNew England Systems Day 2026, Program Committee\nCIDR 2026, Program Committee\nVLDB 2025, Program Committee (Distinguished Reviewer Award)\nContact\nEmail: litianyu AT mit.edu\nOffice: 32-G904B, 32 Vassar St., Cambridge, MA 02139, USA"
  },
