    "homepage_text": "Bangjun Wang\nHong Kong SAR/ Shanghai\ncontact@bangjunwang.com\nBangjun Wang\nCS PhD Student at The University of Hong Kong (HKU)\nHi, I am a first-year Ph.D. student at\nHKU MMLab\n, co-advised by Prof.\nHongyang Li\nand Prof.\nYi Ma\n. I received my Bachelor's degree with honors from the first session of\nGuozhi Class\n(held by\nProf. Xiaoou Tang\nand\nProf. Cewu Lu\n), Shanghai Jiao Tong University. Previously, I was a visiting scholar at the University of Southern California (USC), advised by Prof.\nYue Wang\n, and the National University of Singapore (NUS), advised by Prof.\nLin Shao\n. I also worked with Prof.\nHao Dong\nand Prof.\nJunchi Yan\nbefore during my undergraduate years. My research focuses on\nEmbodied AI, Robotic Manipulation, and Foundation Models\n. Feel free to contact me if you are interested in my research or would like to collaborate on any related topics!\n*My current public version CV is available here:\nCurriculum Vitae (May 2025)\n[Not Updated Yet].\nNews\n2025.10\nGoing to start my PhD career at\nHKU MMLab\n, co-advised by Prof.\nHongyang Li\nand Prof.\nYi Ma\n.\n2025.04\nRoboVerse gets accepted by\nRSS 2025\n🎉 and code has been released!\n2024.12\nI am actively applying for a 2025/2026 PhD position.\n2024.08\nServe as a reviewer for\nCVPR 2025\nand\nICML 2025\n.\n2024.08\nVisiting student at USC, supervised by Prof.\nYue Wang\n.\n2024.08\nInvited to serve as a reviewer for\nAAAI 2025\n,\nICLR 2025\n.\n2024.07\nAttend RSS 2024 on-site and present our work on\nrobot manipulation\n👈 .\n2024.05\nServe as a reviewer for\nNeurIPS 2024\nand\nACMMM 2024\n2024.05\nOne paper(MPI) on robot manipulation has been accepted by\nRSS 2024\n.\n2024.03\nJoin\nPKU-Agibot Lab\nsupervised by Prof.\nHao Dong\n.\n2024.01\nOne paper(LaneSegNet) is accepted by\nICLR 2024\n.\n2023.11\nGoing to serve as a reviewer for\nCVPR 2024\n2023.09\nOne paper(OpenLane-V2) is accepted by\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n2023.07\nServe as the session secretary in\nRACV 2023\n.\n2023.03\nBecome a member of\nOpenDriveLab\n.\n2023.02\nParticipate in MCM/ICM 2023, collaborating with Wenye Yu and Yunlin He.\n2022.11\nBecome a member of\nReThinkLab\n.\n2022.08\nJoin Prof.\nNanyang Ye\n's Laboratory in JHC, Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\n2021.12\nEnrolled in\nGuozhi Class\n.\nPublications\nRoboVerse: Towards a Unified Platform, Dataset and Benchmark for Scalable and Generalizable Robot Learning\nHaoran Geng*, Feishi Wang*, Songlin Wei*, Yuyang Li*,\nBangjun Wang*\n, Boshi An*, Charlie Tianyue Cheng*, Haozhe Lou, Peihao Li, Yen-Jen Wang, Yutong Liang, Dylan Goetting, Chaoyi Xu, Haozhe Chen, Yuxi Qian, Yiran Geng, Jiageng Mao, Weikang Wan, Mingtong Zhang, Jiangran Lyu, Siheng Zhao, Jiazhao Zhang, Jialiang Zhang, Chengyang Zhao, Haoran Lu, Yufei Ding, Ran Gong, Yuran Wang, Yuxuan Kuang, Ruihai Wu, Baoxiong Jia, Carlo Sferrazza, Hao Dong, Siyuan Huang, Koushil Sreenath, Yue Wang†, Jitendra Malik†, Pieter Abbeel† (\nCo-first author among 38 authors\n)\nRobotics: Science and Systems (RSS) 2025\nOral Presentation\nEditor's Pick\nPaper\nCode\nPage\nTwitter\nLearning Manipulation by Predicting Interaction\nJia Zeng*, Qingwen Bu*,\nBangjun Wang*\n, Wenke Xia*, Li Chen, Hao Dong, Haoming Song, Dong Wang, Di Hu, Ping Luo, Heming Cui, Bin Zhao, Xuelong Li, Yu Qiao, Hongyang Li\nRobotics: Science and Systems (RSS) 2024\nOral Presentation\nEditor's Pick\nPaper\nCode\nPage\nTwitter\nLaneSegNet: Map Learning with Lane Segment Perception for Autonomous Driving\nTianyu Li*, Peijin Jia*,\nBangjun Wang*\n, Li Chen, Kun Jiang, Junchi Yan, Hongyang Li\nInternationl Conference on Learning Representation (ICLR) 2024\nPaper\nCode\nPage\nTwitter\nCompetition\nOpenLane-V2: A Topology Reasoning Benchmark for Scene Understanding in Autonomous Driving\nHuijie Wang, Tianyu Li, Yang Li, Li Chen, Chonghao Sima, Zhenbo Liu,\nBangjun Wang\n, Peijin Jia, Yuting Wang, Shengyin Jiang, Feng Wen, Hang Xu, Ping Luo, Junchi Yan, Wei Zhang, Hongyang Li\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2023\nPaper\nCode\nPage\nTwitter\nCompetition\nPreprints\nWorld4Omni: A Zero-Shot Framework from Image Generation World Model to Robotic Manipulation\nHaonan Chen*,\nBangjun Wang*\n, Jingxiang Guo*, Tianrui Zhang, Yiwen Hou, Xuchuan Huang, Chenrui Tie, Lin Shao\nICML 2025 Physical World Modeling Workshop\nPaper\nCode\nPage\nTwitter\nExperience\nNational University of Singapore (NUS)\nVisiting Scholar\n2025.04 - 2025.09\n, Advisor/Supervisor:\nProf. Lin Shao\n↳\nA Zero-Shot Framework from Image Generation World Model to Robotic Manipulation\nUniversity of Southern California (USC)\nVisiting Scholar\n2024.08 - 2025.07\n, Advisor/Supervisor:\nProf. Yue Wang\n↳\nA Unified Benchmark for Scalable and Generalizable Vision-Language Robotic Manipulation\nPKU-AGIBOT Lab, Peking University (PKU) & AGIBOT\nResearch Intern\n2024.03 - 2024.08\n, Advisor/Supervisor:\nProf. Hao Dong\nand\nDr. Maoqing Yao\n↳\nVision-Language-Action(VLA) Framework, Humanoid Bimanual Manipulation\nOpenDriveLab, Shanghai AI Lab & The University of Hong Kong (HKU)\nResearch Intern\n2023.03 - 2024.06\n, Advisor/Supervisor:\nProf. Hongyang Li\n↳\nEmbodied AI, Representation Learning for Robotic Manipulation\n↳\nStructural Understanding for Driving Scenes\nReThinkLab, Shanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU)\nResearch Undergraduate\n2022.09 - 2023.03\n, Advisor/Supervisor:\nProf. Junchi Yan\n↳\nImage Retrieval, Image Matching\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Science\n,\nThe University of Hong Kong\n,\n2025 - Present\nAdvisor: Prof.\nHongyang Li\nand Prof.\nYi Ma\nB.Eng. in Artificial Intelligence\n,\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n,\n2021 - 2025\nSumma Cum Laude,\nGuozhi Class\n. Advisor: Prof.\nCewu Lu\nand Prof.\nXiaoou Tang\nVisiting Scholar\n,\nUniversity of Southern California (USC)\n,\n2024 - 2025\nResearch Advisor: Prof.\nYue Wang\nServices\nReviewer\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2024, 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024, 2025\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA), 2026\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2025, 2026\nACM Multimedia (ACMMM), 2024\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2025, 2026\nWorkshop Co-organizer\nFM4AS\nat CVPR 2024\nE2EAD\nat CVPR 2023\nSchool Roles\nClass Leader of Guozhi Class, 2021 - 2025\nMisc\nMusic\nI have a pretty eclectic taste in music, but my favorites are definitely classical, jazz, blues, and R&B.\nMy favorite classical music is from the mid to the late Romantic period. Specifically, I have a passion for the works of Mahler, Rachmaninoff, and Wagner.\nSports\nI'm a single-backhanded tennis player.\nArt and Design\nRecently, I am learning graphical design and digital art systematically in my spare time."
  },
