  "deep_homepage::Hongyang Li::https://lihongyang.info/": {
    "homepage": "https://lihongyang.info/",
    "all_emails": [
      "recruit@opendrivelab.com",
      "hongyang@hku.hk",
      "hy@opendrivelab.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hongyang Li, Assistant Professor at HKU\nProspective\nBiography\nResearch\nTeaching\nTalk\nHongyang Li\nAssistant Professor, School of Computing and Data Science (CDS) and Institute of Data Science (IDS), The University of Hong Kong (HKU)\nAcademic page at\nCDS\nand\nIDS\nEmail:\nhongyang@hku.hk\nor\nhy@opendrivelab.com\nOffice: Room P307B, Graduate House, 3 University Drive, HKU\nLab location: HW 335 and GH P501\nProspective Students / FTEs\nWe are taking in 2026 Internship. Newbies / undergraduates are welcome! Please refer to\nthis page\nfor more details.\nPost-doc / Ph.D. / MPhil: please send me an email. We usually hire\nHKPFS\nor\nHKU Presidential Scholarship\nlevel candidate\nResearch Assistant / Internship: please send request to\nrecruit@opendrivelab.com\nFor full-time employee (FTE) at HKU (HK and Shanghai both) / Shenzhen Loop Area Institute (SLAI), we would be happy to recruit Research Scientist / Engineer / Staff in Embodied AI and Autonomous Driving!\nFor recruitment in Shanghai Innovation Institute (SII), please refer to the\nofficial website\nBiography\nHongyang Li is an Assistant Professor at The University of Hong Kong and has led OpenDriveLab (\nopendrivelab.com\n) since 2021. His research focus is on autonomous driving and embodied AI. He led the end-to-end autonomous driving project, UniAD and won the IEEE CVPR 2023 Best Paper Award. UniAD has a tremendous impact both in academia and industry, including the recent rollout to customers by Tesla in FSD V12. He created the first large-scale real robot ecosystem, AgiBot World, that systematically investigated the scaling law principles for robotic manipulation and won IROS 2025 Best Paper Finalist. He proposed the bird's-eye-view perception work, BEVFormer, that won Top 100 AI Papers in 2022. He served as Area Chair for CVPR, NeurIPS (including 2023 Notable AC), ICLR, ICCV, ICML, RSS, referee for Nature, Science Robotics, Guest Editor at Automotive Innovations. He is the Working Group Chair for IEEE Standards P3474 under Vehicular Technology Society. He is the Senior Member of IEEE, CCF and CSIG. He is the recipient of China AI Wu Wen Jun Early Career Award 2024.\n中文简介\n李弘扬，香港大学助理教授，OpenDriveLab团队（\nopendrivelab.com\n）联合创始人。研究方向为端到端智能系统在机器人、自动驾驶的应用。他主导的端到端自动驾驶方案UniAD于2022年提出，获IEEE CVPR 2023最佳论文奖。UniAD等系列工作产生了明显的社会经济效益，包括特斯拉于2023年推出的端到端FSD。他构造的超大规模具身智能训练场AgiBot World，是业界首个百万真机、千万仿真数据集，系统研究具身Scaling Law方法论，获IROS 2025最佳论文入围奖。他提出的俯视图感知方法BEVFormer，获2022年百强影响力人工智能论文榜单，成为业界广泛使用的纯视觉检测基准。他多次担任CVPR、NeurIPS、ICLR、ICCV、ICML、RSS等国际会议领域主席（AC），其中获得NeurIPS 2023 Notable AC。他是《自然》、《科学·机器人》的审稿人、期刊《Automotive Innovations》客座编委。IEEE、CCF、CSIG高级会员、IEEE汽车委员会自动驾驶国际标准工作组组长。荣获2024年中国吴文俊人工智能青年科技奖、2023年上海市东方英才计划领军项目。\nResearch\nFocus:  AI for Robotics, Autonomous Driving, 3D Vision, Foundation Models\nGoogle Scholar\nHKU Scholars Hub\nPublications\nat OpenDriveLab\nTeaching\nCCAI9025:\nAI-driven Robotics for Humankind\nMoodle\n,\nHighlight\n,\nField Trip\nFall 2025\nVenue: WLGH, Graduate House\nDATA8017:\nFundamentals of Autonomous Intelligent Systems\nMoodle\nFall 2025\nVenue: IDS P603 Seminar Room, Graduate House\nIDSS2501:\nEmbodied AI 101\nMoodle\nSummer Semester 2025\nVenue: LE2, Main Campus\nTalks\nTalk on \"Towards Generalizable and Intelligent System for Robotic Manipulation\", New York University, USA, September 2025.\nYouTube\nTalk on \"End-to-end Autonomous Driving: Past, Current and Onwards\", Workshop on\nAutonomous Driving\n, CVPR 2025, Nashville, USA.\nYouTube\nTalk on \"What are Good (Pre-training) Representations for Robotic Manipulation?\", TU Delft, Netherlands, July 2024, in conjunction with RSS 2024.\nYouTube\n/\nSlides\nTalk on \"Could Foundation Models really resolve End-to-end Autonomy?\", Tutorial on\nEnd-to-End Autonomy: A New Era of Self-Driving\n, CVPR 2024, Seattle, USA.\nYouTube\n/\nSlides"
  },
