    "homepage_text": "Gangwei JIANG\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nGangwei JIANG\nDoctor of Philosophy (Student)\n,\nDepartment of Computer Science\nh-index\n14\nScopus Citations\n2\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2023\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0000-0003-2052-658X\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Gangwei JIANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n4\nSimilar Profiles\nLarge Language Model\nComputer Science\n100%\nComputational Linguistics\nComputer Science\n46%\nPrompt Tuning\nComputer Science\n36%\nInternal Structure\nComputer Science\n36%\nPre-Trained Model\nComputer Science\n36%\nPre-Trained Language Models\nComputer Science\n36%\nChain-of-Thought\nComputer Science\n36%\nVector Function\nComputer Science\n36%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n5\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\nUnlocking the Power of Function Vectors for Characterizing and Mitigating Catastrophic Forgetting in Continual Instruction Tuning\nJiang, G.\n, Jiang, C.,\nLi, Z.\n, Xue, S., Zhou, J.,\nSong, L.\n, Lian, D. &\nWei, Y.\n,\nApr 2025\n,\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations 2025 (ICLR 2025).\nYue, Y., Garg, A., Peng, N., Sha, F. & Yu, R. (eds.).\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations, ICLR\n,\np. 38268-38293\n26 p.\n( International Conference on Learning Representations, ICLR).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nVector Function\n100%\nInstruction Tuning\n100%\nLarge Language Model\n75%\nRegularization\n25%\nEmpirical Test\n25%\n2\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nWhat Makes a Good Reasoning Chain? Uncovering Structural Patterns in Long Chain-of-Thought Reasoning\nJiang, G.\n(Co-first Author), Liu, Y. (Co-first Author),\nLi, Z.\n, W., V., Zhang, F.,\nSong, L.\n,\nWei, Y.\n& Lian, D.,\nNov 2025\n,\nProceedings of the 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing.\nChristodoulopoulos, C., Chakraborty, T., Rose, C. & Peng, V. (eds.). United States:\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics\n,\np. 6490\n6514 p.\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nFile\nInternal Structure\n100%\nLarge Language Model\n100%\nChain-of-Thought\n100%\nComplex Task\n50%\nBacktracking\n50%\n4\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nMitigate Negative Transfer with Similarity Heuristic Lifelong Prompt Tuning\nWu, C.,\nJiang, G.\n& Lian, D.,\nAug 2024\n,\nFindings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: ACL 2024.\nWu, L.-W., Martins, A. & Srikumar, V. (eds.). Bangkok:\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics\n,\np. 10944-10959\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nPrompt Tuning\n100%\nLifelong Education\n100%\nComputational Linguistics\n50%\nLifelong Learning\n40%\nAlgorithm Selection\n20%\n14\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nUnderstanding and Patching Compositional Reasoning in LLMs\nLi, Z.\n,\nJiang, G.\n, Xie, H.,\nSong, L.\n, Lian, D. &\nWei, Y.\n,\nAug 2024\n,\n62nd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL 2024) - Proceedings of the Conference.\nKu, L.-W., Martins, A. & Srikumar, V. (eds.). Kerrville, TX:\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics\n,\np. 9668-9688\n21 p.\n(Proceedings of the Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nLarge Language Model\n100%\nSelf-Attention\n50%\nLanguage Modeling\n25%\nComputational Linguistics\n25%\nReasoning Task\n25%\n7\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n46\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nTowards Anytime Fine-tuning: Continually Pre-trained Language Models with Hypernetwork Prompts\nJiang, G.\n, Jiang, C., Xue, S., Zhang, J. Y., Zhou, J., Lian, D. &\nWei, Y.\n,\nDec 2023\n,\nFindings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: EMNLP 2023.\nBouamor, H., Pino, J. & Bali, K. (eds.). Singapore:\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics\n,\np. 12081-12095\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nPre-Trained Language Models\n100%\nPre-Trained Model\n100%\nLinguistics\n100%\nKnowledge Transfer\n33%\nComputational Linguistics\n33%\n5\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n30\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)"
