    "homepage_text": "Borong Zhang | UW-Madison\nBorong Zhang\nEmail address:\nbzhang388 <at> wisc <dot> edu\nPostal address:\nBorong Zhang\nVan Vleck Hall\n480 Lincoln Drive\nMadison, WI 53706\nOffice: 818 Van Vleck Hall\nLinks:\nHomepage\n|\nGitHub\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nResearchGate\n|\nAbout Me\nI am a fifth-year Ph.D. candidate in\nApplied and Computational Mathematics\nat the University of Wisconsin-Madison.\nMy research interests include scientific machine learning and inverse problems.\nI am advised by\nDr. Qin Li\nand\nDr. Leonardo Andrés Zepeda Núñez\n.\n            I am a member of\nKinetics at Madison\n.\nI received my B.A. in Applied Mathematics and Computer Science from UC Berkeley in 2020."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Weidong Huang::https://weidonghuang.info/": {
    "homepage": "https://weidonghuang.info/",
    "all_emails": [
      "weidong.huang@uts.edu.au"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Dr. Weidong (Tony) Huang at University of Technology Sydney (UTS)\nAssociate \n\t\t\tProfessor Tony Huang\nCourse D\nirector,\nUTS Data Science and Innovation\nTransdisciplinary School (TD School)\nUniversity of Technology Sydney\nDirector,\nCollaboration and Visual Analytics Research Lab\n(old)\nEmail: weidong.huang@uts.edu.au\nBiography\nDr Huang is an Associate Professor with UTS TD School and serves on the executive committee of UTS Visualisation Institute and the advisory group for UTS Connected Intelligence Centre. He was the program \nleader for Human-Data Interaction at\nSwinburne Data Science Research Institute\nand deputy director of\nMaster of \nInformation Technology Program\nat Swinburne, a senior lecturer at UTAS, and\na senior research scientist at CSIRO ICT Centre (now\nData61\n). At CSIRO, he worked on a number of strategic and commercial multi-million dollar projects related to virtual/mixed/augmented reality, mobile/wearable/ubiquitous computing, computer-supported collaboration, and computer graphics/vision/visualization/multimedia. In these projects, he was a research leader responsible for defining and pursuing research questions. He designed multimodal system interfaces, data visualizations, and interaction methods; investigated HCI, CSCW, and human factors issues; evaluated usability and user experience; conducted data analytics; and provided data-driven solutions across industrial domains including mining, education, health, and manufacturing.\nHe received his PhD in computer science from University of Sydney. He also had formal training in experimental psychology and professional experience in psychometrics. His research interests are broadly in human computer (data) interaction and data science. He has\nover 150 publications\nin these areas including 6 books; one of \nhis books:\nRecent Trends \nof Mobile Collaborative Augmented Reality Systems\n, was among the top 25% most downloaded eBooks of Springer, a major \nacademic publisher. His \nresearch has achieved impact both in\nacademia\nand in\nindustry\n. He gives keynote/plenary speeches, invited talks and seminars at \nconferences and universities worldwide, and has been named among\nthe Standford's top 2% scientists worldwide\neach year since 2020.\nDr Huang served as a general chair, a technical program chair, or an organizing \nchair for a number of international conferences and workshops. He is a PC member \nfor more than 100 conferences and also regularly invited to serve as a reviewer or a guest editor on topics within his fields of expertise such as Nature Scientific Reports, Applied Cognitive Psychology and \nInformation Sciences. He is a grant proposal assessor for the Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council of Canada (NSERC), the Dutch Research Council (NWO) and the Australian \nResearch Council (ARC), and an examiner of PhD theses for ten top Australian \nuniversities. He has been Associate Editor-in-Chief of Journal of Visual Languages and \nComputing, Associate Editor of Behaviour and Information Technology, and a founding chair of the technical committee on Visual Analytics and \nCommunication of IEEE SMC Society, which was awarded the most active technical committee in 2022.\nHe has successfully developed/co-developed a number of projects funded by \ngovernment funding agencies and commercial partners, including prestigious and competitive ARC DP and LP grants, with a\ntotal value of over 3 million dollars. He also provides consulting services to\ninternal research teams and external companies on user requirements analysis,\nuser interface design, human factors, production process optimization issues and\nbusiness data analytics. He has developed a 350-item checklist for heuristic evaluation of\n3d multimodal user interfaces. The external companies he had worked with include EnergyAustralia, Echelon Mining Services, SGE Analytical Science, BHP Billiton, Boeing and Oracle.\nDr Huang is a professional member of  Human Factors & Ergonomics Society of Australia, and a member of IEEE, ACM and ACS. In recent years, he has been a research fellow at University of Sydney and Australian Council for Educational Research (ACER), a visiting researcher at University of Arizona and National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University.\nSelected Grants\nData Analytics and Insights of Occupational Violence for Uplifting OVS Data Informed Practice Capability.\nNSW Department of Education\n. $75,000\nVisual Analytics of Risk Stratification for Water Corporation.\nWater Corporation of Western Australia\n. $140,000\nGuiding Students with Remote Hands for Electronics Troubleshooting.\nCSIRO Science and Industry Endowment Fund\n(SIEF). $5,000\nDevelopment of the \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tviscom technical committee.\nIEEE SMC Society\n. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t$5,600.\nNetCollect - Online social network data \n\t\t\tcollection and visualization platform.\nSNA Think Tank Pty Ltd & \n\t\t\tARC\n. $69,000\nRemote presence for guidance on physical tasks.\nAustralian Research Council Discovery\n\t\t\t\tProject\n(ARC DP). $469,000\nVisual Analytics for Massive\n\t\t\t\tMultivariate Networks.\nAustralian Research Council Linkage\n\t\t\t\tProject\n(ARC LP). $557,650\nHelping hands: an innovative tele-assistance\n\t\t\t\tsystem for clinical skill development.\nAustralian Government Office for Teaching and\n\t\t\t\tLearning\n. $50,000\nRemote Mining Engineer.\nAustralian\n\t\t\t\tGovernment Department of Industry: Researchers in Business\n\t\t\t\tgrant\n. $90,000\nFood Data Science and Advanced Visual Analytics.\nNICTA (Data61)\n. $25,000\nVisual Cues for Efficient Airplane\n\t\t\t\tManufacturing.\nBoeing and CSIRO\n. $1,500,000\nVisual Communication of Massive Sensor\n\t\t\t\tData for Intelligent Mining.\nCSIRO\n. $250,000\nAn innovative tele-assistance system to\n\t\t\t\tsupport education in clinical procedures.\nTasmanian Clinical\n\t\t\t\tEducation Network\n. $35,000\nMaking sense of biology data through\n\t\t\t\tartistic interactions.\nUTAS Cross-Disciplinary Incentive Grant\n.\n\t\t\t\t$16,800\nSmart City Initiative: Regional\n\t\t\t\tDevelopment for Better Living.\nUTAS strategic research grant\n.\n\t\t\t\t$120,000\nQuality metrics for curved graph drawings.\nHIT Lab Australia research collaboration grant\n,\n\t\t\t\t$30,000\nScience Citizenship\nGuest Editor: Special issue on Multimodal User Interaction @\nJournal on Multimodal User Interfaces\nGuest Editor: Special issue on Spatial User Interaction @\nComputers & Graphics\nGuest Editor: Special issue on Visual \n\t\t\t\t\tCommunication Cues for Remote Collaboration @\nJournal of Visual Communication and Image Representation\nGuest Editor: Special Issue on Emerging \n\t\t\t\t\tTechnologies for Home Health Care @\nHealth Informatics Journal\nGuest Editor: Special Issue on \n\t\t\t\t\tAugmented Humanity for \n\t\t\t\t\tHealth and Wellbeing @\nInternational Journal of Human-Computer Studies\nChair:\nTechnical committee on visual analytics and communication, IEEE SMC \n\t\t\tSociety\n(2015- )\nSteering Committee Chair:\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInternational \n\t\t\t\t\tConference on Information Visualisation(2020-2024 )\nAssociate Editor-in-Chief: \n\t\t\t\t\t\tJournal of Visual Languages and Computing\n\t\t\t\t\t(2015-2018)\nAssociate Editor:\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBehaviour and Information Technology \n\t\t\t\t\t(2017-present)\nEditorial Board Member:\n\t\t\t\t\t\tJournal of Computer Languages (2018-2024)\nEditorial Board Member:\n\t\t\t\t\t\tInternational Journal of Cyber Behavior, Psychology and Learning (2013-2021)\n1.\n\t\t\tConference and workshop leadership:\n2026\nConference Chair: The 19th  IEEE Pacific Visualization Conference (\nPacificVis'26\n). April 20-23, 2026, Sydney, Australia\n2026\nConference Chair: The 24th Australasian Data Science and Machine Learning Conference (AusDM'26). December 2026, Sydney, Australia\n2025\nSpecial Session Organizer: The Opportunities and Challenges of AI in Virtual Museums (IEEE SMC'25). October 5-8, 2025, Vienna, Austria\n2025\nProceeding Chair: The 18th International Symposium on Visual Information Communication and Interaction (VINCI'25). December 1-3, 2025, Linz, Austria\n2024\nConference co-chair: The 12th ACM Symposium on Spatial User Interaction (SUI 2024)\n2023\nConference co-chair: The 11th ACM Symposium on Spatial User Interaction (SUI 2023)\n2021\nProgram Committee \n\t\t\t\t\tChair: The 25th International Conference Information \n\t\t\t\t\tVisualisation (IV \n\t\t\t\t\t2021)\n2020\nVisNotes co-chair: The \n\t\t\t\t\t13th IEEE Pacific Visualization Symposium (PacificVis \n\t\t\t\t\t2020)\n2018\nPoster chair: \n\t\t\t\t\tInternational Conference on Artificial Reality and \n\t\t\t\t\tTelexistence & Eurographics Symposium on Virtual \n\t\t\t\t\tEnvironments (ICAT-EGVE \n\t\t\t2018)\n2018\nWorkshop organizer: \n\t\t\t\t\t\tAugmented Humanity using Wearable and Mobile Devices for \n\t\t\t\t\tHealth and Wellbeing at MobileCHI 2018\n2018\nChair of Special \n\t\t\t\t\tSession on \n\t\t\t\t\tVisual and Immersive Analytics at IEEE SMC18\n2017\nPoster chair: International \n\t\t\tConference on Artificial Reality and Telexistence & Eurographics \n\t\t\tSymposium on Virtual Environments (ICAT-EGVE \n\t\t\t2017)\n2017\nWorkshop chair: The 22nd Annual International Conference on 3D Web Technology\n(Web3D 2017)\n2016\nPC chair:\n\t\t\tThe 28th Australian Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (OzCHI 2016)\n2016\nOrganizing chair:\n\t\t\tThe 13th International Conference on Cooperative Design, Visualization and Engineering (CDVE 2016)\n2016\nConference chair: The 13th International Conference on Computer Graphics, Imaging and Visualization (CGiV'16)\n2016\nChair of Short Papers and Posters:\n\t\t\tThe 12th International Conference on Intelligent Environments\n(IE'16)\n2015\nOrganizing chair: The 12th International Conference on Cooperative Design, Visualization and Engineering\n(CDVE2015)\n2015\nChair of Posters and\n\t\t\tDemonstrations: IEEE International Symposium on Big Data Visual\n\t\t\tAnalytics\n(BDVA2015)\n2014\nConference chair: The 7th International Symposium on Visual Information Communication and Interaction\n(VINCI14)\n2013\nConference chair: The 10th International Conference Computer Graphics, Imaging and Visualization (CGIV13)\n2013\nWorkshop organizer: International Workshop on Big Data in Collaborative Environments\n2012\nChair of Special Session on Ubiquitous and Collaborative Computing at IEEE SMC12\n2012\nPC chair: The 24th Australian Computer-Human Interaction Conference (OzCHI 2012)\n2012\nPC chair: The 9th International Conference Computer Graphics, Imaging and Visualization (CGIV12)\n2011\nChair of Short Papers and Posters: The 23rd Australian Computer-Human Interaction Conference (OzCHI 2011)\n2010\nWorkshop organizer: International Workshop on Mobile Collaborative Augmented Reality (MCAR) at ISMAR 2010\n2010\nSymposium chair: International Symposium on 3D Visual Environments (3DVE) at CGIV10\n2009\nSession chair: The 2009 Visual Information Communications- International Symposium (VINCI09)\n2008\nOrganizing Committee member: 19th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation (ISAAC08)\n2007\nOrganizing Committee member: 15th International Symposium on Graph Drawing (GD07)\n2.\n\t\t\tJournal reviewing:\nApplied Cognitive Psychology\nNature Scientific Reports\nComputers in Human Behaviour\nPresence: Teleoperators and Virtual \n\t\t\t\t\tEnvironments\nErgonomics\nComputer Supported Cooperative Work\nInformation Sciences\nInternational Journal of Cyber Behaviour, Psychology and Learning\nJournal on Multimodal User Interfaces\nAdvances in Human-Computer Interaction\nIEEE Transactions on Human-Machine Systems\nIEEE Transactions on Affective Computing\nIEEE Transactions on Learning Technologies\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics\nInformation Visualization\nJournal of Visual Languages and Computing\nACM Computers in Entertainment\nACM Transactions on Interactive \n\t\t\t\t\tIntel