    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/Ivan-Zhong",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yifan Zhong's Homepage\nYifan Zhong\nPh.D. Candidate\nInstitute for Artificial Intelligence\nPeking University\nE-mail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\nBiography\nHi, I'm Yifan Zhong. \n          I am currently a third-year Ph.D. student in the\nPAIR Lab\nat\nPeking University\nguided by\nProf. Yaodong Yang\n. \n          Prior to this, I earned my bachelor's degree from\nTongji University\nin Computer Science and Technology. Earlier in my education, I attended No. 1 experimental class at\nThe High School Affiliated to Renmin University of China\n.\nMy research interests include reinforcement learning, foundation models, generative models, and embodied AI.\n          Please do not hesitate to reach out to me via email at\nzhongyifan@stu.pku.edu.cn\n!\nSelected Publications\n* equal contribution\nA Survey on Vision-Language-Action Models: An Action Tokenization Perspective\nYifan Zhong*\n, Fengshuo Bai*, Shaofei Cai, Xuchuan Huang, Zhang Chen, Xiaowei Zhang, Yuanfei Wang, Shaoyang Guo, Tianrui Guan, Ka Nam Lui, Zhiquan Qi, Yitao Liang, Yuanpei Chen, Yaodong Yang.\narXiv\n/\nPaper List\nDexGraspVLA: A Vision-Language-Action Framework Towards General Dexterous Grasping\nYifan Zhong*\n, Xuchuan Huang*, Ruochong Li, Ceyao Zhang, Zhang Chen, Tianrui Guan, Fanlian Zeng, Ka Nam Lui, Yuyao Ye, Yitao Liang, Yaodong Yang, Yuanpei Chen.\nThe Fortieth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2026.\n(Oral)\nProject\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nVideo\nIn-Context Editing: Learning Knowledge from Self-Induced Distributions\nSiyuan Qi, Bangcheng Yang, Kailin Jiang, Xiaobo Wang, Jiaqi Li,\nYifan Zhong\n, Yaodong Yang, Zilong Zheng.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2025.\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\nPanacea: Pareto Alignment via Preference Adaptation for LLMs\nYifan Zhong*\n, Chengdong Ma*, Xiaoyuan Zhang*, Ziran Yang, Haojun Chen, Qingfu Zhang, Siyuan Qi, Yaodong Yang.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2024.\nPaper\n/\narXiv\nMaximum Entropy Heterogeneous-Agent Reinforcement Learning\nJiarong Liu*,\nYifan Zhong*\n, Siyi Hu, Haobo Fu, QIANG FU, Xiaojun Chang, Yaodong Yang.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2024.\n(Spotlight)\nProject\n/\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nVideo\nCivRealm: A Learning and Reasoning Odyssey in Civilization for Decision-Making Agents\nSiyuan Qi*, Shuo Chen*, Yexin Li*, Xiangyu Kong*, Junqi Wang*, Bangcheng Yang, Pring Wong,\nYifan Zhong\n, Xiaoyuan Zhang, Zhaowei Zhang, Nian Liu, Yaodong Yang, Song-Chun Zhu.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2024.\n(Spotlight)\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\nHeterogeneous-agent reinforcement learning\nYifan Zhong*\n, Jakub Grudzien Kuba*, Xidong Feng*, Siyi Hu, Jiaming Ji, Yaodong Yang.\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (\nJMLR\n), 2024.\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\nSafety gymnasium: A unified safe reinforcement learning benchmark\nJiaming Ji*, Borong Zhang*, Jiayi Zhou*, Xuehai Pan, Weidong Huang, Ruiyang Sun, Yiran Geng,\nYifan Zhong\n, Juntao Dai, Yaodong Yang.\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems Track on Datasets and Benchmarks (\nNeurIPS DB\n), 2023.\nProject\n/\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nDocs\nMARLlib: A Scalable and Efficient Multi-agent Reinforcement Learning Library\nSiyi Hu,\nYifan Zhong\n, Minquan Gao, Weixun Wang, Hao Dong, Xiaodan Liang, Zhihui Li, Xiaojun Chang, Yaodong Yang.\nJournal of Machine Learning Research Machine Learning Open Source Software (\nJMLR MLOSS\n), 2023.\nPaper\n/\narXiv\n/\nCode\n/\nDocs\nMyoChallenge: Learning contact-rich manipulation using a musculoskeletal hand\nYiran Geng*, Boshi An*,\nYifan Zhong*\n, Jiaming Ji, Yuanpei Chen, Hao Dong, Yaodong Yang.\nFirst Place in NeurIPS 2022 Challenge Track (1st in 340 submissions from 40 teams).\nPaper\n/\nChallenge Page\n/\nCode\n/\nSlides\n/\nAward\n/\nMedia (BIGAI)\n/\nMedia (PKU-IAI)\nExperiences\nResearch Intern, Algorithm Department, PsiBot\nSep. 2024 - Present\nTopic: Dexterous Manipulation, Vision-Language-Action Models, Embodied AI\nWork with:\nYuanpei Chen\n.\nSupervised by:\nYaodong Yang\n.\nResearch Intern, Multi-Agent Systems Laboratory, BIGAI\nAug. 2022 - Aug. 2024\nTopic: Reinforcement Learning, Multi-Agent Systems, LLM Alignment\nSupervised by:\nYaodong Yang\n,\nSiyuan Qi\n.\nService and Teaching\nConference Reviewer for NeurIPS (2024, 2025), ICRA (2026).\nArea Chair for DAI (2024).\nTeaching Assistant for \"Large Language Models and Alignment\" (2024 Fall). [\nWebsite\n]\nTeaching Assistant for \"Multi-Agent System\" (2025 Spring). [\nWebsite\n]\nRecent Talks\nI presented a tutorial on \"Vision-Language-Action Models for Robot Manipulation\" (in Chinese). [\nVideo\n]\nSelected Honors & Awards\nPeking University Presidential Scholarship (the highest doctoral research honor)\n2025\nAcademic Star Award, School of Intelligence Science and Technology, Peking University\n2025\nIAI Doctoral Fellowship, Institute for AI, Peking University\n2024\nSecond Prize of BIGAI Research Rising Star Award\n2024\nOutstanding Graduate of Shanghai\n2023\nFirst Place in NeurIPS 2022 Challenge Track\n2022\nCCF Outstanding Undergraduate Student\n2022\nNational Scholarship\n2022, 2020\nThe 46th ICPC Asia Regional Contest (Jinan Site) Silver Medal\n2021\nQidi Scholarship\n2021\nFirst Prize of Undergraduate Outstanding Student Scholarship\n2021\nSports\nI am passionate about sports, especially swimming, badminton, and running. Currently, I am a member of the Peking University swimming team and the AI Department badminton team, where I train regularly. I also serve as the captain of the AI Department swimming team, where I organize and lead training sessions. If you share the same interests, feel free to reach out and connect!"
  },
