    "homepage_text": "Zhun Zhong\nZhun Zhong\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTenure-Track Professor\nSchool of Computer Science and Information Engineering\nHefei University of Technology\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout Me\nExperience:\nI am currently a Tenure-Track Professor at the Hefei University of Technology. I am also an Honorary Associate Professor at the University of Nottingham (UoN). I was an Assistant Professor at University of Nottingham (2023-2024) and University of Trento (2022-2023). I was a Postdoc at University of Trento (UNITN, 2020-2022) working with Prof.\nNicu Sebe\n. I received my Ph.D. degree in 2019 from the Cognitive Science Department at Xiamen University under the supervision of Prof.\nShaozi Li\n. I was also a joint Ph.D. student in 2017-2019 at University of Technology Sydney under the co-supervision of Prof.\nYi Yang\nand Dr.\nLiang Zheng\n. I received the M.S. Degree in Computer Science and Technology in 2015 from China University Of Petroleum, Qingdao, China. I received the B.S. degree from the Information Engineering Department, from East China University of Technology in 2012.\nResearch Interests:\nOur\nLab for Intelligence and VisiON (LION)\ncommits to designing trustworthy intelligent visual recognition systems for real-world applications. To achieve this goal, we mainly focus on the areas of data augmentation, unsupervised/semi- supervised learning, federated learning, domain generalization, domain adaptation and novel class discovery, and investigate their advantages in visual tasks, such as object retrieval, image classification, semantic segmentation, etc.\nJoin Us:\nI am looking for highly-motivated Ph.D. students starting from September 2026; I also welcome visiting students/research assistant.\nI am also a guest researcher at UNITN (\nMHUG\nled by Prof. Nicu Sebe), in which we are hiring highly-motivated Postdoc/Ph.D. students/visiting students/research assistant.\nDrop me an email if you are interested in the above positions. Please use the subject format [Name_Position_AppliedUniversity]. For example, [Jack_PhD_UoN], [Mike_Postdoc_UNITN]. [\nEnglish Version\n] [\nChinese Version\n]\nNews\nSep 28, 2025\nI am invited as Area Chair for ICML 2025, NeurIPS 2025, ACM MM 2025, ICLR 2026, CVPR 2026.\nSep 18, 2025\nOne paper is accepted by TPAMI 2025. Congrats to Dong.\nSep 10, 2025\nOne paper is accepted by EMNLP Finds 2025. Congrats to Junxi (Undergraduate Student).\nSep 1, 2025\nOne paper is accepted by ACM MM 2025. Congrats to Jinjie (Undergraduate Student).\nMay 30, 2024\nI am invited as AE for\nComputer Vision and Image Understanding\n。\nMay 1, 2024\nOne paper is accepted by ICML 2024. Congrats to Chentao.\nApr 15, 2024\nI am invited to serve as an Area Chair (AC) for\nNeurIPS\n2024.\nSelected Publications\nAAAI\nRandom Erasing Data Augmentation\nZhun Zhong\n, Liang Zheng, Guoliang Kang, Shaozi Li, and Yi Yang\nIn AAAI\n2020\nBib\nPDF\nTorchVision\nCIFAR\nImageNet\nReID\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhong2020erasing\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Random Erasing Data Augmentation}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhong, Zhun and Zheng, Liang and Kang, Guoliang and Li, Shaozi and Yang, Yi}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{AAAI}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2020}\n,\n}\nPaperDigest Most Influential AAAI Papers (1st-Place)!\nCitation 2000+!\nTPAMI\nLearning to Adapt Invariance in Memory for Person Re-identification\nZhun Zhong\n, Liang Zheng, Zhiming Luo, Shaozi Li, and Yi Yang\nTPAMI 2021 + CVPR 2019\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@article\n{\nzhong2020memorz\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Learning to Adapt Invariance in Memory for Person Re-identification}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhong, Zhun and Zheng, Liang and Luo, Zhiming and Li, Shaozi and Yang, Yi}\n,\njournal\n=\n{TPAMI 2021 + CVPR 2019}\n,\nyear\n=\n{}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{43}\n,\nnumber\n=\n{8}\n,\npages\n=\n{2723-2738}\n,\ndoi\n=\n{10.1109/TPAMI.2020.2976933}\n,\nissn\n=\n{1939-3539}\n,\n}\n600+ Citations!\nTIP\nCamStyle: A Novel Data Augmentation Method for Person Re-identification\nZhun Zhong\n, Liang Zheng, Zhedong Zheng, Shaozi Li, and Yi Yang\nTIP 2019 + CVPR 2018\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@article\n{\nzhong2019camstylf\n,\ntitle\n=\n{CamStyle: A Novel Data Augmentation Method for Person Re-identification}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhong, Zhun and Zheng, Liang and Zheng, Zhedong and Li, Shaozi and Yang, Yi}\n,\njournal\n=\n{TIP 2019 + CVPR 2018}\n,\nyear\n=\n{}\n}\n700+ Citations!\nCVPR\nRe-ranking person re-identification with k-reciprocal encoding\nZhun Zhong\n, Liang Zheng, Donglin Cao, and Shaozi Li\nIn Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2017 IEEE Conference on\n2017\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhong2017re\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Re-ranking person re-identification with k-reciprocal encoding}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhong, Zhun and Zheng, Liang and Cao, Donglin and Li, Shaozi}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2017 IEEE Conference on}\n,\npages\n=\n{3652--3661}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2017}\n,\norganization\n=\n{IEEE}\n}\nCitation 1000+!\n-->\n\n---\n\nCV | Zhun Zhong\nCV\nGeneral Information\nFull Name\nZhun Zhong\nLanguages\nMandarin, English\nWebSite\nzhunzhong.site\nEducation\n2015-2019\nPhD\nXiamen University, China\nAdvisor -> Prof. Shaozi Li\nComputer Science and Technology\n2017-2019\nJoint PhD\nUniversity of Technology Sydney, Australia\nAdvisor -> Prof. Yi Yang and Dr. Liang Zheng\nComputer Science and Technology\n2012-2015\nMaster\nChina University Of Petroleum, China\nComputer Science and Technology\n2008-2012\nBachelor\nEast China University of Technology, China\nComputer Science and Technology\nExperience\n2024-now\nTenure Track Professor\nHefei University of Technology\n2025-now\nHonorary Associate Professor\nUniversity of Nottingham\n2023-2024\nAssistant Professor\nUniversity of Nottingham\n2022-2023\nAssistant Professor\nUniversity of Trento\n2020-2022\nPostdoc\nUniversity of Trento\nAdvisor -> Prof. Nicu Sebe\nHonors and Awards\n2023\nWorld's Top 2% Scientists 2023 by Stanford University\n2024\nAI 2000 Most Inﬂuential Scholar Honorable Mention in AAAI/IJCAI\n2023\nAI 2000 Most Inﬂuential Scholar Honorable Mention in AAAI/IJCAI\n2022\nWorld's Top 2% Scientists 2022 by Stanford University\n2022\nAI 2000 Most Inﬂuential Scholar Honorable Mention in AAAI/IJCAI\n2021\nOutstanding Reviewer -> NeurIPS 2021\n2020\nOutstanding Reviewer -> CVPR 2020\nAcademic Interests\nLearning Paradigms\nDomain Adaptation\nDomain Generalization\nData Augmentation\nNovel Class Discovery\nUnsupervised Learning\nSemi-Supervised Learning\nFederated Learning\nVisual Applications\nObject Re-identification\nImage Classification\nSemantic Segmentation\nMedical Imaging\nProfessional Activity\nArea Chair / Senior Program Committee\nICML 2024 (Area Chair)\nNeurIPS 2024 (Area Chair)\nICLR 2024 (Area Chair)\nECCV 2024 (Area Chair)\nCVPR 2024 (Area Chair)\nAAAI 2022 (SPC)\nACM MM 2022, 2024 (Area Chair)\nACM MM 2022 (Open Souce Competition Chair)\nIJCAI 2021 (SPC)\nAssociate Editor\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (Guest Editor for Special Issue)\nImage and Visual Computing\nComputer Vision and Image Understanding\nComputer Vision and Image Understanding (Guest Editor for Special Issue)\nInternational Journal of Applied Earth Observation and Geoinformation (Guest Editor for Special Issue)\nElectronics (Guest Editor for Special Issue)\nConference Program Committee\nCVPR\nICCV\nECCV\nNeurIPS\nICML\nICLR\nAAAI\nIJCAI\nACM MM\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE TPAMI\nIJCV\nIEEE TIP\nTMLR\nIEEE TCSVT\nIEEE TMM\nIEEE TNNLS\nIEEE TITS"
