  "deep_homepage::Zhe Lin::https://sites.google.com/site/zhelin625/home": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/site/zhelin625/home",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhe-lin-14ba886/",
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nHome\nZhe Lin\nPh.D. University of Maryland, College Park\nSenior Principal Research Scientist (Senior Director)\nAdobe Research\nAdobe Systems Incorporated\nOffice:\nAdobe Seattle\nEmail:\nlimcher2001 'at' gmail 'dot' com\nEmail (c):\nzlin 'at' adobe 'dot' com\nURL (c):\nhttps://research.adobe.com/person/zhe-lin/\n[\nDBLP\n] [\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nLinkedIn\n]\n[\nInternship/Full-time Opportunities\n] We are hiring self-motivated graduate student interns anytime throughout the year, so please feel free to contact me if you are interested in working with me on a research project in computer vision, imaging, and generative models.\nBio:\nI am a researcher in Imaging and Languages Org, Adobe Research. I received a Ph.D. degree in Electrical  and Computer Engineering from University of Maryland at College Park in May 2009. Prior to that, I obtained a M.S. degree in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science from Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology in August 2004, and a B.Eng. degree in automatic control from University of Science and Technology of China. I have been a member of Adobe Research since May 2009. My research interests include computer vision, image and video processing, generative modeling and artificial intelligence.\nProfessional services:\nLead Area Chair for ICCV 2025\nLead Area Chair for CVPR 2025\nArea Chair for ECCV 2024\nArea Chair for CVPR 2022\nArea Chair for ACM MM 2020\nArea Chair for ECCV 2020\nArea Chair for CVPR 2020\nArea Chair for ICCV 2019\nArea Chair for CVPR 2019\nArea Chair for WACV 2018\nReviewers fo\nr CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, PAM\nI, IJCV since 2009\nCVPR 2016 Tutorial on Recent Techniques for Image Search\nGuest Editor for Pattern Recognition Journal in 2015\nAward/Honor\n:\nGenFill/GenExpand technology in Photoshop, Top AI Invention by TIMES, 2023\nDistinguished inventor: first employee at Adobe to hold 100th and 200th patents\n\"Mask-aware Transformer\" selected\nas a Best Paper Finalist in CVPR 2022\nBest Reviewer Award for ICCV 2021\n\"SmartEye\" selected as a Best Paper Honorable Mention in CHI 2019\nImageNet Challenge (ILSVRC 2014), Top 1 in classification/localization track\nImageNet Challenge (ILSVRC 2013), Top 6 in classification\nPixelNuggets image search demo, PC Magzine Technical Excellence Award, 2011\nSiemens Best Paper Award at ISVC 2008, Las Vegas, NV\nThe best performer at CLEAR 2007 Research Competition, Baltimore, MD\nPublications:\nLu Qi, Jason Kuen, Weidong Guo, Jiuxiang Gu, Zhe Lin, Bo Du, Yu Xu, Ming-Hsuan Yang, AIMS: All-Inclusive Multi-Level Segmentation, NeurIPS 2023 (spotlight).\nLu Qi, Jason Kuen, Weidong Guo, Tiancheng Shen, Jiuxiang Gu, Jiaya Jia, Zhe Lin, Ming-Hsuan Yang, High Quality Entity Segmentation, ICCV 2023 (oral).\nLingzhi Zhang, Zhengjie Xu, Connelly Barnes, Yuqian Zhou, Qing Liu, He Zhang, Sohrab Amirghodsi, Zhe Lin, Eli Shechtman, Jianbo Shi, Perceptual Artifacts Localization for Image Synthesis Tasks, ICCV 2023.\nQiucheng Wu, Yujian Liu, Handong Zhao, Trung Bui, Zhe Lin, Yang Zhang, Shiyu Chang, Harnessing the Spatial-Temporal Attention of Diffusion Models for High-Fidelity Text-to-Image Synthesis, ICCV 2023.\nJeya Maria Jose Valanarasu, He Zhang, Jianming Zhang, Yilin Wang, Zhe Lin, Jose Echevarria, Yinglan Ma, Zijun Wei, Kalyan Sunkavalli, Vishal M. Patel, Interactive Portrait Harmonization, ICLR 2023.\nYu Zeng, Zhe Lin, Jianming Zhang, Qing Liu, John Collomosse, Jason Kuen, Vishal M. Patel, SceneComposer: Any-Level Semantic Image Synthesis, CVPR 2023 (spotlight).\nShaoan Xie, Zhifei Zhang, Zhe Lin, Tobias Hinz, Kun Zhang, SmartBrush: Diffusion-based Multi-modal Image Inpainting, CVPR 2023 (spotlight).\nYizhi Song, Zhifei Zhang, Zhe Lin, Scott Cohen, Brian Price, Jianming Zhang, Soo Ye Kim, Daniel Aliaga, ObjectStitch: Object Compositing with Diffusion Model, CVPR 2023.\nSijie Zhu, Zhe Lin, Scott Cohen, Jason Kuen, Zhifei Zhang, Chen Chen, TopNet: Transformer-based Object Placement Network for Image Compositing, CVPR 2023.\nChuong Huynh, Yuqian Zhou, Zhe Lin, Connelly Barnes, Eli Shechtman, Sohrab Amirghodsi, Abhinav Shrivastava, Single-click Based Distractor Selection for Photo Cleaning, CVPR 2023.\nMang Tik Chiu, Xuaner Zhang, Zijun Wei, Yuqian Zhou, Eli Shechtman, Connelly Barnes, Zhe Lin, Florian Kainz, Sohrab Amirghodsi, Humphrey Shi, Automatic High Resolution Wire Segmentation and Removal, CVPR 2023.\nQiucheng Wu, Yujian Liu, Handong Zhao, Ajinkya Kale, Trung Bui, Tong Yu, Zhe Lin, Yang Zhang, Shiyu Chang, Uncovering the Disentanglement Capability in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models, CVPR 2023.\nLu Qi, Jason Kuen, Yi Wang, Jiuxiang Gu, Hengshuang Zhao, Zhe Lin, Philip H. S. Torr, Jiaya Jia, Open-World Entity Segmentation, TPAMI.\nJeya Maria Jose Valanarasu, He Zhang, Jianming Zhang, Yilin Wang, Zhe Lin, Jose Echevarria, Yinglan Ma, Zijun Wei, Kalyan Sunkavalli, Vishal M. Patel,\nInteractive Portrait Harmonization, ICLR 2023.\nLingzhi Zhang, Yuqian Zhou, Connelly Barnes, Sohrab Amirghodsi, Zhe Lin, Eli Shechtman, Jianbo Shi, Perceptual Artifacts Localization for Inpainting, ECCV 2022, oral.\nHaitian Zheng, Zhe Lin, Jingwan Lu, Scott Cohen, Eli Shechtman, Connelly Barnes, Jianming Zhang, Ning Xu, Sohrab Amirghodsi, Jiebo Luo, Image Inpainting with Cascaded Modulation GAN and Object-Aware Training, ECCV 2022.\nSijie Zhu, Zhe Lin, Scott Cohen, Jason Kuen, Zhifei Zhang, Chen Chen, GALA: Toward Geometry-and-Lighting-Aware Object Search for Compositing, ECCV 2022.\nKhoi Pham, Kushal Kafle, Zhe Lin, Zhihong Ding, Scott Cohen, Quan Tran, Abhinav Shrivastava, Improving Closed and Open-Vocabulary Attribute Prediction using Transformers, ECCV 2022.\nLu Qi, Jason Kuen, Zhe Lin, Jiuxiang Gu, Fengyun Rao, Dian Li, Weidong Guo, Zhen Wen, Ming-Hsuan Yang, Jiaya Jia, CA-SSL: Class-Agnostic Semi-Supervised Learning for Detection and Segmentation, ECCV 2022.\nYuchen Liu, Zhixin Shu, Yijun Li, Zhe Lin, Richard Zhan