    "homepage_text": "Baoxiang Wang\nBaoxiang Wang\nBaoxiang Wang\nAssistant Professor, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nI am an assistant professor at School of Data Science, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen. I work on the broad areas of\nreinforcement learning\nand\ngame theory\n. My recent works have a specific focus on interactions of multiple agents in complicated tasks and games.\nI obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science and Engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong in 2020, fortunate to be advised by\nSiu On Chan\nand\nAndrej Bogdanov\n. Before that, I obtained my B.E. in Information Security from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2014, under Hai Zhao.\nI am currently visiting Vector Institute at Toronto. I was visiting Vector Institute as a visiting researcher during Jan-Aug 2024, with\nYaoliang Yu\n, and University of Waterloo as a visiting assistant professor during May-Aug 2023, with\nPascal Poupart\n.\nEducation\n2014 - 2020 Ph.D. The Chinese University of Hong Kong\n2010 - 2014 B.E. Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nSome topics I am currently investigating\nReinforcement learning algorithms and specifically the LLM-RL and game-theoretic RL settings.\nUnderstanding and learning the interactions amid multiple intelligent agents in mechanism design problems and large-scale games.\nAd-hoc topics in learning theory and game theory that I find interesting\nProspective students\nI am recruiting PhD students for Fall 2026 enrollment (till April 2026). The degree will be issued by CUHK for PhD in Computer Science or PhD in Data Science, with a mark that the study in completed in the Shenzhen campus. The programs are similar to the ones in Hong Kong. See the\nprogram information\n.\nFor candidates, I care mostly about their math background and their motivation on working on new and explorative problems. Students are required to use AI tools to advance their research.\nContact\nOffice: 503 DY, CUHK Shenzhen.\r\nShenzhen, 518172\nPhone: +86 755 235-17020"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Fei Wu::https://sites.google.com/view/feiwukcl": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/feiwukcl",
    "all_emails": [
      "fei.wu@kcl.ac.uk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/M1kuW1ll",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Fei Wu (吴非)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFei Wu (吴非)\n📍\nLondon, UK\nEmail:\nfei.wu@kcl.ac.uk\nX:\n@William33203632\nGithub:\n@M1kuW1ll\nAbout me\nI am a 3rd-year PhD student in Computer Science at the Department of Informatics, King's College London, United Kingdom, supervised by\nDr. Stefanos Leonardos\nand\nProfessor Carmine Ventre\n. Before I started my PhD, I obtained my MSc degree in Computer Science at the University of Southampton, United Kingdom.\nMy research interests center around Decentralized Finance (DeFi) and Crypto-economics. My current focus is the economics of Maximal Extractable Value (MEV) on Ethereum, where I apply a combination of game theory, (agent-based) modeling & simulation, empirical data analysis, and mechanism design. I am fortunate to be advised by researchers from the\nRobust Incentives Group\nof Ethereum Foundation and\nFlashbots\n.\nNews\nNovember 2025, paper \"The Free Option Problem of ePBS\" is accepted by FC 2026.\nOctober 2025, honored to serve\nas a program committee member of AAMAS 202\n6.\nJuly 2025, paper \"Measuring CEX-DEX Extracted Value and Searcher Profitability: The Darkest of the MEV Dark Forest\" is accepted by AFT 2025.\nJuly 2025, paper “From Competition to Centralization: The Oligopoly in Ethereum Block Building Auctions” is accepted by ECAI 2025.\nMay 2025, happy to attend The Latest in DeFi Research (TLDR) Conference 2025 and present a poster on CEX-DEX arbitrages.\nOctober 2024, honored to serve as a program committee member of AAMAS 2025.\nSeptember 2024, our paper \"To Compete or Collude: Bidding Incentives in Ethereum Block Building Auctions\" is accepted by ICAIF 2024.\nJuly 2024, thrilled to announce that I am awarded The Latest in DeFi Research (TLDR) Fellowship 2024 funded by Uniswap Foundation.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nFei Wu (吴非) - CV\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFei Wu (吴非)\nCV\nGeneral Information\nFull Name: Fei Wu（吴非）\nLanguages: Chinese (native), English\nEducation\n2023 - Present\nMPhil/PhD in Computer Science Research,\nKing's College London, London, United Kingdom.\nSupervisors: Dr. Stefanos Leonardos, Professor Carmine Ventre\n2021 - 2022\nMSc in Computer Science,\nUniversity of Southampton, Southampton, United Kingdom.\nClassification: Distinction.\n2017 - 2021\nBSc in Computer Science,\nNew York Institute of Technology, New York, United States.\n2017 - 2021\nBEng in Computer Science and Technology,\nNanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Nanjing, China.\nCV_FeiWu_2025 (1).pdf\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
