    "homepage_text": "Prof. Yu Qiao's Homepage\nMultifunctional Materials Research Laboratory\nYu Qiao, Professor\nDepartment\r\n    of Structural Engineering\nProgram of Materials Science and\r\n    Engineering\nMailing Address:\n9500 Gilman Drive, MC 0085\nUniversity of California, San Diego\nLa Jolla, CA 92093-0085\nPhone:\n858-534-3388\nEmail:\nyqiao@ucsd.edu\nOffice:\nSME Building,\r\n    Rm. 442G\nLab:\nSME Building, Rm. 422\nClick [\nhere\n]\r\n    for the website at SE, UCSD\nClick [\nhere\n] for the\r\n    website at MATS, UCSD\nEducation\nPh.D.\r\n  in Mechanical Engineering, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge,\r\n  Massachusetts (2002)\nM.S.\r\n  in Materials Sci. & Eng., Chinese Academy of Sciences  Institute of\r\n  Mechanics, Beijing, China (1997)\nB.S.\r\n  in Applied Mechanics, University of Science and Technology of China, Hefei,\r\n  China (1994)\nAppointments\n2006\r\n   present: Associate Professor, Professor\nDepartment of Structural Engineering & Program of Materials Science and\r\n  Engineering\nUniversity of California  San Diego, La Jolla, California\n2002\r\n   2006: Assistant Professor\nDepartment of Civil Engineering\nUniversity of Akron, Akron, Ohio\nTeaching\nSE125\r\n   Probability, Statistics, and Reliability\nSE105\r\n   Structural Materials\nSE251A\r\n  / MATS261A  Processing of Polymers and Composites\nSE251B\r\n  / MATS261B  Mechanical Behavior of Composites and Polymers\nSE140\r\n   Structural and Materials Design\nSE290\r\n   Structural Engineering Seminar\nEngineering\r\n  Measurement and Data Analysis\nStatics\nMechanics\r\n  of Solids\nEngineering\r\n  Materials Lab\nAdvanced\r\n  Mechanical Behaviors of Materials\nMicromechanisms\nof Fracture and\r\n  Fatigue\nResearch\r\n  Interests\nThermodynamics and\r\n  statistical mechanics\nEnergy-related\r\n  materials\nAdvanced\r\n  infrastructural and composite materials\nIn-situ resource\r\n  utilization\nSmart materials and\r\n  structures\nProtective materials\r\n  and structures\nMultilayer materials\r\n  and structures\nFailure analysis of\r\n  engineering materials and structures\nSelected\r\n  Publications\n·\nQiao Y. Searching for\r\n  quantum non-thermodynamic phenomena.\nPhys. Rev. E\n111\n, 054108 (2025).\nhttps://escholarship.org/uc/item/55c900dz\n·\nQiao Y, Shang Z.\r\n  Second law of thermodynamics: Spontaneous cold-to-hot heat transfer in a\r\n  nonchaotic medium.\nPhys. Rev. E\n110\n, 054113 (2024).\nhttps://escholarship.org/uc/item/1g6074r3\n·\nQiao Y, Shang Z. On\r\n  the second law of thermodynamics: A global flow spontaneously induced by a\r\n  locally nonchaotic energy barrier.\nPhysica A\n647\n, 129828 (2024).\nhttps://escholarship.org/uc/item/5632b1ts\n·\nQiao Y, Shang Z, Kou\r\n  R. Molecular-sized outward-swinging gate: experiment and theoretical analysis\r\n  of a locally nonchaotic barrier.\nPhys. Rev. E\n104\n, 064133 (2021).\nhttps://escholarship.org/uc/item/5hp0w1vv"
