    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About\nAbout Me\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\nat Auburn University. Previously, I was a Harrison Early Career Assistant Professor in the Department of Statistics at the University of Warwick. I have also held postdoctoral research positions at the Pennsylvania State University with Prof. Runze Li and at the University of Warwick with Prof. Yi Yu. I earned my Ph.D. in Statistics from the University of Geneva under the supervision of Prof. Maria-Pia Victoria-Feser and Prof. Stéphane Guerrier, and I hold an M.Sc. in Statistics from the University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign.\nResearch Interests\nNonparametric estimation in high-dimensions.\nChange point detection and inference.\nHigh-dimensional inference under temporal dependence and contamination.\nContact\nEmail:\nhaotian.xu@auburn.edu\nOffice: 230C Parker Hall\nUniversity Website\n\n---\n\nContact\nEmail:\nfoo@xyz.com\nPhone:\n+91-123123\nMailing Address\n221B, Baker Street\nLondon\nUnited Kingdom\nSocial\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle+\nUniversity Website\n\n---\n\nContact\nEmail:\nfoo@xyz.com\nPhone:\n+91-123123\nMailing Address\n221B, Baker Street\nLondon\nUnited Kingdom\nSocial\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle+\nUniversity Website"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yi Yu::https://home.hiroshima-u.ac.jp/yiyu/index.html": {
    "homepage": "https://home.hiroshima-u.ac.jp/yiyu/index.html",
    "all_emails": [
      "yiyu@hiroshima-u.ac.jp"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/yy1lab",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Yi Yu's Homepage\nYi YU\nPh.D.\nAssociate\nProfessor (\nResearchgate\nGoogle\r\n  Scholar\n)\nDBLP (Yi Yu 0001)\nhttps://dblp.org/pid/99/111-1.html\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-0294-6620\nGenerative Intelligence Team\n,\nGraduate School of Advanced Science and\r\n  Engineering, Hiroshima University,\nJapan\nyiyu\r\n  at hiroshima-u.ac.jp\nPhone\r\n  number : (082)-424-7279\nThis\r\n  photo was taken at Three Broomsticks in Universal Studios Japan in Osaka in\r\n  2025.\nReally enjoyed the Great\r\n  Feast - it felt just like dining in the Great Hall at Hogwarts!\nYi Yu is an associate professor with\r\n  Graduate School of Advanced Science and Engineering\nand Education and\r\n  Research Center for Artificial Intelligence and Data Innovation\n, Hiroshima University. She was an\r\n  assistant professor with NII and a senior research fellow with School of\r\n  Computing, National University of Singapore.\nHer research interests focus on causal\r\n  inference and self-adaptation for understanding multimedia content and\r\n  advancing artificial intelligence, with a focus on multimodal representation\r\n  learning, generative modeling, and information fusion across visual,\r\n  language, audio, speech, music, biomedical, and educational data.\nShe has been working\r\n  with many researchers (\nsee\nstudents\n,\nPhoto2\n＠\n20\n23\r\n  and\nphoto1\n＠\n2019\n), and has also been active in\nteaching&talks\n,\nas well as professional\nactivities\n.\nShe and her team received best poster award from IEEE ISM 2018 and\nbest paper runner up in APWeb-WAIM 2017, were\nrecognized as finalist of the Worlds FIRST 10K best\r\n  paper award in ICME17, won the 2\nnd\nprize in Yahoo Flickr grand\r\n  challenge\n2015\n, were in the top winners (out of 29\r\n  teams) awarded by ACM SIGSPATIAL GIS Cup 2013, and received a best paper\r\n  award from IEEE ISM 2012 (and\nothers\n).\nShe is an Associate Editor for\nIEEE\r\n  Transactions on Multimedia\nand the\nJournal\r\n  of Data Science and Engineering\n, and serve as the General Chair of the\r\n  2025 International Conference of Pioneering Computer Scientists, Engineers\r\n  and Educators (\nICPCSEE\n), which\r\n  was held at Hiroshima University from September 19 to 21, 2025.\nSource Codes and Data\n1.JustLMD\nfor dance generation from music and lyrics\nhttps://github.com/yy1lab/LMD\n2.Neural melody generation\r\nfrom lyrics\nhttps://github.com/yy1lab/Lyrics-Conditioned-Neural-Melody-Generation\n3.Dialogue-attended\r\naudiovisual dataset\nhttps://github.com/lvilaca16/dialogue-av\nSurveys\n1.Recent Advances in\r\nMusic Generation: Methods, Evaluation, and Challenges\nhttps://hal.science/hal-05452282v1\n2.Recent Advances and\r\nChallenges in Deep Audio-Visual Correlation Learning\nhttps://doi.org/10.1145/3696445\nImportant:\nRegarding International\r\nStudent Admission\nSelected Publications by years (\nFull\n)\n1.\nLuís Vilaça, Yi Yu*, and Paula\r\nViana, \nA survey of recent advances and challenges in deep\r\naudio-visual correlation learning, ACM Computing Surveys, 2025, Volume 57,\r\nIssue 12 Article No.: 299, Pages 1 - 46.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1145/3696445\n2.\nShuai Yu, Xiaoliang He, Kangjie\r\nDong, Yi Yu* Every Little Bit Helps: Exploring Better Utilization of Unlabeled\r\nData for\nSemi-supervised\r\nSinging Melody Extraction Using Multi-bands Diffusion Model, accepted by AAAI,\r\n2026.\n3.\nShuai Yu, Xiaoliang He, Kengjie\r\nDong, and Yi Yu*, DUDA: A Two-stage Decoupling Unsupervised Domain Adaptation\r\nFramework for Semi-supervised Singing Melody Extraction from Polyphonic Music,\r\nACM Multimedia (MM), 2025.\n4.\nAnam Fatima, Yi Yu*, Janak\r\nKapuriya, Julien Lalanne and Jainendra Shukla, Semantic frame\r\naggregation-based Transformer: for live video comment generation, IEEE\r\nTransactions on Multimedia, vol. 27, pp. 7821-7833, 2025. DOI:\r\n10.1109/TMM.2025.3604921,\nhttps://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11146668\n, 2025.\n5.\nLuís Vilaça, Paula Viana, and\r\nYi Yu Dialogue-AV: a dialogue-attended audiovisual dataset, 22nd\r\nInternational Conference on Content-Based Multimedia Indexing.\n6.\nYi Yu, Jiwei Zhang, Suhua Tang,\r\nand Wei Li, Dialogue-to-video retrieval via multi-grained attention network,\r\nIEEE access 2025, Vol. 13, pp. 82302-82311.\n7.\nJiwei Zhang, Yi Yu*, Suhua\r\nTang, and Wei Li, Adversarial contrastive autoencoder with shared attention\r\nfor audio-visual correlation learning, IEEE access 2025, Vol. 13, pp.\r\n39753-39764.\n8.\nJiwei Zhang, Yi Yu*, Suhua\r\nTang, Guojun Qi, Haiyuan Wu, and Hirotaka Hachiya Enhancing semantic\r\naudio-visual representation learning with supervised multi-scale\r\nattention\", Pattern Analysis and Applications 2025, 28:40\nhttps://doi.org/10.1007/s10044-025-01414-z\n.\n9.\nGanghui Ru, Jieying Wang,\r\nJiahao Zhao, Yulun Wu, Yi Yu, Nannan Jiang, Wei Wang, and Wei Li, BeatFM:\r\nImproving Beat Tracking with Pre-trained Music Foundation Model, accepted by\r\nIEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME), 2025.\n10.\nYunqi Jiang, Jianwei Zhang,\r\nChaoyang Lin, Yi Yu, and Zhenguo Yang, Scene-guided attention network for\r\nspatial understanding in 3D scenes, accepted by IEEE International Conference\r\non Multimedia Retrieval, 2025.\n11.\nGanghui Ru, Jieying Wang,\r\nJiahao Zhao, Yulun Wu, Yi Yu, Nannan Jiang, Wei Wang, and Wei Li, A\r\nHarmonic-Aware Fine-Tuning Approach for Beat Tracking, accepted by IEEE\r\nInternational Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME), 2025.\n12.\nMaolin Li, Zhuopan Yang, Haoran\r\nXie, Lap-Kei Lee Wang, Yi Yu, and Zhenguo Yang, Chain-of-Thought Prompting\r\nwith Causal Intervention for Multimodal Aspect-based Sentiment Analysis,\r\naccepted by the 30th International Conference on Database Systems for Advanced\r\nApplications (DASFAA), 2025.\n13.\nXiaoliang He, Kangjie Dong,\r\nJingkai Cao, Shuai Yu, Wei Li, and Yi Yu, A Mamba-based network for\r\nsemi-supervised singing melody extraction using confidence binary\r\nregularization, accepted by IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech\r\nand Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2025. [CORE B]\n14.\nJiaming Yang, Jiuxiang You,\r\nZiyue Qiu, Guobo Xie, Yi Yu, and Zhenguo Yang, Visual entity-centric prompting\r\nfor knowledge retrieval in knowledge-based VQA, accepted by IEEE International\r\nConference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2025. [CORE B]\n15.\nChenyang Lyu, Wenxi Li, Tianbo\r\nJi, Liting Zhou, Pintu Lohar, Yi Yu, and Longyue Wang, Enhancing video-text\r\nmatching via sparse stratified sampling, accepted by IEEE International\r\nConference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2025. [CORE B]\n16.\nShijie Zhang, Yulun Wu, Ganghui\r\nRu, Yi Yu, and Wei Li, KCE-UNET: A novel music denoising method with kanconv\r\nECA unet, accepted by IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and\r\nSignal Processing (ICASSP), 2025. [CORE B]\n17.\nZhe Zhang, Yi Yu*, and Atsuhiro\r\nTakasu, Controllable syllable-level lyrics generation from melody with prior\r\nattention, accepted by IEEE Transactions on Multimedia, https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10637751,\r\nDOI: 10.1109/TMM.2024.3443664, 2024.\n18.\nZehang Lin, Jiayuan Xie, Zhenguo Yang, Yi Yu,\r\nand Qing Li, Generalized news event discovery via dynamic augmentation and\r\nentropy optimization, accepted by ACM Multimedia (MM), 2024.\n19.\nShuai Yu, Xiaoliang He, Ke\r\nChen, Yi Yu*, HKDSME: Heterogeneous knowledge distillation for semi-supervised\r\nsinging melody extraction using harmonic supervision, accepted by ACM\r\nMultimedia (MM), 2024.\n20.\nHaonan Jin, Guangwei Gao,\r\nJuncheng Li, Zhenhua Guo, and Yi Yu, Efficient Dual-branch Information\r\nInteraction Network for Lightweight Image Super-Resolution, accepted by IEEE\r\nTransactions on Instrumentation and Measurement.\n21.\nDonghuo Zeng, Yanan Wang,\r\nKazushi Ikeda, and Yi Yu, Anchor-aware deep metric learning for audio-visual\r\nretrieval, ACM International Conference on Multimedia Retrieval (ICMR), 2024,\r\npp.211-219. [CORE B]\n22.\nZhe Zhang, Karol Lasocki, Yi\r\nYu*, Atsuhiro Takasu, Syllable-level lyrics generation from melody exploiting\r\ncharacter-level language model, accepted by European Chapter of the\r\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics (EACL) 2024.\n23.\nWenjie Yin, Yi Yu*, Hang Yin,\r\nDannica Kragic, and Mårten Björkman, Scalable motion style transfer with\r\nconstrained diffusion generation, accepted by The Association for the\r\nAdvancement of Artificial Intelligence Conference on Artificial Intelligence\r\n(AAAI) 2024. [CORE A*]\n24.\nYang, Zhuopan, Zhenguo Yang,\r\nXiaoping Li, Yi Yu, Qing Li, and Wenyin Liu A Progressive Placeholder Learning\r\nNetwork for Multimodal Zero-Shot Learning, accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on\r\nMultimedia\n, 2024. IF: 6.513\n25.\nYiming Tang, Yi Yu, and Yan Qiu Chen\nP\nrototype-guided prior enhancement\r\nand rectification in few-shot semantic segmentation\n,\naccepted\r\nby\nIEEE Conference on Multimedia Expo (ICME)\n2024\n.\n26.\nYulun Wu, Weixing Wei, Dichucheng Li, Mengbo Li, Yongwei Gao,\nYi Yu\n, and Wei Li\nHarmonic\nf\nrequency-\ns\neparable Transformer for\ni\nnstrument-agnostic\nm\nusic\nt\nranscription,\naccepted by IEEE Conference on\r\nMultimedia Expo (ICME) 2024.\n27.\nChenyang Lyu, Wenxi Li, Tianbo\r\nJi, Yi Yu, Longyue Wang, Semantic enrichment for video question answering with\r\ngated graph neural networks, accepted by IEEE International Conference on\r\nAcoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2024. [CORE B]\n28.\nShuai Yu, Jun Liu, Yi Yu, Wei\r\nLi, A scalable sparse transformer model for singing melody extraction,\r\naccepted by IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal\r\nProcessing (ICASSP), 2024. [CORE B]\n29.\nChenyang Lyu, Wenxi Li, Tianbo\r\nJi, Longyue Wang, Liting Zhou, Cathal Gurrin, Linyi Yang, Yi Yu, Yvette Graham,\r\nand Jennifer Foster, Graph-based video-language learning with multi-grained\r\naudio-visual alignment, ACM Multimedia (MM), 2023. [CORE A*]\n30.\nYulun Wu, Jiahao Zhao, Yi Yu, and\r\nWei Li MFAE: Masked frame-level features autoencoder with hybrid-supervision\r\nfor low-resource music Transcription, IEEE International Conference on\r\nMultimedia and Expo (ICME), 2023, pp.1109-1114.\n31.\nXinlu Liu, Jiale Qian, Qiqi He,\r\nYi Yu, and Wei Li, LC-Beating: An online system for beat and downbeat tracking\r\nusing latency-controlled mechanism, IEEE International Conference on\r\nMultimedia and Expo (ICME), 2023, pp. 1098-1103.\n32.\nDichuCheng Li, Mingjin Che,\r\nWenwu Meng, Yulun Wu, Yi Yu, Fan Xi, and Wei Li, Frame-level multi-label\r\nplaying technique detection using multi-scale network and self-attention\r\nmechanism, IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal\r\nProcessing (ICASSP), 2023, pp.1-5. [CORE B]\n33.\nWei Duan, Yi Yu*, and Keizo\r\nOyama, Semantic dependency network for lyrics generation from melody,\r\naccepted by Neural Computing and Applications, 2023.\n34.\nJiwei Zhang, Yi Yu*, Suhua\r\nTang, Wei Li, and Jianming Wu, Multi-scale network with shared cross attention\r\nfor audio-visual correlation learning, https://rdcu.be/dhgSH, Journal of\r\nNeural Computing and Applications, 2023.\n35.\nZhe Zhang, Yi Yu*, and\r\nAstsuhiro Takasu, Controllable lyrics-to-melody generation,\r\nhttps://rdcu.be/dgozv, Journal of Neural Computing and Applications, 2023.\n36.\nJiale Qian, Xinlu Liu, Yi Yu,\r\nand Wei Li, Stripe-Transformer: deep stripe feature learning for music source\r\nseparation, EURASIP Journal on Audio, Speech, and Music Processing, 2023:2,\r\nhttps://doi.org/10.1186/s13636-022-00268-1. IF: 2.114\n37.\nWei Duan,\nYi Yu*, Xulong\r\nZhang, Suhua Tang, Wei Li, and Keizo Oyama, Melody Generation from Lyrics with\r\nLocal Interpretability accepted by ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing,\r\nCommunications, and Applications (TOMCCAP), 2022. IF: 3.275, JCR Q1\n38.\nJiwei Zhang, Yi Yu*, Suhua\r\nTang, Jianming Wu, and Wei Li, Variational Autoencoder with CCA for\r\nAudio-Visual Cross-Modal Retrieval, accepted by\nACM Transactions on\r\nMultimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications (TOMCCAP)\n, 2022. IF:\r\n3.275\n39.\nYi Yu, Zhe Zhang, Wei Duan,\r\nAbhishek Srivastava, Rajiv Shah, and Yi Ren, Conditional Hybrid GAN for Melody\r\nGeneration from Lyrics,\nJournal of Neural Computing and Applications\n,\nhttps://rdcu.be/cXazS\n, doi:\r\n10.1007/s00521-022-07863-5, 2022. IF: 5.102\n40.\nDonghuo Zeng, Jianming Wu, Gen\r\nHattori, Rong Xu, and Yi Yu* Learning Explicit and Implicit Dual Common\r\nSubspaces for Audio-Visual Cross-Modal Retrieval, accepted by\nACM\r\nTransactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications\r\n(TOMCCAP)\n,\nhttps://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3564608\n,\r\n2022.\nIF: 3.275\n41.\nGuangwei Gao,\nYi Yu*, Huimin\r\nLu, Jian Yang, and Dong Yue, Context-Patch Representation Learning with\r\nAdaptive Neighbor Embedding for Robust Face Image Super-resolution,\nIEEE\r\nTransactions on Multimedia\n, 10.1109/TMM.2022.3192769, 2022. IF: 6.513\n42.\nShuai Yu, Yi Yu*, and Wei Li,\r\nA Neural Harmonic-Aware Network with Gated Attentive Fusion for Singing Melody\r\nExtraction, accepted by\nJournal of Neurocomputing\n, 2022. IF: 4.072\n43.\nYiming Tang and Yi Yu,\r\nQuery-Guided Prototype Learning with Decoder Alignment and Dynamic Fusion in\r\nFew-Shot Segmentation, accepted by\nACM Transactions on Multimedia\r\nComputing, Communications, and Applications (TOMCCAP)\n,\nhttps://doi.org/10.1145/3555314\n,\r\n2022. IF: 3.275\n44.\nGuangwei Gao, Guoan Xu,\r\nJuncheng Li, Yi Yu*, Huimin Lu and Jian Yang FBSNet: A Fast Bilateral\r\nSymmetrical Network for Real-Time Semantic Segmentation,\nIEEE Transactions\r\non Multimedia\n, 10.1109/TMM.2022.3157995, 2022. IF: 6.513\n45.\nDawei Zhou, Nannan Wang,\r\nChunlei Peng, Yi Yu, Xi Yang, and Xinbo Gao Towards Multi-domain Face\r\nSynthesis via Domain-Invariant Representations and Multi-level Feature Parts,\r\naccepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia\n, 2021. [CORE A*], IF: 5.452\n46.\nGuangwei Gao, Guoan Xu, Yi Yu,\r\nJin Xie, Jian Yang, and Dong Yue. MSCFNet: A Lightweight Network with\r\nMulti-Scale Context Fusion for Real-Time Semantic Segmentation, accepted by\nIEEE\r\nTransactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n,\r\n2021.\nIF: 6.49\n47.\nShuai Yu, Yi Yu, Xi Chen, and\r\nWei Li, HANME: Hierarchical attention network for singing melody extraction,\nIEEE\r\nSignal Processing Letters\n, vol. 28, pp.1006-1010, 2021. IF:4.18\n48.\nYi Yu, Abhishek Srivastava, and\r\nSimon Canales, Conditional LSTM-GAN for Melody Generation from Lyrics,\r\nhttps://dl.acm.org/doi/fullHtml/10.1145/3424116,\nACM Transaction on\r\nMultimedia Computing Communication and Applications (TOMCCAP)\n, 2020. IF:\r\n3.275\n49.\nGuangwei Gao, Yi Yu, Jian Yang,\r\nGuo-Jun Qi, and Meng Yang, Hierarchical Deep CNN Feature Set-Based\r\nRepresentation Learning for Robust Cross-Resolution Face Recognition,\r\n10.1109/TCSVT.2020.3042178,\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for\r\nVideo Technology (TCSVT)\n, 2020. IF: 4.133\n50.\nGuangwei Gao, Dong Zhu, Huimin\r\nLu, Yi Yu, and Dong Yue, Robust Facial Image Super-Resolution by Kernel\r\nLocality-Constrained Coupled-Layer Regression, accepted by ACM Transactions on\r\nInternet Technology (TOIT), 2020. IF: 3.750\n51.\nGuangwei Gao, Yi Yu, Jin Xie,\r\nJian Yang, Meng Yang, and Jian Zhang, Constructing Multilayer\r\nLocality-Constrained Matrix Regression Framework for Noise Robust Face Super-Resolution,\r\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016...[truncated]"
