    "homepage_text": "Bo Zheng – Associate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nAbout Bo\nBo is an Associate Professor in the\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nat\nTsinghua University\n. He specializes in the atmospheric carbon cycle, atmospheric chemistry modeling, and air pollution and climate change mitigation policies. Bo has published over 100 peer-reviewed articles (\nlist\n), his h index is 78, and has over 35000 times citations (\nGoogle Scholar\n).\nBo is a\nHighly Cited Researcher\nin the field of Cross-Field in 2020, and in the field of Geosciences between 2021 and 2025.\nBo is a topical editor of the journals\nEarth System Science Data\nand\nGeoscientific Model Development\n, an associated editor of the journal\nJournal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres\n, an Editorial Board member of\nEnvironmental Science & Ecotechnology\n, and one of the Editorial Group Members of Earth Sciences in\nNational Science Review\n.\nBo studied at the School of Environment in Tsinghua University between 2007 and 2016. He gained a Bachelor’s degree in 2011 and obtained a PhD in 2016, and since then worked as a postdoctoral researcher with\nPhilippe Ciais\nand\nFrederic Chevallier\nin France from 2016 to 2020.\n\n---\n\nContact – Bo Zheng\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nContact\nAddress\nOffice 403, Building F\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nUniversity Town of Shenzhen, Shenzhen 518055, China\nEmail\nbozheng@sz.tsinghua.edu.cn\nWebsite\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch Gate\nORCID\nResearcherID\n\n---\n\nContact – Bo Zheng\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nContact\nAddress\nOffice 403, Building F\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nUniversity Town of Shenzhen, Shenzhen 518055, China\nEmail\nbozheng@sz.tsinghua.edu.cn\nWebsite\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch Gate\nORCID\nResearcherID\n\n---\n\nBo Zheng – Associate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nAbout Bo\nBo is an Associate Professor in the\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nat\nTsinghua University\n. He specializes in the atmospheric carbon cycle, atmospheric chemistry modeling, and air pollution and climate change mitigation policies. Bo has published over 100 peer-reviewed articles (\nlist\n), his h index is 78, and has over 35000 times citations (\nGoogle Scholar\n).\nBo is a\nHighly Cited Researcher\nin the field of Cross-Field in 2020, and in the field of Geosciences between 2021 and 2025.\nBo is a topical editor of the journals\nEarth System Science Data\nand\nGeoscientific Model Development\n, an associated editor of the journal\nJournal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres\n, an Editorial Board member of\nEnvironmental Science & Ecotechnology\n, and one of the Editorial Group Members of Earth Sciences in\nNational Science Review\n.\nBo studied at the School of Environment in Tsinghua University between 2007 and 2016. He gained a Bachelor’s degree in 2011 and obtained a PhD in 2016, and since then worked as a postdoctoral researcher with\nPhilippe Ciais\nand\nFrederic Chevallier\nin France from 2016 to 2020.\n\n---\n\nBo Zheng – Associate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nAbout Bo\nBo is an Associate Professor in the\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nat\nTsinghua University\n. He specializes in the atmospheric carbon cycle, atmospheric chemistry modeling, and air pollution and climate change mitigation policies. Bo has published over 100 peer-reviewed articles (\nlist\n), his h index is 78, and has over 35000 times citations (\nGoogle Scholar\n).\nBo is a\nHighly Cited Researcher\nin the field of Cross-Field in 2020, and in the field of Geosciences between 2021 and 2025.\nBo is a topical editor of the journals\nEarth System Science Data\nand\nGeoscientific Model Development\n, an associated editor of the journal\nJournal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres\n, an Editorial Board member of\nEnvironmental Science & Ecotechnology\n, and one of the Editorial Group Members of Earth Sciences in\nNational Science Review\n.\nBo studied at the School of Environment in Tsinghua University between 2007 and 2016. He gained a Bachelor’s degree in 2011 and obtained a PhD in 2016, and since then worked as a postdoctoral researcher with\nPhilippe Ciais\nand\nFrederic Chevallier\nin France from 2016 to 2020.\n\n---\n\nBo Zheng – Associate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nSkip to content\nBo Zheng\nAssociate Professor, Tsinghua University, China\nMenu and widgets\nAbout Bo\nBo is an Associate Professor in the\nTsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School\nat\nTsinghua University\n. He specializes in the atmospheric carbon cycle, atmospheric chemistry modeling, and air pollution and climate change mitigation policies. Bo has published over 100 peer-reviewed articles (\nlist\n), his h index is 78, and has over 35000 times citations (\nGoogle Scholar\n).\nBo is a\nHighly Cited Researcher\nin the field of Cross-Field in 2020, and in the field of Geosciences between 2021 and 2025.\nBo is a topical editor of the journals\nEarth System Science Data\nand\nGeoscientific Model Development\n, an associated editor of the journal\nJournal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres\n, an Editorial Board member of\nEnvironmental Science & Ecotechnology\n, and one of the Editorial Group Members of Earth Sciences in\nNational Science Review\n.\nBo studied at the School of Environment in Tsinghua University between 2007 and 2016. He gained a Bachelor’s degree in 2011 and obtained a PhD in 2016, and since then worked as a postdoctoral researcher with\nPhilippe Ciais\nand\nFrederic Chevallier\nin France from 2016 to 2020."
