    "homepage_text": "Minghua Liu\nMinghua Liu\nFounding Member @ Hillbot\nPh.D. @ University of California, San Diego\nminghua@ucsd.edu / m@hillbot.ai\nBio\nI am a founding member at Hillbot Inc. My research primarily focuses on 3D vision and embodied AI. I earned my Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from UC San Diego in 2024, where I was fortunate to be advised by Prof.\nHao Su\n.\nI have gained valuable experience at NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Waymo, Adobe, Sensetime, and USC. Prior to my Ph.D., I completed my undergraduate studies in Computer Science at Tsinghua University in 2019 under the mentorship of Prof.\nShi-Min Hu\n.\nCollaboration/Internship: Feel free to email me if you share similar interests in 3D vision and embodied AI!\nPublications\nFreeArt3D: Training-Free Articulated Object Generation using 3D Diffusion\nChuhao Chen, Isabella Liu, Xinyue Wei, Hao Su,\nMinghua Liu\nSIGGRAPH ASIA 2025\nLARM: A Large Articulated Object Reconstruction Model\nSylvia Yuan, Ruoxi Shi, Xinyue Wei, Xiaoshuai Zhang, Hao Su,\nMinghua Liu\nSIGGRAPH ASIA 2025\nPartUV: Part-Based UV Unwrapping of 3D Meshes\nZhaoning Wang, Xinyue Wei, Ruoxi Shi, Xiaoshuai Zhang, Hao Su,\nMinghua Liu\nSIGGRAPH ASIA 2025\nPaMO: Parallel Mesh Optimization for Intersection-Free Low-Poly Modeling on the GPU\nSeonghun Oh, Xiaodi Yuan, Xinyue Wei, Ruoxi Shi, Fanbo Xiang,\nMinghua Liu\n, Hao Su\nPacific Graphics 2025\nPartField: Learning 3D Feature Fields for Part Segmentation and Beyond\nMinghua Liu*\n, Mikaela Angelina Uy*, Donglai Xiang, Hao Su, Sanja Fidler, Nicholas Sharp, Jun Gao\nICCV 2025\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nMeshFormer: High-Quality Mesh Generation with 3D-Guided Reconstruction Model\nMinghua Liu*\n, Chong Zeng*, Xinyue Wei, Ruoxi Shi, Linghao Chen, Chao Xu, Mengqi Zhang, Zhaoning Wang, Xiaoshuai Zhang, Isabella Liu, Hongzhi Wu, Hao Su\nNeurIPS 2024\n(Oral)\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nSpaRP: Fast 3D Object Reconstruction and Pose Estimation from Sparse Views\nChao Xu, Ang Li, Linghao Chen, Yulin Liu, Ruoxi Shi,\nMinghua Liu*\n, Hao Su*\nECCV 2024\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nOne-2-3-45++: Fast Single Image to 3D Objects with Consistent Multi-View Generation and 3D Diffusion\nMinghua Liu*\n, Ruoxi Shi*, Linghao Chen*, Zhuoyang Zhang*, Chao Xu*, Xinyue Wei, Hansheng Chen, Chong Zeng, Jiayuan Gu, Hao Su\nCVPR 2024\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nSupp\nLearning Reusable Dense Rewards for Multi-Stage Tasks\nTongzhou Mu,\nMinghua Liu\n, Hao Su\nICLR 2024\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nPoster\nSlides\nVideo\nZero123++: A Single Image to Consistent Multi-view Diffusion Base Model\nRuoxi Shi, Hansheng Chen, Zhuoyang Zhang,\nMinghua Liu\n, Chao Xu, Xinyue Wei, Linghao Chen, Chong Zeng, Hao Su\nTechnical Report\nPaper\nDemo\nCode\nOne-2-3-45: Any Single Image to 3D Mesh in 45 Seconds without Per-Shape Optimization\nMinghua Liu*\n, Chao Xu*, Haian Jin*, Linghao Chen*, Mukund Varma T, Zexiang Xu, Hao Su\nNeurIPS 2023\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nCode\nOpenShape: Scaling Up 3D Shape Representation Towards Open-World Understanding\nMinghua Liu*\n, Ruoxi Shi*, Kaiming Kuang*, Yinhao Zhu, Xuanlin Li, Shizhong Han, Hong Cai, Fatih Porikli, Hao Su\nNeurIPS 2023\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nCode\nDistilling Large Vision-Language Model with Out-of-Distribution Generalizability\nXuanlin Li*, Yunhao Fang*,\nMinghua Liu\n, Zhan Ling, Zhuowen Tu, Hao Su\nICCV 2023\nPaper\nCode\nPoster\nPartSLIP: Low-Shot Part Segmentation for 3D Point Clouds via Pretrained Image-Language Models\nMinghua Liu\n, Yinhao Zhu, Hong Cai, Shizhong Han, Zhan Ling, Fatih Porikli, Hao Su\nCVPR 2023\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nSlides\nVideo\nFrame Mining: a Free Lunch for Learning Robotic Manipulation from 3D Point Clouds\nMinghua Liu*\n, Xuanlin Li*, Zhan Ling*, Yangyan Li, Hao Su\nCoRL 2022\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nSlides\nVideo\nLESS: Label-Efficient Semantic Segmentation for LiDAR Point Clouds\nMinghua Liu\n, Yin Zhou, Charles R. Qi, Boqing Gong, Hao Su, Dragomir Anguelov\nECCV 2022\n(Oral)\nPaper\nApproximate Convex Decomposition for 3D Meshes with Collision-Aware Concavity and Tree Search\nXinyue Wei*,\nMinghua Liu*\n, Zhan Lin, Hao Su\nSIGGRAPH 2022 (Journal Track)\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nVideo\nClose the Visual Domain Gap by Physics-Grounded Active Stereovision Depth Sensor Simulation\nXiaoshuai Zhang*, Rui Chen*, Fanbo Xiang**, Yuzhe Qin**, Jiayuan Gu**, Zhan Ling**,\nMinghua Liu**\n, Peiyu Zeng**, Songfang Han***, Zhiao Huang***, Tongzhou Mu***, Jing Xu, Hao Su\nTR-O 2023\nPaper\nDeepMetaHandles: Learning Deformation Meta-Handles of 3D Meshes with Biharmonic Coordinates\nMinghua Liu\n, Minhyuk Sung, Radomir Mech, Hao Su\nCVPR 2021\n(Oral)\nPaper\nProject\nDemo\nCode\nSupp\nMeshing Point Clouds with Predicted Intrinsic-Extrinsic Ratio Guidance\nMinghua Liu\n, Minhyuk Sung, Radomir Mech, Hao Su\nECCV 2020\nPaper\nCode\nSAPIEN: A SimulAted Part-based Interactive ENvironment\nFanbo Xiang, Yuzhe Qin, Kaichun Mo, Yikuan Xia, Hao Zhu, Fangchen Liu,\nMinghua Liu\n, Hanxiao Jiang, Yifu Yuan, He Wang, Li Yi, Angel Chang, Leonidas Guibas, Hao Su\nCVPR 2020\n(Oral)\nPaper\nProject\nCode\nMorphing and Sampling Network for Dense Point Cloud Completion\nMinghua Liu\n, Lu Sheng, Sheng Yang, Jing Shao, Shi-Min Hu\nAAAI 2020\nPaper\nCode\nData\nMulti-task Batch Reinforcement Learning with Metric Learning\nJiachen Li*, Quan Vuong*, Shuang Liu,\nMinghua Liu\n, Kamil Ciosek, Henrik Iskov Christensen, Hao Su\nNeurIPS 2020\nPaper\nCode\nTask and Path Planning for Multi-Agent Pickup and Delivery\nMinghua Liu\n, Hang Ma, Jiaoyang Li, Sven Koenig\nAAMAS 2019\nPaper\nSlides\nHeteroFusion: Dense Scene Reconstruction Integrating Multi-sensors\nSheng Yang, Beichen Li,\nMinghua Liu\n, Yu-Kun Lai, Leif Kobbelt, Shi-Min Hu\nTVCG\nPaper\nSaliency-Aware Real-Time Volumetric Fusion for Object Reconstruction\nSheng Yang, Kang Chen,\nMinghua Liu\n, Hongbo Fu and Shi-Min Hu\nPacific Graphics 2017\nPaper\nServices\nArea Chair\n: CVPR'25\nConference Reviewer\n: CVPR'21'22'23'24, ICCV'21'23'25, ECCV'22'24, SIGGRAPH'23'24'25, SIGGRAPH Asia'23'24'25, NeurIPS'21'22'23'24'25, ICLR'22'23'24, ICML'22'23'24, AAAI'23'24\nJournal Reviewer\n: T-RO, RA-L, TPAMI, TVCG, IJCV, CVMJ\nAwards\nQualcomm Innovation Fellowship, 2020\nPowell Fellowship, 2019\nZhong-Shimo Scholarship, 2018\nChina National Scholarship, 2017\nSilver Medal, National Olympiad in Informatics, 2014\nMisc.\nI was born and raised in Hunan, China, before attending college, and I am a big fan of spicy food!\nI enjoy various outdoor activities like\nhiking\n,\ncamping\n,\nfishing\n, skiing, and more in my free time.\nI'm a dog person and have an adorable Labrador named\nJojo\n, who always keeps me company on my adventures.\nAcknowledgement\nThis website design is based on the template from\nMartin Saveski\n.\nMinghua Liu\nminghua@ucsd.edu / m@hillbot.ai"
