    "github": "https://github.com/ZFancy",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jianing-zhu-8712b518b",
    "homepage_text": "Jianing Zhu @ UT Austin ML\nJianing Zhu\nPostdoctoral Fellow @ UT Austin\nVITA Group\nChandra Department of ECE\nCockrell School of Engineering\n,\nalso affiliated with\nGood Systems Challenge\n,\nEthical AI at UT Austin,\nUniversity of Texas at Austin\n,\nAustin, Texas, USA\n[Google Scholar]\n[Github]\n[Twitter]\n[LinkedIn]\nE-mail: jianing.zhu@austin.utexas.edu or zhujianing9810@gmail.com\nAddress: 3rd floor at EER, UT Austin, 2501 Speedway, Austin, TX 78712, USA\nWe are actively seeking for researchers to share their research work about trustworthy machine learning on TrustML YSS, please see\nthis page\nfor more information and contact us if you are interested in. See\n[video channel]\nfor previous seminars.\nOur TMLR Group also initiated the\nTMLR Young Scientist Seminar\nfor sharing diverse and cutting-edge research.\nRecent News\n[2026.01] Four papers (unlearning, self-envolved training, preference optimization) are accepted by\nICLR 2026\n!\n[2025.12] I will serve as Emergency Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\n[2025.12] One paper is accepted by\nTPAMI\n.\n[2025.12] I will serve as Area Chair for ICML 2026.\n[2025.11] Honored to receive 2025 TrustAI Rising Star Award. Grateful for the recognition of my work on trustworthy AI at\nLock-LLM at NeurIPS 2025\n. Excited to meet and exchange ideas with many brilliant researchers at the venue, see you in San Diego!\n[2025.10] Honored to receive Top Reviewer Award from NeurIPS 2025, and our\nCo-rewarding\nwill be presented in\nMATH-AI Workshop @ NeurIPS 2025\n, see you in Sandiego!\n[2025.10] We are excited to update our new version of\nCo-rewarding\nfor self-envolved reasoning, have a try on our released\ncode and models\n.\n[2025.09] I have arrived at Austin, Texas, USA and am excited about starting my postdoc journey at\nVITA group\nof UT Austin!\n[2025.09] We are excited to deliver our tutorial in AAAI 2026, titled \"Handling Out-of-Distribution Data in the Open World: Principles and Practice for Reliable AI\", stay tuned for more information and see you in Singapore!\n[2025.07] We are excited to release our new research work exploring self-supervised RL for LLM reasoning:\nCo-Reward\n.\n[2025.05] Thrilled to have successfully defended my PhD thesis! Officially a PhD!\n[2025.01] Happy to join in\nCMU MLD\nas a visiting student researcher!\n[2024.09] Our work about OOD Detection and Robust LLM Reasoning are accepted by\nNeurIPS 2024\n. See you in Vancouver!\n[2024.07] Honored to be awarded as ICML 2024\nBest Reviewer\n.\n[2024.05] Returned to Hong Kong after a wonderful internship at\nRIKEN AIP\n.\n[2024.04] Honored to be awarded with Yakun Scholarship Scheme for Mainland Postgraduate Students.\n[2024.03] Assist with the upcoming\nHKBU-COMP & RIKEN-AIP Joint Workshop on AI and ML 2024\n.\n[2023.11] Honored to be awarded as NeurIPS 2023\nTop Reviewer\n.\n[2023.11] Will start my internship at\nRIKEN AIP\nat early December.\n[2023.09] One paper is accepted by\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\n[2023.09] Start my thrid-year research & learning journey.\n[2023.07] Attend\nICML 2023\nand present research work @ Hawaii.\n[2023.06] Honored to receive Research Excellence Award @ HKBU COMP.\nAbout Me\nI am a Postdoctoral Fellow at\nVITA group\nof UT Austin, working with\nProf. Atlas Wang\n. I received my PhD at\nTrustworthy Machine Learning and Reasoning (TMLR) Group\nin the\nDepartment of Computer Science\n,\nHong Kong Baptist University\n,\n    advised by Dr.\nBo Han\n. I was a visiting student researcher at\nCMU MLD\n, fortunately working with\nProf. Pradeep Ravikumar\n, and I was a research intern at\nRIKEN AIP\n, fortunately working with\nDr. Gang Niu\nand\nProf. Masashi Sugiyama\n. Before that, I received my B.Eng. degree of Computer Science and Technology\n(Top-notched Student Program)\nfrom\nSichuan University\nin 2021.\nMy research centers on trustworthy machine learning for building responsible AI, with a focus on robustness, reliability, and transparency under imperfect and dynamic deployment conditions. Guided by these foundations, I recently study machine unlearning and memory management in agentic systems to ensure safety and alignment. My long-term goal is to build adaptive AI systems that remain dependable as they evolve in complex environments.\nRemarkable Projects\n(For more details can click the images)\nResearch Experience\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n, 2025.09 - Present\nVITA Group\n,\nChandra Department of Electrical\nand Computer Engineering\n,\nCockrell School of Engineering\n,\nUniversity of Texas at Austin\nAdvised by\nProf. Atlas Wang\nAustin, Texas, United States\nVisiting PhD Student\n, 2025.01 - 2025.06 \n            Statistical & Symbolic Learning (Neuro-Symbolic AI) Group,\nMachine Learning Department\n,\nSchool of Computer Science\n,\nCarnegie Mellon University\nAdvised by\nProf. Pradeep Ravikumar\nPittsburgh, Pennsylvania, Unite States\nResearch Intern\n, 2023.12 - 2024.05 \n            Imperfect Information Learning Team,\nRIKEN AIP\nAdvised by\nDr. Gang Niu\nand\nProf. Masashi Sugiyama\nRIKEN, Tokyo, Japan\nEducation\nPh.D. student\n, 2021.09 - 2025.07\nTMLR Group\n,\n            Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Science\nHong Kong Baptist University (HKBU), Hong Kong SAR\nB.Eng.\n, 2017.09 - 2021.06\nCollege of Computer Science (Top-notched Student Program)\nSichuan University (SCU), Chengdu, China\nSelected Publication\n(* indicates equal contribution, full list can refer to\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nConference Paper\nZ. Zhang*,\nJ. Zhu*\n, X. Ge*, Z. Zhao*, Z. Zhou, X. Xuan, X. Feng, J. Yao, B. Han.\nCo-rewarding: Stable Self-supervised RL for Eliciting Reasoning in Large Language Models.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2026)\n, Brazil, 2026.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhang2026co,\n        title={Co-Reward: Self-supervised Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Model Reasoning via Contrastive Agreement},\n        author={Zhang*, Zizhuo and Jianing Zhu* and Ge*, Xinmu and Zhao*, Zihua and Zhou, Zhanke and Li, Xuan and Feng, Xiao and Yao, Jiangchao and Han, Bo},\n        booktitle={The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations},\n        year={2026}\n}\nJ. Zhu\n, B. Han, J. Yao, J. Xu, G. Niu, M. Sugiyama.\nDecoupling the Class Label and the Target Concept in Machine Unlearning.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2026)\n, Brazil, 2026.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhu2026decoupling,\n        title={Decoupling the Class Label and the Target Concept in Machine Unlearning}, \n        author={Jianing Zhu and Bo Han and Jiangchao Yao and Jianliang Xu and Gang Niu and Masashi Sugiyama},\n        booktitle={The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations},\n        year={2026}\n}\nJ. Sun*,\nJ. Zhu*\n, J. Yao, G. Niu, M. Sugiyama, B. Han\nBilateral Information-aware Test-time Adaptation for Vision-Language Models.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2026)\n, Brazil, 2026.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{sun2026bilateral,\n        title={Bilateral Information-aware Test-time Adaptation for Vision-Language Models},\n        author={Sun*, Jie and Zhu*, Jianing and Yao, Jiangchao and Niu, Gang and Sugiyama, Masashi and Han, Bo},\n        booktitle={The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations},\n        year={2026}\n}\nZ. Zhang, Q. Wang, S. Ye,\nJ. Zhu\n, J. Yao, B. Han, M. Sugiyama\nTowards Understanding Valuable Preference Data for Large Language Model Alignment.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2026)\n, Brazil, 2026.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhang2026towards,\n        title={Towards Understanding Valuable Preference Data for Large Language Model Alignment},\n        author={Zhang, Zizhuo and Wang, Qizhou and Ye, Sheng and Zhu, Jianing and Yao, Jiangchao and Han, Bo and Sugiyama, Masashi},\n        booktitle={The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations},\n        year={2026}\n}\nQ. Wang, B. Han, Y. Pu,\nJ. Zhu\n, T. Liu, M. Sugiyama.\nTowards Effective Evaluations and Comparisons for LLM Unlearning Methods\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2025)\n, Singapore, 2025.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@misc{wang2024unlearning,\n        title={Unlearning with Control: Assessing Real-world Utility for Large Language Model Unlearning}, \n        author={Qizhou Wang and Bo Han and Puning Yang and Jianing Zhu and Tongliang Liu and Masashi Sugiyama},\n        year={2024},\n        eprint={2406.09179},\n        archivePrefix={arXiv},\n}\nB. Zhang*,\nJ. Zhu*\n, Z. Wang, T. Liu, B. Du, B. Han.\nWhat If the Input is Expanded in OOD Detection?\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)\n, Vancouver, 2024.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhang2024what,\n        title={What If the Input is Expanded in OOD Detection?},\n        author={Zhang, Boxuan and Zhu, Jianing and Wang, Zengmao and Liu, Tongliang and Du, Bo and Han, Bo},\n        booktitle={The Thirty-Eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems},\n        year={2024},\n}\nY. Geng,\nJ. Zhu\n, J. Yao, B. Han.\nSelf-Calibrated Tuning of Vision-Language Models for Out-of-Distribution Detection\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)\n, Vancouver, 2024.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{geng2024self,\n        title={Self-Calibrated Tuning of Vision-Language Models for Out-of-Distribution Detection},\n        author={Geng, Yu and Zhu, Jianing and Yao, Jiangchao and Han, Bo},\n        booktitle={The Thirty-Eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems},\n        year={2024},\n}\nZ. Zhou, R. Tao,\nJ. Zhu\n, Y. Luo, Z. Wang, B. Han.\nBenchmarking the Reasoning Robustness against Noisy Rationales in Chain-of-thought Prompting\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)\n, Vancouver, 2024.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhou2024benchmarking,\n        title={Benchmarking the Reasoning Robustness against Noisy Rationales in Chain-of-thought Prompting},\n        author={Zhou, Zhanke and Tao, Rong and Zhu, Jianing and Luo, Yiwen and Wang, Zengmao and Han, Bo},\n        booktitle={The Thirty-Eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems},\n        year={2024},\n}\nJ. Zhu\n, G. Yu, J. Yao, T. Liu, G. Niu, M. Sugiyama, B. Han.\nDiversified Outlier Exposure for Out-of-Distribution Detection via Informative Extrapolation.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2023)\n, New Orleans, 2023.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{\n        zhu2023diversified,\n        title={Diversified Outlier Exposure for Out-of-Distribution Detection via Informative Extrapolation},\n        author={Jianing Zhu, Geng Yu, Jiangchao Yao, Tongliang Liu, Gang Niu, Masashi Sugiyama, Bo Han},\n        booktitle={Thirty-seventh Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems},\n        year={2023}\n}\nJ. Zhu\n, H. Li, J. Yao, T. Liu, J. Xu, B Han.\nUnleashing Mask: Explore the Intrinsic Out-of-distribution Detection Capability.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2023)\n, Hawaii, 2023.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{zhu2023unleashing,\n        title={Unleashing Mask: Explore the Intrinsic Out-of-distribution Detection Capability}, \n        author={Jianing Zhu and Hengzhuang Li and Jiangchao Yao and Tongliang Liu and Jianliang Xu and Bo Han},\n        booktitle = {International Conference on Machine Learning},\n        year = {2023}\n}\nJ. Zhu\n, J. Yao, T. Liu, Q. Yao, J. Xu, and B. Han.\nCombating Exacerbated Heterogeneity for Robust Models in Federated Learning.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2023)\n, Kigali, 2023.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{\n    zhu2023combating,\n    title={Combating Exacerbated Heterogeneity for Robust Models in Federated Learning},\n    author={Jianing Zhu and Jiangchao Yao and Tongliang Liu and Quanming Yao and Jianliang Xu and Bo Han},\n    booktitle={The Eleventh International Conference on Learning Representations},\n    year={2023},\n    url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=eKllxpLOOm}\n}\nJ. Zhou*,\nJ. Zhu*\n, J. Zhang, T. Liu, G. Niu, B. Han, M. Sugiyama.\nAdversarial Training with Complementary Labels: On the Benefit of Gradually Informative Attacks.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2022)\n, Online, 2022.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n[\nSpotlight\n]\n@inproceedings{\n    zhou2022adversarial,\n    title={Adversarial Training with Complementary Labels: On the Benefit of Gradually Informative Attacks},\n    author={Jianan Zhou and Jianing Zhu and Jingfeng Zhang and Tongliang Liu and Gang Niu and Bo Han and Masashi Sugiyama},\n    booktitle={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems},\n    editor={Alice H. Oh and Alekh Agarwal and Danielle Belgrave and Kyunghyun Cho},\n    year={2022},\n    url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=s7SukMH7ie9}\n}\nJ. Zhu\n, J. Yao, B. Han, J. Zhang, T. Liu, G. Niu, J. Zhou, J. Xu, H. Yang.\nReliable Adversarial Distillation with Unreliable Teachers.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2022)\n, Online, 2022.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{\n    zhu2022reliable,\n    title={Reliable Adversarial Distillation with Unreliable Teachers},\n    author={Jianing Zhu and Jiangchao Yao and Bo Han and Jingfeng Zhang and Tongliang Liu and Gang Niu and Jingren Zhou and Jianliang Xu and Hongxia Yang},\n    booktitle={International Conference on Learning Representations},\n    year={2022},\n    url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=u6TRGdzhfip}\n}\nJ. Zhang,\nJ. Zhu\n, G. Niu, B. Han, M. Sugiyama, and M. Kankanhalli.\nGeometry-aware Instance-reweighted Adversarial Training.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2021)\n, Online, 2021.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n[\nOral\n]\n@inproceedings{\n    zhang2021geometryaware,\n    title={Geometry-aware Instance-reweighted Adversarial Training},\n    author={Jingfeng Zhang and Jianing Zhu and Gang Niu and Bo Han and Masashi Sugiyama and Mohan Kankanhalli},\n    booktitle={International Conference on Learning Representations},\n    year={2021},\n    url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=iAX0l6Cz8ub}\n}\nJournal Paper\nJ. Zhu\n, B. Han, J. Yao, T. Liu, Q. Yao, and J. Xu.\nSlack Federated Adversarial Training.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n, 2025.\n[PDF]\n[Code]\n[BibTeX]\n@inproceedings{\n    zhu2025slack,\n    title={Slack Federated Adversarial Training},\n    author={Jianing Zhu and Bo Han and Jiangchao Yao and Tongliang Liu and Quanming Yao and Jianliang Xu},\n    booktitle={IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n    year={2025},\n}\nWorking Preprint\nG. Zhang,\nJ. Zhu\n, C. Qian, N. Gong, R. Mihalcea, Z. Xu, J. He, J. Ma, Y. Huang, C. Xiao, B. Li, A. Abbasi, D. Lee, H. Ji, D. Zhang\nCopyright Detective: A Forensic System to Evidence LLMs Flickering Copyright Leakage Risks.\nIn\narXiv\n, 2026.\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@article{zhang2026copyright,\n  title={Copyright Detective: A Forensic System to Evidence LLMs Flickering Copyright Leakage Risks},\n  author={Zhang, Guangwei and Zhu, Jianing and Qian, Cheng and Gong, Neil and Mihalcea, Rada and Xu, Zhaozhuo and He, Jingrui and Ma, Jiaqi and Huang, Yun and Xiao, Chaowei and others},\n  journal={arXiv preprin...[truncated]"
