    "github": "https://github.com/Xianjun-Yang",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/xianjun-yang-0062aa1a6",
    "homepage_text": "Xianjun Yang\nXianjun\nYang\nReflection AI\nSan Francisco, CA\nI am a Member of Technical Staff at\nReflection AI\n, working on open intelligence for LLMs. I completed my PhD in Computer Science at University of California, Santa Barbara, where I was co-advised by Professor\nLinda Petzold\n,\nWilliam Yang Wang\n, and\nStephen Wilson\n. Prior to joining Reflection AI, I worked at Meta Superintelligence Lab, where I work across FAIR, GenAI.\nMy recent research focuses on\nAgentic RL\n&\nMid-training\nand previously I worked heavily on\nAI Safety\n,\nLLM Security and Alignment\n,\nMechanistic Interpretability\n. I have published extensively at top-tier venues including ICML(Oral), NeurIPS, ICLR(Oral), and ACL, with around 3k citations.\nPrior to AI, I quited my PhD in Fluid Mechanics when I leart AGI is coming. Then I earned my CS phd within 3 years without any prior cs background. I received my B.S. in Energy and Power Engineering from Tsinghua University.\nnews\nFeb 1, 2026\nExcited to join\nReflection AI\nas a researcher working on open intelligence!\nOct 13, 2023\nAn initial update, keep tuned!\nYou can also contact me by my personal WeChat: Nolan2025\n\n---\n\ncv | Xianjun Yang\ncv\nTBD\nBasics\nName\nXianjun Yang\nLabel\nAI Researcher\nEmail\nxianjun.yang.ai@gmail.com\nUrl\nhttps://xianjun-yang.github.io\nSummary\nAI researcher working on Agentic RL, mid-training, AI safety, and LLM alignment. Member of Technical Staff at Reflection AI. Completed PhD in CS at UC Santa Barbara in 3 years without prior CS background. ~3k citations.\nWork\n2026.02 - Present\nMember of Technical Staff\nReflection AI\nWorking on open intelligence for large language models.\nAgentic RL\nMid-training\n2024.12 - 2025.12\nResearch Scientist\nMeta Superintelligence Lab\nResearch across FAIR, GenAI teams.\nLLM alignment\nMechanistic interpretability\n2024.06 - 2024.10\nResearch Intern\nMeta GenAI\nResearch internship at Meta GenAI, Seattle.\n2024.03 - 2024.06\nResearch Intern\nAmazon\nResearch internship at Amazon, Palo Alto.\n2023.01 - 2023.06\nResearch Intern\nNEC Laboratories America\nResearch internship at NEC Labs America, New Jersey.\n2022.06 - 2022.09\nResearch Intern\nTencent AI Lab\nResearch internship at Tencent AI Lab, Seattle.\nEducation\n2021.10 - 2024.11\nPhD\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nComputer Science\n2020.01 - 2021.09\nPhD (Quit)\nUniversity of California, Santa Barbara\nFluid Mechanics\n2015.09 - 2019.06\nB.S.\nTsinghua University\nEnergy and Power Engineering\nAwards\n2026.01.01\nICLR 2026 Oral\nICLR\nOral presentation for 'Verifying Chain-of-Thought Reasoning via Its Computational Graph'.\n2024.07.01\nICML 2024 Oral\nICML\nOral presentation for 'A Safe Harbor for AI Evaluation and Red Teaming'.\nSkills\nResearch Areas\nAgentic RL\nMid-training\nAI Safety\nLLM Alignment\nMechanistic Interpretability\nLLM Security\nLanguages\nChinese\nNative speaker\nEnglish\nFluent"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Xiujun Li::https://www.utep.edu/science/li/people/dr%20xiujun.html": {
