    "homepage_text": "Dr. XiuJun Li\nSkip to main content\nMinerAlert\nMain Content\nUTEP\nCollege of Science\nDr. Li Research Group\nPeople\nUTEP\nCollege of Science\nDr. Li Research Group\nPeople\nDr. XiuJun (James) Li\nPrincipal Investigator\nDr. XiuJun (James) Li\nProfessor\nDirector, Forensic Science Program\nCouncilor, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\nPast President, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\nChemistry & Biochemistry, & Biomedical Engineering\nEnvironmental Science & Engineering\nDepartment of Chemistry & Biochemistry\nUniversity of Texas at El Paso\n500 W University Ave\nEl Paso, TX, 79968\nWeb:\nhttp://li.utep.edu\nPhone: (915) 747-8967\nOffice: CCSB 2.0112\nLab: CCSB 2.0528\nMedia Profile\nShort Biography\nXiuJun (James) Li, Ph.D., is a full Professor with early tenure in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP), USA. He is also the Director of Forensic Science Program at UTEP. After he obtained his Ph.D. degree in microfluidic lab-on-a-chip bioanalysis from Simon Fraser University (SFU) in Canada in 2008, he pursued his postdoctoral research with Prof. Richard Mathies at University of California Berkeley and Prof. George Whitesides at Harvard University, while holding a Postdoctoral Fellowship from Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council (NSERC) of Canada. Dr. Li’s current research interest is centered on the development of innovative microfluidic lab-on-a-chip and nanotechnology for bioanalysis,  biomedical engineering, forensic science, biomaterial, and environmental applications, including but not limited to low-cost diagnosis, pathogen detection, nano-biosensing, genetic analysis, 3D cell culture, tissue engineering, and single-cell analysis, supported by NIH, NSF, CPRIT, DOT, AAFS, UT System, Philadelphia Foundation, and MCA Foundation multiple funding agencies. His lab has extensive experience in point-of-care detection. He pioneered the novel concept of paper/polymer hybrid microfluidic devices; he, for the first time, developed photothermal biosensors for low-cost quantitative analysis using a common thermometer.\nDr. Li with an Google Scholar H-Index of 53 has coauthored more than 127 journal publications and 26 patents, including three books from Elsevier on microfluidic devices for biomedical applications. He is an Editorial Board member of multiple journals including\nMicrosystems & Nanoengineering\nand\nScientific Reports\nfrom the Nature Publishing Group,\nMicromachines\n, Nano Futures,\nFuture Science OA\n,\nJournal of Analysis and Testing\n, etc, and an Advisory Board member of\nLab on a Chip\nand\nAnalyst\n. He is the recipient of the\n2025 R&I Innovation Award -Established Innovator\n, 2026 National Academy of Inventors\nNAI Senior Memeber, American Academy of Forensic Sciences (AAFS) Full Member, the “Bioanalysis New Investigator Award” in 2014, UT STARS Award in 2012, NSERC Postdoctoral Fellow Award in 2009, Outstanding Faculty Dissertation Research Mentoring Award (2016 & 2018, twice), NIH BUILDING Scholar Mentoring Award for Excellence in Student Research Mentoring in 2017, and so on. In 2024, he was Named World's Top Researchers by Elsevier (2% of the most cited researchers) and Top Scholar by ScholarGPS (Ranked #33 in Microfluidics in recent 5 years).\nCurrent Positions\n2022-\nProfessor.\nDepartment of Chemistry & Biochemistry at University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP)\nForensic Science (FORS), & Border Biomedical Research Center (BBRC), & Biomedical Engineering (BME), UTEP\nEnvironmental Science & Engineering (ESE), UTEP\nMaterials Science and Engineering (MASE), UTEP\n2022-\nDirector, Forensic Science Program\n2024-\nCouncilor, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\n2024-2025\nPast President, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\n2022.01-2024.01\nPresident, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\n2022-2023\nVisiting Professor, Department of NanoEngineering, University of California San Diego (\nUCSD\n) (Host: Prof.\nJoseph Wang\n)\n2017-2022\nAssociate Professor (with early tenure) in Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at UTEP\nBorder Biomedical Research Center (BBRC), UTEP\nBiomedical Engineering (BME), UTEP\nEnvironmental Science & Engineering (ESE), UTEP\nMaterials Science and Engineering (MASE), UTEP\n2021\nPresident Elect, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\n2017\nVisiting Associate Professor, Hamon Center for Therapeutic Oncology Research, & Department of Surgery, UT Southwestern Medical Center\n2012-2017\nTenure-Track Assistant Professor in Department of Chemistry at University of Texas at El Paso\nBorder Biomedical Research Center (BBRC), UTEP\nBiomedical Engineering (BME), UTEP\nEnvironmental Science & Engineering (ESE), UTEP\nMaterials Science and Engineering (MASE), UTEP\nEducation\n2010-2011\nNSERC Postdoctoral Fellow, Harvard University & Wyss Institute for Biologically Inspired Engineering.\nLow-cost medical diagnosis and 3D cell culture\nSupervisor: Prof. George M. Whitesides\n2008-2009\nNSERC Postdoctoral Fellow, UC Berkeley\nIntegrated microdevices for genetic analysis in forensics\nSupervisor: Prof. Richard A. Mathies\n2003-2008\nPh.D. in Bioanalytical Chemistry, Simon Fraser University, Canada\nMicrofluidic single-cell analysis\nSupervisor: Prof. Paul C.H. Li\nHonors & Awards\n2026\nNAI (National Academy of Inventors) Senior Member\n2025\n2025 R&I Innovation Award\n–\nEstablished Innovator\n, UTEP (Only one awardee per year)\n2024\nNamed World's Top Researchers (2% of the most cited researchers, by Elsevier)\n2024\nTravel Grant Award for GEM on the Road’s PFI Programming\n2024\nNamed Top Scholar by ScholarGPS (\nRanked #33\nin Microfluidics in recent 5 years)\n2023\nACS RGVS Outstanding Service Award\n2022\nFaculty development Leave Award, UTEP\n2022\nACS RGVS section Outstanding Service Award\n2021\nCPRIT Grant Award (Cancer Prevention & Researcg Institute of Texas)\n2021\nNSF IIP PFI Grant Award\n2021\nGrant Award of ACUE (Association of College and University Educators) Course in Effective Teaching Practices\n2021\nDOT CARTEEH Grant Award\n2018\nOutstanding Faculty Dissertation Research Mentoring Award, UTEP\n2018\nYoung Scientist Award finalist, Microsystems & Nanoengineering Summit\n2017\nInnovation Center Proof-of-Concept Grant, Medical Center of the Americas Foundation (MCA)\n2017\nNIH BUILDING Scholar Menting Award for excellence in sturdent research mentoring.\n2017\nNIH BUILDing Scholar Summer Sabbatical Award\n2017\nNIH BUILDing Scholars Faculty Travel Award\n2016-2017\nFaculty Research Mentoring Award, UTEP\n2016\nNSF PREM Travel Award\n2015\nNIH/NIAID Grant Award\n2014\n2014 Bioanalysis New Investigator Award.\n2013-2023\nOutstanding Performance Award (9 times), UTEP.\n2013\nNIH/NIGMS Grant Award\n2012-2023\nOutstanding Effort Award (13 times), UTEP\n2011-2013\nUT System STARS Award\n.\n2009-2011\nNSERC Postdoctoral Fellowship (PDF)\n, Natural Sciences & Engineering Research Council (NSERC) of Canada, two years\n2009\nDean of Graduate Studies Convocation Medal\n, Simon Fraser University (SFU)\n2007\nAward of President's Ph.D Research Stipend, Simon Fraser University\n2005\nSFU Graduate Fellowship, Simon Fraser University\n2004\nChinese Award for Outstanding Self-financed Graduate Student Abroad\n2001\nGraduate Future Star Scholarship, Shandong University (SDU)\n1999\nMost Outstanding Graduate of Shandong Province\n1998\nMost Outstanding Student of Shandong Province\n1998,1996\nOutstanding Student of Qingdao University (twice)\n1998,1997\nDistinguished Student Leader of Qingdao University (twice)\n1995\nMost Outstanding Student of Qingdao City\n2017\nAward Evaluation Committee for Early Career Research Award, Future Science OA\n2017\nMicromachines Travel Awards Evaluation Committee\nProfessional & Academic Activities\nGrant Peer Review Panel (\nnot updated anymore\n)\n2020\nSBIR Study Section, NIH\n2020\nBioengineering Study Section, NIH\n2020\nStudy Section of Infectious Diseases, NIH\n2020\nSBIR Study Section, NCI, NIH\n2013, 2015\nNational Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA)\n2013-2017\nNational Science Foundation (NSF), 4 times\n2018\nStudy Section, POCT Center U54, NIH\n2017\nCFRS Study section, NIH\n2016\nNational Institute of Health (NIH)\n2018-\nDepartment of Defense (DoD), 2 times\n2017\nACS Petroleum Research Grant\n2018-\nCanada Foundation for Innovation (CFI)\n2013\nCanadian Institutes of Health Research (CIHR)\n2013\nNetherlands Organisation for Scientific Research (NWO)\n2014\nCCNY-MSKCC Partnership for Cancer Research, Training, and Community Outreach\n2015\nSingapore Ministry of Defence and Singapore University of Technology & Design\n2015\nSingapore Ministry of Education –National Research Foundation\n2015\nInnovation & Technology Commission, Hong Kong SAR Government\n2017\nAmerican Institute of Biological Sciences\nJournals: (Editors: > 7 journals; Reviewer: > 61 journals)\n2023-\nEditorial Board Member\n,\nMicrosystems & Nanoengineering\nfrom Nature Publishing Group (IF 8.0)\n2020-\nEditor-in-Chief,\nPharmaceutical Analytical Letters\n2014-\nEditorial Board member,\nScientific Reports\nfrom Nature Publishing Group\n2020-\nAdvisory Board Member,\nLab on a Chip\n.\n2020-\nAdvisory Board Member,\nAnalyst\n.\n2024-\nEditorial Board member,\nNano Futures\n.\n2020-\nEditorial Board,\nJournal of Analysis and Testing\n2015-\nEditorial Board member,\nMicromachines\n.\n2016-\nEditorial Board member,\nFuture Science OA\n.\n2014-2016\nYoung Ambassador/ Editorial Advisory for Future Science Open from Future Science Group\n2015-2016\nGuest Editor, Special Issue in Current Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Topic, \"Miniaturized platforms and methods for pharmaceutical studies\"\n2011-\nMember of Board of Editorial Advisors,\nCanadian Journals of Pure & Applied Sciences\n2013-\nMember of Board of Editorial Advisors, Annals of Public Health and Research, Journal of Stem Cells Research, Review and Reports\n2010-\nInvited Referee for the Wiley journal of\nElectrophoresis\nand\nBiotech Progress\n, Small, Advanced Materials, Advanced Healthcare Materials\n2010-\nInvited Referee for the RSC journals:\nLab on a Chip\n,\nChem Comm\n,\nNanoscale\n,\nAnalyst\n,\nAnalytical Methods\n,\nRSC Advances\n, &\nMolecular BioSystems\n,\nPhysical Chemistry Chemical Physics\n, Toxicology Research, Chemical Science\n2012-\nInvited Referee for the ACS journals:\nAnalytical Chemistry\n,\nLangmuir\n,\nACS Applied Materials & Interfaces\n, ACS Omega, ACS Applied Bio Materials\n2013-\nInvited Referee for Elsevier: Science and Technology of Advanced Materials, Talanta, Chromatography A, Colloids and Surface B: Biointerfaces, Acta Biomaterialia, Biochemical Engineering Journal, Trends in Analytical Chemistry, Sensors and Actuator B, Catalysis Today, Biotechnology Advances.\n2014\nInvited Referee for Trends in Biotechnology, Scientific Reports, Biomicrofluidics, Plos One, Theranostics, Micromachines, Analytica Chimica Acta, IEEE Sensors Journal, Clinical Chemistry, Analytical & Bioanalytical Chemistry\n...\nThis section will not be updated.\nConferences (\nNot updated anymore\n)\n2019\nTrack Chair,\nPhotocatalysis in Catalysis & Chemical Engineering 2019, Houston, TX.\n2018\nSymposium organizer and Presider (Track Co-Chair)\nfor ICMFLOC 2018 (International Conference of Microfluidics, Nanofluidics, and Lab-on-a-Chip).\n2017\nSymposium Organizer\nand\nPresider\nfor ACS 2017 “Recent Innovations in Nano-Biosensing”.\n2017\nSymposium Organizer\nand\nPresider\nfor Pittcon 2017 “Recent Innovations in Nanosensing”.\n2016\nSymposium Organizer\nfor Optofluidics 2016 “Cost-effective microfluidic devices for bioanalysis”.\n2016.03\nSymposium Organizer and Presider for Pittcon 2016 “Emerging Technologies for Disease Biomarker Detection”.\n2015.03\nSymposium Organizer and Presider for Pittcon 2015 “Platforms of Point of care testing”.\n2015.03\nInvited Session Chair for Pittcon 2015 “Novel Microfluidic Instrumentation and Devices”\n2014.06\nInvited Session Chair for the CSC 2014 Conference in Vancouver, BC.\n2013.05\nInvited Session Chair for the conference of Advances in Microfluidics & Nanofluidics 2013, Notre Dame, IN.\n2012.07\nSession Chairs for 2012 ASME International Conference on Nanofluidics and Microfluidics at Puerto Rico\nMembership & Others\n2025-\nAAFS Full Member,\nAmerican Academy of Forensic Sciences (AAFS)\n2023-2024\nAAFS\nAssociate Member, American Academy of Forensic Sciences\n2014\n2014 Member of the Graduate School Outstanding Thesis and Dissertation Selection Committee, UTEP\n2006-\nACS (American Chemical Society) membership.\n2026-\nTechnical Program Committee (TPC)\nof MicroTAS for the Chemical and Biological Microsystems Society (CBMS)\n2012-2013\nFull Membership, Sigma Xi.\n2012-\nRSC e-Membership\n2004-2005\nMembership of CSC (Canadian Society for Chemistry) & CIC (Chemical Institute of Canada).\nConnect With Us\nThe University of Texas at El Paso\nDepartment of Chemistry and Biochemistry\n500 W. University Avenue\nEl Paso, Texas 79968\nhttp://li.utep.edu\nP: Lab: (915) 747-8051\nP: Office: (915) 747-8967\nModal\nX\n\n---\n\nDr. XiuJun Li\nSkip to main content\nMinerAlert\nMain Content\nUTEP\nCollege of Science\nDr. Li Research Group\nPeople\nUTEP\nCollege of Science\nDr. Li Research Group\nPeople\nDr. XiuJun (James) Li\nPrincipal Investigator\nDr. XiuJun (James) Li\nProfessor\nDirector, Forensic Science Program\nCouncilor, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\nPast President, ACS Rio Grande Valley Chapter\nChemistry & Biochemistry, & Biomedical Engineering\nEnvironmental Science & Engineering\nDepartment of Chemistry & Biochemistry\nUniversity of Texas at El Paso\n500 W University Ave\nEl Paso, TX, 79968\nWeb:\nhttp://li.utep.edu\nPhone: (915) 747-8967\nOffice: CCSB 2.0112\nLab: CCSB 2.0528\nMedia Profile\nShort Biography\nXiuJun (James) Li, Ph.D., is a full Professor with early tenure in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP), USA. He is also the Director of Forensic Science Program at UTEP. After he obtained his Ph.D. degree in microfluidic lab-on-a-chip bioanalysis from Simon Fraser University (SFU) in Canada in 2008, he pursued his postdoctoral research with Prof. Richard Mathies at University of California Berkeley and Prof. George Whitesides at Harvard University, while holding a Postdoctoral Fellowship from Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council (NSERC) of Canada. Dr. Li’s current research interest is centered on the development of innovative microfluidic lab-on-a-chip and nanotechnology for bioanalysis,  biomedical engineering, forensic science, biomaterial, and environmental applications, including but not limited to low-cost diagnosis, pathogen detection, nano-biosensing, genetic analysis, 3D cell culture, tissue engineering, and single-cell analysis, supported by NIH, NSF, CPRIT, DOT, AAFS, UT System, Philadelphia Foundation, and MCA Foundation multiple funding agencies. His lab has extensive experience in point-of-care detection. He pioneered the novel concept of paper/polymer hybrid microfluidic devices; he, for the first time, developed photothermal biosensors for low-cost quantitative analysis using a common thermometer.\nDr. Li with an Google Scholar H-Index of 53 has coauthored more than 127 journal publications and 26 patents, including three books from Elsevier on microfluidic devices for biomedical applications. He is an Editorial Board member of multiple journals includ...[truncated]"
