    "homepage_text": "Website of Yefeng Zheng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWebsite of Yefeng Zheng\nHOME\nWelcome! This is\nYefeng Zheng\n(郑冶枫).\nI am a professor at Westlake University, Hangzhou, China.\nShort Biography\n: Yefeng Zheng  received B.E. and M.E. degrees from the Department of Electronic Engineering, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, in 1998 and 2001, respectively, and\na Ph.D. degree from University of Maryland, College Park, USA, in 2005 with a dissertation on handwritten document image analysis.\nAfter graduation, he joined Siemens Corporate Research in Princeton, New Jersey, USA, first as Research Scientist and later being promoted to Project Manager and Principal Key Expert. He led a team developing efficient machine learning methods for many challenging problems in medical image analysis. He joined Tencent in January 2018 as Director and Distinguished Scientist of\nTencent Jarvis Research Center\n, Shenzhen, China, leading the company's initiative on Medical AI. S\nince July 2024,\nhe has been a professor and director of\nMedical Artificial Intelligence Laboratory\nat Westlake University, Hangzhou, China. His research interests include AI in health, medical image analysis,\ncomputer vision,\nnatural language processing, and large language model. He has published 400+ papers on top journals and conferences in the above fields, which have been cited 26,000+ times with H-index of 82 according to\nGoogle Scholar\n. He invented 563\npatents\n(among them 98\nUS patents\n)\n, including a patent on Marginal Space Learning based heart chamber segmentation, which won the Thomas A. Edison Patent Award of New Jersey R&D Council in 2011. He is a major contributor for several other prestigious awards too, including Siemens Top+ Innovation Award in 2010 and the Techno-College Innovation Award of the European Association for Cardio-Thoracic Surgery (EACTS) in 2010. As a co-developer of an Asian Optical Character Recognition (OCR) system, he won the National Scientific and Technological Progress Award (2nd class) of China in 2003.\nHe is a fellow of the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE), a fellow of American Institute for Medical and Biological Engineering (AIMBE), a fellow of Asia-Pacific Artificial Intelligence Association (AAIA), a Program Co-Chair of International Conference on Medical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention (MICCAI) 2021, an Associate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging (impact factor 10.0) since 2018, and was an Associate Editor of IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics (impact factor 7.0) 2013-2018.\nEducation\nAug. 2001 -- Dec. 2005 (Diploma was officially issued in May 2006)\nPh.D.\nDept. of Electrical & Computer Engineering,\nUniversity of Maryland\n, College Park\nResearch topic: Document Image Analysis and Computer Vision\nAcademic Advisor: Dr. David Doermann\nSept. 1998 -- July 2001\nM.S.\nDept. of Electronic Engineering,\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing, China\nResearch topics: Form Recognition & Processing\nAcademic Advisor: Prof. Xiaoqing Ding\nSept. 1993 -- July 1998\nB.S.\nDept. of Electronic Engineering,\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing, China\nWorking Experience\nJul. 2024 -- Present\nProfessor, Westlake University\nHangzhou, China\nJan. 2018 -- Jul. 2024\nDirector and Distinguished Scientist of Tencent Jarvis Research Center\nTencent\n, Shenzhen, China\nAug. 2015 -- Dec. 2017\nSenior Key Expert -> Principal Key Expert (Research)\nSiemens Healthineers Technology Center\n, Princeton, New Jersey\nJan. 2006 -- Aug. 2015\nResearch Scientist -> Project Manager -> Senior Staff Scientist\nSiemens Corporate Research\n, Princeton, New Jersey\nEmail: yefeng DOT zheng AT gmail DOT com\nLast updated: March 23, 2025\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
