    "homepage_text": "Yue Yu\nProfessor\nDepartment of Mathematics, Lehigh University\nBethlehem, PA\nHome\nBio\nTeam\nPublications\nOutreach Activities\nBackground\nI am currently a Professor of Applied Mathematics at\nDepartment of Mathematics, Lehigh University\n. I am also affiliated with the College of Health and the Institute for Data, Intelligent Systems, and Computation (I-DISC) at Lehigh.\nMy research is centered around\nscientific machine learning (SciML) and numerical analysis for high-order methods\n, and in particular how to obtain useful mathematical and numerical models of complex physical and biological systems. I am particularly interested in\napplying the mathematical analysis knowledges in the design and analysis of mathematical models and numerical schemes\n.\nQuick links:\nMy Curriculum Vitae:\n.pdf\nMy Google Scholar page:\n.html\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests include:\nScientific Machine Learning\n- Nonlocal Operator Learning\n- Graph Neural Networks (GNN)\n- Causal Discovery\nHigh-Order Methods\n- Meshfree Methods\n- Spectral Element Methods\n- Isogeometric Analysis (IGA)\nMultiscale/Multiphysics Problems\n- Fluid--Structure Interaction\n- Local-Nonlocal Coupling Problems\n- Peridynamics and Other Nonlocal Models\nModeling for Real-World Applications\n- Materials\n- Soft Tissues\n- Natural Language Processing\nEducation\n2014\nPh.D.\nBrown University\nApplied Mathematics\nThesis:\nNumerical methods for fluid-structure interactions: analysis and simulations\n2013\nM.Sc.\nBrown University\nMechanical Engineering (Solid Mechanics)\n2008\nB.S.\nPeking University\nMathematics\nContact Information\nName:\nYue Yu\nEmail:\nyuy214 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nOffice:\nChandler Ullmann Hall, Room 243\nPhone:\n610-758-3752\nMailing Address:\nLehigh University, Bethlehem, PA, 18015\nEducation and Academic Experience\nSince Jul. 2023\nProfessor\nDepartment of Mathematics, Lehigh University\nSince Mar. 2022\nAffiliated Faculty\nThe College of Health, Lehigh University\nSince Sep. 2018\nAffiliated Faculty\nInstitute for Data, Intelligent Systems, and Computation (I-DISC), Lehigh University\nNov. 2023-Dec. 2023\nIBM Visiting Professor\nDivision of Applied Mathematics, Brown University, USA\nJul. 2019-Jun. 2023\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Mathematics, Lehigh University\nAug. 2014-Jun. 2019\nTenure-Track Assistant Professor\nDepartment of Mathematics, Lehigh University\nFeb. 2017-Mar. 2017\nVisiting Professor\nInstitute for Computational Engineering and Sciences, The University of Texas at Austin, USA\nHost: Prof. Thomas J.R. Hughes\nJun. 2014-Jul. 2014\nPostdoc Fellowship\nSchool of Engineering and Applied Science, Harvard University, USA\nAdviser: Prof. Chris Rycroft\nSep. 2008-May. 2014\nPh.D. in Applied Mathematics\nDivision of Applied Mathematics, Brown University, USA\nAdviser: Prof. George E. Karniadakis\nSep. 2008-May. 2013\nM.Sc. in Mechanical Engineering (Solid Mechanics)\nSchool of Engineering, Brown University, USA\nSep. 2004-Jul. 2008\nB.Sc. in Mathematics\nSchool of Mathematics, Peking University, China\nAdviser: Prof. Huazhong Tang\nFellowships, Honors and Awards\n2025\nGallagher Young Investigator Medal, USACM\n2024\nLehigh AI Award, Lehigh University\n2023\nIBM Visiting Faculty Fellowship, Brown University\n2022\nRecognition for Outstanding Academic Achivement, Lehigh University\n2022\nAir Force Young Investigator\n2021\nNSF-MAPWISELY Faculty Success Fellowship\n2018\nNational Science Foundation CAREER Award\n2017,2018\nClass of 1968 Junior Faculty Fellowship, Lehigh University\n2014\nDunmu Ji Thesis Award, Brown University\n2012-2013\nSimon Ostrach Fellowship, Brown University\n2008-2009\nGraduate Fellowship, Brown University\n2007\nSouthwest Education Fellowship, Peking University\n2005, 2006\nMary Kay Education Fellowship, Peking University\n2004\nNew Student Fellowship, Peking University\nCourses Taught\nLehigh University\nMath450\n: Numerical PDEs\nMath409\n: Topics in Numerical Analysis\nMath341\n: Mathematical Models and Their Formulation\nMath230\n: Numerical Methods\nMath205\n: Linear Methods\nMath023\n: Calculus III\nBrown University\nAPMA0330\n: Methods of Applied Mathematics I\nAPMA0340\n: Methods of Applied Mathematics II\nSelected Leadership and Professional Activities\n2025 - present\nElected President\nof the\nSociety for Industrial and Applied Mathematics (SIAM) NYNJPA Section\n2022 - 2024\nVice President\nof the\nSociety for Industrial and Applied Mathematics (SIAM) NYNJPA Section\n2020 - present\nCo-Founder\nof the\nOne Nonlocal World project\nand the\nOne Nonlocal World YouTube Channel\n2025 - present\nElected Vice Chair\nof the\nUSACM Technical Thrust Area âMathematical Methodsâ\n2015 - 2019\nCommittee Member\nof the\nComputational Fluid Dynamics and FluidâStructure Interaction Technical Thrust Area (TTA) Committee of USACM\n2025 - present\nSecretary\nof the\nInternational Association for Computational Mechanics (IACM) Female Researchers Chapter\n2023 - 2024\nPublicity Officer\nof the\nInternational Association for Computational Mechanics (IACM) Female Researchers Chapter\n2022 - present\nAssociate Editor:\nAdvances in Computational Science and Engineering (ACSE), Advanced Modelling and Simulation in Engineering Sciences (AMSES)\n2022 - present\nEditorial Board Member:\nComputer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering (CMAME), (Nature) Scientific Reports, Numerical Methods for Partial Differential Equations (NMPDE), Machine Learning: Engineering (MLEng), Finite Element in Analysis and Design (FINEL).\n2023 - present\nGuest Editor:\nFrontiers in Mechanical Engineering, Special Issue on Hybrid Modeling â\r\nBlending Physics with Data\n2021 - present\nCommittee\nmember of the Lehigh I-DISC Data and Computing Equity and Justice (DCEJ) Working group\n2017 - present\nCo-Organizer\nof the Annual High-Performance Computing (HPC) Workshop, Bethlehem, Pennsylvania\n2016 - present\nReviewer/Panelist of Funding Agencies:\nDepartment of Energy, Air Force Office of Scientific Research, National Science Foundation, National Science Centre in Poland, Wallenberg Academy Fellowship Program in Sweden.\n2018 - 2020\nFaculty Advisory Council\nmember of the Lehigh Institute for Data, Intelligent Systems and Computation (I-DISC)\nCurrent Team Members\nStewart Silling\nDistinguished Visiting Research Fellow\nNing Liu\nVisiting Research Fellow\nNaiyu Yin\nEmail: nay224 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPostdoctoral Research Associate\nResearch Interests: Machine Learning, Causal Discovery, Probabilistic Graphical Model\nQi Sun\nEmail: qis325 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPostdoctoral Research Associate\nResearch Interests: Numerical PDEs, Finite Element Method, Fluid--Structure Interaction\nLu Zhang\nEmail: luz319 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPh.D. candidate in Applied Mathematics\nResearch Interests: Scientific Machine Learning, Graph Neural Networks, Natural Language Processing\nJiuzhou Chen\nEmail: jic422 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPh.D. candidate in Applied Mathematics\nResearch Interests: Scientific Machine Learning, Nonlocal Neural Operators, Foundation Model\nZiwei Yang\nEmail: ziy524 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPh.D. candidate in Applied Mathematics\nResearch Interests: Scientific Machine Learning, Computational Mechanics\nEthan Bean\nEmail: etb224 [at] lehigh [dot] edu\nPh.D. candidate in Applied Mathematics\nResearch Interests: Scientific Machine Learning, Mathematical Biology\nFormer Group Members\nJihong Wang\nPostdoctoral Research Associate, Lehigh University\nAssistant Professor in the Mathematics Department, Huazhong University of Science and Technology\nSiavash Jafarzadeh\nC.-C. Hsiung Visiting Assistant Professor, Lehigh University\nEngineer in the Mathematics Department, Dassault SystÃ¨mes SIMULIA Corp\nShang-Huan Chiu\nC.-C. Hsiung Visiting Assistant Professor, Lehigh University\nAssistant Professor in the Mathematics Department, New York City College of Technology\nCory Wright\nC.-C. Hsiung Visiting Assistant Professor, Lehigh University\nAssistant Professor in the Mathematics Department, Milwaukee School of Engineering (MSOE)\nYiming Fan\nPh.D. in Applied Mathematics, Lehigh University\nResearch Scientist, Wayfair\nHuaiqian You\nPh.D. in Applied Mathematics, Lehigh University\nApplied Machine Learning Scientist, TikTok\nNeeraj Tatikola\nM.Sc. in Applied Mathematics, Lehigh University\nResearcher in U.S. Naval Research Lab\nJosiah Mount\nM.Sc. in Applied Mathematics, Lehigh University\nAssistant Professor of Mathematics in Northampton Community College\nKatherine Wu\nM.Sc. in Statistics, Lehigh University\nResearch Engineer at The Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory\nQuinn Zhang\nB.Sc. in Mathematics, Lehigh University\nPh.D. Student of Applied Mathematics at New York University\nAnna Thomas\nB.Sc. in Mathematics, Lehigh University\nPh.D. Student of Mathematics at University of Pittsburgh\nMengran He\nB.Sc. in Applied Mathematics, Lehigh University\nMaster Student of Statistical Practice at Carnegie Mellon University\nCianael Paasewe\nB.Sc. in Biological Science, Northampton Community College\nAwarded as Academic All-Star and member of the All-PA Academic Team by the international honor society Phi Theta Kappa and the Pennsylvania Commission for Community Colleges\nPublications and Preprints\nBook Chapters\nGoswami S, Bora A,\nYu Y\n, Karniadakis G (2023)\nPhysics-informed deep neural operator networks\n. Machine Learning in Modeling and Simulation: Methods and Applications. Editors: Timon Rabczuk, Klaus J. Bathe, 2023.\nYu Y\n(2018)\nFluid-structure interaction modeling in 3D cerebral arteries and aneurysms\n. Lecture\r\nNotes in Applied and Computational Mechanics: Biomedical Technology. Springer, Cham. Pages 123-146.\nYu Y\n, Kirby M, Karniadakis GE (2017)\nSpectral element and hp methods\n. Encyclopedia of Compu-\r\ntational Mechanics, John Wiley and Sons, NY, 1:1-43.\nPublications in Refereed Journals\nKarkaria V, Lee D, Chen Y-P,\nYu Y\n, Chen W (2025)\nAn Attention-based Spatio-Temporal Neural Operator for Evolving Physics\n. Machine Learning: Science and Technology.\nFan Y (Ph.D. student)\n, Najm H,\nYu Y\n, Silling S, D'Elia M (2025)\nEmbedded Nonlocal Operator Regression (ENOR): Quantifying model error in learning nonlocal operators\n. International Journal for Uncertainty Quantification.\nLiu N,\nJafarzadeh S (Postdoc advisee)\n, Lattimer B, Ni S, Lua J,\nYu Y\n(2025)\nHarnessing large language models for data-scarce learning of polymer properties\n. Nature Computational Science, 1-10.\nJafarzadeh S (Postdoc advisee)\n, Silling S,\nZhang L (Ph.D. student)\n, Ross C, Lee C-H, Rahman R, Wang S,\nYu Y\n(2025)\nHeterogeneous Peridynamic Neural Operators: Discover Biotissue Constitutive Law and Microstructure from Digital Image Correlation Measurements\n. Foundations of Data Science (FoDS), 7(1), 226-270.\nLi B,\nYu Y\n, Yang X (2024)\nThe sparse-grid-based adaptive spectral Koopman method\n. SIAM Journal on Scientific Computing 46.5: A2925-A2950.\nYou H (Ph.D. student)\n,\nYu Y\n, Silling S, D'Elia M (2024)\nNonlocal operator learning for homogenized models: from high-fidelity simulations to constitutive laws\n. Journal of Peridynamics and Nonlocal Modeling. Volume 6, pages 709â724.\nLee D,\nZhang L (Ph.D. student)\n,\nYu Y\n, Chen W (2024)\nDeep neural operator enabled concurrent multitask design for multifunctional metamaterials under heterogeneous fields\n. Advanced Optical Materials, 2303087.\nSilling S,\nJafarzadeh S (Postdoc advisee)\n,\nYu Y\n(2024)\nPeridynamic models for random media found by coarse graining\n. Journal of Peridynamics and Nonlocal Modeling, Volume 6, pages 654â683.\nJafarzadeh S (Postdoc advisee)\n, Silling S, Liu N, Zhang Z,\nYu Y\n(2024)\nPeridynamic Neural Operators: a data-driven nonlocal constitutive model for complex material responses\nComputer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering, Volume 425, 116914.\nZhang L (Ph.D. student)\n,\nYou H (Ph.D. student)\n, Gao T, Yu M, Lee