    "homepage_text": "王世金-中国科学院大学-UCAS\n[中文]\n[English]\nResearch Areas\nEducation\nExperience\nPublications\nResearch Interests\nStudents\nGeneral\nWang Shijin, Male, Doctor's Advisor, Northwest Institute of Eco-Environmental Resources, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nEmail: wangshijin@lzb.ac.cn\nE-Mail address: 320 Donggang West Road, Lanzhou City, Gansu Province\nPostcode: 730000\nResearch Areas\nCryosphere and Sustainable Development\nEducation\n1999.09-2001.07, School of Economics, Nankai University, college diploma/graduate in Economics, mainly engaged in population economics research;\n2003.09-2006.07, College of Foreign Languages, Northwest Normal University, B.A. degree of Literature, mainly engaged in English translation work;\n2005.09-2008.07, College of Geography and Environmental science, Northwest Normal University, M.S. degree in Science, mainly engaged in regional development and management research;\n2008.09-2011.07, Cold and Arid Region Environment and Engineering Research Institute, D.S. Degree in Science, mainly engaged in glacier and skiing tourism resources development and planning research;\n2011.09-2013.05, State Key Laboratory of Cryospheric Sciences, Cold and Arid Region Environment and Engineering Research Institute, China Post-doctoral research Work, mainly engaged in Cryosphere disaster risk assessment research;\nExperience\n2013.06-2015.12, Cold and Arid Region Environment and Engineering Research Institute, an Research Assistant, mainly engaged in Cryosphere disaster risk assessment;\n2016.1-,2020.01 Northwest Institute of Eco-Environment and Resources, Chinese Academy of Sciences, associate professor, mainly engaged in Cryosphere service and value assessment.\n2020.01-\n, Northwest Institute of Eco-Environment and Resources, Chinese Academy of Sciences,\nProfessor,\nmainly engaged in Cryosphere and sustainble development.\nPublications\nEdited 8 monographs and participated in editing more than 20 books, Submited 12 decision-making consultation reports, and published more than 80 academic papers as the first author. Among them, 3 SCI/SSCI papers, 3 EI, etc. were published in Landslides, JDMM, Ecol. Indic., J. Glaciol., Global Planet Change, etc. SCI publications cited more than 1250 times.\nPapers\n​\n[1]\nWang S.J., Che Y.J., Wei Y.Q. Spatiotemporal Dynamic Characteristics of Typical Temperate Glaciers in China. Scientific Reports, 2021, 11:657. doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-80418-7.\n[2]\nWang S.J., Zhao Q.D., Pu T. Assessment of Water Stress Level about Global Glacier-Covered Arid Areas: A Case Study in the Shule River Basin, Northwestern China. Journal of Hydrology: Regional Studies, 2021, 37:\ndoi.org/10.1016/j.ejrh.2021.100895\n.\n[3]\nWang S.J., Yang Y.D., Gong W.Y., et al. Reason analysis of the Jiwenco glacial lake outburst flood (GLOF) and potential hazard on the Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau. Remote Sensing, 2021, 13(16), 3114.\n[4]\nWang S.J. Perception by Indigenous People of Climate Change and its Impact on Everest National Nature Preserve. Meteorological Applications, 2021; 28:e1987.\n[5]\nChe Y.J., Wang S.J. *, Ma X.G. et al. Rapid changes to glaciers increased the outburst flood risk in Guangxieco Proglacial Lake in the Kangri Karpo Mountains, Southeast Qinghai\n‑\nTibetan Plateau. Natural Nazards, 2021, doi.org/10.1007/s11069-021-05029-5.\n[6]\nWang S.J., Mu Y.Q., Zhang X.Y., Xie J. 2020. Polar tourism and environment change: opportunity, impact and adaptation. Polar Science, 2020, doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/ j.polar.2020.100544.\n[7]\nWang S.J., Che Y.J., Pang H.X., et al. 2020, Accelerated changes of glaciers in the Yulong Snow Mountain, southeast Qinghai\n-\nTibetan Plateau. Regional Environmental Change, 2020, 20, 38: 1-13.\n[8]\nWang S.J., Che Y.J., Ma X.G. Integrated risk assessment of glacier lake outburst flood (GLOF) disaster over the Qinghai-Tibetan plateau (QTP) Wang S.J., Zhou L.Y., Xie J. China’s Glacier Tourism: Potential Evaluation and Spatial Planning. Journal of Destination Marketing & Management, 2020, 16, in press.\n[9]\nPeng X.Q., Zhang T.J., Frauenfeld O.W., Wang S.J*. Northern Hemisphere 1 greening in association with warming permafrost. JGR: Biogeosciences, 2020, 125(1). DOI.10.1029/2019JG005086.\n[10]\nWang S.J., Wei Y.Q. Water resource system risk and adaptive management of the Chinese Heihe River Basin in Asian arid areas. Mitigation and Adaptation Strategies For Global Change. 2019, 24, 1271–1292.\n[11]\nWang S.J., Zhou L.Y., Wei Y.Q. Integrated Risk Assessment of Snow Disaster (SD) over the Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau (QTP). Geomatics Natural Hazards & Risk, 2019, 10(1):740-757.\n[12]\nWang S.J., Zhou L.Y. Integrated Impacts of Climate Change on Glacier Tourism. Advances in Climate Change Research, 2019, 10(2): 71-79.\n[13]\nWang S.J., Shi X.Y., Cao W.H., Pu T. Seasonal Variability and Evolution of Glacio-chemistry at An Alpine Temperate Glacier on the Southeastern Tibetan Plateau. Water, 2018, 114(10): 1-14.\n[14]\nWang S.J., Chen S.Y., Wei Y.Q., Kang S.C. Risk prevention and control strategies for the severely affected areas of snow disaster in the Three Rivers Source Region (TRSR), China. Sciences in Cold and Arid Regions, 2019, 11 (3): 248-253.\n[15]\nWang S.J. and Zhou L.Y. Glacial lake outburst flood disasters and integrated risk management in China. International Journal of Disaster Risk Science, 2017, 8(4): 493-497.\n[16]\nWang S.J. and Ding B.H. 2017. The active-layer ice temperature (ALIT) increases more obvious on a cold glacier than a temperate glacier during the past 30 years. International Journal of Global Warming, 2017, 13(1): 103-111.\n[17]\nWang S.J., Qin D.H., Xiao C.D. 2015. Moraine-dammed lake distribution and outburst flood risk in the Chinese Himalaya. Journal of Glaciology, 2015, 61(225): 115-126.\n[18]\nWang S.J. and Jiao S.T. Evolution and outburst risk analysis of moraine-dammed lakes in the central Chinese Himalaya. Journal of Earth System Science, 2015, 124(3): 567-576.\n[19]\nWang S.J., Du J.K., He Y.Q. Spatial-temporal characteristics of a temperate-glacier’s active-layer temperature and its responses to climate change: a case study of Baishui Glacier No. 1 (BSG1), southeastern Tibetan plateau. Journal of Earth Science, 2014, 25(4): 727-734.\n[20]\nWang S.J. and Zhang T. Spatially change detection of glacial lakes in the Koshi River Basin, the Central Himalayas. Environmental Earth Sciences, 2014, 72(11): 4381-4391.\n[21]\nWang S.J., Jiao S.T., Xin H.J. Spatio-temporal Characteristics of Temperature and Precipitation in Sichuan Province, Southwestern China in Recent Five Decades. Quaternary International, 2013, 286:103-115.\n[22]\nWang S.J., Zhang T. Glacial lakes change and current status in the central Chinese Himalayas from 1990 to 2010. Journal of Applied Remote Sensing, 2013, 7(1) 073459.\n[23]\nWang S.J., He Y.Q., Song X.D. Impacts of Climate Warming on Alpine Glacier Tourism and Adaptive Measures: A Case Study of Baishui Glacier No. 1 in Yulong Snow Mountain, Southwestern China. Journal of Earth Science, 2010, 21(2), 166-178.\n[24]\nWei Y.Q., Wang S.J., Fang Y.P., Nawaz Z. 2017. Integrated Assessment of the Vulnerability of Animal Husbandry From Snow Disaster Perspective Under Climate Change on the Qinghai -Tibetan Plateau. Global and Planetary Change, 157: 139-152.\n[25]\nWang Shijin and Jiao Shitai. Adaptation models of mountain glacier tourism to climate change: a case study of Mt. Yulong Snow scenic area. Sciences in Cold and Arid Regions. 2012, 4 (5): 0401–0407.\n[26]\nXiao, C.D., Wang S.J*., Qin D.H. A preliminary study of cryosphere service function and value evaluation. Advances in Climate Change Research, 2015, 6(3-4): 181–187.\n[27]\nWang J., Wang Y., Wang S.J. Biophysical and socioeconomic drivers of the dynamics in snow hazard impacts across scales and over heterogeneous landscape in Northern Tibet. Nat Hazards, 2016, DOI 10.1007/s11069-015-2142-7.\n[28]\nYuan L.L. and Wang S.J. 2018. The Recreational Value of Glacier Tourism Resources: A Travel Cost Analysis for China's Yulong Snow Mountain. Journal of Mountain Science, 2018, 15(7):1446-1459. https://doi.org/ 10.1007/s11629-017-4685-4.\n[29]\nWei Y.Q., Wang S.J.*, Liu J. et al. Multi-Source Remote-Sensing Monitoring of the Monsoonal Maritime Glaciers at Mt. Dagu, East Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau, China. IEEE/ACCESS, 2019, 7: 48307-48317.\nResearch Interests\nCryosphere tourism and service potential assessment\nCryospheric disaster and disaster prevention and mitigation\nCryosphere and sustainable development\nCryosphere and global change\nStudents\n已指导学生\n孙振亓  硕士研究生  070502-人文地理学\n周蓝月  硕士研究生  070501-自然地理学\n颉佳  硕士研究生  070502-人文地理学\n王彦霞  博士研究生  070502-人文地理学\n现指导学生\n赵荣芳  博士研究生  070502-人文地理学\n孙振亓  博士研究生  070501-自然地理学\n徐敏  博士研究生  070501-自然地理学\n秦悦  硕士研究生  070501-自然地理学\n秦日政  硕士研究生  070501-自然地理学\n声明：导师网页信息由导师个人维护，仅代表导师本人。教师系统仅提供信息存储空间服务。\n2013 © 中国科学院大学，网络信息中心.\n\n---\n\nSEP 教育业务接入平台\nEng\n本平台为互联网非密平台，严禁处理、传输国家秘密。\n信息门户\n用户名\n密 码\n验证码\n找回用户名密码\n登  录\n新生用户名为国科大邮箱（从上方找回用户名密码链接获取），密码为身份证号。\n下载用户\n服务指南\n教育云服务指南\n研究生\n本科生\n教师\n研究所\n用户权限管理规定\n招生系统启动密钥\n了解相关服务和规定\nservice@ucas.edu.cn\n|\n010-88256622\n|\n网络中心微信服务\n电子邮件\n邮箱\n密 码\n如您无法登录，请访问\n这里\n登录邮箱\n信 息 门 户\n电 子 邮 件\n校 园 网 登 录\nA R P 系 统\n果壳门户小程序\n\n---\n\nSEP 教育业务接入平台\nEng\n本平台为互联网非密平台，严禁处理、传输国家秘密。\n信息门户\n用户名\n密 码\n验证码\n找回用户名密码\n登  录\n新生用户名为国科大邮箱（从上方找回用户名密码链接获取），密码为身份证号。\n下载用户\n服务指南\n教育云服务指南\n研究生\n本科生\n教师\n研究所\n用户权限管理规定\n招生系统启动密钥\n了解相关服务和规定\nservice@ucas.edu.cn\n|\n010-88256622\n|\n网络中心微信服务\n电子邮件\n邮箱\n密 码\n如您无法登录，请访问\n这里\n登录邮箱\n信 息 门 户\n电 子 邮 件\n校 园 网 登 录\nA R P 系 统\n果壳门户小程序\n\n---\n\nSEP 教育业务接入平台\nEng\n本平台为互联网非密平台，严禁处理、传输国家秘密。\n信息门户\n用户名\n密 码\n验证码\n找回用户名密码\n登  录\n新生用户名为国科大邮箱（从上方找回用户名密码链接获取），密码为身份证号。\n下载用户\n服务指南\n教育云服务指南\n研究生\n本科生\n教师\n研究所\n用户权限管理规定\n招生系统启动密钥\n了解相关服务和规定\nservice@ucas.edu.cn\n|\n010-88256622\n|\n网络中心微信服务\n电子邮件\n邮箱\n密 码\n如您无法登录，请访问\n这里\n登录邮箱\n信 息 门 户\n电 子 邮 件\n校 园 网 登 录\nA R P 系 统\n果壳门户小程序\n\n---\n\nSEP 教育业务接入平台\nEng\n本平台为互联网非密平台，严禁处理、传输国家秘密。\n信息门户\n用户名\n密 码\n验证码\n找回用户名密码\n登  录\n新生用户名为国科大邮箱（从上方找回用户名