    "homepage_text": "Yunhao Yang's Website\nYunhao Yang is a 4th-year Ph.D. student in computer science at The University of Texas at Austin. Prior to this, he received B.S. and M.S. degrees in computer science, and a B.A. in mathematics from UT Austin. \n                        He is currently a member of the\nCenter for Autonomy\n, supervised by Prof.\nUfuk Topcu\n. \n                        His research interests include integrating large language models and formal methods for autonomy and uncertainty quantification in AI.\nHe received the\nAmazon Science Research Fellowship\n(by the UT-Amazon Hub) in the 2024~2025 academic year \n                        and interned at Cruise (a subsidiary of GM) in the summer of 2024, conducting research on autonomous driving.\nYunhao Yang\nyunhaoyang234@gmail.com\nDepartment of Computer Science\nThe University of Texas at Austin\nAustin, Texas\nUSA\nGoogle Scholar\nCurriculum Vitae\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nSelected Publications\n* Equal Contribution\nJournal\nYunhao Yang*\n, Minkyu Choi*, Neel Bhatt*, Kushagra Gupta, Sahil Shah, Aditya Rai, David Fridovich-Keil, Ufuk Topcu, Sandeep P Chinchali.\nReal-Time Privacy Preservation for Robot Visual Perception\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research, 2025.\nYunhao Yang*\n, Parham Gohari* and Ufuk Topcu.\nOn the Privacy Risks of Deploying Recurrent Neural Networks in Machine Learning\nProceedings on Privacy Enhancing Technologies 2023.\nYunhao Yang\n, Zhaokun Xue and Andrew Whinston.\nSelf-Enhancing Multi-filter Sequence-to-Sequence Model\nProcedia Computer Science, Elsevier, 2023.\nConference Proceedings\nYunhao Yang\n, Junyuan Hong, Gabriel Jacob Perin, Zhiwen Fan, Li Yin, Zhangyang Wang, Ufuk Topcu.\nLAD-VF: LLM-Automatic Differentiation Enables Fine-Tuning-Free Robot Planning from Formal Methods Feedback\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics & Automation (ICRA) 2026.\nYunhao Yang\n, Yuxin Hu, Mao Ye, Zaiwei Zhang, Zhichao Lu, Yi Xu, Ufuk Topcu, Ben Snyder.\nUncertainty-Guided Enhancement on Driving Perception System via Foundation Models\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics & Automation (ICRA) 2025.\nNeel Bhatt*,\nYunhao Yang*\n, Rohan Siva, Daniel Milan, Ufuk Topcu, Zhangyang Wang.\nKnow Where You're Uncertain When Planning with Multimodal Foundation Models: A Formal Framework\nAnnual Conference on Machine Learning and Systems (MLSys) 2025.\nMinkyu Choi*, Harsh Goel*, Mohammad Omama*,\nYunhao Yang\n, Sahil Shah, Sandeep Chinchali.\nTowards Neuro-Symbolic Video Understanding\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) 2024.\nOral Presentation\nYunhao Yang*\n, Neel Bhatt*, Tyler Ingebrand*, William Ward, Steven Carr, Zhangyang Wang and Ufuk Topcu.\nFine-Tuning Language Models Using Formal Methods Feedback: A Use Case in Autonomous Systems\nAnnual Conference on Machine Learning and Systems (MLSys) 2024.\nYunhao Yang\n, Cyrus Neary and Ufuk Topcu.\nMultimodal Pretrained Models for Verifiable Sequential Decision-Making: Planning, Grounding, and Perception\nInternational Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multi-Agent Systems (AAMAS) 2024.\nOral Presentation\nYunhao Yang\nand Andrew B Whinston.\nA Survey on Reinforcement Learning for Combinatorial Optimization\nIEEE World Conference on Applied Intelligence and Computing (AIC) 2023.\nYunhao Yang\nand Zhaokun Xue.\nTraining Heterogeneous Features in Sequence to Sequence Tasks: Latent Enhanced Multi-filter Seq2Seq Model\nProceedings of Intelligent Systems Conference (IntelliSys) 2022. Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems, Springer.\nBest Student Paper Award\nPatent\nUfuk Topcu,\nYunhao Yang\n, Cyrus Neary, and Jean-Raphaël Gaglione.\nAutomaton-Based Controller and Method with Generative Language Models for Task Execution\nUS Patent App. 18/958,684.\nAwards and Fellowships\nAmazon Fellow\n. Amazon Science Hub, 2024-2025.\nSpecial Departmental Honor in Computer Science\n. College of Natural Science, UT Austin, 2022.\nResearch Distinction\n. College of Natural Science, UT Austin, 2021.\nUndergraduate Research Fellowship\n. College of Natural Science, UT Austin, 2020.\nCommunity Services\nJournal and Conference Review\nArea Chair for MLSys 2025\nReviewer for Journal of Computational and Cognitive Engineering, NeurIPS, ICLR, TMLR, ICML\nProgram Committee for\nCSCT 2023\n,\nCSCT 2023\n,\nICCIS 2023\n,\nICIVC 2023\nVolunteer\nAutoDrive Lab Internship\n, 2025 and 2026\nSTEM Girl Day at UT Austin\n, 2024 and 2025\nMentor for REACT RUE summer program\n, 2023\nVolunteer for TACC Back@TACC, 2022 and 2024\nVolunteer for LASA High School Visit, 2023\nVolunteer for FIRST Technical Challenge: Texas-Central GEMS League Tournament, 2023"
