    "homepage_text": "Yihao Fang's home\nHome\nTeamNet\nCacheNet\nLogographic Subword Model\nYihao Fang\nPh.D.\n|\nCourse Director at York University\n|\nEntrepreneur\nTel: +1(647)632-9766\nEmail: yihao.fang@gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nBio: (\nCurriculum Vitae\n)\nYihao Fang received his Ph.D., M.Eng. from the\nDept. of Computing and Software\n,\nMcMaster University\nand his B.Eng. from Tongji University, P.R. China. In the past, Yihao Fang has worked with leading companies in the industry such as Hewlett-Packard and Oracle. He is an IEEE reviewer, and the CEO and founder of an Artificial Intelligence startup company:\nLexivalley Inc.\nPublications:\nFang, Yihao, Ziyi Jin, and Rong Zheng. \"TeamNet: A Collaborative Inference Framework on the Edge.\" In 2019 IEEE 39th International Conference on Distributed Computing Systems (ICDCS), pp. 1487-1496. IEEE, 2019.\nDou, Yangliu, Yihao Fang, Chuan Hu, Rong Zheng, and Fengjun Yan. \"Gated branch neural network for mandatory lane changing suggestion at the on-ramps of highway.\" IET Intelligent Transport Systems 13, no. 1 (2018): 48-54.\nFang, Yihao, Shervin Manzuri Shalmani, and Rong Zheng. \"CacheNet: A Model Caching Framework for Deep Learning Inference on the Edge.\" arXiv preprint arXiv:2007.01793 (2020).\nDou, Yangliu, Yihao Fang, Chuan Hu, Rong Zheng, and Fengjun Yan. \"Prediction of the Surrounding Vehicles?Discretionary Lane Changing Intention at Freeway: A Gated Recurrent Units Approach.\" DRIVER BEHAVIOUR PREDICTION MODELS USING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE ALGORITHMS AND STATISTICAL MODELING (2019): 71.\nFang, Yihao, Rong Zheng, and Xiaodan Zhu. \"Logographic Subword Model for Neural Machine Translation.\" arXiv preprint arXiv:1809.02592 (2018).\nJuly, 2019\nDr. Fang presented in IEEE 39th International Conference on Distributed Computing Systems (ICDCS).\nMarch, 2019\nDr. Fang received McMaster Faculty of Engineering SummerTech Entrepreneur Fellowship."
  },
