  "deep_homepage::Rong Wang::https://www.rongwangsna.com/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.rongwangsna.com/",
    "all_emails": [
      "r.wang@vanderbilt.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": "r.wang@vanderbilt.edu",
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/rong-w-08a48226/",
    "homepage_text": "Home - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nDr. Rong Wang\nAssistant Professor | Vanderbilt University\nDr. Wang’s work is conceptualized at the intersections of technology, networks and social impact. Always an advocate for a network approach, she is particularly interested in how to leverage the relationship dynamics among civil actors, corporations, government agencies, and individual citizens to help solve wicked social issues.\nResearchgate\nLinkedin-in\nTwitter\nNetwork Dynamics for Social Impact Lab\nDirected by Dr. Wang, the Network Dynamics for Social Impact Lab researches multilevel collaborative efforts to tackle complex social issues, with a focus on the role of nonprofits, social enterprises, and corporations in understanding root causes and locating effective solutions through partnerships.\nLearn More About The Lab\nResearch Projects\nAnti-Asian Hate Campaign (Active)\nU.S. Refugee Crisis (Active)\nCollective Impact & Education Reform\nOpenIDEO &\nCollaborative Crowdsourcing\nTwitter &\nNetworked Social Movements\nAre you interested in network analysis? How about strategic partnerships and tackling complex social issues?\nLet's Collaborate\nScroll to top\n\n---\n\nContact - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nContact\nVanderbilt University\nPeabody College\n230D Mayborn Building\n130 Magnolia Cir.\nNashville, TN 37240\nNew Number TBA\nr.wang@vanderbilt.edu\nFirst Name\nLast Name\nEmail\n*\nSubject\n*\nMessage\nComment\nSUBMIT\nScroll to top\n\n---\n\nContact - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nContact\nVanderbilt University\nPeabody College\n230D Mayborn Building\n130 Magnolia Cir.\nNashville, TN 37240\nNew Number TBA\nr.wang@vanderbilt.edu\nFirst Name\nLast Name\nEmail\n*\nSubject\n*\nMessage\nComment\nSUBMIT\nScroll to top\n\n---\n\nAbout Me - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nAbout Me\nCurrent Curriculum Vitae\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Human and Organizational Development (HOD)\nat\nPeabody College\n,\nVanderbilt University\n. Always an advocate for a network approach, I research collective action, open collaboration, and inter-organizational alliances that are designed to achieve collective goals. Most of my research projects are at the intersection of technology, networks, and social impact. At HOD, I direct the Network Dynamics for Social Change lab where I work with a team of undergraduate and graduate students to investigate how to scale impact for a variety of organizations and coalitions.\nMy work has appeared in major communication and organizational study journals such as Communication Monographs, Management Communication Quarterly, Journalism and Mass Communication Quarterly, Mass Communication & Society, Nonprofit and Voluntary Sector Quarterly, and Journal of Community Psychology. My research has been generously supported by the National Science Foundation, National Institutes of Health, International Development Research Centre (IDRC), the Army Research Office, Peabody College at Vanderbilt, University of Kentucky, DePaul University, and Northwestern University.\nI received my Ph.D. degree in Communication from the\nAnnenberg School for Communication & Journalism\nat the\nUniversity of Southern California (USC)\n. Originally from\nJiangsu China\n, I completed my Bachelor’s degree at\nNanjing University\n. I hold a Master’s degree from the\nDepartment of Communication and New Media\nat the\nNational University of Singapore\nand a Master’s degree in Communication from USC. Prior to joining Vandy, I was an Assistant Professor of Communication at University of Kentucky, and a Postdoctoral Research Associate at\nNetwork for Nonprofit and Social Impact\n, Northwestern University.\nScroll to top\n\n---\n\nAbout Me - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nAbout Me\nCurrent Curriculum Vitae\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Human and Organizational Development (HOD)\nat\nPeabody College\n,\nVanderbilt University\n. Always an advocate for a network approach, I research collective action, open collaboration, and inter-organizational alliances that are designed to achieve collective goals. Most of my research projects are at the intersection of technology, networks, and social impact. At HOD, I direct the Network Dynamics for Social Change lab where I work with a team of undergraduate and graduate students to investigate how to scale impact for a variety of organizations and coalitions.\nMy work has appeared in major communication and organizational study journals such as Communication Monographs, Management Communication Quarterly, Journalism and Mass Communication Quarterly, Mass Communication & Society, Nonprofit and Voluntary Sector Quarterly, and Journal of Community Psychology. My research has been generously supported by the National Science Foundation, National Institutes of Health, International Development Research Centre (IDRC), the Army Research Office, Peabody College at Vanderbilt, University of Kentucky, DePaul University, and Northwestern University.\nI received my Ph.D. degree in Communication from the\nAnnenberg School for Communication & Journalism\nat the\nUniversity of Southern California (USC)\n. Originally from\nJiangsu China\n, I completed my Bachelor’s degree at\nNanjing University\n. I hold a Master’s degree from the\nDepartment of Communication and New Media\nat the\nNational University of Singapore\nand a Master’s degree in Communication from USC. Prior to joining Vandy, I was an Assistant Professor of Communication at University of Kentucky, and a Postdoctoral Research Associate at\nNetwork for Nonprofit and Social Impact\n, Northwestern University.\nScroll to top\n\n---\n\nAbout Me - Rong Wang Ph.D.\nSkip to content\nRong Wang Ph.D.\nContact\nAbout Me\nCurrent Curriculum Vitae\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Human and Organizational Development (HOD)\nat\nPeabody College\n,\nVanderbilt University\n. Always an advocate for a network approach, I research collective action, open collaboration, and inter-organizational alliances that are designed to achieve collective goals. Most of my research projects are at the intersection of technology, networks, and social impact. At HOD, I direct the Network Dynamics for Social Change lab where I work with a team of undergraduate and graduate students to investigate how to scale impact for a variety of organizations and coalitions.\nMy work has appeared in major communication and organizational study journals such as Communication Monographs, Management Communication Quarterly, Journalism and Mass Communication Quarterly, Mass Communication & Society, Nonprofit and Voluntary Sector Quarterly, and Journal of Community Psychology. My research has been generously supported by the National Science Foundation, National Institutes of Health, International Development Research Centre (IDRC), the Army Research Office, Peabody College at Vanderbilt, University of Kentucky, DePaul University, and Northwestern University.\nI received my Ph.D. degree in Communication from the\nAnnenberg School for Communication & Journalism\nat the\nUniversity of Southern California (USC)\n. Originally from\nJiangsu China\n, I completed my Bachelor’s degree at\nNanjing University\n. I hold a Master’s degree from the\nDepartment of Communication and New Media\nat the\nNational University of Singapore\nand a Master’s degree in Communication from USC. Prior to joining Vandy, I was an Assistant Professor of Communication at University of Kentucky, and a Postdoctoral Research Associate at\nNetwork for Nonprofit and Social Impact\n, Northwestern University.\nScroll to top"
