    "homepage_text": "Prof. Xuelong Li, Intelligent Optic-Electronics, Imaging & Image processing\nSearch\nChinese\nHome\nHome\nOverview\nFaculty\nInstitution\nJoin Us\nHome\nOverview\nIntroduction\nLeader\nFaculty\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Professor\nGuest Scholar\nInstitution\nInstitution\nJoin Us\nTalent Introduction\nGraduate Enrollment\nHome\nOverview\nIntroduction\nLeader\nFaculty\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Professor\nGuest Scholar\nInstitution\nInstitution\nJoin Us\nTalent Introduction\nGraduate Enrollment\n×\nOn-site search\nFaculty\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Professor\nGuest Scholar\nFaculty\ncurrent position:\nFaculty\n>>\nProfessor\n>>\nContent\nXuelong Li, Professor\nPersonal Profile\nProfessor Xuelong Li, CTO of China Telecom, National Distinguished Chair, Chief\n                                    Scientist of\niOPEN\nPublications\n: \n[\nGoogle Scholar\n] | [\nDBLP\n] | [\n中文\n]\nResearch interests\n：AI, imaging & image processing, AI flow.\nPostal Address\n:\n127 West Youyi Road, 64#,\nXi'an Shaanxi 710072,\nP. R. China\nE-mail\n:  xuelong_li AT ieee.org\nEducation Background\nXuelong Li received his B.Eng. and Ph.D. degrees from The University of Science and Technology of China (USTC).\nWork Experience\nXuelong Li is the Chief Technology Officer (CTO) of China Telecom since 2023, and the director of the Institute of Artificial Intelligence (TeleAI) of China Telecom (2024). Before that, he was a full professor at The Northwestern Polytechnical University (2018-2023), a full professor at The Chinese Academy of Sciences (2009-2018), a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Reader at The University of London (2004-2009), a Lecturer at The University of Ulster (2003-2004), and he previously took positions at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, The Hong Kong University, The Microsoft Research, and The Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.\nMemberships (year elected)\n2009, Fellow of The Institution of Engineering and Technology (IEE/IET)\n2009, Fellow of The British Computer Society (BCS)\n2010, Fellow of The International Association for Pattern Recognition (IAPR)\n2010, Fellow of The International Society for Optics and Photonics (SPIE)\n2010, Inaugural Member (past) of The Global Young Academy (GYA)\n2011, Academician of The International Eurasian Academy of Sciences (IEAS)\n2011, Fellow of The Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers (IEEE)\n2012, Fellow of The Optical Society of America (OSA)\n2013, Fellow (Member) of The Higher Education Academy (HEA)\n2016, Fellow (FInstP) of The Institute of Physics (IOP)\n2016, Fellow of The American Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS)\n2017, Elected Member of The Academia Europaea/The Academy of Europe (AE)\n2017, Elected Member of The European Academy of Sciences and Arts (EASA)\n2018, Fellow of The Chinese Institute of Electronics (CIE)\n2020, Fellow of The American Institute for Medical and Biological Engineering (AIMBE)\n2020, Academician of The International Academy of Astronautics (IAA)\n2020, Fellow of The Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)\n2021, Fellow of The Asia-Pacific Artificial Intelligence Association (AAIA)\n2021, Fellow of The International Academy of Medical and Biological Engineering (IAMBE)\n2022, Academician of The International Academy for Systems & CYbernetic Sciences (IASCYS)\n2023, Fellow of The Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nAcademic Service\nExecutive Councilor (past) (first in China mainland) of The Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) (2021-2024)\nVice Chair (first in China) of\nIAPR Fellow Committee\n(2022-2024:2024-2026)\nAssociate Editor of IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\nFounding Chair (past) of IEEE SMC Technical Committee on Cognitive Computing\nMember (past) of IEEE CS Conference Activities Committee (CAC)\nSelection Committees for MIT TR35 China, Heidelberg Laureate Forum Young Researcher, fellow committees, international research proposal review committees,\netc.\nRecent Papers (since 2022)\nX. Li\n, \"\nPositive-incentive Noise\n,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (T-NNLS)\n,  vol. 35, no. 6, pp. 8708-8714, 2024.\nJ. Liu, Z. Ji, Y. Yu, J. Cao, Y. Pang, J. Han, and\nX. Li\n, \"Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning for Continual Learning: A Neural Tangent Kernel Perspective\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, 2026.\nH. Zhang, Y. Gu, F. Nie, and\nX. Li\n, \"Top-k Feature Selection in Sparse Learning via Accelerated Coordinate Descent Method\",\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, DOI: 10.1109/TPAMI.2026.3660366.\nH. Zhang, S. Huang, Y. Guo, and\nX. Li\n, \"Variational Positive-incentive Noise: How Noise Benefits Models,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, 2025.\nC. Wang, J. Lin, and\nX. Li\n, \"Structural-Equation-Modeling-Based Indicator Systems for Image Quality Assessment,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, 2025.\nC. Bai, K. Xu, S. Qiu, H. He, B. Zhao, Z. Wang, W. Li, and\nX. Li\n, \"On the Value of Myopic Behavior in Policy Reuse,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, 2025.\nP. Shamsolmoali, M. Zareapoor, H. Zhou, M. Felsberg, D. Tao, and\nX. Li\n, \"From Missing Pieces to Masterpieces: Image Completion with Context-Adaptive Diffusion,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, 2025.\nJ. Zhou, Z. He, D. Zhang, S. Liu, X. Fu, and\nX. Li\n, \"Spatial Residual for Underwater Object Detection,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, DOI: 10.1109/TPAMI.2025.3548652, 2025.\nF. Nie, R. Zhang, W. Yu, and\nX. Li\n, \"Unconstrained Fuzzy C-Means Algorithm,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern  Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\n, DOI: 10.