    "homepage_text": "Mengkang Hu | Homepage\nMengkang Hu 胡梦康\nI am a 2nd-year Ph.D. student at\nThe University of Hong Kong (HKU-MMLAB)\nguided by\nProf. Ping\n                      Luo (main)\nand\nProf.\n                      Wenping Wang\n.\nI am studying agents and particularly focusing on harnessing the potential of Large Language Models (LLMs) to enhance real-world applications.\nI also lead open-sourced projects like\n🦉OWL\nwith more than 15k github stars.\nPreviously, I also worked in Microsoft Research, Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, Tencent Hunyuan etc.\nMy current research agenda encompasses:\n1. General-purpose agentic systems (\nAgentGen\n);\n2. Context Engineering for LLM-based Agent (\nTree-Planner\n,\nHiAgent\n);\n3. World Models for LLM-based Agent (\nAgentGen\n,\nText2World\n).\nI am open to research discussions and collaborations, feel free to get in touch at [mkhu at connect\n                    dot hku dot hk]!\n/\n/\n/\nSelected Publications\nOWL: Optimized Workforce Learning for General Multi-Agent Assistance in Real-World Task Automation\nMengkang Hu\n, Yuhang Zhou, Wendong Fan, Yuzhou Nie, Bowei Xia, Tao Sun, Ziyu Ye, Zhaoxuan Jin, Yingru Li, Qiguang Chen, Zeyu Zhang, Yifeng Wang, Qianshuo Ye, Bernard Ghanem, Ping Luo, Guohao Li\nNeurIPS\n2025\npdf\n|\nsite\nText2World: Benchmarking Large Language Models for Symbolic World Model Generation\nMengkang Hu\n, Tianxing Chen, Yude Zou, Yuheng Lei, Qiguang Chen, Ming Li, Yao Mu, Hongyuan Zhang, Wenqi Shao, Ping Luo\nACL\n2025 Findings\npdf\n|\nsite\nHiAgent: Hierarchical Working Memory Management for Solving Long-Horizon Agent Tasks with Large Language Model\nMengkang Hu\n, Tianxing Chen, Qiguang Chen, Yao Mu, Wenqi Shao, Ping Luo\nACL\n2025\npdf\n|\ncode\nAgentGen: Enhancing Planning Abilities for Large Language Model based Agent via Environment and Task Generation\nMengkang Hu\n, Pu Zhao, Can Xu, Qingfeng Sun, Jianguang Lou, Qingwei Lin, Ping Luo, Saravan Rajmohan, Dongmei Zhang\nKDD\n2024\npdf\nKET-QA: A Dataset for Knowledge Enhanced Table Question Answering\nMengkang Hu\n, Haoyu Dong, Ping Luo, Shi Han, Dongmei Zhang\nCOLING\n2024\npdf\n|\nsite\nTree-Planner: Efficient Close-loop Task Planning with Large Language Models\nMengkang Hu\n, Yao Mu, Xinmiao Yu, Mingyu Ding, Shiguang Wu, Wenqi Shao, Qiguang Chen, Bin Wang, Yu Qiao, Ping Luo\nICLR\n2024\npdf\n|\nsite\nEmbodiedGPT: Vision-Language Pre-Training via Embodied Chain of Thought\nYao Mu, Qinglong Zhang,\nMengkang Hu\n, Wenhai Wang, Mingyu Ding, Jun Jin, Bin Wang, Jifeng Dai, Yu Qiao, Ping Luo\nNeurIPS\n2023\n(Spotlight)\npdf\n|\ncode\n|\nsite\nExperience\nResearch Intern\nat\nShanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory\nFebruary 2023 - February 2024  |  Shanghai, China\nMainly focus on better use of LLMs in Embodied AI (efficiency, world modeling) under the supervision by\nDr. Wenqi Shao\n.\nResearch Intern\nat\nMicrosoft Research Lab – Asia\nFebruary 2022 - September 2022  |  Beijing, China\nMainly focus on intersection of TableQA and Knowledge Graph under the supervision of\nSR. Haoyu Dong\nand\nSR. Research Manager Shi Han\n.\nAwards&Service\nReviewer of ICLR 2025, KDD 2025 (Research Track)\nMost Influential AAAI Papers (Top 11 in AAAI 2025)\nNational Scholarship (top 2%), 2021\nFirst-Class Scholarship, 2019-2022\nMSRA Stars of Tomorrow (Award of Excellent Intern), 2022\nNational First Prize in Mathematical Contest in Modeling (top 1%), 2020\nMathematical Contest in Modeling, Meritorious Winner, 2020,2021\nNational Third Prize in The 14th International Contest of innovAtioN, 2020\nInvited Talks\n2024.04.16\nSharing Tree-Planner at RLChina.\nslides\nLast update on April 2025.\nDesign and source code from\nJon Barron's website"
  },
