    "homepage_text": "WENHAO LI (李文昊) - Wenhao Li\nWENHAO LI (李文昊)\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes\nGoogle Scholar\n​\nSSRN\nEmail\nORCID\nNBER\nAssistant Professor of Finance and Business Economics\n,\nUSC Marshall School of Business\nNBER Faculty Research Fellow\n(Asset Pricing)\nPhD in Finance, 2014-2019,\nStanford GSB\n.\n​My research is at the intersection of macroeconomics and ﬁnance. My research aims to answer broad, policy-relevant questions: How is government debt priced, and how does government debt supply affect the ﬁnancial sector and the real economy? What are the mechanisms of ﬁnancial crises, and what roles do government and central bank interventions play?\nMy approach combines economic modeling, including continuous-time general equilibrium models, with empirical analysis on time-series and panel data, and quantification of dynamic models.\nRecent (and upcoming) presentations:\nFed Board Seminar,  Kansas Fed Seminar,  Yale Finance seminar, Georgetown Finance seminar, MFA meeting, WFA meeting\nSite powered by Weebly. Managed by\nDomain.com\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes\n\n---\n\nCV - WENHAO LI (李文昊)\nWENHAO LI (李文昊)\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes\nDownload my CV here\n.\nYour browser does not support viewing this document. Click\nhere\nto download the document.\nSite powered by Weebly. Managed by\nDomain.com\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes\n\n---\n\nCV - WENHAO LI (李文昊)\nWENHAO LI (李文昊)\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes\nDownload my CV here\n.\nYour browser does not support viewing this document. Click\nhere\nto download the document.\nSite powered by Weebly. Managed by\nDomain.com\nHome\nResearch\nCV\nDiscussions and Others\nData and Codes"
  },
