    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/xijunlee",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/xijun-ted-li-a7a8a1111/overlay/1635461853634/single-media-viewer/",
    "homepage_text": "Xijun Li (李希君)\nXijun Li (李希君)\nAssistant Professor @\nShanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU)\nPh.D. @\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\nE-mail: lixijun AT sjtu DOT edu DOT cn (preferred), xijun.lee AT hotmail DOT com\nAddress: Rm 1411, Software Bldg, 800 Dongchuan Road, Minhang, Shanghai, China\n[\nHomepage@SJTU\n] [\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nCurriculum Vitae\n] [\nGithub\n] [\nCountdown\n]\n【WE WANT YOU】\nFor research interns\n: Our lab is furnished with\nan abundant supply of Robotics/GPU/NPU/CPU\n, etc. We now open\nsufficient positions\navailable for\nresearch intern (科研实习生)\n[\n申请细则 (in Chinese)\n].\nFor prospective students\n: We are seeking self-driven\nPhD, Master and Undergraduate students\nwith a profound interest in\nLearning to Optimize\nand\nLarge Language Model for Optimization/Reasoning\n. If you are willing to collaborate with me, please feel free to send me an email at\nlixijun@sjtu.edu.cn\nalong with your CV to schedule an appointment.\nNews\n[11-03-2025] Congratulations to our group received 19th “Challenge Cup”, “AI+” Category,\nGrand Prize\n(第十九届挑战杯“人工智能+”专项赛\n特等奖\n) [\ncertificate\n] [\nmedia\n] [\npic1\n] [\npic2\n].\n[10-17-2025] I am selected as a\nNeurIPS\n2025 “Reviewer :\nTop Reviewer\n”.\n[09-25-2025] I gave a talk on the workshop of\n2025 Learning to Optimize in the Era of Large ModelsFrom Algorithmic Innovation to Cross-Industry Applications\norganized by Huawei.\n[09-19-2025] Three papers have been accepted by\nNeurIPS\n2025. Congrats to all co-authors!\n[09-05-2025] I have been invited by the organizers of\nICLR\n2026 to serve as an\nArea Chair\n.\n[08-27-2025] I am selected as\nPrincipal Investigator\nas National Natural Science Foundation of China: Young Scientist Program (\n国自然科学青年基金C类\n).\n[06-26-2025] I am selected as\nPrincipal Investigator\nas Shanghai Municipal Basic Research Program: Natural Science Foundation (\n上海市自然科学基金项目\n).\n[06-17-2025] Congratulations to Jiexiang for having his undergraduate thesis selected among the\ntop 5%\nas an\nOutstanding Thesis\nby the School of Computer Science, Shanghai Jiao Tong University!\n[04-09-2025] One paper has been accepted by\nTPAMI\n. Congrats to Yufei!\n[03-20-2025] Two papers have been accepted by\nICLR\n2025. Congrats to Zijie and Haoyang!\n[09-30-2024] I have concluded my period at Huawei Noah's Ark Lab. It was an exceptional chapter in my career. In October, I shall commence my role as an Assistant Professor at the School of Software, Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nAbout\nCurrently, Xijun is an assistant professor in Shanghai Jiao Tong University and a faculty member of the\nShanghai Key Labraotry of Scalable Computing and Systems\n. Previously, he has served as a princinpal researcher in Huawei Noah’s Ark Lab between 2018 and 2024. He has received his Ph.D. degree from the University of Science and Technology of China in March 2024 (HUAWEI-USTC Joint Ph.D. Program) under the supervision of\nProf. Jie Wang\nand received the master degree under the supervision of\nProf. Jianguo Yao\nfrom Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2018. He has published many papers on top peer-reviewed conferences and journals (such as TPAMI, NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, KDD, ICDE, SIGMOD, DAC, etc.) and applied/published a series of patents with Huawei Noah's Ark Lab. He has also won the championship of student learderboard in Dual Track of NeurIPS’21 ML4CO Competition. His recent research interests focus on Learning to Optimization (L2O) and Large Language Model for Optimization/Reasoning. Last but not least, he was one of core developers of the\nHuawei Cloud OptVerse AI Solver\nand\nHuawei Pangu Large Language Models\n.\nExperience\nOn Secondment, Ministry of Science and Technology of the People’s Republic of China, Jan. 2026 - present\nAssistant Professor, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, Oct. 2024 - present\nPrincipal Researcher, Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, Mar. 2024 - Sept. 2024\nSenior Research Engineer A, Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, Mar. 2022 - Feb. 2024\nSenior Research Engineer B, Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, Dec. 2019 - Feb. 2022\nResearch Engineer, Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, Apr. 2018 - Nov. 2019\nResearch Intern, Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, Aug. 2017 - Mar. 2018\nResearch\nRecent Interest\nLearning to Optimize\nLong-Horizon Planning for Robotics\nLarge Language Model for Optimization/Reasoning\nLarge Language Model for Code Optimization\nMathematical Programming Solver\nReinforcement Learning\nOperational Research\nMeta-Heuristic Algorithms\nApplications in Logistics, Supply Chain, Storage Systems, etc.\nPublication\nMengqi Guo,\nXijun Li\n#, Jianguo Yao: Level-Up: Iterative Optimization of Collaborative Planning and Solving Mechanism for Reasoning.\nCSCWD\n2026\nXijun Li\n, Jiexiang Yang, Jinghao Wang, Bo Peng, Jianguo Yao, Haibing Guan: STRCMP: Integrating Graph Structural Priors with Language Models for Combinatorial Optimization.\nNeurIPS\n2025 [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nMingxuan Ye, Jie Wang, Fangzhou Zhu, Zhihai Wang, Yufei Kuang,\nXijun Li\n, Weilin Luo, Jianye HAO, Feng Wu: Dynamic Configuration for Cutting Plane Separators via Reinforcement Learning on Incremental Graph.\nNeurIPS\n2025 [\npdf\n]\nKaijun Zhou, Xingyu Yan, Xingda Wei,\nXijun Li\n, Jinyu Gu: Multimodal Generation Made Efficient with Speculative Diffusion and Speculative Verification.\nNeurIPS\n2025 [\npdf\n]\nYufei Kuang,\nXijun Li\n*, Jie Wang, Fangzhou Zhu, Meng Lu, Zhihai Wang, Jia Zeng, Houqiang Li, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: Accelerate Presolve in Large-Scale Linear Programming via Reinforcement Learning. IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n) [\npdf\n]\nZijie Geng, Jie Wang,\nXijun Li\n, Fangzhou Zhu, Jianye HAO, Bin Li, Feng Wu: Differentiable Integer Linear Programming.\nICLR\n2025 (\nSpotlight\n) [\npdf\n]\nHaoyang Liu, Jie Wang, Zijie Geng,\nXijun Li\n, Yuxuan Zong, Fangzhou Zhu, Jianye HAO, Feng Wu: Apollo-MILP: An Alternating Prediction-Correction Neural Solving Framework for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming.\nICLR\n2025 [\npdf\n]\nHaoyang Liu, Jie Wang, Wanbo Zhang, Zijie Geng, Yufei Kuang,\nXijun Li\n, Bin Li, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: MILP-StuDio: MILP Instance Generation via Block Structure Decomposition.\nNeurIPS\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nJie Wang, Zhihai Wang,\nXijun Li\n, Yufei Kuang, Zhihao Shi, Fangzhou Zhu, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: Learning to Cut via Hierarchical Sequence/Set Model for Efficient Mixed-Integer Programming. IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n) [\npdf\n]\nZhihai Wang, Lei Chen, Jie Wang, Yinqi Bai, Xing Li,\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Jianye HAO, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: A Circuit Domain Generalization Framework for Efficient Logic Synthesis in Chip Design.\nICML\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nYufei Kuang, Jie Wang, Yuyan Zhou,\nXijun Li\n, Fangzhou Zhu, Jianye HAO, Feng Wu: Towards General Algorithm Discovery for Combinatorial Optimization: Learning Symbolic Branching Policy from Bipartite Graph.\nICML\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nHankun Cao, Shai Bergman, Si Sun, Yanbo Albert Zhou,\nXijun Li\n, Jun Gao, Zhuo Cheng, Ji Zhang: Answering the Call to ARMs with PACER: Power-Efficiency in Storage Servers.\nMSST\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nKecheng Huang,\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Ji Zhang, Zili Shao: Joint Directory, File and IO Trace Feature Extraction and Feature-based Trace Regeneration for Enterprise Storage Systems.\nICDE\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nYufei Kuang, Jie Wang, Haoyang Liu, Fangzhou Zhu,\nXijun Li\n, Jia Zeng, Jianye HAO, Bin Li, Feng Wu: Rethinking Branching on Exact Combinatorial Optimization Solver: The First Deep Symbolic Discovery Framework.\nICLR\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nChang Liu, Zhichen Dong, Haobo Ma, Weilin Luo,\nXijun Li\n, Bowen Pang, Jia Zeng, Junchi Yan: L2P-MIP: Learning to Presolve for Mixed Integer Programming.\nICLR\n2024 [\npdf\n]\nZijie Geng,\nXijun Li\n, Jie Wang, Xiao Li, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: A Deep Instance Generative Framework for MILP Solvers Under Limited Data Availability.\nNeurIPS\n2023 (\nSpotlight\n) [\npage\n] [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nYang Li, Xinyan Chen, Wenxuan Guo,\nXijun Li\n, Wanqian Luo, Junhua Huang, Hui-Ling Zhen, Mingxuan Yuan, Junchi Yan: HardSATGEN: Understanding the Difficulty of Hard SAT Formula Generation and A Strong Structure-Hardness-Aware Baseline.\nKDD\n2023 [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nXijun Li\n, Qingyu Qu, Fangzhou Zhu, Jia Zeng, Mingxuan Yuan, Jie Wang: Accelerating Linear Programming Solving by Exploiting the Performance Variability via Reinforcement Learning.\nAAAI\n2023 workshop on AI to Accelerate Science and Engineering [\npdf\n] [\nposter\n] [\nslides\n] [\nvideo\n]\nXijun Li\n*, Zhihai Wang*, Jie Wang, Yufei Kuang, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng, Yongdong Zhang, Feng Wu: Learning Cut Selection for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming via Hierarchical Sequence Model.\nICLR\n2023 [\npdf\n] [\nslides\n] [\ncode (MindSpore)\n] [\ncode (PyTorch)\n] [\nmedia\n]\nHan Lu, Zenan Li, Runzhong Wang, Qibing Ren,\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng, Xiaokang Yang, Junchi Yan: ROCO: A General Framework for Evaluating Robustness of Combinatorial Optimization Solvers on Graphs.\nICLR\n2023 [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nHongduo Liu, Peiyu Liao, Mengchuan Zou, Bowen Pang,\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Tsung-Yi Ho, Bei Yu: Layout Decomposition via Boolean Satisfiability.\nDAC\n2023 [\npdf\n] [\nslides\n]\nYiyuan Yang, Rongshang Li, Qiquan Shi,\nXijun Li\n, Gang Hu, Xing Li, Mingxuan Yaun: SGDP: A Stream-Graph Neural Network Based Data Prefetcher.\nIJCNN\n2023 [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nWenxuan Guo, Hui-Ling Zhen,\nXijun Li\n#, Mingxuan Yuan, Yaohui Jin, Junchi Yan: Machine Learning Methods in Solving the Boolean Satisfiability Problem.\nMachine Intelligence Research\nJournal [\npdf\n]\nJiayi Zhang, Chang Liu,\nXijun Li\n#, Hui-Ling Zhen, Junchi Yan, Mingxuan Yuan: A Survey for Solving Mixed Integer Programming via Machine Learning.\nNeurocomputing\nJournal [\npdf\n]\nQingyu Qu, Kexin Liu,\nXijun Li\n, Yunfan Zhou, Jinhu Lv: Satellite Observation and Data-Transmission Scheduling using Imitation Learning based on Mixed Integer Linear Programming.\nIEEE Transactions on Aerospace and Electronic Systems\n,\nTAES\n[\npdf\n]\nJi Zhang,\nXijun Li\n#, Xiyao Zhou, Mingxuan Yuan, Zhuo Cheng, Keji Huang, Yifan Li: L-QoCo: learning to optimize cache capacity overloading in storage systems.\nDAC\n2022: 379-384 (CORE A, CCF A) [\npdf\n]\nXijun Li\n*#, Yunfan Zhou*, Jinhong Luo, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng, Jianguo Yao: Learning to Optimize DAG Scheduling in Heterogeneous Environment.\nMDM\n2022: 137-146 (CORE A, CCF C) [\npdf\n] [\nvideo\n] [\nslides\n]\nQingyu Qu,\nXijun Li\n#, Yunfan Zhou; Yordle: An Efficient Imitation Learning for Branch and Bound.\nNeurIPS\n2021 ML4CO Competition [\npdf\n]\nXijun Li\n, Weilin Luo, Mingxuan Yuan, Jun Wang, Jiawen Lu, Jie Wang, Jinhu Lü, Jia Zeng: Learning to Optimize Industry-Scale Dynamic Pickup and Delivery Problems.\nICDE\n2021: 2511-2522 (CORE A, CCF A) [\npdf\n] [\nslides\n]\nYingtian Tang, Han Lu,\nXijun Li\n#, Lei Chen, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng: Learning-Aided Heuristics Design for Storage System.\nSIGMOD\n2021: 2597-2601 (CORE A*, CCF A) [\npdf\n] [\nvideo\n]\nZhenkun Wang, Hui-Ling Zhen, Jingda Deng, Qingfu Zhang,\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng: Multiobjective Optimization-Aided Decision-Making System for Large-Scale Manufacturing Planning.\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n52(8): 8326-8339 (2022) (CORE A, CCF B) [\npdf\n]\nHui-Ling Zhen, Zhenkun Wang,\nXijun Li\n, Qingfu Zhang, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng; Accelerate the optimization of large-scale manufacturing planning using game theory.\nComplex & Intelligent Systems\n; 1-12 [\npdf\n]\nXijun Li\n, Mingxuan Yuan, Di Chen, Jianguo Yao, Jia Zeng: A Data-Driven Three-Layer Algorithm for Split Delivery Vehicle Routing Problem with 3D Container Loading Constraint.\nKDD\n2018: 528-536 (CORE A*, CCF A) [\npdf\n] [\nvideo\n] [\nmedia\n]\nXijun Li\n, Jianguo Yao, Mingxuan Yuan, Jia Zeng: A Two-Layer Algorithmic Framework for Service Provider Configuration and Planning with Optimal Spatial Matching.\nCIKM\n2018: 2273-2281 (CORE A, CCF B) [\npdf\n]\nXijun Li\n, Jianguo Yao, Xue Liu, Haibing Guan: A First Look at Information Entropy-Based Data Pricing.\nICDCS\n2017: 2053-2060 (CORE A, CCF B) [\npdf\n]\n李希君\n, 上海, 上海交通大学: 基于信息熵的数据交易定价研究 [\nmaster thesis\n]\nwhere ‘*’ indicates the equal contribution and ‘#’ stands for corresponding author.\nGrant\n(PI)\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China: Young Scientist Program (国自然科学青年基金C类, 2026-2028, 300,000 RMB)\n(PI)\nShanghai Municipal Basic Research Program: Natural Science Foundation (上海市自然科学青年基金, 2025-2028, 250,000 RMB)\n(PI)\n“AI for Engineering” Empowerment Program, Category B, at SJTU (上海交通大学2025年度“Alfor Engineering”赋能计划B类, 2025-2027, 500,000 RMB)\n(PI)\nStartup Fund for Young Faculty at SJTU (SFYF at SJTU, 上海交通大学新进教师启动计划, 2024-2027)\n(PI)\nFunding Program from Aviation Key Laboratory of Science and Technology on Aerospace Vehicle (空天飞行器技术航空科技国家重点实验室基金, 2025-2026)\n(Core)\nNational Key Research and Development Program of China on the Next Generation Artificial Intelligence under the National Science and Technology Innovation 2030 Initiative​ (科技创新 2030 –“新一代人工智能”重大项目,\nCore Member\n, 2022-2025, ~6,000,000 RMB)\nSelected Award\n19th “Challenge Cup”, “AI+” Category,\nGrand Prize\n(第十九届挑战杯“人工智能+”专项赛\n特等奖\n) (as instructor), 2025, 共青团中央，中国科协，教育部等  [\ncertificate\n]\nBattlefield Heroes Award (战地英雄奖), 2024, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nSiye Special Research Award for Pangu LLM (四野特别攻关奖), 2024, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nPresidential Individual Award (总裁个人奖), 2023, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nPresidential Individual Award (总裁个人奖), 2023, Supply Chain Department, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nBattlefield Heroes Award (战地英雄奖), 2022, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nQuality Star Award (质量之星奖), 2021, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nGold Medal Team Award (金牌团队奖), 2020, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate1\n] [\ncertificate2\n]\nInnovation Pioneer Award (创新先锋奖), 2020, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nExcellent New Employee (优秀新员工), 2018, 2012 Labs, Huawei Technologies [\ncertificate\n]\nOutstanding Graduate, Jun 2018, Shanghai Jiao Tong University [\ncertificate\n]\nNational Scholarship\n(国家奖学金  / top 5% out of all students), 2017, Chinese Ministry of Education [\ncertificate\n]\nNational Scholarship\n(国家奖学金 / top 5% out of all students), 2014, Chinese Ministry of Education [\ncertificate\n]\nSkyworth Enterprise Scholarship (创维企业奖学金 / top 5%), First Prize, 2015, Skyworth Enterprise [\ncertificate\n]\nMathematical Contest in Modeling,\nMeritorious Award\n, 2014, Consortium for Mathematics and Its Applications [\ncertificate\n]\nPatent\nCN120996196A 开放具身环境融合模型和符号求解器的长程规划方法及系统：\n李希君\n，朱晔，姚建国\nCN120578395A 面向组合优化问题的结构可感知的代码生成方法及系统：\n李希君\n，姚建国\nCN116661676A 一种带宽控制方法、数据处理系统及相关设备：\n李希君\n，周云帆，李文思，张霁，袁明轩\nCN111738409A 一种资源调度的方法及其相关设备：\n李希君\n，罗威林，陆佳文，袁明轩\nCN116468099A 一种模型结构的优化方法及装置：\n李希君\n，朱方舟，甄慧玲，付小津，陆梦，曾嘉，袁明轩\nCN115496247A 一种业务数据的处理方法以及装置：\n李希君\n，郝晓田，袁明轩，郝建业，曾嘉\nCN117370715A 基于云计算技术的目标函数求解方法、装置和计算设备：\n李希君\n，李建树，王治海，曾嘉\n92041897CN02 一种数学规划实例生成的方法、系统和电子设备：\n李希君\n，安志武，朱方舟，耿子介，王杰\nCN117371674A 目标规划问题的求解方法、选择节点的方法及装置：\n李希君\n，杨沐明，匡宇飞，曾嘉\nCN116933908A 一种计算机任务处理方法及其相关设备：陆梦，甄慧玲，\n李希君\n，朱方舟，袁明轩，曾嘉\nCN111915060A 组合优化任务的处理方法以及处理装置： 甄慧玲，王振坤，\n李希君\n，张青富，袁明轩\nCN114237835A 一种任务求解方法及其装置：朱方舟，罗万千，甄慧玲，\n李希君\n，袁明轩，曾嘉\nCN112818280B 一种信息处理方法以及相关设备：甄慧玲，王振坤，张青富，\n李希君\n，韩雄威\nCN114117715A 多目标任务...[truncated]"
