    "homepage_text": "Yun Cheng's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYun Cheng's Homepage\nYun Cheng\nUniversity of Chicago\nABOUT ME\nI am currently a PhD student  in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\nat the\nUniversity of Chicago\n, and my advisor is\nMatt Emerton\n. I'm expected to graduate in the June of 2019.\nMy research lies in the area of algebraic number theory, in particular concerning Galois representations and modular forms. I aim to understand modular forms from two aspects: the congruence relationship between different modular forms, and the Galois representations that arise from them.\nHere you can find my\nCV\n.\nCONTACT INFORMATION\n5734 S University Ave\nChicago, IL 60615\nEmail: yc9z [at]  math [dot] uchicago [dot] edu\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Chun Kai Ling::https://lingchunkai.github.io/": {
