    "homepage_text": "Academic\nSearch\nChun Kai Ling\nAssistant Professor, Computer Science\nNational University of Singapore, School of Computing\nBiography\nI am an Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer Science in\nNational University of Singapore\n(NUS). My research is on multiagent systems and computational game theory. Prior to joining NUS, I was at Columbia University working with Professors\nChristian Kroer\nand\nGarud Iyengar\n.\nI completed my PhD at Carnegie Mellon University under the supervision of\nZico Kolter\nand\nFei Fang\n, where I studied how to apply machine learning for large scale general-sum game solving, as well as inverse problems in game theory.\nI am interested in (i) modeling games for real-world applications, such as those in cybersecurity, logistics, and select recreational games and (ii) studying and characterizing appropriate equilibrium concepts for such games and how to efficiently compute them.\nMy current projects include attacker-defender structured games played on graphs, language agents for games of negotiation and bayesian persuasion, games with incomplete information, and sound opponent exploitation.\nIf you are a prospective student interested in working in multiagent systems, feel free to send an email reaching out for a discussion!\nDownload my\nresumé\n.\nInterests\nArtificial Intelligence\nMachine Learning\nGame Theory\nEducation\nPhD in Computer Science, 2017-2023\nCarnegie Mellon University\nBEng in Computer Engineering, 2015\nNational University of Singapore\nRecent Publications\nHao Luan\n,\nYi Xian Goh\n,\nSee-Kiong Ng\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n(2026).\nProjected Coupled Diffusion for Test-Time Constrained Joint Generation\n.\n  Accepted to\nICLR 2026 main track\n.\nPreprint\nSalam Afiouni\n,\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nChristian Kroer\n(2025).\nColonel Blotto with Battlefield Games\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2026 main track (Oral)\n.\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChin Hui Han\n,\nChristian Kroer\n,\nGarud Iyengar\n(2025).\nSecurity Games with Layered Defenses: Adaptive Adversaries and Gittins Indices\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2026 main track (Oral)\n.\nLangyuan Cui\n,\nHwee Tou Ng\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n(2025).\nGame of Thought: Robust Information Seeking with Large Language Models Using Game Theory\n.\n  Accepted to\nICAPS 2025 LM4Plan Workshop\n.\nHao Luan\n,\nSee-Kiong Ng\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n(2025).\nDDPS: Discrete Diffusion Posterior Sampling for Layered Graphs\n.\n  Accepted to\nICLR 2025 FPI workshop\n.\nPDF\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChin Hui Han\n,\nChristian Kroer\n,\nGarud Iyengar\n(2025).\nHow Deep Is Your Defense-in-Depth? Hardening Cybersecurity Network Control Against Adaptive Attackers\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2025 Artificial Intelligence for Cyber Security (AICS) workshop\n.\nPreprint\nSalam Afiouni\n,\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nChristian Kroer\n(2024).\nCommitment to Sparse Strategies in Two-Player Games\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2025 main track\n.\nPDF\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nDarshan Chakrabarti\n,\nJingwen Zhang\n,\nGabriele Farina\n,\nChristian Kroer\n,\nGarud Iyengar\n(2024).\nContested Logistics: A Game Theoretic Approach\n.\n  In\nGameSec 2024\n. Best Paper Award (out of 3).\nPDF\nDavin Choo\n,\nThemistoklis Gouleakis\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nArnab Bhattacharyya\n(2024).\nOnline bipartite matching with imperfect advice\n.\n  Accepted to\nICML 2024 main track\n.\nPreprint\nJakub Cerny\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nChristian Kroer\n,\nGarud Iyengar\n(2024).\nLayered Graph Security Games\n.\n  Accepted to\nIJCAI 2024 main track\n.\nPreprint\nPaul Pu Liang\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nYun Cheng\n,\nAlexander Obolenskiy\n,\nYudong Liu\n,\nRohan Pandey\n,\nAlex Wilf\n,\nLouis-Philippe Morency\n,\nRuss Salakhutdinov\n(2024).\nQuantifying Interactions in Semi-supervised Multimodal Learning: Guarantees and Applications\n.\n  Accepted to\nICLR 2024 Main Track\n.\nPreprint\nWeijia Zhang\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nXuanhui Zhang\n(2023).\nDeep Copula-based Survival Analysis for Dependent Censoring with Identifiability Guarantees\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2024 Main Track\n.\nPDF\nYixuan Xu\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nFei Fang\n(2023).\nLearning Coalition Structures with Games\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2024 Main Track\n.\nPDF\nPaul Pu Liang\n,\nYun Cheng\n,\nXiang Fan\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nSuzanne Nie\n,\nRichard J. Chen\n,\nZihao Deng\n,\nNicholas Allen\n,\nRandy Auerbach\n,\nFaisal Mahmood\n,\nRuslan Salakhutdinov\n,\nLouis-Philippe Morency\n(2023).\nQuantifying & Modeling Multimodal Interactions: An Information Decomposition Framework\n.\n  In\nNeurips 2023 Main Track\n.\nPDF\nZimeng Song, Chun Kai Ling, Fei Fang\n(2023).\nMulti-defender Security Games with Schedules\n.\n  In\nGameSec 2023\n. Best Paper Award.\nPDF\nSamuel Sokota\n,\nRyan D'Orazio\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nDavid J Wu\n,\nJ Zico Kolter\n,\nNoam Brown\n(2023).\nAbstracting Imperfect Information Away from Two-Player Zero-Sum Games\n.\n  In\nICML 2023 Main Track\n.\nPreprint\nPDF\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter, Fei Fang\n(2022).\nFunction Approximation for Solving Stackelberg Equilibrium in Large Perfect Information Games\n.\n  In\nAAAI 2023 main track\n(oral).\nPreprint\nCode\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nFei Fang\n(2022).\nSafe Subgame Resolving for Extensive Form Correlated Equilibrium\n.\n  In\nAAAI 2022 main track\n(oral).\nPreprint\nSlides\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nFei Fang\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\n(2020).\nDeep Archimedean Copulas\n.\n  Accepted to\nNeurips 2020 main track\n.\nPDF\nCode\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nNoam Brown\n(2020).\nSafe Search for Stackelberg Equilibria in Extensive-Form Games\n.\n  Accepted to\nAAAI 2021 main track\n.\nPDF\nCode\nSlides\nDmitrii Kharkovskii\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nBryan Kian Hsiang Low\n(2020).\nNonmyopic Gaussian Process Optimization with Macro-Actions\n.\n  In\nAISTATS\n.\nPDF\nGabriele Farina\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nFei Fang\n,\nTuomas Sandholm\n(2019).\nCorrelation in Extensive-Form Games: Saddle-Point Formulation and Benchmarks\n.\n  In\nNeurips main track\n.\nPDF\nGabriele Farina\n,\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nFei Fang\n,\nTuomas Sandholm\n(2019).\nEfficient Regret Minimization Algorithm for Extensive-Form Correlated Equilibrium\n.\n  In\nNeurips main track (Oral)\n.\nPDF\nChun Kai Ling, Fei Fang, J. Zico Kolter\n(2019).\nLarge Scale Learning of Agent Rationality in Two-Player Zero-Sum Games\n.\n  In\nAAAI 2019 main track\n.\nPDF\nCode\nSlides\nChun Kai Ling, Fei Fang, J. Zico Kolter\n(2018).\nWhat game are we playing? End-to-end learning in normal and extensive form games\n.\n  In\nIJCAI 2018 main track\n. Distinguished Paper Award..\nPDF\nCode\nPoster\nChun Kai Ling, J. Zico Kolter, Fei Fang\n(2017).\nWhat game are we playing? Differentiably learning games from incomplete observations\n.\n  In\nNIPS 2017 Deep RL Symposium\n.\nPreprint\nPDF\nPoster\nChun Kai Ling\n,\nLow Kian Hsiang\n,\nPatrick Jaillet\n(2016).\nGaussian Process Planning with Lipschitz Continuous Reward Functions\n.\n  In\nAAAI\n.\nPreprint\nPDF\nPoster\nContact\nchunkail[at]nus.edu.sg\nNational University of Singapore, Computing 1, 13 Computing Drive, Singapore, 117417\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
