    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hongxin Wei\nHongxin Wei\nAssistant Professor, SDS, Southern University of Science and Technology\nI am an Assistant Professor (Principal investigator, PhD supervisor) in\nthe Department of Statistics and Data Science\nat\nSUSTech\n(China, Shenzhen). I obtained my Ph.D. degree at the\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering\n,\nNanyang Technological University\n, supervised by\nProf. Bo An\n. During my Ph.D, I was fortunate to work as a visiting scholar in the group of\nProf. Sharon Yixuan Li\nat the\nUniversity of Wisconsin Madison\nin 2022. Previously I spent a wonderful year as a research assistant in\nthe Institute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences\nat Tsinghua University. Prior to that, I received my B.E. in Software Engineering from\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nin 2016.\nMy research interest falls in the scope of reliable machine learning (uncertainty estimation), and its applications in data optimization and privacy. Generally, we expect deep learning models to produce precise estimation of their uncertainty in predictions, using the form of probabilities (confidences in ML) or conformal prediction sets. Besides, my research is closely related to data-centric machine learning and foundation model, like data quality and efficiency. We are also interested in the statistic theory of data selection in machine learning, which provides theoretical principles to guide the data optimization in machine learning workflows.\nWe are always actively looking for Postdocs, PhDs, and RA/interns to join our research.\nNews\n2025-01\nI will be serving as a reviewer for JASA.\n2025-09\nWe will host NeurIPS 2025 Seminar @ Shenzhen during Nov 22-23,\nClick here to sign up\n.\n2025-09\nI will be serving as a Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\n2025-05\nThree papers are accepted by ICML 2025. Congratulations to Shuoyuan and Hao Zeng!\n2025-02\nI will be serving as a Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025.\n2025-01\nThree papers are accepted by ICLR 2025. Congratulations to Wenyu, and Hengxiang!\n2025-01\nI will be serving as a SPC for IJCAI 2025.\n2024-11\nI will be serving as a Area Chair for ICML 2025.\n2024-09\nTwo papers are accepted by NeurIPS 2024. Congratulations to Hongfu Gao!\n2024-07\nWe release a Chinese Content Moderation Benchmark for LLMs:\nChineseSafe-Benchmark\n.\n2024-05\nI am accepting Mphil and PhD applications (2025 fall). I am always looking for highly-motivated research interns, RAs and PostDocs to join our research (refer to\nthis page\n).\n2024-05\nFour papers are accepted by ICML 2024.\n2024-03\nI will be serving as a Area Chair for NeurIPS 2024.\n2024-01\nThree papers are accepted by ICLR 2024 (Two are Spotlights).\n2023-12\nWe release a Python toolbox for conformal prediction research\nTorchCP\n.\n2022-10\nI am honored to be recognized as\nTop Reviewers\nin NeurIPS 2022.\n2022-05\nTwo papers are accepted by ICML 2022 (Accept rate: 21.9%).\n2021-10\nI am honored to receive NeurIPS 2021\nOutstanding Reviewer Award\n(top 8% of reviewers).\nPapers\nWorking Papers\nSelected Publications\n*\nCorresponding author\n†\nEqual contribution\nLoading publications...\nAcademic Service\nArea Chair\n: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR\nSenior PC\n: IJCAI\nConference Reviewer\n: CVPR, ICCV, KDD, ACL\nJournal Reviewer\n: JASA, JMLR, TPAMI, IJCV, ACM Computing Surveys\nLab Members\nOur research group at SUSTech focuses on reliable machine learning, uncertainty estimation, data optimization, and privacy. We aim to develop deep learning models that can produce precise estimation of their uncertainty and improve data quality and efficiency in machine learning workflows.\nCurrent members\nHao Zeng\nPostdoc\nPh.D., Xiamen University (co-supervised with Prof. B. Jing)\nShuoyuan Wang\nPh.D. Student\nM.S., University of Macau\nHengxiang Zhang\nPh.D. Student\nM.S., UESTC\nHanjie Yang\nPh.D. Student\nM.S., DUT\nXiaoqi Qiu\nPh.D. Student\nM.S., SZU\nZhenlong Liu\nPh.D. Student\nB.S., SUSTech\nBeier Luo\nMaster Student\nB.S., SUSTech\nCong Ding\nMaster Student\nNow Intern at Tencent\nJiaxi Ren\nMaster Student\nB.S., SUSTech\nXuhui Yi\nMaster Student\nB.S., WUST\nHuajun Xi\nResearch Assistant\nB.S., SUSTech\nHaotian Zhang\nResearch Intern\nM.S. student, DUT\nWenbo Liao\nResearch Intern\nPh.D. student, CUHK\nQingyang Hao\nResearch Intern\nM.S., THU(SZ)\nYuhan Li\nResearch Intern\nUndergraduate student, SDU(Weihai)\nZihao Shi\nResearch Intern\nM.S. student, FDU\nPast Members\nJianguo Huang\nResearch Intern (2023-2024)\nPh.D. student at NTU, Singapore\nQiqi Tao\nResearch Intern (2024)\nPh.D. student at SUTD, Singapore\nHongfu Gao\nResearch Intern (2024)\nPh.D. student at NUS\nJianqing Song\nResearch Intern (2024)\nPh.D. student at Nanjing University\nWenyu Jiang\nResearch Intern (2023-2024)\nPh.D. student at Nanjing University\nKangdao Liu\nResearch Intern (2024)\nPh.D. student at University of Macau\nQiang Hu\nUndergraduate student at SUSTech (2025)\nPh.D. student at SUNY Buffalo\nXuanning Zhou\nResearch Intern (2024-2025)\nMphil at CUHK(SZ)"
  },
