    "homepage_text": "Xiao HUANG Homepage\nXiao HUANG\n☰\n×\nHome\nPeople\nResearch\nPublications\nGoogleScholar\nCourses\nXiao HUANG\nAssistant Professor, Department of Computing\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nResearch:\nlarge language models\n(graph retrieval-augmented generation, LLM-based text-to-SQL),\ngraph learning\n(knowledge graphs, collaborative filtering),\nprotein design\n. I am actively recruiting Ph.D. students and postdocs. Feel free to\nemail\nme your CV.\n[2026/2] We released three Surveys:\nAgent Memory\n,\nGraph RAG\n,\nText-to-SQL\n[2026/1] We have three papers accepted by ICLR 2026.\n[2026/1] We have\none paper\naccepted by TheWebConf 2026.\n[2026/1] Our\nGraph RAG for education\nproject has been funded.\n[2025/10] Our ITF project\nGraph RAG\nhas been funded.\n[2025/10] We released three\nGraph RAG\ndatasets.\nSelected Publications (\nmore papers\n)\nRetrieval-augmented generation\nA Survey of Graph Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Customized Large Language Models\n, Qinggang Zhang, Shengyuan Chen, Yuanchen Bei, Zheng Yuan, Huachi Zhou, Zijin Hong, Junnan Dong, Hao Chen, Yi Chang,\nXiao Huang\n, arXiv preprint arXiv:2501.13958, 2025. (\nGitHub\n)\nRetrieval Augmented Zero-Shot Enzyme Generation for Specified Substrate\n, Jiahe Du, Kaixiong Zhou, Xinyu Hong, Zhaozhuo Xu, Jinbo Xu,\nXiao Huang\n, ICML 2025.\nKnowGPT: Knowledge Graph based PrompTing for Large Language Models\n, Qinggang Zhang, Junnan Dong, Hao Chen, Daochen Zha, Zailiang Yu,\nXiao Huang\n, NeurIPS 2024.\nLLM-based text-to-SQL\nKnapsack Optimization-based Schema Linking for LLM-based Text-to-SQL Generation\n, Zheng Yuan, Hao Chen, Zijin Hong, Qinggang Zhang, Feiran Huang, Qing Li,\nXiao Huang\n, IEEE International Conference on Data Engineering, 2026.\nStructure-Guided Large Language Model for Text-to-SQL Generation\n, Qinggang Zhang, Hao Chen, Junnan Dong, Shengyuan Chen, Feiran Huang,\nXiao Huang\n, ICML, 2025 (\nSlides\n).\nNext-Generation Database Interfaces: A Survey of LLM-based Text-to-SQL\n, Zijin Hong, Zheng Yuan, Qinggang Zhang, Hao Chen, Junnan Dong, Feiran Huang,\nXiao Huang\n, IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering, 2025.\nGraph learning\nEach Graph is a New Language: Graph Learning with LLMs\n, Huachi Zhou, Jiahe Du, Chuang Zhou, Chang Yang, Yilin Xiao, Yuxuan Xie,\nXiao Huang\n, ACL (Findings), 2025. (\nCode\n)\nDirichlet Energy Constrained Learning for Deep Graph Neural Networks\n, Kaixiong Zhou,\nXiao Huang\n, Daochen Zha, Rui Chen, Li Li, Soo-Hyun Choi, Xia Hu, NeurIPS, 2021.\nTowards Deeper Graph Neural Networks with Differentiable Group Normalization\n, Kaixiong Zhou,\nXiao Huang\n, Yuening Li, Daochen Zha, Rui Chen, Xia Hu, NeurIPS, 2020.\nProtein design\nRetrieval Augmented Zero-Shot Enzyme Generation for Specified Substrate\n, Jiahe Du, Kaixiong Zhou, Xinyu Hong, Zhaozhuo Xu, Jinbo Xu,\nXiao Huang\n, ICML, 2025.\nKnowledge graphs\nKnowledge Graph Embedding Based Question Answering\n,\nXiao Huang\n, Jingyuan Zhang, Dingcheng Li, Ping Li,\nWSDM\n2019 (\nACM version\n,\nSlides\n,\nCode\n).\nCollaborative filtering\nLLM Collaborative Filtering: User-Item Graph as New Language, Huachi Zhou, Yujing Zhang, Hao Chen, Qinggang Zhang, Qijie Shen, Feiran Huang,\nXiao Huang\n, AAAI, 2026.\nMacro Graph Neural Networks for Online Billion-Scale Recommender Systems\n, Hao Chen, Yuanchen Bei, Qijie Shen, Yue Xu, Sheng Zhou, Wenbing Huang, Feiran Huang, Senzhang Wang,\nXiao Huang\n, TheWebConf, 2024 (\nACM version\n).\nGraph Cross-Correlated Network for Recommendation\n, Hao Chen, Yuanchen Bei, Wenbing Huang, Shengyuan Chen, Feiran Huang,\nXiao Huang\n, IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering, 2024.\nServices\nOrganization committee member:\nICDE 2025 (PhD Symposium Chair)\n,\nPAKDD 2026 (Doctoral Consortium Chair)\nSPC member/Area Chair: KDD 2026, ICLR 2026, PAKDD 2026, EACL 2026, AAAI 2026\nPC member: ICML 2021-2026, SIGIR 2026, ICLR 2022-2026, NeurIPS 2021-2025, IJCAI 2020-2025, AAAI 2021-2023, KDD 2019-2023, TheWebConf 2022-2023, CIKM 2019-2022, WSDM 2021-2023, SDM 2022, ICKG 2020-2021\nReviewer: TPAMI, IEEE TKDE, ACM TKDD, ACM Computing Surveys, ACM TOIS, IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, IEEE Transactions on Big Data, IEEE TCSS, ACM TIST\nSession Chair: WSDM 2023, IJCAI 2023, AAAI 2026\nEditorial board member:\nComputers & Education: X Reality\nAwards and Patents\nBest Paper Award Honorable Mention\nat SIGIR 2023\nBest Poster Presentation Award\nat PolyU Academy for Interdisciplinary Research Conference 2023\nBEST PAPER\nat the International Conference On Web-Based Learning 2022, Tenerife, Spain\nUS Patent,\nKNOWLEDGE-GRAPH-EMBEDDING-BASED QUESTION ANSWERING\n, US 2020/0242444 A1\nMedia Coverage\nPolyU Research and Innovation Office, Technology Showcase\nPolyU COMP News, IEEE final year project competition\nPolyU hosts IEEE ICDE 2025\nBiography\nDr. Xiao Huang is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Computing at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. He earned his Ph.D. in Computer Engineering from Texas A&M University in 2020, an M.S. in Electrical Engineering from the Illinois Institute of Technology in 2015, and a B.S. in Engineering from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2012. His research interests encompass LLM reasoning, retrieval-augmented generation, text-to-SQL, graph learning, knowledge graphs, and recommender systems. His scholarly contributions are highly regarded within the academic community, amassing over 5,700 citations. He received the Best Paper Award Honorable Mention at SIGIR 2023. He has successfully led or completed seven research projects as Principal Investigator, securing total funding exceeding 5 million HKD. He serves as a PhD Symposium Chair for ICDE 2025 and a Doctoral Consortium Chair for PAKDD 2026. He ranked among the World's Top 2% Scientists (Stanford List) for 2023, 2024, and 2025. Before his appointment at PolyU, he gained valuable experience as a research intern at Microsoft Research and Baidu USA.\nLast edited  on February 11\nth\n2026  10:52PM (Time Zone: HKT)."
  },
