    "homepage_text": "Yuhao Zhou\nEmail\n: zhou1437 [at] purdue.edu\nzhou [at] race.t.u-tokyo.ac.jp\nzhou.yuha [at] northeastern.edu\nyzhou035 [at] e.ntu.edu.sg\nYuhao Zhou is a third-year Ph.D. student at\nMARS Lab\n,\nPurdue University\n, working with\nProf. Yu She\n.\nHe did his Master at\nMobile Robotics Laboratory\n,\nThe University of Tokyo\n, supervised by\nProf. Jun Ota\n. Before that, he was with\nNanyang Technological University\n, Singapore. He attended Chengdu Shude High School for his middle and high school education.\nHis current research interests include tactile sensing and dexterous manipulation.\nCurriculum Vitae\n/\nGitHub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\nNews\n[see more]\n[06/2025]: Presented a poster in\nMWRW\n@ TTIC.\n[08/2024]: Our IROS'24 paper is covered by\nTechXplore\n.\n[04/2024]: Presented a poster in\nMWRW\n@ TTIC.\n[09/2023]: Won the Outstanding Master Thesis Award (修士論文優秀賞).\n[07/2023]: Presented a paper in AIM'23 @ Seattle, USA.\n[03/2022]: Received Google Travel Grant.\n[10/2021]: Received JASSO Scholarship from MEXT, Japan.\n[08/2021]: Our robot Jet-HR2 is covered by IEEE Spectrum.\n[06/2020]: Won the Outstanding Undergraduate Thesis Award. (top 3%)\nEducation\n[08/2023 - Present] Purdue University, West Lafayette, IN\nDoctor of Philosophy, Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering\n[08/2023 - 12/2025] Purdue University, West Lafayette, IN\nMaster of Science, Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering\n[10/2021 - 09/2023] The University of Tokyo, Japan\nMaster of Engieering, Department of Precision Engineering\n[Thesis]\n[01/2021 - 05/2021] Nanyang Technological University, Singapore\nMaster Student, School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering\n[09/2016 - 06/2020] Guangdong University of Technology, China\nBachelor of Engieering, Department of Electrical Engineering and Automation\n[Thesis]\nPublications\n(* denotes equal contribution)\nFirst Author:\nYuhao Zhou\n,\nSheeraz Athar\n*,\nZhixian Hu\n*,\nBinghao Huang\n,\nYunzhu Li\n,\nJuan Wachs\n, and\nYu She\nVTAP Gripper: Synergizing Fingertip Sensing and a Visuo-Tactile Active Palm for Dexterous In-Hand Manipulation\nUnder Review\nYuhao Zhou\n,\nWon Suk Lee\n,\nYan Gu\n, and\nYu She\nTactile-Reactive Gripper with an Active Palm for Dexterous Manipulation\nNature Portfolio Journal Robotics\n[Paper]\n[Video]\nYuhao Zhou\n*,\nPokuang Zhou\n*,\nShaoxiong Wang\n, and\nYu She\nIn-Hand Singulation, Scooping, and Cable Untangling with a 5-DOF Tactile-Reactive Gripper\nAdvanced Robotics Research\n[Paper]\n[Video]\n[Website]\nCover Feature\n[link]\nYuhao Zhou\n,\nPokuang Zhou\n,\nShaoxiong Wang\n, and\nYu She\nIn-Hand Singulation and Scooping Manipulation with a 5 DOF Tactile Gripper\nIROS 2024\n[Preprint]\n[Paper]\n[Poster]\n[Video]\n[BibTex]\nCovered by:\n[TechXplore]\n[机器人大讲堂]\nYuhao Zhou\n, Ryota Takamido, Masako Kanai-Pak, Jukai Maeda, Yasuko Kitajima, Mitsuhiro Nakamura, Noriaki Kuwahara, Taiki Ogata, and\nJun Ota\nDevelopment of a Nursing Skill Training System Based on Manipulator Variable Admittance Control\nAIM 2023\n[Paper]\n[BibTex]\nYuhang Li*,\nYuhao Zhou\n*, Junbing Huang, Zijun Wang, Shunjie Zhu, Kairong Wu, Li Zheng, Jiajin Luo, Rui Cao,\nYun Zhang\n&\nZhifeng Huang\nJet-HR2: A Flying Bipedal Robot Based on Thrust Vector Control\nRA-L\nwith\nICRA 2022\noption\n[Preprint]\n[Paper]\n[Video]\n[BibTex]\nCovered by:\n[IEEE Spectrum Column]\n[IEEE Video Friday]\n[GDUT News]\n[机器之心]\nCo-Authored:\nRyota Takamido,\nYuhao Zhou\n, Masako Kanai-Pak, Jukai Maeda, Yasuko Kitajima, Mitsuhiro Nakamura, Noriaki Kuwahara, Taiki Ogata, and\nJun Ota\nImmersive and Manipulator-Based Robot Patient System for Learning Wheelchair Transfers in Nursing Education\nRevision in Progress at\nT-LT\nZhifeng Huang\n, Zijun Wang, Jiapeng Wei, Jingtao Yu,\nYuhao Zhou\n, Pihao Lao, Xiaoliang Huang,\nXuexi Zhang\n&\nYun Zhang\nThree-Dimensional Posture Optimization for Biped Robot Stepping over Large Ditch Based on a Ducted-Fan Propulsion System\nIROS 2020\n[Paper]\n[Video]\n[BibTex]\nTeaching\n[08/2024 - 12/2024]: \r\n                Teaching Assistant,\nIE474 Industrial Control Systems\n, Fall 2024, Purdue University.\n[01/2024 - 05/2024]: \r\n                Teaching Assistant,\nIE574 Industrial Robotics And Flexible Assembly\n, Spring 2024, Purdue University.\nReviewer Service\nIEEE RoboSoft 2026\nIEEE RA-L 2025\nJ-FR 2025\nIEEE T-IE 2025\nIEEE/RSJ IROS 2024\nExperience\n[07/2019 - 08/2019]: \r\n                Summer Intern @\nCloudMinds Robotics (Beijing) Co., Ltd.\nMiscellaneous\nLove traveling alone (been to\n11 countries\n) /\nPhotography\n/ Chinese calligraphy.\nSpeak Mandarin, English, Szechwanese, a little Japanese and Cantonese."
