    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Prof. Dr. Qing Ye -\nDeutsch\nIntern\nIntern\nDE\nStop animation\nProf. Dr. Qing Ye\nProf. Dr. Qing Ye\nContact\nProf. Dr. Qing Ye\nInstitute of Inorganic Chemistry\nUniversity of Würzburg\nAm Hubland\n97074 Würzburg / Germany\nroom: C2.01.026\nphone: +49 931 31 88611 ­\nqing.ye@uni-wuerzburg.de\nProfiles\nORCID\n0000-0002-7238-0407\nResearchGate\nfollow us on Twitter\n@The_Ye_Lab\nThe Ye Group\nResearch\nRecent Publications\nS. Parua, Q. Ye*,\nElectron precise boron-containing three-membered rings\n,\nCoord. Chem. Rev.\n558, 217742 (2026)\nL. Xiang, J. Wang, A. Matler, I. Krummenacher, H. Braunschweig, Q. Ye*,\nA Lewis Superacidic Borirane Derivative Featuring a Tris(carboranyl)borane Environment,\nInorg. Chem.\n64, 25428 (2025)\nNews\n15.2.2026 - Our review paper on electron precise boron-containing three-membered rings has just been accepted by Coord. Chem. Rev. Congrats to Sudipta and the entire team!\n12.2.2026 - Our work on crystalline water adducts of a dual-site Lewis superacidic borane has just been accepted by Inorg. Chem. Congrats to Julius and the entire team!\n30.12.2025 - Our work on harnessing o-carborane to access the BN-ketenimine structure has just been accepted by Inorg. Chem. Congrats to Libo and the entire team!\n09.12.2025 - Our work on a Lewis superacidic borirane has just been accepted by Inorg. Chem. Congrats to Libo and the entire team!\n05.12.2025 - Our work on the isocyanide insertion reaction of a carborane-fused borirane has just been accepted by Inorg. Chem. Front. Congrats to Libo and the entire team!\n08.08.2025 - Our Flash Communication on inorganic alkyne Click (\nia\nClick) has just been accepted by Organometallics. Congrats to Libo and the entire team!\n05.08.2025 - Ms. Bohan Yao and Ms. Beibei Zhang, Visiting Students from Zhengzhou University, have commenced their three-month exchange study in Würzburg. Welcome to the team!\n28.07.2025 - Mr. Martin Lutz has joined us to complete his final thesis for teacher training (Zulassungsarbeit). Welcome to the team!\n11.04.2025 - Our work on bis(alkynyl)boranes has just been accepted by Angew. Chem. Congrats to Chenchang, Alex and the entire team!\n10.03.2025 - Our work on carbophosphinocarbene has just been accepted by Angew. Chem. Congrats to Libo, Junyi and the entire team!\n03.03.2025 - Mr. Albert Vargas Pueyo, an Erasmus student from Spain, has joined us to complete his Bachelor's thesis. Welcome to the team!\n07.10.2024 - Our collaborative work with the Lin Group (HKUST) on antiaromatic 2-azaboroles with π\n4\nσ\n2\nelectronic configuration has just been accepted by\nJACS\n. Congrats to our Ph.D. student, Leibo Tan, and the entire team for this achievement!\n02.10.2024 - Congratulations to our Ph.D. student, Ms. Libo Xiang, whose work on structure-constrained tris(\northo\n-carboranyl)borane has just been accepted by\nChem. Sci.\n30.09.2024 - Two new Ph.D. students! Mr. Ajay Bain and Mr. Sudipta Parua joined our group. Welcome to Germany.\n05.08.2024 - Ms. Yi Jing, a Visiting Student from the Chen group at Zhengzhou university, has commenced her three-month exchange study in Würzburg. Welcome to the team!\n24.06.2024 - Congrats to our Ph.D. student, Ms. Libo Xiang, whose work on 3D 9-bromo-9-borafluorene has just been published in Dalton Trans.\n30.05.2024 - Work led by Prof. Ji on the full electron delocalization across the carborane cluster has been accepted for publication in\nJACS\n. Congratulations!\n04.03.2024 - Ms. Andrea Gisbert Albacar, an Erasmus student from Spain, has joined us to complete her Bachelor's thesis. Welcome to the team!\n12.02.2024 - Our latest collaborative work with the Lin Group (HKUST) has been accepted by\nChem. Sci.\nCongrats to Junyi, Libo and the entire team!\n12.12.2023 - Our review paper on borirane and borirene chemistry has been accepted by\nChem. Eur. J.\nThis is an invited review, dedicated to Professor Holger Braunschweig on the occasion of his 62nd birthday.\n28.09.2023 - Our latest collaborative work with the Holthausen Group (Uni Frankfurt) on benzoborirene chemistry has just been published in\nAngew. Chem.\nCongrats to Xiaocui (Postdoc) and the entire team for this achievement! This work is in memory of Professor Peter Paetzold.\n14.08.2023 - Congrats to Junyi Wang on her outstanding PhD defense. We extend our heartfelt gratitude to co-supervisor Prof. Zhenyang Lin and all the defense committee members at HKUST. We wish Junyi a bright future filled with continued success.\n24.05.2023 - Congrats to Yashi (3rd year Master student) and Wenbo (Postdoc), whose work on SED catalyst has just been published in\nChem. Commun.\n15.05.2023 - New Master student. Mr. Julius Bolch has joined us to complete his Master's thesis. Welcome to the team.\n05.05.2023 - We've just installed another brand new single glovebox station in our lab!\n27.04.2023 - Congrats to our Ph.D. student, Ms. Libo Xiang, whose work on 3D 9-borafluorene radical has just been published in\nChem. Eur. J.\n26.04.2023 - Congrats to our joint Ph.D student, Ms. Junyi Wang, whose work on converting bis(alkynyl)boranes to BN-butafulvenes has been published in\nAngew. Chem.\n17.04.2023 - Two new students, Ms. Aigul Urazova and Mr. Sebastian Knaup, have joined us to complete their Bachelor's thesis. Welcome to the team!\n21.03.2023 - A great honor that our DFG projects have been mentioned in \"\nEinblick\n\". Thanks to\nMr. Emmerich\nfor the kind interview.\n20.03.2023 - Two new students to our group. Ms. Chenchang Ma has joined us to complete her Master's thesis, and Ms. Clara Canals Martí, an exchange student from Spain, has joined us to complete her Bachelor's thesis. Welcome to the team!\n03.03.2023 - Great news! Our DFG proposal on Benzoborirene Chemistry has been recommended for funding. We are thrilled and eagerly look forward to delving deeper into this fascinating class of molecules.\n01.03.2023 - New Postdoc. Dr. Alexander Matler joined our group. Welcome on board.\n20.12.2022 - We are thrilled that our DFG proposal on \"Synthesis and Investigation of Bis(alkynyl)boranes – Coordination Chemistry and Beyond\" has been recommended for funding! This is the best New Year and Christmas gift for the group and we are very excited to persue the Science in the coming years!\n04.11.2022 - Congrats to our undergraduate Mr. Chonghe Zhang and graduate Ms. Junyi Wang, whose work on 3D 9-borafluorenes is published in\nInorg. Chem.\n02.11.2022 - New Master student. Mr. Marvin Linus Richter joined our group. Welcome on board.\n24.10.2022 - Congrats to our undergrate Mr. Yuxiang Wei and graduate Ms. Junyi Wang, whose work on non-coordinated and highly Lewis acidic borirane is published in\nChem. Eur. J.\n18.10.2022 - Congrats to our RAP Dr. Wei Su, whose work on uranium complexes with a pendant borane Lewis acid is published in\nAngew. Chem.\n17.10.2022 - New Ph.D. student. Ms. Libo Xiang has moved with us from SUSTech to JMU. Welcome to Germany.\n07.10.2022 - A brand new single glovebox station stands now in our laboratory. One more is on the way.\n31.07.2022 - New Ph.D. student. Mr. Leibo Tan joined our group. Welcome to Germany.\n17.06.2022 - Congrats to our undergraduate Mr. Chonghe Zhang, whose work on Lewis superacidic azido boranes is published in\nAngew. Chem.\n01.06.2022 - Congrats to our joint Ph.D student Ms. Junyi Wang, whose work on carboranyl iminoborane is published in\nInorg. Chem.\n21.04.2022 - Congrats to our joint Ph.D student Mr. Yan Dai, whose work on 1,6;2,3-bis-BN cyclohexane is published in\nJACS\n.\nYe Group@JMU is officially established in 1/2022\nContact\nUniversität Würzburg\nSanderring 2\n97070 Würzburg\nFind Contact\nSanderring\nRöntgenring\nHubland Nord\nHubland Süd\nCampus Medizin\nHome\nThe University\nStudying at JMU\nResearch\nTeaching\nInstitutions\nInternational\nThe University\nNews\nEvents\nDates and Deadlines\nDegree Programmes and Subjects\nVacancies\nStaff Members\nGlossary of Administrative Terms\nServices\nUniversity Library\nIT Services\nUniversity Sport\nAcademic Advisory Service\nExamination Office\nStudent Affairs\nStudent Representation\nCareer Centre\nYour JMU\nWueStudy\nWueCampus\nClass Schedule\nOnline Enrolment\nLibrary Catalogue\nContact\nPhone and Address Directory\nHow to Find Us\nPress\nHotline of Academic Advisory Service\nTechnical Maintenance Service\nNeed help quickly?\nPage options\nSitemap\nPicture credits\nTo top\nLast update:\n11.03.2026\nPage:\n245049/989\nPicture credits\nImprint + Privacy Policy\nPrivacy Disclaimer\nBarrierefreiheit"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yifan Lu::https://www.pacific.edu/campus-directory/yifan-lu": {
    "homepage": "https://www.pacific.edu/campus-directory/yifan-lu",
    "all_emails": [
      "ylu@pacific.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yifan Lu | University of the Pacific\nSkip to main content\nClose\nAcademics\nSchools & Colleges\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nOnline Graduate Programs\nDual-Degree Programs\nProfessional Development & Continuing Education\nAcademic Support\nResearch & Scholarship\nAdmission & Aid\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nAdmitted Students Next Steps\nLaw\nDental\nPharmacy\nInternational Students\nFinancial Aid & Cost\nFour-Year Guarantee\nCommunity Involvement Program\nAbout Pacific\nOur Campuses\nFast Facts and Rankings\nStudent Outcomes\nCommunity Impact\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion\nSustainability\nPresident Callahan\nUniversity Leadership\nHistory & Mission\nPacific In the News\nPacific Newsroom\nStudent Life\nActivities & Programs\nHousing & Dining\nStudent Services\nCareer Services\nHealth & Wellness\nParent Engagement\nSafety & Conduct\nMore\nsearch\nClose\nClose\nBreadcrumb\nYifan Lu\nYifan Lu\nAssistant Professor\nStockton\nEmail Address:\nylu@pacific.edu\nAt Pacific Since:\n2025\nYifan Lu ’19\n, PhD earned his bachelor of science in pharmaceutical science and master of science in pharmaceutics from Fudan University in Shanghai. He earned his doctor of philosophy in pharmaceutical and chemical sciences from University of the Pacific.\nGrowing up in a family with a pharmacist and a high school chemistry teacher, he developed a deep respect for science and its ability to improve lives. Pursuing pharmaceutical sciences allowed him to combine his creativity, curiosity and enthusiasm for problem-solving into meaningful innovation.\nDr. Lu has experience in analytical research and development, Good Manufacturing Practices, pharmaceutical manufacturing and quality control validation. He earned a Good Clinical Practice training certification at GlaxoSmithKline. Dr. Lu is a member of the American Association of Pharmaceutical Scientists.\nDr. Lu has explored the realms of academia, pharmaceutical industry and entrepreneurship in both Asian and North America. He has firsthand experience with Investigational New Drug and New Drug Application regulatory submissions to the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), the European Union’s European Medicines Agency (EMA) and the People’s Republic of China’s National Medical Products Administration. Dr. Lu also represented different teams during inspections by the FDA, EMA and the California Department of Public Health. These inspections covered a wide range of operations, from manufacturing to clinical trials.\nHe enjoys blending creativity and science, from laboratory formulations to culinary experiments at home. In the kitchen, he combines Asian and international flavors. As a certified youth soccer coach and referee, he promotes teamwork and discipline among young players in the Stockton community. A musician with a wide range of interests, he plays the accordion, piano, guitar and drums.\nEducation\nBS in Pharmaceutical Science, Fudan University, China\nMS in Pharmaceutics, Fudan University, China\nPhD in Pharmaceutical and Chemical Sciences, University of the Pacific\nTeaching Interests\nTeaching Philosophy\n“Teaching through integration — connecting theory with practical application across the drug development lifecycle. My goal is to cultivate curiosity, critical thinking and problem-solving skills, preparing students to navigate real-world challenges.”\nCourses\nBSPS 110 - Introduction to Pharmaceutical Analysis\nBSPS 130 - Quality in Pharmaceuticals: Control and Assurance\nResearch Focus\nResearch Summary\n“My research focuses on how medicines are developed and formulated to ensure they are safe, effective and high-quality — from the initial lab concepts to clinical use.”\nResearch Interests\nPharmaceutical analysis, including analytical method development and validation to meet research and regulatory requirements\nTranslation of academic discoveries into clinically ready pharmaceutical products, with a focus on practical problem-solving and troubleshooting in complex formulation and manufacturing challenges\nNanotechnology-based drug formulation and characterization aligned with regulatory standards\nApplication of AI, computational modeling and advanced analytical instrumentation to support target validation and drug candidate optimization, including binding affinity prediction, ADME profiling, developability assessment and data-driven formulation design\nClose Search"
  },
