    "homepage_text": "Yiqi Zhong | Applied Sciences | Microsoft\nSkip to main content\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nApplied Sciences\nApplied Sciences\nApplied Sciences\nSearch\nSearch or ask a question\nNo results\nCancel\nApplied Sciences\nApplied Sciences\nPeople\nYiqi Zhong\nSenior Researcher\nYiqi Zhong is a senior researcher in Microsoft’s Applied Sciences Group (ASG).\nShe received her Ph.D. degree in computer science from the University of Southern California in 2023, advised by Dr. Ulrich Neumann. \n\t\t\t\t\tHer research interests lie in multimodal deep learning for visual perception and prediction tasks.\nDuring her internships in ASG in 2022 and 2023, she focused on developing efficient video prediction models.\nApart from her research, Yiqi enjoys playing video games, playing sports such as tennis, and spending time with her cat, Pipi.\nContact\nFollow our team\nShare this page on"
