  "deep_homepage::Jike Zhong::https://jike338.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://jike338.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "jikezhon@usc.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/jonbarron",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About — Jike Zhong\nJike Zhong\nI am a second-year PhD student at the University of Southern California (USC). I work primarily with\nProf. Konstantinos Psounis\n(he is fantastic!) on\nmultimodal foundation models\n, I also work closely with\nProf. Sai Praneeth Karimireddy\n. My recent research focuses on\nvisual and multimodal reasoning, post-training with reinforcement learning, and post-training for personalized intelligence.\nBefore PhD I spent a year with the data science team at Salesforce working on LLM products. Prior to that I completed Bachelor's in CS and Stat at Ohio State University (OSU, 2019-2022), advised by great\nProf. Wei-Lun Chao\nand\nDr. Hong-You Chen\n. I have also spent some wonderful time at CCVL lab at Johns Hopkins University (JHU), supervised by\nBloomberg Distinguished Prof. Alan Yuille\n.\nI'm deeply drawn to research that enhances our fundamental understanding of large models, from data curation, pre-training, to post-training. We live in an exciting time of AI revolution, if you have ideas to discuss or collaborate, feel free to reach out! I can be reached at jikezhon@usc.edu\nLast update was in 09/2025.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\nWhat's New\nFull list of publications can be found on my\nGoogle Scholar\npage.\n2025-09:\nTo Think Or Not Think\naccepted to NeurIPS 2025 as Spotlight\n2025-07:\nNew paper on\nautoregressive motion prediction\nwill appear as Oral in MICCAI '25 workshops\n2025-05:\nInternship with congnition team at HRI with\nProf. Shao-Yuan Lo\n2025-04:\nWe release\nTo Think Or Not Think\nand show that thinking is not always beneficial for RL post-training\n2025-04:\nWe release\nMed-R1\n, reinforcement finetuning for medical MLLM reasoning\n2025-03:\nNew paper on\nbenchmarking multimodal performance on EEE\naccepted at CVPR '25\n2024-09:\nNew paper on\nvision-language finetuning\naccepted at EMNLP '24\n2024-08:\nStarted PhD at USC\nMisc.\nI'm a big aviation fan. I love anything related to it, flying, photography, model collection... Check them out below or on\nJetPhotos\nand\nAirliners\n.\nI also enjoy classic piano and opera, especially those by Franz Liszt (Hungarian Rhapsody) and Bellini (I Puritani).\nCode stolen from\nJon Barron\n, many thanks!"
  },
