    "homepage_text": "Jia Li's Homepage\nJia Li (李佳)\nI am the tenure-track Assistant Professor of\nCollege of AI\nat\nTsinghua University\n. I obtained my PhD degree from\nPeking University\nin 2025, supervised by Prof.\nZhi Jin\nand Prof.\nGe Li\n.\nI lead the Tsinghua AI Agent Group and work closely with Prof.\nShi-Min Hu\n. Recently, our group focuses on the following questions:\nHow to improve the foundational capabilities of AI agents? Such as reasoning, memory, tool-calling, efficiency, safety, and multi-agent collaboration.\nHow to build powerful AI agents for real-world tasks? Such as software engineering agents, scientific research agents, etc.\nI am looking for\nhighly-motivated interns\nto join my group. Feel free to email me with your resume attached.\njia_li(at)mail.tsinghua.edu.cn\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nTwitter\nORCID\nNews\n2025\nOur paper (DAVSP) has been accepted by AAAI 2026.\nNov 08\nOur paper (AdapTrack) has been accepted by ICSE 2026.\nOct 16\nOur paper (M2CVD) has been accepted by TOSEM 2025.\nOct 09\nOur paper (aiXcoder-7B-v2) has been accepted by ASE 2025.\nSep 26\nCongratulations! Four of our papers were accepted by NeurIPS 2025, including one Spotlight and three Poster papers!\nSep 19\nI joined the College of AI at Tsinghua University as an assistant professor!\nAug 01\nI passed the defense of my PhD thesis!\nMay 22\nCongratulation, our two papers are accepted by ACL 2025!\nMay 16\nOur paper\nLine-level Semantic Structure Learning for Code Vulnerability Detection\nhas been accepted by Internetware 2025.\nApr 16\nOur paper\nEscalating LLM-based Code Translation Benchmarking into the Class-level Era\nhas been accepted by ISSTA 2025.\nFeb 28\nSelected Publications\n(view all\n)\nSATURN: SAT-based Reinforcement Learning to Unleash Language Model Reasoning\nHuanyu Liu,\nJia Li\n,\nHao Zhu,\nYihong Dong,\nKechi Zhang,\nGe Li\nThe Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2025)\n, Just Accepted, 2025\nSpotlight (3.2%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nSATURN: SAT-based Reinforcement Learning to Unleash Language Model Reasoning\nHuanyu Liu,\nJia Li\n,\nHao Zhu,\nYihong Dong,\nKechi Zhang,\nGe Li\nThe Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2025)\n, Just Accepted, 2025\nSpotlight (3.2%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\naiXcoder-7B: A Lightweight and Effective Large Language Model for Code Processing\nSiyuan Jiang*,\nJia Li*\n,\nHe Zong,\nHuanyu Liu,\nHao Zhu,\nShukai Hu,\nErlu Li,\nJiazheng Ding,\nYu Han,\nWei Ning,\nGe Li\n(*\nequal contribution\n)\nThe 47th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2025 SEIP Track)\n, Pages 215-226, 2025\nOral\n[Paper]\n[Code]\naiXcoder-7B: A Lightweight and Effective Large Language Model for Code Processing\nSiyuan Jiang*,\nJia Li*\n,\nHe Zong,\nHuanyu Liu,\nHao Zhu,\nShukai Hu,\nErlu Li,\nJiazheng Ding,\nYu Han,\nWei Ning,\nGe Li\n(*\nequal contribution\n)\nThe 47th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2025 SEIP Track)\n, Pages 215-226, 2025\nOral\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nEvoCodeBench: An Evolving Code Generation Benchmark with Domain-Specific Evaluations\nJia Li\n,\nGe Li\n,\nXuanming Zhang,\nYihong Dong,\nZhi Jin\n,\nBinhua Li,\nFei Huang,\nYongbin Li\nThe 38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024 D&B Track)\n, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Data]\nEvoCodeBench: An Evolving Code Generation Benchmark with Domain-Specific Evaluations\nJia Li\n,\nGe Li\n,\nXuanming Zhang,\nYihong Dong,\nZhi Jin\n,\nBinhua Li,\nFei Huang,\nYongbin Li\nThe 38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024 D&B Track)\n, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Data]\nStructured Chain-of-Thought Prompting for Code Generation\nJia Li\n,\nGe Li\n,\nYongmin Li,\nZhi Jin\nACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (TOSEM)\n, Volume 34, Issue 2, Pages 1-23, 21 January 2025\n[Paper]\nStructured Chain-of-Thought Prompting for Code Generation\nJia Li\n,\nGe Li\n,\nYongmin Li,\nZhi Jin\nACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (TOSEM)\n, Volume 34, Issue 2, Pages 1-23, 21 January 2025\n[Paper]\nAll publications"
