    "homepage_text": "Home-Wang Group\nOur overall research objective focuses on the development of hierarchically structured nanomaterials to study cell-cell interactions and the cooperative response of cells to extracellular matrixes. We are also interested in the area of bionanomaterials, particularly with the respect of polymers and biomolecules, such as proteins, viruses, and bacteriophages.\nDr. Qian Wang\nChair of Chemistry and Biochemistry, at U\nof\nSC\nCarolina Distinguished Professor\nB.A. (1992) & Ph.D.(1997), Tsinghua University\nPostdoc. (97-99), University of Lausanne\nPostdoc & Senior Res. Associate (99-03),\nThe Scripps Research Institute\nEmail: wang263@mailbox.sc.edu\nPhone: 803-777-8436\nFax: 803-777-9521\nWelcome to Wang Group!\nWelcome to Wang Group!\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nNews\nGroup\nThe W. M. Keck Lab\nGallery\nLink\n03/17/2025\nMany congrats to Jingyu! He has successfully defended his dissertation today on the topic of Engineering Bioactive Surfaces: The Role of TMV-RGD1 in Cell Aggregation and Differenciation. Happy for his big achievement.\n03/07/2025\nCongratulations to Shan! She has been awarded as one of top 3 finailists for the competition for Senior Graduate Student Achievement Awards!!\n04/03/2024\nBig shoutout to Shan for scoring the SPARC Graduate Research Grant with a proposal entitled \"An effective way to immobilize cytochrome P450 monooxygenase using a redox mediator as an electrical wiring to enhance electron transfer efficiency \"\n??\nKeep shining bright, Shan!\n07/01/2023\nCongratulations to Dr. Wang on becoming the new chair of UofSC CHemistry and Biochemistry! We truly believe that with your leadership and insight, you are the perfect fit for leading our department!\n5/15/2023\nNan receives a Research Grants - One-Year Grants for Doctoral Candidates from German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD) to do research at Universität Heidelberg, which is one of top 3 universities in Germany.\nSo proud of you Nan!!\n4/5/2023\nCongratulation to Nan! She recently got 3 travel awards from James R. Durig, ASBMB Grad Students Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Award and Grad School Travel grant.\nSo proud of your hardwork!!\n10/18/2022\nMany Congratulations to\nTao Li\nwho was our former group member!! He was selected as a recipient of\nthe 2022 Emerging Researcher Award\ngranted by ACS Division of Energy and Fuel.\n05/03/2022\nA new cover paper!! Congrats to Yihua!! Please click and check.\n\"Enzyme Immobilization on a Delignified Bamboo Scaffold as a Green Hierarchical Bioreactor.\"\nNews\nClick Here for More News"
  },
