    "homepage_text": "Chenjie WANG\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nDr. Chenjie WANG, 王晨杰\n(Former)\nh-index\n813\nScopus Citations\n16\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2007\n2022\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0000-0001-6556-0824\nScopus Author ID:\n36182177900\nImpact\nMetrics for Academic and Research Impact\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Chenjie WANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n1\nSimilar Profiles\nGauge Theory\nPhysics\n100%\nTopological Phase\nMathematics\n83%\nFermion\nPhysics\n77%\nQuasiparticle\nPhysics\n49%\nDomain Wall\nPhysics\n38%\nNonequilibrium Steady States\nPhysics\n38%\nFluctuation Theorem\nPhysics\n38%\nTransportation\nPhysics\n38%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n19\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n1\nWorking paper\nRotation symmetry-protected topological phases of fermions\nCheng, M. &\nWang, C.\n,\nMay 2022\n,\nIn:\nPhysical Review B.\n105\n,\n19\n, 195154.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nTopological Phase\n100%\nFermion\n100%\nSymmetry Group\n16%\nTwo Dimensions\n16%\nThree-Dimension\n16%\n18\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n240\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nFolding approach to topological order enriched by mirror symmetry\nQi, Y., Jian, C.-M. &\nWang, C.\n,\n15 Feb 2019\n,\nIn:\nPhysical Review B.\n99\n,\n8\n, 085128.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nTopological Order\n100%\nPermutation\n33%\nReflective Symmetry\n33%\nPhysical System\n33%\nTopological Phase\n33%\n13\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n63\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nTopological quantum field theory for Abelian topological phases and loop braiding statistics in (3+1)-dimensions\nWang, Q.-R., Cheng, M.,\nWang, C.\n& Gu, Z.-C.,\n15 Jun 2019\n,\nIn:\nPhysical Review B.\n99\n,\n23\n, 235137.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nQuantum Field Theory\n100%\nQuasiparticle\n33%\nQuantum Statistics\n33%\n27\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n98\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nLattice model constructions for gapless domain walls between topological phases\nBao, C., Yang, S.,\nWang, C.\n& Gu, Z.-C.,\n3 Jan 2018\n,\nCornell University\n,\n16 p.\n(arXiv).\nResearch output\n:\nWorking Papers\n›\nWorking paper\nLattices\n100%\nTopological Phase\n100%\nDomain Wall\n100%\nSymmetry Group\n33%\nTensor\n33%\nLoop Braiding Statistics and Interacting Fermionic Symmetry-Protected Topological Phases in Three Dimensions\nCheng, M., Tantivasadakarn, N. &\nWang, C.\n,\nJan 2018\n,\nIn:\nPhysical Review X.\n8\n,\n1\n, 011054.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nGauge Theory\n100%\n46\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n70\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nView all 20 research outputs\nProjects\n1\nFinished\nECS:\nTheoretical Study on Bulk-boundary Correspondences for 3D Symmetry-protected Topological Phases\nWANG, C.\n(Principal Investigator / Project Coordinator)\n1/01/19\n→\n1/01/19\nProject\n:\nResearch\nLie Groups\n100%\nBroken Symmetry\n100%\nQuantum Computing\n100%\nQuasiparticle\n100%\nTopology\n100%\nA