    "homepage_text": "Yifan Gao\nYifan Gao\nI am a Postdoctoral Scholar advised by Prof.\nJustin Sonnenburg\nat Stanford School of Medicine, Microbiology and Immunology Department. I am closely collaborating with Prof.\nKC Huang\n, Prof.\nJames Zou\n, Prof.\nYejin Choi\n, and Prof.\nWilliam Mitch\n. \n\t\t\t\tPrior to Stanford, I received my Ph.D. in Environmental Microbiology with Prof.\nShaily Mahendra\nfrom UCLA. I was fortunate to closely work with Prof.\nLeonard Rome\n, Prof.\nDianne Newman\n, Prof.\nChong Liu\n, Prof.\nEric Hoek\n, and Prof.\nJunyoung Park\n. Having worked at Prof.\nLisa Alvarez-Cohen\ngroup, I received my M.S. from UC Berkeley in 2019.\nMy long-term research goal is to elucidate the complex relationship between gut microbiota and host inflammation. My primary focuses are employing cutting-edge AI/ML technologies, comprehensive omics approaches, and animal models to accelerate the understanding of the gut microbiome and its role in host health.\nFollow @YifanGao15\n📰 Recent News\n[03/2026]\nNew!\nOur pleasure to release\nEubiota\n, agentic AI for autonomous discovery in the gut microbiome in bioRxiv!\n[03/2026]\nNew!\nExcited to release\nEubiota\nwith the\ninteractive app\n!\n[02/2026]\nNew!\nExcited to share the new\nperspective\nwas published on JACS!\n[05/2024]\nI am honored to receive CAPEES-Elsevier Outstanding Graduate Student Award!\n[04/2024]\nIt's my pleasure to receive 2024 CESASC Scholarship!\n[03/2024]\nI am awarded 2024 CAS Future Leader TOP 100 Winner!\n[01/2024]\nI received 2024 American Chemical Society (ACS) Environmental Chemistry Graduate Student Award! The award is based on research achievement, future career goals and recommendations from colleagues.\n[10/2023]\nMy scientific artwork was published on\nColorMePhD\nfounded by\nProf. Julie Rorrer\n!\n[06/2023]\nI received the\nUCLA Dissertation Year Fellowship\nwith a $20,000 stipend, in addition to tuition and fees!\n[05/2023]\nI will be the speaker of the\n\"WeAreIn\" Workshop\n, organized by Dr. Yujie Men and her team at UC Riverside on Sep. 8th 2023!\n[10/2022]\nI am hosting a series of episodes of Women in Science-we have the power to change the world, posting on\nGradSWE Youtube\n!\nFeatured Publications\nEubiota: Modular Agentic AI for Autonomous Discovery in the Gut Microbiome\nPan Lu*,\nYifan Gao*\n, William G. Peng, Haoxiang Zhang, Kunlun Zhu, Elektra K. Robinson, Qixin Xu, Masakazu Kotaka, Harrison G. Zhang, Bingxuan Li, Anthony L. Shiver, Yejin Choi, Kerwyn Casey Huang, Justin Sonnenburg†, James Zou†\nbioRxiv:2602.27708412\n, 2026\n[Paper]\n(*Co-first authors) (†Corresponding authors)\nSculpting Microbial Microenvironments: Spatiotemporal Control via Programmable Electrochemical Gradients\nHaiyuan Zou*†,\nYifan Gao*\n, Ziji Ding, Chong Liu†\nJournal of the American Chemical Society (JACS)\n, 2026\n,\n[Paper]\n(*Co-first authors) (†Corresponding authors)\nLaccase Immobilized on Arginine-Functionalized Boron Nitride Nanosheets for Enhanced Atrazine Degradation\nYifan Gao\n, Minhao Xiao, Haiyuan Zou, Glenn Nurwono, David Zgonc,Quinn Birch, Mallikarjuna Nadagouda  Junyoung Park, Jens Blotevogel, Chong Liu, Eric MV Hoek, Shaily Mahendra\nEnvironmental Science and Technology\n, 2024\n, 58(34)\n[Paper]\nSorghum-grown fungal biocatalysts for synthetic dye degradation\nYifan Gao\n, Benjamin Croze, Quinn T. Birch, Mallikarjuna N. Nadagouda, Shaily Mahendra\nWater Research X\n, 2023, 100181\n[Paper]\nRoles of various enzymes in the biotransformation of 6:2 fluorotelomer alcohol (6:2 FTOH) by a white-rot fungus\nNancy Merino, Ning Wang,\nYifan Gao\n, Meng Wang, Shaily Mahendra\nJournal of Hazardous Materials\n, 2023, 131007\n[Paper]\nDecolorization and detoxification of synthetic dye compounds by laccase immobilized in vault nanoparticles\nYifan Gao\n, Meng Wang, Kshitija Shah, Shashank Singh Kalra, Leonard H. Rome, Shaily Mahendra\nBioresource Technology\n, 2022, 127040\n[Paper]\nImmobilized fungal enzymes: Innovations and potential applications in biodegradation and biosynthesis\nYifan Gao\n, Kshitija Shah, Ivy Kwok, Meng Wang, Leonard H. Rome, Shaily Mahendra\nBiotechnology Advances\n, 2022, 107936\n[Paper]\nEducation\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles, USA\n, 2019.9 - 2024.6\nPh.D. in Environmental Engineering (Environmental Microbiology)\nUniversity of California, Berkeley, USA\n, 2018.8 - 2019.5\nM.S. in Environmental Engineering (Environmental Microbiology)\nInvited Talk and Presentations\nTwo Oral Presentations\n, ACS Fall 2023, San Francisco, USA, 2023.8\nGuest Speaker\n, UCLA CLUSTER Program 80: Frontiers in Human Aging, UCLA, 2023.5\nOral Presentation\n, Association of Environmental Engineering and Science Professors (AEESP) 2022, St. Louis, Missouri, USA, 2022.6\nOral Presentation\n, Twelfth International Conference on Remediation of Chlorinated and Recalcitrant Compounds, Plam Spring, California, USA, 2022.5\nTeaching\nGuest Lecturer\n, Nanomaterials in Energy and Carbon Capture,\nCEE M165: Environmental Nanotechnology\nGraduate and undergraduate, UCLA, Spring 2023\nTeaching Associate\n,\nCEE M165: Environmental Nanotechnology\nGraduate and undergraduate, UCLA, Spring 2023\nTeaching Associate\n,\nCEE 266: Environmental Biotechnology\nGraduate, UCLA, Winter 2023\nTeaching Volunteer\n,\nCNSI Nanoscience education Outreach Program\nUCLA, Fall 2022\nGuest Lecturer\n, Microbial Enumeration and Classification,\nCEE 266: Environmental Biotechnology\nGraduate, UCLA, Fall 2022\nTeaching Associate\n,\nCEE M165: Environmental Nanotechnology\nGraduate and undergraduate, UCLA, Spring 2022\nTeaching Assistant\n,\nCEE M165: Environmental Nanotechnology\nGraduate and undergraduate, UCLA, Spring 2021\nTeaching Assistant\n,\nCEE 266: Environmental Biotechnology\nGraduate, UCLA, Winter 2021\nTeaching Assistant\n,\nCEE 166: Environmental Microbiology\nGraduate and undergraduate, UCLA, Winter 2020\nProfessional Service\nJournal Reviewer\nEnvironmental Science and Technology\nJournal of Hazardous Materials\nFrontiers\nJournal of Environmental Chemical Engineering\nACS ES&T Water\nConference Reviewer\n2024 National Conference on Undergraduate Research (NCUR)\n, 2024.1\n2023 National Conference on Undergraduate Research (NCUR)\n, 2023.1\nOutreach Service\nYouTube Creator\n,\nWomen in Science Interview Series\n, GradSWE, UCLA, 2022.9-2024.6\nInternational Student Event Officer\n, GradSWE, UCLA, 2022.9-2024.6\nArtist and Scientist\n, ColorMePhD Platform, 2023.1-2024.6\nMentor\n, Science Literacy Workshop, 2023.1-2023.4\nPanelist\n, Womxn in STEMM Panel 2022, UCLA, 2022.9\nUndergradaute Participant\n, 16th IWA World Conference on Anaerobic Digestion, Beijing, China, 2018.5\nSelected Honors\nCAPEES-Elsevier Outstanding Graduate Student Award\n, 2024\nCESASC Scholarship\n, 2024\nCAS Future Leader TOP 100 Winner\n, 2024\nAmerican Chemical Society (ACS) Environmental Chemistry Graduate Student Award\n, 2024\nUCLA Dissertation Year Fellowship\n, 2023\nPeking University \"Xiaoyan Tang\" National Innovation Award\n, Third Prize, 2018\nThe Ministry of Industry and Information Innovation and Entrepreneurship Scholarship\n, National Second Prize, 2017\nNational Student Innovation Project\n, Second Prize, 2016\nThe Top Ten Learning and Comprehensive students\n, Harbin Institute of Technology, 2016\nContact\nFairchild Science Building\nStanford, CA 94305\nyfgao [at] stanford [dot] edu\n© Yifan Gao 2020"
