    "homepage_text": "Wenrui Dai - Faculty & Staff - McWilliams School of Biomedical Informatics at UTHealth Houston\nSkip to Content\nUTHEALTH HOUSTON\nABOUT\nCAREERS\nA-Z\nWEBMAIL\nINSIDE THE UNIVERSITY\nSecured Page\nApply Now\nMenu\nProspective Students\nNew Students\nCurrent Students\nFaculty & Staff\nFaculty and Staff\nStaff Directory\nFaculty Awards\nEducational Technology\nContinuing Education\nResearch\nAbout\nFAQ\nMSBMI Intranet\nApply Now\nUTHEALTH HOME\nABOUT\nCAREERS\nA-Z\nWEBMAIL\nINSIDE THE UNIVERSITY\nSecured Page\nSearch UTHealth Houston\nFaculty and Staff\nStaff Directory\nFaculty Awards\nEducational Technology\nGoogle Scholar\nWenrui Dai, PhD\nFaculty Associate\nWenrui Dai, Ph.D. joined the UTHealth School of Biomedical Informatics (SBMI) on May 1, 2018 as a faculty associate. Prior to arriving at SBMI, he was a post-doctoral researcher at the Department of Biomedical Informatics, UC San Diego. Dai’s research interests include predictive modeling, healthcare privacy and machine learning. His current research focuses on learning-based predictive models for healthcare data.\nContact\n[email protected]\nPhone: 713-500-3940\nFax: 713-500-3929\nStaff Support\nSusan Rojas\nPhone: 713-500-3654\nEducation\nPhD, Electronic Engineering, 2014, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nMS, Electronic Engineering, 2008, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nBS, Electronic Engineering, 2005, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nAreas of Expertise\nPredictive modeling\nHealthcare privacy\nMachine learning"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Hongkai Xiong::https://min.sjtu.edu.cn/En/FacultyShow/4?Vid=14": {
    "homepage": "https://min.sjtu.edu.cn/En/FacultyShow/4?Vid=14",
