    "homepage_text": "Assoc\r\n  Prof\nLU Shijian\nCollege of Computing and Data Science\nNanyang\r\n  Technological University, Singapore, 628798\nEmail:\r\n  Shijian.Lu@ntu.edu.sg\nPhone:\r\n  (65) 6790 4928\nOffice:\r\n  N4-02C-101\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nPatents\nVacancies\nProf Lu received his PhD\r\n  in electrical and computer engineering from the National University of\r\n  Singapore. His research interests include computer vision and deep learning.\r\n  He has published more than 200 internationally referred journal and\r\n  conference papers and co-authored over 10 patents in these research areas. Prof\r\n  Lu is currently an Associate Editor for the journals of Pattern Recognition\r\n  (PR) and Neurocomputing. He has also served in the program committee of a\r\n  number of international conferences such as the Area Chair of CVPR, the Senior\r\n  Program Committee of IJCAI and AAAI, etc.\nCommittee Members:\no\nSenior Program\r\n  Committee (SPC) of the International Joint Conference on Artificial\r\n  Intelligence (IJCAI18  IJCAI21)\no\nSenior Program\r\n  Committee (SPC) of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI18 \r\n  AAAI21)\no\nArea Chair of 15th\r\n  International Conference on Document Analysis and Recognition (ICDAR-19)\no\nArea Chair of IEEE\r\n  Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV-17 and WACV-18)\no\nArea Chair of 14th IAPR International\r\n  Conference on Document Analysis and Recognition (ICDAR-17)\nAwards and Recognitions:\no\nTop winner of\r\n  the ICFHR2014 Competition on Word Recognition from Historical Documents\no\nTop winner of\r\n  the ICDAR 2013 Robust Reading Competition (1\nst\nin the scene text\r\n  segmentation task)\no\nTop winner of\r\n  the\nICDAR 2013 Document Image\r\n  Binarization Contest (DIBCO 2013)\no\nTop winner of the\r\n  H-DIBCO 2010  Handwritten Document Image Binarization Competition\no\nTop winner of the\r\n  ICDAR 2009 Document Image Binarization Contest (DIBCO 2009)"
  },
