    "homepage_text": "Yang Bai's Homepage\nContact\nServices\nWritings\nPublications\nNews\nBio\nYang Bai\nSenior Research Engineer\nByteDance\nbaiyang0522 (at) gmail.com\nAbout Me\nI am currently a senoir research engineer at\nByteDance\n. I received my Ph.D. from\nTsinghua Univeristy\nin June 2022, where I was fortunate to be advised by Prof. Yong Jiang and\nProf. Shu-tao Xia\n. I was also co-supervised by\nProf. Yisen Wang\n. Prior to this, I obtained my bachelor’s degree from Tsinghua University in June 2017. I joined ByteDance in Aug 2024. Before that, I has worked in Tencent Zhuque Lab since 2022 and interned in\nTencent AI Lab\nin 2020.\nMy general research interest is\nResponsbile GenAI\n– with a special focus on building GenAI systems which are data-efficient and robust, especially for commercial foundation models.\nNews\n[Aug. 2025]\nI will serve as an Area Chair of\nCVPR 2026\n.\n[May. 2025]\nI will serve as an Area Chair of\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\n[Mar. 2025]\nOur paper about\nVideo LLMs\nis accepted to\nCVPR 2025\n.\n[Jan. 2025]\nOur paper about\nDMs\nis accepted to\nICLR 2025\n.\n[Jan. 2024]\nOur paper about\nVLMs\nis accepted to\nICLR 2024\n.\n[Dec. 2023]\nI will serve as an Area Chair of\nECCV 2024\n.\n[Sep. 2023]\nOur paper about\ndistributed training\nis accepted to\nECML KDD 2023\n.\n[Sep. 2023]\nOur paper about\nmodel parallelism\nis accepted to\nECML KDD 2023\n.\n[Aug. 2023]\nI will serve as an Area Chair of\nNeurIPS 2023 Workshop\n.\n[Feb. 2023]\nOur paper about\nbackdoor defense\nis accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n.\nShow more\n[Nov. 2022]\nOur paper about\nquery efficiency\nis accepted to\nPattern Recognition\n.\n[Sep. 2022]\nOur paper about\ndataset watermark\nis accepted to\nNeurIPS 2022\n.\n[Sep. 2021]\nOur paper about\nwatermark protection\nis accepted to\nECCV 2022\n.\n[Jul. 2022]\nI will join Tencent as a senior research scientist.\n[Jun. 2022]\nI will receive my Ph.D degree from Tsinghua University.\n[Jan. 2022]\nI have been specifically chosen for Huawei's Top Minds program and Tencent T-Expert program.\n[Sep. 2021]\nOur paper about\nadversarial understannding\nis accepted to\nNeurIPS 2021\n.\n[Sep. 2021]\nOur paper about\nactivation understanding\nis accepted to\nICLR 2021\n.\n[Sep. 2021]\nOur paper about\nquery efficiency\nis accepted to\nECCV 2020\n.\n[Sep. 2019]\nI have been awarded with WTM APAC Scholars of Google.\n[Mar. 2019]\nOur paper about\ndata purification\nis accepted to\nICCV 2019\n.\nPublications\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n[\nDBLP\n]\nSpecial Characters Attack: Toward Scalable Training Data Extraction From Large Language Models\nYang Bai\n, Ge Pei, Jindong Gu, Yong Yang#, Xingjun Ma\n(# Corresponding authors)\nPDF\nCheating Suffix: Targeted Attack to Text-To-Image Diffusion Models with Multi-Modal Priors\nDingcheng Yang,\nYang Bai\n#, Xiaojun Jia, Yang Liu, Xiaochun Cao, Wenjian Yu#\n(# Corresponding authors)\nPDF\nCode\nInducing High Energy-Latency of Large Vision-Language Models with Verbose Images\nKuofeng Gao,\nYang Bai\n, Jindong Gu, Shu-Tao Xia, Philip Torr, Zhifeng Li#, Wei Liu#\n(# Corresponding authors)\nICLR 2024\nPDF\nCode\nOT-Attack: Enhancing Adversarial Transferability of Vision-Language Models via Optimal Transport Optimization\nDongchen Han*, Xiaojun Jia*,\nYang Bai\n, Jindong Gu, Yang Liu, Xiaochun Cao\n(* Equal contributions)\nPDF\nDistributed Adaptive Optimization with Divisible Communication\nAn Xv,\nYang Bai\nECML KDD 2023\nPDF\nCross Model Parallelism for Faster Bidirectional Training of Large Convolutional Neural Networks\nAn Xv,\nYang Bai\nECML KDD 2023\nPDF\nBackdoorBox: A python toolbox for backdoor learning\nYiming Li*, Mengxi Ya*,\nYang Bai\n, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia\n(* Equal contributions)\nICLR 2023 Workshop on Backdoor Attacks and Defenses in Machine Learning\nPDF\nCode\nBackdoor Defense via Adaptively Splitting Poisoned Dataset\nKuofeng Gao*,\nYang Bai\n*, Jindong Gu, Yong Yang, Shu-Tao Xia\n(* Equal contributions)\nCVPR 2023\nPDF\nCode\nQuery efficient black-box adversarial attack on deep neural networks\nYang Bai\n*, Yisen Wang*, Yuyuan Zeng, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia\n(* Equal contributions)\nPattern Recognition\nPDF\nUntargeted backdoor watermark: Towards harmless and stealthy dataset copyright protection\nYiming Li*,\nYang Bai\n*, Yong Jiang, Yong Yang, Shu-Tao Xia, Bo Li\n(* Equal contributions)\nNeurIPS 2022\nPDF\nThe Robust and Harmless Model Watermarking\nYiming Li, Linghui Zhu,\nYang Bai\n, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia\nDigital Watermarking for Machine Learning Model: Techniques, Protocols and Applications\nPDF\nWatermark vaccine: Adversarial attacks to prevent watermark removal\nXinwei Liu, Jian Liu,\nYang Bai\n, Jindong Gu, Tao Chen, Xiaojun Jia#, Xiaochun Cao#\n(# Corresponding authors)\nECCV 2022\nPDF\nCode\nMOVE: Effective and Harmless Ownership Verification via Embedded External Features\nYiming Li, Linghui Zhu, Xiaojun Jia,\nYang Bai\n, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia, Xiaochun Cao\nPDF\nCode\nTest-time Adaptation of Residual Blocks against Poisoning and Backdoor Attacks\nArnav Gudibande, Xinyun Chen,\nYang Bai\n, Jason Xiong, Dawn Song\nCVPR 2022 Workshop\nPDF\nD2Defend: Dual-Domain based Defense against Adversarial Examples\nXin Yan, Yanjie Li, Tao Dai,\nYang Bai\n, Shu-Tao Xia\nIJCNN 2021\nPDF\nClustering Effect of (Linearized) Adversarial Robust Models\nYang Bai\n, Xin Yan, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia, Yisen Wang\nNeurIPS 2021\nPDF\nCode\nImproving Adversarial Robustness via Channel-wise Activation Suppressing\nYang Bai\n*, Yuyuan Zeng*, Yong Jiang, Shu-Tao Xia, Xingjun Ma, Yisen Wang\n(* Equal contributions)\nICLR 2021\nPDF\nCode\nAdaptive Frequency Learning in Two-branch Face Forgery Detection\nNeng Wang,\nYang Bai\n, Kun Yu, Yong Jiang, Shu-tao Xia, Yan Wang\nPDF\nImproving Query Efficiency of Black-box Adversarial Attack\nYang Bai\n*, Yuyuan Zeng*, Yong Jiang, Yisen Wang, Shu-Tao Xia, Weiwei Guo\n(* Equal contributions)\nECCV 2020\nPDF\nCode\nSelf-adaptive Feature Fool\nXinyi Liu,\nYang Bai\n, Shu-Tao Xia, Yong Jiang\nICASSP 2020\nPDF\nHilbert-based Generative Defense for Adversarial Examples\nYang Bai\n*, Yan Feng*, Yisen Wang, Tao Dai, Shu-Tao Xia, Yong Jiang\n(* Equal contributions)\nICCV 2019\nPDF\nWritings\nServices\nArea Chairs\nThe IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2026\nThe Thirty-nineth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2025\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) 2024\nThe Thirty-seventh Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2023 on Robustness of Few-shot and Zero-shot Learning in Large Foundation Models\nConference Reviewers\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2022-2025\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) 2022\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2021-2024\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 2021-2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2022-2024\nAssociation for the Advance of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) 2019-2020, 2025\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI) 2019-2021\nJournal Reviewers\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nNeurocomputing\nContact\nAddress:\n1199 Coleman Avenue, San Jose, CA 95110\nOffice Location:\nByteDance Inc.\nEmail:\nbaiyang0522 (at) gmail.com"
