    "homepage_text": "Shangchen Zhou\nShangchen Zhou\nAbout\nPublications\nCode | Data\nServices\nOthers\nMenu\nAbout\nPublications\nCode | Data\nServices\nOthers\nShangchen Zhou\nResearch Assistant Professor\nCollege of Computing and Data Science\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore\nEmail:\nshangchenzhou[at]gmail.com\nBiography\nShangchen is currently a Research Assistant Professor with\nMMLab@NTU\nat\nNanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore\n. \n                    Before that, he received his Ph.D. (2020-2024) in Computer Science (winner of the CCDS Outstanding PhD Thesis Award) from\nNTU Singapore\n, advised by Prof.\nChen Change Loy\nat MMLab@NTU.\nHis research interests include computer vision and computational photography, with a focus on  working on low-level vision and multimodal generation & editing.\nHis first-author projects have garnered over\n27,000 GitHub stars\n.\n                    Several of his works, including\nCodeFormer\n,\nProPainter\n,\nMatAnyone\n,\nStableSR\n,\n                    and\nFlare7K\n,\n                    have been transferred or licensed to more than 10 companies and institutions.\nVIEW MORE PROJECTS\nNews\n➤ [09/2025]\n: I received the NTU CCDS Outstanding PhD Thesis Award 2025.\n➤ [08/2025]\n: I will serve as an Area Chair for CVPR 2026, ICLR 2026.\n➤ [05/2025]\n: We organize the 4th\nMIPI 2025\nworkshop in ICCV 2025 (\nHawai'i).\n➤ [04/2025]\n: Serving as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025.\n➤ [02/2025]\n: \n                            Our\nMatAnyone\n,\n3DEnhancer\n, \n                            and\nSAR3D\naccepted to CVPR 2025. \n                            Congrats to all authors!\n➤ [02/2025]\n: Our\nGaussianAnything\nis accepted to ICLR 2025.\n➤ [07/2024]\n: I received the CGAOSSA Award 2023.\n➤ [06/2024]\n: Our\nStableSR\nis accepted to IJCV.\n➤ [06/2024]\n: We organize the 3rd\nMIPI 2024\nworkshop in CVPR 2024 (\nSeattle).\n➤ [02/2024]\n: Three papers are accepted to CVPR 2024.\n➤ [01/2024]\n: One paper about local image deblurring is accepted by ICLR 2024.\n➤ [12/2023]\n: One paper about real-world image super-resolution is accepted by AAAI 2024.\n➤ [09/2023]\n: Our\nPGDiff\nis accepted to NeurIPS 2023.\n➤ [07/2023]\n: Our\nProPainter\nand\nCLIP-LIT\nare accepted to ICCV 2023.\n➤ [03/2023]\n: Our\nBracketFlare Dataset\nfor reflective flare removal is accepted by CVPR 2023 as a Highlight paper.\n➤ [01/2023]\n: Our\nUHDFour\non UHD low-light enhancement is accepted by ICLR 2023 as Oral.\n➤ [12/2022]\n: We organize the 2nd\nMIPI 2023\nworkshop in CVPR 2023 (\nVancouver).\n➤ [09/2022]\n: Our\nCodeFormer\nand\nFlare7K Dataset\nare accepted to NeurIPS 2022.\n➤ [07/2022]\n: Our\nLEDNet\nis accepted to ECCV 2022.\n➤ [04/2022]\n: We organize a new workshop called\nMobile Intelligent Photography and Imaging (MIPI)\nin ECCV 2022.\n➤ [03/2022]\n: Two papers are accepted to CVPR 2022.\n➤ [04/2021]\n: [🥇x3 🥈x1] Our\nBasicVSR++\nwon 3 champions and 1 runner-up in\nNTIRE 2021\nChallenges.\n➤ [03/2021]\n: One paper is accepted to CVPR 2021.\n➤ [10/2020]\n: Got my first top 10% outstanding reviewer recognition from NeurIPS 2020.\n➤ [09/2020]\n: One paper is accepted to NeurIPS 2020.\n➤ [07/2020]\n: Two papers are accepted to ECCV 2020.\n➤ [11/2019]\n: Two papers are accepted to AAAI 2020.\n➤ [07/2019]\n: Two papers are accepted to ICCV 2019.\n➤ [04/2019]\n: Our\nStereo Blur Dataset\nis publicly available.\n➤ [03/2019]\n: One paper is accepted to CVPR 2019 as Oral.\nPublications\n[\nG\no\no\ng\nl\ne\nScholar]\nSelected\nFull List\n|\nAll Topics\nPreprint Papers\nConference Papers\nJournal Papers\nConference Papers\nJournal Papers\nPreprint Papers\nCopyright©\nShangchen.\nTop"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yong Xu::https://yongxudm.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://yongxudm.github.io/",
