    "homepage_text": "Yue Bai\nYue Bai\nPh.D. Candidate\nEmail\n: bai.yue [at] northeastern.edu\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nI am a final-year Ph.D. student in\nSmileLab\nat Northeastern University supervised by\nProf. Yun Raymond Fu\n. My research interests lie in multi-modal learning and sparse network training.\nI spent time at\nAdobe Research\nand\nAI2\nas a research intern.\nNews\n2025.02: One paper is accpeted by\nICLR 2025\nfor model distillation.\n2024.08: One paper is accpeted by\nEMNLP 2024\nfor efficient vision-language models.\n2024.06: Start my internship at\nAdobe\n, Seattle, WA.\n2024.02: One paper is accpeted by\nICLR 2024\nfor video representation learning.\n2024.01: One paper is accpeted by\nCVPR 2024\nfor efficient transformers.\n2023.09: One paper is accpeted by\nNeurIPS 2023\nfor graph sparse learning.\n2023.09: One paper is accpeted by\nICDM 2023\nfor deepfake detection.\n2023.06: Start my internship at\nAllen AI (AI2)\n, Seattle, WA.\n2023.02: One paper is accpeted by\nCVPR 2023\nfor adaptive-inference video recognition.\n2022.11: One paper is accepted by\nAAAI 2023\nfor layout representation learning.\n2022.10: One paper is accepted by\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nfor human motion segmentation.\n2022.09: Two papers are accepted by\nNeurIPS 2022\n.\n2022.06: Start my internship at\nAdobe Research\n, San Jose, CA (remotely).\n2022.01: One paper is accepted by\nICLR 2022\n.\n2021.12: One paper is accepted by\nSDM 2022\n.\n2021.06: Start my internship at\nAdobe Research\n, San Jose, CA (remotely).\n2021.03: Our team won the\n1st Prize\nin both RGB and RGB-D tracks of CVPR21 Challenge on Large Scale Signer Independent Isolated Sign Language Recognition\n[code]\n[link]\n[news]\n.\n2021.01: One paper is accepted by\nAAAI 2021\n.\n2020.09: One paper is accepted by\nICDM 2020\n.\n2020.05: One paper is accepted by\nECCV 2020\n.\n2020.01: Begin my new journey at\nNortheastern University\n, Boston, MA.\nProfessonal Activities\nReviewer\nfor ICML, NeurIPS, ICLR, CVPR, ECCV, ICCV, EMNLP, AAAI, IJCAI, TPAMI, TNNLS, TIP, TKDD, etc."
