  "deep_homepage::Jindong Wang::https://jindongwang.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://jindongwang.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "jindongwang@outlook.com",
      "jdw@wm.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/jindongwang",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jindong-wang/",
    "homepage_text": "Jindong Wang\nJindong\nWang\nAssistant Professor,\nWilliam & Mary\njdw [at] wm.edu, jindongwang [at] outlook.com\nIntegrated Science Center 3383, Williamsburg, VA, USA\nGoogle scholar\n|\nDBLP\n|\nGithub\n|\nTwitter/X\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nZhihu\n|\nBilibili\n||\nCV\nPhD and interns:\nPhD recruitment for 2027 Spring\n,\nInternship or collaboration\n. [\nChinese blog\n]\nI am open to industry and university visit, consultant, and more collaboration!\nDr. Jindong Wang is an Assistant Professor at William & Mary Department of Data Science. He is also a faculty member of\nFuture of Life Institute\n. Previously, he was a Senior Researcher in Microsoft Research Asia from 2019 to 2024. His research interest spans machine learning, large foundation models, and generative AI. He is among\nWorld’s Top 2% Highly Cited Scientists\nand\nMost Influential AI Scholars\n. He is associate editor of IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS), guest editor for ACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (TIST), area chair for ICML, NeurIPS, ICLR, KDD, ACL, ACMMM, and ACML, and SPC of IJCAI and AAAI. He published over 60 papers at top-tier venues (23000+ citations, H-index 54). His research is supported by Amazon Research Award, Google Research Award, NVIDIA Academic Research Grant, and others from AMD, Microsoft, and William & Mary Faculty Research Award. His work was integrated into Microsoft\nhealth products\nthat reduced token consumptions by 15%, and\nquant finance\nwith increased stock price prediction accuracy. His work was also reported by\nForbes\n,\nMIT Technology Review\n, and other international media. He received best paper awards at several conferences and workshops. He published a book\nIntroduction to Transfer Learning\nand gave tutorials at\nIJCAI’22\n,\nWSDM’23\n,\nKDD’23\n,\nAAAI’24\n,\nAAAI’25\n,\nCVPR’25\n, and CVPR’26.\nNews\nFeb 21, 2026\nTwo papers and one tutorial are accepted by CVPR 2026. Congrats!\nFeb 11, 2026\nOur AI education paper “Classroom AI: Large Language Models as Grade-Specific Teachers” has been accepted by NPJ Artificial Intelligence (a Nature portfolio journal)!\nFeb 08, 2026\nI received the AAAI 2026 Oustanding SPC Award (35 among 1700+ SPCs)!\nJan 26, 2026\nWe have three papers accepted at ICLR 2026! Congrats!\nJan 16, 2026\nInvited to be a senior program member (SPC) of IJCAI 2026.\nJan 06, 2026\nInvited to be serve on the NSF panel of machine learning and large language models.\nDec 17, 2025\nOur collaborated paper “General scales unlock ai evaluation with explanatory and predictive power” is accepted by\nNature\n! Congrats Lexin! 🎉🎉🎉\nDec 15, 2025\nWe got the\nNVIDIA Academic Research Grant\n(4x RTX Pro 6000 GPUs)!\nNov 24, 2025\nWe have 1 paper accepted by AAAI 2026 and KDD 2026, respectively. Congrats to authors!\nNov 20, 2025\nInvited to be an area chair (AC) of ICML 2026.\nOct 22, 2025\nWe got the prestigious\nAmazon Research Award\n!\nOct 17, 2025\nWe received an\nunrestricted gift (award) from Google Deepmind\n!\nOct 16, 2025\nWe got the AMD University Program HPC Award!\nOct 13, 2025\nOur NeurIPS 2025 workshop on LLM persona has been accepted!\nOct 07, 2025\nWe got the Google Cloud Research Credit award!"
  },
