    "homepage_text": "Haoran You\nHaoran You\nAbout\nI am currently a Research Scientist at Adobe, developing efficient GenAI models with lower serving cost and optimizing deployment on Nvidia, Intel, AMD, and Apple devices.\n    I obtained my PhD from Georgia Tech, advised by Dr. Yingyan (Celine) Lin. My research is dedicated to creating\nefficient ML systems\nthrough\nalgorithm-hardware co-design\n.\n    This involves addressing the challenge posed by the increasing complexity of advanced AI/ML models, such as large language models (LLMs) and large vision models (LVMs), against the constraints of both edge and cloud computing devices.\nMy research work has received recognition, including winning Gold Medal at the ACM Student Research Competition (SRC) at ICCAD'23, securing the Best Poster Award at the SCS Poster Competition of Georgia Tech, and being selected as an IEEE Micro's Top Pick of 2023. Additionally, I was named one of the Machine Learning and Systems Rising Stars of 2023, received the Outstanding Graduate Research Assistant Award, won first place in the University Best Demonstration at DAC'22, and our ViTCoD project was honored with the Meta Faculty Research Award of 2022.\nSelected News\n[01/2026]\nOur efficient GenAI models for\nGenerative Fill\nand\nRemove\nfeatures are shipped in\nPhotoshop v27.3\nwith one third less serving costs (\nsaved 175 H100 GPUs ≈ $1.2K per hour\n) !\n[10\n/\n2025]\nHaoran was selected as a\nTop Reviewer\nby\nNeurIPS 2025\n!\n[07\n/\n2025]\nOne paper accepted by\nMICRO 2025\n!\n[05\n/\n2025]\nOne paper accepted by\nICML 2025\n!\n[02\n/\n2025]\nTwo papers accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n!\n[09\n/\n2024]\nOur\nShiftAddLLM\nwas accepted by\nNeurIPS 2024\n!\n[05\n/\n2024]\nOur\nLinearized-LLM\nwas accepted by\nICML 2024\n!\n[12\n/\n2023]\nHaoran received the NeurIPS 2023 Scholar Award !\n[11\n/\n2023]\nHaoran won\nFirst Place\nat\nACM Student Research Competition\nat\nICCAD 2023\n!\n[05/2023]\nHaoran was selected as one of the\nML and Systems Rising Stars of 2023\n!\n[04/2023]\nHaoran won the\nBest Poster Award\nat the SCS Poster Competition of GaTech !\n[03/2023]\nHaoran was selected by GaTech to receive the\nOutstanding GRA Award\n!\n[01/2023]\nOur\nEyeCoD\nwas selected as the\nIEEE Micro’s Top Pick of 2023\n!\n[09/2022]\nOur\nViTCoD\nwas selected for\nMeta Faculty Research Award of 2022\n!\n[11\n/\n2022]\nOur\ni-FlatCam\nwon first place in\nUniversity Demonstration at DAC 2022\n!\n[12\n/\n2020]\nOur\nEarly-Bird Tickets\nwas accepted as\nSpotlight at ICLR 2020\n!\nServices\nConference Reviewer or TPC\nICML\n: 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024\nNeurIPS\n: 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025\nICLR\n: 2022, 2023, 2024, 2026\nCVPR\n: 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026\nICCV\n: 2023\nECCV\n: 2022, 2024\nAAAI\n: 2023, 2024\nDAC\n: 2026\nDATE\n: 2025\nMICRO\n: 2026\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems Part II (TCAS-II)\nIEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems (TPDS)\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology (JSTC)\nVolunteering Service\nStudent helper and website developer for the\nICCAD HALO Workshop\nStudent helper and website developer for the\nEECS Rising Stars Workshop of 2023\nAbout Me\nHaoran You (\n游浩然\n)\nPhD @ Georgia Tech\nContact\nhaoranyou98@gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nTwitter\n\n---\n\nBios - Haoran You\nHaoran You\nBios\nHaoran You\n2023-01-31\nHi all, welcome to my personal website. I am a 4th year PhD student in the CS department of Georgia Institute of Technology, who is passinoate about efficient/automated ML and algorithm-hardware co-design!\nAbout Me\nHaoran You (\n游浩然\n)\nPhD @ Georgia Tech\nContact\nhaoranyou98@gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nTwitter"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zhe Jiang::https://www.jiangteam.org/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.jiangteam.org/",
    "all_emails": [
      "zhe.jiang@ufl.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhe Jiang | Home\nZhe Jiang Homepage\nZhe Jiang\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Computer & Information Science & Engineering\nUniversity of Florida\nEmail\n: zhe.jiang(at)ufl.edu\nPhone\n: 352-294-6659 (Email preferred)\nOffice\n: Malachowsky Hall 6110\nMail\n: PO Box 116120, Gainesville, FL, 32611\nShort Bio\nDr. Zhe Jiang is an associate professor in the Department of Computer & Information Science & Engineering at the University of Florida, where he is also affiliated with the Center for Coastal Solutions. He received his Ph.D. in Computer Science from the University of Minnesota in 2016 and a B.E. in Electrical Engineering from the University of Science and Technology of China in 2010. His research interests include data mining, machine learning, and artificial intelligence, with a particular focus on spatiotemporal data mining for interdisciplinary applications in Earth sciences (e.g., floods, storm surges), agriculture, transportation, health and medicine. He received the Best Paper Award in ACM SIGSPATIAL 2023 and Best Paper Runner-Up Award in the Blue Sky Vision Track of SIAM Data Mining 2024. He has served as the Program Co-Chair for SDM 2024, Proceedings Co-chair for KDD 2023-2026, Publicity Co-Chair for SDM 2023 and ACMGIS 2022, and Student Travel Award Chair for ICDM 2022. He has served as a Senior Program Committee member (or Area Chair) for AAAI, ICDM, ICML, ACM SIGSPATIAL, SDM, and PAKDD. He is a senior member of ACM and IEEE.\nResearch Interests\nArtificial intelligence and its interdisciplinary applications in Earth sciences and health/medicine.\nOpen Positions\nOur lab is ALWAYS looking for outstanding Ph.D. students. We also welcome remote interns. Please click\nthis link\n.\nNews\n[Paper]\n1/6/2026: Our paper, titled \"A Survey on Uncertainty Quantification Methods for Deep Learning\" has been accepted in ACM Computing Survey! Links:\narxiv\n,\nACM Open Access\n.\n[Paper]\n8/14/2025: Two papers are accepted in ACM SIGSPATAIL 2025. One paper is accepted in Transactions on Machine Learning Research. Earlier, two papers were accepted in AAAI 2025 and one paper was accepted in ICML 2025. Congratulations!\n[SPC]\n2/1/2025: Dr. Jiang was invited to serve as an Area Chair for AAAI 2026 and KDD 2026, a proceedings co-chair for ACM SIGKDD 2025 - 2026 and SIGSPATIAL 2025.\n[PC]\n8/17/2024: Dr. Jiang was invited to serve on the Senior Program Committee of AAAI 2025 and ICDM 2024.\n[Paper]\n4/29/2024: One paper is accepted in IJCAI 2024, one paper accepted in ICDE 2024, and one journal paper is accepted in EEE Transactions on Big Data, Special Issue on\nStream Data Learning and its Applications.\n[Award]\n4/29/2024: Dr. Jiang becomes a senior member of ACM.\n[Award]\n4/21/2024: Our paper received the Best Paper Runner-Up Award of the Blue Sky Track at SIAM Data Mining 2024! Congratulations!\n[PC]\n1/27/2024: Dr. Jiang was invited to serve as the Senior PC Member for PAKDD 2024, Area Chair for ICML 2024, PC Vice Co-Chair for Big Data Learning and Analytics Track, IEEE International Conference on Big Data 2024.\n\"Life isn't about how you survive the storm, but how you dance in the rain!\""
  },
