    "homepage_text": "Long Yang – The Billinge Group: Columbia University\nSkip to content\nThe Billinge Group: Columbia University\nDepartment of Applied Physics and Applied Mathematics\nLong Yang\nLong was born in Wenzhou and grew up in Shanghai, China. He received his B.S. in Optics from Fudan University, and is now pursing his Ph.D. in materials science and engineering at Columbia University. He is interested in applying x-ray and neutron PDF techniques to solve the structure problems in magnetic systems, novel 2D materials, and nanoparticles. Besides research, he likes going on road trips, playing pool, and watching movies.\nResearch\nDeblurring our View of Atomic Arrangements in Complex Materials\nComplex Modeling and Nanostructure Determination\nLattice Dynamics and Bonding Strength of Nanostructured Materials\nMagnetic PDF\nNanostructured and Amorphous Pharmaceuticals and Molecular Materials\nPDF computed Tomography\nRecent News\nStructure-mining: An Automated Tool to Find Candidate Structures\nStoichiometric Control Over Ferroic Behavior in Iron Doped Barium Titanate Nanocrystals\nExamining the size-dependent lattice dynamics of atomically precise CdSe quantum dots\nSolving the Nano-structure Problem in Gold Nanoparticles Using PDF.\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nThe Billinge Group: Columbia University\nSign me up\nAlready have a WordPress.com account?\nLog in now.\nThe Billinge Group: Columbia University\nSubscribe\nSubscribed\nSign up\nLog in\nCopy shortlink\nReport this content\nView post in Reader\nManage subscriptions\nCollapse this bar\nLoading Comments...\nWrite a Comment...\nEmail\nName\nWebsite\n\n---\n\nContact – The Billinge Group: Columbia University\nSkip to content\nThe Billinge Group: Columbia University\nDepartment of Applied Physics and Applied Mathematics\nContact\nDepartment of Applied Physics & Applied Mathematics\nColumbia University\n500 West 120th Street\nRoom 200 Mudd, MC 4701\nNew York, NY 10027 USA\n← Back\nThank you for your response. ✨\