    "homepage_text": "Ruoxi Jia  | Sanghani Center | Virginia Tech\nVirginia Tech®\nhome\nUniversal Access Toggle\nUniversal Access\nClose Universal Access dialog\nUniversal Access Options\nReport a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbarrier\nAccessibility\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tportal\nPause all background videos\nUnderline all links\nSanghani Center for Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics\nSearch\nSearch query\n×\nsearch\nSearch this site\nSearch all vt.edu sites\nPeople search\nFrequent Searches:\nWeb\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nNews\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nFilter search\nCategories\nAcademics\nCampus Experience\nCulture\nImpact\nResearch\nStory type\nFeature\nNotice\nStory\nVideo\nApply filters\nClear filters\nVideo\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nPeople\nresults for\nPeople Results\nSee more\nVT News Results\nSee more\nRuoxi Jia\nContact:\nruoxijia@vt.edu\nWebsite\nRuoxi Jia joined Virginia Tech in 2020 as an assistant professor in the Bradley Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. She is a core faculty member at the Sanghani Center.\nShe earned a bachelor of science degree from Peking University in 2013 and a Ph.D. in electrical engineering and computer sciences from the University of California Berkeley in 2018.\nJia's research interest broadly spans the areas of machine learning, security, privacy, and cyber-physical systems. Her recent work focuses on building algorithmic foundations for data markets and developing trustworthy machine learning solutions.    She is the recipient of several fellowships, including the Chiang Fellowship for Graduate Scholars in Manufacturing and Engineering, the 8108 Alumni Fellowship, and the Okamatsu Fellowship. In 2017, she was selected for Rising Stars in the EECS program.    Her work has been published at professional conferences and featured in multiple media outlets.\nPublications\nGeneral Item\nData Banzhaf: A Data Valuation Framework with Maximal Robustness to Learning Stochasticity\nDate:\nMay 29, 2022\n-\nGeneral Item\nQEKD: Query-Efficient and Data-Free Knowledge Distillation from Black-box Models\nDate:\nMay 22, 2022\n-\nGeneral Item\nNarcissus: A Practical Clean-Label Backdoor Attack with Limited Information\nDate:\nApr 14, 2022\n-\ncurrent page\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\nNext\nPage 1 of 8 | 24 Results\nProjects\nIn the News\nArticle Item\nAmazon-Virginia Tech Initiative awards two student fellowships, five faculty research awards\n, article\nDate:\nOct 23, 2024\n-\nArticle Item\nAmazon-Virginia Tech Initiative announces support for two Amazon Fellows and five faculty-led projects for 2023-24 academic year\n, article\nDate:\nOct 03, 2023\n-\nArticle Item\nAmazon-Virginia Tech Initiative showcases innovative approaches to robust and efficient machine learning\n, article\nDate:\nMay 03, 2023\n-\ncurrent page\n1\n2\nNext\nPage 1 of 2 | 5 Results\nGrants Provided By\nTags\nFaculty\nRuoxi Jia\n\n---\n\nRuoxi Jia  | Sanghani Center | Virginia Tech\nVirginia Tech®\nhome\nUniversal Access Toggle\nUniversal Access\nClose Universal Access dialog\nUniversal Access Options\nReport a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbarrier\nAccessibility\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tportal\nPause all background videos\nUnderline all links\nSanghani Center for Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics\nSearch\nSearch query\n×\nsearch\nSearch this site\nSearch all vt.edu sites\nPeople search\nFrequent Searches:\nWeb\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nNews\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nFilter search\nCategories\nAcademics\nCampus Experience\nCulture\nImpact\nResearch\nStory type\nFeature\nNotice\nStory\nVideo\nApply filters\nClear filters\nVideo\nresults for\nSort by relevance\nSort by date\nPeople\nresults for\nPeople Results\nSee more\nVT News Results\nSee more\nRuoxi Jia\nContact:\nruoxijia@vt.edu\nWebsite\nRuoxi Jia joined Virginia Tech in 2020 as an assistant professor in the Bradley Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. She is a