D. Phung, V. Huynh, Y. Jin, L. Du, W. Buntine\nlink\n,\narxiv\n[ICLR 2021,\nSpotlight, Top 5%\n] Neural Topic Model via Optimal Transport\nH. Zhao\n, D. Phung, V. Huynh, T. Le, W. Buntine\nlink\n,\ncode\n[NeurIPS 2020] OTLDA: A Geometry-aware Optimal Transport Approach for Topic Modeling\nV. Huynh,\nH. Zhao\n, D. Phung\nlink\n[ECCV 2020] Improving Adversarial Robustness by Enforcing Local and Global Compactness\nA. Bui, T. Le,\nH. Zhao\n, P. Montague, O. de Vel, T. Abraham, D. Phung\nlink\n,\narxiv\n,\ncode\n[AISTATS 2020] Variational Autoencoders for Sparse and Overdispersed Discrete Data\nH. Zhao\n, P. Rai, L. Du, W. Buntine, D. Phung, M. Zhou\nlink\n,\ncode\n[NeurIPS 2018] Dirichlet Belief Networks for Topic Structure Learning\nH. Zhao\n, L. Du, W. Buntine, M. Zhou\nlink\n,\ncode\n[ICML 2018] Inter and Intra Topic Structure Learning with Word Embeddings\nH. Zhao\n, L. Du, W. Buntine, M. Zhou\nlink\n,\ncode\n[AISTATS 2018] Bayesian multi-label learning with sparse features and labels, and label co-occurrences\nH. Zhao\n, P. Rai, L. Du, W. Buntine\nlink\n,\ncode\n[ACML 2017] A Word Embeddings Informed Focused Topic Model\nH. Zhao\n, L. Du, W. Buntine\nlink\n,\ncode\n[ICDM 2017,\nLong Paper\n] MetaLDA: A Topic Model that Efficiently Incorporates Meta information\nH. Zhao\n, L. Du, W. Buntine, G. Liu\nlink\n,\narxiv\n,\ncode\n[ICML 2017] Leveraging Node Attributes for Incomplete Relational Data\nH. Zhao\n, L. Du, W. Buntine\nlink\n,\narxiv\n,\ncode\nProfessional Services\nReviewing\nNeurIPS (Area Chair, A top reviewer in 2018), ICLR (Area Chair), ACML (Area Chair), Machine Learning Journal (Editorial board member)\nTutorials and workshops\nOptimal Transport for Unsupervised Learning\nat\nAsian Conference on Machine Learning\n2021\nOT-SDMG: 2025 Workshop on Optimal Transport for Structured Data Modeling and Generation\nat\nThe Web Conference\n2025\nRecent Talks\nBeyond Predictions: Making AI Reliable with Uncertainty and Causal Understanding\nUNSW AI Symposium 2024\nlink\nEnhancing Generalisation and Robustness in Deep Learning with Optimal Transport\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, UNSW Sydney, July 2024\nslides\nLearning Deep Representations with Optimal Transport\nStatistics Seminar, The University of Sydney\nlink\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
