    "homepage_text": "Yixiao Zhou\n      -  The Australian National University\nThe Australian National University Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at The Australian National University\nView Scopus Profile\nAsPr Yixiao Zhou\nAssociate Professor\nArndt-Corden Department of Economics\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0001-7712-2776\nEmail\nyixiao.zhou\nanu.edu\nau\nh-index\nh10-index\nh5-index\n726\nCitations\n12\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n644\nCitations\n11\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n174\nCitations\n6\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1996                 …\n2024\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nBiography\nYixiao Zhou is Associate Professor in Economics at the Arndt-Corden Department of Economics and Director of China Economy Program, Crawford School of Public Policy. Yixiao’s research work focuses on three areas: global macroeconomics, the role of technology and innovation in economic growth, and the Chinese economy. Topics that she has research on include: forecasting international macroeconomic developments and policies in global trade, global competition and technology innovation, and global migration; forecasting economic growth in China and its relationships with the world; and understanding drivers of inclusive growth and development and identifying policies that enhance them.\nShe serves as President of\nthe Chinese Economics Society of Australia (CESA)\n, a member of the Economics Society of Australia ACT Branch (ESA ACT), the Western Economic Association International (WEAI), Australian Agricultural and Resource Economics Society (AARES), and the Chinese Economist Society (CES).\nYixiao earned her PhD in Economics from ANU, and her Bachelor of Economics and Bachelor of Science from Peking University. She is passionate about teaching and mentoring students for advanced, cutting-edge and innovative research with policy impact.\nQualifications\nANU (PhD Econ), PKU (BEcon), PKU (BSci)\nResearch interests\nYixiao is passionate about understanding drivers of inclusive growth and development and identifying policies that enhance them, forecasting international macroeconomic developments and policies, forecasting economic growth in China and its relationships with the world, and various topics on global economic growth and competition such as global trade, global competition and technology innovation, and global migration.\nORCID Publications Record\nGoogel Scholar Citations\nResearchgate\nEducation/Academic qualification\nEconomics, PhD,\nAustralian National University\nAward Date: 15 Dec 2014\nEconomics, Bachelor,\nPeking University\nAward Date: 1 Jul 2009\nPhysics, Bachelor,\nPeking University\nAward Date: 1 Jul 2009\nResearch student supervision\nRegistered to supervise\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Yixiao Zhou is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n3\nSimilar Profiles\nIncome Distribution\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n100%\nChina\nSocial Sciences\n83%\nIndustrialized Countries\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n66%\nStructural Change\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n58%\nLabor Market\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n55%\nMacroeconomics\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n41%\nTechnological Change\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n38%\nProductivity Change\nEconomics, Econometrics and Finance\n38%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nFind out about recent ANU collaborations across the world by selecting a location on the map OR\nview a list of countries/territories here\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n35\nArticle\n10\nChapter\n3\nEdited Book\n2\nBook\n5\nMore\n2\nEditorial\n2\nLiterature review\n1\nReview article\nInternational Differences in Profitability\nBloch, H. &\nZhou, Y.\n,\nMar 2024\n,\nIn:\nEconomic Record.\n100\n,\n328\n,\np. 101-116\n16 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nTime Series\n100%\nAutomation and inequality with taxes and transfers\nTyers, R. &\nZhou, Y.\n,\nFeb 2023\n,\nIn:\nScottish Journal of Political Economy.\n70\n,\n1\n,\np. 68-100\n33 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nWealth\n100%\nTaxation\n100%\nProductivity Change\n100%\nIncome Distribution\n100%\nTechnological Change\n100%\n3\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nGROWTH AND CONVERGENCE THROUGH TECHNOLOGICAL INTERDEPENDENCE\nJin, W. &\nZhou, Y.\n,\n9 Jul 2022\n,\nIn:\nMacroeconomic Dynamics.\n26\n,\n5\n,\np. 1338-1374\n37 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nIncome Distribution\n100%\nOptimal Growth\n100%\nBalanced Growth\n100%\n4\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nManaging China’s transition to a new phase of economic growth and development\nSong, L.\n&\nZhou, Y.\n,\n2022\n,\nChina’s Transition to a New Phase of Development.\nL. S. Y. Z. (ed.).\n1 ed.\nCanberra:\nANU Press\n,\nVol. 1\n.\np. 1-24\nResearch output\n:\nChapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding\n›\nChapter\n›\npeer-review\nChina\n100%\nEconomic Growth\n100%\nDevelopment of Economics\n100%\nGrowth and Development\n100%\nStandard of Living\n100%\nAnatomy of wage rigidity in China: Lessons from the global financial crisis for post-pandemic recovery\nDing, J. &\nZhou, Y.\n,\n9 Nov 2024\n,\nIn:\nEconomic Modelling.\n142\n,\n106932\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nFinancial Crisis\n100%\nWage Rigidity\n100%\nLabor Cost\n66%\nLabor Contract\n33%\n4\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 55 research outputs\nProjects\n1\nActive\n2\nFinished\nAutomation and Income Inequality: Macroeconomic Policy Implications\nBrueckner, M.\n(PI), Tyers, R. (CoI) &\nZhou, Y.\n(CoI)\n3/02/20\n→\n18/07/26\nProject\n:\nResearch\nIncome Distribution\n100%\nPolicy Implication\n100%\nEconomic Policy\n100%\nEconomic Model\n100%\nIncome and Wealth\n100%\nThe Impact of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) on China-Australia Bilateral Trade\nZhou, Y.\n(PI)\n14/02/23\n→\n31/03/24\nProject\n:\nResearch\nRegional Comprehensive Economic Partnership\n100%\nTrade Effect\n66%\nBilateral Trade\n50%\nValue Creation\n33%\nEconomic Welfare\n16%\nThe rise of Chinese corporations and global competition policies\nZhou, Y.\n(PI) &\nSong, L.\n(CoI)\n1/07/19\n→\n13/12/24\nProject\n:\nResearch"
