    "homepage_text": "Fan Wu\nFan Wu\nDoctoral Researcher\nETH Zürich\nAbout Me\nDuring my studies and research experiences in China, Germany, and Switzerland, I focused on developing digital applications and services using AI and data science to tacle complex real-world challenges. From electrical engineering and robotics to digital health, my passion is to develop technologies that improve people’s quality of life.\nInterests\nApplied Artificial Intelligence\nDigital Biomarkers\nMobile- & Wearables\nEmbedded Systems\nEducation\nPhD in Applied machine learning\nETH Zürich\nVisiting Researcher in Acoustic\nHarvard Medical School & Massachusetts General Hospital\nMSc Electrical engineering and information technology\nTechnical University Munich\nBSc Electrical engineering and its automation\nNorth China Electric Power University\nFeatured Publications\nDigital Biomarkers\nThe Bitemporal Lens Model—toward a holistic approach to chronic disease prevention with digital biomarkers\nJul 1, 2024\nWearables\nSmartwatch-Assessed Sleep and Quality of Life in Healthy Individuals\nThis work is continous work following my previous paper on circadian rhythm.\nApr 17, 2024\nWearables\nComparative efficacy of commercial wearables for circadian rhythm home monitoring from activity, heart rate, and core body temperature\nApr 4, 2024\nVoice\nTrends in voice characteristics in patients with heart failure (VENTURE) in Switzerland: Protocol for a longitudinal observational pilot study\nApr 5, 2023\nVoice\nVoice Remote Monitoring System for Patients with Heart Failure (VOMOS)\nOct 4, 2022\nFeatured Projects\nComputer Vision\nVision-based risk quantification on E-bikes for urban cycling\nMaster thesis at the (Computer Vision Lab) CVL, ETH\nMar 1, 2021\nSignal Processing\nSound source localization with head movement\nStudent project at TU Munich\nJul 1, 2019\nBrain-Computer Interface\nRobot movement with mind\nStudent project at TU Munich\nJun 1, 2019\nComputer Vision\nService Robot RoboCup@Home\nStudent project at TU Munich\nJun 1, 2019\nComputer Vision\nSoccer Shoot\nStudent project at TU Munich\nApr 1, 2019"
