    "homepage_text": "Chen Li – Homepage of Prof. Chen Li\nChen Li\nHome\nBiography\nResearch\nPublications\nStudents\nTeaching\nNews\nMiscellaneous\nExternal Links\nDBLP\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nX (Twitter)\nFacebook\nChen Li\nProfessor\nDepartment of Computer Science\n2086 Donald Bren Hall, University of California, Irvine, CA 92697-3435\nchenli AT ics DOT uci DOT edu,  Office: 949-824-9470\nInformation Systems Group\nChen Li is a professor in the Department of Computer Science at UC Irvine. He received his Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from Stanford University, and his M.S. and B.S. in Computer Science from Tsinghua University, China, respectively.  He was a recipient of an NSF CAREER award and several test-of-time publication awards, a part-time visiting research scientist at Google, PC co-chair of VLDB 2015, an ACM distinguished member, and an IEEE fellow. Since January 2020, he’s the treasurer and a board member of the VLDB Endowment.  From July 2020 to June 2024, he was the Faculty Director of the ICS Master of Computer Science Program. He was a co-founder and CTO of a startup to commercialize his research.\nCurriculum Vitae\nResearch\nMy research interests are in the field of data management, including data-intensive computing, databases, query processing and optimization, machine learning-based systems, data science, search, visualization. My current focus is building open-source systems for big data management, data science, and AI/ML.\nMy PhD thesis at Stanford was on data integration, with an emphasis on both theoretical and practical aspects. My recent research, especially after spending a few quarters at Google and a few years doing a startup as its founder and CTO, has a strong preference on engineering and open source system building.  I believe “Computer Science” is a “Science” to support great engineering, and we need to build systems to stay relevant in this fast-paced IT era.\nI was a co-PI of the Apache\nAsterixDB\nproject. Since 2016, our team has been developing the\nTexera\nopen-source system to support cloud-based collaborative data science, AI, and ML using workflows.\nLearn More …\nServices\nSIGMOD 2027 (General co-chair), VLDB Endowment 2020 – now (Treasurer and Board Member), ICDE Steering Committee (2024 – now),\nSIGMOD 2026 (PC member),\nSIGMOD 2025 (PC member), VLDB 2024\nReproducibility\n(PC member), VLDB 2023 (PC member), ICDE 2023 (General Chair), SIGMOD 2022 (PC member), VLDB 2021 (Associate Editor, Industrial co-Chair), ICDE 2021 (PC member), IEEE Big Data 2019 (Tutorial co-Chair), TKDE 2018-2022 (Associate Editor), VLDB 2015 (PC co-Chair).\nNews\n(2/21/26) My team organized the first Reunion event for former PhD students with our current students. Here are some\nphotos\n. Hope to organize more such events in the future 🙂\n(2/26) Yicong received a 2025 UCI CS Best Dissertation Honorable Mention award.  Congratulations!\n(11/25) Students at El Camino College organized a\nData Science for All workshop\nusing the Texera platform.  For the first time we have college students do the organization and teaching all by themselves, and they did an excellent job!\n(9/4/25) At\nVLDB 2025\nLondon, I gave a\npresentation\nof the\nIcedTea\npaper and co-presented a\ntutorial\ntitled “ML-Asset Management: Curation, Discovery, and Utilization.”\n(8/6/25) Yicong has successfully defined his thesis titled “\nUDF-Centric Dataflow Systems for Supporting User-defined Functions in Collaborative and Interactive Data Science, AI, and ML.” Congratulations, Dr. Huang!\n(8/6/25) Our Texera codebase has been officially denoted to the Apache Software Foundation.  The GitHub name has changed from\nhttps://github.com/Texera/texera to https://github.com/apache/texera.\n(7/25)\nYicong received a UC Irvine 2025 Most Promising Future Faculty Award. The award will be celebrated on the UCI Teach Day on\nSeptember 18th, 2025\n. Congratulations!\n(7/21/2025 – 7/23/2025) Together with UCLA and UCSD colleagues, we used the Texera platform to teach 17 biology students data science, AI, and ML as part of a\ndkNet data science bootcamp\n. It’s the first we deployed the whole system on AWS with auto-scaling!\n(7/21/2025) Our team used the Texera platform to teach 32 middle school students data science, AI, and ML. Check the\nphotos\n!\n(7/11/2025) Together with the team of Prof. Wei Wang from UCLA, we have successfully organized the\nData Science For All 2025 program\nat UCI. 33 high-school and college students used Texera to learn data science, AI, and ML.\n(6/2025) Gave a\ntalk\nat TU Berlin titled “\nTexera: An Open-Source System for Cloud-Based Collaborative Data Science and AI/ML Using Workflows” hosted by Prof. Odej Kao.\n(6/2025) Attended the UCI commencement to hood PhD students Yicong Huang and Shengquan Ni.  Congratulations!\n(5/21/2025) My team gave a\npresentation\nat an ACM OC Meetup\nevent\n.\n(5/6/2025) Our paper titled “\nResponsive State Retrieval in Pipelined Executions of Dataflows” was accepted by the\nHILDA workshop\ntogether with the ACM SIGMOD 2025 conference.\n(5/6/2025) Shengquan Ni successfully defended his PhD thesis.  He will join Google after graduation. Congratulations!\n(4/2025)\nYicong\nplans to join\nDatabricks in 2025 then UMass Amherst as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in 2027. Congratulations!\n(4/7/2025) Our team has a major\nTexera release 1.0.0\nwith the\ninstructions\nto install the system on a single machine using Docker.\n(4/2/2025) Our Texera project has been officially accepted by the Apache Incubator!\n(4/1/2025) We plan to organize the “\nData Science for All (DS4ALL)\n” summer program for the third year (together with UCLA) from July 7 to July 11, 2025. We will again use Texera to teach high-school students data science, AI, and ML.\n(3/24/2025) I will participate and teach in the\n2025 dkNET Summer of Data Student Program\n.\n(3/16/2025) Here’s our\nTexera incubation proposal\nto the Apache Software Foundation currently under community review.\n(2/25) Jiadong and I attended the\nDSE-K12 conference\nfrom February 17-19 in San Antonio, TX, and presented the paper titled: “DS4ALL: Teaching High-School Students Data Science and AI/ML Using the Texera Workflow Platform as a Service.” Here’s a\nphoto\nat the conference.\n(1/25) Please check our new\ntexera.io\nweb site! 🙂\n(1/25) In this quarter, for the first time, I am teaching two courses,\nCS 122B\n“Projects in Databases and Web Applications” and\nCS 122C/222\n“Principles of Data Management”.\nPast New\ns\nLatest News\n(7/19)\nGave talks at TU Berlin (Germany), Alibaba (Seattle), and Fudan University (China).\n(7/19)\nGave a tutorial on visualization of big spatial data at the VLDB Summer School, Beijing, China.\n(5/19)\nGlad to receive a UCI Chancellor’s Award for Excellence in Fostering Undergraduate Research.\nMore …\n\n---\n\nBiography – Chen Li\nChen Li\nHome\nBiography\nResearch\nPublications\nStudents\nTeaching\nNews\nMiscellaneous\nExternal Links\nDBLP\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nX (Twitter)\nFacebook\nBio\nChen Li is a professor in the Department of Computer Science at UC Irvine. He received his Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from Stanford University, and his M.S. and B.S. in Computer Science from Tsinghua University, China, respectively.\nHis research interests are in the field of data management, including data-intensive computing, query processing and optimization, visualization, and text analytics.\nHe was a recipient of an NSF CAREER award and several test-of-time publication awards, a part-time visiting research scientist at Google, PC co-chair of VLDB 2015, and an ACM distinguished member. He is\nthe treasurer and a board member of the VLDB Endowment.\nHe was a co-founder and CTO of a startup to commercialize his research results.\nCurriculum Vitae\nAppointments\nUC Irvine, CA\nProfessor\n2001 – present\n2012\nProfessor, UCI\n2007\nAsscociate Professor, UCI\n2001\nAssistant Professor, UCI\nEducation\nPhD (CS)\nStanford University\nStanford CA\n1996-2001\nMS (CS)\nTsinghua University\nBeijing China\n1994-1996\nBS (Management)\nTsinghua University\nBeijing China\n1991-1994\nBS (CS)\nTsinghua University\nBeijing China\n1989-1994\nIndustry\nSRCH2\nIrvine CA\nFounder\n2010-2014\nGoogle Research\nMountain View CA\nVisiting Research Scientist\n2005-2007\nIBM\nSupplemental Research Associate\n2000-2001\nHP Lab\nResearch Intern\nSummer 1998\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\nStudent Visitor\nSummer 1995"
  },
