    "homepage_text": "Zongwei Zhou\ntop of page\nZongwei Zhou, PhD\nAssistant Research Professor\nDepartments of Computer Science and Oncology\nJohns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD\nView CV\nEmail:\nzzhou82@jh.edu\nTel: 1-(480)738-2575\nOffice: 248 Malone Hall, Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD\n​\nOverview\nZongwei Zhou is an assistant research professor in the Johns Hopkins University’s\nDepartment of Computer Science\nwith a joint appointment in Oncology through the\nSchool of Medicine\n’s\nSidney Kimmel Comprehensive Cancer Center\n. As a member of the\nData Science and AI Institute\nand the\nCenter for Imaging Science\n, h\nis research focuses on medical computer vision, language, and graphics for early cancer detection and diagnosis.\n​\nHe is best known for developing UNet++, a widely adopted segmentation architecture cited more than 17,000 times since its publication in 2019. He currently serves as PI on an NIH–NIBIB R01 grant ($2.8M, top 1.0 percentile). His work has earned multiple honors, including the AMIA Doctoral Dissertation Award, Elsevier–MedIA Best Paper Award, and MICCAI Young Scientist Award.\nDr. Zhou also received the President’s Award for Innovation, the highest honor for graduate students at Arizona State University, and has been recognized among the Top 2% of Scientists Worldwide every year since 2022.\n​​\nCurrent Research:\nEarly Cancer Detection by Computed Tomography and Artificial Intelligence\nORCiD: 0000-0002-3154-9851\n​\n​\nAwards and Honors\nRSNA 2025 Certificate of Merit Award | Dec 2025\nMICCAI Best Paper Award,\nRunner-up | Sep 2025\nPrincipal Investigator,\nNIH R01 Grant ($2.8M)\n, 2025-2029 | June 2025\nPresident's Awards for Innovation, Arizona State University\n| Oct 2024\nCo-Investigator, Lustgarten Foundation ($1.9M), 2023-2028 | May 2023\nCo-Investigator, Patrick J. McGovern Foundation ($400K), 2023-2025 | May 2023\nAMIA Doctoral Dissertation Award\n| Nov 2022\nTop 2% Scientists Worldwide\n, Stanford University |\nNov 2022 - 2025\nMICCAI Young Scientist Publication Impact Award Finalist | Sep 2022\nElsevier-MedIA Best Paper Award\n| Oct 2020\nGraduate Fellowship, Arizona State University | Mar 2020\nMICCAI Young Scientist Award\n| Oct 2019\nMICCAI Best Presentation Award Finalist | Oct 2019\nOutstanding Graduate, Dalian University of Technology | June 2016\nRecent News​​\nTwo papers were accepted to\nNeurIPS 2025\n| Sep 2025\n18 abstracts (8/18 oral) were accepted to\nRSNA 2025\nCS News\n| July\n2025\nFour papers were accepted to\nICCV 2025\n| June 2025\nOne paper was accepted to\nMICCAI 2025\n| June 2025\nKeynote talk at\nCVPRW MCV\n(\nrecord\n)| June 2025\nEducation\nPh.D. | Aug 2017-May 2021\nArizona State University\nBiomedical Informatics\nTowards Annotation-Efficient Deep Learning for Computer-Aided Diagnosis\nAMIA Doctoral Dissertation Award\nPresident's Awards for Innovation\nAdvised by\nDr. Jianming Liang\n> View Dissertation\n> View LaTeX\n> View Talk\n> View Slides\n> View Transcript\n​\nB.S. | Sep 2012-Jul 2016\nDalian University of Technology\nComputer Science\nMedical image classification based on deep learning\nAdvised by\nDr. Hongkai Wang\n> View Dissertation\n> View Slides\n​\nExperience\nAssistant Research Professor | Nov 2025-present\nAssistant Research Scientist | May 2024-Nov 2025\nPostdoctoral Researcher | June 2021-May 2024\nJohns Hopkins University\nGroup:\nComputational Cognition, Vision, and Learning (CCVL)\nResearch Internship | Jan 2018-July 2018\nCentre Hospitalier de l’Université de Montréal\nGroup:\nLaboratoire clinique de traitement de l’image (LCTI)\nProjects: Predictive model of colorectal cancer liver metastases response to chemotherapy\nJoint collaboration:\nImagia\nand\nMILA\n​\nResearch Internship | June 2017-Jul 2017\nMayo Clinic, Rochester MN\nGroup:\nRadiology Informatics Lab\nProjects: Thyroid Ultrasound Imaging, Tumor Radiogenomics\nFeatured Talks\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nJHU CS Seminar: Early Cancer Detection by Computed Tomography and Artificial Intelligence\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nKeynote Talk at CVPR 2025 Workshop (Medical Computer Vision)\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nSeminar Talk at Emory University\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nInvited Talk at MICCAI 2024 Workshop - MedShapeNet\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nJob Talk at Cornell University\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nKeynote at MICCAI-2024 AIPAD Workshop\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nPresentation of AMIA 2022 Doctoral Dissertation Award\nPlay Video\nPlay Video\nTowards Annotation-Efficient Deep Learning for Computer-Aided Diagnosis\nbottom of page"
