    "homepage_text": "Jiancheng Liu\nJiancheng (JC) Liu\nI am a Member of Technical Staff at OpenAI, working on LLM post-training. I am one of the\n                        contributors to the\nGPT-5 series\nand the\ngpt-oss\nseries.\nI received my B.E. in computer science from the\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information\n                            Sciences\n(\nYao Class\n), Tsinghua\n                        University. I was fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Shi-Min Hu\non my undergraduate\n                        research and bachelor thesis. In 2018, I had some wonderful times working with\nProf. Wojciech Matusik\nand\nDr. Yuanming Hu\nat MIT.\nBefore joining OpenAI, I completed my M.S. degree in Computer Science at Michigan State\n                        University. During those two years, I focused on enhancing AI trustworthiness through\nMachine\n                            Unlearning\nin collaboration with\nProf. Sijia\n                            Liu\n.\nI am an AASI-certified level 1 snowboard instructor and was a baritone singer in the Tsinghua A\n                        Cappella Club. I love snowboarding and singing. If you are looking for a place to ski, you can\n                        check this\nski resort weather forecast\n.\nEmail:\nljcc (at) openai (dot) com\n                        [\nCV\n]\n                        [\nGoogle Scholar\n]\n                        [\nGitHub\n]\n                        [\nLinkedIn\n]\nIndustrial Reports\nIntroducing GPT-5.2\nOpenAI\n[Product Page]\n[System Card]\nGPT-5.1: A smarter, more conversational ChatGPT\nOpenAI\n[Product Page]\n[System Card]\nIntroducing GPT-5\nOpenAI\n[Product Page]\n[System Card]\nIntroducing gpt-oss\nOpenAI\n[Product Page]\n[Model Card]\nPublications\n( “*” indicates equal contribution.)\nConferences\nLabel Smoothing Improves Machine Unlearning\nICLR 2026\nZonglin Di, Zhaowei Zhu, Jinghan Jia,\nJiancheng Liu\n, Zafar Takhirov, Bo Jiang,\n                            Yuanshun Yao, Sijia Li