    "github": "https://github.com/ZwwWayne",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/wenweizhang-b9769a124/",
    "homepage_text": "Wenwei Zhang, 张文蔚 - Wenwei Zhang\nWenwei Zhang\nPhD student at NTU\nFollow\nSingapore\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nWenwei Zhang, 张文蔚\nWenwei Zhang is a Young Research Scientist at\nShanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory\n. He obtained his Ph.D. degree at\nMMLab\n,\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering\n, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, supervised by Professor\nChen Change (Cavan) Loy\n. Before that, he received his bachelor degree at the\nComputer Science School\n, Wuhan University. You can find his CV\nhere\n.\nHe has been leading a post-training team of\nInternLM\nsince 2023, working on AI Agents and self-improvement (scalable oversight) of Large Language Models. His past works mainly explore\nversatile neural architectures across modalities and perception tasks\nand open-vocabulary perception. He built and released\nMMDetection3D\n, and has been leading the development of\nMMDetection\nand\nMMDetection3D\nsince 2020, respectively, as a core member of\nOpenMMLab\nsince 2019.\nWe have opening positions for PhD/postdoc/intern and full-time researchers. If you are interested please send me an email.\nRecent News\nIntern-S1, state-of-the-art open-source multi-modal foundation model has been released. See\nIntern-S1 Collections\nand\ntech report\n(July, 2025).\nInternLM2.5-StepProver won the\nBest Paper Runner-Up Award\nin ICML2025 AI4Math Workshop.\nInternLM2.5-Chat, state-of-the-art open-source LLMs in\nopencompass\nand\nhuggingface leadboard\n, have been released. See\nInternLM2.5 Model Zoo\n. (July, 2024)\nInternLM2-Chat, state-of-the-art open-source LLMs in\nopencompass\nand\nAlpacaEval2\n, have been released. See\nInternLM2 Model Zoo\n. (Jan., 2024)\n2 papers (\nCLIPSelf\nand\nUniHSI\n) are accepted as\nspotlights\nby ICLR2024. (Jan., 2024)\nWe release\nOpenMMLab 2.0\nwith a new core,\nMMEngine\n. (Sept. 2022)\nVideo K-Net\nis accepted by CVPR 2022 (\noral\n). (May, 2022)\nK-Net\nis accepted by NeurIPS 2021. Code has been released at\nhere\n. (Oct., 2021)\nMMDet3D team obtains\nBest PKL Award\nand best vision-only results in the 3rd nuScenes detection challenge of 5th AI Driving Olympics, NeurIPS 2020. Paper of our multi-modality method is released in\narxiv\n. (Dec., 2020)\nSecond runner up in\nLVIS2020 Challenge\n. Paper can be found\nin arxiv\n.\nWe release\nMMDetection3D\n, OpenMMLab’s next-generation platform for general 3D object detection. (July, 2020)\nWin the\n1st prize\nin\nCOCO 2019 Object Detection Challenge\n(no external data). (Team: MMDet)\nAcademic Service\nArea Chair: CVPR2026\nConference Reviewer: CVPR2020-2025, ICCV2021-2025, ECCV2020-2024, ICLR2022-2026, NeurIPS2021-2025, ICML2023-2024, ACM MM2020.\nCommittee member and speaker of OpenMMLab Tutorials in CVPR\n2021\n/\n2022\n/2023, and\nAAAI2023\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Wenwei Zhang\nWenwei Zhang\nPhD student at NTU\nFollow\nSingapore\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in Wuhan, China, Wuhan University, 2019(expected).\nWork experience\nSpring 2018: Research Intern at\nSensetime\nResearch filed included: Lane Segmentation, Scene Recovery Algorithm, Panorama Stitching.\nSupervisor:\nZhe Wang\nSummer 2018: Research Intern at\niNCML Lab, York University\nResearch filed included: Reading Comprehension Question & Answering Task\nSupervisor: Professor\nHui Jiang\nSkills\nProgram Language: Python, lua, matlab, C++, Java.\nDeep Learning Framework: Pytorch, Torch, Caffe.\nEnglish Skills: IELTS 6.5, TOEFL 91, GRE 321+3.\nPublications\nBefore the Rise of Machines, The beginning of Consciousness and the Human Intelligence\nStripNet: Towards Topology Consistent Strip Structure Segmentation\nRobust Multi-Modality Multi-Object Tracking\nEcoNAS: Finding Proxies for Economical Neural Architecture Search\nSide-Aware Boundary Localization for More Precise Object Detection\nExploring Data Augmentation for Multi-Modality 3D Object Detection\nSeesaw Loss for Long-Tailed Instance Segmentation\nK-Net: Towards Unified Image Segmentation\nVideo K-Net: A Simple, Strong, and Unified Baseline for Video Segmentation\nDense Siamese Network for Dense Unsupervised Learning\nDense Distinct Query for End-to-End Object Detection\nMV-JAR: Masked Voxel Jigsaw and Reconstruction for LiDAR-Based Self-Supervised Pre-Training\nAligning Bag of Regions for Open-Vocabulary Object Detection\nTube-Link: A Flexible Cross Tube Baseline for Universal Video Segmentation\nRobo3D: Towards Robust and Reliable 3D Perception against Corruptions\nPosition-Guided Point Cloud Panoptic Segmentation Transformer"
  },
