    "homepage_text": "Liang Pan\nLiang Pan 潘亮\nBuilding scalable AI agents with MLLMs and robots\nFirst-year Ph.D. student\nSchool of Computing and Data Science\nThe University of Hong Kong\nEmail:\nliangpan1005@163.com\n|\nWeChat: liangpan_time\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n][\nGithub\n][\nX (Twitter)\n][\nLinkedin\n][CV]\nBiography\nI am a first-year CS Ph.D. student at The University of Hong Kong, advised by Prof.\nTaku Komura\n. \n        Prior that, I received my master's degree from Southeast University in 2024 and bachelor's degree from Hangzhou Dianzi University in 2021.\nNews\n[2026/02/04] Two papers got accepted by ICRA 2026:\nAgility Meets Stability\nand\nEmbracing Bulky Objects\n.\n[2025/09/18] One paper got accepted by NeurIPS 2025.\n[2025/06/26] Three papers got accepted by ICCV 2025. See you in Hawaii! 🌴\n[2025/04/21] Invited talks (\nslides\n) on\n\"Towards Behavior Foundation Models of Human-Scene Interactions\"\nat\nElectronic Arts\nhosted by Dr.\nBen Ling\n,\nAnySyn3D\n, and\nShanghai Computer Society\n.\n[2025/04/05] TokenHSI has been selected as an oral paper at CVPR 2025. Top 3.3% of the accepted papers (96/2878).\n[2025/03/12] A brand-new version of SIMS is available. Enjoy the stories created by SIMS!\n[2025/02/27] TokenHSI got accepted by CVPR 2025.\n[Show more]\nSelected Publications (\nFull List\n)\n* denotes equal contribution, and\n†\ndenotes the corresponding author\n2025\n?\nTokenHSI: Unified Synthesis of Physical Human-Scene Interactions through Task Tokenization\nLiang Pan\n, Zeshi Yang, Zhiyang Dou, Wenjia Wang, Buzhen Huang, Bo Dai, Taku Komura, Jingbo Wang\n†\nCVPR 2025\n🏆️ Oral Presentation (Top 3.3%)\nThe 1st Workshop on Humanoid Agents @ CVPR 2025\n🌟 Spotlight\n[\nPaper\n]\n        [\nProject Page\n]\n2024\n?\nSynthesizing Physically Plausible Human Motions in 3D Scenes\nLiang Pan\n, Jingbo Wang, Buzhen Huang, Junyu Zhang, Haofan Wang, Xu Tang, Yangang Wang\n†\n3DV 2024\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n]\n2022\n?\nNeural MoCon: Neural Motion Control for Physically Plausible Human Motion Capture\n        Buzhen Huang,\nLiang Pan\n, Yuan Yang, Jingyi Ju, Yangang Wang\n†\nCVPR 2022\n[\nPaper\n][\nProject Page\n]"
