    "homepage_text": "Xu Han - Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University\nResume - Start Bootstrap Theme\nXu\nHan\nResearch Assistant Professor,\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology,\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing,\n          China.\nContact\nthu [dot] hanxu13 [at] gmail [dot] com\ncst_hanxu13 [at] 163 [dot] com\nRoom 4-506, FIT Building, Tsinghua University\nBeijing, 100084, China\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nHi! I am a research assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science and\n                  Technology\nat\nTsinghua\n                  University\n.\nMy research interests include natural language processing, deep learning, knowledge computing, and machine learning systems. Currently, I am focusing on exploring how to efficiently build effective large foundation models at the intersection between artificial intelligence and high-performance computing. If you are interested in joining us, please email me with your latest resume.\nBefore serving as an assistant professor, I was a Postdoctoral Researcher in the Department of Computer Science and Technology at Tsinghua University under the supervision of Professor Maosong Sun. I also got my bachelor degree and completed my Ph.D. program in the Department of Computer Science and Technology at Tsinghua University under the supervision of Professor Zhiyuan Liu.\nPUBLICATIONS\n(* indicates equal contribution, † indicates corresponding author)\n2024\n1.   Shengding Hu, Xin Liu,\nXu Han†\n, Xinrong Zhang, Chaoqun He, Weilin Zhao, Yankai Lin, Ning Ding, Zebin Ou, Guoyang Zeng, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Predicting Emergent Abilities with Infinite Resolution Evaluation. ICLR 2024. Long Paper.\n2.   Jinyi Hu, Yuan Yao, Chongyi Wang, Shan Wang, Yinxu Pan, Qianyu Chen, Tianyu Yu, Hanghao Wu, Yue Zhao, Haoye Zhang,\nXu Han\n, Yankai Lin, Jiao Xue, Dahai Li, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Large Multilingual Models Pivot Zero-shot Multimodal Learning across Languages. ICLR 2024. Long Paper.\n3.   Shengding Hu, Yuge Tu,\nXu Han†\n, Chaoqun He, Ganqu Cui, Xiang Long, Zhi Zheng, Yewei Fang, Yuxiang Huang, Weilin Zhao, Xinrong Zhang, Zheng Leng Thai, Kaihuo Zhang, Chongyi Wang, Yuan Yao, Chenyang Zhao, Jie Zhou, Jie Cai, Zhongwu Zhai, Ning Ding, Chao Jia, Guoyang Zeng, Dahai Li, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. MiniCPM: Unveiling the Potential of Small Language Models with Scalable Training Strategies. COLM 2024. Long Paper.\n4.   Weilin Zhao, Yuxiang Huang,\nXu Han†\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Zhengyan Zhang, Kuai Li, Chen Chen, Tao Yang, Maosong Sun. CA-LoRA: Adapting Existing LoRA for Compressed LLMs to Enable Efficient Multi-Tasking on Personal Devices. COLM 2024. Long Paper.\n5.   Xinrong Zhang, Yingfa Chen, Shengding Hu, Zihang Xu, Junhao Chen, Moo Hao,\nXu Han†\n, Zhen Thai, Shuo Wang, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. ∞ Bench: Extending Long Context Evaluation Beyond 100K Tokens. ACL 2024. Long Paper.\n6.   Chaoqun He, Renjie Luo, Yuzhuo Bai, Shengding Hu, Zhen Leng Thai, Junhao Shen, Jinyi Hu,\nXu Han†\n, Yujie Huang, Yuxiang Zhang, Jie Liu, Lei Qi, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. OlympiadBench: A Challenging Benchmark for Promoting AGI with Olympiad-Level Bilingual Multimodal Scientific Problems. ACL 2024. Long Paper.\n7.   Yufei Huang,\nXu Han\n, Maosong Sun. FastFiD: Improve Inference Efficiency of Open Domain Question Answering via Sentence Selection. ACL 2024. Long Paper.\n8.   Hanqing Wang, Bowen Ping, Shuo Wang,\nXu Han\n, Yun Chen, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. LoRA-Flow: Dynamic LoRA Fusion for Large Language Models in Generative Tasks. ACL 2024. Long Paper.\n9.   Xiaozhi Wang, Hao Peng, Yong Guan, Kaisheng Zeng, Jianhui Chen, Lei Hou,\nXu Han\n, Yankai Lin, Zhiyuan Liu, Ruobing Xie, Jie Zhou, Juanzi Li. MAVEN-ARG: Completing the Puzzle of All-in-One Event Understanding Dataset with Event Argument Annotation. ACL 2024. Long Paper.\n10.   Chaoqun He, Renjie Luo, Shengding Hu, Yuanqian Zhao, Jie Zhou, Hanghao Wu, Jiajie Zhang,\nXu Han†\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. UltraEval: A Lightweight Platform for Flexible and Comprehensive Evaluation for LLMs. ACL 2024. Demo Paper.\n11.   Xinrong Zhang, Yingfa Chen, Shengding Hu,\nXu Han†\n, Zihang Xu, Yuanwei Xu, Weilin Zhao, Maosong Sun, Zhiyuan Liu. Beyond The Turn-based Game: Enabling Real-time Conversations With Duplex Models. EMNLP 2024. Long Paper.\n12.   Weilin Zhao, Yuxiang Huang,\nXu Han†\n, Chaojun Xiao, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Ouroboros: Speculative Decoding with Large Model Enhanced Drafting. EMNLP 2024. Long Paper.\n13.   Zhengyan Zhang, Chaojun Xiao, Qiujieli Qin, Yankai Lin, Zhiyuan Zeng,\nXu Han\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Ruobing Xie, Maosong Sun, Jie Zhou. Exploring the Benefit of Activation Sparsity in Pre-training. ICML 2024. Long Paper.\n14.   Yingfa Chen, Zhengyan Zhang,\nXu Han†\n, Chaojun Xiao, Zhiyuan Liu, Chen Chen, Kuai Li, Tao Yang, Maosong Sun. Robust and Scalable Model Editing for Large Language Models. COLING 2024. Long Paper.\n15.   Weize Chen,\nXu Han†\n, Yankai Lin, Kaichen He, Ruobing Xie, Jie Zhou, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Hyperbolic Pre-Trained Language Model. IEEE TASLP 2024. Long Paper.\n2023\n1.   Chaojun Xiao, Zhengyan Zhang,\nXu Han†\n, Chi-Min Chan, Yankai Lin, Zhiyuan Liu, Xiangyang Li, Zhonghua Li, Zhao Cao, Maosong Sun. Plug-and-play Document Modules For Pre-trained Models. ACL 2023. Long Paper.\n2.   Zhengyan Zhang, Zhiyuan Zeng, Yankai Lin, Huadong Wang, Deming Ye, Chaojun Xiao,\nXu Han†\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Peng Li, Maosong Sun, Jie Zhou. Plug-and-play Knowledge Injection For Pre-trained Language Models. ACL 2023. Long Paper.\n3.   Weize Chen,\nXu Han†\n, Yankai Lin, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun, Jie Zhou. Stochastic Bridges as Effective Regularizers for Parameter-Efficient Tuning. Findings of ACL 2023. Long Paper.\n4.   Yujia Qin, Cheng Qian,\nXu Han†\n, Yankai Lin, Huadong Wang, Ruobing Xie, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun, Jie Zhou. Recyclable Tuning for Continual Pre-training. Findings of ACL 2023. Long Paper.\n5.   Yujia Qin, Zihan Cai, Dian Jin, Lan Yan, Shih