    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaowen Dong\nXiaowen Dong\nDepartment of Engineering Science\nUniversity of Oxford\nEagle House\nWalton Well Road\nOxford OX2 6ED\nEmail: xdong [at] robots [dot] ox [dot] ac [dot] uk\nTelephone: +44 (0)1865 616633\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTalks\nResources\nTeaching\nGroup\nI am an associate professor in the\nDepartment of Engineering Science\nat the\nUniversity of Oxford\n, where I am a member of the\nMachine Learning Research Group\n. I am also a fellow and tutor in Engineering at\nLady Margaret Hall\n. Prior to joining Oxford, I was a postdoctoral associate at the\nMIT Media Lab\n, and received my PhD degree from the\nÉcole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL)\n. My main research interests concern signal processing and machine learning techniques for analysing data with complex structures, and their applications in social, urban, and financial network analysis.\nNews\nMore\n[2026.02]\nTalk at\nLSE\n.\n[2026.01]\nPaper\n,\nPaper\n,\nPaper\nand\nPaper\naccepted at ICLR'26.\n[2026.01]\nPaper\naccepted in IEEE TSP.\n[2026.01]\nPaper\naccepted at AISTATS'26.\n[2026.01]\nPaper\naccepted at IEEE ICASSP'26.\n[2025.12]\nTop area chair at LoG'25.\n[2025.12]\nPanel at NeurIPS'25 Workshop on\nNew Perspectives in Graph Machine Learning\n.\n[2025.11]\nPaper\npublished in Nature Reviews Physics.\n[2025.10]\nPaper\naccepted at LoG'25.\n[2025.10]\nTop reviewer at NeurIPS'25.\n[2025.09]\nPaper\n,\nPaper\nand\nPaper\naccepted at NeurIPS'25.\n[2025.09]\nTalk at\nCUHK\n.\n[2025.09]\nDepartmental teaching award\nfor academic year 2024-25.\n[2025.09]\nPaper\naccepted at CAMSAP'25."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zhiqi Li::https://zhiqi-li.github.io/": {
