  "deep_homepage::Yaoxin Wu::https://www.tue.nl/en/research/researchers/yaoxin-wu": {
    "homepage": "https://www.tue.nl/en/research/researchers/yaoxin-wu",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yaoxin Wu\nSkip to content\nMenu\nClose the menu\nMenu\nEindhoven\nUniversity of\nTechnology\nEducation\nResearch\nOur university\nWorking at TU/e\nNews and Events\nImpact\nSearch\nSearch\nResearch\nInstitutes\nCasimir Institute\nEindhoven Artificial Intelligence Systems Institute\nEindhoven Institute for Renewable Energy Systems\nInstitute for Complex Molecular Systems\nResearch Areas\nRobotics\nArtificial Intelligence\nSmart Mobility\nEngineering Health\nIntegrated Photonics\nQuantum Technology\nData Science\nHumans and Technology\nResearch Groups\nResearch Labs\nOther labs and facilities\nResearch Projects\nResearchers\nDepartments\nApplied Physics and Science Education\nBiomedical Engineering\nBuilt Environment\nChemical Engineering and Chemistry\nEindhoven School of Education\nElectrical Engineering\nIndustrial Design\nIndustrial Engineering and Innovation Sciences\nMathematics and Computer Science\nMechanical Engineering\nGrants & Awards\nNational Grants\nInternational Grants\nResearch assessments\nWinners TU/e Science Awards\nResearch Support\nAssistant Professor\nYaoxin Wu\nPURE url\nContact\ny.wu2@\nremove-this.\ntue.nl\nAtlas 5.406\nDepartment / Institute\nIndustrial Engineering and Innovation Sciences\nGroup\nInformation Systems IE&IS\nEAISI\nRESEARCH PROFILE\nMy main interests concentrate on deep learning, combinatorial optimization and integer programming. I am currently devoted to the learning for optimization field, with the aim to explore deep learning based methods to solve integer programs and combinatorial optimization problems, including vehicle routing, shop scheduling, airport ground handling, on-demand delivery with UAV, train unit shunting and so on.\nArtificial Intelligence: Deep Reinforcement Learning, Graph Neural Network, LLMs, VAEs & GANs\nOperations Research: Heuristic Search, (Stochastic) Integer Programming, Multi-Objective Optimization\nApplications: Transportation, Scheduling, Network Design, Graph Optimization, Ride-hailing Optimization\nYaoxin Wu is the daily/first supervisor of\n- Xia Jiang (PhD)\n- Igor Smite (PhD)\n- Minshuo Li (PhD)\n- Yue Yu (PhD)\n- Tijmen Bouwman (Master)\n- Olivier Vugts (Master) Congrats on oral defense!\n- Hexiang Gao (Master)\n- Xingyi Li (Master) Congrats on oral defense!\n- Mannepu, Venkata Roshan (Master)\n- Floor Halkes (Master) Congrats on oral defense!\nAnything that can go wrong will go wrong\", said my lovely destiny.\nACADEMIC BACKGROUND\nYaoxin Wu received the Ph.D. degree in computer science from Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in 2023. In the same year, he joined the Information Systems group within the Department of Industrial Engineering and Innovation Sciences at Eindhoven University of Technology as an Assistant Professor.  His research interests include deep learning, combinatorial optimization and integer programming.\nRecent Publications\nSee all publications\nCooperative Multi-Agent Advice Exchange via Topological Graph Learning\nIEEE Transactions on Cognitive and Developmental Systems\n(2026)\nSihan Zhou,Yaqing Hou,Yaoxin Wu,Xiangchao Yu,Liran Zhou,Haiyin Piao,Qiang Zhang\nDeep Reinforcement Learning Based Genetic Framework for Flexible Job-Shop Scheduling Under Practical Constraints\n19th International Conference on Learning and Intelligent Optimization, LION 2025\n(2026)\nRobbert Reijnen,Zaharah Bukhsh,Yaoxin Wu,Yingqian Zhang\nReinforcement learning for solving the pricing problem in column generation for routing\nOperations Research Perspectives\n(2025)\nAbdo Abouelrous,Laurens Bliek,Adriana F. Gabor,Yaoxin Wu,Yingqian Zhang\nA deep reinforcement learning method for solving Two-Echelon Location-Routing Problem\nComputers and Operations Research\n(2025)\nShuo Huang,Yaoxin Wu,Zhiguang Cao,Xuexi Zhang\nBenders decomposition for traveling salesman problem with drone\nTransportation Research Part C: Emerging Technologies\n(2025)\nChenhao Zhang,Yaoxin Wu,Tao Feng,Yibei Zhang,Maocan Song,Lin Cheng\nAncillary Activities\nNo ancillary activities"
  },
