      "ling@cvm.t.u-tokyo.ac.jp",
      "lingxiao@hust.edu.cn",
      "ling@ist.hokudai.ac.jp"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/Dr-LingXiao",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ling-xiao-028262315/",
    "homepage_text": "Ling Xiao — Homepage\nLing Xiao\nTenured Associate Professor（准教授 / 副教授）\nat\nHokkaido University (北海道大学)\n客員研究員 in\nYamasaki Lab\n,\nThe University of Tokyo (東京大学)\nIEEE Senior Member\nFrom 2025.04.01, I joined Hokkaido University as an associate professor and lead Multimodal Agent & Robotic System (MARS) Team. \n                From 2023.10.01–2025.03.31, I was a Project Assistant Professor at CVM (Yamasaki Lab), The University of Tokyo, Japan.\n                From 2021.06 to 2023.10, I was a Project Researcher at CVM (Yamasaki Lab), The University of Tokyo, Japan. \n                In 2020.12, I received my Ph.D. degree at\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\n, P.R. China.\n                From 2018.10 to 2019.11, I was a visiting student at\nThe University of Queensland\n, Australia.\n                From 2014.07 to 2015.08, I was a mechanical engineer at\nBYD Company Limited\n, P.R. China.\nMy research interests focus on:\nAdaptive Intelligent Systems Operating in Complex and Dynamic Environments\nRecommendation Systems\nRobotic AI\nFine-grained Detection\nMultimodal Vision Language Models\nMachine Learning (continual learning, open-world recognition, adversarial attacks, etc.)\nFaculty of Information Science and Technology, Hokkaido University, 9-9 Kita-14-jo Nishi, Kita-ku, Sapporo, Hokkaido 060-0814, Japan\n（〒060-0814 札幌市北区北14条西9丁目 北海道大学 大学院情報科学研究院 10-01号室）\nling(at)ist.hokudai.ac.jp, lingxiaodr(at)gmail.com\nOld:\nlingxiao(at)hust.edu.cn, ling(at)cvm.t.u-tokyo.ac.jp\nGoogle Scholar\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nGitHub\nCollaboration / 共同研究\nSeeking\nacademic–industry collaborations\n.\n産学連携の\n共同研究パートナー\nを募集しています。\nStudents / 学生募集\nLooking for\nhighly motivated Ph.D. students\n.\n意欲のある\n博士課程の学生\nを募集しています。\n入試情報:\nこちら\nNews\n[ 2026.03 ] One paper got IE award!\n[ 2026.02 ] One paper and one findings got accepted to 2026 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)!\n[ 2026.01 ] One paper was accepted to 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing (ICASSP)!\n[ 2025.12 ] One paper was accepted to IEEE Transactions on Multimedia!\n[ 2025.11 ] My friend,\nProf. Xuesu Xiao\nfrom George Mason University, will give a talk titled \"Deployable Robots that Learn\" on Dec. 17th, 2025, (14:00-) at 北海道大学 大学院情報科学研究院 10-21室. Please join us if you are interested.\n[ 2025.11 ] My friend,\nProf. Zhu Li\nfrom University of Missouri, will give a talk titled \"Sparse Feature Pyramid Recovery for Vision Tasks under Adverse Imaging Conditions\" on Nov. 24th, 2025, at 北海道大学 大学院情報科学研究院 10-21室. Please join us if you are interested.\n[ 2025.11 ] My Ph.D student (Xinyu Zhang) achieves Hokkaido University EXEX Doctoral Fellowship.\n[ 2025.08 ] I am a 客員研究員 of\nYamasaki Lab\n,\nThe University of Tokyo\n, from 2025.08.01–2026.07.31.\n[ 2025.07 ] We will organize a workshop on ‘Data-Driven and AI-Empowered Future of Low-Altitude Economy (DALAE 2025) in WISE 2025’, Dec 15–17, 2025, Morocco. Details\nhere\n. Deadline: Jul 30.\n[ 2025.07 ] We achieved Best Paper Award in\nICMR 2025\n!\n[ 2025.05 ] I will co-organize a workshop\nSecure and Safe AI Agents for Big Data Infrastructures\nin\nBigData 2025\n, Dec 8–11, 2025, Macau.\n[ 2025.05 ] I will be an Associate Editor for\nIEICE Transactions on Information and Systems\n, 2025.06.10–2029.06.07.\n[ 2025.05 ] Conference Chair of\nAPIT 2026\n&\nCVCI 2026\n, Jan 9–11, 2026, Hokkaido, Japan.\n[ 2025.04 ] Selected as IEEE Senior Member.\n[ 2025.04 ] Hiring JSPS PD… Please feel free to contact me.\n[ 2025.04 ] Start at\nHokkaido University\nas Associate Professor.\n[ 2025.02 ] Selected as Youth Editorial Board Member of\n智能安全\n.\n[ 2025.02 ] Invited talk at\nIVSP 2025\n, “Revolutionizing AI Applications: Innovative Approaches with Multimodal Large Language Models”.\n[ 2024.09 ] Invited talk at\nCITA 2024\n, “Large multimodal model based recommendation systems”.\n[ 2024.04 ] 若手研究. Project: Efficient and accurate scaling Graph Neural Networks for giant graphs, 2024.04–2026.04, 4,680,000 yen.\n[ 2024.03 ] Invited talk at 信学技報, MVE, “The Past, Current and Future of Fashion Image Retrieval: Toward a User-Centered Orientation”.\n[ 2023.11 ] Adjunct Project Assistant Professor at Beyond AI 研究推進機構.\n[ 2023.10 ] Invited talk at BAI Research Seminar, “Affordable and advanced artificial intelligence in fashion”.\n[ 2023.10 ] Project Assistant Professor,\nYamasaki Lab\n,\nThe University of Tokyo\n.\n[ 2022.09 ] Received AIセンター融合研究促進費. “Explainable Recommendations AI”, 2022.10–2023.04, 2,000,000 yen.\n[ 2022.07 ] Adjunct researcher at Beyond AI 研究推進機構 (“メタバース空間におけるユーザ体験最適化”).\n[ 2021.06 ] Project Researcher,\nYamasaki Lab\n,\nThe University of Tokyo\n.\n[ 2020.12 ] Ph.D.,\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\n, China.\n[ 2018.10–2019.11 ] Visiting student at\nThe University of Queensland\n, Australia.\n[ 2018.06 ] China Scholarship Council Scholarship (No: 20180616011) (1/10)."
  },
