      "gxia@nyu.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Gus Xia | NYU Tandon School of Engineering\nSkip to Main Content\nNYU Tandon Logo\nNYU Tandon Logo\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nDigital Learning\nDepartments\nApplied Physics\nBiomedical Engineering\nCenter for Urban Science and Progress\nChemical and Biomolecular Engineering\nCivil, Urban and Environmental Engineering\nComputer Science and Engineering\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nFinance and Risk Engineering\nMathematics\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nTechnology, Culture and Society\nTechnology Management and Innovation\nDegrees & Programs\nBachelor of Science\nMaster of Science\nDoctor of Philosophy\nDigital Learning\nCertificate Programs\nNYU Tandon Bridge\nK12 STEM\nResources\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nRecords & Registration\nDigital Learning Services\nTeaching Innovation\nSustainability\nQuantum\nEmbodied Intelligence\nEngineering Health\nSystems Engineering\nEngineering & Culture\nOffice of Research\nCenters & Institutes\nLabs & Groups\nStudent Research\nStudent Life\nCareer Hub\nEntrepreneurship\nExperiential Learning\nMakerSpace\nSupport & Resources\nAlumni\nGiving\nIndustry Engagement\nOverview\nMission\nFast Facts\nHistory\nLeadership\nResearch Magazine\nCommunity\nOur Engineers\nBrooklyn\nVisit\nNews & Events\nNews\nEvents\nSocial Media\nSearch NYU Tandon\nFulltext search\nLooking for\nNews\nor\nEvents\n?\nGus Xia\n,\nPh.D.\nAssistant Research Professor\nComputer Science and Engineering\nConnect\nEmail\ngxia\n[at]\nnyu.edu\nPhone\n+86 17717012619\nWebsite\nhttp://www.cs.cmu.edu/~gxia/\nGus (Guangyu) Xia is an Assistant Professor in Computer Science at NYU Shanghai, and also a research Assistant Professor at NYU Tandon. He holds a Ph.D. in Machine Learning from Carnegie Mellon University, where he worked with Prof.\nRoger Dannenberg\n.\nXia's main research field is\nComputer Music\n. His interdisciplinary research encompasses Machine Learning, HCI, Robotics, and Music. His representative works include human-computer interactive performances, autonomous dancing robots, smart music displays, and large-scale content-based music retrieval.\nRecently, he has been building artificial music performers that are able to perform expressively in concert with human musicians by learning musicianship from rehearsals. This effort unifies expressive performance rendering and automatic accompaniment in a machine-learning framework, generating expressive and professional performances by robots and computers. See\nDEMOS\n.\nXia is also a professional DI and XIAO (Chinese flute and vertical flute) player. For more, please visit his\npersonal website\n.\nResearch Interests\nComputer Music, Artificial Music Intelligence, Human-Computer Interaction, Bio-music computing\nEducation\nPeking University\n2010\nB.S., Information Science\nCarnegie Mellon University\n2016\nPh.D., Machine Learning\nEmail\ngxia\n[at]\nnyu.edu\nPhone\n+86 17717012619\nWebsite\nhttp://www.cs.cmu.edu/~gxia/"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Wei Xue::http://wei-xue.com/": {
    "homepage": "http://wei-xue.com/",
    "all_emails": [
      "weixue@ust.hk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "﻿\nHome | Wei Xue\nWei Xue\nWei Xue (雪巍)\nB.Eng., Ph.D.\nAssistant Professsor\nDivision of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC)\nDivision of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas (EMIA)\nHong Kong University of Science and Technology\nEmail:\nweixue@ust.hk\nAddress:\nRoom 1007, IAS Building, HKUST, Clear Water Bay, Hong Kong\nBiography\nWei Xue is currently an Assistant Professor at Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC) and Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas (EMIA), Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST). He is also a founding member of Hong Kong Generative AI Research and Development Centre (HKGAI). He received the Bachelor degree in automatic control from Huazhong University of Science and Technology in 2010, and the Ph.D degree in pattern recognition and intelligent systems from Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences in 2015. From August 2015 to September 2018 he was first a Marie Curie Experienced Researcher and then a Research Associate in Speech and Audio Processing Group, Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Imperial College London, UK. He was a Senior Research Scientist at JD AI Research, Beijing, from November 2018 to December 2021, where he was leading the R&D on front-end speech processing and acoustic modelling for robust speech recognition. From January 2022 to April 2023 he was an Assistant Professor at Department of Computer Sciences, Hong Kong Baptist University. He was a visiting scholar at Université de Toulon and KU Leuven. Wei's research interests are in speech and music intelligence and large language models, including multimodal foundation models, AI music generation, speech enhancement and separation, room acoustics, as well as speech and audio event recognition.\nEnrollments for 2026 Spring/Fall PhD have finished. We have no positions for the RA and Postdoc at present.\nAwards\nBeijing Overseas Talent Aggregation Project, Beijing Government, 2020.\n3rd place in Far-Field Speaker Verification Challenge, FFSVC, 2020.\n3rd place in Sound Event Localization and Detection Task, DCASE, 2019.\nMarie Curie Experienced Researcher Fellowship, European Commission, 2015.\nOutstanding Student Award, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 2014.\nAcademic Activities\nTPC member: IEEE Wireless Communications and Networking Conference (IEEE WCNC) 2017.\nReviewer:  ICASSP, IJCAI, INTERSPEECH, IEEE T-ASLP, IEEE J-STSP\nSession Chair: INTERSPEECH 2020\nTalk:\n1) \"Speech and Audio Technologies and Applications in JD,\" SLT, online, 2021.\n2) \"Advances in Adverse Acoustic Environment Perception and Analysis,\" CCF, online, 2020.\n3) \"Microphone Arrays based 3D Speech processing: Speech Enhancement and Source Localization,\" Baidu Inc., Beijing, China, 2017.\n4) \"Microphone Arrays based 3D Speech processing: Speech Enhancement and Source Localization,\" Beijing Jiaotong University, Beijing, China, 2017.\n5) \"Under-modelled Blind System Identification and its Applications to Time Delay Estimation,\" KU Leuven, Leuven, Belgium, 2016.\n6) \"3D Machine Listening for Robots: From Sound Field Awareness to Spatial Audio Processing,\" London PhD Network Symposium on \"Robotics and Intelligent Systems\", London, UK, 2016.\n7) \"On Noise Robust Direction of Arrival Estimation of Speech Source in Time-Frequency and Bispectrum Domain,\" Université de Toulon, France, 2015.\n8) \"Investigation on HMM-GMM based Chinese Handwriting Recognition,\" Canon Information Technology (Beijing) Co., Ltd., Beijing, China, 2011.\nMembership: IEEE Member."
  },
