    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jian Guo\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJian Guo\nJian Guo\nMy name is Jian Guo, I am currently\nan Associate Professor\n(\nT\nenured) with\nSchool of Physical and Mathematical Sciences\n, and\nCollege of Computing and Data Science\n(Courtesy Appointment),\nNanyang Technological University\nin Singapore. My research interests focus on cryptography, especially cryptanalysis, design and implementation of (lightweight) hash functions, block ciphers, authenticated encryption schemes, and their applications such as message authentication codes\n. As such, I head\nCryptanalysis Taskforce\nat NTU,\npublish papers\n,\ngive talks\n,\nand also actively\nserve the community\n. My team and I have\nwon several open competitions on cryptanalysis\non various symmetric-key cryptography standards\n.\nI am\nconstantly\nlooking for PhD candidates (refer to\nthis page\n) and Postdoc Research Fellows on both symmetric-key cryptography and privacy-preserving technologies, feel free to contact me for more information.\nPGP Public Key\nRecent Services / Appointments\nNTU\nHead\n,\nCryptanalysis Taskforce\n(since 2014)\nProgram Director (Co-Founder),\nMa\nster of Science\nin Cyber\nS\necurity\n(\nsince\n20\n22\n)\nAdjunct/Part-Time Appointments\nAdjunct Outstanding Young Scholar, Shandong University (since 2024)\nConsultant for JD.COM (since 2025)\nConsultant for Huawei (since 2023)\nConsultant for LatticeX Foundation (since 2022)\nResearch Community\nIACR Board of Directors\n(since 2020),\nIACR Schools Committee\n(since 202\n2\n),\nIACR Test\n-\nof\n-\nTime Awards Com\nmittee\n2023\nAsiacrypt Steering Committee\n(since 2017)\nProgram Co-Chair,\nAsiacrypt 202\n3\nGeneral (\nCo-)\nChair,\nAsiacrypt 2021\n,\nFSE 2013\n,\nASK 2011\n(co-founder)\nProgram Committee Member:\nAsiacrypt\n,\nC\nrypto\n,\nEurocrypt\n,\nFSE\nsince 2017, and\nACM CCS\nsince 2024\nKeynote Talks at Inscrypt 2025, 密码算法学术会议 2025, SCOPE 2025, CS 2025, CryptoIC 2024, Huawei STW 2023, ASK 2023, ChinaCrypt 2023, ADSC 2023,\nAsiacrypt 2022,\nFSE 2019, Inscrypt 2014, etc.\nGovernment Agencies / Organizations\nSecurity and Privacy Standards Technical Committee, Singapore\n(since 2017)\nInternational Standards Organization (ISO)\n, SC 27/WG2, Representative for Singapore (since 2017)\nPanel of Experts for\nEnterprise Singapore\n(since 2024)\nIndustry\nPrincipal Investigator for collaborative R&D project with Paypal Inc (2021 - 2023)\nPrincipal Investigator for\ncollaborative R&D project with\nLatticeX Foundation\n(202\n2\n- 202\n5\n)\nCommunity\nSecretary, Residents' Network,\nPeople's Association\n(since 2020)\nAwards\nBest Paper Awards: FSE 2018, ACISP 2022\nNTU/SPMS Collaborative Research Award 2022 (Co-PI)\nNTU/SPMS Young Researcher Award 2021\nNTU Accelerating Creativity and Excellence Award 2020 (Co-PI)\nBest Publication Awards by Temasek Labs@NTU 201\n5\n, 201\n6\n, 201\n7\nWinner of\nThe Keccak Crunchy Crypto Collision and Pre-image Contest\n, for several occasions in 2012~2019\nHiring\n[\n2025/04\n] Several postdoc positions in all areas of cryptology jointly with Wuhan University, China (PI:\nJie Chen\n) and NTU Singapore (myself) are available immediately. See\nhere\nfor more information.\n[\n2024/08\n] There are\nseveral\n2-year postdoc positions on Symmetric-Key Cryptogra\nphy\njointly by Tsinghua University, China (PI:\nXiaoyang Dong\n)\nand NTU Singapore (myself) available immediately. See\nhere\nfor more information.\nThe\nMaster of Science in Cyber Security\nprogram is now offered for every August intake.\nTo my potential PhD or Final Year Project students, refer to\nthis page\nfor information.\nNews\n2024/08: Invited talk at CryptoIC 2024 on \"An Overview on the Links between Cryptanalysis and Side-Channel Attacks\".\n2023/12: Invited talk at ASK 2023 and keynote talk at ChinaCrypt 2023 on \"A Realistic Summary and Projection of Cryptanalysis\"\n2022/12: Invited talk at\nAsiacrypt 2022\non \"\nEvolution of Cryptanalysis: Security Updates on SHA-3 and AES Hashing\"\n2022/11: Joint with L. Song and H. Wang, the paper entitled \"\nKey Structures: Improved Related-Key Boomerang Attack against the Full AES-256\n\" won the Best Paper Award of ACISP 2022. The paper improves the attack with lowest time complexity from 2^99 to 2^91 with the access to more related keys.\n2022/04: Lanuch of\nMaster of Science in Cyber Security\n.\n2022/03/24: humbled to receive\nSPMS Young Reseacher Award 2021\n.\n2022/02/14:\nNews release by NTU/SPMS on the organization of Asiacrypt 2021\n.\n2021/11/17:\nt\nhanks to all for electing me to the\nIACR Board of Directors\n(Term 2022-2024), as promised I will do my best to promote research, education, and collaborations in the crypto community. References:\nthe\nIACR 2021 Election\nand\nnews\nr\nelease by NTU/SPMS\n.\n2021/03: The first preimage attack against 8-round AES hashing:\nnews release by NTU/CoS\n,\neprint\n2019/03: Invited talk at\nFSE 2019\non \"Security of SHA-3 and Related Constructions\"\n2018-02-08: Joint with C. Chaigneau, T. Fuhr, H. Gilbert, J. Guo, J. Jean, J. R. Reinhard, L. Song, the paper entitled \"Key-Recovery Attacks on Full Kravatte\" won the Best Paper Award of FSE 2018. The paper broke the full Kravatte (a PRF design based on the SHA-3 round function), and several subsequent patched versions.\nEducation\n01.2007 - 09.2010\nDoctor of Mathematical Sciences\nSchool of Physical and Mathematical Sciences\nPhD Supervisor:\nHuaxiong Wang\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore\n08.2003 - 11.2006\nBachelor of Engineering\nSchool of Computer Engineering\n(with First Class Honors)\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore\nFYP Supervisor:\nSuiping Zhou\nEmployment\n03.2013 - present\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore\n09.2010 - 02.2013\nInstitute for Infocomm Research, Singapore\n01.2007 - 09.2010\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore\nTeaching\nDiscrete Mathematics (Undergrad\nuate)\n: AY14/15 S2, AY15/16 S2, AY18/19 S1, AY19/20 S1, AY19/20 S2, AY20/21 S1, AY20/21 S\n2\n, AY21/22 S1, AY21/22 S2, AY22/23 S1, AY23/24 S1, AY2\n4\n/2\n5\nS1, AY25/26 S1\nAlgorithms and Computing II (Undergraduate): AY17/18 S2, AY18/19 S2\nBlo\nckchains and Cryptocurrency (MSc Cybersecurity): AY23/24 S1,\nAY2\n4\n/2\n5\nS\n2\nTopics in Crypto and Cyber Security (MSc Cybersecurity): AY23/24 S2,\nAY24/25 S2, AY25/26 S1\nBlockchain Privacy & Scalability (MSc Blockchain): AY23/24 S3\nContacts\nEmail:\nguojian [at] ntu.edu.sg\nAddress:\nSchool of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, 21 Nanyang Link, Singapore 637371.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Nan Duan::https://nanduan.github.io/": {
