    "homepage_text": "Yan Wu | Roboticist, PhD, SMIEEE\nSkip to content\nYan Wu\nSearch\nSearch for:\nYan Wu is a Principal Scientist and the Deputy Head of the Robotics and Autonomous Systems Division, A*STAR Institute for Infocomm Research, Singapore. Yan received his BA(Hons) in Engineering from the University of Cambridge in 2007, and PhD in Electrical Engineering from Imperial College London in 2013. From Aug 2012, he worked concurrently at the UCL Institute of Child Health as a Research Associate and Great Ormond Street Hospital as a Research Fellow. Since Dec 2013, he has been with the A*STAR Institute for Infocomm Research, Singapore. Yan’s research interests include service and assistive robotics, dexterous manipulation, robot learning and human-robot interaction. He is a Senior Member of the IEEE and serves as an Associate Editor at various editorial boards, such as IEEE Robotics and Automation Society Conference Editorial Board, IEEE Intelligent Transport Systems Society Conference Editorial Board and Frontier in Robotics and AI.\nRecent Updates\nVideos\nCollaborative Robot Intelligence\nLearning Nullspace fr Demo\nMultimodal LfD\nLfD using DMP+\niCub Learning to Solder\nRoboticist, PhD, SMIEEE\nPrincipal Scientist\nGroup Leader\nManipulation & Interaction\nDeputy Department Head\nRobotics & Auto. Systems\nA*STAR\nInst. for Infocomm Research\nCo-Lead\nA*STAR Robotics HTCO\n1 Fusionpolis Way\n#21-01 Connexis South\nSingapore 138632\nDID: +65-6408-2719\nEmail: wuy-at-i2r.a-star.edu.sg\nlinkedin\nfacebook\nresearchgate\nmail\n\n---\n\nAbout Me | Yan Wu\nSkip to content\nYan Wu\nSearch\nSearch for:\nAbout Me\nIn 1983, I was born in Shantou, a southern Chinese coastal city. I did my basic education both in my hometown and in Singapore before embarking on my “Journey to the West” for my first degree and PhD studies. Since Dec 2013, I started working as a research scientist at A*STAR in Singapore. Here is my CV in brief:\nEducation\nPhD/DIC, Electrical Engineering, Imperial College London, 2008 – 2012\nMA(Cantab), University of Cambridge, Mar 2011\nBA(Hons), Information and Computer Engineering, University of Cambridge, 2004 – 2007\nWork & Trainings\nPrincipal Scientist & Deputy Department Head (Robotics & Autonomous Systems), A*STAR Institute for Infocomm Research, Singapore Dec 2013 –\npresent\nVisiting Researcher, Imperial College London, UK, Oct 2012 – 2017\nHonorary Research Fellow, Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children, UK, 2012 – 2013\nHonorary Research Associate, UCL Institute of Child Health, UK, Oct 2012 – 2015\nResearch Officer, ASTAR Institute of High Performance Computing, Singapore, 2007 – 2008\nAwards\nKUKA Innovation Award Finalist, 2021\nBest Demo Award, 35th\nAAAI\nConference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2021\nTan Kah Kee Young Inventor Award (Merit), Singapore, 2018\nOutstanding Mentor Award, Ministry of Education (SMP), 2015\nBest Paper Award Finalist, IEEE Int’l Conference on Robotics and Biomimetics (ROBIO), 2010\nCertificate of Merit, World Congress on Engineering, 2008\nNational Science Scholarship(BS-PhD), A*STAR, Singapore, 2004 – 2012\nServices\nSecretary, IEEE Systems, Man and Cybernetics Society, Singapore Chapter, 2020 –\npresent\nTreasurer, Pattern Recognition and Machine Intelligence Association, Singapore, 2020 –\npresent\nSecretary, Chinese and Oriental Languages Information Processing Society, 2019 –\npresent\nGeneral Secretary, Teochew Doctorate Society, Singapore, 2018 –\npresent\nDirector, International Teochew Doctors Association, 2017 –\npresent\nAssociate Editor, Frontiers in Robotics and AI (2021 –\npresent\n); IEEE RAS CEB (2020 –\npresent\n); IEEE ITS  CEB (2018 –\npresent\n),\nProgramme Chair (ICSR 2021, HFR 2018),Finance Chair (ICASSP 2022, IALP 2019/20), Local Arrangement Chair (ASRU 2019), Publicity Chair (HAI 2019, HAI 2016), General Secretary (ITD Forum 2016)\nVolunteer, Games of the XXX Olympiad, London, 2012\nClick here for a copy of my CV in pdf\nDownload\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-4644-0664\nRecent Updates\nVideos\nCollaborative Robot Intelligence\nLearning Nullspace fr Demo\nMultimodal LfD\nLfD using DMP+\niCub Learning to Solder\nRoboticist, PhD, SMIEEE\nPrincipal Scientist\nGroup Leader\nManipulation & Interaction\nDeputy Department Head\nRobotics & Auto. Systems\nA*STAR\nInst. for Infocomm Research\nCo-Lead\nA*STAR Robotics HTCO\n1 Fusionpolis Way\n#21-01 Connexis South\nSingapore 138632\nDID: +65-6408-2719\nEmail: wuy-at-i2r.a-star.edu.sg\nlinkedin\nfacebook\nresearchgate\nmail\n\n---\n\nAbout Me | Yan Wu\nSkip to content\nYan Wu\nSearch\nSearch for:\nAbout Me\nIn 1983, I was born in Shantou, a southern Chinese coastal city. I did my basic education both in my hometown and in Singapore before embarking on my “Journey to the West” for my first degree and PhD studies. Since Dec 2013, I started working as a research scientist at A*STAR in Singapore. Here is my CV in brief:\nEducation\nPhD/DIC, Electrical Engineering, Imperial College London, 2008 – 2012\nMA(Cantab), University of Cambridge, Mar 2011\nBA(Hons), Information and Computer Engineering, University of Cambridge, 2004 – 2007\nWork & Trainings\nPrincipal Scientist & Deputy Department Head (Robotics & Autonomous Systems), A*STAR Institute for Infocomm Research, Singapore Dec 2013 –\npresent\nVisiting Researcher, Imperial College London, UK, Oct 2012 – 2017\nHonorary Research Fellow, Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children, UK, 2012 – 2013\nHonorary Research Associate, UCL Institute of Child Health, UK, Oct 2012 – 2015\nResearch Officer, ASTAR Institute of High Performance Computing, Singapore, 2007 – 2008\nAwards\nKUKA Innovation Award Finalist, 2021\nBest Demo Award, 35th\nAAAI\nConference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2021\nTan Kah Kee Young Inventor Award (Merit), Singapore, 2018\nOutstanding Mentor Award, Ministry of Education (SMP), 2015\nBest Paper Award Finalist, IEEE Int’l Conference on Robotics and Biomimetics (ROBIO), 2010\nCertificate of Merit, World Congress on Engineering, 2008\nNational Science Scholarship(BS-PhD), A*STAR, Singapore, 2004 – 2012\nServices\nSecretary, IEEE Systems, Man and Cybernetics Society, Singapore Chapter, 2020 –\npresent\nTreasurer, Pattern Recognition and Machine Intelligence Association, Singapore, 2020 –\npresent\nSecretary, Chinese and Oriental Languages Information Processing Society, 2019 –\npresent\nGeneral Secretary, Teochew Doctorate Society, Singapore, 2018 –\npresent\nDirector, International Teochew Doctors Association, 2017 –\npresent\nAssociate Editor, Frontiers in Robotics and AI (2021 –\npresent\n); IEEE RAS CEB (2020 –\npresent\n); IEEE ITS  CEB (2018 –\npresent\n),\nProgramme Chair (ICSR 2021, HFR 2018),Finance Chair (ICASSP 2022, IALP 2019/20), Local Arrangement Chair (ASRU 2019), Publicity Chair (HAI 2019, HAI 2016), General Secretary (ITD Forum 2016)\nVolunteer, Games of the XXX Olympiad, London, 2012\nClick here for a copy of my CV in pdf\nDownload\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0002-4644-0664\nRecent Updates\nVideos\nCollaborative Robot Intelligence\nLearning Nullspace fr Demo\nMultimodal LfD\nLfD using DMP+\niCub Learning to Solder\nRoboticist, PhD, SMIEEE\nPrincipal Scientist\nGroup Leader\nManipulation & Interaction\nDeputy Department Head\nRobotics & Auto. Systems\nA*STAR\nInst. for Infocomm Research\nCo-Lead\nA*STAR Robotics HTCO\n1 Fusionpolis Way\n#21-01 Connexis South\nSingapore 138632\nDID: +65-6408-2719\nEmail: wuy-at-i2r.a-star.edu.sg\nlinkedin\nfacebook\nresearchgate\nmail"
