    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/xuanchen-/",
    "homepage_text": "Home | Xuan Chen\n👋 Hey, I’m Xuan\nI am a CS PhD candidate at Purdue University, advised by\nProf. Xiangyu Zhang\n.\nMy research interests include:\nLLM Red-teaming\nRL for Security\nLLM Agents Evaluation\nBackdoor Attacks and Defenses\nSpecifically, I study attacks and defenses for LLMs, LLM agents, and RL systems, including jailbreaking; backdoor attacks, detection, and removal; and broader adversarial robustness. I combine reinforcement learning with programmatic test generation to discover vulnerabilities and failure modes and to develop principled defenses that harden models and agents. Recently, I’m also working on building security-focused LLM agents and stress-testing of LLM agents across key evaluation dimensions.\nDownload my CV"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Wenbo Guo::https://henrygwb.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://henrygwb.github.io/",
