    "homepage_text": "Qiong Wu\nToggle navigation\nQiong Wu @ AT&T Labs Research\nQiong Wu\nQiong Wu is a Senior Inventive Scientist at AT&T Labs Research. Her research focuses on developing robust machine learning algorithms under harsh conditions, such as an excessively large number of features and notoriously low signal-to-noise ratio.\nBefore joining AT&T, Qiong obtained her Ph.D. in computer science at\nWilliam & Mary\n. \nShe received her B.Eng degree from the\nDalian University of Technology\nand M.Sc degree from the\nUniversity of Hong Kong\n.\n[DBLP]\n[Google Scholar]\nResearch\nGoPlaces: An App for Personalized Indoor Place Prediction\nPritam Sen, Xiaopeng Jiang,\nQiong Wu\n, Manoop Talasila, Wen-Ling Hsu, Cristian Borcea\nThe 20th IEEE International Conference on Mobile Ad-Hoc and Smart Systems (MASS), 2023\nSymphony in the Latent Space: Provably Integrating High-dimensional Techniques with Non-linear Machine Learning Models\nQiong Wu\n, Jian Li, Zhenming Liu, Yanhua Li, Mihai Cucuringu\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence AAAI (AAAI), 2023\nDemo: Indoor Place Prediction on Smart Phones\nPritam Sen, Xiaopeng Jiang,\nQiong Wu\n, Manoop Talasila, Wen-Ling Hsu, Cristian Borcea\nACM Conference on Embedded Networked Sensor Systems (SenSys), 2022\nEquity2Vec: End-to-end Deep Learning Framework for Cross-sectional Asset Pricing\nQiong Wu\n, Christopher G. Brinton, Zheng Zhang, Andrea Pizzoferrato, Zhenming Liu, Mihai Cucuringu\nACM International Conference on AI in Finance (ICAIF), 2021\nRosella: A Self-Driving Distributed Scheduler for Heterogeneous Clusters\nQiong Wu\n, Zhenming Liu\nInternational Conference on Mobility, Sensing and Networking (MSN), 2021\nBATS: A Spectral Biclustering Approach to Single Document Topic Modeling and Segmentation\nQiong Wu\n, Adam Hare, Sirui Wang, Yuwei Tu, Zhenming Liu, Christopher G. Brinton, Yanhua Li\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technologies (TIST), 2021\nAdaptive Reduced Rank Regression\nQiong Wu\n, Felix M. F. Wong, Zhenming Liu, Yanhua Li, Varun Kanade\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2020\n[Code]\n[Full Version]\nExtended Abstract: On Embedding Stocks\nQiong Wu\n, Zheng Zhang, Yanhua Li, Zhenming Liu, Mihai Cucuringu\nACM International Conference on AI in Finance (ICAIF), 2020\nExtended Abstract: A Deep Learning Framework for Pricing Financial Instruments\nQiong Wu\n, Zheng Zhang, Andrea Pizzoferrato, Zhenming Liu, Mihai Cucuringu\nACM International Conference on AI in Finance (ICAIF), 2020\nSpeaking with Actions: Learning Customer Journey Behavior\nQiong Wu\n, Wen-Ling Hsu, Tan Xu, Zhenming Liu, Guang-Qin Ma, Guy Jacobson, Shuai Zhao\nIEEE International Conference on Semantic Computing (ICSC), 2019\nNear Neighbor Approach for Learning Random Preferences\nAo Liu,\nQiong Wu\n, Lirong Xia, Zhenming Liu\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence AAAI (AAAI), 2019 (Full Oral Presentation)\nA Magic Cube based Information Hiding Scheme of Large Payload\nQiong Wu\n, Chen Zhu, Jianjun Li, Chin-Chen Chang, Zhi-Hui Wang\nJournal of Information Security and Applications, 2016\nEarly Car Collision Prediction in VANET\nQiong Wu\n, Lucas Chi Kwong Hui, Cheuk Yu Yeung, Tat Wing Chim\nInternational Conference on Connected Vehicles & Expo (ICCVE), 2015\nService\nProgram Committee: AAAI 2023, ICAIF 2022, MSN 2022, ICAIF 2021, MSN 2021\nReviewer: IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (TKDE), IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS), IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems (T-ITS), IEEE Transactions on Wireless Communications (TWC), INFORMS Journal of Computing, IEEE/ACM Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics, IEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics\n© Qiong Wu. Site made with\nJekyll\nusing a template made available by Allan Lab."
