  "deep_homepage::Jie Li::https://www.cake-researcher.com/our-vision": {
    "homepage": "https://www.cake-researcher.com/our-vision",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jie-li-907b2017/",
    "homepage_text": "Delft | Cake Researcher | Vision\ntop of page\nKruisstraat 75\n2611ML Delft\nThe Netherlands\nHi Everyone,\nDue to the high volume of messages I receive daily,\nI will only respond if I have the capacity\nto make your requested cakes.\nPlease note that\nmy studio is not open to the public.\nThank you for your understanding.\nAll the best,\nCake Researcher\nCake Researcher\nNever stop being amazed\nWhy Cake Researcher\nThe founder of Cake Researcher Jie Li is a\ncake addict\nand a full-time\nresearcher (\nhttps://www.jieli-research.com\n)\n. That is where “Cake Researcher” originates from.\n​\nWhat we do\nThe idea behind Cake Researcher is simple: making beautiful and tasty cakes. Inspired by Asian-style desserts, we develop our unique recipes, using high-quality seasonal ingredients, and serving mind-blowing beautiful cakes lower in fat and sugar. You will also find seriously roasted coffee, cake/art workshops, art exhibitions and many other amazing things at our shop.\nEmbracing diversity\nI am Jie, the hands and the brain behind Cake Researcher. Besides Cake Researcher, I am the mother of a little girl and have a full-time job as Head of Research at EPAM Netherlands. I love diversity, so I am continuously experimenting with new cakes and new possibilities in life.\nLooking forward to sharing my happiness with you at Cake Researcher.\nFrom the Clients\n1\ninezsoethof\n“This is an amazingly beautiful cake and I love the fantastic decoration on it and the colors!”\n2\n​Miss Morrison\n“Delft, we hope you can handle the most beautiful cakes ever.”\n3\nShumeng Chang\n“We ordered our wedding cakes from Cake Researcher, and it proves to be the best choice ever! We received a lot of compliments from our guests, many people told us that these are the most beautiful and delicious wedding cakes they've ever had!”\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nDelft | Cake Researcher | Vision\ntop of page\nKruisstraat 75\n2611ML Delft\nThe Netherlands\nHi Everyone,\nDue to the high volume of messages I receive daily,\nI will only respond if I have the capacity\nto make your requested cakes.\nPlease note that\nmy studio is not open to the public.\nThank you for your understanding.\nAll the best,\nCake Researcher\nCake Researcher\nNever stop being amazed\nWhy Cake Researcher\nThe founder of Cake Researcher Jie Li is a\ncake addict\nand a full-time\nresearcher (\nhttps://www.jieli-research.com\n)\n. That is where “Cake Researcher” originates from.\n​\nWhat we do\nThe idea behind Cake Researcher is simple: making beautiful and tasty cakes. Inspired by Asian-style desserts, we develop our unique recipes, using high-quality seasonal ingredients, and serving mind-blowing beautiful cakes lower in fat and sugar. You will also find seriously roasted coffee, cake/art workshops, art exhibitions and many other amazing things at our shop.\nEmbracing diversity\nI am Jie, the hands and the brain behind Cake Researcher. Besides Cake Researcher, I am the mother of a little girl and have a full-time job as Head of Research at EPAM Netherlands. I love diversity, so I am continuously experimenting with new cakes and new possibilities in life.\nLooking forward to sharing my happiness with you at Cake Researcher.\nFrom the Clients\n1\ninezsoethof\n“This is an amazingly beautiful cake and I love the fantastic decoration on it and the colors!”\n2\n​Miss Morrison\n“Delft, we hope you can handle the most beautiful cakes ever.”\n3\nShumeng Chang\n“We ordered our wedding cakes from Cake Researcher, and it proves to be the best choice ever! We received a lot of compliments from our guests, many people told us that these are the most beautiful and delicious wedding cakes they've ever had!”\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nDelft | Cake Researcher | Vision\ntop of page\nKruisstraat 75\n2611ML Delft\nThe Netherlands\nHi Everyone,\nDue to the high volume of messages I receive daily,\nI will only respond if I have the capacity\nto make your requested cakes.\nPlease note that\nmy studio is not open to the public.\nThank you for your understanding.\nAll the best,\nCake Researcher\nCake Researcher\nNever stop being amazed\nWhy Cake Researcher\nThe founder of Cake Researcher Jie Li is a\ncake addict\nand a full-time\nresearcher (\nhttps://www.jieli-research.com\n)\n. That is where “Cake Researcher” originates from.\n​\nWhat we do\nThe idea behind Cake Researcher is simple: making beautiful and tasty cakes. Inspired by Asian-style desserts, we develop our unique recipes, using high-quality seasonal ingredients, and serving mind-blowing beautiful cakes lower in fat and sugar. You will also find seriously roasted coffee, cake/art workshops, art exhibitions and many other amazing things at our shop.\nEmbracing diversity\nI am Jie, the hands and the brain behind Cake Researcher. Besides Cake Researcher, I am the mother of a little girl and have a full-time job as Head of Research at EPAM Netherlands. I love diversity, so I am continuously experimenting with new cakes and new possibilities in life.\nLooking forward to sharing my happiness with you at Cake Researcher.\nFrom the Clients\n1\ninezsoethof\n“This is an amazingly beautiful cake and I love the fantastic decoration on it and the colors!”\n2\n​Miss Morrison\n“Delft, we hope you can handle the most beautiful cakes ever.”\n3\nShumeng Chang\n“We ordered our wedding cakes from Cake Researcher, and it proves to be the best choice ever! We received a lot of compliments from our guests, many people told us that these are the most beautiful and delicious wedding cakes they've ever had!”\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nDelft | Cake Researcher | Vision\ntop of page\nKruisstraat 75\n2611ML Delft\nThe Netherlands\nHi Everyone,\nDue to the high volume of messages I receive daily,\nI will only respond if I have the capacity\nto make your requested cakes.\nPlease note that\nmy studio is not open to the public.\nThank you for your understanding.\nAll the best,\nCake Researcher\nCake Researcher\nNever stop being am