    "homepage_text": "Quanshi Zhang | 张拳石\nLab for Interpretability and Theory-Driven Deep Learning\nLab Member\nGoogle Scholar\nEmail\nQuanshi Zhang\nPrincipal\n                                            Investigator\nCurrently, I am an associate professor at\nShanghai Jiaotong University\n, leading\n                                            the\nLab for Interpretability and Theory-Driven Deep\n                                                Learning\n.\n                                            Before that, I received the B.S. degree in machine intelligence at\nPeking University\n, China, in\n                                            2009. I obtained the M.Eng. degree and the\n                                            Ph.D. degree at\nUniversity of\n                                                Tokyo\n, in 2011 and 2014, respectively, under\n                                            the supervision of Prof. Ryosuke Shibasaki. In 2014, I became a postdoctoral\n                                            associate at the\nUniversity of California,\n                                                Los Angeles\n, under the\n                                            supervision of\nProf. Song-Chun\n                                                Zhu\n.\nHuiqi Deng\nPostdoc\nHomepage\nEmail\nWen Shen\nPostdoc\nHomepage\nEmail\nXu Cheng\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nXin Wang\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nHuilin Zhou\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nJie Ren\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nDongrui Liu\nPhD\nEmail\nSiyu Lou\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nYe Liu\nPhd\nEmail\nLu Chen\nPhD\nEmail\nHuixi Chen\nPhd\nEmail\nQihan Ren\nPhd\nHomepage\nEmail\nDie Zhang\nMaster\nHomepage\nEmail\nHao Zhang\nMaster\nHomepage\nEmail\nMingjie Li\nMaster\nHomepage\nEmail\nShaobo Wang\nMaster\nHomepage\nEmail\nLing Tang\nUndergraduate\nEmail\nXinhao Zheng\nUndergraduate\nEmail\nAbout Our Lab\nDue to the black-box nature of DNNs, interpretable machine learning has become a\n                compelling topic. However, the trustworthiness and applicability of interpretable ML has\n                been widely questioned in recent years. Core critisms include the following five aspects.\nCurrent explanation methods are built upon different heuristics, lacking common theoretical\n                        foundations.\nIt is infeasible to objectively evaluate the correctness of the explanation results, in the\n                        absence of ground truth explanations.\nThere is still a large gap between the semantic explanation result (e.g., the attribution-based\n                        explanation) and the explanation of a DNN’s performance (e.g., the generalization power), which\n                        cannot be unified.\nTraditional semantic explanations cannot be used as feedbacks to guide the designing of DNNs,\n                        thereby boosting DNN performances.\nMost current methods boosting DNN performances are heuristic, and the theoretical mechanisms\n                        behind their success are largely missing.\nTherefore, our team aims to solve two key scientific problems:\nhow to develop a theoretical system to unify different explanations of the semantics encoded in\n                        a DNN (e.g., attribution-based explanations, taxonomy of semantic concepts, and etc) and unify\n                        different explanations of the DNN performance (e.g., the generalization power, adversarial\n                        robustness, adversarial\n                        transferability, and etc). Besides, it is highly desirable to bridge the two types of\n                        explanations. We believe that, an explanation system can be considered as trustworthy if the\n                        methods in the system can be mutually verified.\nhow to extract the common mechanism behind different heuristic methods, which\n                        include both explanation methods and current popular methods boosting the DNN performance.\nResearch Map\nPublications\nInterpretability\n                    Direction\nOther Directions\nDefects of Convolutional Decoder Networks in Frequency Representation\nLing Tang,\nWen Shen\n, Zhanpeng Zhou, Yuefeng\n                                Chen, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nProving Common Mechanisms Shared by Twelve Methods of Boosting Adversarial\n                                    Transferability\nQuanshi Zhang*\n,\nXin Wang*\n,\nJie Ren*\n,\nXu Cheng*\n,\n                                Shuyun Lin, Yisen Wang, Xiangming Zhu\nPreprint\nPaper\nBatch Normalization Is Blind to the First and Second Derivatives of the Loss\nZhanpeng Zhou,\nWen Shen\n, Huixin Chen, Ling\n                                Tang, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nWhy Adversarial Training of ReLU Networks Is Difficult?\nXu Cheng*\n,\nHao Zhang*\n, Yue Xin,\nWen Shen\n,\nJie Ren\n, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nQuantifying the Knowledge in a DNN to Explain Knowledge Distillation for\n                                    Classification\nQuanshi Zhang*\n,\nXu Cheng*\n, Yilan Chen,\n                                and Zhefan Rao\nIEEE T-PAMI 2022\nQuantification and Analysis of Layer-wise and Pixel-wise Information\n                                    Discarding\nHaotian Ma*,\nHao Zhang*\n,\n                                Yinqing Zhang, Fan Zhou, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICML 2022\nPaper\nTowards Theoretical Analysis of Transformation Complexity of ReLU DNNs\nJie Ren*\n,\nMingjie Li*\n,\n                                Meng Zhou, Shih-Han\n                                Chan, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICML 2022\nPaper\nDiscovering and Explaining the Representation Bottleneck of DNNs\nHuiqi Deng*\n,\nQihan Ren*\n,\nHao Zhang\n,\n                                and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICLR 2022 (oral)\nPaper\nCode\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nTechbeat Talk (Chinese)\nExploring Image Regions Not Well Encoded by an INN\nZenan Ling\n, Fan Zhou,\n                                Meng Wei, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nAISTATS 2022\nVideo (English)\nInterpretable Generative Adversarial Networks\nChao Li*, Kelu Yao*, Jin Wang*, Boyu Diao, Yongjun Xu, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nAAAI 2022 (oral)\nPaper\nTrap of Feature Diversity in the Learning of MLPs\nDongrui Liu*,\nShaobo Wang*\n,\nJie Ren\n,\n                                Kangrui Wang,\nSheng Yin,\nHuiqi Deng\n,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nTowards Axiomatic, Hierarchical, and Symbolic Explanation for Deep Models\nJie Ren*\n,\nMingjie Li*\n,\n                                Qirui Chen,\nHuiqi Deng\n,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nRapid Detection and Recognition of Whole Brain Activity in a Freely Behaving\n                                    Caenorhabditis Elegans\nYuxiang Wu, Shang Wu,\nXin Wang\n, Chengtian\n                                Lang,\nQuanshi Zhang\n, Quan Wen, and Tianqi Xu\nPreprint\nPaper\nA Hypothesis for the Aesthetic Appreciation in Neural Networks\nXu Cheng\n,\nXin Wang\n, Haotian Xue, Zhengyang Liang,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nA Game-Theoretic Taxonomy of Visual Concepts in DNNs\nXu Cheng\n,\n                                Chuntung Chu, Yi Zheng,\nJie Ren\nand\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nLearning Baseline Values for Shapley Values\nJie Ren\n,\nZhanpeng Zhou\n, Qirui Chen\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nA Unified Game-Theoretic Interpretation of Adversarial Robustness\nJie Ren*\n,\nDie Zhang*\n,\n                                Yisen Wang*, Lu Chen,\nZhanpeng Zhou\n,\n                                Yiting Chen,\nXu Cheng\n,\nXin Wang\n, Meng Zhou, Jie Shi\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nNeurIPS 2021\nPaper\nCode\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nVideo (English)\nVisualizing the Emergence of Intermediate Visual Patterns in DNNs\nMingjie Li\n,\nShaobo Wang\n,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nNeurIPS 2021\nPaper\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nInterpreting Representation Quality of DNNs for 3D Point Cloud Processing\nWen Shen\n,\nQihan Ren\n,\n                                Dongrui Liu and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nNeurIPS 2021\nPaper\nCode\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nInterpreting Attributions and Interactions of Adversarial Attacks\nXin Wang*\n,\n                                Shuyun Lin*,\n                                Hao Zhang, Yufei Zhu, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICCV 2021\nPaper\nCode\nInterpreting and Disentangling Feature Components of Various Complexity from\n                                    DNNs\nJie Ren*\n,\nMingjie Li*\n,\n                                Zexu Liu,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nICML 2021\nPaper\nCode\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nInterpretable Compositional Convolutional Neural Networks\nWen Shen*\n, Zhihua Wei*, Shikun Huang, Binbin\n                                Zhang, Jiaqi Fan, Ping Zhao and\nQuanshi Zhang\nIJCAI 2021\nPaper\nCode\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nVerifiability and Predictability: Interpreting Utilities of Network\n                                    Architectures\nfor 3D Point Cloud Processing\nWen Shen*\n, Zhihua Wei*, Shikun Huang, Binbin\n                                Zhang, Panyue Chen, Ping Zhao,\n                                and\nQuanshi Zhang\nCVPR 2021\nPaper\nCode\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nVideo\n                                    (English)\nA Unified Approach to Interpreting and Boosting Adversarial Transferability\nXin Wang*\n,\nJie Ren*\n,\n                                Shuyun Lin, Xiangming Zhu,\n                                Yisen Wang, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICLR 2021\nPaper\nCode\nPost\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nInterpreting and Boosting Dropout from a Game-Theoretic View\nHao Zhang\n, Sen Li, Yinchao Ma,\nMingjie Li\n,\n                                Yichen Xie, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICLR 2021\nPaper\nInterpreting Multivariate Shapley Interactions in DNNs\nHao Zhang\n, Yichen Xie, Longjie Zheng,\nDie\n                                    Zhang\n,\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nAAAI 2021\nPaper\nCode\nBuilding Interpretable Interaction Trees for Deep NLP Models\nDie Zhang*\n,\nHuilin Zhou\n,\nHao Zhang\n, Xiaoyi Bao, Da\n                                Huo, Ruizhao Chen,\nXu\n                                    Cheng\n, Mengyue Wu,\nQuanshi Zhang\nAAAI 2021\nPaper\nCode\nRotation-Equivariant Neural Networks for Privacy Protection\nHao Zhang\n, Yiting Chen, Haotian Ma,\nXu Cheng\n,\nQihan Ren\n,\nLiyao Xiang, Jie Shi and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nDeep Quaternion Features for Privacy Protection\nHao Zhang\n, Yiting Chen, Liyao Xiang, Haotian\n                                Ma, Jie Shi and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\n3D-Rotation-Equivariant Quaternion Neural Networks\nBinbin Zhang,\nWen Shen\n, Shikun Huang, Zhihua\n                                Wei, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nECCV 2020\nPaper\nCode\nVideo (English)\nInterpretable CNNs for Object Classification\nQuanshi Zhang\n,\nXin Wang*\n,\n                                Ying Nian Wu,\nHuilin Zhou\n, and Song-Chun\n                                Zhu\nIEEE T-PAMI, 2020\nPaper\nProject Website\nCode\nExtraction of an Explanatory Graph to Interpret a CNN\nQuanshi Zhang\n,\nXin Wang*\n, Ruiming Cao,\n                                Ying Nian Wu, Feng Shi, and Song-Chun Zhu\nIEEE T-PAMI, 2020\nPaper\nProject Website\nCode\nVideo (English)\nMining Interpretable AOG Representations from Convolutional Networks via Active\n                                    Question Answering\nQuanshi Zhang\n,\nJie Ren\n, Ge Huang, Ruiming Cao, Ying Nian Wu,\n                                and Song-Chun Zhu\nIEEE T-PAMI, 2020\nPaper\nTowards a Unified Evaluation of Explanation Methods without Ground Truth\nHao Zhang\n, Jiayi Chen, Haotian Xue, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nExplaining AlphaGo: Interpreting Contextual Effects in Neural Networks\nZenan Ling\n, Haotian\n                                Ma, Yu Yang, Robert C. Qiu1, Song-Chun Zhu, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nPreprint\nPaper\nExplaining Knowledge Distillation by Quantifying the Knowledge\nXu Cheng\n, Zhefan Rao,\n                                Yilan Chen, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nCVPR 2020\nPaper\nCode\nBlog\n                                    (Chinese)\nKnowledge Consistency between Neural Networks and Beyond\nRuofan Liang, Tianlin Li, Longfei Li, Jing Wang, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nICLR 2020\nPaper\nCode\nSynced News (Chinese)\nInterpretable Complex-Valued Neural Networks for Privacy Protection\nLiyao Xiang,\nHao Zhang\n, Haotian Ma, Yifan\n                                Zhang,\nJie Ren\n, and\nQuanshi Zhang\nICLR 2020\nPaper\nExplaining Neural Networks Semantically and Quantitatively\nRunjin Chen\n,\n                                Hao Chen,\nJie Ren\n,\n                                Ge Huang, and\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\nICCV 2019 (oral)\nPaper\nTowards A Deep and Unified Understanding of Deep Neural Models in NLP\nChaoyu Guan*, Xiting Wang*,\nQuanshi\n                                    Zhang\n,\nRunjin Chen\n, Di He, Xing\n                                Xie\nICML 2019\nPaper\nCode\nInterpreting CNNs via Decision Trees\nQuanshi Zhang\n, Yu Yang, Haotian Ma, and Ying Nian Wu\nCVPR 2019\nPaper\