    "homepage_text": "Yaxuan Zhu\n      -  Aalto University's research portal\nAalto University's research portal Home\nACRIS instructions\nLink opens in a new tab\nEnglish\nSuomi\nSearch content at Aalto University's research portal\nContact expert\nYaxuan Zhu\nVisitor (Faculty)\n,\nDepartment of Energy and Mechanical Engineering\nVisitor (Faculty)\n,\nMarine and Arctic Technology\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0001-9908-7510\n2021\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation/Academic qualification\nTekn. toht., konetekniikka\nAward Date: 31 Dec 2025\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 14\nLife Below Water\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Yaxuan Zhu is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n3\nSimilar Profiles\nField Measurement\nEngineering\n100%\nShip Operation\nEngineering\n100%\nCombined Effect\nEngineering\n100%\noperation\nINIS\n100%\nships\nINIS\n100%\nice\nINIS\n100%\nantarctic regions\nINIS\n100%\nIce Floe\nEngineering\n66%\nView full fingerprint\nResearch output\n1\nDoctoral Thesis\nShip ice loads as combined effect of ice conditions and ship operations: Antarctic field measurements\nZhu, Y.\n,\n2025\n,\nAalto University\n.\n150 p.\nResearch output\n:\nThesis\n›\nDoctoral Thesis\n›\nMonograph\nOpen Access\nField Measurement\n100%\nCombined Effect\n100%\nShip Operation\n100%\nships\n100%\nice\n100%\nProjects\n1\nFinished\nANTGRAD:\nWave-Induced Structural Gradients in Antarctic Sea Ice Cover\nTuhkuri, J.\n(Principal investigator) &\nZhu, Y.\n(Project Member)\n01/01/2021\n→\n31/12/2024\nProject\n:\nRCF Academy Project targeted call\nPack Ice\n100%\nRudder\n100%\nPolar Ship\n100%\nTears\n100%\nsinks\n100%\nYour message has successfully been sent.\nYour message was not sent due to an error.\nx\nContact Yaxuan Zhu\nSubject:\n*\nMessage:\n*\nYour name:\n*\nYour email:\n*\nSend me a copy of this message\n*required field\nSee privacy policy in the footer of the page\nCancel\nSend"
