    "homepage_text": "Guan-Horng Liu\nGuan-Horng Liu\nResearch Scientist @ Meta Superintelligence Labs (MSL)\nI develop methods for learning generative models with scientific structures.\nData-driven methods such as\nSchrödinger bridges\n[\nI\n2\nSB\n,\nDeepGSB\n]\nhave advanced diffusion models with optimality structures and physics priors.\nData-efficient methods like\nadjoint-based diffusion samples\n[\nASBS\n,\nDAM\n]\nhave enabled scientific exploration driven by reward and energy functions.\nLately, I’ve been exploring\nRL science in post-training LLMs\n.\nMy research has led to large-scale applications in\nGenerative AI:\nmathematical reasoning\n,\nimage generation\n&\nrestoration\n&\nunsupervised translation\n,\nwatermarked generation\n.\nAI for Science:\nconformer generation\n,\ntransition states\n&\npaths sampling\n,\nprotein folding\n,\nscRNA sequencing\n,\nparticle physics\n.\nAI for Society:\npopulation modeling\n,\nopinion depolarization\n,\nmean-field games\n.\nMy research has received multiple recognitions, including\n5+ Oral/Spotlight presentations\n[accept rate ≤ 3%]\nin major ML conferences (ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS), cover feature in\nNature Machine Intelligence\n,\ncoverage in\nMIT News\n& the\nMetaAI blog\n,\nand GaTech AE Graduate Research Fellowship.\nI’m deeply grateful to my collaborators, mentees, and interns from FAIR, NVIDIA Research, Georgia Tech, MIT, Cornell, and KAIST.\nYou can find more details in my\nCV\n.\nContact:\nghliu [at] meta [dot] com\nguanhorng [dot] liu [at] gmail [dot] com\nFollow:\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nghliu\n|\n𝕏 @guanhorng_liu\nUpdates\n[01/2026] Two papers,\nDAM\nand\nWT-ASBS\n, accepted to ICLR.\n[11/2025] I give talks at\nPrinceton Center for Theoretical Science\nand\nSeminar on Monte Carlo Methods\n.\n[09/2025]\nAdjoint Schrödinger Bridge Sampler (ASBS)\naccepted to NeurIPS (Oral 0.3%).\n[09/2025] Four papers—\nASBS\n,\nNAAS\n,\n3MSBM\n, and\nMDNS\n—accepted to NeurIPS.\n[07/2025] I give talks at\nMSR Generative Modeling & Sampling Seminar\nand Flatiron Institute.\n[04/2025] I co-organize\n        NeurIPS Workshop on\nFrontiers in Probabilistic Inference\n.\n[09/2024] I have joined FAIR, Meta AI as a Research Scientist at NYC.\n[04/2024] I co-organize\n        ICML Workshop on\nStructured Probabilistic Inference & Generative Modeling\n.\n[04/2023] I co-organize\n        ICML Workshop on\nNew Frontiers in Learning, Control, and Dynamical Systems\n.\nSelected Publications\n(∗ Equal contribution, * Core contributors,\n†\nEqual advising,\n‡\nAlphabetical order. See\nGoogle Scholar\nfor the full list.)\nDiscrete Adjoint Schrödinger Bridge Sampler\nWei Guo*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yuchen Zhu\n∗\n,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Xiaochen Du\n∗\n,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Juno Nam\n∗\n,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yongxin Chen\n†\n,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Rafael Gómez-Bombarelli\n†\n,\nGuan-Horng Liu\n†\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Molei Tao\n†\n,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Jaemoo Choi*\nPreprint,\n        \n        \n          2026\npaper\nFunctional Adjoint Sampler: Scalable Sampling on Infinite Dimensional Spaces\nByoungwoo Park,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Juho Lee,\nGuan-Horng Liu\nPreprint,\n        \n        \n          2026\npaper\nDiscrete Adjoint Matching\nOswin So*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Brian Karrer*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Chuchu Fan,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Ricky T. Q. Chen*,\nGuan-Horng Liu*\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR),\n        \n        \n          2026\npaper\nAdjoint Schrödinger Bridge Sampler\nGuan-Horng Liu*\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Jaemoo Choi*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yongxin Chen,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Benjamin K. Miller,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Ricky T. Q. Chen*\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS),\n        \n        \n          2025\n[Oral 0.3%]\npaper\n|\ncode\n|\nslides\nNon-equilibrium Annealed Adjoint Sampler\nJaemoo Choi*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Yongxin Chen,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Molei Tao,\nGuan-Horng Liu*\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS),\n        \n        \n          2025\npaper\nMomentum Multi-Marginal Schrödinger Bridge Matching\nPanagiotis Theodoropoulos,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Augustinos D. Saravanos,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Evangelos A. Theodorou\n†\n,\nGuan-Horng Liu\n†\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS),\n        \n        \n          2025\npaper\nAdjoint Sampling: Highly Scalable Diffusion Samplers via Adjoint Matching\nAaron Havens*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Benjamin Kurt Miller*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Bing Yan*,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Carles DomingoEnrich,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Anuroop Sriram,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Brandon Wood,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Daniel Levine,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Bin Hu,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Brandon Amos,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Brian Karrer,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n\n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Xiang Fu*,\nGuan-Horng Liu*\n,\n              \n            \n        