    "homepage_text": "Tian Zhou - Home\nTian Zhou\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\nHuman robot interaction\nDedicated researcher striving to bridge the communications gaps between robots and their human peers by use of machine learning, computer vision and artificial intelligence.\nRead moRE\nI am currently a Ph.D. candidate  in the Intelligent Systems and Assistive Technologies\nLaboratory\n(\nISAT\n) in the School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University, under the supervision of\nD\nr. Juan P. Wachs\n. Previously, I received the M.S. degree from the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Purdue University in 2016, and B.S. in the School of Information Science of Technology at Southeast University, China in 2013.\nMy research interest lies in human robot interaction and robot vision. I desire to design innovative interaction and communication protocols between humans and robots, and develop innovative frameworks leveraging on computer vision and artificial intelligence to enable a more natural, efficient and coupled cooperation between human and robots. For more details, please refer to my\nresearch\npage.\nTurn-taking Prediction\nHow to enable robots to predict turn-taking events ahead of time and proactively plan its actions to collaborate with human peers in a seamless manner?\nLearn More\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nHow to bring into Operating Room the innovative robotic scrub nurses who can accurately recognize surgical instruments, robustly manipulate and safely deliver to surgeons on request?\nLearn More\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHow to provide the most natural and comfortable interaction scheme to enable surgeons to teleoperate a robot to conduct surgery safely and efficiently?\nLearn More\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - Tian Zhou\nTian Zhou\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\nContact Me\nFeel free to contact me through email or in-website messages.\n*\nIndicates required field\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nComment\n*\nSubmit\nLinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/tian-zhou/\nEmail\nzhou338 [at] purdue [dot] edu\nOffice\nRoom 1332, Michael Golden Laboratories\n610 Purdue Mall, West Lafayette, IN, 47906\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - Tian Zhou\nTian Zhou\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\nContact Me\nFeel free to contact me through email or in-website messages.\n*\nIndicates required field\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nComment\n*\nSubmit\nLinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/tian-zhou/\nEmail\nzhou338 [at] purdue [dot] edu\nOffice\nRoom 1332, Michael Golden Laboratories\n610 Purdue Mall, West Lafayette, IN, 47906\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - Tian Zhou\nTian Zhou\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\nContact Me\nFeel free to contact me through email or in-website messages.\n*\nIndicates required field\nName\n*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail\n*\nComment\n*\nSubmit\nLinkedIn\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/tian-zhou/\nEmail\nzhou338 [at] purdue [dot] edu\nOffice\nRoom 1332, Michael Golden Laboratories\n610 Purdue Mall, West Lafayette, IN, 47906\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\n\n---\n\nAbout - Tian Zhou\nTian Zhou\nHome\nAbout\nResearch\nTurn-taking Prediction\nRobotic Scrub Nurse\nRobot-assisted Surgery\nHand Detection for ADAS\nMIMO Communication\nPublication\nGallery\nContact\nthis is a long path/page\nEducation\n:\nPh.D. in Industrial Engineering, Purdue University (Jan 2014 - present)\nAdvisor:\nJuan P. Wachs\nGPA: 4.0\nM.S. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Purdue University (Aug 2014 - May 2016)\nAdvisor:\nJan P. Allebach\nGPA: 3.94\nB.S. in Electrical Engineering, Southeast University (Aug 2009 - May 2013)\nGPA: 91.2/100, Major GPA:93.8/100.0\nThesis: Efficient Spatial Covariance Estimation of Uplink Communication in LTE-A Systems\nNational Scholarship 2009-2010, 2010-2011\nMost Influential Graduate Honor, Voted as 1st place out of 18 candidates selected from the entire 2013 graduation cohort (like 3500 students). Fun\nvideo\nhere (in Chinese). Missed those great times so much.\nExchange student in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Purdue University (Aug 2012 - Dec 2012)​\nGPA: 3.95, Dean's List\nStudy Abroad Foundation (SAF) Exchange Scholarship\nRuiAn Exchange Scholarship from Southeast University\nCertificate in International Industrial/Academic Leadership Experience program\nChung Yuan Christian University, Zhongli, Taiwan (Jun 2011) ​\nAwards\nSecond place\n, Purdue Industrial Engineering Graduate Student Organization (IEGSO)\nResearch Symposium\n, Purdue, May 2017\nBest Student Paper award\n(6%),  38th\nIntelligent Robotics and Industrial Applications using Computer Vision Conference at\nIS&T International Electronic Imaging Symposium (EI), Jan 2017\nStudent Travel Grant (55%), 2017 IS&T International Electronic Imaging Symposium (EI), Jan 2017\nGoogle PhD Fellowship finalist (1 of 2 Purdue nominees), Nov 2016\nTravel Scholarship, 2016 AAAI Fall Symposium, Nov 2016\nRobotics Fellowship (20%), 2016 AAAI, Feb 2016\nBest poster award, Next Generation Scholar Poster Competition (earned 40% of total votes), Purdue University, Nov 2015\nBest 3-minute presentation, 2015 AAAI Poster session, poster co-authored with Maria E. Cabrera, Jan 2015\nActivities\nPublic Relations Chair, Student Chapter of IEEE Robotics and Automation Society, Purdue University (Jan 2015 - Aug 2015)\nPublic Relations Chair, Industrial Engineering Graduation Student Association (IEGSO), Purdue University (Aug 2014 - Aug 2015)\nRegistered volunteer, Indiana Veteran's Home (Jun 2014 - Aug 2014)\nRegistered volunteer, Boiler out! Volunteer program, Purdue University (Aug 2012 - Aug 2014)\nVice-minister, Cultural Department of Information Science School Student Union, Southeast University (Aug 2009 - Aug 2011)\nThird place in Campus Sales Competition, Southeast University (May 2012)\n​\nCoursework\nRobotics\nECE 569: Introduction to Robotics\nECET 581: Robot Programming with ROS\nIE 590: Robotics & Machine Vision\nMachine learning\nCS 573: Data Mining\nCS 578: Statistical Machine Learning\nBME 595: Deep Learning (audited)\nComputer vision\nECE 661: Computer Vision\nECE 662: Pattern Recognition and Decision Making\nIE 590: Robotics & Machine Vision\nIE 690: Gesture and Bodial System\nManagement and Economics\nMGMT 590: Technology Entrepreneurship and Lean Startups\nECON 671: Econometrics\nECON 511: Intermediate Economics\nIE 577: Human Factors in Engineering\nIE 674: Computer & Communication Methods for Production Control\nMath foundations\n​\nMA 511: Linear Algebra with Applications\nMA 575: Graph The