    "homepage_text": "Liu Laboratory\nLiu Laboratory\nThe Liu Lab\nHarnessing High-Valent Metal Complexes for Sustainable Catalysis\nMultiple Postdoctoral Positions Are Available\nPostdoctoral candidates with a strong background in organic synthesis, catalysis, and/or organometallic are encouraged to apply. Please send a cover letter stating your future career goals, a C.V. and a research summary (less than 3 pages) to liuwei@vt.edu.\nWelcome to Wei Liu's Lab.\nWe are an organic chemistry lab in the Department of Chemistry at Virginia Tech. Research in our group focuses on the areas of organic synthesis, organometallic chemistry and catalysis.\nLab News\n2026\nMar 2026\nOur research paper “Enantioselective difluoromethylation of unactivated alkyl halides via a formal nickel(II/IV) cycle” was published in\nNature Catalysis\n! Congratulations to Xian, Lingfeng, and Chao!\n2025\nDec 2025\nOur research paper “Harnessing CO2 Radical Anion-Mediated Electron Transfer for Scalable Copper-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling\n”\nhas been accepted for publication in\nJACS\n!\nCongratulations to Shuo!\nDec 2025\nOur research paper “\nTrifluoromethylation of alkyl electrophiles with 11C- or 18F-labeled fluoroform for PET applications”\nhas been published in\nScience\n!\nCongratulations to Chao!\nAug 2025\nOur group has relocated from University of Cincinnati to Virginia Tech. We miss all of our friends at Cincinnati.\nMar 2025\nOur research paper “\nS\nynthesis of chiral difluoromethyl cyclopropanes through desymmetric difluoromethylation of cyclopropenes enabled by enantioselective copper catalysis\n” has been published in\nNature Synthesis\n! Congratulations to Decai, Su, and Lingfeng!\nJan 2025\nOur work on radiotrifluoromethylation has been funded by\nNIBIB RO1\n. Thanks NIH for the generosity.\n2024\nNov 2024\nOur research paper  “\nOvercoming Copper Reduction Limitation in Asymmetric Substitution: Aryl-Radical-Enabled Enantioconvergent Cyanation of Alkyl Iodides”\nhas been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n! Congratulations to Su, Decai, and Lingfeng!\nOct 2024\nOur research paper\n“Highly Enantioselective Decarboxylative Difluoromethylation”\nhas been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n! Congratulations to Xian, Chao, and Lingfeng!\nOct 2024\nOur research paper “\nEnantioconvergent Copper-Catalysed Difluoromethylation of Alkyl Halides”\nhas been accepted for publication at Nat. Catal. Congratulations to Decai, Lingfeng and everyone else.!\nMay 2024\nOur research paper “\nCatalytically Relevant Organocopper(III) Complexes Formed through Aryl-Radical-Enabled Oxidative Addition\n”\nhas been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n! Congratulations to Wenhao, Lingfeng, and Chao!\n2023\nNov. 2023\nOur research paper “\nCopper–Carbon Homolysis Competes with Reductive Elimination in Well-Defined Copper(III) Complexes\n” has been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n! Congratulations to Wenhao!\nOct. 2023\nOur graduate student Wenhao Yan has finished his open defense. Congratulations to Dr. Yan!\nAug. 2023\nLingfeng Yin has joined the lab as a graduate student. Welcome Lingfeng!\nMay. 2023\nXian Zhao has joined our lab as postdoctoral fellow. Welcome Xian!\nFeb. 2023\nOur research paper “\nAryl Radical Enabled, Copper-Catalyzed Sonogashira-Type Cross-Coupling of Alkynes with Alkyl Iodides\n” has been published in\nACS Catalysis\n! Congratulations to Xiaojun, Chao, Wenhao, and Aijie!\nJan. 2023\nShengtong Niu and Decai Ding has joined our lab as postdoctoral fellows. Welcome Shengtong and Decai!\n2022\nDec. 2022\nOur group has been awarded the NSF CAREER Award. We thank the funding agency for its generosity.\nNov. 2022\nSu Chen has joined our lab as a postdoctoral fellow. Welcome Su!\nJune 2022\nOur group has been awarded the MIRA grant. We thank NIH for its generosity.\nApril 2022\nOur group has been awarded the Herman Frasch Foundation Grant. We thank ACS for its generosity.\nOct. 2021\nOur research paper “\nCopper-Catalyzed Difluoromethylation of Alkyl Iodides Enabled by Aryl Radical Activation of Carbon–Iodine Bonds\n” has been published in\nAngew. Chem. Int. Ed\n.\n! Congratulations to Aijie, Wenhao, and Chao!\nAug. 2021\nChao Wang has joined the lab as a graduate student. Welcome Chao!\nJune 2021\nGiven our group’s interest in organofluorine chemistry and the widespread of fluorine-containing molecules as agrochemicals, pharmaceuticals, and materials, we decide to create a series of posters that help to educate the importance of fluorinated molecules in our daily life.\nPlease check.\nJune 2021\nOur research paper “\nAryl Radical Activation of C–O Bonds: Copper-Catalyzed Deoxygenative Difluoromethylation of Alcohols\n” has been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\n! Congratulations to Aijie and Wenhao!\nJune 2021\nOur research paper “\nCopper-Catalyzed Carbodifluoromethylation\n” has been published in\nNat. Commun.\n! Congratulations to Aijie, Wenhao, Xiaojun, and Samson!\n2020\nAug. 2020\nOur research group moved to the Department of Chemistry at\nUniversity of Cincinnati\n. We miss all of our friends at Miami University.\nJune 2020\nOur research paper “\nCopper-Catalyzed Deaminative Difluoromethylation\n” has been published in\nAngewandte Chemie\n! Congratulations to Xiaojun, Wenhao, Samson, Aijie and Dongqi!\nFeb. 2020\nXiaojun, Wenhao, Samson and Matt’s benzylic C-H difluoromethylation paper has been highlighted in\nSynfacts\n! Thank you to Prof. Mark Lautens and Rachel Ross for highlighting our work!\nFeb. 2020\nDr. Aijie Cai joins our group as a postdoc. Welcome Aijie!\n2019\nNov. 2019\nOur research paper “\nCopper-Catalyzed, Chloroamide-Directed C-H Difluoromethylation\n” has been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\nCongratulations to Xiaojun, Wenhao, Matt, Dongqi, and Samson!\nNov. 2019\nXiaojun, Wenhao, Samson and Matt’s decarboxylative difluoromethylation paper has been highlighted in\nSynfacts\n! Thank you to Prof. Mark Lautens and Christian Dank for highlighting our work!\nJuly. 2019\nOur research paper “\nCopper-Catalyzed Decarboxylative Difluoromethylation\n” has been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc.\nCongratulations to Xiaojun, Wenhao, Samson, Matt, and Sam!\nMay. 2019\nDr. Liu has presented our research in the Department of Chemistry at Southern Methodist University. Thanks Prof. Isaac Garcia-Bosch for the invitation!\nApril. 2019\nXiaojun Zeng has joined our lab as a postdoctoral fellow. Welcome Xiaojun!\nMarch. 2019\nDr. Liu has presented our research in the Department of Chemistry at Wright State University. Thanks Swamy for the invitaion!\nJan. 2019\nOur research paper “\nCsp3-Csp3 Bond-Forming Reductive Elimination from Well-Defined Copper(III) Complexes\n” has been published in\nJ. Am. Chem. Soc\n.\nCongratulations to Matt, Sam, Will and Elizabeth!\nJan, 2019\nWenhao Yan joined the lab as a graduate student. Welcome Wenhao!\nJan, 2019\nOur research paper\n“\nElectrochemical benzylic oxidation of C–H bonds\n” has been published in\nChemical Communications\n. Congratulations to Jason and Tony.\n2018\nAugust, 2018\nOur research paper\n\"\nTuning Gold Nanoparticles with Chelating Ligands for Highly Efficient Electrocatalytic CO2 Reduction\n\" has been accepted for publication in\nAngewantde Chemie\nas a Hot Paper\n.\nCongratulations to Samson, Elizabeth, Will and Sam.\nJune, 2018\nOur first research paper \"\nCopper Mediated Trifluoromethylation of Benzylic Csp3-H bonds\n\" is published in\nChemistry - A European Journal\n. Congratulations to Matt and Will.\nMay, 2018\nThe group welcomes Ashley as a REU student\nFebruary, 2018\nSam Tyndall, Juliana Livieri andTony Durgham join the group as undergraduate researchers\n2017\nNovember, 2017\nJenn Peters joins the group as an undergraduate researcher\nOctober, 2017\nMatthew Paeth and Kate Bradford  join the group as graduate researchers\nOctober, 2017\nSamson Zacate Joins the lab as an undergraduate researcher\nSeptember, 2017\nWilliam Carson and Elizabeth Hale joins the group as undergraduate researchers and help set up the lab.\nAugust, 2017\nThe lab begins\naaaa"
  },
