    "homepage_text": "Ruixuan Li\nRuixuan Li\nTsinghua University\nShow Contacts\nEmail\nlirx25 [at] mails.tsinghua.edu.cn\nLocation\nFIT 1-213, Tsinghua University, Beijing 100084, P.R.China\nGoogle scholar\nAbout me\nI am a first year PhD student\nNetwork and Information Security Lab (NISL)\nof Tsinghua University.\nMy supervisor is Associate Professor\nBaojun Liu\n.\nMy research focuses on network security and Internet measurement, with particular interests in security of DNS and Email.\nI obtained my Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees from Zhejiang Gongshang University in 2021 and 2024 respectively (advised by Professor\nJun Shao\n). In 2025, I worked as a network security engineer at Tsinghua University.\nRecent News\n[January 2026] Our paper about Iran Internet shutdown was accepted to\nWWW 2026\n! Congrats to Shibo!\n[October 2025] Our paper about email amplification attack was accepted to\nNDSS 2026\n!\n[August 2025] Our paper about email intermediate delivery path was accepted to\nIMC 2025\n!\n[July 2025] Our paper about email invisible HTML settings was accepted to\nESORICS 2025\n! Congrats to Bingyang and Mingxuan!\n[September 2024] Our paper about email blocklist manipulation risk was accepted to\nNDSS 2025\n!\nSelected Publications\n[NDSS 2025]\nHADES Attack: Understanding and Evaluating Manipulation Risks of Email Blocklists\n[IMC 2025]\nUnderstanding and Characterizing Intermediate Paths of Email Delivery: The Hidden Dependencies\n[WWW 2024]\nA Worldwide View on the Reachability of Encrypted DNS Services\nPublications\n2026\nCharacterizing Iran's Phased National Internet Shutdown in 2025: A Progressive and Distributed Action\nProceedings of ACM Web Conference (WWW), Dubai, United Arab Emirates, April 2026\nShibo Cui, Mingxuan Liu, Baojun Liu, Haixin Duan,\nRuixuan Li,\nChaoyi Lu, Jin Zhang, Zhicheng Wang and Jinghua Bai\nCoordMail: Exploiting SMTP Timeout and Command Interaction to Coordinate Email Middleware for Convergence Amplification Attack\nProceedings of the 33rd Network and Distributed System Security (NDSS) Symposium, San Diego, CA, USA, February 2026\n*Ruixuan Li,\nChaoyi Lu, Baojun Liu\n, Yanzhong Lin,\n                  Qingfeng Pan, Jun Shao\nPaper\nData\n2025\nUnderstanding and Characterizing Intermediate Paths of Email Delivery: The Hidden Dependencies\nProceedings of ACM Internet Measurement Conference (IMC), Madison, Wisconsin, USA, October 2025\n*Ruixuan Li,\nChaoyi Lu, Baojun Liu\n, Yanzhong Lin, Haixin Duan,\n                  Qingfeng Pan, and Jun Shao\nPaper\nSlides\nData\nEmail Cloaking: Deceiving Users and Spam EmailDetectors with Invisible ITML Settings\nProceedings of the 30th European Symposium on Research in Computer Security (ESORICS), Toulouse, France, September, 2025\n*Bingyang Guo, *Mingxuan Liu, Yihui Ma,\nRuixuan Li,\nFan Shi, Min Zhang, Baojun Liu, Chengxi Xu, Haixin Duan, Geng Hong, Min Yang, and Qingfeng Pan\nPaper\nData\nHADES Attack: Understanding and Evaluating Manipulation Risks of Email Blocklists\nProceedings of the 32nd Network and Distributed System Security (NDSS) Symposium, San Diego, CA, USA, February 2025\n*Ruixuan Li,\nChaoyi Lu, Baojun Liu\n, Yunyi Zhang, Geng Hong, Haixin Duan, Yanzhong Lin, Qingfeng Pan, Min Yang and Jun Shao\nPaper\nCite\nSlides\nPoster\n2024\nBounce in the Wild: A Deep Dive into Email Delivery Failures from a Large Email Service Provider\nProceedings of ACM Internet Measurement Conference (IMC), Madrid, Spain, November 2024\n*Ruixuan Li,\nShaodong Xiao, Baojun Liu\n, Yanzhong Lin, Haixin Duan,\n                  Qingfeng Pan, Jianjun Chen, Jia Zhang, Ximeng Liu, Xiuqi Lu and Jun Shao\nPaper\nCite\nSlides\nTickets or Privacy? Understand the Ecosystem of Chinese Ticket Grabbing Apps\nProceedings of 33rd USENIX Security Symposium (USENIX Security), Philadelphia, PA, USA, August 2024\n*Yijing Liu, Yiming Zhang, Baojun Liu\n, Haixin Duan, Qiang Li, Mingxuan Liu,\nRuixuan Li,\nand Jia Yao\nPaper\nCite\nA Worldwide View on the Reachability of Encrypted DNS Services\nProceedings of ACM Web Conference (WWW), Singapore, May 2024\n*Ruixuan Li,\nBaojun Liu\n, Chaoyi Lu, Haixin Duan, and Jun Shao\nPaper\nCite\nSlides\nPoster\nVideo\nData\nWebsite\n2023\nA Longitudinal and Comprehensive Measurement of DNS Strict Privacy\nProceedings of IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking (TON), 2023\n*Ruixuan Li,\nXiaofeng Jia, Zhenyong Zhang, Jun Shao\n, Rongxing Lu, Jingqiang Lin, Xiaoqi Jia, and Guiyi Wei\nPaper\nCite\nWebsite\nThe Potential Harm of Email Delivery: Investigating the HTTPS configurations of Webmail Services\nProceedings of IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), 2023\n*Ruixuan Li,\nZhenyong Zhang, Jun Shao\n, Rongxing Lu, Xiaoqi Jia, and Guiyi Wei\nPaper\nCite\nActivities\nMadrid, Spain\nNovember 6, 2024\nInternet Measurement Conference (IMC) 2024\nBounce in the Wild: A Deep Dive into Email Delivery Failures from a Large Service Provider\nSan Diego, USA\nFebruary 26, 2025\nNetwork and Distributed System Security (NDSS) 2025\nHADES Attack: Understanding and Evaluating Manipulation Risks of Email Blocklists\nProjects\nJanuary, 2023\nEncrypted DNS Query\nSupport querying five (encrypted) DNS services to obtain function, configuration, location of the target IP/Domain on the specified port.\nMISC\nSelect category\nLast modified: February 4, 2026"
