    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Youbang Sun | TsinghuaC3I\nSearch\nYoubang Sun\nAssistant Researcher\nAbout Me\nI am currently an Assistant Researcher (å©çç ç©¶å) in the Department of Electrical Engineering at Tsinghua University (2025-now). I am a faculty member of the\nTHU-C3I Lab\n, my current research focuses on the theory and novel applications for LLM reasoning with the help of Reinforcement Learning and Optimization. I am also interested in safe and robust AI systems.\nI obtained my Ph.D. degree in 2025 from the Department of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering at Northeastern University (2021-2025). I am advised by Prof. Shahin Shahrampour. During my Ph.D, my research interest included theory and application of distributed optimization, such as the system dynamics of mirror descent / Riemannian gradient descent algorithms in distributed systems, federated learning and multi-agent reinforcement learning.\nI was previously a Ph.D. student in the Department of Industrial Engineering at Texas A&M University (2019-2021). Prior to that, I obtained my B.S. degree in Electrical Engineering from University of Science and Technology of China (2015-2019) as a member of the School of the Gifted Young.\nInterests\nReinforcement Learning\nOptimization and System Control\nLarge Language Models\nMake Safe AI\nEducation\nMechanical and Industrial Engineering, Ph.D.\nNortheastern University, 2021-2025\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering, Ph.D. Candidate\nTexas A&M University, 2019-2021\nElectronic Engineering, B. Sc.\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China, 2015-2019\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yonggang Zhang::https://yonggangzhangben.github.io/index.html": {
    "homepage": "https://yonggangzhangben.github.io/index.html",
    "all_emails": [
