    "homepage_text": "Qiang Zhou | Research UC Berkeley\nSkip to main content\nSearch\nSearch\nQiang Zhou\nProfessor Emeritus\nDept of Molecular & Cell Biology\nResearch Group\nFaculty Site\nPublications (Google Scholar)\nContact\nEmail\n(510) 643-1697\n(510) 643-6334\nSearch UC Berkeley Directory\nUpdate your profile\nResearch Bio\nQian Zhou is Professor Emeritus of Biochemistry, Biophysics and Structural Biology. His research group is studying the mechanisms and factors that control transcriptional elongation and how this control affects HIV replication, latency activation and cancer progression.\nResearch Expertise and Interest\nbiochemistry of HIV gene expression\n,                          transcriptional elongation\n,                          Tat activation\n,                          stage of transcriptional elongation\n,                          HIV replication\n,                          anti-HIV therapy\nIn the News\nFeatured in the Media\nTeaching\nLoading Class list ..."
