    "homepage_text": "Yuan FANG @ SMU\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYuan FANG @ SMU\nYuan FANG, Ph.D.\nAssociate Professor of Computer Science\nLee Kong Chian Fellow\nSchool of Computing and Information Systems\nSingapore Management University\nOffice:\nSCIS2 Room 4053  |\nEmail:\nyfang \"at\" smu.edu.sg\nShort Biography\nI am currently an Associate Professor (tenured) at the School of Computing and Information Systems, Singapore Management University (SMU). Prior to joining SMU, I was a data scientist at\nDBS Bank\n, and a research scientist at\nA*STAR\n. I obtained a PhD Degree in Computer Science from the\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nin 2014 on a fully funded scholarship from A*STAR, and Bachelor of Computing with First Class Honors from\nNational University of Singapore\nin 2009 as the top student in Computer Science. My full CV can be accessed\nhere\n.\nResearch Interests\nMy general interest lies in the broad areas of data mining, machine learning and artificial intelligence. More specifically, I am working on the following research topics: (1) Learning on graphs and information networks; (2) Web and social media analytics; (3) Recommendation systems; (4) Application of knowledge graphs on data mining problems. More details can be found in my\nresearch statement\n, the\nprojects\npage, and the\npublications\npage\n.\nRecent Updates\n[\n02\n/202\n6\n]\n✅ We have one paper accepted by\nCVPR\n2026.\n[\n01\n/202\n6\n] 🎤\nI am giving an invited talk \"Semantic-Structural Integration in Text-Attributed Graphs\" at the 5th Workshop on Graphs and more Complex Structures for Learning and Reasoning,\nco-located with\nAAAI\n2026, in Singapore. [PDF]\n[01/2026]\n📅 We are organizing the\nSingapore ACM SIGKDD Symposium 2026\n, an in-person event organized by the\nSingapore ACM SIGKDD Chapter\n,\non 20 January 2026 at SUTD.\n[\n11\n/2025]\n🎓 Congratulations to Dr.\nRan Liu\non his successful defense of his PhD dissertation titled \"\nAddressing sparsity for knowledge graph completion: Data and model perspectives.\n\"\n[11/2025]\n🎤\nI am giving an invited talk \"Semantic-Structural Integration in Text-Attributed Graphs\" at\nt\nhe 5th International Symposium on Cognitive and Semantic Computing\nin\nTaiyuan, China [\nPDF\n].\n[11/2025]\n✅ We have\none\npaper accepted by\nAAAI\n2026.\n[10/2025]\n✅ We have\ntwo\npapers accepted by\nWSDM\n202\n6\n.\n[09/202\n5\n]\n🏆 I am honored to be recognized among the\nWorld's Top 2% Scientist\n(Single Year, 2024 data) by Stanford/Elsevier!\n[08/2025]\n✅ We have one paper accepted by CIKM 2025.\n[07/2025]\n✅\nWe have one paper accepted by TNNLS.\n[\n07\n/202\n5\n]\n🎓 Congratulations to Dr.\nJianyuan Bo\non his successful defense of his PhD dissertation titled \"\nEnhancing graph representation learning through self-supervision: An augmentation perspective\n.\"\n[05/2025]\n✅ We have four papers accepted by KDD 2025 (February cycle).\n[0\n4\n/2025]\n✅ We have\none\npaper accepted by\nSIGIR\n2025.\n[04/2025] 🎤\nI am giving a\nn invited\ntalk \"\nWould prompt work for graph learning? An exploration of few-shot learning on graphs\n\" at the\nInternational Workshop on Resource-Efficient Learning for the Web\n, colocated with the WWW'25, Sydney, Australia\n. [\nPDF\n]\n[\n04\n/202\n5\n] 🎤\nWe organiz\ned\na tutorial titled \"Few-Shot Learning on Graphs: From Meta-Learning to LLM-empowered Pre-Training and Beyond\" at\nWWW\n’25\nheld in Sydney, Australia [\nSlides\n] [\nResources\n].\n[0\n4\n/202\n5\n] 🎤\nI am giving a\nn invited online\ntalk \"\nWould prompt work for graph learning? An exploration of few-shot learning on graphs\n\" at\nUQ-DS\nSeminar, University of\nQueensland\n.\n[01/2025] ✅\nOur\nposition paper on graph foundation models have been accepted by\nIEEE TPAMI\n[\nPDF\n].\n[01/2025] ✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nICLR\n2025\n, on\nconditional prompt learning for dynamic graphs\n[\nPDF\n].\n[01/2025] ✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nNAACL\n2025\n, on\nLLM-based heterophilic graph learning\n[\nPDF\n].\n[01/2025]\n✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nWWW 2025\n, on\ntext-free graph foundation models\n[\nPDF\n].\n[12/2024]\n✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nIEEE/ACM TCBB\n, on a graph neural networks-based approach for predicting anti-cancer drug synergy [\nPDF\n].\n[12/2024]\n✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nNeural Networks\n,\non\nexplainable graph neural networks\n[\nPDF\n].\n[12/2024] ✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nAAAI\n2025 on graph few-shot learning [\nPDF\n].\n[11/2024]\n✅ We have a paper accepted by\nKDD\n2025 (August cycle) on\nnon-homophilic graph pre-training and prompt learning\n[\nPDF\n].\n[11/2024]\n🎓 Congratulations to Dr.\nZhongzhou Liu\non his successful defense of his PhD dissertation titled \"Towards trustworthy recommendation systems: Beyond user-item collaborative filtering.\"\n[10/2024]\n✅ We have a paper accepted by\nWACV\n2025, on open-world zero-shot learning [\nPDF\n].\n[10/2024]\n✅ We have a paper accepted by\nNeural Networks\n, on\nend-to-end bi-objective graph partitioning\n[\nPDF\n].\n[\n10\n/2024]\n🏆 Our paper on\nGraphPrompt\n[\nPDF\n]\nis\nranked as the T\nop\n1\nMost Influential Papers in WWW'23\nby Paper Digest (2024-0\n9\nVersion).\n[\n10\n/2024]\n✅\nWe have\ntwo\npapers accepted by\nWSDM\n202\n5\n, on\ncontrastive review-centric recommendation [PDF]\n, and\naspect-aware review-based recommendation [PDF].\n[09/2024]\n🏆 I am honored to be recognized among the\nWorld's Top 2% Scientist\n(Single Year, 2023 data) by Stanford/Elsevier!\n[09/2024]\n✅\nWe have\nthree\npapers accepted by\nEMNLP 2024\n, on adapter tuning for few-shot relation learning on knowledge graphs [\nPDF\n], out-of-scope intent classification (Findings) [\nPDF\n], and a survey on ontology expansion for conversational understanding [\nPDF\n].\n[0\n8\n/2024] 🎤\nI am giving a\nn invited online\ntalk \"\nWould prompt work for graph learning? An exploration of few-shot learning on graphs\n\"\nat CRUISE Seminar, University of New South Wales, Australia\n.\n[07/2024]\n✅\nWe have\ntwo\npapers accepted by\nIEEE TKDE\n, on generalized graph prompt [\nPDF\n] and prompt tuning for text-attributed graphs [\nPDF\n].\n[07/2024]\n✅\nWe have a paper accepted by\nCIKM\n2024, on large language models for recommendation [\nPDF\n].\n[05/2024]\n✅ We have a paper accepted by\nKDD\n2024,\non\ng\neodesic\nd\nistance-\nb\nased\na\nugmentation on\ng\nraphs [\nP\nDF\n].\n[05/2024]\n✅ We have a paper accepted by\nACL Findings\n2024,\non\np\narameter-\ne\nfficient\nf\nine-\nt\nuning [\nPDF\n].\n[05/2024]\n🎤\nWe are organiz\ning\na tutorial titled \"Towards Graph Foundation Models\" at\nWWW\n2024 held in Singapore [\nPart I\n,\nPart II\n&\nPart III\n] [\nResources\n]\n.\n[05/2024]\n🏆 Our paper on\nGraphPrompt\n[\nPDF\n]\nranks among the Top 5\nMost Influential Papers in WWW'23\nby Paper Digest (2024-05 Version).\n[04/2024]\n✅\nWe have\ntwo\npapers accepted by\nIJCAI\n2024,\non\ngeneral\ng\nraph\nm\natching\n[\nPDF\n]\n, and\nheterogeneous\ng\nraph\nt\nransformer\n[\nPDF\n]\n.\n[01/2024]\n✅\nWe have\nthree\npapers accepted by\nWWW\n2024,\non\nmulti-\nt\nask graph prompt\n[\nPDF\n]\n,\nsimple\nt\nransformer for\nd\nynamic\ng\nraphs\n[\nPDF\n]\n, and\ndiffusion-based\nn\negative\ns\nampling on\ng\nraphs\n[\nPDF\n]\n.\n[01/2024]\n🎤\nI am giving an\ninvited\nonline talk \"\nWould prompt work for graph learning? An exploration of few-shot learning on graphs\n\"\nat\nVALSE Webinar\nSeries\n[\nSlides\n]\n.\n📜 Check the full list in the\narchived updates\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
