    "homepage_text": "π’ Homepage\nJiahuan Pei | 裴家欢\nResearcher at CWI | Ph.D.\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nYouTube\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am working as an assistant professor with the\nSocial AI Group\nat Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam, focusing on multimodal agents for conversational AI. Formerly, I worked with\nDIS Group\nat Centrum Wiskunde & Informatica (CWI) and Amazon, focusing on core NLP/IR problems in both industry and academia. I have pursued my Ph.D. with the\nIRLab\nat University of Amsterdam, supervised by\nProf. dr. Maarten de Rijke\nand\nProf. dr. Pengjie Ren\n. My interest includes natural language processing (dialogue systems, word embedding, parsing, summarization) and information retrieval (query understanding, recommender system, matcher embedding).\nUpdates\nAug. 01, 2024\n, I join Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam as an asssistant professor.\nJul. 16, 2024\n, 1 paper has been accepted by ACM Multimedia 2024.\nJul. 02, 2024\n, 1 paper has been accepted by TOIS 2024.\nMay. 16, 2024\n, 2 paper has been accepted by ACL 2024.\nFeb. 20, 2024\n, 1 paper has been accepted by COLING 2024.\nFeb. 07, 2024\n, I give an invited talk at Microsoft Research, Cambridge, United Kingdom.\nDec. 04, 2023\n, I give an invited talk at Utrecht University.\nNov. 29, 2023\n, I give an invited panel talk at Immersive Tech Week.\nOct. 08, 2023\n, 1 paper is accepted by EMNLP 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Data]\n.\nSep. 19, 2023\n, I give an invited talk at Sony AI.\nJul. 24, 2023\n, I give an invited talk at Bosch Center of Artificial Intelligence (BCAI).\nJul. 03, 2023\n, 1 paper is acceted by Transactions of ACL 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n.\nApr. 29, 2023\n, I give an invited talk at Microsoft Research AI4Science.\nApr. 03, 2023\n, I join\nCWI\non-site as a researcher.\nOct. 27, 2022\n, the source code of\nstochastic transformers\nis released by Amazon.\nOct. 10, 2022\n, I give a spotlight talk at AMLC (Amazon Machine Learning Conference) workshop\n[Details]\n.\nJul. 25, 2022\n, I give an invited talk at University College London (UCL)\n[Details]\n.\nApr. 29, 2022\n, I give an invited talk at Search Engine Amsterdam (SEA)\n[Details]\n.\nApr. 02, 2022\n, 1 paper is accepted by SIGIR 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Data]\n.\nDec. 01, 2021\n, 1 paper is acceted by AAAI 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n.\nDec. 01, 2021\n, I join Amazon as an applied scientist.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - π’ Homepage\nJiahuan Pei | 裴家欢\nResearcher at CWI | Ph.D.\nFollow\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nYouTube\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in GitHub, GitHub University, 2012\nM.S. in Jekyll, GitHub University, 2014\nPh.D in Version Control Theory, GitHub University, 2018 (expected)\nWork experience\nSummer 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Tagging issues\nSupervisor: Professor Git\nFall 2015: Research Assistant\nGithub University\nDuties included: Merging pull requests\nSupervisor: Professor Hub\nSkills\nSkill 1\nSkill 2\nSub-skill 2.1\nSub-skill 2.2\nSub-skill 2.3\nSkill 3\nPublications\nChinese Functional Maximal-length Noun Phrase Recognition (Bachelor Thesis)\nJiahuan Pei*\n, \"Chinese Functional Maximal-length Noun Phrase Recognition (Bachelor Thesis).\" Dalian Maritime University, 2014.\nDUT-NLP-CH @ NTCIR-12 Temporalia Temporal Intent Disambiguation Subtask\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Degen Huang, Jianjun Ma, Dingxin Song, Leyuan Sang, \"DUT-NLP-CH @ NTCIR-12 Temporalia Temporal Intent Disambiguation Subtask.\" In Proceedings of the 12th NTCIR Conference on Evaluation of Information Access Technologies (NTCIR 2016), 2016.\nIdentification of English Functional Noun Phrases by CRFs and the Semantic Information\nJianjun Ma,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Degen Huang, \"Identification of English Functional Noun Phrases by CRFs and the Semantic Information.\" Journal of Chinese Information Processing (CCF B, Chinese Journal), 2016.\nCombining Word Embedding and Semantic Lexicon for Chinese Word Similarity Computation\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Cong Zhang, Degen Huang, Jianjun Ma, \"Combining Word Embedding and Semantic Lexicon for Chinese Word Similarity Computation.\" In Natural Language Understanding and Intelligent Applications (NLPCC 2016, CCF C), 2016.\nSemantic graph optimization algorithm based chinesemicroblog opinion summarization\nCong Zhang,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Kaiyu Huang, Degen Huang, Zhangzhi Yin, \"Semantic graph optimization algorithm based chinesemicroblog opinion summarization.\" Journal Of Shandong University (Natural Science), 2017.\nResearch on Chinese Word Semantic Similarity Computation (Master Thesis)\nJiahuan Pei*\n, \"Research on Chinese Word Semantic Similarity Computation (Master Thesis).\" Dalian University of Technology, 2017.\nIncorporating Prior Knowledge into Word Embedding for Chinese Word Similarity Measurement\nDegen Huang,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Cong Zhang, Kaiyu Huang, Jianjun Ma, \"Incorporating Prior Knowledge into Word Embedding for Chinese Word Similarity Measurement.\" ACM Transactions on Asian and Low-Resource Language Information Processing (TALLIP 2018, SCI, JCR-Q2, IF=1.413), 2018.\nSyntactic parsing of clause constituents for statistical machine translation\nJianjun Ma,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Degen Huang, Dingxin Song, \"Syntactic parsing of clause constituents for statistical machine translation.\" International Journal of Computational Science and Engineering (IJCSE 2018, JCR-Q3), 2018.\nRecognition of Syntactic Relationship between Clauses Using CRFs\nJianjun Ma, Mulangma Zhu, Degen Huang,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, \"Recognition of Syntactic Relationship between Clauses Using CRFs.\" In International Journal of Advanced Intelligence, 2018.\nSEntNet: Source-aware Recurrent Entity Network for Dialogue Response Selection\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Arent Stienstra, Julia Kiseleva, Maarten Rijke, \"SEntNet: Source-aware Recurrent Entity Network for Dialogue Response Selection.\" In Proceedings of the 28th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence Workshop on Search-Oriented Conversational AI (IJCAI 2019 SCAI Workshop), 2019.\nA Modular Task-oriented Dialogue System Using a Neural Mixture-of-Experts\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Pengjie Ren, Maarten Rijke, \"A Modular Task-oriented Dialogue System Using a Neural Mixture-of-Experts.\" In Proceedings of the 42nd International ACM SIGIR Workshop on Conversational Interaction Systems (SIGIR 2019 WCIS Workshop), 2019.\nRetrospective and Prospective Mixture-of-Generators for Task-oriented Dialogue Response Generation\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Pengjie Ren, Christof Monz, Maarten Rijke, \"Retrospective and Prospective Mixture-of-Generators for Task-oriented Dialogue Response Generation.\" In Proceedings of the 24th European Conference on Artificial Intelligence (ECAI 2020, CCF B), 2019.\nA Cooperative Memory Network for Personalized Task-oriented Dialogue Systems with Incomplete User Profiles\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Pengjie Ren, Maarten Rijke, \"A Cooperative Memory Network for Personalized Task-oriented Dialogue Systems with Incomplete User Profiles.\" In Proceedings of The Web Conference 2021 (WWW 2021, CCF A), 2021.\nPre-trained Language Models in Biomedical Domain: A Systematic Survey\nBenyou Wang, Qianqian Xie,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Prayag Tiwari, Zhao Li, Jie Fu, \"Pre-trained Language Models in Biomedical Domain: A Systematic Survey.\" Association for Computing Machinery, 2021.\nLearning Embeddings to Represent Information Retrieval Systems\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Danushka Bollegala, Omar Zaidan, \"Learning Embeddings to Represent Information Retrieval Systems.\" In AMLC 2022 Deep Metric Learning and Semantic Similarity Search Workshop, 2022.\nReMeDi: Resources for Multi-domain, Multi-service, Medical Dialogues\nGuojun Yan,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Pengjie Ren, Zhaochun Ren, Maarten Rijke, \"ReMeDi: Resources for Multi-domain, Multi-service, Medical Dialogues.\" In Proceedings of International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR 2022, CCF A), 2022.\nTransformer Uncertainty Estimation with Hierarchical Stochastic Attentions\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Cheng Wang, Gyorgy Szarvas, \"Transformer Uncertainty Estimation with Hierarchical Stochastic Attentions.\" In Proceedings of AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2022, CCF A), 2022.\nCollaborative Agents for Task-oriented Dialogue Systems (Doctoral Thesis)\nJiahuan Pei*\n, \"Collaborative Agents for Task-oriented Dialogue Systems (Doctoral Thesis).\" Univeristy of Amsterdam, 2022.\nIntent-calibrated Self-training for Answer Selection in Open-domain Dialogues\nWentao Deng,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Zhaochun Ren, Zhumin Chen, Pengjie Ren, \"Intent-calibrated Self-training for Answer Selection in Open-domain Dialogues.\" Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics (TACL, CCF B), 2023.\nPre-trained Language Models in Biomedical Domain: A Systematic Survey\nBenyou Wang, Qianqian Xie,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Prayag Tiwari, Zhao Li, Jie Fu, \"Pre-trained Language Models in Biomedical Domain: A Systematic Survey.\" Computing Surveys, 2023.\nSyllogistic Reasoning for Legal Judgment Analysis\nWentao Deng,\nJiahuan Pei*\n, Keyi Kong, Zhe Chen, Furu Wei, Yujun Li, Zhaochun Ren, Zhumin Chen, Pengjie Ren, \"Syllogistic Reasoning for Legal Judgment Analysis.\" In Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP23, CCF B), 2023.\nTalks\nTransformer Uncertainty Estimation with Hierarchical Stochastic Attention\nApril 29, 2022\nInvited Talk at Search Engine Amsterdam (SEA), Amsterdam, Netherlands\nFrontiers of Collaborative Task-oriented Dialogue Systems\nJuly 06, 2022\nInvited Talk at University College London (UCL), London, UK\nLearning Embeddings to Represent Information Retrieval Systems\nOctober 14, 2022\nInvited Conference Talk at Amazon Machine Learning Conference (AMLC), Seattle, WA, US\nGenerative AI towards Scientific Discovery\nApril 06, 2023\nInvited Talk at Microsoft Research AI4Science, Amsterdam, Netherlands\nAdvancements and Prospects in Dialogue Agents and LLMs\nJuly 24, 2023\nInvited Talk at Bosch Center of Artificial Intelligence (BCAI), Renningen, Germany\nLanguage Model Powered Dialogue Agents and Virtual KB\nSeptember 19, 2023\nInvited Talk at Sony AI, Barcelona, Spain\nMaximising efficiency in NLP model training and XR environments\nNovember 29, 2023\nInvited Panel Talk at Immersive Tech Week, Rotterdam, Netherlands\nMultimodal Dialogue Agents Towards Intelligent XR\nDecember 04, 2023\nInvited Talk at Utrecht University, Utrecht, Netherlans\nMultimodal Conversational AI Agents Towards Smarter Assistant\nFebruary 07, 2024\nInvited Talk at Microsoft Research, Cambridge, United Kingdom\nTeaching\nInformation Retrieval (Zoekmachines)\nRole-aware Recurrent Entity Networks for Task-oriented Dialogue Systems (Thesis)\nInformation Retrieval 2\nUsing Source Awareness in Memory End-to-End Task-oriented Dialog Learning (Thesis)\nHierarchical Merchant Category Code Assignment for E-commerce Merchants (Thesis)\nInformation Retrieval (Zoekmachines)\nMedical Dialogue Agents\nConversational Recommendation\nEfficient Fine-tuning for Large Language Models\nBrickDream: Multimodal Immersive Systems in Augmented Reality (Thesis)\nFaithfulness Evaluation of Large Language Models\nLegal Dialogue Generation and Reasoning with Large Language Models\nFine-Grained Vision-Language Modeling for Multimodal Training Assistants in Augmented Reality (Thesis)\nPsychotherapy Dialogue Generation with Large Language Models\nProject Conversational Agents\nService and leadership\nCurrently signed in to 43 different slack teams"
