    "homepage_text": "Zhaochun Ren\nZhaochun Ren\nI am currently an Associate Professor at\nLeiden University\n, the Netherlands. My research focuses on information retrieval and natural language processing, with a particular emphasis on conversational information-seeking, generative retrieval, recommender systems, and large language models. My overarching goal is to develop intelligent agents capable of addressing complex user requests and solving fundamental challenges in NLP and IR. Before joining Leiden, I served as a Professor at Shandong University from 2019 to 2023 and worked as a Research Scientist at JD.com from 2017 to 2019. I earned my PhD in 2016 from the University of Amsterdam, where I was supervised by\nProf. dr. Maarten de Rijke\nand\nProf. dr. Evangelos Kanoulas\n. Prior to that, I completed both my B.E. (2009) and M.E. (2012) at Shandong University and spent time as a short-term visiting scholar at the Max Planck Institute for Informatics in 2012.\nCSC Admission\n: I welcome outstanding CSC-funded candidates to join my research group in 2026. If your research interests align with mine, please feel free to reach out via email for further discussion.\nResearch interests\nInformation Retrieval\n:\nRecommender systems\nConversational IR\nGenerative retrieval\nRetrieval-argumented generation\nNatural Language Processing\n:\nEmpathetic dialogue systems\nKnowledge representation and distillation\nLarge Language Models\n:\nLLMs fine-tuning and alignment\nTool learning and multi-agent with LLMs\nEfficient pre-training and inference\nNews\nSep, 2025\n3 papers have been accepted at NeurIPS 2025!\nAug, 2025\n3 papers have been accepted at EMNLP 2025!\nAug, 2025\n1 papers have been accepted at CIKM 2025!\nMay, 2025\n3 papers have been accepted at ACL 2025!\nApr, 2025\n3 papers have been accepted at SIGIR 2025!\n\n---\n\nCV | Zhaochun Ren\nCV\nTable of contents\nGeneral information\nEducation\nWorking experience\nAwards\nGeneral information\nFull Name\nZhaochun Ren\nContact address\nRoom BE.2.11. Gorlaeusgebouw, Einsteinweg 55 2333 CC Leiden, the Netherlands\nEmail address\nz.ren@liacs DOT leidenuniv DOT nl\nEducation\n2012 - 2016\nPhD in ILPS\nUniversity of Amsterdam, Amsterdam, the Netherlands\nSupervisor\nProf. Maarten de Rijke and Prof. Evangelos Kanoulas\n2009 - 2012\nM.E. in Computer Science and Technology\nShandong University, Qingdao, China\nSupervisor\nProf. Jun Ma\n2005 - 2009\nB.E. in Computer Science and Technology\nShandong University, Qingdao, China\nWorking experience\n2023 - now\n(Tenured) Associate Professor\nLeiden University\n2019 - 2023\nProfessor\nShandong University, China\n2017 - 2019\nResearch Scientist & Senior Research Manager\nData Science Lab at JD.com, China\nWorked on e-commerce recommender systems, text mining, and dialogue systems.\n2016 - 2017\nResearch Associate\nDepartment of Computer Science, University College London, United Kingdom\nWorked on an EPSRC project about early warning for infectious diseases.\n2012-2016\nPhD student\nInformatics Institute, University of Amsterdam, The Netherlands\nWorked on social media analysis.\n2014\nVisiting Scholar\nNatural Language Processing Group, Columbia University, U.S.A\nSupervisor\nProf. Kathleen McKeown\n2012\nVisiting Scholar\nD5, Max Planck Institute for Informatics, Germany\nSupervisor\nProf. Gerhard Weikum\nAwards\n2024\nACM RecSys 2024 Best Full Paper Award\n2024\nSIGIR 2024 Best Paper Honorable Mention Award\n2024\nWSDM 2024 Best Paper Runner-up Award\n2023\nEMNLP 2023 Outstanding Paper Award\n2022\nChina Computer Federation - Rising Star Award on Natural Language Processing\n2020\nTencent “Rhino Bird” Faculty Research Award\n2019\nWSDM 2019 Outstanding Reviewer Award\n2019-2023\nQilu Youth Fellowship, Shandong University\n2018\nWSDM 2018 Best Student Paper Award\n2017\nCIKM 2017 Best Full Paper Runner Up Award\n2015\nChinese Government Award for Outstanding PhD Students"
  },
