    "homepage_text": "Cheng Han\nCheng Han\nAssistant Professor\nchk9k (at) umsystem.edu\nUniversity of Missouri -- Kansas City, USA\nBiography\nI am a Tenure-track Assistant Professor at the School of Science and Engineering, University of Missouri -- Kansas City, USA.\n              My research interests include adaptable and sustainable intelligence, where I design, implement, deploy, and evaluate AI systems that empower communities. I am continuously interested in recruiting Ph.D. students with a strong background in AI agents and systemic efficiency.\nNews (01/21/2026): Website updated for new papers published in TMLR and ICLR. Congrats to all my collaborators!\nNews (09/27/2025): Website updated for new papers published in NeurIPS. Congrats to Runjia and Yiyang!\nNews (08/21/2025): Website updated for new paper published in EMNLP. Congrats to Runjia!\nNews (08/15/2025): Our lab website is online! While it is still under construction, please feel free to check!\nNews (06/29/2025): Website updated for new paper published in ICCV. Congrats to Taowen!\nNews (03/14/2025): Website updated for new papers published in EMNLP and ICLR. Congrats to Taowen and Yiyang!\nTable of Content\nSelected Publications\nServices\nTalks and Presentation\nTeaching\nSelected Publications\nVisual Recognition with Deep Nearest Centriods\n[pdf(arxiv)]\n[code]\n.\n                  W. Wang*†, C. Han*, T. Zhou*, D. Liu†, International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2023 (Spotlight). *Equal Contribution\nPrompt Learns Prompt: Exploring Knowledge-Aware Generative Prompt Collaboration For Video Captioning\n[pdf(IJCAI)]\n.\n                  L. Yan*, C. Han*, Z. Xu, D. Liu†, Q. Wang, International Joint Conferences on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI), 2023. *Equal Contribution\nE^2VPT: An Effective and Efficient Approach for Visual Prompt Tuning\n[pdf(arxiv)]\n[code]\n.\n                  C. Han*, Q. Wang, Y. Cui, Z. Cao, W. Wang, S. Qi, D. Liu†. International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2023.\nUnified 3D Segmenter As Prototypical Classifiers\n[pdf(Openreview)]\n[code]\n.\n                  Z. Qin*, C. Han*, X. Lu, Q. Wang, X, Nie, Y, Yin†. Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023. *Equal Contribution\nCML-MOTS: Collaborative Multi-task Learning for Multi-Object Tracking and Segmentation\n[pdf(arxiv)]\n.\n                  Y. Cui, C. Han, D. Liu†. ACM Journal on Autonomous Transportation Systems (JATS), 2023.\nFacing the Elephant in the Room: Visual Prompt Tuning or Full Finetuning?\n                  C. Han*, Q. Wang, Y. Cui, W. Wang, L. Huang, S. Qi, D. Liu†. International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2024\n[pdf(Openreview)]\n[code]\n.\nImage Translation as Diffusion Visual Programmers.\n                  C. Han, J. C. Liang, Q. Wang, M. Rabbani, S. Dianat, R. Rao, Y. N. Wu, D. Liu†. International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2024.\n[pdf(Openreview)]\n[Website]\n.\nProMotion: Prototypes As Motion Learners.\n                  Y. Lu, D. Liu, Q., C. Han, Y. Cui, Z. Cao, X. Zhang, Y. V. Chen, H. Fan†. IEEE / CVF Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (CVPR), 2024.\n[pdf]\nSSGA-Net: Stepwise Spatial Global-local Aggregation Networks for for Autonomous Driving. Y. Cui, C. Han, D. Liu†.\n[pdf]\nPrototypical Transformer as Unified Motion Learners. C. Han*, Y. Lu*, G. Sun, J. C. Liang, Z. Cao, Q. Wang, Q. Guan, S. A. Dianat, R. M. Rao, T. Geng, Z. Tao†, D. Liu†. International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2024.\n[pdf]\nSelf-supervised Adversarial Training of Monocular Depth Estimation against Physical-World Attacks. Z. Cheng, C. Han, J. C. Liang, Q. Wang, X. Zhang, D. Liu†. IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (IEEE TPAMI), 2024.\n[pdf]\nOptical Flow as Spatial-Temporal Attention Learners. Y. Lu*, C. Han*, Q. Wang, H. Fan, Z. Kong, D. Liu, Y. Chen. IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (IEEE TPAMI), 2024.\nAMD: Automatic Multi-step Distillation of Large-scale Vision Models. C. Han, Q. Wang, S. A Dianat, M. Rabbani, R. M Rao, Y. Fang, Q. Guan, L. Huang, D. Liu†. The European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2024.\n[pdf]\nM^2PT: Multimodal Prompt Tuning for Zero-shot Instruction Learning. T. Wang, Y. Liu, J. C. Liang, J. Zhao, Y. Cui, Y. Mao, S. Nie, J. Liu, F. Feng, Z. Xu, C. Han, L. Huang, Q. Wang, D. Liu. The Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP), 2024.\n[pdf]\nVisual Fourier Prompt Tuning. R. Zeng*, C. Han*, Q Wang, C. Wu, T. Geng, L. Rao, L. Huang, Y. N. Wu, D. Liu. The Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024.\n[pdf]\nRe-Imagining Multimodal Instruction Tuning: A Representation View. Y. Liu, J. C. Liang, R. Tang, Y. Lee, M. Rabbani, S. A Dianat, R. Rao, L. Huang, D. Liu, Q. Wang, C. Han†. The International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2025.\n[pdf]\n[code]\nExploring the Adversarial Vulnerabilities of Vision-Language-Action Models in Robotics. T. Wang*, C. Han*, J. C. Liang*, W. Yang, D. Liu, L. X. Zhang,  Q. Wang,  J. Luo, R. Tang. International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025.\n[pdf]\n[code]\nMEPT: Mixture of Expert Prompt Tuning as a Manifold Mapper. R. Zeng*, G. Sun*, Q Wang, T. Geng, S. A Dianat, X. Han, R. Rao, X. Zhang, C. Han, L. Huang, D. Liu. The Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP), 2025.\n[pdf]\nProbabilistic Token Alignment for Large Language Model Fusion. R. Zeng, J. C. Liang, C. Han, Z. Cao, J. Liu, X. Quan, Q. Wang, T. Geng, D. Liu. The Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025.\n[pdf]\n[project page]\nAll You Need is One: Capsule Prompt Tuning with a Single Vector. Y. Liu, J. C. Liang, H. Fang, W. Yang, Y. Cui, X. Han, L. Huang, D. Liu, Q. Wang, C. Han. The Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2025.\n[pdf]\n[code]\nTokenSeek: Memory Efficient Fine Tuning via Instance-Aware Token Ditching. R. Zeng, Q. Wang, Q. Guan, R. Tang, L. Huang, Z. Wang, X. Zhang, C. Han, D. Liu. The International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026.\n[pdf]\n[project page]\nPrompt-based adaptation in large-scale vision models: A survey. X. Xiao, Y. Zhang, L. Zhao, Y. Liu, X. Liao, Z. Mai, X. Li, X. Wang, H. Xu, J. Hamm, X. Lin, M. Xu, Q. Wang, T. Wang, C. Han. Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR), 2026.\n[pdf]\n[project page]\nServices\nFaculty Search Committee\nat the University of Missouri – Kansas City, 2024\nGraduate Committee\nat the University of Missouri – Kansas City, 2024\nDoctoral Consortium Chair\nat the ACM/IEEE Joint Conference on Digital Libraries (JCDL), 2025\nProgram Committee\n, The Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2023 -- Now.\nProgram Committee\n, SIAM International Conference on Data Mining (SDM), 2024.\nReviewer\n, The Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024.\nReviewer\n, The International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2024.\nReviewer\n, The Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2022 -- Now.\nReviewer\n, IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (IEEE TCSVT), 2022 -- Now.\nReviewer\n, Association for Computational Linguistics Rolling Review (ARR), 2023 -- Now.\nReviewer\n, The International World Wide Web Conference (WWW), 2024.\nReviewer\n, The Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2024 - now\nReviewer\n, The International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2023 – now\nReviewer\n, The International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2023 – now\nReviewer\n, International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV), 2024\nReviewer\n, Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR), 2024 - now\nReviewer\n, IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (IEEE TPAMI), 2024 - now\nReviewer\n, IEEE Transactions on Artificial Intelligence (IEEE TAI), 2025.\nReviewer\n, Neurocomputing, 2024.\nReviewer\n, The International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025.\nReviewer\n, The Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV), 2026.\nTalks and Presentation\nICLR 2023 Spotlight Presentation\n, Visual Recognition with Deep Nearest Centriods\n[YouTube]\n.\nICCV 2023 Presentation\n, E^2VPT: An Effective and Efficient Approach for Visual Prompt Tuning\n[YouTube]\n.\nNeurIPS 2023 Presentation\n, Unified 3D Segmenter as Prototypical Classifiers. New Orleans, USA.\nICLR 2024 Presentation\n, Facing the Elephant in the Room: Visual Prompt Tuning or Full Finetuning?\nICLR 2024 Presentation\n, Image Translation as Diffusion Visual Programmers.\nNSF REU SITE: AI-empowered Cybersecurity Seminar Series (07/12/2024): Prompts as Sustainable Learners.\nEMNLP 2024 Presentation\n, M^2PT: Multimodal Prompt Tuning for Zero-shot Instruction Learning (11/14/2024).\nNaval Research Laboratory Machine Learning Seminar (12/04/2024): Parameter Efficient Finetuning in Large-scale AI Models.\nNSF LEVEL UP AI Roundtable (04/25/2025): Principles and Resources for AI Education for All.\nThe Computing Community Consortium (CCC) Computing Futures Symposium (05/15/2025-05/16/2025): Re-Imagining Multimodal Instruction Tuning from a Parameter-efficient Representation Perspective.\nNSF REU SITE: AI-empowered Cybersecurity Seminar Series (06/30/2025): Efficient Fine-Tuning for X.\nNeurIPS 2025 Presentation\n, All You Need is One: Capsule Prompt Tuning with a Single Vector & Probabilistic Token Alignment for Large Language Model Fusion (12/01/2025).\nNews on Fox4 Kansas City's \"The cost of AI\" series\n, The cost of AI: How Kansas City’s data center boom could impact your health\n[News Link 1]\n& The cost of AI: How Kansas City’s data center boom could affect water, electricity rates\n[News Link 2]\n(01/21/2026).\nTeaching\nUMKC COMP-SCI 5567-0001: Deep Learning\nSpring, 2025, 2026.\nUMKC COMP-SCI 5567-0002: Deep Learning\