    "homepage_text": "Qifan Wang’s Homepage\nQifan Wang\nPrincipal Research Scientist at Meta AI\nFollow\nMenlo Park, California\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nDBLP\nAbout me\nI am a Principal Research Scientist at Meta AI, leading a team building\n                            innovative Deep Learning and Natural Language Processing models for Recommendation System.\n                            Before joining Meta, I worked as a Research Engineer at Google Research, focusing on deep \n                            domain representations and large-scale object understanding. I also worked at Intel Labs for two years. \n                            I received my PhD in computer science from Purdue University in 2015. Prior to that, \n                            I obtained both my MS and BS degrees in computer science from Tsinghua University. \n                            My research interests include deep learning, natural language processing, information retrieval, \n                            data mining, and computer vision. I have co-authored over 100 publications in top-tier conferences and \n                            journals, including NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, SIGKDD, WWW, SIGIR, AAAI, IJCAI, WSDM, EACL, CIKM, TPAMI, TKDE and TOIS. \n                            I also serve as area chairs, program committee members, editorial board members, and reviewers for academic \n                            conferences and journals.\nLatest News\n02/02/26 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for KDD 2026.\n01/25/26 - One paper accepted to ICLR 2026.\n01/23/26 - One paper accepted to TMLR 2026.\n01/13/26 - One paper accepted to WWW 2026.\n12/04/25 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for ACL 2026.\n11/07/25 - One paper accepted to AAAI 2026.\n10/25/25 - Two papers accepted to AACL 2025.\n09/18/25 - Three papers accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n08/20/25 - Seven papers accepted to EMNLP 2025.\n08/04/25 - One paper accepted to CIKM 2025.\n07/11/25 - One paper accepted to ECAI 2025.\n07/04/25 - One paper accepted to ACMMM 2025.\n06/25/25 - Two papers accepted to ICCV 2025.\n06/19/25 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for WSDM 2026.\n05/16/25 - One paper accepted to KDD 2025.\n05/15/25 - Five papers accepted to ACL 2025.\n04/09/25 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025.\n04/04/25 - Two papers accepted to SIGIR 2025.\n03/28/25 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for EMNLP 2025.\n03/16/25 - Invited to serve as SPC for CIKM 2025.\n02/17/25 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for ACMMM 2025.\n01/26/25 - One paper accepted to TKDE.\n01/22/25 - One paper accepted to NAACL 2025.\n01/22/25 - Five papers accepted to ICLR 2025.\n01/21/25 - One paper accepted to AISTATS 2025.\n01/14/25 - One paper accepted to TMLR.\n12/16/24 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for IJCAI 2025.\n12/09/24 - One paper accepted to AAAI 2025.\n12/08/24 - One paper accepted to TNNLS.\n09/25/24 - Three papers accepted to NeurIPS 2024.\n09/22/24 - One paper accepted to TORS\n09/20/24 - Six papers accepted to EMNLP 2024.\n09/18/24 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for WWW 2025.\n09/04/24 - One paper accepted to TPAMI.\n09/01/24 - One paper accepted to TASLP.\n08/19/24 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for ICLR 2025.\n08/13/24 - One paper accepted to TMLR.\n07/01/24 - Two papers accepted to ECCV 2024.\n06/20/24 - Our paper won the\nOutstanding Paper Award\nat NAACL 2024!\n06/07/24 - One paper accepted to TPAMI 2024.\n05/23/24 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for COLING 2025.\n05/22/24 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for WSDM 2025.\n05/17/24 - One paper accepted to KDD 2024.\n05/16/24 - Four papers accepted to ACL 2024.\n05/01/24 - One paper accepted to ICML 2024.\n03/25/24 - One paper accepted to SIGIR 2024.\n03/13/24 - Four papers accepted to NAACL 2024.\n03/11/24 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for CIKM 2024.\n02/26/24 - Two papers accepted to CVPR 2024.\n02/19/24 - One paper accepted to COLING 2024.\n02/11/24 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for ACL 2024.\n01/19/24 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for ACMMM 2024.\n01/18/24 - Two papers accepted to EACL 2024.\n01/16/24 - Four papers accepted to ICLR 2024.\n12/09/23 - One paper accepted to AAAI 2024.\n11/10/23 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for IJCAI 2024.\n10/07/23 - Eleven papers accepted to EMNLP 2023.\n10/04/23 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for NAACL 2024.\n09/21/23 - Three paper accepted to NeurIPS 2023.\n09/04/23 - One paper accepted to Neural Networks.\n07/26/23 - One paper accepted to Transactions on Big Data.\n07/23/23 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for WWW 2024.\n07/14/23 - One paper accepted to ICCV 2023.\n06/29/23 - One paper accepted to ICML 2023 MFPL Workshop.\n06/25/23 - One paper accepted to KDD 2023 FL4Data-Mining Workshop.\n06/18/23 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for WSDM 2024.\n05/25/23 - One paper accepted to TMLR 2023.\n05/25/23 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for EMNLP 2023.\n05/11/23 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for CIKM 2023.\n05/02/23 - Eleven papers accepted to ACL 2023.\n05/01/23 - Our paper won the\nBest Student Paper Award\nat WWW 2023!\n04/19/23 - One paper accepted to IJCAI 2023.\n04/05/23 - One paper accepted to SIGIR 2023.\n03/27/23 - Invited to serve as Program Committee for NeurIPS 2023.\n03/03/23 - Invited to serve as Program Committee for ICCV 2023.\n02/27/23 - Two papers accepted to CVPR 2023.\n02/15/23 - One paper accepted to ICASSP 2023.\n01/25/23 - One paper accepted to WWW 2023.\n12/20/22 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for KDD 2023.\n12/12/22 - Invited to serve as Senior Area Chair for ACL 2023.\n11/18/22 - One paper accepted to AAAI 2023.\n11/15/22 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for IJCAI 2023.\n10/18/22 - One paper accepted to WSDM 2023.\n10/06/22 - Five papers accepted to EMNLP 2022.\n09/14/22 - One paper accepted to NeurIPS 2022.\n09/08/22 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for WWW 2023.\n08/15/22 - Two papers accepted to COLING 2022.\n08/12/22 - One paper accepted to ACM CHASE 2022.\n07/30/22 - Invited tech talk at DataFunSummit 2022.\n07/05/22 - Invited to serve as Senior Program Committee for WSDM 2023.\n07/03/22 - One paper accepted to ECCV 2022.\n06/14/22 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for AAAI 2023.\n06/06/22 - Invited to serve as Area Chair for EMNLP 2022.\n05/19/22 - Two papers accepted to TCSVT 2022.\n05/04/22 - Invited to serve as program committee for ECCV 2022.\n04/27/22 - Invited to serve as program committee for MM 2022.\n04/21/22 - Invited to serve as Session Chair at WWW 2022.\n04/20/22 - One paper accepted to IJCAI 2022.\n03/08/22 - Invited to serve as program committee for CIKM 2022.\n03/01/22 - Invited tech talk at Rochester Institute of Technology.\n02/23/22 - Invited tech talk at Meituan NLP Center.\n01/25/22 - Invited to serve as program committee for IJCAI 2022.\n01/13/22 - Two papers accepted to WWW 2022.\n01/10/22 - Invited to serve as program committee for SIGIR 2022.\n\n---\n\nQifan Wang’s Homepage\nQifan Wang\nPrincipal Research Scientist at Meta AI\nFollow\nMenlo Park, California\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nDBLP\nEducation\nPh.D in Computer Science, Purdue University, West Lafayette, US, 2010-2015\nM.S. in Computer Science, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, 2007-2010\nB.S. in Computer Science, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, 2003-2007\nWork Experience\n2022.01 - present: Research Scientist, Meta AI\n2015.05 - 2022.01: Research Engineer, Google Research\n2013.06 - 2013.08: Research Intern, Google Research\n2012.05 - 2012.08: Research Intern, Linkedin\n2010.08 - 2015.05: Research Assistant, Purdue University\n2008.07 - 2010.05: Research Engineer, Intel Labs Beijing"
