    "homepage_text": "Feng Xue 薛峰\nFeng Xue 薛峰\nMHUG, University of Trento (UniTrento), PostDoc.\nVRobotit Lab, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT), Ph.D.\nvia Sommarive, 9, 38123 Povo, Trento, Italy\nFeng Xue is a postdoctoral researcher working with Prof.\nNicu Sebe\nat the\nMultimedia and Human Understanding Group (MHUG)\n, University of Trento, Italy.\nPreviously, he earned his Ph.D. degree in computer science and technology (2023) from the Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT),\nand his MA.Eng. degree in computer technology (2019) from BUPT, China.\nHis Ph.D. thesis advisor is Prof.\nAnlong Ming\n,\nand he also works closely with Prof.\nYu Zhou\n.\nHis research interests lie in\nOpen-World Visual Perception\nfor Robots and\nOpen-Domain Generalization\n.\nnews\n07.2025\n2 papers has been accepted by\nICCV 2025\n.\n05.2025\n1 paper has been accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n.\n03.2025\n1 paper has been accepted by\nInformation Fusion 2025\n.\n01.2025\nOur work\nEvidence-based Real-time Road Segmentation with RGB-D Data Augmentation\nhas been accepted by\nT-ITS 2025\n!\n08.2024\nOur work\nSM4Depth: Seamless Monocular Metric Depth Estimation across Multiple Cameras and Scenes by One Model\nhas been accepted by\nACMMM 2024\n!\nselected publications\n2025\nINFFUS\nCues3D: Unleashing the power of sole NeRF for consistent and unique instances in open-vocabulary 3D panoptic segmentation\nFeng Xue\n, Wenzhuang Xu, Guofeng Zhong, and\n2 more authors\nIn Information Fusion\n, 2025\narXiv\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@inproceedings\n{\ncues3d\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue, Feng and Xu, Wenzhuang and Zhong, Guofeng and Ming, Anlong and Sebe, Nicu}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{Information Fusion}\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Cues3D: Unleashing the power of sole NeRF for consistent and unique instances in open-vocabulary 3D panoptic segmentation}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{122}\n,\n}\nTITS\nEvidence-based Real-time Road Segmentation with RGB-D Data Augmentation\nFeng Xue✝, Yicong Chang✝, Wenzhuang Xu, and\n3 more authors\nTransactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems (T-ITS)  Journal Version of USNet\n, 2025\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@article\n{\ntits_eviroadseg\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Evidence-based Real-time Road Segmentation with RGB-D Data Augmentation}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue✝, Feng and Chang✝, Yicong and Xu, Wenzhuang and Liang, Wenteng and Sheng, Fei and Ming, Anlong}\n,\njournal\n=\n{Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems (T-ITS)  Journal Version of USNet}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{26}\n,\nnumber\n=\n{2}\n,\npages\n=\n{1482-1493}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{}\n,\n}\n2023\nIJCV\nIndoor Obstacle Discovery on Reflective Ground via Monocular Camera\nFeng Xue\n, Yicong Chang, Tianxi Wang, and\n2 more authors\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n, 2023\narXiv\nBib\nHTML\nCode\nWebsite\n@article\n{\nijcv_org\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Indoor Obstacle Discovery on Reflective Ground via Monocular Camera}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue, Feng and Chang, Yicong and Wang, Tianxi and Zhou, Yu and Ming, Anlong}\n,\njournal\n=\n{International Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{}\n,\nnumber\n=\n{}\n,\npages\n=\n{1573-1405}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{}\n,\n}\nCVPR\nUnknown Sniffer for Object Detection: Don’t Turn a Blind Eye to Unknown Objects\nWenteng Liang✝, Feng Xue✝, Yihao Liu, and\n2 more authors\nIn IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2023\nBib\nPDF\nSupp\nCode\nSlides\nWebsite\n@inproceedings\n{\nunsniffer\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Liang✝, Wenteng and Xue✝, Feng and Liu, Yihao and Zhong, Guofeng and Ming, Anlong}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)}\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Unknown Sniffer for Object Detection: Don't Turn a Blind Eye to Unknown Objects}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\n}\n2022\nICRA\nMonocular Depth Distribution Alignment with Low Computation\nFei Sheng✝, Feng Xue✝, Yicong Chang, and\n2 more authors\nIn IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\n, 2022\narXiv\nBib\nHTML\nCode\n@inproceedings\n{\nDANet2021\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Sheng✝, Fei and Xue✝, Feng and Chang, Yicong and Liang, Wenteng and Ming, Anlong}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)}\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Monocular Depth Distribution Alignment with Low Computation}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2022}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{10.1109/ICRA46639.2022.9811937}\n,\n}\n2021\nPR\nBoundary-induced and scene-aggregated network for monocular depth prediction\nFeng Xue\n, Junfeng Cao,\nYu Zhou\n, and\n3 more authors\nPattern Recognition (PR)\n, 2021\narXiv\nBib\nHTML\nCode\nSlides\n@article\n{\ndepthpr2021\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Boundary-induced and scene-aggregated network for monocular depth prediction}\n,\njournal\n=\n{Pattern Recognition (PR)}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{115}\n,\npages\n=\n{107901}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2021}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue, Feng and Cao, Junfeng and Zhou, Yu and Sheng, Fei and Wang, Yankai and Ming, Anlong}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{10.1016/j.patcog.2021.107901}\n,\n}\n2020\nTIP\nTiny Obstacle Discovery by Occlusion-aware Multilayer Regression\nFeng Xue\n,\nAnlong Ming\n, and\nYu Zhou\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\n, 2020\narXiv\nBib\nCode\n@article\n{\ntip\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Tiny Obstacle Discovery by Occlusion-aware Multilayer Regression}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue, Feng and Ming, Anlong and Zhou, Yu}\n,\njournal\n=\n{IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2020}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{29}\n,\nnumber\n=\n{}\n,\npages\n=\n{9373-9386}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{10.1109/TIP.2020.3026636}\n,\n}\n2019\nICRA\nA Novel Multi-layer Framework for Tiny Obstacle Discovery\nFeng Xue\n,\nAnlong Ming\n, Menghan Zhou, and\n1 more author\nIn IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\n, 2019\narXiv\nBib\nHTML\nCode\nSlides\n@inproceedings\n{\nICRA\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Xue, Feng and Ming, Anlong and Zhou, Menghan and Zhou, Yu}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)}\n,\ntitle\n=\n{A Novel Multi-layer Framework for Tiny Obstacle Discovery}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2019}\n,\nxdoi\n=\n{10.1109/ICRA.2019.8794279}\n,\n}\n\n---\n\ncv | Feng Xue 薛峰\ncv\nThis is a description of the page. You can modify it in 'pages/_cv.md'. You can also change or remove the top pdf download button.\nTable of contents\nBasics\nWork\nEducation\nAwards\nLanguages\nBasics\nName\nAlbert Einstein\nLabel\nScientist\nEmail\nalbert@einstein.de\nPhone\n(912) 123-4567\nUrl\nhttps://alshedivat.github.io/al-folio/\nSummary\nA German-born theoretical physicist, widely ranked among the greatest and most influential scientists of all time\nWork\n1933.01 - 1955.01\nProfessor of Theoretical Physics\nInstitute for Advanced Study, Princeton University\nTeaching at Palmer Physical Laboratory (now 302 Frist Campus Center). While not a professor at Princeton, I associated with the physics professors and continued to give lectures on campus.\nRelativity\nEducation\n1905.01 - 1905.01\nPhD\nUniversity of Zurich, Zurich, Switzerland\nSoftware Development\nTheory of Relativity\nAwards\n1921.11.01\nNobel Prize in Physics\nRoyal Swedish Academy of Sciences\nThe Nobel Prizes are five separate prizes that, according to Alfred Nobel's will of 1895, are awarded to 'those who, during the preceding year, have conferred the greatest benefit to humankind.'\nLanguages\nGerman\nNative speaker\nEnglish\nFluent"
