    "homepage_text": "Binwu Wang (王斌武)- Homepage\nBin-Wu Wang\n王斌武\nAssistant Professor\nData Intelligence Lab\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n📢 Address:\n中国科学技术大学苏州高等研究院\n✉️ Email: wbw2024@ustc.edu.cn\n🤵🏻 About Me\nI am a machine learning researcher specializing in time series forecasting, spatio-temporal data mining, graph learning, and LLM. I obtained my doctoral degree from the Big Data College at the University of Science and Technology of China in June 2024. Currently, I am an assistant professor at the Suzhou Institute for Advanced Study at the University of Science and Technology of China.\nMy research interests include topics in\ntime series\n,\nspatio-temporal data mining\n,\ngraph learning\n, and\ncontinual learning\n. Most recently, I am interested in the following topics:\n📢: 欢迎对机器学习与人工智能感兴趣、具备编程基础且自我驱动力强的同学加入！ 有意者请将个人简历、成绩单及简要自我介绍发送至邮箱：wbw2024@ustc.edu.cn。\n🎉 News\n2026.01\n: Two papers are accepted by\nICLR 2026!\n2025.12\n: One paper is accepted by\nACM WWW 2026!\n2025.12\n: One paper is accepted by\nAAAI 2026!\n2025.10\n: 恭喜王冠军、黄盛、马佳明获得国奖奖学金！\n2025.10\n: Three papers are accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025!\n2025.08\n: One paper is accepted by\nACM MM!\n2025.06\n: One paper is accepted by\nIEEE TMC!\n2025.05\n: One paper is accepted by\nICML 2025!\n2025.04\n: One paper is accepted by\nIJCAI 2025!\n2025.02\n: One paper is accepted by\nVLDB 2025!\n📝 Publications\nConference Papers (#:Corresponding Author)\nOne for Two: A Unified Framework for Imbalanced Graph Classification via Dynamic Balanced Prototype.\nGuanjun Wang,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Jiaming Ma, Zhengyang Zhou, Pengkun Wang, Xu Wang, Yang Wang.\nIn: The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR 2026, CCF-A\n).\nPHAT: Modeling Period Heterogeneity for Multivariate Time Series Forecasting.\nJiaming Ma, Qihe Huang, Guanjun Wang, Haofeng Ma, Sheng Huang, Zhengyang Zhou, Pengkun Wang, Xu Wang,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Yang Wang.\nIn: The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR 2026, CCF-A\n).\nWe Need a More Robust Classifier: Dual Causal Learning Empowers Domain-Incremental Time Series Classification.\nZhipeng Liu, Peibo Duan, Xuan Tang, Haodong Jing, Mingyang Geng, Yongsheng Huang, Jialu Xu, Bin Zhang,\nBinwu Wang#\n.\nIn: The Fourteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nWWW 2026, CCF-A\n).\nDisms-ts: Eliminating redundant multi-scale features for time series classification.\nZhipeng Liu, Peibo Duan,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Xuan Tang, Qi Chu, Changsheng Zhang, Yongsheng Huang, Bin Zhang.\nIn: Proceedings of the 33rd ACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nACM MM, CCF-A\n).\nLess but more: Linear adaptive graph learning empowering spatiotemporal forecasting.\nJiaming Ma,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Xu Wang, Yang Wang.\nIn: The Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS 2025, CCF-A\n).\nMofo: Empowering long-term time series forecasting with periodic pattern modeling.\nJiaming Ma,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Xu Wang, Yang Wang.\nIn: International Conference on Machine Learning (\nNeurIPS 2025, CCF-A\n).\nRobust Spatio-Temporal Centralized Interaction for OOD Learning.\nJiaming Ma,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Xu Wang, Yang Wang.\nIn: International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML 2025, CCF-A\n).\nBiST: A Lightweight and Efficient Bi-directional Model for Spatiotemporal Prediction.\nJiaming Ma,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Xu Wang, Yang Wang .\nIn: International Conference on Very Large Data Bases (\nVLDB 2025, CCF-A\n).\nLLM-AutoDA: Large Language Model-Driven Automatic Data Augmentation for Long-tailed Problems.\nPengkun Wang, Zhe Zhao, Haibin Wen, Fanfu Wang,\nBinwu Wang\n, Qingfu Zhang, Yang Wang.\nIn: The ‌Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems‌ (\nNeurIPS 2024, CCF-A\n).\nSTONE: A Spatio-temporal OOD Learning Framework Kills Both Spatial and Temporal Shifts.\nBinwu Wang\n, Jiaming Zhou, Pengkun Wang, Xu Wang, Yudong Zhang, Zhengyang Zhou, Yang Wang.\nIn: ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (\nKDD 2024, CCF-A\n).\nMake Bricks With A Little Straw: Large-Scale Spatio-Temporal Graph Learning with Restricted GPU-Memory Capacity.\nBinwu Wang\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Zhe Zhao, Wei Xu, Yang Wang.\nIn: International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nIJCAI 2024, CCF-A\n).\nTowards Dynamic Spatial-Temporal Graph Learning: A Decoupled Perspective.\nBinwu Wang\n, Pengkun Wang, Yudong Zhang, Zhengyang Zhou, Xu Wang, Lei Bai, Yang Wang.\nIn: Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI 2024, CCF-A\n).\nKill Two Birds with One Stone: Rethinking Data Augmentation for Deep Long-tailed Learning\n.\nBinwu Wang\n, Pengkun Wang, Wei Xu, Xu Wang, Yudong Zhang, Kun Wang.\nIn: International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR 2024, CCF-A\n).\nWhen Imbalance Meets Imbalance: Structure-driven Learning for Imbalanced Graph Classification\n.\nWei Xu , Pengkun Wang , Zhe Zhao ,\nBinwu Wang\n, Xu Wang , Yang Wang\nIn: Proceedings of the ACM on Web Conference (\nWWW 2024, CCF-A\n).\nCrossGNN: Confronting Noisy Multivariate Time Series Via Cross Interaction Refinement\n.\nQihe Huang, Lei Shen, Ruixin Zhang, Shouhong Ding,\nBinwu Wang\n, Zhengyang Zhou, Yang Wang\nIn: Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems Datasets and Benchmarks  (\nNeurIPS 2023, CCF-A\n).\nPattern Expansion and Consolidation on Evolving Graphs for Continual Traffic Prediction\n.\nBinwu Wang\n, Yudong Zhang , Xu Wang , Pengkun Wang , Zhengyang Zhou , Lei Bai , Yang Wang\nIn: ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (\nKDD 2023, CCF-A\n).\nJournal Papers\nMobiMixer: A Multi-scale Spatiotemporal Mixing Model for Mobile Traffic Prediction.\nJiaming Ma,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Pengkun Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Yudong Zhang, Xu Wang, Yang Wang.\nIn: IEEE Transactionson Mobile Computing (\nIEEE TMC, SQI-1, CCF-A\n).\nModeling Spatio-Temporal Mobility across Data Silos via Personalized Federated Learning.\nYudong Zhang, Xu Wang, Pengkun Wang, Binwu Wang,\nBinwu Wang\n, Yang Wang.\nIn: Advanced Engineering Informatics (\nAEI 2025, SQI-1,CCF-B\n).\nMeta Koopman Decomposition for Time Series Forecasting Under Temporal Distribution Shifts.\nYudong Zhang, Xu Wang, Zhaoyang Sun, Pengkun Wang,\nBinwu Wang\n, Limin Li, Yang Wang.\nIn: IEEE Transactionson Mobile Computing (\nIEEE TMC, SQI-1, CCF-A\n).\nAdaptive and Interactive Multi-Level Spatio-Temporal Network for Traffic Forecasting\n.\nYudong Zhang, Pengkun Wang, Xu Wang,\nBinwu Wang\n, Lei Bai, Yang Wang\nIn:  IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems (\nIEEE TITS, SQI-1区\n), in press, 2024.\nCondition-Guided Urban Traffic Co-Prediction With Multiple Sparse Surveillance Data\n.\nBinwu Wang\n, Pengkun Wang, Yudong Zhang, Xu Wang, Zhengyang Zhou, Yang Wang\nIn:  IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology  (\nIEEE TVT, SQI-2区\n), in press, 2024.\nFace Anti-spoofing with Unknown Attacks: A Comprehensive Feature Extraction and Representation Perspective\n.\nLimin Li,\nBinwu Wang#\n, Xu Wang, Peng-Kun Wang, Yu-Dong Zhang, Yang Wang\nIn:  Journal of Computer Science and Technology (\nJCST，CCF-B\n), in press, 2024.\nKnowledge Expansion and Consolidation for Continual Traffic Prediction With Expanding Graphs\n.\nBinwu Wang\n, Yudong Zhang, Jiahao Shi, Pengkun Wang, Xu Wang, Lei Bai, Yang Wang\nIn:  IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems (\nIEEE TITS, SQI-1区\n), in press, 2023.\n🤝 Activities\nConference Committee\nProgram Committee Member, WWW 2026.\nProgram Committee Member, NeurIPS 2025.\nProgram Committee Member, AAAI 2026.\nProgram Committee Member, ICML 2025.\nJournal Committee\nReviewer for Nature Communications, IEEE TKDE, IEEE TITS, IEEE TVT, etc."
