    "homepage_text": "Wu | General Internal Medicine\nSkip to main content\nPress Spacebar to Enter/Exit Menu\nMENU\nSearch\nSearch\nMake a Gift\nQuick Links\nWorkday\nUW HR Resources\nDOM Intranet\nGIM Intranet\nSocials\nTwitter\nInstagram\nFacebook\nYouTube\nThis is unpublished\nChenwei\nWu\nMD\nwuchen@uw.edu\nFaculty\nHospitalist\nPinned\nAcademic\nClinical Assistant Professor, Medicine\nProfessional\nGME Director, Housestaff Quality & Safety Committee\nEducation & Training\nMD, Duke University, Durham, NC (2008–2012)\nInternal Medicine Internship and Residency, University of Washington, Seattle, WA (2012–2015)\nChief Residency in Internal Medicine, University of Washington, Seattle, WA (2015–2016)\nHonors\nDuke University School of Medicine William G. Anlyan Senior Scholarship (2011)\nAlpha Omega Alpha (2011)\nHoward Hughes Medical Institute Medical Research Fellows Scholarship (2010)\npublication highlights\nWu C\n, Moreira DM, Gerber L, Rittmaster RS, Andriole GL, Freedland SJ.\nDiabetes and prostate cancer risk in the REDUCE trial\n. Prostate Cancer Prostatic Dis. 2011;14(4):326–31.\nWu C\n, Aronson WJ, Terris MK, et al.\nDiabetes predicts metastasis after radical prostatectomy, but only in obese men: Results from the SEARCH database\n. BJU Int. 2013;111(8):E310–8.\nLloyd JC, Masko EM,\nWu C\n, et al. Decreased mitochondrial and insulin pathway gene expression signal in prostate cancer xenograft mouse model with varying dietary fat sources. Prostate Cancer Prostatic Dis. 2013;16(4):285–91."
