    "homepage_text": "About me Ning Liu’s Homepage\nNing Liu (刘宁)\nWelcome to my homepage!\nFollow\nBeijing\nPeking University\nEmail\nResearchGate\nAbout me\nI am currently a Postdoctoral Researcher at the\nBeijing International Center for Mathematical Research\n,\nPeking University\n, where I work in collaboration with Prof.\nXiaobo Liu\n.\nI obtained my Ph.D. degree in Mathematics from the\nSchool of Mathematics\nat\nSouth China University of Technology\nin June 2024, where I was advised by Prof.\nNaihuan Jing\n. During my PhD studies, I conducted research as a visiting scholar at the\nFakultät für Mathematik\nof the\nUniversität Wien\n, under the joint supervision of Prof.\nChristian Krattenthaler\nPrior to my graduate studies, I completed my Bachelor’s degree in Mathematics at the\nSchool of Mathematics and Statistics\n,\nNortheast Normal University\n, graduating in June 2018.\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests lie in Algebraic Combinatorics and Representation Theory. In addition, I am also interested in Vertex Operators of Symmetric Functions.\nPublications\nIrreducible characters and bitrace for the q-rook monoid, Comm. Algebra 54 (2026), no. 4, 1389–1406. (with N. Jing and Y. Wu)\narXiv:2312.13681\nPlethystic Murnaghan-Nakayama rule via vertex operators, J. Algebraic Combin. 62 (2025), no. 4, Paper No. 57. (with Y. Cao and N. Jing)\narXiv:2212.08412\nA multiparametric Murnaghan-Nakayama rule for Macdonald polynomials, J. Combin. Theory Ser. A. 207 (2024), Paper No. 105920. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2310.15730\nA spin analog of the plethystic Murnaghan-Nakayama rule. Ann. Comb. 28 (2024), no. 2, 655–679. (with Y. Cao and N. Jing)\narXiv:2312.13675\nMurnaghan-Nakayama rule and spin bitrace for the Hecke-Clifford algebra. Int. Math. Res. Not. IMRN (2023), no. 19, 17060–17099. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2303.14459\nSpin Kostka polynomials and vertex operators. Pacific J. Math. 325 (2023), no. 1, 127–146. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2303.10664\nQ-Kostka polynomials and spin Green polynomials. Monatsh. Math. 201 (2023), no. 1, 109–125. (with A. Jiang and N. Jing)\narXiv:2304.07439\nOn irreducible characters of the Iwahori-Hecke algebra in type A. J. Algebra 598 (2022), 24–47. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2104.06067\nThe Green polynomials via vertex operators. J. Pure Appl. Algebra 226 (2022), 107032. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2104.04411\nCorrigendum\nPreprints\nDual Murnaghan-Nakayama rule for Hecke algebras in type A. (with N. Jing and Y. Wu)\narXiv:2503.12299\nMurnaghan-Nakayama rule for the cyclotomic Hecke algebra and applications. (with N. Jing)\narXiv:2504.18825\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
