    "homepage_text": "Zhaofei Yu\nZhaofei Yu\nAssistant Professor\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\nNational Engineering Research Center of Visual Technology\nPeking University\nBeijing, China. 100871.\nOffice: Room 2728, Science 2 Buildings\nEmail: yuzf12 αt pku dοt edu dοt cn\nBiography\nI'm an Assistant Professor of the\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence\nat\nPeking University\n, and I am heading the Brain-inspired Vision Lab.  I received the B.S. degree from the Hong Shen Honors School, College of Optoelectronic Engineering, Chongqing University, China, in 2012 and the Ph.D. degree from the Automation Department, Tsinghua University, China, in 2017. From Sep. 2015 to Sep. 2016, I visited Prof.\nWolfgang Maass\n's group at\nGraz University of Technology\nas a visiting student.\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests cover biological and computer vision, neuromorphic computation, and computational neuroscience. I am interested in learning and inference of spiking neural networks, and vision information processing based on neuromorphic visual sensors. I am also interested in extracting meaningful information embedded in high-dimensional neuroscience data and explaining how the visual system implements encoding and decoding.\nOpening\nWe are looking for highly motivated students to join our group. Our group has opening positions for Ph.D. and Undergraduate Internship. If you are interested in researching on brain-like computing, please send me an email with your CV.\nWe are hiring highly motivated postdocs to join our group through the Boya Postdoctoral Fellowship at Peking University. Please send an email with your CV and Research Statement.\nNews\n[2023.03] One paper was accepted by CVPR 2023. Congratulations to Tong Bu!\n[2023.01] Two papers were accepted by ICLR 2023. Congratulations to Yanqi and Zecheng!\n[2023.01] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence. Congratulations to Yajing!\n[2022.11] Three papers were accepted by AAAI 2023. Congratulations to Zecheng, Jiyuan, Shanshan, and Shiyan!\n[2022.10] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Image Processing. Congratulations to Yajing!\n[2022.09] Congratulate Shanshan Jia for the National Scholarship!\n[2022.09] Four papers were accepted by NeurIPS 2022. Congratulations to Jianhao, Yaoyu, Chaoteng, Rui Zhao, Tong Bu, and Wei Fang!\n[2022.07] One paper was accepted by ECCV 2022. Congratulations to Jiyuan!\n[2022.07] Congratulate Tong Bu for \"Top Ten Best Undergraduate Thesis\"!\n[2022.05] One paper was accepted by ICML 2022. Congratulations to Yanqi!\n[2022.04] One paper was accepted by IJCAI 2022. Congratulations to Shiyan!\n[2022.01] One paper was accepted by ICASSP 2022. Congratulations to Junwei!\n[2022.01] One paper was accepted by ICLR 2022. Congratulations to Bu Tong!\n[2022.01] One paper on Vidar camera was accepted by Engineering!\n[2021.12] One paper was accepted by Neural Computation. Congratulations to Yijun!\n[2021.12] One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Computational Imaging. Congratulations to Zhao Jing!\n[2021.12] One paper on the dimensionality reduction of neural spikes was accepted by Cell Patterns! Congratulations to Shanshan!\n[2021.12] Two papers were accepted by AAAI 2022. Congratulations to Ding Gang and Bu Tong!\n[2021.11] One paper on dissecting dynamical circuits of the brain was accepted by PLOS Computational Biology! Congratulations to Shanshan!\n[2021.09] One paper on learning of SNNs was accepted by NeurIPS 2021. Congratulations to Fang Wei!\n[2021.08] One paper on visual neural coding was accepted by Cell patterns! Congratulations to Yajing!\n[2021.07] Two papers were accepted by ICCV 2021. Congratulations to Fang Wei and Zhao Jing!\n[2021.04] Two papers were accepted by IJCAI 2021. Congratulations to Jianhao and Yanqi!\n[2021.03] One paper was accepted by CVPR 2021. Congratulations to Yajing!\n[2021.01] One papers was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics. Congratulations to Shanshan!\nPublications\nIn press\n2023\nCapture the Moment: High-speed Imaging with Spiking Cameras through Short-term Plasticity\nYajing Zheng, Lingxiao Zheng,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Tiejun Huang, Song Wang\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n[\npdf\n]\n1000× Faster Camera and Machine Vision with Ordinary Devices\nTiejun Huang, Yajing Zheng,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Rui Chen, Yuan Li, Ruiqin Xiong, Lei Ma, Junwei Zhao, Siwei Dong, Lin Zhu,\nJianing Li, Shanshan Jia, Yihua Fu, Boxin Shi, Si Wu, and Yonghong Tian\nEngineering\n[pdf]\nSpike-Based Motion Estimation for Object Tracking Through Bio-Inspired Unsupervised Learning\nYajing Zheng,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Song Wang, Tiejun Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n[\npdf\n]\nAsynchronous Spatiotemporal Spike Metric for Event Cameras\nJianing Li, Yihua Fu, Siwei Dong,\nZhaofei Yu\n, Tiejun Huang, Yonghong Tian*\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n[pdf]\nDeep Spike Learning with Local Classifiers\nChenxiang Ma, Rui Yan,\nZhaofei Yu\n, Qiang Yu\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n[pdf]\nSpike Calibration: Bridging the Gap between ANNs and SNNs in ANN-SNN Conversion\nZecheng Hao, Jianhao Ding, Tong Bu, Tiejun Huang,\nZhaofei Yu*\nICLR\n[pdf]\nA Unified Framework of Soft Threshold Pruning\nYanqi Chen,\nZhaofei Yu\n, Wei Fang, Zhengyu Ma, Xiawu Zheng, Yonghong Tian*\nICLR\n[pdf]\nReducing ANN-SNN Conversion Error through Residual Membrane Potential\nZecheng Hao, Tong Bu, Jianhao Ding, Tiejun Huang,\nZhaofei Yu*\nAAAI\n(oral) [pdf]\nLearning Temporal-ordered Representation for Spike Streams Based on Discrete Wavelet Transforms\nJiyuan Zhang†, Shanshan Jia†,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Tiejun Huang\nAAAI\n[pdf]\nSelf-Supervised Joint Dynamic Scene Reconstruction and Optical Flow Estimation for Spiking Camera\nShiyan Chen,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Tiejun Huang\nAAAI\n[pdf]\n2022\nZooming in on the Brain via Data Science\nShanshan Jia,\nZhaofei Yu*\nCell Patterns\n[\npdf\n]\nRepresenting the Dynamics of High-Dimensional Data with Non-Redundant Wavelets\nShanshan Jia, Xingyi Li, Tiejun Huang, Jian K. Liu*,\nZhaofei Yu*\nCell Patterns\n[\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nDecoding Pixel-Level Image Features from Two-Photon Calcium Signals of Macaque Visual Cortex\nYijun Zhang, Tong Bu, Jiyuan Zhang, Shiming Tang,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Jian K. Liu, Tiejun Huang\nNeural Computation\n[\npdf\n]\nRevealing Fine Structures of the Retinal Receptive Field by Deep Learning Networks\nQi Yan†, Yajing Zheng†, Shanshan Jia,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Feng Chen, Yonghong Tian, Tiejun Huang, Jian K. Liu*\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n[\npdf\n]\nReconstructing Clear Image for High-Speed Motion Scene With a Retina-Inspired Spike Camera\nJing Zhao, Ruiqin Xiong*, Jiyu Xie, Boxin Shi,\nZhaofei Yu\n, Wen Gao, Tiejun Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Computational Imaging\n[\npdf\n]\nNeural System Identification with Spike-Triggered Non-Negative Matrix Factorization\nShanshan Jia,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Arno Onken, Yonghong Tian, Tiejun Huang, Jian K. Liu*\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics\n[\npdf\n]\nA Probabilistic Approach for Cooperative Computation Offloading in MEC-Assisted Vehicular Networks\nPenglin Dai, Kaiwen Hu, Xiao Wu, Huanlai Xing, Fei Teng,\nZhaofei Yu\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems\n[\npdf\n]\nNeural Decoding of Visual Information Across Different Neural Recording Modalities and Approaches\nYijun Zhang,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Jian K. Liu, Tiejun Huang\nMachine Intelligence Research\n[\npdf\n]\nSNN-RAT: Robustness-enhanced Spiking Neural Network through Regularized Adversarial\nJianhao Ding, Tong Bu,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Jian K. Liu, Tiejun Huang\nNeurIPS\n(Spotlight) [\npdf\n] [\ncode\n]\nTraining Spiking Neural Networks with Event-driven Backpropagation\nYaoyu Zhu,\nZhaofei Yu*\n, Wei Fang, Xiaodong Xie, Tiejun Huang, Timothée Masquelier\nNeurIPS\n(Spotlight) [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nTemporal Effective Batch Normalization in Spiking Neural Networks\nChaoteng Duan†, Jianhao Ding†, Shiyan Chen