  "deep_homepage::Jun Chen::https://junchen14.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://junchen14.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/github.com",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jun-chen-54a090198/",
    "homepage_text": "Jun Chen\nJun Chen\nI am currently a Research Scientist at Meta AI. I earned my PhD from King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST), where I was fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Mohamed Elhoseiny\n. My research focuses on multimodal learning and developing scalable, efficient models for vision-language understanding. My representative works include\nVisualGPT\n,\nMiniGPT-4\n, and\nMiniGPT-v2\n, among others.\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nTwitter\nNews\n2025-02\nI joined Meta AI as a Research Scientist\n2024-5\nStarted Postdoc at KAUST and very looooong visa waiting\n2023-12\nHad a wonderful internship in Meta (Sunnyvale)\n2023-11\nI succeeded my PhD Defence\n2023-10\nOur paper MiniGPT-v2 is released\n2023-07\nOur paper (ZeroSeg) is selected by ICCV 2023\n2023-05\nMiniGPT-4 team was interviewed by\nTheSequence\nand\nMiT Technology Review\n2023-04\nMiniGPT-4 is repored by\n机器之心\nand\n量子位\n2023-04\nWe released MiniGPT-4 and received github\n10k stars in 3 days\n!\n2023-04\nWe released Video ChatCaptioner\n2023-03\nWe released ChatCaptioner\n2023-02\nOne paper (MammalNet) is selected by CVPR 2023\n2022-08\nHad a wonderful internship in Meta (Menlo Park)\n2022-02\nTwo papers (VisualGPT and RelTransformer) are selected by CVPR 2022\n2020-02\nStart my PhD journey with Mohamed Elhoseiny\n2018-08\nStart my Master jounery in King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST).\nResearch"
  },
