    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "About me - Xiaoguang Wang (王晓光)’s Home Page\nXiaoguang Wang\nA security and system researcher\nFollow\nCDRLC (4454), Chicago, IL\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nAbout me\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat the\nUniversity of Illinois Chicago (UIC)\n. My research focuses on\nsystems and software security\n, with an emphasis on\nsystems support for emerging computer architectures\nand\nsecure software systems design\n. Recently, I have been exploring innovative ways to address\nsystems and security challenges\nusing\nlarge language models (LLMs)\n. My past projects have spanned areas such as\nvirtualization, operating system kernels, and compilers\n, aimed at building more secure and efficient systems.\nI am seeking one\nhighly motivated Ph.D. student\ninterested in\ncomputer systems and security\nto join our research group.\nIf you’re interested, please email me with the subject line: “Prospective Student - [Your Name],” and include your CV and transcript.\nLearn more about the Ph.D. application process here.\nOccasionally, I offer\nfunded research opportunities\nfor UIC master’s and undergraduate students. However, I typically prefer working with students I have taught in my classes. If you’re interested, consider enrolling in one of my courses to start a conversation!\nTeaching\nCS 461: Operating Systems Design and Implementation:\nSpring 2026\n,\nFall 2025\nCS 487: Building Secure Computer Systems:\nFall 2024\n, 2023\nCS 594/561: Adv. Linux Kernel Programming:\nSpring 2025\n, 2024\nNews\n[03/2026] Our paper on enclave offloading for heterogeneous machines has been conditionally accepted at\nACM/IFIP Middleware’26\n!\n[03/2026] Invited to serve as a PC member for\nSYSTOR’26\n,\nPLOS’26\n. Please consider submitting your latest work!\n[03/2026] Our position paper on agentic OS scheduling using policy-level multi-variant execution has been accepted at the\nAgentic OS workshop\n, co-located with ASPLOS’26!\n[08/2025] Welcome Luyao, Chalmers, and Kenan to our group as graduate research assistants!\n[07/2025] Invited to serve as a PC member for PLOS’25.\n[05/2025] Congrats to Edoardo and Robert on successfully defending their MS thesis and project—best wishes ahead!\n[02/2025] Invited to serve as a PC member for SYSTOR’25, ASPLOS’26.\n[11/2024] Our group welcomes Robert David Hernandez, Lily Leith, Edoardo Carlotto, and Edoardo D’Alessio as graduate research assistants!\n[06/2024] We received a gift from\nGoogle\nto improve software security with LLMs. Thanks, Google!\n[04/2024] Our paper on rewriting process states for migrating processes across computer architecture boundaries has been accepted at\nIEEE ICDCS’24\n!\n[03/2024] Our paper on optimizing\nmulti-variant execution\nhas been accepted at\nACM/IFIP Middleware’24\n!\n[09/2023] Our paper on dynamic software customization has been accepted at\nACM/IFIP Middleware’23\n!\n[06/2023] Our work on Linux eBPF fuzzing has been accepted at\nAPSys’23\n!\n[04/2023] I will join the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nUIC\nin Fall 2023!\n… …\nA list of recent\npublications\n.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nXiaoguang Wang (王晓光)'s Home Page\nXiaoguang Wang\nA security and system researcher\nFollow\nCDRLC (4454), Chicago, IL\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Haonan Yuan::https://hnyu.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://hnyu.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/hnyu",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/haonan-yu-9a052845/",
    "homepage_text": "Haonan's page\nHaonan Yu\nGoogle scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nBlog\n/\nLinkedIn\nI am a research scientist at\nSkild AI\n.\t  \n    Previously, I worked at\nHorizon Robotics\n,\nFacebook AI Research\n, \n    and\nBaidu Research\non learning-based robotics and embodied AI.\nI love writing code and building things. I am a co-author and an active maintainer of\nALF\n, an RL framework emphasizing on the flexibility and easiness of implementing\n    a complex RL system involving many different algorithm components.\nMy long-term career goal is to build a generalist robot with a wide range of skills to assist\n      people with tedious daily tasks. By doing so, I aim to free up more time for humans to focus on creative pursuits—such as writing, drawing,\n      and imagining—activities that truly define our humanity.\nEducation\nPh.D. of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), Purdue University\nBachelor of Computer Science (CS), Peking University\nSelected publications\nSoftwares\nALF\n- Agent Learning Framework\n\t  (ALF) is a PyTorch reinforcement learning framework emphasizing on the flexibility\n\t  and easiness of implementing complex algorithms involving many different\n\t  components.\nTAAC\n- Temporally abstract actor-critic\n    algorithm for efficient continuous control.\nXWorld\n- A simulator\n\t  package for RL research with language task support.\nFLARE\n- A reinforcement learning framework for\n    training embodied agents with PyTorch.\nHobbies\nI like playing video games, especially ARPG. So far my favorite games are\n        souls-like, by\nFromSoftware\n."
  },
