    "homepage_text": "Tongfei Chen\nTongfei Chen\n陈桐飞\nI am a research scientist at\nAugment Code\n. Before that, I was a senior researcher at\nMicrosoft Semantic Machines\n.\nI obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science at\nCenter for Language and Speech Processing\nat\nJohns Hopkins University\nunder advisor Prof.\nBenjamin Van Durme\n. Prior to Hopkins, I obtained my B.Sc. in Computer Science from\nPeking University\n.\nIn addition to natural languages, I'm also interested in programming languages: I design expressive, typesafe DSLs for various domain applications (e.g. deep learning).\nMy full CV can be found\nhere\n.\nstyle\nPublications\nMulti-field adaptive retrieval\nspotlight paper\nICLR 2025\nMillicent Li\nTongfei Chen\nBenjamin Van Durme\nPatrick Xia\nLearning to retrieve iteratively for in-context learning\noutstanding paper award\nEMNLP 2024\nYunmo Chen\nTongfei Chen\nHarsh Jhamtani\nPatrick Xia\nRichard Shin\nJason Eisner\nBenjamin Van Durme\nA unified view of evaluation metrics for structured prediction\nEMNLP 2023\nYunmo Chen*\nWill Gantt*\nTongfei Chen*\nAaron Steven White\nBenjamin Van Durme\nBenchCLAMP: A benchmark for evaluating language models on semantic parsing\nNeurIPS 2023 Data & Benchmarks\nSubhro Roy\nSam Thomson\nTongfei Chen\nRichard Shin\nAdam Pauls\nJason Eisner\nBenjamin Van Durme\nIterative document-level information extraction via imitation learning\noutstanding paper award\nEACL 2023\nYunmo Chen\nWilliam Gantt\nWeiwei Gu\nTongfei Chen\nAaron Steven White\nBenjamin Van Durme\nAn empirical study on finding spans\nEMNLP 2022\nWeiwei Gu\nBoyuan Zheng\nYunmo Chen\nTongfei Chen\nBenjamin Van Durme\nComplement lexical retrieval model with semantic residual embeddings\nECIR 2021\nLuyu Gao\nZhuyun Dai\nTongfei Chen\nZhen Fan\nBenjamin Van Durme\nJamie Callan\nLOME: Large Ontology Multilingual Extraction\nEACL 2021 Demo\nPatrick Xia*\nGuanghui Qin*\nSiddharth Vashishtha\nYunmo Chen\nTongfei Chen\nChandler May\nCraig Harman\nKyle Rawlins\nAaron Steven White\nBenjamin Van Durme\nJoint modeling of arguments for event understanding\nCODI@EMNLP 2020\nYunmo Chen\nTongfei Chen\nBenjamin Van Durme\nReading the Manual: Event extraction as definition comprehension\nSPNLP@EMNLP 2020\nYunmo Chen\nTongfei Chen\nSeth Ebner\nAaron Steven White\nBenjamin Van Durme\nHierarchical entity typing via multi-level learning to rank\nACL 2020\nTongfei Chen\nYunmo Chen\nBenjamin Van Durme\nUncertain natural language inference\nACL 2020\nTongfei Chen*\nZhengping Jiang*\nAdam Poliak\nKeisuke Sakaguchi\nBenjamin Van Durme\nEspresso\n: A fast end-to-end neural speech recognition toolkit\nASRU 2019\nYiming Wang\nTongfei Chen\nHainan Xu\nShuoyang Ding\nHang Lv\nYiwen Shao\nNanyun Peng\nLei Xie\nShinji Watanabe\nSanjeev Khudanpur\nAn exact No Free Lunch theorem for community detection\nCOMPLEX NETWORKS 2019\nArya D. McCarthy\nTongfei Chen\nSeth Ebner\nMetrics matter in community detection\nCOMPLEX NETWORKS 2019\nArya D. McCarthy\nTongfei Chen\nRachel Rudinger\nDavid W. Matula\nImproving long distance slot carryover in spoken dialogue systems\nbest paper award\nNLP4ConvAI@ACL 2019\nTongfei Chen\nChetan Naik\nHua He\nPushpendre Rastogi\nLambert Mathias\nLearning to rank for plausible plausibility\nACL 2019\nZhongyang Li\nTongfei Chen\nBenjamin Van Durme\nScaling multi-domain dialogue state tracking via query reformulation\nNAACL 2019 Industry\nPushpendre Rastogi\nArpit Gupta\nTongfei Chen\nLambert Mathias\nImproved lexically-constrained decoding for translation and monolingual rewriting\nNAACL 2019\nJ. Edward Hu\nHuda Khayrallah\nRyan Culkin\nPatrick Xia\nTongfei Chen\nMatt Post\nBenjamin Van Durme\nEnd-to-end anchored speech recognition\nICASSP 2019\nYiming Wang\nXing Fan\nI-Fan Chen\nYuzong Liu\nTongfei Chen\nBjörn Hoffmeister\nConfidence scoring using whitebox meta-models with linear classifier probes\nAISTATS 2019\n/ PMLR 89\nTongfei Chen\nJiří Navrátil\nVijay Iyengar\nKarthikeyan Shanmugam\nNIST TAC SM-KBP 2018 system description: JHU/U