    "homepage_text": "YuxinWen\nSearch\nYuxin Wen\nResearcher\nTencent\nBiography\nI am a Researcher on the Tencent Hunyuan team, specializing in the animation of 3D digital humans.\nI joined Tencent in 2022, initially with Tencent AI Lab. Previously, I earned my Ph.D. from the Gorilla Lab at South China University of Technology (SCUT), advised by Prof.\nKui Jia\n.\nMy research interests lie in computer vision, with a focus on non-Euclidean data, and machine learning.\nWe are seeking motivated research interns for multimodal research at Tencent Hunyuan in Shenzhen. If interested, please send your CV to\nrexwen@tencent.com\n.\nInterests\nComputer Vision\nMachine Learning\nEducation\nPhD in information and Communication Engineering, 2017-2022\nSouth China University of Technology\nBSc in Department of Information Engineering (Elite Class), 2013-2017\nSouth China University of Technology\nRecent Publications\nFor all publications please refer to\nall publications\n.\nStable-SCore: A stable registration-based framework for 3d shape correspondence\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2025\nHaolin Liu\n,\nXiaohang Zhan\n,\nZizheng Yan\n,\nZhongjin Luo\n,\nYuxin Wen\n,\nXiaoguang Han\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nProject\nSurface reconstruction from point clouds: A survey and a benchmark\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), Accepted, 2024\nHuangzhang Jin\n,\nYuxin Wen\n,\nZihao Wang\n,\nJinjuan Ren\n,\nKui Jia\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDataset\nProject\nDeep Optimized Priors for 3D Shape Modeling and Reconstruction\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2021\nMingyue Yang\n,\nYuxin Wen\n,\nWeikai Chen\n,\nYongwei Chen\n,\nKui Jia\nPDF\nCite\nProject\nvideo\nSign-Agnostic Implicit Learning of Surface Self-Similarities for Shape Modeling and Reconstruction from Raw Point Clouds\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2021\nWenbin Zhao\n,\nJiabao Lei\n,\nYuxin Wen\n,\nJianguo Zhang\n,\nKui Jia\nPDF\nCite\nGeometry-Aware Generation of Adversarial Point Clouds\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), Accepted, 2020\nYuxin Wen\n,\nJiehong Lin\n,\nKe Chen\n,\nC. L. Philip Chen\n,\nKui Jia\nPDF\nCite\nCode\nDOI\nSee all publications\nExperience\nResearcher\nTencent\nOct 2022 –\nPresent\nShenzhen\nConducting research in multimodal learning with a specialization in digital human animation.\nResearch Intern / Student Researcher\nDexForce\nNov 2021 –\nSep 2022\nShenzhen\nServes as an algorithm engineer for industrial defect detection.\nResearch Intern\nAlibaba DAMO Academy\nJun 2021 –\nOct 2021\nShenzhen\nServes for DAMO Academy Research Internship program, under the supervision by Prof.\nLei Zhang\n.\nResearch Assistant\nUniversity of Macau\nSep 2019 –\nJan 2020\nMacau\nServes for the FDCT Funded project with the State Key Laboratory of Internet of Things for Smart City.\nContact\nrexwen@tencent.com\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
