    "homepage_text": "Si-Hyung Lee\n      -  Seoul National University\nSeoul National University Home\nSearch content at Seoul National University\nView Scopus Profile\nSi-Hyung Lee\nAssociate Professor\nDermatology\nInstitute of Human-Environment Interface Biology\nSNUH Dermatology\nEmail\nshleedm\nsnu.ac\nkr\nh-index\n1006\nCitations\n16\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2012\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nEducation/Academic qualification\nPhD, Assembly of primary cilia and its role in proliferative skin disorders\n6 Feb 2012\n→\n19 Feb 2016\nAward Date: 19 Feb 2016\nMaster, Role of Epidermal Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor in Melanosome Transfer through Upregulation of Protease-Activated Receptor-2,\nYonsei University College of Medicine\n1 Mar 2009\n→\n28 Feb 2011\nAward Date: 28 Feb 2011\nBachelor,\nYonsei University College of Medicine\n2 Mar 2001\n→\n26 Feb 2007\nAward Date: 26 Feb 2007\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Si-Hyung Lee is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n6\nSimilar Profiles\nFibroblast\nMedicine and Dentistry\n100%\nClinical Feature\nMedicine and Dentistry\n71%\nLentigo\nMedicine and Dentistry\n63%\nLow Level Laser Therapy\nMedicine and Dentistry\n62%\nKeratinocyte\nMedicine and Dentistry\n52%\nDermatitis\nMedicine and Dentistry\n43%\nCongenital Melanocytic Nevus\nMedicine and Dentistry\n42%\nMohs Surgery\nMedicine and Dentistry\n42%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n44\nArticle\n11\nLetter\n2\nComment