    "github": "https://github.com/gaotianyu1350",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Tianyu Gao\nHome\nAbout\nPublications\nBlog\nTianyu Gao 高天宇\nResearch Scientist, Meta MSL TBD Lab\nIncoming Assistant Professor,\nDept of Computer Science and Engineering, UCSD\nPreviously\n, I was a member of technical staff at OpenAI. I completed my PhD at Princeton, advised by\nDanqi Chen\n.  I received my bachelor's degree from Tsinghua University, where I worked with\nZhiyuan Liu\n.\nFind me on\nX\n,\nGoogle Scholar\n, and\nGithub\n!\nEmail:\n[firstname]g@ucsd.edu\nResearch\nI am driven by the exciting potential of LLMs in transformative applications, such as their use as\ninformation-seeking tools\n. I develop principled techniques and evaluations for key components of this emerging paradigm:\nPowerful semantic search with embedding models (\nSimCSE\n,\nLitSearch\n)\nGenerations with citations for verifiability (\nALCE\n)\nLong-context language models (\nCEPE\n,\nHELMET\n,\nProLong\n,\nLongProc\n)\nInstruction following and reward hacking (\nLLMBar\n)\nTo enable these powerful applications in large-scale deployments, I also work on improving the\ncapabilities and efficiency\nof LLMs:\nEfficient fine-tuning methods that require only a few examples (\nLM-BFF\n) and memory footprint comparable to inference (\nMeZO\n)\nCost-effective approaches to build capable small models (\nSheared-Llama\n)\nTechniques to accelerate pre-training (\nhigh masking rate\n,\nMeCo\n)\nUnderstanding LLM capabilities (\nwhat ICL learns\n)\nPlease refer to\npublications\nfor the full list of my research papers.\nThis website is adapted from\nGregory Gunderson\n."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Jianmin Li::https://www.cs.tsinghua.edu.cn/csen/info/1154/3991.htm": {
    "homepage": "https://www.cs.tsinghua.edu.cn/csen/info/1154/3991.htm",
    "all_emails": [
      "lijianmin@mail.tsinghua.edu.cn"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nJianmin LI-Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University\nä¸­æ\nFaculty\nCAS & CAE members\nFull-time Faculty\nPositionï¼\nHome\n>\nFaculty\n>\nTeacher\n> \r\n    Content\nJianmin LI\nJianmin LI\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nJoined Department: 2003\nEmail:\nlijianmin@mail.tsinghua.edu.cn\nURL:\nhttp://csai.tsinghua.edu.cn/researchers/ch_researchers_lab/lijianmin.shtm\nPhone:+86-10-62795869\nFax:+86-10-62782266\nEducation background\nBachelor of Computer Science & Technology, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, 1995;\nPh.D. in Computer Science & Technology, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China, 2003.\nSocial service\nICCI: Financial Chair (2010).\nAreas of Research Interests/ Research Projects\nVisual Information Analysis and Retrieval\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China: Research on Semantic Modeling for Large Quantity Videos (2007-2009).\nResearch Status\nMy research focuses on visual information analysis and retrieval, whose purpose is to improve the precision and recall rate of image and video retrieval with the help of machine learning algorithms. Some of my research results have been published in journals such as IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology and conferences including ACM Multimedia.\nIn the area of visual information analysis, my contributions include a semantic modeling method which fuses rich features under boost framework, and a region annotation method using spatial context in the view of structural prediction. In visual information retrieval, I have investigated methods of extracting users' information requirements from queries and feedbacks. Besides, I have proposed new training and prediction methods for SVM, aiming to support real-time interactive video search. I have also developed a high-performance indexing algorithm for large-scale, high-dimensional databases.\nOur visual information analysis system has achieved best performance for several times in TRECVID, a benchmark for content based video retrieval. Furthermore, some of my proposed algorithms have been adopted in monitoring and management systems for video and audio programs over Internet, and have been deployed in several departments and provincial governments since 2007.\nHonors And Awards\nTechnology Innovation Award by State Administration of Radio Film and Television, Second Class-Monitoring and Management System for Audio-Visual Programs over Internet (2009).\nAcademic Achievement\n[1] D. Wang, Z. K. Wang, J. M. Li, B. Zhang, X. R. Li. Query representation by structured concept threads with application to interactive video retrieval,\nJOURNAL OF VISUAL COMMUNICATION AND IMAGE REPRESENTATION\n, vol. 20, no. 2, pp. 104-116, 2009\n[2] J. H. Yuan, H. Y. Wang, L. Xiao, W. J. Zheng, J. M. Li, F. Z. Lin, B. Zhang. A formal study of shot boundary detection,\nIEEE TRANSACTIONS ON CIRCUITS AND SYSTEMS FOR VIDEO TECHNOLOGY\n, vol. 17, no. 2, pp 168-186, 2007\n[3] J. H. Yuan, J. M. Li, B. Zhang. Exploiting spatial context constraints for automatic image region annotation,\nProceedings of the Fifteenth ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM 2007)\n, 2007, pp. 595-604\n[4] J. H. Yuan, J. M. Li, B. Zhang. Learning concepts from large scale imbalanced data sets using support cluster machines,\nProceedings of the 14th Annual ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM 2006)\n, 2006, pp. 441-450\n[5] J. M. Li, B. Zhang, F. Z. Lin. An Improvement Algorithm to Sequential Minimal Optimization.\nJournal of Software\n, vol. 14, no. 5, pp. 918-924, 2003\nNextï¼\nYixin JIANG\nLinks\nTsinghua University\nLectures\nJob Opportunity\nTeaching Lab\nDownload\nContact us\nMAIL Address: Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, BEIJING, P.R.China\nAdministration Office: +86-10-627-82258      FAX: +86-10-627-95462\nCopyright 2009-2024 Department of Computer Science and Technology  All Rights Reserved\nWechat account"
  },
