    "homepage_text": "Institute of Image Processing and Pattern Recognition, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nJAccount登录\nXiaolin Huang\nIntroduction\nMonograph\nPapers\nPatent\n◆\nResearchers\nFaculty\nPostgraduate\n◆\nProjects\nMachine Learning\nImage Processing and  Computer Vision\nBiomedical Image Analysis\n◆\nResearch\nJournal Paper\nConference Papers\nPatent\nAward\n◆\nData\n◆\nCourse\n◆\nNews\n◆\nCooperation\n◆\nRecruitment\n◆\nGraduates\n◆\nContact Us\n◆\nIntranet\n◆\n中文版\ncurrent location：\nHome\n>>\nResearchers\n>>\nFaculty\nXiaolin Huang\nProfessor\nInstitue of Image Processing and Pattern Recognition\nResearch Interests: Machine Learning, Optimization, and their Applications\nOffice:  SEIEE 2-429,  Dongchuan Road 800, Shanghai 200240, P.R. China\nemail: xiaolinhuang@sjtu.edu.cn\n中文版\nMy Google Scholar\nEducation\n2006-2012\nPh.D.  Tsinghua University\n2002-2006\nB.S.    Xi'an Jiao Tong University\nResearch Experience\n2024-\nFull Professor, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\n2016-2023\nAssociate Professor, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\n2015-2017\nHumboldt Fellow, Friedrich-Alexander Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg\n2015-2016\nFree Researcher, KU Leuven\n2012-2015\nPostdoctoral Researcher, KU Leuven\nProject\nPromoter for\n2024-2027\nNSFC (regular): Dyanmics Analysis and Reduction of Deep Nerual Networks: Theory, Algorithm, and Applications\n2023-2027\nState Key Program: Intelligent Analysis for Food and the Applications\n2022-2024\nShanghai Municipal Science and Technology Commission: Robustness of DNN based on Randomness and Low-dimensinoal Trajectory\n2021-2023\nTraining\nSpeed Up for Multi-media Search\n2021-2022\nMisdetection Detection and Optimization for BN (with Huawei)\n2020-2023\nNSFC (regfular): Multi-layer Kernel Learning: Theory, Algorithm, and Applications\n2019-2020\nRobustness Enhancement for Classification and Detection (with Huawei)\n2018-2021\nKey Technique of Intelligent Endoscopy\n2017\nNational Top Talent (Young Program)\n2017-2019\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China（NSFC, Young Program）：Robust one-bit compressive sensing and its applications\n2015-2017\nHumboldt Foundation:\nPiecewise linear technology in machine learning and applications on medical engineering\n2013-2015\nBilateral scientific cooperation-KU Leuven and Tsinghua University: BIL11/12T\nAcademic Activities\nSenior Member,\nIEEE\n(S’10-M’12 -SM'18)\nSenior Member, Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI)\nMember, Chinese Society of Image and Graphics (CSIG)\nEditor\n: Machine Learning\nArea Chair/Senior TPC member:\nICLR, CVPR, ICCV\n,\nAAAI, ESANN, etc.\nPeople\nProf.\nShuning Wang\n，Tsinghua University\nProf.\nJohan A.K. Suykens\n,  KU Leuven\nProf.\nAndreas Maier\n,\nUniversität Erlangen-Nürnberg\nProf.\nLi Li\n，Tsinghua University\nProf.\nLei Shi\n，Fudan University\nProf.\nYipeng Liu\n，University of Electronic Science and Technology of China\nProf.\nJun Xu\n，Harbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen)\nAssociate Prof.\nMing Yan\n，Chinese University of Hong Kong (Shenzhen)\nAssociate\nProf.\nYunlong Feng\n，State University of New York at Albany\nAssociate\nProf. Siamak Mehrkanoon,  Utrecht Universit\nAssociate\nProf. Chao Shang, Tsinghua University\nCopyright @2018 Institute of Image Processing and Pattern Recognition, Shanghai Jiao Tong University.\nAddress: 2-427 SEIEE Building, 800 Dong Chuan Rd, Shanghai, 200240, P.R.China"
