    "homepage_text": "首頁\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBin Sun's Homepage\nI am a mathematician and postdoctoral research associate of  Michigan State Unviersity. Starting from fall 2026, I will be a tenure-track assisant professor of Michigan State University. Befor, I was a postdoctoral researcher in the University of Oxford and the University of California, Riverside. I obtained my PhD in Vanderbilt University under the supervision of Prof. Denis Osin. I am interested in geometric group theory and L2-invariants. My research is supported by NSF research grant DMS-2507047.\nMy departmental address is\n619 Red Cedar Road\nC212 Wells Hall\nEast Lansing, MI, USA, 48824\nEmail\nsunsun335 \"at\" gmail\"dot\"com\nHoners and Awards\nKamil Duszenko Award, 2025\nNSF standard research grant DMS-2507047\nNSF Conferences and Workshops in the Mathematical Sciences, 2025\nAMS--Simons Travel Grant, 2023 -- 2025\nBjarni Jónsson Prize for Research (Vanderbilt University), 2019\nMy Curriculum Vitae\nVideo of my talks:\nAcylindrical group actions on hyperbolic metric spaces\nWreath-like product groups and rigidity of their von Neumann algebras\nSlides of my public talk to Polish high-school math Olympic students\nResearch Interest\nMy research interest mainly lies in the field of geometric group theory and its application to L2-invariants, and homological methods in group theory. Please see\nmy research statement\nfor more information. Below is a list of my papers.\n\"\nWreath-like products of groups and rigidity of their von Neumann algebras I: W*-sup\nerrigidity,\"\n(with\nIonut Chifan\n,\nAdrian Ioana\n,\nDenis Osin\n)\n,\nAnn. Math. (2), no. 3, 1261–1303\n, 2023.\npublished version\narXiv:2111.04708\n.\n\"Wreath-like products of groups and rigidity of their von Neumann algebras II: Outer automorphisms,\" (with\nIonut Chifan\n,\nAdrian Ioana\n,\nDenis Osin\n),\naccepted by Duke Math. J.\narXiv:2304.07457\n.\n“Agrarian and L2-Betti numbers of locally indicable groups, with a twist,” (with\nDawid Kielak\n),\nMath. Ann.\n1--53, 2024.\narXiv:2112.07394\n.\n“Cohomology of group theoretic Dehn fillings II,”\n(with\nNansen Petrosyan\n),\nAdv. Math. 437, 109421, 2024.\narXiv:1908.01290\n.\n“Invariant subalgebras of von Neumann algebras arising from negatively curved groups,” (with Ionut Chifan and Sayan Das), J. Funct. Anal., 285, no. 9, Page No. 110098, 2023\n.\npublished version\narxiv:2207.13775\n“A dynamical characterization of acylindrically hyperbolic groups,” Algebr. Geom. Topol., 19(4):1711–1745, 2019.\npublished version\narXiv:1707.04587\n“Cohomology of group theoretic Dehn fillings I: Cohen–Lyndon type theorems,” J. Algebra 542:277–307, 2020.\npublished version\narXiv:1809.08762\n\"Wreath-like products of groups and their von Neumann algebras III:\nEmbeddings\n,\" (with\nIonut Chifan\n,\nAdrian Ioana\n,\nDenis Osin\n),\narXiv:2402.19461\n.\n\"Small cancellation and outer automorphisms of Kazhdan groups acting on hyperbolic spaces,\"\n(with\nIonut Chifan\n,\nAdrian Ioana\n,\nDenis Osin\n), ac\ncepted by Algbr. Geom. Topol.,\narXiv:2304.07455\n.\n“On a Planar Six-neighbor Theorem and Its Application,” (with Longxiu Huang, Meiqi Wang, Tao Wang, Wen Zhang and Yusi Zhang), J. Math. Anal. Appl. 523, no. 2, Page no. 127020, 15.\n``L^2-Betti numbers of Dehn fillings,'' (with\nNansen Petrosyan\n), arXiv:2412.16090.\n``Dimensions of finitely generated simple groups and their subgroups,'' (with\nFrancesco Fournier-Facio\n), arXiv:2503.01987.\nTeaching\nSupervision\nO. Jones, ``Superlinear divergence and Morse quasi-geodesics in finitely generated groups,'' master's thesis, preprint, 2022.\nL. Issini, ``Divergence function of solvable groups,'' master's thesis, preprint, 2022.\nM. Penrose, ``Divergence in Thompson groups,'' master's thesis, preprint, 2022.\nB. Plimley, ``Superlinear divergence Of groups with deficiency at least two,'' master's thesis, preprint, 2022.\nAssessment\nTransfer viva for Ph.D. candidate Shanshan Hua, Unviersity of Oxford, Jan 2023\nTransfer viva for Ph.D. candidate Sam Fisher, Unviersity of Oxford, Jan 2022\nInstruction\nSpring 2020 Math 151C Advanced Calculus, University of California, Riverside\nSpring 2020 Math 46\nOrdinary Differential Equations\n, University of California, Riverside\nWinter 2020 Math 9A First-year Calculus\n, University of California, Riverside\nWinter 2020 Math 011 Introduction to Discrete Structures\n, University of California, Riverside\nFall 2019 Math 7A Calculus for Life Science\n, University of California, Riverside\nFall 2019 Math 46 Ordinary Differential Equations\n, University of California, Riverside\nTutorial\nTrinity\n2022,\nGroup Theory\n, University of Oxford, Exeter College\nHilary 2022, Linear Algebra II, University of Oxford, Exeter College\nMichaelmas\n202\n1\n, Linear Algebra I, University of Oxford, Exeter College\nMy Teaching Statement\nHobbies\nI play badminton, swimming,\nChinese Chess\n, and\nReversi\nin my spare time. Sometimes I play Chinese Chess and Reversi on\nPlayOk\n. I am also interested in\nWestern Chess\nand\nGo\n, but know almost nothing about these two games.\nIt would be great if you can play with me or teach me the board games 😊\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
