    "homepage_text": "Chenyu Zheng\nChenyu Zheng (郑晨宇)\nPh.D. Student\nGaoling School of Artificial Intelligence\nRenmin University of China\nEmail:  chenyu.zheng666[at]gmail[dot]com\nLinks:\n[Google Scholar]\n[Github]\n[知乎]\n[CV]\nAbout me\nI am a third-year Ph.D. student in the GSAI-ML Group, Renmin University of China, advised by Prof.\nChongxuan Li\nfortunately.\r\n        Currently, I am also a research intern at\nByteDance Seed\n.\r\n        Before that, I received my B.E. degree from the School of Computer Science, Wuhan University in 2023.\nResearch interests\nMy primary interest is machine learning (theory). Recently, I focus on the\noptimization and scalability in deep learning\n.\nSelected Papers\n[* indicates the equal contribution, # indicates the corresponding author]\nOptimization and Scalability (2023~)\nSpectral Condition for μP under Width-Depth Scaling\nChenyu Zheng\n, Rongzhen Wang, Xinyu Zhang, Chongxuan Li\nICLR Workshop on Deep Generative Models: Theory, Principle, and Efficacy\n(Oral)\n, 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Blog]\nScaling Diffusion Transformers Efficiently via μP\nChenyu Zheng\n, Xinyu Zhang, Rongzhen Wang, Wei Huang, Zhi Tian, Weilin Huang, Jun Zhu, Chongxuan Li\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[机器之心]\nOn Mesa-Optimization in Autoregressively Trained Transformers: Emergence and Capability\nChenyu Zheng\n, Wei Huang, Rongzhen Wang, Guoqiang Wu, Jun Zhu, Chongxuan Li\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slides]\n[Poster]\nMachine Learning Theory (2022~)\nToward Understanding Generative Data Augmentation\nChenyu Zheng\n, Guoqiang Wu, Chongxuan Li\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slides]\n[Blog]\n[Poster]\nRevisiting Discriminative vs. Generative Classifiers: Theory and Implications\nChenyu Zheng\n, Guoqiang Wu, Fan Bao, Yue Cao, Chongxuan Li, Jun Zhu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML)\n, 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slides]\n[Blog]\n[Poster]\nRemote Sensing (2021~2022)\nDomain Adaptive Land-Cover Classification via Local Consistency and Global Diversity\nAilong Ma,\nChenyu Zheng#\n, Junjue Wang, Yanfei Zhong\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing\n(TGRS)\n, 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nExperience\nResearch Intern\n,\nByteDance Seed\n, Beijing, China (2024.11 - Present)\nResearch Intern\n,\nRSIDEA Group\n,\nLIESMARS\n, Wuhan, China (2021.01 - 2022.08) \r\n                Advisors: Dr.\nJunjue Wang\n,\r\n                Prof.\nAilong Ma\n,\r\n                and Prof.\nYanfei Zhong\nSelected Honors\nYoung Scientists (Ph.D.) Fund\n, National Natural Science Foundation of China, 2025\nOutstanding Innovative Talents Cultivation Funded Programs\n, Renmin Univertity of China, 2024\nOutstanding Graduate & Bachelor Thesis Award\n, Wuhan University, 2023\nChina National Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education of China, 2020\nTutorials/Talks\nTutorial: A Brief Review of In-Context Learning Theory\n, 2024.05\n[Slides]\nTutorial: Classical Machine Learning Theory\n, 2023.06\n[Slides]\nAcademic Services\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nIEEE Transactions on Signal Processing (TSP)\nConference Reviewer\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS): 2024, 2025 (\nTop Reviewer\n)\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML): 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR): 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS): 2025, 2026\nConference Program Committee\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AAAI): 2026\nTeaching\nAdvanced Linear Algebra\n, TA, 2025 Fall\nProbability and Randomized Algorithms\n, TA, 2024 Fall\nMiscellaneous\nPlatform Sutra\nand meditation teach me a lot.\n[Platform Sutra viedo]\n[meditation viedo]\n© 2025.12 Chenyu Zheng"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Xiao Yang::https://www.xiaoyang.nyc/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.xiaoyang.nyc/",
