    "homepage_text": "Danqing Wang | 王丹青\nDanqing Wang\n王丹青\nHome\nPublications\nProjects\nAbout Me\nI am now pursuing my Ph.D. degree at LTI in Carnegie Mellon University (CMU), advised by\nProf. Lei Li\n. Before that I studies in UC Santa Barbara as a PhD student as a member of\nUCSB NLP Group\n. I was a full-time researcher of ByteDance AI Lab.\nI obtained my Master’s and Bachelor’s degrees in Computer Science from Fudan University and was a member of\nFudan NLP Group\n, advised by\nProf. Xipeng Qiu\nand\nProf. Xuanjing Huang\n.\nMy research focuses on\nStrategic Planning of Large Language Models\n, including LLM reasoning for complex code and math tasks, and multi-agent cooperation for games. I am also interested in\nAI for Science\n, such as AI-assisted Drug Discovery. You can find my resume / CV\nhere\n.\nEducation\n2024.1-Now: PhD in LTI, CMU\n2022.9-2023.12: PhD in Computer Science, UCSB (Transferred)\n2018.9-2021.1: Master in Computer Science, Fudan University\n2014.9-2018.6: Bachelor in Computer Science and Technology, Fudan University\nExperience\n2025.6-Now: Research Scientist Intern, Meta AI (FAIR)\nMentor:\nAnsong Ni\n,\nAsli Celikyilmaz\nTopic: Multi-agent Communication\n2024.3-2024.5: Research Scientist Intern, Alibaba (Team Qwen)\nMentor:\nJianxin Ma\nTopic: Large Language Model Reasoning\n2023.6-2024.1: Research Scientist Intern, Meta AI (FAIR)\nMentor:\nYuandong Tian\nTopic: Personalized Alignment in LLMs\n2020.4-2022.8: Researcher, ByteDance Research (AI Lab)\nMentor:\nJiaze Chen\n,\nHao Zhou\n,\nLei Li\nTopic: Text Generation, AI for Drug Design\nAwards\n2025 Amazon AI PhD Fellowship\nAcademic Service\nPC Member\nICML (2023-2025), NeurIPS (2023-2025), ICLR (2024-2026)\nACL (2020,2021), NAACL (2021,2024,2025), EMNLP (2020-2024)\nAAAI (2020-2024)\nKDD (2023,2024)\nNLPCC (2022)\nOrganizer\nSocal NLP Symposium\n2022\nTeaching Assistant\nCS190I Deep Learning\nWinter 2023\nCS165B Machine Learning\nSpring 2023\n\n---\n\nAbout | Danqing Wang\nDanqing Wang\n王丹青\nAbout\nNot Pure Poole\nis a simple, beautiful, and powerful Jekyll theme for blogs. It is built on\nPoole\nand\nPure\n.\nFor more information about Not Pure Poole, please browse the\nREADME\nfile.\n\n---\n\nAbout | Danqing Wang\nDanqing Wang\n王丹青\nAbout\nNot Pure Poole\nis a simple, beautiful, and powerful Jekyll theme for blogs. It is built on\nPoole\nand\nPure\n.\nFor more information about Not Pure Poole, please browse the\nREADME\nfile."
