    "homepage_text": "Zhenbang Wu  - CS Ph.D. Candidate @ UIUC\nZhenbang Wu\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\nPh.D. Candidate in Computer Science\nzw12@illinois.edu\nI am a Ph.D. candidate in Computer Science at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. I am fortunate to\nbe advised by\nProf. Jimeng Sun\n. Before this, I received dual bachelor’s degrees from Zhejiang\nUniversity and the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign.\n[Research]\nMy research focuses on developing foundation models—such as large language models and multimodal\nmodels—to interpret complex, multimodal, and longitudinal health data.\n[Application]\nI co-lead the development of PyHealth, an open-source toolkit for predictive modeling\nwith multimodal clinical data. It has received over 1K stars and 140K downloads on GitHub.\nSelected Publications & Preprints (\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nInstruction Tuning Large Language Models to Understand Electronic Health Records\nNeurIPS 2024 Datasets and Benchmarks Track (Spotlight)\nZhenbang Wu\n, Anant Dadu, Mike Nalls, Faraz Faghri\n†\n, Jimeng Sun\n†\n[\npaper\n]\nMultimodal Patient Representation Learning with Missing Modalities and Labels\nICLR 2024\nZhenbang Wu\n, Anant Dadu, Nicholas Tustison, Brian Avants, Mike Nalls, Jimeng Sun, Faraz Faghri\n[\npaper\n]\nAn Iterative Self-Learning Framework for Medical Domain Generalization\nNeurIPS 2023\nZhenbang Wu\n, Huaxiu Yao, David M Liebovitz, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nMedLink: De-Identified Patient Health Record Linkage\nKDD 2023\nZhenbang Wu\n, Cao Xiao, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nPyHealth: A Deep Learning Toolkit For Healthcare Applications\nKDD 2023 Hands-on Tutorial\nChaoqi Yang\n*\n,\nZhenbang Wu\n*\n, Patrick Jiang, Zhen Lin, Junyi Gao, Benjamin Danek, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nMedCLIP: Contrastive Learning from Unpaired Medical Images and Text\nEMNLP 2022\nZifeng Wang,\nZhenbang Wu\n, Dinesh Agarwal, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nAutoMap: Automatic Medical Code Mapping for Clinical Prediction Model Deployment\nECML-PKDD 2022\nZhenbang Wu\n, Cao Xiao, Lucas M Glass, David M Liebovitz, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nKnowledge-Driven New Drug Recommendation\nPreprint (short version presented in the NeurIPS 2022 Workshop on Meta-Learn)\nZhenbang Wu\n, Huaxiu Yao, Zhe Su, David M Liebovitz, Lucas M Glass, James Zou, Chelsea Finn, Jimeng Sun\n[\npaper\n]\nAn asterisk (*) denotes equal contribution, and a dagger (†) denotes co-corresponding authorship.\nSoftware\nPyHealth: A Deep Learning Toolkit For Healthcare Applications\n[\nGitHub\n]\nMedCLIP: Pretrained Vision-Language Model for Medical Images and Text\n[\nGitHub\n]\nInternship Experiences\nMeta\n, Burlingame, CA, USA\nResearch Scientist Intern, with  Dr. Sujeeth Bharadwaj & Dr. Pei Yin\nFoundation model for bio-signals\nMay 2024 - Aug 2024\nNational Institutes of Health\n, Bethesda, MD, USA\nMachine Learning Research Intern, with Dr. Faraz Faghri & Dr. Mike Nalls\nMultimodal learning\nMay 2023 - May 2024\nIQVIA\n, Remote, USA\nMachine Learning Research Intern, with Dr. Lucas M Glass\nPatient record linkage\nMay 2022 - Aug 2022"
  },
