  "deep_homepage::Yihong Sun::https://yihongsun.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://yihongsun.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "yihong@cs.cornell.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/YihongSun",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yihongsun/",
    "homepage_text": "Yihong Sun's Homepage\nYihong Sun\nCS Ph.D. candidate at Cornell University\nEmail\n/\nCV\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nTwitter\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\nContact\n: yihong-AT-cs-DOT-cornell-DOT-edu\nAbout Me\nI am a fourth-year CS PhD candidate at\nCornell University\n, advised by Prof.\nBharath Hariharan\n.\n                Previously, I obtained my Bachelor's degree from\nJohns Hopkins University\n, advised by Prof.\nAlan Yuille\n.\nMy work is supported by\nNSF GRFP\nand my research interests are computer vision and machine learning, especially in building vision systems for real-world and embodied applications.\nIf you would like to chat with me, please drop me an email!\nPublications\nshow selected\nshow all\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nTracking and Understanding Object Transformations\nYihong Sun\n,\nXinyu Yang\n,\nJennifer J. Sun\n,\nBharath Hariharan\nNeurIPS 2025\nPaper\nCode\nPoster\nData\nProject Page\nWe track objects through transformations while detecting and describing these state changes and resulting objects.\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nVideo Creation by Demonstration\nYihong Sun\n,\nHao Zhou\n,\nLiangzhe Yuan\n,\nJennifer J. Sun\n,\nYandong Li\n,\nXuhui Jia\n,\nHartwig Adam\n,\nBharath Hariharan\n,\nLong Zhao\n,\nTing Liu\narXiv 2024\nPaper\nProject Page\nWe generate videos that continue naturally from the context images while carrying out the action concepts from the demonstration videos.\nLearning 3D Perception from Others' Predictions\nJinsu Yoo\n,\nZhenyang Feng\n,\nTai-Yu Pan\n,\nYihong Sun\n,\nCheng Perng Phoo\n,\nXiangyu Chen\n,\nMark Campbell\n,\nKilian Q. Weinberger\n,\nBharath Hariharan\n,\nWei-Lun Chao\nICLR 2025\nPaper\nCode\nProject Page\nWe construct 3D object detectors by learning from the predictions of a nearby unit that is equipped with an accurate detector.\nMOD-UV: Learning Mobile Object Detectors from Unlabeled Videos\nYihong Sun\n,\nBharath Hariharan\nECCV 2024\nPaper\nCode\nPoster\nProject Page\nWe build an unsupervised mobile object detector from unlabeled videos only by leveraging independent motion information.\nDynamo-Depth: Fixing Unsupervised Depth Estimation for Dynamical Scenes\nYihong Sun\n,\nBharath Hariharan\nNeurIPS 2023\nPaper\nCode\nPoster\nProject Page\nWe improve unsupervised monocular depth estimation for dynamical scenes by modeling 3D independent flow and motion segmentation.\nAmodal Segmentation through Out-of-Task and Out-of-Distribution Generalization with a Bayesian Model\nYihong Sun\n,\nAdam Kortylewski\n,\nAlan Yuille\nCVPR 2022\nPaper\nCode\nPoster\nSupplementary\nWe estimate amodal segmentation using a Bayesian generative model trained from non-occluded images and box-level annotations only.\nRobust Instance Segmentation through Reasoning about Multi-Object Occlusion\nXiaoding Yuan\n,\nAdam Kortylewski\n,\nYihong Sun\n,\nAlan Yuille\nCVPR 2021\nPaper\nCode\nWe reason about multi-object self-occlusions by inspecting part-level activations of a Bayesian generative model.\nRobust Object Detection Under Occlusion With Context-Aware CompositionalNets\nAngtian Wang(*)\n,\nYihong Sun(*)\n,\nAdam Kortylewski\n,\nAlan Yuille\nCVPR 2020\n(*) denotes equal contribution\nPaper\nVideo\nData\nWe improve object detection under partial occlusion by regulating contextual bias and enhancing localization via compositional part voting.\nCompositional Convolutional Neural Networks: A Robust and Interpretable Model for Object Recognition under Occlusion\nAdam Kortylewski\n,\nQing Liu\n,\nAngtian Wang\n,\nYihong Sun\n,\nAlan Yuille\nIJCV 2020\nPaper\nCode\nWe propose CompositionalNets, interpretable deep architectures with innate robustness to partial occlusion, for image classification and object detection.\nExperience\nResearch Scientist Intern\nMay 2025 - Present\n- Mentors:\nJoon-Young Lee\n,\nSeoung Wug Oh\n,\nJiahui Huang\nStudent Researcher\nMay 2024 - Dec 2024\n- Hosts:\nTing Liu\n,\nLong Zhao\n,\nHao Zhou\n,\nLiangzhe Yuan\n,\nJennifer Sun\n.\n- Worked on\nVideo Creation by Demonstration\n.\nTeaching\nGraduate Teaching Assistant\nBowers CIS College of Computing and Information Science\n- CS4670/5670 Introduction to Computer Vision (\nSP23\n)\n- CS4787/5777 Principles of Large-Scale Machine Learning (\nFA22\n)\nUndergraduate Course Assistant\nDepartment of Computer Science\n- EN.601.783 Vision as Bayesian Inference (\nSP22\n)\n- AS.050.375/675 Probabilistic Models of the Visual Cortex (\nFA21\n,\nFA20\n)\n- EN.601.226 Data Structures (\nSP21\n,\nFA20\n,\nSP20\n)\n© 2024 Yihong Sun. Website template from Nicklas Hansen and Haian Jin."
  },
