    "homepage_text": "Gen Li\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nGen Li\nGen Li\nAcademic Positions\n2022 -- Present\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Biostatistics\n, University of Michigan\n2020 -- 2022\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Biostatistics\n, University of Michigan\n2015 -- 2020          Assistant Professor\nDepartment of Biostatistics\n, Columbia University\nEducation\n2010 -- 2015        Ph.D.\nDepartment of Statistics and Operations Research\n, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\n2006 -- 2010        B.S.          Department Mathematical Sciences, Beijing Normal University\nResearch Interests\nLow-Rank Models\nTensor Analysis\nNetwork Analysis\nLongitudinal Omics Analysis\nMicrobiome Data Analysis\nData Integration\nAwards\nJohn G. Searle Assistant Professorship\n, School of Public Health, University of Michigan, 2021\nSigma Xi Scientific Research Honor Society Inductee\n, 2019\nSanford Bolton Faculty Scholar\n, Department of Biostatistics, Columbia University, 2018\nCalderone Junior Faculty Award\n, Mailman School of Public Health, Columbia University, 2016\nENAR Distinguished Student Paper Award\n, IBS, 2014\nIMS Travel Award\n, 2014\nTeaching Award\n, Department of Statistics and Operations Research, UNC, 2014\nCambanis-Hoeffding-Nicholson Award\n, Department of Statistics and Operations Research, UNC, 2011\nCV (Updated in July, 2022)\nGoogle Scholar Site\nEmail: ligen AT umich.edu\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
