      "im_kai@hust.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/QwenLM",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Kaiyuan Gao\nKaiyuan Gao (高开元)\nPh.D. Student\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nJoint Ph.D. at Microsoft Research AI4Science\nEmail: im_kai[AT]hust[DOT]edu.cn\n[Google Scholar]\n[CV]\nBiography\nI am a final-year Ph.D. Candidate in a joint program between\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nand\nMicrosoft Research Asia\n, advised by\nProf. Kun He\nand\nDr. Tie-Yan Liu\n. Previously, I received my B.S. degree from the Department of\nAritificial Intelligence and Automation\nof Huazhong University of Science and Technology in July 2021.\nDuring my time at Microsoft Research, I worked on\n3D molecular structure modeling\nand molecule generation using diffusion and language models, with in-depth research on molecular docking. Currently, I am a core contributor to the\nQwen-Image\nproject, where I actively contribute to research on image editing and the development of\nvisual generation\nwithin the Qwen team.\nLooking for industrial research positions. Expect to graduate in June 2026.\nDrop me an email if you feel interested.\nSelected Publications\nVisual Generation:\nQwen-Image Technical Report\nChenfei Wu, Jiahao Li, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Kun Yan, Sheng-ming Yin, Shuai Bai, Xiao Xu, Yilei Chen, Yuxiang Chen, Zecheng Tang, Zekai Zhang, Zhengyi Wang, An Yang, Bowen Yu, Chen Cheng, Dayiheng Liu, Deqing Li, Hang Zhang, Hao Meng, Hu Wei, Jingyuan Ni, Kai Chen, Kuan Cao, Liang Peng, Lin Qu, Minggang Wu, Peng Wang, Shuting Yu, Tingkun Wen, Wensen Feng, Xiaoxiao Xu, Yi Wang, Yichang Zhang, Yongqiang Zhu, Yujia Wu, Yuxuan Cai, Zenan Liu\n[Code:\n4.2k Stars\n]\n[Text-to-Image Model:\n144k Downloads\n]\n[Image Edit Model:\n28k Downloads\n]\n3D Molecular Structure Modeling:\nFabind: Fast and accurate protein-ligand binding\nQizhi Pei*,\nKaiyuan Gao*\n, Lijun Wu, Jinhua Zhu, Yingce Xia, Shufang Xie, Tao Qin, Kun He, Tie-Yan Liu, Rui Yan\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS 2023)\n[Code:\n134 Stars\n]\n[Weights]\nFABind+: Enhancing Molecular Docking through Improved Pocket Prediction and Pose Generation\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Qizhi Pei, Gongbo Zhang, Jinhua Zhu, Kun He, Lijun Wu\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(KDD 2025)\n[Code:\n134 Stars\n]\n[Weights]\nFast and Accurate Blind Flexible Docking\nZizhuo Zhang, Lijun Wu,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Jiangchao Yao, Tao Qin, Bo Han\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR 2025)\n[Code:\n134 Stars\n]\n[Weights]\nPre-training antibody language models for antigen-specific computational antibody design\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Lijun Wu, Jinhua Zhu, Tianbo Peng, Yingce Xia, Liang He, Shufang Xie, Tao Qin, Haiguang Liu, Kun He, Tie-Yan Liu\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(KDD 2023)\n[Code: 53 Stars]\n[Weights]\nCovDocker: Benchmarking Covalent Drug Design with Tasks, Datasets, and Solutions\nYangzhe* Peng,\nKaiyuan Gao*\n, Liang He, Yuheng Cong, Haiguang Liu, Kun He, Lijun Wu\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(KDD 2025)\n[Code]\n[Datasets]\nMultimodal Molecular Learning:\nTokenizing 3d molecule structure with quantized spherical coordinates\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Yusong Wang, Haoxiang Guan, Zun Wang, Qizhi Pei, John E Hopcroft, Kun He, Lijun Wu\n3D-MolT5: Towards Unified 3D Molecule-Text Modeling with 3D Molecular Tokenization\nQizhi Pei, Lijun Wu,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Jinhua Zhu, Rui Yan\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR 2025)\nBiot5: Enriching cross-modal integration in biology with chemical knowledge and natural language associations\nQizhi Pei, Wei Zhang, Jinhua Zhu, Kehan Wu,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Lijun Wu, Yingce Xia, Rui Yan\nEmpirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2023\n(EMNLP 2023)\n[Code:\n118 Stars\n]\n[Weights]\nBiot5+: Towards generalized biological understanding with iupac integration and multi-task tuning\nQizhi Pei, Lijun Wu,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Xiaozhuan Liang, Yin Fang, Jinhua Zhu, Shufang Xie, Tao Qin, Rui Yan\nThe Association for Computational Linguistics\n(ACL 2024 (Findings))\n[Code:\n118 Stars\n]\n[Weights]\nNaturelm: Deciphering the language of nature for scientific discovery\nYingce Xia, Peiran Jin, Shufang Xie, Liang He, Chuan Cao, Renqian Luo, Guoqing Liu, Yue Wang, Zequn Liu, Yuan-Jyue Chen, Zekun Guo, Yeqi Bai, Pan Deng, Yaosen Min, Ziheng Lu, Hongxia Hao, Han Yang, Jielan Li, Chang Liu, Jia Zhang, Jianwei Zhu, Kehan Wu, Wei Zhang,\nKaiyuan Gao\n, Qizhi Pei, Qian Wang, Xixian Liu, Yanting Li, Houtian Zhu, Yeqing Lu, Mingqian Ma, Zun Wang, Tian Xie, Krzysztof Maziarz, Marwin Segler, Zhao Yang, Zilong Chen, Yu Shi, Shuxin Zheng, Lijun Wu, Chen Hu, Peggy Dai, Tie-Yan Liu, Haiguang Liu, Tao Qin\n[Project Page]\n[Code]\n[Weights]\nGraph Learning:\nNAGphormer: A tokenized graph transformer for node classification in large graphs\nJinsong Chen*,\nKaiyuan Gao*\n, Gaichao Li, Kun He\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR 2022)\n[Code:\n129 Stars\n]\nNagphormer+: A tokenized graph transformer with neighborhood augmentation for node classification in large graphs\nJinsong Chen*,\nKaiyuan Gao*\n, Gaichao Li, Kun He\nIEEE Transactions on Big Data\n(TBD)\n* indicates co-first authors.\n© 2025 Kaiyuan Gao"
