    "homepage_text": "Yuxuan Ding – The Muir Lab\nSkip to content (Press Enter)\nThe Muir Lab\nDepartment of Chemistry, Princeton University\nThe Muir Lab\nDepartment of Chemistry, Princeton University\nJune 13, 2025\nchmadmin\nYuxuan Ding\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nEmail Yuxuan\nHometown: Tianjin, China\nYuxuan obtained his Ph.D. in chemistry from Rice University, where he worked with Prof. Zachary Ball on chemical modification of peptides and proteins. In the Muir lab, he is interested in applications of proximity-driven protein trans-splicing. Outside of the lab, Yuxuan enjoys basketball, TV dramas, and traveling.\nAbout the Author\nchmadmin"
  },
