    "github": "https://github.com/tqwei05",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhi Chen, Ph.D. - Homepage\nZhi Chen\nLecturer/Assistant Professor\nAustralia\nUniversity of Southern Queensland\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nI am a Lecturer/Assistant Professor at the School of Mathematics, Physics and Computing, The University of Southern Queensland (UniSQ), Australia. Previously, I worked as an Associate Lecturer and Postdoctoral Research Fellow in the School of EECS, The University of Queensland (UQ), working with Prof. Zi (Helen) Huang from August 2022 to January 2025. From January 2025 to April 2025, I worked as a research fellow in the ODeSI team of the UQ Centre for Clinical Research (UQ-CCR). I obtained my PhD degree in 2023 from UQ, advised by Prof. Zi (Helen) Huang.\nMy research centers around developing generalizable and applicable ML/AI approaches. For fundamental research, I mainly explore the field of computer vision, particularly in\nzero-shot learning\n. For applied AI, I mainly conduct interdisciplinary research on\nAI for Agriculture\nand\nAI for Healthcare\n.\n🚀 I am now looking for highly motivated Ph.D. students, Master’s Students, Research Assistants, and Visiting Scholars working on computer vision and related areas.\n🔥 News\n2026.02\n:   One RUIC program project ($100,000) has been granted by the Queensland Government and CSIRO.\n2026.02\n:   One AEA Ignite Project ($549,886) has been granted by the Department of Education.\n2025.12\n：  Our dataset paper\nPlantSeg\nhas been accepted to Scientific Data (Nature Portfolio, JCR Q1, IF: 6.9).\n2025.12\n:   I gave a talk on AI for Agriculture in the AI4Impact Research Symposium, hosted by UniSQ Business School and SRMIST India.\n2025.12\n:   I gave a tutorial on zero-shot learning in\nDICTA2025\n.\n2025.11\n:   Our paper on Diffusion Quantization has been accepted to AAAI 2026, paper coming soon.\n2025.10\n:   My first-author paper “Distribution Zero-Shot Learning for Visual recognition” has been accepted to IEEE Transactions on Multimedia (JCR Q1, Core A*, IF:9.7). Paper coming soon.\n2025.10\n:   My first-author paper on\nFew-Shot Vision-Language Model Adaptation\nhas been accepted to the journal Pattern Recognition (JCR Q1, Core A*, IF:7.6).\n2025.10\n:   My first author paper on\nSingle-Image Editing\nhas been accepted to the Special Issue: Beneficial Noise Learning in the journal Pattern Recognition (JCR Q1) (Core A*).\n2025.08\n:   Our\nGlobal Wheat Full Semantic Organ Segmentation (GWFSS) Dataset\nhas been accepted to Plant Phenomics (JCR Q1, IF 6.4, No.1 Journal for Phenotyping).\nProject Page\n2025.08\n:   Our benchmark on\nvideo generative models for video retrieval\nhas been accepted to ACM MM Dataset Track.\n2025.07\n:   One paper on Test-Time Adaptation has been accepted to ACM MM 2025. Paper coming soon.\n2025.06\n:   My first author paper on\nZero-Shot Learning\nhas been accepted to ICCV 2025.\n2025.05\n:   Serve as Guest Editor for Complex & Intelligent Systems (JCR-Q1) (\nSpecial Issue on Efficient AI for Resource-Constrained and Complex Applications\n).\n2025.04\n:   One paper on\nContinual Learning\nhas been accepted to IJCAI 2025.\n2025.04\n:   One paper on\nContinual Text-to-Video Retrieval\nhas been accepted to SIGIR 2025.\n2025.04\n:   I have joined the University of Southern Queensland as a Lecturer (Assistant Professor) after working as a Postdoc at UQ for two years.\n2024.12\n:   One paper on\nSource-free Open-Set Domain Adaptation\nhas been accepted to AAAI 2025.\n2024.10\n:   One paper on\nClass-Agnostic Object Detection\nhas been accepted to NeurIPS 2024.\n2024.09\n:   Our\nCoarse-to-Fine Prototype Refining Network for Point Cloud Completion and Reconstruction\nfor CVPPA@ECCV 2025 challenge won the first place solution!\n2024.07\n:   One paper on\nIn-the-wild Multimodal Disease Recognition\nhas been accepted to ACM MM 2024.\n📚 Publications\n2025\nPlantSeg: A Large-Scale In-the-wild Dataset for Plant Disease Segmentation\nTianqi Wei,\nZhi Chen\n, Xin Yu, Scott Chapman, Paul Melloy, Zi Huang\nScientific Data (Nature Portfolio)\nAI for Science\nPaper\n/\ncode\n/\ndataset\nCluster-Aware Prompt Ensemble Learning for Few-Shot Vision-Language Model Adaptation\nZhi Chen\n, Xin Yu, Xiaohui Tao, Yan Li, Zi Huang\nPattern Recognition (PR) (Core A*) (IF: 7.6)\nVLM\nPaper\nFastEdit: Fast Text-Guided Single-Image Editing via Semantic-Aware Diffusion Fine-Tuning\nZhi Chen\n, Zecheng Zhao, Yadan Luo, Yan Li, Xiaohui Tao, Zi Huang\nPattern Recognition (PR) (Core A*) (IF: 7.6)\nImage Editing\nPaper\n/\ncode\nThe Global Wheat Full Semantic Organ Segmentation (GWFSS) Dataset\nZijian Wang, ...,\nZhi Chen\n, ... et, al.\nPlant Phenomics (Q1) (IF: 6.4)\nAI for Science\nPaper\n/\nProject\nAre Synthetic Videos Useful? A Benchmark for Retrieval-Centric Evaluation of Synthetic Videos\nZecheng Zhao, Selena Song, Tong Chen,\nZhi Chen\n, Shazia Sadiq, Yadan Luo\nACM MM 2025\nVideo\narXiv\nPatAug: Augmentation of Augmentation for Test-Time Adaptation\nXinyao Li, Dan Zhang, Zhekai Du, Lei Zhu,\nZhi Chen\n, Jingjing Li\nACM MM 2025\nDA\nPaper\nSVIP: Semantically Contextualized Visual Patches for Zero-Shot Learning\nZhi Chen\n, Zecheng Zhao, Jingcai Guo, Jingjing Li, Zi Huang\nICCV 2025\nZSL\nPaper\nContinual Text-to-Video Retrieval with Frame Fusion and Task-Aware Routing\nZecheng Zhao,\nZhi Chen\n, Zi Huang, Shazia Sadiq, Tong Chen\nSIGIR 2025 (Core A*)\nCL\narXiv\nOn the Discrimination and Consistency for Exemplar-Free Class Incremental Learning\nTianqi Wang, Jingcai Guo, Depeng Li,\nZhi Chen\nIJCAI 2025\nCL\narXiv\nDynamic Target Distribution Estimation for Source-free Open-Set Domain Adaptation\nZhiqi Yu, Zhichao Liao, Jingjing Li,\nZhi Chen\n, Lei Zhu\nThe 39th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence* AAAI 2025 (Core A*)\nDA\npaper\nPhysics-Informed Machine Learning Offers Multi-Scale Remote Estimation of Wheat Biomass Dynamics\nQiaomin Chen*,\nZhi Chen\n*, et al. (Co-First Author)\nIEEE International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium 2025 (IGARSS)\nAI for Science\npaper\n2024\nDiPEx: Dispersing Prompt Expansion for Class-Agnostic Object Detection\nJia Syuen Lim, Zhuoxiao Chen,\nZhi Chen\n, Mahsa Baktashmotlagh, Xin Yu, Zi Huang, Yadan Luo\nNeurIPS 2024\narXiv\n/\ncode\nBenchmarking In-the-wild Multimodal Disease Recognition and A Versatile Baseline\nTianqi Wei,\nZhi Chen\n, Zi Huang, Xin Yu\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM)* 2024. (Core A*)\nAI for Science\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\ndataset\nCF-PRNet: Coarse-to-Fine Prototype Refining Network for Point Cloud Completion and Reconstruction\nZhi Chen\n, Tianqi Wei, Zecheng Zhao, Jia Syuen Lim, Yadan Luo, Hu Zhang, Xin Yu, Scott Chapman, Zi Huang\n1st Place solution to CVPPA@ECCV2024: Shape Completion and Reconstruction of Sweet Peppers Challenge.\nAI for Science\narXiv\n/\ncode\n/\ncompetition\nTrack Any Peppers: Weakly Supervised Sweet Pepper Tracking Using VLMs\nJia Syuen Lim, Yadan Luo,\nZhi Chen\n, Tianqi Wei, Scott Chapman, Zi Huang\n2st Place solution to CVPPA@ECCV2024: Detection and Multi-Object Tracking of Sweet Peppers Challenge.\nAI for Science\npaper\n/\ncompetition\nSnap and Diagnose: An Advanced Multimodal Retrieval System for Identifying Plant Diseases in the Wild\nTianqi Wei,\nZhi Chen\n, Xin Yu, Scott Chapman, Paul Melloy, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia in Asia 2024.\nAI for Science\npaper\nTowards Cost-Efficient Federated Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning with Learnable Aggregation\nYi Zhang, Sen Wang,\nZhi Chen\n, Xuwei Xu, Stano Funiak, Frank de Hoog, Jiajun Liu\nThe Pacific-Asia Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining* (PAKDD) 2024. (Best Student Paper Award)\nRL\npaper\nOn the Element-Wise Representation and Reasoning in Zero-Shot Image Recognition: A Systematic Survey\nJingcai Guo, Zhijie Rao,\nZhi Chen\n, Song Guo, Jingren Zhou, Dacheng Tao\npre-print\nZSL\narXiv\nSecondary analysis of newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes subgroups and treatment responses in the MARCH cohort\nWeihao Wang, Xiaobei Li, Fei Chen, Ran Wei,\nZhi Chen\n, Jingjing Li, Jingtao Qiao, Qi Pan, Wenjing Yang, Lixin Guo\nDiabetes & Metabolic Syndrome: Clinical Research & Reviews.* 2024. (IF:10.0)\nAI for Science\npaper\n2023\nZero-Shot Learning by Harnessing Adversarial Samples\nZhi Chen\n, Pengfei Zhang, Jingjing Li, Sen Wang, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia 2023\nZSL\narXiv\n/\ncode\nFederated Zero-Shot Learning for Visual Recognition\nZhi Chen\n, Yan Luo, Sen Wang, Jingjing Li, Zi Huang\npre-print\nZSL\narXiv\nCal-SFDA: Source-Free Domain-adaptive Semantic Segmentation with Differentiable Expected Calibration Error\nZixin Wang, Yadan Luo,\nZhi Chen\n, Sen Wang, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia 2023\nDA\narXiv\n/\ncode\nOptimizing Taxi Route Planning Based on Taxi Trajectory Data Analysis\nXinyi Yang,\nZhi Chen\n, Yadan Luo\nAustralasian Database Conference* (ADC) 2023.\nAI for Transport\npaper\n2022\nGSMFlow: Generation Shifts Mitigating Flow for Generalized Zero-Shot Learning\nZhi Chen\n, Yadan Luo, Sen Wang, Jingjing Li, Zi Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (TMM) (JCR Q1, Core A*, IF: 9.7)\nZSL\npaper\n/\ncode\nDistinguishing Unseen from Seen for Generalized Zero-shot Learning\nHongzu Su, Jingjing Li,\nZhi Chen\n, Lei Zhu, Ke Lu\nThe IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2022. (Core A*)\nZSL\nPaper\n/\ncode\nPixel Exclusion: Uncertainty-aware Boundary Discovery for Active Cross-Domain Semantic Segmentation\nFuming You, Jingjing Li,\nZhi Chen\n, Lei Zhu\nACM International Conference on Multimedia* (MM) 2022. (Core A*)\nDA\npaper\nApplication of novel subgroups of Chinese inpatients with diabetes based on machine learning paradigm\nWeihao Wang,\nZhi Chen\n,  Sen Wang, Fei Chen, Mingqun Deng, Qi Pan, Lixin Guo\nDiabetes & Metabolic Syndrome: Clinical Research & Reviews. 2022. (JCR Q1) (IF:10.0) (Co-first Author)\nAI for Science\npaper\nFluMA: An Intelligent Platform for Influenza Monitoring and Analysis\nXi Chen,\nZhi Chen\n, Zijian Wang, Ruihong Qiu, Yadan Luo\nAustralasian Database Conference* 2022\nAI for Science\npaper\n2021\nSemantics Disentangling for Generalized Zero-Shot Learning\nZhi Chen\n, Yadan Luo, Ruihong Qiu, Sen Wang, Zi Huang, Jingjing Li, Zheng Zhang\nICCV 2021. (Core A*)\nZSL\npaper\n/\ncode\nMitigating Generation Shifts for Generalized Zero-Shot Learning\nZhi Chen\n, Yadan Luo, Sen Wang, Ruihong Qiu, Jingjing Li, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM) 2021. (Core A*)\nZSL\npaper\n/\ncode\nEntropy-Based Uncertainty Calibration for Generalized Zero-Shot Learning\nZhi Chen\n, Zi Huang, Jingjing Li, Zheng Zhang\n2021 Australasian Database Conference. (Best student paper – Highly Commended)\nZSL\narXiv\nDomain Adaptive Semantic Segmentation without Source Data\nFuming You, Jingjing Li, Lei Zhu,\nZhi Chen\n, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia* (MM) 2021. (Core A*)\nDA\npaper\n/\ncode\nLocal Graph Convolutional Networks for Cross-Modal Hashing\nYudong Chen, Sen Wang, Jianlin Lu,\nZhi Chen\n, Zheng Zhang, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia* (MM) 2021. (Core A*)\nHashing\npaper\n/\ncode\nCausalRec: Causal Inference for Visual Debiasing in Visually-Aware Recommendation\nRuihong Qiu, Sen Wang,\nZhi Chen\n, Hongzhi Yin, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia* (MM) 2021. (Core A*)\nRec\npaper\n/\ncode\nApplication of new international classification of adult-onset diabetes in Chinese inpatients with diabetes mellitus\nWeihao Wang, Xiaobei Pei, Lina Zhang,\nZhi Chen\n, Dong Lin, Xiaoye Duan, Jingwen Fan, Qi Pan, Lixin Guo\nDiabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews. 2021.* (IF: 8.02)\nAI for Science\narXiv\n2020\nCANZSL: Cycle-Consistent Adversarial Networks for Zero-Shot Learning from Natural Language\nZhi Chen\n, Jingjing Li, Yadan Luo, Zi Huang, Yang Yang\nThe IEEE Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV) 2020. (Core A)\nZSL\narXiv\n/\ncode\nRethinking Generative Zero-Shot Learning: An Ensemble Learning Perspective for Recognising Visual Patches\nZhi Chen\n, Sen Wang, Jingjing Li, Zi Huang\nACM International Conference on Multimedia 2020.* (Core A*)\nZSL\npaper\n/\ncode\n🧑🏻‍🏫 Teachings\nAs Instructor\nDATA7002 Responsible Data Science (Co-Instructor with Dr. Michael Vincent, Dr. Hamish MacDonald, Dr. Slava Vaisman) (SECaT: 4.28/5.0)\nSchool of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, University of Queensland\n, 2rd Term 2024\nCourse webpage\nTopics Covered: Responsible Machine Learning, Fairness-Aware Machine Learning\nCloud Computing (Co-Instructor with A/Prof. Sen Wang) (SECaT: 4.53/5.0)\nSchool of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, University of Queensland\n, 2rd Term 2024\nCourse webpage\nTopics Covered: Vector Databases, NoSQL Databases, RDD Computing, Spark Framework\nAdvanced Database Systems (Co-Instructor with Prof. Shazia Sadiq and A/Prof. Sen Wang) (SECaT: 4.63/5.0)\nSchool of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, University of Queensland\n, 2rd Term 2024\nCourse webpage\nTopics Covered: Column-Oriented Databases, Data Lakes, Data Lakehouses\nDATA7002 Responsible Data Science (Co-Instructor with Dr. Michael Vincent, Dr. Hamish MacDonald, Dr. Slava Vaisman) (SECaT: 4.21/5.0)\nSchool of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, University of Queensland\n, 2rd Term 2023\nCourse webpage\nTopics Covered: Responsible Machine Learning, Fairness-Aware Machine Learning\n👔 Services\nConference Service\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2022-2024\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV) 2023\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) 2022, 2024\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM) 2021-2024 (Outstanding Reviewer @ 2024)\nAAAI Conf. on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI) 2022-2024\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP) 2023\nJournal Editorship\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI) 2024\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV) 2024\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (TMM) 2022-2023\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (TCSVT) 2023-2024\nIEEE Transactions on Cognitive and Developmental Systems (TCDS) 2023\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
