  "deep_homepage::Fan Chen::https://homes.luddy.indiana.edu/fc7/": {
    "homepage": "https://homes.luddy.indiana.edu/fc7/",
    "all_emails": [
      "fc7@iu.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/fan-chen-68b98150/",
    "homepage_text": "Fan Chen\nFan Chen\nAssistant Professor\nIntelligent Systems Engineering\nSchool of Informatics and Computing\nIndiana University Bloomington\nOther Affiliations\nQSEc: IU-Quantum Science and Engineering Center\nLAIC: Luddy Artificial Intelligence Center\nEmail:\nfc7@iu.edu\nTel:\n(812) 855-0446\nOffice:\nMESH 113B\n2425 N Milo B Sampson Ln\nBloomington\nIN 47408\nGoogle Map\nFaculty Profile\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\ndblp\nBiography\nFan Chen is an assistant professor in the department of\nIntelligent Systems Engineering\nat the\nIndiana University Bloomington\n, \nand is affiliated with\nIU-Quantum Science and Engineering Center (QSEc)\nand\nLuddy Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC)\n. \nDr. Chen received her Ph.D. from the department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at\nDuke University\n, \nher M.S. and B.S. from\nTsinghua University\nand\nXi’an Jiaotong University\n, China, respectively. \nHer research interests include \nQuantum Computing,\nQuantum Security,\nSustainable AI Systems,\nand Hardware Acceleration for Emerging Applications.\nDr. Chen is \nthe General Chair of GLSVLSI 2026 and IGSC 2026, \nthe Technical Program Chair of GLSVLSI 2025 and IGSC 2024,\nPosters Track Chair of QCE 2025/2024,\nSpecial Session Chair of ISVLSI 2024,\nchair of SIGDA University Booth at DAC 2022/2021,\nthe Publication Chair of ISLPED 2022/2021,\nWeb and Registration Chair of GLSVLSI 2022, \nProceedings Chair of ASAP 2021, \nArrangement Chair of GLSVLSI 2021. \nDr. Chen is the Technical Program Committee members of over 20 international conference series.\nDr. Chen served on the editorial board of IEEE Circuits and Systems Magazine (CAS-M) (2021-2023). \nShe also serves as technical reviewers for over 30+ international conferences/journals, such as\nIEEE TC, IEEE TCAS-I, IEEE TNNLS, IEEE D&T, IEEE IoT-J, ACM TACO, ACM TODAES, ACM JETC, etc.\nDr. Chen is a recipient of \nthe 2024-25 Indiana University Bloomington Outstanding Junior Faculty Award,\nthe 2022 NSF Faculty Early Career Development Program (CAREER) Award, \nthe 2019 Cadence Women in Technology Scholarship. \nHer research has won \nthe Best Paper Finalists at 2024 Design Automation Conference (DAC),\nthe Best Paper Award (3rd Place) at 2023 IEEE International Conference on Quantum Computing and Engineering (QCE), \nthe Best Paper Award and the Ph.D. forum Best Poster Award\nat 2018 Asia and South Pacific Design Automation Conference (ASP-DAC). \nDr. Chen's contributions to the research community has been acknowledged by\nthe 2024 ACM SIGDA Meritorious Service Award,  \nthe 2022 IEEE Best Associate Editor of the Circuits and Systems Society (CASS), and \nthe 2021 Service Recognition Award of Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI).\nResearch Interests\nQuantum Computing, Quantum Security\nSustainable AI Systems, Sustainable Computing\nHardware Acceleration for Emerging Applications\nTwo RA Openings for Students with Physics/Mathematics Backgrounds\nWe seek students with strong foundations in physics, mathematics, or related fields and an interest in quantum computing and machine learning. Please email your CV/transcript if interested.\nHonors and Awards\n2025   Indiana University Bloomington Outstanding Junior Faculty Award\n2024   ACM SIGDA Meritorious Service Award\n2024   DAC Best Paper Finalists\n2023   QCE Best Paper Award - 3rd Place\n2022   IEEE Best Associate Editor of the Circuits and Systems Society (CASS)\n2022   NSF CAREER Award\n2021   Service Recognition Award of GLSVLSI\n2019   Cadence Women in Technology Scholorship\n2018   ASP-DAC Best Paper Award\n2018   ASP-DAC Ph.D. forum Best Poster Award\nCompute Credits\n2025   IBM Quantum Credits ($35,000)\n2024   IBM Quantum Credits ($70,000)\n2023   IonQ Research Credits Program ($10,000)\nIn the News\nLuddy Schoolâs Fan Chen wins Outstanding Junior Faculty Award\n(May 1, 2025)\nChen earns NSF CAREER Award to advance research improving efficiency of genome sequencing\n(Jan 27, 2022)\nProfessional Activities and Service\nConference General Chair:\nGeneral Chair, ACM/IEEE Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI), 2026\nGeneral Chair, ACM/IEEE International Green and Sustainable Computing Conference (IGSC), 2026\nConference Technical Program Chair:\nTPC Chair, ACM/IEEE Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI), 2025\nTPC Chair, ACM/IEEE International Green and Sustainable Computing Conference (IGSC), 2024\nConference Organization Committee (Selected):\nPosters Track Co-Chair, IEEE International Conference on Quantum Computing and Engineering (QCE), 2024, 2025\nSpecial Session Chair, IEEE Computer Society Annual Symposium on VLSI (ISVLSI), 2024\nVice chair/Chair, SIGDA University Booth at DAC (UBooth@DAC), 2021, 2022\nPublication Chair, International Symposium on Low Power Electronics and Design (ISLPED), 2021, 2022\nWeb and Registration chair, ACM Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI), 2022\nPublicity Chair, International Green and Sustainable Computing Conference (IGSC), 2022, 2023\nArrangement Chair, ACM Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI), 2021\nProceedings Chair, IEEE International Conference on Application-specific Systems, Architectures and Processors (ASAP), 2021\nSession Chair, ACM Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI (GLSVLSI), 2020\nConference Technical Program Committee (Selected):\nDesign Automation Conference (DAC) 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025\nIEEE International Conference on Quantum Computing and Engineering (QCE), 2023, 2024, 2025\nInternational Joint Conference on Neural Networks (IJCNN), 2024, 2025\nDesign, Automation & Test in Europe (DATE), 2025\nInternational Conference on Computer-Aided Design (ICCAD), 2025\nAsia and South Pacific Design Automation Conference (ASP-DAC), 2022, 2023, 2024\nInternational Green and Sustainable Computing Conference (IGSC), 2021, 2022\nIEEE Computer Society Annual Symposium on VLSI (ISVLSI), 2020, 2021\nIEEE International Conference on Artificial Intelligence Circuits and Systems (AICAS), 2021\nInternational Conference on Neural Information Processing (ICONIP), 2020\nJournal Editorial:\nEditorial Board, IEEE Circuits and Systems Magazine (IEEE CAS-M), 2021-2023\nJournal Reviewer (Selected):\nACM Transactions on Architecture and Code Optimization (TACO)\nACM Journal on Emerging Technologies in Computing (JETC)\nACM Transactions on Design Automation of Electronic Systems (TODAES)\nIEEE Transactions on Computers (TC)\nIEEE Computer Architecture Letters (CAL)\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems I: Regular Papers (TCAS-I)\nIEEE Design and Test of Computers (Design & Test)\nIEEE Internet of Things (IoT) Journal (IoT-J)\nIEEE Transactions on Emerging Topics in Computing (TETC)\nIEEE Embedded Systems Letters (ESL)\nIEEE Transactions on Nanotechnology (TNANO)\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nIEEE Transactions on Biomedical Circuits and Systems (TBioCAS)\nOthers:\nOrganizing Committee,,\nNSF Principal Investigator (PI) Meeting of the Computer Systems Research (CSR)\n, 2023\nScribe,\nNSF Workshop on Processing-In-Memory Technolog\n, 2021\nTutorial on “Efficient and Secure Hardware Accelerator for Deep Neural Networks”, \nIn\nThe workshop for Women in Hardware and Systems Security (WISE)\n, 2021\nScribe,\nNSF Workshop on Machine Learning Hardware Breakthroughs\n, 2020"
  },
