    "homepage_text": "Hao Wu's Personal Page\nHao Wu\nWelcome to my personal academic website. I obtained my Ph.D. in Chemistry from Harvard University in 2021. At Harvard, I worked at the\nMurthy lab\nin the Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, where I study neuronal coding of olfaction. Here is my\ncurriculum vitae.\nDuring my undergraduate years at UC Berkeley, I worked at the\nGinsberg Lab\ndeveloping microscopy tools to study photovoltaic materials.\nIâm from Shanghai, China. My love for science dates back to 5th grade when my science teacher shot a rocket with citric acid and baking soda. In my free time, I enjoy running and windsurfing.\nContact\nEmail: hwu01 [at] g.harvard.edu\nNews\nJan 2019 - My lab's research of ant navigation is featured in a\nNew York Times article\n, including a short clip of motor-tracked, computer-labeled ant movements that I collected with\nAntCam\nand analyzed with\nDeepLabCut\n.\nPublications\nAll-optical electrophysiology reveals the role of lateral inhibition in sensory processing in cortical layer 1\nFan, L. Z.; Kheifets, S.; BÃ¶hm, U. L.; Wu, H.; Piatkevich, K. D.; Parot, V.; Xie, M. E.; Ha, Y.; Evans, K. E.; Boyden, E. S.; Takesian, A. E.; Cohen, A. E.,\nCell\n,\n2020\nVoltage imaging and optogenetics reveal behaviour-dependent changes in hippocampal dynamics\nAdam, Y.; Kim, J. J.; Shan, L.; Zhao, Y.; Xie, M. E.; Brinks, D.; Wu, H.; Mostajo-Radji, M. A.; Kheifets, S.; Parot, V.; Chettih, S.; Williams, K. J.; Farhi, S. L.; Madisen, L.; Harvey, C. D.; Zeng, H.; Arlotta, P.; Campbell, R. E.; Cohen, A. E.,\nNature\n,\n2019\nAll-optical synaptic electrophysiology probes mechanism of ketamine-induced disinhibition\nFan, L. Z.; Nehme, R.; Adam, Y.; Jung, E. S.; Wu, H; Eggan, K.; Arnold, D. B.; Cohen, A. E.,\nNat. Methods\n,\n2018\n, 15, 823-31\nOrigin of reversible photoinduced phase separation in hybrid perovskites\nBischak, C. G.; Hetherington, C. L.; Wu, H.; Aloni, S.; Ogletree, D. F.; Limmer, D. T.; Ginsberg, N. S.,\nNano Lett.\n,\n2017\n, 17, 1028-33\nExciton dynamics reveal aggregates with intermolecular order at hidden interfaces in solution-cast organic semiconducting films\nWong, C. Y.; Cotts, B. L.; Wu, H.; Ginsberg , N.S.,\nNat. Commun.\n,\n2015\n, 6, 5946.\nRelating the physical structure and optoelectronic function of crystalline TIPS-pentacene.\nSharifzadeh, S.,; Wong, C. Y.; Wu, H.; Cotts, B. L.; Kronik, L.;  Ginsberg , N.S.; Neaton, J. B.,\nAdv. Funct. Mater.\n,\n2015\n, 25, 2038â46.\nRevealing exciton dynamics in a small-molecule organic semiconducting film with sub-domain transient absorption microscopy\nWong, C. Y.; Penwell, S. B.; Cotts, B. L.; Noriega, R.; Wu, H.; Ginsberg , N.S.,\nJ. Phys. Chem. C\n,\n2013\n, 117, 22111-22."
