    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ziang Xiao\nZiang Xiao 肖子昂\ncv\n/\npublications\n/\nabout\nZiang Xiao\nAssistant Professor\nComputer Science\nJohns Hopkins University\nEmail: ziang.xiao [at] jhu (dot) edu\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nTwitter\nNews.\nThe Human-centered Evaluation and Auditing of Language Models (HEAL) workshop is back for its 3rd iteration at CHI'26!\n[Link]\nTiiS's new special issue on Human-Centric Generative AI now out!\n[Link]\nAbout.\nI am an Assistant Professor in Computer Science at\nJohns Hopkins University\n. I completed my Ph.D in Computer Science at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. \n            I was co-advised by\nProf. Hari Sundaram\nand\nProf. Karrie Karahalios\n. \n            I earned my B.S. in Psychology and Statistics & Computer Science at the University of Illinois with\nProf. Dov Cohen\n.\nMy research is motivated by the fundamental question of\nunderstanding humans at scale\n. My goal is to study human-computer interaction to expand our knowledge about our behaviors and decision-making processes. Currently, I want to spend my time on three exciting topics,\nAI for Social Science\n,\nHuman-centered Model Evaluation\n, and\nInformation Seeking\n. Broadly, my work lies in the intersection of\nhuman-computer interaction\n,\nnatural language processing\n, and\nsocial and personality psychology\n.\nTeaching.\n[EN.601.790] Advanced HCI: Research Methods\n[Spring 2025/2026]\n[EN.601.490/690] Introduction to Human-Computer Interaction\n[Fall 2024/2025]\n[EMNLP 2024 Tutorial] Human-Centered Evaluation of Language Technologies\n[Slides]\n[EN.601.792] Advanced Topics in Conversational User Interfaces\n[Spring 2024]\nAdvisees (PhD and Postdoc).\n[2024–now]\nYu Lu Liu\n[2024–now]\nNikhil Sharma\n[2025–now]\nJonathan Ivey\n| Co-advised by Anjalie Field\n[2025–now]\nHan Jiang\n[2025–now]\nJie Gao (Postdoc)\n| Co-advised by Chien-Ming Huang and Mark Dredze\n[2025–now]\nAmama Mahmood (Postdoc)\n| Co-advised by Chien-Ming Huang\nPublications.\nfeatured\n/\nby topic\n/\nby date:all\n(\n■\nindicates student advisees;* indicates equal contribution)\nAI4SocialScience.\nLanguage Technologies.\nInformavore.\nSpatialVis."
  },
