    "homepage_text": "Hongcheng Gao - Homepage\nHongcheng Gao\ngaohongcheng2000@gmail.com\nIncoming PhD at THU, interested in LLM and Agent.\nBeijing, China\nEmail\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nSemantic Scholar\nHongcheng Gao(高鸿成) is an incoming PhD student at\nCollege of AI\nat\nTsinghua University\n. He may receive his M.S. degree in July 2026. He received his Bachelor's degree of Computer Science and Technology at\nChongqing University\nin June 2023.\nHis research interests include\nlarge reasoning models\n,\nAI agents\nand\nunified models\n, spanning both textual and multimodal domains (especially\nspatial\ntasks).\nHis team is looking for collaborators and interns. Please feel free to reach out.\n🔥 News\n2026.1\n: One papers accepted to ICLR’26.\n2025.11\n: One papers accepted to AAAI’26.\n2025.09\n: Two papers accepted to Neurips’25 with one\nOral\n.\n2025.06\n: One paper accepted to ICCV 2025.\n2025.06\n: Invited to serve as\nSenior PC Member\nfor CIKM’25.\n2025.01\n: Two papers accepted to ICLR 2025 with one\nOral\n.\n2024.10\n: Selected as NeurIPS 2024\nTop Reviewer\n.\n2024.09\n: Three papers accepted to NeurIPS 2024 with\ntwo Spotlights\n.\n2024.09\n: Two papers accepted to EMNLP 2024.\n2024.05\n: One paper accepted to ACL 2024.\n2024.04\n: One paper accepted to NAACL 2024.\n2024.01\n: 🎉 One paper accepted to ICLR 2024.\n2023.09\n: 🎉 One paper accepted to NeurIPS 2023 (D&B Track).\n2023.05\n: 🎉 One paper accepted to ACL 2023!\n2022.10\n: 🎉 Two papers accepted by EMNLP 2022!\n2022.08\n: 🎉 One paper accepted by NAACL 2022!\n📝 Preprints\n* indicates equal contribution.\nGuardReasoner: Towards Reasoning-based LLM Safeguards\n[Paper]\nYue Liu,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Shengfang Zhai, Jun Xia, Tianyi Wu, Zhiwei Xue, Yulin Chen, Kenji Kawaguchi, Jiaheng Zhang, Bryan Hooi\nStruEdit: Structured Outputs Enable the Fast and Accurate Knowledge Editing for Large Language Models\n[Paper]\nBaolong Bi, Shenghua Liu, Yiwei Wang, Lingrui Mei,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Junfeng Fang, Xueqi Cheng\nEvaluating the Robustness of Text-to-image Diffusion Models against Real-world Attacks\n[Paper]\nHongcheng Gao\n, Hao Zhang, Yinpeng Dong, Zhijie Deng.\nKimi k1. 5: Scaling Reinforcement Learning with LLMs\n[Paper]\nKimi Team\nKimi-vl Technical Report\n[Paper]\nKimi Team\nKimi k2: Open Agentic Intelligence\n[Paper]\nKimi Team\nKimi k2.5: Visual Agentic intelligence\n[Paper]\nKimi Team\n📝 Publications\n* indicates equal contribution.\n2026\nHow Far Are LLMs from Professional Poker Players? Revisiting Game-Theoretic Reasoning with Agentic Tool Use\n[Paper]\nMinhua Lin, Enyan Dai, Hui Liu, Xianfeng Tang, Yuliang Yan, Zhenwei Dai, Jingying Zeng, Zhiwei Zhang, Fali Wang,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Chen Luo, Xiang Zhang, Qi He, Suhang Wang.\nICLR 2026\n2025\nRepresentation Entanglement for Generation: Training Diffusion Transformers Is Much Easier Than You Think\n[Paper]\nGe Wu, Shen Zhang, Ruijing Shi, Shanghua Gao, Zhenyuan Chen, Lei Wang, Zhaowei Chen,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Yao Tang, Jian Yang, Ming-Ming Cheng, Xiang Li.\nNeurIPS 2025\nGuardreasoner-vl: Safeguarding vlms via reinforced reasoning\n[Paper]\nYue Liu, Shengfang Zhai, Mingzhe Du, Yulin Chen, Tri Cao,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Cheng Wang, Xinfeng Li, Kun Wang, Junfeng Fang, Jiaheng Zhang, Bryan Hooi\nNeurIPS 2025\nMeta-Unlearning on Diffusion Models: Preventing Relearning Unlearned Concepts\n[Paper]\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Tianyu Pang*, Chao Du, Taihang Hu, Zhijie Deng, Min Lin.\nICCV 2025\nSpider 2.0: Evaluating language models on real-world enterprise text-to-sql workflows\n[Paper]\nFangyu Lei*, Jixuan Chen*, Yuxiao Ye, Ruisheng Cao, Dongchan Shin, Hongjin Su, Zhaoqing Suo,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Wenjing Hu, Pengcheng Yin, Victor Zhong, Caiming Xiong, Ruoxi Sun, Qian Liu, Sida Wang, Tao Yu.\nICLR 2025\nIs factuality decoding a free lunch for llms? evaluation on knowledge editing benchmark\n[Paper]\nBaolong Bi, Shenghua Liu, Yiwei Wang, Lingrui Mei, Junfeng Fang,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Shiyu Ni, Xueqi Cheng.\nICLR 2025\n2024\nSpider2-V: How Far Are Multimodal Agents From Automating Data Science and Engineering Workflows?\n[Paper]\nRuisheng Cao, Fangyu Lei, Haoyuan Wu, Jixuan Chen, Yeqiao Fu,\nHongcheng Gao\net al.\nNeurIPS 2024(Spotlight）\nLeveraging Catastrophic Forgetting to Develop Safe Diffusion Models against Malicious Finetuning\n[Paper]\nJiadong Pan*,\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Zongyu Wu, Tanghang Hu, Li Su, Qingming Huang, Liang Li.\nNeurIPS 2024(Spotlight）\nToken Merging for Training-Free Semantic Binding in Text-to-Image Synthesis\n[Paper]\nTaihang Hu, Linxuan Li, Joost van de Weijer,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Fahad Shahbaz Khan, Jian Yang, Ming-Ming Cheng, Kai Wang, Yaxing Wang.\nNeurIPS 2024\nAdaMoE: Token-Adaptive Routing with Null Experts for Mixture-of-Experts Language Models\n[Paper]\nZihao Zeng*, Yibo Miao*,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Hao Zhang, Zhijie Deng.\nFindings of\nEMNLP 2024\n.\nAdaptive Token Biaser: Knowledge Editing via Biasing Key Entities\n[Paper]\nBaolong Bi, Shenghua Liu, Yiwei Wang, Lingrui Mei,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Yilong Xu, Xueqi Cheng.\nFindings of\nEMNLP 2024\n.\nEfficient Detection of LLM-generated Texts with a Bayesian Surrogate Model\n[Paper]\nZhijie Deng*,\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Yibo Miao, Hao Zhang.\nFindings of\nACL 2024\n.\nUniversal Prompt Optimizer for Safe Text-to-Image Generation\n[Paper]\nZongyu Wu*,\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Yueze Wang, Xiang Zhang, Suhang Wang.\nNAACL 2024\nGenerative Pretraining in Multimodality\n[Paper]\nQuan Sun*, Qiying Yu*, Yufeng Cui*, Fan Zhang*, Xiaosong Zhang*, Yueze Wang,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Jingjing Liu, Tiejun Huang, Xinlong Wang\nICLR 2024\n2023\nRevisiting Out-of-distribution Robustness in NLP: Benchmark, Analysis, and LLMs Evaluations\n[Paper]\nLifan Yuan, Yangyi Chen, Ganqu Cui,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Fangyuan Zou, Xingyi Cheng, Heng Ji, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun.\nNeurIPS 2023 (D&B Track)\nFrom Adversarial Arms Race to Model-centric Evaluation: Motivating a Unified Automatic Robustness Evaluation Framework\n[Paper]\nYangyi Chen*,\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Ganqu Cui*, Lifan Yuan, Dehan Kong, Hanlu Wu, Ning Shi, Bo Yuan, Longtao Huang, Hui Xue, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun, Heng Ji.\nFindings of\nACL 2023\n.\n2022\nWhy Should Adversarial Perturbations be Imperceptible? Rethink the Research Paradigm in Adversarial NLP\n[Paper]\nYangyi Chen*,\nHongcheng Gao*\n, Ganqu Cui, Fanchao Qi, Longtao Huang, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun.\nEMNLP 2022\n.\nTextual Backdoor Attacks Can Be More Harmful via Two Simple Tricks\n[Paper]\nYangyi Chen*, Fanchao Qi*,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun.\nEMNLP 2022\n.\nExploring the Universal Vulnerability of Prompt-based Learning Paradigm\n[Paper]\nLei Xu, Yangyi Chen, Ganqu Cui,\nHongcheng Gao\n, Zhiyuan Liu.\nFindings of\nNAACL 2022\n.\n💻 Projects\nRobTest\n: an open-source toolkit for textual model robustness evaluation .\nSpider2-V\n: Spider2-V is a multimodal agent benchmark spanning across the entire data science and engineering workflow\nOpenAttack\n: an open-source Python-based textual adversarial attack toolkit.\nEmu\n: an open multimodal generalist for both image-to-text and text-to-image tasks.\n📄 Academic Services\nArea Chiar/Senior PC Member:\n2025: NeurIPS, CIKM\nReviewer/PC Member:\n2025: ICML, AISTATS, ICCV, ACL, ARR, ECAI\n2024: NeurIPS(\nTop Reviewer\n), ICLR, CVPR, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, ARR, Machine Learning, AISTATS.\n📖 Experiences\n2018.09 - 2023.06\n, Undergraduate Student at Chongqing University.\n2021.06 - 2023.06\n, Intern at THUNLP, Tsinghua University. Mentor:\nProf. Zhiyuan Liu\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
