    "homepage_text": "Yang Deng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYang Deng\nYang Deng\nPh.D. Student\nElectrical & Computer Engineering Department\nDuke University\nEmail: yang.deng [at] duke.edu\nAbout me\nI am an ECE Ph.D. student in Dr. Willie Padilla's group at Duke University. My primary research interests lie at the intersection of metamaterials and machine learning, particularly exploring the new generation of metamaterials through machine learning. Under this research goal, I have worked on the design, simulation, fabrication, and characterization of metamaterial devices. I am also interested in optimizing and accelerating innovation for future prototypes of metamaterials, realizing their substantial potential in energy, sensing, and communication applications.\nI started my journey in the states at the University of Rochester, where I received a B.S. in optical engineering. You can find my Curriculum Vitae\nhere\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nYang Deng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYang Deng\nYang Deng\nPh.D. Student\nElectrical & Computer Engineering Department\nDuke University\nEmail: yang.deng [at] duke.edu\nAbout me\nI am an ECE Ph.D. student in Dr. Willie Padilla's group at Duke University. My primary research interests lie at the intersection of metamaterials and machine learning, particularly exploring the new generation of metamaterials through machine learning. Under this research goal, I have worked on the design, simulation, fabrication, and characterization of metamaterial devices. I am also interested in optimizing and accelerating innovation for future prototypes of metamaterials, realizing their substantial potential in energy, sensing, and communication applications.\nI started my journey in the states at the University of Rochester, where I received a B.S. in optical engineering. You can find my Curriculum Vitae\nhere\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\n\n---\n\nYang Deng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYang Deng\nYang Deng\nPh.D. Student\nElectrical & Computer Engineering Department\nDuke University\nEmail: yang.deng [at] duke.edu\nAbout me\nI am an ECE Ph.D. student in Dr. Willie Padilla's group at Duke University. My primary research interests lie at the intersection of metamaterials and machine learning, particularly exploring the new generation of metamaterials through machine learning. Under this research goal, I have worked on the design, simulation, fabrication, and characterization of metamaterial devices. I am also interested in optimizing and accelerating innovation for future prototypes of metamaterials, realizing their substantial potential in energy, sensing, and communication applications.\nI started my journey in the states at the University of Rochester, where I received a B.S. in optical engineering. You can find my Curriculum Vitae\nhere\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
