    "homepage_text": "Dr Yanxi Li | Deep Learning Researcher\nDr Yanxi Li\nResearch Assistant Professorship (RAP) @ NTU Sg,\nPhD, Google PhD Fellow\nResearch Interests: Trustworthiness & Efficiency\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nEmployment\n9/2025 - Present\nResearch Assistant Professorship (RAP)\nAUMOVIO-NTU Corporate Lab (ANCL)\nNanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore\nEducation\n10/2021 - 2/2025\nDoctor of Philosophy (Computer Science)\nSchool of Computer Science, Faculty of Engineering\nUniversity of Sydney, NSW, Australia\nPublications\nJournal\n[1]\nAdversarially Robust Neural Architectures\n[\nLink\n] [\narXiv\n]\nNEW\nMinjing Dong,\nYanxi Li\n, Yunhe Wang & Chang Xu\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), 2025.\n[2]\nNeural Architecture Search via Proxy Validation\n[\nLink\n]\nYanxi Li\n, Minjing Dong, Yunhe Wang & Chang Xu\nIn IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), 2022.\n[3]\nNeural Architecture Tuning with Policy Adaptation\n[\nLink\n]\nYanxi Li\n, Minjing Dong, Yixing Xu, Yunhe Wang & Chang Xu\nIn Neurocomputing, 2022.\nConference\n[1]\nOptimizing Quantized Diffusion Models via Distillation with Cross-Timestep Error Correction\n[\nLink\n]\nNEW\nYanxi Li\n* & Chengbin Du*\nIn The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2025.\n[2]\nPosition: AI Scaling: From Up to Down and Out\n[\narXiv\n]\nNEW\nYunke Wang*,\nYanxi Li\n* & Chang Xu\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), Position Track, 2025.\n[3]\nState Space Models: A Naturally Robust Alternative to Transformers in Computer Vision\n[\nLink\n]\nNEW\nChengbin Du,\nYanxi Li\n& Chang Xu\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) R2-FM Workshop, 2025.\n[4]\nHarnessing Edge Information for Improved Robustness in Vision Transformers\n[\nLink\n]\nYanxi Li\n, Chengbin Du & Chang Xu\nIn The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2024.\n[5]\nNeural Architecture Retrieval\n[\nLink\n] [\narX