    "homepage_text": "Yue Zhou - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nOur Team\n>\nFaculty\n>\nYue Zhou\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nOur Team\n>\nFaculty\n>\nYue Zhou\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nOur Team\n>\nFaculty\n>\nYue Zhou\nYUE ZHOU\nzhou@utdallas.edu\nOffice: ECSW 4.355B\n800 West Campbell Rd.\nRichardson, TX 75080-3021\nGoogle Scholar Page\nLab Website\nAssociate PROFESSOR\nEducation\nPostdoc, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 2017\nPhD, the Pennsylvania State University, 2015\nMS, Nanjing University, 2011\nBS, Nanjing University, 2008\nResearch Interests\nEnergy storage, Energy conversion, Advanced manufacturing, Electronic materials and devices\nFive Most Recent Journal Publications, Book Chapters, and Books\nJ. Pokharel, A. Cresce, B. Pant, M. Y. Yang, A. Gurung, W. He, A. Baniya, B. Lamsal, Z. Yang, S. Gent, X. Xian, Y. Cao*, W. Goddard III*, K. Xu*, Y. Zhou*, “Manipulating the Diffusion Energy Barrier at the Lithium Metal Electrolyte Interface for Dendrite-free Long-life Batteries”, Nature Communications, Accepted, 2024.\nW. He, Y. Ren, B. Lamsal, J. Pokharel, K. Zhang, P. Kharel, J. J. Wu, X. Xian, Y. Cao*, Yue Zhou*, “Decreasing Water Activity by Tetrahydrofuran Electrolyte Additive for Highly Reversible Aqueous Zinc Metal Batteries”, ACS Applied Materials & Interfaces, 15, 6647 (2023).\nW. He; K. Chen; R. Pathak; M. Hummel; K. M. Reza; N. Ghimire; J. Pokharel; S. Lu; Z. Gu; Q. Qiao; Y. Zhou*, “High-Mass-Loading Sn-based Anode Boosted by Pseudocapacitance for Long-life Sodium-Ion Batteries”, Chemical Engineering Journal, 414, 128638 (2021).\nR. Pathak, K. Chen, A. Gurung, K. M. Reza, B. Bahrami, J. Pokharel, A. Baniya, W. He, F. Wu, Y. Zhou*, K. Xu*, Q. Qiao*, “Fluorinated Hybrid Solid Interface for Dendrite-Free Lithium Deposition”, Nature Communications, 11, 1 (2020).\nK. Chen, R. Pathak, A. Gurung, E. Adhamash, B. Bahrami, Q. He, A. Smirnova, J. J. Wu, Q. Qiao and Y. Zhou*, “Flower-Shaped Lithium Nitride as a Protective Layer via Facile Plasma Activation for Stable Lithium Metal Anodes”, Energy Storage Materials, 18, 389 (2019).\nMajor Honors and Awards\n2023 Jonsson School Assistant Professor Research Award\n2022 ONR Young Investigator Award\n2022 NSF Faculty Early Career Award\nOur Team\nFaculty\nStaff\nAffiliated Faculty\nIndustry Advisory Council\nJonsson School Dean’s Staff\nEngineering Tech Support Staff\nUT Dallas Faculty Staff Directory\nOpenings\nAssistant / Associate Professor in Mechanical Engineering – Robotics\nAssistant / Associate Professor Positions in Mechanical Engineering – Nuclear\nFaculty Orientation\nT.A. Orientation\n\n---\n\nContact - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nCONTACT\nMAIN OFFICE\nECSW 3.140 | 972-883-4660\ncontactME@utdallas.edu\nDong Qian\nAssociate Department Head for Graduate Programs\ndong.qian@utdallas.edu\nECSW 4.355F\n972-883-4890\nLu, Hongbing\nProfessor and Associate Department Head for Undergraduate Studies\nhongbing.lu@utdallas.edu\nECSW 4.355G\n972-883-4647\nDani Fadda\nFaculty Advisor\nfadda@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.150C\n972-883-4626\nRobert Hart\nFaculty Advisor\nrobert.hart@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.150A\n972-883-4225\nMeagan Garner\nSr. Graduate Academic Support Coordinator\nmeagan.garner@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.140\n972-883-4966\nBeth Powers\nGraduate Academic Support Coordinator\nbeth.powers@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.140\n972-883-4857\nAbout\nNews\nEvents\nAwards\nMake a Gift\nContact\n\n---\n\nContact - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nContact\nCONTACT\nMAIN OFFICE\nECSW 3.140 | 972-883-4660\ncontactME@utdallas.edu\nDong Qian\nAssociate Department Head for Graduate Programs\ndong.qian@utdallas.edu\nECSW 4.355F\n972-883-4890\nLu, Hongbing\nProfessor and Associate Department Head for Undergraduate Studies\nhongbing.lu@utdallas.edu\nECSW 4.355G\n972-883-4647\nDani Fadda\nFaculty Advisor\nfadda@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.150C\n972-883-4626\nRobert Hart\nFaculty Advisor\nrobert.hart@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.150A\n972-883-4225\nMeagan Garner\nSr. Graduate Academic Support Coordinator\nmeagan.garner@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.140\n972-883-4966\nBeth Powers\nGraduate Academic Support Coordinator\nbeth.powers@utdallas.edu\nECSW 2.140\n972-883-4857\nAbout\nNews\nEvents\nAwards\nMake a Gift\nContact\n\n---\n\nAbout - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nABOUT\nCreated nearly 20 years ago, the Department of Mechanical Engineering has been a major driver of the University’s rapid growth. Its degree programs are expressly tailored to meet the most current needs of the 21st century mechanical engineer, providing instruction in micro-thermodynamics, micro-fluidics and other key areas.\nSeven teaching labs\nfor undergraduates reinforce the engineering theory taught in lectures through hands-on experimentation.\nThe department offers both bachelor’s and master’s degrees and is committed to interdisciplinary research. Collaboration between mechanical engineers and electrical engineers is particularly promising, having already produced advances in micro-electro-mechanical systems. Robotics research is also expected to accelerate as mechanical engineers, electrical engineers, materials scientists and computer scientists collaborate.\nAbout\nNews\nEvents\nAwards\nMake a Gift\nContact\n\n---\n\nAbout - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nAbout\nABOUT\nCreated nearly 20 years ago, the Department of Mechanical Engineering has been a major driver of the University’s rapid growth. Its degree programs are expressly tailored to meet the most current needs of the 21st century mechanical engineer, providing instruction in micro-thermodynamics, micro-fluidics and other key areas.\nSeven teaching labs\nfor undergraduates reinforce the engineering theory taught in lectures through hands-on experimentation.\nThe department offers both bachelor’s and master’s degrees and is committed to interdisciplinary research. Collaboration between mechanical engineers and electrical engineers is particularly promising, having already produced advances in micro-electro-mechanical systems. Robotics research is also expected to accelerate as mechanical engineers, electrical engineers, materials scientists and computer scientists collaborate.\nAbout\nNews\nEvents\nAwards\nMake a Gift\nContact\n\n---\n\nBioengineering and Mechanical Engineering UTDesign Expo - Mechanical Engineering | The University of Texas at Dallas\nSkip to Main Content.\nSkip to Main Navigation.\nSkip to Main Footer.\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nEvents\n>\nBioengineering and Mechanical Engineering UTDesign Expo\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nEvents\n>\nBioengineering and Mechanical Engineering UTDesign Expo\nUT Dallas\n>\nMechanical Engineering\n>\nEvents\n>\nBioengineering and Mechanical Engineering UTDesign Expo\nBioengineering and Mechanical Engineering UTDesign Expo\nFriday, May 5\n(3:30 p.m. – 5 p.m.)\nSynergy Park North (SPN) 1.2\nThe Departments of Bioengineering and Mechanical Engineering invite you to attend the UTDesign Expo on Friday, May 5, 2023 from 3:30-5pm in the UTDesign Studio at Synergy Park North (SPN).\nThe Expo is open to the public and will showcase the capstone projects completed by student teams in the mechanical engineering senior design course. At the Expo, each team will have an exhibit showing the prototype they designed to solve their specific engineering problem. The Expo is conducted in a project fair format, so visitors are welcome to come at any time to view the projects and speak with the teams.\nAbout\nNews\nEvents\nAwards\nMake a Gift\nContact"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yunfan Yang::https://yunfan1202.github.io/": {
