    "homepage_text": "Xinyu Yuan's Homepage\nXinyu Yuan\nPh.D. student, College of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang University\nEmail: yxy5315@gmail.com\nI am pursuing my Ph.D. at\nZhejiang University\n, where I am part of the\nArcLab\nresearch group \n              led by Prof.\nWenzhi Chen\n.\nBefore that, I received my M.Eng. and B.Eng. from the School of Artificial Intelligence at\nHefei University of Technology\nand School of Information and Artificial Intelligence \n              at\nAnhui Agricultual University\nrespectively, advised by Assoc. Prof.\nYan Qiao\n.\nMy primary research interests includes network systems, machine learning, AI-generated content (AIGC) and embodied intelligence.\n              I am actively working on the (networking) sevices computing and applications empowered by machine learning.\n              I am also working on studying of the powerful generative models, e.g., diffusions and LLMs.\nDownload my\nCV\nPublications\nLearning-based Sketches for Frequency Estimation in Data Streams without Ground Truth\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao*, Meng Li, Zhenchun Wei, Cuiying Feng, Zonghui Wang* and Wenzhi Chen\nTo appear in IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering\n(TKDE)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nRouting-Oblivious and Data-Efficient Network Tomography with Flow-based Generative Model\nYan Qiao, Minyue Li,\nXinyu Yuan\n, Kui Wu, Cuiying Feng, Meng Li* and Kun Xie\nTo appear in IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n(TON)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDivide, Harmonize, Then Conquer It: Shooting Multi-Commodity Flow Problems with Multimodal Language Models\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao, Zonghui Wang* and Wenzhi Chen*\nTo appear in International Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR)\n, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nLᴍᴛᴇ: Putting the \"Reasoning\" into WAN Traffic Engineering with Language Models\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao*, Zonghui Wang*, Meng Li and Wenzhi Chen\nTo appear in IEEE International Conference on Computer Communications\n(INFOCOM)\n, Tokyo, Japan, 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDiffusion Models Meet Network Management: Improving Traffic Matrix Analysis with Diffusion-based Approach\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao*, Zhenchun Wei, Zeyu Zhang, Minyue Li, Pei Zhao, Rongyao Hu and Wenjing Li\nIEEE Transactions on Network and Service Management\n(TNSM)\n, April, 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nAutoTomo: Learning-Based Traffic Estimator Incorporating Network Tomography\nYan Qiao*, Kui Wu and\nXinyu Yuan\nIEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking\n(TON)\n, December, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDiffusion-TS: Interpretable Diffusion for General Time Series Generation\nXinyu Yuan\nand Yan Qiao*\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR)\n, Vienna, Austria, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nRouting-Oblivious Network Tomography with Flow-Based Generative Model\nYan Qiao*,\nXinyu Yuan\nand Kui Wu\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Communications\n(INFOCOM)\n, Vancouver, Canada, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nUnsupervised Anomaly Detection for Multivariate Time Series using Diffusion Model\nRongyao Hu,\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao*, BenChu Zhang and Pei Zhao\nIEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing\n(ICASSP)\n, Seoul, Korea, 2024\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nTraffic Matrix Estimation based on Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Model\nXinyu Yuan\n, Yan Qiao*, Pei Zhao, Rongyao Hu and Benchu Zhang\nIEEE Symposium on Computers and Communications\n(ISCC)\n, Tunis, Tunisia, 2023\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nWorkshop Papers and Preprints\nPatents\nInternet of Things Data Anomaly Detection Model Training Method, Anomaly Detection Method and System\nYan Qiao,\nXinyu Yuan\n, Benchu Zhang et al.\nCN115589608A, 2023\nNetwork Traffic Matrix Estimation and Model Training Method and System based on Deep Learning\nYan Qiao,\nXinyu Yuan\n, Zhenchun Wei et al.\nCN116319378A, 2023\nDiffusion Model-based Missing Network Traffic Matrix Filling Method and System\nYan Qiao,\nXinyu Yuan\n, Zhenchun Wei et al.\nCN118555215A, 2024\nServices\nReviewer:\nNeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, IEEE Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), IEEE Transactions on Network and Service Management (TNSM), Computer Networks (CN), Knowledge-Based Systems (KBS)\nContact Me\nyxy5315 at gmail dot com"
