    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/Guozheng-Ma",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Guozheng Ma's Homepage\nServices\nAwards\nTalks\nPublications\nNews\nBio\nGuozheng Ma\nPhD Student\nNanyang Technological University\nGUOZHENG001 (at) e.ntu.edu.sg\nShort Bio\nCurrently, I am a second-year PhD student at\nNanyang Technological University\n, working under the supervision of\nDacheng Tao\n.\nPreviously, I completed my master's studies and began my research journey at\nTsinghua University\n. Earlier, I obtained my bachelor's degree at\nHunan University\n, where I cherished four wonderful years at the foothills of Yuelu Mountain.\nMy research goal is to unlock the true potential of\nDeep Reinforcement Learning\ntoward practical real-world deployment. \nThis requires RL agents capable of offline-online cooperation, handling multiple tasks, and never stopping learning in open-ended environments. \nTo realize this vision, I currently focus on investigating the fundamental challenges inherent in DRL, particularly optimization pathologies, scalability limitations and exploration inefficiencies.\nMeanwhile, I view RL as a paradigm for understanding and developing intelligence rather than just a technique.\nThis inspires my interest in exploring its potential across domains, from large reasoning models and embodied agents to psychology and social sciences.\nGreatness cannot be planned, so I play with joyful explorations!\nNews\n[2025.05]\nTwo papers accepted at\nICML 2025\n, discussing DRL scalability on Online RL and Multi-Task DT.\n[2024.08]\nKicking off my PhD journey at\nNTU, Singapore\n. Keep going on the road!\n[2024.05]\nHappy to receive\nICLR Financial Assistance Award\n. See you in Vienna!\n[2024.01]\nOur paper investigating\nPlasticity Loss in VRL\nhas been accepted by\nICLR 2024\n.\n[2023.12]\nOur paper about\nVRL's Generalization\ngot an oral at\nAAMAS\n. Congratulations to\nLu Li\n!\n[2023.09]\nOur paper on\n'What makes a effective DA for sample-efficient VRL?'\nwas accepted to\nNeurIPS 2023\n.\nShow more\n[2023.07]\nHonored to be named as an AI Safety and Alignment Fellow by\nConcordia AI\n!\n[2022.10]\nWe released a comprehensive survey of\nDA in VRL\n.\n[2022.04]\nOur\nTLDA\nwas accepted to\nIJCAI 2022\n. The fascinating VRL journey began!\nSelected Publications\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nICML 2025\nNetwork Sparsity Unlocks the Scaling Potential of Deep Reinforcement Learning\nGuozheng Ma*\n, Lu Li*, Zilin Wang, Li Shen, Pierre-Luc Bacon, Dacheng Tao\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n(ICML)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTex\nOral (Top 1%)\nICLR 2024\nRevisiting Plasticity in Visual Reinforcement Learning: Data, Modules and Training Stages\nGuozheng Ma*\n, Lu Li*, Sen Zhang, Zixuan Liu, Zhen Wang, Yixin Chen, Li Shen, Xueqian Wang, Dacheng Tao\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(ICLR)\n, 2024.\nPDF\nCode\n机器之心\nBibTex\nNeurIPS 2023\nLearning Better with Less: Effective Augmentation for Sample-Efficient Visual Reinforcement Learning\nGuozheng Ma\n, Linrui Zhang, Haoyu Wang, Lu Li, Zilin Wang, Zhen Wang, Li Shen, Xueqian Wang, Dacheng Tao\nNeural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 2023.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTex\nIJCV\nA Comprehensive Survey of Data Augmentation in Visual Reinforcement Learning\nGuozheng Ma\n, Zhen Wang, Zhecheng Yuan, Xueqian Wang, Bo Yuan, Dacheng Tao\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\n(IJCV)\n, 2025.\nPDF\nCode\nBibTex\nInvited Talks\nRevisiting Plasticity in Visual Reinforcement Learning: Data, Modules and Training Stages.\nYouth PhD Talk,\nAI TIME\n,\nMarch 2024 |\nRecording (in Chinese)\nThe 6th AI Academic Forum of Beijing Universities,\nApril 2024\nHonors and Awards\nExcellent Graduates\n, Beijing, 2024.\nICLR Financial Assistance Award\n, 2024.\nORDOS Scholarship\n, Tsinghua University, 2023.\nAI Safety and Alignment Fellowship\n, Concordia AI, 2023.\nProvincial Excellent Graduates\n, Hunan Province, 2021.\nFirst Prize of Outstanding Undergraduate Thesis\n, Hunan University, 2021.\nWeisheng Scholarship\n, Hunan University, 2020.\nXiongXiaoge Scholarship\n, Hunan University, 2019\nNational Scholarship\n, Ministry of Education of China, 2019\nAcademic Services\nConference Reviewers\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) 2024-2025\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) 2024-2025\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) 2025\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) 2025\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV) 2025\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) 2024\nConference on Lifelong Learning Agents (CoLLAs) 2025\nJournal Reviewers\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP)\nWorkshop PCs\nNeurIPS 2025:\nARLET Workshop\n.\nICLR 2025:\nMCDC Workshop\n.\nShow more\nNeurIPS 2024:\nContinual FoMo Workshop\n,\nSoLaR Workshop\n.\nICML 2024:\nTiFA Workshop\n,\nAutoRL Workshop\n,\nDMLR Workshop\n.\nNeurIPS 2023:\nSoLaR Workshop\n.\nICML 2023:\nDMLR Workshop\n.\nWorkshop Organizers\nNeurIPS 2025:\nEmbodied World Models for Decision Making Workshop\n.\nCommunity Builders\nCo-founder,\nReinforcement Learning Evolution Foundation\n."
  },
