    "homepage_text": "Guangchen Lan\nGuangchen\nLan\nGuangchen (Eric) Lan\nPh.D. Candidate\nPurdue University, USA\nlan44[at]purdue[dot]edu\nHey! 👋 I am a PhD candidate at\nPurdue University\n.\nMy research focuses on Reinforcement Learning (\nRL\n) Theory and Foundation Model (e.g.,\nLLM\n) Post-Training, especially Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR) & Reinforcement Learning with Unverifiable Rewards (e.g., rubric rewards and RLHF).\nI am actively looking for full-time (2026) opportunities in RL/Post-Training/LLM related fields. Feel free to reach me via email lan44[AT]purdue[DOT]edu.\nNews\nSep 06, 2025\nHello, World! The new personal website has been launched.\nSelected Publications\nTMLR 2025\nMaPPO: Maximum a Posteriori Preference Optimization with Prior Knowledge\nGuangchen Lan\n, Sipeng Zhang, Tianle Wang, Yuwei Zhang, Daoan Zhang, Xinpeng Wei, and\n4 more authors\n(Featured by HuggingFace 🤗 Daily Papers) TMLR\n, 2025\nBib\nPDF\n@article\n{\nlan2025mappo\n,\ntitle\n=\n{{MaPPO}: Maximum a Posteriori Preference Optimization with Prior Knowledge}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Lan, Guangchen and Zhang, Sipeng and Wang, Tianle and Zhang, Yuwei and Zhang, Daoan and Wei, Xinpeng and Pan, Xiaoman and Zhang, Hongming and Han, Dong-Jun and Brinton, Christopher G}\n,\njournal\n=\n{(Featured by HuggingFace 🤗 Daily Papers) TMLR}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\n}\nNeurIPS 2025\nContextual Integrity in LLMs via Reasoning and Reinforcement Learning\nGuangchen Lan\n, Huseyin A Inan, Sahar Abdelnabi, Janardhan Kulkarni, Lukas Wutschitz, Reza Shokri, and\n2 more authors\nIn NeurIPS\n, 2025\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nlan2025contextual\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Contextual Integrity in {LLMs} via Reasoning and Reinforcement Learning}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Lan, Guangchen and Inan, Huseyin A and Abdelnabi, Sahar and Kulkarni, Janardhan and Wutschitz, Lukas and Shokri, Reza and Brinton, Christopher G and Sim, Robert}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{NeurIPS}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\n}\nICLR 2025\nAsynchronous Federated Reinforcement Learning with Policy Gradient Updates: Algorithm Design and Convergence Analysis\nGuangchen Lan\n, Dong-Jun Han, Abolfazl Hashemi, Vaneet Aggarwal, and Christopher G Brinton\nIn ICLR\n, 2025\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nlan2025asynchronous\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Asynchronous Federated Reinforcement Learning with Policy Gradient Updates: Algorithm Design and Convergence Analysis}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Lan, Guangchen and Han, Dong-Jun and Hashemi, Abolfazl and Aggarwal, Vaneet and Brinton, Christopher G}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{ICLR}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\n}\nNeurIPS 2023\nImproved Communication Efficiency in Federated Natural Policy Gradient via ADMM-based Gradient Updates\nGuangchen Lan\n, Han Wang, James Anderson, Christopher Brinton, and Vaneet Aggarwal\nIn NeurIPS\n, 2023\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nlan2023improved\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Improved Communication Efficiency in Federated Natural Policy Gradient via ADMM-based Gradient Updates}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Lan, Guangchen and Wang, Han and Anderson, James and Brinton, Christopher and Aggarwal, Vaneet}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{NeurIPS}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\n}\nIEEE Trans\nCommunication-Efficient Federated Learning for Resource-Constrained Edge Devices\nGuangchen Lan\n, Xiao-Yang Liu, Yijing Zhang, and Xiaodong Wang\nIEEE Transactions on Machine Learning in Communications and Networking\n, 2023\nBib\nPDF\n@article\n{\nlan2023communication\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Communication-Efficient Federated Learning for Resource-Constrained Edge Devices}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Lan, Guangchen and Liu, Xiao-Yang and Zhang, Yijing and Wang, Xiaodong}\n,\njournal\n=\n{IEEE Transactions on Machine Learning in Communications and Networking}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\n}\n\n---\n\nCV | Guangchen Lan\nCV\nBasics\nName\nGuangchen (Eric) Lan\nEmail\nlan44@purdue.edu\nPhone\n+1 (917) 371-1980\nUrl\nhttps://ericglan.github.io/\nSummary\nA PhD candidate at Purdue University, working on AI research.\nWork\n2025.08 - 2025.11\nSeattle, WA\nAmazon\nApplied Scientist Intern @ Stores Foundational AI\n☕️ Mentor: Dr. Lian Xiong, Dr. Lihong Li\n🚀 Topic: Reinforcement Learning with Contextual Rubric Rewards for LLMs.\nAlternating Reinforcement Learning with Contextual Rubric Rewards: Beyond the Scalarization Strategy.\n2025.03 - 2025.05\nRedmond, WA\nMicrosoft Research\nResearch Scientist Intern\n☕️ Mentor: Dr. Huseyin A. Inan, Dr. Robert Sim\n🚀 Topic: LLM Agent Safety via Reasoning & Reinforcement Learning.\nContextual Integrity in LLMs via Reasoning and Reinforcement Learning. NeurIPS 2025.\n📄 Media Coverage: Microsoft Blog\n2024.05 - 2024.08\nBellevue, WA\nTencent America\nResearch Scientist Intern @ Tencent AI Lab\n☕️ Mentor: Dr. Xiaoman Pan, Dr. Hongming Zhang, Dr. Dong Yu\n🚀 Topic: RLHF for LLM & Diffusion Alignment.\nBridging SFT and DPO for Diffusion Model Alignment with Self-Sampling Preference Optimization. TMLR.\nEducation\n2022.08 - 2026.06\nWest Lafayette, IN\nPurdue University\nPh.D.\nArtificial Intelligence\n2020.07 - 2022.02\nNew York, NY\nColumbia University\nMaster of Science\nMachine Learning\n2019.06 - 2020.07\nBerkeley, CA\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nBachelor of Engineering\nEngineering Physics\n2016.08 - 2020.07\nXi'an, CN\nXi'an Jiaotong University\nBachelor of Engineering\nApplied Physics\nAcademic\nReviewer\nNeurIPS 2025, 2024 (Top Reviewer)\nICLR 2024 - 2026\nICML 2025 - 2026\nACL 2026\nICCV 2025\nAISTATS 2024 - 2026\nAAAI 2024 - 2026\nIEEE Global Communications Conference 2023\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR)\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing\nIEEE Transactions on Networking\nIEEE Transactions on Signal Processing\nIEEE Journal on Selected Areas in Communications (Reinforcement Learning track)\nIEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing (Reinforcement Learning track)\nAwards\n2025\nPurdue Graduate Student Government Grant\nPurdue University\n2025\nICLR Grant\nICLR\n2024\nNeurIPS Top Reviewer\nNeurIPS\n2023\nNeurIPS Scholar Award\nNeurIPS\n2020\nNikola Tesla Electrical Engineering Scholarship\nColumbia University\n2020\nOutstanding Student Paper Award Finalist on 2020 IEEE MEMS Conference\nIEEE\n2020\nHonor Student (Top 0.3%)\nXi’an Jiaotong University\n2019\n2nd prize as a team leader in ‘Challenge Cup’ National University Students Academic Science 2019 (Top 0.1%)\nXi’an Jiaotong University\n2017, 2018\nNational Scholarship (The highest honor of undergraduate students in China)\nXi’an Jiaotong University\nProjects\n2021.10 - 2023.04\nElegantRL\nElegantRL implements several model-free deep reinforcement learning (DRL) algorithms as the DRL agent layer for FinRL.\nCore Contributor\nSkills\nProgramming Languages\nPython\nC/C++\nJavaScript/TypeScript\nHTML/CSS\nSolidity\nMATLAB\nLaTex\nTools\nVERL\nPyTorch\nTensorFlow\nRay/RLlib\nSklearn\nNumPy\nPandas\nMySQL\nMongoDB\nGit/GitHub\nUnix/Linux Shell\nDocker\nAWS\nAzure\nGoogle Cloud\nHugging Face\nDeepSpeed\nMegatron-LM\nFSDP\nLanguages\nEnglish\nBilingual\nMandarin Chinese 中文\nNative\nKorean 한국어\nElementary\nSpanish Español\nElementary\nInterests\ncasual\nChess (Provincial Silver Medal)\nBoard Games\nPowerlifting (PR: Deadlift 445 lbs.)\nBodybuilding\nSkiing\nHiking"
