    "homepage_text": "About Me - Rui Lu\nRui Lu\nPh.D. Student at Tsinghua University\nFollow\nBeijing, China\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nThis is the homepage of Rui Lu (卢睿) from Tsinghua University. I will be on job market at Oct 2026! Please contact me if you are interested.\nBiography\nI am a fifth-year Ph.D. student at the Department of Automation at Tsinghua University, advised by\nProf. Gao Huang\n. Prior to that, I received my Bachelor’s degree from Yao Class, the Institute of Interdisciplinary Information Sciences. I was lucky to be advised by\nYang Yuan\nfor my undergraduate thesis. I was also a visiting student at Berkeley BAIR Center in 2019 under the supervision of\nJitendra Malik\nand visiting scholar at Princeton University in 2024 supervised by\nMengdi Wang\n.\nResearch Interest\nMy research interests are broadly in Machine Learning, Computer Vision, and Reinforcement Learning. In post-GPT era, I am also interested in developing LLMs to discover new knowledge that can give inspiration and insight to human. The main focus and ultimate goal of my research is to develop a principled theory for understanding deep learning’s effectiveness, functionality, and limitations. I am also interested in designing better and faster learning algorithms/architectures.\nNews\nOur paper\nDoes Reinforcement Learning Really Incentivize Reasoning Capacity in LLMs Beyond the Base Model?\nis awarded\nBest Paper Runner Up\nat NeurIPS 2025 and\nBest Paper\non AI4Math workshop at ICML 2025!\nOur project\nHow Far is Video Generation from World Model?\nis released and achieves more than 500k views on X(Twitter).\nOur paper “Efficienttrain: Exploring generalized curriculum learning for training visual backbones” is accepted by ICCV 2023!\nOur paper “Provable General Function Class Representation Learning in Multitask Bandits and MDPs” is accepted as\nSpotlight\nin NeuRIPS 2022!\nContact Me\nr-lu21 [AT] mails [dot] tsinghua [dot] edu [dot] cn\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Rui Lu\nRui Lu\nPh.D. Student at Tsinghua University\nFollow\nBeijing, China\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nEducation\nB.S. in Yao Class, IIIS, Tsinghua University, 2016 - 2021\nGPA 3.74 / 4.00, Rank 12 / 38\nPh.D. in Department of Automation, Tsinghua University, 2021 - Now\nGPA 4.00 / 4.00, Rank 1 / 156\nWork experience\nSummer 2019: Intern Student\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nTopic: Indoor 3D detection & Pose Estimation\nSupervisor: Jitendra Malik\nFall 2021 - Fall 2022: Intern Researcher\nSenseTime Company\nTopic: Visual Backbones Research\nSupervisor: Xizhou Zhu\nPublications\nOn the power of multitask representation learning in linear MDP\nOn the Integration of Self-Attention and Convolution\nProvable General Function Class Representation Learning in Multitask Bandits and MDPs\nEfficient-train: Exploring generalized curriculum learning for training visual backbones\nUnderstanding, Predicting and Better Resolving Q-Value Divergence in Offline-RL\nAdaNAT: Exploring Adaptive Policy for Token-Based Image Generation\nDoes Reinforcement Learning Really Incentivize Reasoning Capacity in LLMs Beyond The Base Model?\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant of Pattern Recognition and Machine Learning"
  },
