    "homepage_text": "Yue Gao\nYue Gao\nYue Gao\nyuegao@cs.stanford.edu\nMy name is pronounced as\nyoo-eh\n.\nI am a PhD student in the\nStanford Vision and Learning Lab\n, Department of\nComputer Science\n, at\nStanford University\n.\n              I am advised by\nProf. Jiajun Wu\nand\nProf. Juan Carlos Niebles\n, and my research focuses on dynamic models.\n              I also had the privilege of being advised by\nProf. Bo Zhu\n.\nPreviously, I worked as a researcher at\nMicrosoft Research\n, focusing on video generation and editing.\n              I earned my M.S. with distinction in research from\nPeking University\n, where I specialized in image generation under the supervision of\nProf. Zhouhui Lian\n.\nI am always open to research collaborations. Please feel free to contact me.\nDynamic Physical World\nUnderstanding\nand\nPrediction\nMy primary research interests lie in\ncomputer vision\nand\ncomputer graphics\n. Specifically, I aim to enable computers to\n        understand and predict the physical world by integrating advanced algorithms, such as perception and generative models, with foundational\n        knowledge from physics.\nPublications\n* Equal contribution; † Corresponding author\nSurfPhase: 3D Interfacial Dynamics in Two-Phase Flows from Sparse Videos\nYue Gao*\n,\nHong-Xing Yu*\n,\nSanghyeon Chang\n,\nQianxi Fu\n,\nBo Zhu\n,\nYoonjin Won\n,\nJuan Carlos Niebles\n,\nJiajun Wu\narXiv, 2026\npdf\n/\nwebsite\n/\ncode\nFluidNexus: 3D Fluid Reconstruction and Prediction from a Single Video\nYue Gao*\n,\nHong-Xing Yu*\n,\nBo Zhu\n,\nJiajun Wu\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2025\nOral Presentation\npdf\n/\nwebsite\n/\ncode\nImplicit Motion Function\nYue Gao\n,\nJiahao Li\n,\nLei Chu\n,\nYan Lu\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2024\npdf\n/\nsupp\n/\nwebsite\nHigh-Fidelity and Freely Controllable Talking Head Video Generation\nYue Gao\n,\nYuan Zhou\n,\nJinglu Wang\n,\nXiao Li\n,\nXiang Ming\n,\nYan Lu\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2023\narXiv\n/\npdf\n/\nsupp\n/\nwebsite\nLearning to Prompt for Open-Vocabulary Object Detection With Vision-Language Model\nYu Du, Fangyun Wei, Zihe Zhang, Miaojing Shi,\nYue Gao\n, Guoqi Li\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2022\narXiv\n/\ncode\nAligning Pretraining for Detection via Object-Level Contrastive Learning\nFangyun Wei*\n,\nYue Gao*\n,\nZhirong Wu\n,\nHan Hu\n,\nStephen Lin\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n, 2021\nSpotlight\narXiv\n/\ncode\nHigh-Fidelity and Arbitrary Face Editing\nYue Gao\n,\nFangyun Wei\n,\nJianmin Bao\n,\nShuyang Gu\n,\nDong Chen\n,\nFang Wen\n,\nZhouhui Lian†\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2021\narXiv\n/\nwebsite\nAttribute2Font: Creating Fonts You Want From Attributes\nYizhi Wang*\n,\nYue Gao*\n,\nZhouhui Lian†\nSIGGRAPH, ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG)\n, 2020\narXiv\n/\ncode\nArtistic Glyph Image Synthesis via One-Stage Few-Shot Learning\nYue Gao*\n, Yuan Guo*,\nZhouhui Lian†\n, Yingmin Tang, Jianguo Xiao\nSIGGRAPH Asia, ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG)\n, 2019\narXiv\n/\ncode\nEducation\nStanford University\nPh.D.\nin Computer Science\nStanford Vision and Learning Lab\nSep. 2025 - Present\nStanford University\nRemote Visitor\nStanford Vision and Learning Lab\nAdvisor:\nProf. Jiajun Wu\n,\nProf. Bo Zhu\nMentor:\nKoven Yu\nMar. 2024 - Dec. 2024\nPeking University\nMaster of Natural Science\nin Computer Applied Technology\nAwards:\nExcellent Graduate\nMerit Student\nOutstanding Student of Wangxuan Institute of Computer Technology\nAdvisor:\nProf. Zhouhui Lian\nSep. 2018 - Jun. 2021\nWork\nMicrosoft Research\nResearcher\nJun. 2021 - Mar. 2025\nMicrosoft Research\nResearch Intern\nAward:\nStar of Tomorrow Award (Outstanding Intern)\nMentors:\nFangyun Wei\n,\nJianmin Bao\n,\nDong Chen\nJun. 2020 - Jun. 2021\nApple AI/ML\nResearch Intern\nMentors:\nSam Li\n, Xiaoxu Wu,\nShiyu Li\n.\nDec. 2019 - May 2020\nAcademic Service\nReviewer:\nConferences:\nCVPR (Outstanding Reviewer 2025)\n, ICCV, ECCV, SIGGRAPH, ICML, AAAI, ACM Multimedia, IJCAI, WACV, BMVC\nJournals:\nTOG, TPAMI, IJCV, ACM TOMM, IEEE TMM\nThis website is modified from\nGeorgia Gkioxari\n."
