    "homepage_text": "Zhiyuan Zhang - Research\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZhiyuan Zhang\nResearch\nResearch Interest\n:\nErgodic Theory and Dynamical Systems\nPapers and preprints\n:\n1.\nOn mixing diffeomorphisms of the disc\n, with Artur Avila, Bassam Fayad, Patrice Le Calvez, Disheng Xu, in Inventiones mathematicae 220, 673-714 (2020).\n2. On the spectrums of ergodic Schrodinger operators with finitely valued potentials, in Bulletin de la Société Mathématique de France 145 (2017), no. 2, 295-304.\n3.\nBallistic transport and absolute continuity of one-frequency Schrödinger operators\n, with Zhiyan Zhao, in Communications in Mathematical Physics. May 2017, Volume 351, Issue 3, pp 877-921.\n4.\nOn stable transitivity of finitely generated group of volume preserving diffeomorphisms\n,  in Ergodic Theory and Dynamical Systems.  Volume 39, Issue 2, February 2019, pp. 554-576.\n5.\nOn the smooth dependence of SRB measures for partially hyperbolic systems\n, in Communications in Mathematical Physics. Februrary 2018, Volume 358, Issue 1, pp 45-79.\n6.\nAn effective version of Katok's horseshoe theorem for conservative $C^2$ surface diffeomorphisms\n, with B. Fayad, in Journal of Modern Dynamics, 11 (2017), 425-445.\n7.\n$C^{r}-$prevalence of stable ergodicity for a class of partially hyperbolic systems\n, with Martin Leguil, in J. Eur. Math. Soc. 24, No. 9,\n3379-3438 (2022).\n8.\nOn topological genericity of the mode-locking phenomenon\n, in Mathematische Annalen, 376, 707-728 (2020).\n9.\nThe rigidity of pseudo-rotations on the two-torus and a question of Norton-Sullivan\n, with Jian Wang, in Geometric and Functional Analysis. October 2018, Volume 28, Issue 5, pp 1487-1516.\n10.\nDensity of mode-locking property for quasi-periodically forced Arnold circle maps\n, with J. Wang, in Ergodic Theory and Dynamical Systems, Volume 44, Issue 12, December 2024, pp. 3645-3680.\n11.\n$C^1$ actions on manifolds by lattices in Lie groups\n, with Aaron Brown and Danijela Damjanović, in Compositio Mathematica\n, 158 (2022), 529–549.\n1\n2\n.\nSmooth mixing Anosov flows in dimension three are exponentially mixing\n, with Masato Tsujii,\nin\nAnnals of\nMathematic\ns, 197 (2023), Issue 1, 65-158.\n13.\nOn bifurcation of statistical properties of partially hyperbolic endomorphisms\n, with M\n.\nTsujii,\nin\nErgodic Theory and Dynamical Systems\n, Volume 44, Issue 3, March 2024, pp. 933-944.\n14.\nOn pseudo-rotations of the annulus with generic rotation number\n, with Barney Bramham, to appear in Journal of Modern Dynamics.\n1\n5\n.\nGeometric properties of partially hyperbolic measures and applications to measure rigidity\n, with Alex Eskin and Rafael Potrie\n, arXiv.\n16.\nZimmer's conjecture for non-split semisimple Lie groups\n, with Jinpeng An and A. Brown\n,\narXiv.\nWork in progress\n:\n17. Limit distributions for simultaneous Diophantine approximations, with Dmitry Dolgopyat and B. Fayad.\nSurvey article\n:\nRecent results and open questions on pseudo-rotations, with B. Bramham, in book <<A vision for dynamics in the 21st century>>\nThe legac\ny of Anatole Katok.\nBased on a memorial conference, Bedlewo,\nPoland, August 2019.\nDamjanovic, Danijela (ed.) et al.\nCambridge: Cambridge University Press. 67-93 (2024).\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
