    "homepage_text": "Yong Jiang - Academic Homepage\nYong Jiang\nSenior Algorithm Expert, Ph.D.\nTongyi Lab, Alibaba Group\nHangzhou, China\nEmail:\njiangyong.ml@gmail.com\n|\nGoogle Scholar\nI am a Senior Algorithm Expert at Tongyi Lab, Alibaba Group, where I\nlead a team\nbuilding the next generation of deep research agents. My research focuses on\nLarge Language Models (LLMs)\nand\nAgents\n.\nI received my Ph.D. in Computer Science from University of Chinese Academy of Sciences & ShanghaiTech University in 2019. I was a Visiting Scholar at UC Berkeley in 2016.\nI have published\n150+ papers\nin top-tier conferences including ACL, EMNLP, NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, and AAAI. My work has received multiple best paper awards and outstanding paper awards.\nNews\n[Jan 2026]\n12 Agent-related papers accepted to ICLR 2026!\n[Sep 2025]\nLaunched\nTongyi DeepResearch\n- achieved 17,000+ GitHub stars and ranked #1 on GitHub trending for two weeks!\n[Sep 2025]\nSelected for Hangzhou City Youth Assault Team (杭州市市级青年突击队).\n[Nov 2024]\nSelected for Zhejiang Province Innovation and Effectiveness Competition Gold Award (浙江省创新创效大赛金奖), ranked 1st in the province.\n[Oct 2024]\nReceived NLPCC 2024 Outstanding Paper Award!\n[May 2024]\nSelected as Alibaba Group May 4th Youth Representative for New Quality Productivity (阿里巴巴集团五四青年-新质生产力).\n[Jun 2023]\nReceived ACL 2023 Outstanding Paper Award (39/1074)!\n[May 2023]\nWinner of 9 SemEval 2023 Shared Sub-Tasks and Best System Paper Award!\nResearch\nMy research focuses on\nRetrieval-Augmented Language Models\n,\nAgentic AI Systems\n, and\nKnowledge-Enhanced NLP\n.\n                I am particularly interested in developing autonomous agents that can perform complex reasoning and research tasks.\nCurrent Research Directions:\nDeep Research Agents:\nBuilding autonomous agents capable of conducting comprehensive research across web-scale information (e.g.,\nTongyi DeepResearch\n, WebWalker, WebSailor, AgentFold)\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG):\nDeveloping advanced RAG systems for AI search, query rewriting, and semantic ranking\nKnowledge-Enhanced Entity Understanding:\nImproving named entity recognition, relation extraction, and entity linking through external knowledge retrieval\nAgentic Intelligence:\nScaling agents via continual pre-training and environment scaling toward general agentic intelligence\nKey Projects:\n🔬\nTongyi DeepResearch\n:\nOpen-source deep research agent suite with 17,000+ GitHub stars, ranked #1 on GitHub trending\n🔍\nQwen AI Search\n:\nFull-stack AI search system serving millions of daily API calls with +18% relevance improvement\n🤖 17 Specialized Agents:\nIncluding ZeroSearch, WebWalker, WebSailor, WebWeaver, AgentFold, and more\nSelected Publications\nFor a complete list of publications, please visit\nall publications\nor my\nGoogle Scholar\nprofile.\nLoading publications...\nAwards and Honors\n2025:\nHangzhou City Youth Assault Team (杭州市市级青年突击队) - 1/15 in Hangzhou\n2024:\nZhejiang Province Innovation and Effectiveness Competition Gold Award - 1st in the province (1/27)\n2024:\nAlibaba Group May 4th Youth Representative - New Quality Productivity\n2024:\nNLPCC 2024 Outstanding Paper Award (6/194)\n2023:\nWinner of 9 SemEval 2023 Shared Sub-Tasks (1/30+ competitors)\n2023:\nACL 2023 Outstanding Paper Award (39/1074)\n2023:\nSemEval 2023 Best System Paper Award (1/301 accepted papers)\n2022:\nWinner of 10 SemEval 2022 Shared Sub-Tasks (1/30+ competitors)\n2022:\nSemEval 2022 Best System Paper Award (1/221 accepted papers)\nAcademic Services\nArea Chair:\nEMNLP 2024/2025, NAACL 2024/2025, IJCAI 2024, ARR\nReviewer:\nICLR, ICML, NeurIPS, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL (each year)\nResearch Group\nI'm looking for motivated students at all levels. If you're interested in working with me, please email me with your CV and research interests."
  },
