  "deep_homepage::Hui Xiong::https://hkustai.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://hkustai.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "xionghui@ust.hk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home Page for Prof. Hui Xiong\nProf. Hui Xiong\nAssociate Vice-President\nOffice of Knowledge\n                Transfer\nChair Professor\nAI Thrust, HKUST\n                (Guangzhou)\nAIS, HKUST (Clear Water\n                Bay)\nDirector\nAI+ Lab\nEmail: xionghui@ust.hk\nOffice: C1 W 201\nHui Xiong is a Chair Professor, Associate Vice President (Knowledge Transfer), and Founding Head of the AI\n        Thrust at\nHong Kong University of Science\n          and Technology\n          (Guangzhou)\n.\n        His research interests span Artificial Intelligence, data mining, and mobile computing. He obtained his PhD in\n        Computer Science from the\nUniversity of Minnesota\n,\n        USA. Before joining\n        HKUST(GZ), he was a Distinguished Professor at\nRutgers University\nand held the\n        position of Chief\n        Scientist (Smart City) and Deputy Dean at\nBaidu Research Institute\n,\n        overseeing five research\n        labs.\nDr. Xiong has served on numerous organization and program committees for conferences, including as the Founding\n        Editor-in-Chief of\nNature npj\n          - Artificial intelligence\n, a\n        co-Editor in-Chief of the\nEncyclopedia of GIS (Springer)\n, Program Co-Chair for the\n        Industrial and Government Track\n        for the 18th\nACM\n          SIGKDD International\n          Conference on Knowledge\n          Discovery and Data Mining (KDD)\n, Program Co-Chair for the\nIEEE 2013 International Conference on Data Mining (ICDM)\n,\n        General Co-Chair for the\n2015 IEEE International\n          Conference on Data Mining\n          (ICDM)\n, and Program Co-Chair of the Research Track for the\n2018 ACM SIGKDD\n          International Conference\n          on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n.\nHe has received numerous prestigious honors, including election as a\n        Fellow of the\nACM\nin 2026,\nCCF\nand\nAAAI\nin 2025,\nCAAI\nin 2024,\n        and both the\nAAAS\nand the\nIEEE\nin 2020.\n\n        His awards include the 2021 AAAI Best Paper Award, the 2011 IEEE ICDM Best Research Paper Award,\n        the 2018 Ram Charan Management Practice Award – Grand Prize from the Harvard Business Review,\n        and the Gold Medal together with the Swiss Automobile Club Prize at the 2025 International Exhibition of\n        Inventions of Geneva.\nQuick Links:\nFor more details of my work, please see\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nIf you are interested in working in my research group, please read\nFor Prospective Students\n.\nNEWS\nJan. 2026\nProf. Xiong elected ACM Fellow\nRecognized by the Association for Computing Machinery for outstanding contributions to data mining and AI.\nSource\nDec. 2025\nProf. Xiong elected CCF Fellow\nThe China Computer Federation honored Prof. Hui Xiong as a 2025 CCF Fellow for contributions to data mining\n          and intelligent systems.\nSource\nNov. 2025\nProf. Xiong appointed Counselor to the Guangzhou Municipal Government\nThe Guangzhou Municipal People’s Government appointed Prof. Hui Xiong as a Counselor.\nSource\nSept. 2025\nProf. Xiong elected Vice President of the 7th Council of the Guangzhou Western Returned Scholars\n            Association\nThe first member congress and 110th anniversary celebration were held at the Dongfang Hotel, where Prof. Hui\n          Xiong was elected as Vice President of the 7th Council.\nSource\nSept. 2025\nProf. Xiong named among the World’s Top 2% Scientists 2025 by Stanford University\nProf. Hui Xiong was recognized on Stanford University’s 2025 list of the World’s Top 2% Scientists for his\n          outstanding research impact.\nSource\nSept. 2025\nProf. Xiong attended the 80th Anniversary Victory Day Ceremony in Beijing\nInvited to Tiananmen Square, Prof. Hui Xiong joined national leaders and guests to commemorate the 80th\n          anniversary of victory in the War of Resistance Against Japanese Aggression.\nSource\nMay 2025\nProf. Xiong delivered a keynote at the Guangzhou AI Forum\nHe presented expert insights on AI development and industry integration at the Guangzhou Theoretical Learning\n          Group Session and Learning Forum, attended by top city officials.\nSource\nMay. 2025\nProf. Xiong visited Ambassadors of Singapore and the UAE\nIn Beijing, he met with H.E.\nPeter Tan\nand H.E.\nHussain Al Hammadi\nto discuss AI collaboration\n          and knowledge transfer.\nSource\nMay 2025\nProf. Xiong awarded Guangdong Provincial Model Worker honor\nAt the 2025 May Day celebration in Guangzhou, Prof. Xiong was recognized as a Model Worker in Guangdong\n          Province.\nSource\nApr. 2025\nProf. Xiong received the Gold Medal and the Swiss Automobile Club Prize\nAt the 2025 International Exhibition of Inventions of Geneva, he was honored with these top recognitions.\nSource\nJan. 2025\nProf. Xiong elected as AAAI Fellow\nRecognized for his outstanding contributions to the field of artificial intelligence.\nSource\nGROUP\nI am extremely fortunate to work with a number of excellent students and postdocs.\nYou can learn more about the group\nhere\n.\nTEACHING\nHKUST (Guangzhou)\nFoundations of Data Mining (AI 5030), Fall 2023\nCross-disciplinary Research Methods, Fall 2023\nCross-disciplinary Research Methods, Spring 2023\nFoundations of Data Mining (AI 5030), Fall 2022\nTeaching Evaluation: 4.9 out of 5\nHKUST DBA\nData Mining and Business Intelligence (22:135:703), Spring 2021\nRutgers University\nData Mining (26:198:644) (Graduate Course):\nFall 2006, Spring 2009, Spring 2011, Fall 2011, Fall 2012, Fall 2013, Fall 2014, Spring 2015,\nFall 2015, Spring 2016, Fall 2016, Spring 2017, Fall 2017, Fall 2020, Spring 2021\nInformation Technology for Managers (22:198:504) (Full-time MBA):\nSpring 2008, Spring 2010, Spring 2011\nComputers & Information Systems (22:198:604) (Part-time MBA):\nSpring 2007, Fall 2008\nComputer Network Applications (29:623:375) (Undergraduate):\nFall 2005, Fall 2007, Fall 2008, Spring 2006, Spring 2007, Spring 2010\nData Mining for Business Intelligence (Undergraduate): Fall 2010\nManagement Information Systems (29:623:220) (Undergraduate):\nFall 2005, Spring 2006, Fall 2007\nSERVICE\nHonors and Distinctions\nAAAI Fellow\nCCF Fellow\nAAAS Fellow\nIEEE Fellow\nCAAI Fellow\nACM Fellow\nProfessional Services\nCCF Task Force on Big Data, Deputy Director, September 2023 - Present\nSecretary/Executive Committee, ACM SIGKDD, Present\nThe 2023 IEEE CS Fellow Evaluating Committee\nThe 2021 IEEE CS Fellow Evaluating Committee\nJournal Editorship\nEditor-in-Chief,\nnpj - Artificial Intelligence\n, 2024 - Present\nAssociate Editor,\nIEEE TKDE\n, 2013 - 2018\nAssociate Editor,\nDKE\n, 2018 - Present\nAssociate Editor,\nACM TMIS\n, 2015 - Present\nAssociate Editor,\nACM TKDD\n, 2015 - Present\nAssociate Editor,\nIEEE TBD\n, 2015 - 2020\nAssociate Editor,\nKAIS (Springer)\n, 2007 - Present\nEditorial Board Member,\nJournal of Big Data (Springer)\n, 2014 - Present\nSpecial Issue Editor,\nACM TIST\n, Intelligent Mobile Knowledge Discovery\nSpecial Issue Editor,\nWWW Journal\n, Web Information Management in the Big Data Era, 2013\nConference Service\nArea Chair, ICML 2026\nChair, Test of Time Award, WSDM 2021\nChair, IEEE ICDM Awards Committee, 2020\nGeneral Co-Chair, IEEE DSC 2020\nInvited Talk Chair, KDD 2019\nProgram Co-Chair, KDD 2018\nVice Chair, IEEE ICDM 2017\nProgram Co-Chair, DASFAA 2016\nGeneral Co-Chair, IEEE ICDM 2015\nTutorial Co-Chair, IEEE ICDM 2014\nSponsorship Chair, SDM 2014\nProgram Co-Chair, IEEE ICDM 2013\nPC Chair, WAIM 2013\nDemo Chair, KDD 2013\nIndustry Track Co-Chair, KDD 2012\nPC Vice Chair, IEEE ICDM 2012\nGeneral Chair, NDBC China 2012\nTutorial Chair, WI 2012\nFinance Chair, ICDE 2012\nPC Chair, KSEM 2011\nDemo Chair, KDD 2011\nPC Vice Chair, WI 2011\nTutorial Chair, PAKDD 2011\nPC Vice Chair, IEEE ICDM 2010\nSession Chair, KDD 2010\nPC Chair, SKM 2010\nPC Chair, NDC 2010\nPC Vice Chair, WI 2010\nPublicity Chair, NASA CIDU 2010\nPublication Chair, SDM 2010\nSession Chair, KDD 2009\nSession Chair, INFORMS 2009\nPublicity Chair, KDD 2009\nCo-Chair, SADM@ICDM 2009\nSession Chair, KDD 2008\nCo-Chair, SADM@ICDM 2008\nTrack Chair, AMIGE 2008\nSession Chair, ICDM 2007\nSession Chair, KDD 2007\nSession Chair, SDM 2007\nPublicity Chair, SDM 2007\nAwards Chair, ICMLA 2007\nSession Chair, SDM 2006\nPC Vice Chair, ICTAI 2006\nPublicity Chair, ICDM 2006\nTutorial Chair, ICMLA 2006\nPublicity Chair, WI/IAT 2006\nPC Vice Chair, PRICAI 2006\nMEDIA HIGHLIGHTS\nBelow are selected media interviews and features.\n2020\nInterviewed and Featured by\nScientia\nin the article:\n\"Harnessing Big Data to Identify Ideal Locations for Warehouses and Bike Share Stations\"\nSource\n2016\nInterviewed and Featured by\nThe Economist\nin the article:\n\"Cutpurse capers\"\nSource\n2014\nInterviewed and Quoted by\nForbes\nin the article:\n\"The Ethics of Big Data\"\nSource\n2010\nInterviewed and Quoted by\nStar Ledger\nregarding Rutgers Information Systems\nSource"
