  "deep_homepage::Zhiqiang Tao::https://ztao.cc/": {
    "homepage": "https://ztao.cc/",
    "all_emails": [
      "zhiqiang.tao@rit.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhiqiang-tao-5aa13495/",
    "homepage_text": "ZTao's Homepage\nWelcome to ZTao's Homepage!\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nGroup\nServices\nZhiqiang Tao\nAssistant Professor\n, School of Information\nGolisano College of Computing and Information Sciences\nRochester Institute of Technology, Rochester, NY\nEmail: zhiqiang.tao[AT]rit[DOT]edu\n[Google Scholar]\n[DBLP]\n[Semantic Scholar]\n[LinkedIn]\nBrief Bio\nI am an\nAssistant Professor\nin the School of Information at Rochester Institute of Technology (RIT). Prior to joining RIT, I was an Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at Santa Clara University from 2020 to 2022. I received my Ph.D. degree from the ECE Department at Northeastern University, under the supervision of\nProf. Yun Raymond Fu\n. I obtained my B.E. and M.E. degrees from Tianjin University in 2012 and 2015, respectively.\nMy group focuses on studying\nsmart, scalable, and secure\nmachine learning algorithms through optimization and inference techniques for a wide range of fields, including healthcare, AI education, computational imaging, and data science applications. Particularly, our\nrecent works\ninvestigate large language models (LLM) / large vision-language models (LVLM) toward reliable multimodal understanding, calibrated uncertainties on low-level vision, ranking fairness, and desired preference.\nI am looking for highly-motivated graduate (PhD/MS) and undergraduate students to work with our group. Please drop me an email if interested.\nRecent News:\n2026-02: One paper on\nToken Pruning for Efficient LVLM\nwas accepted by CVPR 2026. Congratulations to Guohao and all the collaborators.\n2025-09: One paper on\nLVLM Reasoning\nwas accepted by NeurIPS 2025. Congratulations to Guohao.\n2025-09: One paper on\nLLM Ranker\nwas accepted by SIGIR-AP 2025. Congratulations to Haowei.\n2025-08: Four papers on\nVisual AutoRegressive modeling\n,\nReasoning LLMs\n, and\nLVLM Fairness\nwere accepted by EMNLP 2025. Congratulations to Jiamian, Ziqi, Prasanna, and Xuyang.\n2025-08: Received an\nNIH R16 Award\nto support our research on medical LVLMs for Dermatology AI.\n2025-08: Received an\nNSF ERI Award\nto support our research on uncertainty quantification for computational imaging.\n2025-06: One paper on\nStructured DPO for LVLMs\nwas accepted by ICCV 2025. Congratulations to Guohao.\n2025-05: I received the RIT GCCIS Emerging Scholar Award.\n2024-12: My little one was born. Hello World!\nMore..."
  },
