    "homepage_text": "IDV Lab\nHome\nPublication\nPeople\nProject\nTeaching\nIDV Lab\nInnovative Dimension Vision Lab, Tianjin University.\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2026\nWan-Alpha: Video Generation with Stable Transparency via Shiftable RGB-A Distribution Learner\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2026\nRecEdit-Drive: 3D Reconstruction-Guided Spatiotemporal Video Editing for Autonomous Driving Scenes\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2026\nHOPS with Attention-Aware Filtering and Affinity-Guided Enhancement\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2026\nMulti-modal Frequency Decomposition Network for Semantic Scene Completion\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2026\nBA-GS: Bayesian Adaptive Gaussian Splatting for SFM-Free 3D Reconstruction\nNews\nRecruitment\nWe are recruiting the self-motivated master, Ph.D. students, and postdoctoral researchers to work on interesting machine vision topics. If your feel interested, please send an email to Prof. Lin.\nSee our works\nServe as AE for TIP.\n21-Feb-2026\n6 papers are accepted at CVPR 2026.\n20-Feb-2026\nOccDriver is accepted at ICLR 2026.\n26-Jan-2026\nSDCL is accepted at TPAMI 2026.\n31-Dec-2025\n4 papers are accepted at AAAI 2026.\n9-Nov-2025\nAbout Prof. Di Lin\nDi Lin\nAssociate Professor\nDoctoral Advisor\nBuilding No.55, College of Intelligence and Computing, Tianjin University\nAnde.lin1988[at]gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nDi Lin is a tenured associate professor with the College of Intelligence and Computing, Tianjin University. He received a Ph.D. degree from the Computer Science and Engineering Department at the Chinese University of Hong Kong and a B.Eng. degree in software engineering at Sun Yat-Sen University, China. His research interests include computer vision and machine learning. He has been recognized as one of the Stanford/Elsevier World's Top 2% Scientists from 2022 to now.\nAbout IDV Lab\nPeople in IDV lab are excited about studying various vision tasks along innovative dimensions. Recently, we conduct research on:"
