    "homepage_text": "Honghua Dong's Personal Website\nSkip to content\nHonghua Dong (董宏华)\nEmail:\ndhh19951@gmail.com\n,\nhonghuad@cs.toronto.edu\nAbout Me\n¶\nI am currently a Ph.D. student at University of Toronto, adviced by Prof.\nXujie Si\n, Prof.\nChris J. Maddison\nand Prof.\nJimmy Ba\n. I have graduated from\nIIIS, Tsinghua University\n(\nYaoClass\n) in 2019, major in computer science.\nResearch Interests\n¶\nMy current research interest is in developing Language Model Agents.\nI am broadly interested in artificial intelligence and have also worked on various topics including Reasoning, Graph Neural Networks, Reinforcement Learning and Computer Vision.\nSelected Projects\n¶\nVictor Barres*,\nHonghua Dong\n*, Soham Ray, Xujie Si, Karthik Narasimhan. τ²-Bench: Evaluating Conversational Agents in a Dual-Control Environment. arXiv preprint arXiv:2506.07982, 2025.\nPaper\n|\nCode\n|\nTwitter\nHonghua Dong\n*, Qidong Su*, Yubo Gao, Zhaoyu Li, Yangjun Ruan, Gennady Pekhimenko, Chris J Maddison and Xujie Si. APPL: A Prompt Programming Language for Harmonious Integration of Programs and Large Language Model Prompts. In\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n, 2025.\nPaper\n|\nWebpage\n|\nCode\n|\nTwitter\nYangjun Ruan*,\nHonghua Dong\n*, Andrew Wang, Silviu Pitis, Yongchao Zhou, Jimmy Ba, Yann Dubois, Chris J Maddison, and Tatsunori Hashimoto. Identifying the risks of lm agents with an lm-emulated sandbox. In\nThe Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations\n, 2024.\n[Spotlight]\nPaper\n|\nWebpage\n|\nCode\n|\nTwitter\nHonghua Dong\n*, Jiawei Xu*, Yu Yang*, Rui Zhao, Shiwen Wu, Chun Yuan, Xiu Li, Chris J Maddison, and Lei Han. Megraph: Capturing long-range interactions by alternating local and hierarchical aggregation on multi-scaled graph hierarchy. In\nThe Thirty-seventh Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n2023.\nPaper\n|\nWebpage\n|\nCode\n|\nPoster\n|\nOpenReview\nYuhuai Wu*,\nHonghua Dong\n*, Roger Grosse, and Jimmy Ba. The scattering compositional learner: Discovering objects, attributes, relationships in analogical reasoning. arXiv preprint arXiv:2007.04212, 2020.\nPaper\n|\nCode\nHonghua Dong\n*, Jiayuan Mao*, Tian Lin, Chong Wang, Lihong Li, and Denny Zhou. Neural logic machines. In\nthe 7th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n, 2019.\nPaper\n|\nWebpage\n|\nCode\n|\nOpenReview\nSee a full list\nExperiences\n¶\nI have won Gold Medal in The 26th International Olympiad in Informatics (\nIOI2014\n).\nI have participated in\nACM-ICPC 2016 World Finals\nas a team member.\nI have interned in\nMegvii Inc. (Face++)\n,\nGoogle China AI Center\n, Google (Beijing) and Tencent Inc. I am currently a research intern at\nSierra\n.\nI have visited University of Southern California (adviced by\nJoseph Lim\n), and University of Toronto (adviced by\nJimmy Ba\n).\nServices\n¶\nI have served as a reviewer for conferences including NeurIPS, ICLR and ICML.\nMisc\n¶\nLast updated June 2025.\nBack to top"
  },
