    "homepage_text": "Hengrui Zhang\nHengrui Zhang\nI am a last year Ph.D. student in Computer Science at Univeristy of Illinois, Chicago.\n                                        My advisor is\nPhilip S. Yu\n.\nBefore that, I received my bachelor's degree from\nShanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU)\n.\nEmail: hzhan55 [at] uic [dot] edu\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\n/\nLinkedIn\nResearch Topics\nI am majorly interested in\ntabular deep learning\n, including but not limited to generative tabular data modeling (synthetic tabular data generation and missing data imputation).\nBefore that, I was doing research on graph deep learning, including Graph Neural Networks and self-supervised learning on graph-structured data.\nPublications\n(* equal contribution)\nProfessional Services\nConference Program Committee:\nAISTATS (2025)\nICML (2022, 2023, 2024, 2025)\nNeurIPS (2022, 2023, 2024, 2025)\nICLR (2023, 2024, 2025)\nKDD (2023, 2024, 2025)\nWWW (2024)\nCVPR (2022, 2023, 2024)\nICCV (2023)\nLOG (2022, 2023)\nJournal Reviewer:\nIEEE TPAMI\nACM TKDD\nIEEE TNNLS\nPattern Recognition\nUpdated at June. 2025\nThanks\nJon Barron\nfor this amazing work"
  },
