    "homepage_text": "Dr. Dong Wang School of Information Sciences University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\nDong Wang\nPh.D.\nProfessor\nSchool of Information Sciences\nSiebel School of Computing and Data Science (Affiliated)\nIllinois Informatics\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\nTel: +1-217-244-6412\nEmail: dwang24 at illinois dot edu\nThe SSI Lab has multiple openings for Ph.D. students in Information Science, Computer Science, and Informatics at UIUC. If you are interested in working with us after reading our research profile and recent publications, please feel free to contact Prof. Wang.\nHome\nSocial Sensing & Intelligence Lab\nPublications\nTeaching & Services\nGoogle Scholar\nBiography\nI am a full professor in the\nSchool of Information Sciences\nand the\nSiebel School of Computing and Data Science\n(affiliated) at the\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\n. I received my Ph.D. degree in\nComputer Science\nat UIUC. I am also affiliated with the\nIllinois Informatics\n, the\nNational Center for Supercomputing Applications (NCSA)\n,  the\nInformation Trust Institute\n,  the\nCarl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology (IGB)\n, and the\nCenter for Social and Behavioral Science (CSBS)\nat UIUC.\nResearch Interests\nSocial Sensing, Intelligence, and Computing\nHuman-Centered AI, Responsible AI, Personalized AI\nAI for Social Good, AI for Science\nCyber-Physical Systems, Edge Computing, Smart Cities\nHonors and Awards\nBest Paper Honorable Mention: 2025 ACM CHI conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI 2025)\nFall 2022, 2023, Spring 2023, 2024, List of Teachers Ranked as Excellent by Their Students at UIUC\nSenior Member, Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)\nBest Paper Award (Research Track): 2022 ACM/IEEE International Conference on Advances in Social Networks Analysis and Mining (ASONAM)\nBest Paper Honorable Mention: 8th IEEE International Conference on Smart Computing (SMARTCOMP)\nNSF CAREER Award\nGoogle Faculty Research Award\nARO Young Investigator Program Award (YIP)\nNSF CISE Research Initiation Initiative (CRII) Award\nWing Kai Cheng Fellowship:  University of Illinois at Urbana Champaign\nBest Paper Award:  16th IEEE Real-Time and Embedded Technology and Applications Symposium (RTAS)"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Bin Zhao::https://zhao.utk.edu/": {
