    "homepage_text": "Tianhe WU\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nMr. Tianhe WU, 吴天鶴\nDoctor of Philosophy (Student)\n,\nDepartment of Computer Science\nh-index\n15\nScopus Citations\n1\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2024\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0009-0007-9557-9818\nScopus Author ID:\n57669652600\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Tianhe WU is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n4\nSimilar Profiles\nImage Quality Assessment\nComputer Science\n100%\nMultimodal Large Language Models\nComputer Science\n50%\nReference Image\nComputer Science\n50%\nImage Quality\nComputer Science\n22%\nAssessment Model\nComputer Science\n18%\nsuper resolution\nComputer Science\n12%\nHuman Perception\nComputer Science\n8%\nGeometric Transformation\nComputer Science\n8%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n2\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\nToward Generalized Image Quality Assessment: Relaxing the Perfect Reference Quality Assumption\nChen, D. (Co-first Author),\nWu, T.\n(Co-first Author),\nMa, K.\n& Zhang, L.,\n2025\n,\n2025 IEEE/CVF CONFERENCE ON COMPUTER VISION AND PATTERN RECOGNITION, CVPR 2025 - Proceedings.\nLos Alamitos, Calif.:\nIEEE\n,\np. 12742-12752\n11 p.\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nReference Image\n100%\nImage Quality Assessment\n100%\nAssessment Model\n37%\nsuper resolution\n25%\nImage Quality\n12%\nA Comprehensive Study of Multimodal Large Language Models for Image Quality Assessment\nWu, T.\n,\nMa, K.\n, Liang, J., Yang, Y. & Zhang, L.,\n2024\n,\nComputer Vision – ECCV 2024: 18th European Conference, Proceedings, Part LXXIV.\nLeonardis, A., Ricci, E., Roth, S., Russakovsky, O., Sattler, T. & Varol, G. (eds.).\n1 ed.\nSpringer, Cham\n,\np. 143-160\n(Lecture Notes in Computer Science (including subseries Lecture Notes in Artificial Intelligence and Lecture Notes in Bioinformatics); vol. 15132 LNCS).\nResearch output\n:\nChapters, Conference Papers, Creative and Literary Works\n›\nRGC 32 - Refereed conference paper (with host publication)\n›\npeer-review\nImage Quality Assessment\n100%\nMultimodal Large Language Models\n100%\nImage Quality\n33%\nExperimental Result\n16%\nGeometric Transformation\n16%\n15\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)"
