    "homepage_text": "Xuezhi Wang Lab\nDr. Xuezhi Wang\nPrincipal Investigator, Associate Professor\nFollow\nChang'an University\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nWelcome\nOur lab aims to uncover the fundamental physics mechanisms in nature. We conduct state-of-the-art research in computational physics and related. We value a wide diversity of views and interdisciplinary thoughts that brings fresh thinking into the understanding of nature.\nLab News\nFeb 2026\nJunwei\ngets the work\nRevisiting phonon thermal transport in penta-graphene via a machine-learning potential-driven large-scale molecular dynamics simulation\npublished on\nComputational Materials Science\n.\nJan 2026\nXuezhi\nsigns an industry-sponsored project with\nD. Co\n.\nDec 2025\nDr. Linghu\nis appointed as an\nassociate professor\nin physics. Congrats！\nXuezhi\nis enrolled as a\nVisiting scholar\nof\nI-Habor, Xi'an Jiaotong University\n. And\nZhengwang\nis enrolled as a\nJointly trained graduates\nwith\nXJTU\n.\nYifan\nlaunches the\nAll Good Project\n.\nNov 2025\nXuezhi\nis invited to give a talk at\nIWMM 2025\nat\nShaanxi University of Science & Technology, Xi'an\n.\nZhengwang, Zhihao, Isha, Beijie and Simiao\ngive their research reports at group meeting.\nSimiao Yan\njoins our lab for undergraduate internship. Welcome!\nLei\nand\nYifan\nlaunch the\nTS\nsoftware v1.0.\nOct 2025\nYifan\nis invited as the session chair of\nAsymmetric U-Net with Gaussian Splatting for Single-View 3D Reconstruction (I)\nat\nIEEE SMC 2025, Vienna, Austria\n.\nXuezhi\nvisits\nProf. Kefu Yi\nat\nChangsha University of Science & Technology, Changsha\n.\nSep 2025\nXuezhi\nand\nJiajun\nattend\nCPS Fall meeting 2025\n,\nHarbin\n.\nJunwei\ngets the work\nSynergistically Enhanced Thermophysical and Mechanical Properties of La2(Hf1‒xCex)2O7 for Thermal Barrier Coatings\npublished on\nCeramics International\n.\nXuezhi\nis selected by the editor as a potential reviewer for\nNature Communications\n.\nAug 2025\nXuezhi\nand\nZhengwang\nget the paper\nAn atomic perspective of crack propagation under thermal stress field at high temperature in biphase high-entropy coupled ceramics composites\npublished on\nMaterials Today Communications\n.\nXuezhi\nvisits\nDr. Lu Wang\nat\nCollege of Pharmacy, the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, MI, United States\n.\nJul 2025\nZhengwang\nwins the\nOutstanding Award\nfrom\nThe Academic Forum on Frontiers of Basic Disciplines and Innovation in Interdisciplinary Studies\n!\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\ngive invited talks\nat\nCMC 2025, Xiamen.\nJun 2025\nXinying Quan\n,\nHaoran Zhang\nand\nXiaona Sun\njoin our lab for undergraduate internship. Welcome!\nYousra\ngives a talk on\nDimension\n, and\nIsha\ngives a talk on\nQuantum Entanglement\nto the undergraduates from Physics Department. Excellent Job!\nMay 2025\nJunwei\nrecieves a funding from\nNatural Science Basic Research Program of Shaanxi Province\n.\nJiajun\ngives a lecture at\nYanshan University, Qinhuangdao\n.\nJiajun\nrecieves a funding from\nFundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities\n.\nApr 2025\nYifan\nand\nJianlin\nrelease\nRM software\nv1.0.\nZhengwang\nand\nXuezhi\nattend\nthe 9th National Congress of Magnetic Materials and Devices\nat\nNanjing\n.\nXuezhi\nis invited as a committee member on\nthe Forum of Condensed Matter Physics.\nXuezhi\nvisits\nProf. Yusheng Wang\nat\nNanjing University of Information Science & Technology, Nanjing\n.\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\nvisit\nProf. Songrui Wei\nat\nShenzhen University, Shenzhen\n.\nJiajie Zhang\n,\nZhihao Zhou\n,\nTianjun Wen\n,\nZidong Liang\n,\nIsha Abdulai Turay\nand\nYousra El Mouloudi\njoin our lab for undergraduate internship. Welcome!\nMar 2025\nDr. Lu Wang\njoins our lab as a research associate from\nThe University of Michigan, MI, United States\n. Welcome!\nXuezhi\nvisits the\nNVIDIA GPU Education Center\nand\nNVIDIA CUDA Teaching Center\nwith\nYifan\nat\nSouthwest Petroleum University, Chengdu.\nFeb 2025\nXuezhi\nvisits\nThe University of Virginia\n, VA, United States\n.\nBeijie Hu\n,\nXuan Zeng\nand\nSsegawa Raymond Mark\njoin our lab for undergraduate internship. Welcome!\nJan 2025\nZhengwang\nand\nJiajun\nhave the paper\nA highly polarization-sensitive near-infrared photodetector based on two-dimensional germanane/a-CdS heterostructure\ngot published on\n2D Materials\n.\nDec 2024\nXuezhi\nreceives a grant from\nNSFC\n. The\nTHIRD ONE\n!\nNov 2024\nXuezhi\nsigns an industry-sponsored project with\nLin Corp\n.\nOct 2024\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\nare invited to give a talk at\nCPS Fall Meeting 2024, Haikou.\nXuezhi\nattends\nSchool and Workshop on Frontiers of Nanomechanics\nhosted by\nthe Abdus Salam International Centre for Theoretical Physics\n(ICTP)\nat\nTrieste, Italy\n.\nMore\nSep 2024\nZhengwang Chen\njoins our lab as a master student. Welcome aboard!\nAug 2024\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\ngive invited talks\nat\nthe 2nd World Materials Conference, Guangzhou\n.\nXuezhi\nvisits\nTsinghua University\n, Beijing\n.\nJul 2024\nJunwei\nhas his work\nDual-channel phonon transport leads to low thermal conductivity in pyrochlore La2Hf2O7\ngot published on\nCeramics International\n.\nDec 2023\nXuezhi\nvisits\nCornell University\n, NY, United States\n.\nOct 2023\nYifan\nhas his work\nFour-phonon scattering significantly reduces the predicted lattice thermal conductivity in penta-graphene: A machine learning-assisted investigation\npublished on\nComputational Materials Science\n.\nSep 2023\nWenjie\nand\nJunwei\nhas the work\nThermal transport properties and lattice vibration modes in crystalline and amorphous LaMgAl11O19\npublished on\nJournal of Alloys and Compounds\n.\nJun 2023\nJiajun\nattends\nthe 11th International Conference on Materials for Advanced Technologies, Singapore\n.\nMar 2023\nJiajun\nhas her work\nComputational prediction of stable semiconducting Zn-C binary compounds\ngot published on\nMaterials Science in Semiconductor Processing\n.\nXuezhi\nhas a publication\nMechanism of amorphous-like thermal conductivityin binary oxide Yb3TaO7\non\nActa Physica Sinica\n.\nJan 2023\nXuezhi\ngets the work\nMechanism of crack propagation in penta-graphene\npublished on\nVacuum\n.\nNov 2022\nXuezhi\ngets a paper\nEffect of yttria on thermal transport and vibrational modes in yttria-stabilized hafnia\npublished on\nCeramics International\n.\nSep 2022\nJunwei\ngets his work\nFluctuating bonding leads to glass-like thermal conductivity in perovskite rare-earth tantalates\npublished on\nActa Materialia\n. Congratulations!\nAug 2022\nXuezhi\nreceives the second grant from\nNSFC\n.\nJun 2022\nXuezhi\nrecieves the second funding from\nFundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities\n.\nMar 2022\nJunwei\ngets his work\nUltralow oxygen ion diffusivity in pyrochlore-type La2(Zr0.7Ce0.3)2O7\npublished on\nJournal of Materials Science & Technology\n.\nJan 2022\nJunwei\ngets his work\nThermal transport property in pyrochlore-type and fluorite-type A2B2O7 oxides by molecular dynamics simulation\npublished on\nInternational Journal of Heat and Mass Transfer\n.\nMar 2021\nJunwei\nhas his paper\nOutstanding sintering resistance in pyrochlore-type La2(Zr0.7Ce0.3)2O7 for thermal barrier coatings material\ngot published on\nCeramics International.\nSep 2020\nXuezhi\nhas two paper\nThe effects of interface layer in LZ/YSZ coupled system during thermal transportation at elevated temperatures: A molecular dynamics simulation study\nand\nPorous effects on heat transfer and ions distribution in YSZ using molecular dynamics simulation\ngot published on\nChemical Physics Letters.\nMar 2020\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\nboth get supports from\nNatural Science Basic Research Program of Shaanxi Province\n.\nJan 2020\nXuezhi\nvisits\nThe University of Tulsa\n, OK, United States\n.\nJiajun\nand\nXuezhi\nrecieve fundings from\nFundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities\n.\nOct 2019\nXuezhi\nreceives a grant from\nNSFC\n. The\nFIRST ONE\n!\nWe do something new.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nXuezhi Wang Lab\nDr. Xuezhi Wang\nPrincipal Investigator, Associate Professor\nFollow\nChang'an University\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nDr. Wang received his Ph.D degree in Materials science and engineering from Xi'an Jiaotong University. He was a visiting scholar at BMW Manufacturing Lab of Clemson University International Center for Automotive Research (CUICAR). He is an expert in MD calculations of advanced functional materials from atomic perspectives. His research focuses on computational physics and related from a perspective of fundamental particles.\nDr. Linghu received her Ph.D degree in Computational material physics from National University of Singapore (NUS). She is an Associate professor in Physics at Chang'an University. She is an expert in first-principles calculations of advanced functional materials. Her research spans the design and adjustment of material structures to achieve desired properties, with applications in solid oxide fuel cells, two-dimensional materials, and optoelectronic materials.\nDr. Jiajun Linghu\nCo-PI\nDr. Che received his Ph.D. degree in Physics from Xi'an Jiaotong University. He was a visiting scholar at Technische Universität Hamburg, Germany. His research interests include high-temperature ceramics, phonon thermal transport, first-principles calculations, molecular dynamics simulations, and machine learning.\nDr. Junwei Che\nCo-PI\nResearch Partners\nDr. Wang received his Ph.D. degree in Human-computer Interaction from The University of Sydney (USYD), Australia. He was a researcher at Wellbeing Tech Lab of USYD. He is an expert on artificial intelligence, image processing, and 3D reconstruction.\nDr. Yifan Wang\nDr. Wang received her Ph.D. degree in Pharmaceutical analysis from Zhejiang University. She was a research fellow at the University of Michigan (UMich), Ann Arbor, MI, United States. Her research focuses on biophysics.\nDr. Lu Wang\nDr. Huang received his Ph.D. degree in Mechanical engineering from Xi'an Jiaotong University. His research focuses on algorithm design and quantum computation.\nDr. Wenjie Huang\nGraduates\nZhengwang received his B.S. in Mechanics from Xi'an University of Science and Technology. His research focuses on crack growth mechanics.\nZhengwang Chen\nUndergraduates\nBeijie Hu\nSsegawa Raymond Mark\nXuan Zeng\nZidong Liang\nYousra El Mouloudi\nJiajie Zhang\nIsha Abdulai Turay\nZhihao Zhou\nTianjun Wen\nXiaona Sun\nHaoran Zhang\nXinying Quan\nSimiao Yan"
  },
