    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yuan Zhang's Homepage\nYuan Zhang\nHome\nPublications\nResearch\nTeaching\nYuan's Group\nYuan Zhang\nAssociate Professor\nSchool of Automation,\nBeijing Institute of Technology\nBeijing, China\nOffice: Room 1005, No.6 Building of the National-Defense Technology Garden\nAddress: 5 Zhongguancun South, Beijing, 100081, China\nTelephone: +86 17801025178\nEmail: zhangyuan14@bit.edu.cn\nGoogle Scholar\nBrief Biography\nCurrently, I am an Associate Professor in the School of Automation, Beijing Institute of Technology, China, and also a visiting research fellow at University of Western Australia, Australia.\r\n    Before, I was\r\n    a Post-doctoral Fellow in the same institute, working with Prof. Yuanqing Xia. \r\n    In October 2019, I obtained\r\nPh.D. degree at\nTsinghua University\n, Bejing, China, under the supervision of Prof. Tong Zhou, who was an IEEE Fellow and CAA Fellow, and also the Associate Editor of the two top journals in control, IEEE TAC and Automatica. \r\nI obtained my bachelor degree majoring in control science and engineering at\r\nTongji University, Shanghai, China, in 2014. \r\n I was born in July, 1993.\nI am looking for self-motivated Ph.D./master/undergraduate students to join my group. Please email me your CV if you are interested.\nResearch Interests\nI focus on combining computational tools from modern computer science theory with analysis and optimization of control systems:\nAnalysis and control of large-scale network systems, with applications to the power networks, cloud control systems, etc.\nCombinatorial optimization with applications to control systems\nCyber-security and data-driven control and analysis\nResearch Projects\nResearch Projects as Principal Investigator:\nAnalysis and Optimization of Generic Properties in Temporal and Switching Linear Networks\n,National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), 500 000 CNY, 2024 to 2027\nStructure-based Resilience Analysis and Optimization for Networked Systems\n, National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), 240 000 CNY, 2021 to 2023\nStructural Resilience Analysis of Large-Scale Networked Systems\n,China Postdoctoral Innovative Talent Support Program, 630,000 CNY, 2020 to 2021\nDetection and Isolation of Topology Failures of Network Systems: Generic Properties and Data-Driven Approaches\n,China Postdoctoral Science Foundation, 120, 000 CNY, 2020 to 2021\nHonors & Awards\nExcellent Doctoral Dissertation Award of Tsinghua University, 2020\nSelected in the China Postdoctoral Innovative Talent Support Program, 2020\nOutstanding Postdoctor of Beijing Institute of Technology,2021\nTop Ten Research Progress of China Postdoctoral Innovative Talent Support Program in 2020,2021\nExcellent Graduate of Department of Automation, Tsinghua University, 2020\nActivities\nOctober 18\n, I was invited to give a talk on\nGeneric Structured Low-Rank Matrix Completion\r\nfor Robustness Analysis of Control Systems\nat Center of System and Control of\nPeking Univerisity\n.\nOctober 26\n, I was invited to give a talk on\nRobust structural controllability of linear systems\nat the\nWorkshop of Beijing Chapter @ IEEE CSS Day\n.\nFrom December 22, 2022\nto\nDecember 22, 2024\n, I am an\nEditorial Board Member\nof the journal\nAutomation, Control and Intelligent Systems (ACIS)\n.\nService\nI am an active reviewer of the following journals and conferences:\nIEEE TAC, Automatica, IEEE TCNS,IEEE L-CSS, IJRNC, Europe Journal of Control, International Journal of System Science, Neurocomputing, the Open Public Health Journal, IEEE CDC, ACC, IFAC, CCC, etc.\nCo-char of CCC 2021. Invited as the Academic Host of the 4th Form of China Postdoctoral Innovative Talent Support Program.\nAdvice for Researchers & Students\nHow to Write Research Articles in Computing and Engineering Disciplines\nby Ivan Stojmenovic.\nHow to Write a Great Research Paper\nby\nSimon Peyton Jones\nTao Xie's Blog on Research and Advising (in Chinese)\nCrafting Your Research Future\nThe Elements of Style\nby Strunk & White\nLinks\nYuanqing XIA\n(Chair Professor@BIT, China)\nTong Zhou\n(Full Professor@THU, China)\nYuan Zhang\n(Associate Professor@BIT, China)"
  },
