    "homepage_text": "Home ←\nChangyou Chen\nHome\nPublication\nCode\nContact\nCourses\nWelcome\nI am an Associate Professor in the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering\nat\nthe University at Buffalo, State University of New York\n. I am interested in general AI techniques, with current research focusing on the topics of\nMulti-Modal Modeling and Learning\nSelf-Supervised Learning\nLarge Language Models\nGenerative Models\nLarge-scale Bayesian sampling and inference\nPreviously, I was an Assistant Professor at the University at Buffalo, a Research Assistant Professor and a Postdoctoral Associate in the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nDuke University\n. I got my PhD from\nCollege of Engineering and Computer Science\n,\nthe Australian National University\nin 2014 (\nPhD thesis\n), and my master and bachelor degrees both from\nSchool of Computer Science\n,\nFudan University\n, Shanghai, China.\nI am an Area Chair for multiple AI conferences including\nICML\n,\nNeurIPS\n,\nAAAI\n,\nIJCAI\n, and an Action Editor for\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n.\nMy CV (outdated) can be downloaded\nhere\n.\nWith the current pace of AI development, it is difficult to maintain an up-to-date\npublication page\n. Please refer to my\nGoogle Scholar page\nfor my up-to-date research.\nHighlights\n(More Recentâ¦)\nWe are orgonizing the 1st workshop on\n[Foundation Models in Vision and Language]\n, held in December 1st in conjunction with ICDM 2022, Orlando, FL, USA. Please click\n[here]\nfor the details. We look forward to your excellent work!\nI will serve as an Area Chair for AAAI 2022.\nI will serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2021-2022.\nI will serve as an Area Chair for IJCAI 2021.\nâ¦\nTwo papers accepted by ICLR 2019.\nTwo papers accepted by NeurIPS 2019.\nOne paper accepted by IROS 2018.\nOne paper accepted by UAI 2018.\nTwo papers accepted by ICML 2018.\nTwo papers accepted by AISTATS 2018.\nStudents\nShijie Zhou\nJiayu Qin\nJingchen Sun\nRohan Jagdish Sharma\nYaman Kumar\nJian Chen\nYufan Zhou\n: Now at Adobe\nPing Yu\n: Now at Meta\nYang Zhao\n: Now at Google\nLe Fang\n: Now at Meta\nDesign by\nMark Reid\n, (\nSome rights reserved\n)\nPowered by\nJekyll\n,\nPandoc\n,\nMathJax\n\n---\n\nChangyou Chen's Contact ←\nChangyou Chen\nHome\nPublication\nCode\nContact\nCourses\nContact Information\nOffice\n: 338L, Davis Hall\nOffice hour\n: 3:00 PM - 5:00 PM, Mondays\nEmail\n: changyou at buffalo dot edu; cchangyou at gmail dot com\nPhone\n: (716) 645-4750\nMailing Address\n: 338L Davis Hall, University at Buffalo, the State University of New York, Buffalo, NY 14260-2000, U.S.A.\nDesign by\nMark Reid\n, (\nSome rights reserved\n)\nPowered by\nJekyll\n,\nPandoc\n,\nMathJax\n\n---\n\nChangyou Chen's Contact ←\nChangyou Chen\nHome\nPublication\nCode\nContact\nCourses\nContact Information\nOffice\n: 338L, Davis Hall\nOffice hour\n: 3:00 PM - 5:00 PM, Mondays\nEmail\n: changyou at buffalo dot edu; cchangyou at gmail dot com\nPhone\n: (716) 645-4750\nMailing Address\n: 338L Davis Hall, University at Buffalo, the State University of New York, Buffalo, NY 14260-2000, U.S.A.\nDesign by\nMark Reid\n, (\nSome rights reserved\n)\nPowered by\nJekyll\n,\nPandoc\n,\nMathJax\n\n---\n\nHome ←\nChangyou Chen\nHome\nPublication\nCode\nContact\nCourses\nWelcome\nThis website contains tutorial pages for CSS2013 â Computational Social Science: Foundations and Frontiers.\nCSS2013 is a summer course to be delivered at Beihang University as part of an\nAustralia-China Science and Research Fund\ngroup mission.\nInfo\nA link to the syllabus and schedule go here.\nTutorials\nHere are links to the list of\nTutorials\npage for the class, organized by topic.\nRecent posts include:\nTwitter\nContacting Twitter for feed about CSS â¦\n=â\nDesign by\nMark Reid\n, (\nSome rights reserved\n)\nPowered by\nJekyll\n,\nPandoc\n,\nMathJax\n\n---\n\nHome ←\nChangyou Chen\nHome\nPublication\nCode\nContact\nCourses\nWelcome\nThis website contains tutorial pages for CSS2013 â Computational Social Science: Foundations and Frontiers.\nCSS2013 is a summer course to be delivered at Beihang University as part of an\nAustralia-China Science and Research Fund\ngroup mission.\nInfo\nA link to the syllabus and schedule go here.\nTutorials\nHere are links to the list of\nTutorials\npage for the class, organized by topic.\nRecent posts include:\nTwitter\nContacting Twitter for feed about CSS â¦\n=â\nDesign by\nMark Reid\n, (\nSome rights reserved\n)\nPowered by\nJekyll\n,\nPandoc\n,\nMathJax"
