    "homepage_text": "Hao Zhu\nHao Zhu\nhe/him/他\n朱昊\nPostdoctoral\nStanford University\n[email protected]\nAI, Cooperation, Language, CogSci, Robotics.\nMe\nI am a researcher with a focus on creating\nAI agents\nthat learn to\ncommunicate\nand\ncooperate\nwith humans, or\nHuman-Agent Interaction\n.\nMy Research\nI take an interactionist approach. This means the priority of my\n          research is to\nbring up\nagents in the realistic open-ended multi-agent embodied\n          environments.\nFor examples of environments, check out\nSotopia\nand\nWebArena\n. We recently studied\n          how to build real-time agents:\nReal-time gym\n. For examples of\n          methods for training agents in these environments, check out\nSotopia-π\nand\nNNetNav-live\n. Lately,\nEgoNormia\nbenchmarked \nthe preparedness of frontier models for embodied interactions with\n          humans.\nAutoLibra\nallows agents to develop self-regulation metrics from human\n          open-ended feedback.\nMy research is built along three major dimensions for agents: the\n          behavior of agents, e.g. like a computer, a robot, or a simulated\n          human; the cognition of agents, e.g. reasoning about humans, other\n          agents, or time and space; and the learning of agents, e.g.\n          through exploration, environment feedback, or human feedback.\nMy\nultimate goal\nis to unravel the mysteries of human intelligence\nthrough building AI.\nMy research not only takes inspiration from but also contributes\n          to a better understanding of humans themselves. You will have the\n          sense of this research taste if you read the first sentence of\n          each of the above papers.\nIf you approach me, consider the following topics that I am mostly\n          interested in:\n1. How to build agents that can think while doing? E.g.\nAgileThinker\n.\n2. What are the new dynamics of Human-AI interaction?\n3. How to enable social learning in AI agents?\nFAQ\nCan I work with you?\nI am always looking for talented students and collaborators\n                from all backgrounds for both research and impactful open\n                source projects. That being said, I invest at least 10 hours\n                per week in each project I manage, so I am currently at full\n                capacity. Feel free to shoot me an email if you are interested\n                in my research, but please understand if I am not able to\n                respond to every email.\nCan I book a meeting with you?\nYes! I am always happy to talk to people. Please\ncheck out my calendar and book a slot\n. If you are at Stanford, I host an office hour every Friday\n                at 9am in Gates 256. Feel free to drop by! Sorry, no online\n                office hours at the moment.\nCan I invite you to give a talk?\nHappy to give a talk! I have several keynotes covering my\n                latest research which are ready to present. Please email me\n                for more details. Current talk topics: “Training agents\n                in the open social world: exploration and\n                reinforcement”, “Building the common ground\n                between humans and AI: norms and risks”.\nRecent Talks\nCMU LLM Course\n09/18/2025\nEvaluation and Learning in Human-Agent Interaction (Guest Lecture)\nACL 2025 BOF\n07/29/2025\nBridging Human Study and LLM Agents for Social Simulation\nJP Morgan AI Research\n04/24/2025\nUshering AI Agents into an Open Social World\nUSC/ISI\n04/17/2025\nUshering AI Agents into an Open Social World\nCMU Flame Center\n04/04/2025\nUshering AI Agents into an Open Social World\nUChicago/TTIC NLP Seminar\n04/03/2025\nUshering AI Agents into an Open Social World\nGaTech\n03/31/2025\nLLM Agent (Guest Lecture at GaTech CS7643)\nEducation\nCarnegie Mellon University\n2024\nPhD (Advised by Graham Neubig, Yonatan Bisk)\nTsinghua University\n2019\nBEng"
  },
