    "homepage_text": "﻿\nGuibing Guo's Page\nDr. Guibing Guo\nis a Professor in the\nSoftware College\n,\nNortheastern University\n, Shenyang, China.  He received a Ph.D degree in computer science at\nNanyang Technological University\n, under the supervision of\nDr. Jie Zhang\nand\nDr. Daniel Thalmann\n. Then, he did a post-doc with\nDr. Feida Zhu\nas a research fellow at\nSingapore Management University\n.\nHis research interests include recommender systems, deep learning, social network analysis and data mining. The main research focus is to resolve the challenges of recommender systems, including\ndata sparsity, cold start, diversity\nand so on. He is the original author (and now the team leader) of the open-source library for recommender systems,\nLibRec\n, which implements a large number (over 90) of recommender algorithms. We advocate the sharing and open-source of recommender algorithms, and encourage algorithm authors to contribute their codes to LibRec.\nI am very open to research collaboration, and welcome Ph.D students to exchange and join my research team.\nFor those (self-motivated) students who are interested in recommender systems, drop me an email to discuss more!\n欢迎有志于从事推荐系统研究和项目的学生加入课题组，可发电子邮件联系我。\nLibRec团队正在招募，查看详情\nSelected Publications\n/\nFull List\nYear\nType\nTitle\nCollection\n2020\nConference\nLeveraging Title-Abstract Attentive Semantics for Paper Recommendatio\nAAAI\n(CCF: A)\n2019\nConference\nDynamic Item Block and Prediction Enhancing Block for Sequential Recommendation\nIJCAI\n(CCF: A)\n2019\nConference\nDiscrete Trust-aware Matrix Factorization for Fast Recommendation\nIJCAI\n(CCF: A)\n2018\nConference\nApproximating Word Ranking and Negative Sampling for Word Embedding\nIJCAI\n(CCF: A)\n2018\nConference\nVSE-ens: Visual-Semantic Embeddings with Efficient Negative Sampling\nAAAI\n(CCF: A)\n2018\nJournal\nPCCF: Periodic and Continual Temporal Co-Factorization for Recommender Systems\nInformation Sciences\n(SCI Q2, IF: 4.832)\n2017\nJournal\nFactored Similarity Models with Social Trust for Top-N Item Recommendation\nKnowledge-based Systems\n(IF: 4.529)\n2017\nJournal\nResolving Data Sparsity by Multi-type Auxiliary Implicit Feedback for Recommender Systems\nKnowledge-based Systems\n(IF: 4.529)\n2016\nConference\nLambdaFM: Learning Optimal Ranking with Factorization Machines Using Lambda Surrogates\nCIKM 2016\n2016\nJournal\nA Novel Recommendation Model Regularized with User Trust and Item Ratings\nTKDE\n(IF: 3.438)\n2016\nJournal\nA Novel Evidence-based Bayesian Similarity Measure for Recommender Systems\nTWEB\n(IF: 1.526)\n2015\nConference\nTrustSVD: Collaborative Filtering with Both the Explicit and Implicit Influence of User Trust and of Item Ratings\nAAAI\n,\nPDF\n,\nCode\n2015\nConference\nLibRec: A Java Library for Recommender Systems\nUMAP Demo\n,\nPDF\n2015\nJournal\nLeveraging Multiviews of Trust and Similarity to Enhance Clustering-based Recommender Systems\nKnowledge-Based Systems (IF: 3.325),\nPDF\n2015\nJournal\nMulti-Faceted Trust and Distrust Prediction for Recommender Systems\nDecision Support Systems (IF: 2.604),\nPDF\n2014\nJournal\nLeveraging Prior Ratings for Recommender Systems in E-Commerce\nElectronic Commerce Research and Applications\n(IF: 1.482),\nPDF\n2014\nConference\nETAF: An Extended Trust Antecedents Framework for Trust Prediction\nASONAM (18% of acceptance)\n,\nPDF\n,\nSlides\n2014\nJournal\nMerging Trust in Collaborative Filtering to Alleviate Data Sparsity and Cold Start\nKnowledge-Based Systems (IF: 2.947),\nPDF\n2014\nConference\nFrom Ratings to Trust: an Empirical Study of Implicit Trust in Recommender Systems\nSAC,\nPDF\n,\nSlides\n2013\nConference\nA Novel Bayesian Similarity Measure for Recommender Systems\nIJCAI\n,\nPDF\n,\nPoster\n2013\nConference\nPrior Ratings: A New Information Source for Recommender Systems in E-Commerce\nRecSys\n,\nPDF\n,\nPoster\n2012\nConference\nA Simple but Effective Method to Incorporate Trusted Neighbors in  Recommender Systems\nUMAP\n,\nPDF\nProfessional Services\nOrganization Service\nCo-chair of the 2018 International Workshop on Multi-dimensional Information Fusion for User Modeling and Personalization (\nIFUP 2018\n)\nGuest Editor of Electronic Commerce Research and Applications (ECRA) Special Issue on\nRecommender Systems with Side Information\n(2017.3 - 2018.6)\nCo-chair of the 2016 International Workshop on Multi-dimensional Information Fusion for User Modeling and Personalization (\nIFUP 2016\n)\nCo-chair of the 3rd International Workshop on Educational Recommender Systems (\nEdRecSys 2016\n)\nProgram Committee member\nThe International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nIJCAI 2016 - 2019\n)\nThe International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR 2018 - 2019)\nThe  ACM Recommender Systems Conference (\nRecSys 2016 - 2019\n)\nThe  ACM/SIGAPP Symposium on Applied Computing (\nSAC 2017 - 2019\n)\nThe 30th International Conference of the Florida Artificial Intelligence Research Society (\nFLAIRS-30\n)\nThe 2015 IEEE/WIC/ACM International Conference on Web Intelligence (WI 2015)\nThe 28th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2014)\nConference Deadlines\nConference\nRank\nAbstract\nFull Paper\nNotification\nDate\nVenue\nAAAI\nA\nSep 10, 2015\nSep 15, 2015\nOct 28-30 / Nov 12, 2015\nFeb 12-17, 2016\nPhoenix, Arizona USA\nACM SIGMOD\nA\nNov 12, 2015\nJul 9, 2015\nNov 19, 2015\nJul 16, 2015\nJan 29, 2016\nSep 18, 2015\nJun 26-Jul 1, 2016\nSan Francisco, USA\nACM WSDM\nB\nJul 31, 2016\nAug 7, 2016\nOct 24, 2016\nFeb 6-10, 2017\nCambridge, UK\nACM CIKM\nB\nMay 9, 2016\nMay 16, 2016\nJul 18, 2016\nOct 24-28, 2016\nIndianapolis, USA\nACM RecSys\nApr 13, 2016\nApr 20, 2016\nJun 14, 2016\nSep 15-19, 2016\nBoston, USA\nACM SIGIR\nA\nJan 14, 2016\nJan 21, 2016\nMar  31, 2016\nJul 17-21, 2016\nPisa, Italy\nACM SIGKDD\nA\nFeb 12, 2016\nMay 12, 2016\nAug 13-17, 2016\nSan Francisco, California\nIEEE ICDE\nA\nOct 19, 2015\nDec 20, 20