    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yijiezhang/",
    "homepage_text": "Yijie Zhang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYijie Zhang\nYijie Zhang\nPh.D. Fellow\nDenmark Learning Theory and Applications\n(DeLTA) Lab\nMachine Learning Section\nDepartment of Computer Science\nUniversity of Copenhagen\n&\nNovo Nordisk A/S\nE-mail\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nBio\n|\nPublications\nI am a Ph.D. student working at the University of Copenhagen\nsupervised by\nChristian Igel\nand\nSadegh Talebi\nand a data scientist working at Novo Nordisk A/S. M\ny goal is to build robust,\nadaptive\n, and scalable machine learning systems that could be valuable to real-world applications.\nIn particular,\nh\nere in Copenhagen, I am working on\nadaptive learning and control of complex stochastic systems in pharmaceutical productio\nn. I am broadly interested in reinforcement learning and control, and probabilistic machine learning.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yongqiang Chen::https://lfhase.win/": {
    "homepage": "https://lfhase.win/",
