    "github": "https://github.com/jameszcheng",
    "linkedin": "https://linkedin.com/in/jamescheng24",
    "homepage_text": "James Cheng\nJames Cheng\nI am a Master's student in Computer Science at Stanford University. Previously, I obtained Bachelor's degrees in Computer Science and Business Administration from UC Berkeley, where I was a Regents' and Chancellor's Scholar.\nI am interested in data curation and reinforcement learning for improving reasoning in language models.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nLinkedIn\nResearch\nFollower Agnostic Methods for Stackelberg Games\nChinmay Maheshwari,\nJames Cheng\n, S Shankar Sastry, Lillian Ratliff, Eric Mazumdar\nCDC\n, 2024\npdf\n/\narXiv\nMethods for leader-follower (Stackelberg) games with follower-agnostic guarantees.\nProjects\nConstrained Text Generation Benchmark\nDesigned a 348-prompt benchmark (local, global, and hybrid constraints) with dual-path verification to quantify autoregressive constraint-following limitations across 6 LLMs on 7,889 expanded variants. Built SFT and DPO fine-tuning pipelines and meta-ablation analyses, confirming a steep difficulty gradient driven by planning bottlenecks.\nMuSR: Murder Mystery Reasoning Benchmark\nExtended the MuSR benchmark (ICLR 2024 Spotlight) with dynamic belief update and counterfactual reasoning tracks, generating graph-structured mystery datasets to evaluate multi-step logical deduction in LLMs. Built streaming evaluation pipeline testing how models revise predictions across evidence rounds.\nLLM-as-Planner vs RL on Procgen\nBuilt hybrid RL-LLM agents with entropy-based mode switching, boosting task success rates up to 2x over RL-only baselines (PPO, DQN) across procedurally generated environments.\nWebsite template from\nJon Barron"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Dadong Wang::https://research.unsw.edu.au/people/dr-dadong-wang": {
    "homepage": "https://research.unsw.edu.au/people/dr-dadong-wang",
    "all_emails": [
      "dadong.wang@unsw.edu.au"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Dr Dadong   Wang | UNSW Research\nSkip to main content\nResearcher\nFields of Research (FoR)\nArtificial Intelligence and Image Processing\n,\nComputer Vision\n,\nPattern Recognition\n,\nSignal Processing\n,\nRadiology and Imaging\nBiography\nDr Dadong Wang is a Conjoint Professor at the University of New South Wales (UNSW), a Senior Principal Research Scientist & the Leader of Imaging and Computer Vision Research Group (ICVG), part of the CSIRO Data61. With over 70 people based at Brisbane, Canberra and Sydney, Australia, the group comprises Research Scientists and Engineers, Postdoctoral Fellows, PhD Students and Visiting Scientists. ICVG has extensive experience and a track...\nview more\nDr Dadong Wang is a Conjoint Professor at the University of New South Wales (UNSW), a Senior Principal Research Scientist & the Leader of Imaging and Computer Vision Research Group (ICVG), part of the CSIRO Data61. With over 70 people based at Brisbane, Canberra and Sydney, Australia, the group comprises Research Scientists and Engineers, Postdoctoral Fellows, PhD Students and Visiting Scientists. ICVG has extensive experience and a track record in developing end-to-end imaging and computer vision solutions and via collaboration with innovation partners bring them to the market.\nDadong is also an adjunct Professor at the University of Technology, Sydney (UTS). Prior to joining the Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO) in 2005, he had worked for two multinational companies for six years, developing large intelligent systems for monitoring and control. His main research interests include image analysis, computer vision, artificial intelligence, machine learning, signal processing and software engineering. He has been developing intelligent solutions for scientific and industrial applications, with the aim of increasing both quality and quantity of information extracted from multi-dimensional image data.\nDadong has published over 150 research papers, book chapters and reports. His research team has been the recipient of Research Achievement Awards by CSIRO, the Engineering Excellence Award by Engineers Australia, the Asia Pacific ICT Alliance Awards (APICTA), National iAwards, NSW, Queensland and ACT iAwards. He is a senior member of the IEEE.\nLooking for PhD Students - my team is looking for outstanding candidates to carry out research in Image Analysis, Video Analytics, Computer Vision, Deep Learning, Augmented Reality & Virtual Reality. Please send me your CV and your research idea/short proposal if interested.\nMy Awards\n2023-2023 Winner of The Asia Pacific ICT Alliance Awards (APICTA) - Research and Development Project of the Year (teamwork)\n2023-2023 Merit recipient of The Asia Pacific ICT Alliance Awards (APICTA) - Artificial Intelligence Project of the Year (teamwork)\n2023-2023 Merit recipient of National iAwards 2023 in Business and Industry Solution category (team work)\n2023-2023 Merit recipient of National iAwards 2023 in Technology Platform category (team work)\n2023-2023 Winner of NSW iAwards 2023 in Business and Industry Solution category (team work)\n2023-2023 Merit recipient of NSW iAwards 2023 in Technology Platform category (team work)\n2020-2022 Distinguished reviewer of IEEE Transactions on Medical Imaging\n2021-2021 CSIRO Non-Cash Reward\n2018-2019 CSIRO Performance Cash Reward\n2015-2015 Merit Recipient (Team), Queensland State iAwards\n2012-2013 CMIS Research Achievement Award\n2012-2013 CSIRO Performance Cash Reward\n2009-2010 CMIS Research Achievement Award\n2009-2009 Engineering Excellence Industry Award for Innovations and Inventions, Sydney region, the Institution of Engineers Australia (team work)\n2006-2007 CSIRO Performance Cash Reward\nView less\nLocation\nEngineering\nSydney, Australia\nContact\n+61 2 9325 3223\ndadong.wang@unsw.edu.au\nPublications\nby Dr Dadong   Wang\nBooks\n1\nBook Chapters\n6\nEdited Books\n1\nJournal articles\n104\nConference Papers\n81\nConference Posters\n2\nPreprints\n2\nView all »\nORCID as entered in\nROS\nhttps://orcid.org/0000-0003-0409-2259\nRelated Links\nMy CSIRO Web page\nUNSW Sydney NSW 2052 Australia Telephone +61 2 93851000\nAuthorised by Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research)\nUNSW CRICOS Provider Code: 00098G ABN: 57 195 873 179\nJoin the conversation\nFacebook\nTwitter\nUNSW Youtube\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nInstagram\nMember Group of Eight\nMember Universitas 21\nMember Global Alliance of Technological Universities\nMember Association of Pacific Rim Universities\nMember\nPLuS Alliance\nHome\n2025 Strategic Initiatives\nUNSW Futures\nInterdisciplinary Research\nWorld Class Research Infrastructure\nGrand Challenges\nThought Leadership & Public Engagement\nKnowledge Exchange\nARTU -  Aggregate Ranking of Top Universities\nContact Us\nDeputy Vice-Chancellor (Research & Enterprise)\nPro Vice-Chancellor (Research)\nGraduate Research\nScholarships\nApplying for a Scholarship\nThesis\nThesis Preparation\nExamination\nGraduation\nHelp and Advice\nArc UNSW – Postgraduate Council\nArc UNSW – Student Life\nFinancial Support\nNew to UNSW Research\nEvents & Workshops\nStudy with Us\nResearch Training\nExtend Your Career\nNetworks\nNew to UNSW Research\nResearch Career Opportunities\nResearch Impact\nUNSW Areas of Research Strength\nFellows of Learned Academies\nResearch News & Stories\nResearch Integrity\nResearch Ethics & Compliance Support\nResearch Integrity for Staff\nSupervisors and Research Integrity\nResearch Ethics and Compliance Support\nAnimal Research Ethics\nHuman Research Ethics\nRadiation Safety\nResearch Export Controls\nResearch Strategy Office\nAbout the RSO\nPartner with us\nContact Us\nPartner With Us\nServices for Researchers\nResearch Grants and Contracts (RGC)\nAbout Us\nCurrent Funding Opportunities\nResources and Quicklinks\nSystems\nResearch Infrastructure\nAnalytical Centre (MWAC)\nContacts & About Us\nData Management, Storage and Tools\nNetwork Labs\nShared Research E