    "homepage_text": "Boyi Liu\nBoyi Liu |\n刘博一\nPh.D. student\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering\n,\nBeihang University\nDepartment of Data Science\n,\nCity University of Hong Kong\n[GitHub]\n[DBLP]\n[Google Scholar]\nEmail: boyliu [at] buaa [dot] edu [dot] cn\nBiography\nBoyi Liu\nis currently a third year Ph.D. student at the\nBeihang University\n, \n                            supervised by\nProf. Yongxin Tong\n.\n                            He is also a joint Ph.D student at the\nCity University of Hong Kong\n, \n                            co-supervised by\nProf. Zimu Zhou\n.\n                            Currently he is based at City University of Hong Kong.\n                            His research focuses on\nEfficient & Personalized Edge AI\n, aiming to unlock the full potential of data on edge devices:\nOn-device Data Preparation\nCross-device Collaborative Training\nEfficient Inference\nPublications\n2026\nTowards Asynchronous Client Collaboration in Personalized Federated Learning\nBoyi Liu\n, Zimu Zhou, Pengfei Gao, Shuo Kang, Yongxin Tong\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Communications\n(\nINFOCOM\n), 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nCAFEDistill: Learning Personalized and Dynamic Models through Federated Early-Exit Network Distillation\nBoyi Liu\n, Zimu Zhou, Yongxin Tong\nPreprint\n, 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nRevisiting Personalized Federated Learning in LLM Era: A Knowledge Sharing Perspective\nBoyi Liu\nTechnique Report\n, 2026\n[Paper]\nHarnessing Asynchrony to Balance Modalities in Multi-Modal Federated Learning\nYiming Ma,\nBoyi Liu\n, Zimu Zhou, Yanfeng Wang, Yongxin Tong\nInternational Conference on Database Systems for Advanced Applications\n(\nDASFAA\n), 2026\n[Paper]\nFedMosaic: Federated Retrieval-Augmented Generation via Parametric Adapters\nZhilin Liang, Yuxiang Wang, Zimu Zhou, Hainan Zhang,\nBoyi Liu\n, Yongxin Tong\nPreprint\n, 2026\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n2025\nPoster: Asynchronous Federated Learning Library and Benchmark with AFL-Lib\nBoyi Liu\n, Shuyuan Li, Zimu Zhou, Shuo Kang, Yiming Ma, Yongxin Tong\nACM Annual International Conference on Mobile Computing and Networking\n(\nMobiCom\n), 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nFedAIMS: Personalized Federated Learning with Adaptive Intermediate Supervision\nShuyuan Li,\nBoyi Liu\n, Zimu Zhou, Jin Dong\nFrontiers of Computer Science\n(\nFCS\n), 2025\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDarkDistill: Difficulty-Aligned Federated Early-Exit Network Training on Heterogeneous Devices\nLehao Qu, Shuyuan Li, Zimu Zhou,\nBoyi Liu\n, Yi Xu, Yongxin Tong\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(\nKDD\n), 2025\n[Paper]\n[Slides]\n[Poster]\nFactor for Agent (FAgent): Collaborative Learning of Large and Small Language Models\nShuyuan Li, Yongxin Tong, Qiang Yang, Zimu Zhou,\nBoyi Liu\nComputing Magazine of the CCF\n(\nCCCF\n), 2025\n[Paper]\n2024 and Before\nCASA: Clustered Federated Learning with Asynchronous Clients\nBoyi Liu\n, Yiming Ma, Zimu Zhou, Yexuan Shi, Shuyuan Li, Yongxin Tong\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining\n(\nKDD\n), 2024\n[Paper]\n[Slides]\n[Poster]\nFederated Computing: Query, Learning, and Beyond\nYongxin Tong, Yuxiang Zeng, Zimu Zhou,\nBoyi Liu\n, Yexuan Shi, Shuyuan Li, Ke Xu, Weifeng Lv\nIEEE Data Engineering Bulletin\n(\nDEB\n), 2023\n[Paper]\nDynamic Graph Learning Based on Hierarchical Memory for Origin-Destination Demand Prediction\nRuixing Zhang, Liangzhe Han,\nBoyi Liu\n, Jiayuan Zeng, Leilei Sun\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nIJCAI\n), 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nNews\n[2026/02] Two papers for early-exit network training and federated retrieval-augmented generation are preprint on arXiv now.\n[2026/01] One paper for multimodal federated learning was accepted by DASFAA 2026.\n[2025/12] One paper for personalized federated learning was accepted by INFOCOM 2026.\n[2025/08] One poster paper for asynchronous federated learning was accepted by MobiCom 2025.\n[2025/07] One paper for personalized federated learning was accepted by Frontiers of Computer Science (FCS).\n[2025/05] One paper for model heterogeneous federated learning was accepted by KDD 2025.\nAcademic Services\nReviewer for Journals: IEEE TKDE, IEEE TBD, ACM IMWUT\nReviewer for Conferences: ICLR, ICML, KDD, NeurIPS\nEducations\nJoint Ph.D.\nDepartment of Data Science, City University of Hong Kong, 2024 - 2028 (Expected)\nPh.D.\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Beihang University, 2023 - 2028 (Expected)\nB.E.\nSchool of Computer Science and Engineering, Beihang University, 2019 - 2023"
