    "homepage_text": "Home | Yan Jiang\ntop of page\nYan Jiang\nBe cool! Be elegant!\nyjiang@cuhk.edu.cn\nLog In\nYan Jiang\nAssistant Professor at Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nWelcome to my website!\nI would like to share my research and life with you here:)\nSearch\nZhaomin Lv was admitted to Ph.D. program at TAMU ECE!\nZhaomin Lv, the final-year undergraduate student in our lab, was admitted to Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Texas A&M University  to continue his Ph.D. study on energy systems!\n彦 江\nMar 2\n1 min read\nZhaomin Lv was awarded Undergraduate Research Award from CUHKSZ!\nZhaomin Lv, a final-year undergraduate student in New Energy Engineering at the School of Science and Engineering, who has been working on a research project related to transient performance control of power systems in my lab, was awarded Undergraduate Research Award from CUHKSZ!\n彦 江\nDec 24, 2025\n1 min read\nTalk at CDC 2025\nIt is my pleasure to give a talk \" Adaptive Pricing for Optimal Coordination in Networked Energy Systems with Nonsmooth Cost Functions \", in Invited Session \"Modelling, Control and Optimization of Electromobility: Synergies between Transportation, Energy, and Markets\" (Organizers: Maria Laura Delle Monache, Mladen Cicic) at the 2025 IEEE 64th Conference on Decision and Control, Rio de Janeiro, BRA, on 12/11/2025.\n彦 江\nDec 13, 2025\n1 min read\nTalk in SSE Weekly Colloquium\nIt is my pleasure to give a talk \" Charting a Stable, Safe, and Incentive Path Towards Green Energy Systems \" in SSE Weekly Colloquium at Chinese University of Hong Kong ,  Shenzhen , School of Science and Engineering, on 11/7/2025.\n彦 江\nNov 10, 2025\n1 min read\nContact\nThanks for your interest in Yan Jiang. For any concern on my research, feel free to get in touch and I will get back to you soon!\nSubmit\nThanks for submitting!\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nAbout | Yan Jiang\ntop of page\nYan Jiang\nBe cool! Be elegant!\nyjiang@cuhk.edu.cn\nLog In\nAbout\nMe\nI am a researcher interested in control theory, power systems, and electricity markets.\nEducation Background\n\"Knowledge is power.\"\nSept 2016 -- Aug 2021\nPh.D. in Electrical Engineering\nM.S.E. in Applied Mathematics and Statistics\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nJohns Hopkins University,\nBaltimore, USA\n​\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics and Statistic\ns\nJohns Hopkins University\n, Baltimore, USA\n​\nAdvisor: Prof. Enrique Mallada\nSept 2013 -- July 2016\nM.S. in Electrical Engineering\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology,\nWuhan, CHN\nAdvisor: Prof. Xinbo Ruan\nSept 2009 -- July 2013\nB.Eng in Electrical Engineering and Automation\nSchool of Electrical Engineering and Automation\nHarbin Institute of Technology\n, Harbin, CHN\n​\nAdvisor: Prof. Fengjiang Wu\nWork Experience\nJune 2024 -- Aug 2024\nVisiting Scholar\nInstitute for Mathematical and Statistical Innovatio,\nUniversity of Chicago\n, Chicago, USA\n​\nAug 2021 -- Aug 2024\nPostdoctoral Scholar\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering,\nUniversity of Washington\n, Seattle, USA\nAdvisor: Baosen Zhang\nJune 2020 -- Aug 2020\nResearch Intern\nPower Systems Engineering Center,\nNational Renewable Energy Laboratory\n, Golden, USA\nManager: Andrey Bernstein\nTeaching Assistant\nFall 2019\nApplied Optimal Control\nJohns Hopkins University\nFall 2018\nNetworked Dynamical Systems\nJohns Hopkins University\nSpring 2018\nControl Systems\nJohns Hopkins University\nHonors and Awards\nNov 2023\nMistletoe Research Fellowship ($10,000 Unfettered Research Grant),\nMomental Foundation\nMarch 2024\nNSF iREDEFINE Professional Development Award,\nECE Department Heads Association\nNov 2023\nClean Energy Institute\nPostdoctoral Gap Supplement ($10,000 Award),\nUniversity of Washington\nOct 2024\nFuture Digileader,\nDigital Futures\nNov 2024\nAsian Deans’ Forum Rising Star Women in Engineering,\nNational University of Singapore\nMay 2023\nClean Energy Institute Travel Grant,\nUniversity of Washington\nMarch 2023\nNYU Tandon Faculty First Look Fellowship,\nNew York University\nApril 2021\nStudent Registration Grant,\n2021 American Control Conference\nApril 2021\nGRO Travel Grant,\nJohns Hopkins University\nSept 2016\nECE Graduate Fellowship,\nJohns Hopkins University\nSept 2013\nAdmission Fellowship,\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nMay 2012\nHuichuan Technology Scholarship,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\nOct 2011\nSiemens A&D Scholarship,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\nMay, Oct 2011\nPeople’s Scholarship,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\nTechnical Reviewer\nJournals\nIEEE Transactions on Power Systems (TPS)\nIEEE Transactions on Smart Grid (TSG)\nIEEE Transactions on Automatic Control (TAC)\nIEEE Transactions on Control of Network Systems (TCNS)\nIEEE Control Systems Letters (L-CSS)\nElectric Power Systems Research (EPSR)\nConferences\nPower Systems Computation Conference (PSCC)\nIEEE Conference on Decision and Control (CDC)\nAmerican Control Conference (ACC)\nEuropean Control Conference (ECC)\nIFAC Conference on Networked Systems (Necsys)\nConference on Information Sciences and Systems (CISS)\nPower and Energy Society General Meeting (PESGM)\nbottom of page\n\n---\n\nAbout | Yan Jiang\ntop of page\nYan Jiang\nBe cool! Be elegant!\nyjiang@cuhk.edu.cn\nLog In\nAbout\nMe\nI am a researcher interested in control theory, power systems, and electricity markets.\nEducation Background\n\"Knowledge is power.\"\nSept 2016 -- Aug 2021\nPh.D. in Electrical Engineering\nM.S.E. in Applied Mathematics and Statistics\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nJohns Hopkins University,\nBaltimore, USA\n​\nDepartment of Applied Mathematics and Statistic\ns\nJohns Hopkins University\n, Baltimore, USA\n​\nAdvisor: Prof. Enrique Mallada\nSept 2013 -- July 2016\nM.S. in Electrical Engineering\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering\nHuazhong University of Science and T