  "deep_homepage::Miao Xiong::https://miaoxiong2320.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://miaoxiong2320.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "miao.xiong@u.nus.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/MiaoXiong2320",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/miao-xiong-9b1892187/",
    "homepage_text": "Miao Xiong\nMiao Xiong\nI am a PhD student at National University of Singapore advised by Prof.\nBryan Hooi\n. I obtained my undergraduate with double majors in Computer Science and Statistics at Zhejiang University.\nMy research interests lie in Trustworthy and Responsible AI, especially addressing trust-related challenges in foundation models. I am currently working on topics around LLMs (hallucination mitigation, RAG, constraint decoding etc). I also study Uncertainty Estimation, in the context of Calibration, Failure Prediction and Out-of-Distribution Detection to enhance the reliability of AI-based decision making system.\nI am passionate about advancing AI towards greater safety, equity, and sustainability, and remain enthusiastic about embracing new challenges in this dynamic field.\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nTwitter\n/\nLinkedin\n/\nEmail\nNews\n2024-06\nI’m happy to share that I’m starting a new position as a Research Intern at Apple!\n2024-04\nOur paper \"In-Context Sharpness as Alerts: An Inner Representation Perspective for Hallucination Mitigation\" is accepted at ICML 2024!\n2024-01\nOur paper \"Can LLMs Express Their Uncertainty? An Empirical Evaluation of Confidence Elicitation in LLMs\" is accepted at ICLR 2024!\n2023-09\nOur paper \"Proximity-Informed Calibration of Deep Neural Networks\" is accepted at NeurIPS 2023 as a Spotlight!\nResearch"
  },
