    "homepage_text": "RLLAB @ Yonsei\nRLLAB @ Yonsei\nHome\nGroup\nPublications\nProjects\nApply!\nWelcome to the Yonsei RLLAB! We develop learning algorithms that enable machines to master complex real-world tasks, especially with robots. Our research spans reinforcement learning, imitation learning, generative modeling, and their applications in robotics.\nJoin us!\nNews\n[Jan, 2026] Two papers were accepted to ICLR 2026\n[Nov, 2025] Youngwoon serves as an area chair for ICLR 2026 and ICML 2026\n[Nov, 2025]\nJunik (Heatz)\nwon\nthe PokeAgent Challenge at NeurIPS 2025\n[Oct, 2025] Youngwoon won 2025 Okawa Foundation Research Grant\n[Aug, 2025] Two papers were accepted to CoRL 2025\n[Jul, 2025] We won two 5-year grants ($150k and $100k per year) on humanoid AI\n[Apr, 2025] Youngwoon will be giving a talk at RSS 2025 workshop on\nRobot Evaluation for the Real World\n[Mar, 2025]\nKwanyoung\nwill join UC Berkeley as a PhD student working with Prof. Sergey Levine and Prof. Pieter Abbeel\n[Mar, 2025] We are co-organizing the workshop on\nWhole-body Control and Bimanual Manipulation\nat RSS 2025\n[Mar, 2025] We collaborate with Microsoft Research on robot foundation models ($70k)\n[Mar, 2025]\nHokyun\nwill start a 6-month research internship at Microsoft Research Asia\n[Feb, 2025] Youngwoon serves as an area chair for NeurIPS 2025\n[Jan, 2025] One paper was accepted to ICLR 2025\n[Dec, 2024] Yonsei AI department won the Brain Korea 21 (BK21) grant ($60k+ per year for each lab)\n[Nov, 2024] Youngwoon will be giving a talk at CoRL 2024 workshop on\nLearning Robotic Assembly of Industrial and Everyday Objects\n[Oct, 2024] Journal extension of\nFurnitureBench\nwas accepted to IJRR\n[Sep, 2024] Youngwoon serves as an associate editor for ICRA 2025\n[Sep, 2024] One paper was accepted to CoRL 2024\n[Aug, 2024] We won two 5-year grants ($100k per year), Global AI Frontier Lab and AI Research Center\n[Aug, 2024] We are co-organizing the workshop on\nWhole-body Control and Bimanual Manipulation\nat CoRL 2024\n[Jun, 2024] One paper was accepted to IROS 2024\n[May, 2024]\nOpen X-Embodiment Datasets and RT-X\nwon the\nIEEE ICRA Best Conference Paper Award\n[May, 2024] Two papers (\nHumanoidBench\nand\nDROID\n) were accepted to RSS 2024\n[Apr, 2024] We won the NRF Outstanding Young Scientist grant ($200k for 5 years)\n[Mar, 2024] Youngwoon serves as an area chair for NeurIPS 2024\n[Mar, 2024] We released\nDROID\n, a large-scale robotic dataset\n[Mar, 2024] We released\nHumanoidBench\n, a simulated humanoid robot benchmark\n[Jan, 2024] One paper was accepted to ICRA 2024\n[Jan, 2024] One paper was accepted to ICLR 2024\n[Jan, 2024] Youngwoon joined\nYonsei University\nas an assistant professor in AI"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Xiaoyan Hu::https://yannxiaoyanhu.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://yannxiaoyanhu.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "xh3@andrew.cmu.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/yannxiaoyanhu",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaoyan's Homepage\nXiaoyan Hu\nPostdoc @CMU RI\nShow Contacts\nEmail\nxh3@andrew.cmu.edu\nLocation\nPittsburgh\nPublication\nGoogle Scholar\nGithub\nyannxiaoyanhu\nTwitter\nYannwith2ns\nAbout me\nHi, thanks for visiting my homepage!\nI'm a postdoctoral researcher working with\nJeff Schneider\nat the\nRobotics Institute (RI)\n, \n            where my focus is on plasma control of the\nDIII-D tokamak\n. My goal is to design better control policies via reinforcement learning (RL) and broader machine learning frameworks.\n            We work closely with the\nPlasma Control Group\nat Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory (PPPL).\nI received my PhD degree in Computer Science and Engineering at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK), where\n            I’m blessed to be under co-supervision of Farzan Farnia and Ho-fung Leung. My thesis research focuses on provably efficient reinforcement learning\n            and its applications to adaptive selections of LLMs and generative AI models.\nResearch Interests\nTokamak Plasma Control\nHow can we design better feedback control of Tokamak plasma via RL?\nProvably efficient RL\nHow optimal behaviors be sample-efficiently learned?\nGenerative AI\nHow can RL and online learning assist the training, generation, and evaluation of generative models?\nBio\nMy full CV can be downloaded\nhere\n.\nProfessional Appointments\nCarnegie Mellon University\n2025 — Present\n- Postdoctoral Reseacher\n- PI: Jeff Schneider\nEducation\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK)\n2021 — 2025\n- Doctor of Philosophy in Computer Science and Engineering\n- Supervisors: Farzan Farnia, Ho-fung Leung\nSun Yat-sen University (SYSU)\n2017 — 2021\n- Bachelor of Sciences in Statistics\n- Supervisor: Li Xia\nResearch & Visiting Experience\nGuest PhD Student @\nDeLTA Lab\n, DIKU, University of Copenhagen\nOct 2023 - Jan 2024 (Host: Professor Mohammad Sadegh Talebi)\nVisiting PhD Student @ Huawei Noah's Ark Lab\nMay — August 2022\nAlgorithm Engineer @ Timi Studio Group, Tencent\nApril — June 2021\nInvited Talks\nAn Information Theoretic Approach to Interaction-Grounded Learning\n[slides]\n@\nScool Team, Inria\n, Jan 11, 2024\nProvably (More) Efficient Offline RL with Options\n[slides]\n@ DeLTA Seminar, Oct 12, 2023\nService\nReviewer\nNeurIPS (2024-), ICLR (2025-), ICML (2025), AISTATS (2025-)\nPublications\nXiaoyan HU, Lauren PICK, Ho-fung LEUNG, and Farzan FARNIA\n2025\nPromptWise: Online Learning for Cost-Aware Prompt Assignment in Generative Models\nPreprint\nXiaoyan HU, Ho-fung LEUNG, and Farzan FARNIA\n2025\nPAK-UCB Contextual Bandit: An Online Learning Approach to Prompt-Aware Selection of Generative Models and LLMs\nIn\nForty-Second International Conference on Machine Learning\n, ICML 2025. Vancouver, Canada. 13-19 July, 2025.\nXiaoyan HU, Ho-fung LEUNG, and Farzan FARNIA\n2025\nA Multi-Armed Bandit Approach to Online Selection and Evaluation of Generative Models\nIn\nTwenty-eighth International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics\n, AISTATS 2025.\n                    Mai Khao, Thailand, 3-5 May 2025.\nXiaoyan HU, Farzan FARNIA, and Ho-fung LEUNG\n2024\nAn Information Theoretic Approach to Interaction-Grounded Learning\nIn\nForty-first International Conference on Machine Learning\n, ICML 2024. Vienna, Austria, 21-27 July 2024.\nYulai ZHAO\n*\n, Wenhao ZHAN\n*\n, Xiaoyan HU\n*\n, Ho-fung LEUNG, Farzan FARNIA, Wen SUN, and Jason D. LEE (*=equal contribution and random ordering)\n2024\nProvably Efficient CVaR RL in Low-rank MDPs\nIn\nTwelfth International Conference on Learning Representations\n, ICLR 2024. Vienna, Austria, 7-11 May 2024. (A shorter version appeared in M3L Workshop @ NeurIPS 2023).\nXiaoyan HU and Ho-fung LEUNG\n2023\nProvably (More) Sample-Efficient Offline RL with Options\nIn\nThirty-seventh Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n, NeurIPS 2023. \n                    New Orleans, United States, 10 Dec-16 Dec 2023. Curran Associates, Inc.\nXiaoyan HU and Ho-fung LEUNG\n2023\nA tighter problem-dependent regret bound for risk-sensitive reinforcement learning\nIn\nProceedings of the 26th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics\n, AISTATS 2023. \n                    Proceedings of Machine Learning Research. Valencia, Spain, 25-27 April 2023. PMLR.\nXiaoyan HU and Ho-fung LEUNG\n2023\nProvably efficient offline learning with options (extended abstract)\nIn\nProceedings of the 22nd International Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems\n, AAMAS '23. \n                    London, United Kingdom, 29 May-2 June 2023. IFAAMS.\nPublications\nAll\nWeb design\nApplications\nWeb development\nSelect category\nAll\nWeb design\nApplications\nWeb development\nFinance\nWeb development\nOrizon\nWeb development\nFundo\nWeb design\nBrawlhalla\nApplications\nDSM.\nWeb design\nMetaSpark\nWeb design\nSummary\nWeb development\nTask Manager\nApplications\nArrival\nWeb development\nContact"
