    "homepage_text": "Jian Kang\n(Photo by my wife Ming Hu)\nJian Kang\nEmail: $FIRSTNAME$ [dot] $LASTNAME$ [at] mbzuai [dot] ac [dot] ae (all lowercase)\nI am an Assistant Professor in Department of Statistics & Data Science and Department of\n                    Computer Science (Division of Computational and Mathematical Sciences) at\nMBZUAI (Mohamed bin Zayed University of\n                        Artificial\n                        Intelligence)\n. Prior to that, I was a faculty member at the University of Rochester and\n                    received my Ph.D. degree in Computer Science at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC),\n                    where I am lucky to be advised by\nDr.\n                            Hanghang Tong\n.\nStudent recruitment:\nI am looking for highly motivated students to work with me as a\n                    MSc student, PhD student, visiting student, or research intern. If you are interested to work with\n                    me at MBZUAI, please send me an email with your CV and a brief introduction of yourself, e.g., your\n                    background, past experiences, research interests, and research proposal (optionally). Please use the\n                    title\n[$TERM$ $YEAR$] $YOURNAME$: $PURPOSE$\nfor your email (e.g., [Fall 2027] Jane Doe: PhD\n                    Application, [Fall 2027] John Doe: Intern Application).\nPlease note that, due to the large amount\n                        of emails, I may not be able to reply to them all.\nResearch\nMy research aims to\ndevelop personalized AI system to model and understand the interconnected\n                    world\n. It mainly investigates the following questions in three big themes:\nData:\nWhere do the data come from? What is the optimal data for a learning task?\nModel:\nCan we trust the model outputs?\nTask:\nHow to let a learning model solve complicated real-world tasks?\nIf your research interests include graph mining, generative AI (e.g., LLMs, diffusion models, flow models),\n            personalization, and trustworthy AI, please feel free to reach out!\nPublications\nFor a full list of publications, please check\nhere\nor my\ngoogle scholar\n.\nAwards and Honors\nEMNLP 2025 SAC Highlights\nOutstanding Reviewer Awards (KDD 2025, LoG 2022, NeurIPS 2022, CIKM 2021, ICLR 2020)\nRising Stars in Data Science, 2022 [\nLink\n]\nMavis Future Faculty Fellow, 2022 [\nLink\n]\nFinalist, 2022 Apple Scholars in AI/ML\nKDD 2020 Student Travel Award\nCIKM 2019 Student Travel Award\nBig Data 2018 Student Travel Award"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Ling Shao::https://ling-shao.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://ling-shao.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "﻿\nLing Shao\nLing Shao\nFounder of IIAI/MBZUAI\nAbout\nDr. Ling Shao was the founder of both the\nInception Institute of Artificial Intelligence (IIAI)\nand the\nMohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence (MBZUAI)\n, the world's first AI university. He also served as the CEO of IIAI (2018-2021) and simultaneously as the Provost and Executive Vice-President of MBZUAI (2019-2021). IIAI and MBZUAI have been pivotal in advancing AI research in the UAE since 2018. Moreover, he was a key founding member (employee #1) and the Chief Scientist of\nGroup 42 (G42)\n, a leading AI and advanced technology group headquartered in Abu Dhabi. In recognition of his scientific contributions, he was awarded the Mohammed bin Rashid Medal for Scientific Distinguishment, the highest scientific honor in the UAE, by His Highness\nSheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum\n, the Prime-Minister and Vice-President of the UAE, and the Ruler of Dubai.\nDr. Shao received his B.Eng. in Electronic and Information Engineering from the\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\n, his M.Sc. in Medical Image Analysis and his Ph.D. (D.Phil.) in Computer Vision from the\nUniversity of Oxford\n. He previously held positions of Chair Professor in Computer Vision and Machine Learning at the\nUniversity of East Anglia\n(2016-2018), Chair Professor in Computer Vision and Machine Intelligence at Northumbria University (2014-2016), Senior Lecturer at the\nUniversity of Sheffield\n(2009-2014), and Senior Scientist at\nPhilips Research\nin the Netherlands (2005-2009). His research interests include Computer Vision, Generative AI, Multimodal AI, Vision and Language, and AI for Healthcare. He has authored/co-authored over 500 papers in top conferences/journals, including CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, TPAMI and IJCV, and holds over 30 US/EU patents.\nDr. Shao has served on the editorial boards of IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology, IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics, and several other journals. He has edited four books and several special issues for journals such as IJCV. He was the General Chair for BMVC 2018, and has been an Area Chair or Program Committee member for numerous top conferences. He was selected as a 'Highly Cited Researcher' by the Web of Science (Clarivate) for 7 consecutive years in 2018-2024. He is an elected Fellow of the IEEE, the IAPR, the British Computer Society, and the IET. He was elected as a Member of the Mohammed bin Rashid Academy of Scientists (the National Academy of the UAE) in 2021.\nNews\nAwarded the Mohammed bin Rashid Medal for Scientific Distinguishment (the highest scientific recognition in the UAE).\nElected as a member of the Mohammed bin Rashid Academy of Scientists (the National Academy of the UAE).\nElected as a Fellow of the IEEE.\nProfessional Experience\nFounder & CEO, Inception Institute of Artificial Intelligence (IIAI), Abu Dhabi, UAE, Jan. 2018-Dec. 2021 (IIAI has been renamed as Inception, a G42 company)\nFounding Member & Chief Scientist, Group 42 (G42), UAE, 2018-2021\nFounder, Provost & Executive Vice-President, Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence (MBZUAI), UAE, 2018-2021\nChief Scientist, JD.com, China, 2017-2018\nChair Professor, University of East Anglia, UK, 2016-2018\nChair Professor, Northumbria University, UK, 2014-2016\nSenior Lecturer, University of Sheffield, UK, 2009-2014\nSenior Scientist, Philips Research, the Netherlands, 2005-2009\nSenior Engineer, Queen's University of Belfast, UK, 2005-2005\nEducation\nPh.D., University of Oxford\nM.Sc. (by research), University of Oxford\nB.Eng., University of Science and Technology of China\nPublications\nRefer to his\nGoogle Scholar profile\nfor more updated publications\nSelected Journal Articles\nLoading journal articles...\nSelected Conference Papers\nLoading conference papers...\nLast updated: July 2025"
  },
