      "zedong.wang@connect.ust.hk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/alshedivat",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jacky-zedong-wang",
    "homepage_text": "Zedong WANG\nzwangmw@cse.ust.hk\nResumé (CV)\nHello, visitor from\nan unknown location?! 🤔\nI am currently a second-year CSE PhD student at\nHKUST\n, advised by Prof.\nDan Xu\n. Prior to this, I was a visiting student at\nWestlake University\n, advised by Chair Prof.\nStan Z. Li\n. I completed my B.Eng in Electronic Information Engineering from\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\n, where I was fortunate to be advised by Prof.\nXinggang Wang\n.\nMy overarching goal is to build multi-modal multi-task machines that understand and interact with the world as holistically and efficiently as humans do. To achieve this, I worked on\n(i) multi-task learning:\nRep-MTL\n(ICCV’25 Highlight, top 2.3%),\n(ii) multi-modal understanding and generation:\nCARE-Edit\n(CVPR’26).\n(iii) efficient model architectures and optimizers:\nMogaNet\n(ICLR’24),\nSGG\n(ACL’25).\nI has been recognized as outstanding reviewer at multiple leading venues, including\nBMVC’25\n,\nICLR’25\n(top 2.6%),\nUniReps’25\n,\nECCV’24\n(top 2.7%),\nMM’24\n, and\nBMVC’24\n.\nNews\nFeb 21, 2026\nOne paper on image editing,\nCARE-Edit\n, got accepted at CVPR 2026. Glad to have worked on this with\nYucheng Wang\n. Thanks\nHugging Face\nfor sharing our work. [\nWechat\n] [\nVideo\n]\nNov 11, 2025\nI was recognized as\nOutstanding Reviewer\nat BMVC 2025 (rate: 21.3%, 247/1,161).\nNov 11, 2025\nI was recognized as\nOutstanding Reviewer\nat NLDL 2026 (1 of 22 awardees).\nOct 14, 2025\nI received the\nBest Reviewer Award\nat UniReps 2025 (one of the two awardees).\nJul 24, 2025\nOne paper on multi-task learning,\nRep-MTL\n, got accepted at ICCV 2025 and was selected as\nHighlight\npresentation\n(rate: 2.3%)\n. Thanks\nHugging Face\nfor sharing our work.\nMay 20, 2025\nI was recognized as\nNotable Reviewer\nat ICLR 2025 (rate: 2.6%, 473/18,323).\nMay 16, 2025\nOne paper on (M)LLM optimizer,\nSGG\n, got accepted at ACL 2025 (main).\nApr 04, 2025\nOne paper on image generation,\nMergeVQ\n, got accepted at CVPR 2025.\nMar 01, 2025\nMy suggestion to introduce distinct\nBorderline Accept/Reject (BA/BR) ratings\nfor initial reviews was\nacknowledged by ICCV’25 PCs\n, and was officially adopted and implemented at ICCV 2025.\nNov 04, 2024\nI was recognized as\nOutstanding Reviewer\nat ACM MM 2024 (rate: 139/x).\nNov 04, 2024\nI was recognized as\nOutstanding Reviewer\nat BMVC 2024 (rate: 19.3%, 166/860).\nSep 24, 2024\nI was recognized as\nOutstanding Reviewer\nat ECCV 2024 (rate: 2.7%, 198/7,293).\nInternship\nJul 2022 - Apr 2024\nWestlake AI Lab\n, working on visual representation learning and AI4Science.\nJun 2021 - Sep 2021\nSIAT-MMLab\n, working on semantic segmentation and text spotting.\nServices\nConference Reviewer / PC Member:\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2024 (TinyPapers), 2025, 2026\nAnnual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2024, 2025\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2024, 2025, 2026\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2025, 2026\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (\nECCV\n), 2024, 2026\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2025\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nACM MM\n), 2024\nIEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (\nWACV\n), 2026\nBMVA The British Machine Vision Conference (\nBMVC\n), 2024, 2025, 2026\nIAPR International Conference on Pattern Recognition (\nICPR\n), 2024\nNorthern Lights Deep Learning Conference (\nNLDL\n), 2026\nJournal Reviewer:\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (\nTIP\n)\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research (\nTMLR\n)\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (\nTKDE\n)\nMembership:\nThe British Machine Vision Association (\nBMVA\n), Student Member, 2025-present\nThe Computer Vision Foundation (\nCVF\n), Member, 2025-present\nChina Computer Federation (\nCCF\n), Student Member, 2024-2026\nChina Society of Image and Graphics (\nCSIG\n), Student Member, 2023-2024\nTeaching Assistant:\nCOMP 5212 Machine Learning, Fall 2025, Instructor: Prof.\nYi R. (May) Fung\nContacts\nWelcome opportunities to connect, exchange ideas, or explore potential collaborations. I am also open to internship and full-time opportunities. Please feel free to drop me emails (zedong.wang@connect.ust.hk).\nGoogle Scholar\nTwitter / X\nLinkedIn\nDINQ\nMisc\nVisitor Statistics"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Xing Wang::https://chemistry.illinois.edu/xingw": {
    "homepage": "https://chemistry.illinois.edu/xingw",
    "all_emails": [
      "xingw@illinois.edu",
      "chemistry@illinois.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xing Wang | Department of Chemistry | Illinois\nSkip to main content\nCollege of Liberal Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of Chemistry\nSearch\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nMeet Our Graduate Students\nWhy Study Chemistry\nStudent Financial Aid\nUndergraduate Application\nGraduate Application\nVisit Illinois\nAcademics\nUndergraduate Studies\nGeneral Chemistry\nGraduate Studies\nPolicy Manual (with bylaws)\nChemistry Learning Center\nCourse Listing\nSCS Academic Advising Office\nResearch\nResearch Overview\nAnalytical Chemistry\nChemical Biology\nInorganic Chemistry\nMaterials Chemistry\nOrganic Chemistry\nPhysical Chemistry\nResearch Concentrations\nUndergraduate Research\nNews & Events\nChemistry Master Calendar\nE-newsletter\nEvents\nHistory\nNews\nPublic Engagement and Outreach\nSeminars\nSesquicentennial Archives\nAnnual Report Archive\nPeople\nAdministration\nFaculty\nAll Faculty & Staff\nStudent Organizations\nCareers\nIllini Chemists\nIn Memoriam\nMerchandise\nNobel Prize Winners\nTeachers Ranked as Excellent by their Students\nHistory\nDiversity\nCommunity Building and Program Climate\nClimate and Diversity Action Plan\nCommunity Building Committee\nCommunity Values & Expectations\nEvents\nInitiatives\nOrganizations\nResources\nAlumni\nAlumni News & Events\nAlumni Awards\nMeet Our Alumni\nDonate to Chemistry\nRecent graduate features\nXing Wang\nContact Information\n0250 Everitt Laboratory (EL)\n1102 Everitt Lab MC 278\n1406 W. Green St\nUrbana, IL 61801\nxingw@illinois.edu\nResearch Areas\nAnalytical Chemistry\nChemical Biology\nMaterials Chemistry\nEdit Your Profile\nAssociate Professor of Bioengineering, and Faculty Affiliate in Chemistry\nWang Group Website\nDNA Star Technology\nPostdoc and Research Assistant Positions are Available\nBiography\nDr. Xing Wang is an Associate Professor in the Department of Bioengineering, affiliated with the Chemistry Department, IGB, HMNTL, and CCIL at UIUC.  He received a Ph.D. in chemistry from New York University and did a postdoc at Princeton University mainly focusing on RNA biology and noncoding RNA-mediated genome editing.  He is an inventor of the DNA Star, DNA Net, and DNA NanoGripper platforms, and developed the concept of pattern-recognition enabled multivalent molecular interactions.  He is a recipient of the Mikashi Award (UIUC) in 2021 and Spoke Award (CZ BioHub Chicago) in 2024.  Before joining UIUC, Dr. Wang was an Assistant Professor in the Department of Chemistry and Chemical Biology and the Center for Biotechnology and Interdisciplinary Studies, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute.\nResearch Interests\nDr. Wang is the inventor of the DNA Star, DNA Net, and DNA NanoGripper platforms that utilizes designer DNA nanostructures (DDNs) to create biosensors and biomedicines.  His Nucleic Acids Programming Lab engineers DDNs that offer a \"plug-and-play\" platform to create functional nanomaterials with aptamers, nanobodies, fluorophores for developing (1) ultrasensitive and inexpensive biosensors for rapid disease diagnostics in both point-of-care and high throughput settings, (2) effective therapeutic candidates for infectious disease treatment/prevention and cancer immunotherapy, (3) new strategies and reagents for high resolution imaging.  His research group is supported by NIH and NSF.\nEducation\nPh.D. in Chemistry, New York University\nAdditional Campus Affiliations\nAssociate Professor, Bioengineering\nAssociate Professor, Micro and Nanotechnology Lab\nAssociate Professor, Carl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology\nAssociate Professor, Chemistry\nAcademic Service\nDr. Wang directs the Nucleic Acids Programming Lab (NAPL) at UIUC.  He is affiliated with HMNTL, IGB, and CCIL.\nHighlighted Publications\nDwivedy, A., Baskaran, D., Sharma, G., Hong, W., Gandavadi, D., Krissanaprasit, A., Han, J., Liu, Y., Zimmers, Z., Mafokwane, T., Hayah, I., Chauhan, N., Zheng, M., Yao, S., Fraser, K., Decker, J. S., Jin, X., Wang, H., Friedman, A. D., & Wang, X. (2025). Engineering Novel DNA Nanoarchitectures for Targeted Drug Delivery and Aptamer Mediated Apoptosis in Cancer Therapeutics.\nAdvanced Functional Materials\n,\n35\n(22), Article 2425394.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/adfm.202425394\nZhou, L., Xiong, Y., Dwivedy, A., Zheng, M., Cooper, L., Shepherd, S., Song, T., Hong, W., Le, L. T. P., Chen, X., Umrao, S., Rong, L., Wang, T., Cunningham, B. T., & Wang, X. (2024). Bioinspired designer DNA NanoGripper for virus sensing and potential inhibition.\nScience Robotics\n,\n9\n(96), Article eadi2084.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1126/scirobotics.adi2084\nChauhan, N., Xiong, Y., Ren, S., Dwivedy, A., Magazine, N., Zhou, L., Jin, X., Zhang, T., Cunningham, B. T., Yao, S., Huang, W., & Wang, X. (2023). Net-Shaped DNA Nanostructures Designed for Rapid/Sensitive Detection and Potential Inhibition of the SARS-CoV-2 Virus.\nJournal of the American Chemical Society\n,\n145\n(37), 20214-20228.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.2c04835\nRen, S., Fraser, K., Kuo, L., Chauhan, N., Adrian, A. T., Zhang, F., Linhardt, R. J., Kwon, P. S., & Wang, X. (2022). Designer DNA nanostructures for viral inhibition.\nNature Protocols\n,\n17\n(2), 282-326.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41596-021-00641-y\nKwon, P. S., Ren, S., Kwon, S. J., Kizer, M. E., Kuo, L., Xie, M., Zhu, D., Zhou, F., Zhang, F., Kim, D., Fraser, K., Kramer, L. D., Seeman, N. C., Dordick, J. S., Linhardt, R. J., Chao, J., & Wang, X. (2020). Designer DNA architecture offers precise and multivalent spatial pattern-recognition for viral sensing and inhibition.\nNature Chemistry\n,\n12\n(1), 26-35.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41557-019-0369-8\nChauhan, N., & Wang, X. (2021). Nanocages for virus inhibition.\nNature Materials\n,\n20\n(9), 1176-1177.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41563-021-01088-y\nLi, N., Canady, T. D., Huang, Q., Wang, X., Fried, G. A., & Cunningham, B. T. (2021). Photonic resonator interferometric scattering microscopy.\nNature communications\n,\n12\n(1), Article 1744.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-21999-3\nHe, Z., Han, Z., Kizer, M., Linhardt, R. J., Wang, X., Sinyukov, A. M., Wang, J., Deckert, V., Sokolov, A. V., Hu, J., & Scully, M. O. (2019). Tip-Enhanced Raman Imaging of Single-Stranded DNA with Single Base Resolution.\nJournal of the American Chemical Society\n,\n141\n(2), 753-757.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.8b11506\nKizer, M. E., Linhardt, R. J., Chandrasekaran, A. R., & Wang, X. (2019). A Molecular Hero Suit for In Vitro and In Vivo DNA Nanostructures.\nSmall\n,\n15\n(26), Article 1805386.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/smll.201805386\nWang, X., Chandrasekaran, A. R., Shen, Z., Ohayon, Y. P., Wang, T., Kizer, M. E., Sha, R., Mao, C., Yan, H., Zhang, X., Liao, S., Ding, B., Chakraborty, B., Jonoska, N., Niu, D., Gu, H., Chao, J., Gao, X., Li, Y., ... Seeman, N. C. (2019). Paranemic Crossover DNA: There and Back Again.\nChemical reviews\n,\n119\n(10), 6273-6289.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/acs.chemrev.8b00207\nView all publications on Illinois Experts\nRecent Publications\nSong, T., Dwivedy, A., Gandavadi, D., Chandran, G., An, Y., Zheng, M., Wang, X., Zhou, L., Zhao, Y., & Wang, X. (2026). DNA Origami-Templated Aptamer Chiral Structures Realize Cellular Enantioselectivity.\nAdvanced Materials\n,\n38\n(12), Article e19007. Advance online publication.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202519007\nBhaskar, S., Wang, W., Lee, H., Liu, L., Umrao, S., Liu, W., Bacon, A., Tibbs, J., Khemtonglang, K., Tan, A., Ayupova, T., Chen, W. C., Wang, X., & Cunningham, B. T. (2025). Photonic Crystal Grating Resonance and Interfaces for Health Diagnostic Technologies.\nChemical reviews\n,\n125\n(14), 6435-6540. Advance online publication.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/acs.chemrev.4c00653\nDwivedy, A., Baskaran, D., Sharma, G., Hong, W., Gandavadi, D., Krissanaprasit, A., Han, J., Liu, Y., Zimmers, Z., Mafokwane, T., Hayah, I., Chauhan, N., Zheng, M., Yao, S., Fraser, K., Decker, J. S., Jin, X., Wang, H., Friedman, A. D., & Wang, X. (2025). Engineering Novel DNA Nanoarchitectures for Targeted Drug Delivery and Aptamer Mediated Apoptosis in Cancer Therapeutics.\nAdvanced Functional Materials\n,\n35\n(22), Article 2425394.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/adfm.202425394\nGandavadi, D., Talbot, H., Dwivedy, A., Umrao, S., Rodriguez, A., Cho, H., Zheng, M., Chandrasekaran, A. R., & Wang, X. (2025). DNA Nanostructure Self-Assembly in an Aqueous Ionic Liquid Solution with Enhanced Stability and Target Binding Affinity.\nJournal of the American Chemical Society\n,\n147\n(46), 42635-42646.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.5c13969\nIm, S., Hong, W., Chandran, G. P., Wang, X., & Zhao, Y. (2025). Probing millikelvin temperature sensitivity in chiral nanoparticles via optical forces.\nAPL Materials\n,\n13\n(10), Article 101112.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1063/5.0282973\nView all publications on Illinois Experts\nCollege of Liberal Arts & Sciences\nDepartment of Chemistry\n505 South Mathews Avenue\nUrbana,\n                    IL\n                    61801\n(217) 333-5071\nEmail:\nchemistry@illinois.edu\nLogin"
