  "deep_homepage::Xiaobo Xia::https://xiaoboxia.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://xiaoboxia.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "xiaoboxia@ustc.edu.cn",
      "xiaoboxia.uni@gmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/xiaoboxia",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaobo Xia's Homepage\nXiaobo Xia\n(夏晓波)\nProfessor & Ph.D. Advisor\nSchool of Information Science and Technology, University of Science and Technology of China\nalso affiliate with\nPh.D. Supervisor,\nArtificial General Intelligence Institute\nE-mail: xiaoboxia [AT] ustc.edu.cn / xiaoboxia.uni [AT] gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nGroup Code Repo on Github\nAbout Me\nDr. Xiaobo Xia currently is a professor at\nSchool of Information Science and Technology, University of Science and Technology of China\n.\nBefore that,\nhe was a postdoctoral research fellow at\nSchool of Computing\nof\nNational University of Singapore\n.\nHe obtained his Ph.D. degree at\nSchool of Computer Science\nof\nThe University of Sydney\nand received his bachelor degree at\nXidian University\n.\nHe is a recipient of Google Fellowship (Google AI), JProcRSNSW Ph.D. Thesis Award, and NeurIPS Top Area Chair Award.\nHe regularly serves as area chairs for ICML/NeurIPS/ICLR/ACM MM.\nHe also serve as an Action Editor for\nTransactions on Machine Learning Research\n.\nGroup\n|\nPublications\n|\nCourse\n|\nExperience\n|\nAwards\n|\nService\nResearch Focus\nOur research is centered on building world models and foundational models that integrate physical laws and spatio-temporal dimensions, leveraging multimodal data and techniques to push the boundaries of AI’s ability to model and reason within complex realistic environments.\nIn our work, we aim to connect fundamental theory and novel algorithms with high-impact applications, particularly in the scientific domain.\nCurrent key words: world models, foundational models, multimodal learning, learning theory.\nRecruitment\nVarious positions (Postdoctoral Researchers/Full-time Ph.D./Master Program/Research Engineers/Assistants) are avaliable. Base: Hefei or Shanghai.\nPlease email me if you are interested in above topics.\nRecent News\n2026.03: Serve as an Acition Editor for Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n2026.02: Three papers are accepted to CVPR 2026.\n2026.02: Serve as an Area Chair for ACM MM 2026.\n2026.01: Two papers are accepted to ICLR 2026.\n2025.11: Two papers are accepted to AAAI 2026 (2 Orals).\n2025.11: Serve as an Area Chair for ICML 2026.\n2025.10: One paper is accepted to Nexus (Cell Press).\n2025.09: Five papers are accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n2025.08: Serve as an Area Chair for ICLR 2026.\n2025.07: One paper is accepted to ACM MM 2025 as Oral.\n2025.06: One paper is accepted to ICCV 2025 as Highlight.\n2025.05: One paper is accepted to ICML 2025.\n2025.02: Serve as an Area Chair for NeurIPS 2025."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Mang Ye::https://marswhu.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://marswhu.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "yemang@whu.edu.cn",
      "mangye16@gmail.com"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/mangye16",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "﻿\nMang Ye - Wuhan University\nMang Ye\nProfessor\nSchool of Computer Science\nWuhan University\n[\nBio\n] [\nGoogle Scholar\n][\nDBLP\n][\nGitHub\n] [\n学校主页\n]\nRoom E503, School of Computer Science, Wuhan University\nEmail:\nyemang AT whu.edu.cn\n,\nmangye16 AT gmail.com\nWelcome to the Multimedia Analysis and ReaSoning (MARS) Group at the Wuhan University, led by Prof. Mang Ye.\nOur research interests include privacy-preserving multi-modal learning and its applications in multimedia analysis and reasoning.\n[\nOpen Positions (25硕博招生、博后招聘、本科实习生)\n]\n      [\n本科生科研入门流程\n]\nLooking for self-motivated Ph.D/M.S./Undergraduate students.\n[25级入学的博士还有名额，2024年11月更新]\nLooking for PostDocs in computer vision.\n[\n重点资助博后\n]\nNews\n[10/2025]\nEight postgraduate students (6 PhD, 2 master) have been awarded the National Scholarship.\n[09/2025]\n12 papers (2 Spotlights) on MLLM Tuning, Multi-modal ReID, Federated Learning are accepted by NeurIPS 2025.\n[08/2025]\nProf. Ye is invited to serve as AAAI 2026, ICLR 2026 and CVPR 2026 Area Chair.\n[05/2025]\nSeveral papers on MLLM Tuning, Emotion Recognition, Federated Learning are accepted by ICML2025/IJCAI 2025.\n[02/2025]\nSeven papers on ReID, MLLM Tuning, Emotion Recognition, Federated Learning are accepted by CVPR 2025.\n[12/2024]\nProf. Ye serves as the Associate Editor for IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (CCF-A).\n[12/2024]\nFour papers on NightTime ReID, Vertical Federated Learning are accepted by AAAI 2025.\n[12/2024]\nProf. Ye is invited to serve as ICML 2025 Area Chair.\n[11/2024]\nOur team is recognized as one of the Outstanding Youth Teams of Wuhan University.\n[link]\n[11/2024]\nWenke Huang (黄文柯, PhD student) and Guancheng Wan (万冠呈, undergraduate student) won the Lei Jun Scholarship (100,000 RMB, awarded to 10 students per year).\n[link]\n[11/2024]\nFive students have been awarded the National Scholarship. Congratulations to Wuxuan Shi (施武轩，PhD student), Xiuwen Fang (方修文，PhD student), Zesen Wu (吴泽森，master student), Tongxin Wang (王同鑫，master student), Chenyue Li (李辰玥，undergraduate student).\n[10/2024]\nOur survey paper on Object ReID is accepted by IJCV.\n[09/2024]\nFour papers on Visible-Infrared ReID, Federated Learning and Continual Learning are accepted at NeurIPS 2024, including contributions from a 2nd-year and a 3rd-year undergraduate.\n[08/2024]\nProf. Ye is invited to serve as ICLR 2025 and CVPR 2025 Area Chair.\n[07/2024]\nTwo papers on Cloth-Changing ReID and Graph Learning are accepted by ACM MM 2024.\n[07/2024]\nThree papers on Multi-Modal Intention Understanding, Widelife ReID and Federated Learning are accepted by ECCV 2024, including contributions from a 2rd-year undergraduate.\n[05/2024]\nProf. Ye serves as the Associate Editor for IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (CCF-A).\n[02/2024]\nFive papers on Federated Learning and Multi-Modal Learning accepted by CVPR 2024, including contributions from two 3rd-year undergraduates.\n[01/2024]\nProf. Ye is invited to serve as ECCV 2024 and ACM MM 2024 Area Chair.\n[12/2023]\nFour papers on Person Generation, Federated Learning and Multi-modal Learning accepted by AAAI 2024.\n[11/2023]\nThree papers on Federated Learning, Visible-Infrared ReID, Sketch ReID accepted by IEEE TPAMI.\n[08/2023]\nA survey on Hetergeneous Federated Learning is accepted by ACM Computing Surveys.\n[arXiv]\n[08/2023]\nProf. Ye is invited to serve as CVPR 2024 Area Chair.\n[07/2023]\nThree papers on Unsupervised VI-ReID, Continual Learning, Federated Learning accepted by ICCV 2023.\n[01/2020]\nA survey on deep person re-identification with a powerful AGW baseline.\n[ArXiv]\n[Code].\nMore News\nBiography\n2019-2020, Research Scientist,\nInception Institute of Artificial Intelligence\n, Abu Dhabi, UAE.\n2016-2019, Ph.D student,\nHong Kong Baptist University\n, supervised by\nProf. Pong C. Yuen\n.\n2018.07-2018.12, Visiting scholar at Columbia University, working with\nProf. Shih-Fu Chang\n.\n2013-2016, MSc,\nNERCMS\n,\nWuhan\n        University\n,\n      working with\nDr. Chao Liang\nand\nProf. Ruimin Hu\n.\n2009-2013,B.E.,\nElectronic Information Science and Technology\n,\nWuhan University\n, China.\nAwards\n2021, Winner of Person Re-Identification Track in ICCV 2021 MMVRAC Challenge\n2021, Young Elite Scientist Sponsorship Program by CAST\n2019, Yakun Scholarship Scheme for Mainland Postgraduate Team\n2019, Excellent Teaching Assistant Performance Award\n2016-2018,\nComputer Science Department RPg Performance Award\n2016-2019,\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship\n2016, Academic Breakthrough Prize awarded by NERCMS\n2015, National Scholarship\n2015,\nGoogle Excellence\n        Scholarship\n2014, National Scholarship\nCopyright © 2024\nMultimedia Analysis & Reasoning (MARS) Lab\nWuhan University 武汉大学"
  },
