    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Ningyuan Li, PhD., P.Eng | Centre for Pavement and Transportation Technology | University of Waterloo\nSkip to main content\nOpen Search Location\nSearch for\nSearch Location\nOn all sites\nOn this site\nNingyuan Li, PhD., P.Eng\nAdjunct Professor\nResearch Interests:\nTransport System Assessment\nAutomation of Pavement Condition Data Collection and Evaluation\nModelling Pavement Performance and Maintenance Programming\nPerformance-based Pavement Design, Construction, and Rehabilitation Specifications and Criteria\nAnalysis of Optimal Investment Strategies for Multi-Year Performance Measures and Preservation Programming\nBiography\nDr. Li is an Adjunct Professor of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Waterloo, and a member of the Principal Researchers in the Pavement Group at the Centre for Pavement and Transportation Technology (CPATT). His research interests are in the areas of road asset management, including highway performance measures and prediction modelling, automation of pavement condition data collection, development of pavement evaluation standards and new technologies, pavement network maintenance programming and investment planning. Dr. Li works for the Ministry of Transportation Ontario (MTO) and his main responsibilities include: technical support of pavement management system operation and its wide applications to various MTO business acitivities. He has over 20 years experience in highway engineering and is a licensed professional engineer in teh province of Ontario. He has authored and co-authored over 90 referred papers and technical reports. Dr. Li has also worked for the World Bank and Asia Development Bank on a large number of road maintenance related international projects.\nSelected Publications\nN. Li and T. Kazmierowski (2008), Engineering Tools for Standard Applied in Preserving Ontario Provincial Highways, in\nProceedings\nof the 7th International Conference on Managing Pavement Assets, Calgary, Ontario.\nS. Tighe, N. Li and T. Kazmierowski (2008), Evaluation of Semi-automated and Automated Pavement Distress Collection for Network-Level Pavement Management,\nTransportation Research Record\n: Journal of the Transportation Research Board, No. 2084, 11-17.\nS. Tighe, N. Li, L. Falls and R. Haas (2007), Incorporating Road Safety into Pavement Mangement, T\nransportation Research Record\n: Journal of the Transportation Research Board, No. 1699, 1-10.\nN. Li, R. Haas and W. Xie (1998), Development of a New Asphalt Pavement Performance Prediction Model,\nCanadian Journal of Civil Engineering\n, Can.J.Civ.Eng.24: 547-559.\nN. Li, R. Haas and M. Huot (1998), Cost-Effectiveness Based Priority Programming of Standardized Pavement Maintenance,\nTransportation Research Record\n: Journal of the Transportation Research Board, No. 1592, 8-16.\nN. Li, R. Haas and M. Huot (1997), Integer Programming of Maintenance and Rehabilitation Treatments for Pavement Networks,\nTransportation Research Record\n: Journal of the Transportation Research Board, No. 1629, 242-248.\nProfessional Affiliations\nRegistered Profession Engineer, Province of Ontario\nEditorial Board of International Journal of Pavement Research Technology\nSteering Committee of Road Profiler Used Group (RPUG)\nCommittee of Pavement Preservation (AHD18), TRB\nCommittee of Pavement Monitoring and Evaluation (AF), TRB\nContact Information\nPhone: (416) 235-3518\nFax: (416) 235-3919\nEmail: nli@uwaterloo.ca\nResearcher"
  },
