    "homepage_text": "Zhouxing Shi\nZhouxing Shi\nAssistant Professor at University of California, Riverside\nI am an Assistant Professor at Department of Computer Science and Engineering, University of California, Riverside.\nI completed Ph.D. at UCLA Computer Science Department in 2025, advised by\nProf. Cho-Jui Hsieh\n.\nI received my B.Eng. degree from the CST department at Tsinghua University in 2020.\nMy research focus is on machine learning (ML), especially developing more trustworthy and reliable AI models.\nSpecifically, some of my current interests include but are not limited to:\nthe interplay between generative AI, verifiers and formal methods;\nLLM alignment;\nformal verification for ML and training verifiable ML models for mission-critical applications;\nrobustness and safety for ML models;\nGroup\nPhD students\nShangjian Yin\n(Fall 2025-)\nProspective Students:\nI am looking for motivated students to join my group. See\nthis page\nfor details.\nAwards\nNVIDIA Academic Grant Program Award, 2025\nUCLA Dissertation Year Award (fellowship), 2024-2025\nAmazon Fellowship (Amazon & UCLA Science Hub fellowship), 2022-2023\n4X first-place winner at the International Verification of Neural Networks Competition (VNN-COMP), 2021-2024\nSelected Publications\n(* Equal contribution)\nCertified Training with Branch-and-Bound for Lyapunov-stable Neural Control\nCode\nZhouxing Shi, Haoyu Li, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Huan Zhang\nL4DC 2026\nNeural Network Verification with Branch-and-Bound for General Nonlinearities\nCode\nBenchmark\narXiv\nZhouxing Shi\n*\n, Qirui Jin\n*\n, Zico Kolter, Suman Jana, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Huan Zhang\nTACAS 2025\nDefending LLMs against Jailbreaking Attacks via Backtranslation\nCode\narXiv\nYihan Wang\n*\n, Zhouxing Shi\n*\n, Andrew Bai, Cho-Jui Hsieh\nACL-Findings 2024\nEffective Robustness against Natural Distribution Shifts for Models with Different Training Data\nDemo\narXiv\nZhouxing Shi, Nicholas Carlini, Ananth Balashankar, Ludwig Schmidt, Cho-Jui Hsieh, Alex Beutel, Yao Qin\nNeurIPS 2023\nAutomatic Perturbation Analysis for Scalable Certified Robustness and Beyond\nCode\narXiv\nKaidi Xu\n*\n, Zhouxing Shi\n*\n, Huan Zhang\n*\n, Yihan Wang, Kai-Wei Chang, Minlie Huang, Bhavya Kailkhura, Xue Lin, Cho-Jui Hsieh\nNeurIPS 2020"
  },
