    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Di Niu @ University of Alberta\nÂ\nÂ\nÂ\nDi Niu @ University of Alberta\nÂ\nÂ\nShort Bio\nIâm currently a Professor in the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nUniversity of Alberta\n.Â  I did my PhD in the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nUniversity of Toronto\n, from 2008 to 2012. I received the B.Eng. degree in 2005 from the Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering,\nSun Yat-sen (Zhongshan) University\n, Guangzhou, China. Now Iâm leading\na team of graduate students\nworking on exciting topics in the cross-disciplinary areas of AI, data science, parallel and distributed computing systems.\nÂ\nProfessor\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Alberta\nEdmonton, Alberta, Canada\nResearch Areas\n: Generative AI, Large Language Model, Diffusion Models, parallel and distributed computing, computing systems to support generative AI, on-device and edge AI acceleration, NLP and knowledge representation, computer vision.\nContact me\nEmail: dniu at ualberta dot ca\nCurriculum Vitae\nCan be provided upon request.\nLinks\nUniversity of Alberta\nECE Department, UofA\nNews\nPapers accepted to MICRO 2025, KDD 2025, MLSys 2025, AAAI 2025, COLING 2025, TMLR.\nOpenings\nI currenlty have openings for PhD, MSc and Postdoc positions in the following areas:\n-\nLLMs, pretraining, fine-tuning, alignment, prompting and reasoning. LLM on-device acceleration.\n-\nDiffusion Models and Image Editing, their pretraining, fine-tuning and on-device acceleration\n-\nSoftware-hardware co-optimization for deep learning acceleration (especially GenAI)\n-\nParallel and distributed systems design, high performance computing for AI\n- Federated and distributed learning\n- Large language models and knowledge representation (for Medical QA and Code generation)\n-\nAI for science\nÂ\nÂ"
  },
