    "homepage_text": "﻿\nHomepage of Xiang Bai\nDr. Xiang Bai,\nProfessor\nEmail:\nxbai(at)hust(dot)edu(dot)cn; xiang.bai(at)gmail(dot)com\n【中文主页】\nAbout me\nI am a professor at the Department of Artificial Intelligence and Automation, Huazhong University of Science and Technology (HUST). I\n          received my Ph.D. in Communication and Information Engineering, HUST. My research interests focus on Computer Vision, Pattern Recognition,\n          and Deep Learning. The developed scene text detection and recognition technology has been widely used in Huawei, Alibaba, Meituan and many\n          other products or systems, and has achieved good economic and social benefits. I lead the Vision and Learning Representation Group and have\n          published more than 250 papers in journals and academic conferences at home and abroad, including more than 80 JCR Q1 journals and CCF Class\n          A papers.\nHere are some previous projects:\nShape Representation, 2D\\3D Shape matching and Retrieval\nScene Text Detection and Recognition:\nA brief survey\n,\nSlice (2014)\n,\nSlice (2017)\nObject Detection and Image Classification, Contour Detection\\Grouping\nOpening Positions\n: (1) I am currently recruiting self-motivated and dedicated Ph.D./M.S. students with\n          solid background in mathematics, programming, or writtern English etc. Please feel free to contact me if you are interested. (2) I plan to\n          host a selected number of PostDocs with strong research background. (3) Looking for fresh faculty members to join our group, please contact\n          me at least half a year ahead of your arriving.\nRecent News\nApr., 2022:\nWe received a letter of appreciation from the Ethiopian Embassy\n                in Beijing.\nJan., 2022:\nWe established HUST-CalmCar Autonomous Driving Technology\n                Center.\nOct., 2021:\nZheng Zhang received ICCV 2021 Best Paper award (Marr Prize).\nSep., 2020:\nDingkang Liang and Chenfeng Xu won the Vision Meets Drone Crowd\n                Counting Challenge 2020 (VisDrone2020).\nOct., 2019:\nDejia Song et al won the Visual Object Tracking Challenge 2019\n                (VOT2019).\nOct., 2019:\nWe won The 5th China College Students' \"Internet Plus\"\n                Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition\nSep., 2019:\nI received the IAPR/ICDAR Young Investigator Award\nJun., 2019:\nBaoguang Shi received the Excellent Doctorate Dissertation\n                Award\nMay., 2019:\nWe won the ICDAR 2019 Robust Reading Competition on Reading\n                Chinese Text on Signboard\nNov., 2018:\nSong Bai received the Excellent Doctorate Dissertation Award\nNov., 2018:\nMinghui Liao received the CCF-CV Academic Emerging Award\nApril., 2017: The invited talk \"Oriented Scene Text Detection\n              Revisited\" at VALSE 2017, Xiamen. [\nPPT\n]\nFeb., 2017: Four papers accepted by CVPR 2017.\nJan., 2017: I become an editorial board member of the journal\n              \"Pattern Recognition\"\nNov.,2016:\nThree papers accepted by AAAI 2017! Congratulations to Song,\n                Minghui and Baoguang!\nJune, 2016: Baoguang got the support from CSC for visiting Cornell\n              University. Congratulations!\nMarch, 2016: We achieved the first place in\nShrec2016 competition: Large-Scale 3D Shape Retrieval\nunder the perturbed case.\nRecent Publications\n(More)\nLiao M, Zou Z, Wan Z, Yao C, Bai X. Real-Time Scene Text Detection\n            with Differentiable Binarization and Adaptive Scale Fusion.\nIEEE transactions on pattern analysis and machine intelligence\n              (TPAMI)\n, 2022\nQi J, Gao Y, Hu Y, et al. Occluded Video Instance Segmentation: A\n            Benchmark.\nInt. Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n,\n            2022\nYuan Y, Liu X, Dikubab W, Liu H, Ji Z, Wu Z, Bai X. Syntax-Aware\n            Network for Handwritten Mathematical Expression Recognition.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nWang H, Liao J, Cheng T, et al. Knowledge Mining with Scene Text for\n            Fine-Grained Recognition.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nTang J, Zhang W, Liu H, et al. Few Could Be Better Than All: Feature\n            Sampling and Grouping for Scene Text Detection.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nLiu X, Bai S, Bai X. An Empirical Study of End-to-End Temporal\n            Action Detection.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nSong S, Wan J, Yang Z, Tang J, Cheng W, Bai X, Yao C.\n            Vision-Language Pre-Training for Boosting Scene Text\n            Detectors.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nXu C, Liang D, Xu Y, Bai S, Zhan W, Bai X, Tomizuka M. AutoScale:\n            Learning to Scale for Crowd Counting.\nInt. Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n, 2022\nServices:\nAssociate Editor of\nPattern Recognition\n(2017-),\nPatten Recognition Letters\n(2016-),\nFrontier of\n            Computer Science\n,\nNeurocomputing\n(2015-)\nGuest Editor of journal special isssue: (1)\nSpecial\n            Section on Deep Learning\n,\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology\n, 2017; (2)\nMulti-Instance\n            Learning in Pattern Recognition and Vision\n,\nPattern Recognition\n, 2017; (3)\nDeep Learning Applications in Computer Vision\n,\nFrontier of Computer Science\n,\n          2017; (4)\nEfficient\n            Shape Representation, Matching, Ranking, and its Applications\n,\nPattern Recognition Letters\n, 2016.\nGeneral Chair of\nthe 6th Vision and Learning Seminar\n(\nVALSE'16\n), Wuhan.\nProgram Chair of\nthe 1st IEEE SPS Signal and Data Science Forum\n(\nSIDAS'16\n), Wuhan.\nOrganizing Chair of\nthe 1st Int. Workshop on Deep Learning for Pattern Recognition\n(\nDLPR'16\n), in conjunction with ICPR'16.\nOrganizaing Chair of\nSpecial Session on Visual Semantic Learning form Big Surveillance Data\n(\nVISA\n), WCCI/IJCNN'16.\nTPC of\nCVPR\n(08-17),\nICCV\n(09-17),\nECCV\n(10-16),\nNIPS\n(15-16),\nAAAI\n(17),\nAISTAT\n(17),\nBMVC\n(16-17), etc;\nSenior TPC of\nIJCAI\n17.\nArea Chair of\nICIP\n17.\nCompetition Chair of\nICPR\n18.\nReviewers of more than 40 int. journals including\nTPAMI, IJCV, TIP, Pattern Recognition, TNNLS, TMM, TCYB, TIE, TIST,\n            TVCG, IVC, CVIU, PRL, SPL, IJDAR, IJPRAI, etc\n.\nAwards and Honors\nIAPR Fellow 2020\nIJCAI 2019 Early Career Invited Reporter\nAAAI 2019 Distinguished Senior Committee Member Award\nIAPR/ICDAR 2019 Young Scholar Award\nKeynote speaker of ICDAR 2017\nTen Thousand Talents Program Young Top Talents 2016\nMost Cited Chinese Researchers, 2014-2016\nHongshan District Outstanding Youth, 2014\nExcellent Young Scientist Foundation of NSFC 2012\nOutstanding Youth Fund 2012\nNew century excellent talent of Ministry of Education, 2012\nNational Excellent Doctoral Dissertation nomination, 2012\nHubei Province Outstanding Doctoral Thesis, 2011\nMicrosoft Fellowship 2007\nStudents\nBaoguang Shi Ph.D. student\nSong Bai Ph.D. student (National PhD Fellowship 2015)\nXinwei He Ph.D. student\nXiaolong Liu Ph.D. student\nPengyuan Lv Master student\nZhichao Zhou Master student\nDuoyou Zhou Master student\nYang Yang Master student\nMingkun Yang Master student\nMinghui Liao Master student\nJieru Mei Undergraduate student\nFormer students\nBo Wang,\n(2010) Hubei Province Excellent Undergradute Graduation\n            thesis, now at Stanford University.\nTianyang Ma\n, (2010) Undergradute Student, HUST; Ph.D. Temple\n              Univerisity; Now at Amazon Company.\nWei Shen\n(2013), Ph.D. HUST, Tencent Fellowship, co-supervised with Prof.\n            Hongyuan Wang, now a faculty member of Shanghai University\nXinggang Wang (2014), Ph.D. HUST, Microsoft Fellowship 2012, National PhD Fellowship, co-supervised with Prof. Wenyu\n            Liu, Ass. Prof. of HUST\nCong Yao (2014), Ph.D. HUST,National PhD Fellowship, co-supervised with Prof. Wenyu Liu, now at Megvil.\nYu Zhou (2014), Ph.D. HUST, co-supervised with Prof. Wenyu Liu, now a faculty member of Beijing University of Post and Telecommunications\nJunwei Wang, Ph.D (2012), HUST co-supervised with Prof. Wenyu Liu, now at 709 Institute, Wuhan\nChunyuan Li\n(2011), Undergradute Student, HUST; Now at Duke\n            University\nChen Shen (2013) , Master HUST, now at Temple University\nCong Rao (2014) , Master HUST, National Master Fellowship, now at Temple University.\nWeichao Qiu (2014) , Master HUST, now at University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\nYan Wang,(2011) Hubei Province Excellent Undergradute Graduation thesi, now at NTU\nQuanming Yao\n(2013), Hubei Province Excellent Undergradute Graduation\n              thesis, now at HKUST\nYueming Wang (2014), Master HUST, National Master Fellowship, now at Taobao Company, Hangzhou\nYi Xiong (2014), Master HUST, now at Tencent Company, Shenzhen\nChangtao Wang (2013), Master HUST, worked in Baidu Company, Beijing\nChao Cai (2013), Master HUST, now at Zhongyuan Electronic Information Corporation, Wuhan\nLe He (2015) Master HUST; now at Toutiao\nTingwu Hou (2015) Master HUST; now at Huawei\nXu Min (2014), Undergradute student, HUST; Now at Tsinghua University\nYajun Gao (2011), Undergadute student, HUST; Georgio Insititute of Technology, Master. Now at Amazon\nZhuotun Zhu (2015) Undergradute student, HUST, Young Microsoft Fellowship; Now at University of California, Los Angeles\n            (UCLA)\nZheng Zhang (2016), Master, HUST, National Master Fellowship 2015, Now at Microsoft, Suzhou.\nChengquan Zhang (2016), Master, HUST, Now at Baidu, Shenzhen.\nHongyang Wang (2016) Undergradute student, HUST. Now at\n            Carnegie Mellon University (CMU)\nPan Chen (2016) Ph.D., HUST, co-supervised with Prof. Wenyu Liu. Now a faculty member in Chinese University of\n            Geosciences\n\n---\n\n﻿\nHomepage of Xiang Bai\nDr. Xiang Bai,\nProfessor\nEmail:\nxbai(at)hust(dot)edu(dot)cn; xiang.bai(at)gmail(dot)com\n【中文主页】\nAbout me\nI am a professor at the Department of Artificial Intelligence and Automation, Huazhong University of Science and Technology (HUST). I\n          received my Ph.D. in Communication and Information Engineering, HUST. My research interests focus on Computer Vision, Pattern Recognition,\n          and Deep Learning. The developed scene text detection and recognition technology has been widely used in Huawei, Alibaba, Meituan and many\n          other products or systems, and has achieved good economic and social benefits. I lead the Vision and Learning Representation Group and have\n          published more than 250 papers in journals and academic conferences at home and abroad, including more than 80 JCR Q1 journals and CCF Class\n          A papers.\nHere are some previous projects:\nShape Representation, 2D\\3D Shape matching and Retrieval\nScene Text Detection and Recognition:\nA brief survey\n,\nSlice (2014)\n,\nSlice (2017)\nObject Detection and Image Classification, Contour Detection\\Grouping\nOpening Positions\n: (1) I am currently recruiting self-motivated and dedicated Ph.D./M.S. students with\n          solid background in mathematics, programming, or writtern English etc. Please feel free to contact me if you are interested. (2) I plan to\n          host a selected number of PostDocs with strong research background. (3) Looking for fresh faculty members to join our group, please contact\n          me at least half a year ahead of your arriving.\nRecent News\nApr., 2022:\nWe received a letter of appreciation from the Ethiopian Embassy\n                in Beijing.\nJan., 2022:\nWe established HUST-CalmCar Autonomous Driving Technology\n                Center.\nOct., 2021:\nZheng Zhang received ICCV 2021 Best Paper award (Marr Prize).\nSep., 2020:\nDingkang Liang and Chenfeng Xu won the Vision Meets Drone Crowd\n                Counting Challenge 2020 (VisDrone2020).\nOct., 2019:\nDejia Song et al won the Visual Object Tracking Challenge 2019\n                (VOT2019).\nOct., 2019:\nWe won The 5th China College Students' \"Internet Plus\"\n                Innovation and Entrepreneurship Competition\nSep., 2019:\nI received the IAPR/ICDAR Young Investigator Award\nJun., 2019:\nBaoguang Shi received the Excellent Doctorate Dissertation\n                Award\nMay., 2019:\nWe won the ICDAR 2019 Robust Reading Competition on Reading\n                Chinese Text on Signboard\nNov., 2018:\nSong Bai received the Excellent Doctorate Dissertation Award\nNov., 2018:\nMinghui Liao received the CCF-CV Academic Emerging Award\nApril., 2017: The invited talk \"Oriented Scene Text Detection\n              Revisited\" at VALSE 2017, Xiamen. [\nPPT\n]\nFeb., 2017: Four papers accepted by CVPR 2017.\nJan., 2017: I become an editorial board member of the journal\n              \"Pattern Recognition\"\nNov.,2016:\nThree papers accepted by AAAI 2017! Congratulations to Song,\n                Minghui and Baoguang!\nJune, 2016: Baoguang got the support from CSC for visiting Cornell\n              University. Congratulations!\nMarch, 2016: We achieved the first place in\nShrec2016 competition: Large-Scale 3D Shape Retrieval\nunder the perturbed case.\nRecent Publications\n(More)\nLiao M, Zou Z, Wan Z, Yao C, Bai X. Real-Time Scene Text Detection\n            with Differentiable Binarization and Adaptive Scale Fusion.\nIEEE transactions on pattern analysis and machine intelligence\n              (TPAMI)\n, 2022\nQi J, Gao Y, Hu Y, et al. Occluded Video Instance Segmentation: A\n            Benchmark.\nInt. Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n,\n            2022\nYuan Y, Liu X, Dikubab W, Liu H, Ji Z, Wu Z, Bai X. Syntax-Aware\n            Network for Handwritten Mathematical Expression Recognition.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nWang H, Liao J, Cheng T, et al. Knowledge Mining with Scene Text for\n            Fine-Grained Recognition.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nTang J, Zhang W, Liu H, et al. Few Could Be Better Than All: Feature\n            Sampling and Grouping for Scene Text Detection.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nLiu X, Bai S, Bai X. An Empirical Study of End-to-End Temporal\n            Action Detection.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nSong S, Wan J, Yang Z, Tang J, Cheng W, Bai X, Yao C.\n            Vision-Language Pre-Training for Boosting Scene Text\n            Detectors.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n              (CVPR)\n, 2022\nXu C, Liang D, Xu Y, Bai S, Zhan W, Bai X, Tomizuka M. AutoScale:\n            Learning to Scale for Crowd Counting.\nInt. Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\n, 2022\nServices:\nAssociate Editor of\nPattern Recognition\n(2017-),\nPatten Recognition Letters\n(2016-),\nFrontier of\n            Computer Science\n,\nNeurocomputing\n(2015-)\nGuest Editor of journal special isssue: (1)\nSpecial\n            Section on Deep Learning\n,\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology\n, 2017; (2)\nMulti-Instance\n            Learning in Pattern Recognition and Vision\n,\nPattern Recognition\n, 2017; (3)\nDeep Learning Applications in Computer Vision\n,\nFronti...[truncated]"
