  "deep_homepage::Xiaowei Zhou::https://www.xzhou.me/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.xzhou.me/",
    "all_emails": [
      "xwzhou@zju.edu.cn"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/zju3dv",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaowei Zhou's Homepage\nHome Page\nGroup Page\nXiaowei Zhou\nå¨æå·\nZhejiang University\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nTwitter\nAbout Me\nI am a Professor in the College of Computer Science & the State Key Laboratory of CAD&CG at\nZhejiang University\n. Before joining ZJU in 2017, I was a postdoctoral researcher at the\nGRASP Laboratory\nat\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n. My research interest lies in the field of 3D Computer Vision, particularly including 3D reconstruction, pose estimation, motion capture, and scene understanding, as well as their applications in mixed reality and robotics. Most of our works are open-sourced, please visit our\nGithub Page\nto know more about our projects!\nI am looking for students, postdocs and research assistants, please fill out\nthis form\nif you are interested in working with me.\nRecent News\nEasyVolcap released, checked it out!\n(\nRead More\n)\nThree papers accepted by ICCV 2023 and two by SIGGRAPH Asia 2023!\nSida will be an assistant professor at Zhejiang University.\n(\nRead More\n)\nOur team won the first place in Image Matching Challenge 2023!\n(\nRead More\n)\nSida and Junting successfully passed their PhD defenses, congratulations!\n(\nRead More\n)\nShow More\nResearch Projects\n2D Feature Matching\nWe develop new image feature matching methods that get rid of the feature detection stage in traditional pipelines (e.g., SIFT), resolving the feature repeatability issue and improving the matching robustness.\nLoFTR\nEfficient LoFTR\nDetector-free SfM\nSpatialTracker\n3D Pose Estimation\nWe develop fast and accurate 3D pose tracking algorithms for both rigid objects and nonrigid human bodies based on monocular or multi-view videos, addressing the challenges from low texture and heavy occlusion.\nPVNet\nOnePose\nDeepSnake\nEasyMocap\n3D Reconstruction\nWe develop a series of neural scene representation and reconstruction methods for reconstructing 3D scenes from 2D images, addressing the challenges of efficiency, scalability, low texture and dynamic appearances.\nNeuralRecon\nNeus-W\nManhattan SDF\nAutoRecon\nLoG\nStreetGaussian\n4D Reconstruction\nWe develop a series of neural scene representation and reconstruction methods for capturing dynamic humans from 2D videos. We also develop new representations for building drivable human avatars.\nNeuralBody\nAnimatable NeRF\nEfficient NeRF\n4K4D\nEasyVolcap\nPublication List\nMore Information at\nGoogle Scholar\n* denotes equal contribution.\nRepresenting Long Volumetric Video with Temporal Gaussian Hierarchy\nZhen\nXu\nYinghao\nXu\nZhiyuan\nYu\nSida\nPeng\nJiaming\nSun\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH Asia)\n2024\nÂ\nWorld-Grounded Human Motion Recovery via Gravity-View Coordinates\nZehong\nShen\nHuaijin\nPi\nYan\nXia\nZhi\nCen\nSida\nPeng\nZechen\nHu\nHujun\nBao\nRuizhen\nHu\nXiaowei\nZhou\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n2024\nÂ\nStreet Gaussians: Modeling Dynamic Urban Scenes with Gaussian Splatting\nYunzhi\nYan\nHaotong\nLin\nChenxu\nZhou\nWeijie\nWang\nHaiyang\nSun\nKun\nZhan\nXianpeng\nLang\nXiaowei\nZhou\nSida\nPeng\nECCV\n2024\nÂ\nIntrinsicAnything: Learning Diffusion Priors for Inverse Rendering Under Unknown Illumination\nXi\nChen\nSida\nPeng\nDongchen\nYang\nYuan\nLiu\nBowen\nPan\nChengfei\nLv\nXiaowei\nZhou\nECCV\n2024\nÂ\nSAM-guided Graph Cut for 3D Instance Segmentation\nHaoyu\nGuo\nHu\nZhu\nSida\nPeng\nYuang\nWang\nYujun\nShen\nRuizhen\nHu\nXiaowei\nZhou\nECCV\n2024\nÂ\nMaPa: Text-driven Photorealistic Material Painting for 3D Shapes\nShangzhan\nZhang\nSida\nPeng\nTao\nXu\nYuanbo\nYang\nTianrun\nChen\nNan\nXue\nYujun\nShen\nHujun\nBao\nRuizhen\nHu\nXiaowei\nZhou\nSIGGRAPH\n2024\nÂ\nSpatialTracker: Tracking Any 2D Pixels in 3D Space\nYuxi\nXiao\nQianqian\nWang\nShangzhan\nZhang\nNan\nXue\nSida\nPeng\nYujun\nShen\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\n4K4D: Real-Time 4D View Synthesis at 4K Resolution\nZhen\nXu\nSida\nPeng\nHaotong\nLin\nGuangzhao\nHe\nJiaming\nSun\nYujun\nShen\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nRelightable and Animatable Neural Avatar from Sparse-View Video\nZhen\nXu\nSida\nPeng\nChen\nGeng\nLinzhan\nMou\nZihan\nYan\nJiaming\nSun\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nHighlight\nDetector-Free Structure from Motion\nXingyi\nHe\nJiaming\nSun\nYifan\nWang\nSida\nPeng\nQixing\nHuang\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nFirst Place in Image Matching Challenge 2023\nEfficient LoFTR: Semi-Dense Local Feature Matching with Sparse-Like Speed\nYifan\nWang\nXingyi\nHe\nSida\nPeng\nDongli\nTan\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nGenerating Human Motion in 3D Scenes from Text Descriptions\nZhi\nCen\nHuaijin\nPi\nSida\nPeng\nZehong\nShen\nMinghui\nYang\nShuai\nZhu\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nCoDeF: Content Deformation Fields for Temporally Consistent Video Processing\nHao\nOuyang\nQiuyu\nWang\nYuxi\nXiao\nQingyan\nBai\nJuntao\nZhang\nKecheng\nZheng\nXiaowei\nZhou\nQifeng\nChen\nYujun\nShen\nCVPR\n2024\nÂ\nNeuralRecon: Real-Time Coherent 3D Scene Reconstruction from Monocular Video\nXi\nChen\nJiaming\nSun\nYiming\nXie\nHujun\nBao\nXiaowei\nZhou\nT-PAMI\n2024\nÂ\nCVPR'21 Best Paper Candidate\nNeural 3D Scene Reconstruction with Indoor Planar Priors\nXiaowei\nZhou\nHaoyu\nGuo\nSida\nPeng\nYuxi\nXiao\nHaotong\nLin\nQianqian\nWang\nGuofeng\nZhang\nHujun\nBao\nT-PAMI\n2024\nÂ\nCVPR'22 Oral Presentation\nShow More\nTeaching\nIntro. to Computer Vision\nComputational Photography"
