    "homepage_text": "Yuexin Ma - Homepage\n's Research Page!\nHome\nPublications\nTeam\n​\nYuexin Ma\nTenured Associate Professor\nShanghaiTech University\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nCV\nEmail:\nmayuexin at shanghaitech.edu.cn\nNew Events\n2026.01: Two papers are accepted by\nICLR\n.\n2025.10: Two papers are accepted by\nNeurIPS\n.\n2025.07: One paper is accepted by\nSIGGRAPH Asia\n.\n2025.07: Four papers are accepted by\nICCV\n.\n2025.07: Two papers are accepted by\nIROS\n.\n2025.02: Five papers are accepted by\nCVPR\n.\n2025.01: Two papers are accepted by\nICRA\n.\n2025.01: One paper is accepted by\nICLR\n.\n2024.12: Three papers are accepted by\nAAAI\n.\n2024.09: One paper is accepted by\nMICCAI\n(Best Paper Award)\n.\n2024.09: Two papers are accepted by\nTPAMI\n.\n2024.09: One paper is accepted by\nNeurIPS\n.\n2024.07: Two papers are accepted by\nMM\n.\n(Best Paper Nomination)\n2024.02: Five papers are accepted by\nECCV\n.\n2024.02: One paper is accepted by\nIJCAI\n.\n2024.02: Eight papers are accepted by\nCVPR\n.\n2024.01: Two papers are accepted by\nICRA\n.\n2023.11: One papers is accepted by\nAAAI\n.\n2023.09: One paper is accepted by\nNeurIPS\n.\n2023.07: Four papers are accepted by\nICCV\n.\n2023.04: Two papers are accepted by\nIJCAI\n.\n2023.02: Four papers are accepted by\nCVPR\n.\n2023.02: Two papers are accepted by\nICRA\n.\n2023.01: One paper is accepted by\nTVCG\n.\n2022.11: Three papers are accepted by\nAAAI\n.\n2022.05: A Large-scale dataset for 3D perception of crowd scenes has been released!\nDataset\n.\n2022.03: One paper is accepted by\nSIGGRAPH\n.\n2022.03: Four papers are accepted by\nCVPR\n.\n2021.11: One paper is accepted by\nIJCV\n.\n2021.08:\nOne paper\nis accepted by\nTOG\n.\n2021.07:\nExtended version of Cylinder3D\nis accepted by\nTPAMI\n.\n2021.06:\nOne paper\nis accepted by\nIJCV\n.\n2021.03:\nThree\npapers are accepted by\nCVPR2021\n(2 Orals and 1 Poster).\n2020.11: We release the code of\nCylinder3D\n, which achieves the\n1st place\nin the\nleaderboard\nof SemanticKITTI Semantic segmentation. Based on Cylinder3D, we also achieve the\n1st place\nin the\nleaderboard\nof SemanticKITTI Panoptic segmentation.\n2020.07: Two papers are accepted by\nECCV2020\n.\nI am looking for self-motivated Ph.D./MPhil. students, RAs, PostDocs, and Visiting scholars to join my group. Please drop me an email with your CV if you are interested.\nAbout Me\nYuexin Ma is an Assistant Professor in SIST, ShanghaiTech University. She received the PhD degree from the University of Hong Kong in 2019. Her research interests include computer vision and artificial intelligence. Particularly, her current research focuses on scene understanding, multi-modal learning, autonomous driving, embodied AI, etc. She has published more than 90 papers, including Science Robotics, TPAMI, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, AAAI, IJCAI, IJCV, TOG, Siggraph, etc. As the first author or corresponding author, she has published over 50 papers in top-tier journals and conferences.\nResearch Experience\nRobotic and Autonomous Driving Lab (RAL) of Baidu\n04.2018 - 12.2018\nThe University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill (UNC)\n09.2017 - 02.2018\nFrench Institute for Research in Computer Science and Automation (INRIA)\n06.2016 - 08.2016\nHonors & Awards\nOutstanding Teaching Award, ShanghaiTech University, 2024\nOutstanding Research Award, ShanghaiTech University, 2023\nOutstanding Individual of Baidu RAL, 2018\nBest Tutor of the University of Hong Kong, 2016\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Award (HKPFS), 2015\nPresidential Scholarship of Shandong University, 2015\nGoogle Merit Scholarship, 2015\nCCF (China Computer Federation) Top 100 Outstanding Undergraduates of China, 2013\nNational Scholarship of China, 2013, 2014"
  },
