    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jiahui Sun\nJiahui Sun\n孙佳辉\nEmail: cgjiahui@gmail.com\n[\nGitHub\n]\nSchool of Computer science and Information Engineering\n,\nHefei University of Technology\nHefei University of Technology, Hefei, Anhui, China\nBio\n|\nResearch and Patent Achievements\n|\nCertificates\n|\nResearch Experiences\n|\nConnections\nBio\nI obtained B.Eng in Hefei University(average score 83.36/100) in 2020 and subsequently completed my Master's degree in School of Computer Science and Information Engineering in Hefei University of Technology(88.13/100) in 2023. \nMy supervisors were Dr.\nWenming Wu\nand Prof.\nLiping Zheng\n.\nDuring my graduate studies, I also had the privilege of being mentored by Prof.\nLigang Liu\non the research project WallPlan.\nMy research interests are centered around developing intelligent algorithms to comprehend and generate both 2D and 3D contents. Currently, I am keenly interested in AIGC on 2D and 3D.\nResearch and Patent Achievements\n†Equal Contribution, * Corresponding Author(s)\n[1]\nJiahui Sun\n, Wenming Wu, Ligang Liu, Wenjie Min, Gaofeng Zhang and Liping Zheng,\n\"WallPlan: synthesizing floorplans by learning to generate wall graphs\",\nACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH)\n2022.\n[2]\nJiahui Sun\n, Liping Zheng, Gaofeng Zhang and Wenming Wu,\n\"BubbleFormer: Bubble Diagram Generation via Dual Transformer Models\",\nComputer Graphics Forum (Pacific Graphics)\n2023 accepted.\n[3]\n\"A method for automatically generating vectorized interior layout floorplans.\",\nCN Patent Application 202210493144X\nPatent Pending.\nCertificates\nJournal Reviewer\nOutstanding Teaching Assistant Award of HFUT, 合肥工业大学优秀助教 2022\nNational Scholarship for Postgraduates, 研究生国家奖学金, 2022\nHonor Graduate, University Level, 校优秀毕业生, 2023\nHonor Graduate, Provincial Level, 安徽省优秀毕业生, 2023\nIELTS: 6.5, 2023\nResearch Experiences\nResearch on floorplan design and optimization for indoor scene modeling.\n2020 – 2023\nSupported by NSFC (62102126), Participating\nStudy of fast computation algorithms for multi-constrained power graphs.\n2020 – 2023\nSupported by NSFC (61972128), Participating\nHorizontal research project: secondary development of automotive wiring harness CAD system.\n2021 – 2022\nParticipating\nConnections\nHuan Zheng\n© Jiahui Sun"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Deyu Meng::https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~deyum/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~deyum/",
    "all_emails": [
      "dymeng@mail.xjtu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Deyu Meng's Homepage, Meng Deyu's Homepage,\nDeyu Meng (ÃÏµÂÓî)\n¡¡\nEmail:\ndymeng AT mail Dot xjtu DOT edu DOT cn\nAddress:\nInstitute for Information and System Sciences\nSchool of Mathematics and Statistics\nXi'an Jiaotong University\nPhone:\n86-29-82663153\nFax:\n86-29-8266 8559¡¡\nAbout me\nGreetings! I received my BA and MS degree in Applied Mathematics, and Ph.D degree in Computer Science, all from Xi'an Jiaotong University. My Ph.D advisor was Prof. Zongben Xu. Currently I work for Xi'an Jiaotong University\r\nas an associate professor. From August 2012 to July 2014, I took my two-year sabbatical leave in Carnegie Mellon University. In August 2012 I joined the Robotics Institute of School of Computer Science, working with Dr. Fernando De la Torre, and in August 2012, I joined Language Technologies Institute of School of Computer Science at Carnegie Mellon University, working with Dr. Alex Hauptmann. My research interests \r\ninclude machine learning and its applications to multimedia content \r\nanalysis and computer vision. My homepage in Xi'an Jiaotong University  is\nhere.\nNew:\n.\nWelcome to experience the performance of our newly published method on MSI denoising:\nYi Peng, Deyu Meng, Zongben Xu, Chenqiang Gao, Yi Yang, Biao Zhang.\nDecomposable Nonlocal Tensor Dictionary Learning for Multispectral Image Denoising\n,\nSupplementary Material\n, CVPR, 2014.\nMatlab code.\n.\nOur robust PCA method can well ?t more complex noise beyond conventional Gaussian, Laplacian, Sparse noise or any combinations of them:\nQian Zhao, Deyu Meng, Zongben Xu, Wangmeng Zuo, Lei Zhang.\nRobust principal component analysis with complex noise\n,\nSupplementary Material\n, ICML, 2014.\nMatlab code.\n.\nOur proposed FastMMD method decreases the time complexity of MMD calculation from conventional O(N^2d) to O(Nlog(d)):\nJi Zhao, Deyu Meng.\nFastMMD: Ensemble of Circular Discrepancy for Efficient Two-Sample Test\n, arXiv:1405.2664, 2014,\nMatlab code\n.\nThe code and slides of our ICMR best-paper-runner-up work are now available:\nLu Jiang, Wei Tong, Deyu Meng, Alexander G. Hauptmann.\nTowards Efficient Learning of Optimal Spatial Bag-of-Words Representations\n,  ICMR, 2014.\nSlides\n. Please download our code in\nJS Tiling webpage\n.\nThe corrected proof to the global optimum of weighted nuclear norm minimization:\nQi Xie, Deyu Meng, Shuhang Gu, Lei Zhang, Wangmeng Zuo, Xiangchu Feng, Zongben Xu.\nOn the optimal solution of weighted nuclear norm minimization\n,  arXiv:1405.6012v1, 2014.\nHome\n|\nSelected Publications\nLinks:\nChenqiang Gao\nAlexander G. Hauptmann\nDong Huang\nLu Jiang\nZhenzhong Lan\nYee Leung\nMing Li\nShiguang Shan\nFernando De la Torre\nZongben Xu\nYan Yan\nYi Yang\nShoou-I Yu\nYaoliang Yu\nZhiding Yu\nLei Zhang\nQingfu Zhang\nJi Zhao\nWangmeng Zuo\n_______________________________________________\nLast modified\nJuly, 2014."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Daquan Zhou::https://zhoudaquan.github.io/homepage.io/index.html": {
