    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": ">\nCunxiang Wang, Westlake University\nCunxiang Wang\nPhD\nZhipuAI & Tsinghua University\nEmail: wangcunxiang303 AT gmail.com, wangcunxiang AT foxmail.com\nBiography\nI  am a tech leader at ZhipuAI and a postdoc at Tsinghua University, fortunately working with Prof.\nJie Tang\nand Prof.\nMinlie Huang\n.\n\n\tPreviously, I obtained my Ph.D. at Zhejiang University & Westlake University joint Ph.D. program, and was fortunately supervised by Prof.\nYue Zhang\n, WestlakeNLP Lab.\nMy current research primarily focuses on Large Language Models, especially LLM Evaluation and General Agent.\nWe are looking for\nself-motivated interns and full-time employees\nto work with us at Tsinghua or ZhipuAI.\n\t\n\tWe will offer cutting-edge technology and insights for LLMs, adequate computing and data resources, a competitive salary, and a research-friendly environment.\n\tIf you are interested, please feel free to contact me.\nNews\n[1/2025] Two papers (1 main and 1 industry) are accepted by NAACL 2025.\n[1/2025] Two papers are accepted by ICLR 2025.\n[1/2025] Our Survey on Factuality in LLMs is accepted by ACM Computing Surveys.\n[9/2024] Four papers (3 main and 1 findings) are accepted by EMNLP 2024.\n[10/2023] Check out our survey on Factuality in LLMs!\n[10/2023] One paper were accepted by EMNLP findings.\n[9/2023] One paper were accepted by Neurips2023 D&B track.\n[5/2023] Two paper were accepted by ACL-2023 findings.\n[4/2021] One paper was accepted by ACL-2021.\n[11/2020] I won the best task paper honorable mention of SemEval (2020).\n[10/2020] I got the National Scholarship Award (PhD Student) from Zhejiang University.\nEducation\nWestlake University & Zhejiang University Co-PhD Promgram\nAug, 2019 - Jun, 2024 (Expected)\nPh.D candidate\nSupervisor:\nYue Zhang\nDegree Granted By: Zhejiang University\nDept. of Computer Science and Technology, Northeastern University, Shenyang\nSep, 2015 - Jul, 2019\nUndergraduate student.\nInterned at Northeastern NLP Lab, 2016-2019, advised by Prof. Feiliang Ren\nExperience\nAmazon AWS AI\nMarch, 2022 - now\nResearch Intern\nMentor: Qipeng Guo and Zheng Zhang\nSelected Publications (As First / Co-First Author) [\nGoogle Scholar\n] [\nSemantic Scholar\n]\n* indicates co-first author.\n† indicates corresponding author.\n2025\nNovelQA: Benchmarking Question Answering on Documents Exceeding 200K Tokens\n\t[\npdf\n][\nGithub Page\n]\nICLR-2025\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Ruoxi Ning*, Boqi Pan, Tonghui Wu, Qipeng Guo, Cheng Deng, Guangsheng Bao, Qian Wang, Yue Zhang.\nSurvey on Factuality in Large Language Models: Knowledge, Retrieval and Domain-Specificity [\npdf\n][\nGithub Page\n]\nAccepted by ACM Computing Surveys\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Xiaoze Liu*, Yuanhao Yue*, Xiangru Tang, Tianhang Zhang, Cheng Jiayang, Yunzhi Yao, Wenyang Gao, Xuming Hu, Zehan Qi, Yidong Wang, Linyi Yang, Jindong Wang, Xing Xie, Zheng Zhang and Yue Zhang.\nStepMathAgent: A Step-Wise Agent for Evaluating Mathematical Processes through Tree-of-Error\n\t[\npdf\n][\nGithub Page\n]\nShu-Xun Yang*,\nCunxiang Wang\n* †, Yidong Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Minlie Huang, Jie Tang\n2024\nRedHat: Towards Reducing Hallucination in Essay Critiques with Large Language Models\n\t[\npdf\n][\nGithub Page\n]\nAndrew Zhuoer Feng,\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Bosi Wen, Boqun Kou, Haohan Chi, Yu Luo, Lin Fan, Xiaotao Gu, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nNash CoT: Multi-Path Inference with Preference Equilibrium\n\t[\npdf\n][\nGithub Page\n]\nEMNLP-2024\nZiqi Zhang*,\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Xiong Xiao, Yue Zhang, Donglin Wang\n2023\nEvaluating Open-QA Evaluation.\nNeurips\n-2023 Dataset and Benchmark Track. Average Score: 7.0.\n[\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n]\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Sirui Cheng*, Qipeng Guo, Zhikun Xu, Bowen Ding, Yunhao Yun, Yidong Wang, Xiangkun Hu, Zheng Zhang and Yue Zhang.\nExploiting Abstract Meaning Representation for Open-Domain Question Answering. [\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nACL\n-2023 findings, reviewer scores: 4, 4, 4 out of 5.\nCunxiang Wang\n, Zhikun Xu, Qipeng Guo, Xiangkun Hu, Xuefeng Bai, Zheng Zhang and Yue Zhang.\nRFiD: Towards Rational Fusion-in-Decoder for Open-Domain Question Answering. [\npdf\n][\ncode and data\n].\nACL\n-2023 findings, reviewer scores: 4, 4, 3 out of 5.\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Haofei Yu* and Yue Zhang.\nKnowledgeable Salient Span Mask for Enhancing Language Models as Knowledge Base.\n[\npdf\n][\ncode and data\n].\nCCF International Conference on Natural Language Processing and Chinese Computing\n(\nNLPCC\n-2023).\nCunxiang Wang\n, Fuli Luo, Yanyang Li, Runxin Xu, Fei Huang and Yue Zhang.\nTRAMS: Training-free Memory Selection for Long-range Language Modeling.\t[\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nEMNLP\n-2023 findings, reviewer scores: 4, 4, 3 out of 5.\nHaofei Yu*,\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Yue Zhang and Wei Bi.\n2021\nExploring Generalization Ability of Pretrained Language Models on Arithmetic and Logical Reasoning [\npdf\n][\ndata\n].\nCCF International Conference on Natural Language Processing and Chinese Computing (\nNLPCC\n-2021)\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Boyuan Zheng*, Yuchen Niu and Yue Zhang.\nCan Generative Pre-trained Language Models Serve as Knowledge Bases for Closed-book QA?  [\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nACL\n-2021\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Pai Liu*, Yue Zhang.\n2020\nSemEval-2020 task 4: Commonsense Validation and Explanation [\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nProceedings of the 14th International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation (\nSemEval\n-2020).\nCunxiang Wang\n*, Shuailong Liang*, Yili Jin, Yilong Wang, Xiaodan Zhu, Yue Zhang.\nCommonsense Knowledge Graph Reasoning by Selection or Generation? Why?\narxiv\n[\npdf\n].\nCunxiang Wang\n, Jinhang Wu, Luxin Liu and Yue Zhang.\n2019\nDoes it Make Sense? And Why? A Pilot Study for Sense Making and Explanation. \n[\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nACL\n-2019\nCunxiang Wang\n, Shuailong Liang, Yue Zhang, Xiaonan Li and Tian Gao.\nDomain Representation for Knowledge Graph Embedding.\n[\npdf\n][\ncodes and data\n].\nCCF International Conference on Natural Language Processing and Chinese Computing (\nNLPCC\n-2019).\nCunxiang Wang\n, Feiliang Ren, Chenxu Zhao, ZhiChao Lin, Tian Xie and Yue Zhang.\nProfessional Activities\nConference Reviews:\nACL, EMNLP, NAACL, IJCAI, SemEval\nSelected Awards\nBest Paper Award:\nBest Task Paper Honorable Mention of SemEval (2020)\nScholarship:\nChina National Scholarship (For Bachelor Students) at Northeastern University\nChina National Scholarship (For Ph.D. Students) at Zhejiang University"
