    "homepage_text": "Prof. Dr. Qipeng Guo\nJump to the content\nDE\nEN\nMagazine Humboldt Kosmos\nNewsroom\nNewsletter\nOpen Search\nOpen Main Navigation\nSearch\nAwards and fellowships\nSearch Humboldtians\nSearch\nSearch for tags\nHumboldt Professorships for AI\nHumboldt Professorships\nKOSMOS - Focus\nKOSMOS - Quick insights\nKOSMOS - Humboldtians in private\nclose\nProf. Dr. Qipeng Guo\nProfile\nAcademic position\nAssociate Professor, Senior Lecturer, Reader\nResearch fields\nPreparative and Physical Chemistry of Polymers,Experimental and Theoretical Physics of Polymers,Metallurgical, Thermal and Thermomechanical Treatment of Materials\nKeywords\nBlock Copolymers, Biodegradable Polymers, Polymers, Polymer Blends, Thermosets\nCurrent contact address\nHost during sponsorship\nProf. Dr. Wolfram Gronski\nInstitut für Makromolekulare Chemie, Albert-Ludwigs-Universität Freiburg, Freiburg\nStart of initial sponsorship\n01/02/2000\nProgramme(s)\n1999\nHumboldt Research Fellowship Programme\nPublications (partial selection)\n2007\nQipeng Guo, Peter Arends, Ralf Thomann, Richard J. Spontak, Wolfraum Gronski: Morphological Development and Rheological Changes of Phenoxy/SAN Blends during In-Situ Polymerization. In: Journal of Polymer Science, Part B: Polymer Physics, 2007, 2614-2619\n2007\nQipeng Guo, Ralf Thomann, Wolfram Gronski: Synthesis and Fractionated Crystallization of Organic-Inorganic Hybrid Composite Materials from an Amphiphilic Polyethylene-block-Poly(ethylene oxide) Diblock Copolymer. In: Polymer, 2007, 3925-3929\n2003\nQipeng Guo, Ralf Thomann, Wolfram Gronski, Rosina Staneva, Rouja Ivanova, Bernd Stuehn: Nanostructures, semicrystalline morphology, and nanoscale confinement effect on the crystallization kinetics in self-organized block copolymer/thermoset blends. In: Macromolecules, 2003, 3635-3645\n2002\nQipeng Guo, Ralf Thomann, and Wolfram Gronski, Thomas Thurn-Albrecht: Phase behavior, crystallization, and hierarchical nanostructures in self-organized th