    "homepage_text": "Xiyang Dai at Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nXiyang Dai\nPrincipal Researcher\nConnect on LinkedIn\nAbout\nI am a Principal Researcher at Microsoft AI.\nMy research interests include: large-scale pretraining, efficient architecture, object detection and video understanding.\nBefore joining Microsoft, I finish my PhD at University of Maryland – College Park under the advising of Prof. Larry Davis. My research interests started with texture/fine-grained classification and settled down with human action understanding.  Before that, I had my master at NYU and studied shortly in Prof. Yann Lecun’s lab doing robots staff.\nOpens in a new tab\nResearch areas\nArtificial intelligence\nComputer vision\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit\n\n---\n\nXiyang Dai at Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nXiyang Dai\nPrincipal Researcher\nConnect on LinkedIn\nOther\nOpens in a new tab\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit\n\n---\n\nXiyang Dai at Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nXiyang Dai\nPrincipal Researcher\nConnect on LinkedIn\nOther\nOpens in a new tab\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit\n\n---\n\nXiyang Dai at Micro