    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jiaming-liu-046816149/",
    "homepage_text": "About me - Jiaming Liu\nJiaming Liu 刘家明\nPostdoc @ Stanford, PhD @ WUSTL\nFollow\nPalo Alto, CA\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nAbout me\nI am Jiaming Liu, a researcher working on computational imaging and generative AI, with a particular emphasis on medical imaging applications. I am currently a postdoctoral researcher affiliated with the Center for Artificial Intelligence in Medicine & Imaging (AIMI) at\nStanford University\n. Previously, I earned my Ph.D. in the Computational Imaging Group (CIG) in the Department of ESE at WashU, where I was advised by\nProfessor Ulugbek S. Kamilov\n. Prior to WashU, I received my bachelor’s degree from UESTC. I have also spent time at research labs at\nMERL\nand\nLLNL\n.\nNews\n2026\nJanuary 20, 2026\nNew Paper Acceptance:\n“\nMerlin: A Computed Tomography Vision–Language Foundation Model and Dataset\n”. Extremely happy to have contributed to this major project, which presents the first vision foundation model for 3D CT imaging and is now accepted by Nature.\nJanuary 02, 2026\nNew Preprint:\n“\nUnified Semantic Bridge Model for Unpaired Image-to-Image Translation\n” We propose the Unified Semantic Bridge Model (USBM), a fully self-supervised framework that learns diffusion bridges from a shared semantic latent space to each domain, enabling geometry-aware translation without cross-domain supervision.\n2024\nSeptember 12, 2024\nPostdoc:\nI am extremely happy to share that I will be joining\nAIMI @ Stanford\nas a postdoctoral researcher in 2024!\nJune 22, 2024\nNew Preprint:\n“\nPrior Mismatch and Adaptation in PnP-ADMM with a Nonconvex Convergence Analysis\n”. We present nonconvex convergence results under prior mismatch for PnP-ADMM. This work has been accepted to ICML 2024!\n2023\nJuly 22, 2023\nNew Preprint:\n“\nDOLCE: A Model-Based Probabilistic Diffusion Framework for Limited-Angle CT Reconstruction\n”. We present DOLCE, a new deep modelbased framework for LACT that uses a conditional diffusion model as an image prior has been accepted by ICCV 2023!\nJune 01, 2023\nMERL Research:\nExtremely happy to share that I will join\nMERL\nas a summer intern in 2023!\n2022\nOctober 05, 2022\nIn Press:\nOur paper “\nOnline Deep Equilibrium Learning for Regularization by Denoising\n” has been accepted at NeurIPS 2022! We proposed a new online deep equilibrium learning framework for data-intensive imaging modalities based on implicit neural network.\nJune 01, 2022\nLLNL Research:\nExtremely happy to share that I will join\nLLNL\nas a summer intern in 2022!\n2021\nOctober 30, 2021\nTCI Accepted:\nOur paper “\nCoIL: Coordinate-based Internal Learning for Imaging Inverse Problems\n” has been on the IEEE Transactions on Computational Imaging (TCI)!! It extends coordinate-based representation to computational imaging. Here is a short video\nsummary\n.\nSeptember 28, 2021\nNeurIPS Accepted:\nOur paper “\nRecovery Analysis for Plug-and-Play Priors using the Restricted Eigenvalue Condition\n” has been accepted at NeurIPS 2021! It establishes theoretical recovery guarantees for PnP/RED in compressive sensing.\nJune 01, 2021\nLANL Research:\nExtremely happy to share that I will join\nLANL\nas a summer intern in 2021!\nMay 24, 2021\nTCI Accepted:\nOur paper “\nSGD-Net: Efficient Model-Based Deep Learning with Theoretical Guarantees\n” has been accepted on the\nIEEE Transactions on Computational Imaging (TCI)\n!\nJanuary 12, 2021\nICLR Accepted:\nOur paper “\nAsync-RED: A Provably Convergent Asynchronous Block Parallel Stochastic Method using Deep Denoising Priors\n” has been accepted to International Coference on Learning Represetations (ICLR) as spotlight.\n2020\nAugust 25, 2020\nJSTSP Accepted:\nOur paper “\nSIMBA: Scalable Inversion in Optical Tomography using Deep Denoising Priors\n” has been published on the\nIEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing (JSTSP)\n!\nMay 28, 2020\nJSTSP Accepted:\nOur paper “\nRARE: image reconstruction using deep priors learned without groundtruth\n” has been published on the\nIEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Signal Processing (JSTSP)\n!\nPage views:\nUnique visitors\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Jiaming Liu\nJiaming Liu 刘家明\nPostdoc @ Stanford, PhD @ WUSTL\nFollow\nPalo Alto, CA\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nCV\nHere\nis a PDF of my CV."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Yan Zhang::https://yzhang2332.github.io/": {
