    "homepage_text": "Runsheng Wang\nSkip to content\nRunsheng Wang\nPhoto by Kai Jiang\nI am a Ph.D. student at Columbia University, advised by\nProf. Matei Ciocarlie\nin the\nROAM Lab\n.\n            My research focuses on robot learning, multimodal perception, human-robot\n            interaction, and wearable robotics.\nEmail:\nrunsheng.w@columbia.edu\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch\n* indicates equal contribution\nReactEMG: Zero-Shot, Low-Latency Intent Detection via sEMG\nRunsheng Wang*\n, Xinyue Zhu*, Ava Chen, Jingxi Xu, Lauren Winterbottom, Dawn M Nilsen, Joel Stein, Matei Ciocarlie\nPreprint\narXiv\n·\nCode & Dataset\n·\nProject Website\n·\nVideo\nFabric Sensing of Intrinsic Hand Muscle Activity\nKatelyn Lee,\nRunsheng Wang\n, Ava Chen, Lauren Winterbottom, Ho Man Colman Leung, Lisa Maria DiSalvo, Iris Xu, Jingxi Xu, Dawn M Nilsen, Joel Stein, Xia Zhou, Matei Ciocarlie\nInternational Conference On Rehabilitation Robotics (ICORR) 2025\narXiv\n·\nPoster\nChatEMG: Synthetic Data Generation to Control a Robotic Hand Orthosis for Stroke\nJingxi Xu*,\nRunsheng Wang*\n, Siqi Shang*, Ava Chen, Lauren Winterbottom, To-Liang Hsu, Wenxi Chen, Khondoker Ahmed, Pedro Leandro La Rotta, Xinyue Zhu, Dawn M. Nilsen, Joel Stein, Matei Ciocarlie\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (RA-L) 2024\narXiv\n·\nCode & Dataset\n·\nProject Website\n·\nVideo\nAn Investigation of Multi-feature Extraction and Super-resolution with Fast Microphone Arrays\nEric T Chang*,\nRunsheng Wang*\n, Peter Ballentine, Jingxi Xu, Trey Smith, Brian Coltin, Ioannis Kymissis, Matei Ciocarlie\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA) 2024\narXiv\nMultidimensional Analysis of Cortical Interneuron Synaptic Features Reveals Underlying Synaptic Heterogeneity\nPatrick D Dummer*, Dylan I Lee*, Sakib Hossain*,\nRunsheng Wang\n, Andre Evard, Gabriel Newman, Claire Ho, Casey M Schneider-Mizell, Vilas Menon, Edmund Au\nPreprint\nbioRxiv"
