    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Jin-Hong's Homepage - Jin-Hong Du\nJin-Hong Du\nAssistant Professor at the University of Hong Kong\nFollow\nHong Kong\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nWelcome to Jin-Hong's Homepage\nI am an HKU-100 Assistant Professor at the University of Hong Kong, beginning in Fall 2025. I hold joint appointments in the\nDepartment of Statistics and Actuarial Science (SAAS)\nand the\nMusketeers Foundation Institute of Data Science (IDS)\n.\nI earned my Ph.D. in Statistics and Machine Learning from Carnegie Mellon University, advised by Professor\nKathryn Roeder\nand Professor\nLarry Wasserman\n. Previously, I obtained an M.S. in Statistics from the University of Chicago, advised by Professor\nLek-Heng Lim\n, and a B.S. in Statistics from Sun Yat-sen University.\n🔍 Research interests\nMy current research interests include statistical methodology for\n📊 Causal inference\n🤖 Interpretable machine learning\n🌐 Statistical network analysis\nas well as applications in\n🧬 Single-cell multiomics\n🧪 CRISPR perturbation analysis\n💹 Quantitative finance\n🔔 Updates\n2026/03 🎓 Our paper ''\nEffects of distance metrics and scaling on the perturbation discrimination score\n'' has been accepted as oral presentation by ICLR 2026 Workshop on Generative AI in Genomics (Gen²): Barriers and Frontiers! 🎉\n2026/01 🎓 Our paper ''\nFlow-Disentangled feature importance\n'' has been accepted by ICLR 2026! 🎉\n2025/12 🎓 Our paper ''\nAssumption-lean post-integrated inference with surrogate control outcomes\n'' has been accepted by Biometrika! 🎉\n2025/12 🎉 In collaboration with researchers from UChicago and Dartmouth, our team\nOutlier\nsecured 3rd place 🥉 in\nThe First Virtual Cell Challenge\n! Huge thanks to everyone who contributed to this amazing achievement! 🚀\n2025/09 🏆 I will receive the IMS Lawrence D. Brown Ph.D. Student Award and present paper\nDisentangled Feature Importance\nat the 2026 IMS Annual Meeting. 🌟\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
