    "homepage_text": "Yingbing Huang\nYingbing Huang\nPh.D. Candidate at University of Illinois, Urbana Champaign\n403 Coordinated Science Lab, 1308 W Main St,\nUrbana, IL 61801, USA\nMy name is\nYingbing Huang (黄滢冰)\n, you can also call me\nWendy\n. I’m a PhD candidate at the\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE)\nat\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\nadvised by\nProf. Deming Chen\n.\nBefore joining UIUC, I obtained my Bachelor’s degree with Honors at Cornell University in 2023, advised by\nProf. Wen Sun\n.\nMy research lies in the various areas, including efficient machine learning, large language models, reinforcement learning, active learning and robotics.\nnews\nAug 15, 2023\nJoined the Ph.D. program under UIUC ECE department\nMay 27, 2023\nGraduated from Cornell Engineering College with Honor B.S. in Computer Science major and Operations Research minor.\n\n---\n\nCV | Yingbing Huang\nCV\nYou can view more details by clicking the top pdf button\nGeneral Information\nFull Name\nYingbing Huang (Wendy)\nLanguages\nEnglish, Mandarin\nEducation\n2023 - Present\nPhD Candidate\nUniversity of Illinois, Urbana Champaign\nWorking in Deming Chen's group\nWorking on LLM inference acceleration\n2019 - 2023\nB.S. with Honors in Computer Science\nCornell University\nWorked with Prof. Wen Sun\nMinor in Operations Research"
  },
  "deep_homepage::José Miguel Hernández-Lobato::https://jmhl.org": {
