h Bayesian neural networks for non-stationary data\nRichard Kurle, Botond Cseke, Alexej Klushyn, Patrick van der Smagt and Stephan GÃ¼nnemann\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2019\n2018 (4 publications)\nGaussian process neurons\nSebastian Urban and Patrick van der Smagt\n2018\nMetrics for deep generative models\nNutan Chen, Alexej Klushyn, Richard Kurle, Xueyan Jiang, Justin Bayer and Patrick Smagt\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS), 2018\nNavigation and planning in latent maps\nBaris Kayalibay, Atanas Mirchev, Maximilian Soelch, Patrick van der Smagt and Justin Bayer\n2018\nActive learning based on data uncertainty and model sensitivity\nNutan Chen, Alexej Klushyn, Alexandros Paraschos, Djalel Benbouzid and Patrick van der Smagt\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS), 2018\n2017 (10 publications)\nDeep variational Bayes filters: Unsupervised learning of state space models from raw data\nMaximilian Karl, Maximilian Soelch, Justin Bayer and Patrick van der Smagt\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2017\nCNN-based segmentation of medical imaging data\nBaris Kayalibay, Grady Jensen and Patrick van der Smagt\narXiv preprint arXiv:1701.03056, 2017\nConnecting artificial brains to robots in a comprehensive simulation framework: the neurorobotics platform\nEgidio Falotico, Lorenzo Vannucci, Alessandro Ambrosano, Ugo Albanese, Stefan Ulbrich, Juan Camilo Vasquez Tieck, et al.\nFrontiers in Neurorobotics, vol. 11, pp. 2, 2017\nKey insights into hand biomechanics: human grip stiffness can be decoupled from force by cocontraction and predicted from electromyography\nHannes HÃ¶ppner, Maximilian Grosse-Dunker, Georg Stillfried, Justin Bayer and Patrick van der Smagt\nFrontiers in Neurorobotics, vol. 11, pp. 17, 2017\nTwo-stream RNN/CNN for action recognition in 3D videos\nRui Zhao, Haider Ali and Patrick van der Smagt\nInternational Conference on Intelli