    "homepage_text": "Qianxiao Li (李千骁) | Department of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nSkip to content\nQianxiao Li (李千骁)\nDepartment of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nAbout\nBiography\nQianxiao Li is an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\n, and a principal investigator in the\nInstitute for Functional Intelligent Materials\n, National University of Singapore. He graduated with a BA in mathematics from the University of Cambridge and a PhD in applied mathematics from Princeton University. His research interests include the interplay of machine learning and dynamical systems, control theory, stochastic optimisation algorithms and data-driven methods for science and engineering.\nCV\nShort CV\nSearch for:\nSearch for:\nRecent Posts\nImplementation of stochastic OnsagerNet in jax\nRecent Papers\nCode Repository\nRecent Papers\nRecent Papers\nRecent Comments\nArchives\nOctober 2024\nAugust 2023\nJanuary 2023\nMay 2022\nDecember 2021\nJune 2021\nMarch 2021\nCategories\nCode\nNews\nPublications and Preprints\nMeta\nLog in\nEntries\nRSS\nComments\nRSS\nBlog.nus\nSkip to toolbar\nLog In\nSearch\n\n---\n\nQianxiao Li (李千骁) | Department of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nSkip to content\nQianxiao Li (李千骁)\nDepartment of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nAbout\nBiography\nQianxiao Li is an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\n, and a principal investigator in the\nInstitute for Functional Intelligent Materials\n, National University of Singapore. He graduated with a BA in mathematics from the University of Cambridge and a PhD in applied mathematics from Princeton University. His research interests include the interplay of machine learning and dynamical systems, control theory, stochastic optimisation algorithms and data-driven methods for science and engineering.\nCV\nShort CV\nSearch for:\nSearch for:\nRecent Posts\nImplementation of stochastic OnsagerNet in jax\nRecent Papers\nCode Repository\nRecent Papers\nRecent Papers\nRecent Comments\nArchives\nOctober 2024\nAugust 2023\nJanuary 2023\nMay 2022\nDecember 2021\nJune 2021\nMarch 2021\nCategories\nCode\nNews\nPublications and Preprints\nMeta\nLog in\nEntries\nRSS\nComments\nRSS\nBlog.nus\nSkip to toolbar\nLog In\nSearch\n\n---\n\nQianxiao Li (李千骁) | Department of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nSkip to content\nQianxiao Li (李千骁)\nDepartment of Mathematics & Institute of Functional Intelligent Materials, National University of Singapore\nAbout\nBiography\nQianxiao Li is an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics\n, and a principal investigator in the\nInstitute for Functional Intelligent Materials\n, National University of Singapore. He graduated with a BA in mathematics from the University of Cambridge and a PhD in applied mathematics from Princeton University. His research interests include the interplay of machine learning and dynamical systems, control theory, stochastic optimisation algorithms and data-driven methods for science and engineering.\nCV\nShort CV\nSearch for:\nSearch for:\nRecent Posts\nImplementation of stochastic OnsagerNet in jax\nRecent Papers\nCode Repository\nRecent Papers\nRecent Papers\nRecent Comments\nArchives\nOctober 2024\nAugust 2023\nJanuary 2023\nMay 2022\nDecember 2021\nJune 2021\nMarch 2021\nCategories\nCode\nNews\nPublications and Preprints\nMeta\nLog in\nEntries\nRSS\nComments\nRSS\nBlog.nus\nSkip to toolbar\nLog In\nSearch"
