    "homepage_text": "Qingsong Wang's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nQingsong Wang's Homepage\nQingsong Wang\nI am currently a Postdoc in the Halıcıoğlu Data Science Institute at UCSD, and my postdoc mentors are Prof.\nMikhail Belkin\nand Prof.\nYusu Wang\n. Previously, I was a postdoc in the Mathematics department of the University of Utah. I received my Ph.D. in math from The Ohio State University under the supervision of Prof.\nFacundo Mémoli\n. In the early years of my Ph.D., I studied complex geometry under the supervision of Prof. Fangyang Zheng.\nEmail: qiw072 at ucsd dot edu\nResearch Interests:\nApplied Algebraic Topology\nMachine Learning\nMetric Geometry\nDifferential Geometry\nPublications:\n2025\n\"\nSeeds of Structure: Patch PCA Reveals Universal Compositional Cues in Diffusion Models\n\"\nwith Zhengchao Wan, Mikhail Belkin, Yusu Wang. to appear in NeurIPS 2025\n\"\nElucidating Flow Matching ODE Dynamics with Respect to Data Geometry and Denoisers\n.\"\narXiv preprint arXiv:2412.18730\n(2024). with Zhenghcao Wan, Gal Mishne, and Yusu Wang\n[arXiv: 2412.18730\n(2024)] ICML 2025.\n2024\n\"\nMonotone Operator Theory-Inspired Message Passing for Learning Long-Range Interaction on Graphs\n\" J\nustin Baker*, Qingsong Wang*, Martin Berzins, Thomas Strohmer, Bao Wang\n[International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTAT 2024)]\n\"Measure Theoretic Reeb Graphs and Reeb Spaces\"\nQingsong Wang, Guanquan Ma, Raghavendra Sridharamurthy, Bei Wang [Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2024)]\n2023\n\"Implicit Graph Neural Networks: A Monotone Operator Viewpoint\"\nJustin Baker*, Qingsong Wang*, Cory D Hauck, and Bao Wang, [\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2023).]\n“Momentum Ensures Convergence of SIGNSGD under Weaker Assumptions”\nTao Sun*, Qingsong Wang*, Dongsheng Li, and Bao Wang, [International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML 2023).]\n2022\n\"\nThe Persistent Topology of Optimal Transport Based Metric Thickenings\n.\n\"  Henry Adams, Facundo Mémoli, Michael Moy\n,\nand\nQingsong Wang\n,\n[\nAlgebraic & Geometric Topology.\narXiv:2109.15061\n]\n.\n2021\n\"\nManifolds with Positive Orthogonal Ricci Curvature\n.\" Lei Ni, Qingsong Wang\n,\nand Fangyang Zheng, [\nAmerican Journal of Mathematics\n143.3 (2021): 833-857.\nar\nX\niv\n:\n1806.10233\n]\n2020\n\"\nOn Bismut Flat Manifolds.\n\"\nQingsong Wang,\nBo Yang, and Fangyang Zheng, Transactions of the American Mathematical Society 373 (8), 5747-5772 (2020) [\nhttps://ar\nXiv\norg/abs/1603.07058\n]\nPreprints:\n2023\n\"It begins with a boundary: A geometric view on probabilistically robust learning\"\nLeon Bungert\n,\nNicolás García Trillos\n,\nMatt Jacobs\n,\nDaniel McKenzie\n,\nĐorđe Nikolić\n,\nQingsong Wang\n,\narXiv preprint arXiv:2305.18779\n\"Extremal spherical polytopes and Borsuk's conjecture\"  with\nMikhail Katz\n,\nFacundo Mémoli\n,[\narXiv.:2301.13076\n, (2023)]\n2022\n\"\nGromov-Hausdorff distances, Borsuk-Ulam theorems, and Vietoris-Rips complexes.\"\nWith Henry Adams, Johnathan Bush, Nate Clause, Florian Frick, Mario Gómez, Michael Harrison, R. Amzi Jeffs, Evgeniya Lagoda, Sunhyuk Lim, Facundo Mémoli, Michael Moy, Nikola Sadovek, Matt Superdock, Daniel Vargas, and Ling Zhou. [\narXiv: 2301.00246\n, (2022)].\n2021\n\"Some results about the Tight Span of spheres.\"\nwith Sunhyuk Lim, Facundo Mémoli, Zhengchao Wan, and Ling Zhou.\n[arXiv:2112.12646\n(2021)]\n\"\nMetric Graph Approximations of Geodesic Spaces.\n\" with Facundo Mémoli\nand\nOsman Okutan[\narXiv:1809.05566\n(2021)].\nServices:\nReview:\nJournals:\n\"Annali della Scuola Normale Superiore di Pisa,\"\n\"Journal of Applied and Computational Topology\n,\"\n\"Journal of Approximation Theory\n,\n\" an\nd\n\"Neurocomputing\n.\n\" \"Foundations of Data Science\"\nConferences:\n\"\nSymposium on Computational Geometry\" 2020, 2022, and 2023, \"TAG for Pattern Recognition with Applications\" (CVPR 23, workshop), \"TAG for Machine Learning\" (ICML 23, workshop), NeurIPS 2023, ICLR 2024, ICML 2024.\nMentoring:\nDirected Reading Program at OSU\n(Spring 2022)\nMentee: Harrison Blake\nProject: “On the Poincaré-Hopf Theorem”\nOthers:\nAssistant of 2022 MRC Summer Conferences on\n\"Data Science at the Crossroads of Analysis, Geometry, and Topology\n\"\nMini-symposium Organizer of\n2nd SIAM Northern States Section Conference\nat Logan, Utah\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
