  "deep_homepage::Yun Yang::https://sites.google.com/view/yun-yang/home": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/yun-yang/home",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yun Yang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYun Yang\nWelcome to Water Resources Lab\nLab News\nOur research has been reported by Cornell Chronicle:\nhttps://news.cornell.edu/stories/2024/08/space-farm-readying-nasa-satellites-help-growers\nAugust 2024 Our lab has officially moved to Soil and Crop Science Section at Cornell University:\nhttps://cals.cornell.edu/yun-yang\nJuly 2024 Dr. Yang has received a faculty position at Cornell University.\nOur research group is moving to Cornell University.\nFebruary 2024 OpenET paper on Nature Water is in the news:\nhttps://science.nasa.gov/earth/openet-moisture-measurement-tool-is-proving-highly-accurate/\nFebruary 2024 OpenET accuracy assessment study is online:\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s44221-023-00181-7\nJanuary 2024 Wildfire impact study is online:\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41559-023-02266-8\nDecember 2023 Dr. Yang gave an invited presentation about\nRemotely sensed ET on forest management\nat AGU Fall Meeting in San Francisco.\nDecember 2023 lab member Dr. Gao gave a poster presentation about V\nineyard water stress using machine learning\nat AGU Fall meeting in San Francisco.\nNovember 2023 Dr. Yang gave a presentation about\nMulti-satellite Data Integration into OpenET\nat Hydrospace in Lisbon, Portugal.\nJune 2023 Dr. Yang gave an presentation about\nglobal satellite evapotranspiration product evaluation and applications\nduring LPVE 2023 meeting at\nEuropean Space Agency\n.\nMay 2023 Thanks to our communication team for the nice article about our group's involvement in\nNASA Acres project\n:\nmedium report\nMarch 2023 Dr. Yang was invited by National Park Service to serve in\nthe panel of NPS remote sensing review\nat Tuscon, AZ.\nDecember 2022 Dr. Yang was invited to give a talk to the\nIEEE GRSS Washington and Northern VA Chapter\n.\nDecember 2022 Dr. Yang was invited to give a talk about\nvegetation water stress monitoring with remote sensing and cloud computing at Cornell University.\nNovember 2022  We are excited that our\nNASA ECOSTRESS proposal\nwas selected for funding to improve vegetation water use change detection and monitoring with multi-source satellite data with cloud computing!\nJuly 2022 Dr. Yang was invited to visit the\nUS Department of Interior and discuss the research work with the Assistant Secretary for Water and Science, Tanya Trujillo.\nJuly 2022 Dr. Yang was invited to the\nLandsat 50 years event on Capitol Hill\nto share her research work about vegetation water use and irrigation scheduling.\nEvapotranspiration Retrieving using Remotely Sensed Data on Google Earth Engine\nForest Health Monitoring\nCrop Water Use\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
