    "homepage_text": "Zhengling Qi\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZhengling Qi\nZhengling Qi\nWelcome! I am an associate professor at School of Business, The George Washington University (GWU). I am also an Amazon Scholar. I finished my  PhD from\nDepartment of Statistics and Operations Research\nat University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill in 2019.  My general research interests are statistical machine Learning and related non-convex optimization. My current research is focused on reinforcement learning and large language models.\nGWU students and potential visitors are welcome to contact me.\nContact Information\nEmail: qizhengling@email.gwu.edu\nAddress: 415E, Funger Hall, 2201 G Street, NW, Washington, DC 20052\nPhone: (202) 994-1970\nExperience\nMarch 2018 - May 2018    Visiting Student at\nDepartment of Industrial and Systems Engineering\n, University of Southern California (Professor\nJong-Shi Pang\n).\nJune 2016 - August 2016  Biostatistics Intern at\nBoehringer Ingelheim\n(Dr.\nDacheng Liu\n).\nMiscellaneous\nHobbies: Badminton, table tennis, travel, texas holdem and food hunting.\nPhoto taken at Horseshoe Bend, Yellowstone and Acadia\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
