    "homepage_text": "Jiaman Li Homepage\nI am an Applied Scientist at Amazon Frontier AI & Robotics (FAR). I obtained my PhD from Stanford University, advised by\nProf. C. Karen Liu\nand\nProf. Jiajun Wu\n.\nMy research interests include human motion modeling and humanoid robot learning, and my long-term goal is to build humanoid agents capable of human-like behaviors that can perceive, move, and interact not only in the virtual world but also in the real world.\nEmail: jiamanli[at]stanford[dot]edu\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\n/\nResume\n/\nTwitter\nPublications\nLifting Motion to the 3D World via 2D Diffusion\nJiaman Li\n,\nC. Karen Liu†\n,\nJiajun Wu†\nCVPR 2025\n(Highlight)\nProject Page\nPaper\nCode\nHuman-Object Interaction from Human-Level Instructions\nZhen Wu,\nJiaman Li\n,\nPei Xu\n,\nC. Karen Liu\nICCV 2025\nProject Page\nPaper\nCode\nZeroHSI: Zero-Shot 4D Human-Scene Interaction by Video Generation\nHongjie Li,\nHong-Xing Yu\n,\nJiaman Li\n,\nJiajun Wu\narxiv 2024\nProject Page\nPaper\nControllable Human-Object Interaction Synthesis\nJiaman Li\n,\nAlexander Clegg\n,\nRoozbeh Mottaghi\n,\nJiajun Wu\n,\nXavier Puig†\n,\nC. Karen Liu†\nECCV 2024\n(Oral)\nProject Page\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nObject Motion Guided Human Motion Synthesis\nJiaman Li\n,\nJiajun Wu†\n,\nC. Karen Liu†\nTOG (SIGGRAPH Asia) 2023\nProject Page\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nMotion Question Answering via Modular Motion Programs\nMark Endo*\n,\nJoy Hsu*\n,\nJiaman Li\n,\nJiajun Wu\nICML 2023\nProject Page\nPaper\nCIRCLE: Capture in Rich Contextual Environments\nJoao Pedro Araujo,\nJiaman Li\n, Karthik Vetrivel, Rishi Agarwal, Deepak Gopinath,\nJiajun Wu\n, Alexander Clegg,\nC. Karen Liu\nCVPR 2023\nProject Page\nPaper\nEgo-Body Pose Estimation via Ego-Head Pose Estimation\nJiaman Li\n,\nC. Karen Liu†\n,\nJiajun Wu†\nCVPR 2023\n(Award Candidate)\nDistinguished Paper Award\nat\nEgoVis Workshop, CVPR 2024\nProject Page\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nScene Synthesis from Human Motion\nSifan Ye*, Yixing Wang*,\nJiaman Li\n, Dennis Park,\nC. Karen Liu\n,\nHuazhe Xu\n,\nJiajun Wu\nSIGGRAPH ASIA 2022\nProject Page\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nGIMO: Gaze-Informed Human Motion Prediction in Context\nYang Zheng\n,\nYanchao Yang\n,\nKaichun Mo\n,\nJiaman Li\n,\nTao Yu\n,\nYebin Liu\n,\nC. Karen Liu\n,\nLeonidas J. Guibas\nECCV 2022\nProject Page\nPaper\nCode\nDenseGAP: Graph-Structured Dense Correspondence Learning with Anchor Points\nZhengfei Kuang\n,\nJiaman Li\n,\nMingming He\n, Tong Wang,\nYajie Zhao\nICPR 2022 (Oral)\nProject Page\nPaper\nTask-Generic Hierarchical Human Motion Prior using VAEs\nJiaman Li\n,\nRuben Villegas\n,\nDuygu Ceylan\n,\nJimei Yang\n,\nZhengfei Kuang\n,\nHao Li\n,\nYajie Zhao\n3DV 2021\nProject Page\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nDynamic Facial Asset and Rig Generation from a Single Scan\nJiaman Li\n*,\nZhengfei Kuang\n*,\nYajie Zhao\n,\nMingming He\n, Karl Bladin,\nHao Li\nTOG (SIGGRAPH ASIA) 2020\nVideo\nPaper\nLearning to Generate Diverse Dance Motions with Transformer\nJiaman Li\n, Yihang Yin,\nHang Chu\n,\nYi Zhou\n,\nTingwu Wang\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nHao Li\narxiv 2020\nVideo\nPaper\nCode\nLearning to Act Properly: Predicting and Explaining Affordances from Images\nChing-Yao Chuang\n,\nJiaman Li\n,\nAntonio Torralba\n,\nSanja Fidler\nCVPR 2018\nProject Page\nPaper\nVirtualHome: Simulating Household Activities via Programs\nXavier Puig\n*, Kevin Ra*, Marko Boben*,\nJiaman Li\n,\nTingwu Wang\n,\nSanja Fidler\n,\nAntonio Torralba\nCVPR 2018 (Oral)\nProject Page\nPaper"
