    "homepage_text": "About me | Xinglu Wang\nXinglu Wang\nHomepage\nView My GitHub Profile\nAbout me\nI am a recent PhD graduate in Computer Science from Simon Fraser University, supervised by Prof. Jiannan Wang and Prof. Jian Pei.\nInterest: LLM Infrastructure Optimization. My two years of experience in large-scale inference systems include exploring failure recovery, disaggregation, and SLO-aware serving.\nLink\nto my CV.\nI obtained a master’s and a bachelor’s degree in Information Engineering at Zhejiang University, supervised by Prof. Yingming Li and Prof. Zhongfei (Mark) Zhang.\nProjects\nPhD thesis: Explore how ML enhances the OR process and how OR enhances the ML lifecycle.\nslide\n,\npdf\nDisaggregated Large Multimodal Model Serving:\npaper\n,\nposter\n,\ncode\nPublications\nWang, X. and Li, Y., 2020, October. Gradient Deconfliction-Based Training For Multi-Exit Architectures. In 2020 IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP) (pp. 1866-1870). IEEE.\nlink\n.\nWang, X. and Li, Y., 2021. Harmonized Dense Knowledge Distillation Training for Multi-exit Architectures. In the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, 2021."
