    "homepage_text": "About me - Zirui Zhou\nZirui Zhou (周子锐)\nhe/his\nCS Ph.D. Student at UIUC\nFollow\n4111,\nSiebel Center\nEmail\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nAbout me\nI’m a first year PhD student at\nSiebel School of Computing and Data Science\nin University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, currently working with\nProf. Charith Mendis\n.\nBefore joining UIUC, I completed my Bachelor’s degree in School of\nElectronics Engineering and Computer Science\nfrom Peking University in 2025. During my time there, I was fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Xin Zhang\nfor my thesis. Also, I feel fortunate to have collaborated with\nProf. Thomas W. Reps\nfrom University of Wisconsin-Madison as a visiting student researcher in summer 2024.\nMy research interests lie in Compilers and Programming Languages, especially about the improvement of tensor compilers for machine learning. Feel free to drop me an email if you are interested about similar topics!\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Zirui Zhou\nZirui Zhou (周子锐)\nhe/his\nCS Ph.D. Student at UIUC\nFollow\n4111,\nSiebel Center\nEmail\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nCV\nEducation\nPh.D in Computer Science, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, Aug. 2025 - Present\nB.S. in Information and Computing Science, Peking University, Sep. 2021 - Jun. 2025\nResearch experience\nJan. 2023 - Jun. 2025: Research Assistant\nProgram Languages Lab, Peking University\nUsing and improving formal verification tools for real-world operating systems\nSupervisor: Prof. Xin Zhang\nJune 2024 – Sept. 2024: Research Assistant\nmadPL, University of Wisconsin-Madison\nImprove analysis result of automatic differentiation via abstract interpretation\nSupervisor: Prof. Thomas W. Reps\nService and leadership\nServe as president of Peking University Student Algorithm Association from Feb. 2024 to Feb. 2025."
  },
