    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home | Yang FU - Research Lab\nYang FU - Research Lab\n#\nHome\nOverview of our research directions and applications.\n#\nLab Overview & Research Focus\nOur research group focuses on cross-scale energy conversion and transport regulation among light, heat, and electricity. At the fundamental level, we investigate photonâelectronâphonon multiparticle coupling mechanisms governing energy transformation (photoelectric / photothermal / thermoelectric processes), establishing new paradigms for directional energy transfer through multiphysics synergistic design. On the applied frontier, leveraging precise programming of energy conversion pathways, we develop advanced intelligent thermal management technologies. Specific research thrusts include:\nPassive radiative cooling\nfor buildings and personal use\nThermal management\nof electronic devices\nSolar photothermal utilization\nLow-carbon sustainable manufacturing technologies\nInverse design and optimization\nof smart materials\n#\nRecent News\n2026.01\nâ Collaborative project âPlasmonic photothermal printing of high-performance metal oxide electronics under room temperatureâ received\n2025 Chinaâs Top 10 Optical Progress (Nomination)\n.\n2026.01\nâ Won\nBest Poster Award\nat the Symposium on Photothermal Regulation Materials and Technologiesï¼åç­è°æ§ææä¸ææ¯ç è®¨ä¼ï¼.\n2025.10\nâ Published research article\nâPhotoluminescent radiative cooling for aesthetic and urban comfortâ\nin\nNature Sustainability\n, and was invited to write a\nResearch Briefing\n(opens new window)\n. The work was featured in\nMatter\n(opens new window)\n.\n2025.07\nâ Appointed as\nYouth Editorial Board Member\nof\nNano-Micro Letters\n.\n2025.06\nâ Co-authored research article\nâPlasmonic printing of high-performance metal oxide electronics under room temperatureâ\nin\nNature Materials\n. The work was featured in\nNature Materials\n(opens new window)\n,\nNature Synthesis\n(opens new window)\n, and\nLight: Science & Applications\n(opens new window)\n.\n2023.04\nâ Co-authored research article\nâUltrathin, soft, radiative cooling interfaces for advanced thermal management in skin electronicsâ\nin\nScience Advances\n. The work was covered by\nScience AAAS (EurekAlert)\n(opens new window)\nand\nTechnology Networks\n(opens new window)\n, among others.\n2023.03\nâ Collaborative project\nâRadiative cooling technic for skin electronicsâ\nwon\nGold Medal\nat the International Exhibition of Inventions Genevaï¼æ¥åç¦å½éåæå±ï¼.\n2022.10\nâ Review article\nâTale of Two Resonances: WaveguideâPlasmon Coupling and High Q-Factor Engineering on the Nanoscaleâ\nwas selected as the cover of\nACS Photonics\n(opens new window)\n.\n\n---\n\nContact | Yang FU - Research Lab\nYang FU - Research Lab\n#\nContact\n#\nYang FU\nProfessor\nSoutheast University\n#\nEmail\nyang.fu@my.cityu.edu.hk\n#\nAddress\nComing soon\n#\nOnline Profiles\nGoogle Scholar\n:\nView Profile\n(opens new window)\nORCID\n:\n0000-0002-7093-7136\n(opens new window)\n#\nOffice Hours\nBy appointment\nFeel free to reach out for collaborations, questions about our research, or data requests.\n\n---\n\nContact | Yang FU - Research Lab\nYang FU - Research Lab\n#\nContact\n#\nYang FU\nProfessor\nSoutheast University\n#\nEmail\nyang.fu@my.cityu.edu.hk\n#\nAddress\nComing soon\n#\nOnline Profiles\nGoogle Scholar\n:\nView Profile\n(opens new window)\nORCID\n:\n0000-0002-7093-7136\n(opens new window)\n#\nOffice Hours\nBy appointment\nFeel free to reach out for collaborations, questions about our research, or data requests.\n\n---\n\nå³äºæ - ä¸ªäººå­¦æ¯ç½ç« | Yang FU - Research Lab\nYang FU - Research Lab\n#\nå³äºæ\næ¬¢è¿æ¥å°æçä¸ªäººç½ç«ï¼\n#\nç®ä»\nè¿éæ¯æçä¸ªäººç½ç«ï¼ç¨äºåäº«æçæ³æ³ãé¡¹ç®åç»éªã\n#\nèç³»æ¹å¼\nEmail: your-email@example.com\nGitHub:\nyour-github\n(opens new window)\næè°¢è®¿é®ï¼\n\n---\n\nå³äºæ - ä¸ªäººå