    "homepage_text": "Canwen Xu\nKevin\nCanwen Xu\nSnowflake AI Research\nude.dscu@uxc\nabout my name\nIn Chinese: 许灿文 (simplified), 許燦文 (traditional)\nHi! I’m doing research on AI and LLMs at\nSnowflake\n. I obtained my PhD degree from UC San Diego in 2024. I was advised by\nProf. Julian McAuley\n. I spent wonderful time doing research at\nMicrosoft\n,\nGoogle\n,\nHugging Face\nand\nBoson AI\n. I got my B.Eng. from Wuhan University in 2020.\nMy research focuses on efficient large language models that reduces carbon footprint, inference delay and computational cost. I have a strong preference for methods that are simple, intuitve and fun.\nservice\nI occasionally serve as reviewer or area chair for the following conferences: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, ACL, EMNLP, NAACL, COLM, WWW, AAAI."
  },
