    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/he-xiaoxin-a130601b4# e.g., ",
    "homepage_text": "Xiaoxin He - Homepage\nXiaoxin He\n何晓昕\nPhD Student, NUS\nSingapore\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nI am a Ph.D. student in the School of Computing at National University of Singapore (NUS), jointly advised by\nProf. Bryan Hooi\nand\nProf. Xavier Bresson\n. Before joining NUS, I received my B.S. in the School of Computer Science at Fudan University.\nMy research interests primary focus on graph learning and large language models (LLMs). I am currently working on topics related to LLMs, such as Retrieval-Augmented Generation and multimodal (graph) reasoning. My research is supported by the\nGoogle PhD Fellowship\n.\nSelected Publications\nG-Retriever: Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Textual Graph Understanding and Question Answering\nXiaoxin He\n, Yijun Tian, Yifei Sun, Nitesh V. Chawla, Thomas Laurent, Yann LeCun, Xavier Bresson, Bryan Hooi\nNeurIPS’24 [\nPaper\n|\nPoster\n|\nBlog\n|\nCode\n]\nHarnessing Explanations: LLM-to-LM Interpreter for Enhanced Text-Attributed Graph Representation Learning\nXiaoxin He\n, Xavier Bresson, Thomas Laurent, Adam Perold, Yann LeCun, Bryan Hooi\nICLR’24 [\nPaper\n|\nPoster\n|\nCode\n]\nA Generalization of ViT/MLP-Mixer to Graphs\nXiaoxin He\n, Bryan Hooi, Thomas Laurent, Adam Perold, Yann LeCun, Xavier Bresson\nICML’23 [\nPaper\n|\nPoster\n|\nCode\n]\nRecent News\n[\n2025.05\n] Two papers were accepted to ICML.\n[\n2025.03\n] Invited by\nRiot Games\nto give a talk on GraphRAG.\n[\n2024.02\n] Invited by\nGlasgow IR Group\nto give a talk on GraphLLM.\n[\n2025.01\n]\nLSCS\nwas accepted to TMLR.\n[\n2024.11\n] Invited by Spanner Graph at Google to give a talk on GraphRAG\n[\n2024.07\n] New family member – I have an adorable\nkitten\n!!!\n[\n2023.06\n] Introduced\nAwesome-Graph-LLM\n, a collection of awesome things about graph-related large language models.\nSelected Awards\nGoogle PhD Fellowship\nin machine intelligence, 2024\nDean’s Graduate Research Excellence Award\n, NUS SoC, 2024\nProfessional Services\nReviewer: ICML’22, NeurIPS’23, NeurIPS’24, ICLR’24, ICLR’25, ICML’25\nOrganizer:\nLoG’24\n, LoG’25,\nWWW’25 Workshop\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
