    "homepage_text": "Qitao Zhao\nQitao Zhao | 赵淇涛\nI'm a Master's student in Computer Vision (\nMSCV\n) at Carnegie Mellon University. I am currently working on sparse-view 3D reconstruction in the wild, advised by Prof.\nShubham Tulsiani\n. \n                Prior to this, I had the privilege of working with Prof.\nChen Chen\nas an undergraduate research intern at the University of Central Florida. I completed my undergraduate studies at Shandong University in June 2023.\nI will be joining the Robotics Institute at CMU as a Ph.D. student this fall.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\ntwitter\nResearch\nMy research focuses on inferring 3D structures from\nsparse\n2D signals, such as predicting a 3D human pose from a few 2D poses or estimating 3D shapes from sparse-view images. I am passionate about recovering visually and physically plausible 3D structures from everyday observations (e.g., photographs or video clips) or through our interactions with the world around us.\nDiffusionSfM: Predicting Structure and Motion via Ray Origin and Endpoint Diffusion\nQitao Zhao\n,\nAmy Lin\n,\nJeff Tan\n,\nJason Y. Zhang\n,\nDeva Ramanan\n,\nShubham Tulsiani\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2025\npaper\n/\nproject page\n/\ncode\nSparse-view Pose Estimation and Reconstruction via Analysis by Generative Synthesis\nQitao Zhao\n,\nShubham Tulsiani\n38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2024\npaper\n/\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\ntwitter thread\nA Single 2D Pose with Context is Worth Hundreds for 3D Human Pose Estimation\nQitao Zhao\n,\nCe Zheng\n,\nMengyuan Liu\n,\nChen Chen\n37th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2023\npaper\n/\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\nvideo\nPoseFormerV2: Exploring Frequency Domain for Efficient and Robust 3D Human Pose Estimation\nQitao Zhao\n,\nCe Zheng\n,\nMengyuan Liu\n,\nPichao Wang\n,\nChen Chen\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2023\npaper\n/\nproject page\n/\ncode\n/\nvideo\nEducation\nCarnegie Mellon University\n, Pittsburgh, PA, USA\n2023.08 - 2024.12 (expected)\nMaster of Science in Computer Vision (\nMSCV\n)\nGPA: 4.11/4.3\nShandong University\n, Qingdao, Shandong, China\n2019.09 - 2023.06\nBachelor of Engineering, Electronic Science and Technology\nGPA: 94.61/100, rank 2/21\nOutstanding Thesis Award\n(Ranked 1st out of 7 finalists among 350+ students in the department)\nNational Scholarship 2020\n(Awarded to the top 0.2% of students nationwide)\nExperience\nCarnegie Mellon University\n, Physical Perception Lab\n2023.09 - Present\nGraduate researcher on\nsparse-view reconstruction in the wild\nAdvisor: Prof.\nShubham Tulsiani\nUniversity of Central Florida\n, CRCV\n2022.04 - 2023.08\nUndergrad research intern on\n3D human pose estimation\nAdvisor: Prof.\nChen Chen\nMiscellaneous\nI enjoy playing basketball 🏀 with friends, and my idol is Kobe Bryant. Kobe impressed me with his diligence, concentration and high standard. He influenced every aspect of my life. R.I.P.\nunique visitors since Nov 2022\nTemplate stolen from\nYijia Weng\n(and also\nJon Barron\n).\nLast updated: Dec 16, 2024"
  },
