    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/microsoft",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jia Zhang's Homepage\nJia Zhang   张佳\nEmail:\njialrs.z[at]gmail[dot]com\nzhangjia[at]microsoft[dot]com\nOffice:\n12114, 12F\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nTower 2, No.5 Danling Street\nHaidian District, Beijing, China\nI am now a senior researcher of the\nMachine Learning Group\nof Microsoft Research Asia (MSRA) and working on intellegence decison (large scale multiple agent \n\t\t\treinforcement learning (MARL), graph knowledge learning, quantum computing etc.). Before join MSRA, I get my Ph.D. degree of Computer Science at the\nInstitute of Computing Technology\n, CAS, and I have worked on online algorithm and \n\t\t\tmechanism design under the guidance of Prof.\nXiaoming Sun\nin the\nAlgorithm & Complexity Group\n.\n        \tBefore joining ICT, I got my bachelor from the \"Wang Daheng Class\" at\nChangchun University of Science and Technology\n.\nPublication\nProject\nCV\nFun\nNote:\nclick the title to see the abstract\nMulti-Agent Resource Optimization Platform (MARO)\n2019.05 - Now\nCo-Leader\n.  MARO is an instance of Reinforcement learning as a Service (RaaS) for real-world resource optimization. It can be applied to many important industrial domains, such as container inventory management in logistics, bike repositioning in transportation, virtual machine provisioning in data centers, and asset management in finance. Besides Reinforcement Learning (RL), it also supports other planning/decision mechanisms, such as Operations Research. More details can be found in the\nGitHub Repo\n.\nDynamic Route Pricing with SF Tech\n2020.05 - 2020.10\nProject Leader\n. With the help of the graph neural network and optimization technology, we dynamically determine the price for the real-time land transportation orders. The goal is to minimize costs and increase automatic turnover rates.\nSupply and Demand Forecasting in Ocean Transportation Netowrk with OOCL\n2020.01 - 2020.09\nProject Leader\n. By using the route and freight relationship in the shipping network, we are aim to forecast the the long-term supply and demand situation of each port.\nMulti-Agent Based Eempty Container Reposition System in Ocean Transportation Network with OOCL\n2018.03 - 2019.08\nProject Leader\n. A multi-agent reinforcement learning system is designed to solve the reposition problem of empty containers in the extremely complex ocean transportation system.\nEducation and Experience:\n2017.07 - present\nSenior Researcher\n, Machine Learning Group, Microsoft Research Asia\n2012.09 - 2017.06\nPh.D. Candidate\n, Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS)\nAdvisor:\nXiaoming Sun\n2015.10 - 2016-04\nResearch Intern\n, Machine Learning Group, Microsoft Research Asia\nMentor:\nTao Qin\n2008.09 - 2012.07\nBachelor\n, School of Computer Science and Technology, Changchun University of Science and Technology\n2005.09 - 2008.07\nShijiazhuang Foreign Language School\nSelected Honors:\n2015&amp2014&amp2013\nOutstanding Student of University of Chinese Academy of Sciences (5%)\n2013\nNational Scholarship for Postgraduate Students (2%)\n2013\nFirst Prize of the 10st National Postgraduate Mathematic Contest in Modeling (2.6% among 3884 teams)\n2012\nOutstanding Graduates of Changchun University of Science and Technology (5%)\n2010\nSecond Prize of ACM/ICPC Contest in Jilin Province (rank 11)\nSocial Activities:\n2013 - 2014\nPresent of Student Branch of Chinese Computer Federation (CCF) in Institute of Computing Technology\n2012 - 2013\nVice Minister of the Ministry of Academic in student union of Institute of Computing Technology\nI like photography. Some selected shoots are listed as follow. For more ones, please visit my\n500px\npage."
  },
