  "deep_homepage::Feng Ji::https://www.feng-ji.org/": {
    "homepage": "https://www.feng-ji.org/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nFeng Ji\nMe chilling in SF, California (fifth one from the right).\nI am a\npsychometrician\n/statistician and data scientist, serving as an Assistant Professor in the Department of\nApplied Psychology and Human Development\nat\nthe University of Toronto\n. I am also the\nCanada Research Chair (Tier II) in Psychometrics and Responsible AI\n.\nI am interested in applying advances from machine learning, statistics, and causal inference literature to answer novel research questions and improve research methods & practice in behavioral, educational, and social sciences research. I am also interested in what roles AI can play around these topics.\nI am an affiliated faculty member of the Collaborative Program in\nNeuroscience(CPIN)\n,\nCenter for Smart Learning and Development\n(CSLD), and\nData Sciences Institute(DSI)\nhere at the\nUniversity of Toronto\n. I serve on the editorial board of journals such as Behavior Research Methods and Psychological Review.\nBefore joining the University of Toronto in 2023, I worked as a research data scientist at\nGoogle\n.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
