    "homepage_text": "Lin-Han Jia @ LAMDA, NJU-CS\nLin-Han Jia @ LAMDA, NJU-CS\nè´¾æç\nLin-Han Jia\nPh.D. Student\nLAMDA Group\nDepartment of Computer Science & Technology\nNational Key Laboratory for Novel Software Technology\nNanjing University\n, Nanjing 210023, China.\nSupervisor\n: Professor\nYu-Feng Li\nEmail\n:\njialh@lamda.nju.edu.cn\nLaboratory\n: Room 912, Computer Science Building, Xianlin Campus of Nanjing University\n[GitHub]\n[Google Scholar]\n[ZhiHu]\nBiography\nCurrently I'm pursuing my Ph.D. degree in the\nDepartment of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nNanjing University\nwhere I'm fortunate to be advised by Prof.\nYu-Feng Li\n. I'm also a member of\nLAMDA Group\n, which is led by Prof.\nZhi-Hua Zhou\n.\nI received my B.Sc. degree from the\nCollege of Computer Science and Technology\nat\nJilin University\nin June 2022.\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests include Machine Learning and Data Mining. Most recently, I focus on Neuro-Symbolic Learning, Unsupervised/Self/Weakly/Semi-Supervised Learning, Transfer Learning, Reasoning Acceleration, Controllable Generation and Quantum Machine Learning.\nPublications\nJournal Papers\nLan-Zhe Guo,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Jie-Jing Shao, Yu-Feng Li. Robust Semi-Supervised Learning in Open Environments. Frontiers of Computer Science. 2025.\n[Paper]\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo, Zhi Zhou, and Yu-Feng Li. LAMDA-SSL: A Comprehensive Semi-Supervised Learning Toolkit. Science CHINA Information Science. 2023.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Slide]\nConference Papers\nWen-Chao Hu, Qi-Jie Li,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Cunjing Ge, Yu-Feng Li, Yuan Jiang, Zhi-Hua Zhou. Curriculum Abductive Learning. In: the 39-th Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS' 25). 2025.\n[Paper]\nShi-Yu Tian, Zhi Zhou, Kun-Yang Yu, Ming Yang,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo, Yu-Feng Li. VC Search: Bridging the Gap Between Well-Defined and Ill-Defined Problems in Mathematical Reasoning. In: Proceedings of the 30-th Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language (EMNLP'25). 2025.\n[Paper]\nSi-Yu Han,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Yu-Feng Li. åºäºæ­£åçç¨³å¥æ°æ®éè½½éå­å­¦ä¹ æ¨¡å. In: Proceedings of the 20-th Chinese Conference on Machine Learning (CCML'25).\nBest Paper Award Nomination\n. 2025.\nLin-Han Jia\n, Wen-Chao Hu, Jie-Jing Shao, Lan-Zhe Guo, Yu-Feng Li. Verification Learning: Make Unsupervised Neuro-Symbolic System Feasible. In: Proceedings of the 42-nd International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'25). 2025.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nXiao-Wen Yang, Jie-Jing Shao, Lan-Zhe Guo, Bo-Wen Zhang, Zhi Zhou,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Wang-Zhou Dai, Yu-Feng Li. Neuro-Symbolic Artificial Intelligence: Towards Improving the Reasoning Abilities of Large Language Models. In: Proceedings of the 34-th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI '2025 Survey Track). 2025.\n[Paper]\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo, Zhi Zhou, and Yu-Feng Li. Realistic Evaluation of Semi-Supervised Learning Algorithms in Open Environments. In: Proceedings of the 12-th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR'24).\nSpotlight Presentation\n. 2024.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nZhi-Zhou, Lan-Zhe Guo,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Ding-Chu Zhang, Yu-Feng Li. ODS: Test-Time Adaptation in the Presence of Open-World Data Shift. In: Proceedings of the 40-th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'23).\nOral Presentation\n. 2023.\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo, Zhi Zhou, Jie-Jing Shao, Yuke Xiang, Yu-Feng Li. Bidirectional Adaptation for Robust Semi-Supervised Learning with Inconsistent Data Distributions. In: Proceedings of the 40-th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML'23).\nOral Presentation\n. 2023.\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nPreprint\nLin-Han Jia\n, Si-Yu Han, Wen-Chao Hu, Jie-Jing Shao, Wen-Da Wei, Zhi Zhou, Lan-Zhe Guo, Yu-Feng Li. When Is Prior Knowledge Helpful? Exploring the Evaluation and Selection of Unsupervised Pretext Tasks from a Neuro-Symbolic Perspective. arXiv preprint arXiv:2508.07299. 2025.\n[Paper]\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo, Zhi Zhou, Si-Yu Han, Zi-Wen Li, Yu-Feng Li. Detecting Scarce and Sparse Anomalous: Solving Dual Imbalance in Multi-Instance Learning. arXiv preprint arXiv:2503.13562. 2025.\n[Paper]\nLin-Han Jia\n, Si-Yu Han, Lan-Zhe Guo, Zhi Zhou, Zhao-Long Li, Yu-Feng Li, Zhi-Hua Zhou. A Smooth Transition Between Induction and Deduction: Fast Abductive Learning Based on Probabilistic Symbol Perception. arXiv preprint arXiv:2502.12919. 2025.\n[Paper]\nSi-Yu Han,\nLin-Han Jia\n, Lan-Zhe Guo. Multiple Embeddings for Quantum Machine Learning. arXiv preprint arXiv:2503.22758. 2025.\n[Paper]\nSoftwares\nLAMDA-SSL: A comprehensive toolkit for Semi-Supervised Learning.\n[Project]\n[Documentation]\n[Examples]\nAwards & Honors\nCCML Best Paper Award Nomination, 2025\nLAMDA Elite Award, 2025\nFirst Prize of the Nanjing University Elite PhD Scholarship, 2024\nOutstanding Graduate Student of Nanjing University, 2023 and 2024\nNational Scholarship, 2023\nOutstanding Graduate of Jilin University, 2022\nOutstanding Undergraduate Thesis of Jilin Uninversity, 2022\nCCF Elite Collegiate Student Award, 2021\nACM-ICPC Asia Regional Contest, Silver Medal, 2021\nOutstanding Student of Jilin University, 2021 and 2020\nFirst Prize Scholarship of Jilin University, 2021 and 2020\nCCPC Jilin Province Collegiate Programming Contest, Gold Medal, 2020\nMathematical Contest In Modeling, Finalist Prize, 2020\nChina Undergraduate Mathematical Contest in Modeling, First Prize of Jilin Province, 2020 and 2019\nAcademic Services\nReviewer for Conferences and Journals: NeurIPS 2023-2025, AAAI 2024-2025, ICLR 2024-2025, IJCAI 2024-2025, ICML 2025, KDD 2024-2025, Neuro Computing, Neural Networks\nVolunteer for IJCLR 2024\nTeaching Assistant, Advanced Machine Learning (NJU, For Graduate Students), 2024\nVolunteer for MLA 2022-2023\nCorrespondence\nEmail\n:\njialh@lamda.nju.edu.cn\nAddress\n: Lin-Han Jia, National Key Laboratory for Novel Software Technology, Nanjing University, Xianlin Campus, 163 Xianlin Avenue, Qixia District, Nanjing 210023, China (åäº¬å¸æ éåºä»æå¤§é163å·, åäº¬å¤§å­¦ä»ææ ¡åº, è½¯ä»¶æ°ææ¯å½å®¶éç¹å®éªå®¤, 210023.)\nLast modified: September 6, 2022."
