    "homepage_text": "Junho Yang's Webpage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJunho Yang's Webpage\nJunho Yang\nAssistant Research Fellow in the Institute of Statistical Science at Academia Sinica\nContact Information\nInstitute of Statistical Science, No. 128, Academia Rd. Sect. 2, Taipei 115, Taiwan.\nEmail\n:\njunhoyang.stat (at) gmail.com; junhoyang (at) stat.sinica.edu.tw\nMain office\n: +886-2-2783-5611\nAbout me\nHi, I am a (tenure-track) assistant research fellow in the Institute of Statistical Science at Academia Sinica.\nMy research interests include, but not restricted to\nspatial point processes,\ntime series analysis\n,\nand\napplied probability focusing on the spectral properties of Toeplitz matrices\n.\nAvailable positions\nI am seeking a\nfull-time R\nesearch Assistant\n(at any level) and / or a\nPostdoctoral Scholar\nworking on the topic of spatial point processes.\nI can also support a\nshort-term visit\n(1 month to 6 months) for current domestic or international graduate students.\nFor those who are interested and can read Mandarin, please refer to the\njob posting\nand follow the application instructions\n. For non-mandarin speakers\n, please\nrefer to\nthe\njob description\n.\nThe position is open as long as this post is active.\nUpcoming Visits / Presentations\n[Mar. 16-23, 2026] Research visit @Korea University. I will be staying in Seoul during this week, so feel free to contact me for discussion.\n[Jun. 13-16, 2026]\nIMS-APRM 2026\n@CUHK, Hong Kong (Invitation from\nWon Chang\n).\n[Jul. 1-21, 2026]\nInternational Summer School\n:\nScientific approach toward nonstationary time series analysis for biomedical artificial intelligence @IoM, Academia Sinica (\nNTU campus\n). I am one of the lecturers for this 3-week intensive lecture series.\nPapers and Preprints (\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nSpatial point processes\n\"On ignorability of preferential sampling in geostatistics\". 2025. (with Changqing Lu, Ganggang Xu, and Yongtao Guan)\n(submitted)\n[\narXiv\n]\n\"Pseudo-spectra of multivariate inhomogeneous spatial point processes\". 2025. (with Qi-Wen Ding and Joonho Shin)\n(Submitted)\n[\narXiv\n]\n\"Fourier analysis of spatial point processes\".\nBernoulli\n. 202\n6\n. (with Yongtao Guan) [\njournal\n][\narXiv\n]\n\"On minimum contrast method for multivariate spatial point processes\".\nElectronic Journal of Statistics\n. 202\n5\n. (with Lin Zhu,\nMikyoung Jun\n, and Scott Cook)\n[\njournal\n]\n[\narXiv\n]\nTime series\n\"On the edge eigenvalues of the precision matrix of the nonstationary autoregressive processes\".\nAdvances in Applied Probabilit\ny\n.\n2025. [\njourn\nal\n]\n[\narXiv\n]\n\"On the asymptotic behavior of a finite section of the optimal causal filter\".\nBernoulli\n. 2024. [\njournal\n][\narXiv\n]\n\"A prediction perspective on the Wiener-Hopf equations for time series\".\nJournal of Time Series Analysis\n. 2023.\n(with\nSuhasini Subba Rao) [\njournal\n][\narXiv\n]\n\"Reconciling the Gaussian and Whittle Likelihood with an application to estimation in the frequency domain\".\nAnnals of Statistics\n.  2021. (with Suhasini Subba Rao) [\njournal\n][\narXiv\n][\nblogpost\n]\n\"\nSpectral methods for small sample time series: A complete periodogram approach\".\nJournal of Time Series Analysis\n.\n2021. (with Sourav Das and Suhasini Subba Rao)\n[\njournal\n]\n[\narXiv\n][\nsoftware\n]\nApplications\n\"\nEvaluating the relationship between lightning and the large-scale environment and its use for lightning prediction\".\nJournal of Geophysical Research: Atmospheres\n.\n2021.\n(with Montana Etten-Bohm, Courtney Schumacher, and\nMikyoung Jun\n)\n[\njou\nrnal\n]\n\"Predictive Statistical representations of observed and simulated rainfall using generalized linear models\".\nJournal of Climate\n. 2019.\n(with\nMikyoung Jun\n, Courtney Schumacher, and R. Saravanan) [\njournal\n]\nMiscellaneous\n\"Local approximations of inverse block Toeplitz matrices and Baxter-type theorems for long-memory processes\".  2023. (with\nAkihiko Inoue\n)\n(\nTechnical Report\n)\n[\narXiv\n]\n\"A new spectral method in time series analysis\". Ph.D. dissertation, Texas A&M University, 2021.\n[\nlink\n]\nSelected Awards\n2030 Cross-Generation Young Scholars Program, Emerging Young Scholars (2030跨世代年輕學者方案, 新秀學者), NSTC\n, Taiwan, 202\n5.\nCareer Development Award (前瞻計畫), Academia Sinica, 2025.\nTa-You Wu Memorial Award (吳大猷先生紀念獎), NSTC, Taiwan, 2024.\nKISS Career Development Award (\nHonorable Mention)\n, Korean International Statistical Society (KISS), 2021.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
