    "homepage_text": "Junseok Lee · homepage\nPersonal homepage about Junseok Lee\n© 2025. All rights reserved.\nJunseok Lee\nhomepage\nAbout me\nI’m a ph.D student in\nIndustrial & System Engineering\nat KAIST, where I am fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Chanyoung Park\nin\nData Science & Artificial Intelligence (DSAIL)\nlab.\nMy research interests lie in realm of\napplied machine learning\n, particularly in harnessing the relationships between data by leveraging the power of Graph Neural Networks (GNNs). Currently, my primary focus involves the application of maching learning to the filed of\nBioinformatics\n, with a particular focus on\nsingle-cell RNA analysis\nand\nprotein design\n.\nGraph Representation Learning\nSingle-cell RNA-seq analysis\nProtein Design\nNews\n[May 2025] A paper got accepted at KDD 2025\n[May 2025] A paper got accepted at ICML 2025\n[January 2025] A paper got accepted at ICLR 2025 (oral)\n[October 2024] I received KAIST Graduate Student Outstanding Paper Award for the paper “Single-cell RNA Sequencing Data Imputation Using Bi-level Feature Propagation” published in Briefings in Bioinformatics.\n[July 2024] I started as a visiting Ph.D student at University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth), USA.\nRead more"
  },
