    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yichen-li-9395101a0",
    "homepage_text": "Yichen Li - Homepage\nYichen Li\nEnjoy the journey!\nPh.D. Candidate of CSE, CUHK\nShaTin, Hong Kong\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nI received my Ph.D degree at the\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\n, under the supervision of\nProf. Michael R. Lyu\n. Previously, I received Bachelor’s degree in Information Security from Huazhong University of Science and Technology in 2021.\nI am dedicated to building next-generation\nAI Coding Agents\nby mastering the full spectrum of techs involved. My goal is to bridge the gap between SE tools and models.\nMy expertise is built on three core pillars:\nCoding Agent Tools & Skills\n: Developing agents grounded in\nProgram Analysis\n, treating static and dynamic analysis as equipable skills that allow agents to be precise and verifiable.\nRepository-Level Context Engineering\n: Optimizing code context and architecture to enable agents to understand and modify large-scale, complex codebases.\nOpen Code World Model\n: Pioneering\nexecution-aware\nproblem solving. Combining SFT/RL with dynamic program analysis, aiming to evolve LLMs from static text generators into agents that understand execution states.\nFeel free to drop me an email if you are interested in my research or just want to talk with me 😆.\n🔥 News\n[09/2025] 🎉 Our\nLogImprover\n,\nErrorPrism\n,\nLogPilot\nhave been accepted by\nASE25\n.\n[07/2025] 🎉 Passed my thesis defense!\n[05/2025] 🎉 Our\nCOFFE\nhas won the\nACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper Award\n[01/2025] 🎉 Our\nCOCA\nhas been accepted by\nICSE25\n.\n[05/2024] I will join the\nMicrosoft Azure Systems Research group\nas a research intern this summer. Meet me @Redmond!\n[04/2024] Check the first & most large-scale empirical study\nLogBench\nabout “LLMs for logging” [\nPaper\n] [\nLogBench\n]!\n[01/2024] 🎉 Our\nSCLogger\nand\nLILAC\nhave been accepted without revision by\nFSE24\n(56/483).\n[01/2024] 🎉 Our\nIDECoder\nhas been accepted by\nICSE-LLM4Code\n.\n[08/2023] 🎉 Our\nAutoLog\nhas been accepted by\nASE23\n(134/629).\n📝 Selected Publications\n(* Equal contribution, # Corresponding author)\nEuroSys'26\nJinyang Liu,\nYichen Li\n, Tieying Zhang, Binbin Chen, Xiao He, Zhihan Jiang, Haipeng Zhang, Gang Wu, Yi Li. “Proactive Change Risk Detection in Production Cloud Systems: ByteDance Experience”. The European Conference on Computer Systems, Edinburgh, United Kingdom, Apr 2026.\nICPC'26\nRenyi Zhong, Yintong Huo, Wenwei Gu,\nYichen Li\n#, Michael R. Lyu. “\nAutoLogger: A Multi-Agent Framework for the End-to-End Automated Logging\n”. The 34th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Program Comprehension, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, May 2026.\nTOSEM\nRenyi Zhong,\nYichen Li\n, Guangba Yu, Wenwei Gu, Jinxi Kuang, Yintong Huo, Michael R. Lyu. “Larger is Not Always Better: Exploring Small Open-Source Language Models in Logging Statement Generation”. ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (Journal-First).\nASE'25\nYichen Li\n, Jinyang Liu, Junsong Pu, Zhihan Jiang, Zhuangbin Chen, Xiao He, Tieying Zhang, Jianjun Chen, Yi Li, Rui Shi, Michael R. Lyu. “Automated Proactive Logging Quality Improvement for Large-Scale Codebases”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Seoul, South Korea, Nov 2025.\nASE'25\nJunsong Pu,\nYichen Li\n, Zhuangbin Chen, Jinyang Liu, Zhihan Jiang, Jianjun Chen, Rui Shi, Zibin Zheng, Tieying Zhang. “\nErrorPrism: Reconstructing Error Propagation Paths in Cloud Service Systems\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Seoul, South Korea, Nov 2025.\nASE'25\nZhihan Jiang, Jinyang Liu,\nYichen Li\n, Haiyu Huang, Xiao He, Tieying Zhang, Jianjun Chen, Yi Li, Rui Shi, Michael R. Lyu. “\nLogPilot: Intent-aware and Scalable Alert Diagnosis for Large-scale Online Service Systems\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Seoul, South Korea, Nov 2025.\nASE-NIER'25\nRuofan Lu,\nYichen Li\n, Yintong Huo. “\nExploring Autonomous Agents: A Closer Look at Why They Fail When Completing Tasks\n” The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Seoul, South Korea, Nov 2025.\nPACMI'25\nVaastav Anand,\nYichen Li\n, Alok Gautam Kumbhare, Celine Irvene, Chetan Bansal, Gagan Somashekar, Jonathan Mace, Pedro Las-Casas, and Rodrigo Fonseca. “\nIntent-based System Design and Operation\n”. Practical Adoption Challenges of ML for Systems (co-located with SOSP), 2025.\nDSN'25\nZhihan Jiang, Rui Ren, Guangba Yu, Yulun Wu, Wenwei Gu,\nYichen Li\n, Yujie Huang, Cong Feng, Zengyin Yang, Yongqiang Yang, Michael R. Lyu. “\nLLMPrism: Black-box Performance Diagnosis for Production LLM Training Platforms\n” the 55th Annual IEEE/IFIP International Conference on Dependable Systems and Networks, Naples, Italy, Jun 2025.\nTOSEM\nRenyi Zhong,\nYichen Li\n, Jinxi Kuang, Wenwei Gu, Yintong Huo, Michael R. Lyu. “\nAutomated Detection and Repair of Specific Defects in Logging Statements\n”. ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (Journal-First).\nICSE'25\nYichen Li\n, Yulun Wu, Jinyang Liu, Zhihan Jiang, Zhuangbin Chen, Guangba Yu and Michael R. Lyu. “\nCOCA: Generative Root Cause Analysis for Distributed Systems with Code Knowledge\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software Engineering, Ottawa, Ontario, Canada, Apr 2025.\nFSE'25\nYun Peng, Jun Wan,\nYichen Li\nand Xiaoxue Ren. “\nCOFFE: A Code Efficiency Benchmark for Code Generation\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Trondheim, Norway, June 2025.\n🏆\nACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper Award\nFSE'25\nZhihan Jiang, Junjie Huang, Guangba Yu, Zhuangbin Chen,\nYichen Li\n, Renyi Zhong, Cong Feng, Yongqiang Yang, Zengyin Yang, Michael R. Lyu. “\nL4: Diagnosing Large-scale LLM Training Failures via Automated Log Analysis\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Trondheim, Norway, June 2025.\nFSE'25\nWeibin Wu, Haoxuan Hu, Zhaoji Fan, Yitong Qiao, Yizhan Huang,\nYichen Li\nand Michael R. Lyu. “\nAn Empirical Study of Code Clones from Commercial AI Code Generators\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Trondheim, Norway, June 2025.\nFSE'24\nYichen Li\n, Yintong Huo, Renyi Zhong, Zhihan Jiang, Jinyang Liu, Junjie Huang, Jiazhen Gu, Pinjia He and Michael R. Lyu. “\nGo Static: Contextualized Logging Statement Generation\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Porto de Galinhas, Brazil, July 2024. [\nProject\n]\nFSE’24\nYizhan Huang,\nYichen Li\n, Weibin Wu, Jianping Zhang and Michael R. Lyu. “\nYour Code Secret Belongs to Me: Neural Code Completion Tools Can Memorize Hard-coded Credentials\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Porto de Galinhas, Brazil, July 2024. [\nProject\n][\nNews🔥\n][\nNews🔥\n]\nFSE’24\nZhihan Jiang, Jinyang Liu, Zhuangbin Chen,\nYichen Li\n, Junjie Huang, Yintong Huo, Pinjia He, Jiazhen Gu and Michael R. Lyu. “\nLILAC: Log Parsing using LLMs with Adaptive Parsing Cache\n”. The ACM International Conference on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Porto de Galinhas, Brazil, July 2024. [\nProject\n]\nTSE\nYichen Li\n*, Yintong Huo *, Zhihan Jiang, Renyi Zhong, Pinjia He, Yuxin Su, Lionel C. Briand and Michael R. Lyu. “\nExploring the Effectiveness of LLMs in Automated Logging Statement Generation: An Empirical Study\n”. IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering (Journal-First). [\nProject\n]\nICSE-LLM4Code'24\nYichen Li\n, Yun Peng, Yintong Huo and Michael R. Lyu. “\nEnhancing LLM-based Coding Tools Through Native Integration of IDE-Derived Static Context\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software Engineering Workshop on Large Language Model for Code, Lisbon, Portugal, Apr 2024.\nISSTA'24\nZhihan Jiang, Jinyang Liu, Junjie Huang,\nYichen Li\n, Yintong Huo, Jiazhen Gu, Zhuangbin Chen, Jieming Zhu and Michael R. Lyu. “\nA Large-scale Evaluation for Log Parsing Techniques: How Far are We?\n”. The ACM SIGSOFT International Symposium on Software Testing and Analysis, Vienna, Austria, Sep 2024. [\nProject\n]\nISSTA'24\nShiwen Shan, Yintong Huo, Yuxin Su,\nYichen Li\n, Dan Li, Zibin Zheng. “\nFace It Yourselves: An LLM-based Two-Stage Strategy to Localize Configuration Errors via Logs\n”. The ACM SIGSOFT International Symposium on Software Testing and Analysis, Vienna, Austria, Sep 2024. [\nProject\n]\nICSE-SEIP'24\nJunjie Huang, Jinyang Liu, Zhuangbin Chen, Zhihan Jiang,\nYichen Li\n, Jiazhen Gu, Cong Feng, Zengyin Yang, Yongqiang Yang, and Michael R. Lyu. “\nFaultProfIT: Hierarchical Fault Profiling of Incident Tickets in Large-scale Cloud Systems\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software Engineering, Lisbon, Portugal, Apr 2024.\nTSE\nXin-Cheng Wen, Cuiyun Gao, Jiaxin Ye,\nYichen Li\n, Zhihong Tian, Yan Jia, Xuan Wang. “\nMeta-path based attentional graph learning model for vulnerability detection\n”. IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering (Journal-First).\nASE'23\nYintong Huo*,\nYichen Li\n*, Yuxin Su, Pinjia He, Zifan Xie and Michael R. Lyu. “\nAutoLog: A Log Sequence Synthesis Framework for Anomaly Detection\n”. The IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Kirchberg, Luxembourg, Sep 2023. [\nProject\n]\nOSR\nYichen Li\n, Xu Zhang, Shilin He, Zhuangbin Chen, Yu Kang, Jinyang Liu, Liqun Li, Yingnong Dang, Feng Gao, Zhangwei Xu, Saravan Rajmohan, Qingwei Lin, Dongmei Zhang, Michael R Lyu. “\nAn Intelligent Framework for Timely, Accurate, and Comprehensive Cloud Incident Detection\n”. ACM SIGOPS Operating Systems Review.\nTSE\nYun Peng, Shuqing Li, Wenwei Gu,\nYichen Li\n, Wenxuan Wang, Cuiyun Gao, Michael R Lyu. “\nRevisiting, benchmarking and exploring API recommendation: How far are we?\n”. IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering (Journal-First). [\nProject\n]\n📖 Educations\n2021.08 ~ 2025.10 Ph.D. student, Chinese University of Hong Kong\n2017.09 ~ 2021.06 Bachelor degree, Huazhong University of Science and Technology\n🎖 Honors and Awards\nACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper Award. 2025.\nNational Scholarship, Ministry of Education of the P.R. China. 2021.\nNational Scholarship, Ministry of Education of the P.R. China. 2020.\nStar of Tomorrow, Microsoft Research Asia.\n🏃 Experiences\n2024.11 - Now: Research Intern, ByteBrain@ByteDance. China.\n2024.06 - 2024.09: Research Intern, Azure System Research@Microsoft Research. US.\n2022.04 - 2022.07: Research Intern, DKI@Microsoft Research Asia. China.\n2020.11 - 2021.06: Research Intern, DKI@Microsoft Research Asia. China.\n💼 Services\nProgram Committee:\n2025: ISSRE’25, EUROSYS’26 (Shadow PC), APSEC’25, FORGE’26, MSR’25 (Junior PC)\n2024: ISSRE’24 (Fast Abstract Track)\nReview Committee:\n2025: TOSEM\nReviewer:\nTOSEM, TSE, CSUR, TIFS, IoTJ, TR, EMSE\nSub-Reviewer:\n2025: ATC\n2024: FSE, ISSTA, ISSRE\n2023: DSN, FSE, ISSRE, ICPE\n2022: FSE, ISSRE\n2021: DSN, ICSE\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
