  "deep_homepage::Di Wu::https://diwu.webflow.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://diwu.webflow.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "d_wu@mit.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/di-wu-13293893/",
    "homepage_text": "Di Wu's Homepage\nDi Wu\nAssistant Professor, ERAU AE\nDirector, XD Lab\nAbout\n‍\nI am looking for motivated and technically strong PhD students to join. XD Lab aims \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tat promoting deep integration of space engineering and artificial intelligence and pushing limit on space engineering methodology innovation for efficient and sustainable anthropogenic space development. If you are interested in Space, Dynamics, Mission Design and AI, please feel free to fill out the\nrecruiting form\nand shoot me an email.\nDi Wu\nreceived his PhD from UC San Diego advised by Aaron Rosengren and worked as a Postdoc in MIT advised by Richard Linares. His research is positioned at the intersection of the rapidly proliferating field of space engineering, the continuous growth of machine learning and artificial intelligence, and the solid foundations in computation, numerical methods, optimization, dynamics, and control, with the application in learning and autonomy in orbit environment and space systems.\nResearch Interests\nEfficient Space System\nEfficiency is increasingly critical in space system design, operation, and research. We innovate in key areas as Numerical Methods (Koopman Operator), Feature Generations (Proper Elements), Dynamical System (Chaos and Manifold Dynamics), and improve Space Sustainability and enable Space System Design.\nSpace AI+\nArtificial Intelligence built for Space offers substantial potential for all space application. We innovate in key areas of GAI application in Space, providing PSA (problem set astrodynamics) Benchmark for LLM, develop reinforcement agent exploring space launching policy, building blocks towards a balanced Space AI+.\nASI\nWe innovate in ASI (Anthropology-Space Interaction), the study of how humans interact with space, and what are the socio-economical impact of such interaction, and the influence on science and technology systematically.\nSelected Publications\nAPBench and Benchmarking Large Language Model Performance in Fundamental Astrodynamics Problems for Space Engineering\n‍\nD Wu, R Zhang, EM Zucchelli, Y Chen, R Linares\nScientific Reports, In-press 2025\nMOCAT on Temporal Analysis and Quantification for Policies in Space Sustainability\n‍\nD Wu, D Jang, M Contreras, R Linares\nAMOS, Best Pitch Reward, September 2024\nEarly Classification of Space Objects based on Astrometric Time Series Data\n‍\nG Lavezzi, P M Siew, D Wu, Z Folcik, V Fernandez, J Price, R Linares\nAMOS, September 2024\nComparative Analysis Of Analytical And Data-Driven Koopman Operators For The J2 Problem With Atmospheric Drag\n‍\nC Hofmann, G Lavezzi, D Wu, S Servadio, R Linares\nAAS, August 2024\nFine Tuned Language Models as Space Systems Controllers\nE Zucchelli, D Wu, J Briden, C Hofmann, V Fernandez, R Linares\nAAS, August 2024\nRSO proper elements: Concept, methods, and application to maneuver detection\n‍\nD Wu, L Dell’Elce, AJ Rosengren\nAdvances in Space Research 73 (1), 64-84, 2024\nAn investigation on space debris of unknown origin using proper elements and neural networks\nD Wu, AJ Rosengren\nCelestial Mechanics and Dynamical Astronomy 135 (4), 44, 2023\nSecular Dynamics based Features for the Characterization of Small Debris Clouds after Fragmentation\nD Wu, AJ Rosengren\nAAS, August 2021\nNeural Network Based TLE Error Modeling And Quantification\nN Reiland, S Jaxy, D Wu, A Rosengren\nAAS, August 2020\nThe arches of chaos in the Solar System\n‍\nN Todorović, D Wu, AJ Rosengren\nScience advances 6 (48), eabd1313, 2020\nContact\nEmail:\nd_wu@mit.edu\nOffice:\n1 Aerospace Boulevard, Daytona Beach, FL 32114-3900\nIf you work on Space Engineering, Space Sustainability, ML/AI/GenAI, and Dynamical System and are interested in joining my lab, please fill out the\nrecruiting form\n.\nDi Wu\nAbout\nHomepage of Prof. Di Wu\nERAU AE\nCopyright © Di Wu"
  },
