    "homepage_text": "Peizhao Li | Home\nPeizhao Li\nResearch Scientist at Google\npeizhaoli05 [AT] gmail.com\nBio\nMy name is Peizhao Li, pronounced as 'Pay-Jow Lee' and written as '李沛钊' in Chinese.\n  I am a Research Scientist with the Apparel Virtual Try-On team at Google.\n  I am based in Seattle, WA.\n  Prior to this, I was a Research Scientist at GE HealthCare, and received my Ph.D. from Brandeis University in 2024.\nI work on productionizing Generative AI at Google.\n  In the past, I worked on Responsible AI, Multimodal Learning, and Computer Vision.\n  My research was recognized by a NIJ Graduate Research Fellowship, a Meta Ph.D. Research Fellowship Finalist, and a CVPR Best Paper Award.\nI was very fortunate to have Prof. Hongfu Liu as my Ph.D. advisor.\nRecent Publications\nMy three most recent papers. For full publications, please refer to my Google Scholar profile.\nUniAR: A Unified model for predicting human Attention and Responses on visual content\nPeizhao Li\n, Junfeng He, Gang Li, Rachit Bhargava, Shaolei Shen, Nachiappan Valliappan, Youwei Liang, Hongxiang Gu, Venky Ramachandran, Golnaz Farhadi, Yang Li, Kai J Kohlhoff, Vidhya Navalpakkam.\nNeurIPS'24: Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024\nPaper\nMMVR: Millimeter-wave Multi-View Radar Dataset and Benchmark for Indoor Perception\nMohammad Mahbubur Rahman, Ryoma Yataka, Sorachi Kato, Pu Wang,\nPeizhao Li\n, Adriano Cardace, Petros Boufounos\nECCV'24: European Conference on Computer Vision, 2024\nPaper\nRich Human Feedback for Text-to-Image Generation\nYouwei Liang, Junfeng He, Gang Li,\nPeizhao Li\n, Arseniy Klimovskiy, Nicholas Carolan, Jiao Sun, Jordi Pont-Tuset, Sarah Young, Feng Yang, Junjie Ke, Krishnamurthy Dj Dvijotham, Katie Collins, Yiwen Luo, Yang Li, Kai J Kohlhoff, Deepak Ramachandran, Vidhya Navalpakkam\nCVPR'24: IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, 2024 (Oral, Best Paper Award)\nPaper\nPeizhao Li\npeizhaoli05 [AT] gmail.com"
  },
