    "homepage_text": "Wei Pan's Home Page\nWei Pan\nProfessor,\nDivision of Biostatistics\nSchool of Public Health,\nUniversity of Minnesota\n2221 University Ave SE, Suite 200\nMinneapolis, MN 55455\nFax: (612)626-0660\nE-mail: panxx014 AT umn DOT  edu\nOther affiliations at the U of M:\nFaculty,\nGraduate \n    Program in Bioinformatics\nMember,\nBiomedical Genomics \n    Center\nMember,\nCancer  \n    Center\nEducation:\nPhD in\nStatistics\n,\nUW-Madison\n, 1997.\nMS in\nComputer Science\n, \n    UW-Madison, 1996.\nBEng in Computer Engineering & BS in Applied Math,\nTsinghua U\n, Beijing, 1989.\nTeaching:\nSpring 2026: PubH 8475/Stat 8056.\nAdvanced Topics in Machine Learning.\nSpring 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2024: PubH (7475/)8475/Stat 8056.\nStatistical Learning and Data Mining.\nFall 2006-2013: PubH 7450.\nSurvival Analysis.\nSpring 2007: PubH 7475/8400.\nStatistical Learning and Data Mining.\nSpring 2006: BINF 5480.\nBioinformatics Journal Club.\nSpring 2006: PubH 7407.\nCategorical Data Analysis.\nSpring 2003:\nPubH 5470-2\nStatistics in Genetics and Molecular Biology.\nPart III\n(Microarray Data Analysis)\nResearch Interests:\nStatistical genetics, especially genetic association testing for\nGWAS and sequencing data.\nBioinformatics: integrative analysis of multiple types of omics data;\nanalysis of microarray gene expression data\n.\n (What is\nbioinformatics\n?\nBioinformatics\nat U of M.)\nStatistical/machine learning/AI: learning from multi-modal data; supervised learning (classification), \nunsupervised learning (clustering), and\nsemi-supervised learning; penalized/regularized methods.\nSurvival analysis and clinical trials: \n    estimation with truncated and/or (interval) censored data.\nGeneralized linear models with correlated responses:\n      GEE, mixed effects models.\nSome recent publications:\nMalakhov MM, Pan W. Co-expression-wide association studies link genetically regulated interactions with complex traits. Nat Commun. 2025 Dec 11;16(1):11061. doi: 10.1038/s41467-025-66039-6. PMID: 41381446; PMCID: PMC12698763.\nLink\nHe R, Ren J, Malakhov MM, Pan W. Enhancing nonlinear transcriptome- and proteome-wide association studies via trait imputation with applications to Alzheimer's disease. PLoS Genet. 2025 Apr 10;21(4):e1011659. doi: 10.1371/journal.pgen.1011659. PMID: 40209152; PMCID: PMC12040266.\nLink\nFang L, Xue H, Lin Z, Pan W. Multivariate proteome-wide association study to identify causal proteins for Alzheimer disease. Am J Hum Genet. 2025 Feb 6;112(2):291-300. doi: 10.1016/j.ajhg.2024.12.010. Epub 2025 Jan 9. PMID: 39793580; PMCID: PMC11866954.\nLink\nYao Y, Zhang MJ, Wang W, Zhuang Z, He R, Ji Y, Knutson KA, Norby FL, Alonso A, Soliman EZ, Tang W, Pankow JS, Pan W, Chen LY. Multimodal data integration to predict atrial fibrillation. Eur Heart J Digit Health. 2024 Nov 4;6(1):126-136. doi: 10.1093/ehjdh/ztae081. PMID: 39846068; PMCID: PMC11750194.\nLink\nWang M, Shen X, Pan W. Causal Discovery with Generalized Linear Models through Peeling Algorithms. J Mach Learn Res. 2024;25:310. PMID: 39758585; PMCID: PMC11699566.\nLink\nLin Z, Pan I, Pan W. On network deconvolution for undirected graphs. Biometrics. 2024 Oct 3;80(4):ujae112. doi: 10.1093/biomtc/ujae112. PMID: 39377517; PMCID: PMC11459367.\nLink\nRamprasad P, Pai N, Pan W. Enhancing personalized gene expression prediction from DNA sequences using genomic foundation models. HGG Adv. 2024 Oct 10;5(4):100347. doi: 10.1016/j.xhgg.2024.100347. Epub 2024 Aug 27. PMID: 39205391; PMCID: PMC11416237.\nLink\nLin Z, Pan W. A robust cis-Mendelian randomization method with application to drug target discovery. Nat Commun. 2024 Jul 18;15(1):6072. doi: 10.1038/s41467-024-50385-y. PMID: 39025905; PMCID: PMC11258283.\nLink\nWang P, Lin Z, Xue H, Pan W. Collider bias correction for multiple covariates in GWAS using robust multivariable Mendelian randomization. PLoS Genet. 2024 Apr 22;20(4):e1011246. doi: 10.1371/journal.pgen.1011246. PMID: 38648211; PMCID: PMC11065275.\nLink\nMalakhov MM, Dai B, Shen XT, Pan W. A bootstrap model comparison test for identifying genes with context-specific patterns of genetic regulation. Ann Appl Stat. 2024 Sep;18(3):1840-1857. doi: 10.1214/23-aoas1859. Epub 2024 Aug 5. PMID: 39421855; PMCID: PMC11484521.\nLink\nRen J, Pan W. Statistical inference with large-scale trait imputation. Stat Med. 2024 Feb 20;43(4):625-641. doi: 10.1002/sim.9975. Epub 2023 Dec 1. PMID: 38038193; PMCID: PMC10848238.\nLink\nChen L, Li C, Shen X, Pan W. Discovery and inference of a causal network with hidden confounding. J Am Stat Assoc. 2024;119(548):2572-2584. doi: 10.1080/01621459.2023.2261658. Epub 2023 Nov 17. PMID: 39980628; PMCID: PMC11841811.\nLink\nLi C, Shen X, Pan W. Nonlinear causal discovery with confounders. J Am Stat Assoc. 2024;119(546):1205-1214. doi: 10.1080/01621459.2023.2179490. Epub 2023 Mar 15. PMID: 39077372; PMCID: PMC11286219.\nLink\nOther research related:\nPrograms\n: Some computer programs used in\n     my papers.\nMy Google Scholar Citations\n.\nSearching\nPubMed. (But many \"Pan W\"'s are NOT me!)\nRecent talks:\nCCBR, U of Minnesota\nslides\n.\nA novel and efficient algorithm for de novo discovery of mutated driver pathways in cancer\nComputer Science, U of Minnesota\nslides\n.\nTwo-sample testing with high-dimensional genetic and neuroimaging data, \nUCI, UT Southwestern Medical Center,\nslides\n, \nUC-Irvine, UT Southwestern Medical Center, U Georgia,\n 2016.\nTesting for  group differences in brain functional connectivity,\nBanff\n, Feb 4, 2016.\nTesting for Genetic Association with Multiple Neuroimaging Traits\nImaging Genetics WG\n, Oct 3, 2014.\nA powerful and adaptive association test for rare variants.\nUNC\n, Sept 2014.\n JSM 2014, Boston,  August 2014. UW-Seattle, April 2014. UT-Houston, March 2014.\nDiscussion\n,\n ENAR Meeting, Baltimore, MD, March 19, 2014.\nA New Framework for Clustering Analysis.\n The Ninth ICSA International Conference\n, Hong Kong, Dec 2013;\nAustralian Statistical Conference/IMS Annual Meeting 2014, Sydney, July 2014.\nAdjusting for Population Stratification with Principal Components and Sequencing Data.\nJSM 2013\n, Montreal, Canada, August 2013.\n U Iowa Biostat Seminar, Sept 2013.\nMichigan State U Stat Seminar, Oct 2013.\nAn introduction to statistical tests in GWAS\n, SIBS, UofM, July 25, 2013;\n    July 22, 2015.\nNetwork-based penalized regression\n, departmental seminars at Duke, PSU, UW-Madison, NYU, UPenn, 2012-2013.\nIBC\n, August 27, 2012.\nStatistics\nseminar\n, Purdue U, Oct 28, 2011.\nIHI\nseminar\n, U of M, MN, Oct 6 2011.\nRenmin U, Biostatistics\nSymposium\n, Beijing, China, July 18, 2010.\nUM Biostatistics\nseminar\n, Minneapolis, MN, Dec 3 2008.\nUM Biostatistics\nseminar\n, Minneapolis, MN, Dec 5 2007.\nSH\n.\nCAMDA 2007\nkeynote\n, Valencia, Spain, Dec 13 2007.\nPSB 2008\ntalk\n, Big Island, Hawaii, Jan 7, 2008.\nSeminars at U of M:\nBiostatistics\nSeminar\nStatistics Genetics and Genomics\nSeminar\nBioinformatics\nSeminar\nHealth Informatics\nSeminar\nStatistics\nSeminar\nProfessional Activities:\nENAR\n(IBS)\n, member\nIMS\n, Fellow (2020-- )\nASA\n, Fellow (2010-- )\nICSA\nStatistics in Medicine\n, Editorial Board, Aug 2002--2006\nJASA, Associate Editor, Oct 2003--2006\nReferee for\nApplied Statistics\n,\nBiometrics\n,\nBiometrical J\n,\nBiostatistics\n,\nComm. in Statist.\n,\nComp. Statist. and\n     Data Analysis\n,\nJASA\n,\nJCGS\n,\nJRSS-B\n,\nLifetime Data Analysis\n,\nScandinavian Journal of Statistics\n,\nStatistics in Medicine\n,\nTechnometrics\nand\nAmerican Journal of Epidemiology\n,\nAmerican Journal of Public Health\n,\nBMC Bioinformatics\n,\nBioinformatics\n,\nNucleic Acids Res\n,\nNature\n,\nPharmacogenomics\n.\nJournals:\nStatistics and bioinformatics journals\nrelated to my research interests\nMedical journals\nPattern Recognition journals"
  },
