    "homepage_text": "James Liang's website\nJames C. Liang\nU.S. Naval Research Laboratory\nHome\nAbout Me\nResearch\nPublications\nJames C. Liang\nU.S. Naval Research Laboratory\nContact me with my work email if you know\nOtherwise jamesliang819 AT gmail DOT com\n[Update 05/2025]\nHome\nAbout Me\nResearch\nPublications\nServices\nAbout Me\nAt present, I'm a computer scientist at the U.S. Naval Research Laboratory. Before that, I earned a Ph.D. in the Department of Computer Engineering at Rochester Institute of Technology in 2024. I am fortunate to be advised by\nDr. Dongfang Liu\nand\nDr. Michael Zuzak\n. I also received the degree of Bachelor of Science in Liberal Arts & Sciences, majoring in Mathematics and Statistics, from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC) in May 2021.\nI am continually seeking long-term collaborators from U.S. academic institutions, who share the same research interests and academic perspectives, especially for DOD proposals such as DARPA, ONR, etc.\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests include machine learning, artificial intelligence, and high-dimensional statistical estimation, ranging from applications to theory.\nComputer Vision:\nImage Classification, Object Detection, Image Segmentation, Single and Multiple Object Tracking\nRemote Sensing:\nFar Seas Geo-localization, Ship Re-identification\nSecurity:\nTrustworthy Machine Learning, Attack and Countermeasure for Perception System\nEmbodied AI:\nVisual Navigation, Multi-agent and Multi-objective Collaborations\nAI for Science:\nAI for Antenna, AI for Radar, AI for Electromagnetism, AI for Maritime Application\nRecent Publications\nSee\ngoogle scholar\nfor my recent publications. The views and conclusions contained in my publications are those of the authors and should not be interpreted as necessarily representing the official policies or endorsements, either expressed or implied, of U.S. Naval Research Laboratory (NRL) or the U.S. Government, unless specified.\nServices\nProgram Committee\n: AAAI\nReviewer\n: ICML, NeurIPS, ICLR, IROS, TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV\nThe template of this website is designed by\ntemplatemo\n."
  },
