  "deep_homepage::Zhuang Liu::https://liuzhuang13.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://liuzhuang13.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/liuzhuang13",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhuang-liu-19306b1b1/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhuang Liu\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nPrinceton University\nEmail:\n35 Olden St, Princeton, NJ 08540\nGoogle Scholar\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGitHub\nZhuang Liu\n[Pronouncing Zhuang]\nI'm an Assistant Professor of Computer Science at Princeton University.\n                    I received my Ph.D. from UC Berkeley, where I worked with Trevor Darrell,\n                    and my B.S. in Computer Science from Tsinghua University (Yao Class).\n                    Before joining Princeton, I was a Senior Research Scientist at Meta FAIR in New York, and I have also spent time at Cornell, Intel, and Adobe.\nI work on building models that see and understand the world, reason over long and multimodal context, and analyze complex inputs to solve challenging problems.\n                    My research spans deep learning and foundation models across vision, multimodal, and language. I value simplicity in the models, methods, and hypotheses that I explore.\nIn this spirit, some of my work has introduced simple, widely used designs in deep networks and efficient models (e.g.,\nDenseNet\n,\nConvNeXt\n,\nNetwork Slimming\n,\nRethinking Pruning\n,\nWanda\n).\n                  More recently, I have worked on multimodal and large language models, ranging from architectures (e.g.,\nDyT\n,\nMetaMorph\n) to mechanism and data analysis (e.g.,\nMassive Activations\n,\ndataset bias\n).\n                  My work has been recognized by 98,000 citations and a CVPR Best Paper Award.\nJoin Us\n[Show more]\nProspective Research Interns:\nI am always excited to collaborate with motivated students on long-term and dedicated research projects. Please get in touch via this\nform\n.\nProspective PhD students:\nI am looking for motivated students. Please apply to\nPrinceton's CS PhD program\nand mention my name.\nProspective Postdocs:\nPlease apply to the\nPLI Postdoctoral Fellow program\nand mention my name.\nResearch Group\n•\nXingyu Fu\n, PLI Postdoctoral Fellow\n•\nGabe Sarch\n, PLI Postdoctoral Fellow\n•\nHaozhe (Tony) Chen\n, PhD Student\n•\nSachin Konan\n, PhD Student\n•\nTaiming Lu\n, PhD Student\n•\nZhuorui Ye\n, PhD Student\n(w/\nDanqi Chen\n)\n•\nYida (David) Yin\n, PhD Student\n•\nBoya Zeng\n, PhD Student\n•\nLinrong (Chris) Cai\n, MSE Student\nTalks and News\nSelected Publications\n(* equal contribution, for full list please see\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nTeaching\nCOS 324: Introduction to Machine Learning, Princeton, Spring 2026\nCOS 597K: Frontiers in Deep Learning, Princeton, Fall 2025\nProfessional Services\nI served or will be serving as an Area Chair for NeurIPS (23, 24, D&B track 22, 24), ICLR (25), ICML (25), CVPR (25, 26), ICCV (23, 25).\nI also regularly served as a Reviewer for CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, and other conferences and journals."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Zhiqiu Xu::https://oscarxzq.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://oscarxzq.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "oscarxzq@seas.upenn.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/OscarXZQ",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/oscar-xu-1250821a1/",
    "homepage_text": "Zhiqiu Xu\nZhiqiu Xu  / Oscar /\nI am a Ph.D. student at University of Pennsylvania, advised by Prof.\nMayur Naik\n. I seek to understand how neural networks work and develop simple methods to improve how we train and use neural networks.\nI complete my Master of Science degree from\nUC Berkeley\n, advised by Prof.\nTrevor Darrell\n, \n                  where I work on computer vision and representation learning.\n\n                 Before that, I was an undergraduate student at UC Berkeley, majoring in Computer Science \n                 and Applied Mathematics. I also interned at\nTwitter\n.\nAlways open to research collaboration, mentoring, and exciting discussions! Feel free to reach out via email or connect with me on social media below.\nYou have my word that I will respond. (bots excluded, at least until they get nicer)\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nTwitter\n/\nGithub\n/\nWechat\n/\nLinkedin\nNews\n(2024/01/16) Our paper\nInitializing Models with Larger Ones\nis accepted to ICLR 2024 as a spotlight presentation! Happy birthday to me 🎂\n(2023/04/24) Our paper\nDropout Reduces Underfitting\nis accepted to ICML 2023!\n(2023/03/31) I will join University of Pennsylvania as a Ph.D. student in Fall 2023!\nResearch\n(* equal contribution)\nDelta Activations: A Representation for Finetuned Large Language Models\nZhiqiu Xu*\n,\nAmish Sethi*\n,\nMayur Naik\n,\nSer-Nam Lim\narXiv\n2025\n[paper]\n[code]\n[project page]\nGenerative Modeling of Weights: Generalization or Memorization?\nBoya Zeng\n,\nYida Yin\n,\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nZhuang Liu\narXiv\n2025\n[paper]\n[code]\n[project page]\nIdiosyncrasies in Large Language Models\nMingjie Sun*\n,\nYida Yin*\n,\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nJ. Zico Kolter\n,\nZhuang Liu\nICML\n2025\n[paper]\n[code]\nA Coefficient Makes SVRG Effective\nYida Yin\n,\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nZhiyuan Li\n,\nTrevor Darrell\n,\nZhuang Liu\nICLR\n2025\n[paper]\n[code]\nInitializing Models with Larger Ones\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nYanjie Chen\n,\nKirill Vishniakov\n,\nYida Yin\n,\nZhiqiang Shen\n,\nTrevor Darrell\n,\nLingjie Liu\n,\nZhuang Liu\nICLR\n2024\n(Spotlight)\n[paper]\n[code]\nDropout Reduces Underfitting\nZhuang Liu*\n,\nZhiqiu Xu*\n,\nJoseph Jin\n,\nZhiqiang Shen\n,\nTrevor Darrell\nICML\n2023\n[paper]\n[code]\nAnytime Dense Prediction with Confidence Adaptivity\nZhuang Liu\n,\nZhiqiu Xu\n,\nHung-ju Wang\n,\nTrevor Darrell\n,\nEvan Shelhamer\nICLR\n2022\n[paper]\n[code]\nMentorship\nI was closely mentored by\nZhuang Liu\nand\nRuiqi Zhong\nat UC Berkeley. They are primarily reasons why I dived into research. (a pleasant surprise since I wasn't planning for that)\nJust like every other field in human society, the flourishing academic community is reliant on passing the torch of knowledge. If you are interested in my research and deep learning related topics and want to chat with me, please don't hesitate to reach out. Here is a list of students I have mentored. One of them said I was a legendary mentor, and let's trust his judgement for this time.\nJoseph Jin\n(Databricks)\nMaolin Mao\nYanjie Chen\nBoya Zeng\n(now Ph.D. student at Princeton University)\nAmish Sethi\nAcademic Services\nReviewer for ICLR, ICML, NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, AAAI, AISTATS.\nMiscellaneous\nMy Chinese name is pronounced as Shoe-Jee-Chyo. I will be very happy if you try to pronounce that in front of me. My name is Xu Zhiqiu. ‘Xu’ (徐) is my family name and conveys a sense of calm or gentle movement. ‘Zhi’ (之) is a classical possessive, and ‘Qiu’ (秋) means autumn.\nI play poker. Statistically speaking, I have been quite lucky on that.\nOccasionally, I post some vlogs on bilibili. Here's my\nhomepage\n. I haven't done that for a while. But let me know if you want to see some by commenting.\nMy profile photo is shot in a studio, I never dress like that in real life.\nI proudly named myself as Oscar after watching\nShark Tale\nat 6 years old.\nWebsite design from\nJon Barron\nBorrowed from\nRuiqi Zhong"
  },
