    "homepage_text": "Xiangyu Liu's Homepage\nHi\nAbout Me\nI am a postdoc researcher at CISPA, hosted by\nDoreen Riepel\n. Previously, I was a postdoc at both Georgia Institute of Technology (GT) and Purdue University (2023-2025), hosted by\nVassilis Zikas\n. I received my doctoral degree from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2023, under the supervision of\nShengli Liu\n. Prior to that, I obtained my master's and bachelor's degrees from Sun Yat-Sen University in 2018 and 2016, respectively, under the supervision by\nFangguo Zhang\n.\nI am interested in cryptography and security in general. During my PhD my research mainly focuses on tight security. Currently I am working on advanced signature schemes, blockchain and MPC.\nLatest News\n(June 2025) Glad to join CISPA.\n(Apr. 2025) I write a\nblog\nfor my 40k hiking at Grand Canyon (during spring break).\n(Mar. 2025) I finished Spartan Beast Race (21k, 30 obstacles). See my blog\nhere\n.\n(Dec. 2024) Glad to join the PC of Africacrypt 2025. Thanks for inviting me!\n(Nov. 2024) Congratulations! I regained the skill of backflip (后空翻) and had a breakthrough on frontflip (前空翻). See\nbackflip\nand\nfrontflip\nfor the videos ^o^.\n(Sept. 2024) Congratulations! I got the skill of side flip with a twist (侧空翻转体). See\nhere\nfor the video ^o^.\n(Sept. 2024) Glad to join the PC of FC 2025 and PKC 2025. Thanks for inviting me!\n(Aug. 2024) I am very glad to join Georgia Institute of Technology as a postdoc researcher, and start my new life in Atlanta (and also Purdue in West Lafayette :D).\n(Aug. 2024) I created a\nlog\nto record my exercise. Inspired by the Paris Olympics 2024, I hope this log will help me stay youthful, energetic, passionful, and always hold a hope to the life. Faster, higher, stronger.\n\nKeep up the good work, and may your journal inspire you to reach new heights!\n(Dec. 2023) I added a part of google map (see below) to record my footprints over the world.\n(Nov. 2023) I won the 2023 Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award of Chinese Association for Cryptologic Research (CACR).\n(Sept. 2023) Congratulations! I have re-unlocked Muscle Ups (双力臂) since 2018. See\nhere\nfor the video ^o^.\nPreprints\nTraceable Ring Signatures Revisited: Extended Definitions, O(1) Tracing, and Efficient Log-Size Constructions\nXiangyu Liu\n[ePrint]\nDeniable Symmetric Signcryption (anonymized title)\nWonseok Choi, Daniel Collins, Joseph Jaeger, Akshaya Kumar,\nXiangyu Liu\n, Vassilis Zikas\n[to appear]\nA Unified Treatment of Anamorphic Encryption\nWonseok Choi, Daniel Collins,\nXiangyu Liu\n, Vassilis Zikas\n[ePrint]\nK-Linkable Ring Signatures and Applications in Generalized Voting\nWonseok Choi,\nXiangyu Liu\n, Lirong Xia, Vassilis Zikas\n[ePrint]\nCVICA: Coordinated Vehicle Infrastructure Cryptography Architecture with Fine-Grained Access Control\nShiqi Ou,\nXiangyu Liu\n[here]\nNote:\nThe technical novelty in this paper is negligible—particularly in cryptography, and it is not intended for publication. Rather, it serves as a personal memento of the authors' Ph.D. journey and a witness for Hoco.\nPublications\nAnonymous Authentication and Key Agreement, Revisited\nYanqi Zhao,\nXiangyu Liu\n,  Min Xie,  Xiaoyi Yang, Jianting Ning, Baodong Qin, Haibin Zhang, Yong Yu\nACSAC 2025\n[ePrint]\nBlockchain Governance via Sharp Anonymous Multisignatures\nWonseok Choi,\nXiangyu Liu\n, Vassilis Zikas\nAFT 2025\n[conference version]\n[ePrint]\n[slides]\nUniversal Adaptor Signatures from Blackbox Multi-Party Computation\nMichele Ciampi,\nXiangyu Liu\n, Ioannis Tzannetos, Vassilis Zikas\nCT-RSA 2025\n[conference version]\n[ePrint]\n[slides]\nAdaptor Signatures: New Security Definition and A Generic Construction for NP Relations\nXiangyu Liu\n, Ioannis Tzannetos, Vassilis Zikas\nASIACRYPT 2024\n[conference version]\n[ePrint]\n[slides]\nFine-grained Verifier NIZK and Its Applications\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Shuai Han, Dawu Gu\nPKC 2023\n[conference version]\n[eprint]\n[slides]\nEKE Meets Tight Security in the Universally Composable Framework\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Shuai Han, Dawu Gu\nPKC 2023\n[conference version]\n[eprint]\n[slides]\nTightly CCA-Secure Inner Product Functional Encryption Scheme\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Dawu Gu\nTheoretical Computer Science 2022\n[journal version]\nTwo-Pass Authenticated Key Exchange with Explicit Authentication and Tight Security\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Dawu Gu, Jian Weng\nASIACRYPT 2020\n[conference version]\n[eprint]\n[slides]\nTightly Secure Chameleon Hash Functions in the Multi-User Setting and Their Applications\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Dawu Gu\nACISP 2020\n[conference version]\n[eprint]\n[slides]\nTightly Secure Identity-Based Signature Scheme\nXiangyu Liu\n, Shengli Liu, Dawu Gu\nJournal of Cryptologic Research, 2021\nA Dynamic Searchable Encryption Scheme on Cloud Storage with Multi-level Access\nXiangyu Liu\n, Huige Li, Fangguo Zhang\nJournal of Cryptologic Research, 2019\nAdademic Service\nProgram Committee Member:\nPKC 2025/2027; FC 2025; Africacrypt 2025/2026.\nConference External Reviewer:\nCRYPTO 2024-2026, EUROCRYPT 2022/2023/2026, ASIACRYPT 2022-2024, PKC 2022/2025, ISC 2024, APKC 2021/2022, ICDCS 2022, Inscrypt 2021, ProvSec 2021, ACISP 2020, ProvSec 2020.\nJournal External Reviewer:\nJournal of Cryptology (JoC), Transactions on Dependable and Secure Computing (TDSC), The Computer Journal, Internet of Things (IoT), Computer Standards & Interfaces (CSI), Transactions on Privacy and Security (TOPS).\nHobbies and Interests\nI am interested in all kinds of sports like wushu (martial arts), judo, free running, gymnastics, climbing, hiking, badminton, table tennis, etc. One of my dreams is,\nto perform a flip (空翻) when I am 80 years old\n.\nSometimes I play the flute, though I am musically challenged to be honest. Hope you never have to suffer through my singing.\nI am thinking about to upload my sport videos into Bilibili/Youtube? Hope you will see them very soon...\nMy Footprints\nI enjoy adventure and have a dream of traveling around the world. I hope to keep walking and continuously explore this vast world. I record my footprints\nhere\n.\nPS:\nYahoo is my English name. As for why I chose this name, it was probably just an inspiration during my first English class in Hefei No.1 High School in 2009. Hope I won't be a real \"Yahoo\" ------ irrational, filthy, and savage beings ------ as depicted in Gulliver's Travels.\nLast updated: Feb 2026\nXiangyu Liu\n刘 翔宇 (Yahoo)\nCISPA\nHelmholtz Center for Information Security\nEmail:\nxiangyu1994liu@gmail.com\nxiangyu.liu@cispa.de\nxliu3028@gatech.edu\n(expired)\nliu3894@purdue.edu\n(expired)\nxiangyu_liu@sjtu.edu.cn\n(expired)\nliuxy55@mail2.sysu.edu.cn\n(expired)"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Xin Zhang::https://xinpl.github.io/": {
