    "homepage_text": "Jianyu Zhang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJianyu Zhang\nJianyu Zhang\nWelcome to Jianyu's home page\nGithub\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nemail\nWelcome\nI am a\nResearch Scientist at Meta FAIR Lab. I got my\nP\nh.\nD.\nfrom\nNYU\nData Science\nadvised by\nLeon Bottou\nand\nYann Le\nC\nun\n. I have broad research interests in machine learning, representation learning and out-of-distribution generalization. Recently, I am interested in\nthe learning principles to build AI for the open-world\n.\nAI for the open-world aims at solving any task that a human could possibly undertake. That is, a\nwide range\nof tasks with\nfewer examples\nand\nless priori knowledge\nfrom human designers. I explores three such learning principles, inluding\nrich features\n,\ndisentangled representation\n, and\ninference-time learning\nto support each of the three requirements above.\nEducation\nPh.D., Data Science, New York University,\nSep. 2020 -\nAug. 2025\nM.S.,\nComputer Science, Tianjin University, Sep. 2016 - Jan. 2019\nB.S.,\nComputer Science, Tianjin University, Sep. 2012 - July. 2016\nExperiences\nResearch Scientist, Meta FAIR Lab, Aug 2025 - present\nVisiting Researcher\n, Meta FAIR Lab,\nSep\n2023 -\nAug 2025\nResearch Scientist Intern, Meta FAIR Lab, May 2023 - Aug 2023\nResearch Intern (AI),\nMeta FAIR\nLab\n, May 2022 - Oct 2022\nResearch Intern, Facebook\nFAIR lab\n, April 2019 - Aug 2019\nResearch Assistant, Sorbonne University, Jan 2019 - Mar 2019\nResearch Intern, Laboratories Hubert Curien, Sep 2017 - Oct 2017\nNews\nAI for the open world: the learning principles\nLearn the principles behind\nOpen-World AI\n(Turing’s vision) and see how they are validated at scale.\nFeb. 23, 2026\nOral talk @NeurIPS 2025\nOur work (with Léon Bottou),\nMemory Mosaics at scale\n[\npaper\n],\nwas presented in NeurIPS 2025 as an Oral talk\n(top 0.36%)\n.\nDec. 5, 2025\nPhd Defense 🎉 🎉 🎉\nThanks Léon Bottou, Yann Lecun, Kyunghyun Cho, Joan Bruna, Alfredo Canziani.\nApril 11, 2025\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
