    "homepage_text": "Dr. Minlie Huang's Homepage\nMinlie Huang(黄民烈)\nFull Professor\r\nDepartment of Computer Science,\r\nInstitute for Artificial Intelligence,\r\nTsinghua University\nDBLP\nGoogle Scholar\nEmail\nai{my_last_name}@tsinghua.edu.cn\nPhone\n+86 - 10 - 62777699\nOffice\nRoom 4-504, FIT Building\nAddress\nDept. of Computer Science,\r\nTsinghua University,\r\nBeijing 100084, China\nAbout\nPublications\nHonors & Rewards\nServices\nCourses\nTalks\nRecruitment\nAbout Me\nMy general interests include artificial intelligence, deep learning, and natural language processing. I am particularly interested in the following fields:\nNatural language generation theories, models & evaluation\nFundamental problems in large language models and multi-modal foundation models\nAI alignment, safety and ethics\nSocial intelligence with large language models (emotion, theory-of-mind, mental health applications)\nI am leading a research group named\nConversational AI\n(CoAI,\nGitHub link\n). This group published more than 100 papers on ACL, ICLR, ICML, Neurips conferences, and has won many paper awards including COLING 2010 best paper, ACL 2012 best student paper, IJCAI 2018 distinguished paper, SIGDIAL 2020 best paper, NLPCC 2015/2020 best paper, ACL 2023/2024 area chair award, etc. We have also highly cited works including\nemotional chatting machine\n(AAAI 2018),\nESC\n(ACL 2021),\nPPT\n(ACL 2022),\nMiniLLM\n(ICLR 2024),\nChatGLM\n(2024, with Prof. Jie Tang), etc.\nA full version of group introduction can be seen\nhere\n.\nWe also welcome talented undergraduates and interns to join us for doing interesting and amazing research. I also supervised and led many undergraduates to do research. Here are my thoughts on\nhow undergraduates can make successful research\n.\nResources\nLearning to Ask Questions in Open-domain Conversational Systems with Typed Decoders\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: yz06)\nAssigning Personality/Profile to a Chatting Machine for Coherent Conversation Generation\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: 0ls2)\nCommonsense Knowledge Aware Conversation Generation with Graph Attention\n(\ndata link\n)\nGenerating Informative Responses with Controlled Sentence Function\n(\ndata link\n, extraction code: hzo0)\nEmotional Chatting Machine\n(\ndata link\n, including emotion classifier and the emotional STC dataset)\nConvLab-3: A Flexible Dialogue System Toolkit Based on a Unified Data Format\n(\nGithub link\n)\nCritiqueLLM: Towards an Informative Critique Generation Model for Evaluation of Large Language Model Generatio\nn\n(\nGithub link\n)\nShieldLM: Empowering LLMs as Aligned, Customizable and Explainable Safety Detectors\n(\nGithub link\n)\nMiniPLM: Knowledge Distillation for Pre-Training Language Models\n(\nGithub link\n)\nCharacterGLM: Customizing Chinese Conversational AI Characters with Large Language Models\n(\nGithub link\n)\nAISafetyLab: A Comprehensive Framework for AI Safety Evaluation and Improvement\n(\nGithub link\n)\nSelected Publications\nSelect category\nCategory\nAll\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n2018\nbefore\nJinfeng Zhou, Yongkang Huang, Bosi Wen, Guanqun Bi, Yuxuan Chen, Pei Ke, Zhuang Chen, Xiyao Xiao, Libiao Peng, Kuntian Tang, Rongsheng Zhang, Le Zhang, Tangjie Lv, Zhipeng Hu, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nCharacterBench: Benchmarking Character Customization of Large Language Models\n.\nAAAI 2025\nZhuang Chen*, Yaru Cao*, Guanqun Bi, Jincenzi Wu, Jinfeng Zhou, Xiyao Xiao, Si Chen, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSocialSim: Towards Socialized Simulation of Emotional Support Conversation\n.\nAAAI 2025\nJiale Cheng, Xiao Liu, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Yida Lu, Dan Zhang, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSPaR: Self-Play with Tree-Search Refinement to Improve Instruction-Following in Large Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nJiaxin Wen, Ruiqi Zhong, Akbir Khan, Ethan Perez, Jacob Steinhardt, Minlie Huang, Samuel R. Bowman, He He, Shi Feng\nLanguage Models Learn to Mislead Humans via RLHF\n.\nICLR 2025\nJiaxin Wen*, Jian Guan*, Hongning Wang, Wei Wu, Minlie Huang\nUnlocking Reasoning Potential in Large Language Models by Scaling Code-form Planning\n.\nICLR 2025\nYuxian Gu, Li Dong, Hongning Wang, Yaru Hao, Qingxiu Dong, Furu Wei, Minlie Huang\nData Selection via Optional Training for Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nYuxian Gu, Hao Zhou, Fandong Meng, Minlie Huang\nMiniPLM: Knowledge Distillation for Pre-Training Language Models\n.\nICLR 2025\nErle Zhu, Yadi Liu, Zhe Zhang, Xujun Li, JinZhou, Xinjie Yu, Minlie Huang, Hongning Wang\nMAPS: Advancing Multi-Modal Reasoning in Expert-Level Physical Science\n.\nICLR 2025\nZhihua Wen, Zhizhao Liu, Zhiliang Tian, Shilong Pan, Zhen Huang, Dongsheng Li, Minlie Huang（ with Assoc. Prof. Zhiliang Tian）\nScenario-independent Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Question Answering via Factor Analysis\n.\nWWW 2025\nMinlie Huang, Yingkang Wang, Shiyao Cui, Pei Ke, Jie Tang\nThe Superalignment of Superhuman Intelligence with Large Language Models\n.\nSCIENCE CHINA  Information Sciences\nChujie Zheng, Ziqi Wang, Heng Ji, Minlie Huang, Nanyun Peng\nModel Extrapolation Expedites Alignment\n.\nACL 2025\nJunxiao Yang, Zhexin Zhang, Shiyao Cui, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nGuiding not Forcing: Enhancing the Transferability of Jailbreaking Attacks on LLMs via Removing Superfluous Constraints\n.\nACL 2025\nYida Lu, Jiale Cheng, Zhexin Zhang, Shiyao Cui, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nLongSafety: Evaluating Long-Context Safety of Large Language Models\n.\nACL 2025\nJinfeng Zhou, Yuxuan Chen, Yihan Shi, Xuanming Zhang, Leqi Lei, Yi Feng, Zexuan Xiong, Miao Yan, Xunzhi Wang, Yaru Cao, Jianing Yin, Shuai Wang, Quanyu Dai, Zhenhua Dong, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nSocialEval: Evaluating Social Intelligence of Large Language Models\n.\nACL 2025\nBosi Wen, Pei Ke, Yufei Sun, Cunxiang Wang, Xiaotao Gu, Jinfeng Zhou, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nHPSS: Heuristic Prompting Strategy Search for LLM Evaluator\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nTianshu Yu, Chao Xiang, mingchuan yang, Pei Ke, Bosi Wen, Cunxiang Wang, Jiale Cheng, Li Zhang, Xinyu Mu, Chuxiong Sun, Minlie Huang\nTraining Language Model to Critique for Better Refinement\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nGuanqun Bi, Zhuang Chen, Zhoufu Liu, Hongkai Wang, Xiyao Xiao, Yuqiang Xie, Wen Zhang, Yongkang Huang, Yuxuan Chen, Libiao Peng, Minlie Huang\nMAGI: Multi-Agent Guided Interview for Psychiatric Assessment\n.\nFindings of ACL 2025\nJiale Cheng, Ruiliang Lyu, Xiaotao Gu, Xiao Liu, Jiazheng Xu, Yida Lu, Jiayan Teng, Zhuoyi Yang, Yuxiao Dong, Jie Tang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nVPO: Aligning Text-to-Video Generation Models with Prompt Optimization\n.\nICCV 2025\nRenmiao Chen, Shiyao Cui, Xuancheng Huang, Chengwei Pan, Xijie Huang, Qinglin Zhang, Xuan Ouyang, Zhexin Zhang, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nJPS: Jailbreak Multimodal Large Language Models with Collaborative Visual Perturbation and Textual Steering\n.\nACM Multimedia 2025\nShiyao Cui*, Qinglin Zhang*, Xuan Ouyang, Renmiao Chen, Zhexin Zhang, Yida Lu, Hongning Wang, Han Qiu, Minlie Huang\nShieldVLM: Safeguarding the Multimodal lmplicit Toxicity via Deliberative Reasoning with LVLMs\n.\nACM Multimedia 2025\nJinfeng Zhou, Yuxuan Chen, Jianing Yin, Yongkang Huang, Yihan Shi, Xikun Zhang, Libiao Peng, Rongsheng Zhang, Tangjie Lv, Zhipeng Hu, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nCrisp: Cognitive Restructuring of Negative Thoughts through Multi-turn Supportive Dialogues\n.\nEMNLP 2025\nChujie Zheng, Hao Zhou, Fandong Meng, Jie Zhou, Minlie Huang\nLarge Language Models Are Not Robust Multiple Choice Selectors\n.\nICLR 2024（Spotlight）\nYuxian Gu, Li Dong, Furu Wei, Minlie Huang\nMiniLLM: Knowledge Distillation of Large Language Models\n.\nICLR 2024\nHaozhe Ji, Pei Ke, Hongning Wang, Minlie Huang\nLanguage Model Decoding as Direct Metrics Optimization\n.\nICLR 2024\nZhibin Gou*, Zhihong Shao*, Yeyun Gong, yelong shen, Yujiu Yang, Minlie Huang, Nan Duan, We