    "homepage_text": "Shu Yang - Professor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nShu Yang – Professor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nShu Yang\nProfessor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nAbout Me\nBackground:\nShu Yang graduated from\nIowa State University\nin 2014 with major in\nMathematics\nand comajor in\nStatistics\nworking with\nJ.K. Kim\nand\nZ. Zhu\n. After graduation, she joined\nHarvard TH Chan School of Public Health\nas a post-doc with\nJudith Lok\n. She then joined\nNC State\nas a faculty member since 2016. She was promoted to Associate Professor in 2021 and became a\nGoodnight Early Career Innovator\nand a\nUniversity Faculty Scholar\nin the same year.\nResearch interests\n:\n⋆ Survey sampling and methodology\n⋆ Missing data analysis and imputation methods\n⋆ Causal inference from longitudinal observational data\n⋆ Semiparametric efficient estimation\n⋆ Spatial data analysis, nonstationary process and spectral methods\n⋆ Individual treatment regime learning, data integration and fusion methods\nEmployment\n:\nNorth Carolina State University\nProfessor\n2025–present\nAssociate professor\n2021–2025\nAssistant professor\n2016–2021\nHarvard University\nPostdoctoral Fellow in Biostatistics\n2014–2016\nEditorial Services (Associate Editor)\n:\nASA Discoveries\n2025–present\nASA Statistics in Biopharmaceutical Research\n2026–present\nASA Statistics in Biopharmaceutical Research (SI)\n2025–2026\nASA Journal of American Statistics Association A&CS\n2024–present\nJournal of the Royal Statistical Society Series A\n2023–2027\nASA Journal of Computational and Graphical Statistics\n2021–present\nBiometrics\n2018–2026\nASA Journal of Agricultural Biological and Environmental Statistics\nSpecial Issue on Causal Inference\n2021–2023\nStatistica Sinica\n2016–2018\nCurriculum Vitae\n:\nCV\n.\nContact\n:\n⋆ Office: SAS Hall 4266\n⋆ Phone: 919-515-1935\n⋆ Email:\nsyang24@ncsu.edu\n⋆ Linkedin:\nShu Yang\nFollow @ShuYangStatNCSU on Twitter\nRecent Posts\nHonored and Grateful: Receiving the Cavell Brownie Mentoring Faculty Award!\n04/23/2024\nHonored and Grateful: Receiving the COPSS Emerging Leader Award!\n03/30/2024\nOur recent PNAS paper: Using Stats to Protect Oceans\n03/04/2024\nExcited to receive FDA Grant for Clinical Trials Enhancement\n09/25/2023\nCongratulations to Siyi Liu – ASA BIOP RISW Student Travel Grant Award\n08/02/2023\nHonored and Grateful: Receiving the NSF SES Award!\n07/31/2023\nShu Yang received a “Thank an Advisor” – A Student Wants to Say Thank You!\n05/12/2023\nYichi Zhang received 2023 JSM Student Paper Award from the ASA Section on Nonparametric Statistics.\n05/12/2023\nShort course “Design and analysis of RCTs with RWD” at Upcoming Conferences\n02/24/2023\nShu Yang receives the 2023 NCSU RISF Climate Change Award.\n12/09/2022\n\n---\n\nShu Yang - Professor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nShu Yang – Professor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nShu Yang\nProfessor of Statistics (University Faculty Scholar)\nAbout Me\nBackground:\nShu Yang graduated from\nIowa State University\nin 2014 with major in\nMathematics\nand comajor in\nStatistics\nworking with\nJ.K. Kim\nand\nZ. Zhu\n. After graduation, she joined\nHarvard TH Chan School of Public Health\nas a post-doc with\nJudith Lok\n. She then joined\nNC State\nas a faculty member since 2016. She was promoted to Associate Professor in 2021 and became a\nGoodnight Early Career Innovator\nand a\nUniversity Faculty Scholar\nin the same year.\nResearch interests\n:\n⋆ Survey sampling and methodology\n⋆ Missing data analysis and imputation methods\n⋆ Causal inference from longitudinal observational data\n⋆ Semiparametric efficient estimation\n⋆ Spatial data analysis, nonstationary process and spectral methods\n⋆ Individual treatment regime learning, data integration and fusion methods\nEmployment\n:\nNorth Carolina State University\nProfessor\n2025–present\nAssociate professor\n2021–2025\nAssistant professor\n2016–2021\