    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chuan Wu: Home\nNavigation\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nBio & CV\nOur Team\nProfessor\nBEng, MEng (Tsinghua); PhD (Toronto)\nIEEE Fellow\nACM Distinguished Member\nDepartment of Computer Science\nThe University of Hong Kong\nI am a Professor in the Department of Computer Science,\nSchool of Computing and Data Science\n, at The University of Hong Kong. I received my Ph.D. degree from the Department of\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nin the\nUniversity of Toronto\n, Canada, and both my M.Engr. and B.Engr. degrees from the Department of\nComputer Science and Technology\nin\nTsinghua University\n, China.\nResearch Interest\nMy current research interests span cloud computing, distributed machine learning systems, distributed learning algorithms, and intelligent technologies for elderly care. My research features performance modeling and algorithm design for various network systems using optimization and machine learning methods, as well as the design and implementation of various systems based on relevant methods. Please see my\nresearch projects\nand\npublications\nfor more details.\nContact\nEmail\n: cwu@cs.hku.hk\nPhone\n: (852) 2857 8459\nFax\n: (852) 2559 8447\nOffice\n: Room 427, Chow Yei Ching Building\nMailing address\n:\nDepartment of Computer Science\nThe University of Hong Kong\nPokfulam Road\nHong Kong\nNews\n**\nI am looking for self-organized, well-motivated PhD students, postdoc researchers and RAs (anytime) to work on a variety of topics in distributed machine learning algorithms and systems, and AI agent systems. Candidates with solid background and/or strong interest in mathematical modeling/analysis, and candidates with solid programming skills and/or strong interest in building systems and innovation/entrepreneurship are all very welcome. Please contact me by email with your CV (please include your GPA and rank).\n**\n[December 30, 2025]\nI received HKU's Outstanding Researcher Award for 2024-2025 😃\n[December 8, 2025]\nBorui's paper \"BROS:Efficient LLM Serving on Hybrid Real-time and Best-effort Requests\" is accepted to INFOCOM 2026. Congratulations!\n[September 27, 2025]\nShiwei's paper \"DyOrc: Efficient Serving of Dynamic Machine Learning Workflows\" is accepted to ACM SOCC 2025. Congratulations!\n[September 19, 2025]\nSheng and Jingqi's paper \"TreeSynth: Synthesizing Diverse Data from Scratch via Tree-Guided Subspace Partitioning\" is accepted to NeurIPS 2025 as a spotlight. Congratulations!\n[August 21, 2025]\nThree papers from our group are accepted to EMNLP 2025. Congratulations!\n[July 12, 2025]\nTwo papers first-authored by Chenyu and Borui, respectively, are accepted to SOSP 2025. Congratulations!\n[May 1, 2025]\nJunwei's two papers are accepted to ICML 2025. Congratulations!\n[March 27, 2025]\nGuicheng's first paper \"ECCheck: Enhancing In-Memory Checkpoint with Erasure Coding in Distributed DNN Training\" is accepted to IEEE ICDCS 2025. Congratulations!\n[January 13, 2025]\nSheng's paper \"MoS: Unleashing Parameter Efficiency of Low-Rank Adaptation with Mixture of Shards\" is accepted to ICLR 2025. Congratulations!\n[December 12, 2024]\nBorui's paper \"A Unified Checkpointing System for Large Foundation Model Development\" is accepted to NSDI 2025. Congratulations!\n[December 6, 2024]\nMengfan's paper \"Optimizing Distributed Deployment of Mixture-of-Experts Model Inference in Serverless Computing\" is accepted to INFOCOM 2025. Congratulations!\n[September 26, 2024]\nXiaoyang's paper \"FaPES: Enabling Efficient Elastic Scaling for Serverless Machine Learning Platforms\" is accepted to ACM SOCC 2024. Congratulations!\n[August 21, 2024]\nGuangming's paper \"HybridFlow: A Flexible and Efficient RLHF Framework\" is accepted to EuroSys 2025. Congratulations!\n[May 16, 2024]\nSheng's two papers are accepted to ACL 2024. Congratulations!\n[Apr 13, 2024]\nXiaoyang's paper \"AdapCC: Making Collective Com- munication in Distributed Machine Learning Adaptive\" is accepted to IEEE ICDCS 2024. Congratulations!\n[Feb 24, 2024]\nTwo papers from our group are accepted to MLSys 2024!\n[Jan 16, 2023]\nJunwei's paper \"PRES: Toward Scalable Memory-Based Dynamic Graph Neural Networks\" has been accepted to ICLR 2024. Congratulations!\n[Sep 12, 2023]\nThree papers from our group are accepted to EuroSys 2024!\n[April 25, 2023]\nJunwei's paper \"Towards Robust Graph Incremental Learning on Evolving Graphs\" has been accepted to ICML 2023. Congratulations!\n[February 18, 2023]\nBorui and Juntao's paper \"Adaptive Message Quantization and Parallelization for Distributed Full-graph GNN Training\" has been accepted to MLSys 2023. Congratulations!\n[December 2, 2022]\nZhe and Ziyue's paper \"Two-level Graph Caching for Expediting Distributed GNN Training\" has been accepted to IEEE INFOCOM 2023. Congratulations!\n[October, 2022]\nZiyue Luo has graduated with Ph.D. and joined Ohio State University as a postdoc researcher. Congratulations!\n[Sep 15, 2022]\nYangrui's paper \"SAPipe: Staleness-Aware Pipeline for Data Parallel DNN Training\" has been accepted to NeurIPS 2022. Congratulations!\n[Sep 6, 2022]\nShiwei's paper \"Accelerating Large-Scale Distributed Neural Network Training with SPMD Parallelism\" has been accepted to ACM SOCC 2022. Congratulations!\n[September, 2022]\nBingqian Du has graduated with Ph.D. and joined Huazhong University of Science and Technology as an assistant professor. Congratulations!\n[Jul 9, 2022]\nYangrui's paper \"BGL: GPU-Efficient GNN Training by Optimizing Graph Data I/O and Preprocessing\" (co-first-authored with Tsinghua collaborator) has been accepted to USENIX NSDI 2023. Congratulations!\n[Jan 15, 2022]\nHanpeng, Yuchen and Chenyu's paper \"A Generic Performance Diagnosis and Optimization Toolkit for Expediting Distributed DNN Training\" has been accepted to MLSys 2022. Congratulations!\n[December 4, 2021]\nZiyue's two papers have been accepted to IEEE INFOCOM 2022. Congratulations!\n[August, 2021]\nXiaodong Yi has graduated with Ph.D. and joined Tencent in Shenzhen as an AI technology researcher. Congratulations!\n[March 25, 2021]\nI received an\nAmazon Research Award\nfor carrying out research on compilation optimization in distributed DNN training 😃\n[December 5, 2020]\nZhe's first paper \"Near-Optimal Topology-adaptive Parameter Synchronization in Distributed DNN Training\" has been accepted to IEEE INFOCOM 2021. Congratulations!\n[November 16, 2020]\nYixin Bao has graduated with Ph.D. and joined Facebook at Seattle, U.S., as a research scientist. Congratulations!\n[October 28, 2020]\nXiaodong, Shiwei and Ziyue's paper \"Optimizing Distributed Training Deployment in Heterogeneous GPU Clusters\" has been accepted to ACM CoNEXT 2020. Congratulations!\n[August 28, 2020]\nXiaodong and Ziyue's paper \"Fast Training of Deep Learning Models over Multiple GPUs\" has been accepted to ACM/IFIP Middleware 2020. Congratulations!\n[August 9, 2020]\nYangrui, Yanghua and Yixin's paper \"Elastic Parameter Server Load Distribution in Deep Learning Clusters\" has been accepted to ACM SOCC'20. Congratulations!\n© 2007-2026 Chuan Wu. Last updated January 2026.\n\n---\n\nChuan Wu: Bio & CV\nNavigation\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nBio & CV\nOur Team\nA Short Biography\nChuan Wu received her B.Engr. and M.Engr. degrees in 2000 and 2002 from the Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, China, and her Ph.D. degree in 2008 from the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Toronto, Canada. Between 2002 and 2004, She worked in the Information Technology industry in Singapore. Since September 2008, Chuan Wu has been with the Department of Computer Science at the University of Hong Kong, where she is currently a Professor. Her current research is in the areas of distributed machine learning systems and algorithms, and intelligent elderly care technologies. She is a Fellow of IEEE, a Distinguished Member of ACM, and an AAIA Fellow. She served as the Chair of the Interest Group on Multimedia services and applications over Emerging Networks (MEN) of the IEEE Multimedia Communication Technical Committee (MMTC) from 2012 to 2014. She is an associate editor of ACM/IEEE Transactions on Networking. She was the co-recipient of the best paper awards of HotPOST 2012, ACM e-Energy 2016, and MSN 2024. She received an Amazon Research Award on AWS AI in 2021.\nCurriculum Vitae\nMy\nCurriculum Vitae\nin Adobe PDF format, as of January 2026.\n© 2007-2026 Chuan Wu. Last updated January 2026.\n\n---\n\nChuan Wu: Bio & CV\nNavigation\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nBio & CV\nOur Team\nA Short Biography\nChuan Wu received her B.Engr. and M.Engr. degrees in 2000 and 2002 from the Department of Computer Science and Technology, Tsinghua University, China, and her Ph.D. degree in 2008 from the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Toronto, Canada. Between 2002 and 2004, She worked in the Information Technology industry in Singapore. Since September 2008, Chuan Wu has been with the Department of Computer Science at the University of Hong Kong, where she is currently a Professor. Her current research is in the areas of distributed machine learning systems and algorithms, and intelligent elderly care technologies. She is a Fellow of IEEE, a Distinguished Member of ACM, and an AAIA Fellow. She served as the Chair of the Interest Group on Multimedia services and applications over Emerging Networks (MEN) of the IEEE Multimedia Communication Technical Committee (MMTC) from 2012 to 2014. She is an associate editor of ACM/IEEE Transactions on Networking. She was the co-recipient of the best paper awards of HotPOST 2012, ACM e-Energy 2016, and MSN 2024. She received an Amazon Research Award on AWS AI in 2021.\nCurriculum Vitae\nMy\nCurriculum Vitae\nin Adobe PDF format, as of January 2026.\n© 2007-2026 Chuan Wu. Last updated January 2026."
  },
