    "homepage_text": "Chen Huang\nSearch\nChen Huang\nDeep Learning Research Engineer\nApple\nAbout me\nChen Huang is a deep learning research engineer at\nApple\n, working on Generative AI with a focus on video/3D. His research focuses on advancing the field of 3D generative AI and developing capabilities at the intersection of vision and language through multimodal large language models. Most recently, he lead a team of scientists and engineers on developing diffusion model for mobile products. Some of the products he has worked on including Apple’s first\nFace ID\non iPhone X and\nObject Capture\non both MacOS and iOS.\nDownload my CV\nEducation\nPhD in Electrical and Computer Science\nUniversity of Missouri\nBachelor in Electrical Engineering\nBeihang University\nInterests\nGenerative AI for Video & 3D\nMultimodal LLM\n3D Scene Understanding\nOn-device Machine Learning\nRecent Publications\nCavia: Camera-controllable Multi-view Video Diffusion with View-Integrated Attention\nDejia Xu\n,\nYifan Jiang\n,\nChen Huang\n,\nLiangchen Song\n,\nThorsten Gernoth\n,\nLiangliang Cao\n,\nZhangyang Wang\n,\nHao Tang\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning 2025\n(ICML 2025)\npaper\nproject\nProjects\nObject Capture\nPhotogrammetry API that enables developers to create 3D models from a series of 2D images on macOS and iOS.\nDocumentation\nWWDC 2023\nWWDC 2024\nWorking Experience\nDeep Learning Research Engineer\nApple\nSep 2017 –\nPresent\nCuppertino, California\nDeep Learning Research Engineer @\nVideo Engineering\n, working on multimodal LLM and generative AI with a focus on video and 3D content generation.\nResearch Intern, Computer Vision\nMicrosoft Research\nMar 2017 –\nSep 2017\nRedmond, Washington\nResearch Intern @\nApplied Science Group\n, mentored by\nPablo Sala\n, and\nVivek Pradeep\n, worked on applying deep learning techniques on new sensing modalities for pedestrian detection, visual tracking and activity recognition\nResearch Intern, Deep Learning\nApple\nMay 2016 –\nSep 2016\nCuppertino, California\nResearch Intern @\nApple Machine Learning Research\nteam, mentored by\nJoshua M Susskind\n, conducting research on compressing convolutional neural networks for confidential projects.\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
  },
