    "homepage_text": "Wen Shen\n      -  Penn State\nPenn State  Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at Penn State\nContact Expert\nView Scopus Profile\nWen Shen\nProfessor\n,\nMathematics\nCenter for Computational Mathematics and Applications (CCMA)\nCenter for Interdisciplinary Mathematics\nh-index\n594\nCitations\n15\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n1996                 …\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 14\nLife Below Water\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Wen Shen is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n4\nSimilar Profiles\nConservation Law\nMathematics\n100%\nTraffic Flow\nKeyphrases\n33%\nInitial Datum\nMathematics\n28%\nGranular Flow\nMathematics\n27%\nCauchy Problem\nKeyphrases\n26%\nApproximate Solution\nMathematics\n25%\nConservation Laws\nKeyphrases\n24%\nDifferential Equation\nMathematics\n22%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nProjects\n4\nFinished\nMathematical Aspects of Some PDE Models for Granular Matter and Fish Harvest\nShen, W.\n(PI)\nNational Science Foundation\n8/15/09\n→\n7/31/12\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nMathematical Aspects\n100%\nMarine Resources\n100%\nFish Harvest\n100%\nPartial Differential Equations\n100%\nGranular Materials\n100%\nMathematical Aspects of Some PDE Models for Granular Matter and Fish Harvest\nShen, W.\n(PI)\n8/15/09\n→\n7/31/12\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nMathematical Aspects\n100%\nMarine Resources\n100%\nFish Harvest\n100%\nPDE Model\n100%\nPartial Differential Equations\n100%\nSCREMS:  Scientific Computing Environments for Mathematical Sciences\nXu, J. (PI), Andrews, G. E. (CoPI), Du, Q. (CoPI),\nZikatanov, L. T.\n(CoPI) &\nShen, W.\n(CoPI)\nNational Science Foundation\n9/1/06\n→\n8/31/07\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nMathematical Science\n100%\nNumerical Simulation\n100%\nMathematical Modeling\n100%\nComputing Environment\n100%\nNatural Sciences Computing\n100%\nSCREMS: Scientific Computing Environments for Mathematical Sciences\nXu, J. (PI), Andrews, G. E. (CoPI), Du, Q. (CoPI),\nZikatanov, L. T.\n(CoPI) &\nShen, W.\n(CoPI)\n9/1/06\n→\n8/31/07\nProject\n:\nResearch project\nMathematical Science\n100%\nNumerical Simulation\n100%\nMathematical Modeling\n100%\nComputing Environment\n100%\nNatural Sciences Computing\n100%\nResearch output\n42\nArticle\n2\nChapter\n1\nBook\nConservation laws with discontinuous gradient-dependent flux: The stable case\nAmadori, D.,\nBressan, A.\n&\nShen, W.\n,\nJun 1 2025\n,\nIn:\nMathematical Models and Methods in Applied Sciences.\n35\n,\n6\n,\np. 1421-1469\n49 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nConservation Laws\n100%\nConservation Law\n100%\nSemigroup\n100%\nSpatially Periodic\n50%\nPeriodic Case\n50%\n1\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nMICROSCOPIC HYSTERETIC TRAFFIC MODEL AND STOP-AND-GO WAVES\nFan, H. &\nShen, W.\n,\nNov 2025\n,\nIn:\nDiscrete and Continuous Dynamical Systems- Series A.\n45\n,\n11\n,\np. 4490-4509\n20 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nTraveling Wave\n100%\nHysteretic\n100%\nWave Profile\n100%\nTraffic Model\n100%\nTraffic Stops\n100%\nA SPACE-TIME NONLOCAL TRAFFIC FLOW MODEL: RELAXATION REPRESENTATION AND LOCAL LIMIT\nDu, Q., Huang, K., Scott, J. &\nShen, W.\n,\nSep 2023\n,\nIn:\nDiscrete and Continuous Dynamical Systems- Series A.\n43\n,\n9\n,\np. 3456-3484\n29 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nModel Parameter\n100%\nFlow Model\n100%\nExponential Function\n100%\nInitial Condition\n100%\nPosedness\n100%\n4\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nA Posteriori Error Estimates for Numerical Solutions to Hyperbolic Conservation Laws\nBressan, A.\n, Chiri, M. T. &\nShen, W.\n,\nJul 2021\n,\nIn:\nArchive for Rational Mechanics and Analysis.\n241\n,\n1\n,\np. 357-402\n46 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nNumerical Solution\n100%\nA Posteriori Error Estimation\n100%\nHyperbolic Conservation Laws\n100%\nConservation Law\n100%\nPosteriori\n100%\n9\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nA POSTERIORI ERROR ESTIMATES for SELF-SIMILAR SOLUTIONS to the EULER EQUATIONS\nBressan, A.\n&\nShen, W.\n,\nJan 2021\n,\nIn:\nDiscrete and Continuous Dynamical Systems- Series A.\n41\n,\n1\n,\np. 113-130\n18 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nNumerical Results\n100%\nNumerical Simulation\n100%\nBounded Domain\n100%\nExact Solutions\n100%\nBoundary Information\n100%\n26\nLink opens in a new tab\nScopus \n citations\nView all 45 Research outputs"
