  "deep_homepage::Jialu Wang::https://jialuwang123321.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://jialuwang123321.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "jialu.wang@keble.ox.ac.uk"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/jialuwang123321",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/wang-jialu-267302280/",
    "homepage_text": "Jialu Wang | University of Oxford\nJialu Wang\nD.Phil. Student\nUniversity of Oxford\njialu.wang@keble.ox.ac.uk\nAbout Me\nI am a D.Phil. candidate in Computer Science at the\nUniversity of Oxford\n, co-supervised by Profs.\nNiki Trigoni\nand\nAndrew Markham\n.\nI plan on submitting my thesis in the coming months and will soon be entering the job market. Feel free to contact me for any research opportunities!\nResearch Interests\nMy research interests primarily focus on advancing robotics and autonomous systems, particularly in achieving human-level perception and comprehensive environmental understanding for mobile robotic platforms. I aim to develop cutting-edge AI techniques and methodologies to enable robust and efficient spatial perception solutions, enhancing the reliability, intelligence, and security of intelligent machines in real-world scenarios. Additionally, my research includes efficient camera localization using state space models for edge-cloud collaborative IoT and terminal devices, further enhancing AI applications in these areas.\nTechniques\n: Visual Localization, Adversarial Training, Data Augmentation, Domain Adaptation, 3D Reconstruction, and Neural Rendering\nApplications\n: Autonomous Driving, Robotics, Virtual Reality, edge-cloud collaborative IoT and terminal devices\nPublications\nRADA\nRADA: Robust Adversarial Data Augmentation for Camera Localization in Challenging Conditions\nJialu Wang , Muhamad Risqi U. Saputra , Chris Xiaoxuan Lu , Niki Trigoni and Andrew Markham\n(IROS 2023)\nPaper\nVideo\nCode\nWSCLoc\nWSCLoc: Weakly-Supervised Sparse-View Camera Relocalization via Radiance Field\nJialu wang, Kaichen Zhou, Andrew Markham and Niki Trigoni\n(IROS 2024, Oral Presentation)\nPaper\nProject Website\nMambaLoc\nMambaLoc: Efficient Camera Localization with State Space Model for Edge-Cloud Collaborative IoT and Terminal Devices\nJialu wang, Kaichen Zhou, Andrew Markham and Niki Trigoni\n(Submitted to  RA-L)\nPaper\nVideo\nREDLoc\nREDLoc: Towards Robust, Efficient, and Deployable Visual Localization\nJialu Wang, Bing Wang, Niki Trigoni\n(Submitted to  CVPR 2025)\nServices\nConference Reviewers\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (\nRA-L\n) 2024\nIEEE International\nConference\non Robotics & Automation (ICRA) 2024\nPowered by Jekyll and\nMinimal Light\ntheme."
  },
  "deep_homepage::Andrew Wang::https://andrewwango.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://andrewwango.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
