    "github": "https://github.com/andrewwango",
    "linkedin": "https://in.linkedin.com/in/andrewwang27",
    "homepage_text": "Andrew Wang's website\nAndrew Wang\nResearcher, entrepreneur, campaigner.\nAbout me\nAbout Blur Labs\nResearch\nPaper: benchmarking self-supervised imaging\nPreprint\non medical imaging\nPaper: fully-unsupervised dynamic MRI reconstruction\nMedical imaging\npaper\nat ISBI 2025\nPaper: perspective-equivariant satellite imaging\nConference\npaper\nat ECCV 2024\nDeepInverse library\nA PyTorch library for imaging inverse problems with deep learning\nTutorial: implementing group transforms for equivariance\nInvertible image transforms for equivariance and augmentation for inverse problems using the DeepInverse library\nTutorial: solving remote sensing problems\nRemote sensing inverse problems with satellite images using the DeepInverse library\nTutorial: playing with advanced MRI physics operators, datasets and neural networks\nMulticoil, dynamic, or 3D MRI inverse problems, raw fastMRI data and unrolled networks using the DeepInverse library\nTutorial: implementing generative adversarial networks\nSolving imaging inverse problems with adversarial networks using the DeepInverse library\nTutorial: implementing the Equivariant Imaging framework\nGeometric transformations for equivariant imaging using the DeepInverse library\nPhysics-informed dynamic latent space models\nMEng thesis in computational statistics and ML\nPaper: FEMDA robust classification\nConference paper at ICASSP 2022\nPaper: London social distance estimation\nBCS Computer Journal paper with the Alan Turing Institute\nData Science Projects\nWebsite and community map for ESEA Outdoors UK\nA Bootstrap\nwebsite\nand\ncommunity map\nTutorial: Node classification with Neo4j and Python\nComparing ML using tabular vs graph data models with the Cora dataset\nTutorial: How to find places of interest along a GPX route\nUsing the Python APIs for Overpass and Google Maps Places\nComparing urban environmental sustainability indicators in Europe\nArticle published on earth.org\nComputer studies in Northern Irish schools\nA tech outreach data analysis\nUK land access rights and sustainability\nArticle published on earth.org\nMapping lost rights of way\nA Python geospatial data analysis\nForest vegetation quantification\nEnvironmental monitoring robotics project report\n\n---\n\nAbout me - Andrew Wang's website\nAndrew Wang\nResearcher, entrepreneur, campaigner.\nAbout me\n2025, Jul 02\nWork\nResearch\nSoftware\nPublications\nTalks\nActivism\nGet in touch\nvia\nemail\nor\nLinkedIn\n.\nWork\nI’m building a startup\nBlur Labs\n! We are building open-source AI foundation models for image reconstruction. Powering the next generation of faster, cheaper imaging devices.\nInterested in imaging? Follow us on\nLinkedIn\nor get in touch with me.\nBlur Labs is based in Paris and proudly supported by\nInria Startup Studio\n.\nResearch\nI was a PhD researcher at the University of Edinburgh, supervised by\nProf Mike Davies\n.\nI design deep learning algorithms for solving real-world imaging inverse problems where we rarely have ground truth, such as accelerating medical imaging or higher resolution Earth observation.\nI’m interested in\ncomputer vision\n,\ninverse problems\n,\nunsupervised deep learning\n,\ngeometric deep learning\n,\nmedical imaging\nand\nEarth observation\n.\nCheck out my\nCV\nand\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSoftware\nI am a lead maintainer for\nDeepInverse\n, the PyTorch library for imaging with deep learning. We’re part of the\nofficial PyTorch ecosystem\n!\nI’m open to freelance work - check out my\nproject portfolio\n.\nPublications\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Perspective-Equivariant Fine-tuning for Multispectral Demosaicing without Ground Truth”\n, on arXiv, 2026.\nJ. Tachella, M. Terris, S. Hurault, A. Wang et al.,\n“DeepInverse: A Python package for solving imaging inverse problems with deep learning”\n, Journal of Open Source Software, 2025.\nA. Wang, S. McDonagh, M. Davies,\n“Benchmarking Self-Supervised Learning Methods for Accelerated MRI Reconstruction”\n, on arXiv, 2025.\nWebsite\n.\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Fully unsupervised dynamic MRI reconstruction via diffeo-temporal equivariance”\n, IEEE 2025\nInternational Symposium on Biomedical Imaging\n(ISBI 2025), Houston. Oral presentation (top 18% of papers).\nWebsite\n.\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging: an Unsupervised Framework for Multispectral Pansharpening”\n,\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV)\nWorkshop on Traditional Computer Vision in the Age of Deep Learning\n, Milan, 2024. Oral presentation.\nWebsite\n.\nJ. Walsh, O. Kesa, A. Wang et al.,\n“Near Real-Time Social Distance Estimation in London”\n, The Computer Journal, 2023. Winner of OUP\nWilkes Award\nfor best paper 2024.\nPress\n,\nPress\n.\nP. Houdouin, A. Wang et al.,\n“Robust Classification with Flexible Discriminant Analysis in Heterogeneous Data”\n, IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2022.\nTalks\n04-10-2026 | Tutorial | TBC, 29th International Conference on Medical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention (\nMICCAI\n) 2026, Abu Dhabi.\n07-04-2026 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“How DeepInverse is solving imaging in science and healthcare with PyTorch”\n,\nPyTorch Conference Europe\n, Paris.\n04-05-2026 | Invited speaker | Workshop on\nImaging inverse problems and generating models: sparsity and robustness versus expressivity\n, International Centre for Mathematical Science, Edinburgh.\n03-03-2026 | Invited speaker |\n“Get started with DeepInverse for image reconstruction with deep learning”\n,\nSymposium on AI and Reconstruction for Biomedical Imaging\n, London Institute for Healthcare Engineering, London.\n18-04-2025 |\nSeminar\n(\nrecording\n) |\n“Learning to solve imaging inverse problems without ground truth”\n, Institute for Foundations of Machine Learning, University of Texas at Austin.\n16-04-2025 |\nTutorial\n|\n“DeepInverse”\n, International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging (\nISBI\n), Houston, Apr 2025.\n16-04-2025 | Oral presentation |\n“Fully unsupervised dynamic MRI reconstruction via diffeo-temporal equivariance”\n, ISBI 2025, Houston.\n25-02-2025 | Seminar (\nrecording\n) |\n“Equivariant imaging with groups of real-world transforms”\n, Maxwell Institute for Mathematical Sciences, Edinburgh.\n19-12-2024 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“Learning to reconstruct accelerated dynamic MRI without ground truth”\n,\nInternational Workshop on Mathematical Imaging and AI Algorithms\n, IPTA 2024, University of Strathclyde, Glasgow.\n04-12-2024 | Seminar |\n“Learning to solve imaging inverse problems without ground truth”\n,\nEdinburgh Vision\n, University of Edinburgh.\n29-09-2024 | Oral presentation | [\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging”\n],\nECCV\nTradiCV workshop\n, Milan, 2024.\n10-06-2024 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging: an Unsupervised Framework for Pansharpening”\n,\nMaths4DL Geometric Deep Learning workshop\n, University of Cambridge.\n🏞️🏞️🏞️\nActivism\nI’m an activist and campaigner for better access to nature and the outdoors for everyone.\nI founded\nESEA Outdoors UK\n, a grassroots community to advocate for better representation, diversity and inclusion in the outdoors.\nI’m on the board of\nNational Trails UK\n, a national charity championing and campaigning for National Trails across the UK.\nTo learn more about these topics, check out my\nlist of Resources\nand\nSubstack\n.\nWriting\nTBC | The Great Outdoors magazine | The view from here\n24-07-2025 | Connecting Threads Journal |\nRunning along rivers\n03-06-2025 | Substack |\nRethinking education for access to the outdoors\n02-12-2024 | Substack |\nAgainst inclusivity-washing in the outdoors\n15-10-2024 | Substack |\nAccess to nature - but for whom?\n18-06-2024 |\nBMC Summit magazine\n|\nDiversity in the Mountains at the Great Lakeland 3 Day\n(free to read)\n21-03-2024 | BMC |\nEast and Southeast Asian people go outdoors too\n18-09-2023 | Earth.org |\nWhy Improving UK Land Access Rights Is Important For A More Sustainable Outdoors\n16-02-2023 | Earth.org |\nComparing Urban Environmental Sustainability Indicators In Europe\nSpeaker\n23-11-2024 |\nKendal Mountain Festival\n|\nThe Human Powered Session - presented by Patagonia\nwith\nEben Myrddin Muse\nand Carlos Casas.\n14-07-2024 | Love Trails Festival |\nLand Access: the need for a true Right to Roam\nwith\nEben Myrddin Muse\n(BMC), Jon Moses (Right to Roam) and Amy-Jane Beer\n12-07-2024 | Love Trails Festival |\nThe Outsiders Project: remarkable people doing remarkable things\nwith Phil Young and Trina Dawkins.\n07-07-2024 | Timber Festival |\nUsing community to tackle racism in the outdoors: an ESEA perspective\n05-05-2024 | SCARPA Great Lakeland 3 Day |\nDiversity & inclusion in the outdoors\n28-11-2020 | Kendal Mountain Literature Festival |\nOpen Mountain - Space and Isolation\n\n---\n\nAbout me - Andrew Wang's website\nAndrew Wang\nResearcher, entrepreneur, campaigner.\nAbout me\n2025, Jul 02\nWork\nResearch\nSoftware\nPublications\nTalks\nActivism\nGet in touch\nvia\nemail\nor\nLinkedIn\n.\nWork\nI’m building a startup\nBlur Labs\n! We are building open-source AI foundation models for image reconstruction. Powering the next generation of faster, cheaper imaging devices.\nInterested in imaging? Follow us on\nLinkedIn\nor get in touch with me.\nBlur Labs is based in Paris and proudly supported by\nInria Startup Studio\n.\nResearch\nI was a PhD researcher at the University of Edinburgh, supervised by\nProf Mike Davies\n.\nI design deep learning algorithms for solving real-world imaging inverse problems where we rarely have ground truth, such as accelerating medical imaging or higher resolution Earth observation.\nI’m interested in\ncomputer vision\n,\ninverse problems\n,\nunsupervised deep learning\n,\ngeometric deep learning\n,\nmedical imaging\nand\nEarth observation\n.\nCheck out my\nCV\nand\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSoftware\nI am a lead maintainer for\nDeepInverse\n, the PyTorch library for imaging with deep learning. We’re part of the\nofficial PyTorch ecosystem\n!\nI’m open to freelance work - check out my\nproject portfolio\n.\nPublications\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Perspective-Equivariant Fine-tuning for Multispectral Demosaicing without Ground Truth”\n, on arXiv, 2026.\nJ. Tachella, M. Terris, S. Hurault, A. Wang et al.,\n“DeepInverse: A Python package for solving imaging inverse problems with deep learning”\n, Journal of Open Source Software, 2025.\nA. Wang, S. McDonagh, M. Davies,\n“Benchmarking Self-Supervised Learning Methods for Accelerated MRI Reconstruction”\n, on arXiv, 2025.\nWebsite\n.\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Fully unsupervised dynamic MRI reconstruction via diffeo-temporal equivariance”\n, IEEE 2025\nInternational Symposium on Biomedical Imaging\n(ISBI 2025), Houston. Oral presentation (top 18% of papers).\nWebsite\n.\nA. Wang, M. Davies,\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging: an Unsupervised Framework for Multispectral Pansharpening”\n,\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV)\nWorkshop on Traditional Computer Vision in the Age of Deep Learning\n, Milan, 2024. Oral presentation.\nWebsite\n.\nJ. Walsh, O. Kesa, A. Wang et al.,\n“Near Real-Time Social Distance Estimation in London”\n, The Computer Journal, 2023. Winner of OUP\nWilkes Award\nfor best paper 2024.\nPress\n,\nPress\n.\nP. Houdouin, A. Wang et al.,\n“Robust Classification with Flexible Discriminant Analysis in Heterogeneous Data”\n, IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP), 2022.\nTalks\n04-10-2026 | Tutorial | TBC, 29th International Conference on Medical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention (\nMICCAI\n) 2026, Abu Dhabi.\n07-04-2026 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“How DeepInverse is solving imaging in science and healthcare with PyTorch”\n,\nPyTorch Conference Europe\n, Paris.\n04-05-2026 | Invited speaker | Workshop on\nImaging inverse problems and generating models: sparsity and robustness versus expressivity\n, International Centre for Mathematical Science, Edinburgh.\n03-03-2026 | Invited speaker |\n“Get started with DeepInverse for image reconstruction with deep learning”\n,\nSymposium on AI and Reconstruction for Biomedical Imaging\n, London Institute for Healthcare Engineering, London.\n18-04-2025 |\nSeminar\n(\nrecording\n) |\n“Learning to solve imaging inverse problems without ground truth”\n, Institute for Foundations of Machine Learning, University of Texas at Austin.\n16-04-2025 |\nTutorial\n|\n“DeepInverse”\n, International Symposium on Biomedical Imaging (\nISBI\n), Houston, Apr 2025.\n16-04-2025 | Oral presentation |\n“Fully unsupervised dynamic MRI reconstruction via diffeo-temporal equivariance”\n, ISBI 2025, Houston.\n25-02-2025 | Seminar (\nrecording\n) |\n“Equivariant imaging with groups of real-world transforms”\n, Maxwell Institute for Mathematical Sciences, Edinburgh.\n19-12-2024 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“Learning to reconstruct accelerated dynamic MRI without ground truth”\n,\nInternational Workshop on Mathematical Imaging and AI Algorithms\n, IPTA 2024, University of Strathclyde, Glasgow.\n04-12-2024 | Seminar |\n“Learning to solve imaging inverse problems without ground truth”\n,\nEdinburgh Vision\n, University of Edinburgh.\n29-09-2024 | Oral presentation | [\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging”\n],\nECCV\nTradiCV workshop\n, Milan, 2024.\n10-06-2024 |\nLightning talk\n|\n“Perspective-Equivariant Imaging: an Unsupervised Framework for Pansharpening”\n,\nMaths4DL Geometric Deep Learning workshop\n, University of Cambridge.\n🏞️🏞️🏞️\nActivism\nI’m an activist and campaigner for better access to nature and the outdoors for everyone.\nI founded\nESEA Outdoors UK\n, a grassroots community to advocate for better representation, diversity and inclusion in the outdoors.\nI’m on the board of\nNational Trails UK\n, a national charity championing and campaigning for National Trails across the UK.\nTo learn more about these topics, check out my\nlist of Resources\nand\nSubstack\n.\nWriting\nTBC | The Great Outdoors magazine | The view from here\n24-07-2025 | Connecting Threads Journal |\nRunning along rivers\n03-06-2025 | Substack |\nRethinking education for access to the outdoors\n02-12-2024 | Substack |\nAgainst inclusivity-washing in the outdoors\n15-10-2024 | Substack |\nAccess to nature - but for whom?\n18-06-2024 |\nBMC Summit magazine\n|\nDiversity in the Mountains at the Great Lakeland 3 Day\n(free to read)\n21-03-2024 | BMC |\nEast and Southeast Asian people go outdoors too\n18-09-2023 | Earth.org |\nWhy Improving UK Land Access Rights Is Important For A More Sustainable Outdoors\n16-02-2023 | Earth.org |\nComparing Urban Environmental Sustainability Indicators In Europe\nSpeaker\n23-11-2024 |\nKendal Mountain Festival\n|\nThe Human Powered Session - presented by Patagonia\nwith\nEben Myrddin Muse\nand Carlos Casas.\n14-07-2024 | Love Trails Festival |\nLand Access: the need for a true Right to Roam\nwith\nEben Myrddin Muse\n(BMC), Jon Moses (Right to Roam) and Amy-Jane Beer\n12-07-2024 | Love Trails Festival |\nThe Outsiders Project: remarkable people doing remarkable things\nwith Phil Young and Trina Dawkins.\n07-07-2024 | Timber Festival |\nUsing community to tackle racism in the outdoors: an ESEA perspective\n05-05-2024 | SCARPA Great Lakeland 3 Day |\nDiversity & inclusion in the outdoors\n28-11-2020 | Kendal Mountain Literature Festival |\nOpen Mountain - Space and Isolation"
  },
