    "homepage_text": "Pan, Weishen\nVIVO\nWeill Cornell Medical College\nSearch form\nWeishen Pan\nResearch Associate in Population Health Sciences\nResearch Associate in Population Health Sciences\n,\nPopulation Health Sciences\n,\nWeill Cornell Medical College\n2025 -\nPublications\nSort by\nNewest\nOldest\nTimes Cited\nPublication Type\nJournal Name\nCo-Author Network\nselected publications\nFederated target trial emulation using distributed observational data for treatment effect estimation.\nNPJ digital medicine\n.\n2025\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nMulticenter target trial emulation to evaluate corticosteroids for sepsis stratified by predicted organ dysfunction trajectory.\nNature communications\n.\n2025\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n9\nIdentification of predictive subphenotypes for clinical outcomes using real world data and machine learning.\nNature communications\n.\n2025\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n3\nFederated Target Trial Emulation using Distributed Observational Data for Treatment Effect Estimation.\n2025\nGET IT\nLearning Phenotypic Associations for Parkinson's Disease with Longitudinal Clinical Records.\nAMIA Joint Summits on Translational Science proceedings. AMIA Joint Summits on Translational Science\n.\n2024\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nCorticosteroids for infectious critical illness: A multicenter target trial emulation stratified by predicted organ dysfunction trajectory.\n2024\nGET IT\nLearning across diverse biomedical data modalities and cohorts: Challenges and opportunities for innovation.\nPatterns (New York, N.Y.)\n.\n2024\nReview\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n25\nAn adaptive federated learning framework for clinical risk prediction with electronic health records from multiple hospitals.\nPatterns (New York, N.Y.)\n.\n2024\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n17\nGeneralizability of a Machine Learning Model for Improving Utilization of Parathyroid Hormone-Related Peptide Testing across Multiple Clinical Centers.\nClinical chemistry\n.\n2023\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n13\nData heterogeneity in federated learning with Electronic Health Records: Case studies of risk prediction for acute kidney injury and sepsis diseases in critical care.\nPLOS digital health\n.\n2023\nAcademic Article\nGET IT\nTimes cited:\n30\nmore ...\nless ...\nResearch\nSort by\nNewest\nOldest\nResearcher Role\nCo-investigator Network\nFunding awarded\nSanofi BP 260464, SPONSORED COLLABORATION RESEARCH AGREEMENT.\nawarded by\nSanofi S.A.\nCo-Investigator\n2025 - 2026\nmissing activity\nCo-Investigator\n2023 - 2026\nmore ...\nless ...\nBackground\neducation and training\nPh.D.,\nTsinghua University (China)\n22\nB.A.,\nTsinghua University (China)\n2015\nContact\nfull name\nWeishen\nPan\nprimary email\nwep4001@med.cornell.edu"
