    "homepage_text": "Zifeng Wang's Homepage\nZifeng Wang\nI am a Research Scientist at Google Cloud AI Research, focusing on large language models (LLMs) and their applications. My research interests span model adaptation, multi-LLM collaboration, and multi-agent systems. I received my PhD in Machine Learning from\nNortheastern University\n's\nSPIRAL Group\n, advised by Prof.\nJennifer G. Dy\n, with close collaboration with Prof.\nStratis Ioannidis\nand Prof.\nYanzhi Wang\n.\n\n                  Prior to my PhD, I earned my BS in Electronic Engineering from\nTsinghua University\n, where I worked on computer vision with Prof.\nJiwen Lu\n(Tsinghua) and Prof.\nJia Deng\n(Princeton), and big data with Prof.\nYong Li\n(Tsinghua).\nI am looking for self-motivated student researchers / research interns with interests and expertise in LLMs! Feel free to contact me if you would like to work on cutting-edge challenges in machine learning and LLMs.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nLinkedIn\n/\nTwitter\n/\nCV\nResearch\nLarge Language Models\nModel alignment and adaptation\nSynthetic data for post-training and evaluation\nLLM agents and multi-agent systems\nCost-effective LLM inference (e.g., Routing, Distillation)\nContinual (Lifelong) Learning\nOpen Set Recognition / Novel Class Discovery\nAdversarial Robustness and Model Compression\nExperience\nAug 2023 - Present, Google,\nResearch Scientist\n                        at\nCloud AI Research\nSep 2018 - July 2023, Northeastern University,\nResearch Assistant at\nSPIRAL Group\nJune 2021 - Jan 2023, Google,\nStudent Researcher / Research Intern\n                        at\nCloud AI Research\nFeb 2017 - July 2018, Tsinghua University,\nResearch Assistant at\ni-Vision Group\nJuly 2017 - Sep 2017, University of Michigan,\nVisiting Researcher\n                        at\nVision & Learning Lab\nSelected Publications\nFilter by Topic:\nAll Papers\nLLM\nContinual Learning\nMisc\nView all on Google Scholar\nInvited Talks\nSparse Continual Learning on the Edge\n-\nContinualAI\n, 2023, Remote\n-\nAI Time\n, 2023, Remote (Chinese\n                          version)\nPrompting-based Continual Learning\n-\nAI Talks SG\n, 2022, Remote\n-\nContinualAI\n, 2022, Remote\n[\nrecording\n]\nRevisiting Hilbert-Schmidt Information Bottleneck for Adversarial Robustness\n-\nINFORMS Annual\n                          Meeting\n,\n                        2022, Indianapolis, Indiana\n[\nabstract\n]\n-\nAI Time\n, 2022, Remote (Chinese\n                        version)\n[\nrecording\n][\nblog\n]\nAwards\nOutstanding Student Award in Research\n, Northeastern University,\n                      2023\nScholar Award\n, NeurIPS 2022\nBest Paper Candidate\n, ICDM 2020\nBest Paper Award\n, DySPAN 2019\nTravel Award\n, DySPAN 2019\nTravel Award\n, NeurIPS 2019\nDean's Fellowship\n, Northeastern University, 2018\nHighest honor awarded to new PhD\n                        students for outstanding academic background.\nEvergrande Scholarship\n, Tsinghua University, 2016\nAwarded to students with excellent\n                          academic performance, scientific potential and overall development.\nAcademic Service\nArea Chair\n: ACL ARR\nConference Reviewer\n: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, CVPR, ICCV\nPC Member\n: SDM\nJournal Reviewer\n: TPAMI, TMLR, Neural Networks\nTemplate Credit:\nJon Barron"
  },
