    "homepage_text": "Feijie (Harli) Wu's Homepage\nFeijie (Harli) Wu\nPh.D. student at\nPurdue\n✉ wu1977[at]purdue[dot]edu\nCopyright ©2020-\nAll rights reserved\nLast Update: December 17, 2025\nAbout\nShort Bio\nI am currently a Ph.D. student advised by\nProf. Jing Gao\nin the\nElmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nat\nPurdue University\n. Before joining Purdue in 2022, I worked with\nProf. Song Guo\nat the\nPervasive Edge Intelligence Laboratory (PEILab)\n. I obtained my B.Sc. degree in Computing (major) and Applied Mathematics (minor) from\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nin 2020. During my doctoral studies, I have conducted research in collaboration with leading technology companies, including Alibaba and Apple. I have served as a reviewer for a number of prestigious conferences, such as ICML, NeurIPS, ICLR, and KDD. I am a recipient of the\nBilsland Dissertation Fellowship\nand the Best Student Paper Award from\nACM BSCI'19\n.\nResearch Interest\nLarge Language Models\nFederated Learning\nLarge-scale Optimization\nAI Agents\nMulti-agent System\nNews\n[Dec. 2025] I receive the Bilsland Dissertation Fellowship from Purdue University.\n[Dec. 2025] Our paper on privacy-preserving split federated learning is accepted by KDD'26.\n[Oct. 2025] A new paper on LLM training for tool use comes out. Check out the paper on\narXiv\n.\n[Oct. 2025] I have created an account on\nX\n. Feel free to follow me.\n[Jul. 2025] Our paper on LLM copyright protection with regularized selective unlearning is accepted by COLM'25.\n[May 2025] I join Apple AIML as an intern this summer.\n[Jan. 2025] Our paper on federated RLHF is accepted by ICLR'25.\n[Oct. 2024] I receive a travel grant from SenSys'24.\n[Sept. 2024] Our paper on model-heterogeneous federated learning is accepted by NeurIPS'24.\n[Sept. 2024] Our paper on LLM copyright protection is accepted by EMNLP'24.\n[Sept. 2024] Our paper on heterogeneous multi-modal federated learning is accepted by SenSys'24.\nEducation\nEducation\nDoctor of Philosophy\nAugust 2022 - Present\nPurdue University\nWest Lafayette, Indiana, United States\nAdvisor:\nProf. Jing Gao\nMaster of Philosophy\nSeptember 2020 - August 2022\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nHong Kong\nAdvisor:\nProf. Song Guo\nLaboratory:\nPervasive Edge Intelligence Laboratory (PEILab)\nThesis: Gradient-wise Optimization for Distributed Machine Learning [\nPDF\n]\nBachelor of Science (Hons) in Computing\nAugust 2016 - September 2020\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nHong Kong\nMinor in Applied Mathematics\nUndergraduate Exchange Programme in Technical Computer Science\nFebruary 2019 - July 2019\nThe University of Twente\nEnschede, Overijssel, Netherlands\nExperience\nWork Experience\nPurdue University\nWest Lafayette, Indiana, United States\nGraduate Research Assistant (Advisor:\nProf. Jing Gao\n)\nAugust 2022 - Present\nApple Inc.\nSeattle, Washington, United States\nMachine Learning Intern (Mentors:\nWeiwu Zhu\n,\nDr. Shawn Zhang\n, and\nSoumya Chatterjee\n)\nMay 2025 - August 2025\nAlibaba Group\nResearch Intern (Mentors:\nDr. Zitao Li\n,\nDr. Fei Wei\n, and\nDr. Yaliang Li\n)\nMay 2024 - August 2024\nAlibaba Group\nBellevue, Washington, United States\nResearch Intern (Mentors:\nDr. Yaliang Li\nand\nDr. Zitao Li\n)\nMay 2023 - August 2023\nPervasive Edge Intelligence Laboratory (PEILab), The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nHong Kong\nResearch Assistant (Advisor:\nProf. Song Guo\n)\nSeptember 2020 - August 2022\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong (Shenzhen)\nShenzhen, Guangdong, China\nResearch Assistant (Advisor:\nProf. Wei Cai\n)\nJuly 2019 - September 2019\nThe University of British Columbia\nVancouver, British Columbia, Canada\nResearch Assistant (Advisor:\nProf. Victor C.M. Leung\n)\nJuly 2018 - September 2018\nTeaching\nTeaching\nENG 2003 Information Technology\nTeaching Assistant @ The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nSpring 2022\nCOMP 1011 Programming Fundamentals\nTeaching Assistant @ The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\nFall 2021\nServices\nProfessional Activities\nConference TPC/Reviewer\nBSCI 2020, ECML-PKDD 2020, ICML 2022, NeurIPS 2022, ICML 2023, NeurIPS 2023, ICLR 2024, ICML 2024, KDD 2024, NeurIPS 2024, ACL Rolling Review 2024, KDD 2025, ICLR 2025, ICML 2025, ACL Rolling Review 2025, NeurIPS 2025\nJournal Reviewer\nIEEE OJ-CS, ACM TOMM, ACM TOIT, IEEE TMC\nPublications\n* indicates equal contribution.\n* indicates equal contribution.\nSwitch to full publication list"
