    "homepage_text": "College of Charleston | Yu Gong\nReturn to College of Charleston homepage\nWhat're you looking for?\nWhat're you looking for?\nSearch\nYu Gong\nAssociate Professor of Physics\nEducation\nDoctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)\nin Ultrafast optical control of magnetic dynamics in ferromagnetic films, The Graduate Center, City University of New York, 2007 – 2013\nMaster's\ndegree in Physics, The Graduate Center, City University of New York, 2007 – 2009\nMaster's\ndegree in Magnetism and Magnetic Materials, Lanzhou University, China, 2004 – 2007\nBachelor's\ndegree in Physics, Physics Dep. Lanzhou University, China, 2000 – 2004\nResearch Interests\nUltrafast electron, phonon and spin dynamics in nano-scale materials and nano-photonic devices and surface plasma resonance in nanostructure materials.\nhttps://blogs.charleston.edu/gongy/\nAffiliations\nCollege of Charleston,\nAssistant Professor, 2019-present\nNature Communications,\nAssociate Editor, 2016-2019\nPacific Northwest National Laboratory,\nPostdoctoral Research Associate, 2013-2016\nCourses Taught\nPhys 340 Photonics\nPhys 320 Electronics\nPhys 120\nPhys 111\nPhys 101\nPhys 420\nSelected Publications\nAlem Teklu, Noah Kern, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Joe Tidwell, Maxwell Rabe, Yu Gong, Wenkai Zhang, Luis Balicas “Experimental Analysis of the Elastic Moduli of Atomically Thin Transition Metal Dichalcogenides”\nJ. Phys. Chem. C\n2024, XXXX, XXX, XXX-XXX https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpcc.4c03861\nNing Fang, Lei Wang, Nico Harris, Alem A Teklu, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Christian Brennan, Kamden Noah Kern, Aeron McConnell, Dali Sun, Ziyao Zhou and Yu Gong, “Control of coherent phonon dynamics in CoFeB/heavy metal heterojunction structures for future hybrid phononic and spintronic devices”\nJ. Phys. D: Appl. Phys.\n58\n045303 (2024)  https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-6463/ad8bd1\nChristian Brennan, Alan G. Jolym, Chih-Feng Wang, Ti Xie, Brian T. O’Callahan, Kevin Crampton, Alem Teklu, Leilei Shi, Ming Hu, Qian Zhang, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Hasitha Suriya Arachchige, Apoorva Chaturvedi, Hua Zhang, David Mandrus, Cheng Gong, Yu Gong, “Strong Surface-Enhanced Coherent Phonon Generation in van der Waals Materials” J. Phys. Chem. Lett. 15,  10442–10450 (2024) https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.4c02208\nYu Gong, Zhonghua Yang, Alem Teklu, Ti Xie, Noah Kern, Andrew F. May, Michael McGuire, Christian Brennan, Er-Jia Guo, Narayanan Kuthirummal, John Cetin, Qian Zhang, Ming Hu, and Cheng Gong, “Efficient Optical Control of Magnon Dynamics in van der Waals Ferromagnets” Ultrafast Sci. 4, 0064. (2024) https://doi.org/10.34133/ultrafastscience.0064\nKT Crampton, AG Joly, Y Gong, P El-Khoury, “Spatiotemporal imaging and manipulation of surface plasmons” Nanophotonics (2024), https://doi.org/10.1515/nanoph-2023-0733\nShengru Chen, Qinghua Zhang, Dongke Rong, Yue Xu, Jinfeng Zhang, Fangfang Pei, He Bai, Yan‐Xing Shang, Shan Lin, Qiao Jin, Haitao Hong, Can Wang, Wensheng Yan, Haizhong Guo, Tao Zhu, Lin Gu, Yu Gong, Qian Li, Lingfei Wang, Gang‐Qin Liu, Kui‐juan Jin, Er‐Jia Guo, “Braiding Lateral Morphotropic grain boundaries in homogenetic oxides” Advanced Materials, 35, 2206961 (2023)\nYu Gong, Xiangdong Bi, Nikki Chen, Marcello Forconi, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Alem Teklu, Bo Gao, Jacob Koenemann, Nico Harris, Christian Brennan, Marisa Thomas, Taylor Barnes, and Ming Hu, “Significant Enhancement of Two-Photon Excited Fluorescence in Water-Soluble Triphenylamine-Based All-Organic Compounds”\nJ. Phys. Chem. B\n2022, 126, 29, 5513–5522 10.1021/acs.jpcb.2c03514\nYu Gong, Ming Hu, Nico Harris, Zhonghua Yang, Ti Xie, Alem Teklu, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Jacob koenemann, Xianghan Xu, Sang-Wook Cheong, Will McLoud and Cheng Gong, “Strong laser polarization control of coherent phonon excitation in van der Waals material Fe3GeTe2”\nnpj 2D Materials and Applications\n6\n, Article number: 9 (2022)\nZhiyin Tu, Ti Xie, Yeonghun Lee, Jinling Zhou, Alemayehu S Admasu, Yu Gong, Nagarajan Valanoor, John Cumings, Sang-Wook Cheong, Ichiro Takeuchi, Kyeongjae Cho, Cheng Gong, “Ambient effect on the Curie temperatures and magnetic domains in metallic two-dimensional magnets”\nnpj 2D Materials and Applications\n5\n, Article number: 62 (2021)\nYu Gong, Gao-Lei Hou, Xiangdong Bi, Narayanan Kuthirummal, Alem Abraha Teklu, Jacob Koenemann, Nico Harris, Peng Wei, Krystal Devera, and Ming Hu, “Enhanced Two-Photon Absorption in Two Triphenylamine-Based All-Organic Compounds” J. Phys. Chem. A 125, 1870–1879 (2021)\nHonors & Awards:\nGrant\nYear\nAmount ($)\nYu Gong\nExpandQISE: Track 1: Topological Phonon Dynamics and Control in Quantum Materials (PI)\n2024\n769,750\nYu Gong\nMRI: Track 1 Acquisition of a Low Voltage Electron Microscope at the College of Charleston (Co-PI)\n2024\n270,756\nYu Gong\nSC EPSCoR, GAIN Collaborative Research Program (GAINCRP): AI Assisted Microfluidics for Precise Exosome Characterization in Cancer Diagnosis (Co-PI)\n2024\n70,000\nYu Gong\nVFP (DOE)\n2024\n18,500\nYu Gong\nMRI: Track 1 Acquisition of a MALDI-TOF/TOF Mass Spectrometer for Research and Training at College of Charleston (Co-PI)\n2023\n350,000\nYu Gong\nVFP (DOE)\n2023\n18,500\nYu Gong\nVFP (DOE)\n2022\n17,000\nYu Gong\nVFP (DOE)\n2021\n14,000\nYu Gong\nEPSCoR MADE in SC, NSF RII Track-1 Award (Co-PI)\n2020\n60,000\n\n---\n\nCollege of Charleston | Page Not Found\nReturn to College of Charleston homepage\nWhat're you looking for?\nWhat're you looking for?\nSearch\n404\nPage Not Found\nWhoops! We can't find the page you're looking for. Please try your search again.\nHomepage\nProgram Finder\n\n---\n\nCollege of Charleston | Page Not Found\nReturn to College of Charleston homepage\nWhat're you looking for?\nWhat're you looking for?\nSearch\n404\nPage Not Found\nWhoops! We can't find the page you're looking for. Please try your search again.\nHomepage\nProgram Finder\n\n---\n\nCollege of Charleston | Page Not Found\nReturn to College of Charleston homepage\nWhat're you looking for?\nWhat're you looki