  "deep_homepage::Ming Yan::https://mingyan08.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://mingyan08.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "yanming@cuhk.edu.cn"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/mingyan08",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ming-yan-%E4%B8%A5%E6%98%8E-1578721b",
    "homepage_text": "Ming Yan (严明) - Ming Yan\nMing Yan\nAssociate Professor at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nFollow\nShenzhen, Guangdong 518172, China\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nMing Yan (严明)\nMing Yan is an\nAssociate Professor\nand\nAssistant Dean\nin the\nSchool of Data Science\nat\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (CUHK-Shenzhen)\n.\nHe spent\nseven years at University of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\n, where he received his B.S. and M.S. degrees in 2005 and 2008. He then spent another\nseven years at University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\n— including a one-year postdoctoral period at Rice University — and obtained his Ph.D. in Mathematics in 2012.\nFrom 2015 to 2022, Ming Yan spent\nseven years at Michigan State University (MSU)\n, where he was a faculty member in both the Department of Computational Mathematics, Science and Engineering (CMSE) and the Department of Mathematics.\nHe joined CUHK-Shenzhen in 2022.\nResearch Overview\nMing Yan’s research lies at the intersection of\noptimization theory\n,\nmachine learning\n, and\nscientific computing\n, where mathematics meets modern data-driven discovery. His work focuses on developing algorithms that are both\ntheoretically grounded\nand\ncomputationally efficient\n, with applications to large-scale and structure-rich problems arising in science and engineering.\nSee more about his\nresearch topics\nand recent\npublications\n.\nOpportunities\nHe is\nrecruiting highly motivated PhD students, postdoctoral researchers, and visiting students\nto join his research group. Preferred backgrounds include mathematics, computer science, or related areas, with strong analytical thinking and solid programming skills.\nThose interested in topics such as\noptimization\n,\nmachine learning\n, or\nAI-driven scientific computing\nare encouraged to visit the\nJoin Us\npage for application instructions.\nAcknowledgments\nHis research is supported by the\nChina\n: National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), Department of Science and Technology of Guangdong Province, and Shenzhen Science and Technology Innovation Commission.\nU.S.\n: National Science Foundation (NSF), Ford Motor Company, and Meta (formerly Facebook)\nLast updated: March 2026\n\n---\n\nAbout Me - Ming Yan\nMing Yan\nAssociate Professor at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nFollow\nShenzhen, Guangdong 518172, China\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nMing Yan is an Associate Professor and Assistant Dean in the School of Data Science at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen. His research interests include optimization theory, machine learning, and scientific computing, with applications to large-scale data and inverse problems.\nEducation\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\nPh.D. in Mathematics, 2012\nAdvisor: Professor\nLuminita A. Vese\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\nM.S. in Mathematics, 2008\nB.S. in Mathematics, 2005\nAcademic Appointments\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (CUHK-Shenzhen)\nAssociate Professor, 2022 – present\nMichigan State University (MSU)\nAssociate Professor, 2021 – 2023\n(on leave from 2022 to 2023)\nAssistant Professor, 2015 – 2021\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\nAssistant Adjunct Professor, 2014 – 2015\nPostdoctoral Scholar, 2013 – 2014\nRice University\nPostdoctoral Fellow, 2012 – 2013\nLast updated: March 2026\n\n---\n\nAbout Me - Ming Yan\nMing Yan\nAssociate Professor at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\nFollow\nShenzhen, Guangdong 518172, China\nEmail\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout Me\nMing Yan is an Associate Professor and Assistant Dean in the School of Data Science at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen. His research interests include optimization theory, machine learning, and scientific computing, with applications to large-scale data and inverse problems.\nEducation\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\nPh.D. in Mathematics, 2012\nAdvisor: Professor\nLuminita A. Vese\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China (USTC)\nM.S. in Mathematics, 2008\nB.S. in Mathematics, 2005\nAcademic Appointments\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (CUHK-Shenzhen)\nAssociate Professor, 2022 – present\nMichigan State University (MSU)\nAssociate Professor, 2021 – 2023\n(on leave from 2022 to 2023)\nAssistant Professor, 2015 – 2021\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles (UCLA)\nAssistant Adjunct Professor, 2014 – 2015\nPostdoctoral Scholar, 2013 – 2014\nRice University\nPostdoctoral Fellow, 2012 – 2013\nLast updated: March 2026"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Aixin Sun::https://personal.ntu.edu.sg/axsun/": {
    "homepage": "https://personal.ntu.edu.sg/axsun/",
    "all_emails": [
      "axsun@ntu.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Aixin Sun homepage\nTop\nDr. Sun Aixin is an Associate Professor and Associate Dean (Undergraduate Education) at the College\r\n                     of Computing and Data Science (\nCCDS\n), Nanyang Technological University (\nNTU\n), Singapore.\nHe received B.A.Sc. (First Class Honours) in Computer Engineering and Ph.D. from NTU in 2001 and 2004, respectively. His research interests include information retrieval, recommender systems, and natural language processing (NLP). He has published around 300 papers, which have garnered over 25,000 citations and an h-index of 72, according to Google Scholar. His work has earned several accolades, including the SIGIR 2025 Test of Time Honorable Mention Award, the Best Student Paper Award at the IEEE International Conference on Services Computing in 2020, and a Best Student Paper Honorable Mention at SIGIR 2016.\nDr. Sun is an associate editor for ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS), ACM Transactions\r\n                     on Recommender Systems (TORS), ACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (TIST), and\r\n                     an editorial board member of the Journal of the Association for Information Science and Technology\r\n                     (JASIST). He has held significant conference roles, including Doctoral Consortium co-chair for\r\n                     WSDM2023, demonstration track co-chair for SIGIR2020, ICDM2018, and CIKM2017, PC co-chair for\r\n                     AIRS2019, and general chair for ADMA2017.\nEmail: axsun AT ntu DOT edu DOT sg Phone: (+65) 6790 5139 Office: S3-B1C-117\nProfessional services\nAssociate Editor and Editorial Board Member:\nACM Transactions on Recommender Systems (\nTORS\n), Feb 2025 -- Present\nACM Transactions on Information Systems (\nTOIS\n), Aug 2022 -- Present\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (\nTIST\n), June 2024 -- Present\nJournal of the Association for Information Science and Technology (\nJASIST\n), Jan 2018 -- Present\nACM Transactions on Asian and Low-Resource Language Information\r\n                                 Processing (\nTALLIP\n),\r\n                                 Aug 2023 -- Dec 2024\nInformation Retrieval Journal, Springer, Oct 2017 -- Dec\r\n                                 2023\nNeurocomputing\n, Aug 2018 -- May 2025\nConference organization and PC members:\n2026: SIGIR (SAC), Action Editor for ARR.\n2025: Action Editor for ARR (ACL, EACL, NAACL), SIGIR (AC, and PC for Perspectives Paper\r\n                              Track), RecSys (SPC), NeurIPS (AC for Datasets and Benchmarks Track)\n2024: WWW (Search Track Co-Chair). Action Editor for ARR (ACL, EACL, NAACL), SIGIR (SPC,\r\n                              and PC for Perspectives Paper Track), RecSys (SPC), NeurIPS (AC for Datasets and\r\n                              Benchmarks Track)\n2023: EMNLP (Publication Chair), SIGIR (SPC, and PC for Perspectives Paper Track), WWW\r\n                              (SPC), IJCAI (AC), WSDM (DC Co-Chair), NeurIPS (AC for Datasets and Benchmarks Track),\r\n                              SIGIR-AP (SPC)\n2022: WWW (SPC), IJCAI (SPC), ECIR, SIGIR(SPC, and PC for Perspectives Paper Track), KDD\r\n                              (PC for Applied Data Science Track)\nRecent papers\nA Task-Centric Perspective on Recommendation\r\n                              Tasks\nAixin Sun. Accepted to Communications of the ACM (CACM).\nRecSys\nOneTrans: Unified Feature Interaction and Sequence Modeling with One Transformer in Industrial Recommender\nZhaoqi Zhang, Haolei Pei, Jun Guo, Tianyu Wang, Yufei Feng, Hui Sun, Shaowei Liu, Aixin Sun. The Web Confernce (WWW2026) Industry Track\nRecSys\nIR\nHesitation and Tolerance in Recommender Systems\nKuan Zou, Aixin Sun, Yitong Ji, Hao Zhang, Jing Wang, Zhuohao (Jerry) Zhang, Xuemeng Jiang. ACM CHI 2026\nRecSys\nA Flexible and Scalable Framework for Video Moment Search\nChongzhi Zhang, Xizhou Zhu, Aixin Sun. SIGIR-AP 2025\nIR\nTVR-Ranking: A Dataset for Ranked Video Moment Retrieval with Imprecise Queries\nRenjie Liang, Chongzhi Zhang, Li Li, Jing Wang, Xizhou Zhu, Aixin Sun. SIGIR-AP 2025\nIR\nA Survey of Real-World Recommender Systems: Challenges, Constraints, and Industrial Perspectives\nKuan Zou, Aixin Sun. Working paper\nRecSys\nTowards Storage-Efficient Visual Document Retrieval: An\r\n                              Empirical Study on Reducing Patch-Level Embeddings\nYubo Ma, Jinsong Li, Yuhang Zang, Xiaobao Wu, Xiaoyi Dong, Pan Zhang, Yuhang Cao, Haodong\r\n                        Duan, Jiaqi Wang, Yixin Cao, Aixin Sun. ACL 2025 Findings\nIR\nNLP\nPunctuation Restoration: A Case Study of BERT-Based Models'\r\n                              Task-Specific Excellence\nQishuai Zhong and Aixin Sun. IEEE ICASSP 2025.\nNLP\nMMLONGBENCH-DOC: Benchmarking Long-context Document\r\n                              Understanding with Visualizations\nYubo Ma, Yuhang Zang, Liangyu Chen, Meiqi Chen, Yizhu Jiao, Xinze Li, Xinyuan Lu, Ziyu Liu,\r\n                        Yan Ma, Xiaoyi Dong, Pan Zhang, Liangming Pan, Yu-Gang Jiang, Jiaqi Wang, Yixin Cao, and Aixin\r\n                        Sun. NeurIPS2024 D&B\nNLP\nIR\nSciAgent: Tool-augmented Language Models for Scientific\r\n                              Reasoning\nYubo Ma, Zhibin Gou, Junheng Hao, Ruochen Xu, Shuohang Wang, Liangming Pan, Yujiu Yang,\r\n                        Yixin Cao, Aixin Sun. EMNLP 2024. Accepted\nNLP\nRight Tool, Right Job: Recommendation for Repeat and\r\n                              Exploration Consumption in Food Delivery\nJiayu Li, Aixin Sun, Weizhi Ma, Peijie Sun and Min Zhang. RecSys 2024 Accepted\nRecSys\nNot All Videos Become Outdated: Short-Video Recommendation\r\n                              by Learning to Deconfound Release Interval Bias\nLulu Dong, Guoxiu He and Aixin Sun. RecSys 2024 Accepted.\nRecSys\nKnowledge-Enhanced Conversational Recommendation via\r\n                              Transformer-based Sequential Modelling\nJie Zou, Aixin Sun, Cheng Long, Evangelos Kanoulas. TOIS 2024.\nRecSys\nOn Context Utilization in Summarization with Large Language\r\n                              Models\nMathieu Ravaut, Aixin Sun, Nancy F. Chen, Shafiq Joty. ACL 2024.\nNLP\nIR\nTowards Verifiable Generation: A Benchmark for\r\n                              Knowledge-aware Language Model Attribution.\nXinze Li, Yixin Cao, Liangming Pan, Yubo Ma, Aixin Sun. ACL 2024 Findings.\nNLP\nParameter-Efficient Conversational Recommender System as a\r\n                              Language Processing Task\nMathieu Ravaut, Hao Zhang, Lu Xu, Aixin Sun, Yong Liu. EACL 2024.\nNLP\nRecSys\nDiffuRec: A Diffusion Model for Sequential\r\n                              Recommendation\nZhihao Li, Aixin Sun, Chenliang Li. ACM TOIS: 42(3), Article 66. May 2024.\nRecSys\nSelected publications Â»\nNews\nJan 2026. Aixin will give a keynote titled \"A Flexible and Scalable Framework for Video Moment Search\" at AAAI 2026 Workshop on New Frontiers in Information Retrieval\nJan 2026. Congratulations to Zhaoqi and Zou Kuan for paper acceptance to WWW26 and CHI26 respectively.\nNov 2025. Aixin gave a keynote titled Storage-Efficient Visual Document Retrieval and Beyond at Information Seeking with Big Models (BigIS) Workshop at IEEE ICDM 2025.\nSept 2025. Aixin gave a keynote on\nMultimodality Recommender Systems\nat the\nDaQuaMRec\nworkshop, RecSys2025, Prague\nSept 2025. Our team has two papers accepted at SIGIR-AP 2025, both addressing ranked video moment retrieval: one on the\nTVR-Ranking\ndataset, and the other on the\nFlexible and Scalable Framework\nJuly 2025. Our paper \"Time-Aware Point-of-Interest Recommendation\" received the\nTest of Time\r\n                        Honorable Mention Award\nat SIGIR 2025.\nJuly 2025. Aixin gave a keynote on Visual Document Understanding at the\nNIP@IR Workshop, SIGIR2025, Padava, Italy\nMay 2025. Thrilled to learn that our\nDecayPop\nalgorithm is the top performer on\nYambda-5B\nâ a massive dataset of ~5\r\n                     billion user-item interactions from Yandex!\nRead more\nPublications\nMost of recent papers are here\nResearch Team\nMy research team and projects\nDatasets\nDatasets used in our research\nTeaching\nAn instructor and tutor\nRevisit Recommender Systems\nA Survey of Real-World Recommender Systems: Challenges, Constraints, and Industrial Perspectives\nWorking paper\nA Task-Centric Perspective on Recommendation\r\n                              Tasks\nAccepted to Communications of the ACM.\nOur\r\n                              Model Achieves Excellent Performance on MovieLens: What Does it Mean?\nTOIS 2024.\nTake a Fresh Look at Recommender Systems from an Evaluation\r\n                              Standpoint.\nSIGIR 2023\nA\r\n                              Critical Study on Data Leakage in Recommender System Offline Evaluation.\nTOIS 2023\nA\r\n                              Re-visit of the Popularity Baseline in Recommender Systems.\nSIGIR 2020 (Short paper)\nRanked Video Moment Retrieval (RVMR)\nA\r\n                              Flexible and Scalable Framework for Video Moment Search\nSIGIR-AP 2025\nTVR-Ranking: A Dataset for Ranked Video Moment Retrieval with Imprecise\r\n                              Queries\nSIGIR-AP 2025\nTemporal Sentence Grounding in Videos: A Survey and Future\r\n                              Directions.\nTPAMI 2023\nSpan-based Localizing Network for Natural Language Video\r\n                              Localization\nACL 2020"
  },
