  "deep_homepage::Eric Gan::https://eric-gan.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://eric-gan.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "ericgan@berkeley.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/eric-gan",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-gan",
    "homepage_text": "Eric Gan\nEric Gan\nHey, I'm Eric!\nI am currently a student at UC Berkeley pursuing simultaneous degrees in Electrical Engineering & Computer Sciences and \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tBusiness Administration. I am passionate about crafting meaningful products at the intersection of technology, business, and people!\nLinkedIn\nGitHub\nResume\nEmail\nFacebook\nInstagram\nSelected Work\nHere are a few of the most recent projects that I have been working on. I am currently working as a Software Engineer Intern at\nCitadel\nin their Equity Quantitative Research (EQR) & Global Trading (GT) team and a research assistant at\nBerkeley Artificial Intelligence Research (BAIR) laboratory\n.\nView all my projects here!\nUber\nWorked under Uber ATG Rider Experience team to automate a start trip flow through automated cabin checks\nYouSearch\nCreated a search service translating speech to text to easily search for what you want within YouTube videos\nStadium Goods\nInvestigated international sales channels and e-commerce markets and proposed a detailed expansion plan\n\n---\n\nEric Gan\nEric Gan\nAbout Me\nBorn in Boston, raised in the Bay, I am currently a student at UC Berkeley studying Electrical\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tEngineering and Computer Sciences and Business Administration. Go Bears! I'm constantly expanding my intellectual \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfrontier, looking for new skills to learn or new opportunities to take on. Using technology to develop meaningful products that empower \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpeople excites me, and I hope to make this technology more accessible to everyone! In my free time, I enjoy\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tplaying basketball, supporting my Boston sports teams, and going on adventures in the Bay Area with friends.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI'm always down to talk about sports analytics, video games (League of Legends and SSBU), and electronic dance music!\nOrganizations\nHere are a few organizations which I have been lucky to be apart of that have provided me with unforgettable experiences and\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thelped me meet amazing people along the way.\nData Science Society at Berkeley\nUC Berkeley's first data science organization. We focus on conducting analytics projects with Bay Area companies and high-growth startups,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tas well as building an inclusive and accessible data science community at Cal for students of all levels and backgrounds. I was previously\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta data science analyst and project manager, getting to work with retail companies like Kyocera and payment companies like PayPal to provide data-driven solutions.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI most recently served as the Director of Consulting and am currently the Internal Vice President.\nWebsite\nCMG Strategy Consulting\nA consulting organization focused on working with Fortune 500 companies in providing market research, product strategy, and competitor analysis.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI am currently a senior analyst and have previously worked with retail companies such as Stadium Goods on international market research.\nWebsite\nAmerican Red Cross\nI served on the Youth Advisory Board for the annual Northern California Leadership Development Center. This completely student-led conference\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taims to empower Red Cross youth from across Northern California through various workshops and camp activities that allow for people to expand their horizons, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treceive training in CPR & First Aid and professional development, and develop a strong, supportive network. Additionally, I led the communications committee, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\twhich held the responsibility of creating all promotional material, photography, and cinematography for the conference.\nWebsite\n\n---\n\nEric Gan\nEric Gan\nAbout Me\nBorn in Boston, raised in the Bay, I am currently a student at UC Berkeley studying Electrical\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tEngineering and Computer Sciences and Business Administration. Go Bears! I'm constantly expanding my intellectual \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfrontier, looking for new skills to learn or new opportunities to take on. Using technology to develop meaningful products that empower \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpeople excites me, and I hope to make this technology more accessible to everyone! In my free time, I enjoy\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tplaying basketball, supporting my Boston sports teams, and going on adventures in the Bay Area with friends.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI'm always down to talk about sports analytics, video games (League of Legends and SSBU), and electronic dance music!\nOrganizations\nHere are a few organizations which I have been lucky to be apart of that have provided me with unforgettable experiences and\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thelped me meet amazing people along the way.\nData Science Society at Berkeley\nUC Berkeley's first data science organization. We focus on conducting analytics projects with Bay Area companies and high-growth startups,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tas well as building an inclusive and accessible data science community at Cal for students of all levels and backgrounds. I was previously\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta data science analyst and project manager, getting to work with retail companies like Kyocera and payment companies like PayPal to provide data-driven solutions.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI most recently served as the Director of Consulting and am currently the Internal Vice President.\nWebsite\nCMG Strategy Consulting\nA consulting organization focused on working with Fortune 500 companies in providing market research, product strategy, and competitor analysis.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tI am currently a senior analyst and have previously worked with retail companies such as Stadium Goods on international market research.\nWebsite\nAmerican Red Cross\nI served on the Youth Advisory Board for the annual Northern California Leadership Development Center. This completely student-led conference\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taims to empower Red Cross youth from across Northern California through various workshops and camp activities that allow for people to expand their horizons, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treceive training in CPR & First Aid and professional development, and develop a strong, supportive network. Additionally, I led the communications committee, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\twhich held the responsibility of creating all promotional material, photography, and cinematography for the conference.\nWebsite"
  },
