    "homepage_text": "Yifan Feng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYifan Feng\nYifan Feng 冯一凡\nDepartment of Analytics and Operations, NUS Business School\nInstitute of Operations Research and Analytics (IORA)\n15 Kent Ridge Dr, BIZ1 8-6\n8\n, Singapore 119245\nEmail: yifan.feng[AT]nus[DOT]edu[DOT]sg\nAbout Me\nI am an Assistant Professor in the Department of Analytics and Operations (DAO) at NUS Business School. I am also affiliated with the Institute of Operations Research and Analytics (IORA) and the Artificial Intelligence Institute at NUS.\nI integrate tools from ML/AI, economics, and optimization to tackle complex challenges in platforms and markets. My primary focus is on learning, experimentation, and information acquisition. I also work on problems for demand fulfillment.\nCV\nGoogle Scholar\nPublications\n1.\nRobust learning of consumer preferences\n(with R. Caldentey and C.T. Ryan).\nOperations Research\n70(2):918-962\n.\n[\nJournal\n] [\nSSRN\n]\n2.\nDynamic learning and market making in spread betting markets with informed bettors\n(with J. R. Birge, N. B. Keskin and A. Schultz).\nOperations Research\n69(6):1746-1766\n.\n[\nJournal\n] [\nSSRN\n]\nPreliminary version in\nEC '19\nFeatured in\nChicago Booth Review\n[\nLink\n]\n3\n.\nDesigning sparse graphs for stochastic matching with an application to middle-mile transportation management\n(with R. Caldentey, L. Xin, Y. Zhong, B. Wang, and H. Hu).\nManagement Science\n70(12):8988-9013.\n[\nJournal\n]\n[\nSSRN\n] [\nData and Codes\n]\nPreliminary version\nin\nMSOM Supply Chain SIG\n'\n22\n4\n.\nDisconnectedness brings robustness?  On network design for matching with vertex interdiction (with E. Ang).\nOperations Research Letters\n63(2025):107352\n.\n[\nJournal\n]\n[\nSSRN\n]\n5\n.\nOptimal partition for multi-type queueing systems\n(with S. Cao, S. He, and Z. Wang).\nF\northcoming in\nMathematics of Operations Research\n.  [\nJournal\n]\n[\nArxiv\n]\nWorking Papers\n1\n.\nNash equilibria in uniform price auctions: Theory, computation, and market insights.\n(with N. Golrezaei\nand Q. Li)\n.  [\nSSRN\n]\n(New)\nPreliminary version in\nSIGMETRICS ’26\n2.\nThe power of one change: Bayesian sequential experimentation under limited flexibility (with H. Zhu and T. Ni).  [\nSSRN\n]\n(New)\n3\n.\nLearning to rank under strategic \"brush wars\" (with Q. Li and H. Chen).  [\nSSRN\n]\n(New)\nPreliminary version in\nEC '24\nPreliminary version in\nMSOM Service SIG '23\n4\n.\nBeyond pairwise: Empowering LLM alignment with ranked choice modeling (with Y. Tang).\n[\nArxiv\n]\n(New)\nPreliminary version in\nICLR\n'2\n6\n5\n.\nCredit rating design under adverse selection\n(with J. Keppo and Q. Li). [\nSSRN\n]\n(New)\nPreliminary version in\nEC '25\n6\n.\nA behavioral model for exploration vs. exploitation:\nT\nheoretical framework and experimental evidence\n(with J. Ding and Y. Rong). [\nArxiv\n]\nPreliminary version in\nEC '25\nSelected into NeurIPS ’25 ML×OR Workshop.\n7\n.\nA Mallows-type model for preference learning from (ranked) choices\n(with Y. Tang). [\nSSRN\n]\nPreliminary version in\nNeurIPS '22\n[\nLink\n]\nSpotlight,\nEC '25 Workshop on New Directions in Social Choice\nThird prize,\nCSAMSE\nbest paper award competition 2023\nFinalist, P\nOMS-HK Best Student Paper Award Competition 2025\n(Entrant: Yuxuan Tang)\n8\n.\nRevisiting gig labor supply curves:\nE\nvidence from a logistics platform\n(with S. Hu and J. Keppo). [\nSSRN\n]\n9. Learning to select and rank from choice-based feedback: A simple nested approach\n(with J. Yang). [\nArxiv\n]\nPreliminary version in\nICML '23\n[\nLink\n]\nFinalist,\n2025 INFORMS JFIG Paper Competition\nSelected into NeurIPS ’25 ML×OR Workshop\nTeaching\nQuantitative Risk Management\n(MS\nBus. Analytics\n): 2020 - present\nAnalytics for Risk Management (BBA spec. Bus. Analytics): 2021 -\npresent\nService\nCurrent PhD students:\nQinzhen Li\n,\nYuxuan Tang\n(co-advised with Xiaobo Li),\nSixing Hu\n(co-advised with Jussi Keppo),\nYuda Ho\n(co-advised with Jussi Keppo)\nGraduated PhD students:\nYvonne Huijun Zhu\n(co-advised with Joel Goh). Placement: Assistant Professor at PSU.\nJunwen Yang (co-advised with Vinvent Tan).\nPostdoc\n:\nJingying Ding. Placement: Assistant Professor at Shanghai University of Finance and Economics (SUFE).\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "deep_homepage::Shenghao Yang::https://shhyang.github.io/": {
