    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Shenghao's Homepage\nShenghao's Homepage\nAbout Me\nAssociate Professor, School of Science and Engineering,\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen\n.\nCo-Founder,\nn-hop technologies\n.\nSee my\nbio\nand\nCV\n.\nAcademic Degrees\nPhD in Information Engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong, 2008.\nMaster's degree in Communication Engineering from Peking University, 2004.\nBachelor's degree in Electronic Information from Nankai University, 2001.\nProfessional Experiences\nBefore joining CUHK(Shenzhen) in 2015, I had been:\nAssistant Professor at Institute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences, Tsinghua University, from 2012 to 2015.\nPostdoctoral Fellow and Research Associate at the Institute of Network Coding, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, from 2010 to 2012.\nPostdoctoral Fellow at the University of Waterloo, from 2008 to 2009.\nI co-founded n-hop technologies in 2018 to develop coding-based network communication technologies.\nResearch\nMy research is mainly in the area of information theory and coding\ntheory, including their applications in network communication and\ncomputation. Some of research topics we have done are further explained in the following links:\nCoding-based network communication\nNetwork scheduling with delay\nNetwork function computation\nShift-XOR codes\nOptimal finite-length codes\nI am also spending more efforts to theories related to security,\nquantum information, and AI.\nSee my publications listed on\nGoogle Scholar\nand\ndblp\n.\nHiring\nStudents\nFor theoretical research, exceptional mathematical skills (beyond mere knowledge) are essential.\nFor system/experimental research, strong programming and hands-on skills are required.\nNo finantial support available for PhD students in 2026. If you are interested in quantum information, please reach out to\nProf. Masahito Hayashi\n, with whom we are co-supervising PhD students.\nA master's degree is not required for admission to the PhD program. For detailed admission requirements, please visit the\nCUHK(SZ) website\n.\nResearch Assistants\nWe welcome undergraduate students from CUHK(SZ) to participate in our research projects, and they can also earn credits through capstone projects and independent study. We also accept visiting students from other universities who are interested in our PhD program.\nEngineers/Researchers\nn-hop technologies\nis hiring engineers and researchers in developing\nthe next generation of networking technologies. Job opportunities are\navailable for all levels and in both Hong Kong and Shenzhen. Please refer to the\ncorresponding job advertisements for more details, or contact me.\nContact Me\nYou can contact me at shyang@cuhk.edu.cn.\nAuthor: Shenghao Yang\nCreated: 2025-07-25 Fri 11:01\nValidate\n\n---\n\nShenghao Yang's Short Biography\nShenghao Yang's Short Biography\nShenghao Yang holds a B.S. degree from Nankai University (2001), an M.S. degree from Peking University (2004), and a Ph.D. in information engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong (2008). He was a Visiting Student at the Department of Informatics, University of Bergen, Norway, in Spring 2007. He served as a Post-Doctoral Fellow at the University of Waterloo from 2008 to 2009 and at the Institute of Network Coding, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, from 2010 to 2012. From 2012 to 2015, he was affiliated with the Institute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences, Tsinghua University. Since 2015, he has been with The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen, where he currently serves as an Associate Professor. His research interests span network coding, information theory, coding theory, and quantum information.\nAuthor: Shenghao Yang\nCreated: 2025-07-25 Fri 11:01\nValidate\n\n---\n\nShenghao Yang's Short Biography\nShenghao Yang's Short Biography\nShenghao Yang holds a B.S. degree from Nankai University (2001), an M.S. degree from Peking University (2004), and a Ph.D. in information engineering from The Chinese University of Hong Kong (2008). He was a Visiting Student at the Department of Informatics, University of Bergen, Norway, in Spring 2007. He served as a Post-Doctoral Fellow at the University of Waterloo from 2008 to 2009 and at the Institute of Network Coding, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, from 2010 to 2012. From 2012 to 2015, he was affiliated with the Institute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences, Tsinghua University. Since 2015, he has been with The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen, where he currently serves as an Associate Professor. His research interests span network coding, information theory, coding theory, and quantum information.\nAuthor: Shenghao Yang\nCreated: 2025-07-25 Fri 11:01\nValidate"
  },
