    "homepage_text": "英文信息\n访客\n校友\n捐赠\n人才招聘\n内网\n邮箱\n中\nEN\n学院新闻\n综合新闻\n学术科研\n教育教学\n交流合作\nSIGS人物\n媒体聚焦\n学院概况\n院长寄语\n关于我们\n学院简介\n学院沿革\n2023\n2021\n2020\n2019\n2018\n2016\n2011\n2010\n2004\n2003\n2002\n2001\n2000\n现任领导\n院长\n党委书记\n副院长\n党委副书记\n院长助理\n组织机构\n职能部门\n教学科研机构\n信息公开\n联系我们\n学科建设\n教育教学\n师资队伍\n研究生教育\n研究生教育\n学术学位教育\n专业学位教育\n课程与教学\n国际化培养\n授权学科\n奖助体系\n创新创业教育\n中心简介\n特色项目\n品牌活动\n实践\n服务\ni-Space\n在线开放教育\n在线教育\n校园开放课程\n校际共享课程\n科学研究\n科研项目\n科研机构\n政府批建机构\n自主设立机构\n联合共建机构\n科研成果\n技术转移\n大型仪器共享\n招生就业\n硕士招生\n博士招生\n国际学生招生\n在职研究生\n非学位项目\n学生职业发展\n合作交流\n国内合作\n国际合作\n国际合作伙伴\n联合培养\n科研合作\n交流访问\n走进SIGS\n校园生活\n学生活动\n教工活动\n生活在SIGS\n食在SIGS\n住在SIGS\n图书馆\n生活在深圳\n实用信息\n校园交通\n周边交通\n校园参观\n宣传资源\n清华校历\n校园风光\n校园安全与健康\n校园安全求助电话\n校园健康服务\n杨文明\n首页\n杨文明\n英文信息\n首页\n师资队伍\nYang Wenming\nProfessor\n，\nPhD supervisor\nTel:\n+86 (0755) 2603-6461\nEmail:\nyang.wenming@sz.tsinghua.edu.cn\nAddress:\nRoom 2110, Information Building\n个人简历\n教学\n研究领域\n研究成果\n奖励荣誉\nBiography\nEducation\n2003.9-2006.7   Ph.D., Information Science & Electronic Engineering (ISEE), Zhejiang University\n1996.9-2003.9   Bachelor's & Master's, Harbin University of Science and Technology\nProfessional\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tExperience\n2025.12- present   Professor, Institute of Data & Information of Tsinghua SIGS\n2017.06-2017.09   Academic Visitor,  Department of Statistical Sciences of University College London\n2013.12-2025.12  Associate Professor,  Division of Information Sciences/ Institute of Data & Information of Tsinghua SIGS\n2010.1-2013.12     Assistant Professor,  Division of Information Sciences of Tsinghua SIGS\n2008.1-2009.12     PostDoc., Tsinghua University\n2006.7-2007.12     Assistant Professor,  China Jiliang University\nAdditional\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPositions\nIEEE Senior Member\n，\nCAAI\n、\nCSIG\n、\nCCF Member\nOpening\nPersonal Webpage\nDownload CV\nCurrent Courses\n《Digital Image Processing & Its Applications\n》\n《Practices of Digital Image Processing\n》\n《Biomedical & Information Experiments\n》\nMaster’s & Ph.D.\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAdvising\nAs a supervisor, he has guided:\n·11 Tsinghua University Outstanding Master’s Theses (Top 5%)\n·10 Tsinghua University or Beijing Municipal Outstanding Master’s Graduates\n·2 National Outstanding Engineering Master’s Internship Achievement Awardees (approximately 100 selected nationwide annually)\n·2 PhD National Scholarship recipients\n·6 Master’s National Scholarship recipients\n·1 Tsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School (TSIGS) Academic Rising Star (Top 0.1%)\n·1 TSIGS Academic Rising Star Nomination\n·2 TSIGS Professional Practice First Prize winners (ranking 1st institute-wide, Top 0.1%)\n·1 Tsinghua University Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation(co-supervisor)\nRecruitment Information:\nHe admits approximately 6–8 Master’s and PhD students each year. He strongly encourages academic innovation, technology translation, and international exchange or further study. Prospective students with strong foundations in mathematics and English are especially welcome to apply.\nLong-term Openings for Postdoctoral Researchers in the following areas: Computer Vision, Deep Learning, Medical Artificial Intelligence, and AI Large Models.\nResearch\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tInterests\nComputer Vision, Deep Learning, Artificial Intelligence and Multimodal Large Models.\nProjects\nAs project leader or core member, Professor Yang has finished more than 10 scientific research projects including of National key research & development program, National Natural Science Foundation of China, Natural Science Foundation Guangdong Province, Key Natural Science Foundation of Shenzhen, and more than 20 technology development projects including of HUAWEI and DJI companies.\nResearch Output\nHis research primarily focuses on the fields of image processing, computer vision, deep learning, and artificial intelligence. Specific areas include visual enhancement and restoration, visual object perception, visual 3D reconstruction, medical AI, deep learning, reinforcement learning, and multimodal large models (covering foundation models, hallucination, chain-of-thought, AIGC evaluation, and vertical applications). As the Responsible Professor, he spearheaded the creation of the nation’s first full-time Master’s program in Large Model Science and Engineering. As the principal investigator, he has led dozens of research projects, including sub-projects of the National Key R&D Program, the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Young Scientists Fund, General Program), the Royal Society International Collaboration and Exchange Fund (UK), the Postdoctoral Science Foundation, the Guangdong Provincial Natural Science Foundation, the Shenzhen Basic Research General Program and Key Program, the Shenzhen Key Technology R&D Program, internal university funds for young researchers, interdisciplinary research funds, international collaboration funds, as well as commissioned R&D and collaborative projects with leading industry partners such as Huawei, DJI, and State Grid.\nIn recent years, he has published nearly 200 papers in prestigious international journals, including Nature Communications, IEEE TPAMI, TSPM, TIP, TNNLS, TCSVT, TMM, TSMC, JBHI, and Pattern Recognition, as well as at top-tier international conferences such as IEEE/CVF ICCV, CVPR, AAAI, ICML, ICLR, ACM Multimedia, ICASSP, and MICCAI. His Google Scholar citation count exceeds 7,500, with 2 ESI Highly Cited Papers and 1 ESI Hot Paper. He has also served as a guest editor, co-organizing two special issues for the renowned international journals Neurocomputing and Signal Processing: Image Communication.\nAdditionally, he has applied for more than 20 invention patents, several of which have been successfully commercialized, generating significant economic benefits.\nSpecial Issue on Neurocomputing\nTopic\n：\nDeep Learning for Image Super-Resolution\nSpecial Issue on Signal Processing\n：\nImage Communication\nTopic\n：\nAdvances in statistical methods based VQA\nSelected\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPublications\n[1]\nZhehan Kan, Xin Li, Yanlin Liu, Xiaochen Yang, Xinghua Jiang, Yinsong Liu, Deqiang Jiang, Xing Sun, Qingmin Liao,\nWenming Yang\n*\n，\nRAR: Reversing Visual Attention Re-Sinking for Unlocking Potential in Multimodal Large Language Models\n，\nICLR 2026\n(Accepted)\n[2]\nJunyang Ji, Shengjun Zhang, Da Li, Yuxiao Luo, Yan Wang, Di Xu, Biao Yang, Wei Yuan, Fan Yang, Zhihai He\n*\n,\nWenming Yang\n*,\nOmniCVR: A Benchmark for Omni-Composed Video Retrieval with Vision, Audio, and Text\n,\nICLR 2026\n(Accepted)\n[3]\nFan Zhang, Sinchee Chin, Jing-Hao Xue,\nWenming Yang\n*, I\nCDiffAD: Implicit Conditioning Diffusion Model for Time Series Anomaly Detection\n,\nICLR 2026\n(Accepted)\n[4]\nZhun Mou\n,\nBin Xia\n,\nZhengchao Huang\n,\nWenming Yang\n*\n,\nJiaya Jia\n,\nGRADEO: Towards Human-Like Evaluation for Text-to-Video Generation via Multi-Step Reasoning\n,\nICML 2025\n[5]\nYuheng Yang\n,\nYudong Lin\n,\nWenming Yang\n*\n,\nGuijin Wang\n,\nQingmin Liao\n,\nSAP-SLAM: Semantic-Assisted Perception SLAM with 3D Gaussian Splatting\n,\nICRA 2025\n: 8493-8499\n[6]\nBin Xia, Yulun Zhang, Shiyin Wang, Yitong Wang, Xinglong Wu, Yapeng Tian,\nWenming Yang\n*, Radu Timofte, Luc Van Gool: DiffI2I: Efficient Diffusion Model for Image-to-Image Translation,\nIEEE Trans. on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence(IEEE TPAMI\n), 47(3):1578-1593 (2025).\n[7]\nYuan Shi, Bin Xia, Xiaoyu Jin, Xing Wang, Tianyu Zhao, Xin Xia, Xuefeng Xiao,\nWenming Yang\n*: VmambaIR: Visual State Space Model for Image Restoration,\nIEEE Trans. on Circuits Systems & Video Technology(IEEE TCSVT)\n, (2025 Accepted).\n[8]\nFanqi Pu, Yifan Wang, Jiru Deng,\nWenming Yang\n*: MonoDGP: Monocular 3D Object Detection with Decoupled-Query and Geometry-Error Priors,\nCVPR 2025\n(Accepted).\n[9]\nJiaqi Lin, Zhihao Li, Binxiao Huang, Xiao Tang, Jianzhuang Liu, Shiyong Liu, Xiaofei Xu, Fenglong Song,\nWenming Yang\n*: 