  "deep_homepage::Weitong Zhang::https://zeroweight.github.io/": {
    "homepage": "https://zeroweight.github.io/",
    "all_emails": [
      "weitongz@unc.edu"
    ],
    "matched_email": null,
    "github": "https://github.com/ZeroWeight",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/weitong-zhang-382671221",
    "homepage_text": "Weitong Zhang - Weitong Zhang\nWeitong Zhang\nAssistant Professor, School of Data Science and Society\nFollow\nOffice 4401, ITS Manning\nUNC, Chapel Hill\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\nWeitong Zhang\nI’m a tenure track assistant professor at the\nSchool of Data Science and Society\nin\nUniversity of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\n. I received my Ph.D. from\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nUniversity of California, Los Angeles\n. I have been fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Quanquan Gu\n. I received my B.E. form\nDepartment of Automation\n,\nTsinghua University\nand M.Sc. during my Ph.D. career. You can find my latest CV\nhere\n.\nFeel free to booking me an appointment\nmy calendar\nif you would like to talk with me!\nI’m looking forward for collaborations! Please drop me an email if you are interested in my research!\nI’m actively seeking for highly motivated student to work with me:\nProspective interns, Current UNC undergrad / grad students / Postdocs\n: Please fill out\nthis form\n(feel free to skip some optional questions) and/or email me at\nweitongz [at] unc [dot] edu\n.\nResearch Interests\nMy research focuses on reinforcement learning, with applications to modern machine learning models (incl. LLMs, diffusion models) and a deeper understanding of the foundations of exploration . My research goal is to\ndevelop\nand\nunderstand\nreinforcement learning and other machine learning models, with theoretical insights—if not yet fully justified. I am also interested in designing AI agents and learnable models for scientific domains, including (electro)chemistry, physics, molecule science, and more. See my\nResearch\nfor a detailed description.\nRecent News\nLatest Update @ 2025-12\n[2025-11] I received the UNC\nJunior Faculty Development Award\n.\n[2025-11] I have been invited to give a presentation at the\nNew Faculty Highlights\nprogram at AAAI 2026.\n[2025-05] One\nspotlight paper\nhas been accepted to ICML 2025\n[2025-03] We have been awarded an NVIDIA Academic Grant.\n[2024-05] I’ve successfully defended my dissertation (\nslides\n). I appreciate the constant support of all my committee members.\n[2024-04] I will be joining UNC SDSS as a tenure track assistant professor.\n[2023-06] It is my great fortune to have been awarded the UCLA Dissertation Year Fellowship.\nTravel\nI love traveling a lot, here is my first visitation to each state (not including the ‘connection airports’ like Houston\nIAH\n)\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected."
  },
