    "homepage_text": "Xinlu Zhang | Computational Science and Engineering Research Group\nSkip to main content\nComputational Science and Engineering Research Group\nled by Professor Linda Petzold\nXinlu Zhang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nM.S. Statistics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2020\nB.S. Statistics and Mathematics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2018\nMy research interests are in machine learning and data mining. My current research projects are related to natural language processing, time series and multimodal learning in the biomedical area.\nxinluzhang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\n\n---\n\nPeople | Computational Science and Engineering Research Group\nSkip to main content\nComputational Science and Engineering Research Group\nled by Professor Linda Petzold\nPeople\nPrincipal Investigator\nLinda R. Petzold\nMehrabian Distinguished Professor\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering\nDepartment of Computer Science\nCV\nPhone:\n(805) 893-5362\nEmail:\npetzold\n[at]\nengineering\n[dot]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nGraduate Students\nDestinee Cheng\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nXinlu Zhang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nM.S. Statistics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2020\nB.S. Statistics and Mathematics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2018\nMy research interests are in machine learning and data mining. My current research projects are related to natural language processing, time series and multimodal learning in the biomedical area.\nxinluzhang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nAbe Kolko\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Mechanical Engineering, UCSB\nB.S. Physics, UC Santa Barbara, 2018\nMy research focuses on mathematical modeling and simulation. My current project involves modeling sodium flow in the brains of rats and humans, and the impact sodium may have on migraines.\nabush\n[at]\numail\n[dot]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nYuqing Wang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nB.S. Mathematics, University of Minnesota, Twin Cities, 2020\nMy research interest is machine learning, including natural language processing, data mining, and time series analysis.\nwang603\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nDengxian (Dara) Yang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nB.S., University of Washington-Seattle, 2019\nMy research interests are in reinforcement learning and modeling human learning behaviors. I find human's brain activity during learning and decision making fascinating.\ndengxian_yang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nXianjun Yang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nBachelor of Energy and Power Engineering, Tsinghua University, 2019\nMy research is on information extraction and data mining from the text in NLP fields.\nxianjunyang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nAditya Dendukuri\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nFormer members\nJamilah Abdur-Rahim\nMontpellier University\nBen Bales\nColumbia University\nDebjani Banerjee\nStubHub\nGiovanni Bellesia\nUCSB\nAndri Bezzola\nSamsung Audio Lab\nKasturi Bhattacharjee\nAmazon Web Services\nJames Bird\nUniversity of Colorado Boulder\nMatt Buoni\nToyon Corp. and UCSB\nYang Cao\nVirginia Tech\nHan Chen\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nBernie Daigle, Jr.\nUniversity of Memphis\nAbolfazl Doostparast\nColumbia University\nBrian Drawert\nUniversity of North Carolina Asheville\nJin Fu\nGoogle\nHamed Ghaffari\nGilead Sciences\nMahdi Golkaram\nIllumina\nMarc Griesemer\nLawrence Livermore Laboratory\nAndrew Hall\nMIT Lincoln Lab\nChris Homescu\nWachovia Bank\nBruno Jacob\nCarpe Data\nLaurent O. Jay\nUniversity of Iowa\nRichard Jiang\nAccenture\nSotiria Lampoudi\nResonant Inc.\nMike Lawson\nCalifornia Institute of Technology\nHong Li\nTeradata\nShengtai Li\nLos Alamos National Lab\nFengLin Liao\nAirbnb\nRone Kwei Lim\nGreen Hills Software\nGeorge Mathew\niRhythm\nKirsten Meeker\nNaval Air Warfare Center, Point Mugu, CA\nBrian Mitchell\nMadrona Group\nArya Pourzanjani\nForesite Labs\nSoumyendu Raha\nIndian Institute of Science\nMuruhan Rathinam\nUniversity of Maryland-Baltimore County\nMin Roh\nIntellectual Ventures\nKevin Sanft\nUniversity of North Carolina Asheville\nRadu Serban\nUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison\nAndrew P.  Strelzoff\nArmy Corps of Engineers\nAviral Takkar\nMicrosoft\nStephanie Taylor\nColby College\nMichael  Trogdon\nScripps Institute\nSt. Elmo Wilken\nHeinrich Heine University Düsseldorf\nSheng Wu\nGoogle\nTie Bo Wu\nProcore Technologies\nJeng Yen\nJet Propulsion Laboratory\nYuanyang Zhang\nGoogle\nYun Zhao\nFacebook\nZheming  Zheng\nCorning\nLuoding Zhu\nIndiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis\nWenjie Zhu\nGuidant\n\n---\n\nPeople | Computational Science and Engineering Research Group\nSkip to main content\nComputational Science and Engineering Research Group\nled by Professor Linda Petzold\nPeople\nPrincipal Investigator\nLinda R. Petzold\nMehrabian Distinguished Professor\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering\nDepartment of Computer Science\nCV\nPhone:\n(805) 893-5362\nEmail:\npetzold\n[at]\nengineering\n[dot]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nGraduate Students\nDestinee Cheng\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nXinlu Zhang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nM.S. Statistics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2020\nB.S. Statistics and Mathematics, Indiana University, Bloomington, 2018\nMy research interests are in machine learning and data mining. My current research projects are related to natural language processing, time series and multimodal learning in the biomedical area.\nxinluzhang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nAbe Kolko\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Mechanical Engineering, UCSB\nB.S. Physics, UC Santa Barbara, 2018\nMy research focuses on mathematical modeling and simulation. My current project involves modeling sodium flow in the brains of rats and humans, and the impact sodium may have on migraines.\nabush\n[at]\numail\n[dot]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nYuqing Wang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nB.S. Mathematics, University of Minnesota, Twin Cities, 2020\nMy research interest is machine learning, including natural language processing, data mining, and time series analysis.\nwang603\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nDengxian (Dara) Yang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nB.S., University of Washington-Seattle, 2019\nMy research interests are in reinforcement learning and modeling human learning behaviors. I find human's brain activity during learning and decision making fascinating.\ndengxian_yang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nXianjun Yang\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nBachelor of Energy and Power Engineering, Tsinghua University, 2019\nMy research is on information extraction and data mining from the text in NLP fields.\nxianjunyang\n[at]\nucsb\n[dot]\nedu\nAditya Dendukuri\nPh.D. Candidate, Department of Computer Science, UCSB\nFormer members\nJamilah Abdur-Rahim\nMontpellier University\nBen Bales\nColumbia University\nDebjani Banerjee\nStubHub\nGiovanni Bellesia\nUCSB\nAndri Bezzola\nSamsung Audio Lab\nKasturi Bhattacharjee\nAmazon Web Services\nJames Bird\nUniversity of Colorado Boulder\nMatt Buoni\nToyon Corp. and UCSB\nYang Cao\nVirginia Tech\nHan Chen\nHuazhong University of Science and Technology\nBernie Daigle, Jr.\nUniversity of Memphis\nAbolfazl Doostparast\nColumbia University\nBrian Drawert\nUniversity of North Carolina Asheville\nJin Fu\nGoogle\nHamed Ghaffari\nGilead Sciences\nMahdi Golkaram\nIllumina\nMarc Griesemer\nLawrence Livermore Laboratory\nAndrew Hall\nMIT Lincoln Lab\nChris Homescu\nWachovia Bank\nBruno Jacob\nCarpe Data\nLaurent O. Jay\nUniversity of Iowa\nRichard Jiang\nAccenture\nSotiria Lampoudi\nResonant Inc.\nMike Lawson\nCalifornia Institute of Technology\nShengtai Li\nLos Alamos National Lab\nHong Li\nTeradata\nFengLin Liao\nAirbnb\nRone Kwei Lim\nGreen Hills Software\nGeorge Mathew\niRhythm\nKirsten Meeker\nNaval Air Warfare Center, Point Mugu, CA\nBrian Mi