    "homepage_text": "Junjun Jiang – Professor@HIT\n跳至内容\nProfessor@HIT\nJunjun Jiang\nHome\n哈工大主页\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nDr. Junjun Jiang is currently a full Professor in the School of Computer Science and Technology,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\n, Harbin, China. Before that he was a Project Researcher with the\nNational Institute of Informatics\n, Tokyo, Japan. He obtained his Ph.D. from School of Computer,\nWuhan University\n, China, in 2014. His current interests mainly focus on computer vision, image processing and hyperspectral image analysis, etc. He has authored and co-authored more than 100 scientific articles (including TPAMI, IJCV, TIP, TMM, TCSVT, TCYB, TGRS, ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, IJCAI, AAAI, ACM MM, ICASSP, ICIP and ICME). Dr. Jiang is the Associate Editor of Remote Sensing and the Guest Editor of IEEE Access, and has been a reviewer of several journals, including IEEE TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, TMM, TCYB, SPL, and TGRS.\nHe received the 2016 China Computer Federation (CCF) Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award and 2015 ACM Wuhan Doctoral Dissertation Award. He was the recipient of the Finalist of the World’s FIRST 10K Best Paper Award at ICME 2017, the Best Student Paper Runner-up Award at MMM 2015, and the Best Paper Award at IFTC 2018.\nNews!!!\n[Open Positions]\nI am actively looking for self-motivated\nundergraduate/graduate students and visiting students\n(3~5 students per year) to join my research group. Feel free to contact me with your CV if you have a background in one or more of the following areas — image and video processing, computer vision, machine learning. （\n每年招收1~2名博士生，1~3名硕士生，研究方向：图像处理与分析，机器学习与深度学习等\n）\n[\n!!!\n] The sources colleted by me about\nFace-Hallucination-Benchmark\n，\nHyperspectral-Image-Super-Resolution-Benchmark\nand\nHyperspectral-Image-Denoising\nare released.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Decomposition Makes Better Rain Removal: An Improved Attention-guided Deraining Network” was accepted to IEEE TCSVT.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Rapid Whole Slide Imaging via Dual-shot Deep Autofocusing” was accepted to IEEE TCI.\n2020.11, One paper titled “A Progressive Fusion Generative Adversarial Network for Realistic and Consistent Video Super-Resolution” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI. (\ncode\n)\n2020.09, One paper titled “Dual-path Deep Fusion Network for Face Image Hallucination” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.09, One paper titled “Ranking list preservation for feature matching” was accepted to Pattern Recognition.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Robust Face Super-Resolution via Position Relation Model Based on Global Face Context” was accepted to IEEE TIP.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Multilayer Spectral-Spatial Graphs for Label Noisy Robust Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Single Image Deraining via Scale-space Invariant Attention Neural Network” was accepted to ACM MM 2020 (\nOral,\ncode\n).\n2020.07, One paper titled “U2Fusion: A Unified Unsupervised Image Fusion Network” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI.\n2020.06, One paper titled “Geometric Estimation via Robust Subspace Recovery” was accepted to ECCV 2020.\n2020.05, One paper titled “Learning Spatial-Spectral Prior for Super-Resolution of Hyperspectral Imagery” was accepted to IEEE TCI. (paper:\narXiv\n,\nIEEE Xplore\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “Multi-Scale Progressive Fusion Network for Single Image Deraining” was accepted to CVPR 2020. (paper:\narXiv\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “DDcGAN: A Dual-discriminator Conditional Generative Adversarial Network for Multi-resolution Image Fusion” was accepted to IEEE TIP. (\ncode\n)\n2020.01, One paper titled “Adaptive Multi-scale Segmentations for Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TGRS.(The code will be available soon..)\nProfessional Services\nAssociate Editor:\nRemote Sensing\nGuest Editor: IEEE Access, Remote Sensing\nTPC: ACM MM 2018/2019/2020, IJCAI 2018/2021, SDM 2018/2019, ICME 2019/2020, ACM MM Asia 2019, AAAI 2020\nReviewer: IEEE TPAMI/TIP/TMM/TCSVT/TCYB/TIFS/TNNLS/TGRS/TBOIM/TIE/Access/SPL/JSTARS/GRSL, Elsevier CVIU/SP/INS/IF/PR/PRL/Neur./DSP/SPIC; IET CV/IP/Biometrics; Springer SIVP/MTAP, CVPR/ICASSP/ICIP\n隐私和 Cookie：此站点使用 Cookie。继续使用此网站，即表示您同意其使用 Cookie。\n要了解包括如何管控 Cookie 在内的更多信息，请参阅此处：\nCookie 政策\nJunjun Jiang\n注册\n登录\n复制短链接\n举报此内容\n管理订阅\n通过 WordPress.com 设计一个这样的站点\n从这里开始\n\n---\n\nJunjun Jiang – Professor@HIT\n跳至内容\nProfessor@HIT\nJunjun Jiang\nHome\n哈工大主页\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nDr. Junjun Jiang is currently a full Professor in the School of Computer Science and Technology,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\n, Harbin, China. Before that he was a Project Researcher with the\nNational Institute of Informatics\n, Tokyo, Japan. He obtained his Ph.D. from School of Computer,\nWuhan University\n, China, in 2014. His current interests mainly focus on computer vision, image processing and hyperspectral image analysis, etc. He has authored and co-authored more than 100 scientific articles (including TPAMI, IJCV, TIP, TMM, TCSVT, TCYB, TGRS, ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, IJCAI, AAAI, ACM MM, ICASSP, ICIP and ICME). Dr. Jiang is the Associate Editor of Remote Sensing and the Guest Editor of IEEE Access, and has been a reviewer of several journals, including IEEE TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, TMM, TCYB, SPL, and TGRS.\nHe received the 2016 China Computer Federation (CCF) Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award and 2015 ACM Wuhan Doctoral Dissertation Award. He was the recipient of the Finalist of the World’s FIRST 10K Best Paper Award at ICME 2017, the Best Student Paper Runner-up Award at MMM 2015, and the Best Paper Award at IFTC 2018.\nNews!!!\n[Open Positions]\nI am actively looking for self-motivated\nundergraduate/graduate students and visiting students\n(3~5 students per year) to join my research group. Feel free to contact me with your CV if you have a background in one or more of the following areas — image and video processing, computer vision, machine learning. （\n每年招收1~2名博士生，1~3名硕士生，研究方向：图像处理与分析，机器学习与深度学习等\n）\n[\n!!!\n] The sources colleted by me about\nFace-Hallucination-Benchmark\n，\nHyperspectral-Image-Super-Resolution-Benchmark\nand\nHyperspectral-Image-Denoising\nare released.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Decomposition Makes Better Rain Removal: An Improved Attention-guided Deraining Network” was accepted to IEEE TCSVT.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Rapid Whole Slide Imaging via Dual-shot Deep Autofocusing” was accepted to IEEE TCI.\n2020.11, One paper titled “A Progressive Fusion Generative Adversarial Network for Realistic and Consistent Video Super-Resolution” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI. (\ncode\n)\n2020.09, One paper titled “Dual-path Deep Fusion Network for Face Image Hallucination” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.09, One paper titled “Ranking list preservation for feature matching” was accepted to Pattern Recognition.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Robust Face Super-Resolution via Position Relation Model Based on Global Face Context” was accepted to IEEE TIP.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Multilayer Spectral-Spatial Graphs for Label Noisy Robust Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Single Image Deraining via Scale-space Invariant Attention Neural Network” was accepted to ACM MM 2020 (\nOral,\ncode\n).\n2020.07, One paper titled “U2Fusion: A Unified Unsupervised Image Fusion Network” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI.\n2020.06, One paper titled “Geometric Estimation via Robust Subspace Recovery” was accepted to ECCV 2020.\n2020.05, One paper titled “Learning Spatial-Spectral Prior for Super-Resolution of Hyperspectral Imagery” was accepted to IEEE TCI. (paper:\narXiv\n,\nIEEE Xplore\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “Multi-Scale Progressive Fusion Network for Single Image Deraining” was accepted to CVPR 2020. (paper:\narXiv\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “DDcGAN: A Dual-discriminator Conditional Generative Adversarial Network for Multi-resolution Image Fusion” was accepted to IEEE TIP. (\ncode\n)\n2020.01, One paper titled “Adaptive Multi-scale Segmentations for Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TGRS.(The code will be available soon..)\nProfessional Services\nAssociate Editor:\nRemote Sensing\nGuest Editor: IEEE Access, Remote Sensing\nTPC: ACM MM 2018/2019/2020, IJCAI 2018/2021, SDM 2018/2019, ICME 2019/2020, ACM MM Asia 2019, AAAI 2020\nReviewer: IEEE TPAMI/TIP/TMM/TCSVT/TCYB/TIFS/TNNLS/TGRS/TBOIM/TIE/Access/SPL/JSTARS/GRSL, Elsevier CVIU/SP/INS/IF/PR/PRL/Neur./DSP/SPIC; IET CV/IP/Biometrics; Springer SIVP/MTAP, CVPR/ICASSP/ICIP\n隐私和 Cookie：此站点使用 Cookie。继续使用此网站，即表示您同意其使用 Cookie。\n要了解包括如何管控 Cookie 在内的更多信息，请参阅此处：\nCookie 政策\nJunjun Jiang\n注册\n登录\n复制短链接\n举报此内容\n管理订阅\n通过 WordPress.com 设计一个这样的站点\n从这里开始\n\n---\n\nJunjun Jiang – Professor@HIT\n跳至内容\nProfessor@HIT\nJunjun Jiang\nHome\n哈工大主页\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nDr. Junjun Jiang is currently a full Professor in the School of Computer Science and Technology,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\n, Harbin, China. Before that he was a Project Researcher with the\nNational Institute of Informatics\n, Tokyo, Japan. He obtained his Ph.D. from School of Computer,\nWuhan University\n, China, in 2014. His current interests mainly focus on computer vision, image processing and hyperspectral image analysis, etc. He has authored and co-authored more than 100 scientific articles (including TPAMI, IJCV, TIP, TMM, TCSVT, TCYB, TGRS, ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, IJCAI, AAAI, ACM MM, ICASSP, ICIP and ICME). Dr. Jiang is the Associate Editor of Remote Sensing and the Guest Editor of IEEE Access, and has been a reviewer of several journals, including IEEE TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, TMM, TCYB, SPL, and TGRS.\nHe received the 2016 China Computer Federation (CCF) Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award and 2015 ACM Wuhan Doctoral Dissertation Award. He was the recipient of the Finalist of the World’s FIRST 10K Best Paper Award at ICME 2017, the Best Student Paper Runner-up Award at MMM 2015, and the Best Paper Award at IFTC 2018.\nNews!!!\n[Open Positions]\nI am actively looking for self-motivated\nundergraduate/graduate students and visiting students\n(3~5 students per year) to join my research group. Feel free to contact me with your CV if you have a background in one or more of the following areas — image and video processing, computer vision, machine learning. （\n每年招收1~2名博士生，1~3名硕士生，研究方向：图像处理与分析，机器学习与深度学习等\n）\n[\n!!!\n] The sources colleted by me about\nFace-Hallucination-Benchmark\n，\nHyperspectral-Image-Super-Resolution-Benchmark\nand\nHyperspectral-Image-Denoising\nare released.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Decomposition Makes Better Rain Removal: An Improved Attention-guided Deraining Network” was accepted to IEEE TCSVT.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Rapid Whole Slide Imaging via Dual-shot Deep Autofocusing” was accepted to IEEE TCI.\n2020.11, One paper titled “A Progressive Fusion Generative Adversarial Network for Realistic and Consistent Video Super-Resolution” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI. (\ncode\n)\n2020.09, One paper titled “Dual-path Deep Fusion Network for Face Image Hallucination” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.09, One paper titled “Ranking list preservation for feature matching” was accepted to Pattern Recognition.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Robust Face Super-Resolution via Position Relation Model Based on Global Face Context” was accepted to IEEE TIP.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Multilayer Spectral-Spatial Graphs for Label Noisy Robust Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TNNLS.\n2020.08, One paper titled “Single Image Deraining via Scale-space Invariant Attention Neural Network” was accepted to ACM MM 2020 (\nOral,\ncode\n).\n2020.07, One paper titled “U2Fusion: A Unified Unsupervised Image Fusion Network” was accepted to IEEE TPAMI.\n2020.06, One paper titled “Geometric Estimation via Robust Subspace Recovery” was accepted to ECCV 2020.\n2020.05, One paper titled “Learning Spatial-Spectral Prior for Super-Resolution of Hyperspectral Imagery” was accepted to IEEE TCI. (paper:\narXiv\n,\nIEEE Xplore\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “Multi-Scale Progressive Fusion Network for Single Image Deraining” was accepted to CVPR 2020. (paper:\narXiv\n;\ncode\n)\n2020.02, One paper titled “DDcGAN: A Dual-discriminator Conditional Generative Adversarial Network for Multi-resolution Image Fusion” was accepted to IEEE TIP. (\ncode\n)\n2020.01, One paper titled “Adaptive Multi-scale Segmentations for Hyperspectral Image Classification” was accepted to IEEE TGRS.(The code will be available soon..)\nProfessional Services\nAssociate Editor:\nRemote Sensing\nGuest Editor: IEEE Access, Remote Sensing\nTPC: ACM MM 2018/2019/2020, IJCAI 2018/2021, SDM 2018/2019, ICME 2019/2020, ACM MM Asia 2019, AAAI 2020\nReviewer: IEEE TPAMI/TIP/TMM/TCSVT/TCYB/TIFS/TNNLS/TGRS/TBOIM/TIE/Access/SPL/JSTARS/GRSL, Elsevier CVIU/SP/INS/IF/PR/PRL/Neur./DSP/SPIC; IET CV/IP/Biometrics; Springer SIVP/MTAP, CVPR/ICASSP/ICIP\n隐私和 Cookie：此站点使用 Cookie。继续使用此网站，即表示您同意其使用 Cookie。\n要了解包括如何管控 Cookie 在内的更多信息，请参阅此处：\nCookie 政策\nJunjun Jiang\n注册\n登录\n复制短链接\n举报此内容\n管理订阅\n通过 WordPress.com 设计一个这样的站点\n从这里开始\n\n---\n\nJunjun Jiang – Professor@HIT\n跳至内容\nProfessor@HIT\nJunjun Jiang\nHome\n哈工大主页\nGoogle Scholar\nGitHub\nDr. Junjun Jiang is currently a full Professor in the School of Computer Science and Technology,\nHarbin Institute of Technology\n, Harbin, China. Before that he was a Project Researcher with the\nNational Institute of Informatics\n, Tokyo, Japan. He obtained his Ph.D. from School of Computer,\nWuhan University\n, China, in 2014. His current interests mainly focus on computer vision, image processing and hyperspectral image analysis, etc. He has authored and co-authored more than 100 scientific articles (including TPAMI, IJCV, TIP, TMM, TCSVT, TCYB, TGRS, ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, IJCAI, AAAI, ACM MM, ICASSP, ICIP and ICME). Dr. Jiang is the Associate Editor of Remote Sensing and the Guest Editor of IEEE Access, and has been a reviewer of several journals, including IEEE TPAMI, TIP, TCSVT, TMM, TCYB, SPL, and TGRS.\nHe received the 2016 China Computer Federation (CCF) Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation Award and 2015 ACM Wuhan Doctoral Dissertation Award. He was the recipient of the Finalist of the World’s FIRST 10K Best Paper Award at ICME 2017, the Best Student Paper Runner-up Award at MMM 2015, and the Best Paper Award at IFTC 2018.\nNews!!!\n[Open Positions]\nI am actively looking for self-motivated\nundergraduate/graduate students and visiting students\n(3~5 students per year) to join my research group. Feel free to contact me with your CV if you have a background in one or more of the following areas — image and video processing, computer vision, machine learning. （\n每年招收1~2名博士生，1~3名硕士生，研究方向：图像处理与分析，机器学习与深度学习等\n）\n[\n!!!\n] The sources colleted by me about\nFace-Hallucination-Benchmark\n，\nHyperspectral-Image-Super-Resolution-Benchmark\nand\nHyperspectral-Image-Denoising\nare released.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Decomposition Makes Better Rain Removal: An Improved Attention-guided Deraining Network” was accepted to IEEE TCSVT.\n2020.12, One paper titled “Rapid Whole Slide Imaging via Dual-shot Deep Autofocusing” was accepted to IEEE TCI.\n2020.11, One paper titled “A Progressive Fusion Generative Adversarial Netwo...[truncated]"
