    "homepage_text": "Hanqing ZHAO\nHanqing\nZHAO\nImage by\nElir Studio\nð·\nÂ\nPlease refer to the\nCV\npage for contact details.\nHanqing Zhao (he/him/il) is an Assistant Professor (Professeur adjoint) in the\nDÃ©partement de gÃ©nie Ã©lectrique et de gÃ©nie informatique\nof\nUniversitÃ© Laval\n. He is a member of the\nLaboratoire de Vision et SystÃ¨mes NumÃ©riques (LVSN)\n.\nPreviously, he was a Postdoctoral Researcher at the\nMIST Lab\nof\nÃcole Polytechnique de MontrÃ©al\n, supervised by\nGiovanni Beltrame\n.\nHanqing began his academic journey at the\nÃcole Centrale de PÃ©kin\n(\nUniversitÃ© Beihang\n). He earned\nIngÃ©nieur civil en informatique\ndegree from\nÃcole Polytechnique de Bruxelles\n(\nUniversitÃ© libre de Bruxelles\n), supervised by\nMarco Dorigo\n. He interned at\nNokia Bell Labs Antwerp\nwith\nJean-FranÃ§ois Macq\nand\nChristoph Stevens\n. He received Ph.D. in Computer Science (robotics) from\nMcGill University\n, supervised by\nGregory Dudek\nand\nXue Liu\n.\nHis research focuses on enabling robots to accomplish complex tasks while remaining resilient to faults and external disturbances. He leverages machine learning, control theory, and advanced consensus achievement techniques, such as (inverse) reinforcement learning, supervised learning, Blockchain technologies and Control Barrier Functions  to develop robust, (especially multi-)robot systems.\nnews\nOct 01, 2025\nOur paper\nâSwarm Oracle: Trustless Blockchain Agreements through Robot Swarmsâ\nis now available as an\narXiv preprint\n.\nAug 18, 2025\nOur paper\nâA Blockchain Framework for Equitable and Secure Task Allocation in Robot Swarmsâ\nhas been accepted for publication in\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (RA-L)\n,\npreprint version\n.\nJul 01, 2025\nI will be joining UniversitÃ© Laval as a Professeur adjoint (Assistant Professor) in September 2025.\nOct 01, 2024\nI joined MIST Lab at Polytechnique MontrÃ©al as a Postdoctoral Researcher with Giovanni Beltrame, working on multi-robot planning in collaboration with\nQuaze Technologies\n.\nJul 09, 2024\nI defended my Ph.D. dissertation, titled\nTowards Secure Robot Intelligence through\nRewards-based Fault Management\n, at McGill University.\nselected publications\n2025\nRA-L\nA Blockchain Framework for Equitable and Secure Task Allocation in Robot Swarms\nHanqing\n            Zhao\n, Alexandre\n            Pacheco, Giovanni\n            Beltrame, and\n3 more authors\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (RA-L)\n,  2025\nBib\nPDF\nVideo\nCode\n@article\n{\nzhao2025blockchain\n,\ntitle\n=\n{A Blockchain Framework for Equitable and Secure Task Allocation in Robot Swarms}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhao, Hanqing and Pacheco, Alexandre and Beltrame, Giovanni and Liu, Xue and Dorigo, Marco and Dudek, Gregory}\n,\njournal\n=\n{IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (RA-L)}\n,\npages\n=\n{10862-10869}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2025}\n,\npublisher\n=\n{IEEE}\n,\n}\n2023\nIROS\nA Generic Framework for Byzantine-tolerant Consensus Achievement in Robot Swarms\nHanqing\n            Zhao\n, Alexandre\n            Pacheco, Volker\n            Strobel, and\n4 more authors\nIn IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)\n,  2023\nBib\nPDF\nVideo\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhao2023generic\n,\ntitle\n=\n{A Generic Framework for Byzantine-tolerant Consensus Achievement in Robot Swarms}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhao, Hanqing and Pacheco, Alexandre and Strobel, Volker and Reina, Andreagiovanni and Liu, Xue and Dudek, Gregory and Dorigo, Marco}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)}\n,\npages\n=\n{8839--8846}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\norganization\n=\n{IEEE}\n,\n}\nIROS\nZero-Shot Fault Detection for Manipulators Through Bayesian Inverse Reinforcement Learning\nHanqing\n            Zhao\n, Xue\n            Liu, and Gregory\n            Dudek\nIn IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)\n,  2023\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhao2023zero\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Zero-Shot Fault Detection for Manipulators Through Bayesian Inverse Reinforcement Learning}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhao, Hanqing and Liu, Xue and Dudek, Gregory}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)}\n,\npages\n=\n{3582--3589}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2023}\n,\nvolume\n=\n{10}\n,\nissue\n=\n{10}\n,\norganization\n=\n{IEEE}\n,\n}\n2022\nIROS\nBehaviour Learning with Adaptive Motif Discovery and Interacting Multiple Model\nHanqing\n            Zhao\n, Travis\n            Manderson, Hao\n            Zhang, and\n2 more authors\nIn IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)\n,  2022\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhao2022behaviour\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Behaviour Learning with Adaptive Motif Discovery and Interacting Multiple Model}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhao, Hanqing and Manderson, Travis and Zhang, Hao and Liu, Xue and Dudek, Gregory}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{IEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS)}\n,\npages\n=\n{10788--10794}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2022}\n,\norganization\n=\n{IEEE}\n,\n}\n2021\nMMAR\nGeneral Dynamic Neural Networks for the Adaptive Tuning of an Omni-Directional Drive System for Reactive Swarm Robotics\nHanqing\n            Zhao\n, Marco\n            Dorigo, and Michael\n            Allwright\nIn International Conference on Methods and Models in Automation and Robotics (MMAR)\n,  2021\nBib\nPDF\nCode\n@inproceedings\n{\nzhao2021general\n,\ntitle\n=\n{General Dynamic Neural Networks for the Adaptive Tuning of an Omni-Directional Drive System for Reactive Swarm Robotics}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Zhao, Hanqing and Dorigo, Marco and Allwright, Michael}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{International Conference on Methods and Models in Automation and Robotics (MMAR)}\n,\npages\n=\n{79--84}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2021}\n,\norganization\n=\n{IEEE}\n,\n}\n\n---\n\ncv | Hanqing ZHAO\ncv\nBasics\nName\nHanqing Zhao\nHeadline\nAssistant Professor at UniversitÃ© Laval\nEmail\nhanqing.zhao@gel.ulaval.ca\nAddress\n1138-G, Pavillon Adrien-Pouliot (PLT), UniversitÃ© Laval, Sainte-Foy, QC, G1V 0A6, Canada\nWork\n2025.09 - Present\nQuÃ©bec, Canada\nProfesseur adjoint (Assistant Professor)\nUniversitÃ© Laval\nDÃ©partement de gÃ©nie Ã©lectrique et de gÃ©nie informatique\nLaboratoire de Vision et SystÃ¨mes NumÃ©riques (LVSN)\n2024.10 - 2025.08\nMontÃ©al, Canada\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nPolytechnique MontrÃ©al\nMIST Lab\nSupervisor: Giovanni Beltrame\n2018.07 - 2018.11\nAntwerp, Belgium\nResearch Intern\nNokia Bell Labs (Nokia Bell N.V.)\nComputational Perception Group\nSupervisors:  Jean-FranÃ§ois Macq and Christoph Stevens\nTopic: Virtual Reality - Driven Simultaneous Localization and Mapping (SLAM) robotics.\nEducation\n2020.01 - 2024.07\nMontrÃ©al, Canada\nPh.D. in Computer Science (Robotics)\nSchool of Computer Science, McGill University\nExogenous analysis of robot behaviours; Robust consensus and control within robot collectives.\nSupervisors: Gregory Dudek and Xue Liu;\nDissertation: Towards Secure Robot Intelligence through Rewards-based Fault Management.\n2017.09 - 2019.08\nBrussels, Belgium\nIngÃ©nieur Civil en informatique\nÃcole Polytechnique de Bruxelles, UniversitÃ© libre de Bruxelles\nAvec la plus grande distinction (with Summa Cum Laude)\nSupervisor: Marco Dorigo;\nTopic: Design and control of an omnidirectional swam robot platform for collaborative construction.\n2013.09 - 2017.07\nBeijing, China\nFormation d'ingÃ©nieur w/ B.S. in Mathematics and Applied Mathmatics\nÃcole Centrale de PÃ©kin, UniversitÃ© Beihang\nResearch supervisor: Zengchang Qin;\nTopic: Machine Learning, Music Information Retrieval, Uncertainty Modelling.\nAwards\n2019.12.01\nPrix dâExcellence Philippe Smets\nAssociation Royale des IngÃ©nieurs Sortis de lâUniversitÃ© Libre de Bruxelles (A.Ir.Br.)\nAward for the top of class in IngÃ©nieur Civil en informatique program at Ãcole Polytechnique de Bruxelles.\n2021.04.30\nBourse de doctorat en recherche (B2X)\nFonds de Recherche