    "homepage_text": "Qi Chu's Homepage\nQi Chu\nå¨ çª\nAssociate Professor\nSchool of Cyber Science and Technology\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n443 Huangshan Road, Hefei, China 230027\nEmail:\nqchu@ustc.edu.cn\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nBiography\nI am currently an Associate Professor at Visual Intelligence and Security (VIS) research group in University of Science and Technology of China (USTC). \n\t\tI received the B.S. degree and the Ph.D. degree from the University of Science and Technology of China (USTC) in 2014 and 2019, respectively.\n\t\tDuring my PhD, I was a visiting student at the\nMultimedia Laboratory\nof the Chinese University of Hong Kong from 2016 to 2017.\n\t\tMy research interest includes deep learning, computer vision and artificial intelligence security.\nNews\n2025/6/26: Our paper on anomaly detection has been accepted by ICCV 2025!\n2025/3/21: Our paper on adversarial examples detection has been accepted by ICME 2025!\n2025/2/27: Our paper on in-context segmentation has been accepted by CVPR 2025!\n2024/12/10: Two papers have been accepted by AAAI 2025!\n2024/10/20: Our paper on audio-visual videl segmentation has been accepted by TCSVT!\n2024/10/10: Our paper on infrared small target detection has been accepted by TGRS!\n2024/10/3: Our paper on monocular 3D object detection has been accepted by TPAMI!\n2024/9/20: Our paper on LLM knowledge injection has been accepted by EMNLP Findings!\n2024/8/20: Our paper on infrared small target detection has been accepted by TGRS!\n2024/3/28: Our paper on image completion has been accepted by TPAMI!\n2024/2/27: Our paper on in-context visual understanding has been accepted by CVPR 2024!\n2024/2/3: One paper has been accepted by TIP!\n2024/1/16: One paper has been accepted by ICLR 2024!\n2023/12/14: Two papers have been accepted by ICASSP 2024!\n2023/12/9: Three papers have been accepted by AAAI 2024!\n2023/8/17: Our paper on Person Re-identification has been accepted by TMM!\n2023/4/25: One paper has been accepted by ICML 2023!\n2023/4/20: Our paper on Infrared Small Target Detection has been accepted by IJCAI 2023(acceptance rate: 15%)!\n2023/3/13: Our paper on Infrared Small Target Detection has been accepted by ICME 2023!\n2023/2/16: Four papers have been accepted by ICASSP 2023!\n2022/12/14: Our paper on face forgery detection has been accepted by TIFS!\n2022/09/22: Our paper on semantic image synthesis has been accepted by TPAMI!\n2022/07/18: Our paper on face forgery detection has been accepted by TIFS!\n2022/07/04: Two papers have been accepted by ECCV 2022!\n2022/03/06: Our paper on face forgery detection has been accepted by ICME 2022!\n2022/03/02: Our paper on image inpainting has been accepted by CVPR 2022!\n2022/01/02: Our paper on multi-object tracking has been accepted by Neurocomputing!\n2021/10/26: Our paper\nAutoMA\non adversarial attacks has been accepted by TMM!\n2021/09/30:\nOur paper\non Deepfake detection has been accepted by TBIOM!\n2021/07/23: Four papers have been accepted to ICCV 2021!\n2021/04/20: Our paper\nCLADE\non semantic image synthesis has been accepted by TPAMI!\n2021/03/06: Two papers have been accepted to ICME 2021!\n2021/03/01: Our paper on semantic image synthesis has been accepted to CVPR 2021!\n2020/12/02: Two papers have been accepted to AAAI 2021!\n2020/10/09: Our paper\nSAFNet\non object detection has been accepted by TIP!\n2020/04/20: Our paper\nGSM\non multi-object tracking has been accepted by IJCAI 2020 (acceptance rate: 12.6%)!\n2020/03/31: Our paper MichiGAN on conditioned hair image generation has been accepted to SIGGRAPH 2020!\n2020/02/24: Two papers have been accepted to CVPR 2020!\n2020/01/28:\nOur paper\non video object segmentation has been accepted to TCSVT!\nEducation\nPh. D., 2014 - 2019, Information and Communication Engineering,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nReaserch Assistant, 2016 - 2017,\nMultimedia Laboratory\n,\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\nB. Eng., 2010 - 2014, Electronic Information Engineering,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nWork Experience\nAssociate Professor, Apr. 2024 - Present,  School of Cyber Science and Technology,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nAssociate Research Fellow, Aug. 2021 - Mar. 2024,  School of Cyber Science and Technology,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nPostdoctoral Fellow, Jul. 2019 - Jul. 2021,  School of Cyber Science and Technology,\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nAwards & Competitions\nTeam Member, Winner of\nImageNet Video Object Detection/Tracking Challenge with provided data\n, 2016\nPublications\n2024\nTransformer based Pluralistic Image Completion with Reduced Information Loss\nQiankun Liu, Yuqi Jiang, Zhentao Tan, Dongdong Chen, Ying Fu,\nQi Chu\n, Gang Hua, Nenghai Yu.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(\nTPAMI\n), early access.\nExploring the Application of Large-scale Pre-trained Models on Adverse Weather Removal\nZhentao Tan, Yue Wu, Qiankun Liu,\nQi Chu\n, Le Lu, Jieping Ye, Nenghai Yu.\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n(\nTIP\n), vol. 33, pp. 1683-1698.\nTowards More Unified In-context Visual Understanding\nDianmo Sheng, Dongdong Chen, Zhentao Tan, Qiankun Liu,\nQi Chu\n, Jianmin Bao, Tao Gong, Bin Liu, Shengwei Xu, Nenghai Yu.\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n), accepted.\nBoosting Vanilla Lightweight Vision Transformers via Re-parameterization\nZhentao Tan, Xiaodan Li, Yue Wu,\nQi Chu\n, Le Lu, Nenghai Yu, Jieping Ye.\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(\nICLR\n), accepted.\nTCI-Former: Thermal Conduction-Inspired Transformer for Infrared Small Target Detection\nTianxiang Chen, Zhentao Tan,\nQi Chu\n, Yue Wu, Bin Liu, and Nenghai Yu.\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n(\nAAAI\n), accepted.\nMotionGPT: Finetuned LLMs Are General-Purpose Motion Generators\nYaqi Zhang, Di Huang, Bin Liu, Shixiang Tang, Ya