    "linkedin": "https://cn.linkedin.com/in/chen-minghai-2223b173",
    "homepage_text": "Yukun Chen\nYukun Chen\nHome\nNotes\nLinks\nProf. James Z. Wang\nProf. Jia Li\nJianbo Ye\nYukun Chen\nYukun Chen (\n陈昱坤\n)\nResearch Scientist @ Facebook\nEmail: cykustc (at) gmail.edu\nAddress: 1 Hacker Way\nMenlo Park, CA, 94025\nBiography\nCurrently, I work as a research scientist at Facebook. I graduated with Ph.D. from\nCollege of Information Sciences and Technology\n(with minor in\nstatistics\n), The Pennsylvania State University in May 2020. I have been advised by\nProf. James Z. Wang\nand\nProf. Jia Li\nat\nIIS research lab\n. My research interests mostly lie in computer vision, multimedia and machine learning. Before that, I received my B.Sc. degree in Applied Physics from\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\nin June 2014.\nExperiences\nSoftware Engineering Intern at\nFacebook\n, (Mentored by\nMinghai Chen\n) Summer 2019\nSoftware Engineering Intern at\nFacebook\n, (Mentored by\nSatish Chandra\nand\nSwarat Chaudhuri\n) Summer 2018\nSoftware Engineering Intern at\nGoogle\n, (Mentored by\nHongbo Deng\nand\nXuanhui Wang\n) Summer 2017\nTeaching Assistant for DS340W Applied Data Sciences, Spring 2018 (Taught by\nProf. James Z. Wang\nand\nProf. Jia Li\n)\nTeaching Assistant for IST816 Web Fundamentals, Fall 2015 (Taught by\nProf. Jim Jensen\n)\nResearch Assistant,\nThe Intelligent Information Systems Research Lab, IST@PSU\n, Sept 2014-Present\nGrading Assistant for IST230 Discrete Mathematics, Fall 2014 (Taught by\nProf. James Z. Wang\n)\nResearch Assistant,\nDepartment of Physics\n, Oxford University, supervised by\nProf. Radu Coldea\nJune 2013-Sept 2013\nResearch Assistant,\nInstitute of Physics\n, Chinese Academy of Science, July 2012\nSelected Publications\nAI-PLAX: AI-based Placental Assessment and Examination using Photos\nYukun Chen\n, Zhuomin Zhang, Chenyan Wu, Dolzodmaa Davaasuren, Jeffery A. Goldstein, Alison D. Gernand and James Z. Wang.\nComputerized Medical Imaging and Graphics, 2020 (accepted)\nMEBOW: Monocular Estimation of Body Orientation In the Wild\nChenyan Wu,\nYukun Chen\n, Jiajia Luo, Che-Chun Su, Anuja Dawane, Bikramjot Hanzra, Zhuo Deng, Bilan Liu, James Z. Wang and Cheng-hao Kuo.\nCVPR 2020\n(poster)\nAI-based Rapid Placental Assessment Tool.\nAlison D. Gernand, Jeffery A. Goldstein, W. Tony Parks,\nYukun Chen\n, Zhuomin Zhang, Dolzodmaa Davaasuren, Chenyan Wu, Celeste Beck, Leigh Taylor and James Z. Wang.\nPlacenta\n, vol. 83, pp. e84-e85, 2019. (Presented at the International Federation of Placenta Associations Meeting, Buenos Aires, Argentina, September 2019)\nPlacentaNet: Automatic Morphological Characterization of Placenta Photos with Deep Learning.\ncoverage:\nPenn State News\neurekalert.org\n[pdf]\nYukun Chen\n, Chenyan Wu, Zhuomin Zhang, Jeffery A. Goldstein, Alison D. Gernand, James Z. Wang.\nMICCAI 2019\nAggregated Wasserstein Distance and State Registration for Hidden Markov Models.\n[an outdated arxiv version]\nYukun Chen\n, Jianbo Ye, Jia Li.\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, 2019 (accepted)\nDetecting Comma-shaped Clouds for Severe Weather Forecasting using Shape and Motion\n[pdf]\n, [Press coverage:\nphys.org\nScienceDaily\n]\nXinye Zheng, Jianbo Ye,\nYukun Chen\n, Stephen Wistar, Jia Li, Jose A. Piedra-Fernandez, Michael A. Steinberg and James Z. Wang.\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, 2019\nA Distance for HMMs based on Aggregated Wasserstein Metric and State Registration.\n[code]\n[slides]\n[poster]\nYukun Chen\n, Jianbo Ye, Jia Li.\nECCV 2016\n, (\nSpotlight\n, Acceptance rate 45/1561=2.9%)\nCourses\nFall 2016 Algorithm Design and Analysis (Taught by\nProf. Sofya Raskhodnikova\n)\nSpring 2016 Numerical Optimization Techniques (Taught by\nProf. Barlow Jesse Louis\n)\nSpring 2016 Statistical Inference (Taught by\nProf. Bing Li\n)\nSpring 2016 Operating System (Taught by\nProf. Trent Jaeger\n)\nFall 2015 Machine Learning: Tools and Algorithms (Taught by\nProf. Dan Kifer\n)\nFall 2015 Deep-learning for Pattern Discovery (Taught by\nProf. Yanxi Liu\n)\nFall 2015 Principles of Artificial Intelligence (Taught by\nProf. Honavar, Vasant Gajanan\n)\nFall 2015 Statistical Computing (Taught by\nProf. Murali Haran\n)\nSpring 2015 Stochastic Process and Monte Carlo (Taught by\nProf. Murali Haran\n)\nSpring 2015 Foundations of Human Centered Design (Taught by\nProf. John M. Carroll\n)\nSpring 2015 Computational Informatics (Taught by\nProf. John Yen\n)\nFall 2014 Data Mining (Taught by\nProf. Jia Li\n)\nFall 2014 Foundations of Social Informatics\nFall 2014 Information Science Research Methods\nDesigned by\nYukun Chen\nusing\njemdoc\n. Last updated at 2020-06-22 23:10:33 PDT."
