    "homepage_text": "Kevin Yao\nYuanshun (Kevin) Yao\nEmail: kevinyaowork [at] gmail.com\n[Resume]\n[Google Scholar]\n[LinkedIn]\nI'm an AI researcher at Meta Superintelligence Labs, working on AI agents and AI safety.\nPreviously, I was a researcher at ByteDance Research, working on LLM alignment\n  and trustworthy AI.\nI received my PhD in Computer Science from the University of Chicago,\nadvised by Prof. Ben Zhao and Prof. Heather Zheng, working on AI safety. Before that,\nI got three B.S. degrees in Computer Science, Mathematics, and Statistics from the\nUniversity of Minnesota Twin Cities. I interned at Google twice and received\nthe Siebel Scholarship.\nI sometimes write for myself to help me figure things out and have fun.\nWriting\nDifferent Ways to Look at the World\nCan You Predict the Future in Investment?\nMental Discipline\nMunger the Stoic\nHow Does Self-Improvement Work?\nWhat Do Pragmatists Look Like?\nWhat Makes Great Value Investors Admirable?\n\n---\n\nIndex of /cv/\nIndex of /cv/\nName\nLast Modified\nSize\nParent Directory\nresume.pdf\n2025-09-15 02:06\n41k\nProudly Served by LiteSpeed Web Server at www.kevyao.com Port 443"
  },
  "deep_homepage::David Alvarez-Melis::https://dmelis.github.io": {
    "homepage": "https://dmelis.github.io",
