    "homepage_text": "Luc Rey-Bellet Home Page - Luc Rey-Bellet Homepage\nLuc Rey-Bellet Homepage\nResearch Interests\nStatistical Mechanics, Applied Probability, Game Theory, Uncertainty Quantification, and Machine Learning.\nA detailed\nCV\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch Gate\nArxiv\nMathscinet\nOrcid\nGrant support\nNSF 2003($101K), 2006($106K), 2010($99K), 2015($280K), 2020($370K), 2023($300K)\nAFOSR 2019($900K), 2021($1.950M)\nDOE 2016($900K)\nParadise Pound at Smith College, Northampton, 06/11/2025\nAcademic appointments\n1998-1999: Postdoctoral Researcher, Rutgers University\n1999-2002: Whyburn Instructor, University of Virginia\n2002-2008: Assistant Professor, UMass Amherst\n2008-2013: Associate Professor, UMass Amherst\nSince 2013: Professor, UMass Amherst\nEducation\nDipl. Phys. (1994),\nEidgenössiche Technische Hochschule Zürich\nPh.D in Mathematics (1998),\nUniversité de Genève\nContact information\nMailing Address\n:\nDepartment of Mathematics & Statistics\nLederle Graduate Research Tower\nUniversity of Massachusetts\n710 N. Pleasant Street\nAmherst, MA 01003-9305, USA\nOffice:\nLGRT 1423 K\nOffice Phone:\n413 545 6020\nEmail:\nluc@cns.umass.edu\nor\nluc.reybellet@gmail.com\nWebsite:\nhttps://luc-umass.github.io\n\n---\n\nLuc Rey-Bellet Home Page - About\nAbout\nAbout this site\n\n---\n\nLuc Rey-Bellet Home Page - About\nAbout\nAbout this site"
