    "homepage_text": "Ningyi Liao\nSearch\nNingyi Liao\nBiography\nI am a Ph.D candidate at the\nCollege of Computing and Data Science\n,\nNanyang Technological University\n, Singapore, supervised by\nProf. Siqiang Luo\n. My research interest lies in graph learning and efficient machine learning, particularly scalable graph neural networks.\nBefore joining NTU, I received my B.Eng. degree in Computer Science from\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\n, where I conducted research with\nProf. Liyao Xiang\nat the\nJohn Hopcroft Center for Computer Science\n. I also interned at\nJD Digits (now JD Technology)\n.\nFeatured Publications\nSIGMOD 2026\n|\nPREMIA Award\nA Comprehensive Benchmark on Spectral GNNs: The Impact on Efficiency, Memory, and Effectiveness\nA comprehensive benchmark on spectral GNNs relating efficiency and effectiveness.\nICML 2025\nUnifews: You Need Fewer Operations for Efficient Graph Neural Networks\nTheoretical spectral bounds for GNN propagation and transformation sparsification.\nVLDB 2024\n|\nPREMIA Award\nGENTI: GPU-powered Walk-based Subgraph Extraction for Scalable Representation Learning on Dynamic Graphs\nA GPU-oriented subgraph representation learning algorithm on dynamic data.\nNeurIPS 2023\nLD²: Scalable Heterophilous Graph Neural Network with Decoupled Embeddings\nA scalable heterophilous GNN with lightweight minibatch training.\nVLDB 2022\nSCARA: Scalable Graph Neural Networks with Feature-Oriented Optimization\nA feature-oriented GNN that scales to billion-scale extremely large graphs.\nPublications\n*\nAll\nGraph Algorithm\nNeural Network\nScalability & Efficiency\nA Comprehensive Benchmark on Spectral GNNs: The Impact on Efficiency, Memory, and Effectiveness\nSIGMOD 2026\n|\nPREMIA Award\nIn\nProceedings of the ACM on Management of Data\n, 3(4): №238\nNingyi Liao\n,\nHaoyu Liu\n,\nZulun Zhu\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nLaks V.S. Lakshmanan\nUnifews: You Need Fewer Operations for Efficient Graph Neural Networks\nICML 2025\nIn\n42nd International Conference on Machine Learning\nNingyi Liao\n,\nZihao Yu\n,\nRuixiao Zeng\n,\nSiqiang Luo\nAdvances in Designing Scalable Graph Neural Networks: The Perspective of Graph Data Management\nSIGMOD 2025\nTutorial\nIn\nACM 2025 International Conference on Management of Data\n: 844–850\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nXiaokui Xiao\n,\nReynold Cheng\nGENTI: GPU-powered Walk-based Subgraph Extraction for Scalable Representation Learning on Dynamic Graphs\nVLDB 2024\n|\nPREMIA Award\nIn\nProceedings of the VLDB Endowment\n, 17(9): 2269–2278\nZihao Yu\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\nScalable Decoupling Graph Neural Networks with Feature-Oriented Optimization\nThe VLDB Journal\n33(3): 667–683\nNingyi Liao\n,\nDingheng Mo\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nXiang Li\n,\nPengcheng Yin\nLD²: Scalable Heterophilous Graph Neural Network with Decoupled Embeddings\nNeurIPS 2023\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 36\n: 10197–10209\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nXiang Li\n,\nJieming Shi\nSCARA: Scalable Graph Neural Networks with Feature-Oriented Optimization\nVLDB 2022\nIn\nProceedings of the VLDB Endowment\n, 15(11): 3240–3248\nNingyi Liao\n,\nDingheng Mo\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nXiang Li\n,\nPengcheng Yin\nAchieving Adversarial Robustness via Sparsity\nMachine Learning\n111: 685–711\nNingyi Liao\n,\nShufan Wang\n,\nLiyao Xiang\n,\nNanyang Ye\n,\nShuo Shao\n,\nPengzhi Chu\nSIGMA: An Efficient Heterophilous Graph Neural Network with Fast Global Aggregation\nICDE 2025\nIn\nIEEE 41th International Conference on Data Engineering\n: 1924–1937\nHaoyu Liu\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\nMachine Learning for Subgraph Extraction: Methods, Applications and Challenges\nVLDB 2023\nTutorial\nIn\nProceedings of the VLDB Endowment\nTutorial, 16(12): 3864–3867\nKai Siong Yow\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nReynold Cheng\nExample Searcher: A Spatial Query System via Example\nICDE 2023\nDemo\nIn\nIEEE 39th International Conference on Data Engineering\n: 3635–3638\nJun Xuan Yew\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nDingheng Mo\n,\nSiqiang Luo\nHiding in the Network: Attribute-Oriented Differential Privacy for Graph Neural Networks\nTIFS 2025\nIn\nIEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security\n20(2025): 7998–8013\nYuxin Qi\n,\nXi Lin\n,\nJiani Zhu\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nJianhua Li\nA Survey on Machine Learning Solutions for Graph Pattern Extraction\narXiv:2204.01057\nKai Siong Yow\n,\nNingyi Liao\n,\nSiqiang Luo\n,\nReynold Cheng\n,\nChenhao Ma\n,\nXiaolin Han\nScaling up Graph Neural Networks\nPhD Confirmation for Admission Report\nNingyi Liao\nNetwork Compression in Federated Machine Learning\nBachelor Thesis\nNingyi Liao\nSCARA: Scalable Graph Neural Networks with Feature-Oriented Optimization\nSingapore Provisional\nNo. 10202203849U\nNingyi Liao\n,\nDingheng Mo\n,\nSiqiang Luo\nTalks\nAdvances in Designing Scalable Graph Neural Networks: The Perspective of Graph Data Management – Specific Algorithms\nTutorial-1,\n2025 International Conference on Management of Data\nJun 22, 2025 09:00 — 12:30\nBerlin, Germany\nScalable Heterophilous Graph Neural Network with Decoupled Embeddings\nSingapore ACM SIGKDD Symposium 2024\nJul 31, 2024 14:45 — 15:00\nSMU, Singapore\nMachine Learning for Subgraph Extraction: Methods, Applications and Challenges – Community Detection & Maximum Common Subgraph\nTutorial-6,\n49th International Conference on Very Large Databases\nAug 31, 2023 10:30 — 12:00\nVancouver, Canada\nAwards\nPREMIA Best Student Paper Awards, Certificate of Commendation\n2025\nPREMIA, Singapore (2 nationwide)\nPREMIA Best Student Paper Awards, Certificate of Merit\n2024\nPREMIA, Singapore (3 nationwide)\nNTU Research Scholarship\n2021\n– 2025\nNanyang Technological University\nEducation\nPh.D. Candidate\nNanyang Technological University\nAugust 2021 –\nPresent\nSingapore\nB.Eng. in Computer Science\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nSeptember 2017 –\nJune 2021\nShanghai, China\nExchange Program\nUniversity of California, Berkeley\nJuly 2019 –\nAugust 2019\nBerkeley, CA, U.S.\nServices\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant\nCZ3002 Advanced Software Engineering\n｜\nNTU 2022 Fall & 2023 Spring\nTeaching Assistant\nCZ4123 Big Data Management\n｜\nNTU 2022 Spring & 2023 Spring\nAcademia Services\nPC Member\nNeurIPS\n2024–2025\n, AISTATS\n2025–26\n, CIKM (Full & Short)\n2022–2025\n, IEEE BigData\n2025\nReviewer\nTNNLS\n2025\n, TJSC\n2025\nVolunteer\nWWW\n2024\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
