    "github": "https://github.com/xuyanwu",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yanwu Xu - Personal Homepage\nHi, I'm Yanwu Xu\nWorking on Generative Something (models and food)\nShort Bio\nMy name is Yanwu Xu, and I currently work at Google Cloud, where I focus on on-device generative models, including text-to-image and text-to-video generation. Prior to joining Google, I was a Research Scientist at Snap Inc.,\n  developing efficient generative models optimized for on-device applications. I earned my Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering from Boston University, under the guidance of\nDr. Kayhan Batmanghelich\nand co-advised by\nDr. Mingming Gong\n. Prior to my current endeavors, I earned an M.S. degree from the Intelligent System Program at the University of Pittsburgh in 2022.\nBlog\nCongrats on our\non-device text2image generative model\naccepted by CVPR2025. In this work, we proposed a super efficient text2image Unet model for generation on device.\nNews\nTwo papers accepted by\nCVPR2025\n.\nOne paper accepted by\nCVPR2024\n.\nOne paper accepted by\nNeurIPS2023\n.\nOne paper accepted by\nICCV2023\n.\nOne paper accepted by\nMICCAI2022\n.\nI will start my 2022 summer internship at\nGoogle\n.\nOne papers is accepted by\nCVPR 2022\n.\nOne papers is accepted by\nACM 2021\n.\nOne papers is accepted by\nICCV 2021\n.\nTwo papers are accepted by\nAAAI 2020\n.\nOne paper is accepted by\nNeurIPS 2019\n.\nOne paper is accepted by\nBraTS Challenge 2018\n.\nOne paper is accepted by\nACCV 2018\n."
  },
