Eriksson Teaching Award, KTH\n2006\nHonourable mention, Gerd Eriksson Teaching Award, KTH\nProfessional memberships\n2021\nâ\nScholar, European Laboratory for Learning and Intelligent Systems (ELLIS)\nService\nOrganising committee\n2023 Senior area chair, 17th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics\n2022 Organiser, First Workshop on Dynamic Adversarial Data Collection (DADC) at the 2022 Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies\n2020 Organiser, Human And Machine in-the-Loop Evaluation and Learning Strategies Workshop at Thirty-fourth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2020)\n2022 Area chair, 2022 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2022)\n2022 Area chair, 2022 Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (NAACL 2022)\n2021 Area chair, 2021 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2021)\n2021 Area chair, 2021 Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (NAACL 2021)\n2020 Area chair, 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2020)\n2019 Publication chair, 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2019)\n2019 Area chair, 57th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL 2019)\n2019 Executive chair, JuliaCon 2019\n2018 Local chair, JuliaCon 2018\n2017 Handbook proofreader, 2017 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP 2017)\n2016 Programme chair, JuliaCon 2016\n2013 Organiser, BioNLP Shared Task\n2011 Organiser, BioNLP Shared Task\nProgramme committee\n2023 17th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (EACL 2023)\n2022 60th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational (ACL 2022)\n2021