    "homepage_text": "Biography - Hongyu Gong’s Homepage\nHongyu Gong\nI'm a research scientist at Facebook AI\nFollow\nSeattle, Washington\nResearchGate\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nBiography\nI am currently a research scientist at Facebook AI Research (FAIR) working on Natural Language Processing (NLP). I earned my Ph.D. degree from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC) with Natural Language Processing as my research area. My research interest lies in language representation learning and text generation. I am lucky to be advised by my Ph.D. advisors Prof. Pramod Viswanath and Prof. Suma Bhat. Prior to my graduate study at UIUC, I got my Bachelor’s degree from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in China, where I was in IEEE pilot class and advised by Prof. Xinbing Wang.\nRecent News\nCheck out my recent research interest\nhere\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nRedirecting…\nRedirecting…\nClick here if you are not redirected.\n\n---\n\nCV - Hongyu Gong’s Homepage\nHongyu Gong\nI'm a research scientist at Facebook AI\nFollow\nSeattle, Washington\nResearchGate\nTwitter\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nCV\nEducation\nPh.D in Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, 2017-2020\nM.S. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, 2015-2017\nB.S in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, 2011-2015\nWork Experience\nResearch intern at Facebook AI, Menlo Park, Summer 2019\nResearch intern at Tencent AI Lab, Bellevue, Spring 2019\nResearch intern at IBM Thomas J. Watson Research Center, New York, Summer 2017\nAcademic Services\nProgram Committee Member\nSenior Area Chair of ACL Rolling Review (\nARR\n)\nAnnual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nNAACL-2021\n)\nThe European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nEACL-2021\n)\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL-2020\n,\nACL-2019\n)\nThe Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (\nEMNLP-2021\n,\nEMNLP-2020\n)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI-22\n,\nAAAI-21\n,\nAAAI-20\n)\nThe European Conference on Machine Learning and Principles and Practice of Knowledge Discovery in Databases (\nECML-PKDD 2020\n)\nThe International Workshop on Deep Learning on Graphs (\nDLG-AAAI 2021\n,\nDLG-KDD 2020\n)\nThe Workshop on Representation Learning for NLP (\nRepL4NLP-2021\n,\nRepL4NLP-2020\n)\nThe Workshop on Figurative Language Processing (\nFigLang 2020\n)\nBiennial Machine Translation Summit (\nMT Summit-2021\n)\nReviewer\nInternational Journal of Intelligent Systems\nThe 41st European Conference on Information Retrieval (ECIR 2019)\nThe ACM Transactions on Sensor Networks (TOSN)\nIEEE 37th International Conference on Distributed Computing Systems (ICDCS 2017)"
